(comment NetworkInformationSystem "The collection of all Network Information Systems (NIS).  A type of #$DistributedDatabaseSystem. NIS is the most common implementation of a DistributedDatabaseSystem in Unix -type environments. It provides access to centrally managed configuration files that contain information about such things as passwords and hostnames. NIS was developed by SunMicrosystemsInc, who called the system \"Yellow Pages\" -- hence many of the programs that are used to manage NIS have names that begin with the string \"yp\". ")
