(comment generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN) is an appropriate formula, along with any well-formed other substitutions of other elements of SET into that formula, provided SET is an extensional set.")
(comment generateFormulasForElements-TermIsa "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermIsa TERM SET) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  The appropriate formula, at this point is determined by whether INS is a collection or a predicate.  If INS is a collection, then (#$isa ?X INS) is the appropriate formula.  If INS is a predicate with arity N, then (INS ?VAR1, ..., VARN) is an appropriate formula, along with any well-formed other substitutions of other elements of SET into that formula, provided SET is an extensional set.")
(comment InfectionDueToFn "(#$InfectionDueToFn ORG-TYPE) returns the collection of infections that are caused by organisms of the type ORG-TYPE. See
#$pathogenSoleCauseOfInfectionType.")
(comment forwardParseNounCompound "(#$forwardParseNounCompound MODIFIER HEAD) means that the string '<MODIFIER> <HEAD>' should be parsed as a noun compound, with the results cached in the KB.")
(comment inferenceRuleForNounCompoundRule "(#$inferenceRuleForNounCompoundRule NCR RULE) means that RULE is a CycL rule assertion that can be used to parse essentially the same noun compounds using the #$CycInferenceEngine as NCR can using the #$CycNounCompoundParser.")
