(comment statusCanAffectStatus "<code>(#$statusCanAffectStatus IND1 IND2)</code> means that the status of individual <code>IND1</code> can affect the status of individual <code>IND2</code>.  This is a very general predicate, meant to capture status dependencies across a wide range of sorts of things.")
(comment MissilePrecisionInstrumentationRadar "A specialization of #$RadarDevice (q.v.).  Each instance of #$MissilePrecisionInstrumentationRadar is a radar that can track missiles.")
(comment RadarAntenna-Parabolic "A specialization of #$BroadcastAntenna, #$ReceivingAntenna and #$ParabolicAntenna.  Each instance of #$RadarAntenna-Parabolic is a parabolic antenna that can be used to send and receive radar signals.")
(comment representationalImageForTermImagePathname "(#$representationalImageForTermImagePathname THING PATHNAME) means that PATHNAME is a pathname (i.e. a designator for a directory or a file) that contains a representational image (e.g. a photograph or representational painting) of THING.")
(comment functionalDiagramImageForTermImagePathname "(#$functionalDiagramImageForTermImagePathname THING PATHNAME) means that PATHNAME is a pathname (i.e. a designator for a directory or a file) that contains a diagram representing the functional structure of THING.")
(comment RadioFrequencySubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$RadioFrequencySubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem devoted to processing RF signals that the radar sends or receives, for example via sub-components such as an RF receiver and an RF feed.")
(comment RangeTrackingSubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$RangeTrackingSubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem devoted to measure target slant range.")
(comment ControlSubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$ControlSubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem that controls the operation of the radar, and possibly other functions, such as data handling.")
(comment OpticsSubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$OpticsSubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem used for optical acquisition of a radar target.")
(comment CalibrationSubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$CalibrationSubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem used to calibrate the angles and range of a radar.")
(comment VideoSubsystemOfRadar "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$VideoSubsystemOfRadar is a radar subsystem used to capture and display video related to the operation of the radar.")
(comment LargeBuilding "The collection #$LargeBuilding is the collection of all buildings that are generally considered to be large compared to other buildings.")
(comment Castle "A specialization of #$LargeBuilding and #$HumanShelterConstruction.  Each instance of #$Castle is a large, fortified structure, intended (at least originally) as a residence of a member of the nobility.  Most castles were built in the middle ages.")
(comment backupOfFor "<code>(#$backupOfFor DEVICE BACKUP CLIENT)</code> means that when <code>DEVICE</code> is unble to provide the service to <code>CLIENT</code> that it ordinarily provides, it is expected that <code>BACKUP</code> witl be able to provide that service.")
(comment AirPurifier "The collection of all air purifiers: devices used for purifying ambient air. These may be used to remove smells, pollen, etc. A type of #$PhysicalDevice. The collection #$AirPurifier is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment multiWordString-Speculative "(#$multiWordString-Speculative . ARGS) means that (#$multiWordString . ARGS) is believed to hold, but has not been verified by a native speaker or qualified linguist.")
(comment NounCompoundParse "The collection of all results of parsing noun compounds.")
(comment NounCompoundParseFn "(#$NounCompoundParseFn HEAD-WORD HEAD-POS DENOT) denotes the output of parsing a noun compound to DENOT, where the head of the compound is interpreted as a HEAD-POS form of HEAD-WORD.")
(comment parsedNounCompound "(#$parsedNounCompound NOUN-COMPOUND-RULE MOD-STRING HEAD-STRING PARSE) means that 'MOD-STRING HEAD-STRING' was parsed using NOUN-COMPOUND-RULE to PARSE.")
(comment parseFodder "(#$parseFodder STRING) means that STRING is a candidate for parsing.")
(comment portalExposes "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation.  <code>(#$portalExposes PORTAL OBJECT)</code> means that <code>PORTAL</code> and <code>OBJECT</code> are such that objects or substances on one side of the object that contains <code>PORTAL</code> (see #$containsPortals) are capable of moving through <code>PORTAL</code> to make contact with <code>OBJECT</code>.  Typically the state of the portal must be in an open state (see #$OpenPortal), or, in the case of <code>OBJECT</code> being exposed to visible light, transparent.")
(comment contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForConditionType "<code>(#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForConditionType TREATMENT-TYPE CONDITION-TYPE)</code> means that <code>TREATMENT-TYPE</code> is contraindicated in patients with the #$AilmentCondition <code>CONDITION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment valveStenosisSeverityWithValve "(#$valveStenosisSeverityWithValve EVT VALVE VALVE-TYPE SEVERITY) means the information associated with the cardiac valve VALVE associated with medical event EVT indicates that the patient's valve of type VALVE-TYPE has severity SEVERITY")
(comment scalingCollectionOfWithRespectToSpatialMetrics "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical of #$SpatialScaleComparableIndividualsFn.")
(comment successiveMeasurementFeaturesOnCollectionType "Where COLLECTION-TYPE is a specialization of #$ComparableScalarIndividualsType and SET is a (#$SetOfTypeFn #$MeasurableQuantitySlot), (#$successiveMeasurementFeaturesOnCollectionType COLLECTION-TYPE SET COMP-PRED) means that SET is a set of quantifiable features shared by all the elements of each instance of COLLECTION-TYPE, and that, moreover, all of the elements of each instance of COLLECTION-TYPE share a common 'natural' range of values on this feature set.")
(comment vesselStenosisDegree "<code>(#$vesselStenosisDegree EVENT CAS CORONARY-ARTERY-TYPE DEGREE)</code> means that according to the information on CAS, that is associated with <code>EVENT</code> the stenosis degree on CORONARY-ARTERY-TYPE is DEGREE.")
(comment partyParticipatingInElections "(#$partyParticipatingInElections ELECTION-GROUP PARTY) means that PARTY is a #$PoliticalParty with candidates fielded in the politically delimited group of #$Elections, ELECTION-GROUP.")
(comment partyParticipatingInElection "(#$partyParticipatingInElection ELECTION PARTY) means that PARTY has fielded one of the candidates competing in ELECTION (see #$electionCandidates).")
(comment ELInferenceBindingSet "Each instance of #$ELInferenceBindingSet represents one complete answer to a CycL Query. An #$ELInferenceBindingSet is a set of #$ELInferenceBindings, with one #$ELInferenceBinding for each free variable present in the query formula.  Such binding sets are constructed for representation in the KB by using the function #$TheSet. <p> Note that the term \"(#$TheSet)\", when used to specify an inference binding set, indicates the result is \"NIL\" (i.e., the inference suspends without being proven.  Also, the term \"(#$TheSet (#$TheSet))\" indicates the result is \"T\" (i.e., the inference is proven true.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet SurgicalProcedure TricuspidValve MitralValve AorticValve PulmonaryValve)))
(disjointWith MedicalPatient (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet SurgicalProcedure TricuspidValve MitralValve AorticValve PulmonaryValve)))
(disjointWith CardiacValveOrProcedure Agent-Generic)
(disjointWith NonAgentTangibleOrSituation Agent-Generic)
(comment valueFromColumnInSKS "(valueFromColumnInSKS SKS LFI NUM) means that the value of the logical field indexical for the row in question corresponds to the value in the cell of the NUMth column.")
(comment derivedFromInput "(derivedFromInput INPUT OUTPUT) means that there is some standard method whereby INPUT was used to produce OUTPUT.  E.g. (#$derivedFromInput Sand-01 SandCastle-01).")
(comment dateOfElection "(#$dateOfElection ELECTION DATE) means that DATE is the time interval at which ELECTION is held by mandate of the #$GeopoliticalEntity that holds ELECTION.")
(comment dateMandatedForPoliticalEvent "(#$dateMandatedForPoliticalEvent EVENT DATE) means that DATE is the date on which EVENT is mandated to occur by some official policy or law of the #$GeopoliticalEntity sponsoring EVENT.")
(comment BeurgersDisease "A condition in which acute inflammation and clotting of arteries and veins affects the hands and feet.")
(comment polityOfElection "(#$polityOfElection ELECTION POLITY) means that POLITY is the social #$Organization (e.g., a #$GeopoliticalEntity like #$NewYork-State) which sponsors ELECTION, often because ELECTION is for an office that plays a governing role with respect to polity.")
(comment localeOfElection "(#$localeOfElection ELECTION REGION) means that REGION is the #$territoryOf the #$Organization that is the #$polityOfElection for ELECTION.")
(comment officeSoughtInElection "(#$officeSoughtInElection ELECTION OFFICE-TYPE) means that ELECTION is held in order to choose who will occupy the position represented by OFFICE-TYPE for a statutory term following ELECTION.")
(comment dataForValveOfEventRecordsOrificeArea "<code>(#$dataForValveOfEventRecordsOrificeArea VALVE EVENT AREA)</code> means that according to the <code>VALVE</code> associated with <code>EVENT</code> (an instance of #$CardiacCatheterization or #$Echocardiogram) the focal valve has the orifice area <code>AREA</code>.")
(comment UnitedStatesElectoralProcessesMt "A #$TheoryMicrotheory that contains axioms and definitions pertaining to how electoral processes work in United States elections at the federal, state, and local levels.")
(comment registeredToVoteInPolity "(#$registeredToVoteInPolity PERSON POLITY TIME-RANGE) means that PERSON is registered to vote in elections occurring in the territory of POLITY.  This means, effectively, that PERSON is constrained by law to cast their vote at a polling location within POLITY, regardless of whether they are voting in an election that involves an office specific to POLITY, or an election for an office that pertains to a #$GeopoliticalEntity that subsumes or controls POLITY.")
(comment votesInElection "(#$votesInElection ELECTION PERSON) means that PERSON votes in ELECTION.")
(comment BronchialArtery "The collection of all bronchial arteries.  A #$BronchialArtery carries #$OxygenatedBlood from the left ventricle of the #$Heart to the #$Lungs.")
(comment AntifibrinolyticAgent "Class of drug products that inhibit or prevent the breakdown of blood clots.")
(comment AntidiureticAgent "Class of drug products that inhibit production of urine in the kidneys.")
(comment SpatialScaleComparableIndividualsFn "A function used for referencing instances of #$ComparableScalarIndividualType-Spatial.  Where DIST-METRIC is a #$UnitOfDistance (e.g., #$Meter), (#$SpatialScaleComparableIndividualsFn DIST-METRIC) denotes the class of all individuals sharing a range of quantifiable spatial features (given by #$successiveMeasurementFeaturesOnCollectionType) whose values on each instance of the collection fall within a given range such that DIST-METRIC defines a scale of measurement for those objects that's natural for human custom and usage.  Thus (#$SpatialScaleComparableIndividualsFn #$Meter) denotes the class of all 'meter-scale' localized spatial things.")
(comment ComparableScalarIndividualsType "A type-level instance of #$FacetingCollectionType designed to establish a typing on #$Individual:  each instance is a collection whose instances are characterized by the fact that all instances share a common and semantically or pragmatically interesting range of values on a certain set of quantifiable features (usually a (#$SetOfTypeFn #$MeasurableQuantitySlot).")
(comment medicalEventHadIncisionApproachAndDetail "relates an operation or surgical procedure to the type of approach and specific type of surgical incision.")
(comment GameEvent "A collection of individual events.  Each instance of #$GameEvent includes the entirety of some game, from the beginning to the point where a conclusion is reached (there is a winner, there is a draw, or the game is abandoned).  
<p>
Each #$GameEvent has as #$subEvents one or more instances of #$PlayingAGame, but may have other sorts of significant #$subEvents as well.  For example, a particular #$FootballGame-American, in its entirety, would be an instance of #$GameEvent.  That game's #$subEvents would include, among other things, instances of (#$PlayingFn #$FootballGame-American) performed by some #$FootballPlayer-American, instances of #$EvaluatingAnAction performed by some #$Referee, and instances of #$MeasuringSomething performed by some #$SportsOfficial.  A game of Monopoly, from beginning to end, would be an instance of #$GameEvent, with subEvents possibly including instances of #$PlayingABoardGame, #$DisputeEvent, #$DistributionEvent, and (#$CleaningFn #$Table-PieceOfFurniture).")
(comment NLPlausibility "The collection of the different degrees of natural-language plausibility that a #$CycLTerm can have. This may be thought of as the likelihood that the term would be found in a native speaker's lexical knowledge.")
(comment nlPlausibilityOfNAT "(#$nlPlausibilityOfNAT NAT PLAUSIBILITY) means that the degree to which NAT is likely to be denoted by a short natural language expression is PLAUSIBILITY.")
(comment nlPlausibilityOfLexicalAssertion "(#$nlPlausibilityOfLexicalAssertion ASSERTION PLAUSIBILITY) means that the degree to which ASSERTION is likely to accurately reflect part of the lexical knowledge of a native speaker is PLAUSIBILITY.")
(comment succeedingScaleComparableTypes "Where COL1 and COL2 are instances of #$ComparableScalarIndividualsType, (#$succeedingScaleComparableTypes COL1 COL2 COMP-PRED) means that for a collection type COMMON-TYPE  of which COL1 and COL2 are both members, and a class of #$MeasurableQuantitySlots SET where (#$successiveMeasurementFeaturesOnCollectionType COMMON-TYPE SET), the value given by an element of set, MEAS-PRED for any instance of COL1 will have the relation COMP-PRED to the value given by MEAS-PRED for any instance of COL2.")
(comment ComparableScalarIndividualType-Spatial "A type-level #$FacetingCollectionType that establishes a typing on #$SpatialThing-Localized:  each instance is a #$Collection whose instances are localized spatial things that exhibit a common and semantically or pragmatically interesting range of values on a specified set of parameters, in most cases a (#$SetOfTypeFn #$MeasurableQuantitySlot).")
(comment bindingInPositionFromUsedInPositionInFor "(#$bindingInPositionFromUsedInPositionInFor QUERY-1 ARG-POS-1 QUERY-2 ARG-POS-2 LF-INDEXICAL ARG-POS-3) means that when QUERY-2 is run -- in the context of some application -- QUERY-1 should be run first and the any answers from the open variable in ARG-POS-1 should be used to created restricted versions of QUERY-2 by binding those answers in ARG-POS-2 in QUERY-2.  Each answer returned by the restricted version of QUERY-2 as a binding for ARG-POS-3 is the assigned value for the the logical field indexical LF-INDEXICAL.  When (#$TheList) is used as the formula arg position in arg 6 , then then QUERY-2  is sent fully bound and either True or False is assigned to the logical field indexical according to whether it returned (NIL) or NIL.")
(comment RedoProcedure "<code>(#$isa PRO RedoProcedure)</code> means that the patient involved in <code>PRO</code> has previously had a procedure of the very same type (via rdf:type).  This relationship is supported for most procedures except the generic heart valve replacement or repairs where the valve type is not specified.  For example, it works for aortic valve replacement, aortic valve repair, aortic valve replacement or repair, but not for the unspecific cardiac valve replacement, cardiac valve repair, or cardiac valve replacement or repair.  Also, this does not work with the specific vascular procedure names.  The full list of allowable procedures can be found in the drop down suggestions menu.")
(comment atLeastHalf "A binary #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional. <code>(#$atLeastHalf SOC1 SOC2)</code> means that at least half (i.e. 50% or more) of the elements of <code>SOC1</code> are elements of <code>SOC2</code>.")
(comment half "A binary #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  (#$half SOC1 SOC2) means that exactly half (i.e. 50%) of the elements of SOC1 are elements of SOC2.")
(comment requirementOfThing "<code>(#$requirementOfThing REQ THING)</code> means that <code>REQ</code> is a requirement imposed by some agent that some further capabilities be provided to support the agent's desired status of <code>THING</code> (or, if <code>THING</code> is a collection, instances of <code>THING</code>).")
(comment requirementOfIndividual "<code>(#$requirementOfIndividual REQ IND)</code> means that <code>REQ</code> is a requirement imposed by some agent that some further capabilities be provided to support the agent's desired status of <code>IND</code>.")
(comment requirementRuleAssertion "<code>(#$requirementRuleAssertion REQ RULE)</code> means that <code>RULE</code> expresses the conent of the requirement <code>REQ</code>.")
(comment LaunchAndTestRangeSystem "The Launch and Test Range System (LTRS) is the group of systems (including, e.g., the telemetry subsystem) supporting both the Eastern and Western ranges.  The #$EasternRangeInstrumentation is a proper subsystem of the LTRS.")
(comment LTRS-ModernizedTelemetrySubsystem "The Modernized Telemetry Subsystem is the group of systems (including, e.g., the telemetry subsystem) supporting both the Eastern and Western ranges.  The #$EasternRangeInstrumentation is a proper subsystem of the LTRS.")
(comment TMSS-TelemetryDesignateProcessingCI "The Telemetry Designate Processing (TMPD) component of the Modernized Telemetry Subsystem.  The TMDP CI is the hardware and software necessary to control how designate data is processed into pointing vectors, which in turn are used for pointing the telemetry antenna.")
(comment TMSS-TelemetryFacilityCI "The Telemetry Facility (TMFC) component of the Modernized Telemetry Subsystem.  The TMFC CI is the hardware and software necessary to provide electrical power and a suitable environment for the equipment that directly supports telemetry operations.")
(comment TMSS-TelemetryRecordAndPlaybackCI "The Telemetry Record and Playback (TMRP) component of the Modernized Telemetry Subsystem.  The TMRP CI provides the capability to coherently record and play back both digital and analog data collected by the TM Sub-System.")
(comment LineReplaceableUnit "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  This is the collection of devices considered to be \"line replaceable units\".")
(comment BootingAComputer "A specialization of #$ProgramAction and #$DeviceStartingARun -- the collection of events in which an instance of
#$Computer runs the instructions on its boot sector, generally in order to get in
normal operating mode. This may entail the instance of #$Computer's
#$stateOfDevice being changed from #$Device-Off to #$Device-On, but not
necessarily.")
(comment ObtainingDeviceStateFn "#$ObtainingDeviceStateFn is a Cyc function and in particular a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  It is used to represent a collection of events in which a device of a certain type changes into a certain state of operation (see #$DeviceTypeByState).  Thus, (#$ObtainingDeviceStateFn DEVICE STATE) returns the collection of events in which devices of type DEVICE change state to STATE.  For example, (#$ObtainingDeviceStateFn #$Dishwasher #$DeviceState-Rinsing) represents all the events in which dishwashers switch into their rinse cycles.  This function is quite useful because often one wants and needs to state rules of the form: after a certain triggering condition occurs, a state-change event of a certain type will be caused and will almost immediately occur.  E.g., after a light switch is flipped off, after an elevator button is pushed, after #$DeviceState-Rinsing ends, etc.")
(comment hardwareComponent "<code>(#$hardwareComponent DEVICE HARDWARE)</code> means that <code>HARDWARE</code> is the hardware component of <code>DEVICE</code>.")
(comment HardwareComponentFn "<code>(#$HardwareComponentFn DEVICE)</code> denotes the hardware component of <code>DEVICE</code>.")
(comment softwareComponent "<code>(#$softwareComponent DEVICE SOFTWARE)</code> means that <code>SOFTWARE</code> is the software component of <code>DEVICE</code>.")
(comment SoftwareComponentFn "<code>(#$SoftwareComponentFn DEVICE)</code> denotes the software component of <code>DEVICE</code>.")
(comment isMostRecentIrrelevanceEvent "<code>(#$isMostRecentIrrelevanceEvent EVENT THING )</code> means that #$DeemingAConceptIrrelevant 
<code>EVENT</code> is later than the concept relevance event that was formerly the most recent via #$mostRecentImportantConceptEvent.
<p>
")
(comment requirementOfType "<code>(#$requirementOfType REQ THING-TYPE)</code> means that <code>REQ</code> is a requirement imposed by some agent that some further capabilities be provided to support the agent's desired status of instances of <code>THING-TYPE</code>.")
(comment TMSS-TelemetryStringControlCI "The Telemetry String Control (TMSC) component of the Modernized Telemetry Subsystem.  The TMSC CI consists of the telemetry string control and processing ands tring network switching equipment.")
(comment DispositionallyPessimisticSecuritiesTrader "#$DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader is an instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$DispositionallyOptimisticSecuritiesTrader is a person, sometimes known as a \"bear\", who behavies as though the value of securities will fall.")
(comment dataForValveOfEventRecordsValveType "<code>(#$dataForValveOfEventRecordsValveType HEART-VALVE EVENT VALVE-TYPE)</code> means that in <code>EVENT</code> the heart valve acted on, HEART-VALVE, was an instance of <code>VALVE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment inRegion-Underspecified "(#$inRegion-Underspecified THING REGION) means that THING is in the region REGION. This is a very general predicate that relates a spatial thing to another spatial thing that it is, in some sense, \"in its region\".  This serves as the primary generalization of #$inRegion and #$situationLocation and can relate either situations or non-situational spatial things to places where they are or occur.")
(comment TurningOnPoweredDevice "The collection of actions in which a #$PoweredDevice changes from #$Device-Off to #$Device-On.")
(comment ConfiguringAPhysicalDevice "The collection of actions in which the configuration of a #$PhysicalDevice changes.")
(comment MonitoringStatusOfIndividualFn "(#$MonitoringStatusOfIndividualFn IND) denotes the collection of events in which IND is monitored.")
(comment FailureIsolation "The collection of events in which the failing component of a device is isolated.")
(comment deviceRFFeedType "<code>(#$deviceRFFeedType DEV FEED-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> supports RF feeds of type <code>FEED-TYPE</code>.")
(comment deviceScanRate "<code>(#$deviceScanRate DEV SCAN-RATE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a scan rate of <code>SCAN-RATE</code>, where <code>SCAN-RATE</code> is a frequency, such as (#$Hertz 30).")
(comment hasAntennaPedestalType "<code>(#$hasAntennaPedestalType DEV PEDESTAL-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a pedestal of type <code>PEDESTAL-TYPE</code>.")
(comment DegreesPerSecond "A measure of #$RateOfRotation.")
(comment antennaPedestalAzimuthTrackRate "<code>(#$antennaPedestalAzimuthTrackRate RADAR SPEED</code> means that the device <code>DEV</code> has an antenna pedestal with an azimuth track rate of <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment antennaPedestalElevationTrackRate "<code>(#$antennaPedestalElevationTrackRate DEV SPEED</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has an antenna pedestal with an elevation track rate of <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment antennaBeamwidth "<code>(#$antennaBeamwidth DEV DIST)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has an antenna beamwidth of <code>DIST</code>.")
(comment antennaSystemGainToTemperature "<code>(#$antennaSystemGainToTemperature DEV INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a system gain-to-temperature of <code>INTERVAL</code>.")
(comment TelemetryDetectionDevice "A specialization of #$ReconnaissanceDevice.  Each instance of #$TelemetryDetectionDevice is an electronic device used to detect telemetry information broadcast by a telemetry broadcast device or system of devices.")
(comment CAEUserWithoutTaskFn "(#$CAEUserWithoutTaskFn ALLOTMENT) denotes a researcher who is not given the task ALLOTMENT.")
(comment generalizations "The most general reified instance of 
#$TaxonomicSlotForAnyThing (q.v.).  #$generalizations relates things
of various kinds to things of the same kind that are correlatively 
at least as general or inclusive as they are.  Thus it relates a set (see 
#$Set-Mathematical) to its supersets, a collection (see #$Collection) 
to the collections that subsume it, a more-specific predicate (see 
#$Predicates) to those predicates that are correspondingly less-specific
than it, etc.  #$generalizations is itself the common generalization 
of a number of more type-specific generalization predicates, such as 
#$subsetOf, #$genls, and #$genlPreds (qq.v.).  When making assertions to
the Cyc Knowledge Base, it is better to use one of these more specific 
predicates instead of #$generalizations whenever possible.")
(comment ShapedBeamAntenna "A specialization of #$Antenna.  Each instance of #$ShapedBeamAntenna is a specially-shaped dish used as an antenna to send or receive electromagnetic signals.")
(comment ParabolicAntenna "A specialization of #$Antenna.  Each instance of #$ParabolicAntenna is a parabolic dish used as an antenna to send or receive electromagnetic signals.")
(comment OnlineAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online service.")
(comment OnlineChatAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online chat (instant messaging) service.")
(comment OnlineECommerceAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online e-commerce service.")
(comment OnlineGamingAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online gaming service.")
(comment OnlineWebPortalAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online web portal service.")
(comment OnlineWebMailAccount "A specialization of #$ComputerAccount.  Each intance of #$OnlineAccount is an account that provides the account holder access to an online web-mail service.")
(comment dataForValveOfEventRecordsStatus "<code>(#$dataForValveOfEventRecordsStatus EVENT STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that according to <code>PRO</code> #$SurgicalProcedure the focal valve of that procedure has the status <code>STATUS-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Document "A specialization of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of #$Document is either an abstract or concrete document of some sort.  Documents, thus broadly construed, may be textual or non-textual.")
(comment Document-CW "A specialization of #$Document.  Each instance of #$Document-CW is a partially abstract document.")
(comment Image "A specialization of #$Document. Each instance of #$Image is either an abstract or concrete image of some sort.  Significant specializations include #$VisualImage, #$Image-CW and #$ComputerImageFile.")
(comment Image-CW "A specialization of #$Image. #$Image-CW is the collection of all conceptal works that are images.")
(comment PersonalProfileDocument "A specialization of #$Document.  Each instance of #$PersonalProfileDocument is a document that describes properties of the document's author.")
(comment PersonalProfileDocument-RDF "A specialization of #$Document.  Each instance of #$PersonalProfileDocument-RDF is a #$PersonalProfileDocument produced in @#RDF-ResourceDescriptionFramework.")
(comment homepageOf "<code>(#$homepageOf PAGE THING)</code> means that <code>PAGE</code>, an instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW, is a homepage focally about <code>THING</code>.")
(comment accountServiceHomepage "<code>(#$accountServiceHomepage ACCOUNT PAGE)</code> means that <code>PAGE</code>, an instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW, is the homepage of the service provider for <code>ACCOUNT</code>.")
(comment onlineAccountProvider "<code>(#$onlineAccountProvider ACCOUNT PROVIDER)<code> means that <code>PROVIDER</code> (an instance of #$SocialBeing) is the provider of services associated with the #$OnlineAccount, <code>ACCOUNT</code>.")
(comment schoolHomepageOfPerson "<code>(#$schoolHomepageOfPerson PERSON PAGE)</code> means that <code>PAGE</code>, an instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW, is the homepage of a school attended by <code>PERSON</code>.")
(comment attendedSchoolAt "<code>(#$attendedSchoolAt PERSON SCHOOL)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> attended school at <code>SCHOOL</code>.")
(comment hasBeenNear "A predicate linking a thing to its prior history; <code>(#$hasBeenNear OBJECT1 OBJECT2)</code> means that the thing <code>OBJECT1</code> has at one time during its lifetime been near (see #$near) the thing <code>OBJECT2</code>.")
(comment frequentlyFoundNear "<code>(#$frequentlyFoundNear OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ1</code> often is located near <code>OBJ2</code>.")
(comment bestGuessRewriteOf "A predicate for expressing the hypothesis that a given non-atomic term that is the result of external source text-extraction is likely to represent a particular cyc constant. (#$bestGuessRewriteOf CONSTANT NAT) says that NAT is likely intended to represent the same object as CONSTANT.")
(comment rewriteExpansion "(#$rewriteExpansion RULE) means that the left-hand side of RULE describes a way to rewrite the right-hand side of RULE. RULE must be an instance of #$CycLRuleAssertion in which the right and left-hand sides each consist of precisely one literal.")
(comment usualLocationOfObject "A #$SpatialPredicate and a specialization of #$hasBeenIn (q.v.).  <code>(#$usualLocationOfObject OBJ PLACE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is usually or primarily (and perhaps permanently) located at <code>PLACE</code>.  This does <i>not</i> entail that <code>OBJ</code> is at <code>PLACE</code> at any particular time, as <code>OBJ</code> may be away from its usual location at various time.  (Cf. #$objectFoundInLocation).  Nor does it even entail that <code>OBJ</code> is at <code>PLACE</code> <i>most</i> of the time.  Rather, it means that <code>PLACE</code> is <code>OBJ</code>'s \"home base\" in some sense.  Thus, #$usualLocationOfObject is more a normative than a temporally quantitative relation.  Its specializations include #$physicalQuarters, #$residesInRegion, #$residesInDwelling, and #$hasHabitat.")
(comment usuallyFoundNear "<code>(#$usuallyFoundNear OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ1</code> is usually located near <code>OBJ2</code>.  This does not entail that <code>OBJ1</code> is near <code>OBJ2</code> at any particular time, as <code>OBJ1</code> may be away from its usual location at various time. Nor does it even entail that <code>OBJ1</code> is at PLACE most of the time. Rather, it means that <code>OBJ2</code> is in the vicinity of <code>OBJ1</code>'s \"home base\" in some sense. Thus, like its specialization, #$usualLocationOfObject (q.v.), #$usuallyFoundNear is more a normative than a temporally quantitative relation.")
(comment soleHolderOfAccount "<code>(#$soleHolderOfAccount AGENT ACCOUNT)</code> identifies <code>AGENT</code> as the unique instance of #$Agent-Generic such that <code>(#$accountHolder ACCOUNT AGENT)</code>.")
(comment yahooChatDisplayID "<code>(#$yahooChatDisplayID AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> when logged into <code>AGENT</code>'s Yahoo! Chat account.")
(comment aimChatDisplayID "<code>(#$aimChatDisplayID AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> when logged into <code>AGENT</code>'s AIM chat account.")
(comment msnChatDisplayID "<code>(#$msnChatDisplayID AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> when logged into <code>AGENT</code>'s MSN chat account.")
(comment icqChatDisplayID "<code>(#$icqChatDisplayID AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> when logged into <code>AGENT</code>'s ICQ chat account.")
(comment workInfoHomepage "<code>(#$workInfoHomepage PERSON PAGE)</code> means that <code>PAGE</code>, an instance of #$WorldWideWebPage-CW, is a page that describes the work of <code>PERSON</code>. This page is typically different from a person's own homepage or the homepage of a business.  It is often a page that describes the professional role that <code>PERSON</code> plays.")
(comment workplaceHomepage "<code>(#$workplaceHomepage PERSON PAGE)</code> means that <code>PAGE</code>, an instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW, is the homepage of a workplace of <code>PERSON</code>.")
(comment topicOfPCW "<code>(#$topicOfPCW PCW TOPIC)</code> says that <code>TOPIC</code> is a topic of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork <code>PCW</code>.  Note that if <code>(#$topicOfPCW CHAPTER TOPIC)</code> and <code>(#$subWorks WORK CHAPTER)</code>, it does <i>not</i> follow that <code>(#$topicOfPCW WORK TOPIC)</code>.")
(comment containsInformationAbout-Focally "This predicate relates sources of information to their focal topics.  <code>(#$containsInformationAbout-Focally IS THING)</code> means that <code>IS</code> is generally \"about\" <code>THING</code> -- which may be any instance of #$Thing at all. This predicate represents a very general notion of aboutness, which does not require that <code>THING</code> be explicitly named in <code>IS</code>, but that it be one of the main topics of <code>IS</code>. 
<p>
Note that <code>IS</code> can have more than one focal topic -- e.g., a textbook can have both logic and set theory as main topics. Use the more specific predicate  #$containsInformationAbout-UniqueMainTopic to associate <code>IS</code> with its unique main topic. Use the more general predicate #$containsInformationAbout to specify that <code>IS</code> contains some information about <code>THING</code>, but that <code>THING</code> is not a main topic of <code>IS</code>.")
(comment containsInformationAbout-UniqueMainTopic "This predicate relates sources of information to their unique main topics. <code>(#$containsInformationAbout-UniqueMainTopic IS THING)</code> means that <code>IS</code> is specifically, focally, and mainly \"about\" <code>THING</code> -- which may be any instance of #$Thing at all.
<p>
Note that <code>IS</code> can have only exactly one unique main topic.  For example, a restaurant review that is about a single restaurant will have that restaurant as its unique main topic.  Often an <code>IS</code> will have several focal topics instead of a unique main topic.  In such cases, use the more general predicate #$containsInformationAbout-Focally.")
(comment nameString "(#$nameString TERM STRING) means that the #$ProperNameString STRING names the thing denoted by TERM. Normally, STRING corresponds to a proper name. For a term that has more than one name associated with it, use #$preferredNameString for the name that is to be used in natural language paraphrase. Note that two name strings for a given thing need not have the same sense or intension; thus, for instance, (#$nameString #$MarkTwain \"Samuel Clemens\") holds.")
(comment blogOfAgent "<code>(#$blogOfAgent AGENT BLOG)</code> means that <code>BLOG</code>, an instance of #$Weblog</code>, is a blog of <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment userDisplayIDs "<code>(#$userDisplayIDs AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> for some account in which <code>AGENT</code> is the #$accountHolder.")
(comment agentInterestedIn "<code>(#$agentInterestedIn AGENT THING)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is interested in <code>THING</code>, in a very general sense of \"interest\".  For example, <code>AGENT</code> may want to know more about <code>THING</code>, or <code>AGENT</code> may have a vested interest in <code>THING</code> (see #$vestedInterest).")
(comment interpretationForSystemString "A predicate used to map representational systems into CycL.  It is used in lieu of #$synonymousExternalConcept when the system uses strings rather than terms to denote some concept, a common practice in rdf-based representations that treat relations as having 'domains' (whose objects are typically represented using terms of the representation language) and 'ranges' (frequently represented using strings, uninterpreted symbols, numerals, and floats).  For example, a system <code>SYS</code> might represent that a particular object <code>OBJ</code> is blue with a triple, '<code>REF color \"blue\"</code>' where '<code>REF</code>' represents <code>OBJ</code>, '<code>color</code>' represents the color relation, and the string \"blue\" represents the color blue.  In order to map this example into Cyc, we would add a #$synonymousExternalConcept assertion associating the SYS terms <code>REF</code>, an #$interpretationForPredWithStringInArg assertion associating <code>color</code> with its CycL correlate, and an assertion of the form <code>(#$interpretationForSystemString BlueColor SYS \"blue\")</code>.  Note that this presupposes that \"blue\" is unambiguous in <code>SYS</code>, which need not be the case. If a string is ambiguous, additional context is needed -- see #$interpretationForSystemStringInContext.")
(comment interpretationForPredWithStringInArg "A predicate used to map representational systems into CycL.  It is used in lieu of #$synonymousExternalConcept when the system uses strings rather than terms to denote some concept, a common practice in rdf-based representations that treat relations as having 'domains' (whose objects are typically represented using terms of the representation language) and 'ranges' (frequently represented using strings, uninterpreted symbols, numerals, and floats).  For example, a system <code>SYS</code> might represent that a particular object <code>OBJ</code> is blue with a triple, '<code>REF color \"blue\"</code>' where '<code>REF</code>' represents <code>OBJ</code>, '<code>color</code>' represents the color relation, represented in CycL as #$mainColorOfObject, and the string \"blue\" represents the color blue.  In order to map this example into Cyc, we would add a #$synonymousExternalConcept assertion associating the SYS terms <code>REF</code>, an #$interpretationForSystemString assertion associating \"blue\" with #$BlueColor, and an assertion of the form <code>(#$interpretationForPredWithStringInArg #$mainColorOfObject SYS color 2)</code> where the integer 2 indicates that <code>color</code> takes a string in its second argument.")
(comment visuallyDepicts "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$VisualInformationBearingThing to instances of #$Thing. <code>(#$visuallyDepicts IBT OBJ)</code> means the object <code>OBJ</code> is depicted by the visual information source <code>IBT</code>. For example, Mount Everest is visually depicted by a photograph of it, and (#$visuallyDepicts #$PietaStatue-Michelangelo #$JesusOfNazareth) is true.")
(comment imageDepicts "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Image to instances of #$Thing. <code>(#$imageDepicts IMG OBJ)</code> means the object <code>OBJ</code> is depicted by the image <code>IMG</code>. IN this sense, Mount Everest is visually depicted by a photograph of it, and a computer image file storing a photograph of it.")
(comment imageDepicts-Focally "<code>(#$imageDepicts-Focally IMG THING)</code> means that <code>IMG</code> is a representative image of <code>THING</code>, and <code>THING</code> is one of the main subjects of <code>IMG</code>.")
(comment jabberDisplayID "<code>(#$msnChatDisplayID AGENT ID)</code> means that the string <code>ID</code> is a display ID used by <code>AGENT</code> when logged into <code>AGENT</code>'s Jabber chat account.")
(comment geekCode "<code>(#$geekCode GEEK CODE)</code> means that the person, <code>GEEK</code>, is described by the code, <code>CODE</code>. Geek code strings are described at http://www.geekcode.com/geek.html .")
(comment planFileString "<code>(#$planFileString PERSON STRING)</code> means that the person, <code>PERSON</code>, if he or she has a .plan file, would have the string <code>STRING</code> as its content.  Use of .plan files is in decline, but there was a time when people tended to store interesting strings in their .plan files.  The program #$Finger-TheProgram implemented a protocol for displaying the contents of people's .plan files, among other things.")
(comment hasInternetMailbox "<code>(#$hasInternetMailbox PERSON MAILBOX)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> has the personal mailbox <code>MAILBOX</code>.  Per RFC 822, <code>MAILBOX</code> is a list of email addresses (see #$EMailAddress) .")
(comment hasInternetMailboxWithSHA1 "<code>(#$hasInternetMailboxWithSHA1 PERSON STRING)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> has a personal mailbox (see #$hasInternetMailbox) referenced by the string <code>STRING</code>, which is a SHA-1 hash of the \"mailto:\" identifier of an internet mailbox.")
(comment ElectoralProcess "Each instance of this collection is a temporally extended process whereby an #$IntelligentAgent comes to be elected to a #$PublicOffice in some polity, starting with an event or process whereby candidates are nominated to run in an election, continuing through one or more temporally parallel election campaigns (see #$PoliticalElectionCampaign), and concluding with a general election for office wherein one of the nominated candidates is elected to the office in question.")
(comment culminatingElectionOfElectoralProcess "For a given #$ElectoralProcess, ELEC-PROC, (#$culminatingElectionOfElectoralProcess ELEC-PROC ELECTION) means that ELECTION is the final #$Election which is the culmination of ELEC-PROC.")
(comment ElectionNominationProcess "The collection of all decision-making processes whereby a candidate is chosen to run in an election.")
(comment PrimaryElectoralProcess-Singular "The collection of all electoral processes (#$ElectoralProcess) consisting in a primary #$PoliticalElectionCampaign culminating in a #$PrimaryElection.")
(comment openID "An open ID is a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) used to uniquely identify an individual, and is intended to replace the need for multiple login and passwords to access various online sites. <code>(#$openID AGENT URI)</code> identifies <code>URI</code> as the URI used by <code>AGENT</code> as an open ID.")
(comment imageThumbnails "<code>(#$imageThumbnails IMAGE THUMB)</code> identifies <code>IMAGE</code> as the instance of #$ComputerImageFile of which <code>THUMB</code>, an instance of #$ThumbnailImage, is a compressed version.")
(comment phoneNumberURI "There are semantic web standards and proposals for standards for representing telephone/fax numbers as Uniform Resource Locators.  <code>(#$phoneNumberURI THING URI)</code> associates a spatio-temporal object, such as an agent, a contact location, or a fax machine, with such a URI that represents a phone number.")
(comment antennaBeamwidth-Min "(#$antennaBeamwidth-Min DEV W) means that DEV supports, at the low end, W beamwidth.")
(comment antennaBeamwidth-Max "(#$antennaBeamwidth-Min DEV W) means that DEV supports, at the high end, W beamwidth.")
(comment PhysicalSchemaForKSFn "A physical schema denoting function.  This function takes a structured knowledge source and a character string to the physical schema for that sks that has that string as a name.")
(comment physicalSchemaWithNameForKS "The corresponding predicate to the physical schema denoting function #$PhysicalSchemaForKSFn")
(comment physicalFieldIndexicalsWithOrder "(#$physicalFieldIndexicalsWithOrder SCHEMA INDEXICAL NUM) means that INDEXICAL is an indexical used to denote the value in a row for a physical field in the physical schema and its corresponding physical field has the NUMth position in the physical schema field list.")
(comment sKSFieldNamesWithOrder "(#$sKSFieldNamesWithOrder SKS NAME NUM) means that SKS has a unique physical schema with a field name of NAME in the NUMth position in the schema field list.")
(comment lesserBinaryListThan "A special case predicate designed to order binary tuples that have an integer in their second position.")
(comment TelemetryDetectionDevice-PhysicalDescriptionTable "A specialization of #$Table-VisualCW.  Each instance of #$TelemetryDetectionDevice-PhysicalDescriptionTable is a table containing information about physical properties of a telemetry detection system.")
(comment openIDDocument "<code>(#$openID AGENT DOC)</code> identifies <code>DOC</code> as the document that <code>AGENT</code>'s as open ID points to.  See #$openID.")
(comment headerStringForColumnInTableType "<code>(#$headerStringForColumnInTableType TABLE-TYPE INTEGER HEADER-VALUE)</code> means that instances of <code>TABLE-TYPE</code> have the string <code>HEADER-STRING</code> in the head cell identified with the column numbered <code>INTEGER</code> (assuming a column numbering scheme in which the left-most column is numbered 1, the columns just to its right is numbered 2, and so on).")
(comment cellValueForSentenceInTableType "<code>(#$cellValueForSentenceInTableType TABLE-TYPE FOCAL-THING SENTENCE INTEGER CELL-VALUE)</code> means that for tables about <code>FOCAL-THING</code> in rows representing the information encoded in <code>SENTENCE</code> instances of <code>TABLE-TYPE</code> have the value <code>CELL-VALUE</code> in the cell identified with the column numbered <code>INTEGER</code> (assuming a column numbering scheme in which the left-most column is numbered 1, the columns just to its right is numbered 2, and so on).")
(comment maximalCampaignOfElectoralProcess "For a given #$ElectoralProcess, ELEC-PROC, (#$maximalCampaignOfElectoralProcess ELEC-PROC CAMPAIGN) means that CAMPAIGN is a campaign of ELEC-PROC that targets and serves as the preamble to the #$Election which is the #$culminatingElectionOfElectoralProcess of ELEC-PROC.")
(comment logicalFieldCorrespondingToPhysicalFieldNameUsesQueryInPosition "(#$logicalFieldCorrespondingToPhysicalFieldNameUsesQueryInPosition KS FIELD-NAME QUERY ARG-POS-1-STRING ARG-POS-2-STRING) means that there is a logical field indexical corresponding to FIELD-NAME in KS and its value is determined by running the base query for KS and plugging the result into ARG-POS-1 in QUERY.  The resulting answer for ARG-POS-2 is the value of the logical field indexical.  The ARG-POS-N-STRINGs are automatically converted into FormulaArgPositionFn terms when populating #$bindingInPositionFromUsedInPositionInFor.")
(comment baseQueryForReportType "(#$baseQueryForReportType QUERY SKS) means that that QUERY is the base form of various restricted queries that are used to provide bindings for other queries run to populate various fields in reports that are defined by SKS.  For example, a query called GET-INDEX-EVENT may be the base query for a particular medical report and when run with some of its open variables bound (typically via a source document) it will provide the event that one or more additional queries will use to populate the fields in the report.")
(comment logicalFieldValueWithFieldName "(#$logicalFieldValueWithFieldName LS NAME LFI) means that LFI is the logical field indexical in LS that corresponds to to the physical field with NAME.")
(comment LogicalSchemaForKSWithNameFn "This function defines a #$LogicalSchema by reference to a structured knowledge source and a character string.  It is expected that the knowledge source has a corresponding physical schema with the same name, otherwise the value is undefined.")
(comment logicalSchemaWithNameForKS "The corresponding predicate to the logical schema denoting function #$LogicalSchemaForKSWithNameFn")
(comment baseQueryUsesAnswersInPosition "(#$baseQueryUsesAnswersInPosition  QUERY POSITION) means that QUERY is used to provide bindings for additional queries based on answers that come back in POSITION.")
(comment capitalCityOfState "<code>(#$capitalCityOfState STATE CAPITAL)</code> means that <code>STATE</code> has the capital city, <code>CAPITAL</code>.")
(comment IndependentCountry-BasicDataTable "A specialization of #$Table-VisualCW.  Each instance of #$IndependentCountry-BasicDataTable is a table containing basic information about an instance of #$IndependentCountry.")
(comment tableTypeTemporalQualificationColumn "<code>(#$tableTypeTemporalQualificationColumn TABLE-TYPE INTEGER)</code> means that instances of <code>TABLE-TYPE</code> have temporal qualification in column numbered <code>INTEGER</code>.")
(comment predTakesFocalTopicInArgForSectionAndTableType "<code>(#$predTakesFocalTopicInArgForSectionAndTableType SUM-PRED TABLE-TYPE PRED INT)</code> means that when sentences with predicate <code>PRED</code> in the arg0 position are displayed in sections delineated by <code>SUM-PRED</code> in tables of the type <code>TABLE-TYPE</code>, the focal term is taken to be the argument to the <code>INT</code> number argument to <code>PRED</code.")
(comment tableTypeWidth "<code>(#$tableTypeWidth TABLE-TYPE INTEGER)</code> means that instances of <code>TABLE-TYPE</code> have <code>INTEGER</code> many columns.")
(comment EmptyCellContent "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$EmptyCellContent is a conceptual work that would be instantiated by leaving a cell of a table free of content.")
(comment IndependentCountry-GroupMembershipTable "A specialization of #$Table-VisualCW.  Each instance of #$IndependentCountry-GroupMembershipTable is a table containing group membership information about an instance of #$IndependentCountry.")
(comment NoTransformationRequired "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical value = physical value.")
(comment fieldValueIsTransformedViaInSKS "(#$fieldValueIsTransformedViaInSKS SKS NAME TRANSFORMATION) means that the value of the logical field indexical corresponding to NAME should undergo TRANSFORMATION before being output to the document.")
(comment kSHasFieldQueryReplacementPositionAndTransformation "(#$kSHasFieldQueryReplacementPositionAndTransformation PS FIELD-NAME QUERY ARG-POS-1 ARG-POS-2 TRANSFORMATION) means that PS has a field with NAME filled by QUERY that undergoes TRANSFORMATION in the encoding statement.  The ARG-POS terms specify how terms are substituted in from some base query and which position represents the value output to the field.  This is a special use predicate equivalent to the conjunction of #$logicalFieldCorrespondingToPhysicalFieldNameUsesQueryInPosition and #$fieldValueIsTransformedViaInSKS.")
(comment valueForFieldNameTakenFromColumnWithTrans "(#$valueForFieldNameTakenFromColumnWithTrans SKS NAME NUM TRANS) means that the value of the field with NAME in SKS is taken directly from the cell in the NUMth column in the input document and subjected to TRANS before encoding.")
(comment queryHasFocalOutputVariablePosition "(#$queryHasFocalOutputVariablePosition  QUERY POSITION) means that in certain contexts the value for the argument POSITION in QUERY after the query is run is assigned to something.  If the query is completely bound after the focal substitution of its input variable (see #$queryHasFocalInputVariablePosition) then POSITION = (TheList).")
(comment queryHasFocalInputVariablePosition "(#$queryHasFocalInputVariablePosition  QUERY POSITION) means that in certain contexts the argument POSITION in QUERY is bound with some specified value and the resulting value for one or more variable positions (or its truth/falsehood if bound) is assigned to something  (c.f. #$queryHasFocalOutputVariablePosition).")
(comment hasPathologyAtLocation "<code>(#$hasPathologyAtLocation CVPD EVENT  LOC-TYPE PATH-TYPE)</code> means that according to the <code>CVD</code> associated with <code>EVENT</code> the focal valve has the pathology <code>PATH-TYPE</code> at the lcoation type <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CardiovascularImplant "A collection of #$Implant-Medical surgically placed or intended to be placed inside living tissue to affect the cardiovascular system.")
(comment KMFPlusPlusOWLClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$KMFPlusPlusOWLClass is a collection that corresponds to one of the classes in the \"KMF Plus Plus\" OWL ontology.")
(comment deviceReceiveFrequencyBand-Max "(#$deviceReceiveFrequencyBand-Max DEV FR) means that DEV supports, at the high end, Receive Frequency band FR.")
(comment deviceReceiveFrequencyBand-Min "(#$deviceReceiveFrequencyBand-Min DEV FR) means that DEV supports, at the low end, Receive Frequency FR.")
(comment deviceReceiveFrequencyBand "<code>(#$deviceReceiveFrequencyBand DEV FR)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> supports Receive Frequency band <code>FR</code>.")
(comment KMFPlusPlusOWLProperty "The collection of binary predicates that correspond to the KMF OWL properties.")
(comment titleForTablesOfType "(#$titleForTablesOfType TABLE-TYPE TITLE) means that tables of type TABLE-TYPE should have the title TABLE.")
(comment Republic "A #$GeopoliticalEntityBySystemOfGovernment
 in which the headOfState is not a Monarch-HeadOfState and is usually a President-HeadOfState.")
(comment SKSISupportedOWLProperty "The collection of OWL properties that have SKSI removal modules generated for them.")
(disjointWith BaseballBase Clothing-Generic)
(comment BaseballBase "The sports implement (#$SportsEquipment) used to mark the vertices of a #$BaseballDiamond in a #$BaseballGame.")
(comment Microwave-XBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element
of #$Microwave-XBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 
having a frequency of approximately 8X10^9 #$Hertz to 12X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-SBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element of #$Microwave-SBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation having a frequency of approximately 2X10^9 #$Hertz to 4X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-CBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element
of #$Microwave-CBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 
having a frequency of approximately 4X10^9 #$Hertz to 8X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-LBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element of #$Microwave-LBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation having a frequency of approximately 1X10^9 #$Hertz to 2X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-KBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element
of #$Microwave-KBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 
having a frequency of approximately 18X10^9 #$Hertz to 27X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-KuBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element
of #$Microwave-KuBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 
having a frequency of approximately 12X10^9 #$Hertz to 18X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment Microwave-KaBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.  Each element
of #$Microwave-KuBand is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 
having a frequency of approximately 27X10^9 #$Hertz to 40X10^9 #$Hertz.")
(comment commonSurgicalComplication "<code>(#$commonSurgicalComplication PROCEDURE AILMENT)</code> means instances of <code>AILMENT</code> are often associated with instances of <code>PROCEDURE</code> and if someone develops the ailment after having the procedure, it is likely that the procedure caused the ailment.")
(comment MarketForCommodityTypeInPolityFn "This function is intended to capture the important economic
concept of a polity's market in some class of good or service, e.g.,
the Los Angeles automobile market, which we would denote as
(#$MarketForCommodityTypeInPolityFn #$CityOfLosAngelesCA  #$Automobile).")
(comment marketForCommodityTypeInPolity "The corresponding predicate
(#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$MarketForCommodityTypeInPolityFn.")
(comment majorTradingCenterByMarketCapitalization "(#$majorTradingCenterByMarketCapitalization EXCHANGE MARKET
INTERVAL) means that stock exchange EXCHANGE is the major trading
center for the stock market MARKET during the entire duration of INTERVAL.")
(comment stockTradedAt "(stockTradedAt COMPANY MARKET YEAR) means that COMPANY's
stocks are regularly traded on the stock market MARKET during the
defined time interval INTERVAL.")
(comment capitalizationOfExchangeOnMarketForYear "(#$capitalizationOfExchangeOnMarketForYear EXCHANGE MARKET CAPITALIZATION YEAR) means that the market capitalzation of the stock exchange EXCHANGE at the stock market MARKET in YEAR is CAPITALIZATION,")
(comment situationAffectsType "(#$situationAffectsType SIT TYPE) means that some instance of TYPE was affected in SIT.  For example, in the situation, SA, consisting of Paul having a stomach ache, (#$situationAffectsType SA #$Stomach) holds.")
(comment Decibel " When referring to measurements of power or intensity, when applied to a number or other #$NumericInterval (pair of numeric-intervals), #$Decibel returns ten times the base-10 logarithm of its argument (the interval between its two arguments) divided by the implicit reference value.  
<p>
Decibels are commonly used to measure sound pressure levels.   When referring to measurements of sound pressure (or amplitude), when applied to a number or other #$NumericInterval (pair of numeric-intervals), #$Decibel returns the instance of #$IntervalOnNumberLine that is twenty times the base-10 logarithm of its argument (the interval between its two arguments) divided by the implicit reference value. The commonly used reference sound pressure in air is pref = 20 micropascals (rms). In underwater acoustics, the reference sound pressure is pref = 1 micropascal (rms).")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding)
(comment diagnosisSiteType "(#$diagnosisSiteType DIAG BODY-PART-TYPE) means that DIAG is a diagnosis or medical finding involving or about a patient's BODY-PART-TYPE.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationTypeByWaveFrequency "A collection of collections.  Each instance of  #$ElectromagneticRadiationTypeByWaveFrequency is a specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.   Notable instances of #$ElectromagneticRadiationTypeByWaveFrequency include the collections #$RadioWave, #$XRay, #$GammaRay,  and #$UltravioletLight.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationModulation "The collection of events in which some aspect of electromagnetic radiation is modulated, e.g. with regard to its frequency (see #$FrequencyModulation) or amplitude (see #$AmplitudeModulation).")
(comment FrequencyModulation "The collection of events in which  electromagnetic radiation is modulated with regard to its frequency.")
(comment PhaseModulation "The collection of events in which  electromagnetic radiation is modulated with regard to its phase.")
(comment receiverModulationFormat "<code>(#$receiverModulationFormat DEV FORMAT)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> supports the modulation format <code>FORMAT</code>.")
(comment AmplitudeModulation "The collection of events in which  electromagnetic radiation is modulated with regard to its amplitude.")
(comment tableTypeForTypeAndSection "<code>(#$tableTypeForTypeAndSection TYPE SUM-PRED TABLE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>TABLE-TYPE</code> is the type of table that should be generated in the sections delineated by <code>SUM-PRED</code> in any factsheet wherein an instance of <code>TYPE</code> is the focal term.")
(comment FactSheetTableType "The collection of all types of fact sheet tables.")
(comment FactSheetTable "A sub-collection of #$Table-VisualCW.  Instances of #$FactSheetTable are used to present information in Cyc factsheets.")
(comment MicrotheoryDesignatingPredicate "The collection of \"decontextualized\" predicates (see #$decontextualizedPredicate) that specify that a given #$CycLSentence-Assertible is to be interpreted in a given #$Microtheory. The sentence will be canonicalized and checked for well-formedness with respect to that microtheory.  Each microtheory-designating predicate thus takes a microtheory (see #$microtheoryDesignationArgnum) and an #$CycLSentence-Assertible (see #$sentenceDesignationArgnum) as arguments.  It may take one or more other arguments as well.")
(comment ist "This predicate relates a microtheory to any sentence that is true in it.  <code>(#$ist MT SENT)</code> means that the CycL sentence <code>SENT</code> (or, if you prefer, the proposition <code>SENT</code> expresses) is true in the microtheory <code>MT</code>.  Note that <code>SENT</code> need not actually be <i>asserted</i> in <code>MT</code>; <code>MT</code> might for example \"inherit\" <code>SENT</code> from a more general microtheory (see #$ist-Asserted), or <code>SENT</code> might be derivable from other sentences that are true in <code>MT</code>.")
(comment ist-Graph "<code>(#$ist-Graph GRAPH-CONTEXT SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true in the context <code>GRAPH-CONTEXT</code>. where <code>GRAPH-CONTEXT</code> is a context denoted by a named graph in a triple store (see #$ContextOfNamedGraphFn).")
(comment ResourcePCWAtURIFn "<code>(#$ResourcePCWAtURIFn URI)</code> is propositional conceptual work associated with the document at <code>URI</code>.")
(comment ContextOfNamedGraphFn "<code>(#$ContextOfNamedGraphFn URI-PCW)</code> is the context associated with the propositional conceptual work associated located at a particular URI constituting the name of a graph in a triple store.")
(comment AilmentTreatmentTable "A specialization of #$FactSheetTable.  Each instance of #$AilmentTreatmentTable is a table containing information about treatments for an #$AilmentCondition.")
(comment nameSpacePrefixForSKS "This relates a structured information source (usually an RDF triple store) to namespaces employed by it and their corresponding prefixes.")
(comment Aardwolf "A specialization of #$Mammal.  Aardwolves are small insectivorous hyena-like mammals native to Africa.")
(comment CoronaryArteryDisease "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CoronaryArteryDisease is an ailment condition that afflicts a #$CoronaryArtery.")
(comment CoronaryArteryDisease-Ischemic "A specialization of #$CoronaryArteryDisease.  Each instance of #$CoronaryArteryDisease-Ischemic is an ailment condition that afflicts a #$CoronaryArtery due to restricted blood flow.")
(comment ERSystemParameterValue "The collection of values of parameters of the ER systems.")
(comment SuperiorVenaCavaSyndrome "Partial blockage of blood flow in the #$SuperiorVenaCava, typically caused by a mass impinging on the vein.")
(comment GeneticArrhythmia "The collection of all #$CardiacArrhythmias that are genetic in nature, or have a substantial genetic component.")
(comment Abacus "A specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive and #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$Abacus is a manual device used to facilitate computing.  These devices consist of rows of parallel rods that support movable counters.")
(comment ChangeOfStatusEvent "A specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer and #$SocialOccurrence.  Elements of #$ChangeOfStatusEvent are events in which the (generally social) status of an object, person, group, or organization changes.")
(comment NamedGraphMicrotheory "A specialization of #$Microtheory.  Each instance of
#$NamedGraphMicrotheory is a context associated with a particular
named graph.  See #$ContextOfNamedGraphFn.")
(comment supportsInMtMayHaveGraphInformation "<code>(#$supportsInMtMayHaveGraphInformation MT)</code> means any support in <code>MT</code> may have source graphs discoverable by issuing an #$ist-Graph query on the support's sentence.")
(comment SlaughterhouseBuilding "A specialization of #$LargeBuilding and #$Workplace.  Each instance of #$SlaughterhouseBuilding is a is a facility where animals are killed and processed into meat products.")
(comment AbandonedConstructionArtifact "This is the collection of all instances of #$ConstructionArtifact that have been abandoned, i.e., no
maintenance operations are conducted to preserve their operability.")
(comment Abandoned-ExistentialStatus "The collection of all living creatures, places, or agents that are in a state of abandonment, meaning they have been the #$objectOfStatusChange in an #$AbandoningSomething event and have yet to go under any sort of rehabilitation, reconstruction, or rescue that would change their current state.")
(disjointWith Abandoned-ExistentialStatus Possession)
(comment Liability-Obligation "A sub-collection of #$Obligation. Each instance is an obligation of one person to provide resources to someone else.")
(comment requirementPertainingToTypeHasText "<code>(#$requirementPertainingToTypeHasText REQ THING TEXT)</code> means that the requirement <code>REQ</code> is pertinent to the thing <code>THING</code>, and is associated with <code>TEXT</code>.")
(comment Overview "A general summary")
(comment ElectronicNoise "Electronic noise is unwanted signal present in an electronic circuit.")
(comment GreatlyEndeavoring "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Endeavoring. In each #$Endeavoring, something tries very hard to do something.")
(comment RevascularizationProcedure "The collection of  revascularization procedures.")
(comment Congregant "member of a congregation")
(comment Idol-Metaphorically "idol in the metaphorical sense: someone who is idolized")
(comment Template "anything that establishes or serves as a pattern, e.g. a #$ShellForCasting")
(comment FirstEventOrProcedureOfTypeRDFTypeRuleApplicable "The collection of valid suggestions for #$firstEventOrProcedureOfType.")
(comment age "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot predicate that relates an existing thing to its current age, expressed as a quantity of time (see #$Time-Quantity).  (#$age THING AMOUNT-OF-TIME) means that THING has been in existence for a total of AMOUNT-OF-TIME.  For people this is measured by calculating the length of time between their birthdate and the current time.  This will only calculate the age of individuals who are not known to be deceased in the current query context. ")
(comment EpicardialCoronaryArtery "The collection of coronary arteries that run at the surface of the heart.")
(comment RightCoronaryArtery-Generic "The collection of all right coronary arteries. A type of #$CoronaryArtery. The collection #$RightCoronaryArtery-Generic is an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType.")
(comment AntennaTypeByShape "A specialization of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$AntennaTypeByShape is a clooection of antennas that have the same basic shape.  For example, #$ParabolicAntenna is an instance of this collection because all its instances are parabolic antennas.")
(comment CuttingDevice-Handheld "A hand-held, human-powered cutting device, such as a #$BoxCutter, pizza cutter, wire cutter, meat cutter, or cookie cutter")
(comment Abbey "The collection of all abbeys, which are Christian monasteries or convents. A type of #$ReligiousBuilding and #$HumanResidence. The collection #$Abbey is an #$ArtifactTypeByFunction, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactualFeatureType.")
(comment Monk-Christian "A specialization of #$ChristianPerson and #$Monk.")
(comment MagicSpell "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork.  Each instance is a verbal formula believed to have magical force.")
(comment Monastery-Residence-Buddhist "A specialization of #$Monastery-Residence.  Each instance of #$Monastery-Residence-Buddhist is a building intended primarily as a residence for Buddhist monks.")
(comment Monastery-Residence-Christian "A specialization of #$Monastery-Residence.  Each instance of #$Monastery-Residence-Christian is a building intended primarily as a place for Christian monks to live.")
(comment AbbreviationEvent "The collection of all events in which a word or phrase is reduced to a shorter form (an #$Abbreviation (q.v.)).")
(comment SuspendingOfStatus "A collection of #$ChangeOfStatusEvents: in each instance of #$SuspendingOfStatus, a person, group, or organization is suspended
from a status that it had previously, so that the agent in question has the status before the suspending event and lacks the status after the event is over.  A suspending from status is ordinarily considered to have 'temporary' effect.")
(disjointWith SuspendingOfStatus ExpellingFromStatus)
(comment Abdicating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ChangeOfStatusEvent. In each #$Abdicating, someone gives up, such as power, as of monarchs and emperors, or duties and obligations.")
(comment PulseTest "The collection of all pulse tests. A type of #$ParameterTest. #$PulseTest is a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment HearingTest "The collection of all hearing tests. A type of #$TrueOrFalseTest. #$HearingTest is a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment Pirate-Sailor "The collection of all pirate sailors - people who sail around robbing and plundering other ships.  A type of #$CrewMemberOnShip and #$Criminal. The concept #$Pirate-Sailor is a #$CriminalTypeByCrimeType and a #$PersonTypeByActivity.")
