(comment schedule-EducationalOrganization "A predicate corresponding to the function #$ScheduleFn-EducationalOrganization.  <code>(#$schedule-EducationalOrganization X (#$ScheduleFn-EducationalOrganization X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment requirementDerivationLevel "(<code>(#$requirementDerivationLevel REQ N)</code> means that <code>REQ</code> is <code>N</code> derivation steps away from a base-level requirement.")
(comment ExportTimeOfDateAs-HH-MM-SS "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which a time in the HH:MM:SS format is extracted from a CycL date.")
(comment ExportDateAs-YYYY-MM-DD-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the day/month/year in YYYY-MM-DD format is extracted from a CycL date.")
(comment hasCorrespondingBooleanNumericValue "(#$hasCorrespondingBooleanNumericValue THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.  This is used in the context of SKSI encoding statement to transform the value of some logical field indexical into its corresponding physical value.")
(comment hospitalAdmitDateMin "<code>(#$hospitalAdmitDateMin EVT DATE)</code> means that if <code>EVT</code> is an instance of #$HospitalCareEvent, then <code>EVT</code> starts no later than <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment hospitalDischargeDateMin "<code>(#$hospitalDischargeDateMin EVT DATE)</code> means that if <code>EVT</code> is an instance of #$HospitalCareEvent, then <code>EVT</code> ends no earlier than <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment minDateOfOperationForComplication "<code>(minDateOfOperationForComplication COMP MIN-DATE)</code> means that the complication, <code>COMP</code>, is a complication of an operation that has a min date of <code>MIN-DATE</code>. ")
(comment DifferenceFn "A binary #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars and an extension of the arithmetic subtraction operation to #$ScalarIntervals (q.v.) generally.  When applied to two arithmetically-comparable scalars, <code>MINUEND</code> and <code>SUBTRAHEND</code>, #$DifferenceFn yields the scalar that is the result of subtracting <code>SUBTRAHEND</code> from <code>MINUEND</code>.  For example, (#$DifferenceFn 88 11) is 77 and (#$DifferenceFn (#$Kilogram 4.2) (#$Kilogram 3)) is (#$Kilogram 1.2).
<p>
Note that when <code>MINUEND</code> and <code>SUBTRAHEND</code> are not arithmetically-comparable, <code>(#$DifferenceFn MINUEND SUBTRAHEND)</code> is undefined.  For example, (#$DifferenceFn (#$MinutesDuration 1) (#$Meter 3)) is undefined, since (#$MinutesDuration 1) is a #$Time-Quantity and (#$Meter 3) is a #$Distance, and time-quantities are not comparable with distances.
<p>
For addition, see #$PlusFn.")
(comment GreaterThan25HoursVentilation1LessThan24HoursZero "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events a duration greater than 24 hours is assigned a \"1\" and durations less than or equal to 24 hours are assigned a \"0\".")
(comment BooleanPhysicalField "The collection of all #$CycL representations of physical fields whole values are expected to represent true or false.")
(comment defaultBooleanStringsForKS "The corresponding predicate to the logical schema denoting function #$LogicalSchemaForKSWithNameFn")
(comment topicOfIndividual "This predicate relates individuals to things they are about, in a very general sense of \"about\".  <code>(#$topicOfIndividual IND THING)</code> means that #$Thing <code>THING</code> is a topic of #$Individual <code>IND</code>. <code>IND</code> may be a #$FieldOfStudy, a token of a newspaper article, a particular conversation, or any other individual which may be said to have a topic.  Thus (#$topicOfIndividual #$Etymology #$LexicalWord) means that the topic of etymology is words, and (#$topicOfIndividual #$WatergateScandal #$RichardNixon) means that the Watergate scandal is about Richard Nixon.  It is  correct to assert (#$topicOfIndividual #$Entymology #$Insect), but even though some insects are shiny, it would be stretching things to say that (#$topicOfIndividual #$Entymology #$Shiny).  Compare this predicate to #$topicOf, which relates instances of #$Collection to things they are about.")
(comment GreatVesselOfTheHeart "The collection of all #$BloodVessels which are considered to be the 'great' vessels of the #$Heart.")
(comment InterduneTrough "A specialization of #$CavityWithWalls. Instances of #$InterduneTrough is a trough formed between parallel longitudinal #$Dunes.")
(comment mutuallyExclusiveSchemaFieldListWRT "This predicate relates a physical schema with the list of its physical fields that have the following property.  A particular specified value of one of the fields -- some value for a physical field indexical, cannot be in more than one field.  This is typically the case when the field types are disjoint classes.")
(comment mutuallyLicensing "<code>(#$mutuallyLicensing TERM1 TERM2 )</code> means that <code>TERM1</code> is licensed by <code>TERM2</code> and <i>vice versa</i>.  For example, believing that a document is about <code>Coal</code> is licensed by learning that the document mentions <code>mining</code>, and <i>vice versa</i>. Implemented via <code>(#$isLicensedBy TERM1 TERM2) and (#$isLicensedBy TERM2 TERM1)</code> ")
(comment isLicensedBy "<code>(#$isLicensedBy LICENSEE LICENSOR)</code> means that <code>LICENSEE</code> is licensed by <code>LICENSOR</code>.  For example, believing that a document is about <code>LICENSEE</code> is licensed by learning that the document mentions <code>LICENSOR</code>.")
(comment primarySeasonOfElectoralProcess "The corresponding predicate (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PrimarySeasonOfElectoralProcessFn.")
(comment ElectoralProcessType-ByPolityAndOffice "A second-order faceting collection, which facets #$ElectoralProcess by polity (#$GeopoliticalEntity) and #$PublicOffice.")
(comment processToElect "The corresponding predicate of #$ProcessToElectFn.")
(comment dateOfElectoralProcess "(#$dateOfElectoralProcess ELEC-PROCESS DATE) means that DATE give the minimal #$TimeInterval at which the #$ElectoralProcess ELEC-PROCESS can be said to happen.")
(comment polityOfElectoralProcess "(#$polityOfElectoralProcess PROCESS POLITY) means that POLITY is the #$GeopoliticalEntity that is the sponsor and #$directingAgent of PROCESS, and that (#$TerritoryFn POLITY) is, by the same token, the place where the campaigning (see #$maximalCampaignOfElectoralProcess) and the culminating election (see #$culminatingElectionOfElectoralProcess) occur.")
(comment officeToBeFilledByElectoralProcess "(#$officeToBeFilledByElectoralProcess PROCESS OFFICE) means that OFFICE is the public office that PROCESS is supposed to fill.  Thus, e.g., it is true that (officeToBeFilledByElectoralProcess (ProcessToElectFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica UnitedStatesPresident (YearFn 2008)) UnitedStatesPresident).")
(comment VascularProcedure-Generic "The collection of vascular procedures either percutaneous or surgical.")
(comment FederalSavingsBank "The collection of all American #$BankOrganizations chartered and regulated by the Office of Thrift Supervision (OTS) and insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC).")
(comment hoursFromFirstVentilationToOpExit "<code>(#$hoursFromFirstVentilationToOpExit OP HOURS-DURATION)</code> means that  the time elapsed from the beginning of the first ventilation event during the hospitalization of the indexed operation OP and the end of that operation is <code>HOURS-DURATION</code>.")
(comment subElections "Where ELECTION is an #$Election held under the auspices of POLITY to fill POSITION-TYPE on DATE (see #$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn), (#$subElections ELECTION SUB-ELECTIONS) means that SUB-ELECTION is the #$properSubEvents of ELECTION consisting in the voting held for POSITION-TYPE on DATE that takes place under the auspices of some SUB-POLITY such that (#$subOrganizations POLITY SUB-POITY).  For example, where (#$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn #$UnitedStatesPresident #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 2004)))) denotes the 2004 US Presidential election and (#$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn #$UnitedStatesPresident #$NewYork-State (DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 2004)))) denotes the sub-part of that election taking place in the territory of #$NewYork-State, it is true that (#$subElections (#$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn #$UnitedStatesPresident #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 2004)))) (#$ElectionForPositionInPolityFn #$UnitedStatesPresident #$NewYork-State (DayFn 4 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 2004))))).")
(comment ElectoralProcessTypeOfPolityForOfficeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction to be used in reifying instances of the faceting collection, #$ElectoralProcessType-ByPolityAndOffice.")
(comment PrimarySeasonOfElectoralProcessFn "An individual denoting function which takes an instance of #$ElectoralProcess, e.g. (#$ProcessToElectFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$UnitedStatesPresident (YearFn 2008)), as its argument, and returns the 'primary season' of that electoral process, i.e. the set of all primaries bearing directly on the outcomes of the party conventions preceding the general election campaigns of the electoral cycle.")
(comment ProcessToElectFn "A partial #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for reifying instances of #$ElectoralProcess.  Specifically, (#$ProcessToElectFn POLITY OFFICE DATE) denotes the unique #$ElectoralProcess carried out by POLITY over the course of DATE, culminating in an election to fill OFFICE.")
(comment willDisambiguate "<code>(#$willDisambiguate LICENSEE LICENSOR)</code> means that <code>LICENSEE</code> will be licensed by <code>LICENSOR</code> appearing in text.  Combines #$generalisesToForLicensing and #$isLicensedBy and is used for testing.")
(disjointWith CardiacAssistDeviceProcedure MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment Intubation "The collection of all medical events where a tube is placed into an internal or external orifice of the body.")
(comment TrachealIntubation "The collection of all medical events where a tube is placed into the body via the #$Trachea.")
(comment SupraventricularTachycardia "A specialization of #$Tachycardia (q.v.).  Each instance of #$SupraventricularTachycardia is an abnormal heart rythm condition originating in the atria or AV nodes (both of which are \"above the ventricles\", hence the term \"supraventricular\" is applied).")
(comment AtrioventricularNode "A specialization of #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$AtrioventricularNode is an area of specialized tissue between the atria and the ventricles of the heart.  This node conducts electrical impulses from the atria to the ventricles.")
(comment SinoatrialNode "A specialization of #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$SinoatrialNode is an area of specialized tissue in the right atrium of the heart, near the entrance of the superior vena cava.  It generates the heart's sinus rhythm.")
(comment BundleOfHis "A specialization of #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$BundleOfHis is an area of specialized tissue that is part of the electrical conduction system of the heart.")
(comment hasAssociatedCMLS "(#$hasAssociatedCMLS THING CMLS AIS) means that SKSI translations involving THING utilize the reified mapping CMLS.  Typically THING will be a predicate whose values for a certain argument place utilize the mappings in CMLS.")
(comment Annulus "A specialization of #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$Annulus is a portion of fibrous tissue at the base of a heart valve.")
(comment EndocarditisVegetation "A growth symptomatic of #$Endocarditis.")
(comment evaluationProducesNormalValuesForTestType "<code>(#$evaluationProducesNormalValuesForTestType EVAL EVAL-TYPE)</code> means that the evaluation <code>EVAL</code> produces results that are considered normal for the test type <code>TEST-TYPE</code>.  Thus, for example, the query, <code>(#$evaluationProducesNormalValuesForTestType ?EVAL #$CreatinineBloodTest)</code> should return as bindings for <code>?EVAL</code> all evaluation events that produced results for a creatinine blood test that are considered to be normal.")
(comment LoeysDietzSyndrome "Loeys-Dietz syndrome is a genetic syndrome similar to Marfan's syndrome, but which is caused by distinct mutations.")
(comment HashimotosThyroiditis "Hashimoto's thyroiditis is an autoimmune disease wherein the patient's own T-cells attack the cells of the patient's thyroid.")
(comment Adjective "A #$SpeechPart and a specialization of #$OpenClassWord.  This is the collection of all adjectives.  An adjective is typically used as a noun modifier to denote a quality of the thing denoted by the noun phrase as a whole (as 'red' in 'the red shoes').  Many adjectives can be used either attributively (as in the foregoing example) or predicatively (as in 'the shoes are red').  Many adjectives have comparative and superlative forms (e.g. 'dark'/'darker'/'darkest').")
(comment Continent "A specialization of #$LandMass and #$Continent-Generic (qq.v.). Each instance is one of the seven land masses traditionally considered to be a continent.   The seven current traditional instances of #$Continent on the #$PlanetEarth are: the six traditional main land masses on the surface of the earth, plus the two #$geographicalSubRegions of Eurasia, Europe and Asia.  The current instances are: #$ContinentOfAfrica, #$ContinentOfAntarctica, #$ContinentOfAsia, #$ContinentOfAustralia, #$ContinentOfEurasia, #$ContinentOfEurope, #$ContinentOfNorthAmerica, #$ContinentOfSouthAmerica.  Cf. #$TrueContinent.")
(disjointWith Continent-Generic Slope-Topographical)
(comment Continent-Generic "A specialization of #$LandMass. Each instance of #$Continent-Generic is a land mass that is large enough to be considered more than a mere island.  Important specializations include #$Continent (which includes, as instances, the seven land masses on the planet earth that are typically considered to be continents by ordinary educated people), and the collection #$TrueContinent (q.v.).")
(comment broaderTerm "<code>(#$broaderTerm TERM1 TERM2)</code> means that <code>TERM2</code> is <i>broader</i> than <code>TERM1</code>, in an extremely general sense of \"broader\".  For example,  <code>TERM2</code> is, in the relevant sense, broader than <code>TERM1</code> if any of the following hold:<br><br>

 <code>TERM2</code> is a collection that subsumes <code>TERM1</code>; <br>
 <code>TERM2</code> is a collection that has <code>TERM1</code> as an instance; <br>
 <code>TERM2</code> is a collection, instances of which have instances of the collection <code>TERM1</code> as parts; <br>
 <code>TERM2</code> has <code>TERM1</code> as a part; <br><br>

This list of reasons for why <code>(#$broaderTerm TERM1 TERM2)</code> could hold is not exhaustive, but it should give a good indication of how general the #$broaderTerm relation actually is.")
(comment SystemRolePredicate "A specialization of #$Role.  Each instance of #$SystemRolePredicate is a binary predicate that relates an agent (an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) to a functional system (an instance of #$FunctionalSystem), specifying a functional role that the agent plays in the system.  Unless there are contextual or system-specific constraints to the contrary (cf. #$FixedFunctionalSystem), an agent may play multiple roles within the same system, and may indeed play different roles at different times in the history of the system.  Each instance of #$SystemRolePredicate is associated with a certain set of expectations (see #$expected-ToBe and #$amenable-ToBe) about how an agent who has a role will behave while playing the role, and also with a set of expected capabilities that the agent playing the role must have or maintain during the time it plays that role.  As a rule, these expectations may be satisfied by an agents's taking any number of actions. ")
(comment skillLevel "This predicate relates performers to types of actions.  (#$skillLevel OBJ ACT-TYPE ROLE PERF-ATT LEVEL) means that the #$SomethingExisting OBJ has the ability to play the role ROLE in instances of the type of #$Event ACT-TYPE, with LEVEL degree of PERF-ATT.  For example, (#$skillLevel Joe #$DiggingAHole #$performedBy #$Agility #$highAmountOf) means that, in general, Joe can dig holes with great agility.  To talk about actual performance in a particular action, use #$performanceLevel.")
(comment InanimateObject-NonNatural "A collection of tangible things.  An instance of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural is a tangible which was created during a #$PurposefulAction by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or a group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles working together) whether or not that creation was intended.  If the creation was intended the thing created is an instance of the more specific collection, #$Artifact.
<p>
Let's consider some positive and negative examples.
<p>
In addition to the obvious human #$Artifacts (buildings, tools, textiles, power lines), this collection includes #$Artifacts made by #$NonPersonAnimals, such as bird nests, termite mounds, and beaver dams.  By-products (see #$byProducts) of #$PurposefulActions, such as wood chips created when chopping down a tree and slag created when obtaining metal from #$MineralOre, are instances of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural but not of #$Artifact.  For more details on what is included in the concept #$Artifact, examine its comment.
<p>
Negative examples include bodily excretions (see #$ExcretionSubstance), most instances of tracks made while walking through mud or snow (both being instances of #$InanimateObject-Natural, and spoken words (being intangible).")
(comment UltimaOnlineService "A collection of computer accounts. In each instance of #$UltimaOnlineService, a subscriber pays a monthly fee for the privilege of being able to play #$UltimaOnline-TheGame.")
(comment investmentAmountDuring "(#$investmentAmountDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the amount of #$MonetaryValue AMOUNT was spent on instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by #$PartiallyTangible PT during the the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, where PT acquired those instances in order to use them as inputs to production. PT will commonly be an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible that is involved in producing goods, such as a #$Business or #$ManufacturingOrganization.")
(comment commonInfectionEntrySite "(#$commonInfectionEntrySite INFECTIONTYPE ORGTYPE
PARTTYPE) means that a common way for instances of ORGTYPE to contract
an INFECTIONTYPE infection is through an #$InfectingEvent that happens
at the ORGTYPE's PARTTYPE. One way to think of this:
(#$commonInfectionEntrySite INFECTIONTYPE ORGTYPE PARTTYPE)
means that if an instance of ORGTYPE is the #$bodilyDoer of an
instance of INFECTIONTYPE, the #$likelihood that the infection began
with an #$InfectingEvent that occurred at an instance of PARTTYPE
belonging to the ORGANISM is #$highAmountOf, if no other relevant facts are
known.")
(comment AChEInactivation "A specialization of #$BiologicalEvent.  Instances are #$ChemicalReactions that take place in the nervous system, typically as the result of exposure to some #$CholinesteraseInhibitingSubstance.  In such reactions, #$Acetylcholinesterase reacts with some #$ChemicalSubstanceType, preventing #$AcetylcholineHydrolysis from taking place.  This, in turn, leads to #$AcetylcholinePoisoning.")
(comment typeProvidesShelterForType "<code>(#$typeProvidesShelterForType SHELTER-TYPE TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>SHELTER-TYPE</code>, a subcollection of #$ShelteringArtifact, are used to provide shelter to instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  For example,
<code>(#$typeProvidesShelterForType #$HumanShelterConstruction #$HomoSapiens)</code> means that human shelter constructions are used to provide shelter to humans.")
(comment quotationOfExternalAgent "(#$quotationOfExternalAgent WORK QUOTE) means that the #$Information-Content of the #$TextString QUOTE (which #$TextString usually either contains quotation marks as its first and last characters or is indented within a #$GraphicalStructure) originated outside of WORK and prior to WORK's creation.  The #$Information-Content of QUOTE can, therefore, be attributed to an #$IntelligentAgent different from the creator of WORK or to another #$ConceptualWork.  For example, a quotation of a person and a quotation from another work would both be related to the #$StructurallySpecificWork within which they are contained by #$quotationOfExternalAgent.")
(comment MarkupLanguageSource "The collection of all #$TextStrings that are written in an SGML language for the purpose of generating hypertext (and non-text) that is intelligible on the web.")
(comment CataloguingWrittenMaterial "A specialization of #$IBOCreation and #$SortingPhysicalObjects. Each instance of this collection is an event in which someone (such as a #$Librarian) creates a #$Catalogue of written materials (by recording and/or filing information about those materials).")
(comment UnitOfFlowRate "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure: the collection of functions which return instances of #$FlowRate (i.e.,the volume of stuff which passes a point per unit of time).  E.g., (#$CubicMeterPerSecond 2000) denotes a #$FlowRate of 2000 cubic meters per second.")
(comment organismsExistentialState "(#$organismsExistentialState ORG ATT) means that ORG, an instance of #$Organism-Whole, is in the existential state, ATT, an instance of #$OrganismTypeByExistentialStatus.")
(comment keyGroupMembers "(#$keyGroupMembers GROUP AGENT) means that the instance AGENT of #$Agent-Generic is essential to the normal functioning of GROUP, an instance of (#$GroupFn #$Agent-Generic).  Notable specializations include #$hasLeaders, which relates a group to those who lead it, and #$organizationKeyMembers, which is restricted to groups that are also organizations (c.f., #$Organization).")
(comment GivingEconomicAid "A collection of events and a specialization of #$GivingSomething and #$MoneyTransaction. In each instance of
#$GivingEconomicAid, a relatively well-off #$Agent-PartiallyTangible gives some money to another, relatively impoverished #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (often a #$Country), in order to aid their economic development. See also (the related but not identical) #$CharitableDonation.")
(comment EntireSurfaceLayerFn "(#$EntireSurfaceLayerFn SPATIALTHING) returns the

contiguous #$EntireSurfaceLayer that covers SPATIALTHING.  We

remain agnostic about whether or not it is the case that

(#$physicalParts SPATIALTHING (#$EntireSurfaceLayerFn

SPATIALTHING)), although this may be the case for instances of certain

classes of #$SpatialThing.  We also remain agnostic as to the nature

of the 'covering' involved--i.e., the working assumption is that

(covers-Generic (SurfaceLayer-WholeThingFn SPATIALTHING)

SPATIALTHING).  Again, for instances of more specific classes of

#$SpatialThing, we may want to introduce assertions that conclude a

more specific 'covering' relation.")
(comment UsingOfTypeFn "An expression of the form (#$UsingOfTypeFn TYPE) is used to denote an instance of #$PurposefulAction that somehow involves an instance of TYPE, some sub-colleciton of #$SomethingExisting in the role of #$instrument-Generic.")
(comment associatedExchangeAgreement "The predicate used to state that an #$Agreement states the terms of some #$ExchangeOfUserRights.  Such #$Agreements are typically #$OwnershipAgreements such as #$TitleAgreements.  Also see #$associatedUserAgreement.")
(comment relyOn-Generic "(#$relyOn-Generic AGENT THING) means that AGENT relies on THING (or instances of THING, if THING is a #$Collection) for a significant part of AGENT's normal activities.  Note that an instance of #$Organization may ``rely upon'' something as well as an animal.  Plants, not being considered instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (in most circumstances) are not covered by this predicate.  See #$relyOnType, #$relyOnObject, and #$relyOnAgent.")
(comment Produce "A specialization of (#$FoodOrDrinkForFn #$Person), #$RawEdibles and #$FruitOrVegetableFood.  Each instance of #$Produce is a fruit or vegetable (in its raw state) that is normally eaten by humans.")
(comment ComplexQuantityPredicate "Each instance of #$ComplexQuantityPredicate is
#$TernaryPredicate which expresses a complex relationship between an
instance of #$SomethingExisting (in the first argument position), an
instance of #$Quantity (in the third argument position), and some
other item.  For example, #$productionRateOfRegion relates a #$GeographicalRegion to the #$Rate at which it produces some type of good, and #$levelOfPresenceIn relates an #$Agent-Generic to its degree of #$Presence in some group, place, etc.  Note that it is possible to convert such predicates into #$QuantitySlots by using the function #$QuantitySlotForArg1Fn and fixing the first (#$SomethingExisting) argument.")
(comment toOrientation "This predicate indicates, for the particular rotational motion ROT, the orientation that the #$primaryObjectMoving in that event has after that motion.  (#$toOrientation ROT ORIENT) means that when ROT ends, the object that moved in ROT has the final position ORIENT, with respect to the current frame of reference.  Examples of orientations include: #$HorizontalOrientation, #$VerticalOrientation, #$UpsideDown.  See also #$fromOrientation, #$OrientationVector.")
(comment HistoryMuseum-Structure "A specialization of #$MuseumStructure.  Each instance of #$HistoryMuseum-Structure is a construct that is used to store and display history exhibits (see #$HistoryMuseum-Organization, and #$MuseumHoldings).")
(comment knowsCommConvention "A #$CognitivePredicate that relates agents to 
communucation conventions that they are able to use.  (#$knowsCommConvention AGENT CONV) means that AGENT knows the #$CommunicationConvention CONV and can use it to encode or decode information.")
(comment PertainingToSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$OriginatingInSomething. In each #$PertainingToSomething, something is a part or attribute of something.")
(comment embeddedRegion "(#$embeddedRegion SMALL BIG) means that BIG not only surrounds SMALL in all horizontal directions, but it also touches it directly [#$touches-Directly] on all (horizontal) sides and #$bordersOn it.  BIG and SMALL do not share any physical part.  Any horizontal vector from SMALL will be within BIG as soon as it emerges from SMALL.")
(comment IssuingLicenseTypeFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction that takes for its value a
specialization of #$License-LegalAgreement TYPE and returns the collection
of all instances in which TYPE was issued.  For example, (#$IssuingLicenseTypeFn DriversLicense) denotes the collection of events in which an agent was issued an instance of #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement.")
(comment LineOfObjectsFn "(#$LineOfObjectsFn ?FOO) denotes the collection of objects of type ?FOO such that for each instance of the non-atomic constant, several instances of ?FOO are arranged in a line.")
(comment Rolling-SomeoneTumbling "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Tumbling-Exercising. In each #$Rolling-SomeoneTumbling, someone executes a roll, in tumbling.")
(comment GameSuperunit "A collection of individual #$Events.  Each instance of #$GameSuperunit is a standard unit of play which includes several #$GameEvents between the same contestants (even if there is only one contestant) as #$subEvents.  A set of rules regarding the #$DevisedStructuredActivity being performed predefines what is necessary for the completion of a #$GameSuperunit.  Examples include tennis sets and matches, baseball double-headers, and bridge rubbers.")
(comment implausibleSentence "(#$implausibleSentence SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information the sentence expresses is \"unlikely\" in a common-sense case.  For example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$MafiaContractor) is an unlikely supposition.  The plausibility of a sentence depends on a reviewer's subjective judgement, the context within which the claim is being made, and what other information is available to the system.")
(comment eventBasicDataSentence "A #$BasicDataPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Event to a quoted instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$eventBasicDataSentence EVENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a basic fact about EVENT.")
(comment MSMyComputerZoneFn "One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be performed when sourced wholly from within the computer itself. The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive.")
(comment needingAgent "Maps from a particular need context to the particular agent that needs what is stated in that context to be true in reality.  Since we have not yet addressed the issue of non-agent's needs, we've restricted the #$arg2Isa to #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.")
(comment usesCommunicationConventionForWork "A ternary predicate. (#$usesCommunicationConvention INFO_STRUCT CC CW) means that the #$InformationStore, INFO_STRUCT, uses the #$CommunicationConvention, CC, to represent the #$ConceptualWork, CW.  For example, the original version of the Iliad uses the #$AncientGreekLanguage as a #$CommunicationConvention, while a modern translation into Tagalog uses the #$TagalogLanguage and, when written, uses the #$WesternEuropeanWriting #$orthography as another #$CommunicationConvention. See also #$usesCommConventionForInfo, which relates an #$AspatialInformationStore, a #$CommunicationConvention and an #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment MiddleEasternPerson "The collection of all #$MiddleEasternPersons. This
collection is a very broad interpretation of what it means to be from
the Middle East and includes such collections as
#$EthnicGroupOfMiddleEasterners and (#$ResidentFn #$MiddleEast-Region).
This enables cyclists to make very broad assertions about the people
of the Middle East.")
(comment PrecipitationParticle "A specialization of both #$InanimateObject-Natural and #$Particle.  Each instance of #$PrecipitationParticle is a particle of liquid or solid water emitted by a cloud in some instance of #$PrecipitationProcess (q.v.).")
(comment statusInConflictEvent "(#$statusInConflictEvent AGENT EVENT STATUS) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT has the given #$ConflictEventStatus STATUS in the #$ConflictEvent EVENT.  An example of this would be (#$statusInConflictEvent #$DenverBroncos SuperBowl33-SecondQuarter #$Winning), which says that the Denver Broncos were winning Super Bowl XXXIII during the quarter mentioned. Statements ascribing an attribute to an agent will in most cases need to be explicitly temporally qualified.  The example given is an exception, because the #$DenverBroncos held #$Winning status throughout the entire second quarter.  If we wanted to assert that the Broncos were winning at some particular time during Super Bowl XXXIII, we would use #$holdsIn or #$holdsSometimeDuring to make explicit when the claim is true.")
(comment ObtainingPermission "The collection of events in which one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible gets permission from another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to do something.")
(comment beliefs "(#$beliefs AGENT SENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT subscribes to the truth of the proposition PROP expressed by SENT (a #$CycLSentence-Assertible).  Note that PROP might or might not actually be true. See also the predicate #$beliefStatements, which relates a belief to a #$BeliefSystem.")
(comment drugOfChoiceAdministeredFor "(drugOfChoiceAdministeredFor DRUGTYPE AILMENTTYPE) means

that a #$providerOfService in the #$MedicalTreatmentEvent that is the

#$treatmentAppliedToCondition of an instance of AILMENTTYPE will

desire that there be an #$AdministeringADrug which occurs as a

#$subEvents of the treatment and in which the drug administered is an

instance of DRUGType, provided the caregiver believes this is not the

case, and also that if PREFDRUG and OTRDRUG are both instances of

#$DrugSubstance that are #$availableForEvent for an instance of

#$AdministeringADrug which is the #$treatmentAppliedToCondition for an

instance of AILMENTTYPE, and such that OTRDRUG is not known to be an

instance of DRUGTYPE, the #$providerOfService in the #$AdministeringADrug

will prefer PREFDRUG to OTRDRUG.")
(comment Discipline-Sexual "This is the collection of sexual activities in which one person 

disciplines another for the purpose of sexual arousal. #$Discipline-Sexual

and #$Bondage-Sexual often go together.")
(comment GenreFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction. #$GenreFn takes as its arguments a subset of #$ConceptualWork and an instance of #$ArtisticTypeByStyle and returns the collection of that kind of #$ConceptualWork that are of that genre, or #$ArtisticTypeByStyle. For example, (#$GenreFn #$LiteraryWork-CW #$PropositionalConceptualWork-ScienceFictionGenre) returns the collection of all science fiction literary works.")
(comment TVShowOnNature "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily provide information           about #$WildernessAreas including information about #$WildAnimals in           their natural #$Habitats.")
(comment dateAwarded "(#$dateAwarded AGENT AWARD DATE) is true iff an #$AwardPractice of
type AWARD was bestowed on an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT on the #$TimeInterval DATE.")
(comment EmploymentTermination "A specialization of both #$EndingAnAgreement and #$OrganizationalTransferOut.  Each instance of #$EmploymentTermination is an event in which some employee (an instance of #$IntelligentAgent) ceases to work for his or her employer.  The termination may be initiated by either party, or it may have been specified in the original #$WorkAgreement (q.v.) that specified the terms of the employment.  Specializations of #$EmploymentTermination include #$ResigningFromEmployment, #$EmployeeLayoff, #$DischargeWithPrejudice, and #$RetirementEvent.")
(comment SelfConfidence "Faith in oneself and one's powers without any suggestion of conceit or arrogance.   If one has a large portion of #$SelfConfidence, their state of mind is often marked by ease and freedom from uncertainty, diffidence, or embarrassment.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  A typical more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityType than #$SelfConfidence is #$Vanity.")
(comment terminalOfTrans-Generic "(#$terminalOfTrans-Generic TRANS THING) means that THING marks one of the             terminal points in the instance TRANS of #$GeneralizedTransfer, either its             beginning or its end.  For example, consider a trip TRANS from Austin to             Omaha, NE.  In this case, it would correct to assert both             (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic TRANS #$CityOfAustinTX) and              (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic TRANS #$CityOfOmahaNE).  Compare this predicate to             #$to-Generic and #$from-Generic: #$terminalOfTrans-Generic is             a generalization of both of these predicates.  Note also that like #$to-Generic and #$from-Generic this predicate is very general.  Here are two more examples to illustrate its generality: (i) someone sends an e-mail in an instance EMailSending03 of #$EMailSending from the instance EMailAddress03 of #$EMailAddress to EMailAddress04.  In this case it would be correct to assert both (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic EMailSending03 EMailAddress03) and (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic EMailSending03 EMailAddress04).  (Note that in this case it would be better to use the more specific predicate #$informationTerminal.)  (ii) in the instance GAIN001 of #$GainingUserRights the instance AGT001 of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible receives something from AGT002.  In this case both (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic GAIN001 AGT001) and (#$terminalOfTrans-Generic GAIN001 AGT002) are correct.  You may also want to look at #$transferRouter-Generic and #$transferRelay-Generic.")
(comment Bibliography "A collection of instances of #$ReferenceWork.  Each instance of #$Bibliography sets forth  references to other works for a particular purpose (e.g., surveying a particular discipline or collecting all of the works of a particular author).  An instance of #$Bibliography may be a stand-alone work or may be a #$subWorks of some larger work (such as an article [#$Article-PCW] or book [#$Book-CW].)")
(comment backgroundTextForComprehensionQuery "(#$backgroundRelevantToConclusion STRING1 STRING2 means that STRING1 is the the background text against which STRING2 should be evaluated")
(comment complaintIssued "A specPred of #$infoTransferred. (#$complaintIssued COMPLAINING COMPLAINT) means that COMPLAINT is the information (an istance of #$AspatialInformationStore that is transferred due to COMPLAINING, and instance of #$Complaining.")
(comment LinksCut-SubSystemFn "A function that, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a set SET of links in SYS (i.e., a subset of (#$LinksFn SYS)) as in (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET), gives the subsystem SUBSYS of SYS obtained by cutting all links in SET from SYS.  The 'cutting' of links will not remove any nodes, but removes those points on the links that are not nodes.  More strictly, SUBSYS is determined as follows: (i) SUBSYS is a subsystem of SYS (i.e., (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds), (ii) (#$NodesInSystemFn SUBSYS) = (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS), (#$LinksFn SUBSYS) = (#$LinksFn SYS) - SET, (#$LoopsInSystemFn SUBSYS) = (#$LoopsInSystemFn SYS) and (#$PointsInSystemFn SUBSYS) = (#$PointsInSystemFn SYS) - {X: X is a non-node-point in SYS and X is on a LINK for some LINK in SET}.")
(comment InoculatingSomething-BiologicalReproductionEvent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Propagating-BiologicalReproductionEvent. In each #$InoculatingSomething-BiologicalReproductionEvent, someone inserts a bud for propagation.")
(comment feelsTowardsPersonType "(#$feelsTowardsPersonType AGENT PERSONTYPE
  QUANT) says that AGENT
  has the quantity of feeling QUANT
  towards PERSONTYPE.  This predicate is useful
  in conveying notions of #$Prejudice and 
   preference -- notions for which 
   #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree are not especially 
    well-suited; having feelings towards a 
group is by no means identical to having 
feelings towards each member of that group.
  Examples of how to use this predicate: To say that
   the KKK feels a great deal of hostility towards
  people of African descent, one can say
 '(#$feelsTowardsPersonType #$KuKluxKlan
   #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks
   (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Hostility)) .'  To say
  that each individual Klansmen is so hostile, we can use
  the rule, '(#$implies (#$hasMembers 
   #$KuKluxKlan ?HICK) (#$feelsTowardsPersonType
 ?HICK #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldBlacks
 (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Hostility))).'  See the
  #$salientAssertions to get a sense of how
  feelings towards a group relate to the 
   individual members of that group.")
(comment precedesInGraphicalStructure "'(#$precedesInGraphicalStructure WHOLE PARTSTRUC1 PARTSTRUC2)' means that, within the #$GraphicalStructure WHOLE, the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE1 comes before the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE2.  There are certain types of #$GraphicalStructure that always precede certain other types of #$GraphicalStructure within an inclusive #$GraphicalStructure.  For example, within a #$CWStructure, an instance of #$TableOfContents always #$precedesInGraphicalStructure an instance of #$TextString that it is an #$alphabeticalIndexTo.")
(comment Enjoyment "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Enjoyment is some agent's feeling of pleasure or satisfaction in some experience or thing. Instances of #$Enjoyment vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or on the subject experiencing the feeling.  Specializations of #$Enjoyment include #$Amusement-Feeling and #$Entertained-Emotion.")
(comment BannerAdvertisementOnWebPage "The collection of 'banner' ads found on web pages. Typically, these banner ads are small and are designed to be visually catchy. Clicking on the banner ad takes the user to the advertiser's website. Many websites sell banner ad space to other companies, so the content of the ad may or may not be closely related to the content of the page that the ad appears on. (#$KathyPanton 8/14/99)")
(comment VaricellaZoster-Virus "The specification of #$Virus that causes #$ChickenPox and #$Shingles-Ailment in #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment performsInsAtLocation "(#$performsInsAtLocation AGENT TYPE LOC) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT performs instances of activities of type TYPE at location LOC.  For example, (#$performsInsAtLocation #$DallasCowboys HomeFootballGames TexasStadium) means that the Dallas Cowboys play home football games at Texas Stadium.")
(comment Precession "Gyration of the rotation axis of a spinning object #$PerpendicularTo a #$TorqueVector being exerted to change the direction of the #$Axis of rotation")
(comment ViticulturalDomain "The collection of geographical regions principally devoted to viticultural activity, a specialization of #$AgriculturalFacility. Instances of #$ViticulturalDomain  have parts that can include various type of building and geographical or agricultural features, their most important parts are fields of grapevine [#$GrapeVine]. They can be in one piece or constituted of many separated areas. The area cultivated may be in one  or many pieces as well. Such domains are administrated by instances of #$Vineyard.")
(comment MeetingSomeone "A collection of actions.  In a #$MeetingSomeone event, one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is moving and meets (comes into close proximity with) another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  This may or may not be purposeful.  It may be done by non-human animals, and occasionally by other sorts of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.
<p>
Note: this does not mean \"being introduced to someone\", but rather \"going to meet with someone\".")
(comment translationOfTextualPCW "(#$translationOfTextualPCW OLDPCW NEWPCW) means that NEWPCW is a translation of OLDPCW.  If OLDPCW is not textually-specific, e.g. a book of the #$Bible is being translated and multiple early versions are being used as source material, use the more general predicate, #$translationOfPCW  Note that this predicate relates two #$TextualPCWs. To say that a certain #$TextString is a translation of a #$TextualPCW, use #$translationOfCWToAIS. To say that one #$TextString (or any #$AbstractInformationStructure) is a translation of another, use #$translationOfAISFromTo.")
(comment EmptyTimeInterval "The collection of all 'empty' time intervals (whether continuous or discontinuous).  Elements are always intangible, abstract  relevant-event-free intervals of time.  An instance of #$EmptyTimeInterval is 'empty' of relevant or salient #$Events;  what is relevant or salient depends on the context.  In a StoryMt a piece of time where nothing notable happens is an instance of #$EmptyTimeInterval.  In a physics context, the background buzz of atoms may be relevant events, whereas that would not be relevant during a non-state-change of an electronic device, or a boring wait for a train.  See also #$TimeInterval.
<p>
Thus #$EmptyTimeInterval does NOT represent a time interval of duration zero (see #$TimePoint), but rather a (possibly long discontinuous) interval of 'empty time', which, analogous to 'empty space' (see #$FreeSpaceRegion), is an
interval of time in which nothing happens. Just as with space, where a region is empty only for some limited period of time, so too is it likely that an #$EmptyTimeInterval only makes sense for some limited region of space and limited context of relevant actions.")
(comment Vegetating-BiologicalReproductionEvent "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Propagating-BiologicalReproductionEvent. In each #$Vegetating-BiologicalReproductionEvent, something propagates asexually.")
(comment wearsSize "A binary version of #$humanMeasurements and a specialization of #$isa.  (#$wearsSize PERSON PERSONBYCLOTHINGSIZE) holds just in case PERSON is an instance of PERSONBYCLOTHINGSIZE.  The second argument to this predicate is an instance of #$HumanTypeByClothingSize and is a collection of persons who wear the same size of a particular type of clothing.")
(comment FamilyMovie "#$FamilyMovie is a collection of instances of #$MovieShowing each of which relates a story which is appropriate for viewing by every member of a family, including minors, and may even be enjoyed by all. (Contrast with #$Children'sMovie which is appropriate for young children, but not likely to be enjoyed by adults.)")
(comment SexuallyMature "Having the gender-specific physical and physiological attributes of the adults of the species.  We expect #$SexuallyMature individuals to be #$FertileAnimal and also that only #$SexuallyMature individuals are #$FertileAnimal.")
(comment InfectionSiteTypeByGrade "An #$QuantityType the values of which describe site of
#$Infections affecting a BLO.")
(comment typeHasStyle "(#$typeHasStyle TYPE STYLE) means that every instance of collection, TYPE, has (in some sense) STYLE.  This is one of the broadest predicates that can be used to ascribe a style to a type of thing.  This is not equivalent to (#$relationAllInstance #$hasStyle TYPE STYLE).  This latter
assertion entails that every instance of Type is an instance of STYLE.  This is a somewhat weaker relation.  Consider the relation between a type of music and its
genre: (#$typeHasStyle #$ReggaeMusic #$MusicalComposition-Reggae) holds but ReggaeMusic is 
a specialization of #$Music which is a specialization of #$InformationBearingThing.  #$InformationBearingThing is disjoint from MusicalComposition of which #$MusicalComposition-Reggae is a specialization.  Hence, (#$relationAllInstance #$hasStyle #$ReggaeMusic #$MusicalComposition-Reggae) is false.  Avoid using this predicate in favor of more specific ones.")
(comment acknowledgements-DocumentPartOf "(#$acknowledgements-DocumentPartOf WORK ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS) means that the #$GraphicalStructure ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and contains an expression of the authors' (or others') gratitude to or appreciation of an individual or organization that was somehow helpful or inspirational to the authors in the creation of WORK.  Acknowledgements may be written by #$Authors, illustrators, or any entity that makes a significant contribution to the work in which the acknowledgements appear.")
(comment DanceRecreationalEvent "What a non-professional person might do for fun at, for instance, a #$DanceClub.  Parts of this event may involve a #$Dancing.  For professionals do see #$Dancer-Performer, #$EntertainmentPerformance, #$Dancing.")
(comment InanimateObject-Natural "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType and a specialization of both #$InanimateObject and #$NaturalTangibleStuff.  Each instance of #$InanimateObject-Natural is an inanimate object that was not created by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in a #$PurposefulAction.  Thus, the #$MoonOfEarth, human #$Sweat staining a shirt, and most footprints left by people in the snow belong to this collection; but wood chips left around a tree being chopped down, tailings left from a mine, and the #$ArcDeTriomphe do not.")
(comment JustifiedByAuthority "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType.  This is the collection of all cyc arguments which are \"justified by authority\".  This collection is used to that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) was purposely added to the Cyc knowledge base by some agent (as opposed to being inferred somehow by Cyc) on the basis of a specific outside authority (e.g. #$ReferenceWork), and is to be treated as sound.")
(comment NewtonianPhysicsSpindle "The microtheory spindle for #$NewtonianPhysicsMt.")
(comment storesInformationPermanently "(#$storesInformationPermanently IBT INFO) means that the #$InformationBearingThing IBT stores permanently the #$AspatialInformationStore INFO. In different contexts, what counts as storing permanently will vary. The information content of a book is stored permanently compared to the information content of a chalkboard.")
(comment PreparingForUndesirableSituation "The collection of #$PurposefulActions in which an agent prepares for a possible situation (#$Situation) that is abnormal, undesirable, and forseeable from the point of view of the agent. The action can be entirely mental, as in #$MakingAPlan, or can involve #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvents, such as buying extra food as a preparation for a possible supermarket shortage. To relate #$PreparingForUndesirableSituations to the #$Situations that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparednessFn. See also #$PreventingFromHappening and #$PreventingFn.")
(comment MilitaryOperationsBackgroundContext-General "This is the collection of microtheories in which general information relevant to all or most military operations is given. Note that information about specific individuals that are relevant to a particular operation, or a set of particular operations (or proposed operations), should not be asserted in a MilitaryOperationsBackgroundContext-General. Rather, information about individuals should be asserted in a #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory (or an instance of a spec thereof).")
(comment sourceWorkForSOEMt "(#$sourceWorkForSOEMt WORK MT) identifies WORK as one of the instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork whose content is drawn upon in determining the features of the graph that is displayed when querying for a graph of the Cyc ontology from the microtheory MT. Typically, WORK will be used to determine what edges to show, and what nodes are focal (of high interest -- see #$defaultCandidateFocalNodeInSystem).  See also #$SOEGlfMt and #$TheCycOntologyGraph.")
(comment Embassy-TheMission "#$Embassy-TheMission is a specialization of #$DiplomaticMission-ThePost.  Each instance of #$Embassy-TheMission is an embassy, which is the official diplomatic representation of a country A in a foreign country B. Not to be confused with the buildings in which such offices are hosted. See #$EmbassyBuilding.")
(comment DocumentTypeByPrintStatus "A collection of attributes. Each instance of #$DocumentTypeByPrintStatus           is an attribute that indicates the printing status of a document (esp.           book).")
(comment physicalReferentOf "This binary predicate is used to assert that a particular

#$PartiallyTangible object or #$PhysicalEvent is the 'physical

referent' used to 'pin down' a particular #$SpatialThing. If a

#$SpatialThing 'exists' in the empirically observable universe, i.e.,

if it is a #$SpatialThing-Localized, then it must be localized in

virtue either of some physical reference point or of some other

#$Intangible #$SpatialThing-Localized.  A spatial system, like the

#$GeodeticCoordinateSystem, must ultimately 'ground out' in 'physical

entities' that are either #$PartiallyTangible, like the

#$RoyalObservatory-Greenwich, or that are #$PhysicalEvents, like the

#$RotationOfEarth.  This predicate is very broad: it could, for

example, be used to represent the case where a boundary stone is used

to mark a property boundary, the case where the rotation of the earth

localizes the geographic poles, and the case of the

#$RoyalObservatory-Greenwich being used to 'ground' the

#$GeodeticCoordinateSystem.  Borderline cases include cases where

borders are instantiated by physical objects, the way the Rio Grande

instantiates part of the US-Mexico border or the way the ridge of

Everest instantiates part of the Nepal-Tibetan border.  Non-examples

include cases where one #$Intangible #$SpatialThing-Localized is used

to localize another: for example, the case where the geographic poles

are used to localize the #$EarthsEquator.")
(comment BlankSurface "A subcollection of #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible, each instance is a surface not written or printed on.")
(comment agreementForbids "This quaternary predicate is used to indicate a type of action that a particular agent is forbidden to play a particular role in under the terms of a particular agreement. (#$agreementForbids AGREEMENT AGENT ACTTYPE ROLE) means that AGREEMENT forbids AGENT to play ROLE in any instance of ACTTYPE.  For example, if a peace accord ACCORD forbids its signatories to wage war against one another, and SIGNER is one such signatory, then (#$agreementForbids ACCORD SIGNER #$War #$performedBy) holds.  Similarly, a business contract may forbid one agent to compete with another after s/he sells rights to a product, design, or practice to a second agent.")
(comment GroupOfNFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting a specific group of objects of a given type and cardinality.  The third argument should be a Cyc term which is somehow indicates which group is created by using this function.  For example, (#$GroupOfNFn #$Waitperson 13 #$Threadgills-NorthLamar) may represent the thirteen waiters at Threadgills in the current context.  To refer to the collection of groups of a certain kind with a certain cardinality, use #$NFn.")
(comment Rainwater "The collection of liquid water that falls as rain from instances of #$RainProcess.  #$Raindrops are composed of #$Rainwater, as are puddles left over after a #$RainStormAsObject.")
(comment posForms "The predicate #$posForms is used to indicate the different parts of speech that a particular English word has associated with it.  (#$posForms WORD POS) means that the #$EnglishWord WORD has a form that can serve as the #$SpeechPart POS.  For example, #$Dot-TheWord has forms for both #$CountNoun and #$Verb.  Forms of a word used for different parts of speech may or may not differ from each other in sound and/or spelling.  To find out, or to specify, the string that represents a particular POS form of a specific word, use #$partOfSpeech.")
(comment maritalStatus "(#$maritalStatus PERSON STATUS) means that the #$Person PERSON has the #$PersonTypeByMaritalStatus STATUS.  For example, (#$maritalStatus #$BillClinton #$Married).  The marital status of a person depends on whether, and when, that person was married to another person, and how the marriage ended.")
(comment Spirit-Intangible "The collection of all intangible supernatural beings.  A spirit may be incarnated in a tangible object such as an organism.  An important specialization of this collection is #$Soul-Spiritual.  Spirits are #$FictionalThings in #$NaturalismMt.")
(comment caseTypeOf "(#$caseTypeOf CASE-TYPE PT) means that the spec of #$CaseProduct, CASE-TYPE, is the collection of  cases of the #$ProductType PT.  Instances of CASE-TYPE are #$PackagedProducts consisting of many instances of PT packaged together in a box.")
(comment tradeBalanceInWithDuring "(#$tradeBalanceInWithDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the difference between the value of the instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 to the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING and the value of the instances of PRODUCT-TYPE imported by REGION1 from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  Thus if the value of REGION1's exports of PRODUCT-TYPE to REGION2 is greater than the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING, REGION1 will have a positive trade balance in PRODUCT-TYPE with REGION2.  If the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE from REGION2 exceeds that of its exports, it will have a negative trade balance in PRODUCT-TYPE with REGION2.  This latter case can be expressed using a #$UnitOfMoney function with a negative number as its argument.")
(comment GeographicalSpaceRegionFn "(#$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn OBJECT) denotes the location in  in geographical space of OBJECT, an instance of #$GeographicalThing.  This function denotes a portion of the geographical surface of reference  (see #$GeographicalSpaceRegion) on which OBJECT is projected, i.e. this function  does *not* denote the spatial extent of object, but a surface projection. The spatial extent in a tridimensional space at a given time is denoted by #$SpaceOccupiedByFn. In order to  denote the instance of #$GeographicalRegion at which OBJECT stands in the context of geography, see #$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn and its corresponding predicate. See  #$exactlyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical, the predicate corresponding to #$GeographicalSpaceRegionFn.")
(comment CredibilityStatus "This attribute denotes the default amount of trust or faith that one agent puts in the statements, predictions, and promises of another.  Of course, agents can be credible in certain contexts and not others -- to specify the credibility of a particular instance of

#$Communicating, see #$credibilityToAgent.")
(comment UnreifiableFunction "A specialization of #$Function-Denotational instances of which are such  that their values are not reified in the Cyc system.  More precisely, an instance of #$UnreifiableFunction is such that closed \"NATs\" (see  #$CycLNonAtomicTerm) built from its standard CycL name are _not_ instances of  #$HLReifiedDenotationalTerm.   Constrast with #$ReifiableFunction.  Usually it is more efficient to make functions reifiable; but it is not desirable  to reify every non-atomic term, such as those built from (names of)  instances of #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars.  For example, it would be cumbersome to reify every term of the form (#$Inch N) that happened to appear in a CycL assertion.")
(comment designedForLocationType "(#$designedForLocationType PRODUCT PLACE_TYPE) means that the #$Artifact, PRODUCT, is designed to be situated in [#$usualLocationOfObject] locations which are instances of PLACE_TYPE.")
(comment laborForceFractionDuring "(#$laborForceFractionDuring REGION COL THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the labor force of the economic sector or occupation COL in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the total labor force of REGION during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor), where the labor force (of an economic sector or occupation) in a region at a point in time is the sum of the number of persons employed and unemployed (in the sector or occupation) in the region.  COL can range from a broad economic sector, such as agriculture, manufacturing, or services to a more specific segment of the economy such as the automobile industry; in either of these cases, COL will be a specialization of the collection #$Industry-Localized.  Alternatively, COL can be an instance of the collection #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that agriculture accounted for 37 percent of Oman's labor force in 1993, we can say (#$laborForceFractionDuring #$Oman #$AgriculturalEconomicSector (#$YearFn 1993) (#$Percent 37)).  See also #$laborForceDuring and #$laborForceOfIndustryOrOccupationDuring.")
(comment genlWorks "<code>(#$genlWorks NARROW-WORK GENERAL-WORK)</code> means that <code>NARROW-WORK</code> is a #$DevisedPracticeOrWork that includes all of <code>GENERAL-WORK</code>, but has additions (refinements).  This is the relationship of a story to its plot, #$GinRummy to #$Rummy, or \"variations on a theme\" to the musical theme itself.")
(comment vestedInterest "(#$vestedInterest AGENT INTEREST) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT has some stake, positive or negative, tangible or intangible, in what befalls the thing INTEREST.  See also the specializations #$positiveVestedInterest, #$negativeVestedInterest.")
(comment Nodding-Drowsing "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Drowsing. In each #$Nodding-Drowsing, someone is almost asleep.")
(comment wantsToRelnA-Inverse "(#$wantsToRelnA-Inverse AGT COL RELN) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible ?AGT wants the following to be the case: (RELN INS AGT) for some generic instance of COL. See also #$wantsToRelnA.")
(comment policyTypeCoversTypes "A predicate that relates an instance of
 #$InsuranceTypeByThingCovered to the type of thing that instances of that policy-type are intended to protect.  (#$policyTypeCoversTypes POLICY-TYPE COVERED-TYPE) says that POLICY-TYPE is a type of insurance plan (see #$InsurancePlan) that insures instances of COVERED-TYPE.  Note that this is not equivalent to (#$relationAllExists #$policyCoversObjects POLICY-TYPE COVERED-TYPE), for from the latter one can derive that (#$relationAllExists #$policyCoversObjects POLICY-TYPE GENLS) for any generalization GENLS of COVERED-TYPE that meets the argGenl constraints of #$policyCoversObjects, whereas one cannot conclude (#$policyTypeCoversTypes POLICY-TYPE GENLS) -- i.e., from the fact that title insurance is, by definition, designed to insure title agreements -- (#$policyTypeCoversTypes #$TitleInsurance #$TitleAgreement) -- we are not licensed to conclude that title insurance is by definition designed to insure agreements, generally -- (#$policyTypeCoversTypes #$TitleInsurance #$Agreement).")
(comment LatitudeLineFn "(#$LatitudeLineFn ?DEG ?MIN ?DIR) returns the latitude line around the earth at the distance from the #$EarthsEquator specified by degree ?DEG, minute ?MIN, and direction ?DIR. For example, the #$ArcticCircle would be specified as (#$LatitudeLineFn (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 66) (#$Minute-UnitOfAngularMeasure 31) #$North-Directly).")
(comment objectAddedTo "(#$objectAddedTo EVENT OBJ) says that OBJ is the instance of #$PartiallyTangible to which a #$thingIncorporated is added during EVENT, an instance of  #$Incorporation-Physical")
(comment Socialist "The collection of #$Persons that believe in the #$Socialism.")
(comment Barrel-Container "The collection of all barrels. A type of #$StorageConstruct and #$HollowCylindricalObject. The collection #$Barrel-Container is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$Barrel-Container is a large cylindrical container, traditionally made of wood.")
(comment accountStatus "The predicate #$accountStatus indicates whether a particular account is paid up, overdue, delinquent, etc.  (#$accountStatus ACCT STATUS) means that the #$Account ACCT has the attribute STATUS (see also #$AccountTypeByStatus).")
(comment MaterialTransporter "A #$DeviceTypeByFunction.  Each instance of #$MaterialTransporter is a #$TransportationDevice whose #$primaryFunction is to move a #$LiquidTangibleThing (e.g. a large amount of #$Oil) or a #$Group of #$InanimateObjects (e.g. a (#$MobFn #$LogOfWood)) from one place to another.  Specializations include #$GarbageTruck, #$Barge, and #$Wheelbarrow.  Note that many #$MaterialTransporters <i>can</i> be used to transport people or animals; but this is not their primary function.  #$WreckerTruck is not a specialization of #$MaterialTransporter, since the #$primaryFunction of a #$WreckerTruck is to tow a single #$RoadVehicle (not a #$Mob of them).  Two borderline cases are #$PickupTruck and #$Forklift.")
(comment subjectivelyEvaluatesIndividualToThing "This predicate can be used to assert that an agent has made a certain essentially subjective assessment or value judgment about a particular individual in relation to a topic.  (#$subjectivelyEvaluatesIndividualToThing AGENT INDIV TOPIC EVAL) means that the AGENT projects upon INDIV the #$EvaluativeQuantity (q.v.) EVAL in regard to the TOPIC.  As the evaluation in question is essentially subjective, the above formula of course does not entail either (i) that INDIV actually has the feature it is subjectively thought to have (or some \"objective\" counterpart thereof) or (ii) that any other given agent would also attribute EVAL to INDIV.  Indeed, outside of contexts explicitly defined so as to represent some particular agent's point of view (e.g. some sentient agent's inner mental world or the world-view espoused by a particular religion), it arguably makes no sense to attribute an #$EvaluativeQuantity to an individual directly.  ")
(comment MSTrustedSitesZoneFn "One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be initiated from the \"Trusted Sites Zone\". The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. The term \"Trusted Sites Zone\" refers to sites which have been explicitly defined for that computer as Trusted\". For the meaning of this term, please consult #$MicrosoftInc documentation.")
(comment harmfulProposition "The predicate #$harmfulProposition is used to state a condition that, if true, would (normally) diminish an agent's chances of success in a particular effort.  (#$harmfulProposition ENDEAVOR PROP GVP) means that if the #$ELSentence-Assertible PROP is true, then AGENT (who is referred to in PROP) will (normally) be hindered in achieving the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR.   GVP is a #$GenericValuePredicate whose role is to suggest how damaging such an occurrence would be to the success of ENDEAVOR.  For example, in a basketball game, it's normally very detrimental if one or more of the team's players is shorter than the average adult.  Thus, for any particular game, a #$highToVeryHighAmountOf disadvantage is indicated if the following #$harmfulProposition (expressed in #$CycL) is true: (#$heightOfObject PLAYER-X (#$RelativeGenericValueFn #$heightOfObject #$HumanAdult #$veryLowAmountOf)). (Rohrbaugh, 2/1998)")
(comment EarthRadius-Equatorial "The radius of the #$PlanetEarth at the #$EarthsEquator, approximately ((#$PerFn #$Mile #$Radian) 3963).")
(comment HaemophilusAegyptius "A collection of #$Bacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells resemble
#$HaemophilusInfluenzae and is the cause of Brazilian purpuric
fever in mainly hot climates, a disease of children characterized by #$Fever, purpura, shock, and death.")
(comment WaterTransportationDevice "A specialization of #$TransportationDevice, each instance of which is a device used for transportation on or through water. (It is thus not to be confused with a collection of devices used for transporting water.)  Specializations of  #$WaterTransportationDevice include #$Ship and #$Sailboard. A particularly important specialization is #$Watercraft : the collection of water transportation devices that protect their passengers from getting wet. See also the second-order collection #$WaterTransportationDeviceTypeByDesign.")
(comment ToplessBeach "The collection of all #$Beaches where it is permitted for women to be #$ToplessPerson.")
(comment ShowingSupportForSomeone "The collection of events in which one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible shows             support for another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (the #$beneficiary).  ")
(comment ConstructionCompany "A specialization of both #$CommercialServiceOrganization and #$PrivateSectorOrganization. Each instance of #$ConstructionCompany is an organization whose main function (see the constant #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction) is constructing or remodeling buildings, houses, dams, bridges, or other construction artifacts (see the collection #$ConstructionArtifact).")
(comment subTextMapping "ARG3 is a list of substrings representing the parts of ARG2 which correspond to the assertion ARG1.  ARG4 is a list of the starting indices within the #$actualTextOfPIT of ARG2 corresponding the positions of the ARG3 substrings.")
(comment objectPaidFor "(#$objectPaidFor EVENT OBJECT) means that in the #$MonetaryExchangeOfUserRights EVENT, the right to possess OBJECT is transferred from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another.  OBJ is not the #$objectTendered but the goods that are bought or rented.")
(comment OpenAccess "The attribute describing objects to which access is completely open.  Kinds of objects with #$OpenAccess include #$Device-Unlocked objects, unencrypted #$InternetCommunication, and unguarded pots of gold.")
(comment ProtectiveAttire "#$ProtectiveAttire is a specialization of #$SomethingToWear.  Each instance of #$ProtectiveAttire is something to wear that is designed to protect its wearer from the elements or from injury.  Notable specializations of #$ProtectiveAttire include the collections #$SnowGoggles, #$SurgicalGlove, #$WeldingMask, #$Helmet, #$BoxingHeadgear, #$Facemask-Baseball, #$FirefightersCoat, #$RainGear.")
(comment ActingCompany "The collection of #$EntertainmentOrganizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to produce and present plays (i.e., instances of #$DramaticPerformance). Actors are essential members of acting companies, as acting is an essential activity of a #$ActingCompany. Other members of an #$ActingCompany will probably include stage managers, costumers, directors, and stage hands. Instances of #$ActingCompany are specifically companies who employ actors for the purpose of presenting plays. #$ActingCompany, which is, among other things, a troupe of actors, should not be confused with #$TheaterCompany, which is a collection of organizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is also to provide instances of #$EntertainmentPerformance, but which doesn't necessarily employ actors. E.g., a company such as United Artists, which owns a chain of movie theaters is a #$TheaterCompany, but not an #$ActingCompany.")
(comment ComputerSoftwareMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$ComputerSoftwareMarketCategory is a computer software product marketed for use with computers.  Examples are spreadsheet software, game software, word processing software, web browsing software, etc.")
(comment DwarfPlanet "An instance of #$ConventionalClassificationType  defined by the #$InternationalAstronomicalUnion as the collection of celestial bodies such that each instance 1) orbits the sun (see #$TheSun), 2) has sufficient gravity to force it into having a round shape, 3) has not \"cleared\" the area around its orbit of other bodies, and 4) is not a satellite to another body (other than the sun).  Contrast with #$PlanetInTheSolarSystem.")
(comment requestReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval "An assertion of the form (#$requestReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval REQUEST PERCENT INDIVIDUAL INTERVAL) states that the #$ResourceRequest REQUEST represents a request to reserve PERCENT percent of the #$Individual INDIVIDUAL's time during the #$TimeInterval INTERVAL. This is a core predicate for describing what an #$ResourceRequest reserves, see also #$requestReservesPercentageOfIndForInterval.")
(comment hasPhysiologicalQuantity "(#$hasPhysiologicalQuantity BLO QUANT) means that the #$BiologicalLivingObject BLO has the #$PhysiologicalQuantity QUANT.  Note that many, perhaps most, assertions made with #$hasPhysiologicalQuantity will be time-dependent; for example, an individual person is not #$Strong throughout his or her life, but only during a portion of it.  For this reason, many assertions made with #$hasPhysiologicalQuantity will need to be temporally qualified.  Note: this predicate is meant to be used with measurable physiological features such as strength, pain etc.  For ascription of non-measureable physiological features use #$hasPhysiologicalFeature.")
(comment SteakKnife "A kind of knife used mainly for cutting pieces of a #$Steak-Beef-MeatCut or other tough meats.")
(comment GainingFreedom "The collection of all #$TransferOfControl events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible of some kind is released from some kind of significant check of his, her, or its freedom-of-action.  The release may be intentional on the part of the agent hitherto exerting control (see #$BeingFreedFromControl) or it may be unintentional (see #$GettingFreeFromControl).")
(comment NodesCut-SubSystemFn "A function that, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a set SET of nodes in SYS (i.e., a subset of (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS)) as in (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET), gives the subsystem SUBSYS of SYS obtained by cutting all nodes in SET from SYS.  The 'cutting' of nodes also removes all their attached loops and links (and points on them if any).  More strictly, SUBSYS is determined as follows: (i) SUBSYS is a subsystem of SYS (i.e., (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds), (ii) (#$NodesInSystemFn SUBSYS) = (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) - SET, (#$LinksFn SUBSYS) = (#$LinksFn SYS) - {LINK: LINK is a link in SYS and X is on LINK for some node X in SET}, (#$PointsInSystemFn SUBSYS) = ((#$PointsInSystemFn SYS) - SET) - {Y: Y is a non-node-point in SYS and Y is on LINK for some LINK in ((#$LinksFn SYS) - (#$LinksFn SUBSYS)), and (#$LoopsInSystemFn SUBSYS) = (#$LoopsInSystemFn SYS) - {LOOP: LOOP is a loop in SYS and X is on LOOP for some X in SET}.  Note that since there is no 'empty' #$PathSystem, SET must be a proper subset of (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) for (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) to be defined.")
(comment oxidationChangeFromTo "(#$oxidationChangeFromTo ELEMENT REACT-NUM PROD-NUM REACTION-TYPE) holds just in case the oxidation number of an instance of ELEMENT changes from REACT-NUM to PROD-NUM in  reactions of type REACTION-TYPE.  This statement holds just in case  (#$oxidationNumberInForm ELEMENT REACT-NUM SOME-STUFF REACTION-TYPE) and  (#$postOxidationNumber ELEMENT PROD-NUM SOME-OTHER-STUFF REACTION-TYPE) hold for some  SOME-STUFF and SOME-OTHER-STUFF.  This is not a functional relationship.  For any given  ELEMENT, it might be the case that ELEMENT appears in multiple places as a reactant or  product.  If this is the case, then two or more distinct #$oxidationChangeFromTo statements could be predicated of ELEMENT.")
(comment basesComplementaryBasePaired "(#$basesComplementaryBasePaired BASE1 BASE2) means that there is a hydrogen bond between #$NitrogenBases BASE1 and BASE2 and that BASE1 and BASE2 are complementary (see #$complementaryBaseTypes).")
(comment PetroleumFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of
#$Fire-ClassB. Instances of #$PetroleumFire have #$Petroleum-CrudeOil as their
#$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment evaluationOutputSentences "(#$evaluationOutputSentences EVALUATION-EVENT EVALUATION-STATEMENT) says that the sentence EVALUATION-STATEMENT is the sentence that expresses the (or a) judgment about the evaluee (see #$objectOfEvaluation) of EVALUATION-EVENT, an instance of #$Evaluating, that resulted from EVALUATION-EVENT.  For example, (#$evaluationOutputSentences BobsDriversTest0632 (#$not (#$isa Bob SafeDriver))) says that as a result of Bob's drivers license exam, it was determined that Bob is not a safe driver.")
(comment commonNickname "A predicate which relates human names (considered as instances of #$LexicalWord) to character strings which represent conventional variants of those names. (#$commonNickname NAME NICKNAME-STRING) means that the #$HumanGivenNameString NICKNAME-STRING is a common nickname for the #$Name NAME. This predicate is to be distinguished from #$nicknames, which (somewhat indirectly) relates a nickname to the thing which has the nickname.")
(comment FurniturePiece "A specialization of #$DurableGoods, #$HumanOccupationConstructObject, 
and #$SolidTangibleArtifact.  Each instance of #$FurniturePiece is a 
durable artifact of a type that is typically used in human dwellings 
(see #$HumanShelterConstruction) to make them more comfortable.  Many
useful specializations of this collection can be classified according 
to the main function their instances serve.  Such functions include: 
(i) providing support for people's bodies while they are seated or 
reclining (e.g. #$Bed-PieceOfFurniture and #$FootStool), (ii) providing 
work or activity surfaces (e.g. #$Desk-PieceOfFurniture and 
#$DiningRoomTable), (iii) providing organized or protective storage 
for one's belongings (e.g. #$Dresser-PieceOfFurniture and 
#$Bookcase), and (iv) providing illumination (e.g. 
#$ElectricLamp).  Most pieces of furniture are #$NonPoweredDevices 
(q.v.) in that they don't need any energy input in order to serve their 
function; but of course there are plenty of exceptions to this, such 
as electric lamps, console TVs, and hospital beds.  Note that 
#$FurniturePiece only includes _whole_ pieces of furniture; e.g. a 
sofa is an instance, but an arm of a sofa is not.")
(comment ObjectControlFrame "This frame is used for words that subcategorize for (i) an NP and (ii) an infinitive phrase which is controlled by the object of the matrix clause, i.e. the semantic subject of the infinitive clause is identical to the syntactic object of the matrix clause. Example: 'Mary convinced John to go to the party'. Note that this could be paraphrased as 'Mary convinced John that *John* (not Mary) go to the party', thus that the *object* (not subject) of the matrix clause is the one going to the party. Contrast this with #$TransitiveSubjectControlFrame.")
(comment ViolentAction "A specialization of #$HostileSocialAction.  Each instance of #$ViolentAction is a purposeful action of a type commonly considered violent -- generally because it is an action which intentionally attacks, damages, or destroys another agent, or attacks, damages, or destroys something close to some (target) agent. (This closeness may be physical or may consist in the fact that the agent owns or feels strong positive regard for the thing attacked.) Notable specializations of this collection include #$War, #$Torture and #$Bombing.")
(comment Pride "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Pride is some agent's feeling of self-esteem based upon her actions, possessions, accomplishments, or relationships.  Instances of #$Pride vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object of the feeling.  Specializations of #$Pride include #$Vanity, #$PrideOfMembership, and #$Triumph.")
(comment ScienceMuseum-Structure "A specialization of #$MuseumStructure.  Each instance of #$ScienceMuseum-Structure is a construct that is used to store and display scientific exhibits (see #$Museum-Organization, and #$MuseumHoldings).")
(comment totalSolutesInAqueousSolution "(#$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution SOLUTION SET-OF-SUBST) holds just in case water is the solvent in SOLUTION and each major solute present in SOLUTION is in SET-OF-SUBST.  SET-OF-SUBST includes both molecular substance types and strong electrolytes -- which appear only as separate ions in the solution.  Normally, it is implicit in the expression \"a .10M HCl solution\" that the solution contains no solutes other than HCl. We can make that assumption explicit by asserting: (#$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution SOLUTION-A (#$TheSet #$HydrogenChloride)).  Note that #$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution allows one to enumerate only the complete accounting of the major solutes in a sample -- #$totalSolutesInAqueousSolution is asserted to be #$completeExtentEnumerable (q.v.).")
(comment resultNotIsa "The predicate is used to indicate that any value returned by a particular denotational function may not be an instance of a certain collection. (#$resultNotIsa FUNC COL) means that FUNC returns a value that is not an instance of COL for any sequence of arguments for which it is defined.  Thus, where FUNC is defined for the sequence ARG1, ..., ARGn, (#$resultIsa FUNC COL) implies (#$not (#$isa (FUNC ARG1...ARGn) COL)).  See also #$resultIsa and #$resultDisjointWith.")
(comment KidnappingForRansomSourceSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle that collects source microtheories in which instances of #$HoldingHostageForRansom are described.")
(comment LowerEyelid "The collection of all lower #$Eyelids.  A #$LowerEyelid is a flap of #$Skin below and in front of the eyeball which half covers the #$Eye when the #$Eyelids are closed.  The #$Eyelids on one side of the face are closed when #$WinkingAnEye.  Those on both sides are closed when #$Blinking or when #$Sleeping")
(comment MethaneFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of
#$Fire-ClassB. Instances of #$MethaneFire have #$Methane as their
#$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment EntertainmentOrArtsProfessional "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation (q.v.) instances of which are persons who use some sort of creative or artistic abilities in carrying out the main function of their jobs. #$EntertainmentOrArtsProfessional includes both professional performing artists and producers of tangible artworks, either creative or commercial.  Note that this collection does _not_ include people working on the business side of those professions, such as producers or art dealers, whose jobs are more similar (see #$jobClass) to those of other business professionals (e.g. managers, marketers, sales representatives) than to the artists'; cf. #$EntertainmentOrArtsAdministrator.")
(comment dataSourcePasswordForSKS "An afterslot relating a #$SKSConnectionSpecification to the password by which it will be accessed.")
(comment SaleWithDelivery "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$SaleWithDelivery, after the object is purchased it is delivered to the buyer. The collection #$SaleWithDelivery is a subset of #$BuyingAnObject in which each instance includes a sub-event which is a #$DeliveryServiceEvent.")
(comment MedicalTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs in which #$Hospitals and activities           associated with them are the main focus in whatever #$Narratives are told in the shows.           This includes only fictional shows.  'ER' is an example.")
(comment ModerateLevelOfVirulence "The median #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionVirulenceLevel.")
(comment EducationalTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs with educational content, e.g. a National Geographic special.")
(comment LodgingOrganization "The collection of all #$ServiceOrganizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to provide temporary sleeping and/or living accommodations.  Typical instances of #$LodgingOrganization include hotel or motel chains (see #$CommercialLodgingOrganization) and single site bed and breakfasts, as well as homeless shelters, youth hostels and battered women's shelters.")
(comment holdsPosture "(#$holdsPosture CONFIG OBJ) means that OBJ is in some #$AnimalTypeByPosture during CONFIG.  The second argument of #$holdsPosture is loosely constrained (by #$PartiallyTangible), so that this predicate may be used to describe mannequins, animals, and other individuals (of whatever kinds) that might have a posture, as well as humans; however, by default Cyc assumes that an object in a posture is a #$Person.  See also #$postureOfAnimal, which relates an #$Animal and a #$AnimalTypeByPosture.")
(comment NaturalGasFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of
#$Fire-ClassB. Instances of #$NaturalGasFire have #$NaturalGas as their
#$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment TopSpin "Moving through the air with a spin so that the top moves forward faster and the bottom moves forward slower or even moves backwards.  The axis of spin is approximately horizontal.  TopSpin produces lift and changes the direction of bounce toward the direction in which the object is spinning.  This usually applies to a #$Sphere object.")
(comment RepeatedBoosterShot "#$RepeatedBoosterShot is the collection of series of #$BoosterVaccinationEvents which are repeated at some #$Frequency.")
(comment willingToPay "A specialization of #$monetaryValueOfThingTo. (#$willingToPay THING VALUE AGENT) means that the economic #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is willing to pay a maximum of #$MonetaryValue VALUE in order to obtain the #$TemporalThing THING (which may be goods or services). This may or may not mean that AGENT actually possesses funds greater than or equal to VALUE (and thus that AGENT would actually buy OBJECT if it were offered at the price VALUE or lower). This predicate is inspired by the economic concept of \"demand price\".")
(comment importAmountDuring "(#$importAmountDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil imported, or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil imported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).  The total value of a region's imports of all goods and services (over a given time period) can be expressed with this predicate using the constant #$Product as the second argument.")
(comment DosageOfByAnimalTypeFn "(#$DosageOfByAnimalTypeFn ?STUFF-TYPE ?ANIMAL) returns the collection of food ?STUFF-TYPE that is ingested by animals ?ANIMAL.  ?STUFF-TYPE is usually something edible.  Useful for talking about #$RelativeGenericValueFn statements e.g. `a lot of chocolate taken orally for a dog', `a small amount of meat taken orally for a person'.  This NAT was motivated by the need to say `if you are a person and drink a_lot_of_coffee_for_a_person, you'll be poisoned.' and `if you are a dog and eat a_lot_of_chocolate_for_a_dog, you'll be poisoned.' #$RelativeGenericValueFn requires these `a lot' collections to be reified and we decided a NAT was the best way to do this.")
(comment searchesQLWithString "An expression of the form (#$searchesQLWithString AGENT STRING) means that the #$Agent-Generic AGENT passes the #$CharacterString STRING to an instance of (#$ProgramProcessFn #$CycBrowserQueryLibraryToolModule) in order to execute a search for relevant queries.")
(comment chapterOf "'(#$chapterOf STRUCTURE CHAPTER)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure CHAPTER is a chapter within the #$CWStructure STRUCTURE.")
(comment Ball "An instance of #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Ball is a #$PortableObject, capable of #$RollingOnASurface, which is designed to be moved about (usually thrown, hit, or kicked) as part of some #$Game or recreational activity.  Most #$Balls are #$Spheres (or at least #$Spheroids), but some, such as instances of #$FootballBall-American, are not.  However, #$Ball is disjoint with #$Cylinder, #$LongThinObject, and #$Polyhedron; hence neither a #$FlyingDisc nor a #$Javelin nor a #$Die-TheCube is considered a #$Ball.")
(comment PoolWater "Chlorinated swiming pool water in liquid or solid state.  Once you boil pool water, the chlorine powder gets distilled away so by default if something is poolwater it is not in the #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter.")
(comment CausallySupported "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType and a collection of cyc arguments.  This collection can be used to indicate that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) is supported by some causal inference chain.")
(comment Manuscript-CW "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each instance of #$Manuscript-CW is an abstract work intended that has not been published in any sense. Instances of #$Manuscript-CW may be instances of many specializations of #$PropositionalConceptualWork, including #$Book-CW, #$Article-PCW, #$PhDThesis, etc.")
(comment MilitaryTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs in which #$MilitaryOrganizations           and #$MilitaryEvents are the main focus in whatever #$Narratives are told in the #$TVShow-IBTs.           This includes only fictional shows.")
(comment ObligationCreatingEvent "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence and #$CreationEvent.  Each instance of #$ObligationCreatingEvent is an event in which some #$Obligation is created.  After an #$ObligationCreatingEvent, some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible has an #$Obligation that he didn't have before.  Two notable specializations are #$MakingAnAgreement and #$MakingAPromise.")
(comment NoChange "An instance of #$LevelOfChange.  #$NoChange is the quantity of change that corresponds to no change at all.")
(comment LowLevelOfInfectivity "The lowest positive #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionInfectivityLevel.")
(comment SpyTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs in which spies and their work           are the main focus in whatever #$Narratives are told in the #$TVShow-IBTs.            Only fictional shows are included.")
(comment Permission "A specialization of #$Agreement.  Each instance of #$Permission is an agreement specifying some rights or privileges which have been granted to an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (q.v.).  A permission may be an informal agreement between individuals, but many instances are formal and involve permissions granted by a government authority to some agent.  Notable specializations of #$Permission include #$License-LegalAgreement and #$Visa-Permit.")
(comment mtSpatialUniverse-2D "A binary #$MicrotheoryPredicate that relates a given context (i.e. #$Microtheory) to a two-dimensional space region (see #$Surface) that constitutes \"the spatial universe\" in that context.  
<p>
<code>(#$mtSpatialUniverse-2D MT UNIVERSE)</code> means that <code>UNIVERSE</code> is the maximal space region of interest in <code>MT</code>.  This implies that 
<code>(#$isa UNIVERSE #$UniversalSpaceRegion-2D)</code> holds in <code>MT</code>. Anything known, in <code>MT</code>, to be a #$Surface is a part (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) of <code>UNIVERSE</code>. 
<p>
See also #$mtSpatialUniverse-3D.")
(comment does-ChangeOfState "The simplest event-predicate template: it expresses the fact that the filler of the 2nd argument place is engaged as the agent or performer in activitity of the type denoted by the first argument. Example: (#$does #$Running #$PeterSuen) is true at a time T iff Peter runs at T.")
(comment TimeIntervalBetweenFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  #$TimeIntervalBetweenFn takes two instances of #$TemporalThing as its arguments and returns an instance of #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.).  (#$TimeIntervalBetweenFn BEFORE AFTER) is the largest time interval strictly between the #$TemporalThings BEFORE and AFTER. That is, it denotes the time interval beginning immediately after the end of BEFORE and ending immediately before the start of AFTER.  It must be true that AFTER starts after BEFORE ends; i.e. (#$startsAfterEndingOf AFTER BEFORE).  Also, the interval between AFTER and BEFORE should not be empty.  Finally, every interval returned by #$TimeIntervalBetweenFn is #$temporallyContinuousDuring (q.v.). See also #$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn, a function that returns a time interval that includes the defining temporal things.")
(comment Investing "A specialization of #$Buying.  Each instance of #$Investing is an event in which an agent buys something (e.g. #$Stock, #$PreciousMetal, #$Antiques, or a stake in some #$BusinessRelationshipActivity) in the expectation that that thing will increase in #$MonetaryValue over time.  Note that #$Investing is disjoint with #$SpendingMoney (q.v.).")
(comment Revolution-Political "A specialization of #$ChangeOfGovernment.  Each instance of #$Revolution-Political is an event in which the previous government of a country or subregion of a country is replaced by a new regime, through political and military actions performed at least in large part by people who ahd been living under the old regime.  This collection includes the full notion of a revolution from the #$EscalationOfHostilities (which may vary from historian to historian), including the actual instance of #$War, and ending with the creation of a new instance of #$RegionalGovernment.
<p>
In short, a #$Revolution-Political is a successful instance of #$Insurgency.")
(comment conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet PROPOSITION1 PROPOSITION2 SETOFPROPOSITIONS) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory,  PROPOSITION1 and PROPOSITION2 are conditionally independent of each other given the truth of all the propositions in the set SETOFPROPOSITIONS.  That is, given the truth of the propositions in the set, the truth or falsehood of either of the two propostion arguments does not increase or decrease the #$derivedProbability that the other is true.  They are, in a sense, irrelevant to each other when the propositions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS is known to be true.  In most microtheories, generally, the #$conditionallyIndependent-GivenSet statement means that when all we know in the #$Microtheory are its accessible #$domainAssumptions, and the assertions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS, then the truths of the two formulae are probabilistically independent.  See also #$conditionalProbability and #$conditionallyIndependent.  To declare two propositions independent given a single proposition (which could be a conjunction), use #$conditionallyIndependentSentences.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment ToxicitySlot "A specialization of #$QuantitySlot. Instances are predicates that relate an instance of #$PartiallyTangible to their #$Toxicity with respect to a particular route, such as inhalation, skin-contact, or eye-absorption.")
(comment givee "This predicate relates the recipient of a gift to the event in which s/he/it is given that gift. (#$givee GIVING AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is the 'givee' in the #$GivingSomething event GIVING. For the gift-giver, see #$giver.")
(comment subRegions "(#$subRegions SUPER SUB) means that SUPER and SUB are both (effectively) two-dimensional regions (see #$SurfaceRegion) and that SUB lies wholly within SUPER (see #$inRegion). SUPER might or might not completely surround SUB.  To relate two instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity in this same way, use the predicate #$geopoliticalSubdivision (if it applies).  For other instances of #$GeographicalRegion, use #$geographicalSubRegions.")
(comment approximatePay "The predicate #$approximatePay relates occupations to  a typical range of pay offered to workers in those occupations.  (#$approximatePay JOBTYPE RATE) means that a person working in the #$PersonTypeByOccupation JOBTYPE makes approximately the #$MonetaryRate RATE as earned income.  RATE might be expressed in, e.g., #$DollarsPerHour, pounds-per-week, or yen-per-year.  RATE refers to average pay for the occupation JOBTYPE, excluding any unearned pay (such as matching 401K contributions) and the value of other employee benefits.")
(comment TransferringOwnership "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$TransferringPossession.  In each instance of #$TransferringOwnership the ownership of some object passes from one agent to another.  That is, there is a transfer from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another of a #$FullUseRights and the #$ExclusiveUserRights over the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer.  Often there is some compensation from the receiving agent (see #$ExchangeOfUserRights).")
(comment SourcesHighlyReliable "Characteristic attribute of a #$WrittenReportOnSituation with  highly reliable sources.")
(comment TVCookingShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs.  Instances of #$TVCookingShow are intended to provide             information about cooking.")
(comment CoilLoosening "The collection of events which consist of the loosening of a coil.  The coil may have a fixed center, a fixed axis or be unconstrained.  Non-fixed points engage in spiral motion about the#$Axis of rotation.  The process is reversed by #$CoilTightening.  #$CoilLoosening releases energy upon passing from a tightened state towards the rest state.  #$CoilLoosening past the rest state requires energy.  The term often means just uncoiling to(wards) the rest state.")
(comment Resentment "Indignation, displeasure, and ill will felt about something regarded as a slight, affront, insult, or indignity.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  More specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Resentment are #$Jealousy and #$Envy.")
(comment Watercraft "A specialization of #$WaterTransportationDevice.  Each instance of this collection is a device for transporting people and/or objects over water (i.e. on the surface) or through water (i.e. under the surface) without getting them wet.  Positive examples include all instances of #$Submarine, #$Rowboat, and #$Ship.  Negative examples include jet-skis and all instances of #$Surfboard and #$Sailboard. See also #$WaterTransportationDeviceTypeByDesign.")
(comment SupportGroupFn-FeelingType "#$SupportGroupFn-FeelingType takes as argument any instance TYPE of #$EmotionalQuantityType and returns the collection of all support groups for persons who have some degree of that quantity.  For example, (#$SupportGroupFn-FeelingType #$Panic) denotes the collection of all support groups for persons who have some quantity of #$Panic.")
(comment QualitativeTimeOfYear "A specialization of #$AnnualEventType.  Each instance of #$QualitativeTimeOfYear is a celestial event, such as an equinox (see #$Equinox) or a solstice (see #$Solstice). Such celestial events are readily qualitatively distiguished from the rest of the year.")
(comment Raininess "A specialization of #$WeatherQuantity.  Each instance of #$Raininess is a measure of the intensity with which it is raining at an instance of #$OutdoorLocation (q.v.).  (At the low extreme, it is not raining at all.)  Use with the #$GenericValueFunctions.  The raininess of a location is indicated with the predicate #$raininessOfRegion.  To represent the qualitative notion of it being a \"rainy area\" use #$RainyArea.")
(comment fromState "This predicate is used in connection with #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent, to identify the state (instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState) that a thing has before the change.  (#$fromState EVENT STATE-COLL) means that immediately prior to EVENT (which is the intrinsic-state-changing action), the thing that is changed in EVENT is an instance of STATE-COLL (and during the EVENT the thing changes from being an instance of that collection to being an instance of another instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState).  For example, prior to any X which is a #$TurningOnAnElectricalSwitch, the switch involved has (#$fromState X #$Device-Off).")
(comment Lesson "The collection of all organized #$temporallyContinuousDuring #$Teaching events in which one (or rarely more) #$Teacher instructs one or more #$Students on some material.  A #$CourseOfStudy is comprised of a series of #$Lessons on the same general subject matter.  Every #$Teacher teaches at least one #$Lesson and every #$Student attends at least one #$Lesson.")
(comment orgDeclaredEnemy "(#$orgDeclaredEnemy ORG AGENT) means that AGENT, an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, has been publicly declared by the #$Organization ORG as an enemy of ORG. #$orgDeclaredEnemy is an instance of #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate, and so applies to an ORG-AGENT pair only if both objects currently exist. (This is a default assumption. This relation could hold between an organization and an agent when, unknown to the organization, that agent recently ceased to exist.) Also, it must be true that the public declaration that AGENT is an enemy of ORG remains in force. This may cease to be the case without there being any public retraction of a declaration of emnity. For example, if an organization declares some state as enemy in 1970 but over the next 30 years develops a strong cooperative relationship with that state, it would no longer be true in 2000 that that state was a declared enemy of that organization, even if there was no public retraction of its declaration.")
(comment PascalChallengeKBContentTest-IRTask "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can solve a particular #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat which is part of the \"IR\" task (c.f.#$PascalChallengeIRTask).")
(comment StageProp "The collection of items set on a stage [#$StageForPerformances] in a play [#$Play-Dramatic] or #$StageProduction, the set in a #$MovieShowing, etc.  The prop is intended to represent an instance of some 

type of object, but may very well not actually be such.")
(comment MortgageAccount "The collection of #$CreditAccounts related to #$MortgageAgreements.  Whereas a #$MortgageAgreement contains the terms of the #$LegalAgreement resulting from a #$EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement, the #$MortgageAccount reflects the balance owed to the lender (the #$fromPossessor in the #$EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement) at any given time.  Use #$owedOnAccount to say what is owed in a #$MortgageAccount.")
(comment subNetwork "This predicate is a more specific version of #$subSystems that applies in particular to instances of #$ComputerNetwork. (#$subNetwork NETWORK SUB_NETWORK) means that the instance SUB_NETWORK of #$ComputerNetwork is a distinct part of the instance NETWORK of #$ComputerNetwork and that (see the #$comment on #$subSystems) SUB_NETWORK could have an 'independent existence and still be more or less the same.'  For example, there are many instances of #$LocalAreaNetwork that could be considered #$subNetworks of the #$Internet.")
(comment movieActorOrDirector "(#$movieActorOrDirector MOVIE PERSON) states

that PERSON was involved in MOVIE either as its #$Director-Movie, or as

an #$Actor, or perhaps even both.")
(comment DungeonMaster "The collection of all #$GamesMasters in playings of the role playing game [#$RolePlayingGame] known as #$DungeonsAndDragons.")
(comment HumanitarianGoal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory.  This attribute describes goals that involve assisting other people for humanitarian reasons and/or promoting human betterment.  For example, the mission of the #$InternationalCommitteeOfTheRedCross is humanitarian.  Promoting education, e.g., by endowments or the building of libraries, is another example.")
(comment closingTagOf "(#$closingTagOf TAG CLOSETAG) means that the #$TextString CLOSETAG is the closing tag form of the generic HTMLTag TAG.  For example, </caption> is the closing tag form of #$Caption-HTMLTag.")
(comment givesSupportToAgent "(#$givesSupportToAgent GIVER RECEIVER SUPPORT-LEVEL) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible GIVER provides the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible RECEIVER with the type and level of support SUPPORT-LEVEL.")
(comment nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation "#$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation is a more specialized form of the predicate #$topicRole.  It relates an instance of #$Investigation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Like #$topicRole it is intended to relate an entity to an event where that entity is part of the content of some mental state of some agent in the role of #$deliberateActors in that event.  In this case, it means that during the course of the #$CriminalInvestigation, the object is a non-focal subject of the investigation (constrast with #$subjectOfInvestigation). For instance, during a particular sub-event of a search for a missing person a detective discovers that the missing person has a vacation home based on looking at the subject's #$AddressBook and decides that the house is worth looking into.  The missing person would play the role of #$subjectOfInvestigation, the #$AddressBook would play the role of #$evidence, and the vacation house would play the role of #$nonFocalSubjectOfInvestigation.")
(comment PascalChallengeKBContentTest "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can solve a particular #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat.")
(comment minimumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint "Let SLOT denote an #$QuantitySlot, SLOT-ARG1 denote the #$arg1Isa constraint on SLOT, SLOT-ARG2 denote the

     #$arg2Isa constraint on SLOT, and VALUE denote the instance of SLOT-ARG2 such that

     (SLOT PATH VALUE).  Then (#$minimumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint

     PATH O-TYPE SLOT MIN) means that PATH is #$pathTrafficableForTransportVia

     #$transporters of type O-TYPE only if (#$greaterThanOrEqualTo VALUE MIN).  See also the related

     predicates #$maximumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint,

     #$maximumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint, and

     #$minimumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint.")
(comment TextualEntailmentConstant "Instances of this collection are terms which are used to represent #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormats.")
(comment PathArtifactSystem "#$PathArtifactSystem is a specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive, #$InanimateObject, and #$CustomarySystemOfLinks.  Each instance of #$PathArtifactSystem is an artificial system consisting of several instances of #$PathArtifact (q.v.). Important specializations of #$PathArtifactSystem include #$ComputerNetwork, #$RoadSystem, and #$SewerSystem")
(comment coverInSituation "(#$coverInSituation SIT COV) means that COV is the thing which is acting as the cover in the #$CoveringSituation, SIT.  COV is often sheetlike, and can conceal the covered objects if it is opaque.")
(comment activeTaskForSession "(#$activeTaskForSession SESSION TASK) means that a goal of the #$ComputerUserInteractiveSession SESSION is to accomplish (or further) the task TASK.")
(comment eventTypeFostersFeelingType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Event to an instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  <code>(#$eventTypeFostersFeelingType EVT-TYPE FEEL-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> often cause or result in instances of <code>FEEL-TYPE</code>.  (This is deliberately a vague notion.)  For example:
<pre>
(#$eventTypeFostersFeelingType #$WatchingTelevision #$Entertained-Emotion);
(#$eventTypeFostersFeelingType #$SexualCopulation #$Pleasure-Feeling);
(#$eventTypeFostersFeelingType #$Resting-Relaxing #$Relaxation).
</pre>")
(comment socialClass "(#$socialClass PRSN CLS) means that in the surrounding culture, the #$Person PRSN has the #$PersonTypeBySocialClass CLS.  As the name suggests, this predicate indicates PRSN's approximate social status as determined by his or her style of life -- quality of life, access to material goods and services, and social associations.  It may also depend on a cultural non-material system of social rank, based on birth, office, manners, vocal accent or other factors.  E.g., (#$socialClass #$DonaldTrump #$UpperClass) was true even when he lost his fortune and was (temporarily) bankrupt; and (#$socialClass #$BillGates #$UpperMiddleClass) was true, at least for a while, after he became a billionaire.  This is a good example of a predicate whose precise meaning, and associated heuristic rules, vary quite a bit from context to context, such as from country to country, from century to century, etc.")
(comment TranscriptCopy "The collection of official written, printed, or typed copies of certain official records or verbatim copies of an #$AnimalUtterance-IBT or series of #$AnimalUtterance-IBTs.")
(comment Embarrassment "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Embarrassment is some agent's feeling of mental confusion or discomposure.  Instances of #$Embarrassment vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or the subject experiencing the feeling.  A notable specialization of #$Embarrassment is #$Shame.")
(comment StockHoldings "A collection of partially tangibles; a subcollection of #$FinancialAssetHoldings.  Each instance of #$StockHoldings is a group of #$Stock shares owned by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  It may consist of shares in only one company or different groups of shares in multiple companies.")
(comment ReviewFn "#$ReviewFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all reviews of that thing or its parts or instances.  For example, (#$ReviewFn #$OperatingSystem) returns the collection of all reviews of operating system software, and (#$ReviewFn #$Threadgills-NorthLamar) returns the collection of all reviews of Threadgills restaurant.")
(comment sqlFlavorForSKS "An afterslot relating a #$SKSConnectionSpecification to the particular type of SQL program that be serving the database.")
(comment eventHasStyle "This predicate expresses that some instance of #$PerformingArtActivity 'has' or 'is performed in' some particular style.  For example, (#$relationAllExists #$eventHasStyle #$BalletDancePerformance #$BalletDancing) expresses that all ballet dance performances are performed in the ballet style.  See also #$hasStyle, which is used to relate instances of #$Artifact-Generic (i.e. conceptual works) to the style that they 'have.'")
(comment Artifact "A specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Artifact is an at least partially tangible thing which was intentionally created by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or a group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles working together) to serve some purpose or perform some function.  In order to create an instance of #$Artifact, it is not necessary that an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible create the matter out of which the #$Artifact is composed; rather, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible can create an instance of #$Artifact by assembling or modifying existing matter.  Examples of #$Artifacts include a wooden flute that's been whittled from a tree branch, a sawhorse that's been put together out of boards and nails, and a coin that's been minted by embossing or by melting liquid silver into a mold.  In addition to the obvious human artifacts (buildings, tools, textiles, power lines), the collection #$Artifact also includes certain sorts of things made by #$Animals, such as bird nests, termite mounds, and beaver dams. Artifacts without any tangible parts are excluded from the collection #$Artifact; they are included in the collection #$Artifact-Intangible.")
(comment succeedingValueOfMunsellHue "#$succeedingValueOfMunsellHue is used to establish the color
sequence of the instances of #$MunsellHue. The hues do not form a
#$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder, and require a special relation to
capture the fact that the sequence is circular. No further assertions
should be made with this predicate. Please see #$MunsellHue for
further information.")
(comment requiresClosingTag "(#$requiresClosingTag TAG) means that the #$MarkupLanguageTag TAG, when used in documents written in the appropriate markup language, requires that #$TextStrings designated by the tag be bounded by both opening and closing tags (see #$OpenTagFn and #$CloseTagFn).")
(comment DateExtractionPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each instance of #$DateExtractionPredicate is a predicate that takes an instance DATE of #$Date and relates it to an instance of #$CalendarCoveringType that is the unique date of that type that intersects DATE.  Examples include #$calendarDayOfDate.  See also #$OfDateFn.")
(comment ownsShare "The predicate #$ownsShare is used to state how much of some thing is owned by a particular #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  (#$ownsShare AGENT SOMETHING SHARE) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT has SHARE #$Percent (q.v.) ownership of the object or company SOMETHING.  Note that SHARE is a percentage and does not refer directly to a number of shares of #$Stock.")
(comment BassGuitarTablatureNotation "The class of #$TablatureNotation musical notation for electric bass guitars (see #$BassGuitar-Electric and #$TablatureNotation).")
(comment ScheduleFn-EntertainmentOrgType "(#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentOrgType ENTTYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include information about #$EntertainmentEvents provided (performed, hosted, organized, broadcast, etc.) by instance of ENTTYPE .  For example (#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentOrgType #$Theater-Organization) returns the collection of all schedules of entertainment events at theaters.")
(comment closingTagForStructure "(#$closingTagForStructure STRUC TAG) means that STRUC, an instance of either #$GraphicalStructure or #$TextString generated from SOURCE, an #$HTMLSource, has, in SOURCE, a closing tag of TAG, a tag that is the result of #$CloseTagFn.")
(comment LevelOfDiscomfort "An #$QuantityType whose elements represent the various levels of discomfort that may be felt by a perceptual agent.  Typically, the agent must be a living entity.  Typically, the sensation is an internal feeling, and is more of a long-lasting dull ache than a sharp pain (see: #$LevelOfPain).")
(comment AutomatedSpeechToTextConversion "A collection of events in which a #$SpeechToTextProgram is used to generate, from some #$AnimalUtterance-IBT, an instance of #$TextualMaterial which contains the same propositional information as is contained in the #$AnimalUtterance-IBT.")
(comment typeIsGenericUseOfTypeFn "An expression of the form (typeIsGenericUseOfTypeFn ACT-TYPE THING-TYPE) is used to relate a sub-collection of #$SomethignExisting to the sub-collection of #$PurposefulAction that involves the use of instance of THING-THING in the role of #$instrument-Generic.  This is the corresponding predicate of the function #$UsingOfTypeFn.")
(comment InstrumentPlayingFn "(#$InstrumentPlayingFn INSTRUMENT) denotes the collection of all events in which a single instrument of type INSTRUMENT is playing.  Thus, in a brass quintet playing there are five instances of (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$BrassInstrument) occurring.  There may also be an overall event of the ensemble making music, but #$InstrumentPlayingFn cannot be used for the composite event, because that would violate the single-instrument constraint.  #$InstrumentPlayingFn is useful for telling Cyc that whenever a musical group, such as a marching band, is playing, there are (probably multiple) sub-events in which individual instruments are playing.  We further specify that each instance of each result of applying

#$InstrumentPlayingFn be a #$temporallyContinuousDuring instance of

#$MakingMusicalSound.  Thus the discontinuous event that was the

musical piece played by a particular trumpet in a performance of

Beethoven's Ninth Symphony would consist of several continuous

instances of (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Trumpet) figuring as

#$subEvents.  However, there is a granularity to what 'continuous'

means in this context: specifically we are not including the miniscule

pauses that may obtain between the playing of one note and the next on

the instrument in question: thus, instances of the results of applying

#$InstrumentPlayingFn may consist of musical playings of more than one

note.  Finally, collections reified by means of this function include only 'live' performances, not digital or analog recordings of performances.")
(comment RadioStation-FM "The collection of #$RadioStation-Organizations that broadcast using the system of frequency modulation of radio waves.")
(comment FreeTourDayInFn "(#$FreeTourDayInFn ?PLACE) returns the collection of all
instances of(#$SightseeingInFn ?PLACE) that occur in ?PLACE as part of
a #$TravelTour, with a #$duration of roughly #$AboutADaysDuration, and
without scheduling constraints of any kind from the tour's
itinerary.")
(comment Paying "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType. Each instance of #$Paying is an instance of #$TransferringOwnership in which one agent (the #$payer) transfers something of value to another agent (the #$toPossessor) in exchange for some goods or services rendered (or to be rendered). In each instance of #$Paying, the #$payer gives the payee #$FullUseRights to the thing(s) transferred to the payee.  See the #$SharedNoteOnTheDifferenceBetweenPayingAndSpendingMoney.")
(comment MyersBriggsPersonalityTrait "The subcollection of #$PersonTypeByPersonalityTraits identified by
the Myers-Briggs personality test.")
(comment Currency "A specialization of #$TenderObject.  Each instance of #$Currency is a physical object generally accepted as legal tender, and used as a means of transferring a quantity of #$MonetaryValue (q.v.) between some instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  Instances of #$Currency may be coins, items of precious metal, paper bills for which precious objects are payable by a government to the bearer on demand, or unbacked paper bills required by a government to be accepted for payment of debts.  Instances of #$Currency are typically backed by and issued by national governments.")
(comment DirectObjectRoleMarker "An instance of #$GrammaticalRoleMarker. This attribute is  used to indicate that an argument of a hypothesized formula correspond to the direct object (loose sense) of the NL expression which the hypothesis has been derived from. See also #$grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention.")
(comment soleProductType "A binary predicate linking a particular #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to the kind of product or service it produces as its only product (aside from any trivial incidental extras).  (#$soleProductType AGENT PRODUCTTYPE) means that AGENT is a person or organization that sells or performs instances of product type PRODUCTTYPE, and virtually all of the sales that AGENT makes are of instances of this type.  See also #$mainProductType and #$makesProductType.")
(comment changesQuantityByAmount "This predicate specifies the amount by which a given quantity changes in a given time period.  (#$changesQuantityByAmount TIME THING SLOT AMOUNT) means that during TIME, THING's #$QuantitySlot SLOT changes by AMOUNT.  TIME is a #$TemporalThing, and AMOUNT is a #$ScalarInterval (which may be positive, negative, or #$noAmountOf).  For instance, (#$changesQuantityByAmount (#$YearFn 1980) #$SaudiArabia #$oilExport (#$MillionBarrelsPerYear 1)) means that in 1980, Saudi Arabia's oil export increased by 1 million barrels per day.  See also: #$changesQuantityByFraction, #$changesQuantityInDirection.")
(comment MonoatomicCation "A specialization of both #$Cation and #$MonoatomicIon. Each
instance of #$MonoatomicCation is a one-atom cation. This means a
single atom has lost a one or more electrons and thus has a positive
charge.")
(comment WorkEnvironment "A collection.  Any instance of #$WorkEnvironment is a #$SpatialThing-Localized subsumed by one's place of work, that is defined by its #$OccupationalPhysicalEnvironmentalQuantitys and #$SocialEnvironmentalAttributes.  An example might be #$Jennifer's usual work environment, which is spatially located in the #$Cycorp lobby, and has certain attributes such as a fair amount of traffic and noise from ringing phones and doors slamming shut.")
(comment EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityTypeFn "(#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn ACTIVITY_TYPE) denotes a collection of equipment types whose elements are used in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (a subset of #$DevisedStructuredActivity].  There are two sufficient conditions for a given collection being an instance of this collection.  One such condition applies to device collections whose major, predominant, or primary function is to play the role of #$deviceUsed in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (see #$primaryFunction-DeviceType).  Another such condition applies to device collections which are always used in performances of instances of ACTIVITY_TYPE (see #$eventTypeUsesDeviceType).  For example, (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$CardGame) denotes ``equipment for playing cards''.  Thus, because #$PlayingCard and #$AutomaticCardShuffler have #$CardGame as one of their main functions, Cyc should infer that these two device types are instances of (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$CardGame).")
(comment OfficeProductMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$OfficeProductMarketCategory is a product typically sold in an office supply store or in office supply catalogs, e.g., cases of xerox paper, desks, and file cabinets.")
(comment CommunistParty "The collection of political parties whose members hold the #$Communism.")
(comment keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom "(#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom ?COL1 ?COL2) states that the constant ?COL1 should never be offered as a precision suggestion from the constant ?COL2. (See #$CycPrecisionSuggestor.) ?COL1 may, however, be offered as a precision suggestion from any other constant that it is normally offered as a precision suggestion from.  For example, #$Queen-HeadOfState should NOT be offered as a precision suggestion from the constant #$FemalePerson, though it is a direct specialization of this constant and would normally be offered in this case.  We do not want to make #$Queen-HeadOfState #$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion, though, because we DO want to offer it as a precision suggestion for #$Monarch-HeadOfState (of which #$Queen-HeadOfState is a direct spec).  Therefore, (#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestionFrom #$Queen-HeadOfState #$FemalePerson) would be a reasonable assertion.")
(comment featureOfTypeWithinDistanceFromPlace "(#$featureOfTypeWithinDistanceFromPlace FEATURE TYPE DISTANCE PLACE) means that FEATURE #$isa TYPE and is roughly within a 4*(DISTANCE)^2 square box centered at PLACE. This predicate is implemented by finding the #$latitude and #$longitude of PLACE and constructing a 'bounding box' around it with sides of length 2*DISTANCE. Note that the 'roughness' of this box is greater away from the #$EarthsEquator, since the #$distanceBetween #$LatitudeLines #$decreasesCausally #$farFrom the #$EarthsEquator.")
(comment loves "(#$loves AGENT1 AGENT2) means AGENT1 loves AGENT2; AGENT2 has a strong emotional affect on AGENT1 whereby AGENT1 is usually loyal and devoted to and wishes well AGENT2, seeks AGENT2's companionship, and will incur substantial personal cost to help AGENT2.  Any #$Agent-PartiallyTangible can love any other #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, though there are specialized types of love which are restricted to two animals, two adult people, a person and a corporation, etc.")
(comment Hope "Expectation of fulfillment or success.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.")
(comment Happiness "The enjoyment of pleasurable satisfaction that goes with well-being, security, effective accomplishments, or satisfied wishes.  As with all #$EmotionalQuantityTypes, this is a #$Collection -- the collection of all possible amounts of happiness one can feel.  One instance of #$Happiness is `extremely happy'; another is `just a little bit happy'.  

Note:  Obviously there are no real units of measure for this quantity, ways of objectively measuring the amount of happiness possessed or gained or lost, etc., but still this has proven to be a useful way for Cyc to represent and reason with emotions.  E.g., one can have a rule that says that most people have a greater `amount' of happiness at their wedding than at their high school graduation, etc.  There are functions, such as #$LowAmountFn, which take a #$PrimitiveOrderedQuantityType (such as the instances of #$EmotionalQuantityType) such as #$Happiness and return as their value a certain-sized amount of that feeling; e.g., (#$LowAmountFn #$Happiness) is an expression whose value is a positive but small amount of happiness, and that in turn will be an instance of #$Happiness (and also will be an instance of #$FeelingAttribute).  #$EmotionalQuantityTypes organize into a lattice; e.g., there are several more specialized forms of #$Happiness that are present in Cyc's ontology, such as #$Elation, #$Delight, #$Triumph, etc.")
(comment SalesAd-CW "The collection of #$ConceptualWorks of advertisements [#$Advertisement-PCW] to sell something.")
(comment RadioStation-Organization "A subset of #$CommunicationsOrganization.  Elements of #$RadioStation-Organization are organizations that broadcast radio programs.")
(comment HumoralImmuneResponse "A collection of those instances of #$ImmuneResponse that are mediated by antibodies [#$AntibodyType]. #$HumoralImmuneResponse is an important defense against organisms that produce toxins or have polysaccharide capsules that interfere with phagocytosis.")
(comment TVShowOnFinance "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily provide information or advice            about #$Investing, saving #$MonetaryValue, taking out loans and related matters.")
(comment Puzzle-TangibleProduct "The collection of objects (often toys) that test one's ingenuity.  An example is #$JigsawPuzzle. See #$Puzzle-Generic for a broader sense of 'puzzle' and #$Puzzle for the #$ConceptualWorks.")
(comment ProductsMadeByFn "#$ProductsMadeByFn takes as argument any instance of #$ManufacturingOrganization and returns the collection of all products manufactured by that organization.  For example, (#$ProductsMadeByFn #$PfizerInc) returns the collection of all products manufactured by Pfizer.")
(comment CharitableDonation "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$CharitableDonation, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible donates money or goods to a charitable organization. See also (the related but not identical) #$GivingEconomicAid.")
(comment CJDCotemporalObjectsSlotTestCollection "This collection is for testing the #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate forward rules template.")
(comment RequirementsForCredentialFn "#$RequirementsForCredentialFn takes as argument any spec of #$Credential and returns the collection of all requirements (instances of #$NeedMicrotheory) which must be met (made true) before a credential of that kind will be issued.  For example, (#$RequirementsForCredentialFn #$HealthCertificate) returns the collection of requirements one must meet before one can be issued a certificate of health.")
(comment DanceCompany "The collection of EntertainmentOrganizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to produce and present instances of #$EntertainmentPerformances in which dancing is the predominant activity (i.e., instances of #$DancePerformance). Dancers are essential worker-members of instances of #$DanceCompany, as dance performances are an essential activity of such companies.  An instance of #$DanceCompany may be a group of people who have come together to perform one work or may be a professional organization for whom the dancers are #$employees [which they are in #$JobMt].  Since the #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction of an instance of #$DanceCompany is to perform dances (in a theatre, in front of an audience...), a night club at which customers dance socially would not be an instance of #$DanceCompany, although it would be an instance of #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization.")
(comment TVBroadcastOfTypeFn "#$TVBroadcastOfTypeFn takes as argument any content-defined spec of #$MovingImage (including specs of #$MovieShowing or #$TVShow-IBT) and returns the collection of events that are TV broadcasts of instances of that spec.   For example, (#$TVBroadcastOfTypeFn #$StarTrek-Classic) returns the collection of television broadcasts of the original Star Trek series.  (#$TVBroadcastOfTypeFn DocumentaryFilm) would return the collection of events that are television broadcasts of documentaries.")
(comment localFaxNumberText "ARG2 is the `local' fax number of the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  This means that ARG2 may include a #$TelephoneExchangeNumber and a #$PhoneSuffix, but it will not include an #$AreaCode or a #$TelephoneCountryCode.")
(comment ProvidingInformationToComputerProcess "The collection of all communication acts [#$CommunicationAct-Single] in which a computer user provides information to  a running computer process [#$ComputerProcessRunning].  If this was solicited information use the more specific, #$ProvidingRequestedInformationToComputerProcess.")
(comment LexicalMtOfLanguageForSystemFn "<code>(#$LexicalMtOfLanguageForSystemFn LANGUAGE SYSTEM)</code> denotes the microtheory that is the <code>LANGUAGE</code>-specific lexicon for the classification system <code>SYSTEM</code>.  For example, <code>(#$LexicalMtOfLanguageForSystemFn #$EnglishLanguage #$TheCycOntology)</code> denotes #$GeneralEnglishMt, the English-specific lexicon for the Cyc ontology.")
(comment BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle "The #$BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle is a neo-Greek-Roman style of building design developed in Europe that became popular in the late 19th and early 20th Centuries for large buildings, especially in #$France, and the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica. It is characterized by the use of symmetric arrangements of columns, ornate pediments, elaborate domes, and Greek and Roman style details.  The U.S. federal and many states' #$StateCapitolBuildings are in the #$BeauxArtsArchitecturalStyle.  It passed out of style in the early 20th Century.")
(comment litigants "(#$litigants TRIAL AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is one of the contending parties in the #$Trial TRIAL.")
(comment DistributionReservoir "A specialization of #$WaterReservoir.  Each instance of #$DistributionReservoir is a reservoir connected with the distribution system of a water supply project, used primarily to accommodate fluctuations in demand which occur over short periods (several hours to several days) and also to provide local storage in case of emergency, such as a break in a main supply line or failure of a pumping plant.")
(comment BalletCompany "The collection of organizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to produce and present theatrical entertainment in the form of instances of #$BalletDancePerformance. Ballerinas and their male counterparts are essential employee-members of instances of #$BalletCompany. Since instances of #$BalletCompany are primarily engaged in the business of producing instances of #$BalletDancePerformance (i.e., instances of #$DramaticPerformance, and thus events which take place in front of an audience, in a theatre, and in which the predominant activity is ballet dancing), a ballet school would not be an instance of #$BalletCompany since the #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction of a ballet school is teaching ballet, not performing. (Of course, most ballet companies are affiliated with ballet schools, which schools generally have the same name - e.g., the American Ballet Theatre (company) and the School of the American Ballet - as the ballet company. But there is a distinction between the two.)")
(comment SugarRefinery "The collection of places where #$Sugar is refined. See also #$OilRefinery.")
(comment ImportExportOrganization "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$ImportExportOrganization is a #$DistributionOrganization whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to import and/or export goods.  It may also sell the goods (see specializations of #$SellingOrganization), or it may simply sell its services as a distributor.")
(comment Fire-ClassB "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$CombustionProcess. Instances of #$Fire-ClassB have as their #$energySourceForEvent flammable liquid or gas, including solvent, tar, oil-based paint, or lacquer.")
(comment fieldsOfPlantType "(#$fieldsOfPlantType PLANTS FIELDS) means that FIELDS is the

collection of fields of instances of PLANTS. This predicate relates a type

of plant to the collection of fields where this type of plant is

predominante. Note in particular that althought FIELDS includes some

cultivated fields [see #$AgriculturalFacility] it also includes wilderness

areas covered with grass or weed [see #$Field-Land]. For instance, (#$FieldFn

#$GrapeVine) is the collection of fields of #$GrapeVine and

(#$fieldsOfPlantType #$GrapeVine (#$FieldFn #$GrapeVine)). See the

corresponding function #$FieldFn.")
(comment HomeAudioAndVideoProductsMC "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$HomeAudioAndVideoProductsMC (i.e., Market Category) is an audio or video device that consumers typically buy for personal use at home, e.g., television sets, stereo systems, telephones.")
(comment infectionReservoir "(#$infectionReservoir ORG INFECTION) relates a type of infection INFECTION to the reservoir ORG that may carry it.  The reservoir is an alternate or passive host that harbors a pathogenic organism, but does not necessarily suffer from the infection itself.  It is, however, a source from which the infection can spread.  For example, rats are the #$infectionReservoir of the #$BubonicPlague.  The rats transmit the infection to fleas, the #$infectionTypeHasVectorTypes of the #$BubonicPlague, which in turn infect humans.")
(comment NullLevelOfCommunicability "The lowest #$AttributeValue of #$InfectionCommunicabilityLevel
qualifying Infections not contagious.")
(comment predicateEncapsulatesScene "(#$predicateEncapsulatesScene PREDICATE SCENE) identifies PREDICATE as an #$AnalysisScriptGeneratedPredicate that is generated from SCENE.  In particular, (#$genls SCENE #$CycQueryRunning), so there is a unique query (see #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified) with a unique #$InferenceSentenceParameter SENTENCE.  Where ARG1 ... ARGN occur as free-variables in SENTENCE, PREDICATE will be a predicate of arity N that holds for exactly those bindings that make SENTENCE true.")
(comment productionRate "(#$productionRate PRODUCER PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the instance of #$SomethingExisting PRODUCER produces instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE at the #$Rate RATE.  PRODUCER might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, an #$Island, or a #$Person; and RATE might be a number per unit of time, or a volume per unit of time, or a #$MonetaryRate.")
(comment TransferringPossession "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$TransferringPossession, the possession of a single object (see #$objectOfPossessionTransfer) is transferred from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another.  Such an event alters the rights of _two_ different agents to use the object in question: one agent loses some #$SituationTypeByUserRights (q.v.) over it, while the other agent gains some #$SituationTypeByUserRights over it.  Thus each #$TransferringPossession event is both a #$LosingUserRights event and a #$GainingUserRights event.  Note that in instances of #$Buying, #$Bartering, or #$Renting, _two_ such #$TransferringPossessions occur, because there are two objects whose possession is transferred.  For example, in buying a car, the right to use the buyer's money is transferred to the auto seller, while the ownership of the car is transferred to the buyer.  In such cases, both of the #$TransferringPossession events (one for each object) are subevents (see #$subEvents) of the instance of #$Buying, #$Renting, or #$Bartering.  See #$ExchangeOfUserRights.")
(comment ExtractionTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of

#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of #$ExtractionTerrainFeatureType are

collections of human made terrain features that are designed for the

extraction of some tangible substance or object, like mineral deposits or 

construction materials. For instance,

#$Quarry and #$Mine-ExcavationFacility are instances as well as some various structures

used for carrying out extraction processes, the collection of rigs and #$Well 

for instance.")
(comment GameForOSFn "(#$GameForOSFn OP-SYS) denotes the class of #$ComputerGamePrograms whose instances all run under OP-SYS.")
(comment ProducerFn-EventType "#$ProducerFn-EventType takes as argument any specialization of #$Event-Organized and returns the collection of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles who produce events of that type. For example, (#$ProducerFn-EventType #$MusicalPerformance) returns the collection of all agents who produce musical performance events.")
(comment CarBomb-BoobyTrap "A specialization of #$Bomb-ProximityTriggered.  Each instance of #$CarBomb-BoobyTrap is a bomb designed to explode when a certain sort of event occurs in the car to which it is wired.  For example, it is common for car bombs to be designed to detonate when an ignition fires.  Cf. #$TruckBomb-VehicleDelivered and #$CarBomb-VehicleDelivered")
(comment Device-Unlocked "The state of being unlocked.  As a #$LockedState, this refers to the state of a locking device.  As a #$IndividualTypeBySecurityStatus, this refers to the state of an object that may have a lock, such as a house, car, or bicycle.  In this sense, #$Device-Unlocked is a kind of #$OpenAccess.")
(comment BitterFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction,
#$ReifiableFunction, and #$UnaryIntersectionFunction. When applied to
a specialization COLLECTION of either #$Odor or #$ObjectTypeByTaste, #$BitterFn
returns as its value the specialization of COLLECTION consisting of
all instances of COLLECTION that are bitter in odor or taste,
respectively. Thus, (#$BitterFn (#$OdorFn #$Almond-TheNut)) is the
collection of all things that have a bitter almond odor. Conversely, (#$BitterFn (#$TasteFn #$Almond-TheNut)) denotes the collection of
all things that have a bitter almond taste.")
(comment ConditionalProbabilitySetFn "A function used for probability statements. (#$ConditionalProbabilitySetFn PROPOSITION SETOFPROPOSITIONS) applied to an #$CycLAssertion and a set of #$CycLAssertions, results in the probability of PROPOSITION being true given that all the propositions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS are known to be true, in the applicable #$Microtheory.  It yields a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true.   In most microtheories, generally, this #$ConditionalProbabilitySetFn refers to the conditional probability that PROPOSITION is true given only that the propositions that are elements of SETOFPROPOSITIONS, and the #$domainAssumptions accessible in the applicable #$Microtheory, are true, without regard to any further evidence or the truth of any other assertions.  See also #$ConditionalProbabilityFn, #$PriorProbabilityFn, #$DerivedProbabilityFn, #$conditionallyIndependent, and the predicate version of this function: #$conditionalProbabilitySet.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment InterArgTypePredicate "The subcollection of both #$InterArgConstraintPredicate and #$ArgTypePredicate (qq.v.) whose instances are used to put conditional argument-type constraints on polyadic relations in regards to two of their argument-places.  Each instance of #$InterArgTypePredicate specifies, with respect to a given #$Relation, that one of its arguments (the \"dependent\" one) must be of a certain type, contingent upon another of its argument's (the \"independent\" one's) either being of a certain (possibly different) type or being identical to a certain thing.  Depending on the particular inter-arg-type predicate, an argument's \"type\" might be specified in terms of either #$isa or #$genls. (For more details see the nearest specializations of #$ArgTypePredicate and
#$InterArgTypePredicate.)
<p>
An inter-argument-type predicate PRED has argument-places for designating the relation and the two argument-types (or an argument-type and a particular thing); the (numerically-specified) identities of the relation's corresponding dependent and independent arguments is in most cases fixed (as in #$interArgIsa1-2), but is in some cases variable and specified via two additional argument-places of PRED's (as in #$interArgIsa).  In cases of the former sort, where the relation's argument-places are fixed, PRED is a #$TernaryPredicate that takes as it first argument (or \"arg1\") a relation, as its arg2 the type specified for the relation's independent argument, and as its arg3 the type (or thing) specified (contingently) for the dependent argument.
<p>
See also the specializations #$InterArgIsaPredicate and #$InterArgEqualsIsaPredicate.")
(comment feelsTowardsObjectToDegree "(#$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree AGT OBJ EMOTYPE DEGREE) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGT feels a feeling of the #$FeelingAttributeType EMOTYPE towards the #$Individual OBJ, with intensity DEGREE.

Note: the first argument can be a non-human intelligent agent, such as a dog or a company, because we often ascribe feelings and emotions to them, and they often behave consistently with having such feelings and emotions.  See also #$feelsTowardsEvent.")
(comment rangeForSightUnderIlluminationCondition "(#$rangeForSightUnderIlluminationCondition SIGHTTYPE CONDITION RNAGE) means that the maximum effective range for SIGHTTYPE under the lighting conditon CONDITION (an instance of #$OutdoorLocationTypeByIlluminationSource) is RNAGE.")
(comment typeInstancesStartAfterEndOfIn "(#$typeInstancesStartAfterEndOfIn LATERTYPE EARLYTYPE MAINTYPE) means that in instances of MAINTYPE, an instance of EARLYTYPE will be followed by an instance of LATERTYPE. Note that this is consistent with no event of type EARLYTYPE occurring in the event of MAINTYPE and a different instance of LATERTYPE occurring prior to an instance of EARLYTYPE in an instance of MAINTYPE.   This is closely related to #$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType but is not restricted to use in #$ScriptedEventTypes and allows for use of more general arguments than those in the range of #$SceneFn.")
(comment FiscalPeriod "Each instance of this collection is a date (usually either a year (see #$FiscalYear) or a calendar quarter (see #$FiscalQuarter)) kept track of by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible as part of its financial accounting procedures.")
(comment predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set "An instance of #$SummaryPredicate useful for summarizing knowledge about more than one term. (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set PRED-TYPE SET SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE's arg0 slot is occupied by an instance PRED of PRED-TYPE and that all of the terms in the set of terms SET occupy other argument positions in SENTENCE. For example, (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set #$LikesPredicate (#$TheSet #$JenniferSullivan   #$Cynthia) (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia)) is true, and means that some instance of #$LikesPredicate occurs as the arg0 in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia), and that all of the terms in the set denoted by (#$TheSet #$JenniferSullivan   #$Cynthia) also occur in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia). This predicate is particularly useful for asking queries with the first and second argument slots bound and the third slot open.  For example,  asking (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set OrganismRequirementsPredicate (#$TheSet (#$AdultFn #$Dog) (#$AdultFn #$Cat)) ?SENTENCE) will mean the system will find any assertions whose arg0 is an instance of OrganismRequirementsPredicate that also contain the terms (#$AdultFn #$Dog) and (#$AdultFn #$Cat).  See also #$predicateTypeSummaryForThing.")
(comment Lambada-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
lambada style.                            ")
(comment renownLevel "A spec pred of #$hasAttributes. (#$renownLevel THING LEVEL) says that THING has the attribute LEVEL, where LEVEL is an instance of #$LevelOfRenown.  For example, (#$renownLevel #$BillClinton #$Famous) says that #$BillClinton is #$Famous.  This predicate is an instance of #$PresuppositionPredicate because one can only truly have an #$LevelOfRenown with respect to some group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.  See #$renownWithinGroup.")
(comment objectTakenCareOf "(#$objectTakenCareOf EVENT OBJ) means that the object OBJ is acted on in the #$TakingCareOfSomething event EVENT by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in order to maintain, preserve, or promote the health or good condition of OBJ.")
(comment Extradition "A specialization of #$TransferOfControl.  In an instance of #$Extradition, a person who has been legally accused of wrongdoing is transferred from the custody of one regional government -- state, provincial, or national -- to the custody of another regional government which is deemed to have a superior right to prosecute the alleged criminal, where that right is usually based on a pre-existing treaty or law to which both governments subscribe.  The accused is the #$transferredThing in an extradition.  The #$from-Generic is the government which originally had the person #$HeldCaptive; the #$to-Generic is the government which gets custody as a result of the extradition.  The extradition is performed by some authorized #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles of the governments involved (see #$performedByPart).")
(comment Repetition "A specialization of #$ContinuedActivity.  Each instance of #$ResumedActivity is an event in which an agent resumes the performance of some discontinuous event (cf. #$temporallyContinuousDuring).")
(comment deliberateActors "<code>(#$deliberateActors ACT ACTOR)</code> means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>ACTOR</code> is conscious, volitional, and purposeful in the #$Event <code>ACT</code>.   <code>ACTOR</code> is aware of acting in <code>ACT</code>, and chooses to play the role he/she/it does in <code>ACT</code>.")
(comment temporalExtentInMt "A ternary #$TemporalPredicate that relates each #$TemporalThing to the #$TimeInterval that it occupies in some particular Microtheory.  (#$temporalExtentInMt TEMP TIME MT) means that, in MT, TIME is the time-interval of longest #$duration (q.v.) during which TEMP exists (if TEMP is a #$SomethingExisting) or occurs (if an #$Event) or obtains (if a #$StaticSituation).  If TEMP is itself a time-interval, the above #$temporalExtentInMt sentence holds if and only if TIME is identical to TEMP.
<p>
Note that if (#$temporalExtentInMt TEMP TIME MT) holds, TIME is a #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.) if and only if TEMP is #$temporallyContinuousDuring in MT (q.v.).
<p>
See also the corresponding function #$TemporalExtentInMtFn.")
(comment NeedMicrotheory "The collection of Microtheories each containing those propositions that describe what some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible needs to be true.  This may be distinct from what the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible wants to be true, and depends on some additional assessment of the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's need by someone else.  It may include physical, financial or formal legal `needs' of the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.")
(comment agentBioDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentBioDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact that is considered by the salient audience to constitute biographical information about AGENT in the current context.")
(comment laborForceOfIndustryOrOccupationDuring "(#$laborForceOfIndustryOrOccupationDuring REGION COL THING NR) means that NR is the average labor force of the economic sector or occupation COL in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, where the labor force of an economic sector or occupation in a region at a point in time is the sum of the number of persons employed and unemployed in the sector or occupation in the region.  COL can range from a broad economic sector, such as agriculture, manufacturing, or services to a more specific segment of the economy such as the automobile industry; in either of these cases, COL will be a specialization of the collection #$Industry-Localized.  Alternatively, COL can be an instance of the collection #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  See also #$laborForceDuring.")
(comment hasCarbonSourceType "(#$hasCarbonSourceType CELLTYPE SOURCE) means that the collection CELLTYPE uses #$ChemicalSubstanceType SOURCE to obtain its #$Carbon requirement.  For example, all autotrophic bacterium obtain their carbon by metabolizing #$CarbonDioxide.  See also #$carbonSourceOf.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Bluegrass "#$MusicalComposition-Bluegrass is the style of music pioneered by Bill Monroe.  The standard bluegrass lineup includes a fiddle player, a banjo player, a mandolin player, and an upright acoustic bass player.")
(comment OrganizationTypeByCustomers "A collection of three disjoint collections, #$OrganizationWithBusinessCustomers, #$OrganizationWithIndividualCustomers, and #$OrganizationWithoutCustomers.  The #$Organizations that are instances of the collections which are instances of #$OrganizationTypeByClients are distinguished by the types of customers they serve or by their lack of customers (customers being used here in the sense of #$customers).")
(comment IAForensicsReport "A collection of instances of #$WrittenReportOnSituation.  Each instance is characterized by being a detailed forensic dissection of a particular IA-related incident.")
(comment License-LegalAgreement "A collection of intangible pieces of information; a subset of #$Permission.   Each element of #$License-LegalAgreement is a credential issued by a granting authority and recorded in some tangible document (see #$License-IBO), which authorizes the agent to whom it is issued to perform actions of a certain kind.  Sample subsets of #$License-LegalAgreement include: #$TrainEngineerLicense, #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement, #$PestControlLicense.")
(comment actionExpressesFeeling "(#$actionExpressesFeeling ACT EMOTYPE) means that the particular action ACT actually expresses the doer's feeling of EMOTYPE. Note: additional

complications arise in using this in inference, as people can `fake' actions such as laughing, crying, etc., to mislead other people. See also

#$actionExpressesFeelingToward. If one wishes to make statements about tendencies rather than actual expressions, e.g. ``smiling tends to express

happiness'', see #$actionTypeExpressesFeelingType.")
(comment failureForAgents "The predicate #$failureForAgents is used to indicate that a particular agent fails to achieve (at least one of) its goals in a particular action.  (#$failureForAgents ENDEAVOR AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT had some purpose in performing ENDEAVOR that was not realized.  See also #$purposeInEvent.")
(comment MedicalLeave-TimeAllocation "A sub-collection of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation.  Instances of #$VMedicalLeave-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization due to that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible needing some time to attend to his or her own health or that of some family member.")
(comment SpreadingStuffOntoSurfaceWithTool "A collection of events. In each #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurface event, a #$Tool is used to spread some stuff onto a surface so that it covers [#$covers-Generic] it.  #$Painting-Activity, #$PavingARoad, and Spackling are specializations of this concept.")
(comment MakingABankWithdrawal "A collection of events; a subset of #$MoneyTransfer.  In an instance of #$MakingABankWithdrawal, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or representative thereof) withdraws currency or other financial tender from a bank account (usually the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's personal bank account, or the bank account of the company for which the agent works).  An agent may make a withdrawal in person at the bank, but it might also be made by mail, over the telephone, electronically via modem, at an ATM machine, etc.")
(comment numberOfPointsOnLoan "(#$numberOfPointsOnLoan LOAN N) identifies N as the number of \"points\" on the instance of #$LoanAgreement LOAN.  One point translates to 1 percent of the loan amount (c.f., #$initialLoanAmount).  To represent the points on a loan as a monetary amount, user #$pointsValueOnLoan.")
(comment Satisfaction "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Satisfaction is some agent's feeling that at least some of her desires or needs have been met.  Instances of #$Satisfaction vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or on the subject experiencing the feeling.  Specializations of #$Satisfaction include #$Approval and #$Contentment.")
(comment TVFamilyShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs intended to be viewed           and to provide entertainment for all ages.")
(comment Estimate "The collection of microtheories containing propositions that represent beliefs by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible which are the result of inexact judgmental reasoning.  For example, IBM's estimate on January 1, 1992, of fourth quarter earnings for 1991. This concept encompasses the common meaning of `estimate' and also `guess'.  This contrasts with beliefs which are derived primarily from rigorous or reliable reasoning, direct observation, or consultation of authoritative sources.  This also contrasts with intentional lies and works of fiction, which are not #$Estimates.")
(comment beneficiary "(#$beneficiary ACT AGT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT benefits from the performance of the action ACT.  Some desire or interest of AGT is served, enabled, helped, or satisfied by the performance of ACT.")
(comment epidemicCommonVehicleType "(#$epidemicCommonVehicleType EPI VEHICLE-TYPE) means that the common vehicle of the #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI is such that every member of that common vehicle is an instance of the type of #$InanimateObject VEHICLE-TYPE. The common vehicle is a group of things contaminated with the #$Microorganism that causes the #$Infections that constitute EPI. In other words, every member of EPI is an #$Infection caused by exposure to a contaminated member of the common vehicle, and every member of the common vehicle is an instance of the type of #$InanimateObject VEHICLE-TYPE. See #$epidemicCommonVehicle.")
(comment agentAlternativeNameDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentAlternativeNameDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses the fact that AGENT goes by a certain alternative name or alias.")
(comment Anger "Intense feeling of displeasure and usually of antagonism.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Anger include #$Belligerence, etc.")
(comment FloaterHoliday-TimeAllocation "A sub-collection of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation.  Instances of #$FloaterHoliday-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization due to that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible taking advantage of an #$Organization's policy of allowing its workers to take time of for rest and recuperation.  This collection is distinct from #$Vacation-TimeAllocation because of the the rules governing its accrual by workers.")
(comment PoliticalCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture many of whose participants share a 
  particular set of political beliefs and attitudes, and
  engage in similar sorts of political activities.  For 
  example, there are instances of #$PoliticalCulture
  associated with most political philosophies (such as
  #$Marxism) and with most instances of #$PoliticalParty
  (such as the #$RepublicanParty-US).")
(comment aFew-RelationFrom "(#$aFew-RelationFrom RELN THING COL) says that a few of the instances INST of COL are such that (RELN THING INST) holds.")
(comment awareOfInfo "(#$awareOfInfo AGENT INFO) means that AGENT is aware of, conceives of, or somehow holds the #$AspatialInformationStore INFO in his/her/its mind/collective-consciousness.  AGENT may or may not believe INFO.")
(comment Mosque-LocalCongregation "A #$Mosque-LocalCongregation is a local Muslim religious organization that 
worships together at a common #$Mosque-Building. They may be led by an official cleric, 
such as a #$Mullah, and #$SunniIslam congregations are often led by an #$Imam-Sunni.")
(comment RadioStation-AM "The collection of #$RadioStation-Organizations that broadcast using the system of amplitude modulation of radio waves.")
(comment MIPS "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfCPUCapacity. It is used to represent the standard unit of CPU capacity -- millions of (machine-code) instructions per second. (#$MIPS 34.0) would represent a #$CPUSpeed of around 34 million instructions per second. It has been argued that this benchmark is \"completely pointless\", since no two chips use exactly the same set of instructions, and the same set of instructions can do vastly more work depending on the chip size and the way the processing task has been structured. (For example, on a chip with #$CISCArchitecture, a single instruction may do many things when executed, whereas on a #$RISCArchitecture chip it may do very little but be dealt with more efficiently). Many other benchmarks exist, including #$MFLOPS, VUPS (\"VAX Units of Performance\"), SPEC (for which, see #$SPECint and #$SPECfp), Linpack, etc.")
(comment wantsToRelnNo "(#$wantsToRelnNo AGT COL PRED NUM) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT #$desires to have the relation PRED to NUM number of instances of the Collection COL.  PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate.")
(comment GiftGiving "A specialization of #$GivingSomething.  In each instance of #$GiftGiving, one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible intentionally gives all use rights over an object (see #$SituationTypeByUserRights) to another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible without taking payment in return.")
(comment ApplyingStuffFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction which takes as its argument a type of thing and returns the specialization of #$ApplyingStuffToSurface in which things of that type are spread or otherwise put onto the surface of some object. (#$ApplyingStuffFn STUFF-TYPE) is the collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible so applies stuff of type STUFF-TYPE. For instance, (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$SunTanLotion) is the collection of all events in which someone applies sun tan lotion (usually to someone's body).")
(comment SituationTypeInWhichFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction, #$SituationTypeInWhichFn takes an instance of #$CycLSentence-Assertible and returns the sub-collection of #$Situation whose  instances are all those situations of which the proposition represented by the #$CycLSentence-Assertible is 'constitutively true.'  A sufficient condition for a situation to be a member of the collection denoted by #$SituationTypeInWhichFn is for the situation itself or the instances of #$SomethingExisting which are actors in that situation to have a set of properties that entail the relevant proposition.  So, the fact that #$WorldWarII involved the use of the #$FatMan bomb makes it an instance of the collection (#$SituationTypeInWhichFn (#$relationExistsExists #$deviceUsed #$War #$AtomicBomb)).")
(comment RightCoronaryArtery-PosteriorDescendingBranch "A specialization of #$CoronaryArtery.  The posterior descending branch is one of two main branches of the #$RightCoronaryArtery-Generic. (The other main branch is the #$RightCoronaryArtery-PosterolateralBranch.)")
(comment ratingTypeCriterion "An assertion of the form (#$ratingTypeCriterion TYPE CRIT) states that the instance of #$EvaluativeQuantity TYPE is derived from the #$EvaluativeCriterion CRIT.  This predicate allows for comparisons of instances of #$EvaluativeQuantity, as well as the individuals who are instances of those collections.")
(comment IncurringDamage "A specialization of #$Event-Localized. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some sort of damage is incurred to an instance of #$SomethingExisting. Examples include denting a car, the breaking of someone's leg, the defacing of a website and slander which negatively impacts someone's reputation. For cases where the thing damaged is a material thing (i.e. an instance of #$PartiallyTangible), or an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, see the more specialized constants #$IncurringPhysicalDamage and #$HarmingAnAgent respectively. For cases where the damage incurred is so extensive that the thing is destroyed, see the more specialized #$DestructionEvent.")
(comment Debunking "A specialization of #$Disapproving-CommunicationAct.  Each instance of #$Debunking is an event in which some agent's pretentious or exaggerated claims are refuted and, at the same time, (at least gently) ridiculed.  Note that, e.g., a #$Scientist refuting an accepted #$ScientificTheory is not necessarily an instance of #$Debunking, since the theory in question need not be pretentious or exaggerated, nor need the refuter intend to ridicule the theory or its proponents.")
(comment AllowsSharedFloppyAccess "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByPassiveCapability. A computer has this capability if it is possible for its #$FloppyDiskDrive to be accessed by someone other than the currently logged on user. For cases where unauthorized users can gain access, see the more specialized #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedFloppyDriveAccess.")
(comment ContractualDispute "The collection of all instances of #$DisputeOverAgreementCW in which the #$disputedAgreement is an instance of #$Contract.")
(comment UsingInstForFn "This function denotes the collection of instances of #$PurposefulAction in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible deliberately uses some particular #$SomethingExisting in some role ROLE. For example, 
(#$UsingAForFn Hammer001 #$ConstructingABuilding #$deviceUsed) denotes the subcollection of #$PurposefulAction in which Hammer001 is used in an instance of #$ConstructingABuilding as a #$deviceUsed. Also see #$UsingAForFn.")
(comment TrafficBarrel "A specialization of #$TrafficObstructionDevice and #$Barrel-Container (qq.v).  Each instance of #$TrafficBarrel is bright white and/or orange plastic barrel that is  typically weighted with water or sand and that is intended to be used to block or redirect automobile traffic.")
(comment Confidence "The positive emotion felt when one is free

from doubt about an event or object from which the agent feeling

#$Confidence expects positive contingencies.  For example, one might

say 'I feel confident that tomorrow it will not be rainy'. Do not

confuse this with a personality disposition, e.g. 'Joe is a confident

person.'  (See #$PersonalityAttribute.)  This is a collection; for an

explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.

More specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes include #$Grief,

#$SelfConfidence, etc.")
(comment ComputerHardwareItem "A specialization of #$ElectronicDevice and #$ComputerMarketCategory. Each instance of this collection is either an entire #$Computer, or a device used with or in computers to accomplish some computing-related task (for instance, computer terminals, printers, keyboards, etc.).")
(comment MedicalLeave-TimeAllocation-8 "A sub-collection of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation.  Instances of #$VMedicalLeave-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization due to that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible needing some time to attend to his or her own health or that of some family member.")
(comment giver "This predicate relates a giver to the event in which s/he/it gives. (#$giver GIVING AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is the giver in the #$GivingSomething event GIVING. For the recipient, see #$givee.")
(comment outputInputSituationTypesInCycleType-Strong "(#$outputInputSituationTypesInCycleType-Strong CYCLE-TYPE OUTPUTTING-TYPE INPUTTING-TYPE means that, where CYCLE-INST is an instance of CYCLE-TYPE then, where OUTPUTTING-INST is an instance of OUTPUT-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, any #$outputs of OUTPUTTING-INST will be an #$inputs of some instance of INPUTTING-TYPE that is also a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, and where INPUTTING-INST is an instance of INPUTTING-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, any #$inputs of INPUTTING-INST will be an #$outputs of some instance of OUTPUTTING-TYPE that is also a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST.")
(comment Fear "Unpleasant emotion manifested by painful agitation in the presence or awareness of danger.   Fear implies anxiety and loss of courage.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.   A more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityType than #$Fear is #$Dread.")
(comment Oxide "An instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and a specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Oxide is a portion of stuff in which each molecule consists of a combination of oxygen atoms with one or more atoms of another element.  Specializations of #$Oxide include #$IronOxide (i.e. rust), #$CarbonDioxide, and (#$PureFn #$Water) (i.e. the collection of portions of chemically pure water).")
(comment TVShowOnHealth "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily provide information or advice            on medical and health related matters (see #$Medicine-FieldOfStudy), including           information about #$Exercising, diet, #$Stress-Feeling, alternative treatments           for illnesses, etc.")
(comment TartingUp-SomeoneDressingUp "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DressingUp. In each #$TartingUp-SomeoneDressingUp, someone dresses up in a cheap and provocative way.")
(comment DomainNameRegistration "The collection of all events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible registers itself as the owner of a domain name. The owner then must pay an annual fee to maintain ownership, and has exclusive rights to use the domain name for internet addresses.")
(comment agentLocationDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentLocationDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact about the places where AGENT has been.")
(comment TasteFn "#$TasteFn takes as its argument a subcollection of #$PartiallyTangible and returns the taste (an instance of #$ObjectTypeByTaste and a subcollection of #$PartiallyTangible) characteristic of instances of that subcollection.  For example, (#$TasteFn #$Pizza) returns the collection of instances of #$PartiallyTangible that possess the taste commonly had by pizza.")
(comment requestedAgent "An assertion of the form (#$requestedAgent REQUEST AGENT) relates an instance of #$ResourceRequest to an instance of #$IntelligentAgent.  This states that the individual #$ResourceRequest represents the content of an attempt to constrain or reserve the time of AGENT.  This should be contrasted with #$allottedAgents, which would entail an actual commitment or obligation on AGENT.")
(comment FormalizingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Declaring-Evaluating. In each #$FormalizingSomething, someone makes something formal or official.")
(comment flawedWRTRoleInSitType "This predicate relates a thing to a role and situation type in which it might be reasonably expected to play the role but is unable to do so adequately because of a flaw.  Note that this only applies to expected capabilities.  For instance, if Cow001 is a #$Cow-FemaleHerdAnimal and is unable to hit a baseball, we would not assert (#$flawedWRTRoleInSitType Cow001 #$BaseballContact #$performedBy).")
(comment ArtMuseum-Structure "A specialization of #$MuseumStructure.  Each instance of #$ArtMuseum-Structure is a construct that is used to store and display art holdings (see #$ArtObject, #$Museum-Organization, and #$MuseumHoldings).")
(comment MakingAnEstimate "A #$Thinking whose instances have a #$resultMt that is an instance of Estimate.  Usually is a subEventOf services which are not instances of #$StandardServiceType. ")
(comment Schizosaccharomyces-Genus "A collection of ascomycetous fungi, see #$Ascomycota-Division. An instance of
#$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment translationOfPCW "(#$translationOfPCW PCW NEWPCW) means that NEWPCW is a translation of PCW. Note that this predicate relates a #$TextualPCW to a #$TextuallySpecificWork.  A translation of the #$Bible, for example, is usually not the direct translation of a single #$TextualPCW, but is created by referencing copies of multiple textually specific versions of the #$Bible, often in multiple languages.  If PCW is also a #$TextuallySpecificWork, use the more specific predicate, #$translationOfTextualPCW.  To say that a certain #$TextString is a translation of a #$TextualPCW, use #$translationOfCWToAIS. To say that one #$TextString (or any #$AbstractInformationStructure) is a translation of another, use #$translationOfAISFromTo.")
(comment Fibrillating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Twitching. In each #$Fibrillating, something makes fine, irregular, rapid twitching movements.")
(comment HexalateralObject "A #$HexalateralObject is an object with a well-defined front, back, left, right, top, and bottom.  These sides are considered to be intrinsic to the object and do not vary as the object changes position.  Any object which is an instance of two different specs of                #$BilateralObject is a #$HexalateralObject as a matter of definition -- e.g. if an object's front and back can be distinguished and its left side can be distinguished from its right, then it also has a well-defined bottom and top.  See also comments for #$BilateralObject and for #$FrontAndBackSidedObject, #$LeftAndRightSidedObject, and                #$TopAndBottomSidedObject.")
(comment JohnHemminge-ActorActress "An instance of #$Actor. English actor who edited the first folio of Shakespeare's plays (1556-1630).")
(comment importRate "(#$importRate COUNTRY PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that COUNTRY imports PRODUCT-TYPE at the rate of RATE. Note that RATE may be expressed as a #$MonetaryRate, but also as rate of volume, mass or number depending on the type of product. For example, for oil which is a fluid we can say both (#$importRate #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$PetroleumProduct (#$MillionDollarsPerYear NR)) and (#$importRate #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$PetroleumProduct (#$MillionBarrelsPerYear NR)). Note that services, i.e. specializations of #$ServiceEvents are included as product types.")
(comment EbolaVirus "A specialization of #$Virus. #$EbolaVirus is a member of a family of RNA viruses known as filoviruses. When magnified several thousand times by an electron microscope, these viruses have the appearance of long filaments or threads. Ebola virus was discovered in 1976 and was named for a river in #$DemocraticRepublicOfTheCongo (then Zaire), where it was first detected. Causes #$EbolaHemorrhagicFeverInfections. The natural animal host, if there is one, is currently unknown.")
(comment CompilerFn "#$CompilerFn takes as argument any instance of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage and returns the collection of all instances of #$Compiler that translate programs from that language. For example, (#$CompilerFn #$C-ProgrammingLanguage) returns the collection of all C compiler programs.")
(comment Action "The collection of #$Events (q.v.) that are carried out by some \"doer\" (see #$doneBy).  Instances of #$Action include any event in which one or more actors effect some change in the (tangible or intangible) state of the world, typically by an expenditure of effort or energy.  Note that it is not required that any tangible object be moved, changed, produced, or destroyed for an action to occur; the effects of an action might be intangible (such as a change in a bank balance or the intimidation of a subordinate).  Note also that the doer of an action, though typically an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (q.v.), need not be (e.g. a falling rock that dents a car's roof).  Depending upon the context, doers of actions might be animate or inanimate, conscious or nonconscious.  For actions that are intentional, see #$PurposefulAction and #$performedBy.")
(comment DirectedTranslation "A specialization of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Each instance of #$DirectedTranslation is a movement event that is #$performedBy an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible that intends for the #$objectMoving to reach a particular #$target.  Examples:  William Tell shooting the apple off his son's head,  John Wilkes Booth shooting Abraham Lincoln, the last time you tossed a frisbee to someone, a pilot landing an airplane, and a skiier skiing one run of the downhill course.")
(comment watchOnDuty "A #$SystemRolePredicate for relating a person playing the role of 'watch' on a vessel to the #$vesselsWholeCrew in which they are playing this role.")
(comment Ethyldichloroarsine "#$Ethyldichloroarsine, also known as ED, is a #$BlisterAgentStuff with chemical formula C2H5AsCl2.")
(comment SupportCommunicationsForEvent "A collection of #$AttributeValues denoting various gradations of communications            support a unit or instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible might provide for an instance of #$Event.            The kind of support intended here includes instances of #$SupplyingMeansOfCommunication.")
(comment usesProgram "The predicate #$usesProgram relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible or a #$ProgramAction to a program (#$ComputerProgram-CW) that is used by that agent or  in that action. (#$usesProgram AGNT-OR-ACT PROG) means the AGNT-OR-ACT uses PROG. Examples include the relationship between a person and their word-processing program, or between a user account and the Unix shell which it is given on startup.")
(comment hasPurposeInWork "(#$hasPurposeInWork WORK DOCSTRUC PURPOSE) means that the #$GraphicalStructure DOCSTRUC is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK (see #$containsStructure-CW) and has the #$DocumentStructurePurposeAttribute PURPOSE within WORK.")
(comment FinancialAssetHoldings "A collection of partially tangibles. An instance of #$FinancialAssetHoldings is a group of financial assets (e.g., stocks, bonds, ... ) owned by individual or corporate #$Agent-PartiallyTangible(s). As a default, we assume that the monetary value of each group equals the sum of the monetary values of the individual assets in that group.")
(comment AssumedBelief "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType which indicates that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) was purposely added to the Cyc knowledge base purely as an assumption, which may or may not be sound.")
(comment TransferOfControl "A collection of events and a specialization of   #$GainingControl and #$LosingControlOfAControlledActor. Each instance of this collection is an event in which an object which is under the control of some agent has that control transferred to another agent different from the first.  'Control' here means the ability on the part of an agent to determine 'what happens to' another object or agent.  In the case where the thing controlled exhibits 'activities' or 'behavior', this extends to a nontrivial ability to direct or circumscribe some important aspect of the behavior that the object or agent exhibits.  An agent with independent goals and purposes that is under 'control' is not able to freely pursue those goals and purposes: i.e., the 'controller' is able to exert some kind of significant and immediate check upon the 'controlled' agent's capacity to pursue its goals at whim.  Every #$TransferOfControl presupposes exactly one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who #$takesControl of the thing being transferred, exactly one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who #$losesControl of the thing being transferred, and one thing that is the #$objectOfControlTransfer, i.e., the object of the transfer of control.  In some cases, e.g., #$CapturingAnAnimal or #$TakingAPersonPrisoner, the agent who #$losesControl coincides with the thing that is the #$objectOfControlTransfer.  You cannot have a #$TransferOfControl without someone or something that #$losesControl, however.  E.g., finding and taking an (unclaimed) penny in the street is merely a #$GainingControl.  A given #$TransferOfControl is not necessarily #$doneBy the agent who #$takesControl or by the agent who #$losesControl:  it could conceivably be instigated by a third party independent of either of these.")
(comment candidateSetOfValuesForBinPredWRTArg "(#$candidateSetOfValuesForBinPredWRTArg BIN-PRED THING SET NUM) means that when THING is in arg NUM in BIN-PRED SET is a set of candidate values for the remaining arg position such that there is a good chance that at least some of the members are such that (BINPRED THING-IN-ARG-NUM MEMBER-OF-SET-IN-OTHER-ARG) is a true sentence.  For example (#$candidateSetOfValuesForBinPredWRTArg #$typicalLocationTypeOfType #$ElectricalToaster (#$TheSet #$Kitchen #$LivingRoom #$Bedroom #$DiningRoom) 1) holds because the set involved is a decent candidate set of possible location types that toasters might be found.")
(comment HighSchoolLevelSportsEvent "The collection of all organized sports events sanctioned by #$HighSchools and performed by #$HighSchoolStudents.")
(comment Slipping "Instances of #$Slipping are instances of #$Sliding-Generic in which some agent did not intend the #$objectMovings to slide.  If an #$objectMoving is an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, then it is a #$nonDeliberateActors in that sliding.  If the #$objectMoving is not an agent, then there exists some agent which intends for it not to slide at the moment of slippage.")
(comment SituationalComedy "A subset of #$TVShow-IBTs, those we normally refer to as situational comedies, e.g.            Mash, Seinfeld or Cheers.")
(comment PostOfficeBuilding "The collection of all buildings, each of which serves as the #$physicalQuarters for some local #$PostOfficeOrganization.")
(comment Popcorn-Popped "The collection of all popcorn. A type of #$CerealFood. The collection #$Popcorn-Popped is a #$SnackFoodType and an #$ExistingStuffType. Each instance of #$Popcorn-Popped is a portion of popped popping corn kernels.")
(comment Quicksand "A specialization
of #$SandySoilRegion.  Each instance of #$Quicksand is sand that
has been saturated with water, which causes heavy objects to sink when 
crossing it's surface.")
(comment Compressibility "A specialization of #$DispositionalQuantity.   Each instance of #$Compressibility is a specific capacity of a physical object to be compressed.  Compressibility may be measured with a #$GenericValueFunction. Compressibilities of objects are indicated with the predicate #$compressibilityOfObject (q.v.).")
(comment Anticipation-Feeling "Emotion accompanying an expectation of something pleasant in the foreseeable future.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness. ")
(comment Loneliness "The disagreeable feeling of being without company.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes are #$Loneliness, #$Solitude, etc.")
(comment FictionalCharacter "This is the collection of instances of #$FictionalThing which are also instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. Thus #$FictionalCharacter excludes such instances of #$FictionalThing as Golden Mountains, which are instances of #$FictionalThing, but are not instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.")
(comment SupportedByMaterialImplication "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType.  This collection is the collection of cyc arguments which are supported by material implication.  This collection can be used to indicate that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) is supported by one or more applications of an if-then rule.")
(comment covers-Paintlike "(#$covers-Paintlike COATING OBJECT) means that COATING adheres to and covers OBJECT like a coat of paint.  Since COATING adheres to OBJECT, COATING directly touches (see the predicate #$touches-Directly) OBJECT.   COATING may be either dry (e.g., dried paint) or liquid (e.g., lubricant spread on a surface, like cooking oil on a baking pan).  (#$covers-Paintlike COATING OBJECT) implies that COATING isn't more cohesive with itself than it is with OBJECT, so (if dry) it would tend to peel or flake off in small pieces, rather than as a whole.")
(comment holdsCaptive "(#$holdsCaptive CAPTOR CAPTIVE) means that #$IntelligentAgent CAPTOR holds #$Agent-PartiallyTangible CAPTIVE in custody.")
(comment NonNumericQuantitySlot "A specialization of #$QuantitySlot (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NonNumericQuantitySlot is a binary predicate that is used to attribute a property to a thing, by relating it to a #$NonNumericScalarQuantity (q.v.) of some sort, typically a #$GenericQuantity.
<p>
Instances of #$NonNumericQuantitySlot include #$levelOfEfficiency and #$qualityOfProduct.
<p>
Cf. #$MeasurableQuantitySlot.")
(comment restenosisOfCoronaryArtery "(#$restenosisOfCoronaryArtery CAS CORONARY-ARTERY-TYPE) means that there is an instance of #$CoronaryArteryStenosis-Finding affecting the patient's CORONARY-ARTERY-TYPE and that there was some previous percutaneous procedure whose site was \"Coronary Artery\".  As necessary more rules concluding to this relation will be added.")
(comment hasIssuedTo "#$hasIssuedTo is a binary predicate that relates an instance of #$Credential to an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  (#$hasIssuedTo AGENT CRED) means that CRED is issued to AGENT.")
(comment ReligiousTVShow "Instances of #$ReligiousTVShow are #$TVShow-IBTs with content usually associated           with religion such as preaching or edification.  They may also present information about           current events or politics from what are commonly considered religious points-of-view.           Examples: 'The 700 Club' or 'Living Word Ministries'.")
(comment PlayingGameTypeFn "(#$PlayingGameTypeFn GAME_TYPE) returns the collection of instances of #$PlayingAGame of some instance of GAME_Type performed by players or competitors.  For example, (#$PlayingGameTypeFn #$CardGame) returns the collection of actions performed by one or more players while playing at some #$CardGame.  Note that the game does not ever have to be completed for these actions to be part of the playing of the game type.  The predicate also applies to non-game sports (see #$Sport).")
(comment hasStatusWRTAssignmentOnDateWithEstimatedTimeRemaining "An assertion of the form (#$hasStatusWRTAssignmentOnDateWithEstimatedTimeRemaining AGENT STATUS-PRED ASSIGN INTERVAL QUANTITY) states that the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT bears the relation STATUS-PRED, an instance of #$WorkStatusBinaryPredicate, to the #$Assignment-Specification during the #$TimeInterval INTERVAL and that AGENT believes there is QUANTITY of work remaining for it to complete it's work on the realization of ASSIGN.  This predicate is designed to work with the FET Template #$ProjectManagement-TemplateTopic and to handle the problem of not being able to substitute values from an FET field into multiple positions within the underlying formula.")
(comment HarmingEnemiesGoal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory.  A goal has this attribute if the 
goal involves taking actions that will cause harm of some kind upon
an enemy or a rival.")
(comment mournsOver "(mournsOver AGENT DEATH) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT mourns over DEATH, and instance of #$DyingOfBLO.")
(comment SideSpin "Moving on a trajectory through the air while spinning along a significantly nonhorizontal axis of spin. This produces sideways lift and changes the direction of bounce toward the direction in which the object is spinning.  This usually applies to a #$Sphere object.")
(comment ambientTemperature "A #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate. The predicate #$ambientTemperature is used to indicate the average temperature in the free space around a particular object.  (#$ambientTemperature OBJ TEMP) means that the space around the tangible object OBJ is at the #$Temperature TEMP.  Used with #$holdsIn (q.v.), #$ambientTemperature expresses the surrounding temperature for a given object at some point in time.  For the temperature of the object itself, use #$temperatureOfObject (q.v.).")
(comment judicialAgents "(#$judicialAgents EV JUDGE) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible JUDGE is acting as a judge in the event EV.")
(comment GuardedByAgent "The attribute describing the security level of those objects guarded by some sort of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, such as a guard at a bank, or the US Army at Fort Knox.")
(comment ListeningDeliberately "The collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible deliberately facilitates and does #$Hearing.")
(comment MediumDuty-PathArtifact "This is the collection of instances of #$PathForWheeledVehicles

that can accomodate medium-heavy loads in all weather; these are likely to

be paved avenues on light foundations. Paths with this attribute will

be instances of #$PavedPath describing the quality of their

surface or preferably one of its specialization that reflects the quality

of their foundation.")
(comment agentGroupMembershipDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentGroupMembershipDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses the fact that AGENT is a member of a particular group (during some time interval).")
(comment MerchandiseRelatedToFn "#$MerchandiseRelatedToFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of products related in some relatively direct way to that thing.  Relevant relations include being designed, made, marketed or sold by that thing, and being about or inspired by that thing.  For example, (#$MerchandiseRelatedToFn #$NewEnglandPatriots) returns the collection of all products by, about, or in some way supporting the Patriots football team, and (#$MerchandiseRelatedToFn #$RepublicanPartyIdeology) returns the collection of all products about, inspired by, or in some way supporting Republican beliefs.")
(comment WorldModelingProgramObject "A specialization of #$ProgramObject.
Each instance of #$WorldModelingProgramObject is the abstract structure of a representation
of an instance of #$Thing.
Computer programs are useful to humans because they are efficient processors and manipulators
of information about things outside of the program that are interesting to humans . 
When this information, about some #$Thing, happens
to be represented in a single instance of #$ComputerDatatypeType, then that instance is almost 
always also a specialization of #$WorldModelingProgramObject. 
Computers were initially designed to handle representations of numbers only. 
But with the advent
of modern programming languages, complex user-defined datastructures allow the representation
of almost arbitrary things, including instances of #$Set-Mathematical, #$Relation, 
or even #$Person. The collection #$WorldModelingProgramObject is useful in distinguishing those
data a program's user will care about from those that are merely implementation details.
See also the unary denotational function #$ProgramObjectValueFn and the binary predicate
#$programObjectRepresentsValue.")
(comment RegisteringAComplaint "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Complaining.  Each instance of #$RegisteringAComplaint is an event in which some agent <i>A</i> presents a complaint to some other agent <i>B</i>, where the following conditions are satisfied:
<p>
(1) <i>A</i> believes that some agent (perhaps, but not necessarily, <i>B</i>) is responsible for the state of affairs being complained about;
<p>
(2) <i>A</i> believes that <i>B</i> is in a position to remediate the state of affairs being complained about.
<p>
Some positive examples: complaining to a hotel front desk that the towels in one's room are dirty; complaining to one's supervisor at work that one hasn't been provided with sufficient resources to complete an assigned task; complaining to the #$BetterBusinessBureau that one has been swindled in a business scam.  Negative examples: complaining to one's doctor about one's constant back pain (condition 1 is not satisfied); complaining to one's friend that one is being treated poorly at work (condition 2 is not satisfied).")
(comment MinisterOfEnergy "A collection of #$PublicOfficials that are head of the department(s) responsible for the energy production/distribution in a country. By (#$positionOfPersonInOrganization PERSON (#$GovernmentFn COUNTRY) #$MinisterOfEnergy) we say that PERSON has this position in COUNTRY. There may be more than one #$MinisterOfEnergy for a country at any one time, if the government structure is divides the responsibility among several officials, e.g. the minister of oil, the minister of nuclear energy, etc.. Also, a minister may have more responsibilities including 'energy', e.g. 'minister of infrastructure'. 

Finally, note that the title for the official in this capacity need not be 'minister', e.g. secretary, chancelor, etc.. ")
(comment PrivilegeEscalationScriptFn "(#$PrivilegeEscalationScriptFn ACCOUINT ACCOUNT_TYPE) denotes a computer script which, when executed at a sufficient level of privilege, confers the privileges associated with ACCOUNT_TYPE onto ACCOUNT.  Thus, (#$PrivilegeEscalationScriptFn (#$UserAccountFn \"blake\" #$Pyrex-Cyc-Com) #$AdministratorAccount) denotes a (let's say) batch file which, when executed, confers all the privileges of an NT administrator account to someone logged in as #$Blake on #$Pyrex-Cyc-Com.")
(comment toState "This predicate is used in connection with #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent, to identify the state (#$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState) a thing has immediately after the change.  (#$toState EVENT STATE-COLL) means that following the intrinsic-state-changing action, EVENT, the object undergoing the change is an instance of STATE-COLL (which is an instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState) and was previously an instance of some other instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState.  For example, after any X which is a #$TurningOnAnElectricalSwitch, the switch involved has (#$toState X #$Device-On).")
(comment BillionDollarsPerYear "A function which returns an element of #$MonetaryRate.  (#$BillionDollarsPerYear 1) equals (#$DollarsPerYear 1000000000).  Note, the dollars here are United States dollars. (#$Dollar-UnitedStates).")
(comment OneLaneRoadway "The collection of #$Roadways that have only a single lane or track. This criterion

belongs to the US Army's nomenclature for roads, or more preciseley, for

roads in foreign areas on large and medium scale maps. See

#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes and its other instances.")
(comment generalizedSpatialProduct "A binary predicate that relates a set  of tangible objects, space regions, or spatially-localized events to their mereological product or intersection.  <code>(#$generalizedSpatialProduct PRODUCT SET)</code> means that <code>PRODUCT</code> is the unique #$SpatialThing (of the same basic type as each element of <code>SET</code>), if there is one, such that a spatial thing intersects (see #$spatiallyIntersects) <code>PRODUCT</code> if and only if it intersects with each element of <code>SET</code>.  
<p>
Note that \"<i>of the same basic type</i>\" in the above means that <code>PRODUCT</code> and the elements of <code>SET</code> are either all #$PartiallyTangibles, all #$SpaceRegions, or all #$Event-Localizeds.  This restriction is needed in order to ensure the uniqueness of <code>PRODUCT</code>, since a tangible object, a space region, and an event can have the same spatial extent (see #$cospatial), despite their being distinct things.
<p>
See the corresponding function #$GeneralizedSpatialProductFn.  Also see #$generalizedSpatialSum and #$spatialProduct.")
(comment MarketingStatement "The collection of all marketing statements. A type of #$TextualDocument-CW.")
(comment typesFollowInSuccession "(#$typesFollowInSuccession SUBTYPE2 SUBTYPE1 MAINTYPE) means that in events of type MAINTYPE, events of type SUBTYPE1 are followed by events of type SUBTYPE2, i.e. there are instances SUBINS1 and SUBINS2, that are subevents of an instance of MAINTYPE such that (#$followsInProgression SUBINS2 SUBINS1 MAININS).  See also, #$nextSubSituationTypeToStart and #$nextSceneToStartInScript-Ternary for versions of this that apply strictly to scripts and scene types that get reified for these scripts.")
(comment HyperlinkOfStructureFn "<code>(#$HyperlinkOfStructureFn STRUCTURE)</code> denotes the instance of #$Hyperlink that spans <code>STRUCTURE</code>, an instance of #$AbstractStructure (typically an instance of #$AbstractInformationStructure or #$ContextualizedInformationStructure).<p>For example,
<pre> (#$HyperlinkOfStructureFn (#$TextualOccurrenceFn 1 \"Cabinda\" (#$AISForFn #$TheSecondSentenceOfTheAngolaWikipediaArticle)))</pre> denotes the link that would be followed if one were to click on \"Cabinda\" in the second sentence of the Wikipedia article on Angola.")
(comment scheduledAttendeeDate "(#$scheduledAttendeeDate EVENT PERSON DATE) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible PERSON is scheduled to be a participant in (#$deliberateActors) the referredTo event starting at the referenced date.  If the starting time for EVENT is unknown, then it would default to DATE, except for certain event types such as #$War.  Similarly, if (#$scheduledAttendee EVENT PERSON) and the starting time of EVENT is known, then that time is the default #$scheduledAttendeeDate.")
(comment physicalStructuralFeatures "(#$physicalStructuralFeatures OBJ ATT) means that the physical structure of the tangible object OBJ is (at least partially) determined or described by its attribute ATT.  See also #$PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalStructuralFeature.")
(comment occasionallyInContactWith "(#$occasionallyInContactWith X Y) means that X and Y have met at least a few times, but possibly often, and continue to meet each other at more or less random intervals in the indefinite present due to whatever circumstances.  Also expressible as (#$acquaintances X Y #$occasionallyInContactWith) and (#$acquaintances Y X #$occasionallyInContactWith).")
(comment OpeningADrawer "The collection of events in which a #$Drawer  is pulled open.  The #$ContainerArtifact the drawer is a part of is also an #$objectActedOn in the event.  Such objects tend to have one or more drawers.")
(comment SpendingMoney "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType. Each instance of #$SpendingMoney is an instance of #$MoneyTransfer whose #$fromPossessor has no intention of getting any of the money (#$moneyTransferred) back. Thus #$SpendingMoney is disjoint with #$Investing, #$Gambling, and #$BorrowingSomething.  See the #$SharedNoteOnTheDifferenceBetweenPayingAndSpendingMoney.")
(comment toneOfInformationThing "The predicate #$toneOfInformationThing is used to characterize the evaluation made or implied by a particular assertion about something.  (#$toneOfInformationThing PROP THING TONE) means that the proposition expressed in the #$ELSentence-Assertible PROP explicitly or implicitly makes an evaluation of THING that has the #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone TONE.  Some possible values of TONE are: #$PositiveTone, #$NegativeTone, #$NeutralTone.  For example, a Cyc formula stating that #$Socrates feels #$Courageousness-Feeling in the face of his execution can be said to be positive in tone about #$Socrates. (Such a formula would utilize #$feelsTowardsEvent.)")
(comment WalkingAPet "The collection of all events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible takes a #$Dog or other #$DomesticPet outside so that the animal can get exercise and/or defecate or urinate.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureMailStorage "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it
with a #$InsecureMailStorageFault-System.")
(comment WritingAComputerProgram "A specialization of #$CWCreation. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible writes some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. This will often (but not always) involve instances of #$ProgrammingAComputer -- physically typing a program into a computer -- a specialization of #$IBTGeneration-Original. See also #$Hacking.")
(comment Advertisement-IBT "A collection of #$InformationBearingThings. #$Advertisement-IBTs are IBTs intended for a large audience, often #$ThePublic. The originator of the corresponding #$Advertisement-PCW pays to have these instantiations made accessible to the intended audience, and intends that people who access one will be affected by it in a way that is favorable to the originator. #$Advertisement-IBTs take many physical forms, including billboards, magazine and newspapers ads, email, direct mail, and radio and television commercials, among others.")
(comment appendix-DocumentPartOf "(#$appendix-DocumentPartOf WORK APPENDIX) means that the #$GraphicalStructure APPENDIX is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and is an appendix in that work.  Appendices usually contain information that supplements the propositional content of the body of the #$StructurallySpecificWork and which is not essential (but which is, perhaps, helpful) to an understanding of the #$Propositions expressed in the #$StructurallySpecificWork as a whole.")
(comment DanceMeditation-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the 
dance meditation style.    ")
(comment wantsToRelnA "(#$wantsToRelnA AGT COL RELN) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible ?AGT wants to be in the relation RELN (expressed by a #$BinaryPredicate) to some element of the collection COL.  The desired object may be indefinite (except for being a member of COL).  E.g., (#$wantsToRelnA #$Muffet #$TennisBall #$possesses).")
(comment GainingUserRights "A specialization of #$ChangeInUserRights.  In each instance of #$GainingUserRights, some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible acquires a right to use an item.  The item in question is identified as the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer, and the agent is the #$toPossessor (that is, the one to whom the possession comes).  The #$Agent-PartiallyTangible may or may not be a #$deliberateActors in the event; for example, buying a car is done on purpose, but receiving a car as a gift isn't. Either of these events, however, would be an instance of the collection #$GainingUserRights.")
(comment Money-DevisedPractice "A specialization of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork.  Each instance of this collection is a currency (more specifically, a #$UnitOfMoney) considered qua devised social institution -- i.e. the many and varied practices (such as locking quantities of gold in a secure vault, manufacturing and distributing #$Currency objects and repossessing the property of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles who default on debt-payments) which underpin the use of that unit of money in particular contexts.  Instances of this collection are usually denoted by wrapping the function  #$Currency-SocialPracticeFn around an instance of #$UnitOfMoney (for instance, (#$Currency-SocialPracticeFn #$Balboa-Panama)).")
(comment iterativeStep "This predicate is used to characterize the unit or quantity corresponding to the `iterative step' of a certain  iterative event. The iterative step is expressed by an #$IterationEventByType in the 2nd arg place. As an example, suppose EVENT is an occurrence of moving up a flight of stairs one step at a time, a type of event which is an instance of #$IterativeEventType. Then it would be true that (#$iterativeStep EVENT (#$IterationTypeFn #$StepOfStairs)).")
(comment HumanShelterConstruction "A specialization of both #$ShelterConstruction and #$HumanOccupationConstruct.  Each instance of #$HumanShelterConstruction is a place designed to shelter people from the elements by allowing them to get indoors.  Specializations include #$ModernHumanResidence, #$SchoolBuilding, #$ShoppingMallBuilding, and many others.   Each instance of #$HumanShelterConstruction must have a roof and typically has sides, though the latter may be flimsy (as in instances of #$Tent) or even absent (as in some instances of #$ParkingGarage).")
(comment hasFlawToDegree "This predicate relates things to the instance of #$LevelOfFlawedness that it has.  Since things are often deemed to be flawed only with respect to some plan, purpose or agent, this predicate may have to be contextualized.  This is a very general relation and it may be preferable to utilize #$flawedWRTRoleInSitType or #$complianceStatus.")
(comment Samba-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
samba style.                            ")
(comment SourcesCertain "Characteristic attribute of a #$WrittenReportOnSituation for which  the source is considered so reliable as to make the information  contained therein virtually certain.")
(comment EconomicSectorType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$EconomicSectorType is a collection of major economic sectors, or general 'super-industries', by function, each of which in turn is the collection of all local or geographically-defined economic sectors that perform such functions.  So the collection #$ManufacturingEconomicSector in general is an instance of #$EconomicSectorType, whereas the the Brazilian manufacturing sector is an instance of #$EconomicSector-Localized.  Every instance of #$EconomicSectorType can have local examples of #$EconomicSector-Localized as its instances.  See also #$IndustryType which is more focused, as well as #$Industry-Localized, #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn, #$IndustryOfRegionFn, and #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.")
(comment ContentTestForNonAnaphoricTEPs "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can solve a particular #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-MemoirGenre "An instance of #$NarrativeGenreType.  Each instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork-MemoirGenre is a narrative emphasizing the author's personal experience of, and interaction with, the events, situations, and people described in that narrative.")
(comment FourLanesOrWiderRoadway "The collection of #$Roadways that have a total of 4 or more than 4 lanes or tracks, both

directions included. This criteria belongs to the US Army's nomenclature

for the representation of roads on large and medium scale maps. See

#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes.")
(comment executePrivilegeOfProgramOnSystem "#$executePrivilegeOfProgramOnSystem PROG SYS PLEVEL) means that the copy, PROG, of the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW on the instance of #$ComputationalSystem, SYS,  executes at #$PrivilegeLevelType PLEVEL. Compare this predicate to #$executePrivilegeOfProgramCopy.")
(comment sentenceTruthFoundToBe "(#$sentenceTruthFoundToBe SENTENCE TRUTH) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE believed that the information the sentence expresses is sound (when TRUTH is #$True) or unsound (when TRUTH is #$False).  See also #$implausibleSentence and #$interestingSentence-Unary.")
(comment OrganizationBySector "A collection of three disjoint collections, #$GovernmentalOrganization, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization and #$PrivateSectorOrganization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationBySector is a set whose elements are distinguished by the sector in which the element #$Organizations operate.  Instances of #$Organizations can be distinguished on the basis of whether they are  governmental (e.g., #$FederalCommunicationsCommission), quasi-governmental (e.g., #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation), or private sector (e.g., #$IBMInc and #$SierraClub).  This collection differs from #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType in that #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType segregates instances of #$Organization on the basis of the specific type of activity they engage in.  For example, #$ResearchOrganization is an element of the collection of #$OrganizationTypeByActivityType, but not of #$OrganizationBySector.  An instance of #$ResearchOrganization might be an instance of any of the collections, #$GovernmentalOrganization, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization, or #$PrivateSectorOrganization.  This collection differs from #$OrganizationTypeByProfitMotive in that #$OrganizationTypeByProfitMotive segregates instances of #$Organization on the basis of whether or not they are motivated by the desire to make a profit for their owners.")
(comment successfulForAgents "The predicate #$successfulForAgents is used to indicate that a particular agent achieves its goal in a particular action.  (#$successfulForAgents ENDEAVOR AGT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT is successful in accomplishing the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR.  This means that each of the purposes AGT had in doing ENDEAVOR has come true.  See also #$purposeInEvent.")
(comment VisitingSomeone "A collection of actions.  In a #$VisitingSomeone event, one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible travels or moves to the vicinity of another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible for the purpose of meeting with that other #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  Each #$VisitingSomeone is purposeful, at least on the part of the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible doing the travelling, and that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is typically a #$Person, and the purpose is often social in nature.")
(comment StudyingReligiousText "Studying religious text, e.g. the Bible (#$Bible-BookCopy), the Quran           or the holy books of other religions.")
(comment actionExpressesFeelingToward "(#$actionExpressesFeelingToward ACTION FEELING OBJECT) means that the

doer (#$doneBy) of ACTION expresses FEELING about OBJECT by doing

ACTION.  Example uses include 'protesters burned a flag to express their hatred of the government', or 'Joe donned a Zoot suit to express his nostalgia for the 1920's.'  See also

#$actionExpressesFeeling, #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree, #$feelsTowardsEvent.  Note that this predicate describes feelings expressed about OBJECT and does not necessarily entail communicating feelings to OBJECT.  To represent the communication of emotions to others see #$CommunicationAct-Single, #$NonVerbalCommunicating.")
(comment signifiesTo "This is the most basic general signification or representation predicate.  (#$signifiesTo THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to AGENT, THING1 signifies THING2.  To AGENT's mind (or other system of semeiosis), the 'sign' THING1 represents, refers to, denotes, describes or depicts its 'object' THING2.  THING2 can be anything, and THING1 can be almost anything, although it is most often a word, phrase, description, string, image or symbol.  Very abstractly speaking,  AGENT must be capable of representation, or semeiosis, whereby AGENT's relationship to the the 'sign' THING1 causes AGENT to come into a related relationship with the 'object' THING2.  Note that this predicate does not state the mechanism by means of which THING1 represents THING2; that can be asserted with more specific predicates.  In order to omit the  explicit mention of the 'interpretant' or AGENT to whom THING1 means THING2, use the short-form #$BinaryPredicate #$signifies.  Often there is a convention (intersubjective understanding and agreement) by which one thing represents another, such as the word 'Dog' referring to dogs in English, or the abstract tetrahedron referring to the element Fire in #$Alchemy.  A pile of three rocks on a path can signify 'danger ahead' and the number thirteen can signify bad luck.  But there need be no specific convention; Deer tracks in the sand can signify the deer to the tracker, and a picture or photograph may signify what ever it is a picture of to anyone who beholds it, in both cases without any prior convention or agreement.  Thus this predicate has more specialized predicates #$signifiesTo-Icon (which represents by means of resemblance, like a picture or a stalactite), #$signifiesTo-Index (which represents by causation, as a deer track represents a deer or a weather vane represents the North Wind), and #$signifiesTo-Symbol (which represents by some convention, as 'dog' represents dogs by the conventions of English).  These are three main kinds of sign in the semiotic theory of #$CharlesPeirce.")
(comment LiveSportsTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs.  Instances of #$LiveSportsTVShow provide coverage           of live sports and recreation events.")
(comment ElectricalDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$ElectricalDevice is a device that requires an input of electrical current (as its #$energySourceForEvent) in order to perform its intended function(s).  Instances of #$ElectricalDevice include both complex devices (for example, instances of the collections #$StereoSystem or #$Computer) and simpler ones (for example, instances of the collection #$ElectricalComponent).")
(comment MultiIndividualAgent-Intelligent "The collection of groups of #$IntelligentAgents whose members operate together to form a kind of collective #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (cf. #$MultiIndividualAgent).  Groups of this sort satisfy the minimal condition for intelligent agency, viz., they are capable of acting purposefully.")
(comment HandlingAnObject "A collection of events and a specialization of #$ActionOnObject, #$ControllingSomething, #$PhysicalContactEvent, and #$SensoryEvent (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$HandlingAnObject is an event in which 
an object (see #$SomethingExisting) is touched and manipulated by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  Specializations of this collection include #$ManipulatingWithFingers and #$HandlingADevice (qq.v.).")
(comment Editorial-CW "The collection of all #$CommentaryArticle-CWs by a periodical or #$MediaOrganization representing the official views of the #$Organization.")
(comment objectFolded "(#$objectFolded EVENT OBJECT) means that OBJECT is physically folded during the #$Folding EVENT.")
(comment PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$BinaryPredicate and #$PhysicalFeaturePredicate.  Each instance of #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate relates some spatial thing to an instance of #$PhysicalAttribute which characterizes that thing.  The attribute may or may not be a quantifiable property.  Examples of #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate include #$objectEmitsOdor, #$viscosityOfSubstance, #$diameterOfObject, #$objectShapeType, and #$xzCrossSectionShapeType.")
(comment movieGenres "(#$movieGenres MOVIE GENRE) states that the #$Movie-CW MOVIE haves a particular GENRE.  For example, (#$movieGenres #$BlazingSaddles-TheMovie #$PropositionalConceptualWork-ComedyGenre).")
(comment oppositeAngle "A ternary predicate that relates a given edge of a #$Triangle to the size of the angle (see #$AngularDistance) opposite that edge.  <code>(#$oppositeAngle EDGE DEGREES TRIANGLE)</code> means that <code>DEGREES</code> is the size of the angle formed by the two sides of <code>TRIANGLE</code> that are not <code>EDGE</code>.
<p>
See also #$angleBetweenEdgesOfObject and #$Angle.")
(comment Dissatisfaction "Feeling of discontent, due to a lack of fulfillment of an agent's desires, needs, or requirements.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.   Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Dissatisfaction are #$Disappointment, #$Frustration, #$Impatience, #$Anger, etc. ")
(comment performsActsOfType-Number "(#$performsActsOfType-Number AGENT ACTION-TYPE-1 ACTION-TYPE-2 NUMBER) holds just in case NUMBER of the instances of ACTION-TYPE-1 that AGENT is known by Cyc to perform are also instances of ACTION-TYPE-2.  For instance, if 40 of the instances of #$TerroristAttack that Hamas is known to perform are also instances of #$Bombing, then (#$performsActsOfType-Percentage #$TerroristOrganization-Hamas #$TerroristAttack #$Bombing 40) holds.")
(comment TVShowOnScience "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily provide information           from areas that are normally considered a           #$ScientificFieldOfStudy, e.g. #$Physics, #$Biology, #$Geology, #$Mathematics or           #$Psychology-Behavioral and provide the information from the point-of-view           of the science in question.")
(comment eventAffectsOrganismPart "(#$eventAffectsOrganismPart EVT PART) says that EVT affects #$OrganismPart PART.  For example, (#$eventAffectsOrganismPart ExposureToRadiation001 CellCluster001) says that CellCluster001 is affected by ExposureToRadiation001.  This is a general predicate the use of which should usually be  superceded in favor of its spec preds,   #$situationAffectsBodyPart and #$eventAffectsPlantPart.")
(comment ThreeLanesOrWiderRoadway "The collection of #$Roadways that have a total of three or more lanes or tracks, both

directions included. This criterion belongs to the US Army's nomenclature

for the representation of roads on medium scale maps. See also

#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes.")
(comment WrittenLegalAgreement "The collection of all written legal agreements. A type of #$TextualDocument-CW and #$LegalAgreement.")
(comment HighLevelOfVirulence "The highest #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionVirulenceLevel.")
(comment ClosingADrawer "The collection of events in which a drawer is closed.  Note that the #$objectActedOn of such an event is a #$ContainerArtifact.  Such objects tend to have one or more drawers.")
(comment MilitaryOperationsBackgroundContext-General "This is the collection of microtheories in which general
information relevant to all or most military operations is given. Note
that information about specific individuals that are relevant to a
particular operation, or a set of particular operations (or proposed
operations), should not be asserted in a
MilitaryOperationsBackgroundContext-General. Rather, information about
individuals should be asserted in a #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory
(or an instance of a spec thereof).")
(comment MakingABankDeposit "A collection of events; a subset of #$MoneyTransfer.  In an instance of #$MakingABankDeposit, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or representative thereof) deposits currency, checks, or other financial tender into a bank account (usually the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's personal bank account, or the bank account of the company for which they work).  An agent may make a deposit in person at the bank, but it might also be made by mail, over the telephone, electronically via modem, at an ATM machine, etc.")
(comment accuracyLevelOfType "(#$accuracyLevelOfType EVTTYPE LEVEL) 

says that every instance of specialization of 

#$Event EVTTYPE has the #$Accuracy LEVEL.")
(comment Museum-Organization "A specialization of #$ProductDisplayOrganization.  Each instance of #$Museum-Organization is an organization which serves primarily to put artifacts on display for the public.  Typically these ortganizations house their displays in instances of #$MuseumStructure (q.v.).")
(comment Jealousy "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Jealousy is some agent's feeling of suspicion and resentment toward a perceived rival.  Instances of #$Jealousy vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or the subject experiencing the feeling.  See also the analogous feeling #$Envy.")
(comment definitionInGlossary "(#$definitionInGlossary WORK GLOSSARY TERM DEFINITION) means that the #$GraphicalStructure GLOSSARY is a glossary contained within (see #$containsStructure-CW) the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and that among the #$subStructures of GLOSSARY are the #$TextString TERM, a term defined in GLOSSARY, and the #$GraphicalStructure DEFINITION, the definition of TERM.")
(comment NthRowOfTableFn "For a particular instance of #$Table-AIS, #$NthRowOfTableFn (#$NthRowOfTableFn TABLE N) returns the #$GraphicalStructure that is the Nth row of TABLE.")
(comment LinearObject-NonPlanar "A specialization of #$LinearObject (q.v.). #$LinearObject-NonPlanar is the collection of all linearly-shaped objects, whether tangible or intangible, that are <i>not</i> embeddable (even roughly) in a #$Plane, and thus are only embeddable in a three-dimensional space region.  Since a #$LinearObject can itself be three-dimensional, we stipulate that non-planar 3-D a linear-object is not even embeddable in a #$FlatSurfaceRegion (q.v.).  
<p>
Note that the criterion for being \"non-planar\" in the present sense varies from context to context.  For example, the standard of non-planarity for the manufacture of wrought-iron railing is less precise than that for pure geometry.  
<p>
Specializations of #$LinearObject-NonPlanar include #$Spiral.  And cf. #$LinearObject-Planar.")
(comment collectionSalientAttribute-VirtuallyRepresented "A #$CollectionSalientAttributePredicate and specialization of #$collectionSalientAttribute-Represented.  <code>(#$collectionSalientAttribute-VirtuallyRepresented COL ATTR)</code> means that <code>ATTR</code> is something (often a predicate, but possibly a function or collection-type) that is or corresponds to a salient attribute of <code>COL</code> that is at present <i>not</i> explicitly represented in the CycL language by a reified term, but that is readily representable by some reifiable CycL term constructable in the current CycL vocabulary.  Thus, anything in the extent of this predicate represents a straightforward opportunity to expand the expressivity of the CycL language in a useful way.
<p>
For more details, see the specializations of this predicate, viz. #$collectionSalientDisjointWith, #$collectionSalientPartitions, #$collectionSalientSharedFeatureAssertions, #$collectionSalientFacetingBinPredVersion, and #$collectionSalientFacetingBinPredInverseVersion.
<p>
Cf. #$collectionSalientAttribute-ActuallyRepresented and #$collectionSalientAttribute-Unrepresented.")
(comment UniqueIDType "Each element of #$UniqueIDType is a collection of ID objects (numbers, strings, etc.) which uniquely identify some class of things.  Some example instances of #$UniqueIDType include:  #$SocialSecurityNumber, whose elements each identify some #$Person; and 'GM vehicle ID number', whose elements would each identify some instance of #$GMAutomobile.  Note that #$SerialNumber-String is not an instance of this class, since it is possible for two manufacturers to use the same number or string to identify different individuals, but specializations of #$SerialNumber-String, such as 'AcmeSerialNumber', might be valid instances.  See also #$uniqueIDForType, which lets you state the class of objects which are uniquely identified by an ID type.  A good rule of thumb is that if you can't come up with a collection of objects that an ID type uniquely discriminates among, then it probably should not be an instance of #$UniqueIDType.")
(comment LinearlyOrderedByStarts "This is the collection of instances of #$ScriptedEventTypes, INS, that have the following feature: for every pair of distinct scenes SCENE1 and SCENE2 that are parts of INS, exactly one of (#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE1 SCENE2) or (#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE2 SCENE1) is true. It is also required that the #$ScriptedEventType not be a single cycle of some continuing process, since in that case the first scene would come both before and after the last scene.")
(comment interestingSentence-Unary "(#$interestingSentence-Unary SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information the sentence expresses is (or would be) worth knowing.  This predicate makes no claims about the <i>correctness</i> of the sentence; for example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$Astronaut) is an interesting sentence which should be asserted into the KB if correct.  See also #$implausibleSentence and #$sentenceTruthFoundToBe.")
(comment BecomingAParticipantInSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Action. In each #$BecomingAParticipantInSomething, someone becomes a participant; is involved in something.")
(comment DoubletonSetOrCollection "A #$SetOrCollectionTypeByCardinality for object types that have two instantiations.")
(comment openingTagOf "(#$openingTagOf TAG OPENTAG) means that the #$TextString OPENTAG is the opening tag form of the generic HTMLTag TAG.  For example, <caption> is the opening tag form of #$Caption-HTMLTag.")
(comment LighterThanAirCraft "A specialization of #$AirTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$LighterThanAirCraft is an air transportation device that depends on lighter-than-air gaseous substances for lift.  Notable specializations of #$LighterThanAirCraft include #$WeatherBalloon and #$Blimp.")
(comment ProducerFn-PTProductType "#$ProducerFn-PTProductType takes as argument any specialization of #$PartiallyTangibleProduct that is an instance of #$ProductType and returns the collection of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles who produce items of that type. For example, (#$ProducerFn-PTProductType #$RadioReceiver) returns the collection of all agents who produce radio receivers.")
(comment AdoptingANorm "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$AdoptingANorm is an event in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible enters into an #$Obligation or adopts a #$Policy.")
(comment HumanTypeByGenericClothingItemSize "The generic sizes (S, M, L, XL, XXL)  The instances of this collection are collections of people such that everyone wears something in that size.  For example, #$Size-Generic-M is the collection of people who can  wear an article of clothing designated as a medium  It is expected that  these instances will be used with the predicate #$clothingSize.   An example assertion would be (#$clothingSize Item01 #$HumanTypeByMensGenericShirtSize #$Size-Generic-M).  That assertion means that Item01 is a medium in men's shirt sizes.  These can also be used with #$humanMeasurements.  (#$humanMeasurements Bob #$HumanTypeByMensGenericShirtSize #$Size-Generic-M) means that Bob is in the collection of people who wear a generic size medium and he is in that collection at least by virtue of his shirt size.  In other words, it means that Bob wears a medium in men's shirts.")
(comment AgentCapacity-CoABS "The collection of instances of
 #$AgentCapacityQuantity that only instances of #$Agent-CoABS can have. 
 Some such capacities will normally be listed on an agent's
 #$Resume-CoABS, representing the sorts of tasks it claims
 it can accomplish.")
(comment agentDocumentationDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentDocumentationDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE documents some fact about AGENT.")
(comment ModerateLevelOfInfectivity "The median #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionInfectivityLevel.")
(comment answerSourceIBTsAccepted "(#$answerSourceIBTsAccepted RESPONSE IBT) says that IBT is one of the instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact that has been accepted by the performer of RESPONSE, an instance of #$ProvidingRequestedInformationToComputerProcess")
(comment PropagatedEpidemic "A collection of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics each of whose instances are such that the cases constituting the #$Epidemic result from the spread of the infectious agent from primary cases to secondary cases and so on. Thus, there is no common source of exposure. The infecting agent must be contagious for an #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic to become a #$PropagatedEpidemic. For example, an #$Epidemic caused by #$Smallpox-Virus would likely be a #$PropagatedEpidemic because #$SmallpoxInfection is highly contagious (#$pathogenContagiousWithContactFromTo #$Smallpox-Virus #$Person #$Person #$highAmountOf).")
(comment UniversalSpaceRegion-2D "A specialization of #$UniversalSpaceRegion  and #$Surface (qq.v.).  This is the collection of two-dimensional spatial universes. In a context whose spatial universe is 2-D (see #$mtSpatialUniverse-2D), every known #$SpatialThing is spatially extended in at most two dimensions, and is spatially subsumed by that universe; and every known 2-D homogeneous extended space region (i.e. #$Surface) is part of (see #$partOfSpaceRegion) that spatial universe.
<p>
See also #$UniversalSpaceRegion-1D and #$UniversalSpaceRegion-3D.")
(comment ScienceFictionTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs.  Instances of #$ScienceFictionTVShow tell a science fiction or fantasy           story.")
(comment groupForAccount "A predicate that relates instances of #$ComputerAccount to the #$UserAccountGroups they belong to. (The #$groupNames of such groups will be listed alongside the account's #$accountIDNumber in the 'etc/passwd' file). (#$groupForAccount ACCOUNT GROUP) means that the account ACCOUNT belongs to the group GROUP. See also #$primaryGroupForAccount.")
(comment ParliamentaryDemocracy "A specialization of #$DemocraticGeopoliticalEntity and #$ParliamentaryGovernment.  Each instance of #$ParliamentaryDemocracy is a country with a democratically elected parliament.")
(comment advertisementUsed-Generally "A predicate relating an advertising event to an advertisement used in all physical advertisements (instances of #$Advertisement-IBT) generated by that event. (#$advertisementUsed-Generally EVENT ADVERT) means that ADVERT, an instance of #$Advertisement-PCW, is instantiated by each instance of #$Advertisement-IBT that is generated by EVENT. For example, an advertising campaign, CAMPAIGN, consisting of many broadcasts of single radio commercial, COMMERCIAL, would be such that (#$advertisementUsed-Generally CAMPAIGN COMMERCIAL). To relate an advertising event to one of several advertisements that it involves, use #$advertisementUsed.")
(comment Uncertainty "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Uncertainty is a feeling of being unsure about something.")
(comment ActorActressTypeByPerformanceType "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Actor whose instances are all of the same performance type.")
(comment OrchestralComposition "The collection of all #$MusicalComposition-Classicals scored for #$Orchestra, with or without soloist(s).")
(comment providerOfService "The predicate #$providerOfService is used to relate a service event to the agent that provides it.  (#$providerOfService SERVICE AGENT) means that the #$ServiceEvent SERVICE is performed or provided by the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT.  Typically, AGENT acts in order to serve the #$recipientOfService (q.v.) in SERVICE.")
(comment IDDocument "A specialization of #$OfficialDocument.  Each instance of this collection is an officially sanctioned credential for identifying some person or physical object.  Important subcollections of #$IDDocument include #$Passport, #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement, #$PersonalCheck.  Other examples include student ID cards, dog tags (worn by military personnel), dog tags (worn by dogs), authentication certificates for an #$ArtObject or an antique.")
(comment SecondaryInfectionSite "#$SecondaryInfectionSite is an instance of #$InfectionSiteTypeByGrade. This is the attribute of instances of #$OrganismPart that play role of secondary infection sites.

Those sites are reached by invasive pathogens in an advenced

stage of an infection. At this time, the pathogenic organisms establish themselve in tissues particularly

suitable for their multiplication. See also #$PrimaryInfectionSite.")
(comment ProbabilityTest "Each instance of #$ProbabilityTest is a #$KBContentTest whose #$InferenceSentenceParameter contains at least one #$CycLProbabilityConstant (e.g.'#$likelihood' or '#$ProbabilityInterval').")
(comment keSuggestionPreds-SpecIns "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and #$RuleMacroPredicate.  (#$keSuggestionPreds-SpecIns <code>COL1 BINPRED COL2)</code> means that for every known specialization <code>SPEC1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>INS2</code> of <code>COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED SPEC1 INS2)</code> is known in the knowledge base.
<p>
For example,
<p>
(#$keSuggestionPreds-SpecIns #$FruitOrVegetableFood #$typicalColorOfType #$Color)
<p>
means that for every known specialization <code>FV-TYPE</code> of #$FruitOrVegetableFood, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>COLOR</code> of #$Color such that <code>(#$typicalColorOfType FV-TYPE COLOR)</code> is known in the knowledge base.
<p>
See also #$keSuggestionPredsInverse-SpecIns.")
(comment StringQuartet-MusicGroup "#$StringQuartet-MusicGroup is the collection of all #$Quartet-MusicalPerformanceGroups who perform #$StringQuartetComposition-CWs. An instance of #$StringQuartet-MusicGroup has two violinists, one cellist, and one violist as members.")
(comment SupplyCompany "A specialization of both #$PrivateSectorOrganization and #$OrganizationWithBusinessCustomers.  Each instance of #$SupplyCompany is an organization whose main function (see the constant #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction) is selling supplies to other organizations.  Instances of #$SupplyCompany include all instances of #$ElectricalSupplyCompany, as well as grocery wholesalers (see the collection #$Wholesaler).")
(comment CashWithdrawal "A collection of events; a subset of #$MoneyTransfer.  In an instance of #$CashWithdrawal, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible receives cash as a withdrawal from its own bank account (or from another account which it is authorized to withdraw funds from).")
(comment RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes "Instances of
#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes indicate the width of an instance PATH of
#$PathArtifact at a given point by indicating the _total_ number of lanes
or tracks in PATH at that point. Note, then, that each instance of
#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes will not correspond to a precise number
representing a distance but rather a scalar interval representing a range
of distances. These belong to US Army's nomenclature for the representation
of roads on maps of large and medium scale.")
(comment AbilitiesOfFn "(#$AbilitiesOfFn AGT) 
denotes the collection of instances of #$AgentCapacityQuantity that are AGT's abilities.")
(comment SubcollectionDisjointWithFn "(#$SubcollectionDisjointWithFn COLLECTION SETOFCOLLECTIONS) specifies the collection of all instances of COLLECTION which disjoint with every collection in SETOFCOLLECTIONS.  For example (#$SubcollectionDisjointWithFn #$RecordedSoundProduct (#$TheSet #$CompactDisc-Audio #$PhonographRecord #$AudioCassette)) would include wax phonograph cylinders, reel-to-reel tapes, and 8-track tapes, but not the recorded music products sold in most #$AudioVideoStores in the late 1990s.")
(comment temporallySubsumesInSituationType "<code>(#$temporallySubsumesInSituationType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation), if instances <code>SIT1</code> and <code>SIT2</code> of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations, then <code>SIT1</code> temporally subsumes <code>SIT2</code>.
<p>
Note that <code>(#$temporallySubsumesInSituationType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> does not imply that instances of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> or <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations of every instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, since <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> may be merely candidate subsituation types of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (see #$candidateProperSubSituationTypes).")
(comment fromConfiguration "(#$fromConfiguration EV CONF) means that CONF, an instance of #$Configuration, is a state of affairs that held prior to the occurrence of EV, an instance of #$ConfiguringEvent.  I.e., just prior to EV, the #$objectConfiguredDuring EV was #$configuredObjects in the #$Configuration CONF.")
(comment Jetty "A specialization of #$FlowControlDevice. Instances of #$Jetty are constructions that extend into a body of water from the shoreline, and are intended to direct currents. Applications incluse, but are not limited to, regulating river channels, fixing river mouths, and influencing the effects of tides. They are frequently made of timbers, earth and stone, or concrete. When constructed of earth and stone, jetties are only distinct from #$Breakwaters in purpose.")
(comment hasEmotionAbout "(#$hasEmotionAbout AGENT THING) means that AGENT has some emotion of some kind about THING.  This means that the agent [#$Agent-PartiallyTangible] is also #$awareOf THING.  One should normally use a more specific predicate than #$hasEmotionAbout, depending upon the type of emotion and whether THING is a proposition [#$ELSentence-Assertible] a collection, a #$TemporalThing, or something else.")
(comment scenarioSentence "A specialization of #$assertedSentence. (#$scenarioSentence SENTENCE)
means that SENTENCE is asserted in an instance of #$ScenarioContext that
can been seen from the current inference context. This predicate is meant
to be used primarily for pragmatic constraints for #$ScenarioGenerationProject.")
(comment statusWithAgent-Gradient "This predicate deals with types of status -- such as credibility, prestige, trust -- that come in degrees. (#$statusWithAgent-Gradient AGENT1 AGENT2 STATUS-AMOUNT) means that AGENT2 assigns STATUS-AMOUNT to AGENT1. E.g., (#$statusWithAgent-Gradient #$Iran #$OPEC (#$LowAmountFn #$Prestige) means that Iran has little prestige within OPEC. (#$statusWithAgent-Gradient #$BillClinton #$HillaryClinton (#$HighAmountFn #$Loyalty)) means that Hillary is very loyal to Bill.  See the collection of quantities #$InterAgentQuantity.")
(comment AccessPageFn-IBT "#$AccessPageFn-IBT takes as argument any instance or specialization of #$ElectroMagneticIBT and returns the collection of all #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS via which one may access this IBT or type of IBT.  For example, (#$AccessPageFn-IBT Yahoo) would return the collection of all web pages via which the Yahoo search engine can be accessed.(#$Kean 10/8/99)")
(comment FoodGroup "A specialization of #$ConventionalClassificationType and hence a collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FoodGroup is a collection of foodstuffs classified according to their nutritional content.  Instances of #$FoodGroup include #$DairyProduct, #$CerealFood, #$FruitOrVegetableFood, #$MeatOrLegumeFood.")
(comment exhibitors "(#$exhibitors GATHERING AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT actively presents information to the attendees of #$SocialGathering GATHERING. AGENT may be marketing a product by putting it or information about it  on display, or AGENT may be displaying artwork, or the results of a scientific study.")
(comment StoringSomethingDangerous "The process in which dangerous objects are stored by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.")
(comment Trio-MusicalPerformanceGroup "A #$Trio-MusicalPerformanceGroup is a group of 3 musicians that perform together.")
(comment pegPartialInterpretations-CycL-ValidatedInInference "(#$pegPartialInterpretations-CycL-ValidatedInInference PEG CYCL) means that some CycL interpretation CYCL of an instance of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg that is a part (see #$properSubExpressions) or rewrite (see #$associatedPegRewrites) has been validated by the inference engine.  See also #$provedCandidateExtractedContents-CycL.")
(comment SupposedToBeMicrotheory "A specialization of #$Microtheory.  Each instance of #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory is a microtheory that describes how things are \"supposed to be\" according to some source.  Instances of this collection can be used to represent things like the policies of a company, the laws of a country, the tenets of a religion, the rules of proper conduct for employees of a particular corporation, etc.  The assertions in a #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory may or may not describe the world as it actually is.  Examples instances include #$BasicWesternLegalConceptsMt, #$SportsRulesOf-BoxingSportsEvent, #$CycStaffCalendar, and #$OfficeCodeOfConduct.")
(comment nodeInGraph "(#$nodeInGraph NODE GRAPH) means that NODE is a node on the #$Graph-AIS, GRAPH.")
(comment hasNumberOfRows "'(#$hasNumberOfRows TABLE N)' means that the #$Table-AIS TABLE has N number of rows (see #$rowOfTable) as component parts.")
(comment BusinessTypeByManufacturingIndicator "A specialization of #$BusinessTypeByActivityType.  Each instance
of #$BusinessPlantTypeByManufacturingStatus is a collection of
#$ChemicalPlant-Organization that may or may not on-site manufacture
chemical substances.")
(comment GradualChange "The #$RateOfChange that indicates a change that takes a long amount of time.")
(comment Effectiveness "#$Effectiveness is the #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType for describing an activity that is done `effectively', namely meeting the goals of that activity as defined within the context of that activity.
Note: This is a very vague #$QuantityType, almost as vague as #$ScriptPerformanceAttribute itself, and should be used ONLY when no more specific attribute type applies.")
(comment evaluationOfType "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate for #$EvaluatingFn.  (#$evaluationOfType EVALUATION-TYPE TYPE) identifies EVALUATION-TYPE as the collection of all instances of #$Evaluating in which some instance of TYPE is evaluated (c.f. #$objectOfEvaluation).")
(comment answerSourceIBTsRejected "(#$answerSourceIBTsRejected RESPONSE IBT) says that IBT is one of the instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact that has been rejected by the performer of RESPONSE, an instance of #$ProvidingRequestedInformationToComputerProcess")
(comment MonoatomicAnion "A specialization of the intersection between #$Anion and
#$MonoatomicIon.  Instances of #$MonoatomicAnion are negatively charged
ions of a single atom.")
(comment AgentTypeByExistentialStatus "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$TemporalThingTypeByExistentialStatus. Instances of #$AgentTypeByExistentialStatus are collections of instances of #$Agent-Generic that share a similar existential state such as #$Disbanded (this state is exclusive to multi-individual agents). See #$agentsExistentialState.")
(comment DriedProduct "The collection of products that were once #$BiologicalLivingObjects, and were then subjected to some #$ProductionEvent where they were dried or dehydrated.  An example is #$Prunes, aka (#$DriedFn (#$FruitFn #$PlumTree)).")
(comment PicturesOfTypeFn-Person "#$PicturesOfTypeFn-Person takes as argument any spec of #$Person and returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting instances of that spec. For purposes of the #$WebSearchEnhancementProject, the specs of #$Person that this #$SubTopicFunction applies to will be limited to those that might be of interest to users of the E-Cyc application.")
(comment GainingControl "A collection of events and a specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer. Each instance of this collection is an event in which something comes under the control of (cf. #$takesControl) some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. 'Control' here means the ability on the part of an agent to determine 'what happens to' another object or agent. In the case where the thing controlled exhibits 'activities' or 'behavior', this extends to a nontrivial ability to direct or circumscribe some important aspect of the behavior that the object or agent exhibits. Examples include capturing a wild longhorn and mining for gold. For cases where the thing controlled was previously under the control of another agent, see #$TransferOfControl. See also #$GainingControlOfFn.
<p>
Note that this collection should not be conflated with #$GainingUserRights. The right (moral, legal, whatever) to make use of something is not the same thing as the ability to control that thing.")
(comment LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation "A sub-collection of #$ResourceAllocationSpecification.  Instances of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization.  These individuals are not the actual instances of #$TimeInterval or any events that occur during those intervals, instead these individuals are descriptions of those intervals.  This is significant because the properties of instances of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation, most notably their temporal extent are distinct from the intervals to which they refer.")
(comment organizationBasicDataSentence "A #$BasicDataPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Organization to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$organizationBasicDataSentence ORG SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a basic fact about ORG.")
(comment WebPageMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories for stating the propositional content of web pages.  See also #$WebPage-AIS.")
(comment Hide-Product "The collection of all instances of (#$DriedFn Skin) which, after removal, have been put through a preservative process, usually tanning, to insure long term durability ")
(comment loudnessOfObject "A #$SensoryAttributeDescriptionPredicate and #$QuantitySlot that relates a #$SomethingExisting to a #$AcousticNoiseLevel.  (#$loudnessLevel OBJECT LEVEL) means that the noise/loudness level of the totality of #$AudibleSounds (see #$loudnessLevel) currently being produced by OBJECT is LEVEL.
<p>
Cf. #$loudnessOfEvent.")
(comment wordForms "(#$wordForms WORD PRED STRING) states that STRING is a PRED form of WORD

in the current context, where PRED is an instance of #$SpeechPartPredicate.

For instance, in the #$EnglishMt and its spec-Mts, (#$wordForms #$Ox-TheWord

#$plural \"oxen\"); (#$wordForms #$Walk-TheWord #$pastTense-Universal \"walked\").

The code support for this predicate looks up irregular forms stated in

the KB -- such as (#$plural #$Ox-TheWord \"oxen\") -- and generates regular forms

such as \"walked\", which need not be stated in the KB.")
(comment TVDocumentary "Instances of #$TVDocumentary are #$TVShow-IBTs in which the all of the content           is either purely factual or objective.  For example, a #$TVDocumentary may contain a           biography of a famous leader, contain information on how a movie was made, or           relate opposing interpretations of some historical event or opposing opinions on some current issue.")
(comment measurementResult "The Cyc predicate #$measurementResult is used to relate a measuring event to the value that it results in.  (#$measurementResult MEAS ATT) means that the measuring activity MEAS yielded a result of ATT, which is a physical quantity.  For example, if the #$measurementResult of weighing a particular domestic letter is (#$Ounce 2.5), I put 55 cents U.S. postage on it.  See also #$MeasuringFn, #$ScalarInterval.")
(comment PositiveChange "An instance of #$LevelOfChange. #$PositiveChange is  the quantity of change that corresponds to any change in the positive direction from very little to very much.")
(comment GeographicalThing-Intangible-FixedLocation "The collection of all intangible things that have a relatively fixed geographic locations, such as the #$EarthsEquator, the #$NorthPole, #$LongitudeLines, stable borders, etc.  Contrast this with #$GeographicalThing-Intangible-MovableLocation.")
(comment objectConfiguredDuring "(#$objectConfiguredDuring EV OBJ) means that OBJ, an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, is configured during EV, an instance of #$ConfiguringEvent. As a result of EV, a new configuration, CONF, will exist in which OBJ will play the role of #$configuredObjects.")
(comment embedCodeInData "(#$embedCodeInData CODE DATA) means that AGENT inserts (the #$ComputerProgram-CW) CODE into (the #$AspatialInformationStore) DATA.  Typically this means that CODE will get executed if DATA is accessed.")
(comment footnoteInWork "(#$footnoteInWork WORK MARK FOOTNOTE) means that the #$GraphicalStructure FOOTNOTE is a footnote in the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and that FOOTNOTE is indicated within WORK by MARK, an instance of #$CharacterString.")
(comment GeographicalPlace-Quadrangle "A subcollection of

#$GeographicalPlace-2D. Instances of #$GeographicalPlace-Quadrangle are portions

of the geographical surface of reference between two latitude lines and two 

longitude lines. 

They can be used to indicate partial geographical location of two or three 

dimensional things within the context of a geography. See 

#$genericallyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical. They can also be 

used to specify the exact extent of an object when specifying an area of 

interest of a particular context (using #$exactlyLocatedAt-Spatial, 

#$mtSpatialUniverse-2D).")
(comment Floundering-SomeoneMakingAStrenousEffort "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingAStrenousEffort. In each #$Floundering-SomeoneMakingAStrenousEffort, someone behaves awkwardly; has difficulties.")
(comment temporalThingTerminated "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates a #$EndingOfTemporalThing TERMINATION to a #$TemporalThing that is terminated (i.e. comes to an end) in TERMINATION.")
(comment verbSemTransPartial "(#$verbSemTransPartial VERB NUM FRAME TRANS) means that part of the translation of word sense number NUM of VERB, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS. #$verbSemTransPartial assertions are designed to facilitate the specification of the semantic translations templates for a series of related frames. For example, for the verb 'model', the 'on' prepositional phrases typically indicate what is being modelled, as in  \"But for Private Ryan, DreamWorks canceled a G.I. Joe action figure modeled on Hanks.\". To avoid having to duplicate the information from the #$verbSemTrans assertion for the #$TransitiveNPFrame frame in that for the TransitivePPCompFrame-On frame, #$verbSemTransPartial can be used. For 'model', the #$verbSemTransPartial assertion for #$TransitiveFrameType would specify that the general interpretaiton for the transitive usage, such as (#$and (#$isa :ACTION (#$MakingFn #$Model-Artifact)) (#$performedBy :ACTION :SUBJECT) (#$outputsCreated :ACTION :OBJECT)), whereas the assertion for TransitivePPCompFrame-On, would just need to specify (#$similarTo :OBJECT :OBLIQUE-OBJECT).")
(comment connectedViaFlexibleConnector "(connectedViaFlexibleConnector OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are connected via a connector which is flexable.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 can move relative to each other due to deformation of the connector.  This predicate is a specialization of #$connectedTo-SemiRigidly and a generalization of #$flapHingedTo.  Positive exemplars are two objects conected by Velcro (tm), the #$GallBladder's connection to the #$Liver, or the front cover of a #$Book-CW's connection to that book's spine.  Negative examples include a hypodermic needle's connection to the IV tube (the tube is flexible, not the connection), a door's connection to the door #$Frame (parts of the hinge rotate relative to other pars, but the hinge does not deform), and a #$Wheel's connection to an #$Axle (no deformation here, either).")
(comment productionValueOfIndustryDuring "(#$productionValueOfIndustryDuring REGION COL THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the value of all the goods and services produced by the specialization of the #$Industry-Localized COL in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Note that COL can range from a broad economic sector, such as agriculture, manufacturing, or services to a more specific segment of the economy such as the automobile industry.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment axialTiltRange "(#$axialTiltRange VEHICLE ANGLE-RANGE) is the range of angles at which VEHICLE can be tilted along the front to back axis and still be able to travel in a straight line (cars are generally able to drive through much steeper turns). For a #$JeepBrandCar the range is probably something like (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -40 40) which means that it will tip over when tilted sideways at a 45 degree angle. This range need not be symmetrical. For #$WaterTransportationDevices the #$axialTiltRange may be surprisingly wide, even (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -180 180) for boats which have such a heavy keel that they return to an upright position even when upside-down.")
(comment Saccharomycetaceae-Family "A collection of ascomycetous fungi, see #$Ascomycota-Division. An instance of
#$BiologicalFamily.")
(comment postalCodeBaseText "(#$postalCodeBaseText LOCATION STRING) means that STRING is the base (non-extended, possibly incomplete) form of the postal code for LOCATION.  For addresses in the United States, STRING would correspond to the 5-digit part of the ZIP code, represented as a character string.  Note that in other parts of the world, the base part of the postal code may consist of letters, numbers, or other symbols as well (e.g., dashes, colons).  See also #$postalCodeOfAddress and #$zipCodeForLocation. The latter assumes that in the context of use (the #$Microtheory in which  relevant assertions are entered), the base part of ZIP  codes will be represented as numbers rather than as character strings.")
(comment InsuranceProvider "A collection of organizations; a subcollection of #$ServiceOrganization. An instance of #$InsuranceProvider is an organization whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to provide financial and material protection to its clients in the event of sickness, death, natural disaster, loss, theft, lawsuits, etc. (Insurers may specialize in one or more of those areas.) Instances of #$InsuranceProvider may belong to either #$CommercialServiceOrganization or #$NonProfitOrganization (including insurance providers belonging to #$LegalGovernmentOrganization). Example instances include State Farm Insurance Co., Aetna Casualty Co., Lutheran Brotherhood, and all fifty members of U.S. #$StateMedicaidAdministrationOrganizations.")
(comment thirdPersonSg-Present "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its third person singular verb form. The regular third person singular for is generated from the infinitive verb form with an 's' suffix. Verbs in the Cyc lexicon will have a #$thirdPersonSg-Present entry only if they are irregular. Regular forms are generated by the morphology component.  Regular example: 'runs'. Irregular example: 'flies'.")
(comment ExclusiveTreatmentType "The collection of types of MedicalCareEvents which people will not usually perform more than one instance of at a time.  For example, AntihistimineTherapy would be an #$ExclusiveTreatmentType, so a patient will not take both ChlorTrimeton and Dimetapp within the same hour, because the scripts would overlap.  The patient might choose to take a cough suppressant at the same time, though, because that would not be exclusive with antihistamines.")
(comment deliveryServiceUsed "A predicate for relating an act of sending some tangible object (not e.g. an email) to a delivery service used for that sending. (#$deliveryServiceUsed SEND SERVICE) means that SERVICE, an instance of #$DeliveryServiceEvent, was used to send the objects sent in the action SEND, an instance of #$SendingSomething.")
(comment NationsPeacefullyCoexisting "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$CoexistingWithSomethingElse. In each #$NationsPeacefullyCoexisting, something coexists peacefully, as of nations.")
(comment DerivedProbability-RangeFn "A function used for probability statements.  (#$DerivedProbability-RangeFn PROPOSITION), applied to the #$CycLAssertion PROPOSITION, yields, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the range of a posteriori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, given (and depending on) the current state of knowledge of other assertions.  This result is a number or range of numbers somewhere within the range 0-1 (either a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true, or an interval between two such numbers).  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the derived range of derived probability that PROPOSITION is true given the probabilities (or probability ranges) of the other #$CycLAssertions and #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.   Contrast this with the predicate form #$derivedProbability-Range and with the functions #$DerivedProbabilityFn and #$PriorProbability-RangeFn.  The result of a use of #$DerivedProbability-RangeFn on a proposition depends at least partially on, and is in some manner derived from or affected by, the probabilities of some or all of the other #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory (whether prior, derived or conditional) along with the #$domainAssumptions.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment LoanUnderwriter "The collection of #$Organizations which perform loan underwritings (see #$UnderwritingOfLoan), actions in which the #$Organization finances some #$Person or other #$Organization, accepting the risk of losing the funds borrowed in that #$LoanAgreement (see #$FinancingByBorrowing), in return for payment, usually in the form of interest.")
(comment RateOfChange "A specialization of #$NonNumericScalarQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RateOfChange is a quantity measuring an amount of change or \"happening\" that occurs (over an unspecified amount of time).  Examples of rates-of-change include #$GradualChange, #$ModerateChange, and #$SuddenChange.
<p>
See also #$Rate.")
(comment hobbyCWPerformedBy "(#$hobbyCWPerformedBy GAME-CW PRSN) means that the instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity is a type of hobby activity performed by #$Person PRSN. For example, (#$hobbyCWPerformedBy #$Golf #$BillClinton) means that #$BillClinton has #$Golf as a hobby. This predicate should be used only when PRSN sometimes plays the role of #$performedBy in events that are performances of GAME-CW. For example, if #$MWakoff enjoys watching #$Golf, but doesn't know how to golf, it would be incorrect to assert (#$hobbyCWPerformedBy #$Golf #$MWakoff). Use #$performancesOfWorkAre to relate instances of #$DevisedStructuredActivity to the events which are performances of them. Use #$hobbyScriptPerformedBy to relate an instance of #$ScriptType to an instance of #$Person who performs this activity as a hobby.")
(comment IonicHydrideType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies formed when #$Hydrogen reacts with any of the #$AlkaliMetalElementTypes, #$Calcium, #$Strontium, or #$Barium.")
(comment FormerPersonTypeFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction. This function takes for its value a specialization of #$TemporallyExistingThing, <b>TYPE</b>, and returns the collection of former instances of <b>TYPE</b>. Thus, for any instance <b>INDIVIDUAL</b> of the collection (#$FormerPersonTypeFn <b>TYPE</b>), <b>INDIVIDUAL</b> was at some previous time an instance of <b>TYPE</b>.")
(comment AllowsSharedCDRomAccess "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByPassiveCapability. A computer has this capability if it is possible for its #$CD-ROMDrive to be accessed by someone other than the currently logged on user. For cases where unauthorized users can gain access, see the more specialized #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedCDRomAccess.")
(comment DorsalDirection "The general direction toward the backside, away from the stomach side, in or near an object that is #$AnimalShapedThing.  In the case of a #$Person this is the #$VectorInterval comprising the cone-shaped set of vectors pointing (from some reference point) within approximately forty-five degrees of straight in back when in an #$UprightPosture.")
(comment FixedFunctionalSystem "A collection of #$FunctionalSystems whose instances are characterized by the fact that their subsystems--the #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles playing functional roles within the system--play their roles invariably, to the point that any particular #$Agent-PartiallyTangible can be readily identified by referring to a particular role or suite of roles.  I.E., in a #$FixedFunctionalSystem there is for each subsystemic #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles  that is a #$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole a role or delimited set of roles   that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible plays all of the time and that may be said to characterize the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  An #$Organism-Whole is an example of a #$FixedFunctionalSystem.")
(comment speechOfCharacter "(#$speechOfCharacter WORK QUOTE) means that the #$TextString QUOTE represents the speech of one of the characters within the fictional #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.")
(comment typicallyLikesRelationshipFromType "(#$typicallyLikesRelationshipFromType AGENT_TYPE REL COLLECTION) means that a typical instance of AGENT_TYPE likes to be in the relationship REL with an instance of COLLECTION [#$likesRelationshipFromType].  If the relationship is a #$Role and the #$Collection is a spec of #$Event, then #$likesRoleInEventType applies among the typical instance of AGENT_TYPE, #$Role, and #$Event type.")
(comment Chest-PieceOfFurniture "Basically just the intersection of #$Box-Container and Furniture.")
(comment PhysicalForceType "These are the types of physical forces currently recognized by #$Physics, namely the #$PhysicalForce-Weak, #$PhysicalForce-Strong, #$PhysicalForce-Electromagnetic, and #$GravitationalForceVector.")
(comment itemInList-Information "'(#$itemInList-Information LIST ITEM)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure ITEM is one of the items listed in the #$List-Information LIST.  All instances of #$List-Information include at least two #$GraphicalStructures that are related to the #$List-Information via #$itemInList-Information.  A particular #$GraphicalStructure that is an item in an instance of #$List-Information is a coherent, self-contained unit of information that is somehow distinguished (whether by numbering, ordering, arrangement, or appearance) from other component items of the list.")
(comment sinner "The wrong-doer in a #$ImmoralAct.")
(comment preface-DocumentPartOf "(#$preface-DocumentPartOf WORK PREFACE) means that the #$GraphicalStructure PREFACE is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and is a preface within that work.  Prefaces precede the body of a work, are written by the author or authors of the main propositional content of the work, and often set forth the origins or purpose of the work, the subjects covered, and the audience for which the work is intended. For prefatory textual material that is written by a person other than the author of the work in which the prefatory material is contained, see #$foreword-DocumentPartOf.")
(comment ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory "Each instance MT of #$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory

has access to the notions of historical possibility and necessity in

#$ReasoningWithMultiFuture-LogicMt.  Such an MT may have

#$mtAlternatives microtheories.  #$mtAlternatives microtheories stand

for the `same moment' relative to different possible futures at the

moment.  Thus for each instance PROP of

#$ELSentence-AssertibleWithoutOpenFutureTrace, PROP is true in MT iff it is true in

all MT's #$mtAlternatives, while a formula that is not an instance of

#$ELSentence-AssertibleWithoutOpenFutureTrace may have different truth values in MT's

different #$mtAlternatives.  A subcollection of this collection is

#$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries.")
(comment grossDomesticProductOf "The Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of a nation is the value of its total domestic output of goods and services in a given period (so the second argument is a #$MonetaryRate). Usually the #$grossDomesticProductOf is given in #$BillionDollarsPerYear.  See also #$grossNationalProduct-Old.")
(comment captionInWorkTo "(#$captionInWorkTo WORK CAPTION STRUC) means that the #$TextString CAPTION is a caption to STRUC and both CAPTION and STRUC are contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.  STRUC is an instance of either #$Table-AIS, #$Graph-AIS or #$AbstractVisualStructure.  Captions are textual descriptions or explanations of parts of documents that are understood or experienced, at least in part, non-textually (i.e. #$AbstractVisualStructures).")
(comment isSubStringOfCDAAtOffset "This is the corresponding predicate of #$CDASubStringAtOffsetWithLengthFn.")
(comment organismGroupExposedToHarmfulSubstance "(#$organismGroupExposedToHarmfulSubstance EXPOSING GROUP) means that every #$groupMembers MEMBER of GROUP such that MEMBER is an #$Organism-Whole plays the role of #$organismExposed in EXPOSING.")
(comment Expectation "The collection of microtheories whose propositions represent what some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or #$Group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles) believes will be true at some future time.")
(comment CollectionArgModeFn "An expression of the form (#$CollectionArgModeFn SYMBOL TYPE) is used to abstractly represent a commented version of the #$Collection TYPE for the purposes of being able to provide semantic information abouta #$Predicate to instance of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingProgram-CW for the sake of making rule induction more efficient. This information will be used by communicated to such systems relative to an instance of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination.")
(comment NodeFinitePathSystem "The collection of all #$PathSystems each of which has finitely many nodes, i.e., the collection of every #$PathSystem SYS such that the set (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) is finite.  See also #$nodeInSystem. Note that there may still be infinitely many 'points' along the links between nodes in such a system.  There could also be infinitely many links, such as between just two nodes.")
(comment backgroundNotRelevantToConclusion "(#$backgroundRelevantToConclusion STRING1 STRING2 means that STRING1 is the the background text against which STRING2 should be evaluated")
(comment alignedCylinderWithin "The predicate (#$alignedCylinderWithin INNER_CYLINDER OUTER_CYLINDER) means that OUTER_CYLINDER (which has #$Cylinder) surrounds all of the INNER_CYLINDER or a section its major axis which extends through the length of OUTER_CYLINDER.  INNER_CYLINDER may be #$physicalParts of OUTER_CYLINDER, or the relationship between them could be #$spatiallyIntersects or #$in-ContGeneric (and thus #$spatiallyDisjoint).")
(comment PersonWithOccupationTypeByJobClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PersonWithOccupationTypeByJobClass is a collection of people with a job in a similar broad class.  Instances of #$PersonWithOccupationTypeByJobClass include #$BlueCollar, #$WhiteCollarWorker, and #$FlexibleWorkingHours.")
(comment defeatedInConflict "(#$defeatedInConflict CONFLICT LOSER) means that in the #$ConflictEvent CONFLICT, the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible LOSER was defeated.")
(comment importCapacityDuring "(#$importCapacityDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE that could be imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars that could be imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil that could be imported, or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil that could be imported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing what would be the average rate of import of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to REGION during the temporal extent of THING if REGION were importing PRODUCT-TYPE at the limit of its capacity.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment Boycott-Economic "A collection of actions, a subset of #$EconomicAction. In each instance, a group refuses to buy products or some type of product, e.g., grapes, or products originating from some area, e.g., #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica, or some agent, e.g., Nike, or some combination of the these, e.g., grapes from #$SouthernCalifornia.")
(comment inappropriateAttireTypeAt "This predicate relates locations to clothing types that are inappropriate clothing items for the kind(s) of event(s) that usually occur at the location. (#$inappropriateAttireTypeAt PLACE ATTIRETYPE) means that if one is a human participating in an instance of a kind of #$HumanActivity that typically occurs at PLACE it would be inappropriate to wear an instance of ATTIRETYPE.  The inappropriateness may result from social conventions or physical factors.  See also #$clothingTypeForSituationTypeAt,

#$clothingTypeFormalit, #$eventTypeAppropriateClothingItem, and #$eventTypeInappropriateClothingItem.")
(comment hobbyScriptPerformedBy "(#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy SCRIPT-TYPE PRSN) means that the instance of #$ScriptType SCRIPT-TYPE is a type of hobby activity performed by #$Person PRSN. For example, (#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy #$FigureSkating #$MWakoff) means that #$MWakoff has #$FigureSkating as a hobby. This predicate should be used only when PRSN sometimes plays the role of #$performedBy in events of type SCRIPT-TYPE. For example, if #$MWakoff enjoys watching surfing but doesn't know how to surf, it would be incorrect to assert (#$hobbyScriptPerformedBy #$Surfing #$MWakoff) Use #$hobbyCWPerformedBy to relate an instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity to an instance of #$Person who has this activity as a hobby.")
(comment TransportWithMotorizedLandVehicle "A collection of transportation events; a subset of #$ControllingATransportationDevice.  An instance of #$TransportWithMotorizedLandVehicle is a transportation event that takes place on land using a motorized vehicle as the transporter.  Examples include instances of the collections #$OffRoadMotorcycleRiding and some of the various #$TransportViaFns.")
(comment dataSourceUserForSKS "An afterslot relating a #$SKSConnectionSpecification to the user name by which it will be accessed.")
(comment VocationalDegreeForFn "(#$VocationalDegreeForFn ?OCCTYPE) denotes the set of degrees from vocational schools, representing training in the #$PersonTypeByOccupation ?OCCTYPE.")
(comment informationStolen "(#$informationStolen STEALING INFO) means that in the #$StealingInformation event STEALING, the #$AspatialInformationStore INFO is stolen.")
(comment MakingAPiratedCopy "The collection of all events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible makes an illegal copy of copyrighted material. Examples include copying a CD owned by someone else for your personal use or for sale to others. Note that some kinds of copying of copyrighted material are not illegal - this collection includes only the illegal kinds.")
(comment ElementStuff "An instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and a specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$ElementStuff is a piece of tangible stuff, composed of a quantity of atoms, all of which are of the same chemical element.  That is, every atom in a given piece of #$ElementStuff has the same number of protons in its atomic nucleus.  For example, all pieces of carbon (i.e. all instances of #$Carbon) are instances of #$ElementStuff.  On the other hand, instances of #$Water, because they are all constituted of both #$Hydrogen and #$Oxygen atoms, do not belong to the collection #$ElementStuff.")
(comment ChickenPox "A highly infectious disease whereby the skin is covered with spotty lesions that itch a lot.  #$ChickenPox is a usually a children's disease.  In adulthood, the same #$Virus (varicella zoster virus) causes the disease called #$Shingles-Ailment which is much more serious.  Only people who have already had #$ChickenPox acquire #$Shingles-Ailment.")
(comment collectionSalientAttribute-ActuallyRepresented "A #$CollectionSalientAttributePredicate and specialization of #$collectionSalientAttribute-Represented.  <code>(#$collectionSalientAttribute-ActuallyRepresented COL ATTR)</code> means that <code>ATTR</code> is a predicate or collection-type that is or corresponds to a salient attribute of <code>COL</code> that is explicitly represented in the CycL language by a reified term.
<p>
For more details, see the specializations of this predicate, e.g. #$collectionSalientIsa, #$collectionSalientGenls, #$collectionSalientFacetingBinPred, and #$collectionSalientFacetingCollectionType.
<p>
Cf. this predicate's sibling #$collectionSalientAttribute-VirtuallyRepresented.")
(comment emulatesType "(#$emulatesType SYSTEM SYSTEM-TYPE) means that SYSTEM is capable of emulating the performance of SYSTEM-TYPE.  SYSTEM must be an instance of #$ComputerMarketCategory -- software, hardware, or a combination of the two.  SYSTEM-TYPE must be a collection that is a specialization of #$ComputerMarketCategory.  See also #$Emulation, #$EmulatorHardware, #$EmulatorProgram.")
(comment CloseContactTransmittedInfection "A specialization of #$Infection.  Instances of #$CloseContactTransmittedInfection are contagious infections, i.e., typically  transmitted from one host to another by contact (#$TouchingEvent for instance). An important  specialization is #$SexuallyTransmittedInfection.")
(comment backgroundRelevantToConclusion "(#$backgroundRelevantToConclusion STRING1 STRING2 means that STRING1 is the the background text against which STRING2 should be evaluated")
(comment StatisticallySupported "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType and a collection of cyc arguments which are supported by some statistical resource.  This collection can be used to indicate  that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) is supported by some statistical regularity, perhaps discovered or calculated by some resource external to Cyc.")
(comment CoverOfIBO "A collection of hardcopy still images. A #$CoverOfIBO is a #$StillImage found on the front outside cover of an #$InformationBearingObject such as a hardcopy book or magazine, the packaging for a #$CompactDisc-Generic or #$PhonographRecord, etc. It generally includes text identifying the contents of the #$InformationBearingObject, and may also contain #$Photographs, artwork, designs, etc.")
(comment reusabilityOfTypeForType "(#$reusabilityOfTypeForType COL EVENTTYPE ROLE QUAN) means that after an instance of COL plays the role ROLE in an event of type EVENTTYPE, then QUAN indicates the likelihood to assign to its  re-usability if one does not know how many times it has played that role before.  If QUAN is a high value this indicates that things are  unlikely to wear out after playing the indicated role.  So we might say that (#$reusabilityOfTypeForType #$Hammer #$HammeringANail #$deviceUsed 

#$veryHighAmountOf) because hammers survive many hammering events without any decrease in functionality.  However, (#$reusabilityOfTypeForType #$FacialTissue BlowingOnesNose #$deviceUsed #$veryLowAmountOf).")
(comment Sharing "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingSomethingAvailable (among other supercollections).  In an instance of #$Sharing, one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible receives #$PrimaryRoleUseRights over an object for a limited time from another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, who doesn't give up his or her own right to use it, too (but does give up exclusive right to it).  Cf. #$BorrowingSomething.")
(comment prefers "(#$prefers AGT PROP1 PROP2) means that the state of affairs picked out by the #$CycLSentence-Assertible PROP1 is preferred by the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT to the state of affairs picked out by the #$CycLSentence-Assertible PROP2.  See also #$prefersToMaximize, #$prefersToMinimize.")
(comment FolkDancing-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
folk style.                            ")
(comment PotentialChemicalThreat-BBNEntityType "A collection which subsumes both #$HarmfulChemicalSubstance and #$ChemicalWeapon.")
(comment UnderwriterOfLoan-Person "The collection of employees of various corporate underwriters (such as #$SecuritiesUnderwriter) who decide whether or not their company should assume any particular #$Underwriting or risk.")
(comment ComingForthFromAStateOfLatency "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ComingForth. In each #$ComingForthFromAStateOfLatency, something comes forth or begins from a state of latency.")
(comment MusicalTheaterCompany "The collection of organizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to provide theatrical entertainment in the form of instances of #$MusicalDrama.")
(comment DisplayingSomething "A subcollection of #$VisualInformationGeneratingAct, #$DisplayingSomething is the collection of #$PurposefulActions in which instances of #$PartiallyTangible play the role of #$instrument-Generic when they are intentionally made to be visually accessible by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, which plays the #$Role #$senderOfInfo.  This particular collection makes no committments on the intentions or success of the #$senderOfInfo in relation to the display reaching an audience.  Thus, #$recipientOfInfo and #$recipientOfInfo-Intended are note necessary roles in instances of this collection.")
(comment PolyatomicAnion "A specialization of both #$Anion and #$PolyatomicIon.
Instances of #$PolyatomicAnion are negatively charged groups of more
than one atom.")
(comment Contempt "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Contempt is a feeling of one agent toward another agent, in which the latter agent is viewed by the former as low, vile, feeble, or ignominious.   Instances of #$Contempt vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, and/or the object of dislike.")
(comment exchangers "The predicate #$exchangers is used to identify the (typically, two) #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles involved in an instance of #$ExchangeOfUserRights.   In such an event, each of the #$exchangers gives up possession of one thing and gains possession of another which was previously possessed by the other agent.  <code>(#$exchangers EXCH AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is one of the parties having such a dual role in the #$ExchangeOfUserRights <code>EXCH</code>.  Every instance of #$ExchangeOfUserRights has two sub-events which are instances of #$TransferringPossession (e.g., a dollar bill goes in one direction and some french fries and a few coins go in the other direction.)  Each of the #$exchangers is both a #$toPossessor (in one of the two #$TransferringPossession sub-events of <code>EXCH)</code> and a #$fromPossessor (in the other sub-event).")
(comment TakingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GainingUserRights.  In an instance of #$TakingSomething, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible takes an object, in the sense of taking it away or using or exercising access to it.  The agent may or may not have any legal right or authorization to use that object.  In an instance of #$TakingSomething, the taker (the #$toPossessor) must intend and actively (attempt to) acquire the #$objectTaken, so the taking event is intentional and thus, strictly speaking, #$performedBy the taker.")
(comment PostOfficeOrganization "A collection of local government organizations.  An element of #$PostOfficeOrganization is a particular Post Office organization -- postal station, mailing facility, or branch office -- having a particular location.  Note that this collection includes only government post offices, not non-government commercial shippers who offer various kinds of shipping services, sometimes including Postal services.")
(comment ChangeInUserRights "A collection of events and a specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  Each instance of #$ChangeInUserRights is an event in which some instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible either gains or loses possession of something.   \"Possession\" means having some right to use a thing that one has in hand or otherwise has access to.  Different types of possession (e.g. ownership, rental, borrowings) can be specified by using the appropriate instance(s) of #$SituationTypeByUserRights (q.v.).  Changes in an agent's user rights can come about in various ways: through buying and selling, renting, borrowing or lending, giving, repossession, etc.  Specializations of this collection include #$LosingUserRights, #$GainingUserRights, and #$ExchangeOfUserRights; in the latter collection, there is an alteration in the rights of two (or more) agents to use two (or more) items -- as in a purchase, when one agent gets full use rights to an object by turning over a sum of money to the object's previous owner.  In addition, some changes in user rights are classified explicitly in #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights (e.g. borrowing, renting), while others are permanent.   Events that involve such changes in user rights all belong in the collection of events, #$ChangeInUserRights.   In any particular #$ChangeInUserRights event, the item which is changing hands is identified as the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer.")
(comment CourseOfStudyFn "#$CourseOfStudyFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all instances of #$CourseOfStudy in which that thing is (a signficant part of) what is studied.  For example, (#$CourseOfStudyFn #$Philosophy-Ancient) returns the collection of all courses in which material from the field of Ancient Philosophy is studied.  (#$CourseOfStudyFn #$HairCuttingEvent) returns the collection of all courses in which hair cutting is the subject of study.")
(comment keSuggestionPreds-InsIns "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and #$RuleMacroPredicate.  <code>(#$keSuggestionPreds-InsIns COL1 BINPRED COL2)</code> means that for every known instance <code>INS1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>INS2</code> of <code>COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INS1 INS2)</code> is known in the knowledge base.
<p>
For example,
<p>
(#$keSuggestionPreds-InsIns #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType #$typicalTasteOfType #$ObjectTypeByTaste)
<p>
means that for every known instance <code>ES-TYPE</code> of #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType, it is suggested that there be some instance <code>TASTE</code> of #$ObjectTypeByTaste such that <code>(#$typicalTasteOfType ES-TYPE TASTE)</code> is known in the knowledge base.
<p>
See also #$keSuggestionPredsInverse-InsIns.")
(comment TemporalExtentFn "A unary #$IndividualDenotingFunction that maps each #$TemporalThing to the #$TimeInterval that it occupies.  (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is the time-interval of longest #$duration (q.v.) during which TEMP exists (if TEMP is a #$SomethingExisting) or occurs (if an #$Event) or obtains (if a #$StaticSituation).  If TEMP is itself a time-interval, (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is identical to TEMP.
<p>
Note that (#$TemporalExtentFn TEMP) is a #$ContinuousTimeInterval (q.v.) if and only if TEMP is #$temporallyContinuousDuring (q.v.).
<p>
See also the corresponding predicate #$temporalExtent.")
(comment inConfigurationType "(#$inConfigurationType OBJECT TYPE) means that OBJECT is one of the objects configured (see #$configuredObjects) in a #$Configuration of TYPE.  (#$inConfigurationType ROPE75 #$KnotConfiguration) means that ROPE75 is in the #$Configuration (or #$Situation) of being in a knot. This predicate is also useful for translating locutions in which shapes are attributed to an object by reference to a shape situation type that the object is in, as in 'All DNA-Molecules are in a helix configuration' or 'The group of people is in a circle': (#$relationAllInstance #$inConfigurationType #$DNAMolecule (#$ShapesConfigurationSituationFn #$Helix)) means that all DNA molecules are in a helix configuration. (#$inConfigurationType GROUPOFPEOPLE (#$ShapesConfigurationSituationFn #$Circular)) means that GROUPOFPEOPLE are in a a circular configuration (or are 'in a circle').")
(comment intendedAudienceSizeOfCW "(#$intendedAudienceSizeOfCW IBT-TYPE NUM) means that NUM is the number of people expected to access instances of IBT-TYPE, a #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType.  For #$Periodicals, and other such subsets of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject, the #$intendedAudienceSizeOfCW will be about equal to the number of copies printed.  See also #$MediaSeriesProductType.")
(comment LevelOfPain "A specialization of #$InternalSensoryQuantity whose elements represent the qualitative levels of pain that may be felt by a perceptual agent.  The source of the pain could be either external or internal; in either case, the subjective feeling is generally `sharper' and hopefully shorter-lived than just `a feeling of discomfort' (see: #$LevelOfDiscomfort.)")
(comment MineField-AntiTankWithGap "Collection of instances of #$MineField characterized as being intended to impede progress of mechanized or tracked units, but with an intentionally inbuilt gap for purposes of canalization.  See #$CanalizingAnEnemyForce.")
(comment TitleAgreement "The collection of #$LegalAgreements conferring ownership of some property upon an #$IntelligentAgent.  All ownership rights in the property indicated in a #$TitleAgreement belong to the holder of the #$TitleAgreement, specified within that agreement.  For representation of the actual title document, see #$TitleDocument.")
(comment num-GenQuantRelnFrom "An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifierRelation (q.v). (#$num-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN THING COL NUM) is true if for exactly NUM instances X of COL (RELN THING X) holds.  For example, (#$num-GenQuantRelnFrom #$neighbors #$BillClinton #$AdultMalePerson 3) means there are exactly three adult males among Bill Clinton's neighbors.  The third argument place of this of this predicate is constrained to instances of #$SetOrCollection -- the more specific #$relationInstanceExistsCount (the third argument place of which is constrained to instances of #$Collection) should be used instead of #$num-GenQuantRelnFrom whenever possible.")
(comment PersonWithManifestParaphilia "The collection of #$Persons with #$ParaphilicSexualBehavior.
These people have sexual behaviors that are deemed deviant or
non-usual by normal social standards. This includes persons who engage
in activities such as #$Pedophilia-TheAction and #$Bestiality.")
(comment TransportationContainerProduct "#$TransportationContainerProduct is a specialization of #$ContainerArtifact and #$Conveyance.  Each instance of #$TransportationContainerProduct is a container in which the primary function is to transport substances or objects.  A few examples are #$Luggage, #$BabyCarrier, and #$Trailer.")
(comment attemptAtPerforming "(#$attemptAtPerforming ATTEMPT ACTIONTYPE) means that
ATTEMPT is an attempt to perform ACTIONTYPE. Specifically, there is an
#$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT who, by virtue of playing the #$performedBy role in
ATTEMPT, is intending to play the #$performedBy role in an instance of
ACTIONTYPE.")
(comment Soul-Spiritual "The collection of all souls.  In some microtheories every #$SentientBeing incarnates a #$Soul-Spiritual.  In some, souls are eternal or immortal.  In some microtheories souls may incorporate multiple times in the same or different types of organisms, while in others a soul incorporates but a single time.  Souls are #$FictionalThings in #$NaturalismMt.")
(comment ExpellingFromPosition "A specialization of #$ExpellingFromStatus and #$TransferOut (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$ExpellingFromPosition is an action in which someone holding a position in some organization (see #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg) is expelled from that position (but not necessarily from membership in that organization; cf. #$ExpellingFromMembership).  Note that this collection does <i>not</i> include voluntary resignations (cf. #$ResigningFromEmployment).")
(comment Modern-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
modern style.                            ")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotone "A #$PredicateType.  #$GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotone is the #$collectionUnion of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-MonotoneIncreasing and #$GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotoneDecreasing (qq.v.).")
(comment issuesCredentialTypeTo "#$issuesCredentialTypeTo is a ternary predicate that relates two instances of#$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a specialization of #$Credential. (#$issuesCredentialTypeTo ISSUER CRED RECIPIENT) means that ISSUER issues CRED to RECIPIENT.")
(comment foreword-DocumentPartOf "(#$foreword-DocumentPartOf WORK FOREWORD) means that the #$GraphicalStructure FOREWORD is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and is a foreword within that work. Forewords precede the body of a work, are written by someone other than the author of the work as a whole (but often praise that author or the work as a whole), and often introduce the author or the subject matter of the work.  Individuals who write forewords are often distinguished in a particular field or otherwise notable for their achievements.  For prefatory textual material that is written by the author of the work, see #$preface-DocumentPartOf.")
(comment PlayOpportunityFn-Online "#$PlayOpportunityFn-Online takes as argument any spec of #$ComputerGameProgram and returns the collection of all opportunities (situations in which normal barriers are absent or minimized) to play games of that type via the internet.  For example, (#$PlayOpportunityFn-Online #$Tetris-TheGame) would return the collection of all opportunities to play the game Tetris online, and (#$PlayOpportunityFn-Online #$Quake-TheGame) would return the collection of all opportunities for online play of the computer game Quake.")
(comment bibliography-DocumentPartOf "'(#$bibliography-DocumentPartOf WORK BIBLIOGRAPHY)' means that the #$TextString BIBLIOGRAPHY is a bibliography within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.")
(comment proposalStatus "The predicate #$proposalStatus is used to indicate the status of a particular proposal.  (#$proposalStatus PROPOS STATUS) means that the #$Proposal PROPOS has STATUS as its #$ProposalTypeByStatus (e.g., #$Acknowledged, #$AwaitingConfirmation, #$Accepted).  Since the status of a proposal changes throughout the process of submission and consideration, assertions made with #$proposalStatus should be temporally qualified (e.g., using #$holdsIn).")
(comment beneficiary-Generic "(#$beneficiary-Generic EVT IND) allows one to say that IND has benefitted in some way from EVT.  Where IND is an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, be sure to use the more specific predicate, #$beneficiary.")
(comment CourseDuringAMeal "A specialization of #$ManipulatingFoodOrDrink.  Each instance of #$CourseDuringAMeal is an event in which one or more diners at a meal consume a single course.  Specializations of #$CourseDuringAMeal include #$AppetizerCourse, #$MainCourse, and #$DessertCourse.")
(comment holdsOwnershipDocument "(#$holdsOwnershipDocument DOCUMENT AGENT) means that the #$OwnershipDocument DOCUMENT records the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT's ownership in some object.")
(comment ProcessPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each element of #$ProcessPredicate is a predicate used in assertions that describe processes.  For example, #$amountOfEnergyUsed, #$signalState, #$toPossessor, #$primaryActivityTypeOfLocation, #$exports, #$monetaryValue.")
(comment Multi-MovementComposition "The collection of all #$MusicalComposition-Classicals that consist of two or more movements. Individual movements are like compositions in their own right, often separated by pauses and in different keys, but they are not typically performed except as a part of the larger composition, and audiences are expected not to interrupt the performance by clapping in between movements.")
(comment DisarmingADevice "The collection of actions in which the #$DeviceTypeByState of a #$PhysicalDevice (such as a #$TrapDevice, #$Bomb, or #$AutomaticFirearm) is changed from armed (or cocked) to idle (or uncocked), without an intervening firing or triggering of the device.  If it is a firing or triggering that causes the state change, that is a discharging of the device, not a disarming of it.
<p>
This collection is general enough to include, e.g., disarming an alarm system.  For the important special case in which the #$deviceDisarmed is a #$Weapon, see #$DisarmingAWeapon.")
(comment BlockingAnInternationalWaterway "A collection of events in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible interferes with traffic on international waters. This may be accomplished with some physical barrier, or with the threat of violence to traffic travelling in that area. Generally, UN regulations prohibit this kind of action.")
(comment TeamAssignment "A specialization of #$Assignment-Specification (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TeamAssignment is an #$Assignment-Specification that bears the #$assignees relation to several instances of #$IntelligentAgent.  Moreover, the obligation associated with such an assignment requires that the action which satisfies the assignment has every one of the assignees as an actor.  Thus, if there are N agents who are assigned to #$TeamAssignment ASSIGN, one action can satisfy ASSIGN, but all N agents must be actors in ASSIGN. This collection should be contrasted with #$DistributedAssignment.")
(comment connects-Underspecified "(#$connects-Underspecified LEFT RIGHT) states that a connection

of an underspecified nature is made between LEFT and RIGHT.  This

connection might be geographical (e.g., if LEFT is a person and

RIGHT is a place, as in 'Bill went to town'), physical (e.g., LEFT

and RIGHT are people who meet, or marry), mental (e.g., LEFT is a

person and RIGHT is an abstract state, as in 'Bill is in trouble' or

'I wish Bob would go to hell') or partially tangible (e.g., LEFT is a

person, RIGHT is #$Influenza, as in 'Bill caught the flu'). Notions

such as #$Marriage-Agreement can be seen as an abstract

connection between two people; indeed, so can #$LegalAgreement,

thereby yielding common metaphors of the form 'AOL married Netscape'.

Conceptual connection is perhaps the most powerful (and general)

operation a symbol system can perform (think of #$conceptuallyRelated,

which is a clear case of conceptual connection).")
(comment WatchingSomething "A specialization of #$Observing, #$VisualPerception and #$Perceiving-Voluntary. Each instance of this collection is an event involving the deliberate direction of #$VisualPerception on the part of an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. See also the specialization, #$EyeContact.")
(comment CycComponentParameterValue "The collection of all #$SubLSExpressions that are passed to the #$SoftwareParameters of #$CycRelatedPrograms.")
(comment Dislike "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Dislike is some agent's feeling of disaffection or disaffinity for an agent, event, or thing.  Instances of #$Dislike vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, and/or the object of dislike.  Specializations of #$Dislike include #$Contempt, #$Hate, and #$Disgust.")
(comment ClassicalVocalComposition "The collection of all #$MusicalComposition-Classicals scored for voices, with or without accompaniment.")
(comment OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate "The collection of #$DifferenceWRTPredicates in which two things are compared along a dimension which has a partial ordering. Contrast (1) comparing two species with respect to possessing wings with (2) comparing two species with respect to the typical height of its members. Only the latter would be an #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate since heights can be ordered but having wings cannot.  #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicates that are defined compositionally have the respect of difference represented explicitly by one or more arguments. Often these arguments will have an instance of either #$PartialOrderAttributeType or #$BinaryAttributePredicate as an argument constraint. In the latter case, the instance of #$BinaryAttributePredicate serving as the argument constraint for the #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate should have an instance of #$PartialOrderAttributeType as its second argument constraint. If the predicate is defined noncompositionally, then the ordering along which things are compared is left implicit (often mentioned only in the constant name). A  positive example of a compositional #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate is #$typesGreaterInQuantity. It is used to represent that one collection has a greater degree of some instance of a #$LinearOrderAttributeType than another collection. A positive example of a noncompositional #$OrderedDifferenceWRTPredicate is #$greaterEffectForSitType-ThanSitType.")
(comment CommunicationBus "A specialization of #$ComputerMarketCategory. Any kind of physical shared medium of communication between devices.
<p>
#$CommunicationBus is a genls of #$ComputerBus, because #$ComputerBus is only for busses internal to and part of a #$Computer.")
(comment ActorTypeByMedium "#$ActorTypeByMedium is a collection of collections. Each element is a collection of #$ActorActresses grouped by the dramatic medium in which they work. Some examples are #$ActorInPlays and #$ActorInMovies. The motivation for creating this collection is to make use of a faceting of #$Actor to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed. Since instances of #$Actor can work in more than one medium, the elements of this collection need not be disjoint.")
(comment infoAdded "(#$infoAdded UPDATE INFO) means that the #$AspatialInformationStore INFO is added to an instance of #$InformationBearingObject (q.v.) in the #$InformationUpdating UPDATE.")
(comment Levitating "A #$TemporalStuffType.  Each instance of #$Levitating is a #$PhysicalEvent in which some #$PartiallyTangible object rises and/or hangs suspended in the air in apparent defiance of #$GravitationalForceVector.")
(comment IBTWithFullTextOfPITTypeFn "#$IBTWithFullTextOfPITTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$PropositionalInformationThing and returns the collection of InformationBearingThings containing the full written text of any PIT of that type.  For example, (#$IBTWithFullTextOfPITTypeFn #$Novel-CW) returns the collection of those IBTs which contain the full written text of any novel, and (#$IBTWithFullTextOfPITTypeFn #$Poem-CW) returns the collection of IBTs containing the written text of any poem.")
(comment personBasicDataSentence "A #$BasicDataPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a #$Person to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$personBasicDataSentence PERSON SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a basic fact about PERSON.")
(comment Peat "The collection of all pieces of peat, a kind of partially decomposed            vegetable matter formed           by the partial decomposition of aquatic and semiaquatic #$Plants.           #$Peat is found naturally occurring in various kinds of #$WetlandRegion in           temperate climates and consists mostly of #$Water.  Peat has many uses, e.g.           as mulch, as a soil conditioner, as an insulating material and, when dried            (see #$Peat-Dried), as fuel.")
(comment ClosingAContainerArtifact "The collection of events in which a #$ContainerArtifact is closed (not necessarily by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, in the #$BaseKB).  NOTE that the #$ContainerArtifact is the #$objectOfStateChange, and that each such object has at least one portal, presumably with a portal covering.  So #$ClosingAContainerArtifact means putting the (or any appropriate) portal covering back in place on the portal (one of the portals) of a container product.")
(comment ComputerHardwareMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$ComputerHardwareMarketCategory is a computer hardware item, either a computer, computer component, or peripheral device for computers.")
(comment Tango-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
tango style.                            ")
(comment maximumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint "Let SLOT denote an #$QuantitySlot, SLOT-ARG1 denote the #$arg1Isa constraint on SLOT, SLOT-ARG2 denote the

    #$arg2Isa constraint on SLOT, and VALUE denote the instance of SLOT-ARG2 such that

    (SLOT PATH VALUE).  Then (#$maximumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint PATH

    O-TYPE SLOT MAX) means that PATH is #$pathTrafficableForTransportVia #$transporters

    of type O-TYPE only if (#$greaterThanOrEqualTo MAX VALUE).  See also the related predicates

    #$minimumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint,

    #$maximumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint, and

    #$minimumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint.")
(comment slotValueSum "(#$slotValueSum SLOT THING SETORCOL) says that the value of SLOT for
THING can be computed by summing the values of SLOT over the elements
of SETORCOL.  For instance, world population is equivalent to the sum
of population over every country: (#$slotValueSum #$numberOfInhabitants
#$PlanetEarth #$Country).  See also #$PlusAll: the value of
SLOT for THING is the value of (#$PlusAll SETORCOL (#$FunctionToArg 2
SLOT)).")
(comment Jazz-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
jazz style.                            ")
(comment (IsotopeFn Hydrogen 2) "A specialization of #$NuclearRelatedMaterial, known as \"deuterium\" or \"H-2\".")
(comment USStateSupremeCourt "A specialization of #$AppealsCourt.  Each instance of #$USStateSupremeCourt is the highest appeals court in the judiciary system of a given #$State-UnitedStates.  Note that this is <i>not</i> the highest appeals court whatsoever located in that state, as each state has an even higher #$USCircuitCourtOfAppeals.")
(comment subDivisionLevelOf "'(#$subDivisionLevelOf STRUCTURE DIVISION N)' means that DIVISION is one of the #$subStructures of N divisions of the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE.  For example, if a work is divided into chapters and there are no higher level divisions within which the chapters are contained, then (#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE CHAPTER 0) where CWSTRUCTURE is a #$TextualPCWStructure.  As another example, consider a titled section within a chapter within the first part of a #$TextualPCWStructure (i.e., Section 1 of Chapter 1 of Part I).  A number of different assertions could be made regarding the different parts of the overall #$GraphicalStructure of the text (e.g., (#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE CHAPTER 1)...(#$subDivisionLevelOf CWSTRUCTURE SECTION 2)...(#$subDivisionLevelOf PART CHAPTER 0)).")
(comment subscribesToPeriodical "An #$Agent-PartiallyTangible subscribes to a particular periodical. Thus, the agent will get each new issue of the product when it comes out.  For example, (#$subscribesToPeriodical #$Cycorp WeeklyWorldNews)")
(comment grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention "(grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention RM EM ROLE)  means that EM, an instance of #$EntityMentionHypothesis, fills the grammatical role ROLE wrt. the #$RelationMentionHypothesis RM.  So, for example, given a sentence like \"the cat is on the mat\", we can use (#$grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention RM1 EM1 #$SubjectRoleMarker) to indicate that the #$EntityMentionHypothesis corresponding to this occurnace of \"the cat\"(EM1) fills the subject role in the #$RelationMentionHypothesis (RM1) associated with this sentence.")
(comment Q-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a short quote within a text.  The quote will not be indented in the #$GraphicalStructure generated by the #$HTMLSource.  For quotes that are to be indented in the document generated, see #$Blockquote-HTMLTag.")
(comment Bartering "The collection of transactions between two #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles in which one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible gives items or services to another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, and the other #$Agent-PartiallyTangible gives items or services in return, and neither of the items or services is money, credit, or payment of money.")
(comment AudioRecordingFn-Downloadable "#$AudioRecordingFn-Downloadable takes as argument any instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible or #$SpecifiedMusicCompositionType and returns the collection of all #$ComputerSoundFiles encoding recordings of that agent and linked to the #$Internet so that they can be downloaded (see #$DownloadingAFile).  For example, (#$AudioRecordingFn-Downloadable #$RollingStones) returns the collection of all downloadable recordings of the Rolling Stones.")
(comment UpperEyelid "The collection of all upper #$Eyelids.  An #$UpperEyelid is a flap of #$Skin above and in front of the eyeball which half covers the #$Eye when the #$Eyelids are closed.  The #$Eyelids on one side of the face are closed when #$WinkingAnEye.  Those on both sides are closed when #$Blinking or when #$Sleeping")
(comment ReachingIntoSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$ExtendingToAnObject. In each #$ReachingIntoSomething, something extends into or up to something else.")
(comment TVConcert "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that show concerts.")
(comment annualDeathsInDueTo "(#$annualDeathsInDueTo PLACE EVENT_TYPE NUM) means that the number of people who die due to events of type EVENT_TYPE in (the territory of) PLACE is NUM.  EVENT_TYPE could be a type of disease, accident, crime, natural disaster, or #$War.")
(comment dislikesEventsOfType "(#$dislikesEventsOfType AGENT TYPE) means that AGENT has

negative feelings associated with events of type TYPE, such that if

EVT is and event of type TYPE, (#$feelsTowardsEvent AGENT EVT

#$Abhorrence Positive).  We also take it that for any role

ROLE such that (#$dislikesRoleInEventType AGENT ROLE ACTIVITYTYPE),

(#$dislikesEventsOfType AGENT ACTIVITYTYPE).")
(comment IrishStepDancing-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
Irish step dancing style.                            ")
(comment FloaterHoliday-TimeAllocation-4 "A sub-collection of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation.  Instances of #$FloaterHoliday-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization due to that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible taking advantage of an #$Organization's policy of allowing its workers to take individual days off.")
(comment GuidedMissileFrigate "The collection of #$ModernFrigates intended to be used for transporting and launching #$GuidedMissiles.")
(comment FinancingByBorrowing "The collection of #$BorrowingSomething events in which money is borrowed.  Examples include borrowing money from a bank under an authorized #$LoanAgreement (a #$Loan-WrittenLegalAgreement) and borrowing money from a friend under a #$Loan-ByInformalOralAgreement.  Specializations of #$FinancingByBorrowing include #$BridgeFinancing and #$EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement.")
(comment totalValueOfAssets "(#$totalValueOfAssets AGENT VALUE) relates the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT to the sum of the value of all assets (cash, physical plant and possessions, receivables, inventory, prepaid rent or mortgage, etc.) held by that agent.  Note that assets change over time, so assertions using #$totalValueOfAssets should be temporally constrained.  For example, (#$holdsIn (#$YearFn 1998) (#$totalValueOfAssets RichieRich (#$USDollarFn 1000000))).")
(comment Artifact-Generic "A collection of things created by #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.  These creations may be either tangible (like a hammer, a bowl, or a bridge) or intangible (like a set of laws, a #$KnowledgeBase, or Beethoven's Ninth Symphony).  Thus, the collection of #$Artifact-Generics is partitioned into #$Artifact and #$Artifact-Intangible (q.v.).")
(comment maximumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint "Let SLOT denote an #$QuantitySlot, SLOT-ARG1 denote the #$arg1Isa constraint on SLOT, SLOT-ARG2 denote the #$arg2Isa constraint on SLOT, and VALUE denote the instance of SLOT-ARG2 such that          (SLOT O-TYPE VALUE).  Then (#$maximumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint          PATH O-TYPE SLOT MAX) means that PATH is #$pathTrafficableForTransportVia          #$transporters of type O-TYPE only if (#$greaterThanOrEqualTo MAX VALUE).  See also the related          predicates #$minimumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint,          #$maximumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint, and          #$minimumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint.")
(comment FinancialObligation "The collection of all #$Obligations of a financial nature--obligations to make a #$MoneyTransfer.  Such #$Obligations can arise from #$Transactions, such as #$BorrowingSomethings, and can thus be related to #$LoanAgreements, or can arise by other means, such as by the imposition of some legislative body in the case of #$Tax-COCs.  In the case of a #$LoanAgreement, the #$borrower is both an #$agreeingAgents and an #$obligatedAgents, but in the case of a #$Tax-COC, the #$obligatedAgents is not an #$agreeingAgents.")
(comment TwoLanesOrWiderRoadway "The colection of #$Roadways that have two or more lanes or tracks. This criterion

belongs to the US Army's nomenclature for the representation of roads on

medium scale maps. See also #$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes.")
(comment ComedyTVShow "Instances of #$ComedyTVShow are #$TVShow-IBTs intended to be funny, e.g. 'Saturday            Night Live' or 'Friends'.")
(comment Training "A specialization of #$Learning and #$ServiceEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible receives instruction in certain skills (usually, but not always, from another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible). See also #$Education, #$Teaching, #$TrainingInFn, #$TrainingForFn.")
(comment typeSoleFunction-AgnosticIntentional "A type-level version of
#$soleFunction. (#$typeSoleFunction-AgnosticIntentional
AGTTYPE SITTYPE ROLE) means that in ordinary or normal circumstances,
instances of AGTTYPE have playing ROLE in situations of type SITTYPE
as their only function in some immediate functional
context. Like #$primaryFunction, the relation is
agnostic as to whether the functionality derives from the intent of
some intentional designer: i.e., the relation is not a spec-pred of
#$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable.  This is not to say that usage of
#$typeSoleFunction-AgnosticIntentional implies that no design
exists: the relation is simply agnostic as to whether a design exists
or not.  For this reason #$typePrimaryFunction is deemed to be a
specialization.  In cases where SITTYPE is itself a #$FunctionalSystem
(say, a kind of #$Cell or a kind of #$Organization in the
#$FunctionalRoleAnalysisMt), SITTYPE itself specifies the functional
context: otherwise, this context is taken to be specified by the
#$Microtheory in which the assertion is made.")
(comment conditionallyIndependent "A predicate used for probability statements. (#$conditionallyIndependent PROPOSITION1 PROPOSITION2) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory, PROPOSITION1 and PROPOSITION2 are conditionally independent of each other, that is, truth or falsehood of one does not increase or decrease the #$derivedProbability that the other is true.  They are, in a sense, irrelevant to each other.  In most microtheories, generally, the #$conditionallyIndependent statement means that when all we know in the #$Microtheory are its accessible #$domainAssumptions, then the truths of the two formulae are probabilistically independent.  See also #$conditionalProbability and #$conditionallyIndependentSentences.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment Halo-CircleOfLight "The collection of all halos of light.  A halo is a circle of light around, e.g., a #$AstronomicalBody.  This is a different concept than symbolic halo, which the constant #$Halo-Symbolic refers to.")
(comment telegramServiceUsed "(#$telegramServiceUsed SENDING SERVICE) means that SERVICE, an instance of #$DeliveryServiceEvent was used to send the telegram sent in SENDING, an instance of #$SendingATelegram.")
(comment interviewer "(#$interviewer INTERVIEW AGT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT is an interviewer in the #$Interviewing event INTERVIEW.")
(comment Respect "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Respect is some agent's feeling of just regard, consideration, or appreciation for the worth of someone or something.  Instances of #$Respect vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object of the feeling.  Specializations of #$Respect include #$Awe, #$Reverence, and #$Admiration.")
(comment CharacterToken-Sounded "The collection of all sounded tokens of individual
  abstract characters.  More precisely, #$CharacterToken-Sounded
  is a specialization of #$CharacterToken each of 
  whose instances is a sound event that represents or 
  realizes a particular instance of #$Character-Abstract in 
  some language or writing system.  Instances can be directly 
  generated by a human voice, a parrot, a loudspeaker 
  (reproducing a ''live'' or recorded signal), or other 
  device, and include certain instances of #$SpokenUtterance-IBT 
  as well as some electronically-generated sounds.
  Sounded characters are identified (both in theory and in
  practice) as tokens of particular abstract characters
  largely by their psychoacoustic contours, though context 
  and creator's intention also figure in.")
(comment businessPartners "The predicate #$businessPartners indicates that two agents have jointly undertaken some business project; they are combining resources in some way to further their interests.  (#$businessPartners AGENT1 AGENT2) means AGENT1 is in partnership with AGENT2 to engage in business activities.  The partners are instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and may belong to either #$Person or #$Organization.  The partnership may be formally recognized (e.g., a #$Partnership or some other form of business) or informal.")
(comment ProbabilityInterval "A specialization of #$ContinuousIntervalOnNumberLine (q.v.).  This is the collection of all continuous numeric intervals (both real numbers and proper intervals on the real line) between 0 and 1 inclusive.  Each instance of #$ProbabilityInterval can be used as an argument to #$ProbabilityFn (q.v.) to represent the #$ProbabilityInterval (q.v.) that a sentence is true.")
(comment numberOfDiscountPointsOnLoan "(#$numberOfDiscountPointsOnLoan LOAN N) identifies N as the number of \"points\" on the instance of #$LoanAgreement LOAN that are paid to reduce the interest rate of the loan (c.f., #$interestRate).  One point translates to 1 percent of the loan amount (c.f., #$initialLoanAmount).  To represent the points on a loan as a monetary amount, user #$discountPointsValueOnLoan.")
(comment Prophet "The collection of leaders / teachers who predict the future 

(e.g., make a #$MakingAPrediction) regarding the actions of God/the gods.")
(comment SoftwareTestOrType "Each instance of #$SoftwareTestOrType is either a collection
whose instances are individual software test definitions or an individual test. The meaning of this collection is equivalent to (#$CollectionUnionFn (#$TheSet #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified #$KBContentTestSpecificationType)). ")
(comment CaudalDirection "The general direction away from the head (towards the tail), in or near an object that is #$AnimalShapedThing.  In the case of a #$Person this is the #$VectorInterval comprising the cone-shaped set of vectors pointing (from some reference point) within approximately forty-five degrees of straight down when in an #$UprightPosture.")
(comment SoundInformationBearingThing "A specialization of both #$AudibleSound and #$InformationBearingWavePropagation. Each instance of #$SoundInformationBearingThing is an sound which is audible by, and thereby capable of providing information to, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  (This information need not necessarily be in propositional form.)  This collection does not include #$InformationBearingWavePropagations that require the use of some sort of electronic device to be rendered in the form of audible sound; thus #$RadioWave  is not a specialization. Genuine specializations include #$Music and #$AnimalUtterance-IBT. Note that, despite the use of the word `Thing' in the  name of this constant, it refers to the sound alone, not to the thing that  makes the sound (e.g. if one's CD player is pumping out music, the #$SoundInformationBearingThing is the #$Music, not the player). Thus, no one  thing can be an instance of both #$SoundInformationBearingThing and #$VisualInformationBearingThing (e.g.).")
(comment registryCapabilityCode "A binary predicate which associates a Microsoft Windows registry key (#$RegistryKey) pathname substring with the functionality which that string refers to (when placed in the appropriate place in the key's #$Pathname). (#$registryCapabilityCode STRING CAPABILITY) means that the #$SubLString STRING refers to the #$ComputerTypeByPassiveCapability  CAPABILITY. Note that setting of the registry key denoted by the pathname containing STRING may in fact switch off the functionality of CAPABILITY. See also #$registrySecurityZoneCode.")
(comment Candida "A fungal organism that can cause #$Candidiasis.")
(comment LosingUserRights "A specialization of #$ChangeInUserRights.  In each instance of #$LosingUserRights, an agent loses a previously held right (i.e., an instance of #$SituationTypeByUserRights) to use some item.  The item in question is identified as the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer (q.v.) in the instance of #$LosingUserRights, and the agent is the #$fromPossessor (q.v.) in the instance of #$LosingUserRights.  The agent may or may not be acting deliberately (see the predicate #$deliberateActors) in the event; e.g., selling one's car is done on purpose, but having one's car repossessed usually isn't.  However, both of those events would be instances of the collection #$LosingUserRights.")
(comment PicturesOfTypeFn-Organization "#$PicturesOfTypeFn-Organization takes specs of #$Organization and returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting instances of that spec of #$Organization. For example, (#$PicturesOfTypeFn-Organization #$City) denotes the collection of all pictures of cities. For purposes of the #$WebSearchEnhancementProject, the specs of #$Organization that this #$SubTopicFunction applies to will be limited to those that might be of interest to users of the E-Cyc application.")
(comment SituationTypeSlot "Every instance of this collection is a #$BinaryPredicate taking a kind of #$Situation as the second argument.  Many of these predicates can be used to represent certain intentional concepts, such as the goals or beliefs of an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible #$Plans to talk about states of affairs that various events or plans are supposed to facilitate or prevent, or that must be facilitated or prevented in order for the plan to count as successful.")
(comment useOfTypeInTypeForRole "<code>(#$useOfTypeInTypeForRole USE-TYPE OBJ-TYPE ACT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means the specialization of #$PurposefulAction <code>USE-TYPE</code> is the type of action in which some instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible uses some instance of the specialization of #$SomethingExisting <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> in an instance <code>ACT-TYPE</code> of #$PurposefulAction in the instance ROLE of #$Role.  Cf. this predicate's corresponding function, #$UsingAForFn.")
(comment dependsOn-Pairwise "This predicate expresses a dependency between two unit-slot pairs.

(#$dependsOn-Pairwise THING1 SLOT1 THING2 SLOT2 DIR) means that the

value of the #$QuantitySlot SLOT1 for THING1 is dependent on the value

of SLOT2 for THING2, in direction DIR.  For instance, to say that

Saudi Arabia's gross domestic product is positively dependent on the

price of oil: (#$dependsOn-Pairwise #$SaudiArabia

#$grossDomesticProductOf #$PetroleumProduct #$basicPriceForType

#$Positive).  See also #$positivelyDependsOn and #$negativelyDependsOn

for collection-level generalizations of this predicate.")
(comment connected-SheetTransectsAlong "(#$connected-SheetTransectsAlong SHEET CYL) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$connectedAlongEdge to the #$InteriorSurface-Tangible of #$Tube object CYL along its length, dividing the (otherwise single) cavity inside TUBE into linearly aligned cavities.")
(comment plausibleSentence "(#$plausibleSentence SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information content of the sentence is (subjectively) \"likely,\" given the system's current knowledge.  This is not to say that the content of SENTENCE is *correct* - for example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$Married) is plausible, but incorrect.  This distinction depends on the context within which the judgement is being made, and is necessarily subjective.  See also #$implausibleSentence.")
(comment referenceInWorkTo "(#$referenceInWorkTo WORK TEXT REFERENT) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK contains (see #$containsStructure-CW) #$TextString TEXT, which TEXT is a reference that points to REFERENT, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent or an instance of #$StructurallySpecificWork external to WORK.  Not any mention of a person or work is a reference.  The sentence 'Bill Clinton served two terms as the American president.' does not contain a reference in the sense of #$referenceInWorkTo.  #$referenceInWorkTo indicates that a #$TextString formally and purposefully points to some other work or person for the purpose of attribution, support, or location.  For #$TextStrings that refer to other #$TextStrings that are contained within the same #$StructurallySpecificWork, see #$crossReferenceInWorkTo.")
(comment HasDisjunctiveBranching "This is the collection of #$ScriptedEventTypes that contain

(at least) three scenes BRANCHSCENE, SCENE1, SCENE2 ... where

(#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE1 BRANCHSCENE),

(#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType SCENE2 BRANCHSCENE) ..., where SCENE1, SCENE2 ...

are temporally incomparable, and where any instantiation of the

#$ScriptedEventType that instantiates BRANCHSCENE must instantiate exactly one of

SCENE1, SCENE2 ....")
(comment Advertisement-Commercial-IBT "IBTs issued by businesses to let potential customers know what products they want to sell, buy, rent, lease, or trade.  See also #$Advertisement-PCW.")
(comment ExcavationPit "An #$ExcavationPit is a part of the #$EarthsTopographicSurface where #$LandStuff, such as sand (#$SandMob) or soil (#$Soil-Generic), is removed by digging for industrial use elsewhere. #$ExcavationPits are similar to #$Quarrys, however the latter are places where #$StoneStuff is removed, often by the use of explosives, whereas #$ExcavationPits are excavated mostly by digging apparatus.")
(comment marketedAs "The predicate #$marketedAs relates a particular item to the market category in which it is being marketed.  (#$marketedAs ITEM MKTCAT) means a tangible ITEM is marketed in the #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory MKTCAT.  For example, a particular scissors may be marketed in the #$OfficeProductMarketCategory (e.g., in an office supply store), while another scissors of the same brand and model is sold in the #$SchoolSuppliesMarketCategory (e.g., at a school book store).")
(comment ClosingADoor "The collection of events in which a door is closed.  Note that the #$objectActedOn of such an event is #$ConstructionArtifact that is also a #$ContainerArtifact.  Such objects tend to have one or more #$Doorways with #$DoorwayCoverings.")
(comment Continuation "A specialization of #$Action.  Each instance of #$Continuation is an event in which an agent continues the performance some previously initiated action. In general, this means that instances of this collection will be non-initial #$subEvents of some non-punctual event (cf. #$DurativeEventType and PunctualEventType). This collection is intended to cover both i) cases in which an agent continues to perform some sort of iterative event (e.g. non-initial #$Breathing events; cf.#$IterativeEventType), as well as ii) cases in which an agent continues or resumes the performance of some (possibly discontinuous) event (cf. #$temporallyContinuousDuring).  Notable specializations include #$Resumption and #$Repetition.")
(comment explanatoryTypeFromContext "#$explanatoryTypeFromContext THING TYPE CONTEXT, is used as part of #$ScenarioGenerationProject to represent the fact that THING is hypothesized because another instance of the same TYPE as THING was hypothesized in CONTEXT.  #$explanatoryTypeFromContext is used within 'meta-expansion modules' (e.g., #$GainingControlScriptConnectorMeta-ExpansionModule) which make hypotheses based on other other hypotheses in order to form more unified hypotheses.")
(comment PublisherOfInformationTypeFn "#$PublisherOfInformationTypeFn takes as argument any type of information and returns the collection of agents who publish information of that type. For example, (#$PublisherOfInformationTypeFn #$Poem-CW) returns the collection of all publishers of poetry.")
(comment covers-Ruglike "An instance of #$CoveragePredicate.  (#$covers-Ruglike MAT OBJECT) means that MAT covers at least part of one surface of OBJECT.  MAT is #$SheetShapedObject, and MAT lies with its two longer dimensions parallel to OBJECT.  See also #$coversWithConformity.")
(comment visuallyDepicts-Type "(#$visuallyDepicts-Type IS TYPE) means that IS visually depicts an object of type TYPE.")
(comment agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole "(#$agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole BINARY-ROLE-PRED AGENT-TYPE SENTENCE) holds just in case SENTENCE is a sentence that describes some state of affairs in which an agent plays some particular role, BINARY-ROLE-PRED, and that agent's being an instance of AGENT-TYPE is sufficient for the truth of SENTENCE.  For instance, a particular movie theater may charge only five dollars if the ticket purchaser is a member of a particular film club.  In that case, a sufficient condition on the truth of the statement that the purchase price of a ticket is five dollars is that the purchaser is a member of that film club.  In CycL we might represent an example of this as 

<code>
 <pre>
(#$agentTypeSufficientForTruthWRTRole #$buyer (#$MemberFn AustinFilmClub)
   (#$relationAllInstance #$purchasePrice 
     (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn  #$EntertainmentPerformanceTicket
       #$publisherOfIBO #$AmcCourthousePlaza8-CinemaOrganization) 
     (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 5)))
</pre>
</code>

We read the above in English as \"the purchase price of tickets issued from Amc Courthouse Plaza8 Cinema is five dollars if the buyer is a member of the Austin film club\"

.")
(comment EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn "(#$EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn PROFESSION-TYPE) denotes the collection of equipment types that are salient to elements of PROFESSION-TYPE conducting their job.  For example, 'spy equipment' may be referred to as (#$EquipmentTypeForOccupationTypeFn #$Spy).  A related term is #$EquipmentTypeForEventTypeFn.  For example 'intelligence gathering equipment' can be denoted by (#$EquipmentTypeForEventTypeFn #$IntelligenceGathering).")
(comment Bar-UnitOfPressure "A unit of pressure, equivalent to 100,000 pascals (1 #$Pascal-UnitOfPressure = 1 #$Newton per square #$Meter) or 0.98697 atmospheres (#$Atmosphere-UnitOfPressure).")
(comment SemiSolidTangibleThing "An instance of #$TangibleStuffStateType (q.v.); the collection of tangible things that are tactually intermediate between solids and fluids.  When a semisolid object is subjected to a sufficient force, it deforms substantially and does not break or crack. It may return to its original shape, like a sponge, or retain the shape which resulted from the applied force, like soft clay.  As with #$SolidTangibleThings, semisolids have shapes independent of their containers (see #$ContainerIndependentShapedThing) and they cannot be poured.")
(comment increaseToAccount "A predicate used for indicating regular increases to an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's account. (#$increaseToAccount AGENT ACCOUNT FREQ AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is added to the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT's #$AccountType ACCOUNT at #$Frequency FREQ intervals. See #$incomeToAccount for cases where AMOUNT is an instance of #$MonetaryValue.")
(comment Quarry "A #$Quarry is an excavated part of the #$EarthsTopographicSurface where #$StoneStuff, such as #$Limestone or #$Granite, are removed by blasting or cutting for industrial use elsewhere.")
(comment GameOfChance-Event "The collection of #$GameEvents that involve either: 1. bets of #$MonetaryValue [#$TenderObject] or #$Property that are based on the outcome of the #$GameOfChance-Event, such as in #$Gambling, or 2. a spec of #$Drawing-RandomSelection, such as #$Lottery or #$Sweepstakes-Event. Each instance of #$GameOfChance-Event is a playing of a #$GameOfChance.")
(comment Restlessness "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Restlessness is some agent's feeling of unease or agitation, marked by a lack of repose.  Instances of #$Restlessness vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or the subject experiencing the feeling.")
(comment InterfaceModifierType "The collection of terms that are used for special purposes in query interfaces.  A common use of these terms is to act as a modifier of a query run in the query library.  For example, the term (#$Quote #$Percent) is used as a numeric modifier.  Certain predicates take that term as an argument position and it determines that the answer returned will be in the form of a percent.  Other examples are #$DeadliestFn, #$Longest-Between, etc.")
(comment jobClass "The predicate #$jobClass describes a type of job as #$BlueCollar, #$WhiteCollarWorker, #$Unionized, etc.  (#$jobClass JOBTYPE CLASS) means that CLASS describes a general property of JOBTYPE.  Note that this predicate applies to instances of #$PersonTypeByOccupation (kinds of occupations, as represented by the collections of persons in those occupations), not to a particular job held by some individual person.")
(comment EscapingFromAPlace "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$LeavingAPlace. In each #$EscapingFromAPlace, something flees; takes to one's heels; cuts and run.")
(comment importFromAmountDuring "(#$importFromAmountDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil imported (by REGION1 from REGION2), or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil imported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION1 from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment InsurancePolicyDescription "A type of #$TextualDocument-CW.")
(comment movieTypeGenres "(#$movieTypeGenres MOVIE-TYPE GENRE) states that the class of movies MOVIE-TYPE have a particular GENRE.  For example, (#$movieTypeGenres #$ComedyMovie #$PropositionalConceptualWork-ComedyGenre).")
(comment sphereOfResponsibilityOfAgentInSituation "This predicate takes a stab at defining a responsible agent's 'sphere of responsibility' (considered as a specialization of #$Situation) in a given #$Situation.  Roughly speaking,(#$sphereOfResponsibilityOfAgentInSituation AGENT SIT SIT-TYPE) means that throughout the course of SIT, AGENT is responsible for making sure that instances of SIT-TYPE happen the way they are supposed to happen.  One very specific facet of this meaning:  where it is known that (#$inheritRolePlayers SUPER-EVENT-TYPE INDEP-EVENT-TYPE DEP-EVENT-TYPE ROLE #$directingAgent) - that is, where it is known that for #$Situations of type SUPER-EVENT-TYPE, anyone who plays ROLE in a #$subSituations of type INDEP-EVENT-TYPE also plays the rule #$directingAgent in any #$subSituations of type DEP-EVENT-TYPE - and where it is known that AGENT plays ROLE in EVENT such that EVENT is a #$subSituations of SUPER-EVENT and SUPER-EVENT is an instance of SUPER-EVENT-TYPE, AGENT has DEP-EVENT-TYPE.  Or to put it a bit more loosely, anytime an #$IntelligentAgent inherits the role of #$directingAgent in a class of #$Situation as the result of a situational 'script', that agent has that class of #$Situation as his or her 'sphere of responsibility' in the #$Situation whose inherited scripting gives rise to the role inheritance.")
(comment InferiorDirection "The general direction away from the top and towards the bottom, in or near an object that is #$AnimalShapedThing and in an #$UprightPosture.  In the case of a #$Person or other #$HumanShaped object, this direction almost always corresponds to #$CaudalDirection.")
(comment GovernmentsAllFn "#$GovernmentsAllFn takes as argument any instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity ?ENTITY and returns the collection of RegionalGovernments which govern or have governed that entity (not including governments of other geopolitical entities with which ENTITY stands in a #$geopoliticalSubdivision relationship). In contrast to (#$GovernmentFn ?ENTITY), which denotes the individual government now in place, (#$GovernmentsAllFn ?ENTITY) denotes a collection which includes not only the current government of ?ENTITY but all other governments which have held that position. For example, as of 12/2/98, while (#$GovernmentFn #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica) denotes the Government Of National Unity, (#$GovernmentsAllFn #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica) returns a collection including not only the Government Of National Unity but also the Apartheid-organized government in place before the 1994 elections.")
(comment tradeBalanceDuring "(#$tradeBalanceDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the difference between the value of the instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING and the value of the instances of PRODUCT-TYPE imported by REGION during the temporal extent of THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  Thus if the value of REGION's exports of PRODUCT-TYPE is greater than the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE during the temporal extent of THING, REGION will have a positive trade balance.  If the value of its imports of PRODUCT-TYPE exceeds that of its exports, it will have a negative trade balance.  This latter case can be expressed using a #$UnitOfMoney function with a negative number as its argument.  A region's overall trade balance for all goods and services (over a given time period) can be expressed with this predicate using the constant #$Product as the second argument.")
(comment VarietyShow "Instances of #$VarietyShow are #$TVShow-IBTs having a variety of features, including           interviews, music and other forms of entertainment.")
(comment GuitarTablatureNotation "The class of #$TablatureNotation for guitars (see #$Guitar), using marks on lines where each line designate a string of a guitar.  The positions of the marks indicate the musical notes (e.g. A,B,C,D,E,F,G in various octaves); each mark corresponds to such a note that is to be played, and it visually corresponds approximately to a physical location on the guitar.")
(comment Schizosaccharomycetales-Order "A collection of ascomycetous fungi, see #$Ascomycota-Division. An instance of
#$BiologicalOrder.")
(comment evaluationInput "(#$evaluationInput EVAL OBJ) means that in the instance of #$Evaluating, EVAL, information about OBJ is evaluated.  The performer (#$performedBy) of the evaluation must be #$awareOf OBJ.  If the result EVAL is one or more assertions about OBJ (see #$objectOfEvaluation), use the more specific predicate, #$evaluee-Direct.  For example, in a reading of animal tracks at a water hole, the tracks are an #$evaluationInput, but not a #$objectOfEvaluation.")
(comment doesTo "This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the
agent (active participant) and the object (passive participant) of an
activity. Example: (#$doesTo #$Cleaning #$PeterSuen PetersDesk) is true iff Peter
cleans Peter's desk (or: is cleaning, depending on the way the assertion is
temporally qualified).")
(comment buyer "An #$AgentiveRole (q.v.) and specialization of #$exchangers  that relates a given #$MonetaryExchangeOfUserRights event to the paying #$Agent-PartiallyTangible(s)  in that event.  <code>(#$buyer EXCHANGE BUYER)</code> means that <code>BUYER</code> purchases goods or  services or access rights for sale in <code>EXCHANGE</code>.  <code>BUYER</code> might make the purchase  either directly or through an agent.  Also see and compare #$buyingPerformer and  #$buyingAgent.")
(comment similarInValueOnRelation "This predicate relates two things in terms of some BinaryPredicate that relates them to similar instances of a given collection of collections. (#$similarInValueOnRelation T1 T2 BINPRED) means that there are similar collections COL1 and COL2, such that (BINPRED T1 COL1) and (BINPRED T2 COL2).  The minimum notion of similarity is that COL1 and COL2 be instances of the same \"faceting\" sort of collection.  For instance, #$HighMountainousRegion and #$HillyRegion are both instances of the collection #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  Furthermore, if the collection type to which they belong is ordered (see #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder), then COL1 and COL2 should be \"close\" together in the ordering.  For instance #$HillyRegion is closer to #$HighMountainousRegion than #$FlatRegion in the ordering on #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  So, it is likely that a region, REG1, such that (#$terrainType REG1 #$HighMountainousRegion) stands in #$similarInValueOnRelation via #$terrainType to a region, REG2, such that (#$terrainType REG2 #$HillyRegion).  But not likely that it stands in such a relation to an instance of #$FlatRegion.  See also #$resemblesInValue.")
(comment ModerateChange "The #$RateOfChange that indicates a change that takes a moderate amount of time.")
(comment LectureSeries-CW "The collection of series of #$Lecture-CW that,

  when taken together, constitute a 

#$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Keep in mind that

 not all (#$GroupFn #$Lecture-CW)'s can be

 considered #$ConceptualWorks, even when 

  their \"conjunction\" constitues an

 official \"course of study.\"  Often,

   #$GraduateSeminarSeriess are performances of

   #$LectureSeries-CW, but this is by no means

 always the case. Note, too, that

  #$LectureSeries-CW is not a spec of #$TextualPCW, as

  the performances of their instances (#$FormalLectureSeries-IBTs)

 often involve much more than a simple

  expression of propositions, e.g., 

  simple experiments.")
(comment LiquidFilm "A collection instances of #$Film-SheetOrCoating that are liquid.  Positive exemplars include a patchy film of oil on water, wet paint, and the surface of soap bubbles.  Note that that collection 'soap bubble' is not a kind of #$LiquidFilm but rather a structure whose parts include elements of #$LiquidFilm.  The complete film of a soap bubble is not an exception to the exception to the general rule that all instances of #$Film-SheetOrCoating are also instances of #$SurfaceRegion-Bounded.")
(comment ClassicalMusicalCompositionType "The collection of all formalized types of #$MusicalComposition-Classical. Elements include #$Symphony, #$ViolinConcerto, and #$CompositionMovement-SonataForm.")
(comment antiSymmetricInArgs "A #$MetaRelation that is used to indicate that a given relation is \"antisymmetric\" with respect to two given argument-places.   (#$antiSymmetricInArgs REL M N) means that REL is antisymmetric  in its Mth and Nth arguments: these arguments are freely  permutable _only_ if they are identical.  This entails that,  given any closed semantically well-formed formula built from  (the CycL term for) REL, inter-substituting the formula's Mth  and Nth arguments (while leaving the other arguments unchanged) will result in a change in the formula's semantic value (i.e.  its truth-value or denotation) _unless_ the Mth and Nth arguments are identical.  If REL is a binary predicate this is equivalent  to its being an #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate.  More generally: (i) If REL is a #$Predicate that holds of given  argument-sequence SEQ, then REL also holds of the sequence SEQ-PERMUTED  obtained by permuting the Mth and Nth items in SEQ (while leaving  the other items unchanged) only if these Mth and Nth items are identical (and thus SEQ and SEQ-PERMUTED are themselves identical  sequences).  (ii) If REL is a #$Function-Denotational whose value  for a given argument-sequence SEQ is VALUE, then REL also has  VALUE as its value for SEQ-PERMUTED (defined as above) only if  SEQ-PERMUTED is identical with SEQ.  For example, a (hypothetical)  ternary predicate called \"greaterThanOrEqualToOnScale\", which  took as arguments two physical objects (_not_ constrained to be distinct) and a scale for measuring some physical property, would  be antisymmetric in its first and second arguments; i.e.  (#$antiSymmetricInArgs greaterThanOrEqualToOnScale 1 2) would hold.  For a function example, a (hypothetical) ternary function called \"TransportToFromViaVehicleTypeFn\" that took as  arguments two locations (_not_ constrained to be distinct, in order to include round-trips) and a vehicle-type (and returned,  say, the collection of all trips from the first location to the  second location in vehicles of that type) would also be  antisymmetric in its first and second arguments.  Note that  (each of) the #$argIsa constraint(s) on REL's Mth argument-place  must not be disjoint with (any of) the #$argIsa constraint(s) on  REL's Nth argument-place (see #$disjointWith), and likewise  for the corresponding #$argGenl constraints (if any). For some discussion of why this is so, see the #$NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement.  See also #$asymmetricInArgs and #$commutativeInArgs.")
(comment TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat "These are tests which require a determination of whether or not some assertion is true on the basis of some particular background text. The predicates #$backgroundTextForTEP and #$queryTextForTEP should be used to specify the background text and queries text, respectively.")
(comment WarrantOfficer-Rank "Rank intermediate between #$SergeantMajorOfTheCorps-Rank and 

  #$ChiefWarrantOfficer-Rank in the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps. 

  (Not to be confused with the collection #$WarrantOfficerTypeByRank, which is an instance of #$MilitaryRankType, or with #$WarrantOfficer, which is the collection of military persons whose ranks are instances of #$WarrantOfficerTypeByRank.)")
(comment internationalMonetaryReservesDuring "(#$internationalMonetaryReservesDuring GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the monetary value of the foreign currency reserves of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (To the extent that there is fluctuation in the amount of GE's foreign currency reserves during the temporal extent of THING, NR should be taken to be an average.)  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment sellsTo "This predicate represents a way that one agent #$doesBusinessWith another, by selling goods or services to it.  (#$sellsTo AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 is the #$sellingPerformer (which could be either a #$sellingAgent or a #$seller) in #$Buying events in which AGENT2 is the #$buyer.  The use of #$sellsTo should indicate multiple #$Buying events -- i.e., repeat business within an ongoing commercial relationship.
Note: #$sellsTo refers to an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (person or organization) who is making the sales; that may be different from the actual provider of the goods or services sold.  For the latter, use #$suppliers.  A #$sellingAgent might represent one or more #$suppliers.")
(comment Mitre-Hat "The collection of all mitres--  tall, often ornate, pointed hats customarily worn by #$Bishop-Clericals, #$Archbishops, and the #$Pope.")
(comment Ia64ProcessorArchitecture "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByArchitecture. #$Ia64ProcessorArchitecture is a type of CISC computer chip, produced by #$IntelCorporation, postdating the popular #$X86ProcessorArchitecture (which included the Pentium), and released around 2001. It also goes by the name of \"Itanium\".")
(comment objectTendered "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$MoneyTransfer to instances of #$TenderObject, and indicates the financial instrument which is used in a particular transfer of money.  (#$objectTendered TRANS OBJECT) means that the #$TenderObject OBJECT is used to transfer funds in the #$MoneyTransfer event TRANS.  Note that OBJECT is distinct from the quantity of #$MonetaryValue (q.v.) transferred in TRANS (see the related predicate #$moneyTransferred), although of course OBJECT has some monetary value --- is `worth' a certain amount, generally calculated from the numbers printed or stamped or engraved on the #$TenderObject OBJECT --- which in turn is an instance of #$MonetaryValue.")
(comment AttributiveReference "A collection of #$TextStrings.  This instance of #$TextStringTypeByReferenceType consists of the collection of #$TextStrings that are a reference in a certain work which attribute some instance of #$AspatialInformationStore to a particular #$IntelligentAgent or other instance of #$ConceptualWork.  For example, works that contain images often include #$TextStrings that attribute those images to an #$IntelligentAgent or other #$ConceptualWork.  The #$TextString that so attributes the visual sub-structure to something external to the work would be an instance of #$AttributiveReference.  #$TextStrings that immediately follow a #$quotationOfExternalAgent often have an #$AttributiveReference.")
(comment AppearancesByFn "#$AppearancesByFn takes as argument any instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and returns the collection of all organized events at which that agent makes a public appearance.  For example, (#$AppearancesByFn #$KeithRichards) returns the collection of all organized events featuring a public appearance by Keith Richards of the #$RollingStones.")
(comment ConceptFilterParameterType-Trigger "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Each instance of this collection is a parameter that tells an application that uses #$ConceptFilters what will trigger the display of terms from the concept filter.  There are currently four instance of this collection: 1. #$TriggerFromConcept, 2. #$TriggerFromConceptOrSpec, 3. #$TriggerFromConceptOrInstance, 4. #$TriggerFromConceptSpecOrInstance.")
(comment sensoryResponse "(#$sensoryResponse EVT ROLE QUANT) means that a #$PerceptualAgent who participates in the #$PhysicalEvent EVT in the manner ROLE has a quantity of the #$SensoryQuantity QUANT. For example, if TOUCH is a touching-something-very-cold action, then (#$sensoryResponse TOUCH #$doneBy (#$PositiveAmountFn #$LevelOfDiscomfort)) is true --- i.e., whoever does that touching action is likely to feel some discomfort.")
(comment Signal "A specialization of #$InformationBearingThing (IBT).  Each instance of #$Signal is an IBT which may be interpreted (whether by a conscious user of learned signalling rules, by a computer program, or even by a cell in terms of its subsequent behaviour) as conveying some specific information. Examples include car-horn honkings, internet packets, and proteins which travel into cells across the plasma membrane. An important specialization of this collection is #$InformationBearingWavePropagation. Note that this collection is intended to embrace only signals themselves, not events of signalling. On the importance of keeping these two separate, see the comment on #$InformationBearingThing. The distinction between this collection and #$SymbolicThing lies in the fact that #$Signals are one-time-only transfers of specific information, whereas a #$SymbolicThing is open to its characteristic interpretation any time it is encountered. See also #$signifiesTo, #$signifies.")
(comment AcademicComposition "The collection of all book reports, essays, term papers, etc. written and/or intended to be submitted by #$Students in fulfillment of #$DoingAHomeworkAssignments.")
(comment ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface "The collection of well-defined surfaces that surround certain spatial objects and which make up the boundary between being outside and inside of the object.  Most discrete objects such as #$Animal or #$PhysicalDevice have a #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface as a #$surfaceParts.  If an object is hollow, such as a #$CavityOrContainer then it has an inside surface but it may or may not have a #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface.  An example of a #$CavityOrContainer which does have a #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface is a #$House-Modern.  Some objects, such as a #$Cave or a #$Ditch are #$CavityOrContainers that do not have a #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface.  If one is in a cave digging into the inside surface of a cave wall, one never knows precisely when one has passed through to the other ``external'' side of the cave's wall.  This is not to say that such objects do not have some definable external surface.  Rather, whatever such surface they may be asserted as having, it is not something which the contextually relevant average person would agree on, know about, or find obviously true.  A #$Hill also does not have a #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface since the external surface of a hill is not a #$SurfaceRegion-Unbounded.  ")
(comment significantColorOfObject "The formula (#$significantColorOfObject OBJCOL) means that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ has a significant amount of the #$Color COL.  The color may be signinficant because it covers over some minimum percent of the surface area of OBJ (as yet undecided) or because it is symbolically important.  For example, the flag of #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica is Green, Red, Blue, Black, White, and Yellow.  Each of these colors is a #$significantColorOfObject of such a flag, even though the yellow covers less than 5% of the flag's surface.  If one refers to an object as being a set of colors, each color is related to the object via#$significantColorOfObject.  The more specialized predicate, #$mainColorOfObject should be used if the object could be referred to as being that color without mentioning any other color.  If we had a shirt that was green with a small, white insignia on the pocket, we WOULD, in this case, say that the #$mainColorOfObject, this shirt, is green.  The white would not be a #$significantColorOfObject.  See also #$objectHasColor and #$uniformColorOfObject.")
(comment PreventingFn "(#$PreventingFn EVENT-TYPE) maps from the collection EVENT-TYPE (a subclass of #$Event) to a collection of preventings of events of type EVENT-TYPE.  Thus the result of (#$PreventingFn #$CriminalAct) would be the collection of crime prevention events (a subclass of #$PreventingFromHappening).  #$PreventingFn operates on the #$Collection level, and is used to talk about kinds of preventings that can occur.")
(comment licenseHolder "A predicate relating an instance of #$License-IBO to an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. (#$licenseHolder LICENSE AGENT) means that LICENSE has been issued to AGENT by the appropriate authority.")
(comment subLists "(#$subLists LIST SUB) means that SUB is a sublist of LIST.  Formally, SUB is a sublist of LIST if and only if for some #$Lists X and Y, (#$JoinListsFn X SUB Y) = LIST.  Note that by this definition (and that of #$JoinListsFn) every list is a sublist of itself and #$TheEmptyList is a sublist of every #$List.  As examples, the following are all sublists of (#$TheList A B C D A B): #$TheEmptyList, (#$TheList A), (#$TheList A B), (#$TheList A B C), (#$TheList B C), (#$TheList B C D A), and LIST itself. Note also that the sublist (#$TheList A B) of LIST above \"occurs\" in LIST as a segment more than once: as an initial segment and also as a final segment.  See #$PositionsOfSublistInListFn.")
(comment ChemicalPlant-Organization "A instance of #$BusinessTypeByActivityType.  Each instance of
#$ChemicalPlant-Organization is a #$Business employed in trade or manufacturing
chemical substances.")
(comment NthColumnOfTableFn "For a particular instance of #$Table-AIS, #$NthColumnOfTableFn (#$NthColumnOfTableFn TABLE N) returns the #$GraphicalStructure that is the Nth column of TABLE.")
(comment ReginaldCareyHarrison-ActorActress "An instance of #$Actor. English actor on stage and in films (1908-1990).")
(comment ZairePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$DemocraticRepublicOfTheCongo, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Backreference-NLAttrType "This #$QuantityType includes all NL attributes which are 'backreferential' in nature, e.g., used to refer to objects which have appeared previously in the discourse. Compare these to #$Demonstrative-NLAttrType, which is used primarily when referring to particular tangible and/or temporal objects.")
(comment Pity "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Pity is some agent's feeling of sorrow for an agent (usually some other agent, but sometimes the pitying agent herself) on account of the undesirable state of affairs that agent is in.  Instances of #$Pity vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object pitied.")
(comment combatForceValueOfUnitTypeWithEchelonSize "#$combatForceValueOfUnitTypeWithEchelonSize helps specify quantitatively a default estimate of the cabilities of units of a particular #$MilitaryUnitSpecialtyType and #$MilitaryEchelon.")
(comment alphabeticalIndexTo "'(#$alphabeticalIndexTo CWSTRUC BODY INDEX)' means that, within the #$CWStructure CWSTRUC, the #$TextString INDEX is an alphabetical index to the #$GraphicalStructure BODY.  The instance of #$GraphicalStructure which is indexed by the #$TextString that is the third argument of #$alphabeticalIndexTo may be the entire #$TextualPCWStructure of which the index is a part (i.e., some indices reference only the body of a work, while others reference the body, the preface, appendices, and other parts of the work).  Consequently, the value for the first and second arguments of #$alphabeticalIndexTo may be identical.")
(comment instantiationOfAIT "(#$instantiationOfAIT IBT AIT) means that the

#$InformationBearingThing IBT is an instantiation, i.e. a concrete

realization, of the #$AspatialInformationStore AIT. Notable specializations include #$instantiationOfAIS and #$instantiationOfGIS. See also #$instantiationOfWork.")
(comment disputedAgreement "(#$disputedAgreement DISPUTE AGREEMENT) identifies the instance of #$Agreement AGREEMENT as the agreement, the content of which is now in dispute, in DISPUTE, an instance of #$DisputeOverAgreementCW.  Note that this predicate is an instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot.  To say that multiple parts of AGREEMENT are in dispute, one must talk about multiple dispute events.")
(comment HomosexualBehavior-Female "The collection of all instances of #$HomosexualBehavior involving two or more females.  Note that this refers only to the sexual behavior itself, not to any other behaviors that may happen to be exhibited by #$HomosexualHumans.")
(comment disprovedCandidateExtractedContents-CycL "<code>(#$disprovedCandidateExtractedContents-CycL PEG CYCL)</code> means that the CycL semantics <code>CYCL</code> assigned to the instance PEG of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg-CompleteUtterance has been rejected (proved false) by the Cyc Inference Engine.")
(comment EmbassyBuildingOfCountryFn "(#$EmbassyBuildingOfCountryFn COUNTRY) returns the collection of physical #$EmbassyBuildings which house the #$Embassy-TheMissions of COUNTRY.")
(comment keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType "An instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate used to constrain the pragmatic relevance of the values of certain properties for things of a given type. Specifically, (keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType BINPRED TYPE SIZE) indicates that we should regard an instance of TYPE as having a known value for the property expressed by the #$QuantitySlot BINPRED only when the instance of #$ScalarInterval that is its value has an #$intervalSize no greater than SIZE.
<p>
For example, we would reasonably claim to <i>know</i> the age of a particular dog Fido if we can prove that (#$age Fido (#$YearsDuration 6)), but not if we could prove merely that (#$age Fido (YearsDuration 1 19)) -- which is most likely true, of course, since it is so of most dogs. But this is fact about (knowledge about) dogs or animals in general. So: (#$keRelevantPrecisionValueForSlotOnType #$age #$Animal (#$YearsDuration 1)) would express this constraint.")
(comment PersonalTax "An instance of #$MicrotheoryType and a subset of #$Tax-COC. Each instance of #$PersonalTax places an obligation upon certain persons to pay a tax to some agent (usually, the agent in question will be the government of some instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity). An instance of #$PersonalTax places no tax obligation on any kind of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (for instance, corporations) other than persons.  A positive example would be a state's tax on personal income, while a negative example would be a state's corporate income tax.")
(comment hasPhysicalFeature "This predicate relates things to their physical features. (#$hasPhysicalFeature OBJ FEAT) means that OBJ has the attribute FEAT which is an instance of #$PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalFeature.")
(comment DeviceStartingARun "A collection of events.  An instance of #$DeviceStartingARun is an event in which some device begins its normal cycle of processes, e.g., an instance of #$AirplaneTakeOff.  This is often --- but not always --- the same thing as a device going from the #$Device-Off state to the #$Device-On state --- e.g., the airplane was `on' for many minutes before it took off.   One could also define the collection dead-start-to-finish-airplane-flight, which would not start with an #$AirplaneTakeOff but rather with a true turning-on of power to the airplane, or even with the pre-ignition check of the aircraft and boarding of the crew.")
(comment OperaCompany "The collection of organizations whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to produce and present theatrical entertainment in the form of instances of #$OperaPerformance. Opera singers are essential employee-members of instances of #$OperaCompany.")
(comment intendedAudience "A binary predicate relating instances of #$InformationBearingThing to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. (#$intendedAudience IBT AGT) means that the #$InformationBearingThing IBT has the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT as its intended audience--viewer, reader, listener, etc.  AGT (possibly along with other agents) is supposed to access the information represented in IBT.  For example, the #$intendedAudience of a personal letter is usually its addressee. Note that AGT is not necessarily an individual person, since the collection #$Agent-PartiallyTangible includes organizations also. Note that this predicate differs from #$informationDestination and its specializations such as #$recipientOfInfo-Intended in that these relate instances of #$InformationTransferEvent (not instances of #$InformationBearingThing) to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. See also #$intendedAudienceType.")
(comment BridgingHomeLoan "An instance of #$LoanAgreementTypeByUse, and a specialization of #$HomeLoan.  Each instance of #$BridgingHomeLoan is a short term loan used to cover the cost of buying a new house before the old one has been sold.")
(comment TheVertexList "#$TheVertexList is a function similar to #$TheList.  The salient differences between the two are that #$TheVertexList (i) returns a list of length at least three, (ii) returns a list of instances of #$Point, (iii) no three consecutive list members are #$collinearPoints, neither are the next to last member, last member, and first member #$collinearPoints, nor are the last member, first member, and second member #$collinearPoints.  These odd restrictions are needed since the result of #$TheVertexList is intended to correspond to the vertices of an instance of #$Polygon where the order of the list corresponds to the order of the vertices when the perimeter is traversed in a counter-clockwise direction.  The first restriction above is required since polygons have at least three sides, while the last condition reflects the convention that no three consecutive vertices are #$collinearPoints.")
(comment body-DocumentPartOf "'(#$body-DocumentPartOf WORK BODY)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure BODY contains the main content of the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.")
(comment ibtCreator "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$InformationBearingThing to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. (#$ibtCreator IBT AGENT) means that AGENT originally created IBT, an #$InformationBearingThing.  For instance, painters are #$ibtCreators of their paintings, programmers are #$ibtCreators of their programs, and speakers are #$ibtCreators of their #$AnimalUtterance-IBTs.  An IBT can have more than one #$ibtCreator if multiple #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles contributed to its creation, as is typically the case with Hollywood movies, for example.")
(comment DeviceStateType "Elements of this collection are themselves collections.  Each is a set of mutually exclusive #$DeviceTypeByStates.  An example of this (i.e., an instance of #$DeviceStateType) is #$ClothesWasherState, whose instances are #$DeviceState-Spin, #$PausedState, #$DeviceState-Washing, #$DeviceState-Rinsing, #$Device-Off.")
(comment FlowControlDevice "The collection of all #$PhysicalDevices which control the flow of fluid.  Some subsets of this collection, like #$Dam, may mainly obstruct flow, but are also used to produce an outflow that is somewhat independent to the inflow to the #$WaterReservoir.   A #$Stopper, although it can be used to halt exiting flow (by its insertion) and later can allow the flow again (by its removal) is not an example of a #$FlowControlDevice because it does not regulate the flow, but merely blocks it upon being positioned by something external to the #$Stopper.")
(comment Contorted-BodyPosition "An instance of #$AnimalBLOTypeByPosition, used as attribute for body positions that most people do not, can not, and would not want to contort their bodies into. The  ability to contort their bodies in such positions is, by contrast, the very skill that makes #$Contortionists worth watching when they perform (in a #$Circus, for example).")
(comment rankTypeOfGeoAgent "(#$rankTypeOfGeoAgent RANK-TYPE COUNTRY BOS-TYPE) means that
the class of #$MilitaryPersonTypeByRanks RANK-TYPE is composed exclusively of
ranks used in COUNTRY's branch-of-service-type BOS-TYPE.  E.g.,
(#$rankTypeOfGeoAgent #$IranianArmyRank #$Iran
#$Army-BranchOfService).")
(comment UprightPosture "The attribute that describes an #$Animal in an upright, i.e. vertically extended, #$AnimalTypeByPosture.  (#$postureOfAnimal ANIMAL #$UprightPosture) is implied by walking and running, as well as by standing.")
(comment socialParticipants "An #$ActorSlot (q.v.) and a specialization of #$actors with respect to social events. (#$socialParticipants SOCIAL-EVENT AGENT) means that the #$Agent-Generic AGENT participates --- in some social role --- in the #$SocialOccurrence SOCIAL-EVENT.  In every culture there is a wide variety of such relations of social participation, thus #$socialParticipants has many specializations. Some #$SocialOccurrences have very elaborate role structures (e.g. a lawsuit in 1990's America), and some are fairly simple (e.g. rudely bumping into someone). Some example specializations are #$bride, #$interviewee and #$tourParticipants.  Note that AGENT's participation in SOCIAL-EVENT need not be deliberate or intentional: one can sleep through a meeting and a newborn baby can attend a picnic.  For social participation that is expressly deliberate, see the specialization #$deliberateSocialParticipants.")
(comment FirewoodFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of
#$Fire-ClassA. Instances of #$FirewoodFire have #$Firewood as their
#$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment NewsMagazineShow "A subset of #$TVShow-IBTs, instances of #$NewsMagazineShow provide information about            current events and issues much like instances of #$NewsShow but in more depth.")
(comment PlacingInAnOrientation "A collection of events.  An instance of #$PlacingInAnOrientation is an event in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible changes an object's #$orientation. The event might be a #$Movement-TranslationEvent, like carrying a book from a shelf and laying it in a #$HorizontalOrientation on a table, or it might be a #$Movement-Rotation, like laying down a standing book without moving it to a different place.  In any case, the action is #$doneBy some participant other than the #$objectMoving. Use #$PlacingInOrientationFn to specify particular #$orientations.")
(comment followingOrEqualValueOnScale "A generalization of #$followingValueOnScale (q.v.) that is used to compare the positions or \"ranks\" of quantities/attributes/properties that are on the same scale.  More precisely, <code>(#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale VALUE1 VALUE2 SCALE)</code> means that <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> are both instances of the #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder (q.v.) <code>SCALE</code>, and that <code>VALUE2</code> is \"greater than or equal to\" (i.e. comes no earlier than) <code>VALUE1</code> in the ordering scheme conventionally associated with <code>SCALE</code>.
<p>
Typically, <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> will either (i) both be instances of #$Quantity (q.v.) or (ii) both be instances of #$FirstOrderCollection (q.v.) such that they correspond to properties of individuals.  In case (i), <code>SCALE</code> will be a #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType and, if <code>VALUE1</code> and <code>VALUE2</code> are not identical, <code>(#$followingValue VALUE1 VALUE2)</code> will also hold.
<p>
For example, all of these hold:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale #$MildlyToxic #$MildlyToxic #$Toxicity)

  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale
    #$Corporal-Rank #$Sergeant-Rank #$USArmyRank) 

  (#$followingOrEqualValueOnScale 
    #$TwoDimensionalThing
    #$PolyDimensionalThing
    #$SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality)  .")
(comment SourcesUnreliable "Characteristic attribute of a #$WrittenReportOnSituation with  unreliable sources.")
(comment Gratitude "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Gratitude is some agent's feeling of appreciation towards another agent for a benefit or favor received from the latter agent.  Instances of #$Gratitude vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object of gratitude.")
(comment disapprovedStatement "#$disapprovedStatement is a specialization of #$ist-Information.  (#$disapprovedStatement INFO DISAPPROVED) means that the #$ELSentence-Assertible DISAPPROVED represents some or all of what the agent disapproves of in the content (INFO) of a disapproval expressed by the agent.  See also #$Disapproving-CommunicationAct.  Cf. #$Approval-CommunicationAct.")
(comment numberOfSexualPartners "(#$numberOfSexualPartners ?ANIM ?NUM) is true if and only if the individual ?ANIM, which 
must be an instance of #$Animal has ?NUM #$sexualPartners, where ?NUM must be an integer. This
must be understood in the same context in which the predicate #$sexualPartners (q.v.)
is understood to apply.")
(comment eventTypesOverlapInEvent "(#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent FIRST SECOND MAIN) means that during an instance, M-INS, of MAIN, any instance of SECOND that is a subevent (#$subEvents) of M-INS will start during some instance of FIRST which is a subevent of MAIN.  For instance, during hockey games, ice cleaning occurs during the intermission so we could assert (#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent Intermission IceCleaning #$PlayingOf-HockeyGame). Note that (#$eventTypesOverlapInEvent FIRST MAIN SECOND) does _not_ imply either that (i) each instance of MAIN has a subevent of type FIRST or of type SECOND, or, given an instance of MAIN, MAIN-INST, that does have a subevent of type FIRST, that (ii) it's having such a subevent entails it having a subevent of type SECOND. See also #$startsDuringInSituationType and #$startsDuringInScript-Ternary for application to scripts.")
(comment LovePoem "This is the collection of instances of #$Poem-CW which are on the topic of love.")
(comment boundaryClusterOfSpaceRegion "A quaternary #$SpaceRegionPredicate that relates a given space region (see #$HomogeneousExtendedSpaceRegion) to triples of #$Points that are clustered around its boundary.
<p>
More precisely, <code>(#$boundaryClusterOfSpaceRegion INTERIOR-POINT BOUNDARY-POINT EXTERIOR-POINT REGION)</code> holds if and only if all of the following conditions are satisfied: (i) <code>INTERIOR-POINT</code> is in the interior of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInInteriorOfSpaceRegion); (ii) <code>BOUNDARY-POINT</code> is in the boundary of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInBoundaryOfSpaceRegion); (iii) <code>EXTERIOR-POINT</code> is in the exterior of <code>REGION</code> (see #$incidentInExteriorOfSpaceRegion); and (iv) both <code>INTERIOR-POINT</code> and <code>EXTERIOR-POINT</code> are arbitrarily close to <code>BOUNDARY-POINT</code> (see #$arbitrarilyClosePoints).")
(comment MysteryTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs.  Instances are mysteries, e.g. 'Murder, She Wrote' or           'Quincy, M.E.'.")
(comment MoviesStarringFn "#$MoviesStarringFn takes as argument any instances of #$Actor and returns the collection of all instances of #$SpecifiedMovieType (Movies by title) starring that actor.  For example, (#$MoviesStarringFn DannyDeVito) would return the collection of all #$SpecifiedMovieTypes featuring Danny DeVito.")
(comment surrounds-3D "This predicate is used to assert that an object (or group of objects) that surrounds another object (or group of objects) in three-dimensional space. (#$surrounds-3D SURROUNDER SURROUNDED) means that #$SpatialThing SURROUNDED is within (see #$spatiallySubsumes) the space defined by the convex hull (see #$MinimalSubsumingConvexSpaceRegionFn) of #$SpatialThing SURROUNDER.  The space occupied by SURROUNDED is not a part of the space occupied by SURROUNDER.  If this predicate is too strong, see also  #$surrounds-Ringlike and #$surrounds-2D.  If SURROUNDER is functioning as a container with respect to SURROUNDED, then #$in-ContGeneric is true as well as #$surrounds-3D. If any ray with an origin within SURROUNDED passes through (see #$spatiallyIntersects) SURROUNDER, then #$surroundsCompletely is the more precise predicate to use.  If SURROUNDER is a #$Group of objects then #$in-Among is more precise. If SURROUNDER is a fluid (#$FluidTangibleThing) in the granularity of the current context, then #$in-ImmersedFully is almost always the more correct and precise relation (unless the fluid has a concavity, e.g. when a meteor has impacted a body of water and the meteor is partially submerged in the water yet within its convex hull in such a case #$in-ImmersedPartly would be the appropriate relation.)")
(comment DesigningAGame "A specialization of #$CWCreation and #$Designing. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible designs some instances of #$Game. Nowadays this will typically involve a fair amount of (#$UsingAFn #$Computer), if only to type up the #$GameRulesFn.")
(comment quoteIn "(#$quoteIn WORK TEXT) means that TEXT is an instance of #$TextString whose first and last characters are quotation marks and which is contained within (see #$containsStructure-CW) the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.   #$quoteIn is the least specific of the predicates which speak to the presence of something within quotation marks within a #$GraphicalStructure.  Use of this predicate simply indicates that there is a #$TextString enclosed within quotation marks; it does not imply any particular use of those quotations marks (e.g., the #$TextString within quotation marks could be the direct quote of an individual or work external to WORK, the quotation marks could indicate a foreign word or phrase, or the quotation marks could indicate the speech of a character within a #$FictionalPCW).  To indicate quotations of external agents or the speech of a character within a fictional work, use the more precise #$quotationOfExternalAgent or #$speechOfCharacter.")
(comment RetaliationGoal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory.  A state of affairs has this attribute for an agent if she seeks to actualize that state of affairs as a means of retaliating against another agent.")
(comment Fender-AutoBodyPart "The collection of all fenders. A type of #$AutoBodyPart and #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory. The collection #$Fender-AutoBodyPart is a #$ManufacturedGoodsType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.  Each instance of #$Fender-AutoBodyPart is a part of an automobile body that frames a wheel well.")
(comment Fire-ClassC "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$CombustionProcess. Instances of #$Fire-ClassC have as their
#$energySourceForEvent live electric power lines or electrical devices.")
(comment currentAccountBalanceDuring "(#$currentAccountBalanceDuring COUNTRY THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the difference between, on the one hand, the sum of the value of all goods and services exported by the #$Country COUNTRY during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING and the transfer payments received by COUNTRY from foreigners during the temporal extent of THING, and, on the other, the sum of the value of all goods and services imported by COUNTRY during the temporal extent of THING and the transfer payments by COUNTRY to foreigners during the temporal extent of THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  Thus if the value of COUNTRY's exports and received transfer payments is greater than the value of its imports and outgoing transfer payments during the temporal extent of THING, COUNTRY will have a positive current account balance.  If the value of its imports and outgoing transfer payments exceeds that of its exports and incoming transfer payments, it will have a negative current account balance.  This latter case can be expressed using a #$UnitOfMoney function with a negative number as its argument.")
(comment typicallyLikesRelationshipToType "(#$typicallyLikesRelationshipToType AGENT_TYPE REL COLLECTION) means that a typical instance of AGENT_TYPE likes to be in the relationship REL with an instance of COLLECTION [#$likesRelationshipToType].  If the relationship is a #$Role and the #$Collection is a spec of #$Event, then #$likesRoleInEventType applies among the typical instance of AGENT_TYPE, #$Role, and #$Event type.")
(comment Pipeline "The collection of pipelines that are used to transport #$FluidTangibleThings. Basically a #$Pipeline is a man-made #$Pipe-GenericConduit that is built to transport fluids in a #$FluidFlowEvent where the force is provided by a #$Pump-Generic or #$GravitationalForceVector. Examples include large oil pipelines which can be very long, spanning countries. Other #$Pipelines are smaller like a water pipe under the sink. When a network of pipelines is meant use #$PipingSystem-Generic. Borderline cases are those long pipelines that are mostly a single tube, but at each end have a network of smaller pipelines.")
(comment goalRoleSlot "#$goalRoleSlot is a simple but powerful means of
representing a desire to play a role in an instance of some kind of
#$Situation.  This predicate relates a #$GoalSituation to a
#$BinaryRolePredicate.  (#$goalSituationType GOAL-SITUATION
DESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE) means that at least one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (such agents
are identified by #$goalAgent) has a goal, desire, want or need to
play a role (this role is identified by #$goalRoleSlot) in some
instance of DESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE.  For example (#$goalSituationType
`GoalSituation001' #$TakingAShower) means that during
`GoalSituation001' any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001' wants to
play some role in #$TakingAShower.  If (#$goalRoleSlot
`GoalSituation002' #$performedBy) is also asserted, then this
specifies that any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001' wishes to play
the role of #$performedBy in some element of #$TakingAShower.  In
other words, \"someone wishes to take a shower\".  If one wishes to
assert that \"Fred wishes to take a shower.\" then one would add the
assertion (#$goalAgent `GoalSituation002' `Fred').  Compared with
#$goalSituationSuccessIf, this predicate has limitations in terms of
expressivity.  However, it has more inferencing power.  See (VersusFn
(TheSet goalSituationType goalRoleSlot) goalSituationSuccessIf) for more
on the expressivity/tradeoff tradeoff issue.")
(comment lockState "'(#$lockState LOCK STATE)' means that the #$Lock LOCK has the #$LockStateAttribute STATE, that is, #$Device-Locked or #$Device-Unlocked.")
(comment pathogenContagiousWithContactFromTo "(#$pathogenContagiousWithContactFromTo LBA ORGTYPE1 ORGTYPE2 LEVEL) means that if the #$LivingBiologicalAgent LBA causes a certain type of infection (see #$pathogenTypeCausesInfectionType) and an instance of ORGTYPE2 comes into physical contact (see #$PhysicalContactSituation) with an instance of ORGTYPE1 while said instance of ORGTYPE1 has an infection of this type, the likelihood of the instance of ORGTYPE2 contracting an infection of the same type is LEVEL.")
(comment performedBy "An #$AgentiveRole (q.v.) predicate that relates an action (see #$Action) to an agent (see #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) who performs it deliberately, i.e. intentionally and volitionally.  <code>(#$performedBy ACT DOER)</code> means that <code>DOER</code> deliberately does <code>ACT</code>.  For example, (#$performedBy #$AssassinationOfPresidentLincoln #$JohnWilkesBooth) holds.  Note that an action can have multiple deliberate performers.  See also the generalizations #$deliberateActors and #$doneBy.")
(comment DynamicSizedData "The collection of all data types whose size in memory can only be 
dynamically determined. For instance, null terminated character strings 
(as in the C Language) are instances of a #$DynamicSizedData.")
(comment Tune "The collection of all simple tunes, whether recorded or not, extant for centuries or composed on the spot, instrumental or sung, etc.  This is not to be confused with  performances of the tune, although musical performances normally enact instances of one or more #$Tunes.  A song (#$Song-CW) normally has a single #$Tune as a #$subWorks, while a Symphony would have several.")
(comment Relief-Feeling "Emotion aroused by the removal or lightening of something oppressive, distressing, or painful.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.")
(comment HighLevelOfInfectivity "The highest #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionInfectivityLevel.")
(comment grossDomesticProduct-Nominal "(#$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the value of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's total domestic production of goods and services (its gross domestic product) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, and that the value of the currency (#$UnitOfMoney) in terms of which MONEY is specified is that which prevailed during the temporal extent of THING.  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a time period -- for example, a calendar year such as (#$YearFn 1997) or a calendar quarter such as (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1997)); but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, (#$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal COUNTRY (#$YearFn 1997) (#$Dollar-UnitedStates NR)) means that COUNTRY's gross domestic product for 1997 was $NR in 1997 US dollars.  See also #$grossDomesticProduct.")
(comment listHasFormat "'(#$listHasFormat LIST FORMAT)' means that the #$List-Information LIST has the #$GraphicalStructureByFormat FORMAT.  The #$GraphicalStructureByFormat characterizes the way in which items of an instance of #$List-Information (see #$itemInList-Information) are arranged spatially or in which such items are otherwise distinguished one from another.")
(comment Bill-Currency "A specialization of #$Currency. Each instance of this collection is an object, generally made of paper (sometimes plastic) used to transfer a quantity of #$MonetaryValue between #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.  The piece of paper iteself is of little value, but the bill has the value it does because, due to governmental and societal agreement, it can be exchanged for objects or services. It is often engraved (see #$Engraving-Print) with a watermark in order to forestall counterfeiting.")
(comment NegativeChange "#$NegativeChange is an instance of #$LevelOfChange that denotes either (i) a negative change (i.e., a decrease) in the second argument of a binary predicate that takes a quantity as its second argument (\"quantity slot\"), or (ii) a negative dependency between the second argument values of two such binary predicates (i.e., independent increase => dependent decrease, and independent decrease => dependent increase).")
(comment UnjustifiedBelief "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType and a collection of cyc arguments which are not justified by appeal to a rule of some sort.  This collection can be used to indicate that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) was purposely added to the Cyc knowledge base by some agent (as opposed to being inferred somehow by Cyc).")
(comment requiresForRole "(#$requiresForRole SIT COL ROLE) means that the success of an agent acting deliberately in the #$Situation SIT (see the predicate #$successfulForAgents) is contingent upon the existence of an instance of the collection COL playing the role ROLE in SIT. Compare this predicate to #$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType.")
(comment LocalGovernmentOrganization "A specialization of both #$LegalGovernmentOrganization and #$LocalOrganization.  Each instance of #$LocalGovernmentOrganization is any government organization -- whether federal, state, county, or municipal -- that is specific to, i.e., has jurisdiction and/or services generally limited to, one (local) location.  For example, a Board of Education of a particular school district is a #$LocalGovernmentOrganization, because its authority extends to schools in a limited (local) area; in the U.S., such a Board answers to another #$LocalGovernmentOrganization, typically a city or township government.  In another example, an instance of #$VeteransAffairsMedicalCenter is a local organization in terms of its service area, but bureaucratically it belongs to the U.S. Federal government; thus, #$VeteransAffairsMedicalCenter is a specialization of both #$LocalGovernmentOrganization and #$USFederalGovernmentOrganization.")
(comment PituitaryGland "The collection of all pituitary #$Glands.  A #$PituitaryGland is a unique #$EndocrineGland attached to the #$Hypothalamus which rests (is #$in-Rooted) in a cavity of the #$Sphenoid bone called the sella turcica.  The #$PituitaryGland produces #$HumanGrowthHormone, #$Prolactin, #$Thyrotropin, #$AdrenocorticotropicHormone, melanocyte-stimulating hormone, #$FollicleStimulatingHormone, #$LuteinizingHormone, #$Vasopressin, and #$Oxytocin.")
(comment PhotographicFilm-Exposed "Elements are pieces of

photographic film that have been exposed to light.  Such elements

contain information subsequent to exposure.  Elements of

#$PhotographicFilm-Exposed are not necessarily elements of

#$VisualInformationBearingThing, since if the film is exposed but not developed, humans can not extract information by viewing it.  Being

able to extract information by viewing is one of the current (Oct

98) aspects of the definition of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.")
(comment CourseOfStudy "The collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible studies some prescribed #$Things.  This refers not to the material studied, but to the agent's action of going through and comprehending some chunk of subject material.")
(comment LongThinObject "The collection of instances of #$PartiallyTangible that are long and thin.  #$LongThinObject is the #$PartiallyTangibleTypeByPhysicalStructuralFeature that characterizes a tangible object which has one dimension whose length exceeds that of each of the other two dimensions by at least a factor of three.  E.g., pencils, straws, telephone wire, submarines, skyscrapers. Cf. #$SheetShapedObject.")
(comment loudnessOfEvent "A #$SensoryAttributeDescriptionPredicate and #$QuantitySlot that relates a #$PhysicalEvent to a #$AcousticNoiseLevel.  (#$loudnessLevel EVENT LEVEL) means that the noise/loudness level of the totality of #$AudibleSounds (see #$loudnessLevel) currently being produced in the course of EVENT is LEVEL.
<p>
Cf. #$loudnessOfObject.")
(comment OwnerFn-RightsToType "#$OwnerFn-RightsToType takes as argument any spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible owning, in part or entirely, the rights to produce or market that class of things.  For example, (#$OwnerFn-RightsToType #$OperatingSystem) returns the collection of all agents owning the rights to produce or market operating systems.")
(comment SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB "#$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB is a collection of #$SharedNotes which serve as pointers to documentation which is outside of the KB.  There is currently (Sept 99) no convention for how such pointers should be specified.  Thus until further use and analysis indicates otherwise it is suggested that one do this by studying other #$comment assertions on other elements of #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB. Although typical elements of #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB will point to text files (via a pathname) on the unix file system at #$Cycorp, one could imagine such that such elements might point to gif images, world wide web sites, sound files, threads of email conversations etc.. An example: #$NLAssertionsForQueryAugmentation is an element of #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB.  Its #$comment points to a text file about making NL assertions for the #$WebSearchEnhancementProject. Eventually, the interface can be modified to allow hotlinking between KB external objects (such as text files) and KB content.  In the meantime, #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB can serve to collect arbitrarily heterogeneous cases of desired linkups between KB content and information external to the KB.   Here are some motivating use cases: Suppose there is a lengthy FAQ document external to the KB which is important to use if one is making assertions using an assortment of constants such as #$acronymString, #$abbreviationString-PN, or #$nameString.  How is a neophyte going to even *know* about the existence of such an FAQ document?  How is an experienced user going to remember the pathname of this FAQ on a filesystem that frequently undergoes reorganizations?  How can someone who knows that information in the FAQ is highly relevant to a predicate that they want to use, yet they can't locate that precious 6 month old email message?  In all these cases, an element of #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB could easily point the user from the constant under consideration to what they need to know.  The predicate #$sharedNotes may be used to do the linking between the constant in question and the element of #$SharedNoteOnDocumentationExternalToTheKB.")
(comment NullSpaceRegion-2D "A specialization of #$NullSpaceRegion (q.v.) and #$TwoDimensionalThing.  #$NullSpaceRegion-2D is the collection of two-dimensional \"null spatial regions\".  There is at most one known instance of #$NullSpaceRegion-2D with respect to any context in which some #$Surfaces (q.v.) are known to have locations, either absolutely or relatively (see #$LocationalPredicate and its immediate specializations).
<p>
By definition, a 2-D null space region is disconnected from (see #$disconnectedSpaceRegions) every 2-D homogeneous space region (i.e. #$Surface), and is the #$spaceRegionComplement of the 2-D \"spatial universe\" (see #$UniversalSpaceRegion-2D).
<p>
The introduction of 2-D null regions into #$RegionConnectionCalculus8Theory helps to allow the functions #$SpaceRegionComplementFn, #$SpaceRegionProductFn, and #$SpaceRegionDifferenceFn to be defined as #$TotalFunctions.  For example, #$SpaceRegionComplementFn can then be defined on instances of #$UniversalSpaceRegion-2D (q.v.), and #$SpaceRegionProductFn can be defined for pairs of two-dimensional regions that are #$discreteSpaceRegions.  (Also see the comment on #$NullSpaceRegion.)
<p>
See also #$NullSpaceRegion-1D and #$NullSpaceRegion-3D.")
(comment requiredTemplateForType "(#$requiredTemplateForType TEMPLATE TYPE) means that when #$FormulaTemplate TEMPLATE is asserted to be an instance of #$FormulaTemplateType (or subtopic) TYPE, that template must be filled out by the user. For example, (#$requiredTemplateForType #$SourceTitleTemplate #$TKBTemplate-Source-JournalForm) means that in the subtopic for journal articles that are TKB sources, 'title' a required field. This assertion should be used for any template that we wish to force a fact enterer to complete. It is recommended that required templates be sorted (via #$higherPriorityTemplateForType) below the #$focalTermIntroduction template, and above all others.")
(comment BLOTypeByPhysiology "a collection of collections each one corresponding to a plant or animal organism's physiological characteristics.  Some examples include #$Flexed, #$DeafAnimal, #$Injured, #$FertileAnimal, #$Swollen, #$AcidIndigestion, etc.")
(comment SingingARecitative "#$SingingARecitative is the collection of musical events which are instances of both #$AnimalUtterance-IBT and #$Song. In other words, a recitative is a speech, which would ordinarily be spoken, but instead is sung. Recitatives occur in operas and musical theatre. (See #$OperaPerformance and #$PlayPerformance-Musical.)")
(comment TemporalPredicate "A specialization of #$ObjectPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TemporalPredicate is used either to say something about the relative positions of two or more temporal things in time, to ascribe a temporal property to something, or to compare time-quantities.  As such, each temporal predicate has at least one (and often two or more) of its argument-places constrained (by #$argIsa) either to take instances of #$TemporalThing or to take instances of #$Time-Quantity.
<p>
An important specialization of #$TemporalPredicate is #$BinaryTemporalRelationPredicate (q.v.).  Examples of temporal predicates that are not in that specialization include #$startsDurationAfterEndingOf, #$temporallyContinuousDuring, #$longerDurationThan, and #$holdsIn.")
(comment ProcardiaXLProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by #$PfizerInc.")
(comment predicateTypeSummaryForThing "An instance of #$SummaryPredicate useful for summarizing knowledge about THING with respect to #$PredicateTypes. (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing PRED-TYPE THING SENTENCE) means that #$CycLSentence-Assertible SENTENCE has PRED (an instance of PRED-TYPE) in its arg0 slot and it has the term THING in some slot other than arg0.  For example, (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing #$LikesPredicate #$JenniferSullivan  (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia)) is true, and means that some instance of #$LikesPredicate occurs as the arg0 in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia), and that #$JenniferSullivan also occurs in (#$likesAsFriend #$JenniferSullivan #$Cynthia).  This predicate is particularly useful for asking queries with the first and second argument slots bound and the third slot open.  For example, asking (#$predicateTypeSummaryForThing OrganismRequirementsPredicate (#$AdultFn #$Dachshund) ?SENTENCE) will mean the system will find any assertions whose arg0 is an instance of OrganismRequirementsPredicate that also contain the term (#$AdultFn #$Dachshund). Cf. #$predicateTypeSummaryForThing-Set.")
(comment License-IBO "A collection of InformationBearingObjects.  Each instance of #$License-IBO is a tangible document recording some #$License-LegalAgreement.For example, the StateOfTexas enters into a LegalAgreement with me which constitutes my #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement, an instance of #$License-LegalAgreement.  That agreement is recorded on the card I carry in my pocket, and instance of #$License-IBO.")
(comment PascalChallengeKBContentTest-IETask "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can solve a particular #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat which is part of the \"IE\" task (c.f.#$PascalChallengeIETask).")
(comment income "An instance of #$QuantitySlot (q.v.) 
that is used to state the income or wage of a person or other agent in 
terms of a #$MonetaryRate (q.v.), such as #$DollarsPerYear or 
#$DollarsPerHour.  (#$income AGENT RATE) means that AGENT has the income 
or wage RATE.  Normally, a agent's yearly earnings are described as 
\"income\", while hourly earnings are called \"wages\"; the predicate 
#$income encompasses both of these.")
(comment SouthAfricanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment costRate "The rate of cost that applies to an individual product.  The rate may be a #$MoneyPerVolumeRatio, #$MoneyPerMassRatio, etc.  Multiplying this rate by the actual quantity involved (e.g. the mass of the object sold/serviced) gives the #$objectBasicPrice or #$serviceBasicPrice of the object or service.  Since this is instance-level, it will always refer to a particular object (or service) sold by a particular agent at a particular rate.  The value on this slot will therefore often be inferred from a #$costRateForType assertion.")
(comment CarrierBattleGroup "A Carrier Battle Group is a self-sufficient group of ships including and focused   on defending and supporting an instance of #$AttackAircraftCarrier. The roles of   the combatant surface ships attached to an instance of #$CarrierBattleGroup can   vary per mission. Each ship typically fulfills roles in various systems in the   #$CarrierBattleGroup. These include providing support to the air system, the   surface system, and even the underwater system. Support to the air system would   include the use of the Aegis system, coordinating air defense among the   #$CarrierAirWing and the other surface combatants.  The surface system would   include those subsystems among the ships designed to deal with surface threats.    The underwater system could include detection and countermeasures for submarine   threats, involving sonar, towed arrays, and depth charges. Typically there are   also one to two friendly attack #$NuclearSubmarines aiding in this system.  For the miltary unit having a #$CarrierBattleGroup as its primary equipment, see #$CarrierBattleGroup-MilitarySpecialty.")
(comment graphicalStructureOfAnalysisScript "An instance of #$FunctionalSlot. (#$graphicalStructureOfAnalysisScript GRAPH SCRIPT) says that the #$Graph-AIS GRAPH depicts SCRIPT, an analysis script (a specialization of #$AnalysisProcedure).")
(comment PublishedEdition-PIT "Each instance is a partial representation of the
propositional content of a particular edition of a public work.
Different editions should be reified as separate PITs.  Every instance
should have a specified #$dateOfPublication-CW.")
(comment answerSourceIBTsAcknowledged "(#$answerSourceIBTsAcknowledged RESPONSE IBT) says that IBT is one of the instances of #$ComputerDataArtifact that has been acknowledged (say by accepting or rejecting it, or by some other means) in RESPONSE, an instance of #$ProvidingRequestedInformationToComputerProcess")
(comment SensoryQuantity "A collection of Quantities.  Each instance of #$SensoryQuantity is a sensory quality detectable by sentient beings.  #$SensoryQuantity includes levels of odors, tastes, sounds, and feels.  Instances of #$SensoryQuantity include #$Rough, #$Smooth, #$Slimy, and (#$HighAmountFn #$AcousticNoiseLevel).")
(comment ConceptFilterParameterType "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Each instance of this collection is a parameter that tells an application that uses #$ConceptFilters how it is allowed to use the filter.  Usually the instances of this collection are used in conjunction with #$ConceptFilterSpecificationFn to denote instances of ConceptFilterSpecification.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-SuspenseGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the 
suspense genre.  Many of #$AlfredHitchcock's movies are in this genre.  ")
(comment (IsotopeFn Hydrogen 3) "A specialization of #$NuclearRelatedMaterial, known as \"tritium\" or \"H-3\".   Tritium is an essential material in U.S. nuclear weapons.  It is an isotope of #$Hydrogen that decays at a rate of about five percent per year (half of it decays in about 12 years).")
(comment GameOfProgramFn "#$GameOfProgramFn is a unary function which returns an instance of #$Game when given an instance of #$ComputerGameProgram as an argument. (#$GameOfProgramFn PROG) denotes the instance of #$Game which is the structured and rule-governed activity in which one engages when one plays with a running copy of PROG.  For example, (#$GameOfProgramFn #$CompleteChess-TheGame) denotes #$Chess.")
(comment LocomotionProcess "The collection of processes in which a #$providerOfMotiveForce moves from one place to another under, or as if under, its own control. This includes not only animals moving around autonomously (c.f. #$LocomotionProcess-Animal), but also locomoting devices such as cars, submarines, and airplanes, which are controlled either internally or remotely by distinct #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles, but share significant properties with locomoting #$Animals - notably that their trajectories are not just functions of forces such as gravity and resistance, but rather can have abrupt changes of direction or speed that are or appear purposeful. This collection also explicitly includes locomoting events in which the #$providerOfMotiveForce is a non-agent natural force such as gravity, so long as the object moving is or appears to be in control of its trajectory of motion. Thus someone downhill skiing or hang-gliding would be a positive example.")
(comment MortgageAgreement "This is a collection of agreements; a subset of #$AuthorizedAgreement.  Each element of #$MortgageAgreement is generated from an instance of #$EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement.  A #$MortgageAgreement contains the terms of a mortgage (in which money is borrowed and a claim against the borrower's property is given to secure the loan).")
(comment Statement "A #$Statement is the #$InformationBearingThing created in a #$StatingSomething.  An #$Agent-PartiallyTangible must create the #$Statement and it contains propositional information.  The illocutionary force of its contents are an #$Inform.")
(comment SmallPrint-PCW "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$SmallPrint-PCW is a part of a #$TextualDocument-CW that contains detailed qualifications of, and restrictions on, the material in the main portion of the document.  In many cases, the author of a document wants to de-emphasize the content of the small print section, either because it contains information that the reader may find disagreeable, or because he does not want the reader to be bothered with it; hence small print sections of documents are typically printed in a tiny font (hence the name), but instantiations of instances of #$SmallPrint-PCW could, in principle, be printed in any font size.")
(comment templateTopicForTask "(#$activeTaskForSession TASK FTTT) means that the #$FormulaTemplateTopicType FTTT can be used to advance the information-gathering goals of the task TASK.")
(comment Riding-LyingInACertainLocation "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$LyingInACertainRelativeLocation. In each #$Riding-LyingInACertainLocation, some #$Watercraft-Surface lies moored or anchored.")
(comment feelsTowardsEvent "(#$feelsTowardsEvent AGT EVT EMOTYPE DEGREE) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGT feels a feeling of the #$EmotionalQuantityType EMOTYPE towards the #$Event EVT, with intensity DEGREE.
Note: the first argument can be a non-human intelligent agent, such as a dog or a company, because we often ascribe feelings and emotions to them, and they often behave consistently with having such feelings and emotions.  See also #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree. ")
(comment RetainingUserRights "A collection of static situations holding between an agent and some #$Thing during which the agent retains some user rights over said thing (see #$SituationTypeByUserRights). Such situations may have subevents but they need not.  For example, saving one's money may involve putting money into a savings account or it may not involve any events at all (as when one simply does not *spend*). See also #$objectRetained and #$agentRetaining.")
(comment InstanceLevelScriptMicrotheory "Mts of this type should detail some event.  One can make such a microtheory a spec mt of some #$SubeventSequenceGraphMicrotheory if the graph mt represents the type (#$graphRepresentsType) of script of which the script is an instance or purports to be an instance (use #$typeConstraintToConsider) and if the subevent sequence graph is constrained by some #$ScriptGraphComplianceMicrotheory against which one wants the script to be evaluated.")
(comment Imam-Sunni "The congregational prayer performed in the #$Mosque-Building is supposed to have 
a leader, and this person is called '#$Imam-Sunni'. In the standard #$SunniIslam 
interpretation, #$Imam-Sunni is neither a profession, nor a qualification: the 
#$Imam-Sunni is not ordained in the manner of Christian priests. Any respected 
Muslim who is normally well-trained in the prayer can be an #$Imam-Sunni. In 
general, it is the most learned and most respected person in the assembly who 
is offered the honour of being #$Imam-Sunni. Customarily, a #$Mosque-LocalCongregation 
will have one person who regularly serves as #$Imam-Sunni and the position often 
confers a great deal of informal authority.")
(comment FiscalQuarter "Each instance of this collection is a 3-month-long interval of time kept track of by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible as part of its financial accounting procedures.  Since the start dates and end dates may vary depending on the organization, instances will be things like Fiscal3rdQuarterOf1995ForCycorp.")
(comment attributionGivenForTo "(#$attributionGivenForTo WORK ATTRIBUTION STRUC CREATOR) means that the #$TextString ATTRIBUTION attributes STRUC, an instance of #$GraphicalStructure or #$TextString that is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK, to CREATOR, an instance of either #$IntelligentAgent or #$ConceptualWork.  #$attributionGivenForTo relates an externally created #$AbstractStructure incorporated into a work to its source.")
(comment IAIncidentReport "A collection of instances of #$WrittenReportOnSituation.  Each instance is characterized by being an initial report concerning the etiology of an IA-related incident.")
(comment Shame "Painful self-conscious feeling of guilt, shortcoming, or impropriety.  #$Shame often accompanies social disgrace or disrepute.  It often leads to #$Remorse.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.")
(comment TwoLaneRoadway "The collection of #$Roadways that have two lanes or tracks, both directions

included. This criterion belongs to the US Army's nomenclature for the

representation of roads on medium scale maps. See also

#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes.")
(comment normProponents "<code>(#$normOpponents NORM AGENT)</code> means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>AGENT</code> likes the #$NormativeSpecification <code>NORM</code> and advocates it.  <code>AGENT</code> need not be related to <code>NORM</code> in any other way (<i>e.g.</i>, via  #$normativelyBoundAgents or #$specifiedActors (qq.v.)).  See also #$normOpponents.")
(comment phoneExtension "The extension number of the #$phoneNumberPart of this Contact Location")
(comment Mistrust "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType, #$Mistrust represents the feeling or attitude an agent has towards something that it considers unreliable, suspicious, or otherwise untrustworthy.")
(comment VisualImageRecording "A specialization of #$InformationRecordingProcess.  Each instance of #$VisualImageRecording is an event in which a #$VisualImage is recorded using a #$VisualInformationRecordingDevice.  Specializations include #$TakingAPhotograph and #$VideoCassetteRecording.")
(comment ArgGenlQuantityTernaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$ArgTypeTernaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlAttributePredicate.  Each instance of #$ArgGenlAttributeTernaryPredicate is a ternary predicate used to place a \"#$quantitySubsumes\" constraint on (and thereby specify an argument-type for) one or more argument-places of a relation.  To be more precise, each instance PRED of #$ArgGenlAttributeTernaryPredicate takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument, a #$NonNegativeInteger N as its second argument, and an #$Quantity QUANT as its third argument. PRED places a \"#$quantitySubsumes\" constraint on RELN's Nth argument-place that is based on QUANT, so that a ground atomic sentence (GAF) of the form (RELN ARG1..ARGN..) is semantically well-formed only if ARGN is subsumed by QUANT (in the sense that (#$quantitySubsumes QUANT ARGN) holds).  An important instance of #$ArgGenlAttributeTernaryPredicate is #$argGenlQuantity.")
(comment ComputerCapabilityQualifier "A specialization of #$IndividualDenotingFunction. Each instance of this collection takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability pertaining to computers which may have certain actions performed on them, and returns a suitably qualified capability attribute. For instance, (#$MSLocalIntranetZoneFn #$CanDownloadActiveXControls-Signed) denotes the capability for signed \"ActiveX\" controls to be downloaded on a particular computer, as long as they originate from the computer's local intranet. See also #$hasCapabilityAttribute.")
(comment HelpingAnAgent "A specialization of both #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$HelpingAnAgent is an event in which some agent (see the collection #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) helps another agent, either by doing something that directly benefits that agent, or by preventing something that would harm that agent.  Notable specializations of #$HelpingAnAgent include #$RescuingSomeone, #$ReliefOperation, and #$ServiceEvent.")
(comment FiletMignon "The collection of all filet mignons. A type of #$Steak-Beef-MeatCut. The collection #$FiletMignon is a #$MeatCutType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment testingEnvironmentForProgram "(#$testingEnvironmentForProgram MICROTHEORY PROGRAM) says that MICROTHEORY is a instance of #$ProblemSolvingCntxt intended for testing some feature of PROGRAM, an instance of #$ApplicationProgram.  Typically, this will involve running a query or an instance of #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified that uses all the information available from MICROTHEORY.")
(comment approximately "(#$approximately INT1 INT2) says that the #$ScalarInterval INT1 and INT2 are very close to being (and in fact might be) #$numericallyEquals.")
(comment Device-Locked "The collection of devices in the locked state.  This includes both locking devices (see #$LockedState) and devices that may have a lock, such as a house, car, or bicycle (see #$IndividualTypeBySecurityStatus and #$LimitedAccess).")
(comment GivingBirthToALitterOfOffspring "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BirthEvent. In each #$GivingBirthToALitterOfOffspring, some animal gives birth to a litter of offspring.")
(comment animalSeverelyWoundedIn "A #$AgentCasualtyPredicate and specialization of #$animalWoundedIn.  (#$animalSeverelyWoundedIn EVENT ANIMAL) means that ANIMAL is severely wounded in EVENT.")
(comment NonNaturalThing "The collection of non-natural individuals.  This collection is hard to precisely define but, roughly, something is an instance of this collection just in case it is one of the following: 1) #$Individual acts that are intentionally performed by #$IntelligentAgents, or 2) #$Individuals that in some significant sense \"could only have been the result\" of the intentional activities of #$IntelligentAgents (or groups thereof).   Positive examples in the first category include #$CesareanBirths, negative examples include eating.  Positive examples in the second category include instances of industrial pollution and tire tracks.  Negative examples include human vomit and human (bare) footprints.")
(comment Laboring-SomeoneMakingAStrenousEffort "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MakingAStrenousEffort. In each #$Laboring-SomeoneMakingAStrenousEffort, something strives and makes an effort to reach a goal.")
(comment calendarDayOfDate "(#$calendarDayOfDate CALENDAR-DAY DATE) means that CALENDAR-DAY is the day of DATE. For example, (#$calendarDayOfDate (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))) (#$SecondFn 54 (#$MinuteFn 48 (#$HourFn 10 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))))))) means that (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972))) is the day of the date (#$SecondFn 54 (#$MinuteFn 48 (#$HourFn 10 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972)))))). Cf. #$dayNumberOfDate.")
(comment GeographicalPlace-OneByOneQuadrangle "A subcollection of

#$GeographicalPlace-2D. Instances of #$GeographicalPlace-OneByOneQuadrangle are 

one degree of latitude high by one degree of longitude wide portions of 

the geographical surface of reference. They can be used to indicate partial 

geographical location of two or three dimensional things within the context 

of a geography. See #$genericallyLocatedAt-SurfaceGeographical. They can also be 

used to specify the exact extent of an object when specifying an area of 

interest of a particular context (using #$exactlyLocatedAt-Spatial, 

#$mtSpatialUniverse-2D).")
(comment Shock "A #$EmotionalQuantityType and specialization of #$Surprise and #$Distress.   #$Shock is the state of being surprised in an extremely unpleasant way.")
(comment Biochip-Generic "An #$ExistingObjectType and a sub-collection of #$Sensor-Device. An instance of #$Biochip-Generic is a device that encapsulates (usually in a very small apparatus) the means for performing a specific type of chemical or biochemical reaction.  These apparatuses are sensors because the chemical reactions are typically designed to determine the presence of specific types of chemicals, compounds, or molecular structures (e.g., #$DNAStuff) within a sample.  For instance, biochips can be used to detect from the presence of #$Anthrax-Bacterium.")
(comment jobPositionDuties "(#$jobPositionDuties JOB ACT-TYPE) means that the #$JobPosition JOB requires that the #$Person filling the position perform #$Events of type ACT-TYPE. This predicate relates an instance of #$JobPosition JOB to the duties required of the person who stands in the #$personWithJobPosition relation to JOB. To relate job duties to a subcollection of #$WorkAgreements, use #$duties. To relate job duties to an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who is obligated to perform them in part because she is an instance of an #$PersonTypeByOccupation, use #$dutiesOfAgentInJob.")
(comment contraryIntervalTypes "(#$contraryIntervalTypes TYPE-1 TYPE-2) says that the #$PrimitiveOrderedQuantityTypes TYPE-1 and TYPE-2 are contrary, in that they cannot both hold of the same object along the same scale to the same degree at the same time.  So, for example, generosity and miserliness are contrary (i.e., (#$contraryIntervalTypes #$Generosity #$Miserliness)): Suppose (#$isa DONATION-001 #$CharitableDonation), and (#$performedBy DONATION-001 PERSON001).  It cannot be the case that (#$and (exhibitsQualityDuringPerformanceOfAction PERSON LEVEL-OF-GENEROSITY DONATION-001) (exhibitsQualityDuringPerformanceOfAction PERSON LEVEL-OF-MISERLINESS DONATION-001)), so long as LEVEL-OF-GENEROSITY and LEVEL-OF-MISERLINESS are of the same degree on the same scale.  For example, the above conjunction would be false if LEVEL-OF-GENEROSITY were (#$HighAmountFn #$Generosity) and LEVEL-OF-MISERLINESS were (#$HighAmountFn #$Miserliness).  However, the above *could* be true if the two differ in degree (e.g., (#$VeryHighAmountFn #$Generosity) versus (#$VeryLowAmountFn #$Miserliness)) or if they appear on different scales (e.g., (#$RelativeGenericValueFn #$degreeOfGenerosity #$UnitedStatesPerson #$veryHighAmountOf) versus (#$RelativeGenericValueFn #$degreeOfMiserliness ObscenelyWealthyPerson #$veryHighAmountOf)).  Notably, contrary properties are capable of combining to form a larger scale that ranges from one #$scaleEndPoints of an interval-type to a #$scaleEndPoints of its contrary interval type (e.g., a scale ranging from the most generous to the most selfish); see #$scaleDefinedByContraries.")
(comment TableInWork-OrdinalFn "A term of the form (#$TableInWork-OrdinalFn (#$ChapterOfWork-OrdinalFn BOOK N) M)
denotes the table in BOOK in chapter N that is numbered M.  If a chapter of BOOK has no tables
or no numbered tables the function is undefined for that chapter.")
(comment HelpingEventTypeFn "This is a function that, applied to a collection (type)  of #$Events, denotes the collection of all #$Events in which one or more #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles help one or more other #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles in an instance of that type of #$Event. (#$HelpingEventTypeFn FOO) denotes the collection of all events in which agents help others in the events of type FOO.   Example: (#$HelpingEventTypeFn #$Buying) refers to the collection of all cases of helping someone to buy or sell something.")
(comment Turbine "The collection of all #$Turbines. Instance of its spec,
#$TurbineEngine, expend #$EnergyStuff to generate #$FluidFlow-Translation while instance of other specs,
e.g. #$HydroPoweredTurbine use #$FluidFlow-Translation to generate #$Electricity.")
(comment recommendedGiftTypeFrom "(#$recommendedGiftTypeFrom REGION PROD-TYPE) means that for people visiting #$GeographicalRegion REGION, gifts of #$ProductType PROD-TYPE are recommended. Typically these gifts will be locally produced and/or products that that region is famous for producing. See #$polityFamousForProductType and #$productTypeOriginatesIn.")
(comment ContentLocator "Instances of #$ContentLocator are abstract objects that are used to
locate #$AspatialInformationStore instances within a system of reference. An
example of a #$ContentLocator would be the location information for a #$Book-CW
in the #$Catalogue of a #$Library-Organization or the document number of a
#$ConceptualWork in a #$Corpus.")
(comment circularAnnulusAtCenterWithRadii "(#$circularAnnulusAtCenterWithRadii REGION CENTER MIN-RADIUS MAX-RADIUS) means that REGION is the circular annulus (region between two concentric circles) determined by the instance CENTER of #$Point and the instances MIN-RADIUS and MAX-RADIUS of #$Distance. The predicate corresponding to the function #$CircularAnnulusFn.")
(comment IssuingAReportAboutASituation "A collection of instances of #$Event.  Each instance is an instance of #$Informing and also of #$CreationEvent in which an #$IntelligentAgent creates and issues an instance of #$WrittenReportOnSituation for an intended target audience.")
(comment AnalysisScriptRelation "A collection of #$Relations, a specialization of
#$SituationTypeRelation.  #$AnalysisScriptRelations are used to specify the
structure of an #$AnalysisProcedure, by application to, or between, a
script, scenes in that script, or actors in those scenes.")
(comment workedOnAssignmentForHoursDuringIntervalWithDescription "An assertion of the form (#$workedOnAssignmentForHoursDuringIntervalWithDescription AGENT ASSIGN QUANT INTERVAL STRING) states that the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT worked on the #$Assignment-Specification ASSIGN for an interval of duration QUANT, some #$Time-Quantity, during the #$TimeInterval INTERVAL and that STRING is a natural language description of that work.  As of August 13, 2004, this is a work-around predicate designed for use with the FET in order to minimize the number of repetitive fields in #$ProjectManagement-TemplateTopic.")
(comment MilitaryScience "A #$FieldOfStudy.  #$MilitaryScience is the discipline that is concerned with the principles of warfare (#$War).")
(comment RadioStation-Shortwave "The collection of #$RadioStation-Organizations that broadcast using a radio wave with a wavelength of between ten and one hundred meters.")
(comment SocialEnvironment "The collection of

 #$Environment-Generics in which #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles interact.")
(comment hasNumberOfCells " '(#$hasNumberOfCells TABLE N)' means that the #$Table-AIS TABLE has N number of cells (see #$cellIn) as component parts.  If the number of rows and columns in a table are known, the number of cells in that table can be calculated.")
(comment ComparisonWRTPredicate "The instances of #$ComparisonWRTPredicate are designed to represent English sentences in which at least two things are explicitly compared with respect to some feature in virtue of which these two things are similar, different, greater, lesser, etc. The respect of comparison serves as an explanation of why/how the two things being compared are similar, different, etc. If it makes no sense to ask for this sort of explanation of a comparison relation, then it is not an instance of #$ComparisonWRTPredicate. For example, #$NumericComparisonPredicates such as #$greaterThan are not #$ComparisonWRTPredicates because it doesn't make sense to ask why/how (#$greaterThan 5 3). A positive example is #$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel because it is used to represent the fact that two things are similar in virtue of the fact that they bear the same relation to similar instances of a given collection. #$similarTo and #$different are negative examples because they do not specify any respect in virtue of which the things in arg1 and arg2 are similar or different. The collection #$ComparisonWRTPredicate can be used to constrain Asks designed to return assertions that represent known comparisons between two specified things. Two important subcollections are #$SimilarityWRTPredicate and #$DifferenceWRTPredicate.")
(comment SubjectRoleMarker "An instance of #$GrammaticalRoleMarker. This attribute is  used to indicate that an argument of a hypothesized formula correspond to the subject (loose sense) of the NL expression which the hypothesis has been derived from. See also #$grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention.")
(comment PuttingSomethingIntoSomething "A specialization of #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomething is an event in which an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible guides a moving object into a new location.")
(comment OperaLibretto-CW "The collection of all #$PlayScripts that supply the narrative structure of an #$Opera-CW. An instance of #$OperaLibretto-CW contains the words to be sung or spoken, as well as the action, scene descriptions, and stage directions of the #$Opera-CW of which it is a #$subWorks. The creator of the #$OperaLibretto-CW may differ from the creator of the #$Opera-CW.")
(comment InherentInItself "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$OriginatingInSomething. In each #$InherentInItself, something is inherent in itself.")
(comment importCapacity "(#$importCapacity REGION PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is the greatest possible rate at which instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE could be imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION.  Note that RATE may be expressed as a #$MonetaryRate, but also as rate of volume, mass or number depending on the type of product.")
(comment DeviceFinishingARun "A collection of events.  An instance of #$DeviceFinishingARun is an event in which some device finishes its normal cycle of processes, e.g., an instance of #$AirplaneLanding.  This is often --- but not always --- the same thing as a device going from the #$Device-On state to the #$Device-Off state --- e.g., the airplane stays `on' for many minutes before it took off.  One could also define the collection dead-start-to-finish-airplane-flight, which would not end with an #$AirplaneLanding but with a true turning-off of the airplane, or even with the exiting of the last crewmember and the post-flight maintenance check of the aircraft.")
(comment amountOfSalesByToDuring "The predicate #$amountOfSalesByToDuring is used to indicate how much of a certain product was sold by a particular seller to a particular buyer.  (#$amountOfSalesByToDuring SELLER BUYER TIMEPD PRODTYPE REVENUE) means that, during the #$TimeInterval TIMEPD, SELLER (an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) sold to BUYER (another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) some amount of the #$ProductType PRODTYPE, worth the total amount of #$MonetaryValue REVENUE.  For example, to say that a restaurant, Threadgills, sold $3000 worth of their pumpkin pies to a local grocery store in November, we would say: (#$amountOfSalesByToDuring Threadgills HEBAt2222 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 1996)) #$PumpkinPie (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 3000)).")
(comment targetPosture "(#$targetPosture TYPE POSTURE) means that POSTURE is the #$AnimalTypeByPosture that the performer will be in at the end of an instance of the #$ChangingPosture type TYPE.")
(comment DeployingMaterial "The collection of all #$Events, particularly in military or terrorist contexts, in which material,           such as #$ExplosiveMaterial or an #$ExplosiveDevice, is moved and placed into a position           serving some strategic purpose for the #$IntelligentAgent performing the deployment.           It is important that the movement and placement serve some strategic purpose for a            particular instance of #$Event to be an instance of #$DeployingMaterial.")
(comment EscapingPrison "The collection of all escapes from #$Prison.  In every instance, some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who was confined to a #$Prison escapes from those confines, against the will of whatever #$Agent-PartiallyTangible was doing the imprisoning (see #$GettingFreeFromControl).  Note that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible doing the escaping may be an individual #$Person or a #$Group of people, provided the #$Group is known to qualify as an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in its own right.")
(comment CoercingAnAgentToMove "A collection of events; a subset of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion.  Each instance of #$CoercingAnAgentToMove is a movement event that is #$performedBy an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. That agent intends for the #$objectMoving, also an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, to move against that agent's desires.  Examples: evicting someone from a residence, taking someone to the police station for questioning, etc.")
(comment FiniteSpatialThing "A specialization of #$SpatialThing.  Each instance of #$FiniteSpatialThing is a spatial thing that measures a finite #$Distance in all of its dimensions (see #$extensionParametersOfObject).  A finite line (see #$LinearObject-Finite) has finite length; an finite surface has a finite length and finite \"width\"; and an finite three-dimensional spatial thing has finite length, finite \"width\", and finite \"height\".
<p>
A finite spatial thing might be tangible or intangible.  Cf. #$InfiniteSpatialThing.")
(comment SegmentedCordlikeObject "The collection of instances of #$CordlikeObject that consists of a series of smaller units, easily identifiable as 'segments.' A prototypical example is a #$Chain, which is a cordlike or strandlike object made up of a series of links.  Though in the typical case, the segments of an instance of #$SegmentedCordlikeObject will be of a different kind than the object itself (the links of a chain are typically not themselves chains), this need not be the case (consider a chain of links that are themselves chains formed into hoops).  Typically, for any instance SEGOBJ of #$SegmentedCordlikeObject, (#$seriesMemberType SEGOBJ TYPE) implies (#$relationInstanceExists #$groupMembers SEGOBJ TYPE).")
(comment FoodServiceOrganization "A subcollection of #$CommercialServiceOrganization. An instance of #$FoodServiceOrganization is a business which prepares and/or serves food as its major function(s). Important subcollections of #$FoodServiceOrganization include #$Restaurant-Organization and #$CateringOrganization. Note that grocery stores -- and airlines -- are not themselves considered elements of #$FoodServiceOrganization, even though some of those may have #$subOrganizations or sub-contractors which are #$FoodServiceOrganizations. Bars or taverns, in contrast to #$Restaurant-Organizations that also prepare and serve food, are also not considered #$FoodServiceOrganizations.")
(comment regionLacksTransportMeans "(#$regionLacksTransportMeans REGION TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity REGION has no regular, major use of or access to transport by means of instances of TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE.  For example, a #$LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity like #$SanMarino may lack #$Ships.")
(comment Visibility "A specialization of #$WeatherQuantity.  Each instance of #$Visibility is a measure of how clear the ambient fluid at a location is.  Higher values indicate one can see farther (than one could have at lower values at the same location).  Different degrees of visibility may be designated using a #$GenericValueFunction.  Visibility at a location is expressed with the predicate #$ambientVisibility.")
(comment PosteriorDirection "The general direction towards the front and away from the back, in or near an object that has attribute #$AnimalShapedThing and has an #$UprightPosture.  In the case of a #$Person or other object that is #$HumanShaped, this direction almost always corresponds to #$VentralDirection.")
(comment SupplyingMeansOfCommunication "This collection comprises a large class of (possibly extensive in time and complex)           instances of #$PurposefulAction.  In each instance of this collection some           instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, an  instance of (#$GroupFn #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) or simply some collection of instances           of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (e.g. the #$Persons in some neighborhood) gain some kind of user rights           to some #$Artifact, e.g. a post office or a radio, that is #$behaviorCapable           of being an #$instrument-Generic in some subcollection of #$InformationTransferEvent.")
(comment MarkingOnASurface "A specialization of both #$MaterialHandling and #$IBOCreation.  Each instance of #$MarkingOnASurface is an event in which visible markings are placed on a surface by an agent (see the collection #$Agent-PartiallyTangible).  The marking may be done by adding material to a surface (as in instances of #$Painting-Activity) or removing material from a surface (as in instances of #$EngravingEvent).")
(comment Latin-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
Latin style.                            ")
(comment Blockquote-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a quote from an external source that will be indented in the #$GraphicalStructure generated by the #$HTMLSource.")
(comment monumentHonors "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$MemorialMarker to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (note that each such instance may be an individual or a group). (#$monumentHonors MONUMENT HONOREE(S)) means that MONUMENT is a #$MemorialMarker constructed to honor or commemorate HONOREE(S), and to cause people who perceive MONUMENT to remember and respect HONOREE(S). As an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, HONOREE(S) must not be an event or a physical object. (For honoring these, see the more general #$artifactHonors).  Usually, but not always, the MONUMENT is built by someone other than HONOREE(S) (but some people build monuments to themselves).  If HONOREE(S) is living when MONUMENT is built, HONOREE(S) may be present at an #$Event of announcing, inaugurating or unveiling the MONUMENT; see #$eventHonors.")
(comment entailsRoleInSubEventOfType "(#$entailsRoleInSubEventOfType SYS-SLOT

SYS-EVENT-TYPE SYS-ACT-SLOT AG-EVENT-TYPE AGT-ACT-SLOT) means that if

an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible plays the functional role SYS-SLOT in a #$FunctionalSystem,

and the system plays the actor role SYS-ACT-SLOT in an event of type

SYS-EVENT-TYPE, then there is an expectation that there exists an

event of type AG-EVENT-TYPE such that it is a #$subEvents of the event

of type SYS-EVENT-TYPE and such that the agent who plays the

functional role SYS-SLOT plays the actor role AGT-ACT-SLOT in it.")
(comment intervalSize "A functional predicate that relates a given #$ScalarInterval to its breadth expressed as an (at least partly numeric) #$ScalarPointValue (<i>q.v.</i>) on the same scale.  <code>(#$intervalSize INTERVAL SIZE)</code> means that <code>SIZE</code> is the breadth of <code>INTERVAL</code>: the difference between the maximum and the minimum value of <code>INTERVAL</code>.
<p>
If <code>INTERVAL</code> is a #$Quantity (<i>q.v.</i>), its size is also a quantity -- measured in the same units (if any; see #$UnitOfMeasure) as <code>INTERVAl</code>.  If <code>INTERVAL</code> is a #$NumericInterval, its size is a #$RealNumber.  If <code>INTERVAL</code> is itself a #$ScalarPointValue, its size is null (see #$ScalarNullValue).
<p>
Note that not all scalar intervals have a size.  For example, instances of #$NonNumericScalarQuantity generally do not.")
(comment NullLevelOfVirulence "The lowest #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionVirulenceLevel.")
(comment Friendliness "Emotion manifested by interest in another person (or, more rarely, in some nonhuman agent), good will towards that individual, and an inclination to favor him or her (or it).  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Friendliness are #$Love and #$Love-Romantic.")
(comment ProtestantPerson "The collection of people who adhere to a faith in

#$ProtestantReligion. The basic tenet of Protestantism is the non-mandatory

role of the #$Priest as an intercessionary between a believer and #$GodOfAbrahamIsaacAndJacob,

or between a believer and the proper interpretation of the holy texts (such as

the #$Bible). As a divergence from #$Catholicism, Protestants generally believe in

a school of Christianity that differs in some key

respects. Among the chief differences are: #$CatholicPerson shows more devotion

to #$Mary-MotherOfJesus, and has a belief in

#$Transubstantiation -- the process whereby bread is turned into the body of 

#$JesusChrist). Some subclasses of #$ProtestantPerson view the latter as being

of symbolic import only (e.g., #$AnglicanReligion), while followers of the #$LutheranReligion

school believe in #$Transubstantiation as a transformation, but deny the

necessary role of the #$Priest as an agent of this transformation.")
(comment BondageAndDiscipline "This is the collection of sexual activities in which both #$Bondage-Sexual and

#$Discipline-Sexual occur. ")
(comment FiscalYear "Each instance of this collection is an annual, year-long interval of time kept track of by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible as part of its operational and financial accounting procedures.  Since the start dates and end dates may vary depending on the organization, instances of this collection are time intervals like FiscalYearOf1989ForMicrosoft")
(comment minimumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint "Let SLOT denote an #$QuantitySlot, SLOT-ARG1 denote the #$arg1Isa constraint on SLOT,  SLOT-ARG2 denote the #$arg2Isa constraint on SLOT, and VALUE denote the instance of SLOT-ARG2 such that          (SLOT O-TYPE VALUE).  Then (#$minimumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint          PATH O-TYPE SLOT MIN) means that PATH is #$pathTrafficableForTransportVia          #$transporters of type O-TYPE only if (#$greaterThanOrEqualTo VALUE MIN).  See also the related          predicates #$maximumTrafficableValue-TransporterConstraint,          #$maximumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint, and          #$minimumTrafficableValue-PathConstraint.")
(comment ComputerGameProgram-SimulationGod "The collection of instances of #$ComputerGameProgram wherein the major playing activity consists in constructing a model
or simulation of some functioning thing. The enjoyment in these games comes from playing God, so to speak. The prime examples of this genre are
the various Sim- games, such as #$SimCityClassic-TheGame. Flying and driving
games are simulations of an experience rather than the creation of a model and 
are not necessarily instances of #$ComputerGameProgram-SimulationGod.")
(comment makesVulnerableToDegree "(#$makesVulnerableToDegree SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE DEGREE) means that when in            situation SITUATION, existing object OBJECT is vulnerable to hardships of type            RESULT-TYPE to degree DEGREE. The baseline level of vulnerability is #$lowAmountOf,           when sound security measures are in place, vulnerability is #$veryLowAmountOf,  and when            more than one situation makes an object vulnerable to the same ill effect,            vulnerability to that effect increases.")
(comment feelsTowardsObject-Ternary "(#$feelsTowardsObject-Ternary AGENT OBJECT FEELING) says that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent AGENT feels the feeling FEELING towards OBJECT.  For example, (#$feelsTowardsObject-Ternary (#$GovernmentFn #$Israel) #$YassirArafat (#$HighAmountFn #$Distrust)) says that the Israeli government feels a high amount of distrust towards Yassir Arafat.  See also #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree.")
(comment agentViolatesObligation "(#$agentViolatesObligation AGENT OB)  means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is in violation of the #$Obligation OB.  Note that the class of #$Obligations is very wide, and can include many  types of 'obligation,' e.g., etiquette, moral codes, military rules of  engagement, etc.  See also #$agentFulfillsObligation.")
(comment Dexterity "#$Dexterity is the #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType for describing actions in which the performer's hands move accurately, quickly, and with economy of motion. Here is an example of the constant in use: (#$skillLevel #$JimiHendrix #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument #$performedBy #$Dexterity

#$veryHighAmountOf)).")
(comment AdjustableRateMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements for which either the #$interestRate charged or the term of the loan (see #$LoanAgreementTypeByTermOption), or both, can change.")
(comment goalSituationType "#$goalSituationType is a simple but powerful means of
representing a desired event type.  This predicate relates a
#$GoalSituation to a #$Collection which has #$Situation as a #$genls.
(#$goalSituationType GOAL-SITUATION DESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE) means that at
least one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (such agents are identified by #$goalAgent) has a
goal, desire, want or need to play a role (this role is identified by
#$goalRoleSlot) in some instance of DESIRED-SITUATION-TYPE.  For
example (#$goalSituationType `GoalSituation001' #$TakingAShower) means
that during `GoalSituation001' any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001'
wants to play some role in #$TakingAShower.  If (#$goalRoleSlot
`GoalSituation002' #$performedBy) is also asserted, then this
specifies that any #$goalAgent for `GoalSituation001' wishes to play
the role of #$performedBy in some element of #$TakingAShower.  In
other words, \"someone wishes to take a shower\".  If one wishes to
assert that \"Fred wishes to take a shower.\" then one would add the
assertion (#$goalAgent `GoalSituation002' `Fred').  Compared with
#$goalSituationSuccessIf predicate has limitations in terms of
expressivity.  However, it has more inferencing power.  See (#$VersusFn
(#$TheSet #$goalSituationType #$goalRoleSlot) #$goalSituationSuccessIf) for more
on this issue.")
(comment Obligation "A specialization of #$NormativeSpecification.  Each instance of the collection #$Obligation is specification of what some agent (related to the obligation via #$obligatedAgents (q.v.)) is obliged to do, or make true, for one or more other agents or possibly 'for' society in general.  An obligation is the most general case of some agent owing something to another.  Obligations may be undertaken in conjunction with various kinds of #$Agreements.   Unlike an agreement, however, an obligation need not have a second known party (though some do).  An obligation can exist and be understood without identifying another particular agent as the 'holder' of the obligation -- and that may be true, even if the beneficiary (#$obligationOwedTo) can be identified.  For example, assuming that parents have an obligation to care for their children, it is not clear with whom a parent has 'agreed' to take care of his or her child.  Some common ways to incur an obligation are through social transactions (e.g. family duties, friendship, favors) or through financial transactions (e.g. a #$PaymentObligation).   In addition, obligations may be imposed on those who are subject to one or more instances of #$CodeOfConduct, e.g. #$SportsRulesOf-BoxingSportsEvent or #$OfficeCodeOfConduct.")
(comment TVLoveStory "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs, those that are primarily intended to tell love stories or          parts of them.")
(comment tasksOfTypeSupport "A predicate that relates specializations of #$PurposefulAction.  (#$tasksOfTypeSupport SUPPORTER SUPPORTED) says that for any assigned task (see #$AssignedActionType) that is a specialization of SUPPORTED, it is expected that there should be a distinct assignment, a specialization of SUPPORTER, such that (#$coaSupportingTask SUPPORTER SUPPORTED).")
(comment SouthAmericanCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located in the #$ContinentOfSouthAmerica.  A person native to an area of South America not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$SouthAmericanCitizenOrSubject.")
(comment Stealing-Embezzlement "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Stealing-InsideJob.  In an instance of #$Stealing-Embezzlement, an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible steals objects, usually money, which that agent was trusted not to steal.  (It is because of that trust that the embezzler has some privileged access to the things stolen, which facilitates the embezzlement.)  The perpetrator need not be in the same physical location with the stolen object during the stealing, since embezzlement is sometimes accomplished by manipulating ledger entries, account balances, bank deposits, funds transfers, and other financial data and activities, which can be done at a site remote from the money, rather than by physically removing the valuables.")
(comment Fraud "The collection of all willful misrepresentations intended to deprive another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible of some right, esp. user rights for a valuable possession or money.")
(comment NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory is an automotive product sold at a new auto dealership (not including the cars themselves).")
(comment Quartet-MusicalPerformanceGroup "A #$Quartet-MusicalPerformanceGroup is a group of 4 musicians that perform together.")
(comment agentIdeologyDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentIdeologyDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses the fact that AGENT has a certain ideology (during some time interval).")
(comment accountHolder "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to instances of #$Account.  (#$accountHolder ACCT AGENT) means that the account ACCT is held by the individual or organization AGENT; thus, money (or some other valuable such as vacation leave) is owed to or from AGENT in the amount shown in the account (see #$accountBalance), and can be added to or drawn upon.")
(comment PreviouslyOwnedFn "The set of arg1's that have already been bought and sold, at least once.  See also #$UsedArtifact.")
(comment feelsSensationInRegionAtLevel "(#$feelsSensationInRegionAtLevel AGT BODYPARTTYPE QUANT) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGT feels on its body, in the area specified by BODYPARTTYPE, the quantity of the #$SensoryQuantity indicated by QUANT.  For example, Cyc's knowledge base contains an assertion that the very same part of one's body doesn't feel both hot and cold at the same time.  #$feelsSensationInRegionAtLevel can also be used to state symptoms, e.g., when you're feverish, your head feels hot.")
(comment nodeCutSetInSystem "(#$nodeCutSetInSystem SET SYS) means that the set SET of nodes in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS is a node-cut set in SYS, i.e., SET is a subset of (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) such that cutting of all nodes in SET from SYS results in a disconnected path system.  More strictly, to say that SET is a node-cut set in SYS, we mean that SET is a proper subset of (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) and (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) is not a #$ConnectedPathSystem.  Note that when (#$nodeCutSetInSystem SET SYS) holds, there could be some proper subset SUBSET of SET such that (#$nodeCutSetInSystem SUBSET SYS) also holds.  If you want a minimal node-cut set, without redundant nodes, use #$nodeCutMinimalSetInSystem instead of #$nodeCutSetInSystem.")
(comment TVHobbyShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs each intended primarily to convey information about a hobby, e.g.             cooking, gardening or woodworking.")
(comment TomTom "The collection of #$DrumInstrument's usually beaten with the hands and generally producing a high pitch (for drums). #$TomTom's are conventionally associated with American Indians (i.e., #$EthnicGroupOfNativeAmericansOfTheUS).")
(comment IndustryType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$IndustryType is a general industry, by function, which is the collection of all local or geographically-defined industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized) that perform that function.  So the funeral industry in general is an instance of #$IndustryType, whereas the Ohio funeral industry is an instance of #$Industry-Localized (as is the worldwide funeral industry whose 'locale' is just large).  Every instance of #$IndustryType can have local examples of #$Industry-Localized as its instances.  See also #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn, #$IndustryOfRegionFn, and #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.")
(comment amountForGenValueColAndPred "(#$amountForGenValueColAndPred VALUE PRED COL GVP) means that
VALUE is the amount which is in the range of the quantity expressed by the 
NART '(#$RelativeGenericValueFn PRED COL GVP)'.  Consider this example, Assertion A: (#$amountForGenValueColAndPred (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 6.5) #$heightOfObject #$BasketballPlayer #$highAmountOf).  This means that 6.5 feet is subsumed by (GenValueFn #$heightOfObject #$BasketballPlayer #$highAmountOf).  The NART itself is the quantity of height that is had by basketball players we consider \"tall\".  So, such an assertion entails that 6.5 feet is tall for a basketball player.  In other words, 6.5 is a high value on the slot #$heightOfObject for any #$BasketballPlayer.")
(comment PersonalAd "A collection of ads (#$Advertisement-PCW) placed by individuals trying to find a person with whom to establish a new romantic or other relationship. They generally include information about the gender, age, physical characteristics, hobbies, profession, etc. of the poster together with a description of what kind of person he or she is seeking.")
(comment Minim-UnitOfVolume "#$Minim-UnitOfVolume is a measurement of volume on a near-microscopic scale.")
(comment AnalysisScriptFromGraphFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction. (#$AnalysisScriptFromGraphFn GRAPH) denotes the specialization of #$AnalysisProcedure that the #$Graph-AIS GRAPH depicts.")
(comment few "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate and #$GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotoneDecreasing.  <code>(#$few SOC1 SOC2)</code> means the same as <code>(#$not (#$many SOC1 SOC2))</code>.")
(comment SportingGoodsMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.   Each element of #$SportingGoodsMarketCategory  is a piece of sports-related equipment, clothing, or accessories sold in sporting goods stores and sporting goods departments, e.g., basketballs, swimsuits, and bicycles.  #$SportingGoodsMarketCategory does NOT include large,  sports-related specialty items such as motorcycles and yachts.")
(comment (ApplyingForFn JobPosition) "The collection of actions in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible makes an application to an #$employer for a job.")
(comment LibraryLoanAgreement "A specialization of #$LoanAgreement.  In each instance of #$LibraryLoanAgreement, a member of #$Library-Organization borrows (see #$BorrowingLibraryItem) some #$Library-Organization items.  The borrower agrees to return (see #$ReturningLibraryItem) the borrowed library-items within the stipulated #$loanTermDuration.  There may be options of #$RenewingLibraryItem also.")
(comment Corundum "An #$AluminumOxide-Al2O3 #$Mineral from which the #$GemStones #$Ruby-Gem and #$Sapphire-Gem are derived.")
(comment PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent "A specialization of #$AttackOnTangible and #$ViolentAction. Each instance of this collection is an event in which one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or a small group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles) physically attacks another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or small group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.) Such attacks often (but not always) result in an instance of #$HarmingAnAgent. Notable specializations of this collection include #$Charging-Rushing, #$HittingAnOpponent, and #$SexualAssault. #$PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent events are also sub-events of each instance of #$Fight-Physical and #$Battle.")
(comment MethylAmmoniumIon "A specialization of #$PolyatomicIon.  Each instance of #$MethylAmmoniumIon is an ion composed of #$MethylGroup and #$AmmoniumIon.")
(comment cwSeriesType "(#$cwSeriesType SERIESTYPE EPISODETYPE) means that each of the #$episodes of every instance of SERIESTYPE #$isa EPISODETYPE. Example: (#$cwSeriesType #$ComputerGameSeries #$ComputerGameProgram) means that every episode of a computer game series is a computer game.")
(comment seller "The predicate #$seller relates an agent to an event in which some item is sold.  <code>(#$seller EXCHANGE AGENT)</code> means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>AGENT</code> sells something in the #$MonetaryExchangeOfUserRights <code>EXCHANGE</code>.")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifier-NonMonotone "A #$PredicateType.  Each instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-NonMonotone is a #$GeneralizedQuantifier that is an instance of neither #$GeneralizedQuantifier-MonotoneIncreasing nor #$GeneralizedQuantifier-RightMonotoneDecreasing (qq.v.).")
(comment IslamicRepublic "A #$SystemOfGovernment in which the #$HeadOfState is not a #$Monarch-HeadOfState and the country's #$majorReligions is #$Islam.--Siegel, May 17, 1996")
(comment SuddenChange "The #$RateOfChange that indicates a change that takes a short amount of time.")
(comment TVActionShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that tell an action or adventure            story.")
(comment mtTime "A #$MicrotheoryPredicate that is used to indicate a period of time throughout which the assertions in a given microtheory hold true. (#$mtTime MT TEMP-THING) means that the assertions in the #$Microtheory MT hold true throughout (the existence, persistence or duration of) TEMP-THING. Since TEMP-THING is restricted only to instances of #$TemporalThing, it covers a wide range of entities -- for e.g. instances of #$Person, #$Event, #$Artifact or (of course) #$TimeInterval. See also #$MtTimeFn and #$publicationTimeOfMTAssertions.")
(comment ThwartingAThreatGoal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory and a spec-attribute of #$PreventionGoal.
As in #$PreventionGoal, a goal has this attribute if the goal involves
taking actions to prevent some kind of event from occurring. In this case,
the agent has reason to believe that the undesirable event will occur since
there has been a #$Threat that suggests that it will.")
(comment Gambling "The collection of acts of wagering #$MonetaryValue or #$Property on an uncertain outcome.  Typically involves a #$GameOfChance.")
(comment PascalChallengeKBContentTest-QATask "These are KBCTs which test whether Cyc can solve a particular #$TextualInferenceProblem-PascalFormat which is part of the \"QA\" task (c.f.#$PascalChallengeQATask).")
(comment Windiness "A specialization of #$WeatherQuantity and #$Speed.  Each instance of #$Windiness is a measure of how windy it is in a particular #$OutdoorLocation.  At the low extreme (#$NoAmountFn #$Windiness), it is calm.  At the high extreme (#$VeryHighAmountFn #$Windiness) The wind is moving extremely fast.  To attribute a particular wind speed (e.g. 35 m.p.h.) use #$ambientWindSpeed.")
(comment Frustration "A feeling of irritation and dissatisfaction arising from unresolved problems or unfulfilled needs.  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.")
(comment MasterSergeant-Rank "The maximal rank a non-commissioned officer may achieve in the U.S. Army.  In the U.S. Army, a person of #$MasterSergeant-Rank is outranked by any person whose rank is a #$CommissionedOfficerTypeByRank or a #$WarrantOfficerTypeByRank.  In the U.S. Marine Corps,  #$MasterSergeant-Rank is intermediate between #$GunnerySergeant-Rank and #$FirstSergeant-Rank.")
(comment SomeExampleFunctionOfTypeFn "(#$SomeExampleFunctionOfTypeFn COL) denotes a term which represents an indeterminate instance of COL for use in generating an example. See also #$SomeExampleNumberFn.")
(comment PreparingForSituation "The collection of #$PurposefulActions in which an agent prepares for a situation (#$Situation). The action can be entirely mental, as in #$MakingAPlan, or can involve #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvents, for example, buying food as a preparation for cooking a meal. The action may make the situation prepared for more likely to happen or it may have no causal bearing on that situation. For example, preparing for college may make it more likely that the agent will attend college. However, preparing for a power outage by buying a flashlight doesn't make it more likely that the power outage will occur. See also #$PreparingForUndesirableSituation. To relate #$PreparingForSituations to the #$Situation types that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparingForSitTypeFn. To relate #$PreparingForUndesirableSituations to the #$Situations that they prepare for, use the function #$PreparednessFn. See also #$PreventingFromHappening and #$PreventingFn.")
(comment ChangingDeviceState "A specialization of both #$PhysicalEvent and #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent (q.v.).  The collection of events in which a device goes from one basic state (the #$fromState) to another (the #$toState).  A change of #$DeviceTypeByState (q.v.) might be due to an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible adjusting the device, or it might happen automatically due to the behavior of the device itself.  The two most general state changes (for powered devices) are from #$Device-On to #$Device-Off, and vice versa.  Many other states peculiar to specific devices can be identified.  For example, the states of a #$Dishwasher include #$DeviceState-Washing and #$DeviceState-Rinsing; and the states of a trapping device might include #$TrapArmed, #$TrapTripped, and #$TrapIdle.  Specializations of #$ChangingDeviceState include #$UnlockingALock, #$ChargingABattery, and #$ComputerCrashing.")
(comment odorThreshold "A binary predicate relating specializations of #$PartiallyTangible to instances of #$ConcentrationStrength. Basically, (#$odorThreshold SUBSTANCE CONCENTRATION) means that CONCENTRATION is the minimum concentration at which SUBSTANCE is smellable; more precisely, it means that if AIR is an arbitrary, sensibly-sized instance of #$Air, and if the concentration of SUBSTANCE in AIR is greater than or equal to CONCENTRATION (see #$concentration), then AIR itself emits the odor associated with SUBSTANCE (see #$objectEmitsOdor and #$OdorFn).")
(comment ObtainingFn "A unary function that returns the class of events in which instances of the function argument are obtained.  For example, (#$ObtainingFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium) returns those events in which #$Anthrax-Bacterium are obtained.  This function is particularly useful for type-level claims about certain kinds of events (e.g., (#$subEventTypes (#$SmugglingFn ?STUFF) (#$ObtainingFn ?STUFF))).")
(comment ComplementaryBasePairingError "#$ComplementaryBasePairingError is the collection of #$BasePairing events in which there is an error in base-pairing.  Normally, the #$NitrogenBases that are paired in an instance of #$BasePairing are complementary (see #$complementaryBases). However, although it occurs infrequently, it is chemically possible for two #$NitrogenBases that are not complementary to become paired. When this happens, biologists regard it as a base pairing error.")
(comment PreventionGoal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory.  A goal has this attribute for an agent if the goal involves taking actions to prevent some kind of event from occurring.")
(comment GeneralAutoMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$GeneralAutoMarketCategory is an automotive product typically sold in auto parts stores, e.g. spark plugs, gaskets, wrenches, fuzzy dice, etc.")
(comment typesDifferInQualitativeFeatureRelatedTo "(#$typesDifferInQuantityRelatedTo COL1 COL2 ATT-COL BINPRED) means that instances of COL1 will be related to a different instance(s) of ATT-COL by BINPRED than will instances of COL2. Note that if ATT-COL is ordered, the collection that will take on \"greater\" instances of ATT-COLL is to appear in the first argument place. ")
(comment SurfaceConstrainedMultiRevolutionRotation "#$MultirevolutionRotation constrained by contact along the surface of the rotating object with another object instead of by a fixed #$Axis (see #$AxisConstrainedMultirevolutionRotation) or by support of a projection of the axis (see #$SpinLikeATop).")
(comment CapturingSomething "Every instance of #$CapturingSomething is an instance of #$TransferOfControl in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is captured, in the sense that his, her, or its freedom of action is circumscribed in some important respect.  In every instance of #$CapturingSomething, the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible that #$losesControl is the same as the #$objectOfControlTransfer:  in fact, this is a definitive feature of instances of the collection.")
(comment BayesNet "The collection of all Bayesian Networks intended for probability reasoning.  A #$BayesNet is a network of nodes in which the nodes are random variables that each typically represent the likelihood of a proposition being true (expressed as a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true).  See #$bayesNetOfMicrotheory.  Each #$BayesNet interconnects a set of propositions (or symbols associated with propositions) together forming a #$DirectedAcyclicGraph in which the links (the #$bayesParent link) represent a probabilistic conditional dependence between the directly linked nodes.  Such a network may be established by asserting (or concluding) #$bayesParent predications linking pairs of propositions.  There is a 'closed-world assumption' for every #$BayesNet, in that pairs of propositions not explicitly linked with #$bayesParent are assumed to be not linked.  In addition, a node is #$conditionallyIndependentSentences the truth values of its #$bayesParents (and no other nodes) - from all nodes other than its 'descendants' in the #$BayesNet.  A #$BayesNet is a representation of the entire (strictly positive) joint probability distribution over the random variables.   The #$derivedProbability of a node can be calculated from the probabilities of its #$bayesParents.  (There are always one or more 'source' nodes with no #$bayesParents.)  Theoretically, viewed as evidential links based on the joint probability distribution, the #$bayesParent links are bidirectional.   The direction of the links is obtained formally due to an asymmetry between 'parents' and 'children': the truth of a node induces a conditional dependence among its #$bayesParents (the 'explaining away' effect), which does not seem to apply to its Bayesian 'child' nodes.  Most Bayesian network theorists consider that the directions on the links correspond to the direction of causal influence, and hence to the direction of time. The name 'Bayesian' is due to the Reverend Thomas Bayes, whose inversion rule was published posthumously in 1763, and later developed by Laplace.  Bayesian Networks were devised chiefly by Judea Pearl in the 1980s.")
(comment interests "(#$interests AGT INT GVP) means that AGT's interest
in INT is described by GVP. For example (#$interests Bob Kayaking #$highToVeryHighAmountOf)
means that Bob is very interested in Kayaking. Note that #$interests can also be used
to describe an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's lack of interest in something.")
(comment SpinLikeATop "Spinning of an object about a near vertical axis.  The #$Axis of rotation rests or moves about a surface which is usually somewhat horizontal.  If the axis of spin is not directly vertical, gravitational force will cause the spinning object to experience #$Precession.  During the spin the velocity of rotation slows down so the #$Stabilizing factor decreases.  The object may translate about the supporting surface as it spins.")
(comment instructionsForEventType "(#$instructionsForEventType INSTRUCTIONS EVENT_TYPE) means that the #$PropositionalConceptualWork, INSTRUCTIONS, contains instructions on how to perform EVENT_TYPE.  People use instantiations of INSTRUCTIONS [#$instantiationOfWork] to know how to perform instances of EVENT_TYPE.  See #$instructionsUsed-IBT.")
(comment VentralDirection "The general direction toward the stomach side, away from the backside, in or near an object with shape #$AnimalShapedThing.  In the case of a #$Person this is the #$VectorInterval comprising the cone-shaped set of vectors pointing (from some reference point) within approximately forty-five degrees of straight in front when in an #$UprightPosture.")
(comment CompositionWithSoloistAndAccompaniment "The collection of all #$MusicalComposition-Classicals with a clear soloist or solists, and another performer or set of performers whose role is to accompany the soloist. Does not include #$ChamberMusicCompositions, where the performers have roughly equal roles, or works for single performers (i.e., instances of #$CompositionForSoloInstrument), which do not have a separate accompaniment.")
(comment opponentsInSitType "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate. 
  (#$opponentsInSitType AGT1 AGT2 TYPE) says that 
  (#$situationTypeIsSuchThat TYPE 
    (#$opponents AGT1 AGT2))).  In other words, situations of type TYPE are typically such that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles AGT1 and AGT2 are opponents.  TYPE need not be a spec of #$ConflictEvent; two units could be opponents in a #$CourseOfAction without directly engaging each other (see, #$coaOpponents).")
(comment similarWRTPartType "This predicate relates pairs of things to the kinds of physical parts they have in common and which are instantiated similarly in each.  (#$similarWRTPartType THING1 THING2 PART-TYPE) means that THING1 and THING2 both have parts that are instances of PART-TYPE and these parts are similar to each other.  For instance, (#$similarWRTPartType MUSCLE-CAR1 MUSCLE-CAR2 #$GasolineEngine) means that MUSCLE-CAR1 and MUSCLE-CAR2 both have instances of #$GasolineEngine as parts and these engines are similar to each other.  Obviously, judgements of similarity are going to be highly context dependent.  To relate things in terms of attributes that they share, see #$resemblesInQuantity and #$identicalInQuantity.  To discuss part similarity at a type level, see #$typesSimilarWRTPartType.")
(comment EntryPointsFn "An instance of #$Function-Denotational and #$UnaryFunction
that takes an
instance of #$PathSystem as an argument and returns the
collection of entry points into that system.  
(#$EntryPointsFn PATH_SYS) denotes the subcollection of
(#$PointsInSystemFn PATH_SYS), i.e. the collection of points of
the instance PATH_SYS
of #$PathSystem, that are entry points into PATH_SYS, i.e.
the collection of all points POINT such that
(#$entryPointToSystem POINT PATH_SYS) holds.  See also
#$entryPointOnPathToSystem and #$entryPathToSystem.")
(comment normOpponents "<code>(#$normOpponents NORM AGENT)</code> means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>AGENT</code> dislikes the #$NormativeSpecification <code>NORM</code> and opposes it.  <code>AGENT</code> need not be related to <code>NORM</code> in any other way (<i>e.g.</i>, via  #$normativelyBoundAgents or #$specifiedActors (qq.v.)).  See also #$normProponents.")
(comment ClassifiedAd "A collection of ads (#$Advertisement-PCW) that are part of a group of ads published together in one section of a #$PeriodicalIssue or otherwise made available together, and arranged into categories depending on the type or content of the ads. #$ClassifiedAds are generally short, consisting of just a few lines of #$TextualMaterial.")
(comment SourcesReliable "Characteristic attribute of a #$WrittenReportOnSituation with  reliable sources.")
(comment DancePerformance "#$DancePerformance is the collection of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent such that (#$PerformingFn #$DancePerformance) returns,

among other things, a set which is the union of the collection,

#$Dancing-Human, and all of which instances are done either live, in

front of an audience, or for a camera, as part of the production of a

film for television or the movies.")
(comment relationExistsAllMany "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.)that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relationship with two collections.  (#$relationExistsAllMany BINPRED COL1 COL2) means that for every instance INST of COL2, there are many (see #$Many-Quant) instances INST(i) of COL1 such that (BINPRED INST(i) INST).  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
(#$implies
(#$isa ?INST COL2)
(#$thereExistRange #$Many-Quant ?INST-I
(#$and
(#$isa ?INST COL1)
(BINPRED ?INST-I ?INST)))) .
<p>
For example, `(#$relationExistsAllMany #$soldAt #$PostageStamp #$PostOfficeOrganization)' means many postage stamps are sold at each post office.  Cf. #$relationAllExistsMany, and see #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
(comment Excitement "A feeling of arousal that stirs up, moves profoundly, or serves as a challenge to one's power, eliciting the desire to do or perceive something.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Excitement include #$Enthusiasm, #$Celebratory-Emotion, #$Triumph, etc.")
(comment GNucleotideCap "The collection of molecular structures appended to the 5' ends of #$EukaryoticMessengerRNAs during #$CappingProcess-ChemicalReaction. Each instance of #$GNucleotideCap consists of a #$GuanineRibonucleotide with a methyl group attached.")
(comment ConceptFilterParameterType-Mode "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Each instance of this collection is a parameter that tells an application that uses #$ConceptFilters what sort of terms it should display.  Currently, this collection has two instances: #$ConceptOnlyFilterParameter and #$ConceptAndInstancesFilterParameter.")
(comment agentFulfillsAssignment "An assertion of the form (#$agentFulfillsAssignment AGENT ASSIGN) asserts that the appropriate sorts of actions have been performed to satisfy the #$Assignment-Specification ASSIGN.  Thus, the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT's obligation has been discharged.")
(comment IndirectObjectRoleMarker "An instance of #$GrammaticalRoleMarker. This attribute is  used to indicate that an argument of a hypothesized formula correspond to the indirect object (loose sense) of the NL expression which the hypothesis has been derived from. See also #$grammaticalRoleWRTRelationMention..")
(comment exportAmountDuring "(#$exportAmountDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile exports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars exported.  In the case of oil exports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil exported, or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil exported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of export of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil exports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).  The total value of a region's exports of all goods and services (over a given time period) can be expressed with this predicate using the constant #$Product as the second argument.")
(comment CircularAnnulusFn "This function returns the spatial difference of two concentric octagons centered at a given point.
More formally, (#$CircularAnnulusFn POINT MIN-RADIUS MAX-RADIUS)
denotes the annulus determined by the instance POINT of
#$Point and the instances MIN-RADIUS and MAX-RADIUS
of #$Distance.  The vertices of the inner octagon are all of a fixed distance MIN-RADIUS from POINT, while the vertices of the outer octagon are all of a fixed distance MAX-RADIUS from POINT.  See also the predicate #$circularAnnulusAtCenterWithRadii.")
(comment MusicVideoTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily show music videos.")
(comment mortalityRiskForCondition "This relation is used to specify the 'mortality risk' for a particular type of #$AilmentCondition.  We conceive this risk to be the prior #$ProbabilityInterval that an individual afflicted with a particular AilmentCondition will die of that condition.  Alternatively (and equivalently) the relation can be viewed as making a prediction about the percentage of individuals in a population afflicted with a certain AilmentCondition that will ultimately die as the result of having that condition, assuming normal conditions and no preventative/ameliorative measures.")
(comment HydroniumOrHydroxideIon "A specialization of #$PolyatomicIon, and the union of #$HydroniumIon and #$HydroxideIon.  Each instance of #$HydroniumOrHydroxideIon is either an instance of #$HydroxideIon or #$HydroniumIon.")
(comment InfotainmentTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that present information or news in a             way intended to be entertaining.")
(comment num-GenQuantRelnTo "An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifierRelation (q.v.). (#$num-GenQuantRelnTo RELN COL THING NUM) is true if for exactly NUM instances X of COL (RELN X THING) holds.  For example, 

 (#$num-GenQuantRelnTo #$objectFoundInLocation #$Pizzeria  #$CityOfAustinTX 5) means that there are exactly five pizzerias in Austin, Tex.  The second argument place of this predicate is constrained to instances of #$SetOrCollection -- the more specific #$relationExistsCountInstance (the second argument place of which is constrained to instances of #$Collection) should be used instead of #$num-GenQuantRelnTo whenever possible.")
(comment MuseumStructure "A specialization of #$Landmark, #$ModernShelterConstruction, and #$DisplayStructure.  Each instance of #$MuseumStructure is a construct used to store and display museum holdings (see #$MuseumHoldings).  An instance of #$MuseumStructure may be a part of a building, a single building, or a set of buildings.  Also, instances of this collection encompass both museaum areas open to the public as well as areas holding the non-displayed holdings as well.  See also #$Museum-Organization for the collection of organizations dedicated to housing displays in these structures.")
(comment Landing "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$ArrivingAtAPlace and #$PhysicalContactMakingEvent.  Each instance of #$Landing is an event in which a (previously) #$Airborne object comes to rest on a flat, horizontal surface--often #$EarthsGround.  Specializations include #$Landing-Aircraft and #$Perching.")
(comment unboundPredicateRules "(#$unboundPredicateRules PREDICATE) means that when the inference engine, in the course of backchaining, is attempting to prove a literal of the form (PREDICATE ARG1 ... ARGN) or the negation of such a literal, rules (in accessible microtheries) containing literals with unbound predicates will be available.  For example, the consequent of the rule (#$implies (#$and (#$seriesOrderedByInverse ?SER ?PRED) (#$seriesLength ?SER ?L) (#$greaterThanOrEqualTo ?L ?N) (#$greaterThan ?N ?M)) (?PRED (#$NthInSeriesFn ?SER ?N) (#$NthInSeriesFn ?SER ?M))) has an unbound predicate, the variable ?PRED.  Given that the KB contains the assertion (#$unboundPredicateRules #$caudalTo), that rule can be used in backchaining to prove, for instance, (#$caudalTo (#$NthInSeriesFn (#$The #$Vertebrae) 20) (#$NthInSeriesFn (#$The #$Vertebrae) 6)).")
(comment epidemicCommonVehicle "(#$epidemicCommonVehicle EPI VEHICLE) means that the (#$GroupFn #$InanimateObject) VEHICLE is the group of things that is the common vehicle of infection for the #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI. This means that every member of EPI is an #$Infection caused by a #$InfectingEvent-VehicleBorneTransmission, and each of those transmission events is mediated by the common vehicle VEHICLE. The common vehicle is a group of things contaminated with the #$Microorganism that causes the #$Infections that constitute EPI. For example, an #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic caused by contaminated pork would be represented as (#$epidemicCommonVehicle EPIDEMIC01 PORKGROUP01) where (#$isa PORKGROUP01 (#$GroupFn #$Pork)). See #$epidemicCommonVehicleType.")
(comment OrganismVarietyBySize "A collection of collections. Each #$OrganismVarietyBySize is
a specialization of some organism type, such that the instances of
that #$OrganismVarietyBySize share a specific size or range of sizes,
in contrast to some other instances of the broader organism type.
Examples include #$GiantSchnauzer and the collection of miniature
horses.")
(comment WaterproofSurface "A specialization of #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible.  Instances of this
collection are surfaces of objects that are impervious to water.")
(comment MiddleEasternStyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
middle eastern style.                            ")
(comment IntervalRangeFn "A binary #$ScalarDenotingFunction that takes two comparable scalar intervals to the (usually proper, usually continuous) interval between and including them.
<p>
Where <code>SCALAR1</code> and <code>SCALAR2</code> are #$ScalarIntervals (q.v.) such that the maximum of the latter is #$greaterThanOrEqualTo the minimum of the former, <code>(#$IntervalRangeFn SCALAR1 SCALAR2)</code> is a #$ScalarInterval <code>RANGE</code> whose minimum (see #$minQuantValue) is the same as that of <code>SCALAR1</code> and whose maximum (see #$maxQuantValue) is the same as that of <code>SCALAR2</code>.  If both <code>SCALAR1</code> and <code>SCALAR2</code> are #$Integers (or proper integer-extents), then <code>RANGE</code> is the <i>contiguous</i> #$IntegerExtent (q.v.) that ranges from the minimum of the former to the maximum of the latter.  Otherwise (e.g. if <code>SCALAR1</code> and <code>SCALAR2</code> are #$RealNumbers or #$Quantity[ies]), then <code>RANGE</code> is the <i>continuous</i> interval that ranges from the minimum of the former to the maximum of the latter.
<p>
Note that <code>RANGE</code> will be a #$ScalarProperInterval (q.v.) except when <code>SCALAR1</code> #$equals <code>SCALAR2</code> and is itself a #$ScalarPointValue (q.v.).  When both of its arguments are the same, #$IntervalRangeFn behaves like an identity function: <code>(#$IntervalRangeFn SCALAR SCALAR) = SCALAR</code> for any scalar interval <code>SCALAR</code>.  When its arguments are #$NumericIntervals that are <i>not</i> integer-extents, #$IntervalRangeFn behaves exactly like #$Unity (q.v.).
<p>
In practice, the two arguments to #$IntervalRangeFn will typically be either non-overlapping #$NonNumericScalarQuantity[ies] (q.v.), distinct point-value #$Quantity[ies], or particular numbers.
<p>
Some examples. (#$IntervalRangeFn #$Cold #$Cool) is #$CoolToCold: the temperature-range from #$Cold to #$Cool.  (#$IntervalRangeFn (#$Mile 5) (#$Mile 7)) is equal to (#$Mile 5 7): the distance-range of between 5 an 7 miles inclusive.  (#$IntervalRangeFn 1 10) is the #$IntegerExtent that comprises the integers from 1 to 10 inclusive. (#$IntervalRangeFn 1.0 10.0) is equal to (#$Unity 1.0 10.0): the #$ContinuousIntervalOnNumberLine that comprises the reals from 1.0 to 10.0 inclusive.
<p>
See also the corresponding predicate #$intervalRange.")
(comment SwimmingSportsEventTypeByDistance "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$SwimmingSportsEventTypeByDistance is a specialization of #$SwimmingRaceEvent, instances of which are such that particular distances must be traversed by the competing individuals or teams.")
(comment withinRangeForEventType "(#$withinRangeForEventType OBJECT1 OBJECT2 SITTYPE) means that OBJECT1 is able to affect OBJECT2 in some SITTYPE. For instance, if #$AlbertGore is five meters away from #$GeorgeWBush, then (#$withinRangeForEventType #$AlbertGore #$GeorgeWBush #$SpokenCommunicating) but not (#$withinRangeForEventType #$AlbertGore #$GeorgeWBush #$ShakingHands).  Different kinds of actions have different ranges, and this predicate can be used to express the conditions for being able to do something to something else via different kinds of actions.")
(comment Tincture-Pharmaceutical "#$Tincture-Pharmaceutical is the collection of all tinctures.  A tincture is a medicinal solution which contains alcohol.")
(comment WhirlingOfFluid "Non-rigid spinning of a fluid often having a tendency to draw objects toward or into the whirl.  The angular velocity of the fluid decreases with distance from the axis.  A circular #$Storm (A #$CycloneAsObject, tornado, ...) whirls.")
(comment Thrush-AilmentCondition "A specialization of #$Candidiasis (q.v.).  Thrush cases are characterized by white patches on teh tongue or other areas.  Pften, when wiped away, these patches will reveal raw or bleeding tissue.")
(comment ForceType "Types of forces. Its place in the hierarchy is parallel to #$QuantityType's place")
(comment instrument-Generic "The predicate #$instrument-Generic is used to link a particular event to any of the objects which play an instrumental role in it.  <code>(#$instrument-Generic EVENT OBJECT)</code> means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible <code>OBJECT</code> plays an intermediate causal role in the #$Event <code>EVENT</code>, facilitating the occurrence of <code>EVENT</code>, and thereby serving some purpose of some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  This can happen in at least two ways: either the 'doer' of <code>EVENT</code> acts on <code>OBJECT</code>, which in turn acts on something else (as when someone uses a hammer to pound in a nail) or the 'doer' of <code>EVENT</code> acts on something, making it possible for <code>OBJECT</code> to act on that thing (as when someone puts wet clothes out in the sun to dry).  Typically, an #$instrument-Generic is not significantly altered by playing that role in an event.  #$deviceUsed is an important specialization of #$instrument-Generic (where <code>OBJECT</code> is an instance of #$PhysicalDevice).")
(comment HTMLTag "The collection of all HTML tags.  Instances of #$HTMLTag identify #$CharacterStrings, #$TextStrings or #$GraphicalStructures within documents written in #$HypertextMarkupLanguage (#$HTMLSources).  Instances of #$HTMLTag specify the appearance of a #$CharacterString, #$TextString, or #$GraphicalStructure, the internal structure of a document, or the type of content of a particular #$TextString or #$GraphicalStructure that appear in documents generated by #$HTMLSources.")
(comment typicalInfectionHost "(#$typicalInfectionHost PATHOGENTYPE HOSTTYPE) means that if (#$pathogenTypeCausesInfectionType PATHOGENTYPE INFECTIONTYPE), and INFECTION is an instance of INFECTIONTYPE such that HOST is the #$infectionHost, and it is not known what kind of organism HOST is, there is a medium-to-high #$likelihood that HOST is an instance of HOSTTYPE.")
(comment ProcardiaProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by #$PfizerInc.")
(comment UnitOfVelocity "The collection of functions which return elements of #$LinearVelocityVector.  This is differentiated from #$UnitOfSpeed, which does not indicate the direction of motion.")
(comment InformationDesignation-MissionCritical "An instance of #$AttributeValue.  #$InformationDesignation-MissionCritical
can be used to designate when an instance of #$AspatialInformationStore
is critical to the success of some mission.  This attribute is most useful
for specifying what information is critical to a given mission within
the mission context, i.e. the instance of #$Microtheory representing
the mission.  For example, if MISSION_MT is an instance of #$Microtheory
representing some military mission, say, and INFO is some instance of
#$AspatialInformationStore critical to the success of MISSION_MT, say
the precise location of a command ship, then one could represent this
by asserting, in MISSION_MT, (#$designationOfInformation INFO
#$InformationDesignation-MissionCritical).  This attribute is also useful
in rules when one wants to use a clause stating that some instance of
#$AspatialInformationStore is critical
to some mission without specifying the mission.  See also the predicates
#$designationOfInformation and #$missionCriticalInformation.")
(comment TakingCustodyOfAChild "A collection of instances of #$TransferringCustodyOfAPerson.  In each instance, custody of a child is handed from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another:  both #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles are #$different from the #$HumanChild whose custody is handed over.")
(comment LawyerTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs in which #$Lawyers and their work are           the main focus of whatever #$Narratives are told in the shows.           This includes only fictional shows.")
(comment MusicalComposition-1980sPop "The Collection of instances of #$MusicalComposition that are in the 1980s pop music style or genre.  As indicated by the constant name, this is the musical genre popular in the 1980s.  Popularity, however, is not the only criterion for being 'pop' music. During that decade, for instance, pop songs would be played on 'Top 40' music stations and pop musicians were major celebrities and cultural icons called upon to represent products and institute fads. Musicians whose style of music is #$MusicalComposition-1980sPop include #$DuranDuran, #$CyndiLauper, #$BonJovi-MusicGroup, and #$NewKidsOnTheBlock-MusicGroup.")
(comment BackSpin "Moving through the air with the top moving forward slower and the bottom moving forward faster.  The axis of spin is approximately horizontal. This produces negative lift and changes the direction of bounce toward the direction in which the object is spinning.  This usually applies to a #$Sphere object.")
(comment MSLocalIntranetZoneFn "One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be initiated from the \"Local Intranet Zone\". The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. The term \"Local Intranet Zone\" refers to the computer's own #$Intranet and actions must be wholly sourced from this zone to be permitted.")
(comment SecondLieutenant-Rank "The minimal commissioned officer rank in the

U.S. Army and in the U.S. Marine Corps.  A person of #$SecondLieutenant-Rank outranks any person whose rank is a #$NonCommissionedOfficerTypeByRank or a #$WarrantOfficerTypeByRank.")
(comment practiceType "This predicate is used for asserting that at least one of the practices with which a particular #$MedicalCareProfessional is associated specializes in work done by medical professionals of a certain #$MedicalSpecialtyType.  If (#$practiceType DOCTOR SPECIALTY), then there exists a medical practice PRACTICE such that, if (#$providerOfService DOCTOR EVENT) and EVENT is a #$MedicalCareEvent and (#$representsAgentInEvent PRACTICE DOCTOR EVENT) then  (#$actsInCapacity DOCTOR #$providerOfService EVENT #$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity ).  A doctor may of course be affiliated with different practices of different specialty types.")
(comment TranslationAlongASurface "A collection of processes.  In instances of #$TranslationAlongASurface an #$objectMoving is moving along a #$motionPathway-Complete in contact with a liquid or solid surface.  The #$objectMoving crosses [see #$trajectoryPassesThrough] the #$Perimeter of any #$toLocation or #$fromLocation that is a #$SurfaceRegion-Bounded.")
(comment ShapesConfigurationSituationFn "(#$ShapesConfigurationSituationFn SHAPEATT) denotes the collection of situations which are exactly the situation of some object holding the shape SHAPEATT, i.e. the situation in which (#$objectShapeType OBJ SHAPEATT).")
(comment eventHonors "(#$eventHonors OCCURRENCE AGENT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT is honored or commemorated by the #$SocialOccurrence OCCURRENCE.  If AGENT is a living #$Person, then (#$eventHonors OCCURRENCE AGENT) usually implies that AGENT is present at OCCURRENCE.  Note that this is the appropriate predicate for relating a #$Funeral to the deceased person for whom the #$Funeral is in honor.")
(comment awardRecipient "(#$awardRecipient CEREMONY RECIPIENT) is true iff RECIPIENT is an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible which was the recipient of an #$AwardPractice in #$AwardsCeremony CEREMONY. This kind of bestowing is really quite different from the #$GeneralizedTransfer events for which the #$toPossessor slot would be
appropriate.")
(comment Gourmet "This is the collection of people who have specialized knowledge about

food together with a particular enthusiasm for fine dining. The English

term is most often used as an adjective. Initially this was incorrect, but

it has become so common that it is now acceptable usage. (See #$GourmetFood).")
(comment SuperiorDirection "The general direction towards the top and away from the bottom, in or near an object that is #$AnimalShapedThing in an #$UprightPosture.  In the case of a #$Person or other object with attribute #$HumanShaped, this direction almost always corresponds to #$CephalicDirection.")
(comment IndividualArgModeFn "An expression of the form (#$IndividualArgModeFn SYMBOL TYPE) is used to abstractly represent an instance of the collection TYPE solely for the purposes of being able to provide semantic information abouta #$Predicate to instance of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingProgram-CW for the sake of making rule induction more efficient. This information will be used by communicated to such systems relative to an instance of #$InductiveLogicProgrammingDetermination.")
(comment IngestingFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a specialization THING-TYPE of #$PartiallyTangible, #$IngestingFn returns the collection of all events in which some instance of THING-TYPE is ingested (see the collection #$Ingesting).  For example, (#$IngestingFn #$Popcorn-Popped) is the collection of all events in which some instance of #$Popcorn-Popped is ingested.")
(comment importRateFrom "(#$importRateFrom REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 imports instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 at the #$Rate RATE.  Note that since things imported are typically measurable in terms of their monetary value, RATE might in some instances be a #$MonetaryRate; in others it will be, for example, a rate of volume, mass, or number.")
(comment changesQuantityInDirection "This predicate specifies the direction in which a given quantity changes in a given time period.  (#$changesQuantityInDirection TIME THING SLOT DIRECTION) means that during TIME, THING's #$QuantitySlot SLOT changes in DIRECTION.  TIME is a #$TemporalThing, and AMOUNT is a #$LevelOfChange.  If DIRECTION is #$Positive, this denotes an increase (#$changesQuantityInDirection (#$YearFn 1980) #$SaudiArabia #$oilExport #$Positive) means that in 1980, Saudi Arabia's oil export increased.  For predicates specifying amounts of change, see: #$changesQuantityByFraction, #$changesQuantityByAmount.  See also #$quantityChangeFunction to describe qualitative aspects of a quantity change, e.g. a spike, net decreasing, curvilinear, or slow change.")
(comment Atmosphere-UnitOfPressure "One #$Atmosphere-UnitOfPressure is defined as the average pressure of the earth's atmosphere at sea level.  It is slightly over 1% higher than one #$Bar-UnitOfPressure.")
(comment actorsPrimaryGenre "(#$actorsPrimaryGenre ACTOR GENRE) states that the given ACTOR primarily acts in movies of a particular GENRE.  For example, #$JohnWayne is primarily an actor in movies of type #$PropositionalConceptualWork-WesternGenre.")
(comment FilmingAVisualImage "Using a camera device to record a visual image, whether the medium is film or videotape.  Recording a movie off of cable with an in-line VCR is *not* part of this collection - see #$VideoCassetteRecording.")
(comment totalExportValue-Rate "(#$totalExportValue-Rate REGION MONETARY-FLOW-RATE) means that the #$MonetaryRate MONETARY-FLOW-RATE is a measure of the rate of export of all goods and services from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION in terms of the monetary value of these goods and services.")
(comment Minaret "A specialization of #$PartOfBuilding,
#$Outdoors-ExposedToWeather, and #$LongThinObject. Each instance of
this collection is a tall spire of a #$Mosque-Building, and historically it was
used to call the faithful to prayer. In modern times, the call to
prayer emanates from a prayer hall through a public announcement
system. As such, the #$Minaret now serves a decorative and tradional
purposes.")
(comment providesMotiveFor "<code>(#$providesMotiveFor INDIV AGT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that <code>INDIV</code> provides <code>AGT</code> with a motive for acting in the specified way -- <i>i.e.</i>, for playing <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.  <code>INDIV</code> will typically be a #$Situation or a state of affairs (expressed by a #$CycLSentence-Assertible). 
<p>
Note that this predicate does not take a particular action as its third argument. It is <i>not</i> used to specify <code>AGT</code>'s motive for participating in some actual event (for this, use #$purposeInEvent or #$reasonsForAction). Also, note that one can have a 'motive' to do A without ever having the corresponding goal or desire to do it. <i>E.g.</i>, <code>AGT</code> might have a motive to kill his business partner (perhaps being cheated in a business deal) even if <code>AGT</code> never actually desires to do this. This is one sense of 'motive' discussed in criminal law contexts -- <code>INDIV</code> provides <code>AGT</code> with a <i>reason</i> to play <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, <i>i.e.</i>, is the sort of event which often does and/or which reasonably could lead an agent to do this.")
(comment AnimalUtterance-IBT "A specialization of both #$AnimalSound and #$SpokenUtterance-IBT.  Each instance of #$AnimalUtterance-IBT is a sound initially generated by some #$Animal speaking or making some sound with his/her/its mouth (note that the sound may or may not have propositional content - i.e. instantiate some #$PropositionalInformationThing).  If such a sound is recorded and played back, the sound generated is still considered an instance of #$AnimalUtterance-IBT.  Examples: one's spouse's `Good morning'; a child's scream at a playmate; Humphrey Bogart's `Here's looking at you' on the set of _Casablanca_. Note that only the sounds themselves are instances of this collection -- not the activities of making them. This collection is not a specialization of #$Action (for that, see #$CommunicationAct-Single and its specializations).")
(comment territoryDisputed "(#$territoryDisputed ?DISPUTE ?AREA) means that control over the #$GeographicalRegion ?AREA is what is being disputed in the #$InternationalTerritorialDispute ?DISPUTE.")
(comment ConnectionPredicate "A #$PredicateType that is a  specialization of #$SpatialPredicate, #$TangibleObjectPredicate, #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate, and #$InterExistingObjectPredicate (qq.v.).   Each instance of #$ConnectionPredicate is a specialization of  #$connectedTo (q.v.), and is used to describe a particular sort of  physical connection between pairs of objects.  Examples include  #$nailedTo, #$rivetedTo, #$connectedTo-Rigidly, #$rotationallyConnectedTo, #$hangsFrom, and #$in-Rooted.")
(comment FrequentlyAskedQuestionsList "Most often referred to by its abbreviation 'FAQ'. A list of questions (and answers thereto) that newcomers to a Usenet newsgroup, etc., frequently ask or that those intimately familiar with the newsgroup, etc., feel that newcomers ought to be informed about before they get further involved. Most newsgroups have a FAQ that is updated and revised regularly, that contains fairly reliable and up-to-date information about the topic of the newsgroup, and that people who want to post something to the newsgroup are expected under established 'netiquette' to read before posting. The use of FAQs has expanded beyond its original domain into informational websites, users manuals, etc. Cf. #$InternetNewsgroup, #$FAQFn.")
(comment academicCourseLevel "(#$academicCourseLevel COURSE COURSE-LEVEL) holds just in case COURSE is 
designed for students who are at the education level corresponding to COURSE-LEVEL.  For 
instance, if (#$academicCourseLevel McXFall02Phil101A-Sec1 #$FreshmanCourseLevel) holds,
then McXFall02Phil101A-Sec1 is designed for persons, PERSON such that 
(#$educationLevel PERSON #$CollegeFreshmanLevel).")
(comment creatorOfPartOfWork "(#$creatorOfPartOfWork WORK DOCSTRUC AGENT) means that AGENT, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent, is the creator of that part of the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK that is represented in the #$GraphicalStructure DOCSTRUC.  For example, forewards (see #$foreword-DocumentPartOf) that are parts of #$StructurallySpecificWorks are written by someone other than the author of the work.  Newspapers and magazines consist of articles authored by different individuals; the agent responsible for the creation of an individual article can be indicated by #$creatorOfPartOfWork.")
(comment HydroPoweredTurbine "The subcollection of #$Turbines use #$FluidFlow-Translation of #$Water to generate #$Electricity.")
(comment fromOrientation "This predicate indicates, for the particular rotational motion ROT, the orientation that the #$objectMoving in that event has at the beginning of that motion.  (#$fromOrientation ROT ORIENT) means that when ROT begins, the object that moves in ROT has the position ORIENT, with respect to the current frame of reference.  For example, the object may have a #$HorizontalOrientation, #$VerticalOrientation, #$RightSideUp orientation, etc.  See also #$toOrientation, #$OrientationVector.")
(comment evaluator "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$Evaluating to the instances of #$IntelligentAgent who perform the evaluation. (#$evaluator EVALUATION EVALUATOR) says that EVALUATOR does the evaluating EVALUATION.  See also #$evaluee-Direct, #$evaluationInputs, #$evaluationOutputSentences and #$objectOfEvaluation.")
(comment TwoOrThreeLanesRoadway "The collection of #$Roadways that have a total of 2 or 3 lanes or tracks, both directions

included. This criterion belongs to the US Army's nomenclature for the

representation of roads on large and medium scale maps. See also

#$RoadwayTypeByNumberOfLanes.")
(comment advertisingMedium "A predicate for relating an advertising event to a type of medium (broadly construed) in which advertisements generated by that event, appear. (#$advertisingMedium ADVERTISING IBTTYPE) means instances of #$Advertisement-PCW used in ADVERTISING (see #$advertisementUsed) appear in instances of IBTTYPE, a specialization of #$InformationBearingThing. For example, (#$advertisingMedium NIKEADCAMPAIGN2331 (#$CopyOfCWFn

(#$MediaSeriesNthFn #$Newsweek-TheMagazine 783))) means that advertisements used in NIKEADCAMPAIGN2331 appear in copies of issue 783 of News Week

magazine. (#$advertisingMedium NIKEADCAMPAIGN2331 (#$BroadcastOfEventTypeFn (#$PlayingFn #$Basketball-TheGame))) means that advertisements used in NIKEADCAMPAIGN2331 appear broadcasts of basketball games.")
(comment CommunicationWithServiceSpecification "The collection of complete #$Specifications required to connect two or more #$Artifact-Agentives via a #$MachineProtocol carried over a #$ProtocolTransportMediumType.")
(comment Disgust "A feeling of repulsion or aversion towards something considered distasteful or repugnant.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Disgust include feelings of #$Abhorrence.")
(comment ComputerTypeByUse "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ComputerTypeByUse is a collection of computers that can be or are
designed to be put to a certain use.  Instances include #$SingleUser-Computer, #$AccountingUse, etc..")
(comment wearsClothing "An instance of #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate. #$wearsClothing is a binary predicate that relates instances of #$SolidTangibleThing to instances of #$SomethingToWear.  (#$wearsClothing OBJ ITEM) means that OBJ wears ITEM. The first argument of #$wearsClothing is loosely constrained to be an instance of #$SolidTangibleThing, so that this predicate may be used to describe mannequins, animals, and other individuals (of whatever kinds) that might wear clothes, as well as humans. However, by default  an individual who #$wearsClothing is an instance of #$Person. See also #$wornOn, which relates the item worn to the body part on which it is worn, and see #$itemWorn, which relates a particular wearable item to the event in which it is worn.")
(comment ImposingSanctions "The collection of all impositions of sanctions, each imposition being performed by an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible upon another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible that has some formal relationship to the imposer.  In events of this type, the main #$Event is an official enactment by the imposer, calculated to lead to events that the recipient is presumed to dislike.  For example, an organization imposes a fine on one of its members, a judge imposes sanctions on an errant lawyer before the court, the Roman Catholic Church excommunicates a miscreant parishioner, or the United Nations declares an oil embargo against a member-state.  The purpose is either to punish the recipient for past disapproved behavior (as in criminal contempt of court, punishing rudeness or dishonesty) or to create an incentive for the recipient to improve future behavior (as in imprisonment for civil contempt of court, designed to force cooperation by a witness).  The imposing #$Agent-PartiallyTangible may or may not have any legitimate legal authority to impose the sanction, and may or may not have any power of enforcing the sanction.  An instance of #$ImposingSanctions is the formal enactment rather than any later acts of enforcement.  This concept is more specific than #$Punishing which includes spanking a baby, pistol-whipping a crime suspect, or retaliation bombing.")
(comment CateringOrganization "The collection of #$FoodServiceOrganizations that bring food to social or
business events on a short-term and usually one-time basis. The services of a 
#$CateringOrganization are customarily paid for by the hosts or sponsors of the event. 
An important employee type in a CateringCompany is #$Caterer-Person.")
(comment GroupActivity "This is the collection of #$Actions #$doneBy a #$Group of #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles.")
(comment NonconformingMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements which are not #$ConformingMortgages.  See #$LimitConformingLoan for a fuller explanation.")
(comment StyrofoamPeanut "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleArtifact.  Each instance of this collection is a peanut-shaped piece of #$Styrofoam, whose primary function is to fill the empty spaces in #$MailableObjects.")
(comment Guilt "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Guilt is some agent's negative, self-accusatory feeling of responsibility for having caused some harm.  Instances of #$Guilt vary depending on the intensity of the feeling or the subject experiencing the feeling.")
(comment ConceptNodesForSetFn "(#$ConceptNodesForSetFn SET)
returns an instance of #$ConceptFilter that has all and only the nodes in SET as nodes.")
(comment requiredDocumentsForEventType "(#$requiredDocumentsForEventType DOCTYPE EVENTTYPE) means that in order to participate in an #$Event of type EVENTTYPE, as a main performer of the action, one must possess documents (or other #$InformationBearingObjects) of type DOCTYPE (i.e. either instances or instantiations depending upon whether DOCTYPE is a type of #$InformationBearingThing or #$ConceptualWork) according to some governing #$CodeOfConduct.  The particular governing #$CodeOfConduct is implicit in the context of the assertion.  For example, (#$requiredDocumentsForEventType (#$TransportViaFn #$Automobile) #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement)")
(comment Guitar-Acoustic "Instances are instances of #$Guitar where the sound produced is an atmospheric waveform caused by the vibration of the guitar strings and amplified in a resonance chamber.")
(comment Locomotion-LiquidImmersed "The collection of all instances of #$LocomotionProcess in which the locomotor is #$in-ImmersedFully and supported by some #$LiquidTangibleThing. Includes both the movement of a submarine while submerged, and the movement of a goldfish in a bowl.")
(comment TerritorialIntegrityGoal "This #$GoalTypeByCategory characterizes goals of a #$GeopoliticalEntity which are aimed at realizing its fundamental goal of maintaining control over its own territory.")
(comment temporalBoundsIdentical "(#$temporalBoundsIdentical X Y) means that X and Y are both #$temporallyCooriginating and #$temporallyCoterminal.  That is, X and Y have the same #$startingPoint and the same #$endingPoint.  Note that if X and Y are both #$temporallyContinuousDuring objects, such as a pair of ashtrays, then

it follows that they are completely #$cotemporal.")
(comment Sadness "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Sadness is some agent's feeling of unhappiness.  Instances of #$Sadness vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the cause of the feeling.  Notable specializations of #$Sadness include #$Grief, #$Despair, and #$Misery.")
(comment CommentaryArticle-CW "The collection of all articles [#$Article-PCW] expressing the opinion of the author(s) on some #$Issue.")
(comment PulmonaryVein-Major "The collection of all #$Veins which directly supply #$OxygenatedBlood to the left #$AuricleOfHeart of a #$Heart from a #$Lung.  There are four such #$Veins in a #$Person.")
(comment LevelOfExhaustion "An #$QuantityType whose elements represent the qualitative degrees of exhaustion that an animal may feel. For instance, the assertion (#$feelsSensation #$JimiHendrix #$LevelOfExhaustion #$Positive),

means that Jimi Hendrix feels some degree of physical exhaustion (a not unlikely state of affairs after one of his guitar solos). Note that this predicate is NOT properly used for purposes such as to describe metal fatigue, or the depletion of natural resources.")
(comment CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType are collections of cyc arguments with a similar sort of justification or support.  These collections are used to represent the support used to justify assertions in some context.  Some examples are #$UnjustifiedBelief, #$AssertedBelief, #$AssumedBelief, #$CausallySupported, #$StatisticallySupported, and #$SupportedByMaterialImplication.  See #$hasArgumentJustificationType, #$assertionJustificationAttribute, and #$mtJustificationType.")
(comment MediaLiaison "A #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg and a subset of #$Person.  Every instance of #$MediaLiaison is a person who represents some agent (an individual or an organization) in instances of #$CommunicatingWithTheMedia.")
(comment Metalloid "An instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and a
specialization of #$ElementStuff.  Each instance of #$Metalloid
is has properties bettwen those of #$MetallicElementType and
#$NonMetallicElementType.")
(comment HomosexualBehavior-Male "The collection of all instances of #$HomosexualBehavior involving two or more males.  Note that this refers only to the sexual behavior itself, not to any other behaviors that may happen to be exhibited by #$HomosexualHumans.")
(comment ReportTypeBySourceReliability "A collection of attributes.  Each instance is an indicator of how reliable the sources of a given #$WrittenReportOnSituation are considered to be, collectively speaking. See also #$reliabilityOfReportSources.")
(comment Butoh-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
butoh style.                            ")
(comment endsDuring "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a specialization of both #$endsAfterStartingOf and #$temporalBoundsIntersect (qq.v.).  (#$endsDuring ENDS GOES-ON) means GOES-ON covers the end of ENDS: the #$endingPoint of ENDS is properly temporally-contained-in (see #$temporalBoundsContain) GOES-ON.
<p>
For example, (#$endsDuring #$AmericanBasketballAssociation (#$YearFn 1976)) states that the ABA ceased to exist in 1976.
<p>
Note that ENDS and GOES-ON might not temporally intersect (see #$temporallyIntersects); though they must intersect if GOES-ON is #$temporallyContinuousDuring.")
(comment GrowlingSound "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$AnimalSound.  Each instance of #$GrowlingSound is either a low-pitched, guttural sound emitted by a #$NonHumanAnimal such as a #$Dog or a #$Bear-Animal (usually as an expression of hostility), or an imitation of such a sound (e.g. the sound made by a human who is growling like a dog).")
(comment CloudlessArea "An instance of #$DegreeOfCloudiness and specialization of #$ClearWeatherArea. Each instance of #$CloudlessArea is an instance of #$OutdoorLocation that has no cloud cover.")
(comment PrepositionalRoleMarkerFn "A Function which takes instances of LexicalWord (implicitly constrained to those for which #$Preposition is known to be a #$partOfSpeech) and returns instances of #$GrammaticalRoleMarker as it's value.")
(comment taskAccomplishesPurpose "The binary predicate #$taskAccomplishesPurpose relates a task to  a purpose. (#$taskAccomplishesPurpose TASK PROPOSITION) means that the task TASK can accomplish the purpose described by PROPOSITION.  TASK must be an individual in the collection #$MilitaryAction.")
(comment annualDeathRateInDueTo "(#$annualDeathRateInDueTo PLACE EVENT_TYPE FRACTION) means that FRACTION (a number between 0 and 1) of the residents of PLACE, die due to events of type EVENT_TYPE annually.  EVENT_TYPE could be a type of disease, accident, crime, natural disaster, or #$War.")
(comment Blimp "#$Blimp is a specialization of #$LighterThanAirCraft, #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, and #$Balloon.  Each instance of #$Blimp is a dirigible, motorized, and lighter-than-air craft (airships).  Each generally consists of a gas-filled gas-sack from which a control and passenger cabin hangs (the gas-sack may or may not have rigid reinforcement such as ribs).  A #$Blimp flies more slowly than an #$Airplane.  They are also called blimps, dirigibles and Zeppelins.")
(comment investigatingAgent "(#$investigatingAgent INQUIRY AGENT) means that AGENT is an instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible carrying out or assisting in INQUIRY.  There may be more than one such individual, and the same individual may be involved in more than one instance of #$Investigation.")
(comment ConferenceSeminar "The collection of #$SeminarSeriess that are

  parts of #$Conferences.")
(comment AssigningAgentToRole "Every instance of #$AssigningAgentToRole involves the placement of an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in a particular #$Situation, #$Role or #$Place, or some combination of the three.  Some examples include placing someone in a drug rehab program, placing a child in a particular class, and placing an employee in a new location.")
(comment Proofreading "The collection of all #$Events in which #$TextualMaterial is read [#$Reading] in order to determine places in which the #$TextString which is instantiated in the the #$InformationBearingObject being examined is not an appropriate #$PropositionalCWText for the #$PropositionalConceptualWork being instantiated.  The intent of #$Proofreading is to create a new #$TextString as a more accurate #$textOfWork of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork being instantiated.  The outputs of a #$Proofreading event is a new #$InformationBearingObject to indicate the new #$TextString.")
(comment TransferringCustodyOfAPrisoner "A collection of instances of #$TransferringCustodyOfAPerson.  In each instance, custody of a prisoner is handed from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another:  both #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles are different from the #$Prisoner whose custody is handed over.")
(comment StoutBeer "A black form of #$Beer (contrast with #$LagerBeer and #$AleBeer) that originated in the British Isles, and is now most recognizably associated with #$IrishRepublic. #$StoutBeer contains a bitterness derived from malted hops, good #$StoutBeer is served chilled, several degrees below room temperature. #$StoutBeers are typically black colored, containing a mixture of #$CarbonDioxide and #$Nitrogen. #$StoutBeers typically possess a distinctively white, creamy froth or 'head'. Even the most ardent #$StoutBeer drinkers find stout to be too heavy for summer consumption, and switch to #$LagerBeer or #$AleBeer in the summer months.")
(comment AgentCasualtyPredicate "A #$PredicateType.  Each instance of #$AgentCasualtyPredicate is a binary #$CasualtyPredicate that relates an #$Event to an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible or #$Organism-Whole that is a casualty in that event.  See also #$NonagentCasualtyPredicate.")
(comment disconnects-Underspecified "(#$disconnects-Underspecified LEFT RIGHT) states that a

disconnection or separation of an underspecified nature is made

between the ideas/things LEFT and RIGHT.  A disconnection might be

geographical (e.g., if LEFT is a person and RIGHT is a place, as in

'Bill left town'), physical (e.g., LEFT and RIGHT are people who

'become distant' or divorce), mental (e.g., LEFT is a person and

RIGHT is an abstract state, as in 'IBM came out of its slump') or

partially tangible (e.g., LEFT is a person, RIGHT is a coma, as in

'Bill came out of his coma'). Conceptual disconnection is the mirror

operation of #$connects-Underspecified.")
(comment Guitar-Electric "Instances are instances of #$Guitar that produce there sound by turning the vibration of their strings into an electronic signal, which is in turn electronically amplified, then transmitted as sound via an electronic speaker.")
(comment IngestionalToxinType "A specialization of #$HazardousChemicalSubstanceType.  Each instance of
#$IngestionalToxinType is a collection whose instances should not
be ingested by people.")
(comment lessLikelyThan-Derived "A predicate used for probability statements. (#$lessLikelyThan-Derived PROPOSITION1 PROPOSITION2) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the <em>a posteriori</em> #$derivedProbability that PROPOSITION1 is true is less than the <em>a posteriori</em> #$derivedProbability that PROPOSITION2 is true, taking into account other evidence and the truth or falsehood of other assertions.  This predicate does not say what the probabilities actually are numerically; it is just an ordering (or rather partial ordering) relation between the two propositions.  In most microtheories, generally, this #$lessLikelyThan-Derived means that the probability that PROPOSITION1 is true is less than the probability that PROPOSITION2 is true, given the probabilities of other #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory and the #$domainAssumptions accessible in the #$Microtheory.  Contrast this with #$atLeastAsLikelyAs (which makes no claim of dependence on or independence from other assertions) and with #$lessLikelyThan-Prior (which does not take into account any dependence on other assertions).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment columnOfTable "'(#$columnOfTable TABLE COL)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure COL is a column within the #$Table-AIS TABLE.")
(comment typesGreaterThanWRTScalar "A #$TernaryPredicate that relates a #$Collection to a #$Collection to a #$QuantitySlot.  <code>(#$typesGreaterThanWRTScalar COL1 COL2 SLOT)</code> means that, in general, instances of <code>COL1</code> have a higher value for <code>SLOT</code> than do instances of <code>COL2</code>.  More specifically, if each of the following hold:
<pre>
  (#$typesGreaterThanWRTScalar COL1 COL2 SLOT)
  (#$isa INST1 COL1)
  (#$isa INST2 COL2)
</pre>
then the following holds:
<pre>
  (#$likelihood (#$largerThan INST1 INST2 SLOT) (#$HighToVeryHighAmountFn #$ProbabilityInterval)).
</pre>")
(comment localPhoneNumberText "ARG2 is the `local' phone number of the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  This means that ARG2 may include a #$TelephoneExchangeNumber and a #$PhoneSuffix, but it will not include an #$AreaCode or a #$TelephoneCountryCode.")
(comment typicalTasteOfType "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate.  <code>(#$typicalTasteOfType COL TASTE)</code> means that instances of <code>COL</code> typically have the #$ObjectTypeByTaste <code>TASTE</code> (see #$tasteOfObject).")
(comment ListOfVertices "A specialization of #$List. Each instance of #$ListOfVertices is a list of #$Points whose length is at least three, and which contains no three consecutive (including rotationally-consecutive) members that are #$collinearPoints.  (Note that there are two \"rotationally-consecutive\" triples in such a list: (i) the sublist consisting of the second-to-last, last, and first members of the list and (ii) the sublist consisting of the last, first, and second members of the list.)
<p>
Each #$ListOfVertices <code>POINTLIST</code> of length <code>N</code> is a list of the vertices of some (actually, many) two-dimensional geometrical figure(s) whose boundary is the closed #$LineString that \"connects-the-dots\" between the consecutive points in <code>POINTLIST</code>.  If all the points in <code>POINTLIST</code> happen to lie in the same #$Plane (see #$coplanarPoints) and the closed line-string they define is geometrically simple (see #$LocallyEuclideanSpatialThing), then <code>POINTLIST</code> is a list of the vertices of a unique <code>N</code>-sided #$Polygon.")
(comment slopeRange "(#$slopeRange VEHICLE ANGLE-RANGE) is the range of angles (downward to upward) at which VEHICLE is able to travel. For a #$JeepBrandCar the range is probably something like (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -60 45) which means that it can go down at a 60 degree angle, and up at a 45 degree angle. The upward angle generally depends on the power of the #$Engine and the type of vehicle. A #$RotaryWingAircraft can go straight up and down so (#$slopeRange ?HELICOPTER (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -90 90).")
(comment Organization "The collection of all organizations.  Each instance of #$Organization is a group whose group-members are instances of #$IntelligentAgent. In each instance of #$Organization, certain relationships and obligations exist between the members of the organization, or between the organization and its members.  Instances of #$Organization include both informal and legally constituted organizations.  Each instance of #$Organization can undertake projects, enter into agreements, own property, and do other tasks characteristic of agents; consequently, #$Organization is a specialization of the collection #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  Notable specializations of #$Organization include #$LegalGovernmentOrganization, #$CommercialOrganization, and #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment meansOfCommunicationFor "This predicate is used to indicate those instances of #$SomethingExisting that are 
used by some instance of
#$Agent-PartiallyTangible in any instance of #$Communicating and that are created for the purpose
of aiding information transfer. 
(#$meansOfCommunicationFor COMM THING AGT) means that the instance AGT of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible uses the 
instance THING of #$SomethingExisting in the instance COMM of #$Communicating and that
(#$meansOfInfoTransfer COMM THING) holds.  For instance, if a 
particular student Student001 uses a particular telephone Telephone001 to
call her father in some instance of #$Communicating Communicating001, we 
could represent this by
(#$meansOfCommunicationFor Communicating001 Telephone001 Student001).  
If her father FatherOfStudent001 uses telephone Telephone002 in this same
instance of #$Communicating, then we would have
(#$meansOfCommunicationFor Communicating001 Telephone002 FatherOfStudent001).
See also #$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact and #$meansOfInfoTransfer-ComputerProgram.
Using the former predicate, for example, we could state for the
above example (#$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact Communicating001 Telephone001) and
(#$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact Communicating001 Telephone002). 
Note that the former of these
implies (#$meansOfInfoTransfer Communicating001 Telephone001).")
(comment FolkPsychologyMt "A #$Microtheory containing principles of commonsense (or \"folk\") psychology.  In particular, this microtheory contains rules expressing various commonsense relations between #$PropositionalAttitudeSlots, #$EmotionalQuantityTypes, etc.")
(comment HTMLSource "The collection of all #$TextStrings that are written in #$HypertextMarkupLanguage for the purpose of generating hypertext (and non-text) that is intelligible on the web.")
(comment glossary-DocumentPartOf "(#$glossary-DocumentPartOf WORK GLOSSARY) means that the #$GraphicalStructure GLOSSARY is a glossary contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.")
(comment OriginatingInSomething "A collection of situations; a subcollection of #$SomethingExisting. In each #$OriginatingInSomething, something originates in something (else).")
(comment numberOfOriginationPointsOnLoan "(#$numberOfOriginationPointsOnLoan LOAN N) identifies N as the number of origination \"points\" on the instance of #$LoanAgreement LOAN.  One point translates to 1 percent of the loan amount (c.f., #$initialLoanAmount) and is charged by the lender to recoup origination costs (see #$LoanOrigination).  To represent the points on a loan as a monetary amount, user #$loanOriginationFee.")
(comment PublishingOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that engage in the publishing of information as a primary activity and as their #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction.")
(comment toPossessor "This predicate relates an agent to an event in which that agent gains some right to use an object.  <code>(#$toPossessor GAIN AGENT)</code> means that immediately after the instance of #$GainingUserRights <code>GAIN</code>, the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>AGENT</code> enjoys being in some #$SituationTypeByUserRights over an object whose possession is transferred in <code>GAIN</code> (the object is related to <code>GAIN</code> via the predicate #$objectOfPossessionTransfer), where the #$SituationTypeByUserRights in question is one which <code>AGENT</code> did not have (at least with respect to the object transferred) at the start of <code>GAIN</code>.")
(comment ListTypeByLength "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$ListTypeByLength is a collection of sequences of specific lengths or a range of lengths.  For example, (#$ListOfLengthFn 2), the collection of lists of exactly two items, is a member of #$ListTypeByLength.  Another instance would be (#$StringOfLengthFn 9), the collection of 9 character strings. Yet another instance would be (#$ListOfLengthFn (#$IntegerFromToFn 0 6).")
(comment Nicotine "A popular alkaloid stimulant, found in #$Tobacco")
(comment Pranking-SomeoneDressingUp "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DressingUp. In each #$Pranking-SomeoneDressingUp, someone dresses up showily.")
(comment TVShowOnTravel "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that primarily provide information            or advice on #$Travel-TripEvents.")
(comment ExchangeOfUserRights "A specialization of both #$SocialOccurrence and #$ChangeInUserRights.  In each instance of #$ExchangeOfUserRights, two instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (the #$exchangers) perform two distinct (though related) instances of #$TransferringPossession with each other.  Two objects are exchanged.  Each agent gains possession -- in the form of some #$SituationTypeByUserRights -- of something (an #$objectOfPossessionTransfer) from the other.  Each transfer is related to the other as some kind of condition, usually as a precondition or an intended result; for example, the news seller will hand over a paper if given fifty cents, and a buyer will give the news seller fifty cents so that the seller will turn over a newspaper to the buyer.  The two #$TransferringPossession events are #$subEvents of the #$ExchangeOfUserRights event.")
(comment providesInformationAbout "The #$Agent-PartiallyTangible ARG1 provides (dispenses, sells) information about or pertaining to the #$Thing ARG2.  See also the similar predicate #$informationAccordingTo .")
(comment ComputerGameProgram-Strategy "The collection of instances of #$ComputerGameProgram such as those in the Civilization series
wherein a significant amount of the player's attention is given to planning
what to do rather than to immediate action. The Civilization games, incidentally, are an example
of the possession of multiple genre attributes, since they may also be considered
to be instances of #$ComputerGameProgram-SimulationGod.")
(comment Affection "A feeling of fondness for someone or something.  Sympathy, liking, warmth, tenderness.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Affection are #$Love, #$Passion, etc.")
(comment MusicalComposition-1990sPop "The collection of instances of MusicalComposition that are in the 1990s pop music style or genre.  As indicated by the constant name, this is the musical genre popular in the 1990s.  Popularity, however, is not the only criterion for being 'pop' music. During that decade, for instance, pop songs would be played on 'Top 40' music stations and pop musicians were major celebrities and cultural icons called upon to represent products and institute fads. Musicians whose style of music is #$MusicalComposition-1990sPop include #$AlanisMorissette, #$SpiceGirls-MusicGroup, #$BarenakedLadies-MusicGroup, and #$BackstreetBoys-MusicGroup.")
(comment PokemonTradingCard "#$PokemonTradingCard is the collection of #$TradingCards used in #$Pokemon-TradingCardGame.")
(comment PropaneFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Fire-ClassB. Instances of #$PropaneFire have #$Propane as their #$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment DestructivePotential "#$DestructivePotential is a collection of attributes representing

scalar indices of the destructive potential of an #$Event or a

#$SomethingExisting.  The thing whose destructive potential is being

gauged may be a particular weather event, like a tornado or a

hurricane, or a situation, like an international arms build-up.  It

may be also be a weapon.  In any case, #$DestructivePotential is

measured primarily by looking at the #$DegreeOfDamage caused by a

typical instance or typical use of the thing whose

#$DestructivePotential is being specified, or by that thing's 'generic' use of other instrumentalities. Note that it makes sense in certain context to cite the #$DestructivePotential of an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, such as a #$Country.")
(comment ConceptNodesForTaxonFn "(#$ConceptNodesForTaxonFn TAXON)
returns an instance of #$ConceptFilter that has all and only the nodes in TAXON as nodes.")
(comment IntangibleObjectRelatingPredicate "A collection of #$IntangibleObjectPredicates used to assert relationships between intangible objects.  As such, each instance of #$IntangibleObjectRelatingPredicate has at least two of its argument-places constrained (see #$argIsa) to instances of #$IntangibleIndividual or some subcollection thereof. Examples include #$subAlgorithms, #$maxQuantValue, #$meanQuantValue, #$expectedValue, #$derivativesOfFunction, #$rangeOfDistribution, #$inverseQuantFunctions-Nonsymmetric, and #$atLeastAsLikelyAs.")
(comment subSitTypesTemporallyDisjointInSitType "<code>(#$subSitTypesTemporallyDisjointInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation), if instances <code>SIT1</code> and <code>SIT2</code> of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations, then <code>SIT1</code> and <code>SIT2</code> do not temporally overlap (see also #$temporalBoundsIntersectInSituationType).
<p>
Note that <code>(#$subSitTypesTemporallyDisjointInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> does not imply that instances of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> or <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations of every instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, since <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> may be merely candidate subsituation types of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (see #$candidateProperSubSituationTypes).")
(comment recognizesHoliday "#$recognizesHoliday is an instance of #$BinaryPredicate that

relates instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to specializations of #$Holiday.

(#$recognizesHoliday AGENT HOLIDAY) means that AGENT recognizes

HOLIDAY, usually by celebrating in some way.  If AGENT is an instance

of #$LegalAgent, and HOLIDAY is an instance of #$LegalHoliday, AGENT

usually suspends or decreases the intensity of normal official

practices.")
(comment HeadwaterReservoir "A specialization of #$WaterReservoir.  Each instance of #$HeadwaterReservoir is a contained in a basin that receives water from no outflow of another reservoir.  The Inflow to a headwater reservoir is typically primarily derived from surface runoff due to precipitation.")
(comment RadioNetwork "A subset of #$CommunicationsOrganization.   Elements of #$RadioNetwork are organizations that produce  radio programs and distribute them either directly to the public  or through intermediaries.  See also #$RadioStation-Organization.")
(comment SourceComputerFn "(#$SourceComputerFn COMPUTER) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose source is COMPUTER.  For example, (#$SourceComputerFn #$Pyrex-Cyc-Com) denotes the collection of all packets whose source is shandra.cyc.com.  The packets themselves will encode this information in their \"Source IP Address\" fields.")
(comment biases "(#$biases AGT PROP) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT has the unsubstantiated belief PROP (represented by a #$ELSentence-Assertible).

Biases generally are so deeply rooted in the agent that the agent may not be consciously aware that PROP is rationally undersupported, and it may be concomittantly harder to change their mind about PROP.

Note:  PROP might or might not turn out to be true (in various contexts); often, PROP is some overgeneralization which is sometimes true but often false, or which once was true but now is usually false, etc.")
(comment RentingFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction,  #$RentingFn takes as its argument a type of #$PartiallyTangible thing and returns a collection of actions which are instances of #$Renting that type of thing.  (#$RentingFn OBJ-TYPE) is the collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible obtains the use (but not the ownership) of an instance of OBJ-TYPE by paying some money to the owner.  For instance, (#$RentingFn #$Automobile) is the collection of all events in which an agent rents a car.")
(comment TripleJ-RadioNetwork "#$TripleJ-RadioNetwork is a publicly owned #$RadioNetwork in Australia.  They are affilated with dozens of #$RadioStation-Organizations and have an official website.  It appeals to a younger audience through rock music and news.  It is similar to the television network MTV, but only for radio.")
(comment exportCapacityDuring "(#$exportCapacityDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE that could be exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile exports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars that could be exported.  In the case of oil exports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil that could be exported, or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil that could be exported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing what would be the average rate of export of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE from REGION during the temporal extent of THING if REGION were exporting PRODUCT-TYPE at the limit of its capacity.  Oil exports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment GrantingMoney "The collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (usually some #$Organization) grants #$MonetaryValue to another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible for some  specified purpose.  Every #$GrantingMoney event can also be thought of as a receiving event.  The receiving #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is expected to apply the money to the purpose (whether specific or generally unrestricted) for which the money is granted.")
(comment GreenlandPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Greenland-Polity, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment pointOfContactInfo "The predicate #$pointOfContactInfo allows one to characterize a string of information as belonging to a certain kind of contact location for a particular agent.  (#$pointOfContactInfo AGENT LOC-TYPE INFO-TYPE STRING) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT's contact locations of type LOC-TYPE (an instance of #$ContactLocationType (q.v.)) have STRING as one of their contact address of INFO-TYPE (where INFO-TYPE is a #$BinaryPredicate such as #$phoneNumberText, #$faxNumberText, or #$addressText).")
(comment agentTypeTypicallyDislikesRoleInEventType "A #$TernaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$BinaryRolePredicate to a specialization of #$Event.  <code>(#$agentTypeTypicallyDislikesRoleInEventType A-TYPE ROLE E-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>A-TYPE</code> typically dislike playing <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>E-TYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, (#$agentTypeTypicallyDislikesRoleInEventType #$DomesticCat #$objectTakenCareOf #$WalkingAPet) means that instances of #$DomesticCat typically dislike playing the role of #$objectTakenCareOf in instances of #$WalkingAPet -- that is, cats don't like to be taken for walks.")
(comment Possessing-SomeoneDominating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Dominating. In each #$Possessing-SomeoneDominating, something enters into someone and controls them with respect to emotions or ideas.")
(comment exportRate "(#$exportRate COUNTRY PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that COUNTRY exports PRODUCT-TYPE at the rate of RATE. Note that RATE may be expressed as a #$MonetaryRate, but also as rate of volume, mass or number depending on the type of product. For example, for oil which is a fluid we can say both (#$exportRate #$SaudiArabia #$PetroleumProduct (#$MillionDollarsPerYear NR)) and (#$exportRate #$SaudiArabia #$PetroleumProduct (#$MillionBarrelsPerYear NR)). Note that services, i.e. specializations of #$ServiceEvents are included as product types.")
(comment GamezProgram "The collection of #$ComputerGamePrograms that are available to be downloaded (see #$DownloadingAFile).")
(comment likesEventsOfType "(#$likesEventsOfType AGENT TYPE) means that AGENT has

positive feelings associated with events of type TYPE, such that if

EVT is and event of type TYPE, (#$feelsTowardsEvent AGENT EVT

#$Enjoyment Positive).  We also take it that for any role

ROLE such that (#$likesRoleInEventType AGENT ROLE ACTIVITYTYPE),

(#$likesEventsOfType AGENT ACTIVITYTYPE).")
(comment ClassicalMusicalCompositionTypeByMusicalForm "A collection of collections. Each element of

#$ClassicalMusicalCompositionTypeByMusicalForm is a collection of

#$MusicalComposition-Classicals, each element of which has the same

musical form or musical structure. For example, all #$Symphonys share

the musical form of a #$Symphony, so #$Symphony is an element of #$ClassicalMusicalCompositionTypeByMusicalForm.")
(comment BiologicalAgentType "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of #$BiologicalAgentStuff instances of a common type. (e.g. #$EbolaVirus or #$Anthrax-Bacterium)")
(comment meetsWith "An instance of #$ComplexActionPredicate.  This is the relation that holds definitionally between the different #$socialParticipants in an instance of #$Meeting-SocialGathering.")
(comment timeSpan "A #$TemporalPredicate and #$MeasurableQuantitySlot (qq.v.) that relates a temporal thing to the total elapsed time (see #$Time-Quantity) from its start to its end.  (#$timeSpan TEMPTHING TIME) means that TIME is the total elapsed time from when TEMPTHING started to exist (if a #$SomethingExisting) or happen (if an #$Event) or obtain (if a #$StaticSituation) to when TEMPTHING ceased to exist or ended.
<p>
Note that if TEMPTHING is #$temporallyContinuousDuring, its #$timeSpan is the same as its #$duration (q.v.): the length of time during which it actually existed or happened or obtained.  But if TEMPTHING is discontinuous, its time-span is strictly greater than its duration.  For example, the playing of the 2004 Super Bowl game has a time-span of several hours, but a duration of just one hour.")
(comment hasExistentialStatus "(#$hasExistentialStatus THING STATUS) means that THING is in the

existential state described by STATUS, an instance of

#$TemporalThingTypeByExistentialStatus.")
(comment AssertedBelief "An instance of #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType whose instances are all cyc arguments which were asserted into the KB by some agent.  This collection can be used to indicate that an assertion or group of assertions (mt contents) was purposely added to the Cyc knowledge base by some agent (as opposed to being inferred somehow by Cyc), and is to be treated as sound.")
(comment PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes a specification
SPEC of #$BiologicalLivingObject and returns the collection
of #$PhysicalEvents in which the outer layers of instances
of SPEC are penetrated via some \"sharp\" object.
(#$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOFn BLO-SPEC) denotes
the collection of all #$PhysicalEvents in which some
\"sharp\" object, say a bullet, insect stinger, tooth,
thorn, needle or knife, penetrates the outer surface of an
instance of BLO-SPEC.  For example,
(#$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLOFn #$Bear-Animal) denotes the
collection of all events in which a the skin of a bear
is penetrated by a \"sharp\" object like a bullet
or an insect stinger.  See #$PenetratingOuterLayerOfBLO.")
(comment Indifference "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Indifference is a feeling of indifference (i.e. not caring) about something.")
(comment GroceryMarketCategory "An element of #$ProductTypeByMarketCategory.  Each element of #$GroceryMarketCategory is a food product typically sold in grocery stores or grocery departments, e.g., canned foods, fresh produce, packaged cookies, frozen dinners.")
(comment surfaceFeatureOfObject "(#$surfaceFeatureOfObject OBJ ATT) means that the 'salient' surface of OBJ has the attribute ATT.  Which surface is 'salient' is a function of context in the broad sense of the term context.  If OBJ is a 'one-sided' object (see #$OneSidedVsTwoSidedObjectNote) such as a cave or room in a building (see #$Cavity) then the salient surface is the inside surface of OBJ.  For elements of #$ConvexTangibleObject, the outside surface is salient.  Thus, we can assert that, e.g., (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Cavity001 #$Concave).  Thus,  'Joe is wet' and 'The cave is wet', are easily translated into (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Joe #$Wet) or (#$surfaceFeatureOfObject Cave001 #$Wet).")
(comment CollapsibleDevice "A specialization of #$Collapsible and a #$MechanicalDevice (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$CollapsibleDevice is a device that is designed so that its shape (i.e., configuration of its parts) can be changed by collapsing (and uncollapsing) it.  This is a secondary function of some devices so that they can take up less space when they aren't being used for their #$primaryFunction.  (So #$CollapsibleDevices are typically devices that either aren't used often and/or must be kept or carried in a small space.)  Most #$CollapsibleDevices are collapsed in their storage (or unused) state and unfolded during use; e.g., instances of #$SofaBed, #$FoldingChair, and #$FoldingTable, also, #$Eyeglasses and most elements of #$Tent.  
<p>
Note: A marginal case, one which is better left outside this collection, is a collapsable front/rear of a car.  While it is a device, and collapsable, most of the things one would wish to state about a typical #$CollapsibleDevice would not be true for the crushable car end.")
(comment DiningAtACafe "An instance of #$Collection and a specialization of #$HavingAMeal. In each instance of #$DiningAtACafe, a person or group of persons has food or beverages at some instance of #$Cafe-Place.")
(comment KeepingSomething "The collection of events in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible deliberately            maintains possession of something.")
(comment soilTypeMovability "#$soilTypeMovability records a factor indicating how easy  it is for a bulldozer to move a given kind of #$Soil-Product.  #$ClaySoil and #$Loam take longer to move than #$Gravel.")
(comment CycLTermStatusCollection "The collection of all possible statuses of #$CycLIndexedTerm.  This includes #$PublicConstant, #$TooGeneral-CycTermStatus, #$InWrongMicrotheory, etc
.")
(comment Flamenco-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
flamenco style.                            ")
(comment Quintet-MusicalPerformanceGroup "A #$Quintet-MusicalPerformanceGroup is a group of 5 musicians that perform together.")
(comment AnnualEventType "#$AnnualEventTypes are events that are synchronized with the calendar and which occur yearly, e.g., the Stanford academic year, holidays, income tax filing date, etc.")
(comment agentFulfillsObligation "(#$agentFulfillsObligation AGT OB)

means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT fulfills the #$Obligation OB. Sometimes

this requires a positive action on the part of the agent, such as

repaying his debts in order to fulfill his financial obligations,

while other times it may mean merely that he does not commit an

action which violates some obligation; e.g., he does not blaspheme.")
(comment Game-CWRecordHoldersFn "(#$Game-CWRecordHoldersFn STRUCTURED_ACTIVITY) returns as its result the collection of all record-holders in performances of #$DevisedStructuredActivity, STRUCTURED_ACTIVITY. For example, (GameRecordHoldersFn TableTennis) returns the collection of all table tennisrecord holders.")
(comment Breakdancing-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
breakdancing style.                            ")
(comment GivingSomethingATry "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Attempting. In each #$GivingSomethingATry, someone tries some activity.")
(comment Spy "The collection of all elements of #$Person that monitor the activities of another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible under false pretenses or in a covert manner.  The goal of a spy's activities is to provide information about the observed #$Agent-PartiallyTangible for the purposes of another party (possibly the same as said spy) which is typically hostile to said #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  ``Corporate spys'', ``amateur spys'', as well as ``intelligence agents'' operating in the interests of indepent countries are possible elements of this collection.  See also #$IntelligenceGathering, #$intelligenceAgentInMission.")
(comment KSTemplateMicrotheory "An instance of #$KSTemplateMicrotheory is a microtheory containing #$ksImportationTemplate assertions for the 'slurping' of particular instances of #$KnowledgeSource-Represented, which are noted by #$ksHasTemplateMt assertions. With the creation of this constant, instances of #$KnowledgeSource-Represented should contain only knowledge source data while instances of #$KSTemplateMicrotheory should contain only #$ksImportationTemplate assertions.")
(comment ChemicalConversionExpansion "#$ChemicalConversionExpansion makes hypotheses about the conversion of a known instance of a chemical substances type into its possible products. That is, given a known mass of a chemical substance type, this expansion module will hypothesize the existence of (1) a #$ChemicalReaction, (2) a chemical product from that reaction, and (3) the mass of the product based on the mass of the initial, known chemical substance.")
(comment SubLAtom "A collection of #$SubLSExpressions that are atomic: they cannot be decomposed into other SubL expressions. Save for certain variables (see #$SubLVariable), instances of #$SubLAtom are rarely used in CycL assertions (other than assertions built with certain #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicates like #$defnIff). Many SubL atoms are not even #$CycLExpressions.  Do not confuse this collection with #$SubLAtomicTerm, which is a #$CycLExpressionType (though its instances are neither CycL constants nor CycL variables).  Note that #$SubLAtom is a \"quoted-collection\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment SergeantMajorOfTheCorps-Rank "The hightest #$NonCommissionedOfficerTypeByRank in the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps; intermediate between #$MasterGunnerySergeant-Rank and 

  #$WarrantOfficer-Rank.")
(comment unwantedMatter "This predicate is used to mark a physical object or piece of stuff as

being undesirable in a certain location, from the perspective of a

certain #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  The unwanted matter is a #$PartiallyTangible, the

location a #$SpatialThing-Localized.  Examples:  a #$Cockroach in a

#$HumanOccupationConstruct; #$Dirt on #$SomethingToWear;  a

#$ToxicSubstance in #$Food or #$Drink; a #$Virus or #$Bacterium

anywhere in the #$WholeBody of the viewpoint #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  See also #$wasteProducts.")
(comment crossReferenceInWorkTo "(#$crossReferenceInWorkTo WORK REF DOCSTRUC) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK contains (see #$containsStructure-CW)  REF, a #$CharacterString, or #$TextString, which REF is a cross-reference to DOCSTRUC, a #$GraphicalStructure or #$TextString that is also contained within WORK.")
(comment Single-MovementComposition "The collection of all #$MusicalComposition-Classicals that are not subdivided into separate #$CompositionMovements.")
(comment interviewee "(#$interviewee INTERVIEW AGT) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT is an interviewee in the #$Interviewing event INTERVIEW.")
(comment RequirementsForLicenseFn "#$RequirementsForLicenseFn takes as argument any spec of

         #$Permission and returns the collection of all requirements (instances of

         #$NeedMicrotheory) which must be met (made true) before a permission of that kind

         will be issued. For example, (#$RequirementsForLicenseFn

         #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement) returns the collection of requirements one must meet

         before one can be issued a drivers license.")
(comment executePrivilegeOfProgramCopy "(#$executePrivilegeOfProgramCopy COPY PLEVEL) means that instance of

#$ComputerProgramCopy COPY executes at #$PrivilegeLevelType PLEVEL on

the #$ComputationalSystem on which it is found.  For instance,

(#$executePrivilegeOfProgramCopy Sendmail001 #$RootPrivilege) means that Sendmail001 runs as root whenever it is executed.  Compare this predicate to #$executePrivilegeOfProgramOnSystem.")
(comment MilitaryIntelligenceProcess "#$MilitaryIntelligenceProcess is the subcollection of
#$IntelligenceAnalysisProcess whose instances involve the collection, analysis,
and dissemination of information for military purposes.")
(comment typeFunctionCapable "(#$typeFunctionCapable TYPE SYSTEMTYPE ROLE) means that
under normal background conditions, a normal instance of TYPE can play
the functional role (see #$SystemRolePredicate) ROLE with respect to the class
of #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEMTYPE.  This means, specifically, that for
some large and nontrivial set of instances of SYSTEMTYPE, it would be
unsurprising if Cyc learned that an instance of TYPE played the role
ROLE with respect to any of those instances.  (#$typeFunctionCapable
TYPE SYSTEMTYPE ROLE) does *not* mean that every instance of TYPE can
play the role ROLE in every instance of SYSTEMTYPE: e.g., a particular
instance of TYPE could not play ROLE in an instance of SYSTEMTYPE that
ceased to exist before the instance of TYPE had come into being.")
(comment Act-Dramatic "#$Act-Dramatic is the collection of all major divisions (#$subEvents) of instances of plays [#$Play-Dramatic or #$PlayPerformance-Musical] and operas [#$OperaPerformance] which are defined as \"acts\". ")
(comment ScalarInterval "A specialization of #$TupleOfIntervals (q.v.).  Roughly put, this is the collection of all things that can be ranked according to some one-dimensional scale.  Instances of #$ScalarInterval are numbers or quantities possessing only sign and magnitude.  They are construed as <i>one-tuples</i> (see #$Tuple) of intervals.  They are to be contrasted with #$VectorIntervals (q.v.), which possess a direction as well as a magnitude, and are construed as two-membered tuples of intervals.
<p>
#$ScalarInterval is partitioned into the two collections #$NumericInterval (which is the collection of numbers and number-ranges of all kinds) and #$Quantity (qq.v).  A #$Quantity is usually specified with a numeric-interval, as with (#$Meter 3)), but it might also be given in a generically-ranked way, as with (#$HighAmountFn #$Happiness); see the specializations #$MeasurableQuantity and #$NonNumericScalarQuantity.  The magnitude of a scalar might be given by a specific number (see #$ScalarPointValue) or by a proper range of numbers (see #$ScalarProperInterval).
<p>
Note that the instances of #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars (q.v.), which include artithmetic functions such as addition (see #$PlusFn) and division (see #$QuotientFn), are defined broadly so as to apply not only to numbers, but to (numerically-measured) scalar intervals generally.  Thus (#$PlusFn (#$Meter 3) (#$Meter 5)) is equal to (#$Meter 8).")
(comment Disapproval "The emotion or state of disapproving of something; a negative attitude towards some situation, proposal, person, or thing, implying a judgment based on explicit or implicit standards (rational, moral, pragmatic, or etc.).  This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  More specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Disapproval are #$Contempt, #$Hate, #$Abhorrence, etc.  More subtly, it is often true that feelings of #$Jealousy or #$Envy manifest in superficial shows of #$Disapproval.  #$Disapproval is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment Cloudiness "A specialization of #$WeatherQuantity.  Each instance of #$Cloudiness is a measure of how overcast it is in a particular #$OutdoorLocation.  At the low extreme (#$NoAmountFn #$Cloudiness), it is clear.  At the high extreme (#$VeryHighAmountFn #$Cloudiness) it is completely overcast.")
(comment pathogenTypicallyAcquiredBy "(#$pathogenTypicallyAcquiredBy PATHOTYPE ORGTYPE ACTIONTYPE) means, colloquially, that instances of ORGTYPE commonly acquire instances of PATHOTYPE, along with an associated infection, by performing instances of ACTIONTYPE.   More precisely, it means that if ORG is an instance of ORGTYPE, and (#$susceptibleToDiseaseCausedBy ORGTYPE PATHOTYPE), and ORG is the #$nonDeliberateActors in an instance of ACTIONTYPE, the likelihood that there will exist an infection caused by this action, in which the #$infectingOrganismMob is a mob of instances of PATHOTYPE and of which ORG is the #$infectionHost, is #$highAmountOf.")
(comment WesternTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs.  Instances of #$WesternTVShow tell a story with characters           and settings from the (mythical) old west.")
(comment screwedIn "(#$screwedIn SCREW OBJ) means that a threaded cylinder, SCREW, (normally a #$Bolt or a #$Screw-Connector) is #$in-Snugly #$rotationallyConnectedTo OBJ.  SCREW may have created or expanded a #$Cavity in OBJ (in the case of a #$Screw-Connector), or may be located in a pre-existing #$Cavity in OBJ threaded so as to match the threads on SCREW.  This is normally the case if SCREW is a #$Bolt or a threaded #$LightBulbIncandescent.")
(comment foodSourceFor "The predicate #$foodSourceFor relates a particular organism to the kinds of things it usually eats.  (#$foodSourceFor ORG OBJTYPE) means that ORG is an organism that typically eats some instances of OBJTYPE for food.  Note that OBJTYPE refers to a type of food source, not a particular object that ORG eats.  For example, (#$foodSourceFor #$RonaldReagan #$Popcorn-Popped) means that #$Popcorn-Popped is a #$foodSourceFor Ronald Reagan, i.e., Ronald Reagan often eats (instances of) popcorn.")
(comment X86ProcessorArchitecture "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByArchitecture. #$X86ProcessorArchitecture is a type of CISC computer processor architecture, produced by #$IntelCorporation. It includes the Pentium. For more recent architecture from Intel, see #$Ia64ProcessorArchitecture.")
(comment harmfulActions "The predicate #$harmfulActions is used to indicate that an agent engaged in a particular effort would (normally) diminish the chances of success in that effort by taking a certain role in events of a certain kind.  (#$harmfulActions ENDEAVOR SIT-TYPE ROLE DEGREE) means that the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR would (normally) be hindered if its agent participated as described by ROLE in a situation of the type SIT-TYPE.  DEGREE is an instance of #$GenericQuantity used to give an estimate of how damaging such an occurrence would be to the success of ENDEAVOR.  For example, for an agent trying to win in a football game, fumbling the ball disadvantages the agent to a #$highToVeryHighAmountOf degree.")
(comment Bedizening-SomeoneDressingUp "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DressingUp. In each #$Bedizening-SomeoneDressingUp, someone dresses up garishly and tastelessly.")
(comment HeavyDuty-PathArtifact "This is the collection of instances of #$PathForWheeledVehicles

that can accomodate heavy loads in all weather; these are usually paved 

avenues. Paths in this collection will also be instances of #$PavedPath for their surface quality and

#$AllWeather-PathArtifact.")
(comment ImpureFn "#$ImpureFn is a #$Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$ImpureFn X)           denotes the subset of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType X whose instances are chemically           impure. Note that #$ImpureFn can be applied only to instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType           (such as #$Fructose or #$Water), but not to mixtures (such as #$Air). See also           #$ImpureCompound as well as #$PureSubstance and #$PureFn.")
(comment AgriculturalResource "The collection of all things used in the pursuit of agriculture. This includes
devices like tractors and plows, any #$AgricultureOrganization, buildings like barns 
and silos, arable land, the #$AgriculturalFacility, and rivers and irrigation systems.
Crops and animals themselves do not constitute #$AgriculturalResources unless they are
to be used in the production of another agricultural product. Examples would include
dairy cows and livestock feed.")
(comment permissionsGrantedToPlayRoleInType "(#$permissionsGrantedToPlayRoleInType GRANTING EVENT SLOT)
means that instances of GRANTING allow, or give permission to some
agent to play the role of SLOT in an instance of EVENT.  For example, (#$permissionsGrantedToPlayRoleInType (#$IssuingLicenseTypeFn #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement) #$TransportInvolvingADriver #$driverActor) means that an instance of (#$IssuingLicenseTypeFn #$DriversLicense-LicenseAgreement) gives an agent permission to operate a motor vehicle.")
(comment AfricanCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located in the #$ContinentOfAfrica.  A person native to an area of Africa not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$AfricanCitizenOrSubject.")
(comment IssueIDFn "(#$IssueAboutFn ?STRING) means the #$Issue uniquely identified by that string. ")
(comment paragraphOf "'(#$paragraphOf STRUCTURE PARAGRAPH)' means that the #$TextString PARAGRAPH is a paragraph within the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE.")
(comment CarbohydrateStuff "The collection of chemical compounds that includes #$Sugar, #$Starch, #$Cellulose, and related compounds. These compounds are produced naturally by green plants from carbon dioxide and water (see #$Photosynthesis-Generic). As food for #$Animals, #$CarbohydrateStuff supplies energy and is used in the production of fats.")
(comment BookmarkForBooks "An object that is intended to be inserted between the pages of a #$Book-CW so that someone may easily find that place in the book.")
(comment permitter "'(#$permitter GRANT AGENT)' means that AGENT is the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who grants permission in the #$GrantingPermission GRANT.")
(comment beliefStatements "(#$beliefStatements SYSTEM BELIEF) means that the belief expressed by the #$ELSentence-Assertible BELIEF is part of the #$BeliefSystem SYSTEM. Note that #$BeliefSystems -- ideologies in terms of which agents make sense of the world -- are instances of #$AspatialInformationStore (q.v.).  In order to relate a belief to an actual #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who believes it, see the predicate #$beliefs.")
(comment TVMusical "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs that show musical dramas, such as 'The Sound            of Music' or 'Oklahoma'.")
(comment itemsStolen "(#$itemsStolen THEFT ITEM) says that ITEM was stolen in THEFT, an instance of #$Stealing.")
(comment styleOfArtist "(#$styleOfArtist ARTIST STYLE) means that the artist ARTIST produces mainly and is known for art of style STYLE. For example, the french painter #$ClaudeMonet-TheArtist would be linked  to Impressionism and the rock group Nirvana to #$MusicalComposition-GrungeRock.")
(comment Groping-AttemptingActivity "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Attempting. In each #$Groping-AttemptingActivity, something searches blindly or uncertainly.")
(comment nodeCutMinimalSetInSystem "(#$nodeCutMinimalSetInSystem SET SYS) means that the set SET of nodes in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS is a minimal node-cut set in SYS, i.e., SET is a subset of (#$NodesInSystemFn SYS) such that (#$nodeCutSetInSystem SET SYS) holds, and such that no proper subset SUBSET of SET satisfies (#$nodeCutSetInSystem SUBSET SYS).")
(comment fiscallyCapableOf "The predicate #$fiscallyCapableOf indicates that an agent has the economic prerequisites needed for playing a certain role in a certain type of situation or event.  (#$fiscallyCapableOf AGENT SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that a particular #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT has the financial resources needed to play ROLE in normal instances of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment hates "(#$hates HATER HATED) means that HATER has a negative, antipathetic disposition towards HATED.  When HATER thinks of HATED, HATER is likely to consciously feel (see #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree) certain negative emotions such as #$Irritation, #$Dislike, #$Hate.  HATER is more likely to avoid than approach HATED.  HATER is more likely to react aggressively than passively or conciliatorily towards HATED.")
(comment CWStructure "The collection of all instances of #$AbstractStructure that are the complete abstract structure of a #$ConceptualWork.")
(comment LimitedAccess "The attribute describing the security level of objects to which access is restricted in some way.  Kinds of #$LimitedAccess include #$Device-Locked, #$PhysicallyRestricted, and #$PasswordProtected.")
(comment oilProduction "This predicate denotes the amount or rate of oil produced by a
country or region.  An increase in this amount usually is correlated
with an increase in export (see #$oilExport), and consequently an
increase in gross domestic product (see
#$grossDomesticProductOf).")
(comment RightCoronaryArtery-PosterolateralBranch "A specialization of #$CoronaryArtery.  The posterolateral branch is one of two main branches of the #$RightCoronaryArtery-Generic. (The other main branch is the #$RightCoronaryArtery-PosteriorDescendingBranch.)")
(comment ComingOfAge "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$GrowingUp. In each #$ComingOfAge, someone reaches a certain age that marks a transition to maturity.")
(comment AbandoningSomething "The collection of events in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible deliberately gives up possession of something, without giving it to another.")
(comment winnerInConflict "(#$winnerInConflict CONFLICT VICTOR) means in the #$ConflictEvent CONFLICT, the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible VICTOR was the winner. ")
(comment PlanningGoalFn "(#$PlanningGoalFn GOAL) denotes the collection of events which are
instances of #$MakingAPlan such that the instance of #$Plan being
created is intended to achieve GOAL.")
(comment evidence "#$evidence is a more specialized form of the predicate #$topicRole.  It relates an instance of #$MentalSituation to an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  Like #$topicRole it is intended to relate an entity to an event where that entity is part of the content of some mental state of some agent in the role of #$deliberateActors in that event and shapes that agent's behavior during the course of that event.  This is a more specialized version, in that it states that this entity acts as evidence for the #$MentalSituation and, so, it promotes other beliefs that guide some agent's behavior.  For instance, a particular fossil could also play the #$evidence in an archaeological investigation.  This predicate provides a coarse representation and buries complex causal and psychological relations. Contrast with #$focalSubject and the other specializations of #$topicRole.")
(comment likesRoleInActivityCW "(#$likesRoleInActivityCW AGT SLOT GAME-CW) means that the instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGT likes playing the role (instance of #$ActorSlot) ROLE in the activity GAME-CW (instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity). For example, (#$likesRoleInActivityCW #$BillClinton #$spectators #$Broomball-SportCW) means that #$BillClinton likes watching #$Broomball-SportCW. Because games and sports can be represented as either instances of #$DevisedStructuredActivity or specs of #$PlayingAGame (see #$PlayingFn), we need a predicate to represent an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's relation to the abstract activity, an instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity. Use #$likesRoleInEventType to represent an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible's relation to collections of #$Events.")
(comment harmfulSubstanceExposedTo "(#$harmfulSubstanceExposedTo EXPOSING SUBSTANCE) means that SUBSTANCE is the instance of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance to which the #$organismExposed in EXPOSING is exposed.")
(comment wantsToRelnInstance "(#$wantsToRelnInstance AGT THING RELN) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible ?AGT wants to be in the relation RELN to THING.")
(comment NewOfTypeFn "The term `(#$NewOfTypeFn TYPE)' denotes the subcollection of TYPE consisting of

those instances which are relatively recent members of TYPE. This is broader than the attribute #$NewArtifact, which only applies to products. For example, `(#$NewOfTypeFn #$Singer)' would denote the collection of persons who have recently become singers, while `(#$NewOfTypeFn #$ElectricalToaster)' would denote

the collection of recently made toasters.")
(comment Vegetarian "The collection of all believers in #$Vegetarianism.")
(comment atypicalInfectionHost "(#$atypicalInfectionHost PATHOGENTYPE HOSTTYPE) means that if (#$pathogenTypeCausesInfectionType PATHOGENTYPE INFECTIONTYPE), and INFECTION is an instance of INFECTIONTYPE such that HOST is the #$infectionHost, and it is not known what kind of organism HOST is, there is a low #$likelihood that HOST is an instance of HOSTTYPE.")
(comment RevolutionaryWar "A specialization of #$War.  Each instance of #$RevolutionaryWar is a war the result of which is a successful revolution (see #$Revolution-Political).")
(comment Stealing "A specialization of both #$GainingControl and #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  In each instance of #$Stealing, an agent (see the collection #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) takes something belonging to another agent without that agent's permission (and possibly without that agent's knowledge).  Note that there may be some cases in which an agent takes something belonging to another agent without that agent's explicit permission that would nevertheless not be categorized as instances of #$Stealing.  For instance, a pair of agents may have an informal agreement or \"understanding\" that would cover casual \"borrowing\" from one another (and thus excuse it from being stealing).")
(comment RequiredResourceTypeForFn "A unary function that returns an instance of #$SecondOrderCollection when given a specialization of #$Situation as an argument. (#$RequiredResourceTypeForFn SIT-TYPE) denotes a collection of collections.  Each instance of (#$RequiredResourceTypeForFn SIT-TYPE) is a collection at least one instance of which is required to bring about an instance of SIT-TYPE.  Thus, (#$RequiredResourceTypeForFn #$GraspingSomethingWithATool) denotes the collection of collections instances of which are required to bring about #$GraspingSomethingWithATool.  If (#$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType #$GraspingSomethingWithATool #$GraspingImplement #$deviceUsed) holds, then #$GraspingImplement is an instance of (#$RequiredResourceTypeForFn #$GraspingSomethingWithATool).")
(comment agentFailsAssignment "An assertion of the form (#$agentFailsAssignment AGENT ASSIGN) asserts that the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT has failed to perform the appropriate sorts of action as specified by the #$Assignment-Specification ASSIGN during the ASSIGN's period and before ASSIGN's deadline (#$assignmentPeriod and #$assignmentDeadline (q.v.)).")
(comment CommunicationsStatusReport "A collection of instances of #$WrittenReportOnSituation.  Each instance is characterized by being about the status of communications services or infrastructure.")
(comment Particle "A specialization of both #$PartiallyTangible and #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Particle is a smallish liquid or solid tangible thing, usually small enough to be blown about by ordinary gusts of wind, and possibly much smaller.  Specializations of #$Particle include the collections #$CornMeal, #$SandParticle, #$Sawdust, #$DustParticle, and #$Sugar-Table.")
(comment Pseudomonadaceae "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the #$BiologicalGenus #$Pseudomonas, and other #$BiologicalGenus: Xanthomonas, Frateuria, and Zoogloea.  #$Pseudomonas includes many #$BiologicalSpecies that are human pathogens. These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$Bacterium-MotileByFlagellum by means of one or several polar flagella.  Although these are #$AerobicBacterium with a strictly respiratory type of metabolism with oxygen as the terminal electron acceptor, they may accept nitrate as an alternate electron receptor.  This allows for some growth to occur anaerobically.  This #$BiologicalFamily contains both oxidase-positive or -negative cells, but they are all chemoorganotrophs and catalase-positive.  Some #$BiologicalSpecies are facultative chemolithotrophs.")
(comment UnclaimedProperty "The collection of all things (including, possibly, money) that are owned by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible but are in the possession of another #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who is waiting for the first #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to come forward and claim the property.  Ordinarily the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in possession does not know where the owner is, or the owner's location is known but the owner has not claimed the property.  (This does not include #$CallLoans or #$DemandLoans.)")
(comment DBSaturationQueryProfilingTest-operatesInRegion2 "#$DBSaturationQueryProfilingTest-operatesInRegion2 is a
collection of three #$ALI_BABAContentTests which profile the
increasing complexity and performance degradation which occurs when
additional #$isa literals are added to the DB Saturation use case #$LDSC-SAICRules-OperatesInRegionMod.")
(comment RailroadStation "A specialization of both #$Building and #$TransportFacility.  Each instance of #$RailroadStation is a building located near railroad tracks whose primary purpose is to be a place where trains discharge and receive passengers (and possibly freight).")
(comment AlphaProcessorArchitecture "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByArchitecture. #$AlphaProcessorArchitecture is a type of RISC computer processor architecture, produced by #$CompaqInc.")
(comment directedIlluminationLevel "In the piece of free space ARG1, from the light source ARG2 a beam of directed light produces illumination of intensity ARG3 in that space.  Thus this is used to describe amount of direct sun- or moonlight.   In other contexts ARG2 should be more general than #$AstronomicalBody.")
(comment LocomotionProcess-Animal "The collection of processes in which an animal moves from one place to another by its own power.  A #$LocomotionProcess-Animal is an activity considered as a #$TemporalStuffType, in which any time-slice of the activity can also be considered an instance of that activity.  Subsets of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal include: #$AnimalWalkingProcess, #$Brachiating, #$Climbing, #$OperatingAWheelchair, #$Boring-Locomotion, etc.")
(comment VoidObject "An instance of #$ComputerDatatypeType. In 
#$C-ProgrammingLanguage, a void data type is used in function declarations to indicate that a function returns no values, or when constructing generic (i.e. typeless) pointers.")
(comment borrower "This predicate identifies an #$IntelligentAgent who gains a temporary right to use an object, subject to some #$Agreement, explicit or not, to return it.  #$BorrowingSomething is a specialization of #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights.  (#$borrower BORROW AGENT) means that after the event BORROW, AGENT enjoys some temporary #$SituationTypeByUserRights over the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer which that agent did not have at the start of BORROW.")
(comment characteristicActivityTypeOfAgentType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a specialization of #$Action.  <code>(#$characteristicActivityTypeOfAgentType AGT-TYPE ACT-TYPE)</code> means that performing instances of <code>ACT-TYPE</code> is what makes one an instance of <code>AGT-TYPE</code>.  This predicate is neutral with respect to whether it is
<blockquote>
(i) having performed <i>at least one</i> instance of <code>A-TYPE</code>;
<br>
(ii) <i>frequently</i> performing instances of <code>A-TYPE</code>; or
<br>
(iii) <i>presently</i> performing an instance of <code>A-TYPE</code>
</blockquote>
that makes one (presently) an instance of <code>P-TYPE</code>.")
(comment exportCapacity "(#$exportCapacity REGION PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is the greatest possible rate at which instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE could be exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION.  Note that RATE may be expressed as a #$MonetaryRate, but also as rate of volume, mass or number depending on the type of product.")
(comment BeingFreedFromControl "The collection of all instances of #$GainingFreedom in which the previously controlling agent wills for the freeing to take place:  i.e., in a #$BeingFreedFromControl, the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who #$losesControl intends for it to happen.")
(comment GullibleUsersPresent "#$GullibleUsersPresent is an instance of
#$ComputerNetworkBySecurityEnvironment.  Systems that have this attribute are
generally susceptible to being compromised by deceptive malefactors.")
(comment lexicalMtOfLanguageForSystem "<code>(#$lexicalMtOfLanguageForSystem LEXICON LANGUAGE SYSTEM)</code> identifies <code>LEXICON</code> as the <code>LANGUAGE</code>-specific lexicon for the classification system <code>SYSTEM</code>.  For example, <code>(#$lexicalMtOfLanguageForSystem #$GeneralEnglishMt #$EnglishLanguage #$TheCycOntology)</code> means that #$GeneralEnglishMt is the English-specific lexicon for the Cyc ontology.")
(comment PicturesFn "#$PicturesFn takes as argument any #$PartiallyTangible thing and returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting that thing.  For example (#$PicturesFn #$PyramidOfCheops) returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting the largest of the #$EgyptianPyramids.  Use #$PicturesFn-Organization (instead of #$PicturesFn) for pictures of #$Organizations such as rock groups, football teams, and geopoliticalEntities.")
(comment ReplacingSomething "A FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$ReplacementEvent.  Each instance of #$ReplacingSomething is a #$PurposefulAction in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible replaces something with something else, in some sense. Examples: changing a baby's diaper, electing a new person to a political office, trading in one's car for a new one, changing one's brand of deoderant, transferring from one university to another, changing clothes, quitting one's old job to take a new one, hiring a new person to take a departing employee's position.  A notable specialization is #$ReplacingAnObject (q.v.).")
(comment monetaryValueOfThingTo "This is a ternary version of the binary predicate #$monetaryValueOfThing, which allows assertions regarding a thing's value to be relativised to those to whom it is so valuable. (#$monetaryValueOfThingTo THING VALUE AGENT) means that the #$TemporalThing THING (which may be goods or services) has a #$MonetaryValue VALUE to the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT. THING might have VALUE to AGENT for a number of different reasons -- it may have been appraised as such, or bought for such, or it may just be what the agent is #$willingToPay. See also #$costTo.")
(comment ClumpConceptTypeByDomainFn "(#$ClumpConceptTypeByDomainFn CLUMP) denotes a collection whose instances -- or, more specifically, elements via #$coreConceptOfDomain -- are the concepts denoted by the terms belonging to CLUMP.")
(comment EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization "#$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization is an organization whose #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction is to provide personal entertainment to customers.  This collection includes organizations that perform or provide other forms of entertainment, as well as organizations which provide spaces in which entertainment is scheduled or provided.  Specific types of #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization include: #$TelevisionStation, #$TelevisionNetwork, #$NightClub, #$TheaterCompany, #$Cinema-Organization, #$AmusementPark, #$Band-MusicGroup.")
(comment Blood "The collection of all volumes of live blood.  Each instance is a portion of fluid that circulates in an #$Animal's #$CirculatorySystem or that is preserved in a living state outside of a body.  Dried blood, blood stains, and scabs are not considered to be #$Blood but (#$DeadPhysicalRemainsFn #$Blood).")
(comment CarnivoreOrder "An instance of #$BiologicalOrder, and a specialization of #$Mammal. Instances of #$CarnivoreOrder are mammals whose teeth are adapted for efficient cutting of meat and tendon. Although instances of #$CarnivoreOrder have teeth adapted for eating meat, not all instances of #$CarnivoreOrder are meat-eaters; #$Bear-Animals are omnivorous, while #$PandaBears are usually vegetarians. See also the collection #$Carnivore.")
(comment ProgrammingAComputer "A specialization of both #$ComputerActivity and #$IBTGeneration-Original. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible programs some #$Computer by physically typing a copy of the program into it. For particularly clever or expert programming feats, see #$Hacking. See also #$WritingAComputerProgram -- the collection of events in which some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible creates a #$ComputerProgram-CW (of course many instances of #$WritingAComputerProgram will also be instances of #$ProgrammingAComputer).")
(comment ClassicalIndian-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
classical Indian style.                           ")
(comment trademarkStringOf "(#$trademarkStringOf AGENT GOOD STRING) means that company or person AGENT (an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) has a government-granted right to market product or service GOOD using as mark some physical embodiment of the string STRING.")
(comment CephalicDirection "The general direction towards the head (away from the tail), in or near an object that has attribute #$AnimalShapedThing.  In the case of a #$Person this is the #$VectorInterval comprising the cone-shaped set of vectors pointing (from some reference point) within approximately forty-five degrees of straight up when in an #$UprightPosture.")
(comment IndustryInfrastructureReqFn "(#$IndustryInfrastructureReqFn INDUSTRYTYPE) returns the collection of all products such that any typical member of an #$Industry-Localized that is an instance of INDUSTRYTYPE will require those products in order to carry out its function.  Usually these products will need to be purchased on the commercial market.  The function takes as its argument an instance of #$IndustryType that is a collection of geographically defined industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized).  Ordinarily, this will be a collection of industries of a particular type, and may be a CycLNonAtomicTerm (NAT) reified via #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn.")
(comment ComputerTypeByArchitecture "A specialization of #$ComputerTypeByHardware. Each instance of this collection is a variety of  computer processor architecture -- for instance #$X86ProcessorArchitecture. Notable specializations of this collection are #$RISCArchitecture and #$CISCArchitecture.")
(comment LowLevelOfVirulence "The lowest positive #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionVirulenceLevel.")
(comment grossNationalProduct-Old "The Gross National Product (GNP) of a nation is the total income of all its citizens and resident corporations, whether obtained from domestic or foreign commercial activities.  The second argument to #$grossNationalProduct-Old is a #$MonetaryRate, usually given in #$BillionDollarsPerYear.  Note:  A nation's #$grossNationalProduct-Old (GDP) is usually considered a better indicator of economic health than its GNP.")
(comment completeDiseaseScriptOf "(#$completeDiseaseScriptOf DIS-TYPE SCRIPT-TYPE) means that the #$ScriptedEventType SCRIPT-TYPE is the complex event-type that charts the typical course of the #$DiseaseType DIS-TYPE from its onset to either recovery or death. The script assumes that the disease is left untreated and that the person undergoing the disease has no immunity. Other relationships might be needed if we want to represent the course of a disease when either or both of these conditions are not met. See #$CompleteDiseaseSituationTypeFn.")
(comment Fire-ClassD "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of
#$CombustionProcess. Instances of #$Fire-ClassD have as their
#$energySourceForEvent combustible metal, including aluminum, magnesium,
titanium, and lithium.")
(comment ManufacturingOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$ManufacturingOrganization is an organization whose main function (see #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction) is the manufacture or production of goods.  Instances of #$ManufacturingOrganization may be departments, suborganizations, companies, or conglomerate enterprises.")
(comment organismExposedToHarmfulSubstanceInAttack "A #$AgentCasualtyPredicate that relates a #$TerroristAttack to an #$Organism-Whole that is exposed to a harmful substance in (some proper subevent of) that attack.")
(comment EMailServiceEvent "The Collection of #$ServiceEvent in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is using the services of a #$EMailServiceProvider-WebBased in order to read or write #$EMailMessageTexts.")
(comment pointsOfContact "The predicate #$pointsOfContact indicates the places at which an agent can be located.  (#$pointsOfContact AGENT LOC) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible AGENT can be contacted at the #$ContactLocation LOC.")
(comment ScriptFunction-CorrespondingPredicate "#$ScriptFunction-CorrespondingPredicates is a sub-collection of #$SituationTypeRelation.  Its instances are the predicates which correspond to the instances of the collection #$SituationTypeFunction.")
(comment Admiration "A feeling of strong approval.  An intense positive attitude towards another person(s) or group.  May be accompanied by emulation.  #$Admiration is different than #$Respect (qv).  This is a collection --- see #$Happiness for an explanation.  Some more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityTypes than #$Admiration are #$Wonder-Admiration, #$Adulation, #$Awe, etc. ")
(comment directionsOfPath "This predicate can be used to state which directions a
(non-directed) spatial path such as a two-way street runs in.  
(#$directionsOfPath PATH DIR1 DIR2) means that PATH runs in a 
relatively straight line from DIR1 to DIR2 (and vice versa, of 
course).  DIR1 and DIR2 must be roughly opposite directions 
(see #$oppositeDirection-Interval).  If PATH is not relatively
straight (see #$CenterLineOfPathFn and #$LinearObject-Straight), or
is an instance of #$DirectedCustomaryPath, the above statement 
will be false or malformed; so #$directionsOfPath should not 
applied to such paths.")
(comment RealityTVShow "A collection of #$TVShow-IBTs, those in which footage is shown from videos taken of            live, usually dramatic or funny, events.  Examples: 'Cops', 'America's Funniest           Home Videos'.")
(comment RecipeFn "#$RecipeFn takes any spec of #$FoodOrDrink and returns the collection of all PropositionalInformationThings which are recipes for (instructions for making)  that type of food or drink.  For example, (#$RecipeFn #$BlackForestCake) returns the collection of all recipes for Black Forest Cake.")
(comment Gerontophilia "The collection of #$ParaphilicSexualBehaviors in which a younger #$Person shows an abnormal erotic interest in some #$OldHuman,  precisely because his/her physical appearance shows all the otherwise unappealing signs of his/her old age.")
(comment MusicTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs primarily intended to            entertain with music or music videos.  There are two main

 type, those that show music videos and those that show concerts.")
(comment Guitar-AcousticElectric "Instances are instances of #$Guitar 

that are acoustic -- i.e., they produce sound

 via string vibration amplified in a resonance 

chamber -- yet they

 are fitted with electronics and are 'plugged

 in' to an amplifier so as to generate a 

  louder and more sculptable sound.")
(comment hasMembers "The predicate #$hasMembers relates a particular organization to the agents who are members of that organization.  This predicate indicates `generic' membership, although there may be specialized kinds of membership in the same organization.  (#$hasMembers ORG AGENT) means that AGENT is a member of the #$Organization ORG; typically, membership eligibility is determined by ORG and accepted with AGENT's voluntary affiliation.  In general, a member may be any #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, including other #$Organizations (such as member countries in the United Nations), although only instances of #$Person can be members of instances of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly.  The truth of an assertion made with #$hasMembers may be time-dependent and, if so, should be qualified appropriately.  For example, (#$holdsIn (#$YearFn 1975) (#$hasMembers #$UnitedNationsOrganization #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina)) is true, but (#$holdsIn (#$YearFn 1995) (#$hasMembers #$UnitedNationsOrganization #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina)) is not.")
(comment QueryMacroPredicate "The collection of predicates that are shorthand for a complicated removal query.  For instance, #$performsActsOfType-Percentage relates an agent to two collections of acts and a number, NUM, just in case the ratio of the instances of the first collection performed by the agent that are also instances of the second collection is NUM.  The actual CycL for this query is rather complicated and requires two uses of #$extentCardinality and #$TheSetOf.  #$performsActsOfType-Percentage abstracts the important replacable terms from that query as argument places in the predicate allowing the query to be easily modifiable.  Each instance of this collection has one or more rules that define the query.  Such rules may or may not be supported in code.")
(comment Willingness "Feeling of willingness to participate in an event or situation; consenting or being prepared to participate.   (#$feelsTowardsEvent AGENT EVENT #$Willingness DEGREE) means that AGENT is willing for EVENT to come about to DEGREE degree.  Note: This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  A more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityType than #$Willingness is #$Eagerness.")
(comment ConformingMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements which meet all requirements (size, type, and age) necessary for them to be eligible for purchase or securitization by federal agencies.  (#$ConformingMortgages are #$LimitConformingLoans, in that they meet the standards of the federal agencies as lenders.)")
(comment negativeVestedInterest "<code>(#$negativeVestedInterest AGT OBJ)</code> means #$Agent-PartiallyTangible <code>AGT</code> has a negative interest in the object <code>OBJ</code> or in the good fortune of <code>OBJ</code>, and a positive interest in its misfortune.  Generally, <code>AGT</code> will be helped or pleased by the destruction, diminution, weakening, or retarding of <code>OBJ</code>, and will be hurt or displeased if <code>OBJ</code> is preserved or enhanced.  See #$positiveVestedInterest.")
(comment NullLevelOfInfectivity "The lowest #$NonNumericScalarQuantity of #$InfectionInfectivityLevel.")
(comment TVGameShow "A subset of #$TVShow-IBTs in which contestants play a game, usually in front of an           audience and for #$MonetaryValue.  Examples include 'Jeopardy' and 'The Price is Right'.")
(comment MysteryMovie "#$MysteryMovie is a collection of instances of #$MovieShowing each of which relates a story involving a mystery.")
(comment takesControl "<code>(#$takesControl TRANSFER AGENT)</code> means that in the #$TransferOfControl, the agent taking control of the #$objectOfControlTransfer is <code>AGENT</code>.  Every #$TransferOfControl features exactly one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible in the role of #$takesControl (albeit this #$Agent-PartiallyTangible may be a #$Group of other #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles).")
(comment Calcium "A metallic element, and one of the heavier instances of #$AlkalineEarthMetalElementType.")
(comment TreatingAsIfEvent "A collection of events. Each element represents a physical
event, mental event, or a composite physical and mental event that can
be characterized as an event in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible behaves (mentally or
physically) as though some #$ELSentence-Assertible were true of some #$Thing. For
example, each of the following are examples of events in which
#$Fred is treating #$Sally as if she were his friend:
<p>
1. Fred says \"Sally is my friend;\"
2. Fred thinks \"Sally is my friend;\"
3. Fred asks Sally to help him move.
<p>
The preds. to use with this event are #$asIfDuringByTo, #$asIfBy, and #$asIfTo.")
(comment Hostility "An instance of #$EmotionalQuantityType.  Each instance of #$Hostility is some agent's feeling of strong antagonism towards some (individual or multi-individual) agent, sufficient to motivate harmful speech or actions against the latter.  Instances of #$Hostility vary depending on the intensity of the feeling, the subject experiencing the feeling, or the object of the feeling. One notable specialization of #$Hostility is #$Hate.")
(comment detects "(#$detects SENSOR STUFF) means that instance 

 SENSOR of #$Sensor has detected STUFF.  Be mindful of the

 difference between #$detects and #$perceives; only 

 #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles perceive, which is (partially) accomplished through

   the detection process via some #$Sensors to which they

    are related.  So, for example, you are a perceiver,

    but your ears (or perhaps your auditory sense system as a whole)

     are detectors.  Only tangible things, #$PhysicalEvents or #$PartiallyTangibles, can be detected")
(comment lessLikelyThan-Prior "A predicate used for probability statements. (#$lessLikelyThan-Prior PROPOSITION1 PROPOSITION2) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the <em> a priori</em> probability that PROPOSITION1 is true is less than the <em> a priori</em> probability that PROPOSITION2 is true.  This predicate does not say what the probabilities actually are numerically; it is just an ordering (or rather partial ordering) relation between the two propositions.  In most microtheories, generally, this #$lessLikelyThan-Prior means that the 'prior' probability that PROPOSITION1 is true is less than the 'prior' probability that PROPOSITION2 is true, given only the truth of the #$domainAssumptions accessible in the applicable #$Microtheory, without regard to any further evidence or the truth of any other assertions.  Contrast this with #$atLeastAsLikelyAs (which makes no claim of dependence on or independence from other assertions) and with #$lessLikelyThan-Derived (which assumes dependence on other assertions).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism <em>versus</em> nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.")
(comment ridiculousSentence "(#$ridiculousSentence SENTENCE) means that the content of #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE (which is usually the subject of a #$suggestedSentence assertion) is patently inappropriate, usually because of type or obvious disjointness checking that should have been performed.  As an example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$InferenceParameter) is ridiculous.")
(comment InfectionTypeByAfflictionType "A collection of #$Collection. Elements of #$InfectionTypeByAfflictionType are specs of #$Infection whose instances share the common property of afflicting the same type of body part, see #$AnimalBodyPart. See #$ailmentTypeAfflictsPartType, #$InfectionFn.")
(comment similarWRTTypeViaBinRel "This predicate is used to make the similarity between two things more explicit.

  (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel THING1 THING2 COL BINPRED) means that

THING1 and THING2 both bear the relation BINPRED to similar instances

of COL, i.e., if there is an instance of COL, COLINS1 such that

(BINPRED THING1 COLINS1) then either (BINPRED THING2 COLINS1) or

there is some similar instance of COL, COLINS2, such that (BINPRED

                              THING2

                              COLINS2).  

 For instance, (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel #$BillClinton

#$GeorgeWBush #$Automobile #$likesObject) means that Clinton and Bush have similar tastes in automobiles.  Note

that (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel THING1 THING2 PRED COL) does not necessarily imply that (#$similarTo THING1 THING2), however, we might expect that claims of similarity between THING1 and THING2 be accompanied by clarification of the respects in which THING1 and THING2 are similar.  Note that this predicate, along with #$similarTo, is intended as a very general starting place for the development of improved vocabulary to discuss similarity in Cyc.  Use or introduce a specification, e.g. #$similarWRTPartType, (or see #$resemblesInQuantity or #$identicalInQuantity) when possible or feasible.")
(comment underwriterOfLoan "The predicate used to identify the #$LoanUnderwriter for a particular instance of #$FinancingByBorrowing.  (#$underwriterOfLoan FINANCE ORG) means ORG is accepting the risk for FINANCE.")
(comment MassOrSpatialQuantity "An instance of #$AtemporalNecessarilyEssentialCollectionType and a specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  This is just the #$collectionUnion of #$Mass and #$SpatialQuantity.")
(comment includedItems "The predicate #$includedItems is used to identify the peripheral items that come with a particular packaged product.  (#$includedItems FORM ITEM) means that the #$Individual ITEM is one of the things that are included in the #$PackagedProduct FORM, along with its #$mainProduct; but ITEM is not the main product itself.  ITEM can be an accessory, owner's manual, warranty agreement, or included service.  ITEM is something that is a regular part of the package.  ITEM does NOT refer to free samples or extras thrown in--for that, see #$includesWithProductType.")
(comment genlSpecifications "A specialization of #$generalizations. (#$genlSpecifications REFINEMENT SPECIFICATION) says that the REFINEMENT, an instance of #$Specification, is a refinement of the instance of #$Specification SPECIFICATION.  This means that any action ACT that is performed in accordance with REFINEMENT (c.f. #$situationConformsToSpecification) is one that is thereby performed in accordance with the more general SPECIFICATION.")
(comment PossiblySelfEmployed "A Cyc #$AttributeValue.  The attribute #$PossiblySelfEmployed is used (in conjunction with the predicate #$jobClass) to describe instances of #$PersonTypeByOccupation whose practitioners are commonly, but not always, remunerated on a contract basis or by selling their goods (or services) by the piece (or performance).")
(comment importRateThrough "(#$importRateThrough REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION imports instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT (on their way from their origin) at the #$Rate RATE.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for example, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  Note that since things imported are typically measurable in terms of their monetary value, RATE might in some instances be a #$MonetaryRate; in others it will be, for example, a rate of volume, mass, or number.")
(comment usedOneAtATime "(#$usedOneAtATime EVENT HEAP) means that in the event EVENT, the things belonging to HEAP are used one at a time. Plausibly, in most uses of this term the event argument will actually be filled by an iterative event, ie., one that is composed of many single subevents of the same type (cf. #$IterativeEventType). The main difference between this predicate and #$iterativeStep: arg2 of #$usedOneAtATime is #$PartiallyTangible (hence we use #$Group), #$iterativeStep can take as its arg2 a wider variety of #$IterationEventByTypes.")
(comment Bazooka "The collection of shoulder-held #$MissileLaunchers that fire #$Missiles which are #$RocketPropelledTransportationDevices and #$AntiArmorWeapons.")
(comment TranscriptOfSpeech-CWIS "The collection of all #$AbstractInformationStructures which specify the words of the #$AnimalUtterance-IBTs in a #$SpokenCommunicating event.")
(comment ailmentTypicallyAcquiredBy "(#$ailmentTypicallyAcquiredBy INFECTIONTYPE ORGTYPE ACTIONTYPE) means, colloquially, that organisms of type ORGTYPE commonly acquire infections of type INFECTIONTYPE via actions of type ACTIONTYPE. To put it more precisely, it means that if organisms of type ORGTYPE are susceptible to a type of #$Microorganism that causes infections of type INFECTIONTYPE, and an organism of type ORGTYPE is the #$nonDeliberateActors in an action of type ACTIONTYPE, the #$likelihood that the organism will acquire an infection of type INFECTIONTYPE is #$highAmountOf.")
(comment structureTaggedByHTMLTag "(#$structureTaggedByHTMLTag DOCUMENT STRUC TAG) means that STRUC, an instance of #$GraphicalStructure, #$TextString, or #$CharacterString, is identified by the #$HTMLTag TAG within the #$HTMLSource for DOCUMENT, a #$GraphicalStructure generated by an #$HTMLSource.  STRUC is necessarily one of the #$subStructures of DOCUMENT and TAG is necessarily one of the #$subStructures of the #$HTMLSource that generated DOCUMENT.  #$structureTaggedByHTMLTag necessarily implies that there is an opening tag for the structure tagged by the HTMLTag (see #$openingTagForStructure); there may also be a closing tag that immediately follows structure and which corresponds to the opening tag (see #$closingTagForStructure).")
(comment Demonstrative-NLAttrType "This #$QuantityType includes all NL attributes which are 'demonstrative' in nature, e.g., this/that/these/those. These should only be used in cases where a specific tangible and/or temporal object is being pointed out, not in purely pragmatic instances (see #$Backreference-NLAttrType).")
(comment CapitalCityOfRegion "A specialization of #$City.  Each instance of #$CapitalCityOfRegion is a city that is the capital of its surrounding region.  This includes capitals of countries as well as capitals of subregions of countries, such as states, provinces, and counties.  Examples include #$CityOfRomeItaly, #$CityOfCardiffWales, #$CityOfAustinTX, #$CityOfAbidjanIvoryCoast, #$CityOfLhasaTibet, and #$CityOfColumbusOH.  See also #$capitalCity and #$capitalCityOfState.")
(comment NeedTypeByImmediacy "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$NeedTypeByImmediacy is a spec of #$NeedMicrotheory whose instances contain assertions about the relative immediacy of a thing's needs.")
(comment trademarkStringOfCW "(#$trademarkStringOfCW AGENT DW STRING) means that company or person AGENT (an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) has a government-granted right to market instantiations of the #$DevisedPracticeOrWork DW using as mark some physical embodiment of the string STRING.")
(comment causes-ThingProp "(#$causes-ThingProp THING PROP) means that THING causes the proposition PROP to become true.  THING may be an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, a #$Situation, or  a #$ELSentence-Assertible.  This is a very general predicate.  It is almost always better to use a more specialized predicate such as #$causes-PropProp, #$causes-EventEvent, or #$causes-SitProp, particularly in rules.  Nonetheless, #$causes-ThingProp can be useful if one wishes to collect all the possible causes of some proposition be they #$Situations, #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles, other propositions (see #$ELSentence-Assertible).  See #$NoteAboutCausationPredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment Number-General "A specialization of #$NumericInterval and #$ScalarPointValue (qq.v.).  This is the most general collection of numbers.   Each instance of #$Number-General is a number in some sense of the word, i.e. an element of some mathematical structure with at least reasonably conventional notions of arithmetic and ordering.  Canonical examples include integers, rational numbers, and real numbers.  Some specializations of #$Number-General are #$RealNumber, #$ComplexNumber, #$PrimeNumber, and #$ProbabilityInterval.")
(comment importThroughAmountDuring "(#$importThroughAmountDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT (on their way from their origin) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for instance, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil imported (by REGION through PT), or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil imported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION through PT during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment HorrorTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-IBTs normally classified            as horror shows.")
(comment MeasurableScalarIntervalType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$MeasurableScalarIntervalType is a collection of #$ScalarIntervals that are quantifiable; i.e. they are either purely numeric (see #$NumericInterval) or quantities that can be assigned a numeric value (see #$MeasurableQuantity).
<p>
Instances of #$MeasurableScalarIntervalType include #$Integer, #$ProbabilityInterval, #$RateOfRotation, and #$Time-Quantity.  Specializations include #$IntegerTypeByRange and #$MeasurableQuantityType.")
(comment DollarsPerYear "An instance of #$UnitOfMonetaryRate.  When applied to a real number REAL (or a sequence of two real numbers INTERVAL), #$DollarsPerYear returns a #$MonetaryRate of REAL #$Dollar-UnitedStates per year (respectively, INTERVAL #$Dollar-UnitedStates per year.")
(comment SecurityInformation "A subset of #$AspatialInformationStore, each instance of which  is about one or more #$IndividualTypeBySecurityStatuss of an individual.")
(comment predExtractsDateOfCalendarCoveringType "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$OfDateFn.  (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical PRED CALENDAR-COVERING-TYPE) means that PRED, an instance of #$DateExtractionPredicate is a predicate that relates a date DATE to the unique instance of #$CalendarCoveringType that intersects DATE.  For example, (#$predExtractsDateOfCalendarCoveringType #$calendarDayOfDate #$CalendarDay) means that #$calendarDayOfDate relates a date DATE to the calendar day that intersects DATE.")
(comment mediaProductTypeLocation "This predicate specifies places in which types of #$MediaProducts are available.  (#$mediaProductTypeLocation PRODUCT-TYPE PLACE) means that a person who is in PLACE at the appropriate time (cf. #$mediaProductTypeDuration) can access instances of PRODUCT-TYPE, which is a #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType (q.v.) and a collection of #$MediaProducts.  Examples: A #$Library-Organization containing a copy of 'Frankenstein' is a #$mediaProductTypeLocation for #$Frankenstein-TheBook, a collection of #$Book-CWs.  A #$TelevisionSet receiving an episode of 'Star Trek' is a #$mediaProductTypeLocation for #$StarTrek-Classic, a #$SpecifiedTVSeriesType.")
(comment ExperiencingEmotion "#$ExperiencingEmotion is the collection of events in which one particular agent experiences emotion or affective feeling (for what constitutes an emotion or affective feeling see #$FeelingAttribute).  See also #$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree, #$feelsTowardsEvent, #$feelsEmotion, #$feelsPotentialEmotion.")
(comment preReformulation-AssignmentTemplateTopic "preReformulation-AssignmentTemplateTopic tells the fact entry tool to use RULE to pre-reformulate an assertions relative to #$ProjectManagement-TemplateTopic.")
(comment PrintReproduction "The collection of #$VisualInformationBearingThings that are reproductions of original works of art (as a painting) made by a photomechanical process.")
(comment templateUsed "An expression of the form (#$templateUsed PROCESS TEMP) means that the (#$ProgramProcessFn #$CycBrowserFactEntryToolModule)  PROCESS used the #$FormulaTemplateType TEMP as part of its operations.")
(comment DerivedProbabilityFn "A function used for probability statements.  (#$DerivedProbabilityFn PROPOSITION), applied to the #$CycLAssertion PROPOSITION, yields, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the a posteriori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, given (and depending on) the current state of knowledge of other assertions.  The result is a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true.  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the derived probability that PROPOSITION is true given the probabilities or truth values of the other #$CycLAssertions and #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.   Contrast this with the predicate form #$derivedProbability and with the functions #$PriorProbabilityFn and #$DerivedProbability-RangeFn.  The result of #$DerivedProbabilityFn depends at least partially on, and is in some manner derived from or affected by, the probabilities of some or all of the other #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory (whether prior, derived or conditional) along with the #$domainAssumptions.  See also #$conditionalProbability.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment AirTravelTestSpecification "A specialization of #$CBRNE-IR-KBTestSpecification.  Instances are queries used to test Cyc's knowledge of airlines, airports, and air travel.")
(comment polityFamousForProductType "(#$polityFamousForProductType GEO PROD-TYPE) means that the instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, GEO is famous for producing instances of the #$ProductType PROD-TYPE. Since this predicate is a #$genlInverse of #$productTypeOriginatesIn, q.v., the same sense of 'produce' applies.")
(comment PrepositionalRoleMarker "A specialization of #$GrammaticalRoleMarker. These attributes provide grammatical role information for arguments which are introduced as the object of a preposition in input text processed by the BBN software.")
(comment GivingSamples "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$GivingSamples, a business #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (typically a #$SalesRepresentative of a #$CommercialOrganization) gives samples of the business's product to a prospective or current customer, in order to increase the likelihood of future sales.")
(comment rowOfTable "'(#$rowOfTable TABLE ROW)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure ROW is a row within the #$Table-AIS TABLE.")
(comment PlaybackFn "(#$PlaybackFn MEDIA) returns the collection of events in which some instance of MEDIA is 'played back' via an automated reader/player.  For example, (#$PlaybackFn #$CompactDisc-Audio) denotes those events in which a #$CompactDisc-Audio is played by a #$CompactDiscPlayer.  'Playing' in this sense consists of reading the item's contents and 'broadcasting' them in some way -- typically, by generating either sound or video or both.  Playings of instances of MEDIA may also include an interactive component, as in the playing of a #$VideoGameCartridge by a #$VideoGameSystem.  The function does not return the complete class of automated 'reading' of encoded contents -- e.g., transferring or loading the contents of a CD into memory of a computer.")
(comment MachineProtocolParticipantType "The types of #$Artifact-Agentives participating in or employing a #$MachineProtocol.")
(comment abstractOfSameWork "(#$abstractOfSameWork WORK TEXT) means that the #$TextString TEXT is an abstract of WORK, the #$StructurallySpecificWork within which TEXT is contained.  Abstracts are short summaries of the content of an instance of #$ConceptualWork.  Although abstracts of works often are contained in other works, the application of #$abstractOfSameWork is restricted to abstracts of the #$StructurallySpecificWork in which the abstract is contained.  For abstracts of works contained in other works, see #$abstractOfOtherWork.")
(comment intendedOrientation-DeviceType "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate.
#$intendedOrientation-DeviceType describes the intended orientation,
with respect to the object acted on, of a #$PhysicalDevice being used
according to its #$intendedPrimaryFunction. The orientation is
required in order for the device to be causally efficacious in
fulfilling the primary function. The orientation is specified in terms
of a spatial relation that a specified type of part of the device must
bear to a specified sort of #$situationConstituents in the device's
intended use.
<p>
In particular, intendedOrientation-DeviceType (DEVICE-TYPE PART-TYPE
ROLE RELATION) means that during an instance of the intended primary
function of a device of type DEVICE-TYPE, the intended orientation of
the device consists in one or more of its physical parts of type
PART-TYPE bearing the relation RELATION to one or more of the things
that play the role ROLE in the event.  For example,
(intendedOrientation-DeviceType WritingPen PenTip objectMarked touchesDirectly)
means that during any instance of MarkingOnASurfaceWithAPen, a #$PenTip of
the #$WritingPen that is the #$deviceUsed should bear
the #$touches-Directly relation to the #$objectMarked.
<p>
Note that the intended orientation need not obtain throughout all of
the intended-use event. Rather it must obtain throughout all of each
of a certain type of subevent of the intended-use event. For
example, although the pen tip need not touch the writing surface during
all of a given writing event (e.g., because the writer might lift the
pen to dot an \"i\"), the pen tip does need to touch the writing
surface throughout all of each of the writing event's subevents that
are of type #$MarkingOnASurfaceWithAPen-Uninterrupted.")
(comment scalarDimensionalRank "A binary predicate that is used to associate a given #$ScalarInterval with a rank (represented by an integer), as determined by the complexity of the dimensional analysis (see #$unitTypeDimensionalAnalysis) relevant to that scalar.  
<p>
<code>(#$scalarDimensionalRank SCALAR RANK)</code> means that <code>SCALAR</code> has rank <code>RANK</code>, where <code>RANK</code> is determined as follows.  If <code>SCALAR</code> is a #$NumericInterval (q.v.) then <code>RANK</code> is 0.  If <code>SCALAR</code> is a #$MeasurableQuantity measurable in units of a #$FundamentalUnitType (q.v.) then <code>RANK</code> is 1.  If <code>SCALAR</code> is a quantity measurable in units of a derived unit-type whose dimensional analysis is:
<pre>
  (#$TheSet
    (#$TheList UNITTYPE-1 EXPONENT-1)
    (#$TheList UNITTYPE-2 EXPONENT-2)
    ...
    (#$TheList UNITTYPE-n EXPONENT-n))
</pre>
<p>
then <code>RANK</code> is the sum of the absolute values of all of the <code>EXPONENT-i (1 <= i <= n)</code>.  Otherwise (e.g. if <code>SCALAR</code> is a #$NonNumericScalarQuantity), it is not associated with any rank.
<p>
For example, the rank of (#$Meter 5) is 1, as #$Meter is a #$UnitOfDistance, which is a #$FundamentalUnitType.  And the rank of (#$MilesPerHour 25) is 2, as #$MilesPerHour is a #$UnitOfSpeed, which has the analysis:
<pre>
  (#$TheSet
    (#$TheList #$UnitOfDistance 1)
    (#$TheList #$UnitOfTime -1)) ;
</pre>
<p>
and 1 + |-1| = 2.  Similarly, the volume (#$CubicFoot 18) has rank 3.")
(comment SyntaxSpecificationSystem "The collection of all specifications of the syntax of relational structures (often #$CharacterStrings, #$TextStrings #$AnimalUtterance-IBTs or whole #$Languages).  The system may or may not be formalized with a precise test for compliance of a given structure with the specification.  Most #$FormalGrammarSpecifications are #$StringGrammars, but there are also #$GraphGrammars and other kinds.  A #$SyntaxSpecificationSystem can specify #$ComputerLanguages, #$NaturalLanguages, decorative patterns, networks, document structures, plan structures, semantic networks, programs, protocols, etc.")
(comment RadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all instances of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable which are specialized for operations involving instances of #$RadarDevice.  Two important specializations are #$DirectionFindingRadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty and #$SignalInterceptionRadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty.  The default expectation is that a #$RadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty will be able to perform a nontrivial subclass of #$MilitaryEvents in which instances of #$RadarDevice play an instrumental role.")
(comment artifactHonors "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$Artifact and #$SymbolicThing to instances of #$TemporalThing, and a specialization of #$honorsThing. (#$artifactHonors ARTIFACT HONOREE) means that ARTIFACT is created or constructed to honor or commemorate HONOREE, and to cause people who perceive ARTIFACT to remember and respect HONOREE.  HONOREE can be a #$Person, a group of people, a pet, an event (such as a battle won) or another physical object (even a body part, in the case of the statue at Saratoga honoring Gen. Benedict Arnold's untainted leg).  For cases where ARTIFACT is an instance of #$MemorialMarker and HONOREE is an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, see the more specific predicate #$monumentHonors.")
(comment nucleotidesBasePaired "(#$nucleotidesBasePaired NUCL1 NUCL2) means that there is a hydrogen bond between the nitrogen bases that are the respective components of #$Nucleotides NUCL1 and NUCL2. Normally, only complementary nitrogen bases are base paired (see #$complementaryBaseTypes), but it is possible for two #$NitrogenBases to be base-paired incorrectly, e.g., a hydrogen bond can be formed between two #$NitrogenBases that are not complementary. In  such a case, the #$Nucleotides of which these bases are components are incorrectly base-paired. Use #$basesComplementaryBasePaired and #$nucleotidesComplementaryBasePaired for the relations when the bases are paired correctly.")
(comment NeglectingToDoSomething "A #$FirstOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$NeglectingToDoSomething is an event in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible fails (intentionally or unintentionally) to do something that it had intended to do, or was in some sense expected or obliged to do.")
(comment ChildrensTVShow "Instances of #$ChildrensTVShow are #$TVShow-IBTs intended primarily for children, e.g.            'Sesame Street' or 'Arthur'.")
(comment scaleUsed "(#$scaleUsed EVALUATION SCALE) identifies SCALE as the instance of #$PrimitiveOrderedQuantityType for which the evaluee (see #$objectOfEvaluation) in the evaluation (see #$Evaluating) EVALUATION is assigned some value.")
(comment Communist "The collection of persons who believe in the #$Communism.")
(comment PoweringADevice "A collection of events; a subset of #$HandlingADevice.  An instance of #$PoweringADevice is an event in which a human or non-human animal #$Agent-PartiallyTangible (or set of them) uses a device which is designed to transform some repetitive muscular motion into useful work, namely into providing the power for some device to function.  E.g., a #$Rowing event is such an event, and causes (provides the power for) the device (the rowboat) to move.  The same for #$PedalingABicycle .  The same for pulling a covered wagon (in which case a team of horses may be providing the power.)")
(comment loudnessLevel "A #$SensoryAttributeDescriptionPredicate and #$QuantitySlot that relates an #$AudibleSound to a #$AcousticNoiseLevel.  (#$loudnessLevel SOUND LEVEL) means that the noise/loudness level of SOUND is LEVEL.")
(comment doesTypeEvery "(#$doesTypeEvery AGENT EVENT-TYPE TIME) means that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible
plays the #$doneBy role in instances of EVENT-TYPE every TIME.
Consider the difference between this predicate and
#$doesTypeWithFrequency.  Arg3 for #$doesTypeEvery an instance of
#$TimeParameter and #$TimeInterval, while arg3 for
#$doesTypeWithFrequency is Frequency.  ")
(comment AccountingUse "The collection of instances of #$Computer that can be or are designed to be put to accounting uses.  To
specify that a computer has this feature use: #$computerPutToUse.  For instance,
(#$computerPutToUse Comp01 #$AccountingUse) states that Comp01 can be used for accounting.")
(comment UniformResidentialLoanApplication "The collection of all uniform residential loan applications. A type of #$TextualDocument-CW.")
(comment PeatFire "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Fire-ClassA. Instances of #$PeatFire have #$Peat-Dried as their #$energySourceForEvent.")
(comment softwareParameterDomain "(#$softwareParameterDomain SOFTWARE-PARAMETER COL) means that the value of SOFTWARE-PARAMETER [see #$softwareParameterValue] is restricted to being an instance of the #$Collection COL. Such restrictions may or may not coincide with a #$ComputerDatatypeType in a language in which the #$SoftwareParameter is coded.")
(comment packagedIn "A predicate for relating an object to a container in which it is packaged. (#$packagedIn OBJECT CONTAINER) means that OBJECT, an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, is packaged in container, an instance of #$ContainerArtifact.")
(comment ClothingSizeType "A collection of collections of collections.  Each instance of #$ClothingSizeType is a type of clothing size. Each instance of an instance is a collection of persons who have that particular size.  For instance, #$ManTypeByShoeSize is an instance of #$ClothingSizeType and each instance of that collection is a collection of people who wear that particular size.  To state a person is a particular size in something use #$humanMeasurements.  To state that an article of clothing is a particular size use #$clothingSize.")
(comment analogousFeelings "(#$analogousFeelings EMOTYPE1 EMOTYPE2) means that a feeling of the type EMOTYPE1 is analogous to a feeling of the type EMOTYPE2.  When #$analogousFeelings holds between two instances of #$EmotionalQuantityType, there is a high probability that an agent feeling an emotion of one of those types is also feeling an emotion of the other type.")
(comment Beryl "A #$Beryllium and aluminum silicate #$Mineral from which the #$GemStones #$Emerald-Gem and #$Aquamarine-Gem are derived.")
(comment emigrants "(#$emigrants COUNTRY PERSON) means that PERSON has emigrated
from COUNTRY to another. In #$Immigration events, COUNTRY plays the #$fromLocation role.")
(comment clumpTermsDenoteDomainConceptsOf "(#$clumpTermsDenoteDomainConceptsOf CLUMP DOMAIN) means that the concepts denoted by the terms which are in the #$CycSubjectClump, CLUMP, are members of (via #$coreConceptOfDomain) the #$ConceptTypeByDomain, DOMAIN.")
(comment iBTTypeIsOfGenre "(#$iBTTypeIsOfGenre IBT-TYPE GENRE) holds just in case for each instance, INS, of IBT-TYPE there is a corresponding instance of GENRE, INS-CW, such that they stand in a certain relationship.  Sometimes this relationship is 'instantiation'.  Consider the collection of actual showings of action movies MOV (not the events but the images and sounds). (#$iBTTypeIsOfGenre MOV #$PropositionalConceptualWork-ActionGenre) holds and the relation in this case is #$instantiationOfWork; (#$relationAllExists #$instantiationOfWork MOV #$PropositionalConceptualWork-ActionGenre). In general, this predicate relates a type of information bearing thing with its genre.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-ActionGenre "The collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks that are of the action genre.  Very similar to the #$PropositionalConceptualWork-AdventureGenre but often with less focus on traveling.")
(comment AnimalBodyRegionType "This is a collection of collections; in particular, it is a #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType (q.v.).  Consider any one element of #$AnimalBodyRegionType, call it X.  X is a collection of subsets of #$AnimalBodyRegion, such that any two elements of X are either disjoint or else one is a subset of the other  E.g., the set consisting of the three elements (#$LeftObjectOfPairFn #$Hand), (#$RightObjectOfPairFn #$Hand), #$Hand, would be a legal element of #$AnimalBodyRegionType.")
(comment abstractOfOtherWork "(#$abstractOfOtherWork WORK TEXT SUMMARIZEDWORK) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK contains (see #$containsStructure-CW) TEXT, a #$TextString which is an abstract of SUMMARIZEDWORK, a #$TextualPCW.  WORK and SUMMARIZEDWORK are necessarily different #$ConceptualWorks.  Instances of #$Bibliography often contain abstracts of the works cited therein.  For abstracts of a work within that work itself, see #$abstractOfSameWork")
(comment GranularFluid "A specialization of #$FluidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$GranularFluid is a mass of some granular substance (where a granular substance is any instance SUBSTANCE of #$PartiallyTangible for which (#$physicalStructuralFeatures SUBSTANCE #$Granular) holds) which is in 

sufficient quantity to behave largely as a liquid. Instances of #$GranularFluid assume the shapes of their containers, and they are capable of being poured and stirred (as in food preparation).")
(comment slotCalculationFormula-Division "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate and #$SlotCalculationFormulaPredicate, used to state a method of calculating the value of a slot (c.f., #$ScalarIntervalSlot) for a given argument through division.  (#$slotCalculationFormula-Division SLOT DIVIDEND-SLOT DIVISOR-SLOT) means that for ARG, the value of VALUE in (SLOT ARG VALUE) can be arrived at by dividing DIVIDEND-SLOT-VALUE in (DIVIDEND-SLOT ARG DIVIDEND-SLOT-VALUE) bu DIVISOR-SLOT-VALUE in (DIVISOR-SLOT ARG DIVISOR-SLOT-VALUE).  For example,
 (#$slotCalculationFormula-Division #$priceToEarningsRatio #$basicPrice #$earningsPerShare-ForStockType) means that one can arrive at the PE ratio of a given stock by dividing its basic price by its 12 months earnings per share.")
(comment Milestone-Goal "An instance of #$GoalTypeByCategory.  A state of affairs has this attribute for an agent if it is pursued as a means of reaching some milestone.  For instance, a hockey player might have a goal of scoring three goals in his next game because the third goal would be the three hundredth goal of his career.  Then scoring three goals in the next game would have the attribute #$Milestone-Goal for the agent.")
(comment advertisementUsed "A predicate relating an advertising event to advertisements used in that event. (#$advertisementUsed EVENT ADVERT) means that ADVERT, an instance of #$Advertisement-PCW, is instantiated in an #$Advertisement-IBT that is generated by EVENT, an instance of #$Advertising. This predicate is useful for relating an advertising campaign to various instances of #$Advertisement-PCW that are used in that campaign. To relate an advertising event to an instance of #$Advertisement-PCW that appears in each instance of #$Advertisement-IBT generated by that event, use #$advertisementUsed-Generally.")
(comment SupportCommunicationsForMission "A collection of #$AttributeValues denoting various gradations of communications            support a unit or instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible might provide for a mission.             The kind of support intended here includes instances of #$SupplyingMeansOfCommunication.")
(comment RegularExpressionGrammar "The collection of all #$StringGrammars that specify sets of 'grammatically valid' strings by defining the acceptable strings by means of #$RegularExpressions.  Often a candidate #$CharacterString is tested against a #$RegularExpression with a computer program that uses a state-change or transition network to help recognize the string as having acceptable substructures.  #$RegularExpressionGrammars are often used in script languages like #$Perl-ProgrammingLanguage.  See also #$ContextFreeGrammar and #$ContextSensitiveGrammar.")
(comment AttackOnIBT "A specialization of #$AttackOnObject.  Each instance of this collection is an action intentionally #$performedBy an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who has the #$purposeInEvent that the action damages the #$objectActedOn.  In such attacks, the attacker intends that the #$AspatialInformationStore that 
is encoded in the IBT (#$InformationBearingThing) attacked, be damaged or changed from one instance of #$AspatialInformationStore to another. Note that the IBT attacked need not be a physical object (though it might be -- for instance a copy of Moby Dick). It might be, for instance, a web-site.")
(comment Mingling "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BecomingAParticipantInSomething. In each #$Mingling, someone gets involved or mixed-up with something.")
(comment assertionJustificationAttribute "(#$assertionJustificationAttribute ASSERTION JUST) means that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION is supported by a justification having the #$CycArgumentTypeByJustificationType JUST (for example, #$CausallySupported, #$JustifiedByAuthority).")
(comment Commission-Organization "The collection of all commissions formally organized and authorized to perform certain duties or functions. #$Commission-Organizations are groups of individuals and are usually named. Each instance of #$Commission-Organization consists of several individual #$hasMembers and may, and include a #$Commissioner-Rank as an #$organizationHead. They are different from #$Committee-Organizations in that they typically granted an #$hasAuthorityOver over #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles who aren't members of the commission's organizational chain, whereas committees are typically advisory in nature.")
(comment functionCapable "(#$functionCapable THING SYSTEMTYPE SYSTEMSLOT) means that
under 'normal' background conditions THING is capable of playing the
functional role (#$SystemRolePredicate) SYSTEMSLOT with respect to the class of
#$FunctionalSystem SYSTEMTYPE.  This means, specifically, that for
some large and nontrivial set of instances of SYSTEMTYPE, it would be
unsurprising if Cyc learned that THING played the role SYSTEMSLOT with
respect to any of those instances.  (#$functionCapable THING
SYSTEMTYPE SYSTEMSLOT) does *not* mean that THING can play the role
SYSTEMSLOT in every instance of SYSTEMTYPE: e.g., in instances of
SYSTEMTYPE that ceased to exist a long time before THING came into
being, or instances that are part of situations in which it has been
otherwise rendered impossible for THING to play the role SYSTEMSLOT in
that instance.")
(comment Poise-UnitOfAbsoluteViscosity "The poise is unit of dynamic viscosity in the CGS system.  A poise is equal to the viscosity of a fluid that would require a shearing force of one dyne to move a square-centimeter area of one of two parallel layers of fluid one centimeter, with a velocity of one centimeter per second, relative to the other layer. In other words, it is the ratio of the shear stress to the shear rate of a fluid, expressed in dyne seconds per square centimeter. More commonly seen in actual use is the (#$Centi #$Poise-UnitOfAbsoluteViscosity), or 0.01 poise.")
(comment RGBFn "An instance of #$TernaryFunction.  #$RGBFn takes three instances of (#$IntegerFromToFn 0 255) and returns the instance of #$ColorPerceptionCategoryType that has red, green, and blue light in the amounts indicated by the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd arguments, respectively.  See also #$colorHasRGBRedValue, #$colorHasRGBGreenValue, and #$colorHasRGBBlueValue.")
(comment actsInCapacity "The predicate #$actsInCapacity indicates the capacity in which an agent participates in certain kinds of actions.  (#$actsInCapacity AGENT ROLE SCRIPT-TYPE CAP) means that the agent AGENT plays the role ROLE in instances of SCRIPT-TYPE, and s/he does that role in the capacity CAP.  CAP is a #$CapacityPredicate (q.v.) which describes the AGENT's mode of participation--e.g., as a job, hobby, main function, support function, etc.  Contrast three cases of acts of #$GreetingSomeone, when #$performedBy: (1) instances of #$Receptionist, in their #$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity and as their #$actsInCapacity-MainFunction; (2) instances of #$FlightAttendant, in their #$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity but as a #$SupportFunction; and (3) instances of #$TrainEngineer, in a #$actsInCapacity-HobbyCapacity (though they do it while working, it's not part of their job).")
(comment InfiniteSpatialThing "A specialization of #$PositiveDimensionalThing.  Each instance of #$InfiniteSpatialThing is a spatial thing that measures an infinite #$Distance (see #$InfiniteScalarInterval) in at least one dimension (see #$extensionParametersOfObject).  An infinite line (see #$LinearObject-Infinite) has an infinite length; an infinite surface has infinite length and/or infinite \"width\"; and an infinite three-dimensional spatial thing has infinite length, infinite \"width\", and/or infinite \"height\".
<p>
An infinite spatial thing might be intangible or (at least in theory) tangible.
Cf. #$FiniteSpatialThing.")
(comment reliabilityOfReportSources "(#$reliabilityOfReportSources ?REPORT ?RELYLEVEL) means that the sources of #$WrittenReportOnSituation ?REPORT are considered to have a collective #$ReportTypeBySourceReliability of ?RELYLEVEL.")
(comment Morris-StyleOfDance "The collection of instances of #$Dancing-Human that are in the
morris style.                            ")
(comment PowerPCArchitecture "An instance of #$ComputerTypeByArchitecture. #$PowerPCArchitecture pertains to computers which have a PowerPC chip -- developed jointly by IBM, Apple and Motorola.  This chip was initially to be found in #$IBMComputers and #$MacintoshComputers, but seems to have survived only in the Mac.")
(comment losesControl "<code>(#$losesControl SIT AGENT)</code> means that in the #$TransferOfControl <code>SIT</code>, <code>AGENT</code> is the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible who loses or relinquishes control over the #$objectOfControlTransfer.")
(comment SugarManufacturingOrganization "The collection of organizations whose primary activity is manufacturing sugar. This process is described in #$SugarManufacturing.")
(comment SponsorFn-StructuredActivity "#$SponsorFn-StructuredActivity takes as argument any instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity and returns the collection of all agents sponsoring performances of such activity.  For example, (#$SponsorFn-Event Baseball-TheGame) would return the collection of agents sponsoring baseball games.")
(comment SystemPrivilege "A #$PrivilegeLevelType in #$MSWindowsNT environments.  The level 

of privilege depends on the particular environment, but normally

#$SystemPrivilege is similar to #$AdministratorPrivilege, and can

sometimes be greater.  See #$SystemAccountForNT.")
(comment Fire-ClassA "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$CombustionProcess. Instances of #$Fire-ClassA have as their #$energySourceForEvent non-metal, non-electrified, solid materials such as wood, paper, rubber, plastic, or cloth.")
(comment AdministeringSomeMedication "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent. In each #$AdministeringSomeMedication, someone gives or applies (medications) to something.")
(comment ProtocolTransportMediumType "The collection of #$SignalTransportMediumTypes through which the signals involved in a #$MachineProtocol are carried (eg a computer network, a bus, a radio signal).")
(comment cellIn "'(#$cellIn STRUC CELL)' means that the #$GraphicalStructure CELL is a cell within the #$GraphicalStructure STRUC.  #$cellIn can relate a particular cell to the #$Table-AIS that it is one of the #$subStructures of or to the #$GraphicalStructures that are rows or columns of which it is a part. ")
(comment Steak-Beef-MeatCut "The collection of all beef steaks. A type of #$Beef and #$Artifact. The collection #$Steak-Beef-MeatCut is a #$MeatCutType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType. Each instance of #$Steak-Beef-MeatCut is a thick slice of beef, cut perpendicular to the muscle fibers.")
(comment InfoStructureOfCWFn "A function taking a #$ConceptualWork, CW, as its argument and returning the collection of all #$AbstractInformationStructures corresponding to the whole CW.  More precisely, (InfoStructureOfCWFn CW) denotes the collection of all #$CWInfoStructures, ?CWIS, such that (#$infoStructureOfCW CW ?CWIS).  For example, (#$InfoStructureOfCWFn #$MobyDickNovel) is the collection of all #$TextStrings whose physical instantiations are copies of Moby Dick (i.e., instances of #$PartiallyTangible).  Similarly, (#$InfoStructureOfCWFn LoveBugVirus-CW) denotes the collection of #$ComputerCode such that any physical instantiation of an instance of that collection is a copy of the LoveBugVirus-CW.")
(comment MSRestrictedSitesZoneFn "One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be initiated from the \"Restricted Sites Zone\". The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. The term \"Restricted Sites Zone\" refers to  sites explicitly defined as such for that particular computer by its user(s).")
(comment LevelOfRelaxationFeeling "A specialization of #$InternalSensoryQuantity whose elements represent the qualitative levels of comfort/relaxation/ease that an animal may have.  This feeling is generally internal, and relatively long-lasting (compared with, e.g., the duration of a painful twinge.)  Any positive degree of this #$LevelOfRelaxationFeeling is incompatible with a high level of #$MuscleTenseness, a high #$LevelOfPain, or a high #$LevelOfDiscomfort.")
(comment partiallyInsideSpaceRegion-Inverse "(#$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion-Inverse REG1 REG2) means 

that REG2 is \"partially inside\" REG1. This is the inverse of #$partiallyInsideSpaceRegion.")
(comment mtSourceType "(#$mtSourceType MT SOURCE-TYPE) means that the information in MT originated with, or is authenticated by, an information source of type SOURCE-TYPE.  SOURCE-TYPE will most commonly be a specialization of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, or of #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment UnitPosition "A collection of #$SystemRolePredicates.  Each instance is a
functional role that an agent may play within an instance of
#$ModernMilitaryOrganization, considered as a functional system: e.g.,
#$unitCommander.")
(comment Shivering "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$MovingInvoluntarily. In each #$Shivering, someone shakes, as from cold.")
(comment FixedTerrainGeologicalRegion "The collection of all (normally extensive) #$GeographicalRegions distinguised by the type of surface growth.  See #$RegionTypeBySurfaceGrowth")
(comment doesToWith "This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the
agent (active participant), the object (passive participant) and the
tool or device of an activity. Example: (#$doesToWith 
#$Cleaning #$PeterSuen PetersFloor
PetersMop)
is true iff Peter cleans (or: is cleaning, depending on the way the assertion is
temporally qualified) Peter's floor with his mop.")
(comment AmorphousThing "A specialization of #$SpatialThing.  Each instance of #$AmorphousThing is a spatial object that has no well-defined shape (though what counts as a \"well-defined shape\" can vary from context to context).  Contrast with #$ShapedObject.")
(comment agentAffiliationDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentAffiliationDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses the fact that AGENT is affiliated with some other agent (during some time interval).")
(comment PublicLibrary "A specialization of #$Library-Organization.  A #$PublicLibrary allows anyone to refer the items within its #$LibraryHoldings.  However, only the members of a particular #$PublicLibrary are allowed to borrow (see  #$BorrowingLibraryItem) the items within its #$LibraryHoldings.  Certain members of the #$PublicLibrary do not have to pay a membership-fee because  they satisfy certain criteria (for example, residing in the city/county/etc. where the library is based) laid down by the #$PublicLibrary.")
(comment ScholarshipAgreement "An instance is a scholarship, a kind of #$Agreement where     one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible gives another some amount of #$MonetaryValue to be used    for their education    imposed on the receiving #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.")
(comment RiskTaking "#$RiskTaking is the collection of all #$PurposefulActions in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is doing something risky, hazardous or dangerous.")
(comment EatingADishOfFood "An instance of #$IterativeSituationType and a specialization of #$EatingEvent.  Each instance of #$EatingADishOfFood is an event in which an individual animal consumes a substantial portion of the food on a dish.")
(comment PerformingArtActivity "The collection of activities that #$Artist-Performers do. Its subsets include things like #$Singing, #$Dancing-Human, #$DramaticActing, #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument, etc. What is being captured in this collection are the actions that #$Artist-Performers do, both in preparation for and during a performance. For the collection of performace events, see #$EntertainmentPerformance.")
(comment ACEInhibitor "Elements are angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors. Each #$ACEInhibitor is an #$Antihypertensive-Drug that reduces the enzymatic conversion of Angiotension I to Angiotension II.")
(comment ApplyingForFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction which takes as its argument a type of thing and returns the specialization of #$ApplyingForSomething in which things of that type are applied for. (This typically involves someone requesting that a contract of some form be entered into with them.)  (#$ApplyingForFn OBJ-TYPE) is the collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible applies for things of that type. For instance, (#$ApplyingForFn #$LoanAgreement) is the collection of all events in which someone applies for a loan.")
(comment LongitudeLineFn "(#$LongitudeLineFn DEG MIN DIR) returns the longitude line around the earth at the distance from the #$PrimeMeridian-Greenwich specified by degree DEG, minute MIN, and direction DIR.")
(comment PersonWithNationality "The collection of persons who have some nationality (cf. the faceting second-order collection #$PersonTypeByNationality), either because they are citizens of some #$Country (cf. #$citizens), or because they are participants in its #$NationalCulture to some significant degree, usually by virtue of having been born or raised there. It is disjoint with #$StatelessPerson.")
(comment CheatsForGameTypeFn "#$CheatsForGameTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$ComputerGameProgram and returns the collection of all instructions for cheating at that type of game.  For example, (#$CheatsForGameTypeFn Quake) would return the collection of all instructions for cheating at the computer game Quake.")
(comment employingAgent "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$WorkAgreement to instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  (#$employingAgent AGREE EMPLOYER) means that the #$Agent-PartiallyTangible EMPLOYER has entered into the #$WorkAgreement AGREE with some employee, and AGREE obligates EMPLOYER to compensate that employee for specified work.  See also #$employedAgent and #$employees (which relates employees to their employers).")
(comment hasCommunicabilityLevel "(#$hasCommunicabilityLevel INF-TYPE LEVEL) means that instances of the #$InfectionType INF-TYPE have the level of contagiousness, LEVEL.  For those exposed to a host of this type of #$Infection, LEVEL would describe the risk of their getting infected.")
(comment ConvEventInfoMicrotheory "A collection of instances of #$Microtheory that contain information about the major events at a given #$Convention-Meeting or #$Conference.")
(comment MSInternetZoneFn "One of a series of functions used to represent Microsoft's \"Internet Security Zone\" concept. The function takes as its argument an instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, which describes some action which it is possible to perform on certain computers, and allows one to state that that action may be initiated from the \"Internet Zone\". The result of this function is therefore also a (qualified) instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. The term \"Internet Zone\" refers to the internet at large, except for any sites which might have been defined for that particular computer as falling in the \"Restricted Sites\" zone, (see #$MSRestrictedSitesZoneFn.).")
(comment StrivingWithDetermination "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Endeavoring. In each #$StrivingWithDetermination, someone strives  with determination.")
(comment correctlyParsedSentence "(#$correctlyParsedSentence SENTENCE) means that a reviewer who looked at the #$CycLPropositionalSentence SENTENCE felt that the information content of the sentence has been correctly parsed from a text source, given the system's current knowledge.  This is not to say that the content of SENTENCE is *correct* or *true* - for example, (#$isa #$Cynthia #$Married) is correctly parsed from 'Cyndy is married.', but incorrect.  This distinction depends on the context within which the judgement is being made, and is necessarily subjective.  See also #$incorrectlyParsedSentence.")
(comment Em-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to mark certain text that will be emphasized in the #$GraphicalStructure generated by the #$HTMLSource.")
(comment Nervousness "Feeling of nervousness and excitability.  One can be nervous ABOUT something in particular, or one can have undirected feelings of anxiety.   For the former, state an assertion of the form (#$feelsTowardsObjectToDegree AGT OBJ #$Nervousness DEGREE) or (#$feelsTowardsEvent AGT EVNT #$Nervousness DEGREE); but for the latter (undirected feelings of anxiety) use (#$feelsEmotion AGT #$Nervousness).

Note: This is a collection; for an explanation of a typical #$EmotionalQuantityType, see #$Happiness.  A more specialized #$EmotionalQuantityType than #$Nervousness is #$Panic.")
(comment SportsClothing-IBO "The collection of #$ClothingIBO

having to do with sports.  This includes jerseys used by actual sports

teams and clothing - e.g., t-shirts, baseball caps, and jackets - sold

 to the public.")
(comment SensoryAttributeDescriptionPredicate "A collection of predicates that relate objects to a sensory attribute.  This category is distinguished from #$PhysicalFeatureBinaryPredicate because instances of this spec describe relations which implicitly assume a perceiver, i.e., things have sensory attributes in virtue of being perceived and the  nature of the attribute is somewhat perceiver dependent and even dependent upon the perceptual conditions.  Sensory attributes are perceiver dependent in a way that other physical attributes are not.  Locke's distinction between secondary and primary qualities is relevant to the distinction alluded to here.")
(comment authenticationPerformedBy "(#$authenticationPerformedBy AUTH_EVENT AGENT) means that the instance of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible, AGENT, performs the instance of       #$AuthenticationEvent AUTH_EVENT in order to gain access to some individual.")
(comment featureOfPathArtifact "This predicate can be used to indicate various properties an
instance of #$PathArtifact may have. (#$featureOfPathArtifact PATH ATT)
means that the instance of #$PathArtifact PATH has the property described
by ATT, which is an instance of #$PathArtifactTypeByStructuralFeature. For instance,
(#$featureOfPathArtifact #$Highway101CA #$PavedPath) means that
Highway 101 is a paved highway.")
(comment TemporaryChangeOfUserRights "A specialization of both #$ChangeInUserRights and #$Transaction.  In each instance of #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights, one agent temporarily gives up user rights (see #$SituationTypeByUserRights) over some object to another agent.  Note that the agent who gives up user rights over the object does so voluntarily.  Notable specializations of #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights include #$Renting and #$BorrowingSomething.")
(comment Vacation-TimeAllocation "A sub-collection of #$LeaveOfAbsence-TimeAllocation.  Instances of #$Vacation-TimeAllocation describe intervals of time when some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible is not available to work for an #$Organization due to that #$Agent-PartiallyTangible taking advantage of an #$Organization's policy of allowing its workers to take periods of time off for rest and recuperation.  This collection is distinct from #$FloaterHoliday-TimeAllocation because of the rules governing its accrual by workers.")
(comment VitalNationalInterest "The #$GoalTypeByCategory used to characterize national interests crucial to a country's survival and of direct concern to its military forces.  Examples of such interests include: maintaining a country's territorial integrity, guaranteeing the well-being of its citizens, guranteeing the security of its allies.  This classification is motivated by the taxonomy presented in the Internation System Framework document prepared by IET-PSR (available in 1998-1999 at http://www.iet.com/Projects/HPKB/resources.html).")
(comment URIInNamespaceFn "<code>(#$URIInNamespaceFn NAMESPACE LOCAL-NAME)</code> denotes the #$UniformResourceIdentifier formed by concatenating NAMESPACE with LOCAL-NAME.")
(comment URIWithFragmentFn "<code>(#$URIWithFragmentFn BASE FRAGMENT)</code> denotes the #$UniformResourceIdentifier formed by concatenating BASE with FRAGMENT, separated by a #.")
(comment uriHasBaseAndFragment "A predicate corresponding to the function #$URIWithFragmentFn. <code>(#$uriHasBaseAndFragment (#$URIWithFragmentFn BASE FRAGMENT) BASE FRAGMENT)</code> will always be true for BASE and FRAGMENT meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment umbelAbstractConceptName "(#$umbelAbstractConceptName THING NAME) means that the name for THING in #$UMBELAbstractConceptNamespace is NAME.")
(comment umbelSubjectConceptName "(#$umbelSubjectConceptName THING NAME) means that the name for THING in #$UMBELSubjectConceptNamespace is NAME.")
(comment LightEmittingDiode "A diode that emits photons when a current passes through it, thus generating light.")
(comment OrganicLightEmittingDiode "The category of #$LightEmittingDiodes whose electroluminescent layer is composed of organic compounds, usually polymers.")
(comment OLEDDisplay "A video display screen for a piece of electronic hardware in which the principal display forming elements are instances of #$OrganicLightEmittingDiode")
(comment CardiacValveRegurgitantJet "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition  and #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$CardiacValveRegurgitantJet is a regurgitant jet that is a cardiac ailment condition.")
(comment Hesitating "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$HumanActivity. In each #$Hesitating, someone pauses or hold back in uncertainty or unwillingness.")
(comment wikipediaArticleURL "(#$wikipediaArticleURL THING URL) means that in #$Wikipedia-WebSite THING is described by an article located at URL")
(comment generalisesToForLicensing "<code>(#$generalisesToForLicensing TERM GENERALISATION)</code> means that <code>GENERALISATION</code> generalises <code>TERM</code> in a manner suitable for licensing. That is to say, if <code>GENERALISATION</code> can be used to license some term (in the <code>#$isLicensedBy</code> sense), then so can <code>TERM<code>. For example,  <code>(generalisesForLicensing #$Whelk #$Shellfish)</code> is true, then any thing that would be licensed by #$Shellfish would also be licensed by #$Whelk.")
(comment ParkingFacility "a facility, typically relatively large where cars can be parked.  Notable specializations include #$ParkingGarage and #$ParkingLot.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationPolarization "The collection of events in which some aspect of electromagnetic radiation is polarized.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation is a propagation of polarized electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-CircularlyPolarized "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation is a propagation of circularly polarized electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-RHCP "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-RHCP is a propagation of right-hand circularly polarized electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-LHCP "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-RHCP is a propagation of left-hand circularly polarized electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-CompositeRHCPAndLHCP "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-CompositeRHCPAndLHCP is a propagation of radiation that is a composite of left-hand circularly polarized electromagnetic radiation and right-hand circularly polarized radiation.")
(comment PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-LinearlyPolarized "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation. Each instance of #$PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-LinearlyPolarized is a propagation of radiation that is linearly polarized (i.e., it is confined to a single plane along the direction of polarization).")
(disjointWith PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-CircularlyPolarized PolarizedElectromagneticRadiation-LinearlyPolarized)
(comment CardiacAblation "The collection of #$Ablations in which the heart is ablated.")
(comment situationHasFocalObjectType "(#$situationHasFocalObjectType SIT OBJECT-TYPE) means that SIT involves an instance of OBJECT-TYPE.  For example, the situation \"TroubleshootingAnAirconditioningUnit01\", has as its focal object type #$AirConditioner.")
(comment hasWikipediaArticle "<code>(#$hasWikipediaArticle THING ARTICLE)</code> means that THING is the topic of the #$WikipediaArticle ARTICLE.")
(comment Homograft "the collection of animal body parts taken from one animal and implanted into another animal of the same species")
(comment MedicalGlossary "This is the collection of glossaries. A glossary is a kind of mini-dictionary, generally listing vocabulary relevant to a particular field, or vocabulary
used in a particle text, together with definitions of these terms.")
(comment RheumaticFever "The collection of all rheumatic fever. #$RheumaticFever is an inflammatory autoimmune disease which typically developts two or three weeks after Group A Streptococcal infections.")
(comment receivedSignalPolarization "<code>(#$receivedSignalPolarization DEV P)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> receives signals with the polarization <code>P</code>.")
(comment Address-ContactInfoString "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString,  Each instance of #$Address-ContactInfoString is a full address capable of being used to establish contact with an individual or an organization.")
(comment Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator "A specialization of #$Address-ContactInfoString.  Each instance of #$Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator is a string that describes the relatively permanent location of an individual or organization.  For example: \"President Bill Clinton, White House, 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue, Washington, DC\".  Addresses that provide an address suitable for delivery of mail are instances of the specialization, #$MailingAddress.")
(comment MailingAddress "A specialization of #$Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator.  Each instance of #$MailingAddress is a string that describes the mailing address of an individual or organization, and includes a street name and number, P.O. Box, or rural route and box number.  It also needs to include a city, state and zip code for mailings within the USA, and may also include a country name.")
(comment medicalTestRelevantToPhysiologicalConditionType "(#$medicalTestRelevantToPhysiologicalConditionType TEST COND) means that instances of TEST are frequently done for patients diagnosed with or suspected of having cases of the #$PhysiologicalCondition COND.")
(comment PrimaryProcedure "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$PrimaryProcedure is a procedure performed during a primary operation (an operation where the patient had no earlier operations.")
(comment OrganTransplantProcedure-Surgical "A type of replacement procedure.  Each instance of #$OrganTransplantProcedure-Surgical is a surgical procedure in which an organ in the body is transplanted.")
(comment GeneralMedicalAnalysisTask "A specialization of #$Allotment that represents general medical research and analysis taskings.")
(comment PotentialMedicalDomainModelPredicate "A collection of predicates that may be useful in modeling various medical domains.")
(comment glossaryDefinitionString "(#$glossaryDefinitionString GLOSSARY TERM DEFINITION) means that the #$Glossary GLOSSARY contains (see #$containsStructure-CW) the #$CharacterString DEFINITION as the definition for TERM.")
(comment MedicalProcedureRelevantPotentialPredicate "A collection of predicates that may be useful in retrieving information related to medical procedures.")
(comment AilmentConditionPotentialPredicate "A collection of predicates that may be useful in retrieving information about particular patient's ailments.")
(comment DrugProductPotentialPredicate "A collection of predicates that may be useful in modeling various medical domains.")
(comment richterMagnitude "<code>(#$momentMagnitudeOfEarthquake QUAKE NUMBER)</code> means that <code>NUMBER</code> is the Richter magnitude of <code>QUAKE</code>.  The Richter magnitude scale is used to indicate the energy released by earthquakes.")
(comment momentMagnitudeOfEarthquake "<code>(#$momentMagnitudeOfEarthquake QUAKE NUMBER)</code> means that <code>NUMBER</code> is the monent magnitude of <code>QUAKE</code>.  The moment magnitude scale as a successor to the Richter scale.  It is used to indicate the energy released by earthquakes. An increase of 1 step on this logarithmic scale corresponds to a 31.6 times increase in the amount of energy released.")
(comment LogarithmicScale "A specialization of #$Scale-Specification.  Each instance of #$LogarithmicScale is a scale based on the logarithm of a measurable quantity.  Examples include the #$PhScale and the #$RichterMagnitudeScale.")
(comment RichterMagnitudeScale "An instance of #$LogarithmicScale.  The Richter magnitude scale quantifies the amount of siesmic energy released by earthquakes.")
(comment PhScale "An instance of #$LogarithmicScale.  The ph scale quantifies the acidity of solutions.")
(comment Spectrum "A specialization of #$Scale-Specification.  Each instance of #$Spectrum is a scale of values that are arranged in terms of wave frequency.")
(comment ElectromagneticSpectrum "An instance of #$Spectrum.  The electromagnetic spectrum is the full range of values of electromagnetic frequencies (it is also expressible in terms of values of EM wavelegths or photon energies).")
(comment slotForScale "<code>(#$slotForScale SCALE SLOT)</code> means that <code>SLOT</code> expresses the sort of quantity that is quantified on <code>SCALE</code>.  For example, (#$slotForScale #$PhScale #$pHOfSample) is true because #$pHOfSample expresses the acidity of solutions, which is what is quantified on the #$PhScale.")
(comment typeHasValueQuantifiedOnScale "<code>(#$typeHasValueQuantifiedOnScale SCALE TYPE)</code> means that some value of (at least possible) instances of <code>TYPE</code> are quantified on <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment properSubScale "<code>(#$properSubScale SCALE SUB-SCALE)</code> means that <code>SUB-SCALE</code> is a scale that is a part of the larger scale, <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment VisibleLight "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Light.  Every instance of #$VisibleLight is an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiation having a wavelength approximately between 3800 and 7750 #$Angstroms, i.e., light visible to human eyes. Notable specializations include #$Moonlight and #$Rainbow.")
(comment VisibleSpectrum "An instance of #$Spectrum.  The electromagnetic spectrum is the full range of values of visible electromagnetic frequencies.")
(comment CompleteScale "A specialization of #$Scale-Specification.  Each instance of #$CompleteScale is a scale that is not properly contained by any other scale.  For example, the #$ElectromagneticSpectrum is a #$CompleteScale because it encompasses all EM frequencies.")
(comment RadioFrequencyBand "An instance of #$Spectrum.  Radio frequency (RF) is the range of frequency values corresponding to frequencies of radio waves.  The RF band is part of the #$ElectromagneticSpectrum.")
(comment SBand "An instance of #$Spectrum.  #$SBand encompasses the full range of frequency values corresponding to S Band microwaves.")
(comment CBand "An instance of #$Spectrum.  #$CBand encompasses the full range of frequency values corresponding to C Band microwaves.")
(comment MusicalScale "A specialization of #$Scale-Specification.  Each instance of #$MusicalScale is a scale which orders musical notes.")
(comment DiatonicScale "A specialization of #$MusicalScale.  Each instance of #$DiatonicScale is a musical scale with seven notes involving five whole steps and two half steps.")
(comment CMajorScale "An instance of #$MajorScale.  #$CMajorScale is a major scale in which the tonic note is C.")
(comment MajorScale "A specialization of #$DiatonicScale.  Each instance of #$MajorScale is a musical scale with seven notes involving two whole steps followed by a half step, followed by three whole steps and a final half step.")
(comment A-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$A-MusicalNote is an A note.")
(comment B-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$B-MusicalNote is a B note.")
(comment C-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$C-MusicalNote is a C note.")
(comment D-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$D-MusicalNote is a D note.")
(comment E-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$E-MusicalNote is an E note.")
(comment F-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$F-MusicalNote is an F note.")
(comment G-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$G-MusicalNote is a G note.")
(comment componentPitchOfScale "<code>(#$componentPitchOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is a component pitch of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment tonicNoteOfScale "<code>(#$tonicNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the tonic note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment supertonicNoteOfScale "<code>(#$supertonicNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the supertonic note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment mediantNoteOfScale "<code>(#$mediantNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the mediant note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment subdominantNoteOfScale "<code>(#$subdominantNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the subdominant note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment dominantNoteOfScale "<code>(#$dominantNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the dominant note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment submediantNoteOfScale "<code>(#$submediantNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the submediant note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment leadingNoteOfScale "<code>(#$leadingNoteOfScale SCALE NOTE)</code> means that <code>NOTE</code> is the leading note of <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment relativeMinorKey "<code>(#$relativeMinorKey SCALE RELATIVE-MINOR-SCALE)</code> means that <code>RELATIVE-MINOR-SCALE</code> is the relative minor key with respect to <code>SCALE</code>.")
(comment MinorScale "A specialization of #$DiatonicScale.  Each instance of #$MinorScale is a musical scale with seven notes involving one whole steps followed by a half step, followed by two whole steps, a half step, and the two more whole steps.")
(comment AMinorScale "An instance of #$MinorScale.  #$AMinorScale is a minor scale in which the first whole step is taken from an A note.")
(disjointWith LogarithmicScale LinearScale)
(comment LinearScale "A specialization of #$Scale-Specification.  Each instance of #$LinearScale is a scale whose values are arrayed in a linear (as opposed, e.g., to a logarithmic) ordering.")
(comment MiddleC-MusicalNote "A specialization of #$C-MusicalNote.  Each instance of #$MiddleC-MusicalNote is a C note with the frequency 261.626 Hertz.")
(comment Vitamin "A specialization of #$Nutrient.  Each instance of #$Vitamin is some portion of a nutrient that is required to be ingested to support the health of an organism.")
(comment VitaminB1 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as Thiamin.")
(comment VitaminB2 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as Riboflavin.")
(comment VitaminB3 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as Niacin.")
(comment VitaminB5 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as Pantothenic Acid.")
(comment VitaminB6 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as pyridoxine.")
(comment VitaminB7 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as biotin.")
(comment VitaminB9 "A kind of #$VitaminB, also known as folic acid.")
(comment VitaminB12 "A kind of #$VitaminB.")
(comment occurredDuringMonth "(#$occurredDuringMonth EVENT MONTH-TYPE) means that EVENT occurred during an instance of MONTH-TYPE.  E.g. If the date of Evt01 is January 1, 2008, then (#$occurredDuringMonth Evt01 #$January) is true.")
(comment MusicalNote "The collection of all musical notes. A type of #$Music.")
(comment MusicalNote-Natural "The collection of all natural musical notes. A type of #$MusicalNote.")
(comment ChemicalByproduct "The collection portions of of stuff that are the byproducts of some chemical reaction or other..")
(comment BiologicalByproduct "The collection portions of of stuff that are the byproducts of some biological process.")
(comment Creatinine "The breakdown product of creatine.")
(comment testTypeAssociatedWithType "A predicate for associating a type of test or evaluation with with the type of thing to which it bears a strong conceptual relationship.  For example, a cholesterol test might measure the level of cholesterol present in a blood sample.  So, (#$testTypeAssociatedWithType CholesterolTest Cholesterol) holds.")
(comment scaleSwept "<code>(#$scaleSwept SWEEP SCALE)</code> means that, during the #$SweepingAScale, <code>SWEEP</code>, the scale <code>SCALE</code> is swept.")
(comment hasCreatinineTestValue "A creatinine blood test is typically performed to assess kidney function.  Currently this predicate is queried with the units of measure implicit.  In the US it is typically measures as the ration of mg/dL.")
(comment CreatinineBloodTest "A creatinine blood test is typically performed to assess kidney function.  In the US it is typically measures as the ration of mg/dL.  See #$hasCreatinineTestValue.")
(comment Console-Device "A collection of tangible things.  An instance of #$Console-Device is the physical part of a device used for controlling or monitoring the device.  E.g., the control console of an early computer, or the control and monitoring console of a power station. Notable specialisations of Console-Device are #$ControlConsole, #$MonitoringConsole and #$ControlAndMonitoringConsole.")
(comment ControlConsole "A collection of tangible things.  An instance of #$ControlConsole is the physical part of a device used for controlling the device.  E.g., the control console of an early computer, or the control and monitoring console of a power station. A notable specialisation of ControlConsole is #$ControlAndMonitoringConsole.")
(comment circulatoryConduitTypeSourceType "<code>(#$circulatoryConduitTypeSourceType CONDUIT-TYPE SOURCE-CONDUIT-TYPE)</code> means that in a typical anatomical system, conduits of type <code>CONDUIT-TYPE</code> connect directly to conduits of type <code>SOURCE-CONDUIT-TYPE</code>, and that instances of <code>SOURCE-CONDUIT-TYPE</code> are the source of circulatory flow for conduits of type <code>CONDUIT-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$circulatoryConduitTypeSourceType #$AorticRoot #$AorticValve) is true because the #$AorticRoot typically attaches directly to the #$AorticValve, and the flow is from the #$AorticValve to the #$AorticRoot.")
(comment PulmonaryHypertension "An instance of #$DiseaseType.  Cases of pulmonary hypertension (PHT) are characterized by high blood pressure in the arteries that supply the lungs.")
(comment Electrophysiology "The scientific discipline concerned with investigating the electrical properties of living tissues.")
(comment CardiacElectrophysiology "The field of scientific discovery concerned with investigating the electrical properties and activities of the #$Heart, and with using this knowledge to formulate diagnostic, interventional, and preventive procedures for combatting the indicated range of cardiac ailments.")
(comment Angioplasty "The collection of all angioplasty procedures.  Angioplasty is a type of procedure performed in order to widen vessels that have been narrowed, through the use of one or more catheters.")
(comment Anastomosis-Surgical "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Anastamosis-Surgical is a procedure in which two structures are joined.  For example, two segments of the intestine may be thus joined after an intermediate segment is resected.")
(disjointWith CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion MedicalDiagnosis)
(disjointWith Catheterization AilmentCondition)
(comment iteratedSubsituationTypeOfSerialCycleType "Where SERIAL-CYCLE-TYPE is a specializatin of #$Cycle-Serial, (#$iteratedSubsituationTypeOfSerialCycleType SERIAL-CYCLE-TYPE ITERATE-TYPE) means that ITERATE-TYPE is 'the' characteristic situation type which is instantiated repeatedly and contiguously in instances of SERIAL-CYCLE-TYPE.")
(comment SingleHumanHeartbeat "The collection of all discrete 'beats' of human hearts (instances of (#$OrganismPartTypeFn HomoSapiens Heart)).")
(comment SinusRhythm-Normal "The collection of all normal human heart rhythms or heart-beating processes, consisting of iterated #$SingleHumanHeartbeats within normal rate parameters for a human being.")
(comment LeftVentricularWallMotionAbnormality "insufficient contraction of the left ventricular wall during systole.")
(comment Hypokinesis "decreased inward movement of the left ventricular wall during systole.")
(comment Akinesis "no inward movement of the left ventricular wall during systole.")
(comment Dyskinesis "outward bulging of the left ventricular wall during systole.")
(comment CardiacEctopy "cardiac ectopy is a disturbance of the conduction system of the heart.  It is characterized by beats that arise from the wrong part of the heart.")
(comment CatheterizationProcedure-Interventional "A specialization of #$Catheterization.  Each instance is a catheterization that is performed for interventional, as opposed to merely diagnostic, reasons. CF. #$Catheterization-Diagnostic.")
(comment Atherosclerosis "A type of #$Arteriosclerosis. Atherosclerosis is a chronic inflammatory response in the walls of arteries, caused by the formation of multiple plaques within the arteries. It is commonly known as a \"hardening\" of the arteries.")
(comment MedialCalcificSclerosis "A specialization of #$Arteriosclerosis.  Medial calcific sclerosis is a condition characterized by hardening of medium-sized arteries caused by calcium deposit accumulation in their walls.")
(comment patientMinimalYearAgeDuringMedicalEvent "<code>(#$patientMinimalYearAgeDuringMedicalEvent PAT EVT TIME-QUANTITY)</code> means that the #$MedicalPatient <code>PAT</code> is at least <code>TIME-QUANTITY</code> old at the time of the start of the event <code>EVT</code>.  Typically, the units are expressed in #$YearsDuration.")
(comment AcuteCoronarySyndrome "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$AcuteCoronarySyndrome is a syndrome involving primarily chest pain, and also sweating, nausea and shortness of breath.")
(comment fieldFostersAdvancedProceduresOfType "(#$fieldFostersAdvancedProceduresOfType FIELD-OF-STUDY PROCEDURE-TYPE) means that research in the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD-OF-STUDY engenders methodological advances in the performance of actitivies of type PROCEDURE-TYPE.  For example, (#$fieldFostersAdvancedProceduresOfType #$ComputerScience #$ProgrammingAComputer) means that computer science fosters advances in computer programming techniques.")
(comment mainInvestigationTypeOfScientificFieldOfStudy "(#$mainInvestigationTypeOfScientificFieldOfStudy FIELD RESEARCH-TYPE means that RESEARCH-TYPE is the principal class of investigatory procedure facilitating advances in FIELD.")
(comment Infarction "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Infarction is a condition causing a region of tissue to necrotize due to loss of blood supply.")
(comment AnginaPectoris "A specialization of (#$PainInFn #$Chest-BodyPart).  Each instance of #$AnginaPectoris involves pain in the chest as a consequence of lack of blood supply to the heart muscle tissue.")
(comment UrinaryCatheterization "A specialization of #$Catheterization.  Each instance of #$CardiacCatheterization is a catheterization that involves inserting a urinary catheter into a patient's bladder via the urethra.")
(comment Catheter-Urinary "A specialization of #$Catheter. Each instance of #$Catheter-Urinary is a catheter used during #$UrinaryCatheterization to drain urine from the bladder.")
(comment FoleyCatheter "A specialization of #$Catheter-Urinary.")
(comment Catheter-IV "A specialization of #$Catheter.  Each instance of #$Catheter-IV is a flexible plastic tube inserted into a vein to administer IV therapy.")
(comment Catheter-PeripheralVenous "A specialization of #$Catheter-IV.  Each instance of #$Catheter-PeripheralVenous is a flexible plastic tube inserted into a peripheral vein to administer medication or fluids.")
(comment Catheter-HickmanLine "A specialization of #$Catheter-IV.  Each instance of #$Catheter-HickmanLine is a flexible plastic tube inserted into a vein to administer medication or fluids, or to extract blood for testing.  Hickman lines may remain in place for long periods of time.")
(comment Catheter-GroshongLine "A specialization of #$Catheter-IV.  Each instance of #$Catheter-GroshongLine is a flexible plastic tube inserted into a vein to administer medication or fluids, or to extract blood for testing.  Groshong lines may remain in place for long periods of time.")
(comment Catheter-Arterial "A specialization of #$Catheter. Each instance of #$Catheter-Arterial is a catheter intended for insertion into an artery.")
(comment Catheter-Balloon "A specialization of #$Catheter. Each instance of #$Catheter-Balloon is a catheter with an inflatable balloon at its distal end.")
(comment Catheter-PICLine "A specialization of #$Catheter-IV.  Each instance of #$Catheter-PICLine is a catheter used for extendsed intravenous access.")
(comment BiologicalTissue "The collection of instances of tissue -- functional groups of cells from a common organism that, though not suffice to define an organ (see #$Organ), are specific to an organ and used by that organ in performing one or more of its biological functions.")
(comment xenograft "An instance of #$ActorSlot and specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$organismPartTransplanted. <code>(#$xenograft EVENT ORGANISM-PART)</code> identifies <code>ORGANISM-PART</code> as the allograft (tissue or organ) that is transplanted from a donor organism into a recipient.  For the tissue or organ to qualify as an xenograft, the donor and recipient must belong to different species.")
(comment allograft "An instance of #$ActorSlot and specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$organismPartTransplanted. <code>(#$allograft EVENT ORGANISM-PART)</code> identifies <code>ORGANISM-PART</code> as the allograft (tissue or organ) that is transplanted from a donor organism into a recipient.  For the tissue or organ to qualify as an allograft, the donor and recipient must be different organisms of the same species.")
(comment isograft "An instance of #$ActorSlot and specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$allograft. <code>(#$isograft EVENT ORGANISM-PART)</code> identifies <code>ORGANISM-PART</code> as the tissue or organ that is transplanted from a donor organism into a recipient.  For the tissue or organ to qualify as an isograft, the donor and recipient must be genetically identical (but different) organisms.  Transplantations that involve an isograph are distinguished from others that involve (mere) allografts because the recipient's immune response will be the same as it would were the transplant an #$autograft.")
(comment autograft "An instance of #$ActorSlot and specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$organismPartTransplanted. <code>(#$autograft EVENT ORGANISM-PART)</code> identifies <code>ORGANISM-PART</code> as the tissue that is transplanted from one area on the donor/recipient to another.")
(comment TissueTransplantSurgery "The collection of instances of #$TransplantSurgery in which bundles of tissue (rather than organs) are transplanted from a donor to a host.")
(comment organismPartTransplanted "<code>(#$organismPartTransplanted TRANSPLANT PART)</code> means that in the #$TransplantSurgery event <code>TRANSPLANT</code>, the organ or tissue transplanted is <code>PART</code>.")
(comment OrganTransplantSurgery "The collection of instances of #$TransplantSurgery in which an organ (see #$Organ) is transplanted from one animal to another.  Contrast with #$TissueTransplantSurgery.")
(comment TransplantSurgeryTypeByOrganismPartType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$TransplantSurgery into sub-collections based on the type of organism part that is transplanted (see #$organismPartTransplanted).")
(comment catheterGuage "<code>(#$catheterGuage CATH GUAGE)</code> means that <code>CATH</code> is a catheter of guage <code>GAUGE</code>, where <code>GAUGE</code> is typically measured in French units.")
(comment FrenchUnit "A unit of measure used to classify catheters.")
(comment CatheterTypeByFrenchGaugeSize "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Catheter whose instances are all of the same size.")
(comment 1FCatheter "The collection of all 1F catheters.")
(comment 2FCatheter "The collection of all 2F catheters.")
(comment 3FCatheter "The collection of all 3F catheters.")
(comment 4FCatheter "The collection of all 4F catheters.")
(comment 5FCatheter "The collection of all 5F catheters.")
(comment 6FCatheter "The collection of all 6F catheters.")
(comment 7FCatheter "The collection of all 7F catheters.")
(comment 8FCatheter "The collection of all 8F catheters.")
(comment 9FCatheter "The collection of all 9F catheters.")
(comment 10FCatheter "The collection of all 10F catheters.")
(comment 11FCatheter "The collection of all 11F catheters.")
(comment 12FCatheter "The collection of all 12F catheters.")
(comment 13FCatheter "The collection of all 13F catheters.")
(comment 14FCatheter "The collection of all 14F catheters.")
(comment 15FCatheter "The collection of all 15F catheters.")
(comment 16FCatheter "The collection of all 16F catheters.")
(comment 17FCatheter "The collection of all 17F catheters.")
(comment 18FCatheter "The collection of all 18F catheters.")
(comment 19FCatheter "The collection of all 19F catheters.")
(comment 20FCatheter "The collection of all 20F catheters.")
(comment 21FCatheter "The collection of all 21F catheters.")
(comment 22FCatheter "The collection of all 22F catheters.")
(comment 23FCatheter "The collection of all 23F catheters.")
(comment 24FCatheter "The collection of all 24F catheters.")
(comment 25FCatheter "The collection of all 25F catheters.")
(comment 26FCatheter "The collection of all 26F catheters.")
(comment 27FCatheter "The collection of all 27F catheters.")
(comment 28FCatheter "The collection of all 28F catheters.")
(comment 29FCatheter "The collection of all 29F catheters.")
(comment 30FCatheter "The collection of all 30F catheters.")
(comment 31FCatheter "The collection of all 31F catheters.")
(comment 32FCatheter "The collection of all 32F catheters.")
(comment 33FCatheter "The collection of all 33F catheters.")
(comment 34FCatheter "The collection of all 34F catheters.")
(comment ArteryTypeByTIMIFlow "A collection of collections. Each instance is a specialization of #$Artery whose instances all have the same TIMI flow grading.")
(comment Artery-TIMIFlowGrading0 "An instance of #$ArteryTypeByTIMIFlow.  Each instance of #$Artery-TIMIFlowGrading0 is a completely occluded infarct-related artery.")
(comment Artery-TIMIFlowGrading1 "An instance of #$ArteryTypeByTIMIFlow.  Each instance of #$Artery-TIMIFlowGrading1 is an artery with some penetration of contract material beyond the point of obstruction but without perfusion of the distal coronary bed.")
(comment Artery-TIMIFlowGrading2 "An instance of #$ArteryTypeByTIMIFlow.  Each instance of #$Artery-TIMIFlowGrading2 is an artery with perfusion of the entire infarct vessel into the distal but with delayed flow compared with a normal artery.")
(comment Artery-TIMIFlowGrading3 "An instance of #$ArteryTypeByTIMIFlow.  Each instance of #$Artery-TIMIFlowGrading3 is an artery with full perfusion of the infarct vessel with normal flow.")
(comment arteryTIMIFlowGrading "<code>(#$arteryTIMIFlowGrading ART FLOW)</code> means that <code>ART</code> has a TIMI flow of <code>FLOW</code>.")
(comment AllensTest "A kind of medical test.  Allen's test is used to assess blood supply to the hand.")
(comment bodyMassIndex "<code>(#$bodyMassIndex HUMAN NUMBER)</code> means that <code>HUMAN</code> has a body mass index (BMI) of <code>NUMBER</code>.")
(comment textSearchPanelEnabled "<code>(#$textSearchPanelEnabled SPECIFICATION BOOLEAN)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, the text search panel (that searches various IR/Web Search engines) is enabled when BOOLEAN is #$True, and disabled otherwise.")
(comment keRelevantPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) that is (along with #$keRelevantInverse) the most general of those that relate a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keRelevantPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, if there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, asserting (BINPRED INST THING) in the Cyc Knowledge Base is worth considering and perhaps advisable.  But note: the specializations of #$keRelevantPreds are #$keWeakSuggestionPreds, #$keStrongSuggestionPreds, #$keConsiderationPreds, and #$keStrongConsiderationPreds (qq.v.); and one should use one of these instead of #$keRelevantPreds itself whenever possible.  In fact, #$keRelevantPreds was created mainly for use in situations where one wants to say something general about all of these specializations.")
(comment instancesOfCollectionTypeRelevantToTermSummary "<code>(#$instancesOfCollectionTypeRelevantToTermSummary COL-TYPE ERM-SUMMARY-PRED)</code> means that if a collection <code>COL</code> is an instance of <code>COL-TYPE</code>, then <code>(#$isa THING COL)</code> should appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment overlappingExternalConcept "A predicate for mapping terms from an external data source to closely related concepts represented in Cyc.  <code>(#$overlappingExternalConcept THING SOURCE STRING)</code> means that in the external data source <code>SOURCE</code>, the meaning of <code>STRING</code> has significant semantic overlap with <code>THING</code>.")
(comment TransplantationTypeByOrganismPartType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$TransplantationProcedure-Surgical into sub-collections based on the type of organism part that is transplanted (see #$organismPartTransplanted).")
(comment Xenotransplantation "The collection of instances of #$TransplantationProcedure-Surgical in which the donor and recipient are of different species.  In such surgeries, the transplanted tissue or organ is known as a \"xenograft\" or \"xenotransplant\" represented using the #$ActorSlot #$xenograft.")
(comment Allotransplantation "The collection of instances of #$TransplantationProcedure-Surgical in which the donor and recipient are of different members of the same species.  In such surgeries, the transplanted tissue or organ is known as an \"allograft\" and is represented using the #$ActorSlot #$allograft.")
(comment Autotransplantation "The collection of instances of #$TissueTransplantProcedure-Surgical in which the donor is also the recipient.")
(comment TissueTransplantProcedure-Surgical "The collection of all instances of #$TransplantationProcedure-Surgical in which tissue (versus an instance of #$Organ) is transplanted from a donor to a recipient.")
(comment TransplantationProcedure-Surgical "The collection of all instances of #$SurgicalProcedure in which tissue or organs are transplanted from a donor to a recipient.")
(comment isLicensedBy2 "<code>(#$isLicensedBy2 LICENSEE LICENSOR)</code> means that <code>LICENSEE</code> is licensed by <code>LICENSOR</code>.  For example, believing that a document is about <code>LICENSEE</code> is licensed by learning that the document mentions <code>LICENSOR</code>.")
(comment abbreviationString "(#$abbreviationString THING STRING) means that THING may be referred to by the abbreviation STRING. A notable specialisation is  #$acronymString where the string is formed by the first letters of each word.")
(comment QRSComplex "The QRS complex is a structure of waves depicted in an ECG graph that corresponds to the depolarization of the ventricles. \"QRS\" refers to Q-wave, R-wave, and S-wave -- waves recorded on an ECG graph -- though only at least one of the three waves are required for it to be a QRS complex.")
(comment qRSDuration "The QRS complex is a structure of waves depicted in an ECG graph that corresponds to the depolarization of the ventricles.  The QRS duration is the duration of the QRS complex from start to finish.  \"QRS\" refers to Q-wave, R-wave, and S-wave -- waves recorded on an ECG graph -- though only at least one of the three waves are required for it to be a QRS complex.")
(comment measurementPredicateAssociatedWithType "A predicate for associating a predicate that relates a thing (typically an object or event) to a measurement.  Asserting this relationship to a predicate and a collection asserts that that predicate measures the stated dimensions of instances of that collection.")
(comment AorticSinus "The collection of all aortic sinuses.  An aortic sinus is a widening of the aorta just above the aortic valve.  They are partitioned into the left, right, and posterior sinuses.")
(comment AorticAnnulus "The collection of ring-like structures that support the leaflets of the aortic valve.")
(comment MitralAnnulus "The collection of ring-like structures that support the leaflets of the mitral valve.")
(comment TricuspidAnnulus "The collection of ring-like structures that support the leaflets of the tricuspid valve.")
(comment PulmonaryAnnulus "The collection of ring-like structures that support the leaflets of the pulmonary valve.")
(comment SinotubularJunction "The collection of all regions of the ascending aorta between aortic sinus and where the ascending aorta begins its regualr tubular dimensions.")
(comment Raphe-Anatomical "the collection continuous ridges of tissue in animals.  Notable examples inlcude the frenulum connecting the tongue to the floor of the mouth.")
(comment DocIngesterUserCreatedTerm "This is the collection of concepts created by users of the Document Ingester.")
(comment subtopicCollectionForCategory "<code>(#$subtopicCollectionForCategory CATEGORY-PRED TYPE)</code> means that 
<code>TYPE</code> is a sub-topic for the category picked out by 
<code>CATEGORY-PRED</code>.")
(comment generateFormulasWithTermForSpecs "(#$generateFormulasWithTermForSpecs COLLECTION TERM) means that any time
a specialization of COLLECTION is seen, TERM will be used
to create formulas.")
(comment generateFormulasWithTermForInstances "(#$generateFormulasWithTermForInstances COLLECTION TERM) means that any 
time an instance of COLLECTION is seen, TERM will be used to  
create formulas.")
(comment AilmentDiagnosisTable "A specialization of #$FactSheetTable.  Each instance of #$AilmentTreatmentTable is a table containing information about the diagnosis of an #$AilmentCondition.")
(comment specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArg "<code>(#$specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which a specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg <code>N</code> should appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment specPredsIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArg "<code>(#$specPredsIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which a specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg <code>N</code> should not appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment Radome "A specialization of #$ContainerArtifact and #$ShelteringArtifact.  Instances are enclosures designed to protect large antennae, such as radar antennae and telemetry antennae (see #$RadarDevice and #$TelemetryDetectionDevice) from the elements.  Radomes can often be found on airplanes or other vehicles with external radar.  When used to protect an antenna on the ground, radomes frequently take the form of geodesic domes (see #$GeodesicDome).")
(comment antennaGain "<code>(#$antennaGain DEV INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a gain of <code>INTERVAL</code>. Gain is a measure of the ability of <code>DEV</code> to increase the power or amplitude of its signal.")
(comment oeSuggestion "(#$oeSuggestion OBJ SENTENCE) states a suggestion for the term OBJ that SENTENCE must be known to be true.  #$oeSuggestion is a generalization of #$oeStrongSuggestion.  #$oeSuggestion is meant to apply to terms that are more ontologically obscure, which an unbtrained knowledge enterer would likely have difficulty understanding.")
(comment oeStrongSuggestion "(#$oeStrongSuggestion TERM FORMULA) states a strong suggestion that FORMULA should be known to be true about TERM.  This is most useful at expressing suggestions or expectations about TERM which can then be used by tools that look for KB omissions, or conditions that explicitly violate these expectations.  #$oeStrongSuggestion is meant to apply to terms that are more ontologically obscure, which an unbtrained knowledge enterer would likely have difficulty understanding.")
(comment oeStrongSuggestionPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$oeStrongSuggestion that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$oeStrongSuggestionPreds COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is strongly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED INST THING) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$oeStrongSuggestionInverse.")
(comment krRelevantPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) that is (along with #$keRelevantInverse) the most general of those that relate a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keRelevantPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, if there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, asserting (BINPRED INST THING) in the Cyc Knowledge Base is worth considering and perhaps advisable.  But note: the specializations of #$keRelevantPreds are #$keWeakSuggestionPreds, #$keStrongSuggestionPreds, #$keConsiderationPreds, and #$keStrongConsiderationPreds (qq.v.); and one should use one of these instead of #$keRelevantPreds itself whenever possible.  In fact, #$keRelevantPreds was created mainly for use in situations where one wants to say something general about all of these specializations.")
(comment krRelevant "This is, by definition, the most general instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate.  It is intended as a generalization for #$keStrongSuggestion, #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keNeighborSuggestion, #$keStrongConsideration and #$kePlausibleConsideration or any other such predicates which may be suggested.  This predicate, along with #$keRelevantPreds, #$keRelevantInverse, #$keGenlsRelevantPreds, #$keGenlsRelevantInverse are designed to facilitate the implementation of rapid knowledge formation tools implementing #$KEFacilitationPredicates. One should almost always use one of its specializations.")
(comment krRelevantInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) that is (along with #$krRelevantPreds) the most general of those that relate a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$krRelevantInverse COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, if there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, asserting (BINPRED THING INST) in the Cyc Knowledge Base is worth considering and perhaps advisable.")
(comment oeRelevantInverse "Allong with #$oeRelevantPreds, this is the most general of the OE facilitation predicates that relate a collection to a binary predicate.")
(comment oeRelevant "This is, by definition, the most general OE facilitation predicate.  The only more general instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate is #$krRelevant.  The specializations of #$oeRelevant pick out terms that are useful and important for adding OE to the Cyc KB, but which untrained knowledge enterers would be unlikely to easily understand.")
(comment oeStrongSuggestionInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and specialization of #$oeRelevantInverse that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$oeStrongSuggestionInverse COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is strongly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED THING INST) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$oeStrongSuggestionPreds.")
(comment oeRelevantPreds "An OE facilitation that is (along with #$oeRelevantInverse) the most general of those that relate a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$oeRelevantPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, if there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, asserting (BINPRED INST THING) in the Cyc Knowledge Base is worth considering and perhaps advisable.")
(comment LBand "An instance of #$Spectrum. #$LBand encompasses the full range of frequency values corresponding to L Band microwaves.")
(comment Governor-Title "The prefix \"Governor\" that may attach to a person's name.")
(comment Senator-Title "The prefix \"Senator\" that may attach to a person's name.")
(comment Microwave-UpperSBand "A collection of events; a subset of #$MicrowaveRadiation.")
(comment UpperSBand "An instance of #$Spectrum. #$UpperSBand encompasses the full range of frequency values corresponding to Upper S Band microwaves.")
(comment numInstancesOfCollStandInPredToValue-Inverse "(#$numInstancesOfCollStandInPredToValue-Inverse BIN-PRED COLL THING NUM) holds just in case the number of instances, INS, of COLL such that (BIN-PRED THING INS) is NUM.")
(comment DiastolicHeartFailure "A kind of #$HeartFailure characterized by the inability of the left ventricle (see #$LeftVentricle) to relax normally, thereby preventing the heart from filling with blood.")
(comment SystolicHeartFailure "A kind of #$HeartFailure characterized by the inability of the left ventricle (see #$LeftVentricle) to contract normally, thereby preventing the heart from pushing blood out to the body.")
(comment RightVentricularHeartFailure "A kind of #$HeartFailure characterized by the inability of the right ventricle (see #$RightVentricle) to pump blood into the lungs.  This kind of heart failure is usually caused by fluid in the lungs, causing a backage that damages the ventricle.")
(comment Diastole "The process by which chambers of the heart fill with blood.")
(comment Systole "The collection of events in which chambers of the heart (see #$HeartChamber) contract, pumping blood.")
(comment AtrialSystole "The collection of instances of #$Systole in which the heart chamber (see #$HeartChamber) that pumps blood is an atrium (see #$Atrium).")
(comment AtrialDiastole "The collection of instances of #$Diastole in which the heart chamber (see #$HeartChamber) that fills with blood is an atrium (see #$Atrium).")
(comment VentricularSystole "The collection of instances of #$Systole in which the heart chamber (see #$HeartChamber) that pumps blood is a ventricle (see #$VentricleOfHeart).")
(comment VentricularDiastole "The collection of instances of #$Diastole in which the heart chamber (see #$HeartChamber) that fills with blood is a ventricle (see #$VentricleOfHeart).")
(comment HypoplasticLeftHeartSyndrome "A specialization of #$CongenitalHeartDisease.  The condition of Hypoplastic Left Heart Syndrome (HLHS)  in one in which the left side of the heart is severely underdeveloped.")
(comment HypoplasticRightHeartSyndrome "A specialization of #$CongenitalHeartDisease.  The condition of Hypoplastic Right Heart Syndrome (HRHS)  in one in which the right side of the heart is severely underdeveloped.")
(comment Hypoplasia "The collection of conditions in which an organ or body structure is underdeveloped.")
(comment BranchPulmonaryArteryHypoplasia "The collection of conditions characterized by a hypoplastic (underdeveloped) pulmonary artery.")
(comment Thrombocytopenia "The collection of conditions characterized by a relatively low platelet count.")
(disjointWith VentricularDiastole AtrialDiastole)
(disjointWith VentricularSystole AtrialSystole)
(disjointWith Diastole Systole)
(comment Ischemia "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition, instances are restrictions of blood supply to an animal's organs or tissue.")
(comment NYHAClass2HeartFailure "One of four instances of #$HeartFailureTypeByNYHAClassification.  Instances of #$NYHAClass2HeartFailure are heart failures characterized by \"mild symptoms (mild shortness of breath and/or angina) and slight limitation during ordinary activity.\" (as per http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NYHA).")
(comment NYHAClass3HeartFailure "One of four instances of #$HeartFailureTypeByNYHAClassification.  Instances of #$NYHAClass3HeartFailure are heart failures characterized by \"Marked limitation in activity due to symptoms, even during less-than-ordinary activity, e.g. walking short distances (20-100 m).
Comfortable only at rest.\" (as per http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NYHA).")
(comment NYHAClass4HeartFailure "One of four instances of #$HeartFailureTypeByNYHAClassification.  Instances of #$NYHAClass4HeartFailure are heart failures characterized by \"Severe limitations. [Patients] experience symptoms even while at rest. [Patients are] mostly bedbound.\" (as per http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NYHA).")
(comment NYHAClass1HeartFailure "One of four instances of #$HeartFailureTypeByNYHAClassification.  Instances of #$NYHAClass1HeartFailure are heart failures characterized by \"No symptoms and no limitation in ordinary physical activity, e.g. shortness of breath when walking, climbing stairs etc.\" (as per http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NYHA).")
(comment MedicalImaging "A specialization of #$MedicalTesting.  Each instance of #$MedicalImaging is a test done to produce images of some body region for the purpose of medical investigation.")
(comment UltrasoundImaging "A specialization of #$MedicalImaging.  Each instance of #$UltrasoundImaging is a test done to produce images with ultrasound waves.")
(comment TransplantationTypeByMajorDonorCategory "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that partitions #$TransplantationProcedure-Surgical into three sub-collections based on donor/recipient relationship: allotransplantation (#$Allotransplantation), in which the donor is a distinct member of the same species of the recipient; autotransplantation (#$Autotransplantation), in which the donor is the recipient; and xenotransplantation (#$Xenotransplantation), in which the donor and recipient are of different species.")
(comment Eplerenone "A chemical compound (see #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies) used pharmaceutically to extend the life expectancy of people suffering from heart failure (#$HeartFailure).")
(comment Hyperkalemia "A type of #$AilmentCondition characterized by elevated levels of potassium in the blood.")
(comment Spironolactone "A chemical compound (see #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies) used pharmaceutically to extend the life expectancy of people suffering from heart failure (#$HeartFailure).")
(comment MineralocorticoidReceptor "A class of #$ReceptorMolecule that, when activated, expresses a protein that effects the reaborption of sodium into the cell, resulting in the excretion of potassium.")
(comment antagonistForReceptorType "<code>(#$antagonistForReceptorType ANTAGONIST RECEPTOR)</code> identifies <code>ANTAGONIST</code> as a class of molecule whose instances have the dispositional capability to bind with instances of the <code>RECEPTOR</code> class, with no resultant cellular response.  Antagonists thus block receptors from binding with potential agonists (molecules that can result in cellular response).")
(comment agonistForReceptorType "<code>(#$agonistForReceptorType AGONIST RECEPTOR)</code> identifies <code>AGONIST</code> as a class of molecule whose instances have the dispositional capability to bind with instances of the <code>RECEPTOR</code> class, causing cellular response (the expression of a protein).")
(comment ligandForReceptorType "<code>(#$ligandForReceptorType LIGAND RECEPTOR)</code> identifies <code>LIGAND</code> as a class of molecule whose instances have the dispositional capability to bind with instances of the <code>RECEPTOR</code> class.")
(comment AldosteroneAntagonistType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose molecules, by virtue of their structure, block the binding of #$Aldosterone molecules by receptors.  Thus the class of molecules of instances of this collection stand in the #$antagonistForReceptorType relation to any class of #$ReceptorMolecule for which the class of #$Aldosterone molecules stand in the #$agonistForReceptorType relation.")
(comment compoundAntagonizesActionOfType "(#$compoundAntagonizesActionOfType COMPOUND TYPE) identifies <code>COMPOUND</code> as an instance of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose molecules, by virtue of their structure, block the binding of molecules of <code>TYPE</code> by receptors.  Thus the class of molecules of instances of <code>COMPOUND</code> stand in the #$antagonistForReceptorType relation to any class of #$ReceptorMolecule for which the class of molcules of <code>TYPE</code> stand in the #$agonistForReceptorType relation.")
(comment Canrenone "A chemical compound (see #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies) used pharmaceutically to extend the life expectancy of people suffering from heart failure (#$HeartFailure).")
(comment GastroesophagealRefluxDisease "A type of #$AilmentCondition, instances of which are characterized by chronic symptoms or mucosal damage produced by the abnormal reflux in the esophagus.")
(comment Hemiplegia "The collection of instances of the condition of hemiplegia. One side (and only one side) of the body is paralyzed.")
(comment termPhrases-CaseInsensitive-Lexical "(#$termPhrases-CaseInsensitive-Lexical TERM CONSTRAINT STRING) means that STRING is a word or phrase explicitly in Cyc's lexicon (i.e. not requiring parsing or generation), modulo case, that denotes TERM and that meets CONSTRAINT. Cf. #$termPhrases-CaseInsensitive.")
(comment specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTSpecsInArg "<code>(#$specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTSpecsInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is a specialization of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which a specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg </code>N</code> should appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment specPredsIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTSpecsInArg "<code>(#$specPredsIrrelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTSpecsInArg PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is a specialization of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which a specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg </code>N</code> should not appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code>.")
(comment summaryPredicateOrderingForInstances "<code>(#$summaryPredicateOrderingForInstances COL LIST)</code> means that in a summary of an instance of <code>COL</code>, the recommended order of summary-predicate delineated sections is given by <code>LIST</code>.")
(comment summaryPredicateOrderingForSpecs "<code>(#$summaryPredicateOrderingForSpecs COL LIST)</code> means that in a summary of a specialization of <code>COL</code>, the recommended order of summary-predicate delineated sections is given by <code>LIST</code>.")
(comment ComputerLinePrinter "A specialization of #$ComputerImpactPrinter.  Each instance of #$ComputerLinePrinter is a printer that prints one line at a time.")
(comment Milrinone "A #$DrugSubstance used to increase heart function by inducing relaxation of the left ventricle.")
(comment PhosphodiesteraseInhibitorType "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose molecules are enzymes capable of breaking phosphodiester bond (see #$PhosphodiesterBond).")
(comment PDE1SelectiveInhibitorType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that inhibit class 1 phosphodiesterases.")
(comment PDE2SelectiveInhibitorType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that inhibit class 2 phosphodiesterases.")
(comment PDE3SelectiveInhibitorType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that inhibit class 3 phosphodiesterases.")
(comment PDE5SelectiveInhibitorType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that inhibit class 5 phosphodiesterases.")
(comment PDE4SelectiveInhibitorType "The collection of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that inhibit class 4 phosphodiesterases.")
(comment PhosphodiesteraseInhibitingSubstance "The collection of all instances of instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose molecules are enzymes capable of breaking phosphodiester bonds (see #$PhosphodiesterBond).")
(comment BreakingAChemicalBond "The collection of chemical reaction events in which a #$ChemicalBond is dissolved.")
(comment PDESelectiveInhibitorType "A specialization of #$PhosphodiesteraseInhibitorType, instances are chemical compounds that inhibit a particular class of phosphodiesterase.")
(comment chemicalBondBroken "<code>(#$chemicalBondBroken EVENT BOND)</code> identifies <code>BOND</code> as the instance of #$ChemicalBond that is the #$inputsDestroyed in the #$BreakingAChemicalBond event <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment PhosphodiesteraseInhibitorTypeByClassification "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$PhosphodiesteraseInhibitorType into specializations based on their classification (whether they are specific to a class of #$Phosphodiesterase and, if so, which class)")
(comment AcuteHeartFailure "A subcollection of #$HeartFailure.  Instances are episodes in which patients experience sudden and severe heart failure symptoms, such as shortness of breath, caused by fluid overflow in the lungs.")
(comment AcuteDecompensationOfChronicHeartFailure "A subclass of #$AcuteHeartFailure, instances are characterized by sudden and severe heart failure symptoms in people suffering from chronic heart failure.")
(comment AcuteHeartFailureDeNovo "The collection of episodes of #$AcuteHeartFailure that are not decompensations of existing heart conditions.")
(comment PDENonselectiveInhibitorType "A type of phosphodiesterase inhibitor that is not specific to any of the five categories of phosphodiesterase.")
(comment NuclearReceptor "A class of #$ReceptorMolecule that has the ability to bind directly to DNA.")
(comment stopWordString "(#$stopWordString ?STRING) means that the string ?STRING should not be treated as having any meaning in contexts which can see the #$stopWordString assertion.")
(comment LeftVentricularHeartFailure "A kind of #$HeartFailure characterized by the inability of the left ventricle (see #$LeftVentricle) to pump blood into the body.  Left ventricular heart failure can be the result of a stiff ventricle that fails to allow the chamber to fill with blood, in which case it is diastolic (see #$DiastolicHeartFailure); or it can be the result of a weak ventricle than cannot pump blood out of the chamber, in which case the failure is systolic (see #$SystolicHeartFailure).")
(comment summaryPredicateCoreOrdering "<code>(#$summaryPredicateCoreOrdering SUM-PRED LIST)</code> means that the list <code>LIST</code> describeds the ordering in which the predicates in the category <code>SUM-PRED</code> should be displayed.")
(comment MedicalAblation "The collection of #$Ablations performed as medical treatment events.")
(comment queryNeedsThingBoundInPosition "(#$queryNeedsThingBoundInPosition QUERY THING ARG-POS) means that before QUERY can be run by the inference engine, THING should be substituted for the free variable at ARG-POS in the query sentence.  That is to say, QUERY has a free variable at ARG-POS but the inference engine should never see that variable -- it is supposed to be replaced by THING in application code before being run.  This is useful when an application needs to run a query to find some value, but the query has parameters that need to come from user input or an SKS at runtime (in this case it is probably true that (#$quotedIsa THING #$IndexicalConcept)).")
(comment equipmentOfFacility "<code>(#$equipmentOfFacility DEV FAC)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> is equipment located at the facility <code>FAC</code>.")
(comment Gain-Electronics "A specialization of #$ScalarQuantity.  Gain is the ability of a circuit to increase the power of a signal.")
(comment CellTypeByTissueType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets the collection of all cells (see #$Cell) into cell-types whose instances are cells of a shared type of tissue.")
(comment cellsOfTissueType "<code>(#$cellsOfTissueType CELL-TYPE TISSUE-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>CELL-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Cell that are the #$basicUnit for biological tissue of type <code>TISSUE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CellTypeOfTissueTypeFn "<code>(#$CellTypeOfTissueTypeFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$Cell that are the basic unit (#$basicUnit) for any instance of tissue type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment CardiacMuscle "The collection of all instances of #$StriatedMuscle that are found in an animals heart.")
(comment NatriureticPeptide "A subcollection of #$PolypeptideMolecule, produced in chemical reactions in cardiomyoctytes (cells of heart muscle tissue).")
(comment BrainNatriureticPeptide "A subcollection of #$NatriureticPeptide, produced by heart muscle cells in response to streching caused by heart enlargement.  High levels of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$BrainNatriureticPeptide) are an indicator of heart failure.")
(comment AtrialNatriureticPeptide "A subcollection of #$NatriureticPeptide produced and released by cardiac muscle cells in response to high blood pressure.")
(comment C-TypeNatriureticPeptide "A subcollection of #$NatriureticPeptide.  Unlike its siblings ANP (#$AtrialNatriureticPeptide) and BNP (#$BrainNatriureticPeptide), CNP is an agonist for B-Type N natriuretic receptor.")
(comment MeasuringTheLevelOfASubstanceInASample "A subcollection of #$MeasuringSomething.  Instances measure the level (the density) of some type of substance  in a sample.  Examples include instances of #$CholesterolTest, tests for levels of contaminants in ground water, etc.")
(comment substanceMeasured "<code>(#$substanceMeasured TEST STUFF-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> as the type of substance being measured in <code>TEST</code>, an instance of #$MeasuringTheLevelOfASubstanceInASample.")
(comment BNPLevelTest "A specialization of both #$MeasuringTheLevelOfASubstanceInASample and #$BloodTest.  Instances test blood samples to determine the level of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$BrainNatriureticPeptide) in the blood; the result of the test (see #$measurementResult) is determined to be the #$bnpLevel for the patient at the time the blood sample was drawn.  A significantly high value (at least 500 pg per ml) is considered a strong indicator that the patient is suffering from acute congestive heart failure.  A level below 50 pg per ml is considered a negative result for CHF.")
(comment DeterminationOfSlotValueFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes an instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot and returns a specialization of #$DeterminingTheValueOfASlot.  <code>(#$DeterminationOfSlotValueFn SLOT)</code> denotes the collection of
events in which the #$arg2 value of <code>SLOT</code> applied to some #$arg1 is determined (come to be known by) some observer.  For example, <code>(#$EvaluationOfSlotValueFn #$temperatureOfObject)</code> denotes the collection of events in which the #$temperatureOfObject for some object is measured.")
(comment signOfAilment "<code>(#$signOfAilment SIGN AILMENT)</code> means that the instance <code>SIGN</code> of #$PhysiologicalConditionType is a sign that its #$bodilyDoer has the ailment <code>AILMENT</code>.  A sign of an ailment is a condition that typically is only detectible through testing or an exam; see #$symptomOfAilment for the predicate used to identify symptoms (conditions phenomenologically detectible by the patient).")
(comment N-TerminalProBNP "A biologically inert #$PolypeptideMolecule that is co-secreted with #$BrainNatriureticPeptide by distressed cardiac muscle cells.  Because it has a relatively long half-life, #$N-TerminalProBNP levels are a good way to test for heart failure.")
(comment NT-ProBNPLevelTest "A specialization of both #$MeasuringTheLevelOfASubstanceInASample and #$BloodTest.  Instances test blood samples to determine the level of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$N-TerminalProBNP) in the blood; the result of the test (see #$measurementResult) is determined to be the #$nt-proBNPLevel for the patient at the time the blood sample was drawn.  A significantly high value is considered a strong indicator that the patient is suffering from acute congestive heart failure.")
(comment bnpLevel "<code>(#$bnpLevel ANIMAL LEVEL)</code> means that the level of BNP (see (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$BrainNatriureticPeptide)) for the instance <code>ANIMAL</code> of #$Animal is <code>LEVEL</code>, an instance of #$Density.")
(comment nt-proBNPLevel "<code>(#$nt-proBNPLevel ANIMAL LEVEL)</code> means that the level of N-Terminal proBNP (see (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$N-TerminalProBNP)) for the instance <code>ANIMAL</code> of #$Animal is <code>LEVEL</code>, an instance of #$Density.")
(comment ailmentSignOrSymptom "<code>(#$ailmentSignOrSymptom AILMENT INDICATOR)</code> identifies <code>INDICATOR</code> as a type of #$PhysiologicalCondition that is a symptom (#$symptomOfAilment) or sign (#$signOfAilment) of the ailment <code>AILMENT</code>.  A symptom is distinguished from a sign in terms of expertise required for detection: A patient can detect and report his or her own symptoms, while signs are detectible via medical exams and testing.")
(comment Nesiritide "The recombinant form (see #$recombinantFormOf) of brain natriuretic peptide see (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn #$BrainNatriureticPeptide), used to treat acute congestive heart failure.")
(comment recombinantFormOf "<code>(#$recombinantFormOf MAN-MADE-TYPE CHEMICAL)</code> identifies <code>MAN-MADE-TYPE</code> as the class of instances of <code>CHEMICAL</code> whose instances are synthesized using recombinant techniques.  Typically, <code>CHEMICAL</code> will be a #$ChemicalSubstanceType that occurs naturally via biological processes, and recombinant techniques are used to increase availability of <code>CHEMICAL</code> for medical purposes.")
(comment VentricularHypertrophy "The collection of instances of #$PhysiologicalCondition in which a ventricle of the heart is enlarged.")
(comment Sound "A specialization of #$WavePropagation.  Each instance of #$Sound is an instance of wave propagation in which longitudinal pressure waves travel through matter.  Notable specializations of #$Sound include #$AudibleSound, #$Ultrasound, and #$Music.")
(comment AudibleSound "A specialization of #$Sound. Each instance of this collection is a sound which is audible to most instances of #$Animal under normal conditions.  Note that \"normal conditions\" may include circumstances in which the listener hears the sound from a stethoscope or headphones.  #$AudibleSound is disjoint with #$Ultrasound.")
(comment Bruit "A specialization of #$EmittingSound.  Each instance of #$Bruit is an emmission of an unusual sound by the passage of blood through a partially obstructed artery.  This type of sound emmission is detectable via the use of a stethoscope.")
(comment CarotidBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$CarotidBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a carotid artery.")
(comment LeftCarotidBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$LeftCarotidBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a left carotid artery.")
(comment RightCarotidBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$RightCarotidBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a right carotid artery.")
(comment FemoralBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$FemoralBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a femoral artery.")
(comment LeftFemoralBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$LeftFemoralBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a left femoral artery.")
(comment RightFemoralBruit "A specialization of #$Bruit.  Each instance of #$RightFemroalBruit is a bruit produced by blood as it rushes past an obstruction in a right femoral artery.")
(disjointWith CarotidBruit FemoralBruit)
(disjointWith LeftCarotidBruit RightCarotidBruit)
(disjointWith LeftFemoralBruit RightFemoralBruit)
(comment HeartMurmur "A specialization of #$EmittingSound.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur is an emission of an unusual sound due to turbulent blood flow in the vicinity of the heart.")
(comment GallopRhythm "A specialization of #$CardiacArrhythmia. Each instance of #$GallopRhythm is a rhythm of heart beats in which the two ordinary beats (which constitute the familiar \"lub-dub\" pattern) known as S1 and S2 are accompanied by one or two additional beats.  Depending on where the occur in the cycle, these additional beats are known as either S3 or S4.")
(comment GallopRhythm-WithS3Beat "A specialization of #$GallopRhythm. Each instance of #$GallopRhythm-WithS3Beat is a rhythm of heart beats in which the two ordinary beats (which constitute the familiar \"lub-dub\" pattern) known as S1 and S2 are accompanied by an additional beat, known as S3.")
(comment GallopRhythm-WithS4Beat "A specialization of #$CardiacArrhythmia. Each instance of #$GallopRhythm-WithS4Beat is a rhythm of heart beats in which the two ordinary beats (which constitute the familiar \"lub-dub\" pattern) known as S1 and S2 are accompanied by an additional beat, known as S4.")
(comment HeartMurmur-Systolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-Systolic is a murmur that occurs between S1 and S2.  C. #$HeartMurmur-Diastolic for murmurs that occur between S2 and S1.")
(comment HeartMurmur-Diastolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-Diastolic is a murmur that occurs between S2 and S1.  C. #$HeartMurmur-Systolic for murmurs that occur between S1 and S2.")
(comment HeartMurmur-LateSystolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-LateSystolic is a murmur that starts after S1 and extends toward S2.")
(comment visitingSportsTeam "Where GAME is a #$CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition and TEAM is a #$SportsTeam, (#$visitingSportsTeam GAME TEAM) means that TEAM is a competitor in GAME (see #$competingSportsTeam) who does not represent the polity within whose territory the game is played (see #$teamRepresentsPolity).")
(comment homeSportsTeam "Where GAME is a #$CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition and TEAM is a #$SportsTeam, (#$homeSportsTeam GAME TEAM) means that TEAM is a competitor in GAME (see #$competingSportsTeam) who represents the polity within whose territory the game is played (see #$teamRepresentsPolity).")
(comment losingSportsTeam "Where GAME is a #$CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition and TEAM is a #$SportsTeam, (#$losingSportsTeam GAME TEAM) means that TEAM is the losing team in GAME.")
(comment winningSportsTeam "Where GAME is a #$CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition and TEAM is a #$SportsTeam, (#$winningSportsTeam GAME TEAM) means that TEAM is the winning team in GAME.")
(comment sportsTeamPlayers "(#$sportsTeamPlayers TEAM MEMBER) means that MEMBER is a player on TEAM in the temporal context of the assertion.")
(comment attendingSpectatorAtSportsCompetition "(#$attendingSpectatorAtSportsCompetition GAME VIEWER) means that VIEWER is one of those physically present at GAME in the capacity of a spectator.")
(comment participatingPlayers "(#$participatingPlayers GAME PLAYER) means that PLAYER is one of the #$IntelligentAgents who participates in game in virtue of being a member of one of the competing teams.")
(comment numberInAttendance "(#$numberInAttendance OCCURRANCE NUM) means that there were exactly NUM individuals who attended OCCURRANCE, some sense of attendance.")
(comment teamRepresentsPolity "(#$teamRepresentsPolity TEAM POLITY) means that TEAM represents, or takes itself to be, the representative of POLITY, and that this branding is recognized legally, or at least formally, by POLITY.  In such cases, it often happens that the representing team is legally and socially empowered to use the name of the represented polity in their own team name.")
(comment Renitec "A medicine marketed by Merck & Co, used to treat hypertension.  It's active ingredient is the ACE inhibitor #$Enalapril.")
(comment Vasotec "A medicine marketed by Merck & Co, used to treat hypertension.  It's active ingredient is the ACE inhibitor #$Enalapril.")
(comment Enalapril "A subcollection of #$ACEInhibitor, marketed by #$MerckAndCo as #$Vasotec and #$Renitec.")
(comment Primacor "A brand name drug whose active ingredient is #$Milrinone.")
(comment HeartMurmur-MidSystolicEjection "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-LateSystolic is a murmur that starts briefly after S1 and extends toward S2.")
(comment HeartMurmur-EarlyDiastolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-Diastolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-EarlyDiastolic starts at the same time as S2 and ends before S1.")
(comment HeartMurmur-MidDiastolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-Diastolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-MidDiastolic starts breifly after S2 and ends before S1.")
(comment DependentEdema "A specialization of #$Edema-Condition.  Each instance of #$DependentEdema is an edema condition where the location of the swelling depends on the orientation of the body.")
(comment Rales "A specialization of #$EmittingSound.  Each instance of #$Rales is an emmission of an unusual rattling noise by the lungs during inhalation.  This type of sound emmission is detectable via the use of a stethoscope.")
(comment CardiacMyocyte "Also known as myocardial cells, #$CardiacMyocytes are a type of cell commonly found in heart tissue.  They are similar to skeletal muscle cells in that they are sometimes multinucleated; however, they ordinarily contain at most two nuclei.  Like #$Neurons, #$CardiacMyocytes are capable of generating spreading action potentials which influence the myocardium.  These in turn serve to generate and regulate the heartbeat.")
(comment SickleCellDisease "A specialization of #$GeneticCondition.  Sickle cell disease is a genetic disorder that affects the shape of red blood cells. A notable specialization is #$SickleCellAnemia.")
(comment DiseaseTypeByPartTypeAffected "A specialization of #$DiseaseTypeByPartTypeAffected.  Each instance of #$DiseaseTypeByPartTypeAffected is a specialization of #$AilmentCondition that affects a particular body part.")
(comment PharmacyProductType "A collection of collections. Instances of this collection are types of pharmaceutical products that may be prescribed by a medical professional. Note that this includes drugs -- specializations of #$DrugSubstance -- as well as pharmaceutical devices such as #$TestStrip or #$HearingAid-Prescription. #$PrescriptionDrugType and #$OverTheCounterDrugType are among the specializations of this collection.")
(comment Plavix "A brand-name drug whose active ingredient is #$Clopidogrel.  Plavix is the trade name used by Bristol-Myers to market Clopidogrel.")
(comment Iscover "A specialization of (#$DrugFn #$Clopidogrel))  Iscover is the trade name used by Sanofi-Aventis to market Clopidogrel.")
(comment Clopilet "A specialization of (#$DrugFn #$Clopidogrel). Clopilet is the trade name used by Sanofi-Aventis to market Clopidogrel.")
(comment DrugSubstanceTypeByMechanismOfAction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$DrugSubstance into collections individuated by the ability of their instances to engage in a common type of biochemical interaction, specific to a particular enzyme or molecule.")
(comment COXInhibitingSubstance "An instance of #$DrugSubstanceTypeByMechanismOfAction.  Instances are substances whose molecules are capable of forming chemical bonds with the enzyme #$Cyclooxygenase in a way that prevents it performing its \"normal\" biological function of bonding with other chemicals to produce prostanoids (which in turn cause inflamation).")
(comment COXInactivation "A subcollection of #$EnzymaticInhibition where the inhibited enzyme (see #$objectChemicallyBonded) is an instance of #$Cyclooxygenase.")
(comment mechanismOfAction "<code>(#$mechanismOfAction DRUG EVENT ROLE)</code> means that for the type of #$DrugSubstance <code>DRUG</code>, one of the mechanisms of action (i.e., the way, at the level of chemical interactions, in which it achieves its expected effects) is for its molecules to play the role <code>ROLE</code> in biochemical events of type <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment notably "The corresponding predicate for the function #$NotablyFn (q.v.) .")
(comment NotablyFn "<code>(#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED)</code> denotes a specialization of <code>BIN-PRED</code>, with the following property:  <code>((#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED) ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds if and only if <code>(BIN-PRED ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds and it is notable that <code>(BIN-PRED ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds.   In other words, if <code>BIN-PRED</code> is a binary relation then <code>(#$NotablyFn BIN-PRED)</code> is the extent of that relation where the relation holds notably. In some cases, this corresponds to the notion of a <i>key</i> relationship. For example (#$suppliers  #$StarbucksCorporation #$Cycorp) holds, but ((#$NotablyFn #$suppliers) #$StarbucksCorporation #$Cycorp) does not. Similarly, ((#$NotablyFn #$makesProductType) #$StarbucksCorporation #$Coffee-Beverage) holds.")
(comment Nifedipine "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$CalciumChannelBlocker.  Nifedipine is used in treating heart disease.")
(comment NonSteroidalAntiInflammatory "Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs.  Notable specializations include aspirin and ibuprofen.")
(disjointWith NonSteroidalAntiInflammatory Steroid)
(comment Naproxen "The collection of all  naproxen.  An #$AntiInflammatory.")
(comment Aleve "The collection of drugs for relieving pain that are produced 
under the brandname Aleve.")
(comment Naprosyn "The collection of drugs for relieving pain that are produced 
under the brandname Naprosyn.")
(comment Anaprox "The collection of drugs for relieving pain that are produced 
under the brandname Anaprox.")
(comment Naprelan "The collection of drugs for relieving pain that are produced 
under the brandname Naprelan.")
(comment Procainamide "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$ClassIAAntiarrhythmicMedication.")
(comment queryMtAssociatedWithTask "<code>(#$queryMtAssociatedWithTask MT TASK)</code> means that MT is associated with task -- typically as the relevant query mt for the task.")
(comment Vertebra "The collection of all vertebrae, which are the bones that constitute spines. A type of #$IrregularBone. The collection #$Vertebra is an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$AnimalBodyPartType.")
(comment sequelTo "<code>(#$sequelTo LATER EARLIER)</code> means that <code>LATER</code> is a conceptuyal work that is a sequel to the conceptual work, <code>EARLIER</code>.")
(comment EndotrachealTube "A tube used during medical procedures to manage the patient's airway.")
(comment EndotrachealTubeAdministration "A specialization of #$AdministeringADrug.  Each instance of #$EndotrachealTubeAdministration is an event in which a medication is administered through an endotracheal tube.")
(comment OrotrachealTube "A specialization of #$EndotrachealTube .  Each instsance of #$OrotrachealTube is an endotracheal tube designed to be inserted through the mouth.")
(comment NasotrachealTube "A specialization of #$EndotrachealTube .  Each instsance of #$NasotrachealTube is an endotracheal tube designed to be inserted through the nostrils.")
(comment Metatarsal "The collection of all metatarsals. A type of #$FootBone and #$LongBone. The collection #$Metatarsal is an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$AnimalBodyPartType.")
(comment FifthMetatarsal "The #$FifthMetatarsal is a #$FootBone which is connected to the LittleToe.")
(comment FirstMetatarsal "The #$FirstMetatarsal is the #$FootBone which is connected to the Great Toe.")
(comment SecondMetatarsal "The #$SecondMetatarsal is the #$FootBone which is connected to the second toe.")
(comment ThirdMetatarsal "The #$ThirdMetatarsal is the #$FootBone which is connected to the third toe.")
(comment FourthMetatarsal "The #$FourthMetatarsal is the #$FootBone which is connected to the fourth toe.")
(comment PolymerMolecule "The collection of all macromolecules formed by the chemical union of five or more identical combining units.  This collection includes natural polymers like polypeptides and polysaccharides, as well as synthetic polymers such as #$Nylon. ")
(comment AntibodyIgD "The collection of all IgD antibodies. A type of #$AntibodyMolecule.  #$AntibodyIgD is a #$ProteinMoleculeType.")
(comment AntibodyIgA "The collection of all IgA antibodies. A type of #$AntibodyMolecule.")
(comment AntibodyIgE "The collection of all IgE antibodies. A type of #$AntibodyMolecule.")
(comment AntibodyIgG "The collection of all IgG. A type of #$AntibodyMolecule.")
(comment AntibodyIgM "The collection of all IgM antibodies. A type of #$AntibodyMolecule.")
(comment ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies "The collection of all instances of #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies whose instances are protein molecules (see #$ProteinMolecule).")
(comment AntibodyTypeByHeavyChainType "The collection of immunoglobin isotypes, the major categories of #$AntibodyMolecule, organized by the presence of a #$HeavyChainPolypeptide of a certain class.")
(comment HeavyChainPolypeptide "A class of #$PolypeptideMolecule defined, in part, by its role as \"a larger chain\" in a larger #$ProteinMolecule.  Heavy chains divide into classes which, in the case of antibodies (see #$AntibodyMolecule), determine the isotype of the antibody.")
(disjointWith GlobularProteinMolecule FibrousProteinMolecule)
(comment GlobularProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$GlobularProteinMolecule is a protein molecule that is water-soluble.  Contrast this class with #$FibrousProteinMolecule, which is the collection of relatively non-soluble protein molecules.")
(comment HumanSerumAlbuminProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$AlbuminProteinMolecule.  Human sewrum albumin molecules play an importan role in regulating osmotic pressure.")
(comment TroponinT "A type of organic substance.  High levels of Troponin T can indicate damage to smooth muscle tissue.")
(comment AntibodyMolecule "A specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, #$GlobularProteinMolecule, and #$BloodProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$AntibodyMolecule is a gamma globulin protein that is used by the immune system of a vertebrate to neutralize foreign bodies (e.g. viruses) in the bloodstream.")
(comment HemoglobinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlobularProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$HemoglobinMolecule is a globular protein molecule typically found within red blood cells and used by vertebrates to transport oxygen.")
(comment MyoglobinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlobularProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$MyoglobinMolecule is a globular protein molecule.")
(comment PureRedCellAplasia "A specialization of #$AplasticAnemia.  PRCA is a condition in which bone marrow produces insufficiently many new red blood cells.")
(comment AplasticAnemia "A specialization of #$Anemia.  Aplastic anemia is a condition in which bone marrow produces insufficiently many new blood cells.")
(comment Polycythemia "The collection of instances of the condition in which there is an overproduction of blood cells.")
(comment PolycythemiaVera "A specialization of #$Polycythemia.  Polycythemia vera is the condition in which there is an overproduction of red blood cells due to an abnormality of the bone marrow.")
(comment SecondaryPolycythemia "A specialization of #$Polycythemia.  Secondary polycythemia vera is the condition in which there is an abnormally high productin of red blood cells due to some cause other then a faulty bone marrow.  Common causes include living at altitude and smoking.")
(comment AlbuminMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$AlbuminMolecule is a globular protein molecule (see #$GlobularProteinMolecule) that, when heated in solution, tends to coagulate.")
(comment FibrousProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$FibrousProteinMolecule is a protein molecule that is not water-soluble.  Contrast this class with #$GlobularProteinMolecule, which is the collection of relatively water-soluble protein molecules.")
(comment NeuroglobinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlobularProteinMolecule.  This protein reversibly binds to oxygen and is notably found in the the nervous system, as well as endocrine tissues, among other body regions.")
(comment PharmaceuticalType "Elements or chemical compounds which have known biological effects and are consumed in order to produce those effects (or some of them, anyway).  Note that not all instances of each of these are consumed to produce those effects. (#$Nitroglycerine would be an example - sometimes it's consumed for its coronary effects, but sometimes it's consumed in explosions.)  This collection was created to distinguish between e.g. #$TetracyclineAntibiotic and a mixture whose #$constituents-Active is #$TetracyclineAntibiotic, but in fact only contains 1% of that substance.")
(disjointWith PubliclyHeldCorporation PrivatelyHeldCorporation)
(disjointWith PubliclyHeldCorporation (CollectionDifferenceFn Organization PubliclyHeldCorporation))
(comment controllingCompany "The predicate #$controllingCompany relates a business to the business which is its parent company.  (#$controllingCompany ORG1 PARENT) means that #$Organization ORG1 is a (partly or wholly owned) subsidiary of #$Business PARENT.  PARENT is the parent company that owns and substantially controls ORG1.  E.g., (#$controllingCompany TheLAWeekly TheVillageVoice).")
(comment controllingOrganization "<code>(#$controllingOrganization PARENT-ORG ORG)</code> means that <code>PARENT-ORG</code> owns <code>ORG</code>, or at least has some fundamental and ongoing control over it, although <code>ORG</code> is distinct enough from <code>PARENT-ORG</code> that it may or may not count as one of its #$subOrganizations.  A prominent specialization is #$controllingCompany, which relates an instance of #$Business to one of its subsidiaries.  #$controllingOrganization also applies in cases where one or both of the organizations is non-commercial, as when a business or school is run by religious or ideological organization, or a business establishes and then oversees a charitable foundation.")
(comment Spoon-SilverwarePiece "The collection of eating implements often used to carry inherently messy, liquid or semi-liquid foods to the mouth.  All instances of #$Spoon-SilverwarePiece are instances of #$SilverwarePiece, but this is not true for all instances of #$Spoon.")
(comment FoodUtensil "A specialization of #$HandTool.  Each instance of #$FoodUtensil is an implement or container used in preparing or consuming food.  Notable specializations of #$FoodUtensil include #$Spoon, #$CarvingKnife, #$CookingUtensil, #$FoodVessel, #$CuttingBoard, and #$Chopstick.")
(comment NocturnalAnimal "The collection of all nocturnal animals, which are animals that are active at night rather than during the day. A type of #$Animal.")
(comment DiurnalAnimal "The collection of all diurnal animals, which are animals that are active at daytime rather than during the night. A type of #$Animal.")
(comment GiantOtter "The collection of all giant otters. A type of #$Otter. #$GiantOtter is a #$BiologicalTaxon.")
(comment CrepuscularAnimal "The collection of all crepuscular animals, which are animals that are active at twilight rather than during the night or day. A type of #$Animal.")
(comment AngleModulation "The collection of events in which an analog electromagnetic signal is modulated by altering its angle.  The two main specializations of #$AngleModulation are #$PhaseModulation and #$FrequencyModulation.")
(comment AmplitudeShiftKeying "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Digital.  ASK is modulation of a digital signal's amplitude.")
(comment FrequencyShiftKeying "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Digital.  FSK is modulation of a digital signal's frequency.")
(comment PhaseShiftKeying "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Digital.  PSK is modulation of a digital signal's phase.")
(comment SingleSidebandModulation "A specialization of #$AmplitudeModulation. Single sideband modulation is a refinement of AM.")
(comment DoubleSidebandModulation "A specialization of #$AmplitudeModulation. Double sideband modulation is a refinement of AM.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Analog "The collection of events in which some aspect of analog electromagnetic radiation is modulated.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Digital "The collection of events in which some aspect of digital electromagnetic radiation is modulated.")
(comment VestigialSidebandModulation "A specialization of #$AmplitudeModulation. Vestigial sideband modulation is a refinement of AM.")
(comment Holography "A specialization of #$VisualImageRecording.  The product of a #$Holography event is a #$Hologram: a recorded image that appears three-dimensional.")
(comment Hologram "A specialization of #$Graphic-VisualIBT.  Holograms are recorded images that appear three-dimensional.  They are the product of #$Holography processes.")
(comment stadiumTypeForSportType "(#$stadiumTypeForSportType SPORT-TYPE STADIUM-TYPE) means that instances of STADIUM-TYPE are designed and built to be places at which instances of SPORT-TYPE are played and observed by large audiences.")
(comment CollegeBaseballTeam "The collection of all college baseball teams. A type of #$MensSportsTeam, #$CollegeSportsTeam, and #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment collegeBaseballTeamOf "A predicate corresponding to the function #$CollegeFootballTeamFn.  <code>(#$collegeFootballTeamOf X (#$CollegeFootballTeamFn X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment CollegeBaseballTeamFn "(#$CollegeBaseballTeamFn COLLEGE) denotes the college baseball team for COLLEGE.  For example, (#$CollegeBaseballTeamFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin) denotes the University of Texas baseball team.")
(comment InstanceWithRelationToFn "'(#$InstanceWithRelationToFn COLLECTION PREDICATE THING)' denotes the unique INSTANCE of COLLECTION such that (PREDICATE INSTANCE THING) holds.  So for example, (#$InstanceWithRelationToFn #$CollegeFootballTeam #$affiliatedWith #$UniversityOfNotreDame) is the University of Notre Dame football team.  To guarantee that this function returns a unique value, the predicate that occurs in the arg2 of any #$InstanceWithRelationToFn NAT must be #$SingleEntry in its arg1.")
(disjointWith ProcedurePerformedDuringReop MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment ProcedurePerformedDuringReop "A specialization of #$SurgicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$ProcedurePerformedDuringReop is a procedure performed during a reoperation (an operation where the patient had an earlier operation.")
(comment representsAgentInOrganization "<code>(#$representsAgentInOrganization AGENT REPRESENTED-AGENT ORG)</code> means that <code>REPRESENTED-AGENT</code> is represented by <code>AGENT</code> in <code>ORG</code>.  This relation is used to describe, for example, the relation a U.S. Senator bears to a U.S. State and the U.S. Senate, or the relation a U.N. Ambassador bears to a nation and the U.N.")
(comment constrainKnownValuesForPredRelativeToIsaInArg-Isa "<pre>(#$constrainKnownValuesForPredRelativeToIsaInArg-Isa PRED COLL-1 N COLL-2 M)</pre> holds just in case COLL-1 is the collection of terms that are known arg N values for a sentence using PRED when an instance of COLL-2 stands in arg M.

<br><br>
For example,   
<br><br>
(#$constrainKnownValuesForPredRelativeToIsaInArg-Isa #$isa (#$FactEntrySourceTypeForProjectFn #$DecisionSupportSBIRProject) 2 #$ConceptualWork 1)<br><br>
means that only instances of (#$FactEntrySourceTypeForProjectFn #$DecisionSupportSBIRProject) should be shown as known values for the arg 2 in #$isa literals when an instance of #$ConceptualWork appears in arg1 of the literal.")
(comment pulseCodingOfTransmitter "<code>(#$pulseCodingOfTransmitter TRANS INTERVAL)</code> means that the transmitter <code>TRANS</code>, an instance of #$Transmitter, has an available pulse width of of <code>INTERVAL</code>.")
(comment Transmitter "A specialization of #$WirelessCommunicationDevice.  Each instance of #$Transmitter is a device used for transmitting electromagnetic signals.")
(comment MicrowaveTransmitter "Device used for transmitting microwave signals.")
(comment SignalMultiplexing "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation.  Each instance of #$SignalMultiplexing is an event in which multiple EM signals are combined into a single signal.")
(comment Demultiplexer "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$Multiplexer is a device used for multiplexing electromagnetic signals.")
(comment SignalDemultiplexing "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation.  Each instance of #$SignalMultiplexing is an event in which multiplexed EM signals are separated into their component signals.")
(comment hasModulationProperty "<code>(#$hasModulationProperty SIGNAL MOD-PROP)</code> means that the signal <code>SIGNAL</code> has been modulated in a modulation event of type <code>MOD-PROP</code>.")
(comment PulseCodeModulation "A specialization of #$TimeDivisionMultiplexing.")
(comment PulseAmplitudeModulation "A specialization of #$TimeDivisionMultiplexing.")
(comment eventPatientInAgeRangeDuringEvent "<code>(#$eventPatientInAgeRangeDuringEvent EVT RANGE)</code> means that during <code>EVT</code> the associated patient's age was in RANGE.  As of 10/27/08, this is supported in the CAE for the following seven different age groups
  <pre>
    Less than 30 years old
    30 - 39 
    40 - 49
    50 - 59
    60 - 69
    70 - 79
    80 or older</pre>.")
(comment TimeDivisionMultiplexing "A specialization of #$SignalMultiplexing.  Each instance of #$SignalMultiplexing is an event in which multiple EM signals are combined into a single signal by physically taking turns on the channel.")
(comment FrequencyDivisionMultiplexing "A specialization of #$SignalMultiplexing.  Each instance of #$FrequencyDivisionMultiplexing is an event in which multiple EM signals are modulated on different frequency channels and combined to form a composite signal.")
(comment WavelengthDivisionMultiplexing "A specialization of #$SignalMultiplexing.  Each instance of #$WavelengthDivisionMultiplexing is an event in which multiple signals are combined by simultaneously using different wavelengths of laser light.")
(comment FeherPatentedQuadraturePhaseShiftKeyingB "A specialization of #$FeherPatentedQuadraturePhaseShiftKeying.")
(comment FeherPatentedQuadraturePhaseShiftKeyingJR "A specialization of #$FeherPatentedQuadraturePhaseShiftKeying.  ")
(comment ShapedOffsetQuadraturePhaseShiftKeyingTG "A specialization of #$ShapedOffsetQuadraturePhaseShiftKeying.")
(comment ContinuousPhaseModulation "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationModulation-Digital.")
(comment Commutator-Electric "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$Commutator-Electric is a device that periodically reverses current.")
(comment CircuitBreaker "A specialization of #$ElectricalSwitch.  Each instance of #$CircuitBreaker is a switch designed to protect a circuit from overload.  Circuit breakers are similar to fuses (see #$Fuse-ElectricalComponent), but can be use multiple times.")
(comment Rectifier "A specialization of#$ElectricalComponent.  Each instance of #$Inverter-Electric ia a device that can convert alternating current to direct current.")
(comment UninterruptiblePowerSupply "A specialization of #$ElectricalComponent.  Each instance of #$UninterruptiblePowerSupply ia a device that maintains continuously supplied battery-backup power to connected devices when main utility power becomes unavailable.")
(comment Inverter-Electric "A specialization of #$ElectricalComponent.  Each instance of #$Inverter-Electric ia a device that can convert direct current to alternating current.")
(comment SurgeProtector "This is the collection of surge protectors. These are devices which regulate the amount of current flowing through a wire in such a way as to prevent surges of electricity from reaching a piece of equipment
and potentially damaging it.")
(comment PowerStrip "This is the collection of power strips. Each instance of #$PowerStrip is a strip of sockets attached to the end of a flexible power cable that can be plugged into e.g. a wall socket.")
(comment LinearPowerSupply "A specialization of #$PowerSupply.  Each instance of #$LinearPowerSupply directly convets voltage from a main source into a lower voltage.")
(comment SwitchedModePowerSupply "A specialization of #$PowerSupply.  Each instance of #$SwitchedModePowerSupply converts voltage from a main source into a lower voltage by slicing it and then involving multiple step-down transformers.")
(comment LEDDisplay "A #$VolatileFlatPanelDisplay screen for a piece of electronic hardware in which the principal display forming elements are instances of #$LightEmittingDiode.")
(comment PlasmaDisplay "A specialization of #$VolatileFlatPanelDisplay.  Each instance of #$PlasmaDisplay is a display widely used for flat-panel televisions.  This technology works by electrifying cells in the creen that are filled with gas.  The gas turns into plasma and emits light.")
(comment AmazonKindle "A specialization of #$EBookReader.  Each instance of #$AmazonKindle is a Kindle e-book reader.")
(comment SonyReader "A specialization of #$EBookReader.  Each instance of #$SonyReader is a Sony Reader e-book reader.")
(disjointWith StaticFlatPanelDisplay VolatileFlatPanelDisplay)
(comment Transducer "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$Transducer is a device used for converting one type of energy into another.")
(disjointWith LightBulb-Flourescent LightBulb-Incandescent)
(comment Lightbulb "A bulb of glass or quartz enclosing material that incandesces or fluoresces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(comment LightBulb-Incandescent "A bulb of glass or quartz enclosing material that incandesces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(comment Accelerometer "A device used to measure acceleration.")
(comment Earphone "The audio devices put very close to the ears to permit personal listening")
(comment Earbuds "Compact audio devices put inside the ears to permit personal listening.")
(comment Receiver "The device used to receive transmissions broadcast in radio frequencies (does not include radio transmitters).")
(comment SchottkyDiode "A specialization of #$Diode.  Each instance of #$SchottkyDiode is a diode with a low forward voltage drop and a fast switching action.")
(comment TunnelDiode "A specialization of #$Diode.  Each instance of #$TunnelDiode (also known as Esaki diodes) are semiconducting diodes that exhibit negative resistance caused by quantum tunneling.")
(comment ZenerDiode "A specialization of #$Diode.  Each instance of #$ZenerDiode is a diode that permits unidirectional current in the forward direction only until a threshold known as the \"breakdown voltage\" is reached, at which point the diode permits current in the reverse direction.")
(comment AvalancheDiode "A specialization of #$Diode.  Each instance of #$AvalancheDiode is a diode that permits backward current when a breakdown threshold is reached, where the breakdown is caused by the \"avalanche\" effect.  Avalance diodes are very similar to #$ZenerDiodes (q.v.).")
(comment LaserDiode "A specialization of #$Diode.  Each instance of #$LaserDiode is a diode that can be made to emit a laser.")
(comment Diode "The collection of all electrical diodes. A type of #$TwoTerminalElectricalDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, #$DirectedCustomaryPath, and #$ElectricalComponent.  Each instance of #$Diode is a two-terminal electronic device that (by default) allows only a unidirectional current flow.")
(comment ElectrolyticCapacitor "A specialization of #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$ElectrolyticCapacitor is a capacitor that uses an ionic conducting fluid as a plate.")
(comment VariableCapacitor "A specialization of #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$VariableCapacitor is a capacitor whose capacitance can be controlled.")
(comment CapacitorTypeByPlateType "A second order collection.  Each instance of #$CapacitorTypeByPlateType is a specialization of #$Capacitor, instances of which all have in common that their plates are made of a particular type od substance.")
(comment PaperCapacitor "A specialization of #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$PaperCapacitor is a capacitor that uses treated paper plates.")
(comment GlassCapacitor "A specialization of #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$GlassCapacitor is a capacitor that uses glass plates.")
(disjointWith NonRechargeableBattery RechargeableBattery)
(comment BipolarJunctionTransistor "A specialization of #$Transistor.  Each instance of #$BipolarJunctionTransistor is a transistor with two junctions: a base/emitter junction and a base/collector junction.")
(comment TransistorTypeByStructure "A specialization of #$SecondOrderCollection. Each instance of this collection is a spec of #$Transistor, instances of which share notable structural features.")
(comment JunctionFET "A variety of #$FieldEffectTransistor.")
(comment SemiconductorStuff "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$SemiconductorStuff can, under varying electrical fields, behave as an electrical insulator at times and an electrical conductor at other times.  Critically, semiconducting sunstances can have impurities introduced into them (i.e. they can be \"doped\") to control their electronic properties.")
(comment HeterojunctionBipolarTransistor "A specialization of #$Transistor.  Each instance of #$BipolarJunctionTransistor is a variety of transistor that can handle higher signal frequencies than BJT transistors.")
(comment CRTDisplay "The collection of CRT displays.")
(comment VacuumTube "The collection of all vacuum tubes. A type of #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$VacuumTube is a device used to modify or create an electrical signal by controlling the flow of electrons in a near-vacuum.")
(comment CathodeRayTube "The collection of all cathode ray tubes. A type of #$VacuumTube.")
(comment LightBulb-Halogen "An incandescent bulb filled with halogen gas.")
(comment LightBulb-CompactFlourescent "A specialization of #$LightBulb-Flourescent.  Each instance of #$LightBulb-CompactFlourescent is a flourescent lamp designed to fit in a fixture in which normal incandescent bulbs can also fit.")
(comment Preamplifier "A collection of devices; a subset of   #$ElectronicComponent. Each instance of #$Preamplifier is a device used to prepare a signal for further processing.")
(comment Touchscreen "The collection of all touch screens. A type of #$ComputerDisplay and #$ComputerInputDevice.")
(comment ConsumerElectronicsTypeByFormFactor "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicsTypeByFormFactor is a collection of devices representing a particular form factor.  Each reified  specialization is a collection of these collections that represent a particular type of form (e.g. brick, bar, flip or swivel form).")
(comment ConsumerElectronicDevice-BarForm "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-BarForm is an electronic device whose form lacks any main joints that enable swivelling, sliding or bending (flipping), and is sleek and thin, like a candybar, unlike the bulkier instances of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-BrickForm (q.v.).")
(comment ConsumerElectronicDevice-BrickForm "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-BrickForm is an electronic device whose form lacks any main joints that enable swivelling, sliding or bending (flipping), and is very bulky (as compared to instances of  #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-BarForm (q.v.)).")
(comment ConsumerElectronicDevice-FlipForm "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-FlipForm is an electronic device whose form includes main joints that enables flipping it open and closed (as opposed to swivelling or sliding).")
(comment ConsumerElectronicDevice-SlideForm "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-SlideForm is an electronic device whose form includes a main joint that enables sliding it open and closed (as opposed to flipping or swivelling).")
(comment ConsumerElectronicDevice-SwivelForm "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-SlideForm is an electronic device whose form includes a main joint that enables swivelling it (as opposed to flipping or sliding it open and closed).")
(comment Cellphone-BarShaped "A specialization of #$CellularTelephone and #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-BarForm.  Each instance of #$Cellphone-BarShaped is a candybar-shaped cellphone.")
(comment Cellphone-FlipForm "A specialization of #$CellularTelephone and #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-FlipForm.  Each instance of #$Cellphone-FlipForm is a  cellphone that flips open and closed.")
(comment Cellphone-Slide "A specialization of #$CellularTelephone and #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-SlideForm.  Each instance of #$Cellphone-Slide is a  cellphone that slides open.")
(comment Cellphone-Swivel "A specialization of #$CellularTelephone and #$ConsumerElectronicDevice-SwivelForm.  Each instance of #$Cellphone-Swivel is a  cellphone that swivels open.")
(comment Touchscreen-Resistive "A specialization of #$Touchscreen.  Each instance of #$Touchscreen-Resistive is a touchscreen designed to respond to being compressed by touches.")
(comment Touchscreen-SurfaceAcousticWave "A specialization of #$Touchscreen.  Each instance of #$Touchscreen-SurfaceAcousticWave is a touchscreen designed to respond to interfernce with ultrasonic waves that pass over the surface of the touchscreen panels.")
(comment Touchscreen-Capacitive "A specialization of #$Touchscreen.  Each instance of #$Touchscreen-Capacitive is a touchscreen designed to respond to changes in the continuous electrical current across the sensor. These changes can be caused by proximity to an object (such as the human body) with stored electrons.")
(comment Touchpad "A computer input device that works by tracking motion from a touch-sensitive pad.  These devices commonly serve by default in the role of a mouse on laptop computers.")
(comment ARTMContinuousPhaseModulation "A specialization of #$ContinuousPhaseModulation.")
(comment hasAntennaWithDiameter "<code>(#$hasAntennaWithDiameter SYSTEM DIAM)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> has the diamter <code>DIAM</code>.")
(comment Smartphone "A specialization of #$CellularTelephone and #$PalmtopComputer.  Each instance of #$Smartphone is a cell phone that supports robust internet connectivity by, for example, enabling web browsing, chatting, or sending and receiving email.")
(comment CellularTelephone "A specialization of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice, #$WirelessCommunicationDevice and #$Telephone.  Each instance of #$CellularTelephone is a mobile telephone unit.")
(comment SemiconductorMemoryChip "The collection of all semiconductor memory chips. A type of #$ComputerStorageDevice and #$IntegratedCircuit. The concept #$SemiconductorMemoryChip is #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment CarSeat-Vinyl "The collection of all vinyl car seats. A type of #$AutomobileSeat. The concept #$CarSeat-Vinyl is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment PolyvinylChloride "The collection of all PVC. A type of #$Solid-StateOfMatter and #$ArtificialMaterial.")
(comment PVCPipe "Rigid tubing made of PVC (#$PolyvinylChloride).")
(comment CarSeat-Leather "The collection of all leather car seats. A type of #$AutomobileSeat. The concept #$CarSeat-Leather is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment CarSeat-Cloth "The collection of all cloth car seats. A type of #$AutomobileSeat. The concept #$CarSeat-Cloth is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment LeatherJacket "The collection of jackets made primarily of leather.")
(comment DenimCloth "The collection of all denim. A type of #$CottonCloth. The collection #$DenimCloth is a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.  Each instance of #$DenimCloth is a rugged cotten textile with a characteristic weave: the weft passes under multiple warp fibers.")
(comment ToiletSeat "A specialization of #$SeatingDevice.  Each instance of #$ToiletSeat is a seating device and lid that is for the top of a toilet bowl.")
(comment Oil "An instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType, and a specialization of #$OrganicMaterial.  Each instance of #$Oil is a portion of some type of typically viscous, primarily hydrophobic (i.e., <i>not</i> readily soluble in water) liquid hydrocarbon.  Notable specializations of #$Oil include #$CookingOil, #$HeatingOil, and #$Petroleum-CrudeOil.")
(comment FoodOrDrinkOrIngredient "The collection of all food, drink and ingredients. A type of #$EdibleStuff. #$FoodOrDrinkOrIngredient is an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment SecretPoliceOrganization "A specialization of #$NationalPoliceOrganization.  Each instance of #$SecretPoliceOrganization is a police agency that operates in secrecy against internal threats to the state.")
(comment NeonLamp "A bulb of glass or other transparent enclosing material filled with neon (or a high neon-content mixture) that fluoresces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(disjointWith GasDischargeLamp LightBulb-Incandescent)
(comment LightBulb-Flourescent "A bulb of glass or quartz enclosing material filled with mercury vapor that fluoresces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(comment GasDischargeLamp "A bulb of glass or quartz enclosing gaseous material that fluoresces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(comment SodiumVaporLamp "A bulb of glass or other transparent enclosing material filled with gaseous sodium that fluoresces when provided with current, thus generating light.")
(comment MeasurableQuantitySlotTypePredicate "A specialization of #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate. Each instance of #$MeasurableQuantitySlotTypePredicate is a binary predicate that is used to attribute a property to every instance of a thing by relating that type of thing to a #$MeasurableQuantity.")
(comment CeilingLight "The collection of all ceiling lights. A type of #$ElectricalLightingDevice. The concept #$WallLight is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Chandelier "The collection of all Cchandeliers. A type of #$ElectricalLightingDevice. The concept #$WallLight is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment TrackLighting "The collection of all track lighting fixtures. A type of #$ElectricalLightingDevice. The concept #$WallLight is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment RecessedLight "The collection of all recessed lights. A type of #$ElectricalLightingDevice. The concept #$WallLight is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Searchlight "A specialization of #$ElectricalLightingDevice .  The collection of all lighting device used to produce powerful beams of light to aid in search.")
(comment Nightlight "A subset of #$ElectricLamp.  The collection of all lamps that are placed in areas that become dark at night to be lit at those times for comfort or convenience.")
(comment SafetySwitch "A specialization of #$ElectricalSwitch.  Each instance of #$SafetySwitch is a switch designed to shut down a circuit for saftey purposes.")
(comment KillSwitch "A specialization of #$SafetySwitch.  Each instance of #$KillSwitch is a switch that is easily operated to deactivate a device in case of emergency.")
(comment DeadMansSwitch "A specialization of #$SafetySwitch.  Each instance of #$DeadMansSwitch is a switch that is automatically operated if the operator becomes incapacitated.")
(comment DimmingLightSwitch "Specifically the light switch found on the wall of a room. Not the one on lights and lamps themselves.")
(comment Attenuator "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instnace of #$Attenuator is an electronic device that is used to reduce the power or amplitude of a signal with minimal distortion of its waveform.")
(comment Thermistor "A type of #$Resistor. Each instance of #$Thermistor is a resistor whose resistance varies greatly with temperature.")
(comment Photoresistor "A type of #$Resistor. Each instance of #$Photoresistor is a resistor whose resistance varies greatly with illumination.")
(comment PrintedCircuitBoard "A specialization of #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$PrintedCircuitBoard is a board used to support and connect electronic components.  These devices are made of rigid and strong non-conductive material, with etched conductive pathways laminated onto them.")
(comment PrintedCircuitAssembly "A specialization of #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$PrintedCircuitAssembly is a #$PrintedCircuitBoard with installed electrical components.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralValveProlapse "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralValveProlapse is a murmur indicative of mitral valve prolapse.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithVSD "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithVSD is a murmur that is indicative of ventricular septal defect.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithTricuspidRegurgitation "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithTricuspidRegurgitation is a murmur that is indicative of tricuspid valve regurgitation or insufficiency.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralRegurgitation "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralRegurgitation is a murmur indicative of mitral valve regurgitation, and which starts at the closing of the mitral valve, at the same time as S1.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithAorticRegurgitation "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-Diastolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithAorticRegurgitation is a murmur indicative of aotic regurgitation.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithHOCM "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-MidSystolicEjection.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithHOCM is a murmur indicative of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralValveStenosis "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-MidDiastolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithMitralValveStenosis is a murmur indicative of mitral valve stenosis.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithAtrialSeptalDefect "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithAtrialSeptalDefect is a murmur that is indicative of atrial septal defect.")
(comment HeartMurmur-Benign "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-Benign is a murmur that is not deemed indicative of an underlying ailment (e.g. it may be explained by youth).")
(comment CardiacValveStenosis "The intersection of #$HeartValveDysfunction and #$Stenosis-Condition.  Each instance of #$CardiacValveStenosis is a stenosis of some cardiac valve.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithPulmonaryValveStenosis "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-Systolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithPulmonaryValveStenosis is a murmur that is indicative of pulmonary valve stenosis.")
(comment HeartMurmur-Pansystolic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-Pansystolic is a murmur that starts at S1 and extends up to S2.")
(comment ElectFn "<code>(#$ElectFn POSITION)</code> denotes the relation that holds between an individual and an organization when that individual who does not yet stand in the relation <code>POSITION</code> to that organization, has won an election to hold the position of <code>POSITION</code> in organization, prior to inauguration.")
(comment electVersionOfPosition "The corresponding predicate for #$ElectFn, <code>#$electVersionOfPosition PRED POSITION)</code> means that for any <code>AGENT</code> and <code>ORG</code>, <code>(PRED ORG AGENT)</code> holds just in case 1) <code>AGENT</code> is the winner of an election for the position <code>POSITION</code> in <code>ORG</code>, 2) <code>AGENT</code> has not been inaugurated, and 3) <code>AGENT</code> currently does not hold that position (so <code>(#$not (POSITION ORG AGENT))</code> holds).")
(comment CardiogenicShock "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$CardiogenicShock is a condition resulting from inadequate circulation of blood due to failure of the ventricles of the heart.")
(comment HypovolemicShock "A specialization of #$Shock-PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$HypovolemicShock is a shock condition resulting from insufficient circulating blood volume.")
(comment CongenitalHeartDisease "A specialization of #$CongenitalCondition and #$HeartCondition.  Each instance of #$CongenitalHeartDisease is a congenital disease of the heart.")
(comment CardiacVentricleWall "A specialization of #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$CardiacVentricleWall is a wall of a cardiac ventricle.")
(comment HeartMurmurConsistentWithAorticValveStenosis "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur-MidDiastolic.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmurConsistentWithAorticValveStenosis is a murmur indicative of aortic valve stenosis.")
(comment HeartMurmur-NonDiagnostic "A specialization of #$HeartMurmur.  Each instance of #$HeartMurmur-NonDiagnostic is a murmur that not diagnostic of a further specific ailment.")
(comment HeartSoundEmission "A specialization of #$SystemCondition and #$EmittingSound.  Each instance of #$HeartSoundEmission is a sound emitted by a heart.  Important specializations include the collection of heart murmurs (#$HeartMurmur) and the collections of the ordinary heart sounds, \"lub\" and \"dub\" (i.e. #$HeartSound-S1 and #$HeartSound-S2, respectively).")
(comment HeartSound-S4 "A specialization of #$HeartSoundEmission.  Each instance of #$HeartSound-S4 is a pathological emission of low-frequency heart sound that is generated under pathologic conditions during forceful atrial contraction.")
(comment HeartSound-S3 "A specialization of #$HeartSoundEmission.  Each instance of #$HeartSound-S3 is an emission of the third, pathological, heart sound.")
(comment HeartSound-S1 "A specialization of #$HeartSoundEmission.  Each instance of #$HeartSound-S1 is an emission of a heart sound that is commonly heard as \"lub\" (as opposed to \"dub\" (for which see #$HeartSound-S2)).")
(comment HeartSound-S2 "A specialization of #$HeartSoundEmission.  Each instance of #$HeartSound-S2 is an emission of a heart sound that is commonly heard as \"dub\" (as opposed to \"lub\" (for which see #$HeartSound-S1)).")
(disjointWith MedicalFinding MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment MedicalFindingFn "#$MedicalFindingFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction that takes as argument any instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType and returns the collection of all instances of     #$MedicalFinding that are medical findings of #$PhysiologicalConditions of that type.")
(comment eventHasDiagnosisOrFinding "(#$eventHasDiagnosisOrFinding EVT DIAG-OR-FINDING) means that the diagnosis or finding DIAG-OR-FINDING is a medical diagnosis or finding that occurred during the medical evaluation event EVT.")
(comment leaseStartDate "<code>(#$leaseStartDate LEASE DATE)</code> means that according to the agreement <code>LEASE</code>, the start date of the #$Leasing event associated with <code>LEASE</code> will be <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment leaseExpirationDate "<code>(#$leaseExpirationDate LEASE DATE)</code> means that according to the agreement <code>LEASE</code>, the expiration date of the #$Leasing event associated with <code>LEASE</code> will be <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment leaseSignDate "<code>(#$leaseSignDate LEASE DATE)</code> means that the signing date of the agreement <code>LEASE</code> is <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment LeaseAgreementTypeByTypeLeased "A second-order collection, each instance of which is a specilization of #$LeaseAgreement.  Each instance of #$LeaseAgreementTypeByTypeLeased is a collection of lease agreements for the same sort of thing (e.g., cars or real estate).")
(comment leaseTerm "<code>(#$leaseTerm LEASE DURATION)</code> means that according to the agreement <code>LEASE</code>, the term of the corresponding #$Leasing will be <code>INTERVAL</code>.")
(comment rangeOfScale "<code>(#$rangeOfScale SACLE RANGE)</code> means that the scale <code>SCALE</code> ranges over the values delineated by <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment AutomobileLeaseAgreement "A specialization of #$LeaseAgreement.  Each instance is a lease agreement that transfers temporary user rights of an automobile.")
(comment LeaseAgreement "A specialization of #$RentalAgreement.  Each instance of #$LeaseAgreement is a relatively long-term agreement between the owner of a property (the lessor) and a lessee who, according to the terms of the agreement, will have temporary user rights over the property.")
(comment ControlTower "The collection of control towers. Instances of #$ControlTower
house persons and equipment used to control the flow of air, rail, or
marine traffic.")
(comment broaderTerm-NonTaxonomic "(#$broaderTerm-NonTaxonomic NARROW BROAD) means that BROAD is broader than NARROW (in the sense of #$broaderTerm), and that there is a support for that claim other than that (#$generalizations NARROW BROAD), which may or may not hold.")
(comment recordsSignalOfType "<code>(#$recordsSignalOfType DEV SIGNAL-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> supports recording signals of type <code>SIGNAL-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CompactDiscPlayer "The collection of all compact disc players. A type of #$MediaPlayingDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$AudioEquipment. The collection #$CompactDiscPlayer is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment MediaPlayingDevice "The collection of all media players. A type of #$ConsumerElectronicDevice, #$MechanicalDevice, and #$ElectronicDevice. The collection #$MediaPlayingDevice is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Each instance of #$MediaPlayingDevice is a device that was designed to play media such as a DVD, photo slide, or digital audio file.")
(comment VaractorDiode "A specialization of #$Diode and #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$VaractorDiode is a diode that can be used as a voltage-controlled capacitor.")
(comment properPhysicalSubSystems "A specialization of #$properSubSystems and #$properPhysicalParts (qq.v.). <code>(#$properPhysicalSubSystems SUPER SUB)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> is a system that is part of the larger system, <code>SUPER</code>, can stand by itself, i.e. have independent existence from <code>SUPER</code> and still be more or less the same. Eg. the amp in a stereo system or the console of a computer. However, the handle of a cup would not typically be considered a subsystem.")
(comment FMTransmitter "A specialization of #$FMTransmitter.  Each instance of #$FMTransmitter is a radio transmitter that sends frequency modulated signals.")
(comment RadarTransmitter "A specialization of #$RadioTransmitter.  Each instance of #$RadarTransmitter is a radio transmitter that can function as the transmitter in a radar system.  It generates a radio signal with an oscillator such as a klystron or a magnetron and controls its duration by a modulator.")
(comment AMTransmitter "A specialization of #$RadioTransmitter.  Each instance of #$AMTransmitter is a radio transmitter that sends amplitude modulated signals.")
(comment HumanSpeechSound "A specialization of #$AnimalSound.  Each instance of #$HumanSpeechSound is a sound produced directly by a human in virtue of that human speaking.")
(comment TelemetryLink "A specialization of #$ElectroMagneticIBT.  Each instance of #$TelemetryLink is an EM trransmission containing telemetry data.")
(comment FMSignal "The collection of information bearing frequency-modulated radio transmissions.")
(comment AMSignal "The collection of information bearing amplitude-modulated radio transmissions.")
(comment PostDSignal "The collection of post-detection signals (i.e. telemetry links that have been demodulated).  Also known as baseband data.")
(comment PreDSignal "The collection of pre-detection signals (i.e. telemetry links that have not been demodulated, but which typically have been down-converted to a standard intermediate frequency).")
(comment Calais-TheWebService "A Web Service that takes English text and produces a semantic annotation in RDF format.")
(comment OpenCalais-TheWebService "A Web Service that takes English text and produces a semantic annotation in RDF format.")
(comment TheCalaisOntology "An ontology used by the Calais and OpenCalais programs to do text annotation.")
(comment holidayObserved "<code>(#$holidayObserved OBSERVING HOLIDAY)</code> means that <code>OBSERVING</code>, an instance of #$ObservingAHoliday, is an observation of the instance <code>HOLIDAY</code> of #$SpecifiedHolidayType.")
(disjointWith SpecifiedHolidayType HolidayTypeByReligion)
(comment SpecifiedHolidayType "A collection that facets #$Holiday by name and celebration criteria.  Instances include #$ChristmasHoliday and #$NewYearsDay but exclude specializations of #$Holiday whose membership criteria allows them to include holidays with different celebration criteria (e.g., #$ReligiousHoliday, subsumes both Christmas and Chanukka) or to exclude holiday instances with the same criteria (e.g., the collection of 'white' Christmases, Thanksgivings that occur during a leap year, etc.")
(comment GenericOWLOntology "An Example ontology term used for the example triple store mapping.")
(comment TripleStoreKS-Generic "A generic triple store representation.  In this example #$rdf-type is supported.  To hook this up to an actual SPARQL endpoing, edit the following assertions to specify the server address and relative access point and register the source using the SKSManager in the Tools section of the browser

<pre>
 
In Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)
(serverOfSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic \"servername.domain.top-level-domain\")

In Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)
(relativePathForAPIAccessToSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic \"path/sparql\")

In Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)
(portNumberForSKS TripleStoreKS-Generic 80)

Normally the port will be 80.

Add mappings to existing Cyc terms via assertions like these:

In Mt : (MappingMtFn TripleStoreKS-Generic)
(codeMapping
       (ReifiedMappingForPredFn rdf-type GenericOWLOntology) \"URI-STRING\" CYCL-TERM)

Or use SchemaObjectFn to wrap URIs you wish to use in your queries,

    (SchemaObjectFn
   (ReifiedMappingForPredFn rdf-type GenericOWLOntology)\"<URI-STRING>\")


</pre>")
(comment TelevisionSignal "A specialization of #$ElectroMagneticIBT.  Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal is an EM transmission that carries information which is intended to be decoded as a video image (either moving or still) or  audio sound by a television reception device.")
(comment TelevisionSignal-NTSCFormat "A specialization of #$TelevisionSignal.  Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal-NTSCFormat is video signal that conforms to the NTSC standard.")
(comment NTSC-TelevisionStandard "The National Television System Committee television broadcast system protocol.")
(comment TelevisionSignal-PALFormat "A specialization of TelevisionSignal. Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal-PALFormat is video signal that conforms to the Phase Alternating Line (PAL) standard.")
(comment PAL-TelevisionStandard "The Phase Alternating Line (PAL) television system protocol.")
(comment TelevisionSignal-Analog "A specialization of #$TelevisionSignal.  Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal-Analog is a signal which encodes video (and possibly audio) information via modulating wave frequency or amplitude.")
(comment VisualInformationRecordingDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$VisualInformationRecordingDevice is a device used for the recording of visual information.  So an instance would be your cam-corder (a #$VideoCamera) or your VCR (#$VideoCassetteRecorder).")
(comment CompactDisc-Generic "The collection of generic compact discs often (but not  necessarily) used for digital information storage, whether audio,  video or other.  Subcollections include #$CompactDisc-Audio,  #$CD-ROM, #$CD-R, #$CD-RW, etc..")
(comment OneInchMagneticTape "The collection of all 1-inch wide magnetic tape media. A type of #$MagneticTape.")
(comment writesToMediaType "<code>(#$writesToMediaType DEV MEDIA-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> writes to media of type <code>MEDIA-TYPE</code>.")
(comment readsFromMediaType "<code>(#$readsFromMediaType DEV MEDIA-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> reads from media of type <code>MEDIA-TYPE</code>.")
(comment PortableCDPlayer "The collection of all portable CD players. A type of #$CompactDiscPlayer and #$PersonalAudioPlayer. The collection #$PortableCDPlayer is a #$PersonalAudioPlayerByComponentType.")
(comment DVD-Disk "A specialization of #$DiscStorageMedium. Each #$DVD-Disk is a round, shiny disk similar in shape and appearance to a #$CompactDisc-Generic, but with a greater storage capacity (several gigabytes, depending on whether it is single- or double-sided and how many layers of information are encoded on each side). Due to their large storage capacity, #$DVD-Disks can be used used for distribution and playback of #$Movie-CWs and multimedia software too large for #$CD-ROMs, and for backup of computer #$HardDiskDrives.")
(comment AudioTapePlayer "The collection of all audio tape players. A type of #$MediaPlayingDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$AudioEquipment. The collection #$AudioTapePlayer is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment DVDWriter "A collection of devices that can read and write data  onto instances of #$DVD-Disk.")
(comment TelevisionSignal-Digital "A specialization of #$TelevisionSignal.  Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal-Analog is a signal which encodes video (and possibly audio) information via digital means.")
(comment TelevisionSignal-HDTVFormat "A specialization of #$TelevisionSignal-Digital.  Each instance of #$TelevisionSignal-HDTVFormat is video signal that conforms to a High Definition Television (HDTV) standard.")
(comment RFCombiner "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$RFCombiner is a device used for combining electromagnetic radio frequency signals.")
(comment AudioTapePlayer-Recorder "The collection of all tape recorders. A type of #$AudioTapePlayer, #$InformationRecordingDevice, and #$BusinessMachine.  Each instance of #$AudioTapePlayer-Recorder is a device that can play and record information on magnetic audio tapes.")
(comment RecordHead "A specialization of #$Transducer.  Each instance of #$RecordHead is a component of a tape recorder that touches the magnetic tape that is being written to by the device.")
(comment ElectronicFilter "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$ElectronicFilter is a device used for removing unwanted signal components or enhancing desired signal components.")
(comment SignalFiltering "Each instance of #$SignalFiltering is an event in which  EM signals have aspects removed or enhanced.")
(comment CalaisOntologyEntityType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections that are classified as classes of \"entities\" in the Calais ontology.  See #$TheCalaisOntology.")
(comment AwardsCeremonyTypeByIndustry "A collection that facets #$AwardsCeremony into subcollections whose instances are award ceremonies celebrating accomplishments in a particular type of industry.")
(disjointWith AwardsCeremonyTypeByIndustry AwardsCeremonyTypeByAwardType)
(comment AwardsCeremonyTypeByAwardType "A collection that facets #$AwardsCeremony into subcollections based on the award.")
(comment AntoinettePerryAwardForExcellenceInTheater "The collection of all Tony awards, granted jointly by the Broadway League and the American Theatre Wing, recognizing excellence in American theater.")
(comment EntertainmentIndustryAwardsCeremony "An instance of #$AwardsCeremonyTypeByIndustry, this is the collection of instances of #$AwardsCeremony that recognize achievements in the entertainment industry.")
(comment AthleticAwardTypeBySport "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$AthleticAward by sport.")
(comment HeismanAward "The Heisman, the most prestigious award in college football, awarded by the Downtown Athletic Club in New York City at the end of each college football season to the best player in football.")
(comment awardSignifiesAchievementInSport "<code>(#$awardSignifiesAchievementInSport AWARD SPORT)</code> means that the instance <code>AWARD</code> of #$AthleticAward signifies an achievment in the sport <code>SPORT</code>.")
(disjointWith IndividualAccolade TeamAccolade)
(comment AmericanStyleFootballAward "The collection of awards that recognize achievement in American football.")
(comment CollegeFootballAward "The collection of awards that recognize achievement in college football.")
(comment HeismanTrophyAwardCeremony "The collection of Heisman Award ceremonies, held once every year at the end of the college football season.")
(comment MVPAward "A specializaton of #$IndividualAccolade, an instance of #$MVPAward is a \"most valuable player\" award given to an individual who is considered to have excelled in some respect beyond all others from a common pool of candidates where, by convention, that pool is typically defined as one of the following: a team or some other organized group who have been working towards a common cause; a league or other organization whose members are teams or organizations operating in competition with one another; or all individuals, regardless of any sort of team affiliation, who have been performing competitvely in some well-defined activity or series of activities.  The notion of a \"most valuable player\" has its origins in sports, but is commonly used outside of that arena.")
(disjointWith TeamMVPAward EventMVPAward)
(disjointWith LeagueMVPAward EventMVPAward)
(disjointWith TeamMVPAward LeagueMVPAward)
(comment SportSeason "The collection of all sports seasons.  Each sports season is specific to a single sport and is an organized event consisting largely of game-performances of that sport.  A single season may subsume (via #$properSubEvents) multiple seasons of the same sport.  For example, the 2010 college football season subsumes the 2010 Big Twelve college football season.")
(comment FootballSeason "The collection of all instances of #$SportSeason where the #$seasonFocalSport is #$Football-American.")
(comment CollegeFootballSeason "The collection of all college football seasons.")
(comment SportsSeasonTypeByFocalSport "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$SportSeason into collections of seasons with a common sport.")
(comment mvpAwardForEvent "<code>(#$mvpAwardForEvent AWARD EVENT)</code> measn that the instance <code>AWARD</code> of #$EventMVPAward is awarded to the \"most valuable player\" of the instance <code>EVENT</code> of #$Event-Organized.")
(comment mvpAwardForTeam "<code>(#$mvpAwardForTeam AWARD ORG)</code> means that the instance <code>AWARD</code> of #$TeamMVPAward is awarded to the \"most valuable player\" belonging to an organization <code>ORG</code> whose members were in <i>de facto</i> competition for the award by virtue of how well they contributed to a particular common goal.")
(comment mvpAwardForLeague "<code>(#$mvpAwardForLeague AWARD ORG)</code> means that the instance <code>AWARD</code> of #$LeagueMVPAward is awarded to the \"most valuable player\" in an organization <code>ORG</code>, where the recipient is not a member of <code>ORG</code> <i>per se</i>, but to an organization <code>ORG-MEMBER</code> that is a member of <code>ORG</code> that was in competition with other member-organizations of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment TeamMVPAward "The collection of all instances of #$MVPAward that are awarded to the member of an organization for in recognition of making the most valuable contributions to the goals of that organization.")
(comment EventMVPAward "The collection of all instances of #$MVPAward that are awarded to the best performer in some organized event.")
(comment LeagueMVPAward "The collection of all instances of #$MVPAward that are given to an individual belonging to one of a number of competing organizations, in recognition that the recipient has contributed to his own organizations goals at a level that surpasses any other individual's contributions to that persons respective organization.")
(comment IndividualAccolade "The collection of instances of #$AwardPractice that are by design awarded to an #$IndividualAgent rather than to an organization.")
(comment TeamAccolade "The collection of instances of #$AwardPractice that are by design awarded to an organization rather than an individual.")
(comment seasonFocalSport "<code>(#$seasonFocalSport SEASON SPORT)</code> means that <code>SEASON</code> is a sports season in which teams or individuals are organized to compete in instantiations of <code>SPORT</code>, an instance of #$Sport.")
(comment AmericanMusicAwardsCeremony "The collection of annually held awards ceremonies at which the American Music Awards are bestowed.")
(comment GrammyAwardsCeremony "The collection of annually held awards ceremonies at which Grammy awards are bestowed.")
(comment TonyAwardsCeremony "The collection of annually held awards ceremonies at which various Antoinette Perry Awards for Excellence in Theater are bestowed,")
(comment NickelodeonKidsChoiceAwardsCeremony "A subcollection of #$EntertainmentIndustryAwardsCeremony.  The Nickelodeon Kids Choice Awards Ceremony is an annually held event sponsored by the Nickelodeon kids television channel, and awards entertainment figures for various achievements, as voted on by their viewers.")
(comment TeenChoiceAwardsCeremony "A subcollection of #$EntertainmentIndustryAwardsCeremony.  The Teen Choice Awards Ceremony is held annually by the FOX network and honors entertainment figures for achievements in various categories as voted on by FOX viewers aged 13 to 19.")
(comment MTVVideoMusicAwardsCeremony "A subcollection of #$EntertainmentIndustryAwardsCeremony.  The MTV Video Music Awards are held annually by MTV (see #$MTV-TVNetwork) and honors entertainers for achievements across various categories.")
(comment FilmIndustryAwardsCeremony "The collection of instances of #$AwardsCeremony designed to celebrate achievements in film-making.")
(comment MusicIndustryAwardsCeremony "The collection of instances of #$AwardsCeremony designed to celebrate achievements in the music industry.")
(comment CountryMusicAssociationAwardsCeremony "A specialization of #$MusicIndustryAwardsCeremony, the Country Music Association Awards ceremony is an annual event in which the Country Music Association honors achievements by American country music artists.")
(comment EmmyAwardsCeremony "An annually held specialization of #$TelevisionIndustryAwardsCeremony that celebrates achievements in American television broadcasting.")
(comment TelevisionIndustryAwardsCeremony "The collection of instances of #$AwardsCeremony designed to celebrate achievements in the area of television broadcasting.")
(comment AwardTypeByAwardingAgent "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$AwardPractice by the agent (or agents) who bestow the award.")
(comment HeismanTrophy "The collection of instances of #$Trophy that are ceremoniously presented each year to the winner of the #$HeismanAward.  A second trophy is also given to the school that the winner represents.")
(comment relationAllExistsUnique "(#$relationAllExistsUnique PRED COL1 COL2) means that, for each instance INS1 of COL1, there is exactly one instance INS2 of COL2 such that (PRED INS1 INS2) holds.  Thus it is equivalent to (#$relationAllExistsCount PRED COL1 COL2 1).")
(comment BasketballSeason "The collection of all basketball seasons.")
(comment SignalProcessing "Each instnce of #$SignalProcessing is an act of processing a signal (e.g., via filtering it, modulating it or combining it with another signal).")
(comment RFSignalCombining "A specialization of #$SignalProcessing. Each instance of #$SignalMultiplexing is an event in which multiple EM signals are combined into a single signal.")
(comment CeramicCapacitor "A specialization of #$Capacitor.  Each instance of #$CeramicCapacitor is a capacitor that uses ceramic plates.")
(comment Bug-InformationGatheringDevice "#$Bug-InformationGatheringDevice is a specialization#$InformationGatheringDevice.  Instances of #$Bug-InformationGatheringDevice are devices with microphones that are typically used for espionage by instances of the collection #$Spy.")
(comment TelephoneWire "The collection of all telephone wire. A type of #$Path-InfoTransfer, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$MultiConductorInsulatedWire.")
(comment Path-InfoTransfer "The collection of all instances of #$Path-Customary intended primarily to serve as communications channels.  Instances of #$Path-InfoTransfer are intended to serve the purpose of allowing the transfer of information, i.e. for being  a #$deviceUsed and an #$infoPathway-Partial in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent  (though this does notpreclude them from being used for other purposes).  Examples include instances of #$FiberOpticCable, #$TelephoneWire, etc.  Generally, instances of, say, #$Highway or #$Railway would not be examples, since, even though one could transfer information along an instance of, say, #$Railway, these are not intended primarily for this purpose.")
(comment CommunicationChannel "A heterogeneous collection that is a specialization of #$Technology-Artifact.  Each instance of #$CommunicationChannel is medium used to convey information.  Instances of this collection range from computer cables and telephone wires to designated ranges of electromagnetic frequencies.")
(comment TelevisionChannel "A specialization of #$RFChannel.  Each instance of #$TelevisionChannel is a range of radio frequencies designated as a specific television channel.")
(comment RFChannel "A specialization of #$Spectrum and #$CommunicationChannel.  Each instance of #$RFChannel is a range of radio frequencies designated as a specific communication channel.  An important specialization is #$TelevisionChannel.")
(comment NickelCadmiumBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery .  Each instance of #$NickelCadmiumBattery is a rechargeable battery made with nickel oxide hydroxide and metallic cadmium.")
(comment LithiumIonBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$NickelCadmiumBattery is a rechargeable battery made with lithium.")
(comment LeadAcidBattery "The collection of all lead-acid batteries. A type of #$Battery and #$ManufacturedGoods.")
(comment NickelHydrogenBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery .  Each instance of #$NickelCadmiumBattery is a rechargeable battery made with nickel and hydrogen.")
(comment SilverOxideBattery "A specialization of #$Battery.  Each instance of #$SilverOxideBattery is a battery made using silver.")
(comment AlkalineBattery "The collection of all alkaline batteries.")
(comment BatteryTypeByStandardSize "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$BatteryTypeByStandardSize is a collection of batteries whose instances are all share a standard size.")
(comment BatteryTypeByConstituentType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$BatteryTypeByConstituentType is a collection of batteries whose instances are all share a common set of significant constituents.")
(comment PP3Battery "The collection of all PP3 (a.k.a. \"9-volt\") batteries.  PP3 batteries are rectangular batteries with snap connectors.")
(comment DCellBattery "The collection of all D cell batteries.")
(comment CCellBattery "The collection of all C cell batteries.")
(comment AAABattery "The collection of all AAA batteries.")
(comment AABattery "The collection of all AA batteries.")
(comment ButtonCell "The collection of all button cells.")
(comment IndianNationalAgency "The collection of all Indian national government agencies. A type of #$GovernmentAgency.")
(comment IssuingAWritOfCertiori "The collection of all issuings of instances of #$WritOfCertiori-LegalDocument by the #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt in connection with an appeal of a #$CourtCase.")
(comment SpaceAgency "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$SpaceAgency is either a public (government or international) space agency or a private space agency.")
(comment primarySpaceport "(#$primarySpaceport AGENCY PORT) means that PORT is the primary spaceport of AGENCY.")
(comment PublicSectorSpaceAgency "The collection of all government or intergovernmental space agencies.")
(comment RangeInstrumentationSystemSubsystem "The collection of immediate subsystems of range systems. See #$rangeSystemImmediateSubSystems.")
(comment rangeSystemImmediateSubSystems "<code>(#$rangeSystemImmediateSubSystems SYSTEM SUB)</code> means that <code>SUB</code> is an immediate subsystem of the range system <code>SYSTEM</code>.")
(comment typeHasProductNumber "<code>(#$typeHasProductNumber TYPE NUMBER)</code> means that the model number of <code>TYPE</code> is <code>NUMBER</code>.")
(comment typeHasModelNumber "<code>(#$ typeHasModelNumberTYPE NUMBER)</code> means that the model number of <code>TYPE</code> is <code>NUMBER</code>.")
(comment AnniversaryCommemoration "An instance of #$AnnualEventType and specialization of #$Commemoration, #$AnniversaryCommemoration is the collection of all commemoration events that are observances of the anniversary of some event.")
(comment eventCommemorated "<code>(#$eventCommemorated COMMEMORATION EVENT)</code> identifies <code>EVENT</code> as the event commemmorated in <code>COMMEMORATION</code>, an instance of #$Commemoration.")
(comment administersNetwork "(#$administersNetwork ADMIN NET) means that the #$SystemAdministrator ADMIN administers the #$ComputerNetwork NET.")
(comment dBPediaOntologyName "<code>(#$dBPediaOntologyName THING NAME)</code> means that DBPedia string <code>NAME</code> denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment GlansPenis "The collection of all glandes penis.  An individual member of this collection is the tip of a #$Penis, which is covered by the #$Foreskin (prepuce) in an uncircumcised male.")
(comment DBPediaOntologyMappingMt "The microtheory designed to contain mappings of terms from the DBPedia ontology into Cyc.")
(comment LymphVessel "The collection of all #$AnatomicalVessels which transport #$Lymph in the body of a chordate [#$ChordataPhylum].")
(comment FilmFestival "A specialization of #$Festival.  Each instance of #$FilmFestival is a festival organized to honor or enjoy films, typically by playing them in one or more movie theaters over the course of one or more days.")
(comment MusicFestival "A specialization of #$Festival.  Each instance of #$MusicFestival is a festival organized to honor or enjoy music, typically by having multiple musical performances in one or more venues over the course of one or more days.")
(comment MixedMartialArtsEvent "The collection of all sports events in which two #$competingAgents fight using a variety of techniques from traditional martial arts fighting styles.")
(comment WomensTennisAssociationTournament "The collection of all women's tennis association tournaments.")
(comment BrainRegionType "A specialization of #$OrganSubPartType.  Each instance of #$BrainRegionType is a collection of significant brain regions.")
(comment AthletePlayerTypeOfSportFn "<code>(#$AthletePlayerTypeOfSportFn SPORT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of atheletes in the sport <code>SPORT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment athletePlayerTypeOfSport "<code>(#$athletePlayerTypeOfSport SPORT-TYPE ATHLETE-TYPE)</code> means <code>ATHLETE-TYPE</code> is the the collection of atheletes in the sport <code>SPORT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Cyclist-Athlete "A specialization of #$Athlete.  Each instance of #$Cyclist is an athlete who participates in bicycle races.")
(comment NCAAProgram "The collection of all NCAA teams. A type of #$CollegeSportsTeam.  Important specializations include the collections of teams based on the NCAA divisions (such as NCAA Division 1).")
(comment hasCardinalityManyDeviceTypeComponents "<code>(#$hasCardinalityManyDeviceTypeComponents SYSTEM NUMBER DEVICE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>NUMBER</code> many instances of <code>DEVICE-TYPE</code> are components of <code>SYSTEM</code>.")
(comment CollegeCoach "The collection of all college coaches. A type of #$SportsCoach, instances of which are employed by colleges or universities.")
(comment ComicsCharacter "The collection of all comics characters. A type of #$FictionalCharacter.")
(comment UNESCOWorldHertitageSite "A specialization of both #$GeographicalThing and #$HistoricTemporalThing.  Each instance of #$UNESCOWorldHertitageSite is a place that is on the list maintained by the international World Heritage Programme administered by the UNESCO World Heritage Committee.")
(comment WebSite "A subset of #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Each instance of #$WebSite is composed of a homepage and zero or more additional instances of #$WebPage-CW connected by hyperlinks to the site's homepage.  A #$WebSite is maintained by a single webmaster or group of webmasters, and is thematically unified in some way, on a single computer, an intranet or on the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource (in which case the more specific term, #$WorldWideWebSite, should be used.  A #$WebSite is normally designed with the intention that a visitor will enter the site via its homepage, and navigate to other pages in the site via hyperlinks.")
(comment CalaisOntologyEventOrFactType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections that are classified as classes of \"entities\" in the Calais ontology.  See #$TheCalaisOntology.")
(comment CalaisOntologyEventOrFactType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections that are classified as classes of \"events\" or \"facts\" in the Calais ontology.  See #$TheCalaisOntology.")
(comment CalaisOntologyResponseType "#$CalaisOntologyResponseType is the collection of classes in the Calais ontology (see #$TheCalaisOntology) used by the Calais text annotation program to type the objects referred to in the input text.")
(comment VascularCatheterization "A specialization of #$Catheterization.  Each instance of #$VascularCatheterization is a procedure used to obtain access to blood vessels with catheters.")
(comment CardiacCatheterization "A specialization of #$VascularCatheterization.  Each instance of #$CardiacCatheterization is a catheterization that involves sending a catheter for diagnostic or interventional reason into the heart or a coronary artery.")
(comment BankruptcyProceeding "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$BankruptcyProceeding is a proceeding in a court to relieve certain debts of a person or business unable to pay its debts.  The proceeding may be initiated either by the debtor or the creditor.")
(comment StockTypeByClass "The collection of classes of stock.  When a stock (i.e., an instance of #$StockTypeByIssuer) is divided into classes, those classes distinguish different levels of voting rights for shareholders.")
(disjointWith StockTypeByIssuer StockTypeByIssuerAndClass)
(disjointWith StockTypeByClass StockTypeByIssuerAndClass)
(disjointWith StockTypeByIssuer StockTypeByClass)
(comment StockTypeByIssuerAndClass "A collection of collections.  An instance of #$StockTypeByIssuerAndClass is a collection of all shares of stock of a particular type in a particular corporation.  For example, ``General Motors Class E Stock''.")
(comment StockTypeByIssuer "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$Stock into subcollections based on the corporation who issues them. (See #$corporationStockType.)")
(comment ClassAStock "The collection of all shares of stock that have been designated as \"class A\" by their issuer.")
(comment ClassBStock "The collection of all shares of stock that have been designated as \"class B\" by their issuer.")
(comment primaryCauseOfDeathEvent "<code>(#$primaryCauseOfDeathEvent DYING CAUSE-SIT-TYPE)</code> means that some instance of <code>CAUSE-SIT-TYPE</code> is the primary cause of the death event <code>DYING</code>.")
(comment HawaiianPizza "A specialization of #$Pizza.  Each instance of #$Pizza-NewYorkStyle is a pizza with at least ham and pineapple as its ingredients.")
(comment ResourceWithURIFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction. Given an RDF  #$UniformResourceIdentifier as its single argument, #$ResourceWithURIFn returns the corresponding resource.")
(comment LeftVentricularSectionType "A type-level collection.  Each instance is one of the canonical classes of left ventricular wall section used in characterizing ventricular wall motion as measured by means of an echocardiogram.")
(comment MutualFundShareTypeByClass "The collection of classes of mutual fund shares.  When a mutual fund is divided into classes, those classes typically distinguish the load (sales fee) size and schedule assessed against holders of those shares.")
(comment LoadedMutualFundShare "The collection of mutual fund shares that are associated with a load, or sales fee.")
(comment shareTypeClassDesignator "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate that relates a collection of stocks or mutual fund shares (either an instance of #$StockTypeByClass or #$MutualFundShareTypeByClass) to the symbol used to identify it as that class.")
(comment RDFSchemaDatatype "#$RDFSchemaDatatype is the collection of datatypes used in RDF.")
(comment sourceInformationEnabled "(#$sourceInformationEnabled SPECIFICATION BOOLEAN) means that in the CAE specification SPECIFICATION, a CAE using SPECIFICATION should attempt to show source information for inference answers (or individual supports of inference answers) iff BOOLEAN is #$True.")
(comment inferenceAnswerCount "<code>(#$inferenceAnswerCount INFERENCE N)</code> means that <code>INFERENCE</code> has <code>N</code> sets of bindings.")
(comment FictionalFn "<code>(#$FictionalFn REAL-COLLECTION)</code> denotes a collection that is a specialization of #$FictionalThing.  Instances of <code>(#$FictionalFn REAL-COLLECTION)</code> are fictional versions of instances of <code>REAL-COLLECTION</code>.  Thus (#$FictionalFn #$Mammal)  denotes the colleciton of fictional mammals.
<p>
For any two collections <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>, if it is true that <code>(#$genls A B)</code>, it will also be true that <code>(#$genls (#$FictionalFn A) (#$FictionalFn B))</code>")
(comment fictionalVersionOfType "<code>(#$fictionalVersionOfType X Y)</code> means that <code>Y</code> is the collection of fictioonal <code>X</code>s.")
(comment Amazon-Warrior "#$Amazon-Warriors (the Amazons) were each one of a nation of #$FemaleHuman warriors of ancient Scythia who burned off the right #$Breast in order to use a #$Bow-Weapon and #$Arrow more effectively.  Female warriors in any nation are sometimes called 'amazons'.  (The word 'amazon' has also become a nick-name for #$BigBeautifulWoman in the 1990's.)")
(comment IrrationalNumber "The collection of all irrational numbers. A type of #$RealNumber. The collection #$IrrationalNumber is a #$MeasurableScalarIntervalType.")
(comment Hypnotherapy "The collection of all #$ServiceEvents where disease is treated with hypnosis.")
(comment Wine "The collection of all wine. A type of #$AlcoholicBeverage. The collection #$Wine is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and an #$ExistingStuffType.  Each instance of #$Wine is a portion of the alcoholic beverage produced by fermenting crushed grapes.")
(comment Set-Extensional "A specialization of #$CycLTerm; the collection of extensionally defined sets.  Each quoted instance of #$Set-Extensional is such that it has been extensionally defined in the the Cyc knowledge base through the use of a function such as #$TheSet, #$ThePartition, or #$TheCovering.")
(comment List-Extensional "A specialization of #$CycLTerm; the collection of extensionally defined lists. Each quoted instance of #$List-Extensional is such that it has been extensionally defined in the the Cyc knowledge base through the use of a function such as #$TheList.")
(comment ProductTypeByBrand "A collection of collections.  Elements of #$ProductTypeByBrand are collections of products distinguished not only by being of the same generic ProductType, but also by sharing the same brand name.  Examples include MicrosoftOperatingSystem, and JosephSchmidtChocolates. For versions of product brands, see the spec #$ProductTypeByBrandVersion.")
(comment soleProviderOfSupportForProductType "A binary predicate used to identify the unique organization that makes a specific type of product.  (#$soleProviderOfSupportForProductType PRODTYPE ORG) means that the #$Organization ORG is the sole provider of technical support for instances of the #$ProductType PRODTYP.")
(comment soleMakerOrSupporterOfProductType "A binary predicate used to identify the unique organization that makes a specific type of product, or provides tech support for a specific type of product.  (#$soleMakerOrSupporterOfProductType PRODTYPE ORG) means that the #$Organization ORG is the sole maker or supporter of the #$ProductType PRODTYP.")
(comment FermentedStuff "The collection of all fermented stuff. A type of #$EdibleStuff.  Each instance of #$FermentedStuff is some substance prepared via fermentation, resulting in the presence of alcohol or acids within it.")
(comment FermentedFood "A specialization of #$Food and #$FermentedStuff. Each instance of FermentedFood is a food that is a fermented stuff.")
(comment FermentedBeverage "A specialization of #$Drink and #$FermentedStuff. Each instance of #$FermentedBeverage is a drink that is a fermented stuff.")
(comment fermentedFormOfType "(#$fermentedFormOfType STUFF-TYPE FERMENTED-TYPE) menas that FERMENTED-TYPE is the collection of fermented instances of STUFF-TYPE.")
(comment FermentedFn "(#$FermentedFn STUFF-TYPE) denotes the collection of fermented instances of STUFF-TYPE.")
(comment Mead "The collection of all mead, which is an alcoholic beverage made by fermenting honey.")
(comment RedGrapeVine "The collection of all grapevines that produce red grapes.")
(comment WhiteGrapeVine "The collection of all grapevines that produce white grapes.")
(comment WineVinegar "The collection of all wine vinegar. The collection #$WineVinegar is a DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment RedWineVinegar "The collection of all red wine vinegar. The collection #$RedWineVinegar is a DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment BalsamicVinegar "The collection of all balsmaic vinegar. The collection #$BalsamicVinegar is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment WhiteWineVinegar "The collection of all white wine vinegar. The collection #$WhiteWineVinegar is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.")
(comment conceptPotentiallyInterestingToForDomainBecause "(#$conceptPotentiallyInterestingToForDomainBecause AGENT CONCEPT DOMAIN REASON) means that AGENT may be interested in CONCEPT in the topic DOMAIN because of REASON.")
(comment NASASpaceMission "A specialization of #$SpaceMission.  Each instance of #$NASASpaceMission is a mission into space directed by #$NASA.")
(comment ApolloSpaceMission "A specialization of #$NASASpaceMission.  Each instance of #$ApolloSpaceMission is a mission that was part of the Apollo program.")
(comment Apollo11SpaceMission "The Apollo 11 mission to the moon.")
(comment DBPediaOntology "An instance of #$Ontology.  The DBPedia ontology is an OWL ontology that contains concepts and relations pertienent to describing the content of Wikipedia.")
(comment MedicalProcedure-Therapeutic "The collection of all #$MedicalProcedures performed for the purpose of treating some #$AilmentCondition, or at least ameliorating its symptoms.")
(comment subjectOfDiagnosis "(#$subjectOfDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS ORGANISM) means that it is the system and internal function of ORGANISM that is the subject of the judgment formed in the #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding DIAGNOSIS.")
(comment evaluationCorrectness "(#$evaluationCorrectness EVALUATION TRUTH-VALUE) means that the sentence which expresses the judgment or evaluation arrived at in the #$Evaluating event EVALUATION has the #$TruthValue TRUTH-VALUE.")
(comment GeminiSpaceMission "A specialization of #$NASASpaceMission.  Each instance of #$GeminiSpaceMission is a mission that was part of the Gemini program.")
(comment astronautOfMission "<code>(#$astronautOfMission MISSION AST)</code> means that one of the astronauts on the #$SpaceMission <code>MISSION</code> was <code>AST</code>.")
(comment MedicalProcedure-Diagnostic "The collection of all #$MedicalProcedures whose purpose is to produce at least one (and possibly more than one) #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding.")
(comment patientHasHistory "Relates a patient to a \"history\" node that may contain various nodes used to specify various boolean checks to see whether the patient had a history of certain types of conditions or activities.  A typical way in which this might be  used is is:  PATIENT has the history HISTORY, HISTORY is associated with a #$FamilyHistoryOfCoronaryArteryDisease node which has the boolean value for #$familyHistoryOfDiseaseStatus #$True.")
(comment IntegratedDBPediaProperty "The collection of terms that denote properties in DBPedia and that have been connected to other core Cyc terms via rules (to a reasonably adequate extent).")
(comment DBPediaOWLClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection that corresponds to one of the classes in the DBPedia ontology.")
(comment laterThanOrCooriginatingWith "(#$laterThanOrCooriginatingWith  DATE1 DATE2) means that the CycL date DATE1 starts no earlier than the CycL date DATE2.  This is currently defined in terms of laterThan with a one second granularity -- DATE1 is strictly later than the date that is one second before DATE2.")
(disjointWith CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval)
(comment DBPediaOWLProperty "The collection of binary predicates that correspond to the DBPedia OWL properties.")
(comment DBPediaOWLPropertyTypeByArg2Isa "A faceting collection for #$DBPediaOWLProperty.  Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$DBPediaOWLProperty with a specific notable #$arg2Isa constraint.")
(comment DBPediaOWLPropertyAutoGeneratedLS "A specialization of #$DBPediaOWLProperty (q.v.).  Each instance of this collection is a DBPedia OWL property for which we want a logical schema automatically generated.")
(comment DBPediaOWLInstance "The collection of Skolemized entities that are the subjects and members of the DBPedia OWL classes in the DBPedia triple store.")
(comment MixedDrink "A specialization of #$AlcoholicBeverage.  Each instance of #$MixedDrink is itself a mixture of an #$AlcoholicBeverages, a #$FlavoringCompound and often a #$Juice. Important specializations include #$CocktailDrink and #$Highball.")
(comment Screwdriver-Drink "The collection of all screwdrivers, which are highballs made with vodka and orange juice.")
(comment Highball "The collection of highball drinks, which are bevarage prepared with a base alcoholic spirit along with another beverage.  Unlike other cocktails, highballs are served during the daytime.")
(comment FuzzyNavel "The collection of all fuzy navels, which are highballs made with peach schnapps and orange juice.")
(comment PeachSchnapps "The collection of all peach schnapps. A type of #$Schnapps. Peach schnapps is an alcoholic beverage produced by flavoring a neutral grain spirit like peaches.")
(comment ButterscotchSchnapps "The collection of all peach schnapps. A type of #$Schnapps. Peach schnapps is an alcoholic beverage produced by flavoring a neutral grain spirit like butterscotch.")
(comment Mezcal "A hard liquor from #$Mexico")
(comment Schnapps "The collection of all schnapps. A type of #$Liqueur. Schnapps is an alcoholic beverage produced by flavoring a neutral grain spirit.")
(comment Liqueur "The collection of all liqueur. A type of #$Liquor-Drink. Liqueur is an alcoholic beverage with a high sugar content.")
(comment CoffeeLiqueur "The collection of all coffee liqueur. A type of #$Liqueur.")
(comment textualPCWSubSectionOfTypeWithID "<code>(#$textualPCWSubSectionOfTypeWithID SUBSECTION PCW PCW-TYPE ID)</code> identifies <code>SUBSECTION</code> as the  instance of <code>PCW-TYPE</code> that is a #$textualPCWSubSections of the #$TextualPCW <code>PCW</code>, distinguished from--and ordered among--other sub-sections of that type by virtue of the ID string <code>ID-STRING</code>.  This is the corresponding predicate to the function #$TextualPCWSubSectionOfTypeWithIDFn.")
(comment dBPediaResourceName "<code>(#$dBPediaResourceName THING NAME)</code> means that DBPedia string <code>NAME</code> denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment rivalsWRT "(#$rivalsWRT EVENT-TYPE AGENT1 AGENT2) means that in events of type EVENT-TYPE, AGENT1 and AGENT2 are especially motivated to outdo one another.")
(comment nand "The #$LogicalConnective that represents the NAND operator in #$CycL. (#$nand P Q) is equivalent to (#$not (#$and P Q)).")
(comment nor "The #$LogicalConnective that represents the NOR operator in #$CycL. (#$nor P Q) is equivalent to (#$not (#$or P Q)).")
(comment DMSDegreeToDecimalDegreeFn "A function which converts an #$AngularDistance expressed in 'degree-minute-second' format (see #$CycLDegreeMinuteSecondTerm) into an equivalent #$AngularDistance expressed in 'decimal-degrees' format (see #$CycLDecimalDegreeTerm).")
(comment Mausoleum "The collection of all mausolea.  Each instance of #$Mausoleum is a free-standing building enclosing one or more tombs.")
(comment DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToAngularDistance "Each instance of  #$DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToAngularDistance is a binary relation that corresponds to a DBPedia OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of #$AngularDistance.")
(comment correspondsWithScopingFunction "A predicate relating scalar instances of #$DegreeOfAcuteness-AilmentCondition to corresponding #$SubcollectionDenotingFunctions used to facet specializations of #$AilmentCondition by degree-of-severity.")
(comment movieActors-WithStarringRole "A binary predicate that relates a given #$Movie-CW to an agent who played a starring role in that movie.  <code>(#$movieActors-WithStarringRole MOVIE ACTOR)</code> means that <code>ACTOR</code> played a starring role in <code>MOVIE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$movieActors-WithStarringRole #$CitizenKane-TheMovie #$OrsonWelles)</code> holds.")
(comment subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique "(#$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique PROCEDURE ORGANISM) means that the #$Organism-Whole ORGANISM is the one and only subject on which PROCEDURE is performed, either for diagnostic or therapeutic purposes.")
(comment ElephantTrunkProcedure-Entire "The collection of all end-to-end #$ElephantTrunkProcedure aortic replacement surgeries subsuming an instance of ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage1-SurgicalProcedure and an instance of #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 as subsituations, in that order.  In an #$ElephantTrunkProcedure-Entire, a surgical incision is first used to replace the aortic valve, the ascending aorta, and the aortic arch, and a dacron tube, the 'elephant trunk', is grafted to the descending aorta and the aorta is wrapped at the diaphragm (the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage1-SurgicalProcedure).  Then, in the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 instance, a stent graft is used to connect the 'elephant trunk' to the wrap graft.  Usually, the #$ElephantTrunkAortaReplacementStage2 is done via a catheter using an endovascular approach from the femoral artery, but in some cases, it may be done surgically instead.")
(comment RDFTriple "The collection of sentences of #$RDF-ResourceDescriptionFramework. Each #$RDFTriple consists of a 3-membered tuple <s p o> such that s= subject - either a blank (skolemized) node or a URI, p= predicate - a URI, and o= object - a URI or a literal (typed or untyped).")
(comment RDFTripleStore-AspatialInformationStore "A specialization of #$RDFGraph. Each RDF triple store is a set of #$RDFTriples encoding some coherent body of information.")
(comment RDFGraph "The collection of all RDF graphs, i.e. graphs that encode sets of #$RDFTriples.")
(comment Revising "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. Each instance of this collection is an act of changing the informational content of some sort of #$InformationStore.")
(comment OWLProperty "A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$OWLProperty is a binary predicate that has been ontologized in at least one OWL ontology.")
(comment rdfGraphLinksToNamespaceVia "(#$rdfGraphLinksToNamespaceVia GRAPH NAMESPACE PROPERTY) means that GRAPH contains triples relating resources via PROPERTY to resources identified using URIs that extend NAMESPACE.")
(comment OpenCycNamespace "The collection of all #$UniformResourceIdentifiers used as namespaces in which OpenCyc terms are identified.")
(comment dateRangeForMedicationStop "<code>(#$dateRangeForMedicationStop MED DATE1 DATE2)</code> means that if <code>MED</code> is an instance of #$MedicationPrescribedOrTaken, then <code>MED</code> has as the min-Date <code>DATE1</code> and max-Date <code>DATE2</code> as the bounds of its #$MedicationStopTime.")
(comment dateRangeForMedicationStart "<code>(#$dateRangeForMedicationStart MED DATE1 DATE2)</code> means that if <code>MED</code> is an instance of #$MedicationPrescribedOrTaken, then <code>MED</code> has min-Date <code>DATE1</code> and max-Date <code>DATE2</code> as the bounds of its #$MedicationStartTime.")
(comment EveryPerFn "(#$EveryPerFn TYPE N) denotes an instance of #$Frequency, indicating the property of occurring once for every N occurrences of TYPE.  For example, (#$EveryPerFn #$CalendarYear 1) denotes the property of occurring yearly (see #$Yearly).  (#$EveryPerFn #$CalendarHour 3 5) denotes the property of occurring every three to five hours.")
(comment drugStatusInEvent "<code>(#$drugStatusInEvent EVENT MED-TYPE STATUS-EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the event <code>EVENT</code>, the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> has the status <code>STATUS-EVENT-TYPE</code>.  E.g. it is contraindicated (#$ContraindicationOfDrug).")
(comment ContraindicationOfDrug "A specialization of #$Evaluating.  Each instance of #$ContraindicationOfDrug is an event in which it is determined that a drug is contraindicated for a patient.")
(comment Medication-LipidLowering-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which lipid-lowering drugs are assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of lipid-lowering drugs are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-LipidLowering-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-LipidLowering-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment hasTransformationOfValueRelativeTo "(#$hasTransformationOfValueRelativeTo THING VALUE REL) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE relative to REL.  This is used in the context of SKSI encoding statement to transform the value of some logical field indexical into its corresponding physical value.")
(comment TrueIsOneAndFalseIsTwo-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"1\" and \"2\", respectively.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ASA-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ASA-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-LipidLoweringSpecificType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which statin is assigned a \"1\" and lipid-lowering non-statins are assigned a \"2\".")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-LipidLoweringSpecificType-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-LipidLoweringSpecificType-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Steroid-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Steroid-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Steroid-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which steroid is assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of steroids are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Inotrope-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Inotrope-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Inotrope-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which an inotrope, alpha adrenergic agonist,  is assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of steroids are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Warfarin-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Warfarin-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Warfarin-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which warfarin is involved are assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of warfarin are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment Medication-ASA-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which aspirin is involved are assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of aspirin are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment Medication-AnticoagulantSpecificType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if unfractionated heparin is involved, export a \"2\" if low molecular heparin is involved, export a \"3\" if direct thrombin inhibitors are used, and export a \"9\" otherwise.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-AnticoagulantSpecificType-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-AnticoagulantSpecificType-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Anticoagulant-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if unfractionated heparin, low molecular heparin, or direct thrombin inhibitors are involved, export a \"3\" if any of these are contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Anticoagulant-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Anticoagulant-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Nitrate-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Nitrate-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ACEInhibitor-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ACEInhibitor-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-ACEInhibitor-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if an ACE inhibitor is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment Medication-Nitrate-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if a nitrate is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-BetaBlocker-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-BetaBlocker-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-BetaBlocker-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if a beta blocker is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment TrueIsOneAndFalseIsZero-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"1\" and \"0\", respectively.")
(comment Tuba "large brass instrument that produces a low pitch.")
(comment Sousaphone "large brass instrument named after John Phillip Sousa.  It is very similar in terms of sound and role in band arrangments to the #$Tuba.  It is used primarily in marching bands.")
(comment SmokerIsOneNonSmokerIsTwo-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the values Smoker and NonSmoker are encoded as \"1\" and \"2\", respectively.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-DiabetesTreatmentModality-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Inotrope-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment DiabetesTreatmentModality-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = None, 2 = Diet, 3 = Oral, 4 = Insulin, 5 = Other.")
(comment Medication-ADPInhibitor-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if an ADP inhibitor is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ADPInhibitor-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ADPInhibitor-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment rdfGraphNamespace "(#$rdfGraphNamespace GRAPH NAMESPACE) means that one or more of the #$RDFTriples GRAPH encodes is of the form (S P O), where S, P, and/or O is a resource identified by a URI in NAMESPACE.")
(comment rdfGraphSubjectNamespace "(#$rdfGraphSubjectNamespace GRAPH NAMESPACE) means that one or more of the #$RDFTriples GRAPH encodes is of the form (S P O), where S is a resource identified by a URI in NAMESPACE.")
(comment rdfGraphPredicateNamespace "(#$rdfGraphPredicateNamespace GRAPH NAMESPACE) means that one or more of the #$RDFTriples GRAPH encodes is of the form (S P O), where P is a resource identified by a URI in NAMESPACE.")
(comment rdfGraphObjectNamespace "(#$rdfGraphObjectNamespace GRAPH NAMESPACE) means that one or more of the #$RDFTriples GRAPH encodes is of the form (S P O), where O is a resource identified by a URI in NAMESPACE.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Antiplatelet-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Antiplatelet-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Antiplatelet-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if an antiplatelet is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-GPInhibitors-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-GPInhibitors-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-GlycoproteinIIbIIIaInhibitors-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if a glycoprotein IIb/IIIa inhibitor is involved, export a \"3\" if it is contraindicated, and export a \"2\" otherwise.")
(comment DBPedia-CW "A work consisting primarily of #$RDFTriples extracted from #$Wikipedia-WebSite.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-GPSpecificType-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-GPSpecificType-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment medicationStopDaysPriorToEvent "<code>(#$medicationStopDaysPriorToEvent MED-TYPE EVENT INT)</code> means that medication of type <code>MED-TYPE</code> ceased being administered <code>INT</code> days ago to the patient treated in <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment dateOfMedicalProcedure "(#$dateOfMedicalProcedure PROCEDURE DATE) means that DATE is the most constrained time interval which it is sensible to give as 'the' date on which PROCEDURE occurs.")
(comment contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForActivityType "(#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForActivityType PROCEDURE-TYPE ACTIVITY-TYPE) means that, if PROCEDURE is an instance of PROCEDURE-TYPE #$performedBy AGENT, and SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique of PROCEDURE, the fact that SUBJECT regularly performs (is the #$performedBy in) instances of ACTIVITY-TYPE at the time of PROCEDURE implies a (#$MediumToHighAmountFn #$Likelihood-QuantityType) that PROCEDURE will be a failure (#$failureForAgents) for AGENT.")
(comment contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForMedicationType "(#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForMedicationType PROCEDURE-TYPE DRUG-TYPE) means that, if PROCEDURE is an instance of PROCEDURE-TYPE #$performedBy AGENT, and SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique of PROCEDURE, the fact that SUBJECT is regularly taking a drug or drugs of type DRUG-TYPE at the time of PROCEDURE implies a (#$MediumToHighAmountFn #$Likelihood-QuantityType) that PROCEDURE will be a failure (#$failureForAgents) for AGENT.")
(comment conditionTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject "(#$conditionTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject PROCEDURE CONDITION-TYPE) means that where SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique, there is a condition COND of type CONDITION-TYPE, such that (#$physiologicalConditionAffects COND SUBJECT) and such that the duration of COND intersects the time of PROCEDURE, and such that PROCEDURE is of a type, PROCEDURE-TYPE, such that (#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForConditionType PROCEDURE-TYPE CONDITION-TYPE).")
(comment activityTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject "(#$activityTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject PROCEDURE ACTIVITY-TYPE) means that, where SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique of PROCEDURE, SUBJECT regularly performs instances of ACTIVITY-TYPE in a time frame which overlaps the time of PROCEDURE, and that PROCEDURE is of a type, PROCEDURE-TYPE, such that (#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForActivityType PROCEDURE-TYPE ACTIVITY-TYPE).")
(comment medicationTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject "(#$medicationTypeRiskFactorForProcedureSubject PROCEDURE DRUG-TYPE) means that, where SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique of PROCEDURE, SUBJECT is taking a prescription medication of type DRUG-TYPE at the time of PROCEDURE, and PROCEDURE is of a type, PROCEDURE-TYPE such taht (#$contraindicatedTreatmentTypeForMedicationType PROCEDURE-TYPE MED-TYPE).")
(comment anatomicalSiteTypeOfProcedure "(#$anatomicalSiteTypeOfProcedure PROCEDURE SITE-TYPE) means that where SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique of PROCEDURE, PROCEDURE is partially carried out at a site INST, which is an instance of SITE-TYPE and at the start time of PROCEDURE, an anatomical part (#$anatomicalParts) of SUBJECT.")
(comment closestEventOfTypePriorToContainsInstanceOfWithValueFor "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToContainsInstanceOfWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 TYPE CONTAINED-TYPE
PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> that contains some instance of <code>CONTAINED-TYPE</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>. This entails that
<pre>
 <code> 
  (#$thereExists ?VALUE
   (#$thereExists ?CONT1
    (#$and
      (PROPERTY ?CONT1 ?VALUE)
      (#$cCF-contains EVT1 CONT1)
      (#$isa ?CONT1 CONTAINED-TYPE))))
</pre>
In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment SweepingAScale "A specialization of #$LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing. Each instance of #$SweepingAScale is a purposeful search across instances of a type that is ordered by a particular scale.  For example, using a radio receiver to scan consecutive broadcast frequencies is an instance of #$SweepingAScale where the relevant scale is the #$RadioFrequencyBand.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-PatientStatus-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-PatientStatus-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-UrgentReason-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-UrgentReason-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment UrgentReason-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = AMI, 2 = IABP, 3 = Worsening CP, 4 = CHF,  5 = Anatomy, 6 = USA, 7 = Rest Angina, 8 = Valve Dysfunction, 9 = Aortic Dissection, 10 = Angiographic Accident, 11 = Trauma.")
(comment PatientStatus-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = elective, 2 = urgent, 3 = emergent, 4 = salvage.")
(comment hasNYHAHeartFailureStatus "(#$hasNYHAHeartFailureStatus PATIENT NYHA-STATUS) means that PATIENT has the heart failure symptom status NYHA-STATUS in the temporal context of the assertion, where NYHA-STATUS is one of the four classes of heart symptom severity as defined by the New York Heart Association.")
(comment nyhaHeartFailureClassOfCareEventRecipient "(#$nyhaHeartFailureClassOfCareEventRecipient CARE-EVENT NYHA-STATUS) means that the patient who is the #$patientInCareEvent in CARE-EVENT has the heart failure symptom status NYHA-STATUS at the time of CARE-EVENT")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-EmergencyReason-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-EmergencyReason-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment EmergencyReason-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which   1 = Shock Circ Support, 2 = Shock No Circ Support, 3 = Pulmonary Edema, 4 = AEMI, 5 = Ongoing Ischemia, 6 = Valve Dysfunction, 7 = Aortic Dissection, 8 = Angiographic Accident, 9 = Cardiac Trauma.")
(comment closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> (#$thereExists ?VALUE
       (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment closestEventPriorToWithValueFor "<code>(#$closestEventPriorToWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event prior to <code>EVT2</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> (#$thereExists ?VALUE
            (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-EjectionFractionMethod-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-EjectionFractionMethod-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment EjectionFractionMethod-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which   2 = Cardiac Catheterization, 5 = Echocardiogram, otherwise 9.")
(comment hasHistoryOfConditionOfType "(#$hasHistoryOfConditionOfType ORG COND-TYPE) means that there is an instance of COND-TYPE, COND, such that (#$physiologicalConditionAffects COND ORG) and such that that the #$startingPoint of COND is, at the latest, temporally coterminous with the starting point of the temporal context of (#$hasHistoryOfConditionOfType ORG COND-TYPE).  Conversely, if it is true that (#$physiologicalConditionAffects COND AGENT), true that (isa COND COND-TYPE), and true that (isa COND-TYPE #$PhysiologicalConditionType, then (#$hasHistoryOfConditionOfType AGENT COND-TYPE) is true in any temporal context whose #$startingPoint is the same as or later than the starting point of COND.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ValveInsufficiency-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-ValveInsufficiency-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment ValveInsufficiency-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" there is no stenosis, export a \"2\" if there is trivial stenosis, export a \"3\" if there is moderate stenosis, and export a \"4\" if there is severe stenosis.")
(comment Medication-GlycoproteinIIbIIIaInhibitorsSpecificType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which we export a \"1\" if ReoPro is involved, export a \"2\" if Integrilin is involved, export a \"3\" if Aggrastat is used, and export a \"9\" otherwise.")
(comment procedureIndicatedBySubjectConditionType "(#$procedureIndicatedBySubjectConditionType PROCEDURE COND-TYPE) means that one of the principal reasons PROCEDURE is carried out is because of a diagnosis of a #$PhysiologicalCondition of type COND-TYPE affecting the procedure subject.  More specifically, if (#$procedureIndicatedBySubjectConditionType PROCEDURE COND-TYPE) and (#$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique PROCEDURE SUBJECT), then there exists an instance of #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding, DIAGNOSIS, such that (#$hasDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS CONDITION-TYPE), (#$subjectOfDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS SUBJECT), (#$startsAfterEndingOf PROCEDURE DIAGNOSIS), and (#$eventOutcomes DIAGONSIS PROCEDURE).")
(comment physicianInRoleForOperationHasName "<code>(#$physicianInRoleForOperationHasName EVENT ROLE NAME-STRING)</code> means that <code>NAME-STRING</code> is the name of the physician who plays <code>ROLE</code> in <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment physicianInRoleForOperationHasNPI "<code>(#$physicianInRoleForOperationHasName EVENT ROLE NAME-STRING)</code> means that <code>NAME-STRING</code> is the name of the physician who plays <code>ROLE</code> in <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment Incidence-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of 0, 1, 2, 3,  are encoded as 1, 2, 3, and 4 respectively. Logical values returned that are integers greater than or equal to 4 are encoded as 5.")
(comment CPBUtilization-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical value #$False is mapped to 1, #$PerfusionTechnique_combination_off_and_on_cardiopulmonary_bypass is mapped to 2, and #$CardiopulmonaryBypass-SurgicalProcedure is mapped to 3.")
(comment FalseIsOneAndTrueIsTwo-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"2\" and \"1\", respectively.")
(comment CPBCombinationUnplannedReason-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Exposure/visualization, 2 = Bleeding, 3 = Inadequate size and/or difuse disease of distal vessel, 4 = Hemodynamic instability (hypotension/arrhythmias), 5 = Conduit quality and/or trauma, 9 = Other.")
(comment BiographicalDirectoryOfTheUnitedStatesCongress "A work containing biographical information about members of the US Congress (#$MemberOfUSCongress).")
(comment congressionalBiographyID "The identification string used for a #$MemberOfUSCongress in #$BiographicalDirectoryOfTheUnitedStatesCongress.")
(comment subjectOfProcedureOnMedicationOfTypeAtTimeOfProcedure "(#$subjectOfProcedureOnMedicationOfTypeAtTimeOfProcedure PROCEDURE MED-TYPE) means that, at the time at which PROCEDURE is carried out, it is correct to say that the subject of PROCEDURE is the recipient of 'regular administrations' of a drug of type MED-TYPE.  More specifically, is PROCEDURE is a #$MedicalProcedure such that (#$subjectOfMedicalProcedure-Unique PROCEDURE SUBJECT) and (#$dateOfMedicalProcedure PROCEDURE DATE), then it is true at DATE that SUBJECT regularly plays the role of #$objectExposed (cf. #$playsRoleInActionTypeRegularly) in instances of the type (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn AdminsteringADrug drugAdministered MED-TYPE).")
(comment Cardiomyopathy-NonIschemic "The collection of all non-ischemic cardiomyopathy conditions.")
(comment IdiopathicCardiomyopathy "The collection of all idiopathic cardiomyopathy conditions.")
(comment HypertensiveCardiomyopathy "The collection of all hypertensive cardiomyopathy conditions.")
(comment ValvularCardiomyopathy "The collection of all valvular cardiomyopathy conditions.")
(comment VentricularTachycardia-Nonsustained "The collection of all cases of nonsustained ventricular tachycardia.")
(comment AtrialPacedRhythm "The collection of all cases of atrial paced heart rhythm.")
(comment AortOccl-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which partial aortic cross clamp is encoded as 4, balloon occlusion  is encoded as 3, aortic cross clamp is recorded as 2, and no aortic occlusion is recorded as 1.")
(comment operationInvolvesCardioplegiaType "(#$operationInvolvesCardioplegiaType OP CPLGIA-TYPE) means that the operation OP involves a performance of the cardioplegia type CPLGIA-TYPE.")
(comment patientStartedOnMedTypeInCareEvent "(patientStartedOnMedTypeInCareEvent OP MED-TYPE) means that the patient in OP started receiving medication of type MED-TYPE during the #$MedicalCareEvent OP.")
(comment minOpEntryDate "<code>(#$minOpEntryDate OP DATE)</code> means that DATE is the min-date of the operating room entry.")
(comment minOpExitDate "<code>(#$minOpExitDate OP DATE)</code> means that DATE is the min-date of the operating room exit.")
(comment CardiacPresentation-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = No Symptoms or Angina
   2 = Symptoms Unlikely to be Ischemia
   3 = Stable Angina
   4 = Unstable Angina
   5 = Non-ST Elevation MI (Non-STEMI)
   6 = ST Elevation MI (STEMI)
.")
(comment NewYorkHeartClass-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Class I, 2 = Class II, 3 = Class III, 4 = Class IV.")
(comment PreviousOtherCardiacPCIStentType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Bare metal, 2 = Drug-eluting, 3 = Unknown.")
(comment PreviousOtherCardiacPCIWhen-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 =  LT = 6 Hours, 2 =  GT 6 hours.")
(comment MIWhen-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 =  LT =6 Hrs, 2 =  GT 6 Hrs but  LT 24 Hrs,  3 = 1 to 7 Days,  4 = 8 to 21 Days, 5 =  GT 21 Days.")
(comment CardiovascularIntervention "The collection of cardiovascular interventions, either surgical or non-surgical.")
(comment opWithCabgHasBypassConduitType-STS "Relates a CABG to the broad bypass conduit type.  This is a specialty predicate used for rules run by the report generator.")
(comment InternalThoracicArteryType-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the type if ITA graft involved is transformed into a positive integer between 1 and 4.")
(comment IMAHarvestType-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the type of ITA harvest technique is transformed into a positive integer between 1 and 4.")
(comment CerebrovascularDisease "The collection of all cerebrovascular disease conditions.")
(comment Gender-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = male, 2 = female.")
(comment PayorGov-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Yes (medicare, medicaid, military, state, indian), 2 = no (commercial, foreign, hmo, self-pay).")
(comment setOfListWithSameMemberInPos "(setOfListWithSameMemberInPos SET-OF-LISTS N LIST-OF-LISTS) means that SET-OF-LIST is a maximal set constructed from the members of LIST-OF-LISTS that have the same #$memberOfList in list position N.  The set of the returned SET-OF-LISTS values effectively partitions out the members of LIST-OF-LISTS into an exhaustive set of disjoint sets.")
(comment ChronicLungDisease-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = no, 2 = mild, 3 = moderate, 4 = severe..")
(comment operationHasComplicationType "<code>(#$operationHasComplicationType OP TYPE)</code> means that <code>OP</code> has a complication that is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment CardiacValveProcedureType-Anuloplastic "A #$CCFHelperConcept used, for now, to assist in determining
whether certain instances of #$CCFEvent incorporating instances of
#$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure qualify as involving
#$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair with #$Anuloplasty.")
(comment CardiacValveProcedureType-Reconstructive "A #$CCFHelperConcept used, for now, to assist in determining
whether certain instances of #$CCFEvent incorporating instances of
#$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure qualify as involving
#$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair with #$Anuloplasty.")
(comment CardiacValveAnatomyType-ReconstructionAndAnuloplastyRelevant "A #$CCFHelperConcept that is used in reporting
various instances of #$CCFEvent that involve instances
#$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure, vis-a-vis the roles of
#$Anuloplasty and #$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair.")
(comment receiverSensitivity "<code>(#$receiverSensitivity DEV INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>DEV</code> has a sensitivity of <code>INTERVAL</code>. Receiver sensitivity is the lowest power level at which the receiver can detect an RF signal and demodulate data.  It is measured in decibels, which are what Wikipedia calls \"dimensionless units\", i.e., intervals on a number line, which is why its second argument is an <code>#$IntervalOnNumberLine</code>.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Dipyridamole-STS "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-Dipyridamole-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment Medication-Dipyridamole-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which dipyridamole is involved are assigned a \"1\" and contraindications of dipyridamole are assigned a \"3\", otherwise a \"2\" is assigned.")
(comment frequencyOfWaveType "This predicate is used to represent  the frequency range for various #$WavePropagationTypes.  The frequencies should be represented as #$MegaHertz, #$Hertz, or  #$Angstrom.")
(comment addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept "(#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept TERM1 TERM2) means that when generating query fragments from query searches in the relevant context the system should add a formula created with TERM1 to any formulas created by TERM2 or, if TERM2 is a collection, any specializations of TERM2.  Note:  Formulas created with Collections are #$isa formulas.  For example, (#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept #$patientTreated #$SurgicalProcedure) means that if a query fragment made with a specialization of SurgicalProcedure will show up in the query search results, then a formula made with #$patientTreated in arg0 should be added to that fragment.  Hence from (isa ?X PericardialWindow) we would instead generate and display (and (patientTreated ?X ?PATIENT) (isa ?X PericardialWindow)).  Here is another example. (#$addFormulaFromConceptToFormulasWithConcept #$patientTreated #$vascularProcedureReason).  This would entail that if (#$vascularProcedureReason ?X ?Y) appears, then we should instead generate (and (patientTreated ?X ?PAT) (#$vascularProcedureReason ?X ?Y)).  There is no assumption that the two fragments will share a variable, but the expected cases are that they will share exactly one variable and that normal query combination rules apply.")
(comment genlRules "(#$genlRules RULE-SPEC RULE-GENL) means that the set of binding tuples that satisfy the open (universally quantified) variables in the consequent of RULE-SPEC via an application of RULE-SPEC will be a subset of the set of binding tuples that satisfy the open (universally quantified) variables in the consequent of RULE-GENL via an application of RULE-GENL.  For example, the following holds

<pre>
   (#$genlRules
      (#$ist FOO
        (#$implies
          (#$and
           (cardiacValveRepairProcedure ?CVRP #$Plication-ValvularProcedure)
           (#$rdf-type ?PROC #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure)
           (contains ?CVD ?CVRP)
           (contains ?PROC ?CVD))
          (#$isa ?PROC #$Plication-ValvularProcedure)))
      (#$ist FOO 
       (#$implies
         (#$rdf-type ?X #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure)
         (#$isa ?X #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure)))) </pre>


Hence, if one was looking to return instances of #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure, all other things being equal, there would be no need to query using both of these rules.  The rule in arg2 of genlRules here would get a superset of the answers that the rule in arg1 would return.
 ")
(comment postOpBldProd "(#$postOpBldProd INDEX #$True) is true just in case INDEX
contains an instance PROD such that PROD is an instance of
#$CCFBloodProductGiven, and such that (#$cCFBloodbankProductType PROD
TYPE) where TYPE is one of the four known instances of #$CCFBloodProductTypeType.")
(comment IABPWhen-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = preop, 2 = intraop, 3 = postop.")
(comment ArrhythmiaCorrectionDevice-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = None, 2 = Permanent Pacemaker, 3 = Permanent Pacemaker with  Cardiac Resynchronization Technique (CRT), 4 = Automatic Implanted Cardioverter Defibrillator (AICD), 5 = AICD with CRT.")
(comment Endocardium "The collection of all endocardia.  An #$Endocardium is a layer of tissue that lines the chambers of the #$Heart.")
(comment Epicardium "The collection of all epicardia.  An #$Epicardium is the outer layer of tissue of the #$Heart.")
(comment LeadPlacement-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = Epicardial, 2 = Endocardial.")
(comment patientPlacedOnIABPInEventWRTOperationDate "(#$patientPlacedOnIABPInEventWRTOperationDate EVT OP WHEN) means that in EVT, the patient treated in OP is placed on an intra-aortic balloon pump at time WHEN, and this is placement is relevant to OP.  E.g., for the purposes of STS reporting, EVT occurs within 2 weeks prior to OP.")
(comment patientPlacedOnIABPInEventWRTOperationWhen "(#$patientPlacedOnIABPInEventWRTOperationWhen EVT OP WHEN) means that for EVT, the patient treated in OP is placed on an intra-aortic balloon pump at WHEN.")
(comment IABPIndication-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Hemodyn Instab, 2 = PTCA Support, 3 = Unstable Angina, 4 = CPB Wean, 5 = Prophylactic.")
(disjointWith InformationStorageMedia InformationRecordingDevice)
(comment OCarAFib-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = None, 2 = Standard Surgical Maze Procedures, 3 = Other Surgical Ablative Procedure, 4 = Combination of Standard and Other Procedures.")
(comment VADIndication-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Bridge to Transplantation, 2 = Bridge to Recovery, 3 = Destination, 4 = Postcardiotomy Ventricular Failure (Separation from CPB), 5 = Device Malfunction, 6 = End of Life.")
(comment VHSVideoTape "Magnetic tape suitable for video recording or having been recorded with video information.  Each #$VHSCassette has some length of such tape as a physical part.")
(comment BetamaxVideoTape "Magnetic tape suitable for video recording or having been recorded with video information.  Each Betamax video cassette has some length of such tape as a physical part.")
(comment VADImplantType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = RVAD - Right Ventricular Assist Device, 2 = LVAD - Left Ventricular Assist Device, 3 = BiVAD - BiVentricular Assist Device, 4 = TAH - Total Artificial Heart.")
(comment LeftInflow-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = Left Atrium, 2 = Left Ventricle.")
(comment percentBornIn "<code>(#$percentBornIn PLACE-OF-RESIDENCE PLACE-OF-BIRTH PERCENT)</code> means that PERCENT of the residents of PLACE-OF-RESIDENCE were born in PLACE-OF-BIRTH")
(comment VADProductType-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which   1 = HeartQuest VAD, 2 = Lion Heart, 3. = Novacor LVAS, 4 = Heartsaver VAD, 5 = Jarvic 2000, 6 = DeBakey VAD, 7 = TandemHeart pVAD,  8 = AB-180 iVAD, 9 = CardioWest TAH, 10 = Thoratec IVAD, 11 = HeartMate VE, 12 = HeartMate IP LVAS, 13 = HeartMate SNAP-VE, 14 = HeartMate XVE, 15 = HeartMate II, 16 = HeartMate III, 17 = BVS5000i, 18 = AbioCor, 19 = Incor, 20 = Excor, 21 = Other;")
(comment DrugStatusType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection represents the \"status\" a particular medication type has with respect to some prescription or contraindication.")
(comment hospitalizationMedicationStatusForEvent "<code>(#$hospitalizationMedicationStatusForEvent EVENT MED-TYPE STATUS)</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the event <code>EVENT</code>, the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> has the status <code>STATUS</code> during the hospitalization that is associated with  <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment ReadmitReason-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which   2 = Arrhythmia/Heart Block 
    3 = Congestive Heart Failure 
    5 = Myocardial Infarction and/or Recurrent Angina 
    6 = Pericardial Effusion and/or Tamponade 
    7 = Pneumonia or other Respiratory Complication 
    8 = Valve Dysfunction 
    9 = Infection - Deep Sternum 
   14 = Renal Failure 
   15 = TIA 
   18 = Permanent CVA 
   19 = Acute Vascular Complication 
   20 = Anticoagulation Complication - Valvular 
   21 = Anticoagulation Complication - Pharmacological 
   22 = Coronary Artery Dysfunction 
   23 = Infection - Conduit Harvest Site 
   24 = Subacute Endocarditis 
   25 = VAD Complication 
   26 = Transplant Rejection 
  998 = Other - Related Readmission 
  999 = Other - Nonrelated Readmission")
(comment hospitalizationInvolvesMedicationType "<code>(#$hospitalizationInvolvesMedicationType EVENT MED-TYPE SPECIFIC )</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the event <code>EVENT</code>, the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> with the status SPECIFIC (either a specific name or a more restricted class) was administered or prescribed during the hospitalization that is associated with <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment ReadmitPrimaryProcedure-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 10 = OR for Bleeding, 20 = Pacemaker, 30 = PCI, 40 = Pericardiotomy/Pericardiocentesis, 50 = OR for Coronary Arteries, 60 = OR for Valve, 70 = OR for Sternal Debridement/Muscle Flap
, 80 = Dialysis, 90 = OR or Vascular, 700 = No Procedure Performed, 710 = Other Procedure, 720 = Unknown")
(comment HospitalDischargeLocation-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1=Home, 2=Extended Care/TCU, 3=Other Hospital, 4=Nursing Home, 777=Other")
(comment OpMitral-Tricuspid-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding/decoding events associated
with STS variable sts:OpMitral, wherein
a response of #$False is encoded as 1, (#$ComplementOfInFn
#$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair #$Anuloplasty) (anuloplasty
without reconstruction) is encoded as 2,
#$Replacement-SurgicalProcedure is encoded as 3, (#$CollectionIntersectionFn (#$TheSet
#$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair #$Anuloplasty))
(reconstruction with anuloplasty) is encoded as 4, and (#$ComplementOfInFn #$Anuloplasty
#$Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair) (reconstruction without
anuloplasty) is encoded as 5.")
(comment |factbook:HIVorAIDSAdultPrevalenceRate| "An estimate of the percentage of adults (aged 15-49) living with HIV/AIDS.")
(comment SecondVADImplantType-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = RVAD - Right Ventricular Assist Device, 2 = LVAD - Left Ventricular Assist Device, 3 = BiVAD - BiVentricular Assist Device, 4 = TAH - Total Artificial Heart.")
(comment RightInflow-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = Right Atrium, 2 = Right Ventricle.")
(comment adultHIVPrevalencePercent "An estimate of the percentage of adults (aged 15-49) living with HIV/AIDS.")
(comment VADDischargeStatus-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = With VAD, 2 = Without VAD, 3 = Expired in Hospital Where Initial VAD was Implanted.")
(comment ProperNamePredicate-Stub "Instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Stub are all the lexical predicates that can be used for the purpose of temporarily and rapidly registering the information that a certain STRING is (one of the) name(s) for a certain FORT.  The salient feature of the predicates that are instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Stub is they should eventually be replaced with assertions using predicates that contain more grammatical information, such as instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict. A prototypical example of such a predicate would be #$termStrings.  These differ from predicates that are merely instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose in that those may be missing grammatical information (and are thus difficult to use in understanding text), but are nevertheless not intended to be removed when assertions with more grammatical information become available.")
(comment defaultWellformednessCheckingMt "<code>(#$defaultWellformednessCheckingMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, MT is the appropriate #$Microtheory to use when performing well-formedness checking on queries.  It will commonly be the case that this #$Microtheory will have tighter constraints than are otherwise found in the general Cyc KB, as it is focused more strongly on weeding out ridiculous sentences than on admitting all sentences that might possibly be correct.")
(comment defaultCAEGuidanceMt "<code>(#$defaultCAEGuidanceMt TASK MT)</code> means that for the task <code>TASK</code>, the microtheory <code>MT</code> is the context from which the CAE should gather the assertions that dictate what query fragments to generate, what terms to use to augment query fragments, and what terms to use to populate drop-down substitution suggestion menus.  If no specific microtheory is specified with this predicate, the CAE will use the microtheory specified by #$defaultWellformednessCheckingMt (q.v.).")
(comment AssistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskFn "<code>(#$AssistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskFn TASK)</code> denotes the #$MicrotheorySpindle designed to hold source microtheories whose contents are authored using the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader by users while working on <code>TASK</code>.")
(comment assistedReaderSourceSpindleForTask "<code>(#$assistedReaderSourceSpindleForTask TASK SPINDLE)</code> means that <code>SPINDLE</code> is the #$MicrotheorySpindle designed to hold source microtheories whose contents are authored using the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader by users while working on <code>TASK</code>.")
(comment AssistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskAndUserFn "<code>(#$AssistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskAndUserFn TASK USER)</code> denotes the #$MicrotheorySpindle designed to hold source microtheories whose contents are authored using the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader by <code>USER</code> while working on <code>TASK</code>.")
(comment assistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskAndUser "<code>(#$assistedReaderSourceSpindleForTaskAndUser TASK USER SPINDLE)</code> means that <code>SPINDLE</code> is the #$MicrotheorySpindle designed to hold source microtheories whose contents are authored using the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader by <code>USER</code> while working on <code>TASK</code>.")
(comment candidateWikipediaArticleName-ManyToOne "(#$candidateWikipediaArticleName-ManyToOne THING NAME) means that there is an article whose title is NAME in #$Wikipedia-WebSite that may describe THING, but there is at least one other thing it may describe.")
(comment defaultCUREGuidanceMt "<code>(#$defaultCUREGuidanceMt TASK MT)</code> means that for the task <code>TASK</code>, the microtheory <code>MT</code> is the context from which the CURE assisted reader should gather the assertions that dictate how to form sentence fragments.")
(comment AssistedReaderSourceSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle which collects source microtheories and SME-authored contexts for use by the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader.")
(comment RupturedChordae "A laceration or tearing of the chordae tendineae of one of the heart valves, most commonly seen as a serious consequence of an acute myocardial infarction.")
(comment defaultNLDomainMt "<code>(#$defaultNLDomainMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, MT is the appropriate #$Microtheory to use when trying to determine domain facts while performing natural language generation or parsing.  Typically, this Mt will be either the same as or a spec-mt of the #$defaultQueryMt, as the domain assumptions seen by the NL system should be roughly the same as those used by the application for question answering. This Mt is not used for finding lexical assertions.  Those are gated by #$defaultParaphraseMt or #$defaultParsingMt.")
(comment defaultParaphraseMt "<code>(#$defaultParaphraseMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, MT is the appropriate #$Microtheory to use for lexical and other generation-related assertions when performing natural language generation.  If domain knowledge needs to be checked, it will be lookeup from the #$defaultNLDomainMt.")
(comment defaultParsingMt "<code>(#$defaultParaphraseMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, MT is the appropriate #$Microtheory to use for lexical and other NL-related assertions when performing natural language understanding.  If domain knowledge needs to be checked, it will be lookeup from the #$defaultNLDomainMt.")
(comment sentenceToExportForOntology "<code>(#$sentenceToExportForOntology ONTOLOGY SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is a CycL sentence that should be exported from Cyc as part of the export of ontology <code>ONTOLOGY</code>. The export of <code>SENT</code> may involve translating  <code>SENT</code> from CycL into the native language of the exported ontology (e.g. OWL).")
(comment termToAugmentOntology "<code>(#$termToAugmentOntology TERM ONT)</code> means that <code>TERM</code>is an extant CycL term that should augment the ontology <code>ONT</code>.")
(comment xDimensionOfAilmentConditionDiagnosed "A binary predicate used for relating a #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the x coordinate of the diagnosed ailment condition, as given by a linear distance within a localized coordinate framework.")
(comment yDimensionOfAilmentConditionDiagnosed "A binary predicate used for relating a #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the y coordinate of the diagnosed ailment condition, as given by a linear distance within a localized coordinate framework.")
(comment zDimensionOfAilmentConditionDiagnosed "A binary predicate used for relating a #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the z coordinate of the diagnosed ailment condition, as given by a linear distance within a localized coordinate framework.")
(comment xYZCoordinatesOfAilmentConditionDiagnosed "A binary predicate used to specify the 3D coordinate location of the delineating symptomology of a diagnosed ailment condition, within some localized coordinate framework.  Intuitively, where (#$xYZCoordinatesOfAilmentConditionDiagnosed DIAGNOSIS COORDINATES), (#$hasDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS CONDITION-TYPE) and (#$evaluationCorrectness DIAGNOSIS #$True), then, where SUBJECT is the #$subjectOfDiagnosis in DIAGNOSIS, and FEATURE is some physical feature that is the physical delineation of an instance of CONDITION-TYPE afflicting SUBJECT at the time of DIAGNOSIS, FEATURE has the location COORDINATES within SUBJECT.")
(comment diameterOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed "A #$BinaryQuantityPredicate used to relate a metrical #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the diameter of the anatomical feature that it measures.  Assuming that (#$diagnosisSiteType DIAGNOSIS PART-TYPE), that (#$subjectOfDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS SUBJECT), that (#$anatomicalParts SUBJECT PART), that (#$isa SUBJECT ORG-TYPE) and (#$isa PART PART-TYPE), and that (#$uniquePhysicalPartTypes ?ORG-TYPE ?PART-TYPE), then, where (#$diameterOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed DIAGNOSIS DIAMETER) and given that (#$evaluationCorrectness DIAGNOSIS #$True), it follows that (#$diameterOfObject PART DIAMETER) at the time of DIAGNOSIS.")
(comment areaOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed "A #$BinaryQuantityPredicate used to relate a metrical #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the area of the anatomical feature that it measures.  Assuming that (#$diagnosisSiteType DIAGNOSIS PART-TYPE), that (#$subjectOfDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS SUBJECT), that (#$anatomicalParts SUBJECT PART), that (#$isa SUBJECT ORG-TYPE) and (#$isa PART PART-TYPE), and that (#$uniquePhysicalPartTypes ?ORG-TYPE ?PART-TYPE), then, where (#$areaOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed DIAGNOSIS AREA) and given that (#$evaluationCorrectness DIAGNOSIS #$True), it follows that (#$areaOfObject PART AREA) at the time of DIAGNOSIS.")
(comment volumeOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed "A #$BinaryQuantityPredicate used to relate a metrical #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the area of the anatomical feature that it measures.  Assuming that (#$diagnosisSiteType DIAGNOSIS PART-TYPE), that (#$subjectOfDiagnosis DIAGNOSIS SUBJECT), that (#$anatomicalParts SUBJECT PART), that (#$isa SUBJECT ORG-TYPE) and (#$isa PART PART-TYPE), and that (#$uniquePhysicalPartTypes ?ORG-TYPE ?PART-TYPE), then, where (#$volumeOfAnatomicalFeatureDiagnosed DIAGNOSIS VOLUME) and given that (#$evaluationCorrectness DIAGNOSIS #$True), it follows that (#$volumeOfObject PART VOLUME) at the time of DIAGNOSIS.")
(comment ontologyAugmentsOntology "<code>(#$ontologyAugmentsOntology AUG-ONT ONT)</code> means that <code>AUG-ONT</code> is an ontology that augments <code>ONT</code>.")
(comment at-UnderspecifiedLandmark "(#$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark ACT ATLOC) states that an abstract
locational relation holds between ACT and ATLOC, where ATLOC is a
#$Landmark-Underspecified.  #$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark is an underspecified
semantic representation that may be elaborated to represent either a
spatial example of physical landmarks (as in 'at Dublin') or a
temporal use of landmarks ('at 9pm' etc.) or metaphorical landmarks
('at 6 billion dollars, Bill Gate's wealth is simply staggering', etc.).
Note the distinction between #$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark and
#$in-UnderspecifiedContainer: while one can say 'in June', one cannot say
'at June' (at least not in #$EnglishSpeakingCultureMt where #$TimePoints
but not #$CalendarMonths can be conceptualized as
#$Landmark-Underspecified, and #$CalendarMonths but not #$TimePoints can be
conceptualized as #$Container-Underspecified).  Likewise, one can say 'at
9pm' but not 'in 9pm'.")
(disjointWith Relation (CollectionDifferenceFn Thing Relation))
(comment KMFPlusPlusImplicitUnitProperty "The collection of properties introduced to augment the KMF ontology, which correspond to Cyc properties but have implicit units of measurement.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationModulationTypeByModulatedFeature "The collection of all types of electromagnetic radiation modulation.  Each instance of this collection is a type of modulation.")
(comment exportsToOntologyWithCycIndentifier "<code>(#$exportsToOntologyWithCycIndentifier THING ONT)</code> means that when creating an export of Cyc terms to the ontology <code>ONT</code>, a Cyc indentifier should be used for the term denoting <code>THING</code>.")
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject (CollectionDifferenceFn TemporalThing BiologicalLivingObject))
(comment firstVADInsertForOperation "(#$firstVADInsertForOperation OP INSERT) means that INSERT is the first VAD insert for the patient treated in OP during the same hospitalization in which OP occurred.")
(comment secondVADInsertForOperation "(#$secondVADInsertForOperation OP INSERT) means that INSERT is the second VAD insert for the patient treated in OP during the same hospitalization in which OP occurred.")
(comment thirdVADInsertForOperation "(#$thirdVADInsertForOperation OP INSERT) means that INSERT is the third VAD insert for the patient treated in OP during the same hospitalization in which OP occurred.")
(comment executiveVicePresident "<code>(#$executiveVicePresident ORG PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> is an executive vice-president of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment companyHasCEO "<code>(#$companyHasCEO COMPANY CEO)</code> identifies <code>CEO</code> as the Chief Executive Officer of <code>COMPANY</code>, a #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment seniorVicePresident "<code>(#$seniorVicePresident ORG PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> is a senior vice-president of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment corporateVicePresident "<code>(#$seniorVicePresident ORG PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> is a senior vice-president of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment ExecutiveVicePresident-CorporateOfficer "A specialization of #$VicePresident-CorporateOfficer.  Each instance of #$ExecutiveVicePresident-CorporateOfficer is an executive vice president of a commercial organization.  Typically, executive vice presidents rank higher than senior vice presidents.")
(comment SeniorVicePresident-CorporateOfficer "A specialization of #$VicePresident-CorporateOfficer.  Each instance of #$SeniorVicePresident-CorporateOfficer is a senipr vice president of a commercial organization.  Typically, senior vice presidents rank lower than executive vice presidents.")
(comment ChiefDevelopmentOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasCDO to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefInformationOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasCIO to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefAccountingOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefAccountingOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefAdministrativeOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefAdministrativeOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefAnalyticsOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefAnalyticsOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefBrandOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefBrandOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefChannelOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefChannelOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefComplianceOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefComplianceOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefCommunicationsOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefCommunicationsOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefDataOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefDataOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefInformationSecurityOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefInformationSecurityOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefKnowledgeOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefKnowledgeOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefLearningOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefLearningOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefLegalOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefLegalOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefMarketingOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefMarketingOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefNetworkingOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefNetworkingOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefProcurementOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefProcurementOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefRiskOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefRiskOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment ChiefScienceOfficer "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasChiefScienceOfficer to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment GeneralCounsel "The collection of instances of #$Person who bear the relation of #$companyHasGeneralCounsel to some instance of #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment seeAlsoURI "<code>(#$seeAlsoURI THING URI)</code> means that a description of the resource identified by URI is likely to contain information pertinent to THING.  This predicate is roughly equivalent to rdfs:seeAlso.")
(comment synsetDenotes "<code>(#$synsetDenotes SYNSET THING)</code> means that <code>SYNSET</code> denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment companyIsInIndustryType "(#$companyIsInIndustryType COMPANY INDUSTRY-TYPE) means that the #$CommercialOrganization COMPANY is in the type of #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment agencyRegulationsAffectIndustryType "<code>(#$agencyRegulationsAffectIndustryType AGENCY INDUSTRY)</code> means that the regulations of <code>AGENCY</code> impact the operations of companies in <code>INDUSTRY</code>.")
(comment RightBundleBranch "Bundle of specialized fibers and part of a #$Heart's electrical conduction system.  In a normal #$Heart, the #$RightBundleBranch extends from the #$BundleOfHis, and incorporates the #$RightBundleBranchFascicle, which ultimately subdivides into millions of Purkinje fibers which enervate individual cardiac myocytes, allowing for rapid, synchronous contraction of the #$Ventricles.")
(comment RightBundleBranchFascicle "The #$RightBundleBranch includes one fascicle of Purkinje fibers that enervates a large number of myocytes in the Myocardium.")
(comment LeftBundleBranch "Bundle of specialized fibers and part of a #$Heart's electrical conduction system.  In a normal #$Heart, the #$RightBundleBranch extends from the #$BundleOfHis, and incorporates the #$LeftBundleBranchAnteriorFascicle and the #$LeftBundleBranchPosteriorFascicle, both of which into millions of Purkinje fibers which enervate individual cardiac myocytes, allowing for rapid, synchronous contraction of the #$Ventricles.")
(comment LeftBundleBranchAnteriorFascicle "The #$LeftBundleBranch includes two fascicles of Purkinje fibers that enervates a large number of myocytes in the Myocardium: the #$LeftBundleBranchAnteriorFascicle and the #$LeftBundleBranchPosteriorFascicle.")
(comment LeftBundleBranchPosteriorFascicle "The #$LeftBundleBranch includes two fascicles of Purkinje fibers that enervates a large number of myocytes in the Myocardium: the #$LeftBundleBranchAnteriorFascicle and the #$LeftBundleBranchPosteriorFascicle.")
(comment RightBundleBranchBlock "A pathological interruption of the #$Heart's electrical conduction system affecting the #$RightBundleBranch.  #$RightBundleBranchBlock can be instrumental in causing dissynchronous contraction of the #$Ventricles.")
(comment LeftBundleBranchBlock "A pathological interruption of the #$Heart's electrical conduction system affecting the #$LeftBundleBranch.  #$LeftBundleBranchBlock can be instrumental in causing dissynchronous contraction of the #$Ventricles.")
(comment signifies "A very general signification or representation predicate. <code>(#$signifies SIGNIFIER SIGNIFIED)</code> means that the #$Thing <code>SIGNIFIED</code> is signified by the #$Individual <code>SIGNIFIER</code>.  That is, <code>SIGNIFIER</code> somehow represents, refers to, denotes, or depicts <code>SIGNIFIED</code>.  As an instance of #$Thing, <code>SIGNIFIED</code> can be anything. <code>SIGNIFIER</code> can be almost anything, although it is most often a word, phrase, description, string, image or symbol.  Note that this predicate does not state to whom <code>SIGNIFIER</code> represents <code>SIGNIFIED</code>; that is some assumed 'interpreter' or 'community of interpreters' in the given context, and it is left implicit by this binary predicate.  In order to mention explicitly the interpreter or agent to whom <code>SIGNIFIER</code> means <code>SIGNIFIED, use the ternary predicate #$signifiesTo.
<p>
Often there is a convention (intersubjective understanding and agreement) by which one thing represents another, such as the word 'Dogs' referring (in English) to dogs, or the abstract tetrahedron referring to the element Fire in #$Alchemy.  A pile of three rocks on a path can signify 'danger ahead' and the number thirteen can signify bad luck (such signification is sometimes called \"symbolic\".)  But there need be no specific convention; deer tracks in the sand can signify the deer (such signification is sometimes called \"indexical\"), and a picture or photograph may signify whatever it is a picture of (such signification is sometimes called \"iconic\"), in both cases without any prior convention or agreement. An important specialization of this predicate is #$denotes, which restricts <code>SIGNIFIER</code> to instances of #$CycLExpression, and the relationship between <code>SIGNIFIER</code> and <code>SIGNIFIED</code> to that of denoting (i.e. directly referring to).")
(comment ontologyIncorporatesTaxonomy "(#$ontologyIncorporatesTaxonomy ONT TAX) means that the ontology ONT includes the taxonomic relations ecoded in the taxonomy TAX.")
(comment OntologyToBeExportedInSKOSFormat "The collection of all ontologies to be exported from Cyc as SKOS format taxonomies.")
(comment |skos:broader| "(#$skos:broader A B) means that B is a broader \"concept\" than A.")
(comment competingSportsTeam "(#$competingSportsTeam COMPETITION TEAM) means that TEAM is a #$SportsTeam competing at the maximal or top level (see #$competingAgents-TopLevel in the #$TeamSportsCompetition COMPETITION.")
(comment SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout "The collection of all #$SportsCompetitions in which the same 'top-level' competitors (see #$competingAgents-TopLevel) compete with each other throughout the competition.  Thus, for example, a single #$BaseballGame is a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout, because the same #$competingAgents-TopLevel - the same pair of baseball teams - compete with each other for the entire duration of the game.  Likewise, a single inning within said #$BaseballGame is a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout for the same reason.  A playoff series that includes the #$BaseballGame is NOT a #$SportsCompetition-SameCompetitorsThroughout, however, precisely because different teams compete with each other in different games within the series.  Another positive example:  a discus throw within the Beijing Olympics.  Another negative exampe:  the Beijing Olympics.")
(comment TeamSportsCompetition-Entire "The collection of all #$TeamSportsCompetitions which are also #$SportsEvents, i.e., which have pre-defined starting times, and which conclude with an evaluation and ranking of the competing #$SportsTeams.")
(comment competingAgents-TopLevel "(#$competingAgents-TopLevel COMPETITION AGENT) means that AGENT is a competitor (#$competingAgents) in COMPETITION and there is no other agent of which AGENT is a part which is also a competitor in COMPETITION.  Thus, for example, consider the #$NewYorkGiants and some #$FootballGame-American GAME such that (#$competingAgents GAME #$NewYorkGiants).  The #$NewYorkGiants is not a part of any larger corporate entity which can also be said to be a #$competingAgents in GAME:  hence, it is true that (#$competingAgents-TopLevel GAME #$NewYorkGiants).  Consider, in contrast, a team member of the #$NewYorkGiants, PLAYER, who plays in GAME.  Because (#$competingAgents GAME #$NewYorkGiants), it is also true that (#$competingAgents GAME PLAYER):  however, because player is a member of the #$NewYorkGiants, it is NOT true that (#$competingAgents-TopLevel GAME PLAYER).")
(comment ConventionalWeapon "#$ConventionalWeapon is a specialization of #$Weapon.  Each instance of #$ConventionalWeapon is a weapon which is not classified as a nuclear weapon, a biological weapon, or a chemical weapon.")
(comment PressureSensitiveDetonatingWeapon "A specialization of #$Weapon and #$ExplosiveDevices.  Each instance of #$PressureSensitiveDetonatingWeapon is a device that contains a pressure-sensitive sensor to control detonation.")
(comment ConcussionHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to generate sufficient explosive power to harm its targets through explosive force alone.")
(comment PercussionHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to explode on impact with its target.")
(comment SmokeHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to output large quantities of smoke.")
(comment GasExpellingHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to output gas (e.g. tear gas) to affect its target.")
(comment IncendiaryHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to generate intense heat.")
(comment StunHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to disorient human targets by generating intense light or sound (or both).")
(comment AntiTankHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to penetrate the armor of a tank.")
(comment UnitedStatesMilitaryWeapon "The collection of weapon models that have been, at one time or another, adopted for use by the military of the United States.")
(comment BritishMilitaryWeapon "The collection of weapon models that have been, at one time or another, adopted for use by the British armed forces.")
(comment IsraeliMilitaryWeapon "The collection of weapon models that have been, at one time or another, adopted for use by the Israeli armed forces.")
(comment ChineseMilitaryWeapon "The collection of weapon models that have been, at one time or another, adopted for use by the Chinese armed forces.")
(comment RussianMilitaryWeapon "The collection of weapon models that have been, at one time or another, adopted for use by the military of Russia.")
(comment M26-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M26A1-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M26A2-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M33-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M33A1-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M57-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M59-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M61-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M67-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment M68-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment MkII-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade. This kind of grenade was the kind most commonly used by American forces during World War II.")
(comment MkIIA1-FragmentationGrenade "A kind of American fragmentation grenade.")
(comment exportOfOntologyIncludesProperty "(#$exportOfOntologyIncludesProperty ONT PROP) means that when ONT is exporte, the applicable extent of predicate PROP should be included.")
(comment Gun "A specialization of both #$Weapon and #$ProjectileLauncher.  Each instance of #$Gun is a weapon used to fire projectiles (see the collection #$ProjectileWeapon), where each of the projectiles is propelled by an explosion inside the weapon.  The trajectory of the projectile fired by the gun can be direct (as for most instances of the collection #$Gun-Portable) or indirect (as for instances of the collection #$MortarLauncher).")
(comment MilitaryWeaponTypeByMajorNationalUser "A collection of collections.  Each member <code>TYPE</code> of #$MilitaryWeaponTypeByMajorNationalUser is a specialization of #$Weapon or #$WeaponSystem instances of which have, at some point in time, been used or commissioned to be used by a major national military.")
(comment ArtilleryShellRemoteDetonatedBomb "A specialization of #$ImprovisedExplosiveDevice and #$RemoteControlledBomb
(qq.v).  Each instance of #$ArtilleryShellRemoteDetonatedBomb is an
artillery shell fitted with an apparatus that enables it to be
remotely detonated.")
(comment BiologicalBomb-Homemade "A specialization of #$HomemadeBomb and #$BiologicalWeapon (qq.v).
Each instance of #$BiologicalBomb-Homemade is a homemade explosive
biological weapon.")
(comment TimeBomb-Homemade "A specialization of #$HomemadeBomb and #$TimeBomb (qq.v).
Each instance of #$TimeBomb-Homemade is a homemade time bomb.")
(comment LitFuseDetonatingDevice-Homemade "A specialization of #$HomemadeBomb and #$LitFuseDetonatingDevice
(qq.v).  Each instance of #$LitFuseDetonatingDevice-Homemade is a
homemade bomb constructed to be detonated via a lit fuse.  An
important specialization is #$PipeBomb.")
(comment priorHistoryOfConditionWRTEvent "<code>(#$priorHistoryOfConditionWRTEvent EVENT CONDITION-TYPE)</code> means that the patient treated in <code>EVENT</code> has a prior history of <code>CONDITION-TYPE</code>.  The length of time prior is typically implicit to the condition-type and context of use.")
(comment skosName "(#$skosName THING STRING] means that STRING is the local name for THING in the #$SKOSCoreNamespace.")
(comment eventOfTypeClosestToEvent "(#$eventOfTypeClosestToEvent EVT1 EVT2 TYPE) means that EVT1 is the closest instance of TYPE to EVT2.  It can be before or after.")
(comment competingPlayers "(#$competingPlayers COMPETITON PLAYER) means that PLAYER is a playing member (#$sportsTeamPlayers) of a #$SportsTeam that is a #$competingSportsTeam in GAME, and that PLAYER actually plays during the course of GAME.")
(comment sportsTeamParticipatesInSport "A FunctionalPredicate used to identify the particular TeamSport that a SportsTeam plays.  (#$sportsTeamParticipatesInSport TEAM SPORT) means that SPORT is the #$TeamSport which TEAM was formed to play and to which TEAM is dedicated.")
(comment Fandango-MovieFn "(#$Fandango-MovieFn NAME ID) denotes the movie identified on the website http://www.fandango.com as having the string NAME as its canonical title and the integer ID as its unique identifier within the site.  For example, (#$Fandango-MovieFn 'Iron Man' 98591) denotes the movie 'Iron Man' starring Robert Downey, Jr. that was released in 2008.")
(comment Fandango-TheaterFn "(#$Fandango-TheaterFn NAME ID-STRING) denotes the theater identified on the website http://www.fandango.com as having the string NAME as its canonical name and ID-STRING as its unique identifier within the site.  For example, (#$Fandango-TheaterFn 'Alamo Drafthouse Village' 'aappy') denotes the Alamo Drafthouse movie theater in the Village shopping center in Austin,TX.")
(comment closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor-CYC "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> (#$thereExists ?VALUE
       (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment closestEchoOrCathEventPriorToWithinIntervalWithValueFor-CYC "<code>(#$closestEventPriorToWithinIntervalWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 INTERVAL PROPERTY )</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event prior to <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code>
     (thereExists ?VALUE 
          (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment maxDateForEvent-Direct "<code>(#$maxDateForEvent EVT DATE)</code> means that if <code>EVT</code> is an instance of #$CCFEvent, then <code>EVT</code> starts no later than <code>DATE</code>. If EVT is some procedure that's a subevent of some instance of a CCF operation, <code>INS</code>, then <code>INS</code> starts no later than <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment teamRepresentsOrganization "A predicate that serves as a common generalization for both #$teamRepresentsPolity and #$schoolSportsTeams")
(comment TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors "The collection of all instances of #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire in which the same 'top-level' competitors (see #$competingAgents-TopLevel) compete with each other throughout.")
(comment homeStadium "(#$homeStadium TEAM STADIUM) means that STADIUM is the home stadium of TEAM.")
(comment TheTextPrismUser "#$TheTextPrismUser denotes the current user of the TextPrism system.")
(disjointWith ReflexiveAction IrreflexiveAction)
(comment HidingAnObject "A specialization of #$AnimalActivity.  In each instance of #$HidingAnObject, one agent hides a physical object from another (or others).  'Hiding' an object means deliberately changing its location with the aim of making its discovery by others unlikely.  Note that an object may be hidden by moving it (to a location believed to be obscure), or by moving <b>other</b> things so as to obscure its current location (e.g., by covering the object with leaves).  For the first sort of case, see #$HidingAnObjectByMovingIt.  Also note that the object hidden may be the performer herself, as in a game of hide-and-go-seek (cf. #$HidingOneself).  Finally, there is a distinction between the act of #$HidingAnObject and the subsequent state of affairs in which the object remains 'hidden.'  The latter is a merely a type of #$Situation.")
(comment ActionOnObject "A specialization of both #$Action and #$PhysicalEvent; the collection  of physical events in which some doer acts on an object.  Each instance  of #$ActionOnObject is an action in which both the roles of #$doneBy  and #$objectActedOn (qq.v.) are filled.  Examples include someone typing on a keyboard, a dog scratching itself, and a tornado destroying a building.  Non-examples include a person dancing and wind blowing.")
(comment Dropping "The collection of physical events in which an object is released from support, falls, and collides with whatever's in the way (such as the ground, a floor, or other support surface).  For more specialized types of events in which some <i>agent</i> must release the object, see
#$DroppingAnObject and #$DroppingAnObject-Purposeful.")
(comment IrreflexiveAction "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject (q.v.). Typically, each instance of #$IrreflexiveAction is an action wherein the doer (i.e the filler of the #$doneBy role) is different than the object acted on (i.e. the filler of the #$objectActedOn role).  #$Murder and #$Surgery are representative specializations of this collection.  Contrast this collection with #$ReflexiveAction.")
(comment ReflexiveAction "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject (q.v.).  Typically, each instance of #$ReflexiveAction is an action wherein the doer of the action (i.e. the filler of the #$doneBy role) is the same as the object acted on (i.e. the filler of the #$objectActedOn role).  Representative specializations are #$Suicide and #$ScratchingOneself.  Contrast this collection with #$IrreflexiveAction.")
(comment soleMakerOfProductType "A binary predicate used to identify the unique organization that makes a specific type of product.  (#$soleMakerOfProductType PRODTYPE ORG) means that the #$Organization ORG is the sole maker of the #$ProductType PRODTYPE.  Cf. #$makesProductType, #$madeBy, #$mainProductType and #$soleProductType.")
(comment MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition "The collection of all #$SportsCompetitions which are themselves composed of multiple distinguishable #$SportsEvents.  Examplse include any particular instantiation of the Olympics, the Baseball World Series, etc.")
(comment TeamSportsGameSeries "A special (and commonly referenced) kind of #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition, in which the competitive 'components' (#$properSubSituations) are individual instances of #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors, i.e., #$SportsEvents in which the 'top-level' competitors (#$competingAgents-TopLevel) are #$SportsTeams and where the same competitors compete througout. A good example is a particular year's instance of the American Baseball World Series, which is composed of a series of #$BaseballGames, each of which is a #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors.")
(comment playoffSuccessors "(#$playoffSuccessors GAME-BEFORE GAME-AFTER) means that GAME-AFTER and GAME-BEFORE are succeeding #$SportsEvents in the order determined by a common #$Playoff.")
(comment PlayoffChampionship "The final game of a #$Playoff which determines the #$playoffWinners.")
(comment sportsEventInPlayoff "The relation that holds definitionally between a #$Playoff and every #$SportsEvent which occurs as a competition or match in that #$Playoff.")
(comment fanOf "<code>(#$fanOf FAN THING)</code> means that <code>FAN</code> is a fan of <code>THING</code>.  Typically, <code>THING</code> will be an at least relatively well-known person or group (such as a pop star or a professional sports team).  Usually <code>FAN</code> and <code>THING</code> temporally intersect, but this isn't always the case.  For example, a teenager today could be a fan of the young Elvis.")
(comment secCentralIndexKey "(#$secCentralIndexKey THING ID) means that in the computer systems of the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission, THING is identified by ID.")
(comment TerrorismTargetVenueType "The collection of terrorism attack venue types.  These are kinds of places terrorist attacks have been known to occur.")
(comment CongenitalSeptalDefectRepairSurgery "Repair of congenital septal defects by patch or suture.  This includes atrial and ventricular septal defect repairs.")
(comment VentricularSeptalDefectRepairProcedure-Congenital "The collection of all ventricular septal defect repair procedures by patch or suture.")
(comment AtrialSeptalDefectRepairProcedure-Congenital "The collection of all atrial septal defect repair procedures by patch or suture.")
(comment BankingOrFinanceCompany "The collection of companies whose business is bank or finance related broadly conceived.  This includes banking organizations proper as well as mortgage lenders and insurers, underwriting companies, etc.")
(comment LandTransportationDevice "A specialization of #$TransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$LandTransportationDevice is a device used for transportation across land.  Specializations of #$LandTransportationDevice include the collections #$Automobile, #$Snowmobile, #$Truck, #$HorseCarriage, #$BabyCarriage, #$Bus-RoadVehicle, and #$Skateboard.")
(comment Snowbike "The collection of all snow bikes  -- essentially, bicycles with skis instead of wheels.")
(comment owlExportDefinitionalSentence "(#$owlExportDefinitionalSentence THING SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE encodes definitional information about THING suitable for exporting in OWL format.")
(comment sportOfMultiGameCompetition "Where COMPETITION is a #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition, (#$sportOfMultiGameCompetition COMPETITION SPORT-CW) means that every #$SportsEvent in COMPETITION instantiates the #$ConceptualWork SPORT-CW.")
(comment SingleEliminationTournament "A #$SingleEliminationTournament isa a type of #$Playoff where the loser of each #$sportsEventInPlayoff is eliminated from winning the #$PlayoffChampionship:  however, this does not always mean the defeated competitor is forbidden from further competition in the tournament.")
(comment CollegeBasketballTeam "The collection of all college basketball teams.")
(comment organizationResponsibleForImplementingActivityType "(#$organizationResponsibleForImplementingActivityType ORG ACT-TYPE) means that ORG is in a strong sense charged or responsible for staging or implementing regularly scheduled instances of ACT-TYPE, as a matter of formal charter.")
(comment establishmentDateForMultiGameSportsEventClass "(#$establishmentDateForMultiGameSportsEventClass GAMES-TYPE DATE) means that DATE is the date on which the instantiation of GAMES-TYPE was officially incepted and instances began to occur by official sanction.")
(comment TeamSportsCompetition "The collection of all #$SportsCompetitions wherein at least two #$SportsTeams compete.  Note that this may mean they compete as a team (as in Basketball) or simply that they're scored as a team (as in team combined exercises in gymnastics).")
(comment tournamentClassTeam "(#$tournamentClassTeam TOURNAMENT-CLASS TEAM) means that TEAM is one of the teams that is authorized and expected to compete in instances of TOURNAMENT-CLASS as they occur, as a matter of official sanction.")
(comment applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization "(#$applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization ?VAR COLL CYCL-RULE) means that CYCL-RULE (an asserted rule that has an occurrence of ?VAR in the antecedent) should be pruned by the inference engine if ?VAR is explicitly typed in the problem via #$isa or rdf-type, unless it is typed by some specialization of COLL.  For example,

<pre> 
(applicableWhenTypedOnlyWhenSpecialization ?EVT ThingWithDirectTemporalData
    (implies
       (and
           (rdf-type ?TD EventDate)
           (cCFDateTimeMax ?TD ?DATE)
           (cCF-contains ?EVT ?TD)
           (cCF-contains ?REC ?EVT)
           (rdf-type ?REC PatientRecord))
       (maxDateForEvent ?EVT ?DATE)))
</pre>
The above states that if ?EVT is explicitly typed, the above rule should only fire when one of the typing collections is a specialization of ThingWithDirectTemporalData.  You would make an assertion like this  instead of adding a condition to the body of the rule when efficiency concerns dictate we don't want to solve 

<pre>
 (and
  ...
  (isa ?EVT ?TYPE)
  (genls ?TYPE <b>COLL</b>)  
</pre>
 in the traditional way.  Or when directly solving 

<pre>
 (isa ?EVT <b>COLL</b>)  
</pre>
is difficult or impossible.")
(comment StainlessSteel "An alloy of steel and chromium.")
(comment mostChampionshipsWonInPlayoffClass "(#$mostChampionshipsWonInPlayoffClass PLAYOFF-TYPE AGENT) means that, in the context of the assertion, AGENT is known to be a #$playoffWinners in more distinct instances of PLAYOFF-TYPE than any other agent in the class of #$playoffWinners of instances of PLAYOFF-TYPE.")
(comment mostChampionshipsWonInPlayoffClassAsOf "(#$mostChampionshipsWonInPlayoffClassAsOf PLAYOFF-TYPE AGENT DATE) means that, in the context of the assertion, AGENT is known to be a #$playoffWinners in more distinct instances of PLAYOFF-TYPE occurring on or before DATE than any other agent in the class of #$playoffWinners of instances of PLAYOFF-TYPE.")
(comment DrugParaphernalia "The collection of equipment used for administering illegal drugs.")
(comment polityOfMultiSportsEventSportsCompetitionClass "(#$polityOfMultiSportsEventSportsCompetitionClass GAMESERIES-CLASS POLITY) means that POLITY is the #$GeopoliticalEntity which traditionally hosts or supports instances of CAMESERIES-CLASS, in the sense that every instance of GAMESERIES-CLASS, and every #$SportsEvent that is a #$properSubSituations of any instance of GAMESERIES-CLASS, occurs in the territory of POLITY, and in the sense that POLITY provides support for the #$organizationResponsibleForImplementingActivityType of GAMESERIES-CLASS.")
(comment ConflictOutcomeFn "Where CONFLICT is a #$ConflictEvent, (#$ConflictOutcomeFn CONFLICT) denotes the result of CONFLICT, where this subsumes the status of respective adversaries with respect to each other and to CONFLICT at the end of CONFLICT and in its immediate aftermath.")
(comment outcomeOfConflict "(#$outcomeOfConflict CONFLICT OUTCOME) means that OUTCOME is the #$StaticSituation that includes the states of the respective adversaries (#$adversaryInConflict) at the end of CONFLICT and in the immediate aftermath.")
(comment ConflictOutcome-Draw "A very important subclass of #$ConflictOutcome.  In an instance of #$ConflictOutcome-Draw, the adversaries in the prior conflict (see #$outcomeOfConflict) are in a state of 'stalemate', so that no one has the status of a clear winner or loser with respect to the conflict or its subsequent outcome.")
(comment DefeatedSituation "The collection of all states applying to the aggregate of agents who are 'losers'of a #$ConflictEvent in the immediate aftermath of the conflict.")
(comment VictorySituation "The collection of all states applying to the aggregate of agents who are 'winners' of a #$ConflictEvent in the immediate aftermath of the conflict.")
(disjointWith DefeatedSituation VictorySituation)
(comment OutcomesOfConflictsOfTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for reifying the #$Collection of all #$ConflictOutcomes of the instances of a given class of #$ConflictEvent.")
(comment collectionOfConflictOutcomesOfType "Where CONFLICT-TYPE is a #$Collection of #$ConflictEvents, (#$collectionOfConflictOutcomesOfType CONFLICT-TYPE OUTCOME-TYPE) means that OUTCOME-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ConflictOutcome that are outcomes (#$outcomeOfConflict) of instances of CONFLICT-TYPE.")
(comment ConflictOutcome "A #$Collection of #$StaticSituations.  Each instance is a #$Situation that constitutes the result or aftermath of a particular #$ConflictEvent, construed as a #$StaticSituation starting no later than the end of the conflict, and consisting in the states of the respective adversaries in the conflict (#$adversaryInConflict) at the end of the conflict and immdiately thereafter.  Every complete #$ConflictEvent is considered to have one and only one #$ConflictOutcome in this sense (although it might have any number of other #$eventOutcomes).  Each #$ConflictOutcome that is not a #$ConflictOutcome-Draw in turn decomposes into one #$VictorySituation, the #$victoryStateInOutcome, which is the state of the aggregate of conflict winners at the conclusion of the conflict, and one #$DefeatedSituation, the #$defeatedStateInOutcome, which is the state of the aggregate of conflict losers at the conclusion of the conflict.")
(comment defeatedStateInOutcome "In our situational model of conflict aftermath, every #$ConflictEvent is regarded as having one and only one immediate aggregate 'result' or 'outcome' state (the #$outcomeOfConflict).  Where clear winners and losers result from the conflict, this outcome decomposes into a #$DefeatedSituation instance that is collective state of all of the losers of the conflict, in the outcome, and a #$VictorySituation instance that is the collective state of all the winners of the conflict in the outcome.  (#$defeatedStateInOutcome OUTCOME DEFEAT) means that DEFEAT is the unique #$DefeatedSituation in the #$ConflictOutcome OUTCOME consisting in the aggregate state in OUTCOME of all of the defeated agents in the conflict of which OUTCOME is the #$outcomeOfConflict.")
(comment victoryStateInOutcome "In our situational model of conflict aftermath, every #$ConflictEvent is regarded as having one and only one immediate aggregate 'result' or 'outcome' state (the #$outcomeOfConflict).  Where clear winners and losers result from the conflict, this outcome decomposes into a #$DefeatedSituation instance that is collective state of all of the losers of the conflict, in the outcome, and a #$VictorySituation instance that is the collective state of all the winners of the conflict in the outcome.  (#$victoryStateInOutcome OUTCOME VICTORY) means that VICTORY is the unique #$VictorySituation in the #$ConflictOutcome OUTCOME consisting in the aggregate state in OUTCOME of all of the winning agents in the conflict of which OUTCOME is the #$outcomeOfConflict.")
(comment SportsTeamTypeBySportFn "A collection-denoting function.  Where SPORT is a #$TeamSport qua #$ConceptualWork, (#$SportsTeamTypeBySportFn SPORT) denotes the collection of all instances of #$SportsTeam devoted to playing SPORT, or more specifically, the collection of all instances INST of #$SportsTeam such that (#$sportsTeamParticipatesInSport INST SPORT).")
(comment generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg "(#$generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg PRED TERM NUM) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then a sentence using PRED with the spec of TERM in the NUM position will be returned.  This overrides #$suppressIsaFormulasForCollections, which might otherwise prevent this formula.  For example, (#$generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg #$isa #$Animal 2) means that the term #$Person will trigger the return of the sentence (#$isa ?X #$Person).")
(comment generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg "(#$generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg PRED TERM NUM) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then a sentence using PRED with the instance of TERM in the NUM position will be returned.  This overrides #$suppressIsaFormulasForCollections, which might otherwise prevent this formula.  For example, (#$generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg #$isa #$Collection 2) means that the term #$Person will trigger the return of the sentence (#$isa ?X #$Person).")
(comment suppressIsaFormulasForCollections "(#$suppressIsaFormulasForCollections #$True) means that sentences of the form (#$isa ?X TERM) will not be generated by default for all collections (TERM) in the valid term set.  Note that (#$isa ?X TERM) sentence can still be generated using #$generatePredFormulasWithSpecInArg or #$generatePredFormulasWithInstanceInArg.")
(comment predicateConfidenceThreshold "(predicateConfidenceThreshold PRED PROB) states that when a closed atomic sentence
with predicate PRED has a probability of being true at or above PROB, we can conclude that it is true.")
(comment playoffWinners "The role relationship that holds between a #$Playoff and the #$competingAgents-TopLevel who is the #$winnerInConflict of the #$PlayoffChampionship.")
(comment physicianPlayedRoleInEvent "This relates a physician an event and a role just in case the physician played that role in that event.  This is a helper relation that combines the clauses that a physician is associated with an event and a physician plays a certain role.")
(comment RDFOWLInstance "The collection of resources that are the subjects and members of the OWL classes in some RDF triple store.")
(comment collegeSportTeamOf "The corresponding predicate of #$CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolFn. (#$collegeSportTeamOf SCHOOL SPORT TEAM) means that TEAM is the #$CollegeSportsTeam which represents INSTITUTION (see #$schoolSportsTeams) and is dedicated to SPORT, in the sense of being an instance of (#$SportsTeamTypeBySportFn SPORT).  See also sportsTeamParticipatesInSport.")
(comment CommercialAirliner "The collection of all airliners. A type of #$Airplane.")
(comment TelecommunicationHardwareStandard "A telecommunication hardware standard a kind of product specification, applicable to telecommunication hardware, such as cellular telephones.")
(comment 3GTelecommunicationStandard "The 3G telecommunication standard.")
(comment standardTypeGermaneToIndustryType "(standardTypeGermaneToIndustryType STANDARD-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE) means that the #$ProductStandard type STANDARD-TYPE pertains to the industry type, INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment SIMCard "A specialization of #$SemiconductorMemoryChip.  Each instance of #$SIMCard is a Subscriber Identity Module card.  Such cards are essential components of modern cellular telephones.")
(comment industryTypeInvolvesProductType "(#$industryTypeInvolvesProductType IND-TYPE PROD-TYPE) means that the industry typr IND-TYPE involves (e.g. in manufacturing or servicing) PROD-TYPE.")
(comment broadcasterOfTeam "(#$broadcasterOfTeam PERSON TEAM) means that PERSON  performs broadcasts about TEAM.")
(comment centersOfExcellenceForTreatmentOfConditionType "(#$centersOfExcellenceForTreatmentOfConditionType CONDITION-TYPE PLACE) means that PLACE is a center of excellence for treatment of CONDITION-TYPE.")
(comment interestedInVisiting "(#$interestedInVisiting PERSON REGION) means PERSON is interested in visiting REGION.")
(comment bondHolders "<code>(#$bondHolders AGENT-1 AGENT-2)</code> means that <code>AGENT-2</code>, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent, own at least one bond (see #$Bond-Agreement) issued by <code>AGENT-1</code> an instance of #$LegalAgent.")
(comment agentTravelDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentTravelDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact that is considered by the salient audience to constitute travel-related information about AGENT in the current context.")
(comment operationType "relates an operation to the standard CCF classification -- e.g. \"cabg only\" \"valve + cabg\", etc.  Note these are only fully populated on events prior to 2008.")
(comment collegeSportTeamBySex "The corresponding predicate of #$CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolBySexFn. (#$collegeSportTeamBySex SCHOOL SPORT SEX TEAM) means that TEAM is the #$CollegeSportsTeam which represents INSTITUTION (see #$schoolSportsTeams), is dedicated to SPORT, in the sense of being an instance of (#$SportsTeamTypeBySportFn SPORT), and which is segregated by SEX.")
(comment CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolBySexFn "Where INSTITUTION is a #$HigherEducationInstitution, SPORT is a #$TeamSport, and SEX is a #$SexType, (#$CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolFn INSTITUTION SPORT SEX) denotes the #$CollegeSportsTeam which represents INSTITUTION (see #$schoolSportsTeams), is dedicated to SPORT in the sense of being an instance of (#$SportsTeamTypeBySportFn SPORT), and which is segregated by SEX.  Thus, e.g. (#$CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolBySexFn #$UniversityOfKansas #$Basketball-TheGame #$FemaleHuman) denotes the University of Kansas Women's Basketball Team.")
(comment Intra-Op-TimeInterval "The collection of maximal time intervals between the start and finish of a medical operation.")
(comment operationHasBloodProduct "Relates an operation to the blood products administered intra or post operatively.")
(comment Allograft-SurgicalProcedure "A transplant process wherein a tissue or organ is taken from a donor and placed into a recipient (Stand-in definition used pending official definition from CCF)")
(comment PhysicianNameString "A subcollection of #$UniqueID, each instance of this collection is an ID string that identified a medical patient in a medical record.")
(comment annualEventOfYearForType "The corresponding predicate of #$AnnualEventOfYearFn.")
(comment AnnualEventOfYearFn "Where ANNUAL-TYPE is an #$AnnualEventType, (#$AnnualEventOfYearFn ANNUAL-TYPE YEAR) denotes the instance of ANNUAL-TYPE which occurred on YEAR.  Thus, e.g., April Fool's Day of 2009 can be represented as (#$AnnualEventOfYearFn #$AprilFoolsDay (#$YearFn 2009)).")
(comment qualifiesToCompeteIn "(#$qualifiesToCompeteIn COMPETITION AGENT) means that, prior to COMPETITION, AGENT undergoes some kind of qualifying or sanctioning procedure that authorizes or licences AGENT to compete in COMPETITION.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament "The #$Collection of all NCAA Men's Division 1 Regional Basketball Tournaments, or more colloquially, 'regionals'.  Every such tournament is a subevent (#$properSubEvents) within a larger #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament, a.k.a. 'March Madness' tournament, and every #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament includes exactly four instances of #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament, running more or less concurrently.  The four #$playoffWinners of these four tournaments are considered the 'final four' teams of the particular subsuming #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament (see #$finalFourTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament) and advance to the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballNationalSemiFinalGames.")
(comment MarchMadnessRegionalTournamentFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for referring to instances of NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament, which are individuated by the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament they are part of and by the NCAA 'regional brackets they cover.")
(comment marchMadnessRegionalSubTournaments "The corresponding predicate of #$MarchMadnessRegionalTournamentFn.  (#$marchMadnessRegionalSubTournaments TOURNAMENT REGION SUBTOURNAMENT) means that SUBTOURNAMENT is the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament associated with REGION and part of the NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament TOURNAMENT")
(comment sweetSixteenTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament "The relationship which holds definitionally between a given #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament and each of the sixteen teams which advance to regional semifinals games (#$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalSemiFinalGames) within the tournament.")
(comment eliteEightTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament "The relationship which holds definitionally between a given #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament and each of the eight teams which advance to the regional finals (#$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalFinalsGames) in the tournament.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalFinalsGame "The #$Collection of all regional finals games in that occur in #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament.  Each such game functions as the respective #$PlayoffChampionship of the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament that it concludes:  hence there are four such games in any given 'March Madness' tournament.  The eight teams which advance to compete in the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalFinalsGames of a given #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament are known as the 'elite eight' (#$eliteEightTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament), and the winners of these games are known as the 'final four' of the tournament (#$finalFourTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament).")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballNationalChampionshipGame "The #$Collection of all #$PlayoffChampionship games of #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballNationalSemiFinalGame "The collection of all NCAA Men's Division 1 Basketball National Semifinal games.  In a #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament, the national semifinals follow the four #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament. There are two  #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballNationalSemiFinalGames, in which the four winners of the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments (see #$finalFourTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament) play one another.")
(comment Pandemic "A specialization of #$Epidemic.  Each instance of #$Pandemic is an epidemic in which an infectious disease affects a large segment of a population across a broad geographical region.")
(comment conceptSetPotentiallyInterestingToForDomainBecause "(#$conceptPotentiallyInterestingToForDomainBecause AGENT SET-OF-CONCEPTS DOMAIN REASON) means that AGENT may be interested in concepts in SET-OF-CONCEPTS in the topic DOMAIN because of REASON.")
(comment scoringPlayers "(#$scoringPlayers GAME PLAYER) means that PLAYER is a competing player (see #$competingPlayers) who scores in GAME.")
(comment winnerInOutcome "(#$winnerInOutcome OUTCOME WINNER) means that, where (#$outcomeOfConflict CONFLICT OUTCOME), WINNER, during the period of OUTCOME has the social or cultural status associated with being one of the 'victors' in CONFLICT.  What this status is varies with respect to the type of conflict of which OUTCOME is the #$outcomeOfConflict.  E.g., in the case of a #$War, it often entails having certain rights of control over the loser, while in the case of a #$SportsEvent, it usually means having the accolades of the masses, etc.")
(comment loserInOutcome "(#$loserInOutcome OUTCOME LOSER) means that, where (#$outcomeOfConflict CONFLICT OUTCOME), LOSER, during the period of OUTCOME has the social or cultural status associated with being one of the 'losers' or defeated agents in CONFLICT.  What this status is varies with respect to the type of conflict of which OUTCOME is the #$outcomeOfConflict.  E.g., in the case of a #$War, it oten entails being the subject of enforceable claims on the part of the winner , while in the case of a #$SportsEvent, it usually means having the opprobrium of ones fans, etc.")
(comment earliestDateForCollectionMembers "(#$earliestDateForCollectionMembers COL DATE) means that every instance of COL starts no earlier than DATE.")
(comment CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolFn "Where INSTITUTION is a #$HigherEducationInstitution and SPORT is a #$TeamSport, (#$CollegeSportTeamOfSchoolFn INSTITUTION SPORT) denotes the #$CollegeSportsTeam which represents INSTITUTION (see #$schoolSportsTeams) and is dedicated to SPORT, in the sense of being an instance of (#$SportsTeamTypeBySportFn SPORT).  See also #$sportsTeamParticipatesInSport.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalSemiFinalGame "The #$Collection of all regional semi-finals games which occur in #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournaments.  Every such game occurs as part of one of the four #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments included in the overall #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament, and each #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournament includes two #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalSemiFinalGames.  The sixteen teams which advance to compete in the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalSemiFinalGames of a given tournament are known as the 'sweet sixteen' (#$sweetSixteenTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament), and the eight teams which win their respective semi-finals are known as the elite eight (#$eliteEightTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament).")
(comment finalFourTeamOfMarchMadnessTournament "The relationship which holds definitionally between a given #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament and each of the four winners of the four respective #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments of the tournament.")
(comment Restaurant-Organization "#$Restaurant-Organization is a specialization of #$ServiceEstablishment, #$FoodServiceOrganization, and #$OrganizationWithIndividualCustomers.  Each instance of #$Restaurant-Organization is an organization that operates individual restaurants.  For example, the group of individuals that operates the Threadgills on Lamar in Austin (and no other restaurants) is an instance of #$Restaurant-Organization, while the #$Organization that owns and operates both Threadgills (the one on Lamar and the one on Barton Springs) is not an instance of this collection (that organization would be an instance of #$FoodServiceOrganization).  Instances of #$Restaurant-Organization operate out of #$RestaurantSpaces.")
(comment RestaurantSpace "An #$ExistingObjectType.  Each instance of #$RestaurantSpace is a #$Workplace which serves, or is designed to serve, as an operating facility for a #$Restaurant-Organization.")
(comment hasInvestmentInterestInCommodityType "(#$hasInvestmentInterestInCommodityType AGENT C-TYPE) means that AGENT has a financial interest in the value of C-TYPE.")
(comment hasInvestmentInterestInEconomicSectorType "(#$hasInvestmentInterestInEconomicSectorType AGENT S-TYPE) means that AGENT has a financial interst in the happenings of S-TYPE.")
(comment VascularBiopsy-VascularProcedure "The collection of all biopsies. A type of #$MedicalTesting, #$SurgicalProcedureNonCongenital, and #$VascularProcedure-Surgical. #$Biopsy-SurgicalProcedure is a #$DisjointSurgicalProcedureType.")
(comment Sprinter "The collection of all persons who engage in the athletic activitiy of sprinting. A type of #$Runner and #$PersonWithOccupation. #$Sprinter is a #$PersonTypeByOccupation.")
(comment eliminationMatchFor "(#$eliminationMatchFor MATCH TEAM) entails that (#$losingSportsTeam MATCH TEAM) and means, further, that where MATCH is #$sportsEventInPlayoff of a #$Playoff, PLAYOFF, there can be no #$playoffSuccessors of MATCH in PLAYOFF in which TEAM competes (is a #$competingAgents).")
(comment eliminatedFromPlayoff "Where PLAYOFF is a #$Playoff such that it includes a #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors, MATCH such that (#$eliminationMatchFor PLAYOFF TEAM), it follows that (#$eliminatedFromPlayoff PLAYOFF TEAM).  Also, where TEAM is a #$SportsTeam and (#$eliminatedFromPlayoff PLAYOFF TEAM), it follows that everyone who is a member of TEAM at the time of PLAYOFF is also #$eliminatedFromPlayoff with respect to PLAYOFF.  (#$eliminatedFromPlayoff PLAYOFF AGENT) entails that (#$loserOfGameInMultiGameCompetition PLAYOFF AGENT), and, more specifically, where AGENT is a #$SportsTeam, that there is a #$sportsEventInPlayoff, GAME, such that (#$eliminationMatchFor GAME AGENT).")
(comment loserOfGameInMultiGameCompetition "(#$loserOfGameInMultiGameCompetition GAME-SERIES AGENT) means that AGENT is the loser (#$defeatedInConflict) of at least one #$SportsEvent that is a #$properSubEvents of the #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition GAME-SERIES.")
(comment winnerOfGameInMultiGameCompetition "(#$winnerOfGameInMultiGameCompetition GAME-SERIES AGENT) means that AGENT is the winner (#$winnerInConflict) of at least one #$SportsEvent that is a #$properSubEvents of the #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition GAME-SERIES.")
(comment teamSeed "(#$teamSeed TEAM TOURNAMENT NUMBER) means that the 'seed' assigned to TEAM on qualifying
for TOURNAMENT is NUMBER.  Under most circumstances, this assignment will determine which opening
game of TOURNAMENT TEAM competes in (#$competingSportsTeams).  See also
#$seedsCompeteInPlayoffsOfType and #$OpeningGameOfPlayoffBySeedsFn.")
(comment openingGameOfPlayoffSeededBy "The corresponding predicate of #$OpeningGameOfPlayoffBySeedsFn.")
(comment OWLLiteOntology "A specialization of #$OWLOntology (q.v.).  Each instance of #$OWLLiteOntology is an OWL ontology that meets the restrictions specified by W3C that qualify an ontology as conforming to the OWL Lite standard.")
(comment currentNumberOfHitsForStringOnSearchEngine "An #$EvaluatablePredicate.  (#$currentNumberOfHitsForStringOnSearchEngine STRING SEARCH-ENGINE N) means that the #$CharacterString STRING returns N hits when searched on the #$SearchEngine SEARCH-ENGINE.")
(comment nameStringHasHighestNumberOfHitsOnEngine "(#$nameStringHasHighestNumberOfHitsOnEngine THING ENGINE STRING) means that, of the known #$nameStrings of THING, STRING generates more hits on the #$SearchEngine ENGINE than any other.")
(comment searchAttestedQuoteString "(#$searchAttestedQuoteString THING ENGINE NAMESTRING) means that NAMESTRING is a known #$nameString of THING which, when enclosed in double-quotes (\") and searched in ENGINE, returns a nonzero number of hits.")
(comment currentNumberOfHitsForQuotedStringOnSearchEngine "(#$currentNumberOfHitsForQuotedStringOnSearchEngine STRING ENGINE NUMBER) means that the number of hits returned on ENGINE by the string that results from enclosing STRING in double-quotes (\") is NUMBER.")
(comment mostStronglySearchAttestedQuoteString "(#$mostStronglySearchAttestedQuoteString THING ENGINE STRING) means that STRING is a #$nameString of THING such that, when STRING is enclosed in double-quotes (\") and run as a search on ENGINE, it produces the largest number of hits of any quoted #$nameString of THING on that same #$SearchEngine.")
(comment programParameterOverrideForTask "(#$programParameterOverrideForTask PARAM PROGRAM TASK VALUE) means that any task or topic defaults for the PARAM in PROGRAM should be overridden with VALUE when PROGRAM is using TASK.")
(comment specificationVariesOnlyInParameterValue "<code>(#$specificationVariantInParameterValue VARIANT SPEC PARAMETER VALUE)</code> identifies <code>VARIANT</code> as the instance of #$ProgramSpecification that is identical to the specification <code>SPEC</code> but for its setting the parameter <code>PARAMETER</code> to the value <code>VALUE</code>.")
(comment SpecificationVariesOnlyInParameterValueFn "<code>(#$SpecificationVariantFn SPEC PARAMETER VALUE)</code> denotes the instance of #$ProgramSpecification that is identical to the specification <code>SPEC</code> but for its setting the parameter <code>PARAMETER</code> to the value <code>VALUE</code>.")
(comment specificationVariantInParameterValue "<code>(#$specificationVariantInParameterValue VARIANT SPEC PARAMETER VALUE)</code> identifies <code>VARIANT</code> as the instance of #$ProgramSpecification that results from setting the parameter <code>PARAMETER</code> to the value <code>VALUE</code> in the specification <code>SPEC</code>.  VARIANT will differ from SPEC in at least one value, but often will differ in many others as well.")
(comment SpecificationVariantFn "<code>(#$SpecificationVariantFn SPEC PARAMETER VALUE)</code> denotes the results of setting the parameter <code>PARAMETER</code> to the value <code>VALUE</code> in the #$ProgramSpecification <code>SPEC</code>.  The denoted specifciation will differ from SPEC by at least the changed parameter, but will often differ in other parameters as well.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalRound2Game "The collection of all 'second round' games in #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments.  A NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament begins with four separate 'regionals' or regional tournaments, the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments.  Each of these tournaments is seeded with sixteen starting teams (see #$teamSeeds) and starts with eight separate opening round games (#$NCCAMensDivision1BasketbalRegionalRound1Games) in which these teams are matched against each other.The tournament is not re-seeded after the first round, and a second round of four games (the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalRound2Games) follows in which the winners of the playoff-predecessors of these games are matched against each other (see #$playoffSuccessors-Direct).")
(comment usingExpandedGraphTrigger "Setting this to True and turning forward the genlRules rule on ExpandedGraphRDF-TypeCCFOWLClass will propagate the meta assertions on the rules for the specs of those expanded graph terms which will instruct the inference engine to only use the general rule and not the spec rule when generating results for the genl term.  If the system is querying unexpanded graphs as well, then the rule should be turned backwards and a null edit performed to remove the dependents.  Currently there is no after adding or similar piece of code associated with this to perform this clean-up and it has to be done by manually turning the rule forward or backward.  So, for now, this simply serves a documentation purpose.")
(comment TermIndexCountFn "(#$TermIndexCountFn TERM) returns the current number of assertions in the KB indexed off of TERM.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalRound1Game "The collection of all 'first round' games in #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments.  A NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament begins with four separate 'regionals' or regional tournaments, the #$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalTournaments.  Each of these tournaments is seeded with sixteen starting teams (see #$teamSeeds) and starts with eight separate opening round games (#$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballRegionalRound1Games) in which these teams are matched against each other.")
(comment Barium "The collection of all barium, a type of #$UnalloyedMetal. #$Barium is an #$AlkalineEarthMetalElementType.")
(comment Silicon "The collection of all silicon, a type of #$Metalloid #$SemiconductorStuff. #$Silicon is a #$MetalloidElementType.")
(comment Radium "The collection of all radium, a type of #$UnalloyedMetal and #$RadioactiveStuff. #$Radium is an #$AlkalineEarthMetalElementType.")
(comment Copper "The collection of all copper, a type of #$UnalloyedMetal and #$Mineral. #$Copper is a #$TransitionMetalElementType.")
(comment Carbon "The collection of all pieces or quantities of pure carbon. #$Carbon is a #$NonMetallicElementType and #$OrganismConstituentType.")
(comment scheduledBy "(#$scheduledBy EVENT AGENT) means that AGENT scheduled EVENT, i.e. decided that EVENT should occur at a certain #$Date.")
(comment PeriodicEventSeries "A collection of series of events. Each instance of #$PeriodicEventSeries is a sequence of similar events that occur at regular intervals.")
(comment inferenceDatastructure "(#$inferenceDatastructure INF STRUCT) means that STRUCT is the #$CycInference datastructure for the inference process denoted by INF.")
(comment intervalTypeOfPeriodicSeries "(#$intervalTypeOfPeriodicSeries SERIES INTERVAL-TYPE) means that each event in SERIES starts during an instance of INTERVAL-TYPE, and that exactly one event in SERIES starts during each instance of INTERVAL-TYPE from the start of SERIES to the end.")
(comment nextDateToRunScheduledQuery "(#$nextDateToRunScheduledQuery QUERY-SERIES DATE) means that the next member of QUERY-SERIES should be started at DATE.")
(comment probableYetRejected "(#$probableYetRejected PROP) states that PROP is a statistically probable sentence that
can nevertheless be rejected via background knowledge.")
(comment scheduledStartingDate "(#$scheduledStartingDate THING DATE) means that THING is or was scheduled to start on DATE.")
(comment encryptedPasswordForUser "(#$encryptedPasswordForUser CYCLIST STRING) means that STRING is the encrypted version of CYCLIST password for access to Cyc applications and the browser.")
(comment Therapod "A specialization of #$Dinosaur and #$Biped (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Therapod is a bipedal dinosaur.   Recent studies prove that birds (see #$Bird) are the descendants of small nonflying theropods.  Well-known specializations of #$Therapod include #$TyrannosaurusRex and #$Velociraptor.")
(comment IPodTouch "An instance of #$ProductTypeByBrand.  Each instance of #$IPod is a portable digital media playing device manufactured by #$AppleInc.")
(comment Netbook "A specialization of #$LaptopComputer.  Each instance of #$Netbook is a small laptop designed primarily for wireless access to the internet for web-browsing.")
(comment maxStopDateForEvent "<code>(#$maxStopDateForEvent OP DATE)</code> means that DATE is the max-date of the event's stop date.")
(comment nextFutureDateToRunScheduledQuery "(#$nextFutureDateToRunScheduledQuery QUERY-SERIES DATE) means that the next future date when a member of QUERY-SERIES should be started is DATE. DATE may not subsume the current instant, even if QUERY-SERIES should have a member during such a date and is not known to have one.")
(comment SMTPAccount "The collection of all #$SimpleMailTransferProtocol accounts, which allow users to communicate with #$SMTPServerPrograms, e.g. to send email.")
(comment SMTPAccount-Anonymous "The collection of all #$SMTPAccounts that do not require authentication.")
(comment SMTPAccount-Authenticated "The collection of all #$SMTPAccounts that require authentication.")
(comment smtpHostname "The hostname of the SMTP server.")
(comment smtpPort "The port number of the SMTP server. Default is 25.")
(comment cyclistSMTPAccounts "(#$cyclistSMTPAccounts CYCLIST ACCOUNTS) means that when Cyc sends email on behalf of CYCLIST, it should try to use one of ACCOUNTS, preferring ones eariler in the list.")
(comment NounCompoundFilterFromDecisionTreeFn "(#$NounCompoundFilterFromDecisionTreeFn DECISION-TREE-STRING) returns the #$NounCompoundFilterFromDecisionTreeFn defined by DECISION-TREE-STRING, i.e. the string representation of the corresponding decision tree.")
(comment resultsShouldBeEmailedToAddress "(#$resultsShouldBeEmailedToAddress ACTION ADDRESS) means that notification of the results of ACTION should be emailed to ADDRESS.")
(comment resultsShouldBeEmailedToAddress-CC "(#$resultsShouldBeEmailedToAddress-CC ACTION ADDRESS) means that notification of the results of ACTION should be emailed to ADDRESS as a carbon-copy recipient.")
(comment AdHocDataQuery "The collection of all queries defined for use by the ad hoc reporting infrastructure.")
(comment PosIsOneAndNoDataIsTwo-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"1\" and \"0\", respectively.")
(comment priorPositiveConnectionWithHarmed "A #$TemporallyQualifiableRolePredicate which relates an #$IntelligentAgent to an #$AdverseSocialAction.  (#$priorPositiveConnectionWithHarmed ADVERSE-ACT AGENT) is true in a temporally qualified context TEMPORAL-MT just in case it is true in TEMPORAL-MT that there exists a #$SomethingExisting SOMETHING which is an #$objectHarmed in ADVERSE-ACT and it is also true in TEMPORAL-MT that either (#$was (#$positiveVestedInterest SOMETHING AGENT)) or (#$was (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT SOMETHING)):  i.e., (#$priorPositiveConnectionWithHarmed ADVERSE-ACT AGENT) is true in a temporal context iff something is harmed in ADVERSE-ACT which either was a positive interest of AGENT at some time prior to ADVERSE-ACT, or had a positive interest in AGENT at some time prior to ADVERSE-ACT.")
(comment AdHocReportTemplate "The collection of report templates representing ad hoc data reports.")
(comment Selenium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of selenium; typically, these will be tightly bound into  form, but not necessarily.")
(comment Sunglasses "A specilaization of #$Eyeglasses.  Each instance of #$Sunglasses is a pair of glasses with dark lenses that can shield the eyes from bright light (such as sunlight).")
(comment Eyeglasses "A cpecialization of #$Eyewear.  Each instance of #$Eyeglasses is a pair of lenses mounted in a in frame designed to be worn on the face such that the lenses are suspended in front of the eyes.")
(comment durationOfMedicalEvent "<code>(#$durationOfMedicalEvent EVT DURATION)</code> means that the time elapsed between the min-start and min-stop of EVT is DURATION.  Or, if EVT is a medical procedure it is the time elapsed between the min-start and min-stop of its governing top level event.")
(comment StructuredKnowledgeSource-Public "The collection of all #$StructuredKnowledgeSources that are freely available to the general public")
(comment Bull-Cattle "The collection of all male bovines. A type of #$Bull-MaleHerdAnimal and #$Cattle-Domestic. The #$Bull-Cattle is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment (FemaleFn Cornish-Fowl) "The collection of all Cornish hens. A type of #$Cornish-Fowl and #$FemaleAnimal. The Cornish hen is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment (MaleFn Chicken) "The collection of all roosters. A type of #$Chicken and #$MaleAnimal. The rooster is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment (JuvenileFn Sheep) "The collection of all lambs. A type of #$Sheep and #$JuvenileAnimal. The lamb is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment Parakeet "The collection of all parakeets. A type of #$Parrot. The #$Parakeet is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment TabbyCat "The collection of all Tabby cats. A type of #$DomesticCat. The #$TabbyCat is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment Horse-Domesticated "The collection of all domesticated horses. A type of #$Horse and #$DomesticatedAnimal. The #$Horse-Domesticated is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment TropicalFish "The collection of all tropical fish. A type of #$Fish. The #$TropicalFish is a #$DomesticatedAnimalType.")
(comment successorGameOfInBracketPlayoff "Where GAME1 and GAME2 are both instances of #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors and are #$sportsEventInPlayoffs in a 'bracket' #$Playoff wherein each game except for the opening round games is preceded by exactly two games whose winner 'inherit' to the successor, (#$successorGameOfInBracketPlayoff GAME1 GAME2 SUCCESSOR) means that SUCCESSOR is the  #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors in the same #$Playoff which is the #$playoffSuccessors-Direct of GAME1 and GAME2.  This is the #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical of #$SucceedingGameInBracketPlayoffFn, which will ordinarily be used to reify the third argument.")
(comment Proposal "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork via #$GoalOrientedSpecification.  Each instance of #$Proposal is a potential agreement in the 'proposal' stage -- i.e., a potential agreement which is under consideration but which has not yet been adopted.  The making and consideration of #$Proposals is an important part of such activities as #$Negotiating and legislative #$Debate (qq.v.).  Examples of #$Proposals include instances of #$BidOnSale, job offers, proposed codes of conduct (including proposals for new #$Laws), and proposed punishments.")
(comment callForProposalsPostedAt "Where URL is a uniform resource locator expressed as a #$ControlCharacterFreeString, (#$callForProposalsPostedAt CALL-CW URL) means that there is an online posting with the information structure given by CALL-CW at URL.")
(comment contentOnFileAt "(#$contentOnFileAt AIS SYSTEM PATH) means that the information content denoted by the #$AspatialInformationStore AIS is the #$fileCopyContents of a #$HostedComputerFile accessible on the #$ComputationalSystem SYSTEM via the #$Pathname PATH.")
(comment SubmittingAProposal "The collection of all instances of #$SubmittingSomething wherein the #$infoTransferred is a #$Proposal, in the sense of an abstract #$PropositionalConceptualWork.")
(comment respondingProposal "(#$respondingProposal CALLING PROPOSAL-CW) means that PROPOSAL-CW is the #$infoTransferred in a #$SubmittingAProposal that happens #$inReactionTo the #$CallingForProposals-CommunicationAct CALLING.  I.e., PROPOSAL-CW is a #$Proposal submitted in response to CALLING.")
(comment BAAWithIDFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to create instances of #$BroadAgencyAnnouncement-CW using the ID strings used as their agency identifiers.")
(comment bAAHasID "The corresponding predicate of #$BAAWithIDFn.")
(comment CWEntitledFn "A function used for denoting instances of #$ConceptualWork by title.")
(comment cwEntitled "The corresponding predicate of #$CWEntitledFn.")
(comment CallingForProposalsFn "Function that denotes a #$CallingForProposals-CommunicationAct via the #$CallForProposals-CW that is its reified content.")
(comment callingForProposalsContent "The corresponding predicate of #$CallingForProposalsFn.")
(comment propertiesPanelEntry-WithPredicate "(#$propertiesPanelEntry-WithPredicate TERM PREDICATE TASK PROPERTY VALUE) means that an informational panel describing TERM when it is an argument to PREDICATE to a user working on TASK should include VALUE as a value for PROPERTY.")
(comment propertiesPanelEntry "(#$propertiesPanelEntry TERM TASK PROPERTY VALUE) means that an informational panel describing TERM to a user working on TASK should include VALUE as a value for PROPERTY.")
(comment ontologyForTask "(#$ontologyForTask ONT TASK) means that ONT is an ontology that plays a very relevant role in TASK.  Examples are an ontology that provides the vocabulary for a knowledge retrieval task or an ontology that is used to tag a corpus of documents in a document search task.")
(comment removeStartAndEndBracketsFromSchemaObjectFnTerm " A special case predicate that associates a SchemaObjectFn term encapsulating a URI with open and close brackets -- < > with the corresponding URI within the brackets.")
(comment HeartValveReplacement-SurgicalProcedure "The collection of surgical heart valve replacements.")
(comment CAEDocumentationPredicate "The collection of predicates whose values provide some form of documentation during CAE tasks.")
(comment valveRegurgitationSeverity "<code>(#$valveRegurgitationSeverity EVENT VALVE-OR-PROCEDURE VALVE-TYPE SEVERITY)</code> means that according to the information on VALVE-OR-PROCEDURE, a cardiac valve of VALVE-TYPE, that is associated with <code>EVENT</code> (an instance of #$CardiacCatheterization, #$Echocardiogram, #$Operation) the focal valve has the regurgitation severity SEVERITY.")
(disjointWith MedicalPatient SurgicalProcedureOrCardiacValve)
(disjointWith Agent-Generic SurgicalProcedureOrCardiacValve)
(comment KeyFieldQuery "The collection of all queries whose columns in a structured report may not be excluded from a run that runs a subset of the columns.")
(comment ReportGeneratorTemplate "The collection of report templates representing ad hoc data reports.")
(comment valveReplacementInvolvesImplantType "returns #$True if the operation contains a replacement procedure with an implant of of the specified type.  Returns #$False otherwise.")
(comment propertyValueAssociatedWithEvt "returns the value for a particular property that is associated with the indexed event in some way.")
(comment OWLPropertyPatientDomain "A specialization of #$OWLProperty.  Each instance of OWLPropertyPatientDomain is a property whose arg1 is typically a medical patient.")
(comment resultIsaArgIsa "(#$resultIsaArgIsa FUNC INT) means that the NAT resulting from a use of FUNC is a member of the same explicitly asserted collections that the term
in arg position INT is a member of.")
(comment binaryPredicateRestriction "The corresponding predicate to #$BinaryPredicateRestrictionFn.  (#$binaryPredicateRestriction PRED1 PRED2 THING PRED3) means that PRED3 is equivalent to a specPred of PRED1 with PRED1's arg1 restricted to just those that stand in arg1 in PRED2 with THING in arg2.")
(comment PredicateWithDomainContainedByPatient "A specialization of #$OWLProperty.  Each instance of OWLPropertyPatientDomain is a property whose arg1 is something directly associated with the patient such as an address or telephone number.")
(comment hospitalizationMedicationStatusForEvent-NonExpanded "<code>(#$hospitalizationMedicationStatusForEvent-NonExpanded EVENT MED-TYPE STATUS)</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the event <code>EVENT</code>, the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> has the status <code>STATUS</code> during the hospitalization that is associated with  <code>EVENT</code>.  This predicate is meant to be used in non-expanded datasets.  If the dataset is an expanded dataset use hospitalizationMedicationStatusForEvent instead.")
(comment medicalDiagnosisFocalAilmentAndBodyPartType "(#$medicalDiagnosisFocalAilmentAndBodyPartType DIAGNOSIS-TYPE  AILMENT-TYPE PART-TYPE) means that the DIAGNOSIS-TYPE is a diagnosis of AILMENT-TYPE on PART-TYPE.")
(comment AilmentType-NonSiteSpecific "the collection of types of ailments that are close generalizations of region specific types of ailments.  For example, #$AcuteDissection-AscendingAorta would not be a member of this collection because it is site specific, but its close, not site specific generalizations AcuteDissection and Dissection would be.")
(comment SpecificBodyPartType "the collection of body part types that are collections of specific parts of the body and not general regions or systems.  For example, #$LeftVentricle would be an instance of the collection, but #$HumanBody or #$CirculatorySystem would not.")
(comment DiseaseOfTheDescendingThoracicAorta "These specifically refer to diseases of the descending-thoracic aorta.")
(comment DiseaseOfTheDescendingAorta "These specifically refer to diseases of the descending aorta.")
(comment userAnnotationString "A predicate to allow users to annotate concepts.  In general this predicate is not designed for use by ontologists and its extent should be entirely customer created.")
(comment |time:intervalContains| "an OWL relation used to associate a temporal thing with another (non-point) temporal thing it properly temporally subsumes.")
(comment startsNoEarlierThan "(#$startsNoEarlierThan TEMPTHING1 DATE) means that TEMPTHING1 starts no earlier than the start of DATE.   This is the #$startsNoEarlierThanStartingOf relation with the arg2 restricted to #$Date.")
(comment startsNoLaterThan "(#$startsNoLaterThan TEMPTHING1 DATE) means that TEMPTHING1 starts no later than the start of DATE.   This is the #$startsNoLaterThanStartingOf relation with the arg2 restricted to #$Date.")
(comment stopsNoEarlierThan "(#$stopsNoEarlierThan TEMPTHING1 DATE) means that TEMPTHING1 stops no earlier than the start of DATE.   This is the #$endsNoEarlierThanStartingOf relation with the arg2 restricted to #$Date.")
(comment stopsNoLaterThan "(#$stopsNoLaterThan TEMPTHING1 DATE) means that TEMPTHING1 stops no later than the start of DATE.   This is the #$endsNoLaterThanStartingOf relation with the arg2 restricted to #$Date.")
(comment AntiRetroviralDrug "The collection of all antiretroviral drugs (types of drugs that stop or supress the action of a retrovirus). A type of #$DrugSubstance.")
(comment HAARTDrugCocktail "The collection of all HAART drug cocktails. A type of #$AIDSDrugCocktail.")
(comment Tab-TheCharacter "The tab character.")
(comment ReportGeneratorReportSpecification "Each instance of #$ReportGeneratorReportSpecification gives a description of how a particular report should be generated. At minimum, this description includes the relevant #$ReportGeneratorTemplate, the selection clause, and output filename and delimiter character")
(comment scheduledReportSpecification "(#$scheduledReportSpecification EVENT SPEC) means that during EVENT, a report based on SPEC is scheduled to be generated.")
(comment reportSpecificationTemplate "(#$reportSpecificationTemplate SPEC TEMPLATE) means that TEMPLATE is the template that should be used when generating a report based on SPEC.")
(comment reportSpecificationDelimiterCharacter "(#$reportSpecificationDelimiterCharacter SPEC CHARACTER) means that CHARACTER is the character that should be used to separate data when generating a report based on SPEC. Typical examples include #$Comma-TheSymbol and #$Tab-TheCharacter.")
(comment reportSpecificationSelectionSentence "(#$reportSpecificationSelectionSentence SPEC SELECTION-SENTENCE) means that SELECTION-SENTENCE is the sentence that should be used to identify the set of focal terms when generating a report based on SPEC. SELECTION-SENTENCE should have exactly one open variable, whose bindings will be the focal terms.")
(comment reportSpecificationClobberMultipleValues "(#$reportSpecificationClobberMultipleValues SPEC BOOLEAN) means that if we get more than one answer for a report cell while generating a report according to SPEC we should take the first one and ignore the rest (if BOOLEAN is #$True), or mark the report cell as containing multiple values (if #$False).")
(comment reportSpecificationOutputFile "(#$reportSpecificationOutputFile SPEC FILE) means that FILE is where a report based on SPEC should be written to.")
(comment reportSpecificationPlaceholder "(#$reportSpecificationPlaceholder SPEC PLACEHOLDER) means that PLACEHOLDER should be entered in any cell in a report based on SPEC for which no values are found.")
(comment reportSpecificationFields "(#$reportSpecificationFields SPEC FIELD) means that FIELD is the identification number of a field that should be included when generating a report based on SPEC. Cf. #$sKSFieldNamesWithOrder.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic CardiacValveFindingorHeartRhythm)
(comment HeartRhythm-DiagnosisOrFinding "The collection of all reports of a  #$MedicalCareProvider coming to a diagnosis or judgment about a #$HeartRhythm")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic MedicalProcedureOrData)
(comment KMF3OWLProperty "The collection of binary predicates that correspond to the KMF OWL properties.")
(comment KMF3OWLClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$KMFOWLClass is a collection that corresponds to one of the classes in the KMF3 OWL ontology.")
(comment KMF3OWLInstance "The collection of Skolemized entities that are the subjects and members of the KMF OWL classes in the KMF triple store.")
(comment PonziScheme "A type of financial fraud, in which early investors are paid off with the money paid in by later investors.  Because there is no real investment (and associated earnings), these eventually become unable to pay off their investors and collapse.")
(disjointWith Person MedicalDetailContainingEntity)
(disjointWith TimeInterval MedicalDetailContainingEntity)
(disjointWith PartiallyTangible MedicalProcedureOrData)
(disjointWith Reconstruction-CardiacValveRepair (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Oversewing (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith AnnuloplastyWithRing (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Plication-BicuspidLeaflet (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith ResectionOfPannus (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith CompleteAnnuloplastyWithRing (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Resection-CardiacValve (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Exploration-SurgicalProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith RootReconstruction (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Reorientation-CardiacValveRepair (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith ProstheticValveDebridement (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Plication-ValvularProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Debridement-VascularProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(disjointWith Thrombectomy (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(comment AfibSurgeryLesionData "The collection of data nodes about lesions received during surgery to correct atrial fibrillation or flutter .")
(comment afibProcedureHasAssociatedLesion "Relates an afib procedure to data about a lesion segment created during that event.")
(disjointWith Animal MedicalDetailContainingEntity)
(comment unemploymentRate "(#$unemploymentRate REGION NR) means that NR is the average unemployment rate of the #$GeographicalRegion REGION, where the unemployment rate of a region at a point in time is the quotient of the number of unemployed persons in the region and the region's labor force (that is, the sum of the number of employed and unemployed persons in the region).   For example, to express the fact that the United States' unemployment rate in 1996 was 5.4%, we can say in an Mt temporally qualified to (#$YearFn 1996) that (#$unemploymentRate #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica .054).")
(comment DecreaseOnSlotFn "<code>(#$DecreaseOnSlotFn SLOT)</code> denotes the collection of events in which something decreases its value on <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot. For example, (#$DecreaseOnSlotFn #$appraisedValue) denotes the collection of events in which some item decreases in appraised value.")
(comment indicatesInfectionType "relates an instance of InfectionData to the type of infection indicated.")
(comment CAEInfectionType "the subcollection of #$InfectionType specifically supported via #$indicatesInfectionType")
(comment Autopsy "A specialization of #$MedicalDiagnosing.  Each instance of #$Autopsy is an event in which  a dead animal is examined to determine or confirm the cause of its death.")
(disjointWith Situation MedicalDiagnosis)
(comment MedicalDiagnosis "The propositional output of #$MedicalDiagnosing events.  See also #$MedicalDiagnosisFn.")
(comment MedicalDiagnosing "The subcollection of #$Diagnosing that consist of the diagnosing of some medical condition after examination of a medical patient.  The output of these events will be instances of #$MedicalDiagnosis.  Instances of #$MedicalDiagnosing often involve instances of #$MedicalTesting.")
(comment Strontium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of strontium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment MatterTypeByPhysicalState "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState is a collection of instances of #$PartiallyTangible (q.v.) that are in one of the basic physical states of matter. Four significant instances of this collection are
#$Solid-StateOfMatter, #$Liquid-StateOfMatter, #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter,
and #$Plasma-StateOfMatter.  Although the chemical composition of a
substance does not change when its basic physical state changes, many
of its intrinsic physical properties do change -- including its density,
viscosity, brittleness, color, and size.  States of matter concern
the organization of matter at the molecular level, as determined by
temperature and pressure. Sufficiently large changes in temperature or pressure will cause matter in one physical state to transform into another (see
#$StateOfMatterChangeEvent).")
(comment intervalBetweenStages-EndToStart-Min "An assertion of the form <code>(#$intervalBetweenStages-EndToStart-Min INT-SPEC QUANT)</code> is used to represent the duration of an interval which will exist between the subsituations of instances of a given type of #$Situation.  Given the assertions <code>(#$sitTypeHasInterStageSpec SIT-TYPE INT-SPEC)</code> <code>(#$earlierStage INT-SPEC TEMP1)</code> and <code>(#$laterStage INT-SPEC TEMP2)</code> hold, in any instance of the sub-collection of #$Situation, <code>SIT-TYPE</code> any subsituation which falls under the #$TemporalStageSpecification <code>TEMP2</code> will begin only after a #$TimeInterval of duration <code>QUANT</code> has passed since the ending of any subsituation which falls under the #$TemporalStageSpecification <code>TEMP1</code>.")
(comment MedicalLaboratory "A specialization of #$Laboratory.  Each instance of #$MedicalLaboratory is a place equipped for medical research, experimentation or testing.")
(comment Laboratory "The collection of all laboratories. A type of #$HumanOccupationConstruct. Each instance of #$Laboratory is an area that facilitates performing scientific experimentation, research or testing.")
(comment cardinalityAtLeast "<code>(#$cardinalityAtLeast SET N)</code> means that <code>SET</code> contains at least N elements. Example: (#$cardinalityAtLeast (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$Cat #$mainColorOfObject #$BlackColor) 3) if and only if there are at least 3 black cats.")
(comment dataForValveEtiologyInProcedure "<code>(#$dataForValveEtiologyInProcedure EVT VALVE-TYPE ETIOLOGY-TYPE)</code> means that the  patient's <code>VALVE-TYPE</code> associated with <code>EVT</code> the focal valve has the etiology <code>ETIOLOGY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment hasVascularProcedureDevice "<code>(#$hasVascularProcedureDevice PRO DEVICE-TYPE)</code> states that the vascular procedure, <code>PRO</code>, was a procedure involving an instance of <code>DEVICE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typicalLocationTypeOfEventType "<code>(#$typicalLocationTypeOfEventType EVENT-TYPE LOC-TYPE)</code> means that for any given instance <code>EVENT</code> of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, it is reasonable to assume, in the absence of information to the contrary, that <code>EVENT</code> occurs at an instance of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$typicalLocationTypeOfEventType #$CookingFood #$Kitchen) means for any given instance <code>COOKING</code> of #$CookingFood, it is reasonable to assume, in the absence of information to the contrary (e.g. the information that <code>COOKING</code> is also an instance of #$BarbecuingFood), that <code>COOKING</code> occurs at an instance of #$Kitchen.")
(disjointWith Sphere RugbyBall)
(comment BatAndBallGame "#$BatAndBallGame is the collection of games in which the competing teams take turns in the role of attempting to bat a ball while the other team fields.")
(comment PeripheralVascularDisease "A specialization of #$VascularDisorder.  Each instance of #$PeripheralVascularDisease is a condition in which a large artery of the arm or leg is obstructed.")
(comment Arteriosclerosis "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Arteriosclerosis is a condition characterized by hardening of the arteries.  The most common form of arteriosclerosis is #$Atherosclerosis, which is arteriosclerosis caused by the presence of atheromatous plaque..")
(comment Arteriolosclerosis "A specialization of #$Arteriosclerosis.  Arteriolosclerosis a condition in which arteries are hardened due to hypertension and/or diabetes.")
(comment firstEventOrProcedureOfType "<code>(#$firstEventOrProcedureOfType EVT EVT-TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the first event of the type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> for the patient acted on in <code>EVT</code>.  This relationship is supported for morbidities, evaluation events and surgical and percuataneous procedures.")
(disjointWith MakingAMedicalIncisionInABLO VascularProcedure-OtherOrAorta)
(comment Prolog-ComputerLanguage "A #$DeclarativeProgrammingLanguage, introduced around 1972.")
(comment PlannerLanguage "A #$DeclarativeProgrammingLanguage designed by Carl Hewitt at MIT around 1969.")
(comment softwareParameterFromSyntax "A predicate corresponding to the function #$SoftwareParameterFromSyntaxFn.  <code>(#$softwareParameterFromSyntax X (#$SoftwareParameterFromSyntaxFn X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.  <code>(#$softwareParameterFromSyntax X Y)</code> means <code>Y</code> is the parameter corresponding to <code>X</code>.")
(comment MultiIndividualAgentNowDisbanded "This collection contains all the multi-individual agents that have the attribute of being disbanded.  It is reified solely for the purposes of decreasing the number of assertions and forward rules required for effective web search enhancement.")
(comment HospitalTransfer "#$HospitalTransfer is the collection of events in which a person is transported to a hospital.  In many cases, this involves leaving one hospital and going to another.  It also includes cases in which a person is brought to a hospital from the scene of an accident.")
(comment BinaryPredicateRestrictionFn "A binary predicate denoting function.  (#$BinaryPredicateRestrictionFn PRED1 PRED2 VALUE) returns a predicate that is a specialization of the arg1 predicate whose domain is restricted to just those that have VALUE in arg2 of PRED2. More formally,  

<pre>  

((#$BinaryPredicateRestrictionFn PRED1 PRED2 VALUE) A B) 

     iff

((#$Kappa (?X ?Y)
  (#$and
    (PRED1 ?X ?Y)
    (PRED2 ?X VALUE)) A B)
</pre>")
(disjointWith MedicalPatientOrDonor Situation)
(disjointWith MedicalPatientOrDonor CharacterString)
(comment standardFieldNameForQuery "(#$standardFieldNameForQuery QUERY STRING) means that STRING will be the default field name for reports utilizing the query unless otherwise specified.")
(comment standardReportTransformationForQuery "(#$standardReportTransformationForQuery QUERY TRANSFORM) means that TRANSFORM will be the default transformation for reports utilizing the query unless otherwise specified.")
(comment CADPresentation-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = No symptom, no angina, 2 = Symptom unlikely to be ischemic, 3 = Stable angina, 4 = Unstable angina, 5 = Non-STEMI, 6 = STEMI.")
(comment assistedReaderAssertionMtForTaskAndUser "<code>(#$assistedReaderAssertionMtForTaskAndUser TASK USER MT)</code> means that <code>MT</code> is the #$Microtheory in which assertions by USER while working on TASK will be made by the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader.  If there is a specification for this, assertions will be made in this #$Microtheory instead of in an Mt in the spindle specified with #$assistedReaderSourceSpindleHeadForTaskAndUser")
(comment CardiacValveProsthesis-Biological-Bovine "The collection of valve prostheses made from bovine tissue.")
(comment CardiacValveProsthesis-Biological-Porcine "The collection of valve prostheses made from porcine tissue.")
(comment closestEventOfTypePriorToWithinIntervalWithValueForOf "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 TYPE INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that  <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> 
       (PROPERTY EVT1 VALUE)</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment eventOfTypePriorToWithinIntervalWithValueForOf "<code>(#$eventOfTypePriorToWithinIntervalWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 TYPE INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that  <code>EVT1</code> is an event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> 
       (PROPERTY EVT1 VALUE)</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment doneBy "A very general #$ActorSlot predicate that relates events to the things that \"do\" them.  <code>(#$doneBy EVENT DOER)</code> means that <code>DOER</code> is a \"doer\" in the event <code>EVENT</code>: some activity on the part of <code>DOER</code> causes or carries out <code>EVENT</code>.  This predicate is agnostic as to whether <code>DOER</code> does <code>EVENT</code> intentionally or not.  Note that <code>DOER</code> need not even be animate or an agent; e.g. the famous volcanic eruption that buried Pompeii was #$doneBy Mt. Vesuvius.  Note also that an event might have more than one doer; consider a chess game.
<p>
See the specializations #$performedBy and #$bodilyDoer for cases in which the \"doer\" is, respectively, an #$Agent-Generic acting deliberately and an #$Organism-Whole behaving non-deliberately.")
(comment MedicalFinding "The collection of medical findings understood as the content of or statement of a medical discovery that the patient has a certain condition.")
(comment MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding "A specialization of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding is either a medical diagnosis (see #$MedicalDiagnosis) or a medical finding (see #$MedicalFinding).")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAfterWithValueForOf "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>EVT2</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> 
       (PROPERTY EVT1 VALUE)</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment IschemiaRisk-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = low risk, 2 = intermediate risk, 3 = high risk, 4 = unavailable")
(comment TestQualitativeResult-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  1 = positive, 2 = negative, 3 = indeterminant, 4 = unavailable")
(comment CardiologyReferenceOntologyConcept "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a concept that corresponds to one of the concepts in the Cardiology Reference Ontology.")
(comment CTAQualitativeResult-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which  0 = no disease, 1 = 1 vessel disease, 2 = 2 vessel disease, 3 = 3 vessel disease, 4 =indeterminant, 5 = unavailable")
(comment additionalFieldNameAndTransformationPairForQuery "(#$additionalFieldNameAndTransformationPairForQuery QUERY STRING TRANS) means that STRING will be a field name paired with the transformation TRANS for reports.")
(comment minStopDateForEvent "<code>(#$minStopDateForEvent EVT DATE)</code> means that DATE is the min-date of the event stop.")
(comment quantityChangeInterval "#$quantityChangeInterval relates an instance of
#$QuantityChangeEvent to the amount by which the relevant value
changed during that event.  (#$quantityChangeInterval
<code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> <code>INTERVAL</code>) means that the difference
between the #$startingQuantity and #$endingQuantity (qq.v.)  of
<code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> is
<code>INTERVAL</code>. <code>INTERVAL</code> may be positive or negative.  INTERVAL may be any sort of #$ScalarInterval, including fractions (e.g. #$Percent) and quantities (e.g. #$Dollar-UnitedStates).")
(comment ClosestWithPropertySubstitutionPredicate "the collection of binary predicates used as suggestions for \"closestPrior\" type predicates in the SRA.")
(comment ClosestWithPropertyEvaluationSubstitutionPredicate "the collection of binary predicates used as suggestions for \"closestPrior\" type predicates in the SRA where the prior event was an evaluation event.")
(comment NumberFrame "A frame for nouns that are represented as numeric value taking functions.")
(comment officialAirForce "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Organization to instances of #$AirForce.   <code>(#$officialAirForce ORG AIRFORCE)</code> means that the official air force of <code>ORG</code> is <code>AIRFORCE</code>.  See also #$AirForceFn.")
(comment FoodBlender "The collection of all food blenders. A type of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$FoodBlender is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment Dishwasher "The collection of all dishwashing machines. A type of #$CleaningDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$Dishwasher is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment BatteryCharger "The collection of all battery rechargers. A type of #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ExternallyPoweredDevice. The collection #$BatteryCharger is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment GarbageDisposal "The collection of all garbage disposals. A type of #$WasteConversionDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The concept #$GarbageDisposal is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment IceCubeMaker "The collection of all ice cube maker devices. A type of #$WaterCoolingDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance, and #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice. The concept #$IceCubeMaker is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment Refrigerator "The collection of all refrigerators, which are devices designed to keep the objects in their interiors cold, but not quite freezing cold. A type of #$RefrigeratedStorageDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$Refrigerator is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment VacuumCleaner "The collection of all vacuum cleaners. A type of #$DomesticCleaningTool, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The concept #$VacuumCleaner is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment ClothesWasher "The collection of all clothes washing machines. A type of #$CleaningDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$ClothesWasher is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment CoffeeMaker "The collection of all coffee makers, whether drip style, espresso, percolater, etc. A type of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, #$RigidPortableObject, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The concept #$CoffeeMaker is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment EspressoMachine "The collection of all espresso makers. A type of #$CoffeeMaker. The collection #$EspressoMachine is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment ClothesSteamer "The collection of all clothes steamers. A type of #$WrinkleRemovingDevice and #$ManufacturedGoods. The collection #$ClothesSteamer is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment Refrigerator-Freezer "The collection of all refrigerator-freezers, which are devices that have both refrigerator and freezer parts. These are commonly used to store food, and are often found as household objects. A type of #$RefrigeratedStorageDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$Refrigerator-Freezer is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment BreadMaker "The collection of all bread makers. A type of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$BreadMaker is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment Knife-Electric "The collection of all electric knives. A type of #$CarvingKnife and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$Knife-Electric is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment RoasterOven "The collection of all roaster ovens. A type of #$CookingVessel, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$RoasterOven is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment SlowCooker "The collection of all crock-pots. A type of #$CookingVessel, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance. The collection #$SlowCooker is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment MicrowaveOven "The collection of all microwave ovens, which are ovens that heat food and drink by innundating them with microwave radiation. A type of #$Oven, #$ManufacturedGoods, #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance, and #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice. The collection #$MicrowaveOven is a #$DeviceTypeByFunction.")
(comment FixedOrderCollection "A #$CollectionType and the collection of all and only those #$Collections whose own instances are all of the same fixed \"order\", where order is understood as follows.  Let individuals (i.e. instances of #$Individual) be \"zeroth-order\" things, collections of (only) individuals \"first-order\" collections, ..., and collections of (only) <code>N</code>th-order things \"<code>(N</code>+1)th-order\" collections. More precisely, then, a #$Collection <code>COL</code> is a #$FixedOrderCollection if and only if it is an <code>N</code>th-order collection (for <code>N</code> >= 1).
<p>
Instances of #$FixedOrderCollection include #$Individual, #$FirstOrderCollection, #$SecondOrderCollection, #$ThirdOrderCollection, #$FourthOrderCollection, and all specializations of these.  Specializations of #$FixedOrderCollection include all of the preceding examples except #$Individual and its specializations.
<p>
An example of a collection that is <i>not</i> fixed-order is #$AbstractThing, which is a varied-order collection since it contains both (zeroth-order) abstract individuals and (first-and-higher-order) collections.
<p>
Note that, although they are mutually disjoint, #$FixedOrderCollection and #$VariedOrderCollection (q.v.) do <i>not</i> constitute a partition of #$Collection: since the notion of order described above is not applicable to sets, #$Set-Mathematical (e.g.) and its specializations are neither fixed-order nor varied-order collections.")
(comment PersonTypeBySocialFeature "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PersonTypeBySocialFeature is a collection of people that share some property relating to human social status: role or rank (formal or informal) in the surrounding culture.  Most assertions should be made in terms of some specialization of this collection.  Members of this collection include: #$LowerMiddleClass, #$FourthGradeLevel, etc.")
(comment RoadVehicleType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicleType is a collection of instances of #$RoadVehicle categorized in some manner.  Notable specializations of #$RoadVehicleType include #$AutomobileTypeByBrand and #$RoadVehicleTypeByBodyStyle.")
(comment properPhysicalPortions "(#$properPhysicalPortions WHOLE PART) means that PART is a representative proper physical part of WHOLE, in the sense that the intrinsic physical properties of WHOLE are also properties of PART.  Proper physical parts of WHOLE which are not representative in this sense should not be related to WHOLE by #$properPhysicalPortions, but rather by #$properPhysicalParts or #$properPhysicalDecompositions (qq.v.).  For example, the SpaghettiSauce001 which is part of SpaghettiDinner001 would not be related to SpaghettiDinner001 by #$physicalPortions, since SpaghettiSauce001 differs from SpaghettiDinner001 in its composition (the latter has constituents -- noodles, parmesan cheese, and so on -- that the former does not have).  On the other hand, a #$physicalPortions of the dinner would include parts of all the constituents of the dinner.")
(comment StuffType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$StuffType is a collection that is stuff-like in at least one respect. A collection <code>COL</code> is stuff-like just in case there is some sense of 'part' according to which every part of an instance of <code>COL</code> is itself an instance of <code>COL</code>. More precisely, for a collection to be an instance of #$StuffType it is sufficient that there be some spec-pred <code>PARTPRED</code> of #$properParts (that is, some predicate <code>PARTPRED</code> for which<code> (#$genlPreds PARTPRED #$properParts)</code> holds), such that if <code>(#$isa OBJECT1 COL)</code> and <code>(PARTPRED OBJECT1 OBJECT2)</code>, then <code>(#$isa OBJECT2 COL)</code>. Here are two examples.  Consider #$Breathing. Take an instance of that, say a ten minute long period in which a person is breathing. Imagine some two minute snippet of that, one of its #$properTimeSlices (a spec-pred of #$properParts). That, too, is an instance of #$Breathing. So #$Breathing is a #$StuffType, since all #$properTimeSlices of an instance of #$Breathing are also instances of #$Breathing.
<p>
Consider #$Water. Take any instance of #$Water -- say the water in the Pacific Ocean. Now take any portion of that water -- say a handful of it that a person scoops up near Honolulu, one of its #$properPhysicalPortions (a spec-pred of #$properParts). That handful is itself an instance of #$Water. Hence #$Water is a #$StuffType, in virtue of the fact that all #$properPhysicalPortions of all instances #$Water are themselves instances of #$Water.
<p>
Other examples are: #$AspatialInformationStore, which is stuff-like with respect #$containsInformation; #$CharacterString, which is stuff-like with respect to #$subCharacterStrings; and #$List, which is stuff-like with respect to #$subLists. These examples are somewhat exceptional -- most #$StuffTypes are like the examples of #$Breathing and #$Water.  See #$ObjectType, for the contrasting (but not disjoint) notion of being object-like.")
(comment ExistingStuffType "A collection of collections, and a specialization of #$TemporalStuffType.  Each instance of #$ExistingStuffType is a collection of things (including portions of things) which are both temporally and spatially stufflike.  Division in time or space does not destroy the stufflike quality of the object (down to a certain granularity).
<p>
<code>(#$isa STUFFTYPE #$ExistingStuffType)</code> implies both (i) for most instances <code>STUFF</code> of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, for any proper physical part (see #$properPhysicalDecompositions) <code>PART</code> of <code>STUFF</code>, <code>PART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code> and (ii) for all instances <code>STUFF</code> of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, for most proper physical parts <code>PART</code> of <code>STUFF</code>, <code>PART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, every piece of wood is temporally stufflike: if W-168 is a piece of wood during 1996, then it's also a piece of wood for the one-minute time-slice 9:05am 7/7/96.  It's also spatially stufflike: if we take that piece of wood W-168 and cut it in half, we have two things which are both pieces of wood.  Since every piece of wood is both temporally and spatially stufflike, #$Wood is an instance of #$ExistingStuffType.  Other instances of #$ExistingStuffType include the collections #$IceCream, #$Diamond, #$WaxedPaper, and #$StriatedMuscle. See the comment for #$StuffType to learn more about the distinctions between, and the need for, these four collections: #$StuffType, #$ObjectType and #$ExistingObjectType.")
(comment stufflikeWRTPred "This predicate relates collections to the parthood relationships by which the collection is deemed \"stuff-like\".
<p>
<code>(#$stufflikeWRTPred STUFFTYPE PARTHOODPRED)</code> means that if <code>STUFF</code> is an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, <code>(PARTHOODPRED STUFF STUFFPART)</code>, and <code>STUFFPART</code> is above the granularity level for <code>STUFFTYPE</code>, then <code>STUFFPART</code> is also an instance of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>.
<p>
For instance, if one takes a proper temporal slice (see #$properTimeSlices) of an instance of #$Sightseeing, that temporal slice will also be an instance of #$Sightseeing (if it meets granularity requirements). Hence, (#$stufflikeWRTPred #$Sightseeing #$properTimeSlices).  In fact, for any instance, <code>TST</code>, of #$TemporalStuffType it will be the case that <code>(#$stufflikeWRTPred TST #$properTimeSlices)</code> and for any instance of #$ExistingStuffType, <code>EST</code>, it will be the case that (#$stufflikeWRTPred EST #$properPhysicalDecompositions).")
(comment CollectionClosedUnderSpecialization "A collection of collections.  Every instance of #$CollectionClosedUnderSpecialization is a collection <code>COLL-TYPE</code> with the following property: If the collection <code>COLL</code> is an instance of <code>COLL-TYPE</code>, then for any specialization <code>SPEC</code> of <code>COLL</code>, <code>SPEC</code> is also an instance of <code>COLL-TYPE</code>.  Notable examples include #$Collection and #$Thing.")
(comment FieldGoal "A generic method of #$ScoringPoints in the course of playing a #$SportsGame.  What counts as a #$FieldGoal in a sport is determined by the rules of that sport.")
(comment MakingAFreeThrow-Basketball "The collection of events in which a point is scored in basketball by making a free throw (an unchallenged shot from the foul line).")
(comment FieldGoal-Basketball "A method of scoring in #$Basketball-TheGame, in which the ball falls through the basket during the course of regular play (as opposed to a free throw).")
(comment ScoringPointsByMethod "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that facets #$ScoringPoints into sub-classes based on the method by which the points are scored.  What counts as a \"method\" is determined by the rules of the game involved.  For example, <i>making a free-throw</i> is recognized as a method of scoring according to the rules of basketball, but its arbitrary sub-collections (e.g., <i>making a free-throw during a night game</i>) do not count as scoring methods in the sense described here.")
(comment ScoringMethodInFn "<code>(#$ScoringMethodInFn GAME)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ScoringPointsByMethod that are, by definition of the rules of the game <code>GAME</code> ways of scoring points in playings of <code>GAME</code>.")
(comment scoringMethodsIn "<code>(#$scoringMethodsIn METHOD-TYPE GAME)</code> identifies <code>METHOD-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$ScoringPointsByMethod that are, by definition of the rules of the game <code>GAME</code> ways of scoring points in playings of <code>GAME</code>.")
(comment Gray-UnitOfMeasure "#$Gray-UnitOfMeasure is a measure of the amount of ionizing radiation absorbed.  One gray is the absorption of one joule of energy in the form of ionizing radiation by one kilogram of matter.")
(comment RadiationDose "#$RadiationDose is the collection of quantities of energy deposited in objects by ionizing radiation.")
(comment IonizingRadiation "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.  Ionizing radiation is radiation that is sufficiently energetic to ionize atoms or molecules by stripping them of electrons.")
(comment mutuallyCoherent "(#$mutuallyCoherent ARG1 ARG2) holds when the concepts ARG1 and ARG2 have a certain (nebulous) degree of semantic relatedness.  In its current implementation, it means that either ARG1 and ARG2 co-occur in some assertion or that they stand in some sort of generalization relationship (#$isa, #$genls, #$partTypes, or spatial or politicial subsumption).")
(comment CathLab "The collection of all cath labs, whcih are rooms intended for the performance of medical catheterizations for interventional or diagnostic purposes.")
(comment CardiacAssistDeviceTiming-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = in place at start of procedure, 2 = inserted during procedure and prior to PCI, and 3 = inserted after pci has begun")
(comment CardiacTransType-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = donor for cardiac transplant, 2 = candidate to receive a cardiac transplant, 3 = post-cardic transplant follow-up")
(comment axialTilt "<code>(#$axialTilt OBJ ANG-DIST)</code> indicates that <code>ANG-DIST</code> is the angle between the axis of rotation of <code>OBJ</code> and the plane perpendicular to the ecliptic of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment CycLExpressionType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$CycLExpressionType is a type (i.e. a subcollection) of #$CycLExpression.")
(comment DCathTreatment-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = none, 2 = medical therapy and/or counseling, 3 = PCI without planned CABG, 4 = CABG, 5 = Other cardiac therapy without CABG or PCI")
(comment SmokerIsOneNonSmokerIsZero-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the values Smoker and NonSmoker are encoded as \"1\" and \"0\", respectively.")
(comment AccessSite-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1= femoral, 2 = brachial, 3 = radial, 4 = other.")
(disjointWith MedicalPatient MedicalProcedureContainedByEvent)
(comment PCIIndication-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Immediate PCI for STEMI, 2 = 
    PCI for STEMI (Unstable, >12 hrs from Sx onset), 3 = PCI for STEMI (Stable, >12 hrs from Sx onset), 4 = PCI for STEMI (Stable after successful full-dose Thrombolysis) , 5 = Rescue PCI for STEMI (after failed full-dose lytics) , 6 = PCI for high risk Non-STEMI or unstable angina , 7 = Staged PCI , 8 = Other  .")
(comment CoronaryArteryDominance-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = left, 2 = right, 3 = co-dominant.")
(comment AdmitSource-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = left, 2 = right, 3 = co-dominant.")
(disjointWith CharacterString MedicalProcedureContainedByEvent)
(comment closestEventOfTypeAfterWithinIntervalWithValueForOf "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypeAfterWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 TYPE INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that  <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> 
       (PROPERTY EVT1 VALUE)</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment AnginalClass-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = no symptoms, no angina, 2 = CCS I, 3 = CCS II, 4 = CCS III, 5 = CCS IV")
(comment CKMBNM-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = 30-200 and 0 = <30 or >220. ")
(comment Lesion-SegmentID-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which ACC codes are assigned to coronary artery segments. ")
(comment reportGenerationEnabled "This specifies whether report-generator functionality should be available at all.")
(comment reportGenerationTemplateRootCollection "This specifies which templates should be used, if report-generator functionality is available at all. See #$reportGenerationEnabled.")
(comment Lesion-TIMI-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = TIMI-0, 2 = TIMI-1, 3 = TIMI-2, 4 = TIMI-3.")
(comment Lesion-PrevLesionTime-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = < 1 month, 2 = 1-5 months, 3 = 6-12 months, 4 = 1-2 years, 5= >2 years, 6 = unknown.")
(comment Lesion-InRestenosis-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Yes and 0 = No.")
(comment Lesion-LesionGraft-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 0 = Not in graft, 1 = Vein graft, 2 = LIMA, 3 = Other.")
(comment Lesion-LocGraft-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Aortic, 2 = Body, 3 = Distal.")
(comment Lesion-LesionComplexity-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Aortic, 2 = Body, 3 = Distal.")
(comment ClosureDevID-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which hemostasis methods are assigned ACC codes.")
(comment priorHistoryofEventWRTEvent "<code>(#$priorHistoryOfConditionWRTEvent EVENT EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that the patient treated in <code>EVENT</code> has a prior history of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>.  The length of time prior is typically implicit to the event-type and context of use.")
(comment HavingAVADInPlace "The extended event that consists of the duration of a ventricular assist device being located in a particular patient.  The start of the event corresponds to the insertion of the device and the event ends when the device is removed.")
(comment SuppressUnitOfMeasure-Simple-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the raw value from a unit of measure NAT is the encoded or decoded term.  Note: This transformation is defined only for unit of measure NATs that have a single argument.")
(comment Pre-VAD-RVEF-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which ventricular function is coded as  1 = Normal,
   2 = Mildly Impaired,
   3 = Moderately Impaired,
   4 = Severly Impaired
.")
(comment propertyStatusForNthVadForOperation "Indicates a compiled status with respect to some property of the Nth VAD relative to an indexed operation or other event.  (#$propertyStatusForNthVadForOperation EVT STATUS N PROPERTY) means that STATUS is a summary of the condition specified by PROPERTY, recorded on the Nth Ventricular assist device insertion in the hospitalization that EVT occurs.")
(comment ExplantRemovalReason-STS-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which CardiacAssistDeviceRemovalReason_transplant_operation_performed =  1  
WeanedOffPatientImproved  = 2
CardiacAssistDeviceRemovalReason_transfered_to_another_device = 3
CardiacAssistDeviceRemovalReason_device-related_infection  = 4
CardiacAssistDeviceRemovalReason_assist_device_malfunction =  5
CardiacAssistDeviceRemovalReason_end_of_device_use-life  = 6.")
(disjointWith IntentionalMentalSituation PostVADCranialBleeding)
(comment PCIDelayReason-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 
1 = difficult vascular access,
2 = cardiac arrest and/or need for intubation before PCI,
3 = patient delays in providing consent for the procedure,
4 = difficulty in crossing the culprit lesion during the PCI,
5 = other,
6 = none")
(comment CathLabVisit "A specialization of #$VisitingASite.  Each instance of #$CathLabVisit is an event in which some individual visits a cath lab and has one or more diagnostic or interventional vascular catheterizations.")
(comment CABGAnastomoticDeviceType-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which CABG anastomotic devices are coded as 1=glue, 2=magnets, 3=clips, 4=staples, 9=Other")
(comment StemiFirstNoted-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 
0 = first ECG, 
1 = subsequent ECG")
(comment RelatedToManyLogicalSchemata "The collection of PhysicalSchemas that have a one to many relationship to associated LogicalSchemas.  This is used primarily for gating forward inference.")
(comment StructuredParaphrase "The collection of all structured #$SententialConstituents either produced by, or structurally analogous to those produced by, the #$CycNLGenerationProgram.")
(comment AtomicParaphrase "The collection of all #$SententialConstituents with opaque internal structure either produced by, or analogous to those produced by, the #$CycNLGenerationProgram.")
(comment GenerateGKEGlossWrtMtFn "(#$GenerateGKEGlossWrtMtFn SENTENCE MT) denotes a #$StructuredParaphrase for SENTENCE using MT as the domain mt.")
(comment StructuredParaphraseFn "(#$StructuredParaphraseFn STRING SUBPHRASES) denotes the #$StructuredParaphrase whose surface string is STRING and whose internal structure is represented by SUBPHRASES.")
(comment SubParaphraseFn "(#$SubParaphraseFn STRING DENOT ARG-POSITION OPEN-TAG CLOSE-TAG OFFSET) denotes the #$AtomicParaphrase of DENOT whose surface string is STRING, whose HTML tags are OPEN-TAG and CLOSE-TAG, and that represents a paraphrase of the term at ARG-POSITION in a larger expression. STRING begins at the OFFSET-th character of the larger paraphrase of which this sub-paraphrase is a part.")
(comment UnlinkedSubParaphraseFn "(#$UnlinkedSubParaphraseFn STRING OFFSET) denotes the #$AtomicParaphrase whose surface string is STRING, which begins at the OFFSET-th character of the larger paraphrase of which this sub-paraphrase is a part. It is not itself a paraphrase of any part of the larger expression.")
(comment gkeGlossWrtDomainMt "(#$gkeGlossWrtDomainMt SENTENCE MT PARAPHRASE) means that PARAPHRASE is a #$StructuredParaphrase for SENTENCE using MT as the domain mt.")
(comment Lesion-StentType-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = drug eluting, 2 = non drug eluting,  3 = unknown")
(comment UnlinkedSubParaphraseWithHTMLFn "(#$UnlinkedSubParaphraseFn STRING OFFSET OPEN-TAG CLOSE-TAG) denotes the #$AtomicParaphrase whose surface string is STRING, which has HTML tags OPEN-TAG and CLOSE-TAG and begins at the OFFSET-th character of the larger paraphrase of which this sub-paraphrase is a part. It is not itself a paraphrase of any part of the larger expression.")
(comment cathLabDrugStatusWhenForCathOrPCI "<code>(#$cathLabDrugStatusWhenForCathOrPCI EVENT MED-TYPE WHEN-TYPE STATUS-EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the diagnostic or interventional cath <code>EVENT</code>, at qualitative time <code>WHEN</code> (either during the cath lab visit or at discharge) the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> has the status <code>STATUS-EVENT-TYPE</code> relative to some #$CathLabVisit that subsumes both the medication and the diagnostic or interventional cath.  E.g. it is contraindicated at discharge.")
(comment DCLocation-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1=Home, 2=Extended Care/TCU, 3=Other Hospital, 4=Nursing Home, 5=Hospice, 6=Other")
(disjointWith WeatherEvent FluidFlowFromAContainer)
(comment FluidFlowFromAContainer "The collection of instances of #$FluidFlow-Translation in which some fluid flows from a container.")
(comment FluidOverflowing "The collection of instances of #$FluidFlowFromAContainer in which fluid flows out of a container because fluid has been added to the fluid in an already #$Full container, resulting in spillage, or overflow.  Note that to qualify as an instance of #$FluidOverflowing, the capacity of the container must be exceeded; contrast with #$SpillingSomething, whose instances have many of the same characteristics as the instances of #$FluidOverflowing, but can be accomplished without the addition of displacing fluid, by, e.g., altering the orientation of the container so that the fluid is no longer contained, and gravity forces the fluid outward.")
(comment LiquidFlowEvent "The collection of instances of #$FluidFlowEvent in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is some instance(s) of #$LiquidTangibleThing.")
(comment LiquidOverflowing "The collection of instances of #$FluidOverflowing in which the fluid that is the #$primaryObjectMoving is an instance of #$LiquidTangibleThing.")
(disjointWith ElectricalEvent LiquidFlowEvent)
(comment SpillingLiquid "The collection of #$SpillingSomething events in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is some #$LiquidTangibleThing.")
(comment patientStartedOnMedTypeStatusWRTEvent "(#$patientStartedOnMedTypeStatusWRTEvent OP MED-TYPE ?STATUS) means that the MED-TYPE has STATUS true if the patient in OP started receiving medication of type MED-TYPE during the #$MedicalCareEvent OP and FALSE if they received meds but not of MED-TYPE.")
(comment Angiogram "A specialization of #$MedicalImaging and #$MedicalProcedure-Diagnostic.  Each instance of #$Angiogram is test that images blood vessels using x-rays.")
(comment Venogram "A specialization of #$Angiogram.  Each instance of #$Venogram is an angiogram wherein the imaged blood vessels are veins.")
(comment thingImaged "<code>(#$thingImaged CREAT THING)</code> means that in the #$ImageCreation event <code>CREAT</code>, the thing imaged is <code>THING</code>.")
(comment CarotidAngiogram "A specialization of #$Arteriogram.  Each instance of  #$CarotidAngiogram is an arteriogram performed to study the arteries that supply blood to the brain.")
(comment Catheterization-Diagnostic "A specialization of #$Catheterization and #$MedicalProcedure.  Each instance of #$Catheterization-Diagnostic is a catheterization performed in order to gather information to support a medical diagnosis rather than to treat a medical condition. Cf. #$CatheterizationProcedure-Interventional.")
(comment Arteriogram "A specialization of #$Angiogram.  Each instance of #$Arteriogram is an angiogram wherein the imaged blood vessels are arteries.")
(comment Ventriculogram "A specialization of #$Catheterization-Diagnostic.  Each instance of #$Ventriculogram is a diagnostic catheterization wherein the imaged objects is a ventricle of a heart.")
(comment OutpatientConvertedToInpatient "The collection of all #$MedicalPatients who begin an episode of care as outpatients but are converted to inpatients during the episode.")
(comment procedureOfTypePerformedPriorTo "(#$procedureOfTypePerformedPriorTo EVENT1 TYPE EVENT2) means that EVENT1 is a procedure that is an instance of TYPE, and it started before EVENT2 started.  Both EVENT1 and EVENT2 focally involved the same patient.")
(comment getOpIdForComplication "<code>(minDateOfOperationForComplication COMP URI)</code> means that the complication, <code>COMP</code>, is a complication of an operation that has the URI <code>URI</code>. ")
(comment opHasPostEventOfType "This means that the post-op event's min-start date is later than the max-stop date of the operation")
(comment mortalityStatusWithinIntervalWRTEvt "<code>(#$mortalityStatusWithinIntervalWRTEvt EVENT DURATION STATUS)</code> means that The patient treated in EVENT within the DURATION after the starting date of EVENT has the mortality status STATUS.")
(comment NLAgreementPredicate "The collection of all predicates that specify strings whose grammatical attributes (person, number, gender) are useful to know for the purpose of generating correct subject-verb agreement.  This includes both semantic predicates like #$nameString and part-of-speech predicates like #$singular.")
(comment nameString-Plural "This predicate should be used for names of individuals that trigger plural verb agreement, such as (the) \"Oakland Raiders\".  The \"the\" part should be left out, because these names can sometimes appear without \"the\", as in \"How about those Raiders?\" and \"a Raiders fan\".  In other words, the string should be an N-bar, in the sense that it is compatible with a preceding determiner.  This predicate should NOT be used with apparently plural names like \"Abbott Laboratories\", because these trigger *singular* verb agreement, e.g. \"Abbott Laboratories is/*are working on a cure for cancer.\"")
(disjointWith Heart-LocusOfFeelings PhysicalSituation)
(comment SetOfValuesOfFn "(#$SetOfValuesOfFn LOGICAL-FIELD-VALUE) denotes the set of zero or more values of LOGICAL-FIELD-VALUE in the current context.")
(comment NLIndexAttribute "The collection of NL attributes that determine pronoun form: person, number, and gender.  These also determine subject-verb agreement.  The name INDEX is a reference to HPSG (Pollard and Sag 1994), in which the INDEX slot of a sign carries these features.  INDEX features can be contrasted with CONCORD features; the CONCORD features are case, number, and gender, and determine NP-internal agreement, rather than pronoun and subject-verb agreement (Wechsler and Zlatic, 1999, 2001, 2003).")
(comment reportVariantLFIHasOverridingQuery "<code>(#$reportVariantLFIHasOverridingQuery TEMPLATE LFI QUERY-SPEC)</code> means that for the logical field indexical <code>LFI</code>, the report generator template variant <code>TEMPLATE</code> has the overriding query value: <code>QUERY-SPEC</code>.")
(comment reportVariantLFIHasOverridingTransformation "<code>(#$reportVariantLFIHasOverridingTransformation TEMPLATE LFI TRANS)</code> means that for the logical field indexical <code>LFI</code>, the report generator template variant <code>TEMPLATE</code> has the overriding transformation value: <code>TRANS</code>.")
(comment ReportGeneratorTemplateVariant "The collection of report templates representing reports that vary from original report definitions primarily in that they specify overriding queries and transformations for certain logical fields.")
(comment LogicalFieldValueWithFieldNameFn "(#$TheLogicalFieldValueFn SCHEMA NAME) denotes an indexical referent in SCHEMA that is the value, after encoding, of the field with the field name NAME in the corresponding physical schema.")
(comment Nt-TheSuffix "This is an unusual suffix in that it only attaches to inflected forms, rather than #$baseForm forms. Indeed, many linguists have analyzed it as a clitic instead of a suffix.  But the idea that this is a suffix rather than a clitic was argued for by Zwicky and Pullum (1983) in Language, on the following grounds: (A) \"n't\" is very picky about what it attaches to (only finite auxiliary verbs, not any verb that can precede \"not\", such as \"try\"); (B) there are arbitrary gaps in the paradigm (*amn't, *mayn't); (C) there are morphological idiosynracies (won't, shan't, can't); (D) there are semantic idiosynracies: mustn't means must(not) but can't means not(can).")
(comment Boolean-NoData-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"1\" and \"2\", respectively.")
(comment situationORPITTypeHasFocalObjectType "(#$situationORPITTypeHasFocalObjectType TYPE OBJECT-TYPE) means that instances of TYPE involve an instance of OBJECT-TYPE as one of its focal objects.  This means that instances of TYPE typically involve instances of OBJECT-TYPE or are about OBJECT-TYPE in some central way.  For example, the situation type \"TroubleshootingAnAirconditioningUnit\", has as its focal object type #$AirConditioner.  An instruction manual for troubleshooting an airconditioning unit also has as its focal object type #$AirConditioner.")
(comment previouslyTreatedLesion-CathPCI "(#$previouslyTreatedLesion-CathPCI  LESION means that LESION had previously been treated, per the definition of prior treatment put forth in the CathPCI coder's data dictionary.")
(comment closestHistoryPriorToStopDateWithStatus "<code>(#$closestHistoryPriorToWithStatus HIST EVT2 STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that <code>HIST</code> is the nearest #$PastPatientHistory prior to <code>EVT2</code>'s max date of the stop date that contains an instance of <code>STATUS-TYPE</code>.")
(comment reportHasVariant "<code>(#$reportHasVariant REP-TEMPLATE VARIANT-TEMPLATE)</code> means that <code>VARIANT-TEMPLATE</code> is a variant of <code>REP-TEMPLATE</code> that overrides values for queries and transformations associated with logical fields in <code>REP-TEMPLATE</code>.")
(comment reportGeneratorSKSWithName "(#$reportGeneratorSKSWithName SKS NAME) means that SKS was created as a report definition template and was assigned NAME.")
(comment kSHasQueryForLogicalFieldIndexical "(#$kSHasQueryForLogicalFieldIndexical KS LFI QUERY) means that KS has a logical field indexical LFI whose value is provided by QUERY.")
(comment kSVariantHasFieldQueryWFocalArgPosAndTransformation "<code>(#$kSVariantHasFieldQueryWFocalArgPosAndTransformation KS-VARIANT LFI NEW-FIELD-NAME QUERY TRANSFORMATION)</code> means that <code>KS-VARIANT</code> has a field with <code>NEW-FIELD-NAME</code> that has a semantics defined by the logical field indexical <code>LFI</code> with a value provided by <code>QUERY</code> that undergoes <code>TRANSFORMATION</code> in the encoding statement.  <code>KS-VARIANT</code> thereby differs from the KS from which it is declared to vary (see #$reportHasVariant).")
(comment fieldEncodingWRTKS "The same thing as #$fieldEncoding with the addition of an argument position that references the top level knowledge source.  This allows us to associate different encodings with the same PS, LS, PFI, and LFI when those entities are reused in the context of a different top level knowledge source.")
(comment associatedWithPhysicalSchemaSourceMapAndLogicalSchemaSourceMap "(#$physicalSchemaSourceMap SCHEMA SOURCE) relates a physical schema (SCHEMA) to the knowledge source (SOURCE) where it is defined.  For example, the #$OFAC-main-PS physcial schema is defined in the #$OFAC-main-KS (#$physicalSchemaSourceMap #$OFAC-main-PS #$OFAC-main-KS).  A physical schema may have more that one source.")
(comment reportLFIHasFieldName "<code>(#$reportLFIHasFieldName TEMPLATE LFI STRING)</code> means that for the logical field indexical <code>LFI</code>, the report generator template variant <code>TEMPLATE</code> has the  field name: <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment reportPFIHasFieldName "<code>(#$reportPFIHasFieldName TEMPLATE PFI STRING)</code> means that for the physical field indexical <code>PFI</code>, the report generator template variant <code>TEMPLATE</code> has the  field name: <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment overridingNoResponseValueForPFIinKS "(#$overridingNoResponseValueForPFIinKS KS PFI VAL) means that, in the context of KS, the default no response value for PFI should be overridden and VAL inserted in its place.")
(comment compatibleReportTransformationForQuery "(#$compatibleReportTransformationForQuery QUERY TRANSFORM) means that TRANSFORM is a compatible transformation for reports utilizing the query.")
(comment PreOp-Diagnosis-AdHocDataQuery "The collection of all queries that return true or false depending on PreOp H & P diagnosis.")
(comment AdHocTemplate-Original "The collection of report templates representing reports defined in accordance with a particular specification, but that are available as the source for user variants.")
(comment operativeMedicationDosage "(#$operativeMedicationDosage OP MED-TYPE DOSE) means that the patient in OP received DOSE of MED-TYPE during the course of the event OP.")
(comment TransformationOfBooleanValue "This is the collection of situation types in which boolean values are transformed into other values in the context of SKSI encoding or decoding statements.")
(comment adHocReportSRAParameters "(#$adHocReportSRAParameters KS LFI PFI QUERY TRANS LABEL ORDER-NUM TYPE) means that KS is a report with a corresponding LFI and PFI that is associated with QUERY that should be encoded via TRANS whose output column is labeled LABEL and whose order is given by ORDER-NUM.  The TYPE determines whether or not the report is a variant of a previously defined report.  For variants, only the overriding field names, queries and transformations are returned.")
(comment kSHasFieldQueryWithTransformation "(#$kSHasFieldQueryWithTransformation KS FIELD-NAME QUERY TRANSFORMATION) means that KS has a field with NAME with a value provided by QUERY that undergoes TRANSFORMATION in the encoding statement.")
(comment AdHocReportVariant "The collection of report templates representing ad hoc data reports.")
(comment StandardReportGeneratorTemplate "The collection of report templates representing standard data reports.")
(comment defaultAutotypeSuggestionFromType "An instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate used to derive default typing information for new things introduced into Cyc's domain of discourse via automatic or semi-automatic knowledge acquisition methods.  <code>(#$defaultAutotypeSuggestionFromType COL #$isa)</code> means that, given some instance INS of #$Thing for which we can determine is either an instance or specialization of the collection <code>COL</code>, then, given the absence of any other evidence, we should conclude that <code>(#$isa INS COL)</code>.  <code>(#$defaultAutotypeSuggestionFromType COL #$genls)</code> means that, given some instance INS of #$Thing for which we can determine is either an instance or specialization of the collection <code>COL</code>, then, given the absence of any other evidence, we should conclude that INS is a #$Collection and that <code>(#$genls INS COL)</code>.")
(comment eventHasAssociatedCABG-CathPCI "(#$eventHasAssociatedCABG-CathPCI  EVENT means that a CABG was performed on the focal patient of EVENT during the  hospital visit during which EVENT occurs.")
(comment eventHasAssociatedOtherMajorSurgery-CathPCI "(#$eventHasAssociatedOtherMajorSurgery-CathPCI  EVENT means that a major operation was performed on the focal patient of EVENT prior to the  hospital visit during which EVENT occurs.")
(disjointWith Mass AorticValveArea)
(disjointWith Rate AorticValveArea)
(comment languagePublishedIn "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$PublishedMaterial that is also an instance of #$TextualPCW to a #$Language.  (#$languagePublishedIn CW LANG) means that CW has been published in LANG.  Note that a conceptual work may be published in multiple languages; thus #$languagePublishedIn is not a #$FunctionalPredicate.")
(comment closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueForOf "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> 
       (PROPERTY EVT1 VALUE)</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment Actinobacillus-Genus "A collection of #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment ComputerSoftwareLibrary-CW "The collection of all computer libraries which contain software modules.")
(comment ComputerDataLibrary-CW "The collection of all conceptual computer libraries which contain data but not software modules.")
(comment PCI-CathEvent-AdHocDataQuery "The collection of all queries that return data for indexed cath or PCI events.")
(comment hasHospitalVisit "This relates a patient's #$HospitalVisit to the patient's events that occur in the hospital during that hospital visit.")
(comment GrammaticallyEncodedDomainRestrictionType "This is a collection of the concepts/collections that are grammatically encoded in languages' pronoun systems.  For example, the interrogative pronoun 'who' and the indefinite pronoun 'someone' are used for variables that are restricted to the #$Agent-Generic domain, while their counterparts 'where' and 'somewhere' are used for variables restricted to the #$Place domain.")
(comment Safari "This is the collection of planned overland journeys in Africa with a focus on the activity of either hunting or taking photographs.")
(comment Conifer "A member of the Pinophyta division.  Usually a tree, usually evergreen.")
(comment TaxaceaeFamily "The collection of all members of the Taxaceae family.  The #$TaxaceaeFamily is a #$BiologicalFamily of #$Conifers commonly known as the \"yew\" family.")
(comment CommonYew "A specialization of #$TaxaceaeFamily. #$CommonYew is a #$BiologicalSpecies.")
(comment InternetTelephony "A specialization of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$ComputerNetwork).  Each instance of #$InternetTelephony is an event in persons communicate via voice through signals transmitted over an IP network.")
(comment Australopithecus "A specialization of #$HominidaeFamily and an instance of #$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment Ardipithecus "A specialization of #$HominidaeFamily and an instance of #$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment HomoHabilis "An instance of #$BiologicalSpecies and a subtaxon of #$HomoGenus.")
(comment MRSharedVocabularyTerm "The collection of instances of #$CycLTerm that comprise the shared vocabulary for use by all participants in the #$MachineReadingProject.  The terms have been defined by the evaluation team for that project.")
(comment MRAPITerm "The collection of instances of #$MRSharedVocabularyTerm that comprise the basic vocabulary for representing features of text and for interacting with any sanctioned domain specific inference engine used in the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment MRStarterRelationalVocabularyTerm "The collection of instances of #$MRSharedVocabularyTerm that denote \"starter\" relations (presumably cross-domain), as determined by the evaluation team of the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment MRNFLUsecaseTerm "The collection of instances of #$MRSharedVocabularyTerm that comprise the vocabulary specifically designed for representing readable and inferable facts about the #$NationalFootballLeague, a usecase for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment gameWinner "<code>(#$gameWinner GAME AGENT)</code> means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent <code>AGENT</code> is the winner of the instance <code>GAME</code> of #$GameEvent.  For example, that Deep Blue was the winner of Game 1 in its 1996 competition with Kasparof would be represented using this relation: <code>(#$gameWinner DeepBlueVKasparof1996Game1 DeepBlue)</code>.")
(comment MRSharedOntology "The \"received\" ontology (see #$Ontology) developed for use by all reading agents developed for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment gameLoser "<code>(#$gameLoser GAME AGENT)</code> means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent <code>AGENT</code> is a loser of the instance <code>GAME</code> of #$GameEvent.  For example, that Kasparof was the loser of Game 1 in its 1996 competition with Deep Blue would be represented using this relation: <code>(#$gameLoser DeepBlueVKasparof1996Game1 GaryKasparof)</code>.")
(comment PlayoffSeries "An important specialization of #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition.  Each instance of #$PlayoffSeries is a #$MultiSportsEventSportsCompetition in which a partial order is defined on the subsidiary competitions via the #$playoffSuccessors-Direct relation which maps two or more #$SportsEvents to single #$SportsEvents in a tree structure that converges to a final 'root' node, the #$PlayoffChampionship.  Where it is true the (#$playoffSuccessors-Direct PRIOR-GAME SUCCESSOR-GAME) and WINNER is a #$competingAgents-TopLevel in PRIOR-GAME and a #$winnerInConflict in PRIOR-GAME, it follows that (#$competingAgents-TopLevel SUCCESSOR-GAME WINNER):  moreover, no #$competingAgents-TopLevel who is a loser (#$defeatedInConflict) in PRIOR-GAME can be a #$competingAgents in SUCCESSOR-GAME.  Thus, the winners of games in the #$playoffSuccessors-Direct tree structure inherit as competitors to their games' immediate successor, and so on down the tree until the #$PlayoffChampionship determines a #$playoffWinners.")
(comment NFLGame "The collection of all NFL football games.")
(comment Chancroid "A specialization of #$SexuallyTransmittedInfection characterized by painful sores on the genitals of infected persons.")
(comment HaemophiliusDucreyi "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These small #$GramNegativeBacterium rods cause #$Chancroid, a
#$SexuallyTransmittedInfection.  These #$ProkaryoticCells grow poorly on most laboratory media.")
(comment GranulomaInguinale "A specialization of #$SexuallyTransmittedInfection characterized by genital ulcers.")
(comment FieldGoal-Football "A method of scoring in #$Football-American, in which the ball is kicked between the goal posts for three points.")
(comment ScoringATouchdown "A method of scoring in #$Football-American, in which the team with possession of the ball scores six points by moving part of the ball into into the opposing team's end-zone.")
(comment ScoringATwoPointConversion "A method of scoring in #$Football-American, in which the team with possession of the ball scores two points by moving part of the ball into into the opposing team's end-zone.")
(comment ScoringAOnePointConversion "A method of scoring in #$Football-American, in which the team with possession of the ball scores one point by kicking the ball between the goal posts.")
(comment ScoringASafety "A method of scoring in #$Football-American, in which the team with possession of the ball downs the ball inside their own end zone, awarding two points to the team without possession of the ball.")
(disjointWith ScoringOnAConversionInFootball FieldGoal)
(comment touchdownConversion "<code>(#$touchdownConversion TD CONVERSION)</code> identifies <code>TD</code> as the instance of #$ScoringATouchdown for which <code>CONVERSION</code>, an instance of #$ScoringOnAConversionInFootball, is the conversion event.")
(comment KickingABall "The collection of all instances of #$KickingAnObject in which the #$objectActedOn is an instance of #$Ball.")
(comment ScheduledQueryDaemon-CW "A program to run scheduled queries and record the results in the KB.")
(comment OpeningGameOfPlayoffBySeedsFn "Where PLAYOFF is a #$PlayoffSeries of a type with a 'seeded' opening round (see #$seedsCompeteInPlayoffsOfType), (#$OpeningGameOfPlayoffBySeedsFn PLAYOFF N M) denotes the opening game of PLAYOFF in which the Nth and Mth seeded teams compete.")
(comment SucceedingGameInBracketPlayoffFn "Where GAME1 and GAME2 are both instances of #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors and are #$sportsEventInPlayoffs in a 'bracket' #$PlayoffSeries wherein each game except for the opening round games is preceded by exactly two games whose winner 'inherit' to the successor, (#$SucceedingGameInBracketPlayoffFn GAME1 GAME2) denotes the  #$TeamSportsCompetition-Entire-SameCompetitors in the same #$PlayoffSeries which is the #$playoffSuccessors-Direct of each of the two games.")
(comment ProFootballSeason "The collection of all professional football seasons.")
(comment NFLRegularSeason "The collection of all NFL regular seasons.")
(comment NFLSeason "The collection of entire (i.e., from pre-season through the superbowl) NFL seasons.")
(disjointWith SportSeason-Whole SportPreSeason)
(disjointWith SportSeason-Whole SportPostSeason)
(comment MRNFLDSRSOntology "The #$subWorks of #$MRSharedOntology that comprises the ontology (see #$Ontology) used by the NFL DSRS developed for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment NFLPreSeason "The collection of all NFL pre-seasons.")
(comment SportPreSeason "The collection of all pre-seasons -- i.e., periods of time in a #$SportSeason prior to the regular season of that season, during which the outcomes of contests do not count for or against the record of the participants in the regular season.")
(comment preSeason "<code>(#$preSeason SEASON PRE-SEASON)</code> identifies <code>PRE-SEASON</code> as the pre-season of <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment regularSeason "<code>(#$regularSeason SEASON REG-SEASON)</code> identifies <code>REG-SEASON</code> as the regular season of <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment postSeason "<code>(#$postSeason SEASON POST-SEASON)</code> identifies <code>POST-SEASON</code> as the post season of <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment postSeasonGames "<code>(#$postSeasonGames SEASON GAME)</code> means that <code>GAME</code> is one of the post-season games in <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment preSeasonGames "<code>(#$preSeasonGames SEASON GAME)</code> means that <code>GAME</code> is one of the pre-season games in <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment regularSeasonGames "<code>(#$regularSeasonGames SEASON GAME)</code> means that <code>GAME</code> is one of the regular-season games in <code>SEASON</code>, an instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment NFLRegularSeasonGame "The collection of instances of #$NFLGame that take place during the regular season (see #$regularSeasonGames).")
(comment NFLPostSeasonGame "The collection of instances of #$NFLGame that take place during the post-season (see #$postSeasonGames).")
(comment NFLPreSeasonGame "The collection of instances of #$NFLGame that take place during the pre-season (see #$preSeasonGames).")
(comment SportSeason-Regular "The collection of all regular sport seasons.  A regular season is one that stands in contrast to a pre-season (see #$SportPreSeason) and a post-season (see #$SportPostSeason), in that it is the main part of a sport season, by virtue of either being a #$SportSeason-Whole that has no pre- or post-season, or by being the main proper part of a #$SportSeason-Whole (represented using the relation #$regularSeason) that follows a pre-season or leads up to a post-season.")
(comment RegularSeasonGame "The collection of instances of #$SportsEvent that are regular-season games of some #$SportSeason-Whole.  See also #$regularSeasonGames and #$SportSeason-Regular.")
(comment PreseasonGame "The collection of instances of #$SportsEvent that are games in the pre-season of some #$SportSeason-Whole (see #$preSeasonGames).")
(comment PostseasonGame "The collection of instances of #$SportsEvent that are games in the post-season of some #$SportSeason-Whole (see #$postSeasonGames).")
(comment NFLPostSeason "The collection of all NFL post-seasons.")
(comment SportSeason-Whole "A specialization of #$SportSeason.  Instances are entire sport seasons, covering not only the regular season (see #$SportSeason-Regular), but, when present, the pre-season (see #$SportPreSeason) and post-season (see #$SportPostSeason).  A #$SportSeason-Whole may also be a #$SportSeason-Regular, if the season has no pre- or post- seasons.")
(comment SportPostSeason "The collection of instances of #$SportSeason that are post-seasons (see #$postSeason) for some instance of #$SportSeason-Whole.")
(comment SportsSeasonTypeBySanctioningBody "A collection that facets #$SportSeason-Whole by the organization responsible for organizing and running that season.  Examples include #$NFLSeason, which is the collection of entire NFL football seasons.")
(comment gameInSeason "<code>(#$gameInSeason GAME SEASON)</code> means that the instance of #$SportsEvent GAME is a game played as part of the instance <code>SEASON</code> of #$SportSeason.  Note that a game may be part of multiple seasons, e.g., the annual Texas vs Oklahoma football game is part of the Big Twelve season, the Big Twelve South season, and the NCAA FBS season.")
(comment GameEventTypeByRoleInSeasonalStructure "A collection that facets #$GameEvent by whether its instances are played in the pre-, regular, or post-season of some #$SportSeason.")
(comment playoffSuccessors-Direct "(#$playoffSuccessors-Direct COMP-BEFORE COMP-AFTER) means that COMP-AFTER is the direct successor to COMP-BEFORE in the order dictated by a common #$PlayoffSeries, meaning that a 'top-level' competitor (see #$competingAgents-TopLevel) who is the winner (#$winnerInConflict) of COMP-BEFORE is guaranteed a position as a #$competingAgents-TopLevel in COMP-AFTER, and no loser (#$defeatedInConflict) in COMP-BEFORE can compete in COMP-AFTER.")
(comment satisfiesHeadSyntacticConstraintsForNCR "(#$satisfiesHeadSyntacticConstraintsForNCR NODE RULE) means that the #$SyntacticNode NODE satisfies all of the syntactic constraints (cf. #$NounCompoundRuleConstraint-Syntactic) imposed by the #$NounCompoundRule RULE on the head.")
(comment outputInputSituationTypesInCycleType-Weak "(#$outputInputSituationTypesInCycleType-Weak CYCLE-TYPE OUTPUTTING-TYPE INPUTTING-TYPE) means that, where CYCLE-INST is an instance of CYCLE-TYPE then, where OUTPUTTING-INST is an instance of OUTPUT-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, there exists some  #$outputs of OUTPUTTING-INST that is an #$inputs of some instance of INPUTTING-TYPE that is also a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, and that where INPUTTING-INST is an instance of INPUTTING-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST, there exists some #$inputs of INPUTTING-INST that will be an #$outputs of some instance of OUTPUTTING-TYPE that is also a #$properSubSituations of CYCLE-INST.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAtOrPriorToWithValueFor "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> (#$thereExists ?VALUE
       (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment LeftCoronaryArtery-Generic "The collection of all left coronary artery segments including the main left coronary artery and any of its named branches.")
(comment PercutaneousCoronaryIntervention "The collection of percutaneous intervention events that include procedures on coronary arteries or existing bypass grafts of coronary arteries.")
(comment TimeLimitedGameEvent "Game events which are played for a specified amount of time and at the end of that time, the competitors are ranked, or, in the case of a single-player game, the player's performance is assigned a final score or assessment.")
(disjointWith OvertimePeriodOfPlay RegulationPeriodOfPlay)
(comment OvertimePeriodOfPlay "The collection of all periods of play that are overtime, as opposed to regulation (#$RegulationPeriodOfPlay) periods.")
(disjointWith GameCompletedInRegulation GamePlayedIntoOvertime)
(comment RegulationPeriodOfPlay "The collection of all periods of play that are regulation periods, as opposed to overtime (#$OvertimePeriodOfPlay) periods.")
(disjointWith PlayingAGame Quarter-PeriodOfPlay)
(disjointWith PlayingAGame Half-PeriodOfPlay)
(comment GamePlayedInPeriods "A specialization of #$TimeLimitedGameEvent.  Instances are games whose time-limit is a function of the time (distinct from wall-clock time) assigned to distinct and well-defined sub-events, or periods, that comprise the game.  To relate a game to its periods, use #$periodsOfPlay.")
(comment periodClockDuration "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay to the quantity of time that is alloted for play during that period.")
(comment GamePlayedInThreePeriods "A specialization of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.  Instances are game events divided into three periods of play.")
(comment GamePlayedInHalves "A specialization of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.  Instances are game events divided into two halves of play.")
(comment GamePlayedInQuarters "A specialization of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.  Instances are game events divided into four quarters of play.")
(comment lastPeriodOfPlay "<code>(#$lastPeriodOfPlay GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>PERIOD</code> as the final period (see #$periodsOfPlay) in <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.")
(comment overtimePeriodsOfPlay "<code>(#$overtimePeriodsOfPlay GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>GAME</code> as the instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods of which <code>PERIOD</code>, an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay, is an overtime period.")
(comment periodsOfPlay "<code>(#$periodsOfPlay GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>GAME</code> as the instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods of which <code>PERIOD</code>, an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay, is a period.")
(comment regulationPeriodsOfPlay "<code>(regulationPeriodsOfPlay GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>GAME</code> as the instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods of which <code>PERIOD</code>, an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay, is a regulation (as opposed to overtime) period.")
(comment firstQuarterOfPlay "<code>(#$firstQuarterOfPlay GAME QUARTER)</code> identifies <code>QUARTER</code> as the first of four instances of #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay that comprise <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInQuarters.")
(comment secondQuarterOfPlay "<code>(#$secondQuarterOfPlay GAME QUARTER)</code> identifies <code>QUARTER</code> as the second of four instances of #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay that comprise <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInQuarters.")
(comment thirdQuarterOfPlay "<code>(#$thirdQuarterOfPlay GAME QUARTER)</code> identifies <code>QUARTER</code> as the third of four instances of #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay that comprise <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInQuarters.")
(comment fourthQuarterOfPlay "<code>(#$fourthQuarterOfPlay GAME QUARTER)</code> identifies <code>QUARTER</code> as the fourth of four instances of #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay that comprise <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInQuarters.")
(comment lastRegulationPeriod "<code>(#$lastRegulationPeriod GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>PERIOD</code> as the final regulation period that comprises <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.")
(comment firstPeriodOfPlay "<code>(#$firstPeriodOfPlay GAME PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>PERIOD</code>, an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay as the first of <i>n</i> periods that compries <code>GAME</code>, an instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods.")
(comment GamePlayedIntoOvertime "A specialization of #$TimeLimitedGameEvent.  Instances are games that continued after their regulation periods are over (typically due to a tie) and so continue into overtime.")
(comment GameCompletedInRegulation "A specialization of #$TimeLimitedGameEvent.  Instances are games that end at the end of their regulation time.")
(comment Quarter-PeriodOfPlay "A specialization of #$RegulationPeriodOfPlay.  This is the collection of all quarters of play that are #$periodsOfPlay in a game event.")
(comment periodClockCurrentTime "An instance of #$TimeDependentRelation used to represent, at a particular time <i>t</i> the official amount of time allocated to play in a #$PeriodOfPlay.  <code>(#$periodClockCurrentTime PERIOD TIME-LEFT)</code> identifies <code>TIME-LEFT</code> as that remaining amount of time for <code>PERIOD</code>.")
(comment Half-PeriodOfPlay "A specialization of #$RegulationPeriodOfPlay.  This is the collection of all halves of play that are #$periodsOfPlay in a game event.  Note that this is distinct from the notion of a half of a game, such as football or professional basketball, that admits of halves by virtue of having an even number of #$periodsOfPlay (see, e.g., #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay).")
(comment GameEventTypeByPeriodOfPlayType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$GamePlayedInPeriods into specializations whose instances all decompose into the same number of periods (see #$PeriodOfPlay and #$periodsOfPlay).")
(disjointWith KEClarifyingCollectionType GameEventTypeByPeriodOfPlayType)
(comment FIFASoccer-CW "The game of soccer as played at the highest level, according to the rules of the International Federation of Association Football.")
(comment PeriodOfPlay "The collection of all periods of play that, by virtue of the rules of the game, are the units of timed play that comprise a #$GamePlayedInPeriods event.  Examples include halves of college basketball games, quarters of football games, and periods of hockey games.")
(comment PeriodOfPlayTypeByCardinality "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$RegulationPeriodOfPlay into specializations by the number of instances that must be combined to comprise a complete #$GamePlayedByPeriods.  Instances include #$Half-PeriodOfPlay and #$Quarter-PeriodOfPlay.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAtOrPriorToWithValueFor "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypePriorToWithValueFor EVT1 EVT2 TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> beginning prior to or starting at the same time as <code>EVT2</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code>.  This entails that 
  <pre>
   <code> (#$thereExists ?VALUE
       (PROPERTY EVT1 ?VALUE))</code>
 </pre>

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment NFLGamePeriod "The collection of all NFL periods of play (see #$periodsOfPlay).")
(disjointWith ScoringPoints GameEvent)
(disjointWith ScoringPoints PeriodOfPlay)
(comment scores "<code>(#$scores COMPETITION SCORING)</code> means that <code>SCORING</code> is one of the #$ScoringPoints events that takes place as a part of the instance <code>COMPETITION</code> of #$Competition.")
(comment scoringPlayer "<code>(#$scoringPlayer SCORING PLAYER)</code> identifies <code>PLAYER</code> as the player who scores in <code>SCORING</code>, an instance of #$ScoringPoints.")
(comment eventOfTypeAtOrPriorToWithinInterval "<code>(#$eventOfTypeAtOrPriorToWithinInterval EVT1 EVT2 TYPE INTERVAL)</code> means that  <code>EVT1</code> is an event of <code>TYPE</code> prior to <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code>.  In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment hasCathLabVisit "(#$hasCathLabVisit EVT VST) means EVT is an event involving a particular patient that occurs during VST, which is a #$CathLabVisit by that patient.")
(comment gameHasNumberOfPeriods "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate that relates an instance <code>GAME</code> of #$GamePlayedInPeriods to the number of periods that comprise <code>GAME</code>.  <code>(#$gameHasNumberOfPeriods <code>GAME</code> <code>INT</code>)</code> is shorthand for  
  <code>(#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$periodsOfPlay GAME #$PeriodOfPlay INT)</code>.")
(comment eventOccursAtPeriodClocktime "<code>(#$eventOccursAtPeriodClocktime EVENT TIME)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> is an event such that there exists an instance <code>PERIOD</code> of #$PeriodOfPlay and a date <code>DATE</code> such that 1) <code>(#$properSubEvents PERIOD EVENT)</code>, 2) <code>(#$dateOfEvent EVENT DATE)</code>, and 3) at <code>DATE</code>, <code>(#$periodClockCurrentTime PERIOD TIME)</code> is true.")
(comment eventOccursDuringPeriodNumberN "<code>(#$eventOccursDuringPeriodNumberN EVENT INT)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> is an event such that there exists an instance <code>GAME</code> of #$GameEvent and an instance <code>PERIOD</code> of #$PeriodOfPlay such that <code>(#$properSubEvents PERIOD EVENT)</code> and <code>(#$nthPeriodOfPlay GAME PERIOD INT)</code>.")
(comment nthPeriodOfPlay "Where <code>GAME</code> is an instance of #$GamePlayedInPeriods, <code>PERIOD</code> is an instance of #$PeriodOfPlay and <code>INT</code> is an instance of #$PositiveInteger, <code>(#$nthPeriodOfPlay GAME PERIOD INT)</code> identifies <code>PERIOD</code> as the <code>INT</code>th #$periodsOfPlay that occurs in <code>GAME</code>.")
(comment PreMaritalSexualBehavior "The collection of all instances of #$SexualBehavior in which at least one of the participants is not #$Married and has not been married in the past.")
(comment Seduction "The collection of all instances of #$SexualBehavior in which one of the participants deliberately entices the other to engage in human sexual behavior.")
(comment seducer "The predicate #$seducer relates a seduction to the agent who initiated the occurrence.  (#$seducer EVENT AGENT) means that the agent AGENT initiated the #$Seduction.  For example, (#$seducer SeductionOfJuliusCaesar #$Cleopatra-HistoricPerson) would claim that Cleopatra VII was the seductress in the seduction of Roman Emperor Julius Caesar.")
(comment seduced "The predicate #$seduced relates a seduction to the targeted agent in the occurrence.  (#$seduced EVENT AGENT) means that the agent AGENT who was the one persuaded by the person in the #$seducer role in the #$Seduction.  For example, (#$seduced SeductionOfJuliusCaesar #$JuliusCaesar-HistoricPerson) would claim that Julius Caesar was persuaded into intimacy with Cleopatra VII by her.")
(disjointWith Game-LowScoreWins Game-HighScoreWins)
(comment MultiPartyGame "The collection of all instances of #$Game typically played by two or more #$competingAgents (either #$Person or #$Team).")
(disjointWith NonTeamGame TwoPersonGame)
(comment NFLRulesFootball "The game of football, as played by NFL rules.")
(disjointWith Game-TiesDisallowed Game-TiesAllowed)
(comment Game-LowScoreWins "The collection of instances of #$MultiPartyGame in which the rules dictate that whichever competitor has the lowest score at some specific point is the winner.  Notable instances include #$Golf and popular basketball derivatives, such as HORSE and PIG.")
(comment Game-HighScoreWins "The collection of instances of #$MultiPartyGame in which the rules dictate that whichever competitor has the highest score at some specific point is the winner.")
(comment OneOnOneBasketball-TheGame "A version of basketball that involves one person competing against another, rather than teams.")
(comment GameWithTwoCompetitors "The collection of all instances of #$MultiPartyGame whose rules dictate that there are exactly two #$competingAgents-TopLevel when played.")
(comment deathOf "An #$ActorSlot and specialization of #$doneBy that relates a given living thing (see #$BiologicalLivingObject) to the event of its death (see #$DyingOfBLO). (#$deathOf DEATH BLO) means that DEATH is the event of BLO's dying.")
(comment DyingOfBLO "A #$PunctualEventType and a specialization of both #$BiologicalProcess and #$SingleDoerAction (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$DyingOfBLO is an event of some #$BiologicalLivingObject's dying.  For the more specific collection of deaths of whole organisms, see #$Dying.  Also see #$deathOf.")
(comment ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState "A subcollection of #$TimeDependentCollection.  Each instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState is a collection of things in a similar intrinsic state.  Each instance represents a state in which some object can be. Instances of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState include #$Device-On, #$OffHook as well as states that living objects can be in like #$EndosporeState, or #$Deceased.")
(comment rdfURI "<code>(#$rdfURI THING URI)</code> means that URI, when considered as an #$RDF-ResourceDescriptionFramework identifier, denotes <code>THING</code>.")
(comment Game-TiesAllowed "The collection of instances of #$MultiPartyGame whose rules allow for the provision that the game may end with a tie among competitors.")
(comment Game-TiesDisallowed "The collection of instances of #$MultiPartyGame whose rules dictate that the game not end in a tie.")
(comment infectionTypeResistantToPharmaceuticalType "<code>(#$infectionTypeResistantToPharmaceuticalType INF-TYPE MED-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the infection type <code>INF-TYPE</code> is reistant to being treated by medication <code>MED-TYPE</code>.")
(comment FormulaArgFn "A binary function that returns an instance of #$CycLTerm when given an instance of #$NonNegativeInteger and an instance of #$CycLFormula as arguments.  (#$FormulaArgFn N RELATION-EXPRESSION) denotes the term appearing as the Nth argument within RELATION-EXPRESSION. (Note that RELATION-EXPRESSION may be a sentence or a NAT). For example:
<p>
(#$FormulaArgFn 2 (#$loves #$Gilbert #$Muffet)) and
(#$FormulaArgFn 1 (#$BirthFn #$Muffet))
<p>
both denote #$Muffet.")
(comment sksiLaterThanOrCooriginatingWith "#$sksiLaterThanOrCooriginatingWith is intended to only be solved via an external knowledge source.  <code>(#$sksiLaterThanOrCooriginatingWith LATE-DATE EARLY-DATE)</code> is true when <code>LATE-DATE</code> and <code>EARLY-DATE</code> are #$Dates, and <code>LATE-DATE</code> either starts at <code>EARLY-DATE</code> or after <code>EARLY-DATE</code> is over.")
(comment closestEventPriorToWithinIntervalWithValueForOf "<code>(#$closestEventPriorToWithinIntervalWithValueForOf EVT1 EVT2 INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE )</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event prior to <code>EVT2</code> within <code>INTERVAL</code> that has some value for <code>PROPERTY</code> and <code>VALUE</code> is that value.  In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment homeVenueOfTeam "(#$homeVenueOfTeam  TEAM VENUE) means that VENUE is the home venue of the sports team, TEAM.")
(comment performancesDisjoint "<code>(#$performancesDisjoint WORK1 WORK2)</code> means that the instances <code>WORK1</code> and <code>WORK2</code> of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork are such that they have no performances in common.  For example, <code>(#$performancesDisjoint Macbeth-ThePlay AMidsummersNightDream-ThePlay)</code> holds, as no performance of Macbeth is also a performance of A Midsummers Night Dream.")
(comment ScoringOnAReturnedConversionAttempt "A method of scoring in college football in which the defense returns a fumbled, intercepted, or blocked-kick ball into the opponent's end-zone, where that fumble recovery, interception, or block marks the end of an attempted conversion (see #$ScoringOnAConversionInFootball) by the offense.")
(comment ScoringOnAConversionInFootball "The collection of all instances of scoring in #$Football-American that are conversions of touchdowns -- i.e., successful attempts to \"tack on\" points to those scored to a touchdown that occured just prior. To relate a conversion to its touchdown, use #$touchdownConversion.")
(comment TouchdownTypeByRelationshipToSubsequentPATAttemptOutcomeOrAbsenceThereof "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that partitions #$ScoringATouchdown into three sub-collections: #$TouchdownNotSucceededByASuccessfulConversionAttempt, the collection of all touchdowns that are never succeeded by a conversion; #$TouchdownSucceededByASuccessfulPAT, the collection of touchdowns that are succeeded by a 1-point conversion; and #$TouchdownSucceededByASuccessfulTwoPointConversionAttempt, the collection of touchdowns that are succeeded by a 2-point conversion.")
(comment TouchdownSucceededByASuccessfulTwoPointConversionAttempt "The collection of touchdowns that are succeeded by a 2-point conversion.")
(comment TouchdownSucceededByASuccessfulPAT "The collection of touchdowns that are succeeded by a 1-point conversion.")
(comment TouchdownNotSucceededByASuccessfulConversionAttempt "The collection of all touchdowns that are never succeeded by a conversion.")
(comment touchdownConversionAttempt "<code>(#$touchdownConversionAttempt TD PLAY)</code> means that <code>PLAY</code> is an attempt to score a conversion for the touchdown <code>TD</code>.")
(comment HuntingOfAnimal "A specialization of #$Foraging.  Each instance of #$HuntingOfAnimal is an event in which a hunter searches for animals in order to and capture or kill them.")
(comment ExternalResourceSupportVocabularyTerm "The collection of instances of #$CycLTerm that have been added to the CycL vocabulary solely to support the mappings of specific external knowledge sources into Cyc, either by virtue of having shared semantics with a term from that source (see, e.g., #$synonymousExternalConcept) or by contributing the axiomatization of the mapped vocabulary.  CycL terms should be tagged as instances of this collection only if their addition to the KB is not justified beyond the specific mapping task in question.  For example, the term #$NFLGame was introduced to facilitate a specific mapping task for #$MachineReadingProject; however NFL games are of general interest, and we would anticipate reuse of this term and not include it in this class of terms.  However, #$TouchdownNotSucceededByASuccessfulConversionAttempt is an instance of this class of terms: it was only introduced to be a target for a term of the source ontology, as it is a 'mix-in' whose semantics we would have otherwise represented as a rule.")
(disjointWith TieGame NFLPostSeasonGame)
(comment NFLGameTeamSummaryScore "A collection whose instances are objects that encapsulate information on, and used used by the #$MRNFLDSRSOntology inference engine to do probabilistic reasoning about, how a given NFL team scored during a given football game.")
(comment gameSummaryScores "<code>(#$gameSummaryScores GAME SUMMARY)</code> identifies <code>GAME</code> as the instance of #$NFLGame for which <code>SUMMARY</code> is the #$NFLGameTeamSummaryScore.")
(comment gameFinalSummaryScores "<code>(#$gameSummaryScores GAME SUMMARY)</code> identifies <code>GAME</code> as the instance of #$NFLGame for which <code>SUMMARY</code> is the #$NFLGameTeamSummaryScore.")
(comment diagnosticProcedureSubsumesDiagnosis "A typed spec-pred of #$subEvents.  (#$diagnosticProcedureSubsumesDiagnosis PROCEDURE DIAGNOSING) means that the #$MedicalProcedure-Diagnostic PROCEDURE situationally subsumes the #$MedicalDiagnosing event, DIAGNOSING.")
(disjointWith Area Pressure)
(comment drugTypeMolecularInstancesBindToMoleculeTypeInstances "Where SUBS-TYPE is a specialization of #$DrugSubstance and MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$Molecule, (#$drugTypeMolecularInstancesBindToMoleculeTypeInstances SUBS-TYPE MOL-TYPE) means that molecules of instances of SUBS-TYPE bind to molecules of MOL-TYPE under optimal or pharmaceutically intended conditions.")
(comment SummaryScoreCountSlot "The collection of instances of #$BinaryPredicate used by the NFL DSRS to calculate partial or complete counts of scoring events at specific points in time for specific teams in specific games.")
(comment SummaryScoreCompleteCountSlot "The collection of instances of #$SummaryScoreCountSlot used by the NFL DSRS to calculate exact counts of scoring events at specific points in time for specific teams in specific games.")
(comment SummaryScorePartialCountSlot "The collection of instances of #$SummaryScoreCountSlot used by the NFL DSRS to calculate partial counts of scoring events at specific points in time for specific teams in specific games.")
(comment eventOfTypeAfterWithinIntervalWithLowestValueForOf "<code>(#$eventOfTypeAfterWithinIntervalWithLowestValueForOf EVT TYPE INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that there exists an event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>EVT</code> occurring within <code>INTERVAL</code> after <code>EVT2</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property <code>PROPERTY</code>, where no other event of type <code>TYPE</code> occurs during that period with a lower value for property <code>PROPERTY</code>. 

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment Leuprorelin "#$Leuprorelin is a gonadotropin-releasing hormone agonist used in the treatment of prostate cancer, endometriosis, uterine fibroids, and premature puberty.  (LinkedLife DB http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment InterferonBeta-1b "#$InterferonBeta-1b is a drug in the interferon family used to treat the relapsing-remitting and secondary-progressive forms of multiple sclerosis.  It is approved for use after the first MS event.  It is administered by sub-cutaneous injectin and has been shown to slow the advance of the afflication as well as reduce the frequency of the attacks.  Studies have determined that interferon-beta improves the integrity of the blood-brain barrier (which generally breaks down in MS patients). (LinkedLife DB http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment Predinsolone "The active metabolite of #$Prednisone, #$Prednisolone is used for the treatment of primary or secondary adrenocortical insufficiency, such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia and thyroiditis.  It is Also used to treat psoriatic arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, bursitis, acute gouty arthritis and epicondylitis.  Also indicated for treatment of systemic lupus eytematosus, and pemphigus and acute rhematic carditis.  It also can be used in the treatment of leukemias, lymphomas, thrombocytopenia purpura and autoimmune hemolytic anemia, as well as celiac disease, insulin resistance, ulcerative colitis and liver disorders. (LinkedLife DB http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment Ketoprofen "Ketoprofen (RS)2-propionic acid is one of the #$PropionicAcid class of non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs with analgesic and antipyretic effects.  It acts by inhibiting the body's production of prostaglandin.  Ketoprofen was available over-the-counter in the United States, but the product has been discontinued.  It remains available by prescription.  It is used in the treatment of pain (muscular and rheumatic), sprains, strains, backache and neuralgia and for the management of the signs and symptoms of rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis.")
(comment Rhodamine6G "A chemical compound and fluorescent dye, often used as a tracer dye to determine rate and direction of transport in biotechnology applications.  (Wikipedia http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodamine_6G)")
(comment eventOfTypeAfterWithinIntervalWithHighestValueForOf "<code>(#$eventOfTypeAfterWithinIntervalWithHighestValueForOf  EVT TYPE INTERVAL PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means thatthere exisits an event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>EVT</code> occurring within <code>INTERVAL</code> after <code>EVT2</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property <code>PROPERTY</code>, where no other event of type <code>TYPE</code> occurs during that period with a higher value for property <code>PROPERTY</code>. 

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment eventOfTypeAfterWithinBoundsWithHighestValueForOf "<code>(#$eventOfTypeAfterWithinBoundsWithHighestValueForOf EVT TYPE LOW-BOUND HIGH-BOUND PROPERTY VALUE)</code> means that there exists an event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>EVT</code> occurring no sooner than <code>LOW-BOUND</code> after <code>EVT</code> and no later than <code>LOW-BOUND</code> after <code>EVT</code> that has <code>VALUE</code> for property <code>PROPERTY</code>, where no other event of type <code>TYPE</code> occurs during that period with a higher value for property <code>PROPERTY</code>. 

In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(disjointWith IntangibleIndividual HistoricFigure)
(disjointWith Artifact-Generic HistoricFigure)
(comment HistoricFigure "Each instance of this collection is a current or former instance of #$Person who has historical significance.  Examples include  #$Pericles and #$MartinLuther-ReligiousFigure.")
(disjointWith HistoricFigure PlantBLO)
(comment GonadotropinReleasingHormoneReceptor "The collection of receptor molecules for gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) that mediate the action of GnRH to stimulate the secretion of the gonadotropic hormones LH and FSH.  (LinkedLife data http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment VasopressinReceptor "The collection of receptor molecules for arginine vasopressin.")
(comment InterferonAlphaBetaReceptor "The collection of receptor molecules for alpha and beta interferons.")
(comment Serpina6 "A class of #$GlobularProteins.  #$Serpina6 is the major transport protein for glucocorticoids and progestins in the blood of almost all vertebrate species (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment ProstaglandinG-HSynthase1 "A type of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances may play an important role in regulating or promoting cell proliferation in some normal and neoplastically transformed cells (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment ProstaglandinG-HSynthase2 "A type of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances may play a role as a major mediator of inflammation and/or a role for prostanoid signaling in activity-dependent plasticity (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment Hroat1 "Class of #$ProteinMolecule whose instances play a role in carbohydrate transport and metabolism (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment Interleukin8 "Instances of #$Interleukin8 (IL8) are cemotactic factors that attract neutrophils, basophils, and T-cells, but not monocytes, and are also involved in neutrophil activation.  They are released from several cell types in response to an inflammatory stimulus (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment Gabra2 "The primary receptor molecule in the neuronal membrane to which GABA, the major inhibitory neurotransmitter in the vertebrate brain, binds in order to mediate synaptic inhibition (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment NDPKinase "A class of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances play a major role in the synthesis of nucleoside triphosphates other than ATP. (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com)")
(comment AcrAB "A class of drug efflux protein with a broad substrate specificity (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com). ")
(comment HTHTypeTranscriptionalRegulator-qacR "The collection of transcriptional repressors of qacA. (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com)")
(comment regexStringMatch "A variable-arity text-processing predicate used to indicate a match between a 'regular expression template' and a string of characters. (#$regexStringMatch REGEX STRING) means that the #$RegularExpression template (or 'regex') REGEX matches some substring within STRING. This is like the predicate #$substring, except that it allows for 'wildcard characters' and other regular expression features in the template. When used with three or more arguments, the argument after the second are bound to any strings that are captured by the regular expression.  For example, a query using the sentence:<p>
<code>(#$regexStringMatch \"dogs(.*)cats(.*)\" \"dogs hate cats but love mice\" ?MATCH1 ?MATCH2)</code><p>
returns the following bindings:<p>
<code>(((?MATCH1 . \" hate \") (?MATCH2 . \" but love mice\")))</code><p>

Note that predicate currently supports only variables in the arg3+ argument position, and that arg1 and arg2 must be fully bound.<p>

The rules for what characters to use in the regex, and what constitutes a valid match, depend on the particular regular expression matcher being used. (Regular expressions are used for matching in the GREP, EGREP, AWK, VI, TCL, Emacs, PERL and PYTHON programs.) Some regex features are common to all such programs, including these: . [...] [^...] char ? * + ^ $ \\< \\> | (...) \\1,\\2,\\3,... Some other features vary. This predicate assumes that the PERL specification is used for regular expression matching. Briefly: The period matches 'any character'. Square brackets match a class of characters, those listed, possibly with ranges like A-Z or a-z or 1-8. Square brackets with a caret-character as the first included character match the class of characters other than those listed between the brackets. Backslash-character means the following special character is directly matched and is not treated as a special character. Caret matches the position of the start-of-line. Dollar-sign matches the position at the end-of-line. \\< matches any start of word. \\> matches any end-of-word. Parentheses group whatever they enclose. A character or group followed by a question-mark is optional; it matches zero or one occurence of that group or charater. A character or group followed by an asterisk matches any number of repetitions that group or character, including zero. A character or group followed by a plus-sign matches one or more repetitions of that group or character. A vertical bar | separates alternative matches -- either may succeed. \\1,\\2,\\3, etc. are backreference variables to which each matched group is assigned in order, and they will match later occurrences of the assigned group. For further details, see standard documentation for regular expressions or for PERL.  See also #$regexFileMatch.")
(comment ReligiousFigure "The collection of current or expired human beings (some probably fictional, some probably not) whose lives (or the perception thereof) have played a central role in the development and tenets of some religion.  Positive examples include #$Mary-MotherOfJesus, #$MartinLuther-ReligiousFigure, Buddah, and Mohammed. Negative examples include specific Popes (generally, St. Peterbeing an exception), cult leaders (e.g. Jim Jones, David Koresh), and most religious leaders.")
(comment LinkedLifeOntology "Ontology term used for the LinkedLife triple store mapping.")
(comment httpdRequestUnboundOnlySubLParsingProgramForSKS "(#$httpdRequestUnboundOnlySubLParsingProgramForSKS WEB-PAGE SUBL) means that
the web service WEB-PAGE can be parsed into a result set by applying
the SubL program SUBL to the result of tokenizing the resulting XML 
stream provided by connecting to the service. This differs from a parsing program declared using #$httpdRequestSubLParsingProgramForSKS in that the latter is expected to return values for all logical fields in the query sentence, while the former returns only unbound values.")
(comment AutoHood "The collection of all automobile hoods. A type of #$AutoBodyPart, #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory, and #$ContainerLid. Each instance of #$AutoHood is a part of an automobile body which consists of a hinged cover of the engine compartment.")
(comment BigOWLBridgingMt "Bridging microtheory for linking robust inferential predicates to #$OWLProperty instances used in connection with the BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS mapping.")
(comment objectEndingDate "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate.  <code>(#$objectEndingDate EXISTENT ENDDATE)</code> means that <code>EXISTENT</code> ceased to be an instance of #$SomethingExisting during <code>ENDDATE</code>.  See also #$objectStartingDate.")
(comment objectStartingDate "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate.  <code>(#$objectStartingDate EXISTENT STARTDATE)</code> means that <code>EXISTENT</code> became an instance of #$SomethingExisting during <code>STARTDATE</code>.  If <code>EXISTENT</code> is an #$Animal, <code>STARTDATE</code> is the date at which it was born (see the more specialized predicate #$birthDate).  See also #$objectEndingDate.")
(comment SexuallyExperienced "An instance of #$TerminalCollection.  Each instance of #$SexuallyExperienced is an #$Animal who has performed at least one instance of #$SexualCopulation.  #$SexuallyExperienced is, of course, disjoint with #$Virgin.")
(comment Leper "#$Leper is an instance of #$PersonTypeByPhysiologicalConditionType and a subset of #$HomoSapiens. It is the collection of people who have symptoms of #$Leprosy caused by the bacterium #$MycobacteriumLeprae.")
(comment Leprosy "#$Leprosy is a disease casued by the bacteria #$MycobacteriumLeprae.   The bacteria invade nerve cells, causing numbness.  In unsanitary conditions, infected persons who do not notice injuries to numb areas often develop secondary infections. In the middle ages, such secondary infections were often caused by rat bites.")
(comment MedicalDegreeLevel "The collection of all medical degree levels. A type of #$DoctoralLevel. The collection #$MedicalDegreeLevel is a #$TerminalCollection and a #$PersonTypeByEducationLevel.")
(comment PhDLevel "The collection of all persons who have achieved a PhD level of education. A type of #$DoctoralLevel. The collection #$PhDLevel is an #$TerminalCollection and a #$PersonTypeByEducationLevel.")
(comment NonInitialCollection "A specialization of both #$TimeDependentCollection and #$FirstOrderCollection (qq.v.).  Each instance NIC of #$NonInitialCollection is a collection such that nothing can be an instance of NIC at the start of the thing's existence.  Thus nothing can be an instance of NIC for its entire existence.  Instanceship in NIC is typically \"acquired\" at some point in time T after the would-be instance INST comes into existence, where T might occur either during or after INST's existence (i.e. \"posthumously\").  #$NonInitialCollection is agnostic regarding whether INST is an instance of NIC \"intermittently\" (see #$IntermittentCollection).  Examples of non-initial collections are #$AdultAnimal, #$Veterinarian, and #$MinedArea.")
(comment ExistenceCotemporalCollection "A specialization of #$InitialCollection (q.v.). This is the collection of all first-order collections whose instances belong to them throughout the entire time during which they are also instances of #$SomethingExisting, and only then.  That is, each instance ECC of #$ExistenceCotemporalCollection is such that (i) a thing can be an instance of ECC only while the thing is also an instance of #$SomethingExisting and (ii) if a given thing is ever an instance of ECC, there is no time during the time during which the thing is also an instance of #$SomethingExisting at which it is not an instance of ECC.")
(comment TerminalNonInitialCollection "A specialization of #$NonInitialCollection  (q.v.).  Each instance EDTC of #$TerminalNonInitialCollection is a collection such that: (i) a thing can be an instance of EDTC only while it is also an instance of #$SomethingExisting, (ii) once a thing becomes an instance of EDTC it necessarily remains so until such time as it is no longer an instance of #$SomethingExisting, (iii) nothing can be an instance of EDTC for the entire time during which it is an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  It follows from these conditions that (iv) nothing starts out as an instance of EDTC and (v) any instance of EDTC ceases to be such when it ceases to be an instance of #$SomethingExisting.  An example of an #$TerminalNonInitialCollection is (#$GraduateFn #$College), the collection of college graduates.  Cf. #$InitialCollection.")
(comment InitialCollection "A specialization of #$TimeDependentCollection (q.v.).  Each instance EDIC of #$InitialCollection is a collection such that (i) a thing can be an instance of EDIC only while the thing is also an instance of #$SomethingExisting, (ii) any instance of EDIC starts as an instance of it, and (iii) if an instance of EDIC changes to no longer being an instance it can never become an instance again.  For example, #$Virgin is such a collection.  Cf. #$NonInitialCollection and #$TerminalNonInitialCollection.")
(comment NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem "A classification system developed by the #$OfficeOfManagementAndBudget in cooperation with #$Canada and #$Mexico to facilitate standardized representations of economic data. It was adopted in 1997 and revised in 2002 and 2007.")
(comment NAICSIndustryOrEconomicSectorType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$NAICSIndustryOrEconomicSectorType is a classification in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem.")
(comment naicsCodeOfIndustryType "(#$naicsCodeOfIndustryType INDUSTRY-TYPE CODE) means that CODE is the two-to-six-digit code for INDUSTRY-TYPE in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem.")
(comment naicsTitle "(#$naicsTitle INDUSTRY-TYPE TITLE) means that TITLE is the human-readable gloss or name for INDUSTRY-TYPE in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem.")
(comment NAICSSector "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$NAICSSector is a sector in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem. Each such instance is represented with a two-digit #$naicsCodeOfIndustryType.")
(comment NAICSSubSector "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$NAICSSubSector is a subsector in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem. Each such instance is represented with a three-digit #$naicsCodeOfIndustryType.")
(comment NAICSIndustryGroup "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$NAICSIndustryGroup is an industry group in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem. Each such instance is represented with a four-digit #$naicsCodeOfIndustryType.")
(comment NAICSIndustry "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$NAICSIndustry is an industry in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem. Each such instance is represented with a five-digit #$naicsCodeOfIndustryType.")
(comment genlIndustry "(#$genlIndustry SMALL LARGE) means that the industry or economic sector LARGE encompasses SMALL.")
(comment AncientCivilization "The collection of former instances of #$GeographicalAgent that thrived during some period of ancient history.  Examples include #$AncientEgypt, ancient Greece, or the Aztec kingdom.")
(comment ReignOfRomanCommanderAegidius "An instance of #$Reign, the #$ReignOfRomanCommanderAegidius was the eight year rulership of #$Aegidius-RomanCommander over the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks during the absence of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing in the #$KingdomOfThuringians.")
(comment RaymondNonnatus "Raymond Nonnatus, a 13th-century Spanish Priest canonized by the Roman Catholic Church as the patron saint of childbirth.")
(comment NFLTeam "The collection of all teams that play in the #$NationalFootballLeague.")
(comment CFLTeam "The collection of all teams that play in the #$CanadianFootballLeague.")
(comment AFLTeam "The collection of all teams that play in the #$AmericanFootballLeague.")
(disjointWith Organ Neoplasm)
(comment Tumor "A specialization of #$Neoplasm.  Each instance of #$Tumor is an abnormal tissue mass found in an animal.  Instances of #$Tumor include both malignant (cancerous -- see the collection #$Cancer) and benign (non-cancerous) growths which have no normal physiological cause or function.")
(comment Neoplasm "A specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$Neoplasm is abnormal mass of tissue.")
(disjointWith TumorCondition Leukemia)
(comment NeoplasmCondition "The collection of cases in which someone has an abnormal proliferation of genetically altered cells, such as a tumor.")
(comment TumorCondition "The collection of cases in which someone has a tumor.")
(comment AbsoluteMonarchy "An instance of #$GeopoliticalEntityBySystemOfGovernment.  Each instance of #$AbsoluteMonarchy is a country ruled by a monarch who has absolute power over the government.")
(comment DirectDemocracy "A system of government (a kind of #$DemocraticGeopoliticalEntity) according to which citizens vote directly upon nearly all matters of governmental concern.  See also #$RepresentativeDemocracy.")
(comment PoisonousMushroom "The collection of all mushrooms that are poisonous to eat.")
(comment HallucinogenicMushroom "The collection of all mushrooms that can cause hallucinations. A type of #$Mushroom and #$Hallucinogen.")
(comment EdibleMushroom "The collection of all mushrooms that are edible.")
(disjointWith ToxicSubstance EdibleMushroom)
(comment Truffle-Mushroom "The collection of truffle mushrooms, some species of which are highly prized for cooking.")
(comment virulenceOfInfection "(#$virulenceOfInfection INFECTION LEVEL) means that instances of the #$InfectionType INFECTION have the level of virulence LEVEL. LEVEL is a measure of the severity of the disease caused by INFECTION.")
(comment TriploidOrganism "The collection of all triploid organisms.  Organisms which are triploid have somatic (body) cells which are triploid.  Cells which are #$TriploidCells have three #$Chromosome sets.  ")
(comment TetraploidOrganism "The collection of all tetraploid organisms.  Organisms which are tetraploid have somatic (body) cells which are tetraploid.  Cells which are #$TetraploidCells have four sets of #$Chromosomes.  ")
(comment HexaploidOrganism "Cells which are #$HexaploidCells have six #$Chromosome sets.  Organisms which are hexaploid have somatic (body) cells which are hexaploid.")
(comment PolyploidOrganism "The collection of all polyploid organisms.  Organisms which are polyploid have somatic (body) cells which are polyploid.  Cells which are #$PolyploidCells have more than two #$Chromosome sets.  A #$PolyploidCell is normally either a #$TriploidCell, #$TetraploidCell, or #$HexaploidCell.")
(comment TetraploidCell "The collection of all tetraloid cells. A type of #$EukaryoticCell. #$TetraploidCell is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment TriploidCell "The collection of all triploid cells. A type of #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment HexaploidCell "The collection of all hexaploid cells. A type of #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment ploidy-Cell "(#$ploidy-Cell CELL PLOIDY-LEVEL) holds just in case CELL has the number of copies of its chromosome set characterized by PLOIDY-LEVEL.  If CELL is an instance of #$Gamete from a #$DiploidOrganism then (#$ploidy-Cell CELL #$HaploidCell) holds because CELL has one copy of its basic chromosome set.")
(comment sksiEqualsAny "#$sksiEqualsAny is a binary predicate similar to #$sksiEquals as it is intended to only be solved via an external knowledge source.  <code>(#$sksiEqualsAny THING1 SET-OF-THINGS)</code> is true when <code>THING1</code> and any element of <code>SET-OF-THINGS</code> are determined by the external source to be equal.")
(disjointWith OWLPropertyPatientDomain PredicateWithDomainContainedByPatient)
(comment GolgiApparatus "An organelle found in most eukaryotic cells that processes and packages macromolecules (e.g. proteins and lipids).")
(comment Archaea "One of the three Domains of life on Earth in conjunction with #$Bacterium and #$EukaryoticOrganisms.")
(comment BiologicalDivision "A specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon.  Each instance of #$BiologicalDivision is a main taxonomic subdivision of some instance of #$BiologicalKingdom.  In the #$Animal Kingdom, however, the main taxonomic subdivisions are instances of #$BiologicalPhylum (q.v.), rather than #$BiologicalDivision.")
(comment BiologicalDomain "A specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon.  In the three-domain system, the threee instances of #$BiologicalDomain partition all of life on Earth.")
(disjointWith Bacterium Archaea)
(comment AerobicBLO "Tissues or organisms with #$AerobicBLO are those that cannot live in the absence of oxygen")
(comment AnaerobicOrganism "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole and #$AnaerobicBLO.  Each instance of #$AnaerobicOrganism is an organism that can live in the absence of oxygen.")
(comment AerobicOrganism "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole and #$AerobicBLO.  Each instance of #$AerobicOrganism is an organism that requires the presence of oxygen to live.")
(comment MycobacteriumTuberculosis "A subset of #$Bacterium, #$MycobacteriumTuberculosis is a collection of bacteria that can cause #$Tuberculosis.")
(comment WhoopingCough "A collection of #$BacterialInfections caused by #$BordetellaPertussis.   The disease, formerly common in children is characterized by paroxysms of coughing.")
(comment RickettsiaAkari "The collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Rickettsia that causes #$Rickettsialpox.  Its vector is bloodsucking mites.  These mites are found on mice where Rickettsialpox has occured.")
(comment OrientiaTsutsugamushi "The collection of #$ProkaryoticCells that causes the #$BacterialInfection #$ScrubTyphus.  These are smaller than the #$Rickettsia.  These organisms are found in the Orient.")
(comment baseQueryForReport "(#$baseQueryForReport QUERY SKS) means that that QUERY is a query that together with the selection query for a report will generate the focal entities for the report -- the entities the report is about.  The selection query is conjoined with the base query and the input variable for the base query is unified with the free variable in the selection sentence.  The output variable of the base query is then unified with the input variables of the column queries when the report is run.")
(comment VolumeOfCWSeries-Periodic "A specialization of #$EditionOfCWSeries-Periodic.  Each instance is an individual #$ConceptualWork consisting in an ordered sequence of #$ConceptualWorks comprising a 'volume' in some #$ConceptualWorkSeries-Periodic.")
(comment issueOfPeriodicalWithNumberAndVolume "The corresponding predicate of #$IssueOfPeriodicalWithNumberAndVolumeFn.")
(comment IssueOfPeriodicalWithNumberAndVolumeFn "A binary, individual-denoting, reifiable function used for representing instances of #$PeriodicalIssue which are individuated by volume (#$VolumeOfCWSeries-Periodic) and issue number.  Where Nth is a #$NonNegativeInteger and VOLUME is a #$VolumeOfCWSeries-Periodic, (#$IssueOfPeriodicalWithNumberAndVolumeFn N VOLUME) denotes the Nth #$PeriodicalIssue in the sequence comprising VOLUME.")
(comment computerSpeed "A predicate relating instances of #$Computer to the processing speed of their #$CentralProcessingUnits. (#$computerSpeed COMP FREQ) means that COMP is a computer which has a central processing unit with speed FREQ (usually stated using #$MegaHertz or #$GigaHertz). Note that a single computer can have multiple processors and hence have multiple frequencies associated with it.")
(comment primaryNaicsCodeOfCompany "(#$primaryNaicsCodeOfCompany COMPANY CODE) means that CODE is the two-to-six-digit code for the industry that best characterizes COMPANY's primary business.")
(comment naicsCodeOfCompany "(#$naicsCodeOfCompany COMPANY CODE) means that CODE is the two-to-six-digit code for an industry of which COMPANY is a part.")
(comment companyHasPrimaryIndustryType "(#$companyHasPrimaryIndustryType COMPANY INDUSTRY-TYPE) means that the #$CommercialOrganization COMPANY is primary does the type of commercial activity associated with the type of #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment RNAStrand "The collection of all #$Polynucleotides whose
#$polymericSubComponents are the #$NitrogenBases #$Adenine-Base,
#$Guanine-Base, #$Cytosine-Base, and #$Uracil-Base, joined in ester linkages to a #$Ribose moiety: i.e., ribonucleic acid #$PolymerMolecules.")
(comment HomoPolymer "The collection of all #$PolymerMolecules such that the #$polymericSubComponents of a given instance will all be the same kind of #$Monomer.  More specifically, if POL is an instance of #$HomoPolymer and MOL is a #$polymericSubComponents of POL, then MOL will be an instance of any and all specs of #$Monomer that any other #$polymericSubComponents of POL is.")
(comment HeteroPolymer "The collection of all #$PolymerMolecules whose instances are characterized by having more than one type of #$Monomer as #$polymericSubComponents.  More specifically, if HET is an instance of #$HeteroPolymer, then there are least two different #$Monomers such that both are #$polymericSubComponents of HET and each is an instance of a different spec of #$Monomer.")
(comment Polynucleotide "The collection of all #$PolymerMolecules which have instances of #$Nucleotide as their monomeric subcomponents.  This class includes RNA and DNA molecules and segments among its subclasses (see #$RNAStrand, #$DNAPolymer).")
(comment Poliovirus "The collection of all polio. A type of #$Virus. The concept #$Poliovirus is a #$VirusType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment SMEDI-Disease "A kind of #$ViralInfection, SMEDI (stillbirth, mummification, embryonic death, and infertility) is a disease that affects the reproductive systems of swine.")
(comment FelineLeukemia "The collection of all feline leukemia infections. A type of #$ViralInfection and #$LifeThreateningCondition (for cats).")
(comment Oncovirus "The collection of all cancer-causing viruses.")
(comment Epstein-BarrVirus "The specification of #$Virus that causes #$Mononucleosis.")
(comment GuanaritoVirus "The virus that causes Venezuelan Hemorrhagic Fever.")
(comment VenezuelanHemorrhagicFever "A specialization of #$ViralInfection.  Instances of #$VenezuelanHemorrhagicFever are characterized by gradual onset of malaise, headache, and sustained fever progressing to hemorrhagic symptoms including nose bleed, bloody vomit, and blood in stool or urine.")
(comment JuninHemorrhagicFeverVirus "A specialization of #$Virus.  #$JuninHemorrhagicFeverVirus is the type of virus that causes instances of  #$JuninHemorrhagicFever (q.v.).")
(comment KyasanurForestDiseaseVirus "A specialization of #$Flavivirus. #$KyasanurForestDiseaseVirus is the type of virus that causes instances of #$KyasanurForestDisease.")
(comment KyasanurForestDisease "A specialization of #$ViralHemorrhagicFeverInfection. Instances of #$KyasanurForestDisease are characterized by a sudden onset of chills, headache, fever, pain in the lower back and limbs, severe prostration, red and inflamed eyes, diarrhea and vomiting progressing to hemorrhage from gums, nose, GI tract and lungs. Recovery may be prolonged. Found principally in the Shimoga and Kanara district of Karnataka, India; common in young adults exposed during the dry season in the forest.")
(comment MarburgVirus "A specialization of #$Filovirus.  #$MarburgVirus is the type of virus that causes instances of #$Marburg, a severe hemorrhagic fever.")
(comment SmallpoxVirus "A specialization of #$Virus. Each instance of #$SmallpoxVirus is a virus of the type that causes smallpox (see the collection  #$SmallpoxInfection).")
(comment RiftValleyFeverVirus "A specialization of #$Virus.  #$RiftValleyFeverVirus is a type of virus that causes instances of #$RiftValleyFever.")
(comment Nasopharynx "The collection of all nasopharynges.  Each #$Nasopharynx is the superior section of a #$Pharynx, being located behind (dorsal to) the nasal cavities.")
(comment cWRelevantToResearchersInField "Where CW is a #$ConceptualWork and FIELD is a #$FieldOfStudy, (#$cWRelevantToResearchersInField CW FIELD) means the the general topic of CW should be familiar to experts in FIELD.")
(comment fieldInvolvesResearchingDiseaseType "A typed specialization of fieldInvolvesResearchOnType, specializing to instances of #$DiseaseType.")
(comment sequenceCodesForBindingSiteOfSubstanceType "A predicate linking genetic information structures (instances of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS) to subclasses of #$DrugSubstance whose binding sites are coded for by the gene.  Specifically, (sequenceCodesForBindingSiteOfSubstanceType GENE-GIS DRUG-TYPE) means that one of the kinds of molecules ordinarily bound by individual molecules of instances of DRUG-TYPE is coded for by the gene (genetic information structure) GENE-GIS.")
(comment hasInterestInKnowingCW "Where CW is a #$ConceptualWork and AGENT is an #$IntelligentAgent, (#$hasInterestInKnowingCW AGENT CW) means that, in the context of the assertion, it is in the interest of AGENT to know something about the content of CW.")
(comment broadcastTypeHasIntendedTransmissionMedium "<code>(#$broadcastTypeHasIntendedTransmissionMedium BROADCAST-TYPE MEDIUM)</code> identifies <code>MEDIUM</code> as the specialization of #$MediaTransmitting that each instance of <code>BROADCAST-TYPE</code>, an instance of
 #$BroadcastTypeByIntendedTransmissionMedium, was intended for.")
(comment isACountOfType "<code>(#$isACountOfType COUNT-QTY TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the instance of #$ObjectType for which the instance <code>COUNT-QTY</code> of #$CountQuantity is a count.  For example, <code>((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 212)</code> is a doughnut count; hence <code>(#$isACountOfType ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 212) #$Doughnut)</code> holds. ")
(comment isACountOfQuantity "<code>(#$isACountOfQuantity COUNT-QTY N)</code> identifies <code>N</code> as the instance of #$IntervalOnNumberLine for which the instance <code>COUNT-QTY</code> of #$CountQuantity is a count of.  For example, <code>((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 212)</code> is count of 212; hence <code>(#$isACountOfQuantity ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 212) 212)</code> holds. ")
(comment sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType "<code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType SITUATION COUNT-QTY ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>SITUATION</code> of #$Situation is such that there are a total number of <code>N</code> instances of <code>TYPE</code> that play the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that are sub-situations of <code>SITUATION</code>, where <code>N</code> is the number such that <code>(#$isACountOfQuantity COUNT-QTY N)</code> and <code>TYPE</code> is the collection such that <code>(#$isACountOfType COUNT-QTY TYPE)</code>.  For example, <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobEatingBreakfast-212 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 3) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that a total of 3 donughts are eaten (play the #$consumedObject role in an instance of #$EatingEvent) in the course of (i.e., these eating-events are #$subSituations of) BobEatingBreakfast-212.  <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobEatingBreakfast-352 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 0) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that no donughts are eaten in the course of BobEatingBreakfast-352, <code>(#$sitHasUnitOfCountInRoleInSubSitOfType BobsDiet-517 ((#$UnitOfCountFn #$Doughnut) 40) #$consumedObject #$EatingEvent)</code> means that 40 doughnuts are eaten in the course of BobsDiet-517,and so forth.")
(comment assistDeviceAssociatedWith "Relates a surgical assist device removal or insertion to the assist device involved in the procedure.")
(comment properVersionOfReflexivePred "A functional predicate that relates an instance of #$ReflexiveBinaryPredicate <code>P</code> to its asymmetric \"version\" -- i.e., to a predicate <code>P'</code> such that if <code>(P ARG1 ARG2)</code> holds, then <code>(P' ARG1 ARG2)</code> is guaranteed to hold so long as <code>ARG1</code> and <code>ARG2</code> are different (see #$different). <code>(#$properVersionOfReflexivePred P' P)</code> identifies <code>P'</code> as the asymmetric version of <code>P</code>.")
(comment hasCorrespondingNumericValue-PatientStatus-CathPCI "(#$hasCorrespondingNumericValue-PatientStatus-STS THING VALUE) means that, for report generation purposes, the representation of THING is VALUE.")
(comment PatientEventStatus-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = elective, 2 = urgent, 3 = emergent, 4 = salvage.")
(comment MSWordFile "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AISs encoded according to the MS Word standard.")
(disjointWith Situation MultiIndividualAgentNowDisbanded)
(comment retiredFromField "(#$retiredFromField AGT OCTYPE) means that    AGT is retired from OCTYPE.  From this it follows that    (#$occupation AGT OCTYPE) *was* true at some time prior to when (#$retiredFromField AGT OCTYPE) is true, and that it is false while the first assertion is true.  Thus, if one intends to use     this predicate, one must be certain to     carefully time-index the assertions in which it is used, as well as any #$occupation assertions with which it might conflict.")
(comment NBATeam "An instance of #$SportsTeamTypeByLeague; this is the collection of all NBA basketball teams.")
(comment collectionOfGroupMembers "<code>(#$collectionOfGroupMembers COLL GROUP)</code> identifies <code>COLL</code> as the collection of all members of the group <code>GROUP</code>.")
(comment SportsTeamTypeByLeague "A collection that facets #$SportsTeam by the leagues in which sports teams play.  For any instance <code>TEAM-TYPE</code> of #$SportsTeamTypeByLeague, every instance of <code>TEAM-TYPE</code> will stand in the #$sportsTeamCompetesInLeague to the same instance of #$SportsLeague.")
(comment sportsTeamCompetesInLeague "<code>(#$sportsTeamCompetesInLeague TEAM LEAGUE)</code> means that the instance <code>TEAM</code> of #$SportsTeam is one of the teams that belongs to <code>LEAGUE</code> an instance of #$SportsLeague.")
(comment SouthwestDivision-NBA "the Southwest division of the NBA")
(comment NorthwestDivision-NBA "the Northwest division of the NBA")
(comment SoutheastDivision-NBA "the Southeast division of the NBA")
(comment CharlotteBobcats "The NBA team.")
(comment LosAngelesLakers "The NBA team.")
(comment ailmentDeveloping "<code>(#$ailmentDeveloping DEVELOPING AILMENT)</code> means that the instance <code>DEVELOPING</code> of #$DevelopingAilment is a developing of the ailment <code>AILMENT</code>, an instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType.  For example <code>(#$ailmentDeveloping FredCatchingACold-212 #$CommonCold)</code> means that <code>FredCatchingACold-212</code> a catching of the common cold.")
(comment DevelopingAnInfectiousDisease "The subcollection of #$DevelopingAilment show instances are such that the #$ailmentDeveloping is an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseType.")
(comment MetaphorTypeByBasisType "A collection that facets #$Metaphor into sub-collections that share a common semantic basis, understood as a collection whose features are drawn upon when the metaphor is invoked.  For example, #$OcularMetaphor is the instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType whose basis is #$VisualPerception.  To relate an instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType to its basis, use #$metaphorTypeBasisType.")
(comment metaphorBasisType "<code>(#$metaphorBasisType METAPHOR TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the instance of #$Collection upon which <code>METAPHOR</code>, an instance of a specialization of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType, is based.")
(comment AcquisitionMetaphor "The instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType whose basis is #$AcquiringAnObject.")
(comment metaphorTypeBasisType "<code>(#$metaphorTypeBasisType METAPHOR-TYPE TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the instance of #$Collection upon which all instances of <code>METAPHOR-TYPE</code>, an instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType, are based.")
(comment metaphorAppliesToType "<code>(#$metaphorAppliesToType METAPHOR TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the type of thing to which <code>METAPHOR</code> applies, i.e., is the type of thing described when <code>METAPHOR</code> is used.")
(comment MetaphorTypeAppliedToFn "<code>(#$MetaphorTypeAppliedToFn METAPHOR-TYPE TYPE)</code> denotes the instance of <code>METAPHOR-TYPE</code>, an instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType, that is the applied to, i.e., used to describe, <code>TYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$MetaphorTypeAppliedToFn #$OcularMetaphor #$Comprehending)</code> denotes the ocular metaphor used to characterize understanding (e.g., \"I see.\").")
(comment metaphorOfTypeAppliesToType "The predicate that corresponds to #$MetaphorTypeAppliedToFn. <code>(#$metaphorOfTypeAppliesToType METAPHOR METAPHOR-TYPE TYPE)</code> identifies <code>METAPHOR</code> as the instance of <code>METAPHOR-TYPE</code> used to characterize <code>TYPE</code>.  For example,<code>(#$metaphorOfTypeAppliesToType (#$MetaphorTypeAppliedToFn #$OcularMetaphor #$Comprehending) #$OcularMetaphor #$Comprehending)</code> means that the object denoted by the expression in its arg1 position is the ocular metaphor used to characterize understanding.")
(comment OcularMetaphor "An instance of #$MetaphorTypeByBasisType.  Instances are metaphors based on vision.")
(comment CAERecipe "The collection of \"recipes\" for putting together CAE fragments into larger fragments.  Each recipe will have a number of components, identified by number, associated with patterns.  Whether a pattern matches a recipe component is indicated by rules concluding to #$matchesCAERecipeComponent.")
(comment matchesCAERecipeComponent "(#$matchesCAERecipeComponent ?QUOTED-SENTENCE ?CAE-RECIPE ?NUMBER) holds if ?QUOTED-SENTENCE -- for example (#$Quote (#$temperatureOfObject ?X ?Y)) -- matches the pattern associated with the ?CAE-RECIPE component indicated by ?NUMBER.")
(comment numberOfComponentsInCAERecipe "#$numberOfComponentsInCAERecipe holds of ?CAE-RECIPE and ?N if ?CAE-RECIPE has ?N components.")
(comment OWLProperty-RelationToQuantity "the collection of OWL properties which are (often implicitly) attributions of some quantity either directly to some entity or via an intervening evaluation event or data node.")
(comment nthOccasionOnWhich "<code>(#$nthOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE ROLE-LIST ROLE-PLAYER-LIST N)</code> means that the instance <code>SIT</code> of #$Situation is the <code>N</code>th situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the objects in the list <code>ROLE-PLAYER-LIST</code> play the respective roles in <code>ROLE-LIST</code>.  For example, <code>(#$nthOccasionOnWhich Event-212 #$TrainPassengerTransportation (#$TheList #$passengers) (#$TheList Sally) 3)</code> means that <code>Event-212</code> is Sally's third train ride, while <code>(#$nthOccasionOnWhich Event-212 #$TrainPassengerTransportation (#$TheList #$passengers #$passengers) (#$TheList Sally Jose) 1)</code> means that it is Sally's first train ride with Jose, and <code>(#$nthOccasionOnWhich Event-212 #$TransportInvolvingADriver (#$TheList #$transportees #$transportees) (#$TheList Sally Jose) 5)</code>. means that it is the fifth ride they've shared together.")
(comment occasionOnWhich "<code>(#$occasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE ROLE-LIST ROLE-PLAYER-LIST)</code> means that the situation <code>SIT</code> is the an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that each <code>ACTOR</code> in <code>ROLE-PLAYER-LIST</code> plays the respective <code>ROLE</code> in <code>ROLE-LIST</code>.  Hence <code>(#$occasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE ROLE-LIST ROLE-PLAYER-LIST)</code> means the same as <code>(#$thereExists ?X (#$nthOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE ROLE-LIST ROLE-PLAYER-LIST ?X))</code>.")
(comment finalOccasionOnWhich "<code>(#$finalOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> means that the situation <code>SIT</code> is the final instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the actors play the roles specified in <code>SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS</code>. For example, <code>(#$finalOccasionOnWhich (#$BirthFn #$AbrahamLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthChild #$AbrahamLincoln))</code> means that the birth of Abraham Lincoln is the last #$BirthEvent situation in which Lincoln plays the #$birthChild role. ")
(comment firstOccasionOnWhich "<code>(#$firstOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> means that the situation <code>SIT</code> is the first instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the actors play the roles specified in <code>SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS</code>. For example, <code>(#$firstOccasionOnWhich (#$BirthFn #$AbrahamLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthChild #$AbrahamLincoln))</code> means that the birth of Abraham Lincoln is the first #$BirthEvent situation in which Lincoln plays the #$birthChild role. <code>(#$firstOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> is shorthand for <code>(#$nthOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS 1)</code>.")
(comment onlyOccasionOnWhich "<code>(#$onlyOccasionOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> means that the situation <code>SIT</code> is the only instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the actors play the roles specified in <code>SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS</code>. For example, <code>(#$onlyOccasionOnWhich (#$BirthFn #$AbrahamLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthChild #$AbrahamLincoln))</code> means that the birth of Abraham Lincoln is the only (i.e., first and last) #$BirthEvent situation in which Lincoln plays the #$birthChild role. ")
(comment finalOccasionThusFarOnWhich "<code>(#$finalOccasionThusFarOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> at a time <i>t</i> means that the situation <code>SIT</code>, whose ending date coincides with the start of <i>t</i> is the most recent instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the actors play the roles specified in <code>SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS</code>. I.e., there are no other situations whose ending dates are subsumed by <i>t</i> such that those same actors play those same roles. For example, <code>(#$finalOccasionThusFarOnWhich (#$BirthFn RobertToddLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthParent MaryToddLincoln))</code> means that the birth of Robert Todd Lincoln is the last #$BirthEvent situation in which Mary Todd Lincoln plays the #$birthParent role, and so is true from time Robert Todd Lincoln is born until the birth of her second child, Edward, at which point <code>(#$finalOccasionThusFarOnWhich (#$BirthFn EdwardBakerLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthParent MaryToddLincoln))</code> is true, until the birth of William Lincoln, and so on.  See also #$finalOccasionOnWhich, which does not admit of temporal qualification.")
(comment onlyOccasionThusFarOnWhich "<code>(#$onlyOccasionThusFarOnWhich SIT SIT-TYPE SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS)</code> at a time <i>t</i> means that the situation <code>SIT</code>, whose ending date coincides with the start of <i>t</i> is the only instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that the actors play the roles specified in <code>SET-OF-ROLE-ACTOR-PAIRS</code>. I.e., there are no other situations whose ending dates are prior to or subsumed by <i>t</i> such that those same actors play those same roles. For example, <code>(#$onlyOccasionThusFarOnWhich (#$BirthFn RobertToddLincoln) #$BirthEvent (#$TheSet (#$TheList #$birthParent MaryToddLincoln))</code> means that the birth of Robert Todd Lincoln is the only #$BirthEvent situation in which Mary Todd Lincoln plays the #$birthParent role, and so is true from time Robert Todd Lincoln is born until the birth of her second child, Edward.  See also #$onlyOccasionOnWhich, which does not admit of temporal qualification.")
(comment DatastoreTargetPredicate "The collection of predicates (part of) whose extent is to be mirrored in an external datastore. In particular, GAF assertions using one of these predicates asserted in an instance of #$DatastoreTargetMicrotheory are to be mirrored.")
(comment DatastoreTargetMicrotheory "The collection of microtheories (part of) whose contents are to be mirrored in an external datastore. In particular, GAF assertions using an instance of #$DatastoreTargetPredicate asserted in one of these microtheories are to be mirrored.")
(comment subsequentECGDate "<code>(#$subsequentECGDate EVENT DATE)</code> means that relative to <code>EVENT</code> the date of the non-initial ECG that diagnoses STEMI is <code>DATE</code> .")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure CardiacAssistDeviceRemoval)
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure CardiacAssistDeviceInsertion)
(comment Lesion-BifurcationLesion-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of encoding or decoding evaluation events in which 1 = Yes and 0 = No.")
(comment Alpha1-Antitrypsin-Stuff "Instances are pieces of 'stuff' composed of instances of #$Alpha1-AntitrypsinMolecule, a glycoprotein proteinase inhibitor which prevents excess accumulation of active nutrophil elastase and hence, proteolysis of elastin tissues in alveolar lung structures.  This in turn prevents development of emphysema.")
(comment Alpha1-AntitrypsinMolecule "A glycoprotein proteinase inhibitor which prevents excess accumulation of active nutrophil elastase and hence, proteolysis of elastin tissues in alveolar lung structures.  This in turn prevents development of emphysema.")
(comment Alpha1AntitrypsinDeficiency "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Instances are characterized by low levels of #$Alpha1-Antitrypsin-Stuff in the blood.  Discovered in 1963, the condition has been identified as a potential cause of #$Emphysema, Cirrhosis, and #$ChronicObstructivePulmonaryDisease")
(comment Bronchologist "The collection of doctors specializing in the treatment of bronchial disorders.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntity AbstractTheoreticalDestinationPoint)
(comment intensionalAbstractionOfThingAs "<code>(#$intensionalAbstractionOfThingAs ABSTRACTION THING TYPE)</code> identifies <code>ABSTRACTION</code> as the instance of #$IntensionalAbstraction arrived at by abstracting away the properties of <code>THING</code> so as to arrive at an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, an instance of #$IntensionalAbstractionTargetType.")
(comment QuaFn "<code>(#$QuaFn THING TYPE)</code> denotes the instances of #$IntensionalAbstraction that results from abstracting away all properties of <code>THING</code> until what remains is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, an instance of #$IntensionalAbstractionTargetType.")
(comment AbstractTheoreticalDestinationPoint "The collection of all instances of #$EnduringThing-Localized that humans tend to treat as points, or \"immediate\" locations, i.e., as places where one might be used to answer questions such as \"where you are right now?\" or \"where can I meet you?\" in a way that assumes a high likelihood that someone familiar with the answer would know (pretty much) exactly where one is.  Accordingly, typical instances are places where, or objects around which, people might be expected to convene.  Thus typical instances are stationary objects or locations that 1) are easy to identify and to describe to others and, 2) are not so small or so large that it would be implausible or impractical to characterize them as meeting places or places where one might \"find\" a specific object or person (however, a particularly small object, such as a short line drawn in the sand or an unusual rock might count as an instance of this collection in situations where it has been designated as such (e.g., \"walk towards me, but stop once you get to <i>that blue pebble</i>.\").  Common examples include desks, parked cars, buildings, and landmarks.  Counterexamples include geopolitical entities (e.g., cities, counties, etc. are simply too large -- you can be located \"in\" them, but not located \"at\" them -- at least not in any sense where it would make sense to identify such a thing as a meeting place or an \"immediate\" location.")
(comment IntensionalAbstraction "A collection of objects that are arrived at via a specific process of abstracting away the properties of an \"input\" object until only one focal property is left, and the object that remains is in some sense a \"version\" of the initial object, but with the one focal property in common.    See #$QuaFn for a function that takes an object and a type and returns an #$IntensionalAbstraction of that object (as an instance of that type).")
(comment closestHistoryPriorToMaxStopDateWithStatusAndValueFor "<code>(#$closestHistoryPriorToWithStatus HIST EVT2 STATUS-TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that HIST is the nearest #$PastPatientHistory prior to EVT2's max date of the stop date that contains an instance of STATUS-TYPE that has some value for PROPERTY.")
(comment closestHistoryPriorToMaxStartDateWithStatusAndValueFor "<code>(#$closestHistoryPriorToWithStatus HIST EVT2 STATUS-TYPE PROPERTY)</code> means that HIST is the nearest #$PastPatientHistory prior to EVT2's max date of the start date that contains an instance of STATUS-TYPE that has some value for PROPERTY.")
(comment suppressFormulasForElements-TermGenls "(#$suppressFormulasForElements-TermSpecs TERM SET) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), INS, should NOT have appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  See #$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls for more information about formula generation.")
(comment CABGLocation-CathPCI-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which at your facility = 1, transferred to another facility = 2")
(comment eventHasPreviousPCI-CathPCI "(#$eventHasPreviousPCI-CathPCI EVENT) means that a PCI was performed on the focal patient of EVENT prior to the  hospital visit during which EVENT occurs.")
(comment FalseIsOneAndTrueIsZero-Transformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which the logical values of True and False are encoded as \"0\" and \"1\", respectively.")
(comment cabgLocation-AtYourFacilityOrTransfer "(#$cabgLocation-AtYourFacilityOrTransfer EVENT LOC) means that after the event EVENT, a CABG was performed at LOC.")
(comment cellularLocationText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:cellularLocation.")
(comment cellularLocationTypeOfMoleculeType "(#$cellularLocationTypeOfMoleculeType MOL-TYPE LOC-TYPE) means that under normal cytological conditions, molecules of type MOL-TYPE are found in cell parts of type LOC-TYPE, such that normal instances of LOC-TYPE feature instances (usually many such) of MOL-TYPE as proper physical parts.")
(comment Acrosome "A class of cellular #$Organelle.  Instances are derived from Golgi bodies and cover the heads of animals' spermatozoa.  The purpose of the #$Acrosome is to enable molecular penetration of the ovum.")
(comment Vacuole "A type of #$Organelle found in many kinds of cell:  notably, as an anatomical feature of plant and fungal cells, and also in many kinds of animal cells.  A #$Vacuole is an enclosed, single-membrane cellular cavity filled with water that often contains organic and/or inorganic molecules in solution.")
(comment Peroxisome "A type of #$Organelle found in all #$EukaryoticCells.  Peroxisomes harbor enzymes that help the cell cleanse itself of toxic peroxides.")
(comment Lysosome "A class of spherical #$Organelles found in animal cells, containing acidic hydrolase digestive enzymes.  Cells use lysosomes in digesting worn-out #$Organelles and food particles, as well as bacteria and viruses that have been rendered inert by antibodies.  They also play a role in some forms of pre-programmed cell death.")
(disjointWith GeneticInformationStructure TypographicalStructure)
(comment TypedRoleSitSpecFn "<code>(#$TypedRoleSitSpecFn ROLE TYPE)</code> denotes the collection <code>SIT-TYPE</code> of all instances of #$Situation <code>S</code> such that <code>(#$relationInstanceExists ROLE S TYPE)</code>.")
(comment SitTypeSpecificationFn "<code>(#$SitTypeSpecificationFn STYPE-1, ..., STYPE-N)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$Situation that are instances of <code>STYPE-1</code> through <code>STYPE-N</code>.")
(comment recommendedRoleInTypeForType "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate.  <code>(#$recommendedRoleInTypeForType TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that for all instances <code>INS</code> of type <code>TYPE</code>, it is recommended that <code>INS</code> play the role <code>ROLE</code> in some situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, i.e., <code>(#$recommendedRoleInType INS SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code>.")
(comment eventOccursAtOrgFacility "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$Event to an organization.  <code>(#$eventOccursAtOrgFacility EVENT ORG)</code> means that there exists a facility <code>FACILITY</code> such that <code>(#$eventOccursAt EVENT FACILITY)</code> and throughout the temporal extent of <code>EVENT</code>, <code>(#$orgFacilities ORG FACILITY)</code> holds.")
(comment SubSitTypeSpecificationFn "A function from a subcollection of #$Situation <code>S</code>, an instance of #$ActorSlot <code>A</code>, and a thing <code>T</code> to a subcollection of <code>S</code>.  Which subcollection of <code>S</code> results depends on whether <code>T</code> is an instance or a specialization of #$TemporalThing.  If <code>T</code> is an instance of #$TemporalThing, <code>(#$SubSitTypeSpecificationFn S A T)</code> denotes the subcollection <code>SUB</code> of <code>S</code> such that every instance of <code>SUB</code> stands in the relation <code>A</code> to <code>T</code> -- i.e., <code>(#$subcollectionOfWithRelationTo S A T SUB)</code>.  If <code>T</code> is a specialization of #$TemporalThing, then <code>(#$SubSitTypeSpecificationFn S A T)</code> denotes the subcollection <code>SUB</code> of <code>S</code> such that every instance of <code>SUB</code> stands in the relation <code>A</code> to some instance of <code>T</code> -- i.e., <code>(#$subcollectionOfWithRelationToType S A T SUB)</code>.")
(comment RoleBasedSituationTypeSpecifierFunction "A collection of instances of #$Function-Denotational that take roles (instances of #$BinarySituationPredicate) and return specializations of #$Situation whose identity is based on their instances relationship to those roles.")
(comment BoundRoleSitSpecFn "<code>(#$BoundRoleSitSpecFn ROLE IND)</code> denotes the collection <code>SIT-TYPE</code> of all instances of #$Situation <code>S</code> such that <code>(ROLE S IND)</code>.")
(comment SituationTypeSpecifierFunction "A subcollection of #$CollectionDenotingFunction, each instance of which returns a subcollection of #$Situation.")
(comment eventOccursWithin "<code>(#$eventOccursWithin EVENT OBJECT)</code> means that <code>(#$eventOccursAt EVENT OBJECT)</code> in a precise way, by virtue of being inside it or within its boundaries.")
(comment Dexlansoprazole "The collection of all dexlansoprazole. A type of #$ProtonPumpInhibitor. #$Dexlansoprazole is a #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment AutocatalyticProcessOfSystemFn "A denoting function used for referencing an instance of #$AutocatalyticProcess by the #$FunctionalSystem it implements.  (#$AutocatalyticProcessOfSystemFn SYSTEM) denotes the complex process consisting in multiple thermodynamic work cycles that serves to sustain SYSTEM as a set of operational parameters.")
(comment FootballSafety "The collection of all persons who play the position of safety in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballSafety is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballCornerback "The collection of all persons who play the position of cornerin American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballCornerback is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballDefensiveBack "The collection of all persons who play the position of defensive back in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballDefensiveBack is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballOffensiveLineman "The collection of all persons who play the position center in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballCenterLineman is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballTightEnd "The collection of all persons who play the position tight end in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballTightEnd is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballNoseTackle "The collection of all persons who play the position nose tackle in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballNoseTackle is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment FootballWideReceiver "The collection of all persons who play the position wide receiver in American football. A type of #$FootballPlayer-American. #$FootballTightEnd is a #$FootballPlayer-AmericanTypeByPosition.")
(comment goClassificationProcessText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:goClassificationProcess.  This predicate is used to link a so-called 'drug target', i.e., a molecular binding site, to a noun phrase such as 'cell communication' or 'signal transduction' describing the cellular process that binding site mediates.")
(comment specificFunctionText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:specificFunction.  This predicate is used to link a so-called 'drug target', i.e., a molecular binding site, to a paragraphy describing the site's cytological function in some detail.")
(comment generalFunctionText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:generalFunction.  This predicate is used to link a so-called 'drug target', i.e., a molecular binding site, to a short phrase describing the site's general cytological function.")
(comment goClassificationCompositionText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:goClassificationComposition.  This predicate is used to link a so-called 'drug target', i.e., a molecular binding site, to a noun phrase describing the molecule's cytological siting and degree of physical integration in the location, e.g. 'integral to membrane'.")
(comment goClassificationFunctionText-DrugBank "A database-specific predicate used in the #$BigOWLIMLinkedLifeTripleStoreKS, corresponding to the Linked Life relation drugbank:goClassificationFunction.  This predicate is used to link a so-called 'drug target', i.e., a molecular binding site, to a noun phrase describing the molecule's cytological role.")
(comment reportVariableNumberForQuery "(#$standardFieldNameForQuery QUERY STRING) means that STRING is the variable number for reports utilizing the query unless otherwise specified.")
(comment RGDatasetType "The collection of types of dataset for the report generator.")
(comment generateFormulasForTerm "(#$generateFormulasForTerm TERM SET) means that if TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET ( a set or collection), SET-TERM, should have the appropriate formulas generated for them. If SET-TERM is a predicate with arity N, then (SET-TERM VAR1, ..., VARN) is an appropriate formula, along with any well-formed other substitutions of other elements of SET into that formula, provided SET is an extensional set.")
(comment CellWall "The collection of all cell walls.  Cell walls are external coverings of some types of cells, used both to afford limited protection to the cell and to let in and retain water.  Notably, cell walls do not occur in animal cells.")
(comment ProkaryoticCellWall "The collection of instances of #$CellWall that are #$anatomicalParts of some instance of #$ProkaryoticCell.")
(comment Metaphase "An instance of #$MitosisSubprocessType.  Each instance of #$Metaphase is stage of mitosis during which chromosomes line up along the equatorial plane (also known as the \"metaphase plate\") of a cell.")
(comment Chromatin "#$Chromatin is a specialization of #$OrganicMaterial.  Each instsance of #$Chromatin is a portion of the genetic material from which chromosomes are formed.  Chromatin exists in a variety of states during the #$CellCycle.")
(comment Nucleosome "A specialization of #$CellPart.  #$Nucleosome is the most basic kind of #$Chromatin structure.  Each instance of #$Nucleosome consists of protein cores (which themselves consist of eight histone molecules) around which DNA is coiled.")
(comment NucleicAcidPolymerase "The collection of #$EnzymeMolecules that catalyze polymerization reactions such as the synthesis of #$DNAMolecules and #$RNAMolecules.")
(comment Nuclease "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Nuclease is an enzyme that can break down nucleic acids into their nucleotide subunits.")
(comment RibosomalRNASynthesis "The process of rRNA sythesis, which occurs in the #$Nucleosome.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAtOrPriorTo "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypeAtOrPriorTo EVT1 EVT2 TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> beginning prior to or starting at the same time as EVT2.  In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.  Note this relationship is not supported for procedures -- only for top level events like operations, caths, etc")
(comment DesignTask "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Instances are collections of instances of #$PurposefulAction, bound together by a common goal of producing a #$Design that meets some specification as given in the task description.")
(comment Plastid "A specialization of #$Organelle.  Each instance of #$Plastid is an organelle of a plant or algae cell.  Significant specializations of #$Plastid include #$Chloroplast, #$Chromoplast and #$Leucoplast.")
(comment Chromoplast "A specialization of #$Plastid.  Each instance of #$Chromoplast is an organelle found in cells of photosynthetic eukaryotic species.  Chromoplasts synthesize and store pigments.")
(comment Leucoplast "A specialization of #$Plastid.  Each instance of #$Leucoplast is a pigment-free organelle found in cells of photosynthetic eukaryotic species.")
(comment relationNotExistsExists "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to two collections.  <code>(#$relationNotExistsExists BINPRED COL1 COL2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, no instance <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$not
    (#$and
      (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)
      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)
      (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)))
</pre>
<p>
So #$relationNotExistsExists (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.
<p>
For example, '(#$relationNotExistsExists #$performedBy #$Hunting #$Herbivore)' means that no herbivore hunts animals.")
(comment Microtubule "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Microtubules are the thickest of the three kinds of fibers that are constituents of cytoskeletons.")
(comment Microfilament "A specialization of #$CytoskeletonFiber.  Microfilaments rods made of actin that are part of the cytoskeleton.")
(comment TubulinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$TubulinMolecule is a globular protein molecule (see #$GlobularProteinMolecule). Tubulin is the primary constituent of #$Microtubules.")
(comment ActinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$ActinMolecule is a globular protein molecule (see #$GlobularProteinMolecule). Actin is the primary constituent of #$Microfilaments.")
(comment IntermediateFilament "A specialization of #$CytoskeletonFiber.  Intermediate filaments are a diverse class of filaments that are wider than #$Microfilaments and narrower than #$Microtubules.")
(comment CytoskeletonFiber "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Cytoskeleton fibers are the polymer molecules that constitute cytoskeletons -- they include #$Microtubules, #$Microfilaments and #$IntermediateFilaments.")
(comment Clone "The collection of organisms that are genetically identical to the organisms of which they are progeny.).")
(comment CyclicalProcessType "The collection of all cyclical event types.  An event type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> is considered cyclical in the requisite sense if its instances 1) decompose into stages, or \"scenes\" and 2) \"spawn\" subsequent instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.  This notion of \"spawning\" can be understood in terms of one event bringing about a state that serves as sufficient intitial conditions for the other to begin.  Accordingly, cyclical process types all feature a focal input/output class; that is, for any instance <code>EVT</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there is some type <code>TYPE</code> such that one or more instances of <code>TYPE</code> are inputs, and by virtue of the way <code>EVT</code>, one or more instances of <code>TYPE</code> are outputs that are situated so as to become inputs to subsequent instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.  To relate a cyclical process to its focal input/output type, use #$cyclicalProcessTypeFocus.")
(disjointWith MeiosisSubprocessType MitosisSubprocessType)
(comment ProphaseI "The first stage of #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment uniqueFirstProperSubEventTypes "The intersection (see #$predicateIntersection) of #$firstProperSubEventTypes and #$uniqueFirstProperSubSituationTypes, <code>(#$uniqueFirstProperSubEventTypes TYPE SUB)</code> identifies <code>SUB</code> as the collection that is both the first type of subevent in <code>TYPE</code> and the only subevent type of the type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle "One of the two major phases that make up the cell cycle (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), interphase is a period of growth, following by a period of chromosome replication, followed by another period of growth.")
(comment MeiosisSubprocessType "The collection of events-types instances of which are stages of meiotic cell division.")
(comment ProkaryoticCellCycle "The cell division cycle of prokaryotic cells.")
(comment CellDivisionCycleTypeByCellType "A specialization of #$CyclicalProcessType.  Instances are cell division cycles applicable to a common type of cell.")
(comment CellTypeByPloidy "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$EukaryoticCell into subcollections based on the #$numberOfChromosomeSets of their instances.")
(comment AtomOrMoleculeBindingEvent "The collection of all binding events wherein one #$ChemicalObject (usually characterizable as at least an #$Atom, #$Ion, or #$Molecule) becomes 'tightly associated with another to the extent that it is reasonable to distinguish the bound partners a single connected #$ChemicalObject:  either through the sharing of valence electrons (covalent bonding), trading of electrons (ionic bonding), or through weaker electrical force interactions (e.g., van der Waals bonding).")
(comment signalMoleculeInBindingEvent "Where ?BINDING is an #$AtomOrMoleculeBindingEvent, (#$signalMoleculeInBindingEvent BINDING MOL) means that, in a larger situational context of which BINDING is a part, MOL is a molecule  that transmits a signal which will mediately or immediately trigger a cytological 'response', either in isolation or in concert with several other typologically identical binding events.")
(comment organismHaploidNumber "<code>(#$organismHaploidNumber ORG N)</code> identifies <code>n</code> as the number of chromosomes in any (normal) #$Gamete of the organism <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment organismMonoploidNumber "<code>(#$organismMonoploidNumber ORG X)</code> identifies <code>X</code> as the number of chromosomes in a complete set of chromosomes belonging to the organism <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment cellSource "<code>(#$cellSource CELL SOURCE)</code> means that the instance <code>CELL</code> of #$Cell originates from (in the sense that it is a #$physicalDecompositions of, or has been extracted from) <code>SOURCE</code>, an instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject, be it some biological tissue, an organ, or an instance of #$Organism-Whole.")
(comment cellHasNumberOfChromosomes "<code>(#$cellHasNumberOfChromosomes CELL NUMBER)</code> identifies <code>NUMBER</code> as the number of chromosomes present in <code>CELL</code>, an instance of #$EukaryoticCell.  Note that this is an instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation, as the number of chromosomes may change depending on where in the cell cycle a cell is.")
(comment organismTypeHaploidNumber "<code>(#$organismTypeHaploidNumber ORG-TYPE N)</code> identifies <code>n</code> as the number of chromosomes in any (normal) #$Gamete of organisms of type <code>ORG-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest "The collection of instances of #$KBContentTest used to measure progress in answering questions for the cytological process project.")
(comment CytologicalProcessBaseContentTest "The collection of all instances of #$CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest that form the basis of the test suite of queries in development for testing knowledge of cellular biology.  Queries belong in this collection if they test that the biological knowledge is present to find the right answer to some potential or actual AP-style choice question, and so do not test whether knowledge or meta-knowledge is available to help rule out wrong or misleading answers given in a multiple-choice format. These queries are typically not part of the AP-style question test-suite.")
(comment CPTComputationAndReasoningTest "The collection of instances of #$CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest that test the system's ability to do algebraic computations relevant to the domain of cytological processes.")
(comment Aneuploidy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has an abnormal number of chromosomes.")
(comment PercutaneousProcedureName "The collection of specific percutaneous procedures.  The named subcollections of this collection constitute specific percutaneous procedure types that are of interest to major hospitals.")
(comment interestedInBuying "(#$interestedInBuying PERSON PRODUCT-TYPE) means PERSON is interested in buying an instance of PRODUCT-TYPE.")
(comment TravellingToPlaceFn "(#$TravellingToPlaceFn PLACE) returns the collection of all instances of #$TransportationEvent in which the destination is PLACE.")
(comment travelDestinationOfType "(#$travelDestinationOfType TRAVEL-TYPE PLACE) means that during instances of TRAVEL-TYPE, a spec of #$TransportationEvent, PLACE is the destination.")
(comment desiresSitRole "This predicate relates agents to types of situations that the agent wants to actualize. (#$desiresSitRole AGENT SITUATION ROLE) means that AGENT desires that some instance of SITUATION occurs in which s/he plays the role ROLE in the situation.  See also #$desires.")
(disjointWith DevisedPracticeOrWork SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption)
(comment MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification "The collection of all instances of #$CycLQuerySpecification that represent multiple choice questions.  Multiple choice questions have one or more possible answers; these are related to the question via the #$candidateAnswers predicate.")
(comment candidateAnswers "<code>(#$candidateAnswers QUESTION ANSWER)</oode> identifies </code>ANSWER</code>, and instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption, as one of the possible answers associated with the instance <code>QUESTION</code> of #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionExclusionSet "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a given possible answer for a multiple choice question (an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption) to its content (see #$multipleChoiceOptionContents), where that content consists in the exclusion of other answers from the choice set as correct options.  Specifically, where <code>QUESTION</code> is a multiple choice question (see #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification) such that <code>CHOICE</code> is one of its possible answers (i.e., <code>(#$candidateAnswers QUESTION CHOICE)</code>, <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionExclusionSet CHOICE SET)</code> means that <code>CHOICE</code> is the option that the elements of <code>SET</code> are incorrect answers for <code>QUESTION</code>.  For example, where <code>CHOICE-A</code>, <code>CHOICE-B</code>, and <code>CHOICE-C</code> are, along with <code>CHOICE</code> the choices for <code>QUESTION</code>, and <code>CHOICE</code> is the choice that \"None of the above\" then this would be represnted as <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionExclusionSet CHOICE (#$TheSet CHOICE-A CHOICE-B CHOICE-C))</code>.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionAffirmationSet "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a given possible answer for a multiple choice question (an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption) to its content (see #$multipleChoiceOptionContents), where that content consists in the affirmation that one or more of the other answers from the choice set is correct.  Specifically, where <code>QUESTION</code> is a multiple choice question (see #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification) such that <code>CHOICE</code> is one of its possible answers (i.e., <code>(#$candidateAnswers QUESTION CHOICE)</code>, <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionAffirmationSet CHOICE SET)</code> means that <code>CHOICE</code> is the option that the elements of <code>SET</code> are correct answers for <code>QUESTION</code>.  For example, where <code>CHOICE-A</code>, <code>CHOICE-B</code>, and <code>CHOICE-C</code> are, along with <code>CHOICE</code> the choices for <code>QUESTION</code>, and <code>CHOICE</code> is the choice that \"A and C\" then this would be represnted as <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionAffirmationSet CHOICE (#$TheSet CHOICE-A CHOICE-C))</code>.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionPayload "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a given possible answer for a multiple choice question (an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption) to its content (see #$multipleChoiceOptionContents), where that content consists in a proposed binding set for variables posed in the question.   For example, where <code>QUESTION</code> asks for bindings for some variable ?NUM, and <code>CHOICE</code> is the choice that proposes 12 as a binding, then this would be represented as <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionPayload CHOICE (#$TheSet
   (#$ELInferenceBindingFn ?NUM 12))
</code>.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionContents "The most general predicate that relates an instance of  #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption to its content.  In general, a multiple choice option has one of two kinds of content: it either offers an answer (e.g., that 12 is the answer to some calculation), or its content consists in the affirmation and/or exclusion of other possible answers.   For multiple choice options of the first kind, one should use the more specific predicate, #$multipleChoiceOptionPaylod.  For multiple choice options of the second kind one should use #$multipleChoiceOptionExclusionSet and/or #$multipleChoiceOptionAffirmationSet.")
(comment SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption "The collection of all specified options (\"possible answers\") to multiple choice questions.  <i>Specified</i> options are structured objects that are (typically) unique to a particular question, and have <i>content</i> that is frequently a <i>payload</i> that is a proposed binding for some variable (e.g., a specified option might be that <i>12</i> is the right answer), but is sometimes an affirmation and/or exclusion of some other specified option(s) for the same question (e.g., \"A and B,\" or \"A and B but not C\" or \"none of the above\").")
(comment MCQuestionNthOptionFn "An instance of #$PartialFunction that takes an instance of #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification and an integer and returns an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption that is the integer<i>th</i> option in the list of options given for that question.  <code>(#$MCQuestionNthOptionFn QUESTION N)</code> denotes the <code>N</code>th option for the multiple choice question <code>QUESTION</code>.")
(comment mcQuestionNthOption "<code>(#$mcQuestionNthOption QUESTION N OPTION)</code> identifies <ocde>OPTION</code> as the <code>N</code>th option (see #$candidateAnswers) specified for <code>QUESTION</code>, an instance of  #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification.  This is the predicate that corresponds to the function #$MCQuestionNthOptionFn.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel "A predicate used to represent informal features common to the presentation of multiple choice questions.  Specifically, in human-targeted representatons of questons, options are typically given an index (often a numeral or a letter) used as a shorthand way to refer to that option within the context of that question.  <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel OPTION INDEX)</code> identifies the string <code>INDEX</code> as the string used to assign an index to <code>OPTION</code>.")
(comment multipleChoiceOptionFullLabel "A predicate used to represent informal features common to the presentation of multiple choice questions.  Specifically, in human-targeted representations of questions, options are typically given an index (often a numeral or a letter) followed by an string that expresses the content of the answer.  <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel OPTION DESC)</code> identifies the string <code>DESC</code> as the full string (index + answer) assigned to <code>OPTION</code>.  For example, if <code>OPTION</code> appears (or is intended to appear) in text as \"iv. Meoisis II\" this would be represented as <code>(#$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel OPTION. \"iv. Meoisis II\")</code>.  See also #$multipleChoiceOptionIndexLabel.")
(comment LivingBiologicalAgent "A specialization of both #$BiologicalAgentStuff and #$Microorganism.  Each instance of #$LivingBiologicalAgent is a living micro-organism that is also a biological agent.")
(comment Cytokinesis "An instance of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  In each instance of #$Cytokinesis the cytoplasm of a single eukaryotic cell is divided to form two daughter cells.")
(comment Centromere "The collection of centromeres.  A centromere is a series of nucleotide pairs on a fully formed strand of chromatin (see #$ChromatinStrand) where the two constituent chromatids (see #$chromatids) of a duplicated chromosome (see #$DuplicatedChromosome) meet.  During Anaphase, kinetochores (see #$Kinetochore) attached to the centromeres become attached to spindle fibers which separate the chromatids, resulting in two chromosomes.  The collection #$Centromere is to be distinguished from the more general notion of the centromeric region (see #$centromericRegion), which, by convention, is a property of chromosomes, and not chromatids, which, by virtue of containing fully formed DNA molecules, do have centromeres.  Moreover, every chromosome has a single centromeric region, while a chromosome (specifically, a duplicated chromosome, by virtue of having two chromatids) may have two centromeres.  In the biological literature, \"centromere\" almost always refers to the unique centromeric region of a chromosome, but its sense \"slides\" to the more precise sense represented by #$Centromere when discussions turn to the details of cell division.")
(comment centromericRegion "<code>(#$centromericRegion CHROMOSOME REGION)</code> identifies <code>REGION</code> as the so-called \"primary constriction\" of <code>CHROMOSOME</code>, an instance of #$Chromosome.  The centromeric region consists of, in the case of a #$UnduplicatedChromosome, its centromere (see #$Centromere), but in the case of a #$DuplicatedChromosome, the mereological sum of the centromeres of its constituent chromatids (see #$chromatids).")
(comment UnduplicatedChromosome "An instance of #$ChromosomeTypeByDuplicationLevel.  Instances are fully condensed instances of #$ChromatinStrand that are the results of two chromatids (see #$chromatids) having been pulled apart from their \"parent\" chromosome (see #$DuplicatedChromosome).")
(comment PartiallyDuplicatedChromosome "An instance of #$ChromosomeTypeByDuplicationLevel, instances are chromosomes that are in the process of duplication, and so are neither fully duplicated (see #$DuplicatedChromosome) nor completely unduplicated (see #$UnduplicatedChromosome).")
(comment ChromatinStrand "The collection of all fully formed (i.e., containing a complete instance of #$DNAMolecule) strands of #$Chromatin. Instances of this collection are either instances of #$Chromosome, or are as-yet-to-be-separated chromatids (see #$chromatids) that are about to be re-classified as chromosomes.")
(disjointWith DuplicatedChromosome ChromatinStrand)
(disjointWith PartiallyDuplicatedChromosome ChromatinStrand)
(comment chromatids "<code>(#$chromatids CHROMOSOME CHROMATID)</code> identifies <code>CHROMOSOME</code> as the instance of #$DuplicatedChromosome for which <code>CHROMATID</code> is one of its two constituent chromatids.")
(comment CytoplasmicReceptorMolecule "The collection of all instances of #$ReceptorMolecule that are located within a #$Cytoplasm.")
(disjointWith MembraneReceptorMolecule CytoplasmicReceptorMolecule)
(comment ChemicalObjectBindingEvent "The collection of all reactions in which one #$ChemicalObject (in particular, an atom, molecule, or ion) binds to another (i.e., another atom, molecule or ion) via a chemical bond of some kind (an ionic or covalent bond, or through weaker electrical force attraction).")
(comment candidateReceptorTypeForLigand "Where RECEPTOR-TYPE is a specialization of #$ChemicalObject and MOL is a particular instance of #$ChemicalObject, (#$candidateReceptorTypeForLigand RECEPTOR-TYPE MOL) means that MOL is capable of binding to instances of RECEPTOR-TYPE in reactions that ordinarily trigger responses at the cellular scale, either immediately or mediately in virtue of transduction pathways.")
(disjointWith HydrophilicChemicalObject HydrophobicChemicalObject)
(comment HydrophilicChemicalObject "The collection of nanoscopic entities (primarily molecules, ions, atoms) which show an electrochemical affinity for liquid water, such that a chemical substance composed of these entities can be thoroughly incorporated into a sample of liquid water by mixing.")
(comment ProphaseII "The first stage of #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment MetaphaseII "The second stage of #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment AnaphaseII "The third stage in #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment TelophaseII "The fourth stage in #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment MetaphaseI "The second stage #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment TelophaseI "The fourth stage #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment Anaphase "The collection of events which are the fourth phase of #$Mitosis. In this phase, the paired chromatids separate to form two daughter chromosomes, and they are pulled to the spindle pole on each side of the dividing cell nucleus. Chromosome separation is aided both by the shortening of the kinetochore microtubules and the spindle poles moving apart.")
(comment MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle is an event in which a eukaryotic cell undergoes both #$Mitosis and #$Cytokinesis.")
(comment SecondMeioticCellDivision "A type of cell division which is the second step of #$Meiosis. Its two sub-event types are #$MeiosisII and #$Cytokinesis.  The two offspring cells get one copy of each #$Chromosome.")
(comment FirstMeioticCellDivision "A type of cell division which is the first step of #$Meiosis. The two major sub-event types of this event type are #$MeiosisI and #$Cytokinesis.  The two offspring cells get one copy of each replicated (doubled) #$Chromosome, which later splits in two in the second division.")
(comment MeiosisI "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  In each instance of #$MeiosisI, the nucleus of a eukaryotic germ cell divides.  #$MeiosisI is the first stage of #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment MeiosisII "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  In each instance of #$MeiosisII, the nucleus of a eukaryotic germ cell divides.  #$MeiosisII is the first stage of #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment StateInCountryFn "(#$StateInCountryFn COUNTRY) returns the collection of #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions for COUNTRY.  For example, (#$StateInCountryFn #$Liberia) will return the collection of cities in #$Liberia.")
(comment statesOfCountry "A relation relating a #$Country to the collection of its #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions.  If true, (#$statesOfCountry #$State-UnitedStates  #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) means that all and only instances of #$State-UnitedStates are #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions of #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  In fact, (#$statesOfCountry #$State-UnitedStates  #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) is not true, because #$DistrictOfColumbia (among others) is also a #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivision of the United States. ")
(comment HydrophobicChemicalObject "The collection of all nanoscopic entities (primarily molecules, ions, atoms) which have a tendency to electrochemically repel molecules of liquid water, such that a chemical substance composed of these entities will separate out of and resist mixing with water.")
(comment CPTProcessStageOrderingTest "The collection of instances of #$CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest that test the system's ability to reason about the ordering of stages in a (class of) process.")
(comment MultipleChoiceKBContentTest "The collection of all KB content tests that test an instance of #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification.")
(comment queryContentString "<code>(#$queryContentString QUERY STRING)</code> identifies the string <code>STRING</code> as the NL string representation of the content of <code>QUERY</code>, an instance of #$CycLQuerySpecification.")
(comment NorepinephrineMolecule "The collection of molecules of the stress hormone substance #$Norepinephrine, chemical formula C8H11NO3.  As a stress hormone, norepinephrine affects those parts of the brain controlling attention and response.")
(comment DopamineMolecule "The collection of all molecules of #$Dopamine, chemical formula C8H11NO2. Instances can function as neurotransmitters, activating at least five different types of dopamine receptor molecules in the brain.")
(comment TestosteroneMolecule "The collection of all molecules of #$Testosterone, chemical formula C19H28O2.")
(comment ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent "The collection of all events in which a chemical bond (molecular, covalent, or ionic) is broken, and previously bonded #$ChemicalObjects begin to act on their environment as separate units.")
(comment typesBondedInBindingEventType "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for #$ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn")
(comment typesSeparatedInUnbindingEventType "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for #$ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn")
(comment ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent classes by means of the types of #$ChemicalObject whose binding characterizes the class.  More specifically, where MOL-TYPE1 and MOL-TYPE2 two are classes of #$ChemicalObject, (#$ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn MOL-TYPE1 MOL-TYPE2) denotes the collection of all #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvents such that a #$ChemicalObject of tye MOL-TYPE1 bonds chemically with a #$ChemicalObject of type MOL-TYPE2, resulting in a new #$ChemicalObject with instances of MOL-TYPE1 and MOL-TYPE2 as physical parts.   See also the #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical, #$typesBondedInBindingEventType.")
(comment partTypesAbsent "<code>(#$partTypesAbsent INDIVIDUAL PART-TYPE)</code> means that the instance of #$Individual <code>INDIVIDUAL</code> is unusual with respect to other instances of some collection of which it is an instance, in that it is lacking an instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as a part.")
(comment closestHistoryAndPhysicalWithDiagnosis "<code>(#$closestHistoryAndPhysicalWithDiagnosis EVT1 EVT2 DIAG-TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> beginning prior to or starting at the same time as EVT2 that is associated with a medical diagnosis of DIAG-TYPE.")
(comment Kinetochore "The collection of kinetochores.  Kinetochores are structures comprised of protein molecules that play a role in cell division. Kinetochores attach to chromatids of duplicated chromosomes and subseqently bind with microtubules that eventually pull the chromatids apart, resulting in two new chromosomes.")
(comment CellCyclePhaseType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType instances of which are all and only those specializations of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that are significant sub-processes of the eukaryotic cell cycle.")
(comment rgDatasetIsForLDSReport "A predicate used to indicate whether the current dataset is to be used for a limited dataset report.")
(comment rgDatasetCurrentType "A unary predicate used to indicate what type of dataset is currently available to the report generator.")
(comment County-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"counties\".")
(comment District-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"districts\".")
(comment Region-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"regions\".")
(comment Circumscription-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"circumscriptions\".")
(comment IslandGroup-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"island groups\".")
(comment Municipality-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"municipalities\".")
(comment Island-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"islands\".")
(comment Division-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"divisions\".")
(comment Governorate-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"governates\".")
(comment Department-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"departments\".")
(comment Parish-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"parishes\".")
(comment Quarter-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"quarters\".")
(comment Zone-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"zones\".")
(comment Commune-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"communes\".")
(comment AutonomousCommunity-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"autonomous communities\".")
(comment Emirate-State-Geopolitical "The subcollection of #$State-Geopolitical which are also known as \"emirates\".")
(comment eventOrPreopEvalWithinIntervalInvolvesMedicationType "<code>(#$eventOrPreopEvalWithinIntervalInvolvesMedicationType EVENT INTERVAL MED-TYPE STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that <code>MED-TYPE</code> has STSTUS-TYPE within <code>INTERVAL</code> prior to the occurrence of <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment closestHAndPPriorWithMedAndStatus "<code>(#$closestHistoryAndPhysicalWithDiagnosis EVT1 EVT2 MED-TYPE STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that <code>EVT1</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> beginning prior to or starting at the same time as EVT2 that is associated with MED-TYPE that has STATUS-TYPE.")
(comment ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent "The collection of all #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvents wherein information is transferred at the cellular level by means of the translocation of one or more signaling #$ChemicalObjects (individual atoms, molecules, or ions).  #$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent instances may happen between #$Cells (see #$ChemicalObjectInterCellularSignalTransmissionEvent) or they may be confined within the #$Cytoplasm and/or nucleus of a single #$Cell (see #$ChemicalObjectIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent).")
(comment ChemicalObjectInterCellularSignalTransmissionEvent "An important specialization of #$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent.  Each instance is a case of#$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent in which the information transfer involved occurs between two different #$Cells, one of them the identifiable #$fromLocation of the translocation, and the other the identifiable #$toLocation, through the intercellular medium between them.  One or more #$ChemicalObjects (individual atoms, ions, molecules) serve as the #$meansOfInfoTransfer. ")
(disjointWith ChemicalObjectIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent ChemicalObjectInterCellularSignalTransmissionEvent)
(comment ChemicalObjectIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvents that begin and end within the #$Cytoplasm of a single #$Cell.")
(comment ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjects (atoms, ions, molecules) that can serve as chemical messengers mediating a cellular response in terms of morphology and/or behavior, and that are (defeasibly) able to travel through the inter-cellular medium from the point of emission in order to reach their binding sites.  The binding site itself may be in the cell membrane or located within the cytoplasm.")
(comment ExclusivelyIntracellularSignalingChemicalObject "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjects (individual atoms, ions, molecules) that under normal conditions are only characteristically capable of mediating #$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvents that occur entirely within the cytoplasms of individual cells.  E.g., protein kinase molecules, which ordinarily function in signal transduction pathways within #$Cells only.")
(disjointWith ProteinMolecule CellularSignalingSecondMessenger)
(comment CellularSignalingSecondMessenger "A very important ExclusivelyIntracellularSignalingChemicalObject subclass.  As a rule, #$CellularSignalingSecondMessenger instances are small #$Ions or #$Molecules that are not coded for in the genome (i.e., are not #$ProteinMolecules) and that are 'broadcast' within a #$Cell to facilitate various tranduction pathways, e.g., through triggered release from the #$EndoplasmicReticulum.")
(comment PhospholipaseCMolecule "A class of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of cleaving instances of a plasma membrane phospholipid class, Pip2, into DiacylGlycerol (DAG) andthe #$CellularSignalingSecondMessenger Ip3.")
(disjointWith ReversibleProcess TakingAUrineSample)
(disjointWith ReversibleProcess DissolutionOfNuclearEnvelope)
(comment Mitosis "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel. Each instance of #$Mitosis is an event in which the nucleus of a #$EukaryoticCell divides to result in a separation of the raw materials suitable for constructing two new nuclei, each with the same chromosome number and genomic content as the parent cell. This is the type of nuclear division that occurs in the somatic cells of multicellular eukaryotic organisms. Each #$Mitosis event is a sub-event of a #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle during which an instance of #$Cytokinesis happens after the mitosis.")
(comment rolePlayerTypeDeterminedBySubSitType "<code>(#$rolePlayerTypeDeterminedBySubSitType SUPER-TYPE ROLE TYPE SUB-TYPE)</code> means that whether any instances of <code>TYPE</code> play the role <code>ROLE</code> in an instance <code>I</code>of <code>SUPER-TYPE</code> is dependent on the existence of an instance of <code>SUB-TYPE</code> as a #$subSituations of <code>I</code>.  Specifically, the exact number of instances/amount of <code>TYPE</code> such that <code>ROLE</code> relates those instances/that amount to <code>I</code> must be exactly the same number/amount that are so related to the relevant instance of <code>SUB-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Telophase "An instance of #$MitosisSubprocessType.  Each instance of #$Telophase is the final stage of some #$Mitosis process, occuring right before #$Cytokinesis.  During #$Telophase, a nuclear membrane forms around each set of chromosomes, the nucleoli reappear, and the chromosomes start to decondense.")
(disjointWith IntermediateFilament Microtubule)
(disjointWith Microfilament Microtubule)
(disjointWith Microfilament IntermediateFilament)
(comment EntityOfTypeBetweenStagesFn "A collection denoting function used for denoting classes of role players that are temporally 'at' certain stages in situations that are instances of 'scripted' #$TemporalObjectTypes.  Specifically, where OBJ-TYPE is a kind of #$SomethingExisting, SIT-TYPE is a class of #$Situation in whose instances instances of OBJ-TYPE are known to play a 'constituent' role (see #$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType), SUBSIT-TYPE1 is a known 'stage' of instances of SIT-TYPE (see #$properSubSituationTypes), SUBSIT-TYPE2 is a known 'stage' of instances of SIT-TYPE succeeding instances of SUBSIT-TYPE1 (see #$properSubSituationTypes and #$startsAfterEndOfInSituationType), (#$EntityOfTypeBetweenStagesFn OBJ-TYPE SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2) deonoes the collection of all instances of OBJ-TYPE such that they are #$actors in an instance of SIT-TYPE, and such that they are at the instant of having completed an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1 in the SIT-TYPE instance, and have yet to undergo a succeeding instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2.")
(comment iterationCardinality "<code>(#$iterationCardinality EVENT N)</code> identifies <code>N</code> as the number of iterations through events of the type <code>TYPE</code> for which <code>EVENT</code> is an instance of #$IteratedEventScene.  <code>(#$iterationCardinality EVENT N)</code> thus entails <code>(#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$properSubEvents EVENT TYPE N)</code> for the requisite type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment eventSceneIterationType "<code>(#$eventSceneIterationType EVENT TYPE)</code> identifies </code>TYPE</code> as the type of event that <code>EVENT</code>, an instance of #$IteratedEventScene iterates through.")
(comment EntityOfTypeBetweenStages-ScriptImplicitFn "A collection denoting function used for denoting classes of role players that are temporally 'at' certain stages in situations that are instances of 'scripted' #$TemporalObjectTypes.  Specifically, where OBJ-TYPE is a kind of #$SomethingExisting, and SUBSIT-TYPE1 and SUBSIT-TYPE2 are known successive 'stages' of a instances some 'scripted' situation type in whose instances instances of OBJ-TYPE are known to play a role, (#$EntityOfTypeBetweenStagesFn OBJ-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2) deonotes the collection of all instances of OBJ-TYPE at the instant of having completed an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1 in the SIT-TYPE instance, and have yet to undergo a succeeding instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2.")
(comment entityOfTypeBetweenStages-ScriptImplicit "The corresponding predicate of EntityOfTypeBetweenStages-ScriptImplicitFn.")
(comment Prophase "An instance of #$MitosisSubprocessType.  Each instance of #$Prophase is a sub-event of the mitosis of a cell during which the nucleolus disappears, chromosomes thicken, and centrioles generate spindle fibers.  Prophase is the first stage of #$Mitosis.")
(comment criticalPhysicalPartTypeForFunctioningOfWholeType "<code>(#$criticalPhysicalPartTypeForFunctioningOfWholeType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that in order to serve its primary function (see #$primaryFunction) as a device (see #$deviceUsed), any instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> must have a working instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as a physical part.")
(comment criticalPhysicalPartForFunctioningOfWhole "<code>(#$criticalPhysicalPartForFunctioningOfWhole WHOLE PART)</code>  means that <code>PART</code> is a proper physical part of <code>WHOLE</code>, and that in order to serve its primary function (see #$primaryFunction) as a device (see #$deviceUsed), <code>WHOLE</code> must have <code>PART</code> as a physical part.")
(comment SituatedObjectType "A specialization of #$TimeDependentCollection, this is the collection of all collections of objects that, by definition, are currently playing a specific role (see #$BinarySituationPredicate) in a situation of a particular type.  For example, the (fictionally reified) #$BatterAtThePlate is an instance of #$SituatedObjectType, as it is the collection of instances of people who are currently playing the role of #$batter in some instance of (#$PlayingFn #$Baseball-TheGame).")
(comment situationTypeFocalObjectType "<code>(#$situationTypeFocalObjectType SIT-TYPE OBJECT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code> as the unique instance of #$SituatedObjectType such that, by definition, its instances are all playing a specific role in some instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Situation.")
(comment situatedObjectTypeFocalRole "<code>(#$situatedObjectTypeFocalRole OBJECT-TYPE ROLE)</code> identifies <code>ROLE</code> as the central role that each instance of <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code> is actively playing in the situation type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> for which <code>(#$situationTypeFocalObjectType SIT-TYPE OBJECT-TYPE)</code> holds.")
(comment 8ByteIntegerDatatype "The collection of all computer data types that employ exactly 8 bytes to represent some subset of the integers or values related to representing integer values such as NAN. Note that this does not specify, for example, whether the data type represents positive integers only, or is in two's complement representation.")
(comment stageTypeDependsOnStageType "(#$stageTypeDependsOnStageType PROCESS-TYPE DEP-STAGE-TYPE INDEP-STAGE-TYPE) means that if ATTEMPT is an instance of (#$AttemptingFn PROCESS-TYPE), then ATTEMPT situationally subsumes an instance of DEP-STAGE-TYPE only if it subsumes an instance of INDEP-STAGE-TYPE; conversely, if ATTEMPT does NOT subsume an instance of INDEP-STAGE-TYPE, it will not assume an instance of DEP-STAGE-TYPE.")
(comment SignedFn "(#$SignedFn TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of TYPE that are signed.")
(comment UnsignedFn "(#$UnsignedFn TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of TYPE that are unsigned.")
(comment signedVersionOfDatatype "(#$signedVersionOfDatatype TYPE SIGNED-TYPE) means that SIGNED-TYPE is the signed (i.e. two's complement) version of TYPE.")
(comment unsignedVersionOfDatatype "(#$signedVersionOfDatatype TYPE UNSIGNED-TYPE) means that UNSIGNED-TYPE is the unsigned version of TYPE.")
(comment stageTypeDependsOnOutputTypeFromStageType "(#$stageTypeDependsOnOutputTypeFromStageType PROCESS-TYPE DEP-STAGE-TYPE OUTPUT-TYPE INDEP-STAGE-TYPE) means that if ATTEMPT is an instance of (#$AttemptingFn PROCESS-TYPE), then it situationally subsumes an instance of DEP-STAGE-TYPE only if it situationally subsumes an instance of INDEP-STAGE-TYPE wherein an instance of OUTPUT-TYPE is the #$outputsCreated.")
(comment eventHasMedication "Relates a medical event to a drug substance associated with that event.")
(comment TypeOfThingWithLargeFanBase "instances of this collection are types of things with more or less widespread fan bases either mainstream or subculture.  These are the types of things that people form fan groups about, etc.  See the sister collection that is about individuals #$IndividualWithLargeFanBase.")
(comment IndividualWithLargeFanBase "instances of this collection are individuals with more or less widespread fan bases either mainstream or subculture.  These are the things that people form fan groups about, etc.  See the sister collection that is about collections #$TypeOfThingWithLargeFanBase.")
(comment existsAgentOfTypeInRoleFromSubSituationOfType "A rule-macro predicate for encapsulating a certain existential claim about #$Situation instances, their #$properSubSituations, and role players in those #$properSubSituations.  Specifically, where SIT is a #$Situation, AGT-TYPE is a specialization of #$SomethingExisting, SUBSIT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Situation, and ROLE is a #$BinarySituationPredicate, (#$existsAgentOfTypeInRoleFromSubSituationOfType SIT AGT-TYPE ROLE SUBSIT-TYPE) holds if and only if there exists an instance AGT of AGT-TYPE and an instance SUBSIT of SUBSIT-TYPE, such that (ROLE SUBSIT AGT) and (#$properSubSituations SIT SUBSIT).")
(comment ExtraSensoryPerception "The collection of all #$Perceiving events in which information is transferred to an intelligent being through some means other than the generally recognized senses.")
(comment hospitalVisitDrugStatusWhenForCathOrPCI "<code>(#$hospitalVisitDrugStatusWhenForCathOrPCI EVENT MED-TYPE WHEN-TYPE STATUS-EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that relative to the patient treated in the hospital visit <code>EVENT</code>, at qualitative time <code>WHEN</code> (either during the cath lab visit or at discharge) the medication type <code>MED-TYPE</code> has the status <code>STATUS-EVENT-TYPE</code>.  E.g. it is contraindicated at discharge.")
(comment EDGAR-DATA-PS "A physical schema for #$EDGAR-DATA-KS.")
(comment EDGAR-REPORT-PS "A physical schema for #$EDGAR-REPORT-KS.")
(disjointWith HumanCyclist NonHumanCyclist)
(comment CMUReadTheWebOntology "The ontology (see #$Ontology) used by the #$CMUReadTheWebSystem.")
(comment venueInCity "(#$venueInCity PLACE CITY) means that the #$ConstructionArtifact PLACE has the relationship #$inRegion to the territory of the #$City CITY.  This is intended to represent 'venues' such as sports stadiums, concert halls, or other locations where public gathering take place.")
(comment ReportTestParameterSpecification "The collection of specifications for running tests on Cyc-generated medical reports.")
(comment sksOfReportTest "(#$sksOfReportTest REP-PARAM-SPEC SKS) means that the #$ReportTestParameterSpecification REP-PARAM-SPEC requires SKS to be registered.")
(comment pathnameForReportDefinition "(#$pathnameforReportDefinition REP-PARAM-SPEC PATH) means that the #$ReportTestParameterSpecification REP-PARAM-SPEC uses the report defined at the absolute pathname PATH.")
(comment baselineDirectoryForReport "(#$baselineDirectoryForReport REP-PARAM-SPEC PATH) means that the #$ReportTestParameterSpecification REP-PARAM-SPEC uses the files in PATH as baselines.")
(comment MRExternalOntology "The #$Ontology used with the MachineReadingData-KS developed for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment TissueTypeByOrganType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$BiologicalTissue into subcollections based on the type of organ that the tissue comprises.")
(comment tissueTypeOfOrganType "<code>(#$tissueTypeOfOrganType TISSUE-TYPE ORGAN-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TISSUE-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that is tissue from an organ of type <code>ORGAN-TYPE</code>.")
(comment TissueTypeOfOrganTypeFn "<code>(#$TissueTypeOfOrganTypeFn ORGAN-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that is tissue from an organ of type <code>ORGAN-TYPE</code>.")
(comment EpidermalTissue "The collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue comprised of epidermal cells, a kind of skin cell.")
(comment DermalTissue "The collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue comprised of dermal cells, a kind of skin cell.")
(disjointWith DermalTissue EpidermalTissue)
(comment reportTestComparesFilenamesWRTKeycolumn "(#$reportTestComparesFilenamesWRTKeycolumn PARAMETER-SPECIFICATION BASELINE-FILENAME OUTPUT-FILENAME KEY-COLUMN) means that the values of the baseline file BASELINE-FILENAME1 and output file OUTPUT-FILENAME should be compared on the rows with the same values in the column labeled KEY-COLUMN.")
(comment sitTypeRequiresRolePlayerOfTypeInSubSitType "(#$sitTypeRequiresRolePlayerOfTypeInSubSitType SIT-TYPE AGT-TYPE ROLE SUBSIT-TYPE) means that every instance of SIT-TYPE must feature both an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE as a #$properSubSituations and an instance of AGT-TYPE playing ROLE in that subsituation.")
(comment processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType "(#$processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType PROCESS-TYPE REACTION-TYPE ENZYME-TYPE) means that where PROCESS-TYPE is a specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel, instances of PROCESS-TYPE ordinarily require at least one instance of the the #$ChemicalReaction type REACTION-TYPE to be catalyzed by an instance of the #$EnzymeMolecule type ENZYME-TYPE to complete successfully.")
(comment ActivatedFormOfEnzymeFn "Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$ActivatedFormOfEnzymeFn MOL-TYPE) in a given context denotes the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are capable (#$behaviorCapable) of catalyzing the 'target' reaction supported by MOL-TYPE in a cellular process context (see #$processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType), usually as the result of having been activated in an #$EnzymeActivationEvent instance.")
(comment activatedFormOfEnzyme "The corresponding predicate of #$ActivatedFormOfEnzymeFn. Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$activatedFormOfEnzyme MOL-TYPE ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE) in a given context means that ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are capable (#$behaviorCapable) of catalyzing the 'target' reaction supported by MOL-TYPE in a cellular process context (see #$processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType), usually as the result of having been activated in an #$EnzymeActivationEvent instance.")
(comment GuanosineDiphosphate "A collection of nucleotides involved in energy metabolism and transduction pathways.  They contain a #$Guanine-Base linked to a #$Ribose and two phosphates.")
(comment GProteinActivationEvent "The collection of all events in which a #$GProteinMolecule is 'activated' by being chemically unbound from a molecule of #$GuanosineDiphosphate and subsequently bound to a molecule of #$GuanosineTriphosphate. ")
(comment Form10K "An #$AnnualBusinessReport filed by US companies to the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission.")
(comment Form10Q "A #$QuarterlyFinancialStatement filed by US companies to the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission.")
(comment Form8K "A report filed by US companies to the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission to report important changes or updates in between regular periodic reports.")
(comment ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used to represent the class of 'activations' of a given type of enzyme.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'active' in the sense of being enabled to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of (#$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically unbound from an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which otherwise blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, followed immediately by a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is bound to an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) which enables it to catalyze the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.")
(comment enzymeTypeActivatedInActivationType "The corresponding predicate of #$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeActivatedInActivationType MOL-TYPE ACTIVATION-TYPE) means that ACTIVATION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'active' in the sense of being enabled to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of ACTIVATION-TYPE will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically unbound from an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which otherwise blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, followed immediately by a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is bound to an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) which enables it to catalyze the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.")
(comment activationFactorForEnzyme "A type level predicate that links a class of #$EnzymeMolecule to a class of #$ChemicalObject.  (#$activationFactorForEnzyme FACTOR-TYPE ENZYME-TYPE) means that ordinarily, instances of FACTOR-TYPE 'activate' instances of ENZYME-TYPE when bonded to them chemically, in the strict sense that the activated instance is enabled to catalyze certain kinds of chemical reaction.")
(comment AdenylylCyclaseMolecule "An important class of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are able to catalyze large-scale production of cyclic AMP (cAMP) within the cellular cytosol when they are 'activated' by having their #$AdenosineDiphosphate component replaced with an #$AdenosineTriphosphate component.")
(comment AdenosineDiphosphate "A kind of #$Nucleotide.  Instances play an important role in several kinds of chemical reaction involving cellular metabolism and enzyme activation.")
(comment organismDiploidNumber "<code>(#$organismDiploidNumber ORG N)</code> identifies <code>N</code> as the number of chromosomes in any (normal) instance of #$SomaticCell of the organism <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment EDGARDatumFromIDsFn "(#$EDGARDatumFromIDsFn REPORT-ID CONCEPT-ID) denotes the datum in the report whose ID is REPORT-ID that assigns a value for the concept identified by CONCEPT-ID.")
(comment mediaOrganizationPrimaryServiceArea "(#$mediaOrganizationPrimaryServiceArea ORG PLACE) means that ORG's primary area of service (typically, the place it claims to represent in its ads) is PLACE.  In rare cases, it may be possible that the organization is not headquarted in PLACE.  Examples of this would include dissident media that is run by exiles from a country.")
(comment newspaperPrimaryServiceArea "(#$newspaperPrimaryServiceArea PAPER PLACE) means that PAPER's primary area of service (typically, the place it claims to represent in its ads) is PLACE.  In rare cases, it may be possible that the newspaper is not headquarted in PLACE.  Examples of this would include dissident media that is run by exiles from a country.")
(comment mediaOrganizationInCity "(#$mediaOrganizationInCity MEDIA CITY) is true when MEDIA is a media organization headquartered in CITY, and whose primary service area includes CITY.  In the United States, this is the most common relationship between media organizations and cities (i.e. WABC and New York, KNBC and Los Angeles).  Notable examples where this relationship will not hold include exile media outlets such as  Radio y Television Marti, which is based in Miami, but which is designed primarily to serve the population of Cuba.")
(comment CoilingOfChromatinStrand "The collection of all events in which a single strand of chromatin coils.")
(comment uniqueProperSubEventTypes "<code>(#$uniqueProperSubEventTypes SUPER-EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance <code>E</code> of <code>SUPER-EVENT-TYPE</code> there is exactly one instance of <code>SUB-EVENT-TYPE</code> that is a (proper) sub-event of <code>E</code>.")
(comment inactivatedFormOfEnzyme "The corresponding predicate of #$InactivatedFormOfEnzymeFn. Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$inactivatedFormOfEnzyme MOL-TYPE INACTIVE-MOL-TYPE) in a given context means that INACTIVE-MOL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are incapable (#$behaviorIncapable) of catalyzing the 'target' reaction supported by MOL-TYPE in a cellular process context (see #$processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType), usually because the molecule in question needs to be activated in an #$EnzymeActivationEvent instance. ")
(comment stringPrecedes "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$CharacterString to another intance of #$CharacterString. <code>(#$stringPrecedes EARLY LATER)</code> means that <code>EARLY</code> is a string that comes earlier than <code>LATER</code> using the standard lexicographic sort for strings.  For example, (#$stringPrecedes \"cat\" \"dog\"). See also #$stringPrecedes-CaseInsensitive for the case insensitive analog of this predicate.")
(comment stringPrecedes-CaseInsensitive "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$CharacterString to another intance of #$CharacterString. <code>(#$stringPrecedes-CaseInsensitive EARLY LATER)</code> means that <code>EARLY</code> is a string that comes earlier than <code>LATER</code> using the standard lexicographic sort for strings when case is ignored.  For example, (#$stringPrecedes-CaseInsensitive \"cat\" \"DOG\"). See also #$stringPrecedes for the case sensitive analog of this predicate.")
(comment mrExternalRelation "An SKSI-specific predicate meant to relate a SPARQL b-node (in this case, what's basically a Cyc assertion) with the predicate in that b-node.")
(comment mrExternalArg1 "An SKSI-specific predicate meant to relate a SPARQL b-node (in this case, what's basically a Cyc assertion) with the first argument of that b-node.")
(comment mrExternalArg2 "An SKSI-specific predicate meant to relate a SPARQL b-node (in this case, what's basically a Cyc assertion) with the second argument of that b-node.")
(comment StringCharacterListFn "(#$StringCharacterListFn STRING) returns a list of the characters in STRING as strings.
For example, (#$StringCharacterListFn \"dog\") returns (#$TheList \"d\" \"o\" \"g\").")
(comment SecondInListFn "(#$SecondInListFn LIST) returns the second element of LIST.  
For example, (#$SecondInListFn (#$TheList #$Dog #$Cat)) returns #$Cat.")
(comment ListPositionTupleSetFn "(#$ListPositionTupleSetFn LIST) returns a set of (#$TheList INDEX ITEM) tuples for each ITEM in LIST.  
For example, (#$ListPositionTupleSetFn (#$TheList #$Dog #$Cat)) returns (#$TheSet (#$TheList 1 #$Dog)(#$TheList 2 #$Cat)).")
(comment CanonicalAnagramFn "(#$CanonicalAnagramFn STRING) returns a canonical string which is an anagram of STRING.
For example, (#$CanonicalAnagramFn \"Mississippi\") returns \"iiiimppssss\".")
(comment requiredAssertionForReportTest "(#$requiredAssertionForReportTest REP-PARAM-SPEC MT BIN-PRED ARG-2-VALUE) means that the #$ReportTestParameterSpecification REP-PARAM-SPEC requires the assertion an assertion to be made in MT with BIN-PRED as the arg0 value, ARG-2-VALUE as the arg2 value and , and the sksOfReportTest of REP-PARAM-SPEC to be arg1 value, and for no other assertion for the indicated predicate in the indicated microtheory to be asserted of the sksOfReportTest of REP-PARAM-SPEC.")
(disjointWith EnzymeInactivationEvent EnzymeActivationEvent)
(comment parentCell "<code>(#$parentCell REPRODUCTION CELL)</code> identifies <code>CELL</code> as the instance of #$Cell that is the parent cell in <code>REPRODUCTION</code>, an instance of #$BiologicalReproductionEvent and #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  The #$parentCell in such an event is the cell that divides in the course of the event.")
(comment SparqlURIString "The collection of #$ControlCharacterFreeStrings that are suitable for use as #$SPARQL-Language universal resource identifier (uri) strings.  These differ from most other URI strings in that #$SparqlURIString start and end with angle-brackets (e.g. '<http://www.cyc.com>').")
(comment stageMultiplicationFactor "(#$stageMultiplicationFactor SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-INDEP-TYPE SUBSIT-DEP-TYPE BASE EXP) means that, where SIT is an instance of SIT-TYPE and N is equal to the number BASE rased to the EXPth power, each instance of SUBSIT-INDEP-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of SIT will cause on the order of N instances of SUBSIT-DEP-TYPE as #$properSubSituations of SIT, thereby insuring that SIT situationally subsumes at least N instances of SUBSIT-DEP-TYPE.")
(comment Chromatid "The collection of all instances of chromatids.  A chromatid is a chromatin strand that contains a full DNA strand and is bound to a strand with an identical DNA strand at a point called a \"centromere.\"  Together, they form a duplicated chromosome.  When separated, the two strands cease to be chromatids, but are chromosomes in their own right.")
(comment HTTP-URL-DecodeFn "(#$HTTP-URL-DecodeFn STRING) evaluates to a version of STRING decoded from the style used for HTTP URLs.  In particular, '+' characters are converted to spaces, and hexadecimal encoding sequences of the form %HH where HH is the character code of the character expressed in hexadecimal  are converted to the corresponding ASCII characters.")
(comment OpenCycURIFn "Given a Cyc term as its single argument, #$OpenCycURIFn returns the canonical OpenCyc #$UniformResourceIdentifier for that Cyc term.")
(comment openCycURI "<code>(#$openCycURI THING URI)</code> means that the OpenCyc #$UniformResourceIdentifier for THING is URI.")
(comment ProteinKinaseMolecule "An important specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of phosphorylating (and in many cases, thereby activating) instances of other enzyme species.")
(comment objectTypeReleasedInCytoplasmDuring "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of CytosolicReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn.  Where OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject, (#$objectTypeReleasedInCytoplasmDuring OBJ-TYPE RELEASE-TYPE) means that RELEASE-TYPE is the collection of all events wherein an instance of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn OBJ-TYPE) is subject to a general release (qua #$materialDispersed) throughout the cytoplsam (#$Cytoplasm) of some cell.")
(comment Glucose1PhosphateMolecule "The collection of all glucose-1 phosphate molecules, also known as cori ester.  Instances are characterized by the presence of a phosphate group on the 1' carbon.  Instances figure prominently in anabolic and catabolic reactions within eukaryotic cells.")
(comment workplaceOfIndividual "<code>(#$workplaceOfIndividual AGENT WORKPLACE)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code>'s primary place of work is <code>WORKPLACE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$workplaceOfIndividual #$BarackObama #$TheWhiteHouse)</code> means that Barack Obama's work place is the White House.")
(comment candidateAudienceMemberForMediaOrganization "(#$candidateAudienceMemberForMediaOrganization MEDIA PERSON) is true when MEDIA is a media organization has a reasonable likelihood of reaching PERSON. The exact criteria under which a particular person is a candidate audience member is likely to change from context to context.  Thus, different rules concluding to this relation are likely to be found in different #$Microtheorys.")
(comment CanonicalURIFn "Given a Cyc term as its single argument, #$OpenCycURIFn returns the canonical OpenCyc #$UniformResourceIdentifier for that Cyc term.")
(comment canonicalURI "<code>(#$canonicalURI THING URI)</code> means that the canonical #$UniformResourceIdentifier for THING is URI.  For example, the canonical URI for a Cyc term is 'http://sw.opencyc.org/concept/ID', where ID is the compact hl external ID for the Cyc concept.")
(comment pathStageFacilitatesCellularResponseType "A predicate for relating a characteristic stage in a transduction pathway type (#$TransductionPathwayMultiStageReactionType) to a cellular response type mediated by the #$TransductionPathwayMultiStageReactionType.  Where TRANSDUCTION-TYPE is a kind of #$TransductionPathway-MultiStageReaction, PATH-STAGE is a kind of #$Situation, and RESPONSE-TYPE is a #$CellularProcessType, (#$pathStageFacilitatesCellularResponseType TRANSDUCTION-TYPE PATH-STAGE RESPONSE-TYPE) means that, where TRANSDUCTION is an instance of TRANSDUCTION-TYPE with an instance of PATH-STAGE as a #$properSubSituations, there will normally exist a 'mass' event composed of PATH-STAGE instances (a (MassEventOfTypeFn PATH-STAGE)) that temporally subsumes the aforementioned PATH-STAGE instance, and that in turn is a subsituation of an instance of RESPONSE-TYPE that figures among the causes of that instance of RESPONSE-TYPE.")
(comment GlycogenMolecule "The collection of all glycogen molecules.")
(comment specificValueOfTypeForArgUnknown "A predicate used to represent a certain kind of incompleteness of knowledge, <code>(#$specificValueOfTypeForArgUnknown SENTENCE TYPE N)</code> means that the true sentence <code>SENTENCE</code> contains a skolemized or otherwise indeterminate instance of <code>TYPE</code> in its <code>N</code>th place, and that no specific, determinate instance of <code>TYPE</code> is known to be identical to that indeterminate instance.")
(comment ChromosomeDecondensation "The collection of all chromosome decondensation events, in which the chromosome \"uncoils\" and lengthens.")
(comment PhosphateOrPolyphosphateGroup "The collection of all molecules or molecules parts composed of one or more phosphate groups")
(comment AdenosineMonophosphate "A kind of #$AdenineNucleotide.  Instances of some kinds of #$AdenosineMonophosphate, e.g. #$CyclicAdenosineMonophosphate, play important roles in cellular signaling and metabolism.")
(comment CyclicAMPProduction "Chemical reaction in which a #$DiphosphateGroupMolecule is lysed from #$AdenosineTriphosphate to form #$AdenosineMonophosphate, and a bond is formed between the phosphate atom of the remaining #$MonophosphateGroupMolecule and the 3' hydroxyl of the sugar base, to form #$CyclicAdenosineMonophosphate.  Instances of this reaction are often catalyzed in transduction pathways by #$AdenylylCyclaseMolecules.")
(comment IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn "Where OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject, (#$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn OBJ-TYPE MEDIUM-TYPE) denotes the collection of all events wherein an instance of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn OBJ-TYPE) is dispersed into an instance of MEDIUM-TYPE, where MEDIUM-TYPE is a kind of #$InternalAnatomicalPart (often the human #$Bloodstream).")
(comment objectTypeReleasedIntoIntercellularMediumDuring "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn.  WhereWhere OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject and MEDIUM-TYPE is a class of #$InternalAnatomicalPart, (#$objectTypeReleasedIntoIntercellularMediumDuring OBJ-TYPE MEDIUM-TYPE RELEASE-TYPE) means that RELEASE-TYPEis the collection of all events wherein an instance of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn OBJ-TYPE) is dispersed into an instance of MEDIUM-TYPE.")
(comment maximalProperSubSituationTypes "A #$RuleMacroPredicate expressing an important relationship between types of #$Situation.  Specifically, where SIT-TYPE and SUBSIT-TYPE are both specializations of #$Situation, (#$maximalProperSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE) means that for any two different instances of SUBSIT-TYPE, SUBSIT-1 and SUBSIT-2 that are both #$properSubSituations of an instance of SIT-TYPE, neither (#$properSubSituations SUBSIT-1 SUBSIT-2) nor (#$properSubSituations SUBSIT-2 SUBSIT-1) is true.")
(comment cellularProcessTypeFromSignalTypeToResponseType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn.  Where SIGNAL-TYPE is a specialization of an 'organism-wide' dispersal of a substance composed of instances of some kind of signal molecule such as #$EpinephrineMolecule (said dispersal type will often be represented using #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn) and RESPONSE-TYPE is a kind of cellular level response (a specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel),(#$cellularProcessTypeFromSignalTypeToResponseType SIGNAL-TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE PROCESS-TYPE) means that PROCESS-TYPE is the collection of all instances #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse which begin with an instance of SIGNAL-TYPE and conclude with many cells undergoing a response of RESPONSE-TYPE.")
(comment characteristicResponseOfSignalProcessType "Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of  #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse and RESPONSE-TYPE is a kind of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel, (#$characteristicResponseOfSignalProcessType PROCESS-TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE) means that instances of PROCESS-TYPE normally terminate in a 'mass' event consisting in an aggregation of many instances of RESPONSE-TYPE.")
(comment transductionPathTypeOfSignalProcessType "Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse and TRANSDUCTION-TYPE is a kind of #$TransductionPathway-MultiStageReaction, (#$transductionPathTypeOfSignalProcessType PROCESS-TYPE TRANSDUCTION-TYPE) means that instances of PROCESS-TYPE incorporate many parallel instances of TRANSDUCTION-TYPE in separate cells.")
(comment characteristicStimulusOfSignalProcessType "Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse and SIGNAL-TYPE is a kind of 'organism-wide' dispersal of a substance composed of signaling molecules (see #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn), (#$characteristicStimulusOfSignalProcessType PROCESS-TYPE SIGNAL-TYPE) means that instances of SIGNAL-TYPE commonly initiate instances of PROCESS-TYPE.")
(comment EnzymaticInhibition "A subcollection of #$ChemicalBonding, each instance of which involves the binding of an #$EnzymeMolecule, where the bonding has the effect of \"tying up\" that enzyme so as to prevent it from forming the sorts of bonds that allow it to fulfill its \"normal\" biological function.  Thus of all the various bonds a given enzyme might form, this collection represents those bond-formings that are typically of medical interest: instances of this collection are commonly abnormal for the organism, and many are artificially induced by the introduction of some #$DrugSubstance in that organism's body.")
(comment disrupts-SitTypeSitType "(#$disrupts-SitTypeSitType SITTYPE1 SITTYPE2) means that each instance SIT of SITYPE1 disrupts some instance SIT2 of SITTYPE2.")
(comment InhibitionSituation "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$Situation.  Each instance of #$InhibitionSituation is a #$Situation in which some other situation is inhibited.")
(comment DisruptionEvent "A #$FirstOrderCollection and specialization of #$InhibitionSituation.  Each instance of #$DisruptionEvent is an #$Event in which some other event is disrupted, i.e. prevented from occurring as usual, expected, or planned.")
(comment prevents-SitTypeSitType "An instance of 
#$RuleMacroPredicate. (#$prevents-SitTypeSitType SITTYPE1 SITTYPE2) 
means that for any instance SIT of SITYPE1, (#$prevents-SitSitType SIT SITYPE2).")
(comment inhibits-SitTypeSitType "An instance of 
#$RuleMacroPredicate. (#$inhibits-SitTypeSitType SITTYPE1 SITTYPE2) 
means that for any instance SIT of SITYPE1, (#$inhibits-SitSitType SIT SITYPE2).")
(comment prevents-SitSitType "(#$prevents-SitSitType SIT SITTYPE) means that SIT prevents a situation of type SITTYPE from coming about.  In particular, there would have been some instance of SITTYPE that would have occurred had SIT not itself occurred.")
(comment disrupts-SitSitType "(#$disrupts-SitSitType SIT SITTYPE) means that SIT disrupts a situation of type SITTYPE.  In particular, the occurrence of SIT disrupts the occurrence of some particular instance of SITTYPE that would have occurred in a less disrupted manner had SIT itself not occurred.")
(comment inhibits-SitSitType "(#$inhibits-SitSitType SIT SITTYPE) means that SIT inhibits a situation of type SITTYPE.  In particular, the occurrence of SIT inhibits the occurrence of some particular instance of SITTYPE that would have occurred in a less inhibited manner had SIT itself not occurred.")
(comment MicrotubuleProduction "A specialization of #$Polymerization and #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of #$MicrotubuleProduction  is an event that occurs in a cell wherein instances of #$Microtubule are created.")
(comment Polymerization "A specialization of #$PhysicalSynthesis and #$ChemicalReaction.  Each instance of #$Polymerization is a chemical reaction in which polymers are produced.")
(comment RegulatoryProteinMolecule "The collection of #$EnzymeMolecules that  bind to specific regulatory sequences of DNA and act to switch genes on and off.")
(comment CyclinProduction "A specialization of #$PhysicalSynthesis and #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of #$CyclinProduction is an event that occurs in a cell wherein #$Cyclin is created.")
(comment UncoilingOfChromatinStrand "The collection of all events in which a single strand of chromatin uncoils.")
(disjointWith CoilingOfChromatinStrand UncoilingOfChromatinStrand)
(disjointWith ShorteningEvent Elongation)
(disjointWith Deceased BiologicalLivingObject)
(comment MitoticSpindleAssembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusAssembly.  Each instance of #$MitoticSpindleAssembly is an event during which a #$MitoticSpindle forms in a cell.")
(comment MitoticSpindle "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatus.  Each instance of #$MitoticSpindle is an assembly of #$Microtubules and proteins that facilitates chromosome movement during #$Mitosis.")
(comment SpindleApparatus "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$SpindleApparatus is an assembly of #$Microtubules and proteins that facilitates chromosome movement during either #$Mitosis of #$Meiosis.")
(comment MeioticSpindle "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatus.  Each instance of #$MitoticSpindle is an assembly of #$Microtubules and proteins that facilitates chromosome movement during #$Meiosis.  Note that during meiosis, distinct meiotic spindle apparati will appear during #$MeiosisI and #$MeiosisII.")
(comment FirstMeioticSpindle "A specialization of #$MeioticSpindle.  Each instance of #$FirstMeioticSpindle is a spindle apparatus that appears during  during #$MeiosisI.")
(comment SecondMeioticSpindle "A specialization of #$MeioticSpindle.  Each instance of #$SecondMeioticSpindle is a spindle apparatus that appears during  during #$MeiosisII.")
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindle SecondMeioticSpindle)
(disjointWith MeioticSpindle MitoticSpindle)
(comment SpindleApparatusAssembly "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of  #$SpindleApparatusAssembly is an event in which a #$SpindleApparatus forms in a cell.")
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly MitoticSpindleAssembly)
(disjointWith SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly MitoticSpindleAssembly)
(comment FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusAssembly.  Each instance of #$FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly is an event during which a #$FirstMeioticSpindle forms in a cell.")
(comment SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusAssembly.  Each instance of #$SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly is an event during which a #$SecondMeioticSpindle forms in a cell.")
(disjointWith SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly)
(disjointWith BirthEvent Dying)
(comment CoilTightening "The collection of events which consist of the tightening of a coil.  The coil may have a fixed center or a fixed axis.  Non-fixed points engage in spiral motion about the axis of rotation.  The process is reversed by #$CoilLoosening.  There is a mechanical limit to the amount of #$CoilTightening which can be done, which in some cases is easy to reach.  Winding a #$Wristwatch is an example of #$CoilTightening.  #$CoilTightening is differentiated from #$Reeling in, in that in #$CoilTightening the object is in a tighter coil after the #$CoilTightening process, whereas when reeling in the coil remains about the same tightness, but a greater perportion of the object is in the coil.  #$CoilTightening takes energy to tighten some objects beyond their rest state, but releases energy when tightening back to the rest state after forcefully being uncoiled.  Making a coil of rope from an uncoiled rope by pulling it onto a spinning reel is #$Reeling; tightening that coil is #$CoilTightening.")
(comment LosingAnErection "The collection of events in which the corpora cavernosa of the #$Penis of a #$MaleAnimal become less filled with with blood following a #$GettingAnErection event.")
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica supplyRate)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica supplyRate)))
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica demandRate)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica demandRate)))
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica priceChargedFor)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg1Fn UnitedStatesOfAmerica priceChargedFor)))
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil totalInventoryInRegion)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil totalInventoryInRegion)))
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil supplyRate)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil supplyRate)))
(disjointWith (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil demandRate)) (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil demandRate)))
(disjointWith (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil priceChargedFor)) (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn Petroleum-CrudeOil priceChargedFor)))
(disjointWith ShorteningEvent (IncreaseOnSlotFn lengthOfObject))
(disjointWith Elongation (DecreaseOnSlotFn lengthOfObject))
(disjointWith (DecreaseOnSlotFn lengthOfObject) (IncreaseOnSlotFn lengthOfObject))
(comment CPTOppositeInverseStateTransitionsTest "The collection of instances of #$CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest that test the system's ability to reason about the opposite or inverse state transitions.")
(disjointWith ForbiddingSomething GrantingPermission)
(comment outputsCreated-TypeType-Precise "#$outputsCreated-TypeType-Precise is a predicate with similar semantics to #$outputsCreated-TypeType.  The salient distinction is that #$outputsCreated-TypeType-Precise is <i>not</i> transitive through #$genls in the second argument position.")
(comment inputsDestroyed-TypeType-Precise "#$inputsDestroyed-TypeType-Precise is a predicate with similar semantics to #$inputsDestroyed-TypeType (q.v.).  The salient distinction is that #$inputsDestroyed-TypeType-Precise is <i>not</i> transitive through #$genls in the arg2 position.")
(comment TranscriptionFactorEnzyme "The collection of all #$ProteinMolecules which are capable of binding to subsections of a eukaryotic cell's chromatin in a way which renders that subsection serviceable for #$Transcription-DNAToRNA.")
(comment SpindleApparatusDisassembly "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of  #$SpindleApparatusDisassembly is an event in which a #$SpindleApparatus breaks apart in a cell.")
(comment MitoticSpindleDisassembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusDisassembly.  Each instance of  #$MitoticSpindleDisassembly is an event in which a #$MitoticSpindle breaks apart in a cell.")
(disjointWith MitoticSpindleAssembly MitoticSpindleDisassembly)
(disjointWith SpindleApparatusDisassembly SpindleApparatusAssembly)
(comment SumOfSubsitsOfTypeInFn "A #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  Where SIT is a #$Situation with one or more instances of SUBSIT-TYPE as #$properSubSituations, (#$SumOfSubsitsOfTypeInFn SIT SUBSIT-TYPE) denotes the #$Situation SUM such that i) every instances SUBSIT-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of SIT is a #$subSituations of SUM and ii) no #$Situation that is not an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE is a #$properSubSituations of SUM unless it is temporally subsumed by some instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that is a #$subSituations of SUM.")
(comment sumOfSubsitsOfTypeIn "A #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate and the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$SumOfSubsitsOfTypeInFn.  Where Where SIT is a #$Situation with one or more instances of SUBSIT-TYPE as #$properSubSituations, (#$sumOfSubsitsOfTypeIn SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUM) means that SUM is the unique #$Situation such that i) every instances SUBSIT-TYPE that is a #$properSubSituations of SIT is a #$subSituations of SUM and ii) no #$Situation that is not an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE is a #$properSubSituations of SUM unless it is is temporally subsumed by some instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that is a #$subSituations of SUM.")
(comment schemaName-SKS "(#$schemaName-SKS SCHEMA STRING) means that the #$SubLString, STRING is the
name of the #$PhysicalSchema SCHEMA.")
(comment schemaNameSchema-SKS "(#$schemaNameSchema-SKS SCHEMA STRING) means that the #$SubLString STRING is the namespace schema for the #$PhysicalSchema SCHEMA.")
(comment numberOfInhabitants "The predicate #$numberOfInhabitants is used to indicate the number of people living in a #$GeographicalRegion or the territory of a #$GeopoliticalEntity.  (#$numberOfInhabitants GEO NUMBER) means that the #$GeographicalThing, GEO, has the #$NonNegativeInteger NUMBER of inhabitants living there.  Note that, for any particular country, NUMBER is not necessarily the same as the number of its citizens, since citizens may be living abroad, and aliens may be residing in the country.  Note also that assertions using #$numberOfInhabitants will generally need to be temporally qualified (e.g., by using #$holdsIn), since the number of people living in a region often changes over time.  Examples: (#$numberOfInhabitants #$CityOfRomeItaly 2800000); (#$numberOfInhabitants #$CityOfTokyoJapan 8300000).  See also #$populationOfRegion.")
(comment availabilityTestForSource "(#$availabilityTestForSource SOURCE TEST) means that TEST is a very basic #$KBContentTest for the #$StructuredKnowledgeSource SOURCE. Its intent is to test whether SOURCE is mapped, available, and working properly at the barest level of expected functionality. Such tests are also expected to succeed very quickly (less than a second).")
(comment TemporallyQualifiableRelation "The collection of all #$Relations whose extentions (see #$relationExtension) change, at least somewhat, over time.  A relation <code>RELN</code> is an instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation if and only if there is sequence <code>SEQ</code> and times <code>T1</code> and <code>T2</code> such that <code>RELN</code> holds among <code>SEQ</code> at <code>T1</code> but not at <code>T2</code>.  
<p>
Note that <code>RELN</code> might nevertheless hold of <i>some</i> sequences eternally.  An example of such a relation is #$isa.  On the one hand, the sentence
<pre>
  (#$isa #$GeorgeWBush #$UnitedStatesPresident)
</pre>
is true at some times and false at others, and so requires temporal qualification.    On the other hand, the sentence
<pre>
  (#$isa #$UnitedStatesPresident #$FirstOrderCollection)
</pre>
is true eternally and requires no temporal qualification.
<p>
If a given temporally-qualifiable relation holds of <i>no</i> sequences eternally (e.g. #$likesAsFriend), it is an instance of the specialization #$TimeDependentRelation (q.v.).
<p>
Cf. #$TimeIndependentRelation.")
(comment totalInventoryInRegion "(#$totalInventoryInRegion <code>REGION</code>
<code>TYPE</code> <code>AMOUNT</code>) means that total quantity of
<code>TYPE<code> that exists in inventories in <code>REGION</code> is
<code>AMOUNT</code>.  Such inventory levels are sensitive to, and thus
often treated as indicators of, the ratio between supply and demand
for <code>TYPE<code>.")
(disjointWith (IncreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn DNAMolecule amountPresentAt)) (DecreaseOnSlotFn (QuantitySlotForArg2Fn DNAMolecule amountPresentAt)))
(comment CPTNecessaryAndSufficientConditionsForCausalEffectsTest "The collection of instances of #$CytologicalProcessProjectKBContentTest that test the system's ability to reason about the the ramifications of interference with a causal process.")
(comment only-TC "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel to a more restrictive version of that predicate.  In particular, each instance <code>CPTL</code> of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel has the following semantics: <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds iff every instance of <code>TYPE</code> has the relevant capability (curried into <code>CPTL</code>) of playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>; however <code>(#$only-TC CPTL RCPTL)</code> identifies <code>RCPTL</code> as the ternary predicate that restricts this capability to <i>only</i> instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  Thus <code>(RCPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds just in case <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> and for no collections <code>COL</code>, <code>(CPTL COL SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds unless <code>COL</code> is a specialization of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment Only-TC-Fn "The function that corresponds to the predicate, #$only-TC, <code>(#$Only-TC-Fn PRED)</code> denotes the instance <code>SPEC-PRED</code> of #$TernaryPredicate such that <code>(#$only-TC PRED SPEC-PRED)</code>, where <code>PRED</code> is an instance of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel. <code>SPEC-PRED</code> is a more restrictive version of that <code>Pred</code>.  In particular, each instance <code>CPTL</code> of #$CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel has the following semantics: <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds iff every instance of <code>TYPE</code> has the relevant capability (curried into <code>CPTL</code>) of playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>; however <code>(#$only-TC CPTL RCPTL)</code> identifies <code>RCPTL</code> as the ternary predicate that restricts this capability to <i>only</i> instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  Thus <code>(RCPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds just in case <code>(CPTL TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> and for no collections <code>COL</code>, <code>(CPTL COL SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> holds unless <code>COL</code> is a specialization of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment activationOfEnzymeTypeAssociatedWithReaction "<code>(#$activationOfEnzymeTypeAssociatedWithReaction ACTIVATION-TYPE REACTION-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>REACTION-TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$ChemicalReaction that is, under ordnary circumstances, likely to be instantiated due to the activation of a particular type of enzyme, where the class of such activations is <code>ACTIVATION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ReactionTypeAssociatedWithActivationFn "The function that corresponds to  #$activationOfEnzymeTypeAssociatedWithReaction, <code>(#$ReactionTypeAssociatedWithActivationFn ACTIVATION-TYPE)</code> denotes the subcollection of #$ChemicalReaction associated with precuror #$EnzymeActivationEvent instances of type <code>ACTIVATION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment sksRegistered "(#$sksRegistered ?SOURCE) means that the #$StructuredKnowledgeSource SOURCE is currently registered in this Cyc image.")
(disjointWith CytologicalProcessBaseContentTest CPTFinalQuestionSetRegressionTest)
(comment temporallyDisjoint "<code>(#$temporallyDisjoint OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> do not temporally intersect, i.e., that there are no time points which are common to both.  If both <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> are #$temporallyContinuousDuring, then it also follows that their temporal boundaries do not intersect  (cf. #$temporalBoundsIntersect).  Otherwise, their temporal boundaries may still overlap.  Consider the discontinuous events denoted by \"Fred sleeping this week\" and \"Fred driving this week,\" which are presumably #$temporallyDisjoint even though they are \"interleaved\" during the same week.")
(comment CellCycle "The collection of all events in which a single cell enlarges and then divides, to produce two new cells (see #$daughterCells) that are genetically identical to the initial cell (see #$parentCell).  For the collection of all iterations through #$CellCycle instances along a single path (i.e., the cell cycle <i>as a cycle</i>, in which one of the #$daughterCells of a given iteration goes on to be the #$parentCell in the next), see #$TheCellCycle.")
(comment TheCellCycle "A specialization of #$Cycle-Serial.  Instances are complete iterations through individual growth and division periods for a cell, in which one of the outputs of a given iteration (see #$daughterCells) is the input (see #$parentCell) to the next iteration.  For the collection of all single iterations (i.e., the cell cycle as a localized process in which a single cell grows and divides), see #$CellCycle.")
(comment daughterCells "<code>(#$daughterCells CELL-REPRODUCTION CELL)</code> means that <code>CELL</code> is one of the instances of #$Cell that is the result of the cell reproduction event <code>CELL-REPRODUCTION</code>.")
(disjointWith SPhase Mitosis)
(comment SemiconductorProcessingConstant "The set of terms that pertain to semiconductor processing.")
(comment SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer "The collection of various processing activities used to process #$SemiconductorWafers into semiconductor devices.")
(comment SemiconductorDeviceManufactureFacility "Each #$SemiconductorDeviceManufactureFacility (called a \"fab\") is a facility where #$SemiconductorWafers are processed into #$SemiconductorDevices")
(comment operationHasComplicationType-Boolean "<code>(#$operationHasComplicationType-Boolean OP TYPE TV)</code> means that it is  <code>TV</code> that <code>OP</code> has a complication that is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ChemicalObjectOfTypePenetratesMembraneOfTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject and MEMBRANE-TYPE is a a class of natural or artifical #$Membrane, (#$ChemicalObjectOfTypePenetratesMembraneOfTypeFn OBJ-TYPE MEMBRANE-TYPE) consists of all molecule-scale instances in which a single #$ChemicalObject instance of type OBJ-TYPE penetrates a natural or synthetic membrane of type MEMBRANE-TYPE, either by entering through a molecular pore or conduit within the membrane, or by effecting a permantent or temporary change in the molecular structure of the membrane.")
(comment penetrationsOfMembraneTypeByChemObjectType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ChemicalObjectOfTypePenetratesMembraneOfTypeFn.  Where OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject and MEMBRANE-TYPE is a a class of natural or artifical #$Membrane, (#$penetrationsOfMembraneTypeByChemObjectType OBJ-TYPE MEMBRANE-TYPE EVENT-TYPE) means that EVENT-TYPE is the class of all molecule-scale instances in which a single #$ChemicalObject instance of type OBJ-TYPE penetrates a natural or synthetic membrane of type MEMBRANE-TYPE, either by entering through a molecular pore or conduit within the membrane, or by effecting a permantent or temporary change in the molecular structure of the membrane.")
(comment Cyclin "A specialization of #$ProteinStuff.  Cyclin is important in regulating the phases of the cell cycle (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle).")
(comment KinaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of phosphorylation, the process of transfering of a phosphate group to an organic molecule.")
(comment SingleIterationThroughCycleTypeFn "The function that corresponds to #$iteratedSubsituationTypeOfSerialCycleType. <code>(#$SingleIterationThroughCycleTypeFn CYCLE-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection <code>COLL</code> of sub-events of the specialization of #$Cycle-Serial <code>CYCLE-TYPE</code> such that <code>(#$iteratedSubsituationTypeOfSerialCycleType CYCLE-TYPE COLL)</code> -- i.e., <code>COLL</code> is comprised of the smallest sequence of events that comprise one single iteration through an instance of <code>CYCLE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment DegradationOfChemicalCompoundFn "<code>(#$DegradationOfChemicalCompoundFn OBJECT)</code> denotes the subcollection of #$ChemicalDecomposition in which a single molecule of type <code>OBJECT</code> is destroyed (plays the #$chemicalReactants role).")
(comment chemicalCompoundTypeDegraded "<code>(#$chemicalCompoundTypeDegraded DECOMPOSITION OBJECT)</code> identifies <code>DECOMPOSITION</code> as the subcollection of #$ChemicalDecomposition in which a single molecule of type <code>OBJECT</code> is destroyed (plays the #$chemicalReactants role).  This is the corresponding predicate for #$DegradationOfChemicalCompoundFn.")
(comment CyclinDegradationInMPhase "A stage in MPhase (see #$MitoticPhaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle) consisting of all iterations of Cyclin degradation events in that phase.")
(comment Ubiquitin "A specialization of #$ProteinStuff.  Ubiquitin is a protein that exists in every #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment DecreasedCyclinProductionInMPhase "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel, temporally coincident with a period of rapid #$Cyclin decomposition during M-Phase in the eukaryotic cell cycle.")
(comment ProteinKinaseDegradationInMPhase "An instance of #$EmptyCollection.  The constant #$ProteinKinaseDegradationInMPhase represents a fictional stage in M-Phase that is a period of degradation of #$ProteinKinaseMolecules.")
(comment CDKDegradationInMPhase "An instance of #$EmptyCollection.  The constant #$CDKDegradationInMPhase represents a fictional stage in M-Phase that is a period of degradation of #$CyclinDependentKinaseMolecules.")
(comment IncreaseOfCellsVolumeToGenomeRatioInMPhase "An instance of #$EmptyCollection.  The constant #$IncreaseOfCellsVolumeToGenomeRatioInMPhase represents a fictional stage in M-Phase that is a period during which the ratio of the cell-volume to the number of constituent genomes goes up.")
(comment ContinuousPeriodOfCyclinProductionInEukaryoticCellCycle "A stage in the Eukaryotic cell cycle that starts in Interphase and ends during M-Phase, during which #$Cyclin is steadily produced.")
(comment PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule "The collection of all events in which an #$Ion consisting of one or more phosphate groups is transferred from a molecule of #$AdenosineTriphosphate to an #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances of #$PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule are often themselves catalyzed by 'dedicated' #$EnzymeMolecules.  The phosphate-bound #$EnzymeMolecule which is the #$outputsCreated of a #$PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule is thereby activated (see #$activatedFormOfEnzyme), and hence enabled to execute its catalytic role within the context of an encompassing #$TransductionPathway-MultiStageReaction.")
(comment currentReportingPeriod "A unary predicate used to indicate what type of dataset is currently available to the report generator.")
(comment QuasiTemporalVersionFn "The function that corresponds to #$quasiTemporalVersionOfTemporalRelation.")
(comment InactivatedFormOfEnzymeFn "Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$InactivatedFormOfEnzymeFn MOL-TYPE) in a given context denotes the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are incapable (#$behaviorIncapable) of catalyzing the 'target' reaction supported by MOL-TYPE in a cellular process context (see #$processTypeNeedsReactionTypeCatalyzedByEnzymeType), usually because the molecule in question needs to be activated in an #$EnzymeActivationEvent instance.")
(comment Cohesin "A specialization of #$ProteinComplex. Each instance of #$Cohesin is a protein complex that can bind sister chromatids together.")
(comment BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel "The collection of instances of
 #$BiologicalProcess that occur at the cellular level (i.e., an instance of #$Cell plays the #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell role).  Most instances of #$PhysiologicalProcess will have instances of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel as #$subEvents.")
(comment PhotosensitiveSubstanceType "A collection of collections.  Instances
 are types of photosensitive substances.")
(comment PhysicalTransformationEvent "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent. In each instance of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent at least one thing is transformed into another. An important specialization of this collection is #$PhysicalTransformationProcess, the collection of #$PhysicalTransformationEvents that are also instances of #$TemporalStuffType. See also the predicate #$transformedInto.")
(comment PolynuclearCell "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$PolynuclearCell is a cell with more than one nucelus.")
(comment SimplifiedSKSIConstant "The collection of #$CycLConstants created to assist with simplified SKSI source mapping.")
(comment SimpleDatabase "The collection of SQL databases that can be accessed in a 'simple' way.  To be precise, simple databases consist entirely of physical fields with 'simple' mappings to logical fields.  A mapping is 'simple' if it is one-to-one, and the transformation is the identity transformation, a functional transformation, or a code mapping.  Note: This collection bears no relation to Amazon's SimpleDB.")
(comment DB2Database "The collection of databases that use #$IBM-DB2-TheProgram.")
(comment SimpleDB2Database "The collection of simple databases that use #$IBM-DB2-TheProgram.")
(comment DatabaseTable "The collection of abstract works whose propositional content is expressed in the form of a database table.")
(comment DatabaseColumn "The collection of all columns of all #$DatabaseTables.")
(comment tableInDBNamed "(#$tableInDBNamed TABLE DB NAME) means that TABLE is a #$DatabaseTable named NAME in the database DB.")
(comment TableInDBNamedFn "(#$TableInDBNamedFn DB NAME) denotes the #$DatabaseTable in DB named NAME.")
(comment columnInDBTableNamed "(#$columnInDBTableNamed COLUMN TABLE NAME) means that COLUMN is a #$DatabaseColumn named NAME in the database table TABLE.")
(comment ColumnInDBTableNamedFn "(#$ColumnInDBTableNamedFn TABLE NAME) denotes the #$DatabaseColumn in TABLE named NAME.")
(comment DBTable-ContentMtRelationship "The collection of predicates that relate a #$DatabaseTable to its #$SKSIContentMicrotheory.")
(comment schemaTranslation "An unspecified type of translation relating a #$DatabaseTable to an #$SKSIContentMicrotheory. Use a specPred instead.")
(comment objectSchemaTranslation "A #$DBTable-ContentMtRelationship relating a #$DatabaseTable to an #$SKSIContentMicrotheory. (#$objectSchemaTranslation <code>TABLE</code>
<code>MT</code>) means that if a CycL sentence <code>S</code> is an object schema translation of one of the cells in <code>TABLE</code>, then (#$ist <code>MT</code> <code>S</code>) is true. A sentence <code>S</code> is an object schema translation of a cell <code>C</code> just in case <code>S</code> has the form (<code>PRED</code> <code>X</code> <code>Y</code>) where <code>PRED</code> is the #$objectSchemaColumnPredicate for <code>C</code>'s column, <code>X</code> is a CycL translation of the #$tablePrimaryKey-SingleColumn value in the row intersecting <code>C</code>'s column, and <code>Y</code> is a CycL translation of the value in <code>C</code>.  See #$SharedNoteOnSimpleDatabaseTranslation for information on the translation of X and Y.")
(comment relationshipSchemaTranslation "A #$DBTable-ContentMtRelationship relating a #$DatabaseTable to an #$SKSIContentMicrotheory. (#$relationshipSchemaTranslation <code>TABLE</code> <code>MT</code>) means that if a CycL sentence <code>S</code> is a relationship schema translation of a list of cells in <code>TABLE</code> then (#$ist <code>TRANS-MT</code> <code>S</code>) is true, where <code>TRANS-MT</code> is equal to <code>MT</code> if <code>TABLE</code> is a #$NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable; otherwise <code>TRANS-MT</code> is the appropriate temporal microtheory (q.v. #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable) with <code>MT</code> as its monadic component. A sentence <code>S</code> is a relationship schema translation of sequence of cells C1...Cj, just in case 1) <code>S</code> has the form (<code>PRED</code> X1...Xk); 2) <code>PRED</code> is the #$dBTablePredicate of <code>TABLE</code>; 3) <code>C1...Cj</code> occur in the same row (not necessarily in this order); 4) there is a <code>LIST</code> such that (#$dBTableArgNumMapping <code>TABLE</code> <code>LIST</code>); 5) <code>LIST</code> is equal to (#$TheList COLUMN(C1)... COLUMN(Cj)), where COLUMN(C) denotes the #$DatabaseColumn containing the cell C; 6) (#$TheList TRANS(C1)... TRANS(Cj)) is (#$TheList X1...Xk), where TRANS(Ci) is the CycL translation of the value of Ci, as specified in the #$SharedNoteOnSimpleDatabaseTranslation.")
(comment assertionSchemaTranslation "A #$DBTable-ContentMtRelationship relating a #$DatabaseTable to an #$SKSIContentMicrotheory.  It is similar to #$relationshipSchemaTranslation except that the predicate is also determined by the value of a cell in the database instead of via a #$dBTablePredicate assertion.  (#$assertionSchemaTranslation <code>TABLE</code> <code>MT</code>) means that if a CycL sentence <code>S</code> is an assertion schema translation of a list of cells in <code>TABLE</code>, then (#$ist <code>TRANS-MT</code> <code>S</code>) is true, where <code>TRANS-MT</code> is equal to <code>MT</code> if <code>TABLE</code> is a #$NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable; otherwise <code>TRANS-MT</code> is the appropriate temporal microtheory (q.v. #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable) with <code>MT</code> as its monadic component. A sentence <code>S</code> is an assertion schema translation of sequence of cells P, C1...Cj, just in case 1) <code>S</code> has the form (<code>PRED</code> X1...Xk); 3) P is in the #$assertionTablePredicateColumn for <code>TABLE</code>; 4) TRANS(P) is <code>PRED</code>, where TRANS(X) is the translation of the value of cell X according to #$SharedNoteOnSimpleDatabaseTranslation; 5) C1...Cj occur in the same row as P (not necessarily in this order); 6) there is a <code>LIST</code> such that (#$dBTableArgNumMapping <code>TABLE</code> <code>LIST</code>); 5) <code>LIST</code> is equal to (#$TheList COLUMN(C1)... COLUMN(Cj)), where COLUMN(C) denotes the #$DatabaseColumn containing the cell C; 7) (#$TheList TRANS(C1)... TRANS(Cj)) is (#$TheList X1...Xk), where TRANS(Ci) is the CycL translation of the value of Ci, as specified in the #$SharedNoteOnSimpleDatabaseTranslation.")
(comment tablePrimaryKey-SingleColumn "(#$tablePrimaryKey-SingleColumn <code>TABLE</code> <code>COLUMN</code>) means that <code>COLUMN</code> is the primary key for <code>TABLE</code>.")
(comment objectSchemaColumnPredicate "A #$BinaryPredicate relating a #$DatabaseColumn to a #$BinaryPredicate. (#$objectSchemaColumnPredicate <code>COLUMN</code> <code>PRED</code>) means that in an #$objectSchemaTranslation, for each row <code>ROW</code> in the table to which <code>COLUMN</code> belongs, the referent, X, of the primary key value in <code>ROW</code>, and the referent Y, of the intersection of <code>ROW</code> and <code>COLUMN</code>, are such that (<code>PRED</code> <code>X</code> and <code>Y</code>).  See #$objectSchemaTranslation for a more precise explanation of the translation.")
(comment assertionTablePredicateColumn "(#$assertionTablePredicateColumn <code>TABLE</code> <code>COLUMN</code>) means that the <code>COLUMN</code> column in <code>TABLE</code> is the column corresponding to the predicate (arg0) argument of the assertions translated via an #$assertionSchemaTranslation.  See #$assertionSchemaTranslation for a more precise explanation of the translation.")
(comment dBTableArgNumMapping "(#$dBTableArgNumMapping <code>TABLE</code> <code>COLUMN-LIST</code>) specifies the order in which to translate the columns in <code>TABLE</code> as arguments to a predicate in a #$relationshipSchemaTranslation or an #$assertionSchemaTranslation (q.q.v.)")
(comment dBTablePredicate "(#$dBTablePredicate specifies the predicate to use when translating via a #$relationshipSchemaTranslation (q.v.)")
(comment CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable "A subcollection of #$DatabaseTable. Each #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable <code>TABLE</code> has two columns, <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>, specified by (#$temporalTranslationColumns <code>TABLE</code> <code>A</code> <code>B</code>). Their datatypes are timestamp, and the values within a row, R, for <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> respectively state the starting and ending times of any propositions that are translations of sequences of cells in R. In CycL translations of DB table contents, the microtheory component of the translation (see the instances of #$DBTable-ContentMtRelationship) is (#$MtSpace MT (#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn TRANS(A) TRANS(B)) TimePoint)), where MT is the #$contentMt for <code>TABLE</code>, and TRANS(A) and TRANS(B) are direct translations from the database's timestamp type into a CycL #$Date. Contrast with #$NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable.")
(disjointWith CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable)
(comment NonCanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable "A subcollection of #$DatabaseTable in which the microtheory component of translated propositions is simply the #$contentMt for the table. Contrast with #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable.")
(comment tableFieldNameList "(#$tableFieldNameList <code>TABLE</code> <code>LIST</code>) means that the members of <code>LIST</code> are the physical field names of the database table <code>TABLE.</code>")
(comment identityTranslationColumn "(#$identityTranslationColumn <code>COLUMN</code>) means that when translating <code>COLUMN</code> via an #$assertionSchemaTranslation, assume that values of cells in <code>COLUMN</code> are to be treated as self-denoting. See #$SharedNoteOnSimpleDatabaseTranslation for a more precise explanation.")
(comment temporalTranslationColumns "(#$temporalTranslationColumns <code>TABLE</code> <code>START-COLUMN</code> <code>END-COLUMN</code>) means that, when translating the database table <code>TABLE</code> via a #$schemaTranslation, the values from <code>START-COLUMN</code> are to be used for the starting points of the translated temporal interval, and the values from <code>END-COLUMN</code> are to be used for the ending points of the translated temporal interval. See #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTable for a more precise explanation.")
(comment temporalColumnNullMapsTo "(#$temporalColumnNullMapsTo <code>COLUMN</code> <code>TIME</code>) means that null values from <code>COLUMN</code> will be translated to <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment temporalFieldNullMapsTo "(#$temporalFieldNullMapsTo <code>FIELD</code> <code>TIME</code>) means that null values from <code>FIELD</code> will be translated to <code>TIME</code>.")
(comment CMLSFn "(#$CMLSFn <code>PHYSICAL-FIELD</code>) denotes the canonical CMLS (code mapping logical schema, c.f. #$ReifiedMapping) for <code>PHYSICAL-FIELD</code>.  This CMLS will, by default, be used to encode and decode values in <code>PHYSICAL-FIELD</code>.")
(comment canonicalCodeMappingLogicalSchema "The corresponding predicate to the CMLS-denoting function #$CMLSFn")
(comment SKSIDateDecodeFn "An SKSI-specific version of #$DateFromStringFn that supports special cases for SKSI. One such special case is #$temporalFieldNullMapsTo.")
(comment TriviallyTranslatableThing "The collection of objects that are conventionally denoted by a trivial translation when appearing in a data source.  Canonical examples include strings and numbers.  Note that this is a collection of things, not a quoted collection of terms.")
(comment synonymousExternalConceptToken "(#$synonymousExternalConceptToken THING SOURCE TOKEN) means that as it occurs in the external data source SOURCE, the token TOKEN denotes THING.  Use #$synonymousExternalConceptToken when SOURCE may use numbers to denote objects.  Use #$synonymousExternalConcept when SOURCE only uses strings to denote objects.")
(comment dBTablePredicate-Internal "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$meaningSentenceOfSchema for #$relationshipSchemaTranslation and #$assertionSchemaTranslation.")
(comment dBTableLogicalFieldIndexicalForArgNum "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$meaningSentenceOfSchema for #$relationshipSchemaTranslation and #$assertionSchemaTranslation.")
(comment dBTableTemporalLogicalFieldIndexicals "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$meaningSentenceOfSchema for #$CanonicallyTemporallyIndexedDBTables. Arg 2 is the indexical for the starting time and arg 3 is the indexical for the ending time.")
(comment logicalFieldIndexicalTranslationType "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$fieldEncoding and #$fieldDecoding for #$schemaTranslation.  Supported values for arg2 are #$SchemaObjectFn and #$IdentityFn.")
(comment dBFieldTranslationInputs "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$fieldDecoding for #$schemaTranslation.")
(comment predicateAndArgnumForLogicalFieldIndexical "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$fieldDecoding for #$schemaTranslation.")
(comment nonContextualizedMeaningSentence "An intermediate predicate used for deducing #$meaningSentenceOfSchema for #$schemaTranslation.")
(comment SimplifiedSKSITestingConstant "The collection of #$CycLConstants created to assist with testing simplified SKSI source mappings.")
(comment StringPreremoveFn "#$StringPreremoveFn is an evaluatable function that takes two strings as its arguments.
(#$StringPreremoveFn STRING1 STRING2) tests to see if the n tokens in STRING2 exactly match the first n tokens in STRING1. If so, the
function will then remove STRING2 from the beginning of STRING1 and return the resulting string. Otherwise the function will
simply return STRING1. For example, (#$StringPreremoveFn \"I like to bicycle\" \"I like\") returns \" to
bicycle\". However, (#$StringPreremoveFn \"like to\" \"I like to bicycle\") would return \"like to\".")
(comment StringPostremoveFn "#$StringPostremoveFn is an evaluatable function that takes two strings as its arguments. (#$StringPostremoveFn STRING1 STRING2) tests to see that the n tokens in STRING2 exactly match the last n tokens in STRING1. If so, the function will then remove STRING2 from the end of STRING1 and return the resulting string. Otherwise the function will simply return STRING1. For example, (#$StringPostremoveFn \"I like to bicycle\" \"to bicycle\") returns \"I like \". However, (#$StringPostremoveFn \"like to\" \"I like to bicycle\") would return \"like to\".")
(comment AnucleatedCell "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$AnucleatedCell is a cell without a nucleus.")
(comment MatureRedBloodCell "A specialization of #$RedBloodCell.  Each instance of #$MatureRedBloodCell is a red blood cell that is mature.")
(comment MammalianRedBloodCell "A specialization of #$RedBloodCell.  Each instance of #$MammalianRedBloodCell is a red blood cell of a mammal.")
(comment MatureMammalianRedBloodCell "The intersection of #$MatureRedBloodCell and #$MammalianRedBloodCell.  Mature mammalian red blood cells are unique red blood cells in that they are non-nucleated.  They also lack organelles and ribosomes.")
(comment PerformanceMetric "Each instance of this collection is a specification of the measure of some aspect of a complex entity like an organization or a piece of software.")
(comment metricHasAssociatedFormula "(#$metricHasAssociatedFormula METRIC FORMULA) means that the #$CycLFormula FORMULA expresses the operative calculation for METRIC.")
(comment CardiologyPerformanceMetricQuery "The collection of all queries created to generate metrics for cardiology outcomes reporting.")
(comment MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstant "The collection of instances of #$CycLTerm playing a developmental role in the #$GlobalFoundriesProject.")
(comment MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstant-Extant "The collection of all #$MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstants whose creation dates predate the inception of the #$GlobalFoundriesProject.")
(disjointWith MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstant-Novel MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstant-Extant)
(comment MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstant-Novel "The collection of all #$MicroelectronicProcessingProjectConstants reified during the course of the #$GlobalFoundriesProject.")
(comment SingleUnitRun-MEProcessing "The collection of all distinct 'steps' in Global Foundries product fabrication.")
(comment MEPhotoLayerIDString "The collection of all ID strings used to identify microelectronic processing photo layers.")
(comment M1Stepper "The collection of M1 Steppers.")
(comment ProcessDefinedByThread "The collection of all instances of #$SingleUnitRun-MEProcessing that are 'overlay' operations.")
(comment OverlayProcessType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance is a specialization of #$OverlayProcess characterized by a set of distinguishing features.")
(comment R0Stepper "The collection of R0 Steppers.")
(comment SDReticle "The collection of all reticles used for SD layer patterning.")
(comment SDStepper "The collection of all steppers used in SD layer masking.")
(comment photoLayerIDOfOverlay "A typed spec-pred of #$termStrings.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and MEPLID is an #$MEPhotoLayerIDString (#$photoLayerIDOfOverlay OVL MEPLID) means the MEPLID is the unique ID for the photolayer acted on in OVL.")
(comment m1StepperUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and M1STEP is an #$M1Stepper, (#$m1StepperUsedInOverlay OVL M1STEP) means that M1STEP is the #$M1Stepper used in OVL.")
(comment r0StepperUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and R0STEP is an instance of #$R0Stepper, (#$r0StepperUsedInOverlay OVL R0STEP) means that R0STEP is the #$R0Stepper instance used in OVL.")
(comment maskingLayerReticleUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and MLRET is an instance of #$MaskingLayerReticle, (#$maskingLayerReticleUsedInOverlay OVL MLRET) means the MLRET is the #$MaskingLayerReticle used in OVL.")
(comment sDReticleUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and SDRET is an #$SDReticle, (#$sDReticleUsedInOverlay OVL SDRET) means that SDRET is the #$SDReticle instance used in OVL.")
(comment sDStepperUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and SDSTEP is an #$SDStepper, (#$sDStepperUsedInOverlay OVL SDSTEP) means that SDSTEP is the #$SDStepper instance used in OVL.")
(comment lotProcessStepperUsedInOverlay "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a typed spec-pred of #$deviceUsed.  Where OVL is an #$OverlayProcess and LOTSTEP is an #$LotProcessStepper, (#$lotProcessStepperUsedInOverlay OVL LOTSTEP) means that LOTSTEP is the #$LotProcessStepper instance used in OVL.")
(comment tablePrimaryKey "(#$tablePrimaryKey <code>TABLE</code> <code>COLUMN-LIST</code>) means that <code>COLUMN-LIST</code> comprises the primary key for <code>TABLE</code>.")
(comment meOperationUID "Where RUN is a #$SingleUnitRun-MEProcessing, (#$meOperationUID RUN ID) means that ID is the uniquifying ID of RUN.")
(comment outlierStageWithRespectToChangeInSlotValue "<code>(#$outlierStageWithRespectToChangeInSlotValue EVT-TYPE SUB-EVT-TYPE SLOT)</code> identifies <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code> as the stage in <code>EVT-TYPE</code> during which changes to the arg2 value of the instance of #$QuantitySlot <code>SLOT</code> takes place.  There is a presupposed level of granularity in the notion of \"stage\" here: <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code> counts as stage in the relevant sense if and only if there is a recognized level of decomposition of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> (representable via #$coveringOfEventType) according to which <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code> is one of among several sub-event-types that jointly comprise <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typeChangesQuantityByFactor "<code>(#$typeChangesQuantityByFactor EVT-TYPE ROLE ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE QUANTITY-SLOT FACTOR)</code> means that during instances <code>I</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, where <code>(#$and (ROLE I PLAYER) (#$isa PLAYER ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE))</code>, the value of <code>?X</code> in <code>(QUANTITY-SLOT I ?X)</code> changes from a given value at the start of <code>I</code> to a value arrived at by multiplying <code>?X</code> by <code>FACTOR</code>.")
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-DistributedAmongMultipleCells BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell)
(comment BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-DistributedAmongMultipleCells "The collection of instances of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that take place  within multiple cells.  Contrast with #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.")
(comment BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell "The collection of instances of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that take place entirely within a single cell.  Contrast with #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-DistributedAmongMultipleCells.")
(comment doorToBalloonTimeInMinutes "<code>(#$doorToBalloonTimeInMinutes PCI TIME-QUANTITY)</code> means that for the percutaneous coronary intervention, the door-to-balloon time is <code>TIME-QUANTITY</code>.  When STEMI is diagnosed on the first ECG, <code>TIME-QUANTITY</code> is the time between hospital arrival and the first device activation.  When STEMI is diagnosed on a subsequent ECG, <code>TIME-QUANTITY</code> is the time between the subsequent ECG and the first device activation.")
(disjointWith OwlSemanticDataType (CollectionDifferenceFn Collection OwlSemanticDataType))
(comment ChangeOnSlotFn "<code>(#$ChangeOnSlotFn SLOT)</code> denotes the collection of events in which something changes its value on <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot. For example, (#$ChangeOnSlotFn #$appraisedValue) denotes the collection of events in which some item changes in appraised value.")
(comment quantityChangeTypeForSlot "<code>(#$quantityChangeTypeForSlot EVT-TYPE SLOT)</code> identifies <code>EVT-TYPE</code> as the collection of events in which something changes its value on <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot. This is the predicate that corresponds to the function #$ChangeOnSlotFn.")
(comment EDGARRatio "The collection of #$EDGARConcepts that are computed from more basic concepts.")
(comment MEP-Overlay-50days-overlay-PS "A physical schema for #$MEP-Overlay-50days-overlay-KS.")
(comment Oogenesis "A specialization of #$Gametogenesis.  Each instance of #$Oogenesis is an event in which at least one #$Ovum is created.")
(comment PrimaryOocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$PrimaryOocyte is a female gametocyte that can divide by mitosis into further oocytes or by meiosis into secondary oocytes.")
(comment Oocytogenesis "Each instance of #$Oocytogenesis is an event in which at least one #$PrimaryOocyte is created.")
(comment Ootidogenesis "A specialization of #$Meiosis.  Each instance of #$Ootidogenesis is an event in which at least one #$Ovum is created.")
(disjointWith Oogenesis Spermatogenesis)
(comment Spermatidogenesis "A specialization of #$Gametidogenesis.  Each instance of #$Spermatidogenesis is an event in which at least one #$Spermatid is created.")
(comment Spermatid "A specialization of #$Gametid.  Each instance of #$Spermatid ia a male gametid.")
(comment Gametogonium "A specialization of #$GermCell.  Each instance of #$Gametogonium is a eukaryotic germ cell that is formed early in the life of a fetus and which can undergo #$Gametocytogenesis to produce #$Gametocytes.")
(comment GermCell "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  Each instance of #$GermCell is a cell that can undergo either mitosis or meiosis and can ultimately be an input to a process that outputs a #$Gamete.")
(comment Ootid "A specialization of #$Gametid.  Each instance of #$Ootid ia a female gametid.")
(comment Spermatogonium "A specialization of #$GermCell.  Each instance of #$Gametogonium is a eukaryotic germ cell that is formed early in the life of a fetus and which can undergo #$Gametocytogenesis to produce #$Gametocytes.")
(comment Oogonium "A specialization of #$GermCell.  Each instance of #$Oogonium is a eukaryotic germ cell that is formed early in the life of a fetus and which can undergo #$Oocytogenesis to produce #$PrimaryOocytes.")
(comment nthInList "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$NthInListFn.")
(comment trueOf "A specialization of #$termFormulas, <code>(#$trueOf TERM SENTENCE)</code> is true just in case <code>(#$termFormulas TERM SENTENCE)</code> and <code>(#$trueSentence SENTENCE)</code> are true.")
(disjointWith SomaticCell GermCell)
(disjointWith Gamete-Mature SomaticCell)
(disjointWith DiploidCell HaploidCell)
(comment RuleSentenceAntecedentFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  #$RuleSentenceAntecedentFn takes a (quoted) instance of #$CycLRuleAssertion and returns a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable that is the antecedent of the rule.  For example,  <code>(#$RuleAssertionAntecedentFn (#$forAll ?MIC (#$implies (#$isa ?MIC #$Microtheory)
               (#$genlMt ?MIC #$BaseKB)))))</code> evaluates to <code>(#$isa ?MIC #$Microtheory)</code>.  For a related function that takes a rule sentence and evaluates to its antecedent, see #$RuleAssertionAntecedentFn.")
(comment SecondaryOocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$SecondaryOocyte is a female gametocyte that can divide by meiosis II into an #$Ootid and a polar body.")
(comment PolarBody "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  Each instance of #$PolarBody is a cell produced during #$Ootidogenesis.  Polar bodies have less cytoplasm than the #$SecondaryOocytes or #$Ootids produced during #$Ootidogenesis, and polar bodies typically degenerate after they are produced.")
(comment R0Reticle "The collection of all reticles used for SD layer patterning.")
(comment PhotochemicalReaction "The class of all #$ChemicalReaction instances wherein an instance of some kind of #$ElectromagneticRadiation plays a causal role.")
(comment MELotProcessingStep-SingleIteration "The collection of all events wherein a single member of an #$MEProcessingWaferLot is subjected to a processing regimen that constitutes a distinct step within the microelectronic semiconductor fabrication process.")
(comment MELotProcessingStep "The collection of all events in which all of the members of an #$MEProcessingWaferLot are contiguously subjected to a common processing regimen constituting a 'step' within a semiconductor fabrication process.")
(comment MELotMetrologyStep "The collection of all events in which automated process control metrics are generated for an #$MEProcessingWaferLot, relative to a prior (usually immediately prior #$MELotProcessingStep).  As a rule, a few lot members (instances of #$SemiconductorWafer) are randomly sampled and measured for certain key control parameters:  the metrology generated for the lot as a whole will consist in weighted averages of these measurements.")
(comment metrologyStepMeasuresProcessingStep-ME "(#$metrologyStepMeasuresProcessingStep-ME MET-STEP PROC-STEP) means that MET-STEP is the #$MELotMetrologyStep used in generating the metrology for the #$MELotProcessingStep PROC-STEP.")
(comment PhotoresistSolubilityAlteration-PhotochemicalReaction "The collection of all #$PhotochemicalReactions wherein an instance of #$Photoresist-Substance has the solubility of some portion of its surface are altered by photoexposure. Every instance of #$PhotoresistExposure includes a #$PhotoresistSolubilityAlteration-PhotochemicalReaction that follows the #$MaskingReticleProjection")
(comment MEProcessingWaferLot "The collection consisting of all 'lots' of composed of instances of #$SemiconductorWafer.  More specifically, an #$MEProcessingWaferLot is a delimited group of #$SemiconductorWafers such that the group members are subjected to the same processing regimen (#$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer) contiguously and within a bounded time period, using essentially the same thread process parameters at each #$MELotProcessingStep.")
(comment EukaryoticCellDivision "An instance of #$CellDivisionTypeByCellType, this is the subcollection of #$CellDivision  that takes place in (#$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell) an instance of #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment CellDivisionTypeByCellType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$CellDivision into sub-collections whose instances all take place in (via the #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell role) a common type of #$Cell.")
(comment cellDivisionTypeForCellType "<code>(#$cellDivisionTypeForCellType DIVISION-TYPE CELL-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>DIVISION-TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$CellDivision that takes place in cells of type <code>CELL-TYPE</code>, a specializaton of #$Cell.")
(comment AnaphaseA "A specialzation of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell, and one of the two top-level stages in #$Anaphase, a phase of #$Mitosis.  In #$AnaphaseA, all of sister chromatids (see #$sisterChromatids) comprising the duplicated chromosomes (see #$DuplicatedChromosome) in the cell (see #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell) are separated.")
(comment AnaphaseB "A specialzation of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell, and one of the two top-level stages in #$Anaphase, a phase of #$Mitosis.  In #$AnaphaseB, all of the newly created chromosomes that were the result of #$AnaphaseA move to the poles in the cell.")
(comment ProcessingAllotment "The collection of all 'lots' of items compiled for industrial group processing and fabrication.")
(comment ProcessingAllotmentType "A second-order collection. #$ProcessingAllotmentType is the collection of all types of 'lot' (#$ProcessingAllotment) used in industrial group processing and fabrication processes.")
(comment StandardIndustryProcessingLotTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used for representing important collection instances of #$ProcessingAllotmentType.  Where IND-TYPE is an #$IndustryType and ARTIFACT-TYPE is a kind of #$Artifact-Generic, (#$StandardIndustryProcessingLotTypeFn IND-TYPE ARTIFACT-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ProcessingAllotment composed of instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE that are ordinarily subject to factory processing and fabrication in IND-TYPE.")
(comment standardNumberOfElementsInLotTypeInstances "Where LOT-TYPE is a #$ProcessingAllotmentType, (#$standardNumberOfElementsInLotTypeInstances LOT-TYPE N) means that under normal conditions of processing and fabrication in the industry for which instances of LOT-TYPE are devised, an instance of LOT-TYPE contains N distinct elements which are subject to processing.")
(comment processingStepTypeForLotType "(#$processingStepTypeForLotType LOT-TYPE STEP-TYPE) means that there is an industrial fabrication process that uses instances of LOT-TYPE wherein STEP-TYPE is a characteristic 'step' or stage accepting instances of LOT-TYPE as inputs:  where ITERATION-TYPE is the #$lotProcessingIterationType of STEP-TYPE, an instance of ITERATION-TYPE will be performed on every member of the input instance of LOT-TYPE in the STEP-TYPE instance.")
(comment standardProcessingLotTypeForIndustry "The corresponding predicate of #$StandardIndustryProcessingLotTypeFn..  Where IND-TYPE is an #$IndustryType and ARTIFACT-TYPE is a kind of #$Artifact-Generic, (#$standardProcessingLotTypeForIndustry IND-TYPE ARTIFACT-TYPE LOT-TYPE) means that LOT-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ProcessingAllotment composed of instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE that are ordinarily subject to factory processing and fabrication in IND-TYPE.")
(comment strategyHasApplicationCondition "(#$strategyHasApplicationCondition STRAT COND) means that the applicability of the strategy is gated by COND.")
(comment strategyHasAssociatedQuery "(#$strategyHasAssociatedQuery STRAT QUERY) means that STRAT is the applicable query modification strategy for QUERY.  A query may be associated with several strategies and a particular reified strategy may be associated with many queries.")
(comment QueryModificationStrategy "A collection of strategies for modifying a query in order to generate relevant results.  Some strategies may apply before the query is run, while others may only be relevant to iterative runs of successively modified queries.  In general, When a \"strategy\" is active in a given query session, the applicability condition is checked and if the condition holds, the strategy is applied and the query is run or rerun.  Each instance of this collection is typically associated with at least one query to which it applies, an applicability condition -- the condition that gates whether to apply the strategy, and some number of additional features like ordering conditions, definitions of how the strategy is applied, etc. ")
(comment QueryResultSetCardinalityFn "An individual denoting unary function.  Uses of this term denote the cardinality of the result set of the query in argument 1 in the context of a particular inference.")
(comment strategyHasPredicateOrder "(#$strategyHasPredicateOrder STRAT LIST) means that when the strategy executes, LIST is the predicate order used in accordance with the particular algorithm employed.")
(comment causes-SubSitTypeSubSitType "<code>(#$causes-SubSitTypeSubSitType SIT CAUSE-TYPE EFFECT-TYPE)</code> means that in events of type <code>SIT</code>, events of type <code>CAUSE-TYPE</code> cause events of type <code>EFFECT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment LotProcessingStep-Serial "A specialization of #$Cycle-Serial. #$LotProcessingStep-Serial is the collection of all industry processing events wherein a delimited 'step' or 'stage' in an industry fabrication process model is iteratively repeated for every element in a processed 'lot' (#$ProcessingAllotment), with the #$LotProcessingStep-Serial consisting exclusively of repetitions of this stage for as many elements are in the #$ProcessingAllotment.")
(comment lotProcessingIterationType "Where STEP-TYPE is a kind of #$LotProcessingStep-Serial and ITERATED-TYPE is a kind of #$ProcessingEvent, (#$lotProcessingIterationType STEP-TYPE ITERATED-TYPE) means that means that ITERATED-TYPE is the class of #$ProcessingEvent that is repeated in instances of STEP-TYPE, such that each member of the #$ProcessingAllotment processed in an instance of STEP-TYPE is subjected to exactly one instance of ITERATED-TYPE.")
(comment hasOverlayType "A typed spec-pred of #$isa.  Where OVL is a #$ProcessDefinedByThread and OVL-TYPE is an #$OverlayProcessType, (#$hasOverlayType OVL OVL-TYPE) means that OVL is an instance of the #$OverlayProcessType OVL-TYPE.")
(comment ProjectionDevice "The collection of all devices which project images by means of a source of electromagnetic radiation.  Projection may be for display purposes (see #$ProjectionDisplayDevice) or might have another industrial purpose (cf. #$Stepper-Photolithography.")
(comment tablePrimaryKeyValues "(#$tablePrimaryKeyValues <code>TABLE</code> <code>VALUE-1</code> ... <code>VALUE-N</code>) means that <code>VALUE-1</code> through <code>VALUE-N</code> appear in some row of <code>TABLE</code> as a set of primary key values. The order of the values corresponds with the order of the columns in <code>TABLE</code>'s #$tablePrimaryKey.")
(comment uniqueSuperEventTypes "<code>(#$uniqueSuperEventTypes SUB SUPER)</code> means that every instance <code>I</code> of the event-type <code>SUB</code> is a part (in the sense of #$properSubEvents) of exactly one instance of the event-type <code>SUPER</code>.")
(comment LifeTypeByBLOType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$Living into subcollections based on the type of #$BiologicalLivingObject that does the (plays the #$lifeOf role in the) living.")
(comment lifeTypeOf "<code>(#$lifeTypeOf LIFE-TYPE BLO-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> as the unique instance of #$LifeTypeByBLOType that stands in the #$lifeTypeOf relation to <code>BLO-TYPE</code>.  Equivalently, it identifies <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> as the unique subcollection of #$Living, each instance of which stands in the #$lifeOf relation to an instance of <code>BLO-TYPE</code>.")
(comment LifeTypeFn "<code>(#$LifeTypeFn BLO-TYPE)</code> denotes the unique instance of #$LifeTypeByBLOType that stands in the #$lifeTypeOf relation to <code>BLO-TYPE</code>.  Equivalently, it denotes the unique subcollection of #$Living, each instance of which stands in the #$lifeOf relation to an instance of <code>BLO-TYPE</code>.")
(comment MaskingReticle "The collection of all masking reticles or photomasks used to generate the images produced by instances of #$Stepper-Photolithography during instances of #$OverlayProcess-SingleIteration.")
(comment PhotoresistExposure-Stepped "A class of iterative process wherein the image generated by a #$MaskingReticle is successively projected onto different sections of a #$SemiconductorWafer with a #$Photoresist-Substance deposition, thereby selectively altering the solubility of different subsections of the resist.  Each #$PhotoresistExposure-Stepped consists entirely in repeated but spatially distinct instances of #$PhotoresistExposure.")
(comment PhotoresistExposure "The collection of all semiconductor wafer processing events (#$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer) wherein an image generated by means of a #$MaskingReticle is projected onto a layer of #$Photoresist-Substance that has been deposited onto a wafer substrate, and the chemical properties of the exposed resist are thereby altered to either heighten their solubility (positive resist) or reduce it (negative resist). Each instance of #$PhotoresistExposure thus consists in the reticle projection (#$MaskingReticleProjection) followed by the solubility alteration #$PhotoresistSolubilityAlteration-PhotochemicalReaction.")
(comment ResistLayer "The collection of all deposited layers of #$Photoresist-Substance, where each such layer completely covers (see #$covers-Paintlike) a single instance of #$SemiconductorWafer.")
(comment StartingOfSitTypeFn "<code>(#$StartingOfSitTypeFn SITTYPE)</code> denotes the collection of situations that are the start of situations of type <code>SITTYPE</code>.")
(comment G1Checkpoint "A specialization of #$ConfigurationOfComplexObject and one of three so-called \"checkpoints\" in the Eukaryotic Cell Cycle.  The G1 checkpoint is a state in which the Eukarotic cell contains CDK/Cyclin complexes of the right types in the right amounts, \"signaling\" that the cell is in a position to move into #$SPhase of the cell cycle.")
(comment G2Checkpoint "A specialization of #$ConfigurationOfComplexObject and one of three so-called \"checkpoints\" in the Eukaryotic Cell Cycle.  The G2 checkpoint is a state in which the Eukarotic cell contains sufficient levels of activated MPF that the cell is in a position to move into M Phase of the cell cycle.")
(comment MCheckpoint "A specialization of #$ConfigurationOfComplexObject and one of three so-called \"checkpoints\" in the Eukaryotic Cell Cycle.  The M checkpoint is a state in which the Eukarotic cell contains sufficient levels of activated APC that the cell is in a position to move into #$Anaphase of the cell cycle.")
(comment EukaryoticCellCycleControlSystem "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Instances are comprised of all sub-events and sub-situations of a given instance of #$EukaryoticCellCycle that are conceptualized by biologists as \"guiding\" the cell (see #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell) through the different phases of the cycle.")
(comment CyclinLevelChangingDuringTheEukaryoticCellCycle "The collection of all single-cell iterations through  #$CyclinLevelFluctuationThroughTheEukaryoticCellCycle.  Each instance is an event during which the level of #$Cyclin rises in a cell steadily through #$Interphase, then dropping off rapidly during the #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle.")
(comment NuclearLamina "A layer of protein molecules between the inner and outer membranes of the #$NuclearEnvelope.  During the cell cycle, levels of active MPF rise to a point where a chemical reaction occurs, and the molecules comprising the lamina phosphorylate, causing the nuclear envelope to break down.")
(comment CellCycleCheckpointType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that consists of the three checkpoints of the cell cycle: #$G1Checkpoint, #$G2Checkpoint and #$MCheckpoint.")
(comment startingTypeOfSitType "The predicate that corresponds to the function, #$StartingOfSitTypeFn, <code>(#$startingTypeOfSitType START-TYPE SIT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>START-TYPE</code> as the collection of all situations that are the starts of instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment MPFActivityRisingToG2CheckpointTriggeringLevel "A sub-event of the eukaryotic cell cycle in which MPF levels rise to a point where the cell is configured so as to meet the \"specifications\" of the #$G2Checkpoint, which \"signals\" to the cell that it is ready to enter M Phase (#$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle).")
(comment systemControls "A specialization of #$systemComponents, <code>(#$systemControls SYSTEM CONTROL)</code> means that <code>CONTROL</code> is a component of <code>SYSTEM</code> that plays the role of a control, in a very general sense.  In a mechanical system, <code>CONTROL</code> might be a physical knob or button that an operator uses, or it might be a device (such as spring-based thermostat in a car) that reacts when conditions are \"right\", thereby allowing certain sub-routines to proceed.  In a biological system, <code>CONTROL</code> might be a biological analogue to an internal device, or it might be a configuration within a biological object that must be attained for certain biological functions to proceed normally.")
(comment systemInternalControls "A specialization of #$systemControls, #$systemInternalControls relates a system to its internal controls.  An internal control is one that originates in or consists of some part of the object being controlled.  If the system controls a process, then an internal control is some step of that process that is instantiated by some some part of the \"focal\" object that undergoes that process.  Contrast with #$systemExternalControls.")
(comment CellCycleControlSystem "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Instances are comprised of all sub-events and sub-situations of a given instance of #$CellCycle that are conceptualized by biologists as \"guiding\" the cell (see #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell) through the different phases of the cycle.")
(comment ProcessControlSystem "A specialization of #$System.  Instances are any systems that \"guide\" a process through its various steps.")
(comment ProcessControlSystemTypeByProcessType "A collection that facets #$ProcessControlSystem into sub-collections whose instances instantiate controls systems for a common type of process.")
(comment controlSystemForProcess "<code>(#$controlSystemForProcess SYSTEM PROCESS)</code> identifies <code>SYSTEM</code> as the instance of #$ProcessControlSystemTypeByProcessType whose instances are controls systems for a the process-type <code>PROCESS</code>.")
(comment processStepGatedByControlType "<code>(#$processStepGatedByControlType PROCESS STEP CONTROL)</code> means that <code>CONTROL</code> is a sub-step of <code>PROCESS</code> that plays the role of #$systemControls in control systems that \"guide\" instances of <code>PROCESS</code>; moreover, <code>CONTROL</code> determines whether <code>STEP</code> takes place.")
(comment systemExternalControls "A specialization of #$systemControls, #$systemExternalControls relates a system to its external controls.  An external control is one that originates in some object or process that starts outside of the object being controlled.  If the system controls a process, then an external control is some step of that process that also belongs to an external process (i.e., one that does not involve the \"focal\" object that undergoes that process).  Contrast with #$systemInternalControls.")
(comment PhotoresistReferenceLayerType "A second-order collection.  Each instance is a commonly-identified type of #$ResistLayer used in semiconductor processing.")
(comment M2ResistLayer "A commonly-identified type of #$ResistLayer used in semiconductor processing.")
(comment M1ResistLayer "A commonly-identified type of #$ResistLayer used in semiconductor processing.")
(comment overlayStepHasReferenceLayerType "Where OVL is an instance of #$OverlayProcess-SingleIteration and LAYER-TYPE is a #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$overlayStepHasReferenceLayerType OVL LAYER-TYPE) means that the type of #$ResistLayer deposited in the #$PhotoresistDeposition step of OVL is LAYER-TYPE.")
(comment overlayLotProcessingHasReferenceLayerType "Where OVL-LOTPROC is an #$OverlayProcess-LotProcessingStep and LAYER-TYPE is a #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$overlayLotProcessingHasReferenceLayerType OVL-LOTPROC LAYER-TYPE) means that each individual #$OverlayProcess-SingleIteration wafer processing composing OVL-LOTPROC has LAYER-TYPE as the reference layer type (overlayStepHasReferenceLayerType): i.e., the #$ResistLayer laid down in each #$PhotoresistDeposition occuring in each #$OverlayProcess-SingleIteration in OVL-LOTPROC is an instance of LAYER-TYPE.")
(comment hasReferenceLayerType "Where EVT is a #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer and LAYER-TYPE is a #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$hasReferenceLayerType EVT LAYER-TYPE) means that EVT has a #$ResistLayer of type LAYER-TYPE as its focal object.")
(comment roleHasSubEventsVersion "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$SubEventRoleFn.  <code>(#$roleHasSubEventsVersion ROLE GENERALIZTION)</code> means that <code>(GENERALIZATION SIT ROLE-PLAYER)</code> holds if, and only if <code>(ROLE SUB-EVT ROLE-PLAYER)</code> holds for some event <code>SUB-EVT</code> such that <code>(#$subEvents SIT SUB-EVT)</code>.")
(comment RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  #$RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn takes a (quoted) instance of #$CycLRuleAssertion and a list of bindings, and returns a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable that is the antecedent of the rule, with variables replaced with bindings from the list (in canonical order).  For example,  <code>(#$RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn (#$ist #$BaseKB (#$implies (#$isa ?MIC #$Microtheory)
               (#$genlMt ?MIC #$BaseKB))) (#$TheList #$BiologyMt))</code> evaluates to <code>(#$isa #$BiologyMt #$Microtheory)</code>.  For a related function that takes a rule sentence and evaluates to its (unbound) antecedent, see #$RuleSentenceAntecedentFn.")
(comment RuleAssertionBoundConsequentFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  #$RuleAssertionBoundConsequentFn takes a (quoted) instance of #$CycLRuleAssertion and a list of bindings, and returns a (quoted) instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable that is the consequent of the rule, with variables replaced with bindings from the list (in canonical order).  For example,  <code>(#$RuleAssertionBoundAntecedentFn (#$ist #$BaseKB (#$implies (#$isa ?MIC #$Microtheory)
               (#$genlMt ?MIC #$BaseKB))) (#$TheList #$BiologyMt))</code> evaluates to <code>(#$genlMt #$BiologyMt #$BaseKB)</code>.")
(comment otherwiseDerivable "A specialization of #$rejectedSentence, <code>(#$otherwiseDerivable SENTENCE)</code> means that the #$CycLSentence <code>SENTENCE</code> is false, and has a rejected proof via a rule for which the non-0 arguments in <code>SENTENCE</code> form an exception.  Specifically, there is a #$CycLRuleAssertion <code>RULE</code> for which some list of bindings </code>BINDINGS-LIST</code> is abnormal (i.e., <code>(#$abnormal RULE BINDINGS-LIST)</code>, such that substituting the appropriate bindings from <code>BINDINGS-LIST</code> for the variables in <code>RULE</code> results in a rule sentence whose antecedent is true.  Yet, because the list is #$abnormal for the rule, <code>SENTENCE</code>, which is the consequent that results from this substitution, is rejected.")
(comment eventHasAssociatedCardiacValveOfType "<code>(#$eventHasAssociatedCardiacValveOfType EVENT HEART-VALVE VALVE-TYPE)</code> means that in the evaluation <code>EVENT</code> there was a finding, <code>HEART-VALVE</code>, associated with a cardiac valve of <code>VALVE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment QueryRelaxationStrategy-RemoveLiteralViaSpecifiedOrder "This is a collection of iterative modification strategies.  By definition instances of this collection never apply unless their associated query has been run.  In this case the strategy is to successively remove literals, in the order specified, until the query returns results or you get to the end of the specified order -- i.e. you run out of literals to remove.  In general,  after the initial query is run, the applicability condition on the instance of the strategy is checked and if the query plus result set satisfies the condition, then the strategy is executed and the query rerun.  This continues recursively until the condition fails or the end of the ordering is reached.  All results from all iterations are compiled, filtered according to any result filters, and presented as the binding set for the iterated query sequence.")
(comment PhotolithographyProcess-LotProcessingStep "The collection of all events wherein all of the members of an #$MEProcessingWaferLot are contiguously and successively subjected to instances of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration, one instance per member.")
(comment PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration "The collection of all manufacturing events wherein a single member of an #$MEProcessingWaferLot (an instance of #$SemiconductorWafer is subjected to a process wherein an instance of #$Photoresist-Substance is deposited in a layer over the wafer substrate and an image is burned into the photoresist via a process of stepped projection:  depending on whether the resist is 'positive' or 'negative', exposed or unexposed portions of the resist are then washed away by means of a solvent to which they have been sensitized by the radiation exposure.  Every instance of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration thus consists of at least three sub-stages:  deposition (#$PhotoresistDeposition), stepped exposure (#$PhotoresistExposure-Stepped) and development with solvent (#$PhotoresistDevelopment).")
(comment PhotoresistDeposition "The collection of all events in which a mostly-uniform layer of #$Photoresist-Substance is spread onto a #$SemiconductorWafer.  Every instance of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration begins with an instance of #$PhotoresistDeposition, preparator to stepped exposure of the masking reticle image (#$PhotoresistExposure-Stepped).")
(comment MaskingReticleProjection "The collection of all semiconductor wafer processing events (#$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer) in which the image formed by a #$MaskingReticle is projected onto a layer of #$Photoresist-Substance that has been deposited onto a wafer substrate.")
(comment PhotoresistDevelopment "The collection of all instances wherein some parts of a layer of #$Photoresist-Substance are washed from a #$SemiconductorWafer by a solvent, these parts having previously been sensitized to the solvent by selective photoexposure.  #$PhotoresistDevelopment is the final step of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration.")
(disjointWith Meiosis AsexualLifeCycle)
(disjointWith ReproductiveFertilizationEvent AsexualLifeCycle)
(disjointWith BiologicalLifeCycle BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell)
(comment BiologicalLifeCycle "The collection of all life cycles, sequences of generational succession of organisms of a certain type.")
(comment SexualLifeCycle "The collection of all life cycles characterized by sexual reproduction.")
(comment AsexualLifeCycle "The collection of all life cycles characterized by asexual reproduction.")
(disjointWith (SingleIterationThroughCycleTypeFn SexualLifeCycle) (SingleIterationThroughCycleTypeFn AsexualLifeCycle))
(comment LifeCycleTypeByPloidy "A specialization of #$LifeCycleTypeByOrganismType whose three instances form a partition over the collection of sexual life cycles (see #$SexualLifeCycle).  Each instance is a collection of life cycles in organisms that share a common pattern with respect to the ploidy of the participants at certain points in the cycle.")
(comment EukaryoticOrganismTypeByLifeCycleType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that partitions #$EukaryoticOrganism into three classes corresponding to the three major types of #$SexualLifeCycle that are based on the patterns of ploidy change in the participants (see #$LifeCycleTypeByPloidy).")
(comment HaplonticZygote "The collection of instances of #$Zygote-SingleCelled that are also #$Haplont.  These divide meiotically (see #$Meiosis) to produce haploid cells (see #$HaploidCell).")
(comment Zygote-SingleCelled "The collection of all zygotes that consist of a single cell.  Every zygote starts out as a member of this collection; in animals and most plants, these go on to develop into multicellular organisms.")
(comment Zygote "An instance of #$LifeStageType.  Zygotes (in their single-celled form; see #$Zygote-SingleCelled) are the direct result of fertilization.  In animals and (most) plants, zygotes divide to form more complex multicellular organisms.")
(comment Zygote-MultiCellular "An instance of #$LifeStageType, this is the subcollection of #$Zygote whose instances are multicellular, and so have developed via cellular division from some instance of #$Zygote-SingleCelled.")
(comment HaplodiplonticZygote "The collection of plant and fungal zygotes that are #$Haplodiplont organisms.")
(comment AnimalLifeCycle "The life cycle (see #$SexualLifeCycle) for animals.")
(comment TheHumanLifeCycle "The life cycle (see #$SexualLifeCycle) for humans.")
(comment LifeCycleTypeByOrganismType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets the collection of life cycles (see BiologicalLifeCycle) into subcollections, each of which is a collection of life cycles that occur in the same type of organism.")
(comment lifeCycleTypeOfOrganismType "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that relates a type of #$BiologicalLifeCycle to the type of organism it is specific to.")
(comment negationSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceQuery "(#$negationSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceQuery QUOTED-SENTENCE QUERY) means that when generating negated versions of the query for the multiple choice query <code>QUERY</code>, the sentence <code>QUOTED-SENTENCE</code> should be used.")
(comment organismTypeDevelopmentalStageTypes "A binary predicate that relates a type of #$Organism-Whole to its #$LifeStageTypes.")
(comment organismTypeFirstDevelopmentalStageType "A binary predicate that relates a type of #$Organism-Whole to the first of its #$LifeStageTypes.")
(comment endingTypeOfSitType "The predicate that corresponds to the function, #$EndingOfSitTypeFn, <code>(#$endingTypeOfSitType END-TYPE SIT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>END-TYPE</code> as the collection of all situations that are the ends of instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment EndingOfSitTypeFn "<code>(#$EndingOfSitTypeFn SITTYPE)</code> denotes the collection of situations that are the end of situations of type <code>SITTYPE</code>.")
(comment EtchedWaferPattern "The collection of all incisions and groups of incisions in #$SemiconductorWafers that have been deliberately occasioned by one or more instances of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer.")
(comment EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerType "A second-order collection.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$EtchedWaferPattern such that all of its instances are characterized by having originated at a specific type of photolithography step (an instance of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration) characterized by a specific type of #$ResistLayer (e.g., an #$SDResistLayer) at the #$PhotoresistDeposition stage.")
(comment EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used to represent collection instances of the type-level collection #$EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerType.  Where LAYER-TYPE is a collection instance of #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn LAYER-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$EtchedWaferPatterns deriving from #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration instances wherein the #$ResistLayer involved was an instance of LAYER-TYPE.")
(comment patternTypeOriginatesFromResistLayerOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn.  Where LAYER-TYPE is a collection instance of #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$patternTypeOriginatesFromResistLayerOfType LAYER-TYPE ETCH-TYPE) means that ETCH-TYPE is the collection of all #$EtchedWaferPatterns deriving from #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration instances wherein the #$ResistLayer involved was an instance of LAYER-TYPE.")
(comment RegulatingTheLevelOfASubstanceInASystem "The collection of all events which consist in the regulation of the level of substance(s) in some system.")
(comment substanceWithLevelRegulated "<code>(#$substanceWithLevelRegulated REGULATING SUBSTANCE)</code> identifies <code>SUBSTANCE</code> as the substance-type (the instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType) whose level is regulated in <code>REGULATING</code>, an instance of #$RegulatingTheLevelOfASubstanceInASystem.")
(comment regulatorySubstances "<code>(#$regulatorySubstances REGULATING SUBSTANCE)</code> identifies <code>SUBSTANCE</code> as one of the types of substances that, by virtue of its presence in the system in greater or lesser amounts, helps to maintain the level of the substance being regulated (see #$substanceWithLevelRegulated) in <code>REGULATING</code>.")
(comment regulatorySubstanceGivesPositiveFeedback "<code>(#$regulatorySubstanceGivesPositiveFeedback REGULATING SUBSTANCE)</code> means that <code>SUBSTANCE</code> provides positive feedback (i.e., helps drive the level upward) to the substance being regulated in <code>REGULATING</code>, an instance of #$RegulatingTheLevelOfASubstanceInASystem.")
(comment regulatorySubstanceGivesNegativeFeedback "<code>(#$regulatorySubstanceGivesNegativeFeedback REGULATING SUBSTANCE)</code> means that <code>SUBSTANCE</code> provides negative feedback (i.e., helps drive the level downward) to the substance being regulated in <code>REGULATING</code>, an instance of #$RegulatingTheLevelOfASubstanceInASystem.")
(comment substancesCounteractInRegulation "<code>(#$substancesCounteractInRegulation REGULATING SUB1 SUB2)</code> means that the substance-types <code>SUB1</code> and <code>SUB2</code> work in \"opposite directions\" with respect to the regulation of a given substance in <code>REGULATING</code>.")
(comment CalciumRegulationInTheBloodstream "The regulation of level of Calcium in the bloodstream of an animal.")
(comment ParathyroidGland "A type of #$EndocrineGland, responsible for the secretion of #$ParathyroidHormone.")
(comment CirculatingCalciumRegulationSystem "the system that regulates the levels of calcium in animals' bloodstreams.")
(comment HomeostaticRegulatorySystem "The collection of all physiological systems that serve to regulate the amount of some substance in the body of a living organism.")
(comment Somatropin "The kind of growth hormone produced by recombinant DNA technology.")
(comment Glucagon "A kind of #$Hormone secreted by the Pancreas that increases levels of sugar in the blood.")
(comment Phosphodiesterase "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Each instance of #$Phosphodiesterase is a n emzyme molecule that has the capacity to break a #$PhosphodiesterBond.")
(comment ProteinPhosphataseMolecule "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Each instance of #$ProteinPhosphataseMolecule is an enzyme molecule that can remove phosphate groups from proteins.  Cf. #$ProteinKinaseMolecule.")
(comment IntentionallyInjuringAnotherPerson "The subcollection of  #$IntentionallyCausingAnotherInjury in which the injured is an instance or group of persons, and the injurers is an instance or group of persons.")
(comment GovernmentSanctionedSecurityProvider "The collection of agents who are officially tasked with security and security-related tasks for a region, by the authority in charge of that region.")
(comment Calmodulin "A specialization of #$ProteinStuff.  Calmodulin is a protein that is present in high levels in #$EukaryoticCells.")
(comment interfaceDisplayString "Associates a display string for use in UIs")
(comment replaceableValueForPredInArg "(#$replaceableValueForPredInArg PRED NUM THING) in the context of instantiating a literal through a UI or in a query search results, means that in a literal with PRED in arg0, THING in argument postion NUM should be thought of as a place holder for a user specified value.")
(comment Diglyceride "The collection of all diglycerides, also known as diacylglycerol. In a diglyceride molecule, two molecules of one or more different fatty acids are linked to a glycerol molecule.")
(comment Monoglyceride "The collection of all monoglycerides. In a monoglyceride molecule, one molecule of a fatty acid is linked to a glycerol molecule.")
(comment Glyceride "The collection of all glycerides. In a glyceride molecule, one or more molecules of a fatty acid is linked to a glycerol molecule in an ester bond.")
(comment Citizenship "A specialization of #$Situation.  Each instance is a state involving exactly one person and exactly one instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity to which that person stands in the #$citizens relationship.")
(comment citizen-BinarySituationPredicate "An instance of #$BinarySituationPredicate, <code>(#$citizen-BinarySituationPredicate CITIZENSHIP PERSON)</code> identifies <code>PERSON</code> as the person for which there is a geopolitical entity <code>E</code>, such that throughout <code>CITICZENSHIP</code>, <code>(#$citizens E PERSON)</code> holds.")
(comment sksiForwardRule "(#$sksiForwardRule RULE) means that the instance RULE of #$CycLRuleAssertion may be used during SKSI forward inference in which an SKSI sentence in a content microtheory triggers such a rule and generates conclusions to add to the same content microtheory.")
(disjointWith ExclusivelyIntracellularSignalingChemicalObject ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject)
(comment QueryRelaxationStrategyChangeValueInArgAccordingToSpec "This is a general strategy that says after each query iteration, there is particular value in one of the arguments of a particular formula in the query that is changed according to some determined process.  One such way to specify a value change is with #$valueChangeListForStrategy.  In general, if a particular reified strategy is a member of this collection, then the system should respect assertions on that strategy that invlove PRED in arg0 where PRED is (#$strategyTypeGatedByPred #$QueryRelaxationStrategyChangeValueInArgAccordingToSpec PRED)")
(comment strategyTypeGatedByPred "(#$strategyTypeGatedByPred STRAT-TYPE PRED) means that instances of STRAT-TYPE should have an assertion involving PRED in arg0 in order to execute.")
(comment valueChangeListForStrategy "(#$valueChangeListForStrategy STRAT TEMPLATE POSITION LIST) means that for each iteration of the strategy the argument in POSITION within any occurrences of TEMPLATE is replaced with a member of LIST.  Upon the first execution of the strategy, the specified term is replaced with the first member of the list, for all subsequent Nth iterations of the strategy, the term is replaced with the Nth term in the list.  If the end of the list is reached before the strategy is finished executing, then no replacement occurs.")
(comment schemaObjectFnSubStringForBinPred "(#$schemaObjectFnSubStringForBinPred CM PRED ARG1 ARG2 STRING) means that in the context of CM pred stands in ARG1 to ARG2 and that ARG2 is a SchemaObjectFn NAT with STRING a substring of the string in arg2.")
(comment CytosolicReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn "Where OBJ-TYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject, (#$CytosolicReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn OBJ-TYPE) denotes the collection of all events wherein an instance of (#$ChemicalSubstanceFn OBJ-TYPE) is subject to a general release (qua #$materialDispersed) throughout the cytoplasm (#$Cytoplasm) of some cell.")
(comment mepReticleHasSameProductNumber "(#$mepReticleHasSameProductNumber ARG1 ARG2) means that the distinct reticles ARG1 and ARG2 are associated with the same product ID.  This product ID is not an identifier of the reticle, rather it is an identifier of the type of thing the reticle is used to process.")
(comment citizenshipPolity "An instance of #$BinarySituationPredicate, <code>(#$citizenshipPolity CITIZENSHIP POLITY)</code> identifies <code>POLITY</code> as the geopolitical entity for which there is a person <code>P</code>, such that throughout <code>CITIZENSHIP</code>, <code>(#$citizens POLITY P)</code> holds.")
(comment metaphasePlateOfCell "<code>(#$metaphasePlateOfCell CELL PLATE)</code> means that <code>PLATE</code> is the is the metaphase plate or \"equatorial plane\" of <code>CELL</code>.")
(comment ChromosomeLinesUpAtMetaphasePlate "A collection during which a chromosome lines up at the metaphase plate (see #$metaphasePlateOfCell).")
(comment SisterChromatidsCutByEnzyme-Mitosis "The collection of events in which proteolytic enzymes sever the connections between the chromatids in the #$Anaphase stage of
#$Mitosis. The daughter chromosomes are then pulled by the
microtubules to the spindle poles of the cell.")
(comment Capsid "The collection of all capsids, which are the protein shells that house the genomes of viruses.")
(comment Virus "A specialization of #$Microorganism.  Each instance of #$Virus consists mainly of a #$Capsid (capsule chamber) containing viral DNA or RNA.  Viruses have no cells, but reproduce by inserting into living cells the viral DNA or RNA, which then uses cellular mechanisms to create new viruses.  Viruses cause many diseases in all other types of  organisms; some can even infect instances of #$Bacterium.  Note that #$Virus excludes prions, bacteria, rickettsia, and protists.")
(comment BinaryFission "A collection of events in which a #$Cell divides into two approximately identical organisms.  This process is the form of reproduction of all #$ProkaryoticCells and some #$Protozoans.")
(comment valueChangeFunctionForStrategy "(#$valueChangeListForStrategy STRAT TEMPLATE POSITION FUNCTION INTEGER) means that for each iteration of the strategy FUNCTION is applied to the argument in POSITION within any occurrences of TEMPLATE and the resulting value substituted into TEMPLATE.  This should proceed iteratively until the termination condition of the strategy obtains, there have been INTEGER iterations (counting the first), or the application of the function to the argument fails to produce a value.")
(comment referenceLayerTypeOfPhotolithographyStepType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PhotolithographyStepTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn.  Where LAYER-TYPE is a collection instance of #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$referenceLayerTypeOfPhotolithographyStepType LAYER-TYPE STEP-TYPE) means that STEP-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration wherein an instance of LAYER-TYPE is the #$outputsCreated in the #$PhotoresistDeposition step, and the #$objectActedOn in the #$PhotoresistExposure-Stepped and #$PhotoresistDevelopment steps, and an instance of (#$EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn LAYER-TYPE) as the #$outputsCreated in the #$PhotoresistDevelopment step.")
(comment PhotolithographyStepTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn "A collection denoting function used to reify and reason about collections of photolithography steps.  Specifically, where LAYER-TYPE is a collection instance of #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$PhotolithographyStepTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn LAYER-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration wherein an instance of LAYER-TYPE is the #$outputsCreated in the #$PhotoresistDeposition step, and the #$objectActedOn in the #$PhotoresistExposure-Stepped and #$PhotoresistDevelopment steps, and an instance of (#$EtchedWaferPatternTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn LAYER-TYPE) as the outputsCreated in the #$PhotoresistDevelopment step.")
(comment initialThreadValueForThreadReconstruction "(#$initialThreadValueForThreadReconstruction LOTID OVLTYPE LAYER STEPPER SDSTEPPER SDRETICLE M1STEPPER RETICLE PROC-DATE) means that a thread is uniquely determined by LOTID and PROC-DATE and that OVLTYPE, LAYER, etc. are the values for those properties associated with the thread.")
(comment sksiPredhasArgLogicalFieldType "(#$sksiPredhasArgLogicalFieldType PRED NUM TYPE LS) means that in the context of SKSI logical field mappings for LS,PRED has the logical field type TYPE corresponding to arg position NUM.")
(comment WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all processes wherein a photomasked instance of #$SemiconductorWafer is exposed to an etching agent that engraves the unmasked portions of the wafer, within the context of an overarching #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography process.")
(comment MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography "The collection of all end-to-end processes in microelectronic fabrication wherein a single #$SemiconductorWafer is submitted to a #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration followed by a #$WaferEtchingProcess-SingleIteration followed by a #$PhotoresistStrippingProcess-SingleIteration.  Each #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography consists in exactly one of these stages, involving a single instance of #$ResistLayer that is deposited in the #$PhotoresistDeposition stage of the #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration.")
(comment MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerType "A second-order collection which partitions #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography.  Each collection instance of #$MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerType is a specialization of #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography where the #$ResistLayer involved is individuated by its order in the production process, that is, by #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType.")
(comment MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing and reasoning about instances of #$MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerType.  Where LAYER-TYPE is a #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn LAYER-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography wherein the #$ResistLayer instance being operated on is of type LAYER-TYPE.")
(comment referenceLayerTypeOfEngravingType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$MEWaferEngravingTypeByReferenceLayerTypeFn.  Where LAYER-TYPE is a #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType, (#$referenceLayerTypeOfEngravingType LAYER-TYPE ENGRAVING-TYPE) means that ENGRAVING-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography wherein the #$ResistLayer instance being operated on is of type LAYER-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ProkaryoticCellDivision EukaryoticCellDivision)
(disjointWith BinaryFission MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle)
(disjointWith ReproductiveFission EukaryoticCellDivision)
(comment ProkaryoticCellDivision "A specialization of #$ReproductiveFission. An instance of #$CellDivisionTypeByCellType, this is the subcollection of #$CellDivision  that takes place in (#$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell) an instance of #$ProkaryoticCell.")
(comment MEP-Data-40days-overlay-PS "A physical schema for #$MEP-Data-40days-overlay-KS.")
(comment MEP-Data-40days-stepper-PS "A physical schema for #$MEP-Data-40days-stepper-KS.")
(comment Spermatogenesis "A specialization of #$Gametogenesis.  Each instance of #$Spermatogenesis is an event in which at least one #$SpermCell is created.")
(comment PrimarySpermatocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$PrimarySpermatocyte is a male gametocyte that can divide by mitosis into further spermatocytes or by meiosis into secondary spermatocytes.")
(comment SecondarySpermatocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$SecondarySpermatocyte is a male gametocyte that can divide by meiosis II into #$Spermatids.")
(comment Spermiogenesis "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of #$Spermiogenesis is a final stage in a #$Spermatogenesis, during which a #$Spermatid matures into a #$SpermCell.")
(comment TissueTypeByOrganismPartType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$BiologicalTissue into subcollections based on the type of organism part that the tissue comprises.")
(comment TissueTypeOfOrganismPartTypeFn "<code>(#$TissueTypeOfOrganTypeFn PART-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that is tissue from an organism part of type <code>PART-TYPE</code>.")
(comment tissueTypeOfOrganismPartType "<code>(#$tissueTypeOfOrganismPartType TISSUE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TISSUE-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that is tissue from an organism part of type <code>PART-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Dermis "A specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$Dermis is an inner layer of some (#$SkinOnFn #$WholeBody).")
(comment Epidermis "A specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$Epidermis is an outermost layer of some (#$SkinOnFn #$WholeBody).")
(comment DensityDependentInhibition "A subcollection of #$InhibitionSituation.  Instances are situations in which a population of instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject are inhibited from growing due to its density relative to environmental factors.")
(comment growthInhibitedPopulation "<code>(#$growthInhibitedPopulation INHIBITION POPULATION)</code> means that <code>POPULATION</code> is a population of instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject whose growth is inhibited in <code>INHIBITION</code>, an instance of #$DensityDependentInhibition.  In populations of animals, this will typically mean that the birth and death rates within the population largely stay the same.  In populations of cells (e.g., instances of #$BiologicalTissue), this will typically mean that the cells are inhibited from dividing.")
(comment KinetochoreConnectsToCentromere "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction that takes place during cell division, in which a kinetochore (see #$Kinetochore) in the cell cytoplasm binds to a centromere (see #$Centromere) on a chromatid in a duplicated chromosome.")
(comment threadHasSDReticleAndReticleOrGroupProductID "(#$threadHasSDReticleAndReticleOrGroupProductID THREAD KEY-LOTID SDRETICLE RETICLE GROUPPRODUCTID) means that either THREAD is associated with SDRETICLE (via #$sDReticleUsedInOverlay) and RETICLE (via #$maskingLayerReticleUsedInOverlay) or THREAD is associated with GROUPPRODUCTID (via #$overlayProductGroupID) and is not associated with SDRETICLE and RETICLE.")
(comment hasOvertimePlay "<code>(#$hasOvertimePlay GAME #$True)</code> means that the game <code>GAME</code> has at least one overtime period, while <code>(#$hasOvertimePlay GAME #$False)</code> means it does not.")
(comment SummaryScoreMaxCountSlot "The collection of instances of #$BinaryPredicate used by the NFL DSRS to calculate lowest maximum number of scoring events at specific points in time for specific teams in specific games.")
(disjointWith AFCChampionshipGame NFCChampionshipGame)
(disjointWith SuperBowlGame AFCChampionshipGame)
(disjointWith SuperBowlGame NFCChampionshipGame)
(comment championshipTypeForSportsLeague "<code>(#$championshipTypeForSportsLeague CHAMPIONSHIP-TYPE LEAGUE)</code> identifies <code>CHAMPIONSHIP-TYPE</code> as the instance of #$SportsChampionshipEventTypeBySportsLeague whose instances are championship competitions to determine a champion for the member of <code>LEAGUE</code>, an instance of #$SportsLeague.  For example, <code>(#$championshipTypeForSportsLeague #$SuperBowlGame #$NationalFootballLeague)</code> identifies the super bowl as the class of competitions that determine the NFL champion, and <code>(#$championshipTypeForSportsLeague #$WorldSeries #$MajorLeagueBaseball)</code>.")
(comment SportsChampionshipEventTypeBySportsLeague "An instance of #$FacetingCollectionType whose instances are collections of instances of #$ChampionshipCompetition, each instance of which is a competition that determines the champion of a particular sports league.")
(comment divisionInhibitedCell "<code>(#$divisionInhibitedCell INHIBIT CELL)</code> means that <code>CELL</code> is an instance of #$Cell that is inhibited from dividing by virtue of its being a member of a population of cells that is experiencing <code>INHIBIT</code>, an instance of #$DensityDependentInhibition.")
(comment CancerCell "The collection of all cancer cells.")
(comment NeoplasticCell "The collection of all cells that have a propensity to divide without regard to the population density of the surrounding cells in the tissue in which it \"resides.\" An important subcollection of this is #$CancerCell.")
(comment requiredTypeForSubSituationType "(#$requiredTypeForSubSituationType TYPE SITTYPE SUBSITTYPE) means that any instance SIT of the specialization of #$Situation SUBSITTYPE that is #$subSituations of some instance of SITTYPE requires a #$SomethingExisting of type TYPE as resource.")
(comment BloodProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  Each instance of #$BloodProteinMolecule is a molecule of a protein that naturally occurs in the blood of a living animal.  Important specializations include immunoglobulins (see #$AntibodyMolecule) and albumins (see #$AlbuminMolecule).")
(comment SDResistLayer "A commonly-identified type of #$ResistLayer used in semiconductor processing.  The SD or 'source drain' resist layer is the first pattern photomask used in defining the transistors on a #$SemiconductorWafer")
(comment R0ResistLayer "A commonly-identified type of #$ResistLayer used in semiconductor processing.  The R0 resist layer is the photomask that lays down the first alignment marks used in overlay metrology.")
(comment Hepatocyte "A specialization of #$LiverCell.  Each instance of #$Hepatocyte is a cell in liver tissue.  Hepatocytes make up the majority of a liver's cytoplasmic mass.")
(comment Myocyte "Also known as muscle cells.  Each instance of #$Myocyte is a cell in muscle tissue.")
(comment YellowMarrow "Tissue that is found in the center of bones consisting mainly of #$FatCells.")
(comment EmbryonicStemCell "A specialization of #$StemCell. Each instance of #$EmbryonicStemCell is a pluripotent stem cell derived from a blastocyst.")
(comment Blastocyst "A specialization of #$Embryo. Each instance of #$Blastocyst is an early-stage embryo.")
(disjointWith AdultStemCell EmbryonicStemCell)
(comment AdultStemCell "A specialization of #$StemCell. Each instance of #$AdultStemCell is a multipotent stem cell with ability to undergo mitosis to produce additional adult stem cells.")
(comment HematopoieticStemCell "A specialization of #$AdultStemCell. Each instance of #$HematopoieticStemCell is a multipotent stem cell with the ability to differentiate into any type of #$BloodCell.")
(comment HematopoieticTissue "A specialization of #$BiologicalTissue.  Each instance of #$HematopoieticTissue is tissue that produces blood cells.")
(comment predicateHasLogicalSchemaForPS "(#$predicateHasLogicalSchemaForPS PRED PS LS) means that LS is the logical schema associated with PRED and its corresponding physical schema is PS.")
(comment HomologousChromosomesCutByEnzyme "The collection of events in which proteolytic enzymes sever the connections between the homologous chromatids in the #$AnaphaseI stage of #$Meiosis. The daughter chromosomes are then pulled by the microtubules to the spindle poles of the cell.")
(comment SisterChromatidsCutByEnzyme-Meiosis "The collection of events in which proteolytic enzymes sever the connections between the sister chromatids in the #$AnaphaseII stage of #$Meiosis. The daughter chromosomes are then pulled by the microtubules to the spindle poles of the cell.")
(comment primaryPhysicalPartType "A specialization of #$properPhysicalPartTypes. Where <code>TYPE1</code>  and <code>TYPE2</code> are both specializations of #$PartiallyTangible, <code>(#$primaryPhysicalPartType TYPE1 TYPE2)</code>  means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> has an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as a proper physical part, and one or more instances of <code>TYPE2</code> are the primary components of <code>TYPE1</code> in the sense that the portion of any instance <code>INST</code> of <code>TYPE1</code> constituted by instances of <code>TYPE2</code> is greater than any other non-arbitrary portion of <code>INST</code>.  For example, it is true that (#$primaryPhysicalPartType #$RoseBouquet #$RoseFlower).")
(comment PhysicalDevice "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleArtifact and #$ObjectWithUse. Each instance of #$PhysicalDevice is an artifact with a relatively rigid, set shape, designed for a specific use or to perform a specific function.  Specializations of #$PhysicalDevice thus include (among others) #$RoadVehicle, #$Motorboat, #$HandTool, and #$PlumbingFixture. Artifacts which have a specific use or function, but which do not have a relatively rigid, set shape are <i>not</i> instances of #$PhysicalDevice; for this reason, neither #$GasolineFuel nor #$AntiFreeze are specializations of #$PhysicalDevice.")
(comment killers "<code>(#$killers KILLING KILLER)</code> means that <code>KILLER</code> is one of the instances of #$IntelligentAgent that performed (see #$performedBy) <code>KILLING</code>, an instance of #$KillingByOrganism.")
(comment injurers "<code>(#$injurers INJURING INJURER)</code> means that <code>INJURING</code> is one of the instances of #$IntelligentAgent that performed (see #$performedBy) <code>INJURING</code>, an instance of #$IncurringAnInjury.")
(comment bombTypeUsed "A specialization of #$deviceTypeUsed, <code>(#$bombTypeUsed BOMBING BOMB)</code> means that the type of #$Bomb used in the instance of #$Bombing <code>BOMBING</code> is <code>BOMB</code>.")
(comment weaponTypeUsed "A specialization of #$deviceTypeUsed, <code>(#$weaponTypeUsed EVENT WEAPON-TYPE)</code> means that the type of #$Weapon used in the event <code>EVENT</code> is <code>WEAPON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment mostSpecificCommonMemberType "A specialization of #$groupMemberType, <code>(#$mostSpecificCommonMemberType GROUP TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the most specific collection such that all members of <code>GROUP</code> are instances of that collection.")
(comment nearestCommonIsaOfSet "<code>(#$nearestCommonIsaOfSet SET COL)</code> means that
<code>COL</code> is the nearest collection of which each element in <code>SET</code> is an instance.")
(comment marriageSituationPartners "A specialization of #$situationConstituents, <code>(#$marriageSituationPartners MARRIAGE PARTNER)</code> means that <code>PARTNER</code> is one of the people in the marriage <code>MARRIAGE</code>.")
(comment mostSpecificCommonBuildingClass "A specialization of #$mostSpecificCommonMemberType, restricted to instances of #$BuildingCluster in its arg1.")
(comment mostSpecificCommonHumanAgentClass "A specialization of #$mostSpecificCommonMemberType, restricted to instances of <code>(#$GroupFn (#$CollectionUnionFn
   (#$TheSet #$Person #$MultiPersonAgent)))</code> in its arg1.")
(comment mostSpecificCommonPersonClass "A specialization of #$mostSpecificCommonMemberType, restricted to instances of <code>(#$GroupFn #$Person)</code> in its arg1.")
(comment SisterChromosomeMovesToPole-Mitosis "Here, the chromosomes are separated and are
being pulled to the opposite poles of the cell nucleus by the microtubules.")
(comment AnaphaseI "The third stage of #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment ChromosomeMovesToPole "Here, the chromosomes are separated and are
being pulled to the opposite poles of the cell nucleus by the microtubules.")
(comment EdwardsSyndrome "A specialization of #$Trisomy that affects the 18th chromosome.")
(comment PatauSyndrome "A specialization of #$Trisomy that affects the 13th chromosome.")
(comment DownsSyndrome "A specialization of #$Trisomy that affects the 21st chromosome.")
(comment ChromosomeAbnormality "A specialization of #$GeneticCondition.  Each instance of #$ChromosomeAbnormality is an abnormal physiological condition which developed in a particular organism due to that organism's having an atypical numer of chromosomes or an atypical structure of one or more chromosomes.")
(comment Tetrasomy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has four copies of a particular chromosome, instead of the normal two.")
(comment Trisomy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has three copies of a particular chromosome, instead of the normal two.")
(comment AutosomalTrisomy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has three copies of a particular autosomal chromosome, instead of the normal two.")
(comment SexChromosomeTrisomy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has three copies of an X or Y chromosome, instead of the usual number.")
(comment TripleXSyndrome "A specialization of #$SexChromosomeTrisomy characterized by the presence of an extra X chromosome in each cell of a human female.")
(comment SexChromosome "A specialization of #$Chromosome. Each instance of #$SexChromosome is a chromosome that determines the development of sexual characteristics in an organism.")
(comment Autosome "A specialization of #$Chromosome. Each instance of #$Autosome is a chromosome that is not a #$SexChromosome.")
(disjointWith SexChromosome Autosome)
(comment Monosomy "An abnormal genetic condition in which an organism has one of a particular chromosome, instead of the normal two.")
(comment Chromosome1-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 1 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome2-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 2 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome3-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 3 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome4-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 4 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome5-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 5 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome6-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 6 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome7-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 7 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome8-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 8 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome9-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 9 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome10-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 10 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome11-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 11 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome13-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 13 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome14-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 14 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome15-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 15 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome16-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 16 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome17-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 17 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome18-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 18 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome19-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 19 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome20-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 20 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome21-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 21 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment Chromosome22-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 22 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment YChromosome-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$SexChromosome.  Normally, male humans have one unduplicated copy of the \"Y\"chromosome in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes, whereas normally female humans have two unduplicated copy of the \"X\"chromosome in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment DuplicatedChromosomeMovesToPole "Each instance of #$DuplicatedChromosomeMovesToPole occurs during #$AnaphaseI of #$Meiosis. During each instance of #$DuplicatedChromosomeMovesToPole duplicated chromosomes move toward the pole away from their homologues.")
(comment HumanCell "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  Each instance of #$HumanCell is a cell of a #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment HumanSpermCell "A specialization of #$SpermCell and #$HumanCell. Each instance of #$HumanSpermCell is a sperm cell of a homo sapiens.")
(comment HumanOvum "A specialization of #$HumanCell and #$Ovum.  Each instance of #$HumanOvum is an egg cell of a #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment MaleAnimalCell "The collection of #$Cells that male #$Animals and parts of male #$Animals are made of.")
(comment FemaleAnimalCell "The collection of #$Cells that female #$Animals and parts of female #$Animals are made of.")
(comment MonitorPort "The collection of all monitor ports. A type of #$ComputerOutputDevice. The concept #$MonitorPort is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment RackMounted "The collection of #$ElectronicDevices that are designed to be mounted in computer hardware racks.")
(comment TowerStyleComputer "The collection of #$Computers that are designed to sit vertically on a desk or on the floor.")
(comment eventOccursInPolity "<code>(#$eventOccursInPolity EVT GEO-ENTITY)</code> means that the event <code>EVT</code> occurs within the boundaries of the geopolitical entity <code>GEO-ENTITY</code>.")
(comment PredicateIntersection2Fn "<code>(#$PredicateIntersection2Fn PRED1 PRED2)</code> denotes the predicate that is the intersection (see #$predicateIntersection) of <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED2</code>.")
(comment groupCardinalityMax "<code>(#$groupCardinalityMax GROUP NUM)</code> the #$Group <code>GROUP</code> has at most <code>NUM</code> members.")
(comment groupCardinalityMin "<code>(#$groupCardinalityMin GROUP NUM)</code> the #$Group <code>GROUP</code> has a minimum of <code>NUM</code> members.")
(comment weightValueListForMetrologyRelationForThread "(#$weightValueListForMetrologyRelationForLotSet ID MET-PRED ORDER LIST) means that LIST is the list consisting of a weight and a value, (#$TheList WGT VAL), assocated with each ID for which (MET-PRED ID VAL) holds.  The value for WGT is partially determined by value for ORDER")
(comment MRReadingTargetVocabulary "The collection of instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" is either a collection (where what is actually learned are that instances of the collection are mentioned in the text) or a relation (in which case what is learned is a sentence).")
(comment MRSecondaryReadingTargetVocabulary "The collection of instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are primary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" is either a collection (where what is actually learned are that instances of the collection are mentioned in the text) or a relation (in which case what is learned is a sentence).")
(comment MRPrimaryReadingTargetVocabulary "The collection of instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are primary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" is either a collection (where what is actually learned are that instances of the collection are mentioned in the text) or a relation (in which case what is learned is a sentence).")
(comment MRPrimaryReadingTargetCollectionDenotingTerm "The collection of collection-denoting instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are primary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" is this sense means that the system learns are that instances of the collection are mentioned in the text.")
(comment MRPrimaryReadingTargetRelationDenotingTerm "The collection of relation-denoting instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are primary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" in this sense is a sentence formed with this term is learned.")
(comment MachineReadingProjectUseCaseDocumentationConstant "A collection of collections of CycL terms.  Instances are used to document the role that CycL terms play within the usecases devised for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment DSRSSupportedVocabulary "The collection of terms that are expected to be supported by the DSRS for the specific usecase at hand.")
(comment DSRSBuiltin "The collection of terms that are expected to be supported by the DSRS via specialized reasoning modules for the specific usecase at hand.")
(comment MRSecondaryReadingTargetCollectionDenotingTerm "The collection of collection-denoting instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are secondary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" is this sense means that the system learns are that instances of the collection are mentioned in the text.")
(comment MRSecondaryReadingTargetRelationDenotingTerm "The collection of relation-denoting instances of #$CycLDenotationalTerm that are primary targets for learning in usecases for the #$MachineReadingProject.  A \"target for learning\" in this sense is a sentence formed with this term is learned.")
(comment dateOfSituation "A specialization of #$startingDate and #$endingDate, <code>(#$dateOfSituation SIT DATE)</code> identifies <code>DATE</code> as the date during which the situation <code>SIT</code> obtains.")
(comment MRInferenceTargetRelationDenotingTerm "The collection of relation-denoting terms, sentences built from which are expected to be inferred, as opposed to directly extracted from text.")
(comment resistLayerTypeDesignation "(#$resistLayerTypeDesignation LAYER-TYPE STRING) means that STRING is the character code by which the #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType LAYER-TYPE is typically designated in semiconductor fabrication.")
(comment reticleCompatibleWithLayerType "(#$reticleCompatibleWithLayerType RETICLE LAYER-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, the #$MaskingReticle RETICLE is capable of being used in #$PhotoresistExposures occurring as part of a #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration wherein the #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType involved is LAYER-TYPE (see #$referenceLayerTypeOfPhotolithographyStepType and its corresponding function.")
(comment reticleDesignedForLayerType "(#$reticleDesignedForLayerType RETICLE LAYER-TYPE means that the #$MaskingReticle RETICLE is designed so that being a device used in #$PhotoresistExposures occurring as part of a #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration wherein the #$PhotoresistReferenceLayerType involved is LAYER-TYPE is its #$intendedPrimaryFunction.")
(comment ExhibitionGame "The collection of instances of #$GameEvent that are played, primarily, in order to entertain an audience, and are typically not part of a participant's \"season\" in any meaningful sense.  As such, scores and player statistics compiled during such games, if kept, are typically not considered part of the participants' \"official statistics,\" and outcomes do not contribute to win-loss records (though they might be used in some arcane way -- e.g., since 2003, the all-star game in Major League Baseball has been used to determine home-team and away-team roles in the first World Series game).")
(disjointWith RegularSeasonGame ExhibitionGame)
(disjointWith PostseasonGame ExhibitionGame)
(disjointWith ChampionshipCompetition ExhibitionGame)
(disjointWith AllStarTeam NFLTeam)
(disjointWith NBATeam AllStarTeam)
(disjointWith AFLTeam AllStarTeam)
(disjointWith ThePrototypicalSportsTeamTypeByLeague AllStarTeam)
(comment NFLProBowl "The collection of all pro-bowl games, annual all-star games held by the NFL, typically after the end of the NFL season.")
(comment AllStarGame "A specialization of #$ExhibitionGame.  Instances are team competitions in which the teams are comprised of exceptional or popular players from several different teams who would ordinarily compete against one another.")
(comment AllStarTeam "The collection of all short-lived sports teams that are assembled for the purpose of playing in all-star games (or other exhibition games).")
(comment parameterToArgMappingForTermInInformationStore "A relation used to facilitate the mapping of terms from external information stores into CycL.  <code>(#$parameterToArgMappingForTermInInformationStore CYCL-TERM STORE PARAM INT)</code> means that the relation-denoting term from the instance <code>STORE</code> of #$AspatialInformationStore that is synonymous with (see #$synonymousExternalConcept) the CycL term <code>CYCL-TERM</code>, is such that its parameter <code>PARAM</code> maps onto the CycL argument-place <code>INT</code>.")
(comment newEstimateForEWMAValue "(#$newEstimateForEWMAValue CURRENT PRIOR NEW) means that NEW is the result of plugging the CURRENT and PRIOR values into the EWMA formula along with the current EWMA filter contant value.")
(disjointWith AmitoticTissue MitoticTissue)
(disjointWith AmitoticTissue PartiallyMitoticTissue)
(disjointWith PartiallyMitoticTissue MitoticTissue)
(comment AmitoticTissue "The collection of samples of #$BiologicalTissue that contains no cells currently undergoing #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle.")
(comment PartiallyMitoticTissue "The collection of samples of #$BiologicalTissue that contains both sub-samples of #$MitoticTissue and sub-samples of #$AmitoticTissue.")
(comment threadListHasWeightedAvrForPredValue "(#$threadListHasWeightedAvrForPredValue LIST BIN-PRED FUNCTION AVR) means that AVR is the weighted average of the values for BIN-PRED for the threads in LIST by a recursive application of FUNCTION.")
(comment ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn "(#$ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn LIST SEED FN) returns the result of applying FN, an evaluatable function, first to the first item in LIST and SEED, then to the second item in LIST and the result of the first application, and so on, for every item in LIST.  For example, (#$ApplyFunctionRecursivelyFn (#$TheList 2 4 6 8) 1 #$TimesFn)) = 384. By definition, if ARGS is empty, the result is SEED.  Every member of LIST and SEED must be a valid argument for FN.  This is currently only defined for functions with an arity less than 3.  Note that if FN is a unary function, this simply results in the value you would get by applying FN to the last item in LIST.")
(comment MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer "The collection of all fabrication processes wherein a single instance of #$SemiconductorWafer is repeatedly subjected to successive instances of #$MEWaferEngravingViaPhotolithography, resulting in the creation over time of an array of fully-articulated #$SemiconductorDevices.")
(comment MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType "A collection of specializations of #$Molecule.  Each instance of #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType is a collection of molecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules of a particular type of chemical compound (see #$ChemicalSubstanceType).  Cf. the more specific collection #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies,  which is a collection of collections whose instances have the same chemical structure and formula.")
(comment AnabolicSteroid "A powerful chemical compound produced either synthetically or derived from the male hormone testosterone. They help stimulate skeletal muscle development and growth and are also responsible for the development and maintenance of secondary sexual characteristics. They are used by some athletes who claim they improve muscle strength and endurance.")
(comment Phospholipid "A specialization of #$Lipid.  Phospholipids can form lipid bilayers and so they are a major component of cell membranes.")
(comment PhosphorylationCascade "Each instance of #$PhosphorylationCascade is a sequence of events in which different enzymes in a pathway are phosphorylated in turn, causing a chain reaction leading to the phosphorylation of a large number of molecules.")
(comment SemiconductorWaferSubstratePreparation "The collection of all steps in #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration wherein the #$SemiconductorWafer instance being processed is prepared for #$PhotoresistDeposition, in the strict sense that actions are taken to promote adhesion of the #$ResistLayer to the substrate surface.  These actions may included chemical cleaning of the semiconductor wafer to remove films and oxides (#$SubstrateCleaning-PreDepositionSemiconductorWafer), baking to expurgate adsorbed water (#$SubstrateDehydrationBake-SemiconductorWafer) and application of an adhesion promoter to the wafer substrate (#$AdhesionPromoterApplication-SemiconductorWafer).")
(comment SubstrateCleaning-PreDepositionSemiconductorWafer "The collection of all events wherein a #$SemiconductorWafer is cleaned in preparation for a #$PhotoresistDeposition step in semiconductor manufacture.")
(comment SubstrateDehydrationBake-SemiconductorWafer "The collection of all events wherein a #$SemiconductorWafer is heated in order to drive out adsorbed H20 preparatory to #$PhotoresistDeposition during an instance of #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration.")
(comment AdhesionPromoterApplication-SemiconductorWafer "The collection of all event wherein an adhesion promoter such as hexamethyldisilizane, is applied to a #$SemiconductorWafer instance to promote adhesion of the #$ResistLayer in a subsequent #$PhotoresistDeposition.")
(comment TransferOfPhosphateFromATPToProtein "The collection of events in which a phosphate is transferred from an ATP molecule to a protein molecule, during the phosphorylation of the protein molecule.")
(disjointWith TransferOfPhosphateFromATPToProtein (ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn AdenosineTriphosphate PhosphateIon))
(disjointWith (ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn AdenosineTriphosphate PhosphateIon) (ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn ProteinMolecule PhosphateIon))
(disjointWith TransferOfPhosphateFromATPToProtein (ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn ProteinMolecule PhosphateIon))
(comment LotProcessingOfInWithFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to represent and reason about various important types of #$LotProcessingStep-Serial.  Where ARTIFACT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Artifact-Generic and ITERATION-TYPE is a specialization of #$ManufacturingASingleObject such that instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE are typically processed in instances of ITERATION-TYPE and such that instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE are typically composed into 'lots' for processing in INDUSTRY-TYPE (see #$standardProcessingLotTypeForIndustry), (#$LotProcessingOfInWithFn ARTIFACT-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE ITERATION-TYPE) denotes the collection of all events wherein an industrial 'lot' composed of instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE is processed in association with INDUSTRY-TYPE in the strict sense that an instance of ITERATION-TYPE is applied successively to each instance of ARTIFACT-TYPE in the lot.")
(comment lotProcessingsHaveAsSubEventsWith "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$LotProcessingOfInWithFn. Where ARTIFACT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Artifact-Generic and ITERATION-TYPE is a specialization of #$ManufacturingASingleObject such that instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE are typically processed in instances of ITERATION-TYPE and such that instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE are typically composed into 'lots' for processing in INDUSTRY-TYPE (see #$standardProcessingLotTypeForIndustry), (#$lotProcessingsHaveAsSubEventsWith ARTIFACT-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE ITERATION-TYPE LOT-STEP-TYPE) means that LOT-STEP-TYPE is the collection of all events wherein an industrial 'lot' composed of instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE is processed in association with INDUSTRY-TYPE in the strict sense that an instance of ITERATION-TYPE is applied successively to each instance of ARTIFACT-TYPE in the lot.")
(comment Protease "#$Protease is a general collection of enzymes that have the capacity to break down proteins.")
(comment CellSignalingProcess-WithPathway-Amplificatory "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that involve the amplification of a signal, via an enzyme cascade.")
(disjointWith CellSignalingProcess-WithPathway-Amplificatory CellSignalingProcess-WithPathway-Non-amplificatory)
(comment CellSignalingProcess-WithPathway-Non-amplificatory "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that involve the focused signal transmissions without amplifying cascades.")
(comment ReceptorMolecule "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule.  Receptors reside either in the plasma membrane of a cell or in the cytoplasm, and can bind with other molecules (called \"ligands\") to evoke a cellular response.  The ability to so bind is a function of the chemical structures of the type of receptor and type of ligand.  Ligands that have an appropriate structure to evoke a cellular response are considered <i>agonists</i> with respect to the class of receptors in question.  Ligands that can bind without evoking a response are considered <i>antagonists</i>.")
(comment ReceptorBindingWithLigand "The collection of all chemical binding events in which a #$ReceptorMolecule binds with a ligand.")
(comment CellularLevelResponseToSignal "The collection of all cellular-level responses as a consequence of signalling events taking place within said cells.")
(comment DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToDate "Each instance of #$DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToDate is a binary relation that corresponds to a DBPedia OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of #$CalendarDay.")
(comment enzymeTypeActivatedByEnzymeTypeInActivationType "The corresponding predicate of #$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeByEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE1 and MOL-TYPE2 are classes of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeActivatedByEnzymeTypeInActivationType MOL-TYPE1 MOL-TYPE2 ACTIVATION-TYPE) means that ACTIVATION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE1 is rendered 'active' by an instance of MOL-TYPE2.")
(comment ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeByEnzymeOfTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used to represent the class of 'activations' of a given type of enzyme by another type of enzyme. Where <code>MOL-TYPE1</code> and <code>MOL-TYPE2</code> are class of #$EnzymeMolecule, <code>(#$ActivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL1-TYPE MOL2-TYPE)</code> denotes the class of all occurrences in which an instance of <code>MOL1-TYPE</code> is activated by an instance of  <code>MOL2-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Activity "A specialization of #$Quantity.  Each instance of #$Activity is a specific degree to which a thing is active, in the sense that some change is going on within it.")
(disjointWith DimerMolecule TrimerMolecule)
(comment TyrosineKinaseMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinKinaseMolecule.  Tyrosine-specific protein kinases phosphorylate tyrosine amino acid residues.")
(comment ReceptorTyrosineKinaseMolecule "A specialization of #$TyrosineKinaseMolecule.  A receptor tyrosine kinase is a membrane receptor with a tyrosine kinase domain that extends into the cytoplasm.")
(comment SerineOrThreonineSpecificProteinKinase "A specialization of #$ProteinKinaseMolecule.  Each instance of #$SerineOrThreonineSpecificProteinKinase is a potein kinase that phosphorylates the OH group of #$Serine or #$Threonine.")
(comment phosphorylatedMolecule "<code>(#$phosphorylatedMolecule PHOSPHORYLATION MOLECULE)</code> identifies <code>MOLECULE</code> as the organic molecule that is phosphorylated (is the recipient of an instance of #$PhosphateIon) in <code>PHOSPHORYLATION</code>, an instance of #$Phosphorylation.")
(comment Phosphorylation "A type of #$ChemicalInteraction that consists of three steps: the unbinding of an instance of #$PhosphateIon from an organic molecule, the transfer of that ion to a second organic molecule, and the binding of the ion with that new molecule.")
(comment phosphateIonTransferred "<code>(#$phosphateIonTransferred PHOSPHORYLATION ION)</code> identifies <code>ION</code> as the instance of #$PhosphateIon that is transferred from one organic molecule to another in <code>PHOSPHORYLATION</code>, an instance of #$Phosphorylation.")
(comment phosphateIonSourceMolecule "<code>(#$phosphateIonSourceMolecule PHOSPHORYLATION MOLECULE)</code> identifies <code>MOLECULE</code> as the source of the instance of #$PhosphateIon that is transferred in <code>PHOSPHORYLATION</code>, an instance of #$Phosphorylation.")
(comment molecularSubUnits "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Molecule to proper parts that are themselves molecules. <code>(#$molecularSubUnits BIG SMALL)</code> means that <code>SMALL</code> is an instance of #$Molecule that is a proper part of the molecule <code>BIG</code>.")
(comment dataValidAsOf "(#$dataValidAsOf INFO-STORE DATE) means that the data in INFO-STORE is valid as of DATE.")
(comment frequencyOfRevision "(#$frequencyOfRevision INFO-STORE FREQUENCY) means that INFO-STORE is regularly revised with the frequency FREQUENCY.")
(comment DimerMolecule "The collection of all molecules formed by the chemical union of two structurally similar units.  If the units are chemically identical, the dimer is an instance or the specialization #$HomodimerMolecule; otherwise, it is a #$HeterodimerMolecule.")
(disjointWith HomodimerMolecule HeterodimerMolecule)
(comment HomodimerMolecule "A specialization of #$DimerMolecule.  A homodimer molecule is a molecule formed by the chemical union of two chemically identical units.")
(comment HeterodimerMolecule "A specialization of #$DimerMolecule.  A heterodimer molecule is a molecule formed by the chemical union of two structurally similar but not chemically identical units.")
(comment WaterDimerMolecule "A specialization of #$HomodimerMolecule.  A water dimer molecule is a molecule that consists of two loosely bound water molecules.")
(comment polymericSubComponents "(#$polymericSubComponents POL MON) means that MON is a monomeric subcomponent of the #$PolymerMolecule POL.")
(disjointWith DimerMolecule TetramerMolecule)
(disjointWith TrimerMolecule TetramerMolecule)
(comment TrimerMolecule "The collection of all molecules formed by the chemical union of three structurally similar molecular combining units.")
(comment TetramerMolecule "The collection of all molecules formed by the chemical union of four structurally similar molecular combining units.")
(comment MultimerMolecule "The collection of all molecules formed by the chemical union of one to four structurally similar molecular combining units.")
(disjointWith PolymerMolecule MultimerMolecule)
(comment EnzymeMolecule "This is the collection of (individual) enzyme molecules, which are globular protein molecules that can act as biological catalysts in a broad spectrum of biochemical reactions.")
(comment BiocatalyticMolecule "This is the collection of (individual)  molecules which catalyze a broad spectrum of biochemical reactions.  Important specializations are #$EnzymeMolecule and #$RibozymeMolecule.")
(disjointWith EnzymeMolecule RibozymeMolecule)
(comment DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToString "A specialization of DBPediaOWLProperty (q.v.). Each instance of DBPediaOWLProperty-RelationToString is a binary relation that corresponds to a DBpedia OWL property whose arg2 constraint is a specialization of CharacterString.")
(comment LinkedMovieDatabase-CW "A work consisting primarily of #$RDFTriples about #$Movie-CWs, extracted from #$Wikipedia-WebSite and Freebase.")
(comment LinkedMovieDatabaseOntology "An instance of #$Ontology.  The Linked Movie Database ontology is an OWL ontology that contains concepts and relations pertinent to describing movies.")
(comment linkedMovieDatabaseActorID "<code>(#$linkedMovieDatabaseActorID ACTOR ID)</code> means that the id number for ACTOR in #$LinkedMovieDatabase-CW is ID.")
(comment linkedMovieDatabaseDirectorID "<code>(#$linkedMovieDatabaseDirectorID DIRECTOR ID)</code> means that the id number for DIRECTOR in #$LinkedMovieDatabase-CW is ID.")
(comment linkedMovieDatabaseSubjectID "<code>(#$linkedMovieDatabaseSubjectID SUBJECT ID)</code> means that the id number for SUBJECT in #$LinkedMovieDatabase-CW is ID.")
(comment linkedMovieDatabaseFilmID "<code>(#$linkedMovieDatabaseFilmID FILM ID)</code> means that the id number for FILM in #$LinkedMovieDatabase-CW is ID.")
(comment AdrenergicReceptor "The collection of G protein-coupled receptor molecules  for noradrenaline and adrenaline molecules.")
(comment GProteinLinkedReceptor "An important specialization of #$MembraneReceptorMolecule.  Instances of #$GProteinLinkedReceptor consist in seven interlinked alpha helices spanning the cell membrane, with an extra-membranal binding site to which a signal molecule such as an #$EpinephrineMolecule may link.  When activated by this binding, the #$GProteinLinkedReceptor acquires the ability to 'swap' instances of #$GuanosineDiphosphate for instances of #$GuanosineTriphosphate in #$GProteinMolecules, thereby activating these molecules in signal transduction pathways.")
(comment ReceptorLigandBindingEventTypeByReceptorType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand into two disjoint collections, those whose instances are such that the #$receptorSiteInBindingEvent is an instance of #$CytoplasmicReceptorMolecule, and those such that the #$receptorSiteInBindingEvent is an instance of #$MembraneReceptorMolecule.")
(comment cellTargetedForSignaling "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot and #$ActorSlot that relates the pre-response portion of a cell-signaling event to the cell that is the \"target\" of the signal.")
(comment LargeCell "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$LargeCell is a cell that is large (for a cell).")
(comment LargePolynuclearCell "A specialization of #$LargeCell and #$PolynuclearCell.  Each instance of #$LargePolynuclearCell is a cell that with more than one nucelus and which is large (for a cell).")
(comment ligandTypeHasTargetCellType "<code>(#$ligandTypeHasTargetCellType LIGAND-TYPE CELL-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>CELL-TYPE</code> as the subcollection of #$EukaryoticCell whose instances are appropriate target cells for signaling initiated by instances of <code>LIGAND-TYPE</code>, an type of #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject.")
(comment occursDuringHospitalVisitWithHospitalAdmit "This relates a patient's #$HospitalVisit that contains a #$CCFHospitalAdmitDate to the patient's events that occur in the hospital during that hospitalization.")
(comment Cytosol "The liquid part of the #$Cytoplasm in a cell.")
(comment cellularSignalInitiator "<code>(#$cellularSignalInitiator SIGNALING MOLECULE)</code> identifies <code>MOLECULE</code> as the instance of #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject that initiates the instance <code>SIGNALING</code> of #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell by virtue of playing the #$signalMoleculeInBindingEvent role in the instance of #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand that is the first #$subEvents of <code>SIGNALING</code>.")
(disjointWith CellularLevelResponseToSignal SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(comment signalTransductionInitiator "A specialization of #$causalActors, <code>(#$signalTransductionInitiator TRANSDUCTION MOLECULE)</code> identifies <code>MOLECULE</code> as the instance of #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject that plays the #$signalMoleculeInBindingEvent role in the instance of #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand that immediately precedes the instance
TRANSDUCTION of 
#$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-MultiStageReaction in the larger #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell-WithPathway event that subsumes both.")
(comment SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-SingleReaction "A subcollection of #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess that is, in some sense, a degenerate case of transduction, as there is no chain of reactions involved; rather each instance immediately follows a #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand event in which the activated receptor travels to a #$DNAMolecule, binds to it, and evokes a cellular response.")
(comment CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell-NoPathway "A variation on the cell signaling script (see #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) that involves a cytoplasmic receptor (#$CytoplasmicReceptorMolecule) and hence a degenerate transduction (#$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-SingleReaction) in which the activated receptor moves directly to the relevant instance of #$DNAMolecule, evoking a cellular response (#$CellularLevelResponseToSignal).")
(comment YChromosome "A subcollection of #$SexChromosome the presence or absence of which determines the sex (male or female, respectively) in most types of mammal.")
(comment CellSignalingProcessTypeByPathwayComplexity "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets the collection of cell-signaling events (see #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) into sub-collections based on the complexity of their \"pathways\" -- i.e., on the complexity of the transduction (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess) events they subsume.")
(comment CellularCommunication "An important concept in molecular signaling in cells.  Generally speaking, a cellular signaling event begins with a general release or dispersion of many instances of a type of signal molecule, such as epinephrine (#$EpinephrineMolecule) into the intercellular medium, usually through release into the #$Bloodstream (see IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn).  Instances of the signal molecule type either penetrate cells by diffusion through the phospholipid bilayer to bind with intracellular receptor molecules in the cellular cytoplasm, or bind to membrane receptors.  In the latter case, the mebranal binding of a signal molecule is invariably the first step in what is commonly known as a 'transduction path' or 'transduction pathway' (#$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) wherein a train of characteristic protein activations will be triggered.  Either as the result of the signal molecule bindings within cellular cytoplasms, or the triggering of parallel transduction paths within cells, many cells will undergo cellular-level morphological or metabolic changes (#$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel) which en masse constitute a cellular response that terminates the signaling process.")
(comment chemicalObjectsOfTypeAreSecondMessengersInSignalProcess "Where PROCESS is an instance of #$CellularSignalingProcess-SignalToResponse and OBJ-TYPE is a kind of #$ChemicalObject, (#$chemicalObjectsOfTypeAreSecondMessengersInSignalProcess PROCESS OBJ-TYPE) means that instances of OBJ-TYPE play the role of 'second messengers' with respect to transduction pathways (#$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell) occurring within PROCESS.")
(comment CyclicAdenosineMonophosphate "A kind of #$AdenosineMonophosphate.  In each instance, a bond exists between the 3' hydroxyl of the sugar base and the phosphate atom of the single #$PhosphateGroupMolecule.  #$CyclicAdenosineMonophosphate (cAMP) serves as a second messenger in many cellular signal transduction pathways (#$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell).")
(comment MitoticTissue "The collection of all samples of #$BiologicalTissue that are mitotic -- i.e., their constituent cells are undergoing the #$EukaryoticCellCycle.")
(comment languageCodeDigraph "(#$languageCodeDigraph LANG CODE) means that CODE is an internationally recognized two-letter abbreviation for the name of LANG.  Values are based on ISO 639-1.")
(comment secondMessengerObject-CellularSignaling "Where MOL is an instance of #$ChemicalObject and PROCESS is an instance of #$ChemicalReaction, (#$secondMessengerObject-CellularSignaling PROCESS MOL) means that MOL participates in a general cytosolic release of objects of a like type in a way that qualifies the #$ChemicalObjects that are dispersed as 'second messengers'.")
(comment Glucose1PhosphateRelease-GlycogenBreakdownTransductionPathway "A specialization of (#$MassEventOfTypeFn #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent).  Each instance of #$Glucose1PhosphateRelease-GlycogenBreakdownTransductionPathway is an event consisting of a large number of chemical unbinding events in which glucose-1-phosphate molecules are released from glycogen, as the cellular-level response that is the culmination of a glycogen breakdown transduction pathway.")
(comment EpinephrineMolecule "The collection of all molecules of the substance variously known as adrenaline or #$Epinephrine, chemical formula C9H13NO3.  The substance is a powerful 'fight or flight' hormone playing a central role in short-term stress reactions mediated by #$EpinephrineMolecules binding to various chemical receptors triggering various transduction pathways.")
(comment AdministrationOfStuffToTissue "Administering something to tissue.")
(comment AdministrationOfStuffTypeToTissueTypeFn "(#$AdministrationOfStuffTypeToTissueTypeFn STUFF-TYPE TISSUE-TYPE) denotes the collection of events in which STUFF-TYPE is administered to tissue of type TISSUE-TYPE.")
(comment administrationOfTypeToTissueType "(#$administrationOfTypeToTissueType STUFF-TYPE TISSUE-TYPE ADMIN-TYPE) means ADMIN-TYPE is the collection of events in which STUFF-TYPE is administered to tissue of type TISSUE-TYPE.")
(comment ExposureOfStuffTypeToStuffTypeFn "(#$ExposureOfStuffTypeToStuffTypeFn STUFF-TYPE1 STUFF-TYPE2) denotes the collection of events in which some STUFF-TYPE1 is exposed to some STUFF-TYPE2.")
(comment exposureOfStuffTypeToStuffType "(#$exposureOfStuffTypeToStuffType STUFF-TYPE1 STUFF-TYPE2 EXPOSURE-TYPE) means EXPOSURE-TYPE is the collection of events in which some STUFF-TYPE1 is exposed to some STUFF-TYPE2 .")
(comment ArchiveOfIBTTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to represent certain types of archival holding.  Where IBT-COL is a class of #$InformationBearingThing, (#$ArchiveOfIBTTypeFn IBT-COL) denotes the collection of all #$ArchiveHoldings whose members (#$groupMembers) consist exclusively in instances of IBT-COL.")
(comment CellCultureFn "(#$CellCultureFn CELL-TYPE) denotes the collection of cell cultures produced from cells of type CELL-TYPE.")
(comment EnzymaticActivity "The collection of events in which #$EnzymeMolecules catalyze chemical reactions.")
(comment PrintRDFSLabelTransformation "The collection of SKSI encoding or decoding evaluation events in which a Cyc term is transformed into its rdfs:label.")
(comment closestProcedureOfTypePerformedPriorTo "(#$closestProcedureOfTypePerformedPriorTo EVENT1 TYPE EVENT2) means that EVENT1 is a procedure that is an instance of TYPE, and it started before EVENT2 started, and EEVNT1 is the most recent event of that type performed on the focal patient.")
(comment XChromosome "A subcollection of #$SexChromosome, which, along with #$YChromosome, is one of the two kinds of chromosome that determine the sex (male or female) in most types of mammal.")
(disjointWith YChromosome XChromosome)
(comment injectionInto "<code>(#$injectionInto INJECTION OBJECT)</code> means that the instance <code>INJECTION</code> of #$AdministeringAnInjection is an injection into the object <code>OBJECT</code>.")
(comment stuffInjected "<code>(#$stuffInjected INJECTION STUFF)</code> means that the instance <code>INJECTION</code> of #$AdministeringAnInjection is an injection of the tangible <code>STUFF</code>.  Note that #$stuffInjected is transitive via #$physicalParts in the arg2; if <code>(#$physicalParts STUFF PART)</code>, then <code>(#$stuffInjected INJECTION PART)</code> also holds.")
(comment CytosolicReleaseOfAChemicalSubstance "A subcollection of #$DispersionOfStuff, instances are the release of chemicals inside the #$Cytosol of an instance of #$Cell.")
(comment ChromosomeTypeOfOrganismTypeFn "(#$ChromosomeTypeOfOrganismTypeFn ORG-TYPE) denotes the class of #$Chromosomes which are found in organisms of type ORG-TYPE.")
(comment chromosomeTypeOfOrganismType "(#$chromosomeTypeOfOrganismType CHROME-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that CHROME-TYPE is the type of chromosome found in the type of organism ORG-TYPE.")
(comment ChromosomeTypeByOrganismType "A specializaton of #$SecondOrderCollection that forms a partition on the collection of chromosomes (see #$Chromosome).  Instances are collections of chromosomes whose instances are anatomical parts of certain kinds of organism.")
(comment CellTypeByOrganismType "A specializaton of #$SecondOrderCollection that forms a partition on the collection of cells (see #$Cell).  Instances are collections of cell whose instances are anatomical parts of certain kinds of organism.")
(comment cellTypeOfOrganismType "(#$cellTypeOfOrganismType CELL-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that CELL-TYPE is the type of cell found in the type of organism ORG-TYPE.")
(comment CellTypeOfOrganismTypeFn "(#$CellTypeOfOrganismTypeFn ORG-TYPE) denotes the class of #$Cells which are found in organisms of type ORG-TYPE.")
(disjointWith EukaryoticChromosome ProkaryoticChromosome)
(comment EukaryoticChromosome "A specialization of #$Chromosome.  Each instance of #$EukaryoticChromosome is a microscopic body formed by the incorporation of chromatins in the cell nucleus during mitosis or meiosis.")
(comment ProkaryoticChromosome "A specialization of #$Chromosome and #$ProkaryoticDNAMolecule.  Each instance of #$ProkaryoticChromosome consists of a single structured strand of DNA.")
(comment ProkaryoticChromosome-Circular "A specialization of #$ProkaryoticChromosome.  Each instance of #$ProkaryoticChromosome-Circular is a circular strand of prokaryotic DNA that functions as a chromosome in a #$ProkaryoticCell.")
(comment ProkaryoticChromosome-Linear "A specialization of #$ProkaryoticChromosome.  Each instance of #$ProkaryoticChromosome-Linear is a linear strand of prokaryotic DNA that functions as a chromosome in a #$ProkaryoticCell.")
(disjointWith ProkaryoticChromosome-Linear ProkaryoticChromosome-Circular)
(comment Chromosome "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$Chromosome is a microscopic structure of DNA (and, in the case of #$EukaryoticChromosomes, protein) found in a cell. Chromosomes carry the #$Gene-HereditaryUnits that convey hereditary characteristics, and are constant in number for each species. Each instance of #$Chromosome is either a #$ProkaryoticChromosome or a #$EukaryoticChromosome.")
(comment AtLeastApproximatelyCircularRegion "A specialization of both #$PlaneFigure and #$RoundObject (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all two-dimensional space regions the boundaries of which are at least approximately circular (see #$AtLeastApproximatelyACircle).")
(comment AtLeastApproximatelyACircle "A specialization of #$RoundObject (q.v.).  This is the collection of all one-dimensional space regions that are at least approximately circular (cf. #$AtLeastApproximatelyCircularRegion).")
(comment WatchingAMovieAtTheCinema "Watching a movie or film at the cinema.")
(comment WatchingTelevision "A specialization of #$WatchingSomething and #$AccessingAnIBT.  Each instance of #$WatchingTelevision is an event in which a person watches (and typically listens to) a television broadcast.")
(comment LookingAtArtObject "A specialization of #$WatchingSomething and  #$AccessingAnIBT.  Each instance of #$LookingAtArtObject is an event in which a person looks at an art object to appreciate its aesthetic qualities.  This is the typical focal activity in visits to art museums where paintings, statues, etc. are on display.")
(comment WatchingAFilmOrMovie "Watching a movie or film.")
(comment payorSelfForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorSelfForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place is the patient treated.")
(comment payorCommercialInsuranceForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorCommercialInsuranceForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that commercial health insurance is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorGovIHSForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovIHSForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that IHS is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorGovMedicaidForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovMedicaidForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that Medicaid is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorGovMedicareForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovMedicareForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that Medicare is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorGovMilForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovMilForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that U.S. military insurance is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorGovStateForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovStateForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that state health insurance is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment payorNonUSForHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorNonUSForHospitalVisit INDEX #$True) means that non-U.S. (i.e., foreign) insurance is a payor for the hospital visit during which INDEX takes place.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasRamusStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasRamusStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that a the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the ramus artery prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasLeftMainStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasLeftMainStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the left main coronary artery prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasCIRCStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasCIRCStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that a the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the circumflex, obtuse marginals, and, depending on dominance, the left posterolateral and left posterior descending artery branches of >=2.0 mm in diameter prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasProxLADStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasProxLADStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the proximal left anterior descending artery prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasRCAStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasRCAStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the right coronary artery prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasMidDistalLADStenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasMidDistalLADStenosis INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in the mid/distal left anterior descending (LAD), including all diagonal coronary artery branches that are >=2.0 mm in diameter prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasObstructionInMidDistalLADGrafts "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasObstructionInMidDistalLADGrafts INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in a graft supplying the mid/distal LAD coronary artery territory prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasObstructionInCIRCGrafts "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasObstructionInCIRCGrafts INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in a graft in the circumflex artery territory prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasObstructionInProxLADGrafts "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasObstructionInMidDistalLADGrafts INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in a graft supplying the proximal LAD coronary artery territory prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasObstructionInRCAGrafts "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasObstructionInMidDistalLADGrafts INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in a graft supplying the RCA territory prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment cathOrPCIHasObstructionInRamusGrafts "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathOrPCIHasObstructionInMidDistalLADGrafts INDEX STEN-VALUE) means that the best estimate of the most severe percent stenosis in a graft supplying the Ramus territory prior to INDEX is STEN-VALUE.")
(comment pciHasIndication "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasIndication PCI INDICATION-TYPE) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the indication was INDICATION-TYPE.")
(comment pciHasEDPresentDatetime "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasEDPresentDatetime PCI DATETIME) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the Emergency Department present datetime was DATETIME.")
(comment pciHasDiabetesTreatmentModality "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasDiabetesTreatmentModality PCI THERAPY-TYPE) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the most aggressive therapy for diabetes that the patient presented with at arrival for the hospital visit subsuming the pCI was THERAPY-TYPE.")
(comment pciHasFirstDeviceActivationDatetime "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasFirstDeviceActivationDatetime PCI DATETIME) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the first device activation datetime was DATETIME.")
(comment pciHasPreviousPCIDatetime "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPreviousPCIDatetime PCI DATETIME) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the datetime of the most recent prior PCI was DATETIME.")
(comment pciHasFamilyHistoryOfCAD "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasFamilyHistoryOfCAD INDEX #$True) means that prior to INDEX there is a documented family history of premature CAD for the patient treated in INDEX.")
(comment hasPreProcTroponinT-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcTroponinT-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure Troponin T value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPreProcCreatinine-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcCreatinine-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure Creatinine value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPreProcCKMB-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcCKMB-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure CK-MB value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPreProcTroponinI-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcTroponinI-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure Troponin I value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPreProcHemoglobin-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcHemoglobin-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure Hemoglobin value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPostProcTroponinI-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostProcTroponinI-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the post-procedure Troponin I value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPostProcTroponinT-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcTroponinT-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the pre-procedure Troponin T value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPostProcHemoglobin-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreProcHemoglobin-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the post-procedure Hemoglobin value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) is REAL.")
(comment hasPostProcCKMBNM-CathPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostProcCKMBNM-CathPCI PCI REAL) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the post-procedure CK/MB value (per the CathPCIv4 definition) used to determin if CK/MB is normal is REAL.")
(comment pciHasPriorCardiacArrestWithin24Hours "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorCardiacArrestWithin24Hours INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior cardiac arrest within 24 hours.")
(comment pciHasPriorCardiogenicShockWithin24Hours "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorCardiacArrestWithin24Hours INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior cardiogenic shock within 24 hours.")
(comment pciHasPriorIntravenousThrombolysisWithin1Week "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorCardiacArrestWithin24Hours INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior intravenous thrombolysis shock within 1 week.")
(comment pciHasMostRecentPriorThrombolyticsDatetime "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasMostRecentPriorThrombolyticsDatetime PCI DATETIME) means that for the #$InterventionalCatheterization PCI, the most recent datetime of thrombolytics (within 1 week) prior to PCI was DATETIME.")
(comment pciHasStressTestWithSPECTMPI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorStressTestWithCMR INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior stress test with SPECT MPI (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment SubLFloat "The collection of all non-integer number-denoting expressions in the CycL language that are _not_ CycL constants or NATs, but are terms of SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system.  #$SubLFloats  are numeric strings of the Arabic decimal system that include the decimal point and/or scientific notation.")
(comment pciHasStressEcho-IschemiaRisk "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorStressTestWithCMR-IschemiaRisk INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior stress echo showing ischemia risk of RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment pciHasCardiacStress-IschemiaRisk "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasPriorStressTestWithCMR-IschemiaRisk INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is a PCI with a prior cardiac stress showing ischemia risk of RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment FloatifyScalarFn "A macro-function that takes a real number or a scalar quantity and converts #$SubLIntegers in its numeric component to #$SubLFloats. For instance, (#$FloatifyScalarFn 2) evaluates to 2.0, as does (#$FloatifyScalarFn 2.0), and (#$FloatifyScalarFn (#$Inch 1)) evaluates to (#$Inch 1.0).")
(comment healthInsuranceClaimNumberForPCI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$payorGovIHSForHospitalVisit INDEX STRING) means that STRING is the HIC for the percutaneous coronary intervention INDEX.")
(comment stageName "(#$stageName PERS NAME) relates a person to the name that person uses for public performances.  Stage names are relatively common for musicians and actors, but are also used by a variety of other performers, such as magicians.")
(comment hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is an event  with a prior cardiac computed tomography (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography-CalciumScore "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography-CalciumScore INDEX VAL) means that INDEX is an event with a prior cardiac computed tomography (per the CathPCIv4 definition) with a calcium score of VAL.")
(comment hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography-QualitativeResult "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCardiacComputedTomography-QualitativeResult INDEX QR) means that INDEX is an event with a prior cardiac computed tomography (per the CathPCIv4 definition) with a qualitative result of QR.")
(comment hasPriorCardiacStressTest "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCardiacStressTest INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress test (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorCardiacStressTest-QualitativeResult "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCardiacStressTest-QualitativeResult INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior cardiac stress test showing qualitative result RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressEcho "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressEcho INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress echo (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressEcho-QualitativeResult "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressEcho-QualitativeResult INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress echo showing qualitative result RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressTestWithCMR "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressTestWithCMR INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is a #$CathLabVisit with a prior stress test with CMR (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressTestWithCMR-IschemiaRisk "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressTestWithCMR-IschemiaRisk INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress test with CMR showing ischemia risk of RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressTestWithCMR-QualitativeResult "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressTestWithCMR-QualitativeResult INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress test with CMR showing qualitative result RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressTestWithSPECTMPI-IschemiaRisk "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressTestWithSPECTMPI-IschemiaRisk INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress test with SPECT MPI showing ischemia risk of RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPriorStressTestWithSPECTMPI-QualitativeResult "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorStressTestWithSPECTMPI-QualitativeResult INDEX RESULT) means that INDEX is an event with a prior stress test with SPECT MPI showing qualitative result RESULT (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasIABPTimingType "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasIABPTimingType INDEX TIMING) means that INDEX is an event with an IABP timing type of TIMING.")
(comment hasCardiacAssistDeviceTimingType "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasCardiacAssistDeviceTimingType INDEX TIMING) means that INDEX is an event with cardiac assist device timing type of TIMING.")
(comment pciDelayReason "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciDelayReason INDEX REASON) means that INDEX is a PCI with the delay reason REASON.")
(comment pciHasHospitalAdmitCardiacPresentation "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasHospitalAdmitCardiacPresentation INDEX PRESENTATION) means that INDEX is a PCI with the hospital admit cardiac presentation PRESENTATION.")
(comment lesionHasPercutaneousProcedureSite "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasPercutaneousProcedureSite LESION SEGMENT) means that LESION is a #$CoronaryArteryLesion in SEGMENT.")
(comment lesionHasFFRRatio "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasFFRRatio LESION VAL) means that LESION is a coromanry artery lesion witha qualifying FFR performed (per the CathPCIv4 definition) with result VAL.")
(comment lesionLocationInGraft "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionLocationInGraft LESION LOC) means that LESION is a #$CoronaryArteryLesion in LOC within a coronary artery graft.")
(comment pciHasOperatorWithNPI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasOperatorWithNPI  INDEX STRING) means that STRING is the NPI for the operator that performed INDEX.")
(comment pciHasAdmitSource "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasAdmitSource INDEX SOURCE) means that INDEX is a PCI with the admit source.")
(comment pciHasCardiomyopathyIndication "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$pciHasCardiomyopathyIndication PCI #$True) means that PCI is a percutaneous coronary intervention with a cardiomyopathy indication (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment lesionHasFFR "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasFFR LESION #$True) means that LESION is a coronary artery lesion with a qualifying FFR performed (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasIABPUsed "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasIABPUsed INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is an event in which an IABP was used.")
(comment hasPostTransfusion "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostTransfusion EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has a post-procedure transfusion.")
(comment hasPostCardiogenicShock "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostCardiogenicShock EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has a post-procedure cardiogenic shock.")
(comment hasPostCVA "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostCVA EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has a post-procedure CVA.")
(comment hasPostGIBleed "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostGIBleed EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure GI bleeding.")
(comment hasPostTamponade "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostTamponade EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure tamponade.")
(comment hasPostOtherBleed "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostOtherBleed EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has other post-procedure bleeding (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPostOtherVascularComplications "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostOtherVascularComplications EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has other post-procedure vascular complications (per the CathPCIv4 definition).")
(comment hasPostMI "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostMI EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure myocardial infarction.")
(comment hasPostHematoma "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostHematoma EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure hematoma.")
(comment hasPostHeartFailure "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostHeartFailure EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure heart failure.")
(comment hasPostRetroperitonealBleeding "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostRetroperitonealBleeding EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure retroperitoneal bleeding.")
(comment hasPostBleeding "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostBleeding EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure bleeding.")
(comment hasPostGUBleeding "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostGUBleeding EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure GU bleeding.")
(comment hasPostHemorrhagicStroke "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostHemorrhagicStroke EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure stroke due to bleeding.")
(comment hasPostBleedingAtAccessSite "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostBleedingAtAccessSite EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure bleeding at the access site.")
(comment hasPostNewRequirementForDialysis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPostNewRequirementForDialysis EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has post-procedure new requirement for dialysis.")
(comment hasPostHematoma-Size "hasPostHematoma-SizehasPostNewRequirementForDialysis EVENT SIZE) means that EVENT has post-procedure hematoma of diameter SIZE.")
(comment hasPriorCalciumScoreAvailable "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorCalciumScoreAvailable INDEX True) means that INDEX is an event with a prior calcium score available.")
(comment hasPrecathCardiogenicShock "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPrecathCardiogenicShock EVENT #$True) means that EVENT has pre-procedure cardiogenic shock.")
(comment hasEvalIndicationForCath "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasEvalIndicationForCath INDEX True) means that INDEX was indicated as a pre-operative evaluation.")
(comment patientTreatedHasHispanicEthnicity "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$patientTreatedHasHispanicEthnicity INDEX True) means that INDEX is an event in which the patient treated is of hispanic ethnicity.")
(comment birthdateOfPatientTreated "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$birthdateOfPatientTreated EVENT DATE) means that the birthdate of the patient treated in EVENT is DATE.")
(comment sexOfPatientTreated "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$sexOfPatientTreated EVENT SEX-TYPE) means that the sex of the patient treated in EVENT is SEX-TYPE.")
(comment lesionPreviouslyTreated "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionPreviouslyTreated LESION #$True) means that LESION has been previously treated.")
(comment lesionHasThrombus "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasThrombus LESION #$True) means that LESION has a thrombus, and (#$lesionHasThrombus LESION #$False) means that LESION does not have a thrombus.")
(comment lesionHasInStentThrombosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasInStentThrombosis LESION #$True) means that LESION has in-stent thrombosis, and (#$lesionHasInStentThrombosis LESION #$False) means that LESION does not have in-stent thrombosis.")
(comment lesionHasInStentRestenosis "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasInStentRestenosis LESION TYPE) means that LESION has in-stent restenosis of TYPE.")
(comment lesionHasIVUS "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasIVUS LESION #$True) means that LESION has had an IVUS.")
(comment lesionHasChronicTotalOcclusion "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasInStentRestenosis LESION #$True) means that LESION has chronic total occlusion.")
(comment lesionHasGuidewireCrossing "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasGuidewireCrossing LESION #$True) means that LESION has had a guidewire crossing.")
(comment lesionHasPreviousStent "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$lesionHasPreviousStent LESION #$True) means that LESION has had a previous stent.")
(comment hasPriorHeartFailureWithinTwoWeeks "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPriorHeartFailureWithinTwoWeeks EVENT #$True) means that the patient involved in EVENT had prior heart failure within two weeks.")
(comment eventHasDiagnosticCathDuringSameHospitalVisit "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$eventHasDiagnosticCathDuringSameHospitalVisit EVENT #$True) means that the patient involved in EVENT had diagnostic cath during the smae hospital visit in which EVENT occurs.")
(comment cathPCISmokerStatus "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$cathPCISmokerStatus INDEX COL) means that COL is the smoker status for INDEX, per the CathPCIv4 definition.")
(comment hasPreviousValveProcedure "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreviousValveProcedure INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is performed on a patient who had a previous valve procedure.")
(comment hasPreviousCABG "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$hasPreviousCABG INDEX #$True) means that INDEX is performed on a patient who had a previous CABG.")
(comment mostRecentPriorCMHeightOfPatient "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$mostRecentPriorCMHeightOfPatient EVENT N) means that N is the most recent prior height (in centimeters) of the patient treated in EVENT.")
(comment mostRecentPriorKGWeightOfPatient "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$mostRecentPriorKGWeightOfPatient EVENT N) means that N is the most recent prior weight (in kilograms) of the patient treated in EVENT.")
(comment deviceUsedOnLesionID "A #$CCFHelperPredicate.  (#$deviceUsedOnLesionID DEV ID) means that ID is the ID of the coronary artery lesion on which DEVICE is used.")
(comment assertiveWFFRule "(#$assertiveWFFRule <code>RULE</code>) means that <code>RULE</code> is a #$CycLRuleAssertion to be used by the #$CycWellFormednessChecker in 'assertive' mode.  'Assertive' mode is the mode in which assertions are allowed into the KB as long as they are not provably disjoint with existing knowledge, and then forward inference (constrained to rules of which #$assertiveWFFRule holds) may conclude additional facts based on the newly asserted knowledge.")
(disjointWith HeartAttack Endocarditis-Generic)
(comment GroupOfRelativelyHomogenousObjects "The collection of instances of  
  (#$GroupFn #$PartiallyTangible) whose members are largely homogenous (are identical or close to identical in terms of their measurable physical properties).")
(comment suppressOpenSubquery "<code>(#$suppressOpenSubquery QUERY)</code> means that when running the instance <code>QUERY</code> of #$MultipleChoiceQuerySpecification, the open subquery (the query specified via #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification) should not be run.  This is the case when the test-taking strategy of \"calculate the answer and compare with the multiple choice options\" is known to be un- or counter-productive.")
(comment SpecifiedChemicalInteractionType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection whose instances are sub-collections of #$ChemicalInteraction.  Each instance is a collection of interactions that have enough properties in common that one can make general claims about the constraints on their role players, e.g., that no #$catalyst in any interaction of such a type can be among the #$chemicalProducts for an instance of that type.")
(comment relationExistsNoMember "(#$relationExistsNoMember PRED COLL GROUP) means that for no MEMBER such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEMBER) does there exist any instance INS of collection COLL such that (PRED INS MEMBER).")
(comment amountPresentAt "<code>(#$amountPresentAt PLACE TYPE QUANTITY)</code> means that <code>QUANTITY</code> is the amount of <code>TYPE</code> that is at <code>PLACE</code>.  For example, (#$amountPresentAt #$EiffelTower #$Person 2000) means that 2000 people are at the Eiffel Tower.  Similarly, (#$amountPresentAt #$CityOfAustinTX #$FiberOpticCable (#$Meter 1000000)) means there are one million meters of fiber optic cable in Austin, TX.")
(comment NAICSCode "The collection of all two-to-six-digit codes for industry types in the #$NorthAmericanIndustryClassificationSystem.")
(comment asMuchAs "(#$asMuchAs PROP STUFF-TYPE SCALAR-QUANT) means the level of property PROP that all STUFF-TYPE has is SCALAR-QUANT.")
(comment XMLValueStringFn "(#$XMLValueStringFn URL FIELD-NAME STALENESS-CUTOFF) evaluates to the XML value for FIELD-NAME at URL. The value is always returned as a plain string. If there is a cached value the system knows about that is less than STALENESS-CUTOFF old, it will be returned.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentConditions "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentConditions STATION-ID FIELD-NAME VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) value for FIELD-NAME at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentRelativeHumidity "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentRelativeHumidity STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) relative humidity value at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationFor "(#$nwsWeatherStationFor THING STATION-ID) means that STATION-ID is the ID of a #$NationalWeatherService station whose reported values are a good approximation for those of THING. Typically, this means that the station in question is located in or near THING.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentTemperature "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentRelativeHumidity STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) relative humidity value at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentWeather "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentWeather STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) weather at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment CompassDirectionFn "(#$CompassDirectionFn ANGULAR-DISTANCE) denotes the #$GeographicalDirection corresponding to ANGULAR-DISTANCE, where #$North-Directly is (#$CompassDirectionFn (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 0)) #$East-Directly is (#$CompassDirectionFn (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 90)), etc.")
(comment ambientWindDirection-NWS "(#$ambientWindDirection-NWS X DIR) means that in the vicinity of X the wind is blowing from the direction DIR.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindDirection "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindDirection STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) wind direction at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindSpeed "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindSpeed STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) wind speed at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment ambientWindSpeed-NWS "(#$ambientWindSpeed-NWS X SPEED) means that in the vicinity of X the wind is blowing at approximately SPEED.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentPressure "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentPressure STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) atmospheric pressure at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment ambientPressure-NWS "(#$ambientPressure-NWS X VALUE) means that in the vicinity of X the atmospheric pressure is approximately VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentHeatIndex "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentHeatIndex STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) heat index at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindChill "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentWindChill STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) wind chill at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentDewPoint "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentDewPoint STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) dew point at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationCurrentVisibility "(#$nwsWeatherStationCurrentVisibility STATION-ID VALUE) means that the current (or most recently reported) visibility at the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID is VALUE.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationObservationTime "(#$nwsWeatherStationObservationTime STATION-ID TIME) means that the current (or most recently reported) observations for the #$NationalWeatherService station whose ID is STATION-ID were made at TIME.")
(comment nwsWeatherStationObservationTimeRelevant "(#$nwsWeatherStationObservationTimeRelevant ID) means that data available for the #$NationalWeatherService weather station whose ID is ID is relevant to the current temporal context.")
(disjointWith RoughEndoplasmicReticulum SmoothEndoplasmicReticulum)
(comment SmoothEndoplasmicReticulum "A collection.  Instances are ER whose cytoplasmic surface lacks ribosomes.")
(comment RoughEndoplasmicReticulum "A collection.  Instances are ER whose cytoplasmic surface is studded with ribosomes.")
(comment EndomembraneSystem "A collection of systems of cell parts. Each instance of #$EndomembraneSystem consists of membranes suspended in the cytoplasm of a #$EukaryoticCell. The membrances in an endomemrane system divide a cell into #$Organelles.  However, some organelles are not part of endomembrane systems (such as #$Mitochondrion or #$Chloroplast organelles).")
(comment facilityTypeInstancesHostDatabasesOfType "(#$facilityTypeInstancesHostDatabasesOfType FACILITY-TYPE DB-TYPE) means that every instance of FACILITY-TYPE supports one or more information storage components which in turn support one or more instances of #$Database-AbstractContent that are also instances of DB-TYPE (where DB-TYPE is itself a specialization of #$Database-AbstractContent.")
(disjointWith Flagellum Cilium)
(comment Flagellum-Prokaryotic "The collection of flagella that are
#$physicalParts of bacteria. Flagella are whip-like tails that enable the #$Bacterium that have them to move. #$Flagellum-Prokaryotic are one-tenth the width of #$Flagellum-Eucaryotic and also differ in that they are not covered by the #$CellMembrane like the flagellum of #$EukaryoticCells.")
(disjointWith Flagellum-Eukaryotic Flagellum-Prokaryotic)
(comment Flagellum "The collection of flagella that are
#$physicalParts of cells. Flagella are whip-like tails that enable the cells that have them to move.")
(comment FlagellateLocomotion "A specialization of #$LocomotionProcess.   Each instance of #$FlagellateLocomotion is an event in which something propells itself with a flagellum.")
(comment Flagellum-Eukaryotic "The collection of flagella that are #$physicalParts of #$EukaryoticCells. Flagella function to move the cell. Note that not all #$EukaryoticCells move by a #$Flagellum-Eukaryotic.")
(comment Cell-Motile "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$Cell-MotileByCilium is a cell that can move by using locomotor appendages (see #$Cilium and #$Flagellum).")
(comment Cell-MotileByCilium "A specialization of #$Cell-Motile.  Each instance of #$Cell-MotileByCilium is a cell that can move by using cilia (see #$Cilium).")
(comment Cell-MotileByFlagellum "A specialization of #$Cell-Motile.  Each instance of #$Cell-MotileByFlagellum is a cell that can move by using a #$Flagellum.")
(comment LocomotorAppendage-Cell "The collection of appendages that cells can use to move about.")
(comment termPhrases-Lexical "(#$termPhrases-Lexical TERM CONSTRAINT STRING) means that STRING is a word or phrase explicitly in Cyc's lexicon or an accessible external lexicon (i.e. not requiring parsing or generation) that denotes TERM and that meets CONSTRAINT. Cf. #$termPhrases.")
(comment assertiveWFFEnabled "(#$assertiveWFFEnabled) is true iff #$CycWellFormednessChecker is in assertive wff mode, which means that WFF will actively try to make assertions to make an incoming assertion true.")
(comment GlycoproteinMolecule "This is the collection of chemical objects consisting of proteins covalently bonded to carbohydrates.")
(comment GlycoproteinStuff "An organic material consisting of glycoprotein molecules.")
(comment Collagen "A protein substance, sometimes put into women's face creams.  Collagen accounts for nearly one third of the total protein in the bodies of mammals.")
(comment GlycolipidStuff "An organic material consisting of glycolipid molecules.")
(comment GlycolipidMolecule "This is the collection of chemical objects consisting of lipids covalently bonded to carbohydrates.")
(comment PlantTissue "The collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that comes from a plant.  Each instance of #$PlantTissue consists of plant cells.")
(comment Elastin "A protein substance that is an abundant constituent of the extracellular matrix (see #$ExtracellularMatrix and #$ConnectiveTissue).")
(comment AnimalTissue "The collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that comes from an animal.  Each instance of #$AnimalTissue consists of cells embedded in #$ExtracellularMatrix.")
(comment Fibronectin "A protein substance that is an abundant constituent of the extracellular matrix (see #$ExtracellularMatrix and #$ConnectiveTissue).  Fibronectin molecules connect the ECM to cell membranes.")
(comment Laminin "A specialization of #$ProteinStuff.  Laminins are a kind of protein substance that is an abundant constituent of the #$ExtracellularMatrix.")
(comment ExtracellularMatrix "An instance of #$OrganismPartType and a specialization of #$AnimalBLO.  Each instance of #$ExtracellularMatrix is the extracellular portion of an animal's constituent tissue.")
(comment ExtracellularFluid "A specialization of #$BodilyFluid.  Each instance of #$ExtracellularFluid is a quantity of the fluid that exists in the bodies (but outside the cells) of multi-cellular animals.")
(comment InterstitialFluid "A specialization of #$ExtracellularFluid.  Each instance of #$InterstitialFluid is a quantity of the fluid that is found in the interstitial spaces of multi-cellular animals.")
(comment TranscellularFluid "A specialization of #$ExtracellularFluid.  Each instance of #$InterstitialFluid is a quantity of the fluid that is found in the epithelial lined space of multi-cellular animals.")
(comment KrebsCycle "An instance of #$CyclicalProcessType and a specialization of #$BiologicalProductionEvent and #$BiologicalDestructionEvent.  Each instance of #$KrebsCycle consists of a sequence of chemical reactions that take place in the #$MitochondrialMatrix.")
(comment Glycolysis "A process that occurs in the cytosol, during which glucose molecules are destoyed and pyruvate molecules are created.")
(comment PyruvicAcid "The collection of samples of pyruvic acid; CH3COCOOH.")
(comment OrganicAcid "The collection of organic substances that are acidic.")
(comment PyruvateIon "The collection of pyruvate ions; CH3COCOO (-).")
(comment CarboxylicAcid "A specialization of #$OrganicAcid.  Carboxylic acids are organic acids containing the carboxyl group (-COOH).")
(comment DichloroaceticAcid "The collection of samples of dichloroacetic acid; CHCl2COOH.")
(comment TrichloroaceticAcid "The collection of samples of trichloroacetic acid; CCl3CO2H.")
(comment TrifluoroaceticAcid "The collection of samples of trifluoroacetic acid; CF3CO2H.")
(comment Thioester "A collection of substances created via reaction between a #$Thiol and a #$CarboxylicAcid.")
(comment Thiol "The collection of organic substances that contain the group -SH (the thiol group).")
(disjointWith CarboxylicAcid UricAcid)
(comment PortableCassetteRecorder "A subcollection of #$PersonalAudioPlayer. Instances of #$PortableCassetteRecorder are usually used to record human speech, for dictating letters for example.")
(comment UricAcid "The collection of samples of uric acid; C5H4N4O3.")
(comment strongestAssertedSentence "(#$strongestAssertedSentence <code>SENTENCE</code>) means that SENTENCE is asserted in the Cyc KB, and that no strictly 'stronger version' of SENTENCE is asserted in the Cyc KB.  For an explanation of what constitutes a 'stronger version', see #$assertedMoreSpecifically.  #$strongestAssertedSentence is basically a conjunction of #$assertedSentence and #$not #$assertedMoreSpecifically.")
(comment SarcoplasmicReticulum "A specialization of #$SmoothEndoplasmicReticulum.  Each instance of #$SarcoplasmicReticulum is SER found in muscle tissue (i.e., within #$Myocytes).")
(comment GlycoconjugateStuff "A specialization of #$OrganicMaterial.  Each instance of #$GlycoconjugateStuff is organic material consisting of glycoconjugate chemical objects (objects which are carbohydrates covalently bonded to other carbohydrates covalently linked with other chemical objects such as lipids or proteins).")
(comment GlycoconjugateMolecule "This is the collection of chemical objects consisting of carbohydrates covalently bonded to other chemical objects such as lipids or proteins.")
(comment GlycopeptideMolecule "This is the collection of chemical objects consisting of peptides covalently bonded to carbohydrates.")
(comment GlycopeptideStuff "An organic material consisting of glycopeptide molecules.")
(comment Actin "A type of globular protein that is the primary constituent of #$Microfilaments.")
(comment Mucin "A type of glycoprotein notable for being a component of the gel-like substances secreted by organisms.")
(comment IntegrinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlycoproteinMolecule and #$ReceptorMolecule.  Integrins are receptor molecules and adhesion molecules.")
(comment CellularAdhesionMolecule "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule.  Cellular adhesion molecules attach cells to other cells or to the #$ExtracellularMatrix.")
(comment CellularAdhesion "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent.  Each instance of cell adhesion is an event in which a cell adheres to a surface (such as the surface of another cell) or to the #$ExtracellularMatrix.")
(comment SelectinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlycoproteinMolecule and #$ReceptorMolecule.  Integrins are receptor molecules and adhesion molecules.")
(comment IntegralMembraneProtein "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule.  Integral membrane proteins are proteins that are permanently attached to membranes.")
(comment TransmembraneProtein "A subcollection of #$IntegralMembraneProtein.  Integral transmembrane proteins are proteins that are permanently attached to membranes, and span the entire membrane to which they are attached.")
(disjointWith TransmembraneProtein IntegralMonotopicProtein)
(comment provableViaDefns "(#$provableViaDefns <code>SENTENCE</code>) means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is an atomic sentence with a predicate of #$isa or #$quotedIsa that is provable using #$defnIff and #$defnSufficient assertions, and the relationships between them (via #$genls).  Notably, <code>SENTENCE</code> is provable <i>without</i> using any asserted #$isa or #$quotedIsa assertions.")
(comment ICUseCaseOntology "The #$subWorks of #$MRSharedOntology that comprises the ontology (see #$Ontology) used by the Intelligence Community usecase developed for the #$MachineReadingProject.")
(comment operationalOutcomeTypes "Where SYSTEM is an #$AgentAndInstrumentSystem, (#$operationalOutcomeTypes SYSTEM OUTCOME-TYPE) means that OUTCOME-TYPE is a kind of #$Situation that the implementation of SYSTEM is intended to maintain throughout the time it is going on.")
(comment seedsCompeteInPlayoffsOfType "Where PLAYOFF-TYPE is a specialization of #$PlayoffSeries, (#$seedsCompeteInPlayoffsOfType PLAYOFF-TYPE N M)  means that, in the opening round of a given instance of PLAYOFF-TYPE, the Nth and Mth seeded #$SportsTeams (see #$teamSeed) are pitted against each other in an opening game, as part of the regular procedure for tournaments of type PLAYOFF-TYPE")
(comment extractedRelnSourceText "<code>(#$extractedRelnSourceText EXTRACTION TEXT)</code> identifies the string <code>TEXT</code> as the source of the instance <code>EXTRACTION</code> of #$RelationExtraction.")
(comment TypicalHumanFemaleActivityType-AtLeastOnce "The collection of specializations of #$HumanActivity such that female persons typically are involved in (#$actors) at least one instance of the activity type in their lifetime.")
(comment BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary "A specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent.  Each specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary is a type of event each instance of which is done without conscious volition.  Consequently, in each instance of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary, the `doer' of the event is a non-deliberate actor in that event (see the predicate #$nonDeliberateActors).  Specializations of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary include #$InvoluntaryBodyMovement and #$ExperiencingHunger.")
(comment MenstrualCycle "An instance of #$CyclicalProcessType and a specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary.  Each instance of #$MenstrualCycle consists of a sequence of events undergone by a fertile female human or ape and which involves ovulation and menstruation.")
(comment FollicularPhaseOfMenstrualCycle "A specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary.  Each instance of #$FollicularPhaseOfMenstrualCycle is an early phase in some instance of #$MenstrualCycle.  The follicular phase is also known as the proliferative phase.")
(comment LutealPhaseOfMenstrualCycle "A specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary. Each instance of #$LutealPhaseOfMenstrualCycle is an early phase in some instance of #$MenstrualCycle. The luteal phase is also known as the secretory phase.")
(comment Ovulation-Menstrual "A specialization of #$Ovulating.  Each instance of #$Ovulation-Menstrual is an event in which  an ovum is discharged by an ovary during a menstrual cycle (see #$MenstrualCycle).")
(comment FertileFn "#$FemaleFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. <code>(#$FertileFn TYPE)</code> returns the subcollection of <code>TYPE</code> (itself a subcollection of #$Animal) that includes all and only the fertile instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$FertileFn #$FemaleHuman) and denotes the collection of all fertile human females.")
(comment fertileTypeOfType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$FertileFn.  <code>(#$fertileTypeOfType X (#$FertileFn X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment Libertarianism "An instance of #$PoliticalBeliefSystem.  Agents having this ideology advocate laissez faire economics and an extremely limited federal government whose primary functions are national defense, protection from violent crime, and the enforcement of contracts.")
(disjointWith MountainRange HumanScaleObject)
(disjointWith Ocean HumanScaleObject)
(disjointWith Mountain HumanScaleObject)
(comment (TransportViaFn AirTransportationDevice) "A collection of events.  An instance of (#$TransportViaFn #$AirTransportationDevice) is a transportation event in which a #$vehicle designed to travel through the atmosphere is used.  Examples include instances of the would-be collections hang gliding, airplane tranportation, flying the space shuttle, hot air ballon transport.  Note: This collection does not include #$Flying-FlappingWings, which is what birds do.")
(comment Ape "A specialization of #$Primate. Each instance of #$Ape is a tailless primate belonging to the family Hominidae or Hylobatidae.")
(comment naicsCodeOfCW "(#$naicsCodeOfCW CW CODE) means that CODE is the NAICS code for an industry with which CW is associated. This is a weak predicate, and may only be inferentially productive for specific kinds of CW")
(comment Malting "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ConvertingSomething. In each #$Malting, someone converts grain into malt.")
(comment Milling "A specialization of #$Grinding.  Each instance of #$Milling is an event in which grain is ground.")
(comment Lautering "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgentActivity.  Each instance of #$Lautering is an event in which the wort is separated from the grains during brewing.")
(comment elicitableRolesForEventType "A #$MetaPredicate and a specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$rolesForEventType. #$elicitableRolesForEventType holds only of those ROLEs and EVENTTYPEs in the relation rolesForEventType for which the argument of the role might reasonably be expected to be elicited from a human being familiar with some EVENT that is an instance of EVENTTYPE.")
(comment elicitableRequiredRolesForEventType "A #$MetaPredicate and a specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$elicitableRolesForEventType and #requiredActorSlots. #$elicitableRolesForEventType holds only of those ROLEs and EVENTTYPEs in the relation rolesForEventType for which the argument of the role might reasonably be expected to be elicited from a human being familiar with some EVENT that is an instance of EVENTTYPE, and for which requiredActorSlots holds between ROLE and EVENTTYPE, suggesting that the ROLE is definitional for an instance of EVENTTYPE.")
(comment Wort "A specialization of #$LiquidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$Wort is a liquid created during a #$Brewing process which will eventually be turned into #$Beer.")
(comment Mash "A specialization of #$LiquidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$Mash is a liquid created during a #$Brewing process which will eventually be turned into #$Wort and then #$Beer.")
(comment Mashing "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgentActivity. Each instance of #$Mashing is an event in which milled grain is mixed with a liquid (during some #$Brewing event) to produce some #$Mash.")
(comment NeuroLexKnowledgeBase "The collection of every #$KnowledgeBase Extracted from NeuroLex (NeuroLex.org) under the terms of its licence.")
(comment stuffBrewed "(#$stuffBrewed BREWING STUFF) mean the stuff brewed in BREWING is STUFF.  This stuff is mashed lautered, fermented, etc., and ultimately becomes #$Beer.")
(comment groupTypeCharacterisicallyLacksSitTypeParticipants "(#$groupTypeCharacterisicallyLacksSitTypeParticipants  GT ST) means that it is definitionally characteristic of GT (a specialization of #$Group) that it has no members participating in a situation of type ST.")
(comment HumanSomaticCell "A specialization of #$SomaticCell and #$HumanCell. Each instance of #$HumanSomaticCell is a somatic cell of a homo sapiens.")
(comment sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation "(#$sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT SIT) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during SUB-SIT, (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values during SUB-SIT relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT.
<p>
For example, (#$sustainsPeakDuringSubSituation #$productionRateOfRegion #$eventOccursAt  #$PetroleumProduct  #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran #$IranHostageCrisis) means that, since #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran occurs at #$Iran, there is a value QUANT such that (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct QUANT)is first true during the #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran and during every other unsubsumed sub-event of #$IranHostageCrisis (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct OTHER-QUANT) is such that OTHER-QUANT is less than or equal to QUANT.")
(comment sustainsPeakDuringSubSituationType "(#$sustainsPeakDuringSubSituationType
COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during any instance of SUB-SIT-TYPE that is a sub-situation of SIT  (an instance of SIT-TYPE), (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT prior to SUB-SIT, and has maintained those peak levels through SUB-SIT.")
(comment reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType "(#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType
COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during any instance of SUB-SIT-TYPE that is a sub-situation of SIT  (an instance of SIT-TYPE), (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values during SUB-SIT relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT.
<p>
For example, (#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituationType
 #$amountPresentAt #$objectActedOn #$Shampoo (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$Shampoo) #$WashingHair) means that, since in any instance APP of (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$Shampoo) that is a sub-event of some instance WASH of #$WashingHair the #$objectActedOn is some instance HOH #$HairOnHead, there is a value QUANT such that (#$amountPresentAt #$Shampoo QUANT) is first true immediately after some phase of APP and during every other unsubsumed sub-event of  WASH (#$amountPresentAt #$Shampoo OTHER-QUANT) is such that OTHER-QUANT is less than or equal to QUANT.")
(comment reachesPeakDuringSubSituation "(#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituation COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE THING SUB-SIT SIT) means that for the ROLE-PLAYER that plays the role ROLE during SUB-SIT, (COMP-QUANT-PRED ROLE-PLAYER THING QUANT) is such that QUANT first reaches its highest values during SUB-SIT relative to all other unsubsumed sub-situations of SIT.
<p>
For example, (#$reachesPeakDuringSubSituation #$productionRateOfRegion #$eventOccursAt  #$PetroleumProduct  #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran #$IranHostageCrisis) means that, since #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran occurs at #$Iran, there is a value QUANT such that (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct QUANT)is first true during the #$TerroristAttack-November-4-1979-Tehran-Iran and during every other unsubsumed sub-event of #$IranHostageCrisis (#$productionRateOfRegion #$Iran #$PetroleumProduct OTHER-QUANT) is such that OTHER-QUANT is less than or equal to QUANT.")
(comment Herd "A specialization of (#$GroupFn #$Animal).  Each instance of #$Herd is a social group of animals that is either wild or maintained by people typically for some purpose.  For example, wild herds of bison used to roam the Great Plains of North America, and herds (known as flocks) of geese will migrate together.  Similarly, cattle are sometimes kept in herds so they may ultimately be eaten, and sheep are sometimes kept in herds for the same reason, or so they may ultimately have their wool harvested.")
(comment CrabFishery "A type of #$Fishery.")
(comment Fishery "The collection of all fisheries. A type of #$Organization.  Fisheries are organizations devoted to raisiong or capturing aquatic animals (usually from a specific region) including fish, mollusks, crustaceans (such as lobsters and crabs (see #$CrabFishery).")
(comment Histamine "The collection of all portions of histamine. #$Histamine a relatively ubiquitous chemical substance in animal tissue, involved in many processes such as neurotransmission and the triggering of the inflammatory response.")
(comment LabileCell "The collection of all cells that spend virtually the entirety of their existence dividing.")
(comment DensityIndependentCellDivision "A specialization of #$Abnormal-Unusual, this is the collection of cell division events that violate the density dependence associated with healthy cell division events.")
(comment ScreenName "A collection of #$IDStrings. Each #$Username is a #$CharacterString that represents a distinct user of a #$Computer or the #$agreeingServiceRecipient of a #$ComputerAccount.")
(comment ScreenName "A collection of #$IDStrings. Each #$ScreenName is a #$CharacterString in some language that represents a distinct user of a computerised information service, and that serves as a public indentifier for that user amongst users of that service. It is distinct from a Username, in as much as it is a means of identifying a user, not a means of controlling access to the service. ScreenNames, like most identifiers, are not limited to being SubL strings.")
(comment twitterScreenNameOfAgent "(#$usernameForAccount USERNAME ACCOUNT) means that USERNAME is a character string in the collection #$Username that, typically along with the use of a character string in the collection #$Password-Computer, enables access to ACCOUNT on a computational system.")
(comment twitterScreenNameOfAgent "(#$twitterScreenNameOfAgent <#$ScreenName> <#$IntelligentAgent>) that that IntelligentAgent has that ScreenName on Twitter. The specificity of this predicate is brought to you by the inadequacy of the middle ontology for computer systems, services and programs, and the relationship between them, especially with regard to web-based and networked services (like, twitter)")
(comment personFoundInLocation "(#$personFoundInLocation PERSON LOCATION) means that the PERSON, an instance of #$Person, is found within the bounds of LOCATION.")
(comment JellyfishShaped "#$JellyfishShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing.  Each instance of #$JellyfishShaped is something that has the typical shape of a jellyfish.")
(comment InsectShaped "#$InsectShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$InsectShaped is something that has the typical shape of any type of insect.")
(comment OctopusShaped "#$OctopusShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$OctopusShaped is something that has the typical shape of an octopus.")
(comment SquidShaped "#$SquidShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$SquidShaped is something that has the typical shape of a squid.")
(comment BirdShaped "#$BirdShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$BirdShaped is something that has the typical shape of a bird.")
(comment ClamShaped "#$ClamShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$ClamShaped is something that has the typical shape of a clam.")
(comment FishShaped "#$FishShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$FishShaped is something that has the typical shape of a fish.")
(comment HumanoidShaped "#$HumanoidShaped is a specialization of #$AnimalShapedThing. Each instance of #$HumanoidShaped is something that has the typical shape of a humanoid.")
(comment ShapedAsFn "(#$ShapedAsFn PT) denotes the collection of objects that are shaped like typical members of the specialization of #$PartiallyTangible, PT.  For example, (#$ShapedAsFn #$Castle) denotes the collection of objects that are shaped like castles.")
(comment shapeTypeOfType "(#$shapeTypeOfType TYPE SHAPE-TYPE) means that SHAPE-TYPE is the collection of objects that are shaped like members of TYPE.")
(comment ChessPiece "A specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$ChessPiece is an object intended to be used in a game of chess as one either a king, queen, bishop, knight, rook or pawn.")
(comment WhiteChessPiece "A specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$ChessPiece is an object intended to be used in a game of chess as one either a king, queen, bishop, knight, rook or pawn.")
(comment BlackChessPiece "A specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$BlackChessPiece is an object intended to be used in a game of chess as either a king, queen, bishop, knight, rook or pawn of the \"black\" player.  These pieces are traditionally black, but need not be.  Iny any set they must simply be a different color than the \"white\" pieces (see #$WhiteChessPiece).")
(comment WhiteChessPiece "A specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$WhiteChessPiece is an object intended to be used in a game of chess as either a king, queen, bishop, knight, rook or pawn of the \"white\" player.  These pieces are traditionally white, but need not be.  In any set they must simply be a different color than the \"black\" pieces (see #$BlackChessPiece).")
(comment Aster-CellPart "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$Aster-CellPart is a cellular structure shaped like a star that forms around a centrosome during #$Mitosis.")
(comment Soma "A specialization of #$CellPart whose instances are a structure in neurons.  The soma contains the organelles of the cell, including the nucleus, and, in typical neurons, is attached to the axon.")
(comment ProjectedCellPart "The collection of instances of #$CellPart that protrude from the \"main body\" of the cell, analgous, in many ways to the way that limbs or tails protrude from the torsos of anmials or the way branches protrude from the trunk of a tree.")
(comment FractionOfTypeFn "(#$FractionOfTypeFn TANGIBLE-TYPE N) denotes the collection of tangibles which can be thought of as incomplete instances of TANGIBLE-TYPE, and which are the fraction N of a whole.  For example, (#$FractionOfTypeFn #$Bread-Slice 0.5) denotes the collection of half-slices of bread.  Typically, an instance of (#$FractionOfTypeFn TANGIBLE-TYPE N)  would not be considered an instance of TANGIBLE-TYPE unless N = 1.0, but there may be contexts in which it would make sense to do so. ")
(disjointWith G0Phase AnchorageIndependentCellGrowth)
(disjointWith G0Phase AnchorageDependentCellGrowth)
(disjointWith AnchorageIndependentCellGrowth AnchorageDependentCellGrowth)
(comment fractionTypeOfType "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for #$FractionOfTypeFn.")
(comment AnchorageIndependentCellGrowth "A kind of cell growth, characteristic of cancer cells (see #$CancerCell) in which growth happens without the cell being bound to some surface, such as the plastic wall of a petri dish or the layer of cells in the surrounding tissue.")
(comment AnchorageDependentCellGrowth "A kind of normal cell growth which requires the cell being bound to some surface, such as the plastic wall of a petri dish or the layer of cells in the surrounding tissue.")
(comment chromosomes "(#$chromosomes CELL CHROM) is a #$PhysicalPartPredicate which relates an instance of #$Cell, CELL, to one of the #$Chromosomes, CHROM, that bears the cell's genetic information.")
(comment Bishop-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$Bishop-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with two bishops.")
(comment BlackBishop-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Bishop-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackBishop-ChessPiece is a black chess piece.  The black player in a game starts with two black bishops.")
(comment WhiteBishop-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Bishop-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$WhiteBishop-ChessPiece is a white chess piece.  The white player in a game starts with two white bishops.")
(comment King-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$King-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with one king.")
(comment BlackKing-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$King-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackKing-ChessPiece is a black chess piece.  The black player in a game starts with one black king.")
(comment WhiteKing-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$King-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$WhiteKing-ChessPiece is a white chess piece.  The white player in a game starts with one white king.")
(comment Queen-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$Queen-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with one queen.")
(comment BlackQueen-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Queen-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackQueen-ChessPiece is a black chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with one black queen.")
(comment Knight-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$Knight-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with two knights.")
(comment Rook-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$Rook-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with two rooks.")
(comment BlackRook-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Rook-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackRook-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  The black player in a game starts with two black rooks.")
(comment WhiteRook-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Rook-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$WhiteRook-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  The white player in a game starts with two white rooks.")
(comment WhiteKnight-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Knight-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$WhiteKnight-ChessPiece is a white chess piece.  The white player in a game starts with two white knights.")
(comment BlackKnight-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Knight-ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackKnight-ChessPiece is a black chess piece.  The black player in a game starts with two black knights.")
(comment Pawn-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$ChessPiece.  Each instance of #$Pawn-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  Each player in a game starts with eight pawns.")
(comment BlackPawn-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Pawn-ChessPiece and #$BlackChessPiece.  Each instance of #$BlackPawn-ChessPiece is a chess piece.  The black player in a game starts with eight black pawns.")
(comment WhitePawn-ChessPiece "A specialization of #$Pawn-ChessPiece and #$WhiteChessPiece.  Each instance of #$WhitePawn-ChessPiece is a white chess piece.  The white player in a game starts with eight white pawns.")
(comment Tire "The collection of all tires. A type of part for wheeled vehicles.  Each instance of #$Tire is a circular enclosure for the wheel of a wheeled vehicle, intended to protect the wheel.")
(comment WirelessCommunication "A specialization of #$Telecommunication.  Each instance of #$WirelessCommunication is a communication  event in which  the information is carried by electromagnetic spectrum waves without an electromagnetic or optical conductor.")
(comment closestHistoryPriorToWithStatus "<code>(#$closestHistoryPriorToWithStatus HIST EVT2 STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that HIST is the nearest #$PastPatientHistory prior to EVT2 that contains an instance of STATUS-TYPE.")
(comment closestHistoryPriorToEventStopWithStatus "<code>(#$closestHistoryPriorToEventStopWithStatus HIST EVT2 STATUS-TYPE)</code> means that HIST is the nearest #$PastPatientHistory prior to the end of the stop date of EVT2 that contains an instance of STATUS-TYPE.")
(comment internalParts "A #$PhysicalPartPredicate and a specialization of both #$properPhysicalParts  and #$physicallyContains (qq.v.).  <code>(#$internalParts OBJ PART)</code> means that  <code>OBJ</code> has <code>PART</code> as one of its internal physical parts.  That is, <code>PART</code> is  totally inside <code>OBJ</code> and is a proper part of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment internalPartTypes "<code>(#$internalPartTypes OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that every instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> has some instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as one of its internal physical parts (see #$internalParts).")
(comment externalPartTypes "<code>(#$externalPartTypes OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that every instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> has some instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as one of its external physical parts (see #$externalParts).")
(comment TextileFloorCovering "A specialization of #$TextileArtifact and #$FloorCovering.  Important specializations include #$Rug and #$Carpet.")
(comment Exit "The collection of all exits. A type of #$Portal.")
(comment EmergencyExit "A specialization of #$Exit.  Each instance of #$EmergencyExit is an exit that is deemed appropriate (by the relevant authorities) for being used as an exit in the event of an emergency.")
(comment ComputerProcessCrashing "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$ComputerProcessCrashing is an event in which a computer process exits unexpectedly.  Typically, an instance of #$ComputerCrashing (q.v.) is comprised of many instances of #$ComputerProcessCrashing.")
(comment Bread "An instance of #$ProductType, and a specialization of #$Baked. Each instance of #$Bread is a baked food made of a dough or batter containing some instance of #$FlourOrMeal, and usually water or milk. The dough from which the bread is made will often (but not always) contain some leavening agent, such as #$Yeast.")
(comment LoafOfBread "A specialization of #$Bread and #$Food-ReadyToEat.  Each instance of #$LoafOfBread is a loaf of baked bread, which may be either sliced or unsliced, but is otherwise ready to eat.")
(comment Baguette "A specialization of #$LoafOfBread.  Each instance of #$Baguette is a long thin loaf of French bread with a crisp crust.")
(comment Butterfinger "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  Butterfinger is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment Snickers "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  Snickers is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment MilkyWay-CandyBar "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  Milky Way is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment KitKat "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  KitKat is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment CharlestonChew "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  Charleston Chew is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment NestleCrunch "A specialization of #$CandyBar.  Nestle Crunch is a brand of candy bar.")
(comment AccountSystem "#$AccountSystem is a specialization of #$ComputationalSystem.  Each instance of #$AccountSystem is a computational system which is such that users must log on to it to make use of it.  Instances  of #$AccountSystem can consist of one or many nodes (i.e. computers).  Each node in an #$AccountSystem shares a given set of accounts with any other nodes in that #$AccountSystem (such that someone with an account can log in at any node).  See also #$nodeInAccountSystem, #$accountForSystem, and #$ComputerAccount.")
(comment HaplonticLifeCycle "The specialization of #$SexualLifeCycle that occurs in haplonts (see #$Haplont).  In this cycle, the predominant, multicellular form of the organism is haploid (see #$HaploidOrganism).  The diploid phase is limited to the zygote (see #$Zygote), which does not divide mitotically to produce a multicellular organism, but rather divides via #$Meiosis to produce #$HaploidCells sometimes called spores.  These spores divide mitotically to generate the mature haploid organism (see #$HaploidOrganism).  When sexually mature, the haploid phase can produce gametes (see #$Gamete); these can participate in fertilization to produce a #$Zygote.")
(comment Haplont "The collection of organisms that particpate in the #$HaplonticLifeCycle.  In this cycle, the predominant, multicellular form of the organism is haploid (see #$HaploidOrganism).  The diploid phase is limited to the zygote (see #$Zygote), which does not divide mitotically to produce a multicellular organism, but rather divides via #$Meiosis to produce #$HaploidCells sometimes called spores.  These spores divide mitotically to generate the mature haploid organism (see #$HaploidOrganism).  When sexually mature, the haploid phase can produce gametes (see #$Gamete); these can participate in fertilization to produce a #$Zygote.")
(comment DiplonticLifeCycle "The specialization of #$SexualLifeCycle that occurs in diplonts (see #$Diplont).   In this cycle, the predominant multicellular form of the organism is diploid (see #$DiploidOrganism).  Meiosis (see #$Meiosis) occurs in the sex organs of the mature diploid individual to produce the only haploid form of the organism, the gametes (see #$Gamete), which are single cells that do not divide mitotically.  Instead, two gametes (one male, one female) fuse in fertilization (see #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent)  to form a diploid zygote (see #$Zygote) that then divides by mitosis to develop into the predominant, multicellular diploid form.")
(comment Diplont "The class of organisms whose #$SexualLifeCycle is the #$DiplonticLifeCycle.  In this cycle, the predominant multicellular form of the organism is diploid (see #$DiploidOrganism).  Meiosis (see #$Meiosis) occurs in the sex organs of the mature diploid individual to produce the only haploid form of the organism, the gametes (see #$Gamete), which are single cells that do not divide mitotically.  Instead, two gametes (one male, one female) fuse in fertilization (see #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent)  to form a diploid zygote (see #$Zygote) that then divides by mitosis to develop into the predominant, multicellular diploid form.")
(comment DiplobionticLifeCycle "A specialization of #$SexualLifeCycle that is exhibited haplodiplontic organisms (see #$Haplodiplont).  This includes most plants, some algae and some fungi.  In this cycle, mitotic cell division (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle) occurs in both the haploid and the diploid phases of the cycle; thus, both haploid and diploid multicellular invididuals exist (see #$HaploidOrganism and #$DiploidOrganism).  This life cycle type is also called ''alternation of generations.''  The zygote (see #$Zygote) divides mitotically to develop into a diploid multicellular organism, also called a sporophyte (see #$Sporophyte).  When mature, meiosis (see #$Meiosis) occurs in the sex organs of this organism to produce haploid cells (see #$HaploidCell) called spores.  These spores divide mitotically to develop into a multicellular haploid organism called a gametophyte (see #$Gametophyte).  When this organism is mature, certain cells undergo mitosis to produce gametes (see #$Gamete).  Two gametes of opposite kinds (most commonly called male and female) fuse in fertilization (see #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent) to form a diploid zygote, and the cycle repeats.<br>

In a particular species, the haploid and diploid forms may be similar in appearance and adaptation, or very different.  Typically the diploid sporophyte is larger and longer lived than the gametophyte, and in the case of vascular plants gametophytes are not free-living but are dependent on the sporophyte.  In some plants, such as most mosses and liverworts, the haploid gametophyte is larger and longer-lived.")
(comment Haplodiplont "An instance of #$EukaryoticOrganismTypeByLifeCycleType, this is the collection of organisms that participate in the diplobiontic life cycle (see #$DiplobionticLifeCycle), a life cycle typical of plants and some algae.")
(comment CellDivision "The collection of events in which a cell divides to produce two offspring cells, which contain cytoplasm, genetic material, and other subcomponents derived from the parent cell.  For details on how the genetic material is divided, see the specs #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle, #$ReproductiveFission, #$FirstMeioticCellDivision and #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment Gametocytogenesis "A specialization of #$BiologicalProductionEvent.  Each instance of #$Gametocytogenesis is an event in which at least one #$Gametocyte is created.")
(comment CellWithAbnormalChromosomeCount "The collection of instances of #$EukaryoticCell that are exceptional with respect to the number of chromosomes they would be expected to have, as determined by normal biological considerations, e.g., haploid and diploid number.")
(comment TextCorrectionProduct-Stationery "The collection of products whose primary purpose is to cover up errors in printed or written text.")
(comment CorrectionTapeDispenser "The collection of dispensers of correction tape designed to cover errors in printed or written text.  Note that instances of this include dispenser that are full and ones needing refills.  It does not cover the refills by themselves.")
(comment CorrectionFluid-Vial "The collection of vials of fluids which are intended to be used to cover over misprints so that they can be retyped or rewritten.  The fluid in the vials is meant to dry quickly and is intended to match the color (normally white) of the surface (normally paper) upon which the correction is being made.  Since in normal cases these vials are not refilled, the product is gone when the contents of the vial are gone.  Contrast this with other dispensers of products that can be sold empty or filled.")
(disjointWith PrimarilyPaperStationeryProduct Device-OfficeProduct-Stationery)
(comment NewThingFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction with an #$arity of 0 
that can be used to add new constants to the CycL language on the fly.  
Evaluating <code>(#$NewThingFn)</code> will result in the creation of 
a new #$CycLConstant with a global unique identifier (GUID -- see 
#$GUIDString) that can be used to denote an object in the universe by 
stipluating a reference and adding CycL assertions to it.  
#$NewThingFn is very similar in this way to instances of #$SkolemFuncN 
introduce terms that can be used to describe objects, but without the 
indeterminacy of denotation feature of skolem functions.")
(comment SignalTransductionCascade "A specialization of #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-MultiStageReaction that serves to \"amplify\" a chemical signal by virtue of consisting of an ever-increasing number of chemical interactions of a similar type, until a threshold of a level of chemical substance within a cell is reached, sufficient to evoke a cellular response.  A notable (at least common and highly studied) specialization of this is #$PhosphorylationCascade.")
(comment Autodidact "A specialization of #$Person.  Each instance of #$Autodidact is a person who is self-taught in one or more significant areas of learning.")
(comment islandInBodyOfWater "(#$islandInBodyOfWater ISLAND BOW) means that ISLAND is an island in BOW.")
(comment peninsulaInBodyOfWater "(#$peninsulaInBodyOfWater P BOW) means that P is a peninsula in BOW.")
(comment landInBodyOfWater "(#$landInBodyOfWater LAND BOW) means that LAND is land (e.g., a peninsula or an island) in BOW.")
(comment Fludiazepam "Fludiazepam (marketed under the brand name Erispan) is a drug which is a benzodiazepine derivative. It possesses anxiolytic, anticonvulsant, sedative, and skeletal muscle relaxant properties, and is used for the short-term treatment of anxiety disorders. It is a scheduled drug in the U.S., but is available in Japan. (LinkedLife DB http://www.linkedlifedata.com).")
(comment CellularLevelResponseToSignal-Amplified "A specialization of #$CellularLevelResponseToSignal, instances of which are mass productions of some chemical, caused by a cascading transduction of chemical reactions.  The number of chemicals of the relevant type produced is dependent on the number of activated molecules produced by the transduction, which rises as the transduction proceeds, which leads biologists to talk about this process in terms of a signal amplification metaphor.")
(comment ChemicalProcess "The collection of all instances of chemical interactions and series of chemical interactions.")
(comment catalyticSteps "<code>(#$catalyticSteps PROCESS STEP)</code> identifies <code>STEP</code> as an instance #$ChemicalProcess that is a #$properSubEvents of the chemical process <code>PROCESS</code> and consists in one or more chemical interactions that involve a #$catalyst.")
(comment processCatalyticStepTypes "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>(#$processCatalyticStepTypes PROCESS STEP)</code> means <code>(#$relationAllExistsUnique #$catalyticSteps PROCESS STEP)</code>.")
(comment CommonFruitFly "A type of fruit fly which is used extensively in
genetics research because its chromosomes are particularly large and relatively simple.")
(comment Chiasma-Chromosomal "A specialization of #$PhysicalPartOfObject.  Each instance of #$Chiasma-Chromosomal is an X-shaped region on a chromosome where homologous chromosomes have exchanged genetic material through crossing over during meiosis.")
(comment CrossingOver-Chromosomal "Each instance of #$CrossingOver-Chromosomal is an event during which homologous chromosomes trade segments, causing instances of #$Chiasma-Chromosomal to appear on the affected chromosomes.")
(comment justification-Partial "<code>(#$justification-Partial ASKABLE JUSTIFICATION)</code> means that <code>JUSTIFICATION</code> is an instance of #$CycLSentence that appears as a node in a proof tree for <code>ASKABLE</code>, an instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable.")
(comment TetradsBeingHeldTogetherByChiasmata "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Each instance of #$TetradsBeingHeldTogetherByChiasmata is an event in which a tetrad is held together at one or more chiasmata (see #$Chiasma-Chromosomal).")
(comment DisappearanceOfNucleolus "The collection of events in whcih a nucleolus dissapears -- an event that occurs during #$Prophase and #$ProphaseI.")
(comment SisterChromosomeMovesToPole-Meiosis "Each instance of #$SisterChromosomeMovesToPole-Meiosis is an event that occurs during Anaphase II, during which a chromatid moves away from its sister toward a pole of the cell.")
(comment NoncancerousCell "The collection of all cells that spend virtually the entirety of their existence dividing.")
(comment GrowthFactor "This is the collection of all growth factor.  Growth factor is any substance that is capable of stimulating cellular growth, proliferation or differentiation.")
(comment EpidermalGrowthFactor "This is the collection of all epidermal growth factor.  Growth factor is any substance that is capable of stimulating cellular growth, proliferation or differentiation by binding to the receptor EGFR.")
(comment MorphogenicFactor "This is the collection of all morphogenic factor.  Morphogenic factor is any stimulating cellular signaling substance that acts directly on cells to produce specific cellular responses.")
(comment objectTypeGenerallyParticipatesInSituationType "<code>(#$objectTypeGenerallyParticipatesInSituationType SIT-TYPE OBJECT-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code> typically spend the majority of the duration of their existence playing at least an #$actors role in some instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Situation.")
(comment EpidermalGrowthFactorReceptor "The collection of receptors for #$EpidermalGrowthFactor.")
(comment wholeOfTypeHasPartTypeOfPortion "(#$wholeOfTypeHasPartTypeOfPortion WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE PERCENT) means that a typical instance of WHOLE-TYPE will have PERCENT of its \"size\" (i.e, its duration if it is a #$TemporallyExtendedThing, or its volume if it is a #$PartiallyTangible) of PART-TYPE.")
(comment Mitogen "A specialization of #$GrowthFactor and #$ProteinStuff. A mitogen is a protein that promotes mitosis.")
(comment PlateletDerivedGrowthFactor "A specialization of #$Mitogen. Platelet-derived growth factor (PDGF) is a protein that promotes mitosis.")
(comment CyclinSynthesis "The collection of protein synthesis events that produce #$Cyclin.")
(comment CyclinBSynthesis "The collection of protein synthesis events that produce #$CyclinB.")
(comment SisterChromatidsCutByEnzyme "The collection of events in which proteolytic enzymes sever the connections between the sister chromatids in the #$AnaphaseII stage of #$Meiosis or the #$Anaphase stage of #$Mitosis. The daughter chromosomes are then pulled by the microtubules to the spindle poles of the cell.")
(disjointWith MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle SisterChromatidsCutByEnzyme)
(disjointWith SecondMeioticCellDivision SisterChromatidsCutByEnzyme)
(comment MaternalChromosome "A specialization of #$EukaryoticChromosome. Each instance of #$MaternalChromosome is a chromosome in a cell C whose genetic information is identical to the genetic information of the chromosomes in the maternal gamete that gave rise to the organism that is the source of C.")
(comment PaternalChromosome "A specialization of #$EukaryoticChromosome. Each instance of #$PaternalChromosome is a chromosome in a cell C whose genetic information is identical to the genetic information of the chromosomes in the paternal gamete that gave rise to the organism that is the source of C.")
(disjointWith PaternalChromosome MaternalChromosome)
(comment EukaryoticChromosomeTypeByParentSource "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$EukaryoticChromosome whose instances are all of the same parent source.")
(comment MicrotubuleConnectedToKinetochore "The collection of configurations in which one #$Microtubule is connected to one #$Kinetochore.")
(comment DualMicrotubuleConnectedKinetochore "The collection of all #$Kinetochores that are connected at either end to separate #$Microtubules, antecedent to separation in #$Anaphase. (in the case of #$Mitosis) or #$AnaphaseI or #$AnaphaseII (in the case of #$Meiosis).")
(comment MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction that takes place during cell division, in which a microtubule (see #$Microtubule) in the cell cytolplasm binds to a #$Kinetochore on a duplicated chromosome.")
(comment MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore-ProphaseII "A specialization of #$MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore.  The collection of events in which microtubules connect to kinetochores during #$ProphaseII.")
(comment MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore-ProphaseI "A specialization of #$MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore.  The collection of events in which microtubules connect to kinetochores during #$ProphaseI.")
(comment hourNumberOfDate "(#$hourNumberOfDate HOUR DATE) means that month HOUR is the hour of DATE.  For example, (#$hourNumberOfDate 12 (#$MinuteFn 13 (#$HourFn 12 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972)))))) means that 12 is the hour of the date (#$MinuteFn 13 (#$HourFn 12 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 1972)))))).")
(comment MicrotubuleOrganizingCenter "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$MicrotubuleOrganizingCenter is a part of a cell that is involved in microtubule organizing.")
(comment Centrosome "A specialization of #$Organelle and #$MicrotubuleOrganizingCenter.  Each instance of #$Centrosome is an organelle that is involved in cell-cycle progression and microtubule organizing.")
(comment BasalBody "A specialization of #$Organelle and #$MicrotubuleOrganizingCenter.  Each instance of #$BasalBody is an organelle that serves as a nucleation site for the growth of axoneme microtubules.")
(comment partTypeCount "<code>(#$partTypeCount OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE INT)</code> means that <code>INT</code> is the number of parts of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that every instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> has. For example (#$partTypeCount #$Book-CW #$Chapter-PCW 15) says that every book has fifteen chapters.  To talk about physical parts, use the more specific #$physicalPartTypeCount.")
(comment properPartTypeCount "<code>(#$properPartTypeCount OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE INT)</code> means that <code>INT</code> is the number of proper parts of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that every instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> has. For example (#$partTypeCount #$Book-CW #$Chapter-PCW 15) says that every book has fifteen chapters as proper parts.  To talk about proper physical parts, use the more specific #$properPhysicalPartTypeCount.")
(comment physicalPartTypeCount "<code>(#$physicalPartTypeCount OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE INT)</code> means that <code>INT</code> is the number of parts of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that elements of the set <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> have. See also #$hasPhysicalPartCount.")
(comment properPhysicalPartTypeCount "<code>(#$properPhysicalPartTypeCount OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE INT)</code> means that <code>INT</code> is the number of proper parts of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that elements of the set <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> have. See also #$hasPhysicalPartCount.")
(comment uniqueProperPhysicalPartTypes "The predicate #$uniqueProperPhysicalPartTypes relates two sub-collections of #$PartiallyTangible.  <code>(#$uniqueProperPhysicalPartTypes BIG SMALL)</code> means that every instance of  <code>BIG</code> has exactly one instance of <code>SMALL</code> as a proper physical part (see the predicate #$properPhysicalParts).")
(comment Axoneme "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$Axoneme microtubule-based cyctoskeletal structure that is a part of cilia and eukaryotic flagella.")
(comment AbnormalFn "<code>(#$AbnormalFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of abnormal instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment positiveSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceQuery "<code>(#$positiveSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceQuery QUOTED-SENTENCE QUERY)</code> means that when generating bound versions of the query for the multiple choice query <code>QUERY</code>, the sentence <code>QUOTED-SENTENCE</code> should be used.")
(comment HomologousChromosomesCutByEnzymeAndDuplicatedChromosomesMoveToPole "The collection of events in which proteolytic enzymes sever the connections between the homologous chromosomes in the #$AnaphaseI stage of #$Meiosis, followed by the now severed duplicated chromosomes migrating to opposite poles of the cell.")
(comment CollectionIntersection2Fn "<code>(#$CollectionIntersection2Fn COL1 COL2)</code> denotes the collection which is by definition the intersection of the collections COL1 and COL2.")
(comment EukaryoticCell "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$EukaryoticCell is a cell that serves as the basic structural unit of a eukaryotic organism.  These cells have a membrane-bound nucleus and other organelles.  Multicellular organisms generally have #$EukaryoticCells; #$EukaryoticCell DNA has introns.  Certain #$EukaryoticCells, like the red blood corpuscles of #$Persons with heathy #$Spleens, lack nuclei.")
(comment GrasshopperShaped "#$GrasshopperShaped is the typical shape of a grasshopper.")
(comment cellCytoplasm "(#$cellCytoplasm CELL CYTOPLASM) identifies <code>CYTOPLASM</code> as the (entire) cyctoplasm of the cell <code>CELL</code>.")
(comment Separation-Complete-ObjectDestroyed "The collection of instances of #$Separation-Complete in which a physically stuff-like object is #$separatedIntoPortions and thereby destroyed, resulting in the creation of similar stuff-like objects that previously jointly comprised the original.")
(comment separationOfStuffTypeIntoNEqualPortions "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalPredicate, <code>(#$separationOfStuffTypeIntoNEqualPortions SEPARATION STUFF-TYPE N)</code> identifies <code>SEPARATION</code> as the collection of instances of #$Separation-Complete-ObjectDestroyed in which an instance of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> is #$separatedIntoPortions such that the result is <code>N</code> instances of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> of (approximately) equal size and shape.")
(comment separatedIntoPortions "An actor slot that relates an instance #$Separation-Complete-ObjectDestroyed to the object that is separated into portions (and is thus destroyed).")
(comment TreeFrog "The collection of all tree frogs. A type of #$Frog. #$TreeFrog is an #$OrganismClassificationType.  Instances of #$TreeFrog are mambers of frog species that typically spend most of their lives in trees.")
(comment Hemiphractidae "A specialization of #$TreeFrog.")
(comment PoisonDartFrog "A specialization of #$Frog. Poison dart frogs are a group of species of frogs that are native to Central and South America, where natives once used secretions from these animals to create poison darts.")
(comment Caecilian "A specialization of #$Amphibian.  Each instance of #$Caecilians is an amphipian in the order Gymnophiona, which are amphibians that superficially resemble snakes.")
(comment Anura "An instance of #$BiologicalOrder, and a specialization of #$Amphibian.  Members of the order Anura are frogs and toads.")
(comment Dinosaur "The collection of all dinosaurs, extinct (from the point of view of Now) reptile-like animals, some of which were huge.  The relationship between dinosaurs and reptiles is not agreed upon, but I have made Dinosaur a subset of Reptile in accord with general scholarly consensus.  Still at issue is whether or not some dinosaurs were warm-blooded.")
(comment largeVarietyOfType "<code>(#$largeVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually large instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment abnormalVarietyOfType "<code>(#$abnormalVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all abnormal instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment smallVarietyOfType "<code>(#$smallVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually small instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment LargeFn "<code>(#$LargeFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are larger than ordinary.")
(comment SmallFn "<code>(#$SmallFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are smaller than ordinary.")
(comment Marmot "A genus of large ground squirrels.")
(comment GiantSalamander "The collection of salamanders that are naturally larger than ordinary.  This collection includes hellbenders, the Japanese giant salamanders, and the Chinese giant salamanders.")
(comment TallFn "<code>(#$TallFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are taller than ordinary.")
(comment tallVarietyOfType "<code>(#$tallVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually tall instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ShortFn "<code>(#$ShortFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are shorter than ordinary.")
(comment shortVarietyOfType "<code>(#$shortVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are shorter than usual.")
(comment ThinFn "<code>(#$ThinFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are thinner than ordinary.")
(comment ThickFn "<code>(#$ThickFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are thicker than ordinary.")
(comment thinVarietyOfType "<code>(#$thinVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all thin instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment thickVarietyOfType "<code>(#$thickVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all thick instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment LightFn "<code>(#$LightFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are lighter than ordinary.")
(comment HeavyFn "<code>(#$HeavyFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are heavier than ordinary.")
(comment heavyVarietyOfType "<code>(#$heavyVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually heavy instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment lightVarietyOfType "<code>(#$lightVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually light instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ruleParaphraseTarget "(#$ruleParaphraseTarget RULE NL) means that NL is a string that the paraphrase system should generate for RULE.")
(comment nonSisterChromatids "<code>(#$nonSisterChromatids C1 C2)</code> holds just in case C1 and C2 are #$chromatids of distinct instances of #$DuplicatedChromosome that are part of a single instance of #$Tetrad-Chromosomal.")
(comment TetradLinesUpAtMetaphasePlate "A collection during which a chromosome lines up at the metaphase plate (see #$metaphasePlateOfCell).")
(comment TetradLinesUpAtMetaphasePlate "The collection of events in which a single instance of #$Tetrad-Chromosomal moves towards the center of the cell in which it \"resides\" so as to line up with the #$metaphasePlateOfCell.  The entirety of such events comprises #$MetaphaseI of #$Meiosis.")
(comment ExchangeOfChromosomalSegments "A specialization of #$PhysicalTransformationProcess, each instance of which is the 1-1 exchange of corresponding regions of #$nonSisterChromatids.  The entirety of such events during #$ProphaseI comprises #$CrossingOver-Chromosomal.")
(comment creation "A predicate corresponding to the function #$CreationFn.  <code>(#$creation X (#$CreationFn X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment SaltwaterCrocodile "A species of crocodile.  The saltwater crocodiles are the largest living reptiles.")
(comment Caiman "The collection of all caimans; a subset of #$Crocodilian.")
(comment Alligatoridae "A specialization of #$Crocodilian.  #$Alligatoridae includes #$Alligator, #$Caiman, #$Melanosuchus and #$Paleosuchus.")
(comment Alligator "The collection of all alligators; a subset of #$Crocodilian.  #$Alligator includes the American Alligators and Chinese Alligators.  Cf. #$Crocodile.")
(comment Telomere "The collection of telomeres.  Telomeres are repetitive DNA sequences located at the ends of linear chromosomes.  They are believed to serve as a defense against the copying errors that are otherwise likely to occur during DNA replication at chromosomal termini.")
(disjointWith Telomere Centromere)
(comment CellProliferation "A specialization of #$IncreaseEvent.  Each instance of #$CellProliferation is an event in which the size of a cell poplulation increases due to members of the populations undergoing #$CellDivision (q.v.).")
(comment TimeOnDayFn "(#$TimeOnDayFn DAY TIME) denotes the subinterval of DAY that is an instance of TIME.")
(comment workplaceHasSchedule "(#$workplaceHasSchedule WORKPLACE DAYTYPE START-TIME END-TIME) means that at WORKPLACE on typical instances of DAYTYPE, some workers start working at START-TIME and stop working at END-TIME.")
(disjointWith SeaTurtle FreshwaterTurtle)
(comment FreshwaterTurtle "The collection of all freshwater turtles. A type of #$Turtle and #$AquaticOrganism. #$FreshwaterTurtle is an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment Trionychidae "A specialization of #$Turtle.  Trionychidae is a taxonomic family consisting of turtles commonly referred to as \"softshell\" turtles.")
(comment workplaceWorkersPerShift "(#$workplaceWorkersPerShift WORKPLACE NUM) means that during any shift at WORKPLACE there will be about NUM workers there.")
(comment placeHasSchedule "(#$placeHasSchedule PLACE DAYTYPE START-TIME END-TIME EVENT-TYPE) means that at PLACE on typical instances of DAYTYPE, some instance of EVENT-TYPE starts at START-TIME and ends at END-TIME.")
(comment Aftershock "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$Aftershock is an earthquake that occurs after a previous main earthquake, in the same general area.")
(comment MainShock-Earthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$Aftershock is an earthquake that occurs after a previous main earthquake, in the same general area.")
(disjointWith Aftershock MainShock-Earthquake)
(comment BlindThrustEarthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$BlindThrustEarthquake is an earthquake that occurs along a #$BlindThrustFault (a thrust fault that does not show signs on the Earth's surface).")
(comment Fault-Geological "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion. Each instance of #$Fault-Geological is a fracture in a volume of rock, across which there has been displacement.   Energy release during rapid slippage along faults causes earthquakes (see #$Earthquake).  Not every fault marks the surface of the Earth (see #$BlindThrustFault), but many do (see #$Fault-Topographical).")
(disjointWith Fault-Topographical BlindThrustFault)
(comment ThrustFault "A specialization of #$Fault-Geological.  Thrust faults are faults where there has been a break in the Earth's crust across which there has been relative movement.")
(comment BlindThrustFault "A specialization of #$ThrustFault.  Blind thrust faults are faults where there has been a break in the Earth's crust across which there has been relative movement, but which is not noticable from any topographical clues.")
(comment DeepFocusEarthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$DeepFocusEarthquake is an earthquake that occurs at depths between 300 and 700 kilometers beneath the Earth's surface.")
(comment InterplateEarthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$InterplateEarthquake is an earthquake that occurs at the boundary of two tectonic plates.")
(comment IntraplateEarthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$IntraplateEarthquake is an earthquake that occurs away from the boundary of a  tectonic plate.")
(comment MegathrustEarthquake "A type of #$Earthquake. Each instance of #$MegathrustEarthquake is an earthquake that occurs at a subduction zone at a destructive tectonic plate boundary.  No ther known mechanism for producing eathquakes produces earthquakes as large and powerful as megathrust earthquakes.")
(comment Avalanche "A specialzation of #$NaturalHazard.  Each instance of #$Avalanche is an event in which a large amount of snow and ice falls down the side of a steep natural incline (such as the side of a mountain).")
(comment typicalNumberOfAttendeesInEventsOfTypeAtPlace "(#$typicalNumberOfAttendeesInEventsOfTypeAtPlace PLACE EVT-TYPE NUM) means that instances of EVT-TYPE held at PLACE typically have NUM attendees.")
(comment SynaptonemalComplex "The collection of synaptonemal complexes.  These are structures that form between two homologous chromosomes during meiosis.")
(comment GiantTortoise "#$GiantTortoise is the collection of giant tortoises.")
(comment ScaledReptile "A #$BiologicalOrder. Squamata,includes #$Lizard (Lacertilia) and #$Snakes (Serpentes). Members of #$ScaledReptile have skins with horny scales.")
(comment Vulpes "Vulpes is a biological genus.  It is a sub-taxon of Canidae. Members of Vulpes are referred to as 'true foxes'.")
(comment Fox "The collection of all foxes. A type of #$Scavenger and #$CanineAnimal. #$Fox is a #$BiologicalTaxon.  The 'true foxes' are members of the genus #$Vulpes (q.v.).")
(comment Bluegill "The Bluegill is a species of small freshwater fish.")
(comment FreshwaterFish "Fish which live in the fresh waters of ponds, lakes, or streams.")
(comment FreshwaterOrganism "Organisms which live immersed in the fresh waters of, e.g. ponds, lakes, or streams. ")
(comment Sunfish "The Sunfish is a family of freshwater fish.  Species in the family include the #$Bluegill and #$Bass-Fish.")
(comment SaltwaterFish "The collection of all sea turtles. A type of #$Turtle and #$MarineOrganism. #$SeaTurtle is an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(disjointWith FreshwaterFish SaltwaterFish)
(comment Baud "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfBandwidth, used to represent a standard unit of computer data transmission speed -- one symbol or pulse per second, encoding one or more bits per second. Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a quantity of symbols per second (which is an instance of #$Bandwidth). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is also an instance of #$Bandwidth).")
(comment Bandwidth "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity. Each member of this collection is some particular measure of computer bandwidth. Instances of this collection are often denoted using functions such as #$Baud (the number of symbols per second that can be processed by a device), which fall into the collection #$UnitOfBandwidth.")
(comment promptForArgOfPred "(#$promptForArgOfPred PRED ARG PROMPT) means that when prompting a user to supply the ARGth argument for a formula whose arg0 is PRED and whose other values are fixed, an interface can use the string PROMPT.")
(comment CellPlate "The collection of all cell plates.  Cell plates form during the cytokinesis phase of both mitosis and meiosis (see #$Cytokinesis, #$Mitosis, #$Meiosis) in the cells of plants.  Cell plates mature, growing stiff and flat, and become a portion of the cell wall of the cells that result from cytokinesis.  Notably, cell plates do not occur in animal cells.")
(comment entityOfTypeBetweenStages "The corresponding predicate of #$EntityOfTypeBetweenStagesFn.")
(disjointWith SomaticCell Gamete)
(comment Gamete "Gamete is the collection of all gametes, whether mature (see #$Gamete-Mature) or immature (see #$Gametid).")
(comment ProperSubSituationTypeFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  <code>(#$ProperSubSituationTypeFn SIT-TYPE SUB-SIT-TYPE)</code> picks out the unique proper subsituation type of type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation) in <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment InterphaseOfGametogenesis " A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Each instance of #$InterphaseOfGametogenesis is an interphase process that occurs at a germ cell immediately prior to that cell becoming an input to #$Meiosis.")
(disjointWith InterphaseOfOogenesis InterphaseOfSpermatogenesis)
(comment InterphaseOfSpermatogenesis " A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Each instance of #$InterphaseOfSpermatogenesis is an interphase process that occurs at a germ cell immediately prior to that cell becoming an input to #$Spermatidogenesis.")
(comment InterphaseOfOogenesis " A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Each instance of #$InterphaseOfOogenesis is an interphase process that occurs at a germ cell immediately prior to that cell becoming an input to #$Ootidogenesis.")
(comment BiologicalSuperorder "A specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon.  Each instance of #$BiologicalSuperorder has as an immediate taxonomic subdivision some instance of #$BiologicalOrder.")
(comment allInRelnToRolePlayerOfTypePlayRoleInScript "<code>(#$allInRelnToRolePlayerOfTypePlayRoleInScript TYPE RELN ROLE ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE SCRIPT ROLE-FOR-TYPE)</code> means that in every instance <code>SCRIPT-INS</code> of the situation-type <code>SCRIPT</code> and every object <code>OBJ</code> of type <code>ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE</code> such that <code>(ROLE INS OBJ)</code>, if at any point in <code>INS</code> is there a second object <code>OTHER</code> of type <code>TYPE</code> such that <code>(RELN OTHER OBJ)</code>, then it follows that <code>(ROLE-FOR-TYPE INS OTHER)</code>.")
(comment allInRelnFromRolePlayerOfTypePlayRoleInScript "<code>(#$allInRelnFromRolePlayerOfTypePlayRoleInScript TYPE RELN ROLE ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE SCRIPT ROLE-FOR-TYPE)</code> means that in every instance <code>SCRIPT-INS</code> of the situation-type <code>SCRIPT</code> and every object <code>OBJ</code> of type <code>ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE</code> such that <code>(ROLE INS OBJ)</code>, if at any point in <code>INS</code> is there a second object <code>OTHER</code> of type <code>TYPE</code> such that <code>(RELN OBJ OTHER)</code>, then it follows that <code>(ROLE-FOR-TYPE INS OTHER)</code>.")
(comment Grylloblattidae "A family of extremophile insects (see #$Insect).  Commonly known as \"ice crawlers\" or \"icebugs\".")
(comment Dragonfly "The collection of all dragonflies. A specialization of #$Odonata.  #$Dragonfly is an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment Damselfly "The collection of all damselflies. A specialization of #$Odonata.")
(disjointWith Dragonfly Damselfly)
(comment Hemiptera "A specialization of #$Insect.  The order Hemiptera consists of the \"true bugs\".")
(comment Hymenoptera "A collection of animals; a subset of #$Insect. #$Hymenoptera is one of the largest and most-significant-to-humans orders in the #$Insect class, and includes #$Ants, #$Wasps, and #$Bees.  Insects in #$Hymenoptera range from about 0.21 mm (0.008 in.) to about 5 cm (2 in.) in length; usually have membranous wings with relatively few veins, have mouthparts modified for chewing and/or sucking, have large compound eyes, and sometimes have stingers. Many have complex social organizations.")
(comment Wasp "The collection of all wasps. A type of #$Hymenoptera and #$VenomousAnimal. #$Wasp is an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment ClothingAlterationsShop "Local (one site) service organizations which have as one of their main functions to alter or repair clothing for customers for a fee.")
(comment TailorShop "Local (one site) service organizations which have as one of their main functions to do tailoring of clothes for customers for a fee.")
(comment restaurantHasMenuItem "(#$restaurantHasMenuItem FOOD-OUTLET SPECIFIED-DISH) means that the organization FOOD-OUTLET has the #$SpecifiedFoodDishType SPECIFIED-DISH on its menu")
(comment objectsInAttachment "A specialization of #$configuredObjects.  (#$objectsInAttachment ATTACH THING) means that THING is one of the objects attached to the other objects participating in the #$Attachment configuration, ATTACH.")
(comment Attachment-Binary "Instances of #$Attachment-Binary are #$Configurations in which precisely two physical objects are attached to each other.")
(comment thingAttached "A specialization of #$objectsInAttachment. <code>(#$thingAttached ATTACH THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is attached to some other object (see the predicate #$thingAttachedTo) in the attachment configuration <code>ATTACH</code>.")
(comment thingAttachedTo "A specialization of #$objectsInAttachment. <code>(#$thingAttachedTo ATTACH THING)</code> means that some other object is attached to <code>THING</code> in the attachment configuration <code>ATTACH</code>.")
(comment suppressFormulasForElements-TermIsa "(#$suppressFormulasForElements-TermIsa TERM SET) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the search query results, then elements of SET (a set or collection), INS, should NOT have the appropriate formulas generated for them.  This predicate is used in the CAE query search.  See #$generateFormulasForElements-TermIsa for more information on the generation of formulas in the CAE.")
(comment GlobalInformationGridContentDeliveryServiceSystem-NCES "The #$GlobalInformationGridContentDeliveryService-NCES is an information distribution services fielded by the #$DefenseInformationSystemsAgency that optimizes the delivery of Web content and applications by distributing them on globally deployed servers.  End users access content via the geographically closest enclave, resulting in increased connection speed and minimal download time.")
(comment EnterpriseFileDeliveryServiceSystem-NCES "This enterprise service fields a standalone lightweight application that is used to synchronize between geographically separated sites, thereby helping to achieve Wide Area Network bandwidth savings.")
(comment NetCentricEnterpriseService "Net-Centric Enterprise Services (NCES) constitute a family of systems fielded by the #$DefenseInformationSystemsAgency that enable information sharing through timely connection of information sources with potential consumers. NCES elements work to create better access to information, enhancing information reach, usability, and depth as a way to support improved decision-making across the DOD community.")
(comment EnterpriseMessagingSOAFServiceSystem-NCES "An NCES messaging service enterprise that provides a federated, distributed, and fault-tolerant enterprise messaging bus, with infrastructure for applications that produce or consume messages.")
(comment Rorqual "A family of #$BaleenWhales, including at least nine species.")
(comment DuplicatedChromosome "The collection of all instances of #$Chromosome that are fully duplicated -- i.e., they consist of two fully-condensed chromatin strands joined at the centromeric region, forming (at least in the non-telocentric case) the distinctive \"X\" shape associated with chromosomes in biological literature.")
(comment MomentMagnitudeScale "An instance of #$LogarithmicScale.  The moment magnitude scale quantifies the amount of siesmic energy released by earthquakes.")
(comment restaurantSpaceHasMenuItem "(#$restaurantSpaceHasMenuItem FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE SPECIFIED-DISH) means that the restaurant space FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE has the #$SpecifiedFoodDishType SPECIFIED-DISH on its menu")
(comment restaurantSpaceServesCuisine "(#$restaurantSpaceServesCuisine FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE CUISINE) means that the restaurant FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE serves food of the #$Cuisine, CUISINE")
(comment restaurantSpaceHasChef "(#$restaurantSpaceHasChef FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE CHEF) means that the restaurant FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE has the $#Chef CHEF")
(comment restaurantSpaceHasWaitperson "(#$restaurantSpaceHasWaitperson FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE WAIT) means that the restaurant FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE has the $#Waitperson waiting on the customers who visit it")
(comment restaurantSpaceHasSousChef "(#$restaurantSpaceHasSousChef FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE SCHEF) means that the restaurant FOOD-OUTLET-SPACE has the $#Sous-chef SCHEF")
(comment CodeAnalysisConstant-Extant "The collection of all pre-existing #$CycLConstants deemed particularly salient to the #$StoneSoupProject.")
(disjointWith CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseOne CodeAnalysisConstant-Extant)
(comment TheQuerySearchFocalTerm "A quoted instance of #$IndexicalConcept.  This indexical concept is used to show where the current focal term should be inserted into the query sentence.  See #$generateSentenceForInstances and #$generateSentenceForSpecs for query-search predicates that admit sentences.")
(comment HomologousChromosomesAttachToOneAnother "A specialization of #$CreationEvent and #$AttachmentEvent.  Each instance of #$HomologousChromosomesAttachToOneAnother occurs during #$ProphaseI of #$Meiosis. During each instance of #$HomologousChromosomesAttachToOneAnother the two members of a #$HomologousChromosomePair attach to one another to form a #$Tetrad-Chromosomal.")
(comment relationMemberExistsCount "(#$relationMemberExistsCount PRED GROUP COLL N) means that for every MEMBER such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEMBER), there exists exactly N instances INS of collection COLL such that (PRED MEMBER INS) is true. This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group without referencing the members.")
(comment relationMemberExistsUnique "(#$relationMemberExistsUnique PRED GROUP COLL) means that, for every MEM such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEM), there is exactly one instance INST of COLL such that (PRED MEM INST) holds.  Thus it is equivalent to (#$relationMemberExistsCount PRED GROUP COLL 1).")
(comment relationExistsMemberCount "(#$relationExistsMemberCount PRED COLL GROUP N) means that for every MEMBER such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEMBER), there exists exactly N instances INS of collection COLL such that (PRED INS MEMBER) is true. This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group without referencing the members.")
(comment relationExistsMemberUnique "(#$relationExistsMemberUnique PRED COLL GROUP) means that, for every MEM such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEM), there is exactly one instance INST of COLL such that (PRED INST MEM) holds.  Thus it is equivalent to (#$relationExistsMemberCount PRED COLL GROUP 1).")
(comment ComputerCodeLoop "The collecion of all instances of #$ComputerCode that exhibit recursive specifications, i.e., that specify an iterated process wherein the output of one iteration serves as input for the next iteration, so long as some (hopefully terminating) condition is satisfied.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByProcedureTypeSpecified "A type-level collection.  Each #$Collection instance is a type of #$ComputerCode whose instances are subject to a common characterization concerning the procedures they specify.")
(comment CodeTypeByProcedureTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used for reifying types of #$ComputerCode on the basis of the kind of program action specified. Where PROCEDURE-TYPE is a specialization of #$ProgramAction, (#$CodeTypeByProcedureTypeFn PROCEDURE-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if implemented under normal conditions in a typical run-type environment (see #$codeExecuted) will result in an instance of PROCEDURE-TYPE being implemented by the implementing architecture.")
(comment procedureTypeSpecifiedByCodeTypeInstances "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CodeTypeByProcedureTypeFn.  Where PROCEDURE-TYPE is a specialization of #$ProgramAction, (#$procedureTypeSpecifiedByCodeTypeInstances PROCEDURE-TYPE CODE-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if implemented under normal conditions in a typical run-type environment (see #$codeExecuted) will result in an instance of PROCEDURE-TYPE being implemented by the implementing architecture.")
(comment codeExecuted "(#$codeExecuted ACTION CODE) means that ACTION is performed by a machine implementing a universal Turing machine architecture within a context of standard computer operating procedures that accepts either a numerical encoding of CODE or a numerical encoding of some base code of which CODE is an assembled or compiled version, together with a numerical encoding of some input, such that ACTION can be interpreted as the implementation of a computable arithmetic function indicated by CODE on that input.  Under ordinary circumstances, ACTION is also subject to at least a secondary interpretation according to which it constitutes some non-numeric operation specified by the terminology of CODE.")
(comment codeImplementsProgramActionType "(#$codeImplementsProgramActionType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that any #$ProgramAction which executes CODE in a normal runtime environment (see #$codeExecuted) will be an instance of ACTION-TYPE.")
(comment Elephantidae "A biological taxon. Elephantidae is the family that includes all elephants and mammoths.")
(comment AfricanElephant "The collection of all African #$Elephants.  A biological genus; #$AfricanElephants are native to the #$ContinentOfAfrica and have larger #$Ears than #$AsianElephants.")
(comment IndianElephant "The collection of all Indian #$Elephants, and a subspecies of #$AsianElephant. #$IndianElephants are native to the subcontinent of India.")
(comment AsianElephant "A species of #$Elephant.  Asian elephants are native to Asia and have smaller #$Ears than #$AfricanElephants.")
(comment chooseTerm "(#$chooseTerm TERM) is true for any closed Cyc TERM, and indicates that TERM has been chosen from the set of terms in the universe of discourse.  This predicate is primarily used as a pragmatic hint that a variable should become bound as soon as possible in order to maximally assist inference progress.  There should never be methods for generating bindings for non-closed #$chooseTerm literals.  See also the related #$termChosen.")
(comment codeHasString "(#$codeHasString CODE STRING) means that the information structure of CODE is manifested in the #$CharacterString STRING.")
(comment characterLengthOfCode "(#$characterLengthOfCode CODE LENGTH) means that the #$ComputerCode CODE has a character length of LENGTH.")
(comment computerCodeIncludesCode "A #$NonPhysicalPartPredicate.  (#$computerCodeIncludesCode CODE SUB-CODE) means that the #$AbstractInformationStructure SUB-CODE is a structural part (#$subInfoStructures) of the #$AbstractInformationStructure CODE.")
(comment codeSubsumesCodeOfType "(#$codeSubsumesCodeOfType CODE SUB-CODE-TYPE) means that there exists an instance of SUB-CODE-TYPE, SUB-CODE, such that (#$computerCodeIncludesCode CODE SUB-CODE).")
(comment codeHasPropensityForActionOfType "(#$codeHasPropensityForActionOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that if CODE is executed on a computing architecture in typical run-time conditions, there is a non-trivial potential (medium-to-very-high) of the architecture exhibiting #$ComputerActivity of type ACTION-TYPE, other things being equal.")
(comment codeExecutionEntailsProgramActionOfType "(#$codeExecutionEntailsProgramActionOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that any #$ProgramAction which executes CODE under normal operating conditions (see #$codeExecuted) will subsume an instance of ACTION-TYPE as a #$subEvents.")
(comment codeMitigatesProgramActionOfType "(#$codeMitigatesProgramActionOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, any instance of #$ComputerCode, SUPER-CODE that includes CODE will have a relatively low potential (low to very low) of resulting in an action of type ACTION-TYPE when run in a typical run-time environment.")
(comment codeLiableToUndesirableProgramActionOfType "A typed spec-pred of #$codeHasPropensityForActionOfType.  (#$codeLiableToUndesirableProgramActionOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that if CODE is executed on a computing architecture in typical run-time conditions, there is a non-trivial potential (medium-to-very-high) of the architecture exhibiting an instance of a class of #$UndesirableProgramAction given by the collection ACTION-TYPE, other things being equal.")
(comment authorOfProgramWithAIS "(#$authorOfProgramWithAIS PROGRAM-CODE AGENT) means that AGENT is the author of an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW that exhibits the #$AbstractInformationStructure (more specifically, the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS) PROGRAM-CODE.")
(comment CharacterLengthOfCodeFn "The corresponding function of #$characterLengthOfCode (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical).  Where CODE is an instance of #$ComputerCode, (#$CharacterLengthOfCodeFn CODE) denotes the character length of CODE.")
(comment codeLanguage "(#$codeLanguage CODE LANGUAGE) means that the #$ComputerCode CODE is expressed in the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage LANGUAGE.")
(comment codeLiableToCondition "(#$codeLiableToCondition CODE SENTENCE) means that in any context wherein CODE is executed in a typical computing architecture, there is a non-trivial (medium to very high) likelihood of SENTENCE being true, other things being equal.")
(comment generateOpaqueSentenceForSpecs "(#$generateOpaqueSentenceForSpecs TERM SENT) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then SENT will be added to the set of sentences triggered by TERM.  If #$TheQuerySearchFocalTerm is present in SENT, it will be replaced with the specialization of TERM that triggered the inclusion of the sentence, but no further substitutions into SENT will be allowed.")
(comment generateOpaqueSentenceForInstances "(#$generateOpaqueSentenceForInstances TERM SENT) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then SENT will be added to the set of sentences triggered by TERM.  If #$TheQuerySearchFocalTerm is present in SENT, it will be replaced with the instance of TERM that triggered the inclusion of the sentence, but no further substitutions into SENT will be allowed.")
(comment generateSentenceForInstances "(#$generateSentenceForInstances TERM SENT) means that if an instance of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then SENT will be added to the set of sentences triggered by TERM.  If #$TheQuerySearchFocalTerm is present in SENT, it will be replaced with the instance of TERM that triggered the inclusion of the sentence.")
(comment generateSentenceForSpecs "(#$generateSentenceForSpecs TERM SENT) means that if a specialization of TERM is a valid term in the query search results, then SENT will be added to the set of sentences triggered by TERM.  If #$TheQuerySearchFocalTerm is present in SENT, it will be replaced with the specialization of TERM that triggered the inclusion of the sentence.")
(comment positiveSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceOption "<code>(#$positiveSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceOption QUOTED-SENTENCE OPTION)</code> means that when generating the bound version of a query <code>Q</code> for the multiple choice option <code>OPTION</code>, such that <code>(#$candidateAnswers Q OPTION)</code>, the sentence <code>QUOTED-SENTENCE</code> should be used.")
(comment negationSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceOption "<code>(#$negationSentenceTemplateForMultipleChoiceOption QUOTED-SENTENCE OPTION)</code> means that when generating the negated version of a query <code>Q</code> for the multiple choice option <code>OPTION</code>, such that <code>(#$candidateAnswers Q OPTION)</code>, the sentence <code>QUOTED-SENTENCE</code> should be used.")
(comment Nucleotide "The collection of all nucleotides.  Instances of this
collection are chemical compounds consisting of a phosphate group, a
simple 5-carbon sugar, and a #$NitrogenBase.  This collection divides
into two groups: #$Ribonucleotide, whose instances use #$Ribose as the
simple 5-carbon sugar, and #$Deoxyribonucleotide, whose instances use
#$Deoxyribose as the simple 5-carbon sugar. When joined in a chain to form a polymer, #$Nucleotides make up the nucleic acids (see #$PolynucleotideMolecule) RNA and DNA (see #$RNAMolecule, #$DNAMolecule).")
(comment GeneticMutationEvent "Instances of #$GeneticMutationEvent are occurrences in which the genetic content of a #$BiologicalLivingObject (BLO) changes.  Specifically, the sequence of #$Nucleotides in the BLO's genetic material is different after the #$GeneticMutationEvent from what it was before, in some way that is not the result of the copying that occurs during normal replication of the genetic material.")
(comment GeneticMutationEvent-Cellular "Instances of #$GeneticMutationEvent-Cellular are mutation events that affect the genetic material of a #$Cell.  In the case of a #$EukaryoticCell, the nucleotide sequence of one or more of the cell's #$Chromosomes changes.  This can be contrasted with #$GeneticMutationEvent-Organelle, in which the genetic material of mitochondria (see #$Mitochondrion) or #$Chloroplasts is affected.")
(disjointWith GeneticMutationEvent-Organelle GeneticMutationEvent-Cellular)
(comment OrbWeaverSpider "The collection of orb-weaver spiders. They are builders of large spiral webs.")
(comment Stridulating "A specialization of #$BodyMovementEvent.  Stridulation is the production of sound by rubbing together body parts.")
(comment Sicariidae "The collection of spiders in the Sicariidae family. This family of spiders contains many venomous species.")
(comment Sicarius "The collection of spiders in the Sicarius genus (Sicariidae family). The most well-known of these is the Sicarius hahni, commonly known as the \"six-eyed sand spider\".")
(comment congeners "<code>(#$congeners  A B)</code> means that <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> are two distinct organisms that belong to the same biological genus.")
(comment conspecifics "<code>(#$conspecifics A B)</code> means that <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> are two distinct organisms that belong to the same biological species.")
(comment PrimarilyPaperStationeryProduct "The collection of stationery products that are primarily composed of paper.  This includes such things as notepads, index cards, memo or appointment books, etc.")
(comment CorrectingAnErrorInATextualArtifact "The collection of events in which some error or other, e.g. a typographic error, is corrected in a textual artifact (some instance of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject).")
(comment CorrectingAnErrorInSomething "The collection of events in which some error or other is corrected in something. This includes removing bugs from computer code, correcting typos in printed works, etc. Note that the thing corrected must have some existence before the correction and continue to exist after the correction. Hence, a school teacher's correction of a student's verbal pronunciation is not an instance of this collection because the teacher's example of how to correctly pronounce the words is not strictly a correction in this sense, rather it is a demonstration -- the original utterance can not be corrected and the teacher's demonstration is no guarantee that the student's behavior is corrected. Whether strict identity is maintained is dependent on the type of thing corrected, but continuity is required.")
(disjointWith StationeryProduct OfficeFurniture)
(comment CorrectionTapeRefill "The collection of rolls or bundles of correction sold as refills for dispensers of correction tape.")
(comment Binder-ThreeRing "The collection of standard 3-ring binders.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuff OfficeProductRefill)
(comment OfficeProductRefill "The collection of all office products sold as \"refills\" for other office products.  This collection includes bundles of staples, pencil leads for mechanical pencils, etc.")
(comment MechanicalPencilLead-Refill "The collection of packages of pencil lead (graphite) intended as refills for mechanical pencils.")
(comment typeTypicallyIncludesType "(#$typeTypicallyIncludesType TYPE1 TYPE2) means that instances of TYPE1 typically include some instance of TYPE2 either as a physical part (#$physicalParts) or as something it spatially contains (#$spatiallyIncludes).  This is meant to be somewhat weaker than the normal \"default\" assumption of normal conditions that would be appropriate to say that cars have wheels, doors have handles, etc.  This also covers cases where, while you might expect some TYPE1 to include some TYPE2, encountering one that lacked it would not entirely surprise you.  E.g. there is typically gas in cars, staples in staplers, ink in a writing pen, etc.")
(comment refillTypeForProductType "(#$refillTypeForProductType PROD-TYPE REFILL-TYPE) means that REFILL-TYPE is the collection of products that are designed and marketed as refills for instances of PROD-TYPE.  E.g. this relation holds between staplers and boxes of staples, mechanical pencils and refill leads, etc. Note that his holds both in the general cases (between, say, mechanical pencils and refill leads) and in the specfic cases (between, say, PentelQuickerClicker5MM-MechanicalPencil and PentelHiPolymer5MM-Hard2H-LeadRefill). ")
(comment PadOfPaper "The collection of all pads composed of sheets of paper. A type of #$Artifact. The concept #$PadOfPaper is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Notepad "The collection of all notepads. A subcollection of #$PrimarilyPaperStationeryProduct and #$PadOfPaper. This collections consists of pads of paper made for personal writing and note taking.  Note that this is properly a subcollection of #$PadOfPaper as the latter would include pads of paper designed for wrapping or cleaning, etc. #$Notepad is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment SheetOfPaper "Paper that comes in thin sheets.  Each instance of this collection is a sheet of paper either free or as part of a #$PadOfPaper.")
(comment SheetOfWritingPaper "a sheet of paper used primarily to be written on.")
(comment mainFunctionalComponent-TypeType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible to another specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  <code>(#$mainFunctionalComponent-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> has an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as its #$mainFunctionalComponent.")
(comment mainFunctionalComponent "A predicate that relates objects to parts of it which are its main functional components.
<code>(#$mainFunctionalComponent WHOLE PART)</code> means that <code>WHOLE</code> is at least partially made of <code>PART</code> (<code>(#$physicalParts WHOLE PART)</code> holds), and (as a default) the purpose or function of <code>WHOLE</code> derives from the physical properties of <code>PART</code>.  For example a medication may have certain active ingredients.  Many, if not most, of the properties of the whole medication may be very different than the properties of the active ingredients -- e.g. the medication is pill-shaped, has a sweet coating, is made mostly of inert materials, etc.  In a case such as that, the pill stands in the #$mainFunctionalComponent relationship to the portion of drug that is the active ingredient.  Accordingly, #$activeIngredients is a specialization of this predicate.")
(comment packagedProductTypePrimaryProductType "(#$packagedProductTypePrimaryProductType TYPE1 TYPE2) means that all instances of the product type TYPE1 have some portion of TYPE2 as their primary product.  For example, the collection of boxes of staples have the individual staples/rows of staples as their primary product.  Note this does not entail that instances of TYPE1 are primarily composed of TYPE2 as the volume or mass of the packaging materials of TYPE1 may exceed that of the primary product it wraps.  Typically TYPE2 will be an instance of #$ExistingStuffType, but this is not required.")
(comment componentInSystem-FunctionalRoleTypeType "(#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRoleTypeType SYSTEM-TYPE TYPE) means that every instance of SYSTEM-TYPE has some instance of TYPE that plays a functional role within the system.  The is shorthand for <code>(#$relationAllExists #$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole X Y)</code>")
(comment provisioningOf "(#$provisioningOf THING TYPE) means that TYPE is the collection of provisionings of THING.")
(comment NetworkHardwareChassis "This is the collection of network hardware chassis ... i.e. the collection of containers to which network hardware like routers and switches can be mounted.")
(comment ComputerNetworkDevicePowerSupply "The collection of all computer network device power supplies. A type of #$PowerSupply and #$ComputerHardwareItem. The collection #$ComputerPowerSupply is a #$ComputerHardwareDeviceType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment Transceiver "The collection of 
#$CommunicationDevices which have as parts both transmitters and receivers which are combined into a single unit or housing.")
(comment ComputerNetworkProduct "This collection of technology artifacts designed for computer networks like routers, switches, ethernet cables.  This collection also includes groups of items sold as units, e.g self-install kits, etc.")
(comment OpticalTransceiver-Computer "The collection of transceivers in which the network traffic is carried by light.")
(comment totalNumberOfSpecifiedComponentsOfTypeAssociatedWithSystemType "(#$totalNumberOfSpecifiedComponentsOfTypeAssociatedWithSystemType TYPE1 TYPE2 NUM)</code> means that it is specified (in the context) that there are NUM instances of TYPE2 that are associated as either components or subcomponents that are provisionable.")
(comment NetworkSwitchChassis "This is the collection of network switch chassis ... i.e. the collection of containers in which switches and assorted peripherals are mounted.")
(comment typeQuantityPredHasInstanceCorrelate "(#$typeQuantityPredHasInstanceCorrelate TYPE-PRED INSTANCE-PRED) means that INSTANCE-PRED is a #$QuantitySlot and (typically) a more general instance level version of TYPE-PRED.  In most cases (TYPE-PRED ARG1 QUANTITY) will entail (#$relationAllInstance INSTANCE-PRED ARG1 QUANTITY).")
(comment ComputerCodeExpression "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which serve as identifying expressions for other objects within a designated scope.")
(comment ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract "The collection of all #$AbstractInformationStructures that can be considered containers or sites used for storing information.")
(comment l-ValueInComputerCodeStatement "(#$l-ValueInComputerCodeBlock EXPRESSION LOCATION BLOCK) means that, within the scope of the #$ComputerCodeBlock BLOCK, the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION indicates the #$ComputerCodeLocation-Abstract LOCATION.")
(comment expressionAssignedInNameAssignment "(#$expressionAssignedInNameAssignment ASSIGNMENT EXPRESSION) means that the #$ComputerCodeExpression instance, EXPRESSION, is assigned a value or location in ASSIGNMENT.")
(comment locationAssignedInNameAssignment "(#$locationAssignedInNameAssignment ASSIGNMENT LOC) means that LOC is the #$ComputerCodeLocation-Abstract assigned to some #$ComputerCodeExpression in the #$LocationAssignment-ProgramAction ASSIGNMENT.")
(comment scopeOfNameAssignment "(#$scopeOfNameAssignment ASSIGNMENT BLOCK) means that BLOCK is the #$ComputerCodeBlock which constitutes the scope for the assignation of expression value or location that occurs in ASSIGNMENT.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatement "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that specify an encapsulated procedure with correspondingly scoped value and location assignments for instances of #$ComputerCodeExpression.")
(comment Waterfowl "The collection of all waterfowl.")
(comment Anatidae "The collection of birds in the Anatidae family. This family of birds includes ducks, geese and swans.")
(comment middleCharacter "<code>(#$middleCharacter CHAR ODD-STRING)</code> means that the middle character of the odd length string ODD-STRING is given by the single character string CHAR.  For example, (#$middleCharacter ''F'' ''JFK'')")
(comment NameAssignment-ComputerProgramRelated "The collection of all #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvents wherein a #$ComputerCodeExpression (the #$expressionAssignedInNameAssignment) is either assigned to a #$ComputerCodeLocation-Abstract or is assigned a value.")
(comment LocationAssignment-ProgramAction "The collection of all instances of #$NameAssignment-ComputerProgramRelated wherein there is some #$locationAssignedInNameAssignment. ")
(comment ValueAssignment-NamingSomething "The collection of all instances of #$NameAssignment-ComputerProgramRelated wherein there is some #$valueAssignedInNameAssignment.")
(comment valueAssignedInNameAssignment "(#$valueAssignedInNameAssignment ASSIGNMENT VALUE) means that VALUE is assigned as the value of some #$ComputerCodeExpression in the #$ValueAssignment-NamingSomething ASSIGNMENT.")
(comment r-ValueInComputerCodeStatement "(#$r-ValueInComputerCodeBlock EXPRESSION THING BLOCK) means that, within the scope of the #$ComputerCodeBlock BLOCK, the #$ComputerCodeExpression is assigned the value THING.")
(comment BiologicalFamily "A collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions below #$BiologicalFamily (or #$BiologicalSubfamily) and above #$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment codeSpecifiesNoProgramActionOfType "(#$codeSpecifiesNoProgramActionOfType CODE ACT-TYPE) means that the structure of code is such that, other things being equal, if CODE is executed in a normal run-time environment (see #$codeExecuted), no #$ProgramAction of type ACTION-TYPE will be part (#$subEvents) of the execution.")
(comment codeSpecifiesCountProgramActionsOfType "(#$codeSpecifiesCountProgramActionsOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE N) means that, other things being equal, the structure of CODE is such that a normal execution of CODE (see #$codeExecuted) will contain exactly N instances of ACTION-TYPE as #$subEvents.")
(comment nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValue "(#$nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValue CODE ACTION-TYPE N SIT-PRED THING) means that CODE has a structure such that, other things being equal, the Nth occurrence of an instance of ACTION-TYPE in a normal execution of CODE will feature THING in the situational role SIT-PRED.")
(comment nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithNoValueForParameter "(#$nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithNoValueForParameter CODE ACTION-TYPE N SIT-PRED) means that the structure of CODE is such that, other things being equal, an ordinary execution of CODE will feature no agent in the situation role of SIT-PRED in the Nth instance of ACTION-TYPE occuring in the execution. ")
(comment nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValueOtherThan "(#$nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValueOtherThan CODE ACTION-TYPE N SIT-PRED THING) means that the structure of CODE is such that, other things being equal, anything that plays the situational role SIT-PRED in the Nth occurrence of type ACTION-TYPE in a normal execution of CODE will be #$different from THING.  I.e., the structure of CODE is such that THING can*not* ordinarily play the role SIT-PRED in the Nth occurrence of SIT-TYPE that occurs as part of any normal execution of CODE.")
(comment nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValueOfType "(#$nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithParameterValueOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE N SIT-PRED VALUE-TYPE) means that the structure of CODE is such that, other things being equal, the Nth instance of ACTION-TYPE that occurs as part of any ordinary execution of CODE will feature an instance of VALUE-TYPE in the situational role SIT-PRED.")
(comment nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithNoValueOfTypeOnParameter "(#$nthProgramActionTypeSpecifiedWithNoValueOfTypeOnParameter CODE ACTION-TYPE N SIT-PRED VALUE-TYPE) means that the structure of CODE is such that, other things being equal, the Nth occurrence of ACTION-TYPE that happens as part of any normal execution of CODE will feature *no* instance of VALUE-TYPE in the situational role SIT-PRED.")
(comment Selection-Generic "Instances of #$Selection-Generic are events in which one or more items from among a group of candidates is chosen for, or happens to become subject to, different treatment than the others.  Note that instances may involve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.  #$Selection-Generic occurs when lighting strikes a forest, and two trees out of hundreds are hit. #$Selection-Generic also occurs when one person of three is elected mayor.")
(comment SelectionOfMultipleItems-Generic "Instances of #$SelectionOfMultipleItems-Generic are events in which two or more items from among a group of candidates isare chosen for, or happen to become subject to, a different outcome than the others.  Note that instances may involve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.")
(comment selectionPool "(#$selectionPool SEL GROUP) means that GROUP is the group of items from among which one or more items is chosen for, or happens to become subject to, particular treatment in the #$Selection-Generic event SEL.")
(comment thingSelected "(#$thingSelected SEL THING) means that THING is one of the items chosen for, or becoming subject to, particular treatment in the #$Selection-Generic event SEL.")
(comment groupSelected "(#$groupSelected SEL GROUP) means that GROUP is the group of items chosen for, or becoming subject to, a particular outcome in the #$SelectionOfMultipleItems-Generic event SEL.")
(comment RandomSelectionEvent "Instances of #$RandomSelectionEvent are events in which one or more items from among a group of candidates is randomly chosen for, or happens to become subject to, a different outcome than the others.  Note that instances may involve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.  Choosing a playing card from a shuffled (randomized) deck would be an instance of #$RandomSelectionEvent, but so would the ''choice'' of heads or tails for a lost coin that fell onto the ground.")
(comment RandomSelectionOfOneFromGroup "Instances of #$RandomSelectionEventOfOneFromGroup are events in which one item from among a group of candidates is randomly chosen for, or happens to become subject to, a different outcome than the others.  Note that instances may involve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.  The probability that a particular item is randomly selected from a group of size N is 1/N.  Likewise, the number of possible single choices from a group of N is N.")
(comment RandomSelectionOfMultipleItemsFromGroup "Instances of #$RandomSelectionOfMultipleItemsFromGroup are events in which more than one item from among a group of candidates is randomly chosen for, or happens to become subject to, a different outcome than the others.  Note that instances mayinvolve, but do not necessarily involve purposeful action on the part of an agent.  The probability that any particular combination of M items are randomly selected from among a group of N is [(N-M)!*M!]/N! .  Likewise, the number of possible combinations of M items randomly selected from a group of N is N!/[(N-M)!*M!] .")
(comment selectionPoolMembers "(#$selectionPoolMembers SEL THING) means that THING is one of the items from among which one or more items is chosen for, or happens to become subject to, a particular outcome in the #$Selection-Generic event SEL.")
(comment selectionPoolMembers "(#$selectionPoolMembers SEL THING) means that THING is one of the items from among which one or more items is chosen for, or happens to become subject to, particular treatment in the #$Selection-Generic event SEL.")
(comment MemCpyOperation "The collection of all #$ProgramActions that qualify as memory copy operations in program executions.")
(comment sourceOfMemCopy "(#$sourceOfMemCopy COPY SOURCE) means that SOURCE is the source buffer of the #$MemCopyOperation COPY.")
(comment destinationOfMemCopy "(#$destinationOfMemCopy COPY DESTINATION) means that DESTINATION is the destination buffer of the #$MemCopyOperation COPY.")
(comment codeHasConditionOnSpecifiedActionParameters "(#$codeHasConditionOnSpecifiedActionParameters CODE ACTION-TYPE N BIN-PRED SIT-PRED-1 SIT-PRED-2) means that the structure of CODE is such that the relation BIN-PRED will hold between any two agents that satisfy the parameters SIT-PRED-1 and SIT-PRED-2 in the Nth occurrence of an instance of ACTION-TYPE that occurs during any normal exection of CODE, for at least the duration of the ACTION-TYPE instance.")
(comment codeLacksConditionOnSpecifiedActionParameters "(#$codeLacksConditionOnSpecifiedActionParameters CODE ACTION-TYPE N BIN-PRED SIT-PRED-1 SIT-PRED-2) means that the structure of CODE is such that it is consistent for the relation BIN-PRED not to hold between two agents that satisfy the parameters SIT-PRED-1 and SIT-PRED-2 in the Nth occurrence of an instance of ACTION-TYPE that occurs during any normal exection of CODE, during the time that the ACTION-TYPE instance occurs.")
(comment Bedbug "The collection of bedbugs, a type of true bug.  Bedbugs are small insects that are notorious for infesting mattresses and feasting unnoticed on sleeping people.")
(comment StinkBug "The collection of stink bugs, a type of true bug.  Stink bugs are capable of emitting a foul-smelling excretion.")
(comment AgriculturalPest "A specialization of #$Vermin.  #$AgriculturalPest is the collection of organisms that are notorious for posing a threat to agricultural crops.")
(comment BrownMarmoratedStinkBug "The collection of brown marmorated stink bugs, which are agricultural pests.")
(comment Larva "A collection of stages in the lives of individual organisms; a subset of #$BiologicalStageOfDevelopment.  Each element of #$Larva is a stage of a metamorphic invertebrate immediately after hatching, during which it frequently has a body form very different from the #$AdultAnimal.  Examples include #$Caterpillar, the #$Larva of instances of #$Lepidopteran, which are wingless and often wormlike.")
(comment Nymph "An instance of #$LifeStageType.  Each instance of #$Nymph is a young insect.  Nyphs are distinct from larva, in that they more closely resemble their adult forms.")
(comment relationInstanceNotExists "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to a thing, INST1, and some collection.  <code>(#$relationInstanceNotExists BINPRED INST1 COL2)</code> means that no instance <code>INST2</code> of <code>COL2</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$not
    (#$and
      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)
      (#$isa ?INST2 COL2)))
</pre>
<p>
So #$relationInstanceNotExists (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.
<p>
For example, '(#$relationInstanceNotExists #$owns #$Pittman #$Diamond-Gem)' means that #$Pittman owns no diamonds.")
(comment relationNotExistsInstance "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to a thing, INST2, and some collection.  <code>(#$relationNotExistsInstance BINPRED COL1 INST2)</code> means that no instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>COL1</code> is such that <code>(BINPRED INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$not
    (#$and
      (BINPRED INST1 INST2)
      (#$isa ?INST1 COL1)))
</pre>
<p>
So #$relationNotExistsInstance (and its defining axiom; see #$expansion) enables this common type of rule to be stated more tersely.
<p>
For example, '(#$relationNotExistsInstance #$performedBy #$BalletDancing #$Pittman)' means that #$Pittman does not perform any ballet dancing.")
(comment LocusFn "<code>(#$LocusFn STR)</code> denotes the genetic locus at the location specified by the string <code>STR</code> (where <code>STR</code> is written according to the standard nomenclature, and either specifies a single location, such as \"6p21.3\", or a range of locations, such as \"11q1.4-q2.1\").")
(comment equatorOfSpheroid "A specialization of the binary predicate #$parallelOfSpheroid (q.v.) that relates any #$Spheroid that is not a perfect #$Sphere to its unique equator.  <code>(#$equatorOfSpheroid EQUATOR SPHEROID)</code> means that <code>EQUATOR</code> is an #$AtLeastApproximatelyACircle that is a section of <code>SPHEROID</code> centered at the same point as it, and perpendicular to <code>SPHEROID</code>'s #$axisOfSurfaceOfRevolution. 
<p>
See also #$greatCircleOfSphere.")
(comment AtLeastApproximatelyAnEllipse "A specialization of #$RoundObject (q.v.).  This is the collection of all one-dimensional space regions that are at least approximately elliptical.")
(comment AspatialInformationStore-Location "A specialization of #$AspatialInformationStore.  Each instance of #$AspatialInformationStore-Location contains information about the location of something.")
(comment specifiesLocationOf "<code>(#$specifiesLocationOf INFO IND)</code> means that <code>INFO</code> specifies the location of <code>IND</code>.")
(comment GeneLocusFn "<code>(#$GeneLocusFn GENE-TYPE)</code> denotes the default locus of the specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit, <code>GENE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment locusOfGene "<code>(#$locusOfGene GENE LOCUS)</code> means that the locus of <code>GENE-TYPE</code> is <code>LOCUS</code>.")
(comment relativePositionToTypeAlongPath "<code>(#$relativePositionToTypeAlongPath LOC TYPE PATH)</code> means that LOC is a location that is determined relative to instances of TYPE on PATH.  For example, <code>(#$relativePositionToTypeAlongPath Locus-Genetic-101 #$Gene-HereditaryUnit Chromosome-101) </code> means that <code>Locus-Genetic-101</code> is a location that is determined relative to the instances of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit that are on the path <code>Chromosome-101</code>.")
(comment Locus "A #$Locus is the location of a specific gene on a chromosome.")
(comment nucleicAcidSequence "<code>(#$nucleicAcidSequence ACID-MOLECULE LIST)</code> means that <code>LIST</code> is the  exact sequence of nucleotides that comprise <code>ACID-MOLECULE</code>.")
(comment lengthOfMemCopy "(#$lengthOfMemCopy COPY LENGTH) means that the number of characters copied in the #$MemCopyOperation COPY is LENGTH.")
(comment codeSpecifiesUndesirableActionOfType "Where ACTION-TYPE is a specialization of #$UndesirableProgramAction, (#$codeSpecifiesUndesirableActionOfType CODE ACTION-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, executing CODE in a normal run-time environment will result in an execution that includes an instance of ACTION-TYPE as a sub-event (#$subEvents).")
(comment CharacterLengthOfMemoryLocationFn "A #$UnaryFunction used to reference and evaluate the length of particular locations in abstract machine memory.  Where MEMLOC is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract, (#$CharacterLengthOfMemoryLocationFn MEMLOC) in a given context returns the number of characters that can be held in MEMLOC.")
(comment charLengthOfMemoryLocation "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CharacterLengthOfMemoryLocationFn.  Where MEMLOC is a #$ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract, (#$charLengthOfMemoryLocation MEMLOC NUM) means that the number of characters that can be held in MEMLOC is NUM.")
(comment SettingAMemoryLocationLength "The collection of all #$ProgramActions that set the length of some instance of #$ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract to be a certain value.")
(comment memLocationLengthSet "(#$memLocationLengthSet SETTING LENGTH) means that the length to which the instance of #$ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract is set in SETTING is LENGTH.")
(comment memLocationOfSetting "(#$memLocationOfSetting SETTING MEMLOC) means that the #$ComputerMemoryLocation-Abstract whose location is set in SETTING is MEMLOC.")
(comment G1Phase "The first of the three phases of interphase (see #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle), G1 phase is a period of growth that occurs prior to the S (synthesis of DNA) phase.")
(comment SPhase "The second of the three phases of interphase (see #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle), S phase is the phase when DNA synthesis (see #$Replication-DNA) occurs inside the nucleous of the cell.")
(comment G2Phase "The last of the three phases of interphase (see #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle), G2 phase is a period of growth that occurs subsequent to the S (synthesis of DNA) phase.")
(disjointWith CellDivision Interphase-Generic)
(disjointWith MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle Interphase-Generic)
(disjointWith Meiosis InterphaseOfMeiosis)
(disjointWith InterphaseOfMeiosis EukaryoticCellCycle)
(comment InterphaseOfMeiosis "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Instances of #$InterphaseOfMeiosis occur in #$EukaryoticCells just before they enter #$Meiosis.  During this period the cell's chromosomes and centrosomes duplicate.")
(comment Interphase-Generic "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell.  Instances of #$Interphase-Generic are periods between times when a cell is actually dividing, during which the cell is  replicating its genetic material (e.g., #$Replication-DNA) and possibly growing (see #$CellEnlargementEvent).  Specializations of #$Interphase-Generic include #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle and #$InterphaseOfMeiosis.")
(comment Gametogenesis-Meiotic "A specialization of #$BiologicalProductionEvent.  Each instance of #$Gametogenesis-Meiotic is an event in which at least one #$Gamete is created.  Furthermore, such #$Gametes are the direct result of #$Meiosis.  This is the type of gametogenesis that occurs in humans and all other animals.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatement-Executable "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement which are executable code.")
(disjointWith ComputerCodeStatement-Declaration ComputerCodeStatement-Executable)
(comment ComputerCodeStatement-Declaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements which declare parameter values.")
(comment parameterSetViaDeclaration "(#$parameterSetViaDeclaration STATEMENT PRED DECLARATION) means that the value of PRED on STATEMENT is specified by DECLARATION.")
(comment ComputerCodeVariable "The collection of all computer code variables, qua #$AbstractInformationStructures.")
(disjointWith ComputerCodeConstant ComputerCodeVariable)
(comment ComputerCodeConstant "The collection of all computer code constants, qua #$AbstractInformationStructures.")
(comment CodeConstantNamedFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used in referring to instances of #$ComputerCodeConstant.  (#$CodeConstantNamedFn NAME PROGRAM) denotes the #$ComputerCodeConstant that NAME identifies within the scope of PROGRAM.")
(comment codeConstantName "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CodeConstantNamedFn.  Where NAME is a #$CharacterString and PROGRAM is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS, (#$codeConstantName NAME PROGRAM CONSTANT) means that CONSTANT is the #$ComputerCodeConstant that NAME identifies within the scope of PROGRAM.")
(comment codeConstantValue "(#$codeConstantValue CONSTANT VALUE) means that VALUE is the value associated with CONSTANT via a #$ConstantDeclaration in the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS wherein CONSTANT appears.")
(comment CodeVariableNamedFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to refer to #$ComputerCodeVariables.  (#$CodeVariableNamedFn NAME CODE-BLOCK) denotes the variable that NAME references within the scope of CODE-BLOCK.")
(comment codeVariableName "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CodeVariableNamedFn.  Where NAME is a #$CharacterString and BLOCK is a #$ComputerCodeBlock, (#$codeVariableName NAME BLOCK VAR) means that VAR is the variable that NAME references within the scope of BLOCK.")
(comment objectFoundInLocation "A #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate and specialization of #$inRegion (q.v.).  <code>(#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ LOC)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has the location <code>LOC</code>, in the sense that at least some part of <code>OBJ</code> is at <code>LOC</code> (as long as <code>LOC</code> itself is not part of  <code>OBJ</code>).
<p>
<code>OBJ</code> might or might not be a physical part (see #$physicalDecompositions) of <code>LOC</code>.  Thus, both (#$objectFoundInLocation #$MountEverest #$HimalayaMountains) and (#$parts #$HimalayaMountains #$MountEverest) are true, and both (#$objectFoundInLocation #$PietaStatue-Michelangelo #$StPetersBasilica) and (#$not (#$parts #$StPetersBasilica #$PietaStatue-Michelangelo)) are true.
<p>
However, <code>LOC</code> must <i>not</i> be a proper part of <code>OBJ</code>: (#$objectFoundInLocation #$HimalayaMountains #$MountEverest) is false.")
(comment CellTypeByChromosomalDuplicationStatus "A specialization of #$TimeDependentCollection that forms a facet on the collection of eukaryotic cells (see #EukaryoticCell). Instances are collections of cells whose instances are characterized by whether their chromosomes are unduplicated (see #$UnduplicatedChromosome), duplicated (see #$DuplicatedChromosome), or partially duplicated (see #$PartiallyDuplicatedChromosome).")
(comment Cell-ChromosomesDuplicated "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  All of the chromosomes of each instance are duplicated (see #$DuplicatedChromosome).")
(comment Cell-ChromosomesUnduplicated "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  All of the chromosomes of each instance are unduplicated (see #$UnduplicatedChromosome).")
(comment Cell-ChromosomesPartiallyDuplicated "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  All of the chromosomes of each instance are partially duplicated (see #$PartiallyDuplicatedChromosome).")
(comment ChromosomeTypeByDuplicationLevel "A specializaton of #$TimeDependentCollection that forms a partition on the collection of chromosomes (see #$Chromosome).  Instances are collections of chromosomes whose instances are characterized by whether or not they are duplicated (consist of two sister chromatids), unduplicated (consist of a single DNA strand), or are somewhere during the process of #$ChromosomalDuplication and are thus partially duplicated.")
(comment Gametocyte "#$Gametocytes are eukaryotic germ cells that have begun #$Meiosis.")
(comment PrimaryGametocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$PrimaryGametocyte is a gametocyte that has entered #$MeiosisI.")
(comment SecondaryGametocyte "A specialization of #$Gametocyte.  Each instance of #$SecondaryGametocyte is a gametocyte that is the output of some #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(disjointWith DiploidCell SecondaryGametocyte)
(comment PrimaryGermCell "A specialization of #$GermCell.  Each instance of #$PrimaryGermCell is a eukaryotic germ cell that is formed early in the life of a fetus and which can become a #$Gametogonium.")
(disjointWith Gametogonium PrimaryGermCell)
(comment Spermatocytogenesis "Each instance of #$Spermatocytogenesis is an event in which at least one #$PrimarySpermatocyte is created.")
(comment nthAtomicStatementOfStatement "(#$nthStatementOfCodeBlock BLOCK STATEMENT N) means that, of the 'top level' coding elements (#$ComputerCodeBlocks) composing BLOCK, STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement appearing in the Nth position in BLOCK.")
(comment ComputerCodeDeclarationType "A type level #$Collection and a collection instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance of #$ComputerCodeDeclarationType is a collection of #$AbstractInformationStructures whose instances are distinguished in virtue of being computer code that declares a value for some other abstract computer code object (e.g., a function, a constant, or a variable).")
(comment ComputerCodeInvocationType "A type-level #$Collection and a collection instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance of #$ComputerCodeInvocationType is a collection of #$ComputerCodeBlocks whose instances invoke some characteristic type of executable code object.")
(comment ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable "The collection of all executable code statements (#$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable) that invoke executable functions.")
(comment MachineTargetStatement-Declaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are target code declarations.")
(comment ConstantDeclaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are constant declarations.")
(comment VariableDeclaration "The collecion of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Declaration wherein a value is specified for a variable according to the normal interpretation of the code.")
(comment parameterSetViaInvocation "(#$parameterSetViaInvocation STATEMENT PRED EXECUTABLE) means that the value of PRED on STATEMENT is determined by executing the #$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable EXECUTABLE.")
(comment standardArithmeticOperationOfFunctionInvocation "(#$standardArithmeticOperationOfFunctionInvocation INVOCATION FUNCTION) means that the executable function call (#$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) INVOCATION calls the standard arithmetic function FUNCTION.")
(comment argumentSetViaDeclaration "(#$argumentSetViaDeclaration EXECUTABLE EXPRESSION DECLARATION) means that the value of the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION as it occurs in the #$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable EXECUTABLE is set by the #$ComputerCodeStatement-Declaration DECLARATION.")
(comment ExecutableResultFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used in representing and reasoning about the results of evaluating executable code.  Where EXECUTABLE is a #$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable, and FUNCTION-DEC is a #$FunctionDeclaration (#$ExecutableResultFn EXECUTABLE FUNCTION-DEC) refers to the result of invoking EXECUTABLE in the context of FUNCTION-DEC.")
(comment ComputerCodeParameterDocumentationPredicate "A class of #$TernaryPredicates whose instances are used in keeping track of how a #$ComputerCodeInvocationParameter or a #$ComputerCodeExpression is assigned a value within a #$ComputerCode context.")
(comment FunctionDeclaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that declare functions.")
(comment Prophase-Generic "#$Prophase-Generic is the generalization of the prophase steps of mitosis (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle), meiosis I, and meiosis II (see #$FirstMeioticCellDivision and #$SecondMeioticCellDivision). Each instance of #$Prophase-Generic is a sub-event of a cell division event (either mitotic or meiotic) during which a spindle assembly forms.  Chromosomes condense if they haven't already.  The nuclear membrane and nucleolus dissolve if they are present.  Instances of #$Prophase-Generic are the first stages of the cell division of which they are a part. ")
(comment FormalArgumentDeclaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are individual formal argument declarations; i.e., each instance of #$FormalArgumentDeclaration is a declaration of a single formal argument.")
(comment DataDirectiveDeclaration "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are data directive declarations.")
(comment numericComparatorOfFunctionInvocation "(#$numericComparatorOfFunctionInvocation INVOCATION COMPARATOR) means that the executable function call (#$ComptuerFunctionInvocation-Executable) INVOCATION applies the #$NumericComparisonPredicate to a list of arguments (the #$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation) as a Boolean operator.")
(comment codeLacksConditionOnOperationType "(#$codeLacksConditionOnOperation CODE ACTION-TYPE BIN-PRED SIT-PRED-1 SIT-PRED-2) means that the structure of CODE is such that an occurrence of ACTION-TYPE will feature in any normal execution of CODE, and nothing requires that the relation BIN-PRED holds between agents satisfying the parameters SIT-PRED-1 and SIT-PRED-2 in such an occurence of ACTION-TYPE.")
(comment Gametid "#$Gametids are eukaryotic germ cells that are the product of the meiosis of a #$Gametocyte.  In some contexts, gametids are considered to be gametes, but to become mature gametes (see #$Gamete-Mature) a gametid typically has to undergo a maturation process in the final stages of #$Gametogenesis-Meiotic.")
(comment Handcuffs "The collection of handcuffs, which are devices used to restrain people by the wrists.")
(comment ComputerCodeWithStructuralDeficiency "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which exhibit a deficiency in the abstract information structure that insures or risks undesirable program behavior at execution time.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency "A second-order faceting collection.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeWithStructuralDeficiency whose instances are deficient with respect to a shared set of salient features.")
(comment MitreCWEConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms which denote concepts which are referenced in the Mitre Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) ontology.")
(comment MitreCWEResearchViewConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms which denote concepts appearing in the 'Research View' of the Mitre Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) ontology.")
(comment MitreCWEResearchViewPillarConstant "The collection of #$CycLTerms denoting concepts which are considered 'pillars' of the 'Research View' of the Mitre COmmon Weakness Enumeration (CWE) ontology.")
(comment mitreCWEDesignation "(#$mitreCWEDesignation CONCEPT NAME) means that NAME is the name Mitre uses to denote CONCEPT in the Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) ontology.")
(comment mitreCWEID "(#$mitreCWEID CONCEPT ID) means that ID is the numeric ID whereby Mitre encodes CONCEPT in the Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) ontology.")
(comment codeHasDeficiency "(#$codeHasDeficiency CODE DEFICIENCY-TYPE) means that CODE belongs to the class DEFICIENCY-TYPE.")
(comment codeDeficiencyEntailsUndesirableActionType "(#$codeDeficiencyEntailsUndesrableActionType DEFICIENCY-TYPE ACTION-TYPE) means that if an instance of #$ComputerCode that belongs to the deficiency class (#$codeHasDeficiency) DEFICIENCY-TYPE is executed in a typical run-time environment then, other things being equal, the occurance of an instance of the #$UndesirableProgramAction type ACTION-TYPE is certain or virtually certain.")
(comment codeDeficiencyLiableToUndesirableActionType "(#$codeDeficiencyLiableToUndesirableActionType DEFICIENCY-TYPE ACTION-TYPE) means that if an instance of #$ComputerCode that belongs to the deficiency class (#$codeHasDeficiency) DEFICIENCY-TYPE is executed in a typical run-time environment then, other things being equal, there is a medium-to-very-high likelihood of an occurrence fo an instance of the #$UndesirableProgramAction type ACTION-TYPE.")
(comment conditionEntailsCodeDeficiency "(#$conditionEntailsCodeDeficiency CONDITION DEFICIENCY-TYPE) means that any instances of #$ComputerCode which satisfies the formula given by CONDITION will, under ordinary circumstances, belong to the deficiency class DEFICIENCY-TYPE: i.e., CONDITION is a sufficient condition (other things being equal) for membership in DEFICIENCY type.")
(comment codeDeficiencyEntailsCondition "(#$codeDeficiencyEntailsCondition DEFICIENCY-TYPE CONDITION) means that an instance of #$ComputerCode belongs to the deficiency class DEFICIENCY-TYPE only if it satisfies CONDITION: i.e., CONDITION is a necessary condition (other things being equal) for a piece of code's instantiating DEFICIENCY-TYPE.")
(comment CodeWithCodingStandardsViolation "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that do not follow certain heuristics or best practices for development with respect to features exhibited within the code.")
(comment CodeWithExceptionHandlingDeficiency "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that do not make provision, or make improper provision, for handling exception conditions that may occur during normal execution.")
(comment CodeThatImproperlyAccesesIndexableResource "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that fail to restrict, or otherwise incorrectly restrict operations that occur within the boundaries of a resource accessed with an index or pointer, due to features exhibited by the code structure.")
(comment CodeWithDeficientResourceControl "All instances of #$ComputerCode that fail to maintain or incorrectly maintain control over a resource through its lifetime of creation, use, and release, due to a structural feature that the code exhibits.")
(comment CodeWithImproperMessageWFFCheck "All instances of #$ComputerCode that either fail to implement or incorrectly implement well-formedness checking of structured messages prior to transmission from an upstream component to a downstream component, due to features exhibited by the code.")
(comment CodeWithImproperDataStructureWFFCheck "All instances of #$ComputerCode that either fail to implement or incorrectly implement well-formedness chcking of structured data prior to transmission from an upstream component to a downstream component, due to features exhibited by the code.")
(comment CodeWithIncorrectComputation "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode such that the code specifies a computation guaranteed (other things being equal) to generate an incorrect result.")
(comment CodeWithInsufficientComparison "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode such that the code either fails to perform an indicated comparison check, performs a comparison check that fails to include one or more indicated factors, or performs a comparison check that checks one or more factors incorrectly.")
(comment CodeWithInsufficientControlFlowManagement "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that fail to specify adequate control flow relative to execution, resulting in vulnerability to external and possibly malicious control flow modification.")
(comment CodeSubjectToInteractionError "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode such that there is some other instance of #$ComputerCode, or class of such instances, where the code is expected to execute in an environment that entails interaction with the other code (or a member of the other code class), and where the interaction is liable to generate a run-time error.")
(comment CodeWithProtectionMechanismFailure "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that either do not use or incorrectly use an indicated protection mechanism to guard against directed attack.")
(comment CodeInsufficientlyRandomized "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that specify insufficiently randomized values relative to security contexts where randomization is indicated, e.g., for generating encryption keys.")
(comment typeConnects "<code>(#$typeConnects TYPE OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that an instance <code>INS</code> of <code>TYPE</code> is such that <code>(#$connectionJoins INS OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>.")
(comment agentCareerDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$agentBioDataSentence AGENT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact that is considered by the salient audience to constitute biographical information about AGENT in the current context.")
(comment haveThisInCommon "A predicate used to identify what facts are commonly true of distinct objects, by relating ojects in a set or collection to a sentence template into which terms denoting those objects can be substituted, producing a true sentence in each case. <code>(#$haveThisInCommon SET FORMULA)</code> means that substituting each element of SET in for the designated meta-variable :TERM in FORMULA will result in a #$CycLSentence-Askable that is #$True.  For example, <code>(#$haveThisInCommon (#$TheSet #$Dog #$Cat #$Emu) (#$and (#$isa :TERM #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls :TERM #$Animal)))</code> means that replacing #$Dog, #$Cat, and #$Emu for :TERM in the arg2 will result in three sentences, (#$and (#$isa #$Dog #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Dog #$Animal)), (#$and (#$isa #$Cat #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Cat #$Animal)), and (#$and (#$isa #$Emu #$FirstOrderCollection) (#$genls #$Emu #$Animal)) that are all true.")
(comment Metaphase-Generic "#$Metaphase-Generic is the generalization of the metaphase steps of mitosis (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle), meiosis I, and meiosis II (see #$FirstMeioticCellDivision and #$SecondMeioticCellDivision). Each instance of #$Metaphase-Generic is a sub-event of a cell division event (either mitotic or meiotic) during which the chromosomes line up on the metaphase plate (see #$metaphasePlateOfCell).  In the case of #$MetaphaseI in the first meiotic division, chromosomes line up as tetrads (see #$Tetrad-Chromosomal).")
(comment StackBasedBufferOverflow "The collection of all instances of #$BufferOverflow occasioned by the fact that the executing code allocates the buffer being overwritten on the stack.")
(comment HeapBasedBufferOverflow "The collection of all #$BufferOverflows occasioned by the fact that the executing code allocates the overwritten buffer in the heap portion of memory.")
(disjointWith StackBasedBufferOverflow HeapBasedBufferOverflow)
(comment CodeTypeWithPropensityForActionTypeFn "A collection denoting function used for reifying classes of computer code.  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning, (#$CodeTypeWithPropensityForActionTypeFn PROCESS-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if they are executed in a typical run-time environment, have a higher-than-medium likelihood of resulting in an instance of PROCESS-TYPE occurring during the execution.")
(comment codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CodeTypeWithPropensityForActionTypeFn.  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning, (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType CODE-TYPE PROCESS-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if they are executed in a typical run-time environment, have a higher-than-medium likelihood of resulting in an instance of PROCESS-TYPE occurring during the execution.")
(comment CodeTypeThatSpecifiesActionTypeFn "A collection-denoting function that is used to refer to specializations of #$ComputerCode based on the type of action that instances of the type are guaranteed to instantiate at run time.  Thus, where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of #$ComputerProcessRunning, (#$CodeTypeThatSpecifiesActionTypeFn PROCESS-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if executed in a normal run-time environment, will result in an occurrence of PROCESS-TYPE.")
(comment codeTypeThatSpecifiesActionType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of CodeTypeThatSpecifiesActionTypeFn.  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of #$ComputerProcessRunning, (#$codeTypeThatSpecifiesActionType CODE-TYPE PROCESS-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode which, if executed in a normal run-time environment, will result in an occurrence of PROCESS-TYPE.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByLanguage "A #$FacetingCollectionType and a #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance is defined relative to a given #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, and is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode authored in that language.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByLanguageFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used in faceting #$ComputerCode by #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage. Where LANGUAGE is an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, (#$ComputerCodeTypeByLanguageFn LANGUAGE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that are authored in LANGUAGE.")
(comment languageCharacterizesCodeType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of ComputerCodeTypeByLanguageFn. Where LANGUAGE is an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, (#$languageCharacterizesCodeType LANGUAGE CODE-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCode that are authored in LANGUAGE.")
(comment bitWidthOfInvocation "A general predicate for linking executable code statements (instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable) to the bit widths they specify.")
(comment ExecutableArithmeticOperation "The class of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are #$ExecutableArithmeticOperations.  As a rule, instances of this class in C-- (CMinusMinus-ProgrammingLanguage) are code statements containing an equals (=) sign relating two expressions.")
(comment bitWidthOfExecutableArithmeticOperation "A specialization of #$bitWidthOfInvocation: (#$bitWidthOfExecutableArithmeticOperation EXEC-OP WIDTH) means that the bit width specified for the #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation instance EXEC-OP is WIDTH.")
(comment symbolicNameOfExecutableArithmeticOperation "Where EXEC-OP is an #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation (#$symbolicNameOfExecutableArithmeticOperation EXEC-OP NAME-STRING) means that NAME-STRING is the symbolic name associated with the operation EXEC-OP.  By convention, this is the string appearing to the left of the equals sign (=) in the operation.")
(comment arithmeticFunctionOfExecutable "A general #$ComputerCodeInvocationParameter used to reference the arithmetic function invoked in an executable code statement.")
(comment arithmeticFunctionOfExecutableArithmeticOperation "(#$arithmeticFunctionOfExecutableArithmeticOperation EXEC-OP FUNCTION) means that FUNCTION is the #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars invoked by the #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation instance, EXEC-OP.")
(comment actualArgumentListOfExecutable "The most general #$ComputerCodeInvocationParameter used for attaching a list of arguments to an executable code statement (an instance of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Executable).")
(comment actualArgumentListOfExecutableArithmeticOperation "Where EXEC-OP is an #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation, (#$actualArgumentListOfExecutableArithmeticOperation EXEC-OP ARG-LIST) means that ARG-LIST is the list of arguments called by EXEC-OP.")
(comment statementIntroducesExpression "Where EXPRESSION is a #$ComputerCodeExpression, (#$statementIntroducesExpression STATEMENT EXPRESSION) means that STATEMENT is the instance of #$ComputerCodeStatement that introduces EXPRESSION.")
(comment LevelOfExpertise "A sub-collection of #$AgentCapacityQuantity. Each instance is some degree of expertise in an activity or subject matter.")
(comment hasExpertiseToDegree "(#$hasExpertiseToDegree AGT ACT-TYPE LEVEL) means that AGT (an instance of #$IntelligentAgent) can perform (#$performedBy) instances of  skilled activity ACT-TYPE at least at the level of expertise indicated by LEVEL.")
(comment TechnicalProductRelatedProblem "The collection of technical product related problems.  This is a very broad collection that ranges from corrupt registry entries in computers to malfunctioning hardware to problems with cell phones, etc.  Note that this also includes problems that are not necessarily problems intrinsic to the hardware or software like problems starting a program because of files installed by the user in an incorrect location.  In general, this covers all the sorts of problems one might expect a technical hardware or software help desk to help resolve.")
(comment TechnicalProductRelatedProblemRegardingFn "(#$TechnicalProductRelatedProblemRegardingFn THING) denotes the collection of #$TechnicalProductRelatedProblem associated with THING.  E.g. (#$TechnicalProductRelatedProblemRegardingFn MSWord) denotes the collection of problems associated with MSWord.")
(comment TechnologyProductSupportSession "The collection of all customer support sessions that deal with technology products (hardware or software).  Each instance of this collection is an activity primarily performed by the support representative where he or she attempts to diagnose the cause of the problem and propose or implement solutions for the problem encountered by the customer.")
(comment FinancialServicesAgreement "A subcollection of #$LegalAgreement.  Each instance of #$FinancialServicesAgreement is an agreement between two or more agents whereby some sort of financial service is provided to some of the parties by one or more of the other parties.  For example, one may contract with a brokerage firm to purchase X shares of stock in company Y under certain conditions.  Another example would be subscribing to a news service that provides various stock tickers, financial news feeds and dashboards, etc.  The latter type of service would typically be a subcollection of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing.")
(comment FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing "A subcollection of #$LegalAgreement.  Each instance of #$FinancialServicesAgreement is an agreement between two or more agents whereby some sort of ongoing financial service is provided to some of the parties by one or more of the other parties.  An example would be a subscription to a news service that provides various stock tickers, financial news feeds and dashboards, etc.  Another example would be an agreement with a financial adviser for ongoing consultation.")
(comment BloombergProfessionalService-Agreement "A subcollection of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing.  Each instance of this collection is a subscription to the Bloomberg Professional Service.  This service includes the use of certain hardware and software and allows users to place trades for financial products and monitor real time financial data including stock purchases, price quotes, news feeds, etc.")
(comment AdobeComputerProgram "Software products made by #$AdobeSystems.")
(comment IntegratedDevelopmentEnvironmentSoftware-Program "The collection of software packages that provide an integrated development environment (IDE) for programming languages or complex software environments.  IDE software typically tries to combine all the major functions associated with a particular programming environment into a tightly organized whole with a unified interface.")
(comment AquaFold-Company "Software company from Sunnyvale California.  they make database interface/IDE programs.  Their flagship product is #$AquaDataStudio-TheProgam.")
(comment ArtemisProjectManagementProgram "The collection of all instances of  #$ComputerProgram-CW that are in the \"Artemis\" family of products by Artemis International Solutions Corporation.")
(comment ArtemisInternationalSolutions-Company "A project management software company.")
(comment ActivationOfProductOrService "A specialization of #$MakingAnAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is the action taken to activate a particular service or program with respect to a particular device or artifact -- e.g. a cell phone, an internet device, a program copy.  Typically some major or main function of the device or program is inactive or has limited functionality before the activation.  Full functionality is only achieved after activation and is typically associated with an ongoing agreement that covers the length of the period during which the product's functionaity is available and the responsibilities of the agreeing parties.  \"Activations\" of services not associated with a particular artifact are not covered under this concept and are typically represented as either service events of some sort or agreements -- e.g. a periodical subscription is an agreement for the publisher to provide you with copies of or (in the case of online subscriptions) allow access to the periodical on an ongoing basis.  The \"activation\" in those cases would be the agreement between the publisher and the customer and would not be an instance of this collection.")
(comment ActivationOfProductFn "A unary function that takes a product type requiring activation such as a specific type of program copy or particular type of device like a cell phone and returns the subcollection of #$ActivationOfProductOrService that consists in just those instances of #$ActivationOfProductOrService that are activations of the product type in arg1.  E.g. (#$ActivationOfProductFn #$BlackBerry-Smartphone) is the collection of actions which are the activations of particular BlackBerrys.  See the corresponding predicate #$activationOfProductType.")
(comment Technology-ArtifactRequiringActivation "The collection of technology artifacts that require some sort of activation (see #$ActivationOfProductOrService) in order to have full functionality.")
(comment ElectronicTradingPlatform "The collection of all electronic trading platforms.  Also called \"trading turrets\".  A trading turret is an electronic device designed to aid the trading of stocks, bonds, etc.  Typically they can record transactions, provide authentication to trading services and otherwise provide a large number of the functions required for trading financial products.")
(comment BTTradingTurret "The collection of all electronic trading platforms (see #$ElectronicTradingPlatform) that are manufactured for use with services provided by British Telecommunications (#$BritishTelecom).")
(comment CapitalIQFinancialServices-Agreement "A subcollection of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing.  Each instance of this collection is a subscription to one of Capital IQ's financial services.  These services are primarily related to financial product research and analysis.")
(comment TechnologyServicesAgreement "A subcollection of #$LegalAgreement.  Each instance of #$TechnologyServicesAgreement is an agreement between two or more agents whereby some sort of technology service is provided.  This includes internet service, phone service, a contract to install a piece of electronic equipment, etc.  Basically any agreement that intrinsically involves the installation, maintenance, or ongoing service of consumer or business electronics is an instance of this collection.  For the collection of ongoing technology service agreements see #$TechnologyServicesAgreement-Ongoing.")
(comment TechnologyServicesAgreement-Ongoing "A subcollection of #$TechnologyServicesAgreement and #$AgreementForOngoingService.  Each instance of #$FinancialServicesAgreement is an agreement between two or more agents whereby some sort of technology service is provided in an ongoing fashion.  This includes internet service, phone service, computer based subscriptions.  This includes financial services and other sorts of ongoing services when they are tied to particular pieces of hardware.")
(comment AgreementForService "A collection of agreements in which one party agrees to provide a service to another party.  Examples include one-off agreements like hiring a plumber to fix your sink and continuing agreements like internet service.  During the agreement the recipient has the right to be the #$beneficiary in one or more #$ServiceEvents.")
(comment ServicesForAgreementTypeFn "A unary collection denoting function.  This function takes a type of agreement for services (#$AgreementForService) and denotes the subcollection of service events that are the particular service events performed for that type of agreement.  For example (#$ServicesForAgreementTypeFn #$FinancialServicesAgreement) is the subcollection of #$ServiceEvent that consists in all the various financial service events performed primarily for the satisfaction of some financial services agreement or other.")
(comment serviceEventTypeForAgreementType "(#$serviceEventTypeForAgreementType AGREE-TYPE SERVICE-TYPE) means that SERVICE-TYPE is the subcollection of #$ServiceEvent that corresponds to service events performed primarily to satisfy some agreement of AGREE-TYPE.  The is the corresponding predicate to #$ServicesForAgreementTypeFn.")
(comment TelephoneService "A collection of agreements between, typically, some telecommunications company and a customer where the company agrees to provide ongoing telephone service of some kind or other to the customer in exchange for payment.  The customer is then able to use the service provided by the company to perform instances of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$Telephone) via the company's network of #$TelephoneSubscriberLines.")
(comment TelephoneService-InternetProtocol "A subcollection of #$TelephoneService.  Each instance of this collection is an agreement to provide IP (#$InternetProtocol) telephone service.")
(comment CiscoIPT "A subcollection of #$TelephoneService-InternetProtocol.  Each instance of this collection is an agreement between #$CiscoSystemsInc and some customer to provide IP (#$InternetProtocol) telephone service.")
(comment InternetProtocolTelephoneSystem "The collection of all #$TelephoneSystem that where the voice signal is converted to a digital signal and sent over a computer network via an internet protocol (typically TCP).")
(comment agreementTypeRequiresSystemType "(#$agreementTypeRequiresSystemType AGREE-TYPE SYSTEM-TYPE) means that some instance of SYSTEM-TYPE is required for the #$agreeingServiceProvider to provide the agreed upon service in an #$AgreementForOngoingService.  Typically, the #$agreeingServiceRecipient  needs to provide and maintain at least some portion of this instance of SYSTEM-TYPE for the #$agreeingServiceRecipient.  For example, to provide telephone service there must exist a particular system of phone wires that the house is connected to that ultimately connect up to the provider's network.  Note that while some ongoing service agreements require some sort of ongoing system, many do not.  A service agreement for someone to mow your lawn every other week requires no particular system in this sense.")
(comment FinancialDataCommunicationSystem "The collection of instances of #$FunctionalSystem designed and configured to provide information and communication regarding financial products.  Typical examples includes systems that provide real time financial news data feeds, stock quotes, etc.")
(comment Telephone-InternetProtocol "The collection of all telephones that are designed to send voice over IP.")
(comment productTypeOfManufacturer "(#$productTypeOfManufacturer
PRODUCT-TYPE AGENT AGENT-PRODUCT-TYPE) means that AGENT-PRODUCT-TYPE is the subcollection of PRODUCT-TYPE manufactured by AGENT.  The is the corresponding predicate to #$ProductTypeOfManufacturerFn.")
(comment ProductTypeOfManufacturerFn "(#$ProductTypeOfManufacturerFn PRODUCT-TYPE AGENT) denotes the subcollection of PRODUCT-TYPE, an instance of #$ProductType and a specialization of #$Artifact, manufactured by AGENT.  Note this function is restricted to \"artifactual products\".  Hence, non-artifact product types like some services or events are not covered.")
(comment CiscoUnifiedApplicationEnvironment "A suite of software programs developed by Cisco that serve as an integrated development environment for applications that involve voice and video and which are typically deployed over a corporate data network.")
(comment AquaDataStudio-TheProgam "A database IDE (integrated development environment) with support for scripting of SQL queries, source code and file system integration and data modeling.")
(comment DesktopComputerHardwareItem "A type of #$ComputerHardwareItem. Each instance of this collection is a #$ComputerHardwareItem designed for use with personal computers (as opposed to, e.g. enterprise servers).  Note this includes (despite the name) laptop computers as well as traditional \"desktop\" computers.")
(disjointWith SmartPhoneOS DesktopComputerOperatingSystem)
(disjointWith ServerComputerOperatingSystem SmartPhoneOS)
(comment ServerComputerOperatingSystem "A type of #$OperatingSystem. Each instance of this collection is an operating system program whose program copies are typically installed on a dedicated server machine.  Note that this collection is disjoint with Smartphone operating systems (#$SmartPhoneOS), but not disjoint with #$DesktopComputerOperatingSystem as there are varieties of linux (and other OSs) that are often used as both a server OS and workstation OS.")
(comment DesktopComputerOperatingSystem "A type of #$OperatingSystem. Each instance of this collection is an operating system program whose program copies are typically installed on a personal computer (laptop or standard).  Note that this collection is disjoint with Smartphone operating systems (#$SmartPhoneOS), but not disjoint with #$ServerComputerOperatingSystem as there are varieties of linux (and other OSs) that are often used as both a server OS and workstation OS.")
(comment FinancialTradingSoftware "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are written as utilities to help financial product traders.  This collection includes complex subscription based software packages that present live financial data and quotes and allow users to make trades through their network as well as  financial trading software designed simply to monitor prices and data feeds.  this does not include general purpose software that may be useful for financial trading like spreadsheet or word processing programs.")
(comment EclipseTrader-TheProgram "An open source utility program for use within an online trading system.  It is built on the Eclipse Java platform.")
(comment ArubaPhoneAtHome "A subcollection of #$TelephoneService-InternetProtocol.  The collection of agreement products that allow a customer to hook up a Cisco IP phone to their home internet network and access their company's IP voice service.")
(comment Telecommunication-Teleconference "The collection of all teleconferencing activities.  The collection is the collection of all long distance communications that occur during a teleconference.  So there will typically be at least one subevent of this sort during each instance of #$Teleconference, though there will be many other communication acts that are not instances of this collection over the course of a #$Teleconference.  Accordingly, do not confuse this collection with the collection #$Teleconference which is the collection of all complete teleconference events.")
(comment LauncherProgram "Software designed to allow users to launch other programs either via scripting or though a unified UI.")
(comment EnterpriseContentManagementProgram "The collection of all enterprise content management (ECM) programs (#$ComputerProgram-CW).  An ECM is a suite of programs designed to help users management the documents and other files associated with the business processes and corporate memory of their organization.  Typically these programs offer a unified storage/retrieval system along with integrated version and document policy control.")
(comment BusinessObjects-TheProgram "A relational database query and report generation application by Oracle.  This product is designed to work with Oracle OLAP supported relational databases.")
(comment PlaybackOfARecordedCall "A subcollection of #$PlayingAnAudioRecordedObject.  This is the collection of events in which someone plays back a recorded phone call.")
(comment AudioVideoEquipment "A collection of electronic devices.  Each instance of AudioVideoEquipment is an electronic device used for recording, playback, editing, etc. of audio or video data either analog or digital.")
(comment FoxTrader-TheProgram "A software system designed for use by financial products traders that uses business logic and various algorithms to provide trading advice.")
(comment FoxRiverExecution-Company "Software company from Sunnyvale California.  they make database interface/IDE programs.  Their flagship product is #$AquaDataStudio-TheProgam.")
(comment CitrixComputerProgram "Software products made by #$CitrixSystems.")
(comment EclipseDevelopmentEnvironment-TheProgram "An IDE (integrated development environment) with support for several main programming languages.")
(comment USBAuthenticationDevice "A collection of plug-in USB devices that perform authentication functions.  These devices plug into the USB port of a computer or other electronic device and provide a unique key or serial number that allows the user to perform some function of the device.  This collection includes USB Keys that are intended to provide copy protection for #$ComputerProgramCopys as well as keys that work with software to perform other sorts of authentication functions such as digitally signing software or documents or encrypting files.")
(comment driverProgramForDeviceType "(#$driverProgramForDeviceType COMP-PROG DEVICE-TYPE) means that COMP-PROGRAM is a #$DeviceDriverProgram designed to interface devices of DEVICE-TYPE with another electronic system.  For example, this relation holds between a USB memory device and its driver which allows the operating system of the computer it is plugged into to access its functions in a standard way.")
(comment DocumentTransmissionProgram "The collection of all document transmission/submission programs. Instances of this collection are programs whose primary functions include the generation and submission or transmission of computer document files.  Instant messaging and email programs are prominent specializations.  Programs such as TurboTax would also be instances as it is a prominent feature of those programs that the resulting document created can be submitted or transmitted to their destination by the program.  On the other hand, word processing programs whose primary function is the creation of documents but which may have methods for invoking the user's email service to transmit the files would not be members of this collection.")
(comment Essbase-TheProgram "A database IDE (integrated development environment) originally developed by Hyperion Solutions but now maintained by Oracle and incorporated into the Business Intelligence Suite of tools and programs.")
(comment DatabaseReportGeneratorProgram "A specialization of #$DatabaseClientProgram. Each instance of this collection is some instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW which allows users to query databases and provides utilities to further manipulate the output into reports, charts, etc.")
(comment DataAggregationProgram "the collection of programs which aggregate data from various sources often allowing the user to tailor the presentation according to their preferences.")
(comment Factset-TheProgram "A data aggregation program.  Factset allows users to view data collated from various market data sources and allows them to organize that data and create reports in Adobe Acrobat PDF format.")
(comment FactsetResearchSystemsInc "Financial software company that provides financial data aggregation and reporting software.")
(comment instancesInvolveType "A very general predicate that relates two collections just in case instances of the first are \"involved\" in some main but unspecfied way.  (#$instancesInvolveType COLL1 COLL2) means that some instance of COLL2 is involved in instances of COLL1 in some primary or main capacity.  This predicate is primarily useful as a predicate used in querying.  Most knowledge representation will occur at the level of the various specializations of the predicate")
(comment WebBasedMappingService "The collection of websites either free or by subscription that provide mapping services like naviagational aid, customized trip planning, etc.  #$GoogleMaps is an example of an instance of this collection.")
(comment IntellijIdea-TheProgram "An IDE (integrated development environment) for building Java based applications.")
(comment JetBrains-TheCompany "Software company based in the Czech Republic.  They design software development environments for Java and web-based applications.")
(comment AllianceTradingTurret "A specialization of #$ElectronicTradingPlatform.  Each instance of this collection is an Alliance model trading turret by IPC.")
(comment EQMXTradingTurret "A specialization of #$ElectronicTradingPlatform.  Each instance of this collection is an EQMX model trading turret by IPC.")
(comment IQMAXTradingTurret "A specialization of #$ElectronicTradingPlatform.  Each instance of this collection is an EQMAX model trading turret by IPC.")
(comment AVContentDeliverySystem-InternetProtocol "The collection of instances of #$FunctionalSystem designed that are set up to provide video/audio content over the internet.  The Netflix movie streaming system is one such instance of this collection.")
(comment TelevisionContentDelieverySystem-InternetProtocol "The collection of instances of AVContentDeliverySystem-InternetProtocol that are designed to stream television content over the internet.")
(comment JavaProgram "A specialization of #$LocalProgram.  Each instance of this collection is an application that is written in the #$JavaProgrammingLanguage and requires the user have the appropriate instance of #$JavaVirtualMachine running on their machine in order to run the program.")
(comment situationTypeForServiceType "(#$situationTypeForServiceType  AGREE-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that it is a requirement of any instance of AGREE-TYPE that there be appropriately related situations of SIT-TYPE.  How these situations are related to the service provided depends on the type of service.  For example, if one has subscribed to an email service, one should be able to log in, retrieve email, send email, etc.  In general, SIT-TYPE refers to a collection of situations which the service enables and the user of the service plays some role in making come about.  contrast this with (#$ServicesForAgreementTypeFn  AGREE-TYPE) which refers to the collection of services provided by the agreement, but which are performed by the service provider like \"setting up the customer's account on the server\" and so forth.")
(comment FinancialInformation "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalInformationThing (information or data) that are specifically related to transactions, prices, company profiles, etc in the financial product domain.")
(comment MarketData-PIT "The collection of instances of #$FinancialInformation that are related to prices, quotes, number of shares exchanged, etc. of financial products traded on various stock exchanges.")
(comment TechnologyArtifactNotProvidedByGS "The collection of technology artifacts that are used by GS employees during the course of their work, but are not provided to that employee through normal GS procurement channels.")
(comment PBXCapableTelephone "A collection of telephones. Each #$PBXCapableTelephone is a telephone capable of executing a large number of the functions of a #$PrivateBusinessExchange.")
(comment MeridianDigitalTelephone "The collection of all Meridian Digital telephones.  Typically these sorts of telephones have extra fucntions to take advantage of the features of a PrivateBusinessExchange.")
(comment MitelDigitalTelephone "The collection of all Mitel Digital telephones.  Typically these sorts of telephones have extra fucntions to take advantage of the features of a PrivateBusinessExchange.")
(comment Telephone-MultiMediaConference "The collection of telephones designed to be used in audio or video teleconferencing.  These phones have additional functions which make them easier to use for teleconference of various sorts.  Some have high quality speaker and microphone systems so that when used as a speaker phone they can cover a large area.  Others have built in support for video conferencing.")
(comment PolycomMultiMediaConferencePhone "The collection of multimedia conference telephones manufactured by #$PolycomInc.")
(comment RapidSQL-TheProgram "A database IDE (integrated development environment) with support for scripting of SQL queries, source code and file system integration and data modeling.")
(comment Embarcadero-Company "Software company from San Francisco California.  they make database interface/IDE programs.")
(comment ReutersFinancialDataServices "A subcollection of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing.  Each instance of this collection is a subscription to one of Reuters financial data services.  These services are primarily related to financial product research and analysis.")
(comment Siebel-CRM-TheProgram "A customer relationship management program tailored to individual users that allows them to manage information about their clients and contacts.")
(comment SybaseAdvantageDatabaseServer-TheProgram "Sybase's Advantage relational database management system.")
(comment SystemAdministration-ComputerNetwork "A specialization of #$MaintainingSomething and #$ComputerActivity.  The is the collection of activities typcially #$performedBy #$SystemAdministrators as part of the job duties.  An instance of computer or network maintenance activity will be an instance of this collection if it is #$performedBy an instance of #$SystemAdministrator as part of their task of maintaining the computer system to which they are assigned.")
(comment TA2000-FinancialRecordkeepingSystem "A mutual fund shareholder recordkeeping system by DSTSystems, Inc.")
(comment Voicemail "The collection of all #$AudioRecordedObjects that are recordings of vocal messages recorded (typically) onto a telephone answering system.  The audio of each recorded message will be associated with a particular textual information structure (#$PropositionalCWText) that is itself associated with a #$PropositionalConceptualWork -- i.e. the abstract propositional content of the message.")
(comment WebIce "WebICE is a proprietary browser-based front-end to ICE's electronic trading platform.")
(comment XyrisComputerProgram "Software products made by Xyris Software, Inc.")
(comment AgreementTypeByAccountSystem "The collection of subcollections of #$AgreementForOngoingService, AGR-TYPE, where each agreement in AGR-TYPE has the same #$agreeingServiceProvider and each #$agreeingServiceRecipient logs onto the same account system.  For instance the collection of agreements for internet service with Time Warner Cable is an instance of this collection because, in some sense, each service recipient's account is on the same Time Warner system.  Contrast this #$InternetService in general, although a specialization of #$AgreementForOngoingService, the service providers vary and there is no unique account system the customers of the services are connecting to.")
(comment AccountSystemForAgreementTypeFn "(#$AccountSystemForAgreementTypeFn AGREEMENT-TYPE) denotes the #$AccountSystem associated with AGREEMENT-TYPE.  This function's domain is restricted to #$AgreementTypeByAccountSystem whose instances, by definition, are associated with a single #$AccountSystem.")
(comment agreementTypeAssociatedWithAccountSystem "(#$agreementTypeAssociatedWithAccountSystem  AGREE-TYPE ACCOUNT-SYS) means that ACCOUNT-SYS is the unique #$AccountSystem associated with instances of AGREE-TYPE.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$AccountSystemForAgreementTypeFn .")
(comment MacroForComputerProgram "The collection of all \"macros\" defined for computer programs.  Each instance of this collection is computer code that defines a particular function in terms of other more basic functions.")
(comment orgTechSupportedProgram "(#$orgTechSupportedProgram ORG PROGRAM) means that ORG provides tech support for internal uses of PROGRAM either directly or via a 3rd party or internal technical support system.")
(comment providesTechSupportFor "(#$providesTechSupportFor  AGT1 AGT2) means that AGT2 provides tech support services to employees or agents of AGT1.  This predicate represents ongoing customer tech support services given to employees or agents of AGT1 by AGT2 or its agents.  Note that this covers the relationship between an independent customer support service and a particular company that has contracted that service as well as the relationship between individual tech support representatives that work for contracted service companies or that are employees of the supported organization.")
(comment ExpertiseRoutingRelation "The collection of relations (either predicates or #$Function-Denotational) that are involved in relating tech support products to each other and associated services and events.")
(comment IPTelephoneRouter "The collection of all routers designed for use with #$InternetProtocol telephones.")
(comment ArubaIPTelephoneRouter "The collection of all routers designed for use with #$InternetProtocol telephones.")
(comment SoftphoneProgram-InternetProtocol "the collection of dedicated client programs that allow one to make phone calls over the internet without any further equipment other than a standard headphone and microphone set.")
(comment SoftwareAgentTypeOfProgram-CWFn "A unary collection denoting function that takes a particular #$ComputerProgram-CW and returns the collection of software agents that are realizations in a running environment of that program.  See #$SoftwareAgent.")
(comment softwareAgentTypeOfProgram-CW "The corresponding predicate to #$SoftwareAgentTypeOfProgram-CWFn.  This related an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW to the collection of software agents that are realizations in a running environment of that program.  See #$SoftwareAgent.")
(comment orgTechSupportedArtifactType "(#$orgTechSupportedArtifactType ORG ARTIFACT-TYPE) means that ORG provides tech support for internal uses of instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE either directly or via a 3rd party or internal technical support system.  For a more general class of artifact to be so related means that at least 70% of its nearest subtypes are supported by ORG in this way. ")
(comment WirelessLocalAreaNetwork "A kind of #$LocalAreaNetwork.  Each instance of #$WirelessLocalAreaNetwork (Wi-Fi)  is a network linked via wireless access points.  These access points may be chained, but ultimately bottom out in some other basic connection to the network or internet (e.g. a wired or cellular connection). #$WirelessLocalAreaNetwork networks have a relatively short area of access compared to cellular networks.")
(comment activationOfProductType "(#$activationOfProductType TYPE ACT-TYPE) means that ACT-TYPE is the collection of instances of #$ActivationOfProductOrService that are activations of instances of TYPE.")
(comment Scanner-Optical "Devices which use light to read a code or copy the target into a computer file.  Examples include barcode scanners, document scanners, etc.")
(comment AligningSomething "The collection of events in which something is aligned with another thing.  This alignment is relative to the goals/intentions of the agent or system doing the alignment.  Note that the intended alignment required in members of this collection is stricter than that of its generalization #$LocatingInIntendedPosition.  E.g. A placement of a book on a shelf would be an instance of #$LocatingInIntendedPosition if the intended position were simply between this book and that one.  That event would not necessarily be an instance of this collection in that case.  On the other hand, a book placement where the achieved goal was to line up the bindings of the placed book with the bindings of the other book would be an instance of this collection.")
(comment SynchronizingData "The collection instances of #$AligningSomething in which the things aligned are data files.  Typcially the synchronization event results in a target file with duplicate content (modulo file versioning annotations)   Examples include updating a local directory from a version control system and vice versa, updating a smart phone with the latest version of an operarating file from a central server, etc.")
(comment FinancialDataCommunicationSystem-Dedicated "The collection of instances of #$SystemOfDevices designed and configured to provide information and communication regarding financial products.  This includes systems that involve some dedicated equipment or other (dedicated servers, client artifacts, etc.), but doesn't include communication systems that consist only of software products that only provide compilation services of existing data feeds from other sources.  A positive example would be the system involved in the Bloomberg Professional Service where there is dedicated client software and servers and a physical authentication device required for client log-on.  A negative example would be a software system that runs on the user's existing machine and connects to the internet via the user's existing connection and compiles snippets of financial data from third party websites.")
(comment NetworkConnectionIndicatorLight "The collection of all lights on electronic devices that indicate a positive connection to the network.")
(comment TelephoneSubscriberLine-Private "The collection of all #$TelephoneSubscriberLines that operate along predetermined transmission paths which allow communication between pre-established specific locations.  For example, the Washington-Moscow hot-line established during the Cold War operates on a #$TelephoneSubscriberLine-Private.")
(comment CiscoIPPhone-Model7961 "The collection of Cisco Internet Protocol telephones that are model number 7961")
(comment CiscoIPPhone-Model7960 "The collection of Cisco Internet Protocol telephones that are model number 7960")
(comment CiscoIPPhone-Model7962 "The collection of Cisco Internet Protocol telephones that are model number 7962")
(comment equipmentTypeForServiceType "(#$equipmentTypeForServiceType AGREE-TYPE DEVICE-TYPE) means that DEVICE-TYPE is a collection of client devices typically closely associated with AGREE-TYPE.  For instance, for cable-based internet service, the client is typically required to lease a cable modem.  For digital cable TV service, a set-top box is usually leased by the customer.  Note this relationship does not cover incidental devices such as cables, power cords, etc.  This relationship associates consumer device types with ongoing service types while its \"sister\" relationship #$agreementTypeRequiresSystemType covers associated infrastructure systems that are prerequisites for the service type. ")
(comment PBXPhoneAddOnModule "The collection of all add on modules to PBX capable phone.  These modules add additional functionality like line monitoring and more sophisticated line transfer and switching functions.")
(comment AccessingACiscoIPTelephoneAdministrationPage "the collection of activities which consist of logging in and accessing administration functions for a Cisco IP telephone.")
(comment ProgrammingAComputerizedDevice "The subcollection of #$ProgrammingAComputer in which the programmer is programming or configuring a device that contains a computer (in the broad sense of #$Computer).  Typically the perfomers of these actions are not writing code directly, but are accessing programmable functions via the device's built in APIs -- often connected via a built in GUI.")
(comment AccessingDeviceAdministrationPage "the collection of activities which consist of logging in and accessing administration functions for some device (typically a computer network device of some sort).  In the typical case, these functions are accessed via logging in via a standard web browser into a web page generated by the device.")
(comment TextualMessageExchanging-RealTime-Internet "The collection of messaging/communication events where textual messages are exchanged between participants in real time (or close to it).  This includes chat room communications, continuously connected peer-to-peer textual communications, group connect messaging, etc.  It does not include non-real time messaging communications like an exchange of cell phone text messages, email exchanges etc.  Each connected participant's messaging connection/software must be able to transmit and receive messages within the same session in real time.")
(comment InternetConferencingClientProgram "The collection of client applications (often downloadable as applets at connect time) that connect to internet collaboration servers.  These servers and clients allow for internet sharing of desktop contents, chat, IP telephony, etc.  Prominent examples include clients for the following services WebEx, GoToMeeting, and MS Live Meeting.")
(comment StopMessageCondition "The collection of dysfunctional computer state conditions that result in the \"Stop message\" (also called \"blue screen of death\" or \"BSOD\") in computers running Windows operations systems.")
(comment BusinessCardReader "The collection of portable scanners designed to scan and read into a file typical business cards.  These scanners can often populate address book software and otherwise parse the text on the card into discrete data.")
(comment OpticalComputerStorageDevice "The collection of all optical storage devices. A type of #$DiskDrive and #$OpticalDevice.  The most prevalent examples are Compact Disc drives and DVD drives.")
(comment TravelPlanningWebsite "The collection of websites that provide travel planning assistance.")
(comment ComputerIcon "A collection of small files (#$ComputerFile-CW) associated with images used in a
graphical user interface (or \"GUI\"). Particular icon copies generally link to a
#$ComputerFileCopy or a #$ProgramAction, and the computer user can
initiate the #$ProgramAction or perform various operations on the
#$ComputerFileCopy by pointing to its #$ComputerIcon and clicking. Other
#$ComputerIcons simply appear in a designated part of a display to
represent to the user some information about the internal state of the
#$Computer.")
(comment ComputerDesktopIconGroup "The collection of all computer desktop icon groups.  Each instance of this collection is a group of computer desktop icons (small files associated with a graphic that link to another file or program).")
(comment FinancialRecordkeepingSystem "A collection of software designed to keep records of finances, financial products, and other financial data.  This includes software for personal use as well as software for use by analysts, traders, and for regulatory compliance.")
(comment PyxisMobileInc "Software company founded in 1998.  Pyxis creates enterprise software for mobile devices.  They have offices in Boston, New York, and Chicago.")
(comment PasswordAuthenticationDevice "The collection of small electronic devices that generate passwords.  These devices provide extra characters or numbers needed to login to a secure system and are synchronized with a host or server's password.")
(comment ContentCreationSoftware "An instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction. Each instance of this collection is a computer program designed to allow users to easily create documents, graphics, etc typically by giving them document templates or by setting up collaboration environments.  They are distinguished from simple text editors and word processing programs in that they typically involve a suite of functions that convert formats, publish or transmit documents, etc. ")
(comment UniversalSerialBus "The collection of all Universal Serial buses (USB).  Each instance of this collection is a port compatible with the USB protocol into which devices can be plugged (typically without restarting the host device.")
(comment WebCam-Device "The collection of small, relatively low resolution, cameras designed to be plugged in to computers to allow for pictures or video to be generated and dynamically streamed over the internet.")
(comment Applet-Generic-ComputerProgram "Applets are small computer programs typically designed to perform a single task.")
(comment ExcelFormula-ProgramCode "This is the collection of all expressions of Excel formulas that conform to the Excel formula syntax.")
(comment DataSummarizationTool-Program "The collection of all stand-alone or add-on module data summarization tools.  These programs typically work with a database or data visualization program to provide user definable summaries of data elements.")
(comment MeridianM2616-DigitalPhone "The collection of meridian PBX telephones that are model M2616")
(comment MeridianM3904-DigitalPhone "The collection of meridian PBX telephones that are model M3904")
(comment MeridianM5209-DigitalPhone "The collection of meridian PBX telephones that are model M5209")
(comment MeridianM5312-DigitalPhone "The collection of meridian PBX telephones that are model M5312")
(comment ReceivingAFaxedDocument "The collection of all events in which a particular FAX message is received and the corresponding hard copy printed out.")
(comment FaxingADocument "The collection of all events in which a hardcopied piece of text is converted to electronic signals by a fax machine, and transmitted to another machine.")
(disjointWith ConfigurationFile EmailFolder)
(comment EmailFolder "The collection of computer files that serve as holders or organizers of email message files.")
(comment AvayaDigitalTelephone "The collection of all Avaya Digital telephones.  Typically these sorts of telephones have extra functions to take advantage of the features of a #$PrivateBusinessExchange.")
(comment LucentAvayaModel6424D "The collection of Avaya PBX phones that are model 6424D+")
(comment LucentAvayaModel2420 "The collection of Avaya PBX phones that are model 2420")
(comment LucentAvayaModel8434 "The collection of Avaya PBX phones that are model 8434")
(comment computerAccountStorageShare "(#$computerAccountStorageShare ACCOUNT SIZE) means that there is SIZE amount of kilobytes/gigabytes/etc. available for use by the holder of ACCOUNT.  This includes file shares on network drives as well as storage limits for other sorts of computer accounts like those found in collaboration software.")
(comment RestoringFromBackup-IBTGeneration "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration-Replication.  Each instance of #$RestoringFromBackup-IBTGeneration is an event where a particular set of computer files that constitute some functional system are reinstalled or recopied from file copies based on some previously saved state of the files.")
(comment Speakerbus-IPCommunicationSystem "The collection of self-contained VOIP monitor/transmit systems by Speakerbus.  Some are of these product are listen only while others allow for transmission of voice communications.")
(comment Speakerbus-ModelID100 "4 channel audio monitoring system by Speakerbus")
(comment Speakerbus-Company "Speakerbus Group plc is a privately owned communications technology developer and manufacturer headquartered in the UK.")
(comment Speakerbus-ModelID114 "audio transmit/receive system by Speakerbus")
(comment Speakerbus-ModelSE612 "Single channel desktop audio receive/transmit station.  Compatible with \"Hoot 'n' Holler\" paging systems.")
(comment Dataroom "The collection of instances of #$ServerRoom that are dedicated to file storage.")
(comment MappingComputerHardDriveToFileSystem "A collection of actions each of which consists of the actions taken by a computer user or system administrator that maps a hard disk drive to a particular computer's file system.")
(comment AllocationOfResources "The collection of events in which some resource (broadly defined) is allocated (i.e. reserved or made available for use) to something or other.  This includes assignment of storage space, assignment of team members to a project, etc.")
(comment AllocationOfComputerStorage "The collection of events in which some amount of computer file system storage (Some number of Gigabytes, etc.) is reserved for use by a particular computer account.  In general this results in the amount of computer storage available to increase.  (See #$computerAccountStorageShare).  Note that this is distinguished from its generalization (#$IncreaseOnSlotFn #$computerAccountStorageShare) by virtue of the fact that one's storage share can increase without their being an allotment of additional resources -- e.g. by removing files or otherwise freeing up space.")
(comment VirtualMachineMonitorProgram "The collection of programs which monitor the concurrent running of multiple operating system on a single computer.  These programs act as an intermediary between the host computer's BIOS and the guest OS.")
(comment Headset "a communications device which is worn on the head and has speakers which cover one or more of the ears.  Typically they have a microphone integrated into the unit -- often as a boom piece connected to the frame near the an ear piece.")
(comment PlantronicsHeadset "The collection of headsets manufactured by Plantronics.")
(comment SennheiserHeadset "The collection of headsets manufactured by Sennheiser.")
(comment PolycomRoundTable-ConferencePhone "The collection of multimedia conference telephones manufactured by #$PolycomInc that are Round Table models.")
(comment PolycomTradingTurretCombo-ConferencePhone "The collection of multimedia conference telephones manufactured by #$PolycomInc that also have some electronic trading platform (trading turrets) functionality.")
(comment ElectronicVoiceMailNotificationProgram "A small program or plug-in designed to notify users that they have a voice mail.")
(comment VoicemailIndicatorLight "The collection of all lights on electronic devices that indicate a new voicemail.")
(comment FormattingText "The collection of all #$Events in which #$TextualMaterial within a single file or document is organized according to some format or other.")
(comment informationStoreUsesProgram "(#$informationStoreUsesProgram STORE PROGRAM) means that STORE can be utilized in running program copies of PROGRAM in some way.  This is a very general relationship that can hold between a data file and a program that can read the file, or a formatting template and a word processing program, or even between two programs etc.")
(comment objectTransferredInExecutableArithmeticOperation "(#$objectTransferredInExecutableArithmeticOperation EXEC-OP OBJ) means that the value of OBJ is transferred from one memory location to another in EXEC-OP.")
(comment functionCalledInFunctionInvocation "(#$functionCalledInFunctionInvocation EXECUTABLE FUNCTION) means that the executable functions call (#$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) EXECUTABLE calls the #$FunctionalRelation FUNCTION.")
(comment rdfDate "(#$rdfDate DATE DATE-SPEC) relates a CycL #$Date with an #$RDFTypedLiteralFn nat that represents the same date. An example use is (#$rdfDate (#$DayFn 13 (#$MonthFn #$December (#$YearFn 1984))) (#$RDFTypedLiteralFn \"1984-12-13\" (#$URIFn \"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#Date\"))).")
(comment predQueryPragmatics "<code>(#$predQueryPragmatics PRED SENTENCE-TEMPLATE)</code> means that queries containing the predicate <code>PRED</code> as a literal should be augmented with a pragmatic constraint given by the template <code>SENTENCE-TEMPLATE</code>.  Templates are specified as #$CycLSentences that make use of specific meta-variables. To place a pragmatic constraint on the literal itself, use the keyword \"<code>:SENTENCE</code>\": -- for example, <code>(#$predQueryPragmatics #$dateOfEvent (#$assertedSentence :SENTENCE))</code> means that when asking a sentence of the form <code>(#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE)</code> the pragmatic <code>(#$assertedSentence (#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE))</code> should be applied.  Other constraints can be applied to argument-places within the literal can be specified using the meta-variables <code>:ARG0</code>, <code>:ARG1</code>, <code>:ARG2</code>, etc.  For example, <code>(#$predQueryPragmatics #$dateOfEvent (#$isa :ARG1 #$PurposefulAction))</code> means that when asking a query of the form, <code>(#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE)</code> the pragmatic <code>(#$isa EVT #$PurposefulAction)</code> should be applied. Naturally, pragmatics can be complex formulae, e.g., <code>((#$predQueryPragmatics #$dateOfEvent (#$and (#$assertedSentence :SENTENCE) (#$isa :ARG1 #$PurposefulAction)))</code> means that queries of the form, <code>(#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE)</code> should have an associated pragmatic of the form (#$and (#$assertedSentence #$eventOccursAt) (#$isa :ARG1 #$PurposefulAction)), <code>(#$predQueryPragmatics #$dateOfEvent (#$thereExists ?X (#$thereExists ?Y (#$and (#$subEvents :ARG1 ?X) (#$perpetrator ?X ?Y) (#$assertedSentence :SENTENCE) (#$isa :ARG1 #$PurposefulAction)))))</code> means that queries of the form, <code>(#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE)</code> should have an associated pragmatic of the form (#$thereExists ?X (#$thereExists ?Y (#$and (#$subEvents EVT ?X) (#$perpetrator ?X ?Y) (#$assertedSentence (#$dateOfEvent EVT DATE)) (#$isa EVT #$PurposefulAction)))), and so on.")
(comment SeriesOfCellDivisionRounds "Instances of #$SeriesOfCellDivisionRounds are sequences of cell division events starting from a single parent cell.  This cell divides in the first round of division to produce two cells.  In the next round, one or both cells divide (each in its own individual cell division event) to produce a total of up to four cells.  In the third round, some or all of the products of the second round divide, and so on. Although the preceding description gives the impression that individual divisions in a round occur synchronously, the only round that must complete before the next one begins is the first.  Rounds that come later in the series can become unsynchonized if some cell lineages progress through their divisions more quickly than others.")
(comment ancestorCell "(#$ancestorCell NEWERCELL OLDERCELL) states that NEWERCELL is descended from OLDERCELL via a series of one or more #$CellDivision events.")
(comment originatorCell "Each instance of #$SeriesOfCellDivisionRounds begins with a single cell which is the parent cell (see #$parentCell) in the division event that makes up the first #$RoundOfCellDivision in the series.  (#$originatorCell SERIES CELL) relates a #$SeriesOfCellDivisionRounds, SERIES, to this cell CELL.")
(comment MapleTree "The collection of all maple trees. A type of #$SoapberryOrder, #$Tree-ThePlant, and #$DeciduousPlant. The collection #$MapleTree is a #$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment BodilyFluid "The collection of all fluids produced by the human (or animal) body.  Note that these need not be in a #$Liquid-StateOfMatter; they can be frozen, boiled, etc.")
(comment IteratedEventScene "Specializations of #$IteratedEventScene are event-types instances of which are events in which some event is repeated (in sequence, synchronously or haphazardly) at least twice, possibly indefinitely, and sometimes until a terminal condition (such as a goal event) is achieved.  By convention, the terminal state type is considered to be a sub-event type of the iterated event type, but it need not be the same type as the iterated event.  For example, mixing a cake batter may involve iterations of stirring the batter, and they are terminated when the batter reaches a certain consistency, but reaching a consistency is not itself a stirring.  Some terminal conditions of iterated event types are of the same kind as the iterated events -- for example, in a script that requires taking eight leaps, taking the 8th leap may be the terminal event, and it itself is a leap (which is also the iterated event type).")
(comment RoundOfCellDivision "Each instance of #$RoundOfCellDivision consists of one or more #$CellDivision events which often, but don't necessarily, occur simultaneously.  What defines a set of divisions as being part of the same #$RoundOfCellDivision is that the parent cells in each division all share the same ancestor cell, from which they are descended via the same number of cell divisions.")
(comment eventSceneIterations "(#$eventSceneIterations ITERATED-SCENE ITERATION) states that ITERATION is one of the events of a particular type that is repeated to make up ITERATED-SCENE.  Note that #$eventSceneIterations is a specialization of #$subEvents, not #$properSubEvents, to allow for degenerate forms in which an #$IteratedEventScene has only one iteration, which is the event itself.  An example of this from the biology domain is #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle.")
(comment nthTypeInSeriesType "(#$nthTypeInSeriesType SERIES-TYPE ITEM-TYPE N) means that for every instance S of SERIES-TYPE, there is some instance I of ITEM-TYPE such that (#$nthInSeries S I N).  Furthermore, for every instance S of SERIES-TYPE, if (#$nthInSeries S I N), then I is an instance of ITEM-TYPE.")
(comment nthSubSituationTypeOfType "The predicate corresponding to the function, #$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn.  (#$nthSubSituationTypeOfType SUPER-TYPE TYPE N SUB-TYPE) states that SUB-TYPE is collection of #$Situations that are the Nth #$subSituations of instances of SUPER-TYPE that are instances of TYPE.")
(comment Pipelined "The collection of all computers with pipelined microprocessors.  The collection #$Pipelined is a #$ComputerTypeByArchitecture, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and a #$ManufacturedGoodsType.")
(comment officialArmedForcesBranch "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Organization to instances of #$BranchOfMilitaryService.  <code>(#$officialArmedForcesBranch ORG MIL)</code> means that <code>MIL</code> is one of the official #$BranchOfMilitaryServices for ORG.")
(comment UnknownScalarInterval "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  If a quantity is an instance of #$UnknownScalarInterval, Cyc may know what kind of quantity it is (it may also be a #$Distance or a #$NegativeNumber, e.g.), but its size is explicitly not known.  This is a signal to the inference engine that when this quantity appears as an argument to mathematical functions, full evaluation of the functional term is not required, and the functional term itself (possibly with some simplification) can be returned as an answer.  Hypothetical queries that propose an unspecified value will lead to that value being hypothesized as an instance of #$UnknownScalarInterval.  For example, the English query ''Suppose Fred has N pairs of shoes.  How many individual shoes does he have?'' would be represented in CycL this way: 
<pre>
<code>
(#$implies (#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$possesses #$Fred (#$PairFn #$Shoe) ?N)
           (#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$possesses #$Fred #$Shoe ?HOWMANY))
</code>
</pre>
The variable ?N will be instantiated as an #$IndeterminateTerm and instance of #$PositiveInteger - say, #$HYP-PositiveInteger-1 - and Cyc will conclude that it is an instance of #$UnknownScalarInterval.  Thus (#$TimesFn 2 #$HYP-PositiveInteger-1) will be allowed as a binding for ?HOWMANY.")
(comment PartwiseDisjointType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$PartwiseDisjointType is a collection C, where any two different instances of C are part-wise disjoint (see #$partwiseDisjoint) with one another.
<p>
For example, the collection #$BaseballGame is an instance of #$PartwiseDisjointType, since no two different baseball games share parts.")
(comment excerptString "(#$excerptString TERM STRING) means that STRING is a string that is used to describe TERM.  It may or may not be a name for TERM, but is a string used somewhere to describe TERM.")
(disjointWith CharacterString ListOfVertices)
(comment mathematicalProductOf "The predicate corresponding to #$TimesFn.  (#$mathematicalProductOf PRODUCT NUM-1 . NUM-N) holds just in case multiplying the numbers <code>NUM-1</code> through <code>NUM-N</code> is <code>PRODUCT</code>; that is, just in case  <code>(#$TimesFn NUM-1 . NUM-N)</code> evaluates to <code>PRODUCT</code>.  For example, <code>(#$mathematicalProductOf 1 2 0.5)</code> is true because 2 x 0.5 = 1.")
(comment mathematicalSumOf "The predicate corresponding to #$TimesFn.  (#$mathematicalSumOf SUM NUM-1 . NUM-N) holds just in case adding the numbers <code>NUM-1</code> through <code>NUM-N</code> is <code>SUM</code>; that is, just in case  <code>(#$PlusFn NUM-1 . NUM-N)</code> evaluates to <code>SUM</code>.  For example, <code>(#$mathematicalSumOf 2.5 2 0.5)</code> is true because 2 x 0.5 = 2.5.")
(comment largerThanByFactor "<code>(#$largerThanByFactor OBJ-1 OBJ-2 SLOT MULTIPLE)</code> means that the value of <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot, for the argument <code>OBJ-1</code> is #$greaterThan that of <code>OBJ-2</code> by a factor of <code>MULTIPLE</code>.")
(comment mathematicalDifference "The predicate corresponding to #$DifferenceFn.  <code>(#$mathematicalDifference MINUEND SUBTRAHEND DIFFERENCE)</code> holds just in case the result of subtracting <code>SUBTRAHEND</code> from <code>MINUEND</code> is <code>DIFFERENCE</code>; that is, just in case  <code>(#$DifferenceFn MINUEND SUBTRAEND)</code> = <code>DIFFERENCE</code>.  For example, (#$mathematicalDifference 88 11 77) is true because 88 minus 11 is 77.")
(comment MitosisSubprocessType "The collection of events-types instances of which are #$Prometaphase, #$Prophase, #$Metaphase, #$Anaphase and #$Telophase.")
(comment superEventTypes "A #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that is a specialization of #$temporallySubsumedBy-TypeType and #$normalWholeTypeForPartType (qq.v),  and is a type-level inverse correlate of #$subEvents (q.v.).  This predicate is used to state that events of one given type always have events of another given type as superevents.  <code>(#$superEventTypes SUBTYPE SUPERTYPE)</code> means that for every instance <code>SUBINST</code> of <code>SUBTYPE</code>, there is an instance <code>SUPERINST</code> of <code>SUPERTYPE</code>, such that <code>(#$subEvents SUPERINST SUBINST)</code>.  For example, (#$superEventTypes #$Sentencing-Legal #$Trial-Criminal) means that every legal sentencing is a subevent of a criminal trial.  
<p>
See also #$subEventTypes; and note that <code>(#$subEventTypes SUPERTYPE SUBTYPE)</code> is neither necessary nor sufficient for <code>(#$superEventTypes SUBTYPE SUPERTYPE)</code>.")
(comment Attachment "Instances of #$Attachment are situations in which two or more #$PartiallyTangible things are physically connected.  In the case where the attached objects are more or less equivalent in size, behavior, etc. they both play the role of #$objectsInAttachment. Where one may be considered more dominant, it plays the role of #$thingAttachedTo in the #$Attachment, while the other party or parties play the role of #$thingAttached.")
(comment connectorInAttachment "A specialization of #$configuredObjects.  (#$connectorInAttachment ATTACH THING) means that THING is an object which actually makes the physical connection between the things attached (see #$objectsInAttachment, #$thingAttached and #$thingAttachedTo) in the #$Attachment configuration, ATTACH.")
(comment SisterChromatidsAttached "Instances are #$Attachment configurations in which two #$Chromatids are attached by a #$Centromere.")
(comment situationOverlaps "This predicate relates overlapping situations. (#$situationOverlaps SIT1 SIT2) means that SIT1 and SIT2 share a common sub-situation.  That is, there is a SUBSIT such that both (#$subSituations SIT1 SUBSIT) and (#$subSituations SIT2 SUBSIT) hold.")
(comment Cell-PreChromosomalDuplication "An instance of #$CellTypeByChromosomalDuplicationStatus, instances are cells whose chromsomes are unduplicated (see #$UnduplicatedChromosome) but are in a state prior to chromosomal duplication and separation.")
(comment Cell-PostChromosomalDuplication "The collection of instances of #$EukaryoticCell that are at a state after chromosomal duplication.")
(comment shareParts-TypeType "A #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that is a type-level correlate of #$shareParts (q.v.).   <code>(#$shareParts-TypeType T1 T2)</code> means that for every instance <code>I1</code> of type <code>T1</code> there exists at least one instance <code>I2</code> of type <code>T2</code> such that (#$shareParts <code>I1 I2)</code> holds.  Note that #$shareParts-TypeType is antisymmetric and reflexive, but not transitive.")
(comment shareParts "(#$shareParts <code>I1 I2</code>) means that <code>I1</code> and <code>I2</code> share a common part.  That is, there is a <code>I3</code> such that both (#$parts <code>I1 I3</code>) and (#$parts <code>I2 I3</code>) hold.  Note that #$shareParts is reflexive and symmetric, but not transitive.")
(comment expectedMinTemporalOverlapOnArgs "Where PRED is a #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate, (#$expectedMinTemporalOverlapOnArgs PRED DUR) means that, if (PRED ARG1 ARG2) holds in any context that accesses the context of the #$expectedMinTemporalOverlapOnArgs assertion, the expectation is that the temporal overlap between ARG1 and ARG2, as established by their start and end times, is at least DUR.  For example, asserting (expectedMinTemporalOverlapOnArgs spouse (YearsDuration 18)) means that, in the context of the assertion, if (spouse ARG1 ARG2) holds, there is an expectation that the temporal overlap between ARG1 and ARG2 is at least 18 years.")
(comment declarationConditionOnExecutable "(#$declarationConditionOnExecutable FN-DECLARE COND INVOKE) means that the #$FunctionDeclaration FN-DECLARE contains (#$codeBlockHasBlocks) the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable INVOKE with condition COND specified for the ivokation so that the operation specified by INVOKE will not execute in a normal run-time execution of FN-DECLARE unless COND is met.")
(comment BitWidthOfLocationDenotedByFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reference and reason about the parameters of memory locations denoted by #$ComputerCodeExpression instances.  Where EXPRESSION is a #$ComputerCodeExpression denoting a location in computer memory, (#$BitWidthOfLocationDenotedByFn EXPRESSION) denotes the bit width of the memory location that EXPRESSION denotes.")
(comment bitWidthOfLocationDenotedBy "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$BitWidthOfLocationDenotedByFn. Where EXPRESSION is a #$ComputerCodeExpression denoting a location in computer memory, (#$bitWidthOfLocationDenotedBy EXPRESSION WIDTH) means that WIDTH denotes the width of the memory location denoted by EXPRESSION.")
(comment Synapsis "Each instance of #$Synapsis is an event that occurs during some #$ProphaseI, wherein the two members of each homologous chromosome pair attach together along their lengths.  Each attachment is mediated by a protein structure called the synaptonemal complex.  During synapsis, \"crossing over\" occurs and the attached homologous chromosomes trade segments.")
(comment restrictionOnSlot "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for #$RestrictionOnSlotFn, <code>(#$restrictionOnSlot RESTRICTED-SLOT TYPE SLOT)</code> identifies <code>RESTRICTED-SLOT</code> as the restriction of <code>SLOT</code> to objects of type <code>TYPE</code> in its arg1.")
(comment partwiseDisjoint-TypeType "A first-order collection predicate and a specialization of #$disjointWith (q.v.).  <code>(#$partwiseDisjoint-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE1)</code> means that no instances of <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code> share any parts.  I.e., if <code>I1</code> and <code>I2</code> are instances of <code>ITYPE1</code> and <code>ITYPE2</code> respectively, then there are no individuals <code>I</code> such that both <code>(#$parts I1 I)</code> and <code>(#$parts I2 I)</code>.  For example (#$partwiseDisjoint-TypeType #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLPostSeason) is true because there is no part of any instance of #$NFLPreSeason that is also a part of some instance of #$NFLPostSeason.")
(comment CellLifeStageType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType instances of which are all and only those specializations of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that are significant steps in the propagation of cells by mitotic division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle) or in the production of gametes by meiotic division (see #$Gametogenesis-Meiotic).")
(comment GametogenesisSubprocessType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType instances of which are all and only those specializations of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that are significant sub-processes of the the production of gametes by meiosis.")
(comment CellTypeByCellLifeStageFn "<code>(#$CellTypeByCellLifeStageFn PHASE-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of eukaryotic cells that are participating in <code>PHASE-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$CellTypeByCellLifeStageFn #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle) denotes the collection of all M-phase cells.")
(comment cellTypeParticipatingInCellLifeStage "<code>(#$cellTypeParticipatingInCellLifeStage PHASE-TYPE CELL-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>CELL-TYPE</code> are cells that are participating in <code>PHASE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CellTypeByCellLifeStage "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$EukaryoticCell subcollections based on the cell life stage in which they are participating.")
(comment MedicalEvaluationWithImaging "This collection represents the type of medical evaluations that can employ imaging of some sort or other.")
(comment Tetrad-Chromosomal "A specialization of #$HomologousChromosomePair and a physical object consisting of two attached #$DuplicatedChromosomes.  A #$Tetrad-Chromosomal forms during #$ProphaseI of #$Meiosis when the two members of a #$HomologousChromosomePair come together (see #$HomologousChromosomesAttachToOneAnother).")
(comment StandardCodingLibrary "The collection of all standard coding libraries.  A standard library is conventionally made available for every implementation of a range of programming languages.  In some cases, the library is described in the language specification; in other cases, the contents are determined by informal practices of the programming commmunity.  Most standard libraries include definitions for at least commonly-used algorithms, data astructures (lists, trees, hash tables), and interactions with the host platform, including input/output and operating system calls.  Depending on the constructs made available by the host language(s), a standard library may also include subroutines, macro definitions, class definitions, global variables, and templates.  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Library")
(comment CodingFunction "The collection of all functions, or, more generally, #$StrictlyFunctionalRelations, that may be invoked in executable computer code (see #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable.")
(comment StandardLibraryFunction "The collection of all instances of #$CodingFunction which belong to instances of #$StandardCodingLibrary.")
(comment formalParameterOfCodingFunctionIsa "A typed specialization of #$argIsa used to specify the argument constraints for instances of #$CodingFunction.  Where FN is a #$CodingFunction, (#$formalParameterOfCodingFunctionIsa FN N COL) means that the correct type for a value supplied as the Nth argument of FN is COL.")
(comment expressionDenotesParameterValue "(#$expressionDenotesParameterValue EXPRESSION INVOCATION N) means that in the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable INVOCATION, the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION is used to denote the Nth parameter of the #$CodingFunction  that is the #$codingFunctionInvoked.")
(comment nameOfCodingFunction "(#$nameOfCodingFunction FN NAME) means that the name whereby FN is denoted in standard libraries (instances of #$StandardCodingLibrary) is NAME.")
(comment codingFunctionDefined "(#$codingFunctionDefined FN-DECLARE FN) means that FN is the #$CodingFunction defined by the #$FunctionDeclaration FN.")
(comment FunctionInitializedInDeclarationFn "A #$FunctionDenotingFunction used in referencing the #$CodingFunction defined by a given #$FunctionDeclaration.  Where FN-DECLARE is a #$FunctionDeclaration, (#$FunctionInitializedInDeclarationFn FN-DECLARE STRING) denotes the #$codingFunctionDefined by FN-DECLARE with the #$symbolicNameOfFunctionDeclaration STRING.")
(comment codingFunctionInvoked "Where INVOCATION is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$codingFunctionInvoked INVOCATION FN) means that FN is the #$CodingFunction which is invoked in INVOCATION, in the strict sense that the #$ComputerActivityType carried out by any execution of INVOCATION will be an instance of any #$codingFunctionOperationTypes of FN.")
(disjointWith ChromosomeLongArm ChromosomeShortArm)
(comment ChromosomeRegionType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Instances are the basic types of decomposition of a #$Chromosome.")
(comment ChromosomeTypeByCentromericPosition "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets the collection of chromosomes (#$Chromosome) into sub-collections based on the relative location of the centromere (#$Centromere).")
(comment MetacentricChromosome "The collection of instances of #$Chromosome whose centromeres are exactly in the middle, so that their arms are of equal length.")
(comment SubmetacentricChromosome "The collection of instances of #$Chromosome whose centromeres are not in the middle, so that they have both long and short arms.")
(comment ChromosomeArm "The collection of instances of #$ChromatinStrand that constitute an \"arm\" of a chromosome, extending from the #$Centromere to one of the two #$Telomeres.")
(comment ChromosomeShortArm "The collection of all instances of #$ChromosomeArm that run from the #$Telomere of a #$Chromosome to the chromosome's #$Centromere, which connects it to a longer arm (an instance of #$ChromosomeLongArm) that runs to the other #$Telomere.")
(comment ChromosomeLongArm "The collection of all instances of #$ChromosomeArm that run from the #$Telomere of a #$Chromosome to the chromosome's #$Centromere, which connects it to a shorter arm (an instance of #$ChromosomeShortArm) that runs to the other #$Telomere.")
(comment replicatedDNAMolecules "<code>(#$replicatedDNAMolecules DNA1 DNA2)</code> means that via the process of #$Replication-DNA, the instances of #$DNAMolecule DNA1 and DNA2 are #$physicalCopies of one another.")
(comment mcTestOpenSubqueryTest "The predicate that corresponds to #$OpenSubqueryKBCTestFn, <code>(#$mcTestOpenSubqueryTest MC-TEST TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the instance of #$KBContentTest that is defined so as to inherit all of the parameters of the open-subquery generated by running <code>MC-TEST</code>, an instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest.")
(comment OpenSubqueryKBCTestFn "A function that takes an instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest and returns an instance of #$KBContentTest that inherits all of the parameters of the open-subquery generated by running the multiple choice test.")
(comment primaryConstituent-TypeType "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible to another specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  <code>(#$primaryConstituent-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> has an instance of <code>TYPE2</code> as its #$primaryConstituent.")
(comment mcTestOptionPositiveSubqueryTest "The predicate that corresponds to #$PositiveSubqueryFromMCOptionTestFn, <code>(#$mcTestOptionPositiveSubqueryTest MC-OPTION TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the instance of #$KBContentTest that is defined so as to inherit all of the parameters of the positive-subquery for the #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption <code>MC-OPTION</code> generated by running the instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for which <code>MC-OPTION</code> is an option.")
(comment PositiveSubqueryFromMCOptionTestFn "A function that takes an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption and returns an instance of #$KBContentTest that inherits all of the parameters of the positive subquery for that option generated by running the instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for which the option is an option.")
(comment NegationSubqueryFromMCOptionTestFn "A function that takes an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption and returns an instance of #$KBContentTest that inherits all of the parameters of the negation subquery for that option generated by running the instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for which the option is an option.")
(comment mcTestOptionNegationSubqueryTest "The predicate that corresponds to #$PositiveSubqueryFromMCOptionTestFn, <code>(#$mcTestOptionPositiveSubqueryTest MC-OPTION TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the instance of #$KBContentTest that is defined so as to inherit all of the parameters of the positive-subquery for the #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption <code>MC-OPTION</code> generated by running the instance of #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for which <code>MC-OPTION</code> is an option.")
(comment mcTestOptionSubqueryTests "<code>(#$mcTestOptionSubqueryTests MC-OPTION TEST)</code> means <code>(#$or (#$mcTestOptionPositiveSubqueryTest MC-OPTION TEST) (#$mcTestOptionNegationSubqueryTest MC-OPTION TEST))</code>.")
(comment GeneratePositiveSubquerySentenceFromMCOptionFn "A function that takes an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption and, upon evaluation, returns an instance of #$CycLSentence that is the sentence parameter for the positive sub-query for that multiple choice option that is generated when the  #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for that option is run.")
(comment GenerateNegationSubquerySentenceFromMCOptionFn "A function that takes an instance of #$SpecifiedMultipleChoiceOption and, upon evaluation, returns an instance of #$CycLSentence that is the sentence parameter for the negation sub-query for that multiple choice option that is generated when the  #$MultipleChoiceKBContentTest for that option is run.")
(comment KioskProgram "A type of #$UserInterfaceProgram and #$SecurityProgram.  A Kiosk program is designed to run on a Kiosk and lock down crucial files and functions to prevent user's from exploiting or damaging the Kiosk system.")
(comment situationInvolvesServiceType "(#$situationInvolvesServiceType SIT SERVICE-TYPE) means that some instance of SERVICE-TYPE was involved (in some unspecified manner) in the situation SIT.")
(comment ProblemPreservingSubcollectionPredicate "The collection of predicates that when used in the second argument of #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn produce a subcollection whose technical problems are closely associated with technical problems about the thing related in Arg2 of the predicate.  For example, #$informationStoreUsesProgram is a member of this collection because a technical problem relating to, e.g., a computer profile that is used by MS Active directory can can considered a problem relating to MS Active directory.")
(comment softwareForServiceType "(#$softwareForServiceType SERVICE-TYPE PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM is designed for SERVICE-TYPE -- either directly or as a result of SERVICE-TYPE being a member of a particular class of services -- and that the program copies of PROGRAM play an essential role in the utilization or provision of the service.")
(comment supportingActivityInvolvingProductType "(#$supportingActivityInvolvingProductType ACT AGENT) means that ACT involves an artifact whose type is in general supported by AGENT and that one of AGENT's representatives is directly supporting ACT.  For example, if ACT is an instance of connecting to a cell phone service and AGENT is the vendor of the cell phone used, then when the user of the cell phone calls the help service provided by AGENT, this relationship holds.")
(comment networkUtilized "An instance of #$ActorSlot and a specialization of #$deviceUsed, (#$networkUtilized ACT NETWORK) means that ACT made intrinsic use of network during the course of ACT.  For example, a Google search and a particular Wi-Fi hotspot would be so related when the search utilized the network for internet connectivity would results in those things being related via this predicate.  On the other hand, being connected to that same hotspot while composing a word document would not be sufficient.")
(comment SplitLiabilityBilling-TelephoneService "A subcollection of #$TelephoneService.  A type of telephone service account.  Each instance of this collection is a \"split liability\" account where one party assumes responsibility for one portion of the bill and another party has responsibility for other types of charges.  A common example of this is with corporate cell phone accounts where the company is responsible for base and data charges while the user is responsible for voice charges above and beyond the allotted minutes.")
(comment DisplayingAnImageOnAScreen "The collection of events in which an image is displayed on some screen or other either by projection or by internal production of the image by the device.")
(comment DisplayingAnImageOnAComputerDisplay "The collection of events in which data for an image is processed through a computer and output to a computer display.")
(comment MacintoshOperatingSystem "#$MacintoshOperatingSystem is a specialization of #$OperatingSystem.  It is the collection of all operating systems developed for use with Macintosh computers either personal or server.")
(comment CommonRoom "The collection of all rooms that are shared living, assembly, or working spaces.")
(comment LaptopComputer-Loaner "A specialization of #$LaptopComputer.  This is the collection of laptops that are designated as \"loaners\".  That is, each instance of this collection is a laptop owned by an organization that is not permanently assigned or slated to be permanently assigned to any particular person.  Rather it is lent out to organization members for temporary use.  Each instance of #$LaptopComputer-Loaner the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer in a #$BorrowingSomething event.")
(comment programAccessed "(#$programAccessed ACTIVITY PROGRAM) means that in the computer account accessing activity ACTIVITY, a running program copy of PROGRAM was utilized and was the interaction destination during the course of ACTIVITY.  This is a specialization of #$programUsed and is intended to capture a direct and purposeful use of PROGRAM during the course of some accessing a computer account.  Positive examples include logging on with an SSH client and accessing an Outlook email client.  In that case the Outlook email client would be the #$programAccessed during the SSH connection.  Although the SSH client was a #$programUsed during the SSH connection, it was not a #$programAccessed during this activity because it was not the interaction destination.")
(comment webSiteAccessed "(#$webSiteAccessed BROWSE SITE) means that during BROWSE, SITE was accessed.  This entails that one or more #$WebPage-AIS were accessed (#$webPageAccessed).")
(comment NetworkDesktopSolution-Session "The establishment of a NDS (Network Desktop Solution) session via a remote login.  An NDS session allows the user to connect to a virtual machine that has been assigned to them.")
(comment RemoteDesktopProtocolSession "The establishment of a RDP (Remote Desktop Protocol) session via a remote login.  An RDP session allows the user to connect to a physical machine inside the organization's firewall.")
(comment RemoteDesktopProtocol "Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP).  This is the protocol used when establishing RDP sessions from a remote login to a physical machine inside the organization's firewall.  This is a proprietary protocol developed by Microsoft")
(comment MitelDigitalTelephone-Model4150 "The collection of all Mitel Digital telephones that are model 4150.")
(comment MitelDigitalTelephone-Model7961 "The collection of all Mitel Digital telephones that are model 7961.")
(comment MitelSuperConsole2000 "PBX attendant console manufactured by Mitel for use in their PBX telephone networks.")
(comment PrivateBusinessExchange "The collection of telephone systems/ exchanges designed for internal connections within a business.  Also called a \"private branch exchange\".")
(comment PBXAttendantConsole "The collection of network call routing and switch systems for #$PrivateBusinessExchange telephone networks.  These are often realized in a PBX phone that has additional switching, call routing, and administrative functions above and beyond what PBX phones typically carry.")
(comment FreeMessage-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a message generated by a computer program to the effect that the current user of the program is available for interaction.")
(comment AwayMessage-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a message generated by a computer program to the effect that the current user of the program is unavailable for interaction.")
(comment FreeOrAwayMessage-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a message generated by a computer program to the effect that the current user of the program is either available (free) or unavailable (busy/away) for interaction.")
(comment MeetingStatus-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a message generated by a calendar or scheduling program regarding a planned meeting.")
(comment ReminderMessage-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a message generated by a a planning program of some sort that is intended to remind the user of an activity, meeting, appointment, etc.")
(comment ContactList "Each instance of this collection is a list of #$ContactInfoString for some person or organization.")
(comment attachedToEMail "(#$attachedToEMail ATTACH MESSAGE) means that the data object ATTACH is attached to the message MESSAGE.  MESSAGE is an instance of #$EMailMessage and ATTACH is an instance of #$ComputerAIS.")
(comment EmailFiltering "The class of all algorithmically-executed processes in which a email computer files are filtered according to some set of criteria.  Most often this is used to block unwanted email like Spam.")
(comment EMailSending-ExternalRecipient "The collection of email sending events in which the email is sent to an email address that is external to the email domain (or overall email infrastructure of an organization in cases where there are multiple domains in an organization) of the email sender.")
(comment EMailSending-InternalRecipient "The collection of email sending events in which the email is sent to an email address that is internal to the email domain (or overall email infrastructure of an organization in cases where there are multiple domains in an organization) of the email sender.")
(comment DeliveryReceipt "A document that indicates delivery of some item or other.  This includes hardcopy receipts as well as electronic delivery receipts.")
(comment EmailIn-OutBox "The collection of email folders which are top level folder for a given email client applcation.  These are typically titled \"mailbox\" or \"inbox\".")
(comment CreatingAnEmailDocument "A specialization of #$EditingAnElectronicDocument.  Each instance of CreatingAnEmailDocument is an event in which someone or other creates an instance of #$EMailMessage.")
(comment MovingAComputerFile-Generic "A specialization of #$FileOperation and #$GeneralizedTransfer. In each instance of #$MovingAComputerFile-Generic, a computer changes or indexes a file in such a way that it appears in a user interface to have moved to a different location.  This collection covers cases where the actual file remains where it is but an icon or pointer to the file is moved to a new location and cases where a file is copied to a new location and the source file destroyed.")
(comment MovingEmailFiles "A specialization of #$MovingAComputerFile-Generic.  Each instance of this collection is the operation of moving one or more email files to a new location.")
(comment OutOfOffice-EMailMessage "A specialization of #$EMailMessage. Each instance of this collection is an electronic mail message sent to a sender of a prior email to indicate the recipient of that email is currently out of office.")
(comment UserStatusSpecification "A specialization of #$Specification. Each instance of this collection is a declaration or specification of some state of affairs reflecting the status of the program user or the status of the system as specified by the user.  Positive examples include entries for a meeting in a calendar application or declarations of availability in a chat program like \"free\" or \"busy\".  Other positive examples include the specification of specific instructions to the program like sending a reminder email.  A negative example would be a \"working\" message generated by the program in response to a particular program state.  In that case the message is not intended to provide feedback to someone about the user or program state.")
(comment DoNotForward-StatusSpecification "A specialization of #$UserStatusSpecification.  Each instance of this collection is a specification to an email program to refrain from forwarding messages under certain conditions.")
(comment Reuters3000XtraTerminal-DataService "A subcollection of #$ReutersFinancialDataServices.  Each instance of this collection is a subscription that allows access to the Reuters 3000 Xtra hosted financial data terminal.")
(comment EnterpriseProductManagementSystem-Program "The collection of programs that are used to manage \"in-house\" ordering of supplies, applications, etc.")
(comment DiskDrive-Partition "The collection of all computer disk drive partitions.  Each instance of this collection is a \"virtual\" disk drive that can appear and interact with the user and OS as a stand-alone disk drive.")
(comment HeadsetVoiceTube "A flexible tube designed to carry sound from a user's mouth into an internal microphone in a headset.  Typically the tube is connected to the headset near the earpiece and extends to somewhere near the mouth of the user.")
(comment NotifiyingTheUserOfAStateChange "The collection of all instances of #$InformingProgramUser where the user is informed of some change of state.  This is distinguished from the more general #$InformingProgramUser in that the user can be given information in those events that are not the result of a state change -- e.g. by displaying the currently running processes or resources available.")
(comment VoiceMailProgram "The collection of applications that allow recording, storage, and retrieval of telephone voice messages.")
(comment hasExpertiseToDegree "unassert for testing 

(#$implies 
  (#$and 
    (#$supportSessionTypeFor ?PROB-TYPE ?SESSION-TYPE) 
    (#$hasExpertiseToDegree ?X ?SESSION-TYPE ?EXP)) 
  (#$hasExpertiseToDegree ?X ?PROB-TYPE ?EXP))
")
(comment orgTechSupportedEventType "(#$orgTechSupportedEventType ORG EVENT-TYPE) means that ORG provides tech support for employees performing instances of EVENT-TYPE.  For example, partitioning a hard drive, connecting to the company intranet, etc.")
(comment preservedInIterativeTotality "(#$preservedInIterativeTotality ROLE-PRED) means that when a actor plays ROLE-PRED in a situation of SIT-TYPE, and SIT-TYPE is iterated into an #$IteratedEventScene of type ITERATED-TYPE as part of some larger situation of type SUPER-TYPE (in other words, (#$iterativeSubEventTypesTotality SUPER-TYPE SIT-TYPE ITERATED-TYPE)), then each such actor also fills ROLE-PRED in the #$IteratedEventScene of type ITERATED-TYPE.  For example, 
(#$preservedInIterativeTotality #$objectActedOn).")
(comment iterativeTotalityVersion "(#$iterativeTotalityVersion ROLE-PRED1 ROLE-PRED2) means that when an actor plays ROLE-PRED1 in a situation of SIT-TYPE, and SIT-TYPE is iterated into an #$IteratedEventScene of type ITERATED-TYPE as part of some larger situation of type SUPER-TYPE (in other words, (#$iterativeSubEventTypesTotality SUPER-TYPE SIT-TYPE ITERATED-TYPE)), then each such actor plays the different role, ROLE-PRED2, in the #$IteratedEventScene of type ITERATED-TYPE.  For example, (#$iterativeTotalityVersion #$primaryObjectMoving #$objectMoving)")
(comment sitPreventsOccurrenceOfSitTypeDuringSit "(#$sitPreventsOccurrenceOfSitTypeDuringSit S1 S2 S-TYPE) means that the occurrence of S1 causes it to be the case that S2 has no sub-event that is an instance of S-TYPE.")
(comment OysterMushroom "The collection of oyster mushrooms.")
(comment ShiitakeMushroom "The collection of shiitake mushrooms.")
(comment AgaricusBisporus "The collection of Agaricus bisporus mushrooms, commonly known as \"white mushrooms.")
(comment Chanterelle "The collection of chanterelles.")
(comment equivalentRolePlayersOfType-SitTypeToSubSitType "<code>(#$equivalentRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType SITTYPE ROLE SUBSITTYPE ROLE2 TYPE)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SITTYPE</code>, where <code>SUBSIT</code> is a subsituation of <code>SIT</code> of the type <code>SUBSITTYPE</code>, whatever things of type <code>TYPE</code> play <code>ROLE</code> in <code>SIT</code> also play <code>ROLE2</code> in <code>SUBSIT</code>, and vice versa.")
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly)
(disjointWith SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly)
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly SpindleApparatusAssembly)
(comment FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusDisassembly.  Each instance of  #$FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly is an event in which a #$FirstMeioticSpindle breaks apart in a cell during #$TelophaseI.")
(disjointWith SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly SpindleApparatusAssembly)
(disjointWith SecondMeioticSpindleAssembly SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly)
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindleAssembly SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly)
(comment SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly "A specialization of #$SpindleApparatusDisassembly.  Each instance of  #$SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly is an event in which a #$SecondMeioticSpindle breaks apart in a cell during #$TelophaseII.")
(disjointWith FirstMeioticSpindleDisassembly SecondMeioticSpindleDisassembly)
(comment CMUMachineReadingOntology "The #$subWorks of #$MRSharedOntology that comprise the ontology (see #$Ontology) specifically developed by the Machine Reading Team at Carnegie Mellon University headed by Tom Mitchell.")
(comment FormationOfNucleolus "The collection of events in which a nucleolus forms -- an event that occurs during #$Telophase and #$TelophaseII.")
(comment Nucleolus "#$Nucleolus is a specialization of #$Organelle.  Each instance of #$Nucleolus is a structure found in a #$CellNucleus which serves to synthesize #$RibosomalRNA and to assemble ribosomes. A #$CellNucleus may have more than one #$Nucleolus.  At the beginning of #$Prophase and #$ProphaseI, the nucleoli disappear; new nucleoli form at the end of cell division in #$Telophase and #$TelophaseII.  In some types of eukaryotes, nucleoli also form in #$TelophaseI and disperse in #$ProphaseII.")
(comment partTypesFactsForType "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate used to query for salient facts about the #$partTypes of a type of #$Individual. <code>(#$partTypesFactsForType TYPE SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is a true statement about <code>TYPE</code> with respect to #$properParts of instances of <code>TYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$partTypesFactsForType #$Pizza (#$partTypes #$Pizza #$PizzaCrust))</code> means that it is true pizza that pizza has a pizza crust.")
(comment BindingOfEpinephrineToGProtein-linkedReceptor "A specialization of #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand.  Each instance of #$BindingOfEpinephrineToGProtein-linkedReceptor is a chemical binding event in which an epinephrine molecule binds to a G protein-linkd receptor to initiate a glycogen breakdown transduction pathway.")
(comment ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent classes by means of the types of #$ChemicalObject whose separation characterizes the class.  More specifically, (#$ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn MOL-TYPE-BROKEN MOL-TYPE-SEPARATED) denotes the class of all breakings of chemical bonds wherein an instance of MOL-TYPE-SEPARATED separates from an instance of MOL-TYPE-BROKEN, resulting in a new #$ChemicalObject. See also the #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical, #$typesSeparatedInUnbindingEventType.")
(comment yesNoQueryFolderEnabled "This specifies whether the CAE will produce a folder of yes/no queries for the task.")
(comment allowsImplies "This specifies whether the CAE will include #$implies among the list of allowed connectives.")
(comment allowsAnd "This specifies whether the CAE will include #$and among the list of allowed connectives.")
(comment allowsOr "This specifies whether the CAE will include #$or among the list of allowed connectives.")
(comment allowsUnknownSentence "This specifies whether the CAE will include #$unknownSentence among the list of allowed \"connectives\".")
(comment allowsNot "This specifies whether the CAE will include #$not among the list of allowed connectives.")
(comment MemoryLocationCopyingFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions that can be employed to copy a numeric entry in binary code from one location in computer memory to another.")
(comment ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType "A #$SecondOrderCollection faceting #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages.  Each instance of #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType is a collection of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages sharing a number of characteristic coding features, such as the characterization of the entry point of the program.")
(comment codeLanguageFamily "(#$codeLanguageFamily CODE FAMILY) means that the #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType of the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage CODE is written in is FAMILY.")
(comment hasProgrammingLanguageFamily "A typed specialization of #$isa.  (#$hasProgrammingLanguageFamily LANGUAGE LANGUAGE-FAMILY) means that the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage LANGUAGE belongs to the #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType LANGUAGE-FAMILY.")
(comment C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily "The 'C' programming family of languages, whose instances include #$C-ProgrammingLanguage, #$CPlusPlus-ProgrammingLanguage, and #$CMinusMinus-ProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment entryPointOfProgram "Where PROGRAM is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS, (#$entryPointOfProgram PROGRAM DECLARATION) means that DECLARATION is the #$FunctionDeclaration that is the main executable code of the program, utilizing whatever other functions, constants, and variables are locally defined for the program together with such library functions as are called.")
(comment CodingCheckSpecification "The collection of all declarative code statements (instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Declaration) which specify conditions that determine whether or not a particular piece of executable code (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) gets executed or not.  Essential attributes include #$conditionCheckAppliesTo (identifies the executable code that the condition applies to) #$comparisonConditionChecked (identifies the #$NumericComparisonPredicate, if any, used in checking the condition, and #$nthArgForConditionCheckDenotedByExpression (used to identify the #$ComputerCodeExpression that denotes the term appearing in the Nth argument of the statement of the condition to be checked.")
(comment conditionCheckAppliesTo "(#$conditionCheckAppliesTo SPECIFICATION EXECUTABLE) means that SPECIFICATION states the condition that must be satisfied in order for EXECUTABLE to be executed in the program (#$ComputerProgram-CWIS) that subsumes both SPECIFICATION and EXECUTABLE.")
(comment comparisonConditionChecked "(#$comparisonConditionChecked SPECIFICATION COMP-PRED) means that the #$NumericComparisonPredicate COMP-PRED is explicitly referenced by SPECIFICATION as the condition to check on a binary tuple of values denoted by #$ComputerCodeExpressions.")
(comment nthArgForConditionCheckDenotedByExpression "(#$nthArgForConditionCheckDenotedByExpression CHECK-SPEC N EXPRESSION) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK-SPEC explicitly references EXPRESSION as denoting the value associated with the Nth argument of the condition it is checking.")
(comment conditionCheckComparison-ParameterToValue "(#$conditionCheckComparison-ParameterToValue CHECK-SPEC COMP-PRED N VALUE) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK-SPEC checks to see whether the input supplied as the Nth parameter value for the function in the executable code being checked (the code which is what the #$conditionCheckAppliesTo) has the relation COMP-PRED to VALUE.")
(comment conditionCheckComparison-ValueToParameter "(#$conditionCheckComparison-ValueToParameter CHECK-SPEC COMP-PRED VALUE N) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK-SPEC checks to see whether VALUE has the relation COMP-PRED to the input supplied as the Nth parameter value for the function in the executable code being checked (the code which is what the #$conditionCheckAppliesTo).")
(comment codeLanguageOfCodingFunction "(#$codeLanguageOfCodingFunction CODE-FN LANGUAGE) means that the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN can be invoked in the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage LANGUAGE using a reserved name in LANGUAGE.")
(comment codeLanguageFamilyOfCodingFunction "(#$codeLanguageFamilyOfCodingFunction CODE-FN LANGUAGE-FAMILY) means that the same reserved name is used for invoking the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN in all of the languages of LANGUAGE-FAMILY.")
(comment receptorSiteInBindingEvent "Where BINDING is an #$AtomOrMoleculeBindingEvent, (#$receptorSiteInBindingEvent BINDING RECEPTOR) means that in a larger situational context of which BINDING is a part, RECEPTOR is a #$Molecule that functions as a 'receptor' for some #$signalMoleculeInBindingEvent:  binding this molecule to RECEPTOR will mediately or immediately trigger a cytological 'response', either in isolation or in concert with several other typologically identical binding events.")
(disjointWith AminoAcidTypeByChemicalSpecies ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(comment ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$Molecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules of a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex, and all are of the same #$ChemicalSubstanceType.  Cf. the more specific collection #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies, which is a collection whose instances all share the same chemical formula and structure.  Note that proteins, with their large complex molecules, are often given the same name despite subtle variations in structure.  The collection containing all the variants would be an instance of  #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType, while only particular variants would be instances of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies.  For example, #$AdenylylCyclaseMolecule has ten known variants in mammals that differ in their sequence of anmino acids and are coded for by different genes.  It is therefore an instance of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType.")
(comment cellMembranePotential "(#$cellMembranePotential CELL VOLTS) states that the voltage difference across the #$CellMembrane of CELL is the #$Voltage VOLTS.  Membrane potential is determined by subtracting the voltage of the environment outside the cell (which may be the external enviroment if the cell is a single-celled organism, or the #$ExtracellularFluid if the cell is part of a larger organism) from the voltage of the cytoplasm inside the cell.")
(comment IonChannelBindingWithLigand "Instances are events in which a #$LigandGatedIonChannel receptor binds with its ligand (see #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject).  This binding causes the ion channel to open or close, thus promoting or halting movement of ions (which, depending on the type of #$IonChannel, may be of a very specific type), thus causing the electrical potential across the cell's membrane to change.  #$IonChannelBindingWithLigand is a part of #$CellMembranePotentialRegulation.")
(comment CellMembranePotentialRegulation "Instances of #$CellMembranePotentialRegulation are events in which the potential across a cell's plasma membrane (see #$cellMembranePotential) is controlled via the relative concentration of #$Ions, which are ejected or emitted by the cell's #$IonChannels.")
(comment ChangeInCellIonConcentration "Instances are changes in the concentration of #$Ions, where the region affected is an instance of #$Cell.")
(comment PhosphorylatedTyrosineKinaseDimer "A #$ProteinComplex formed during the activation of tyrosine-kinase receptors.")
(comment similarityFactsForTypes "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate used to query for salient facts about the #$partTypes of a type of #$Individual. <code>(#$similarityFactsForTypes TYPE1 TYPE2 SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is a true statement about the similarity of <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment resultTypesFactsForType "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate used to query for salient facts about the outputs and results of a type of #$CreationEvent. <code>(#$resultTypesFactsForType TYPE SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is a true statement about <code>TYPE</code> with respect to the results of instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment Ficus-WoodyPlant "The biological genus Ficus is a group of woody plants (including species of trees, vines and shrubs).")
(comment FigTree "The collection of all common fig trees. The collection #$FigTree is an #$OrganismClassificationType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment CytologicalProcessesQueryPredicate "A specialization of #$Predicate.  Each instance of #$CytologicalProcessesQueryPredicate is a predicate that, in the context of cytological processes, is to be used only for querying.")
(comment VQBPredicate "The collection of predicates supported by the Visual Query Builder (a tool that is found in the CAE).")
(comment generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls-Conditional "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermGenls-Conditional SET-1 SET-2) means that if a specialization of each term that is an element of SET-1 is a valid term in the search query results, then the elements of SET-2 should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.")
(comment generateFormulasForElements-TermIsa-Conditional "(#$generateFormulasForElements-TermIsa-Conditional SET-1 SET-2) means that if an instance of each term that is an element of SET-1 is a valid term in the search query results, then the elements of SET-2 should have the appropriate formulas generated for them.")
(comment organizationPostsCallsOfTypeAtURLString "(#$organizationPostsCallsOfTypeAtURLString ORG PROPOSAL-TYPE URL-STRING) means that URL-STRING is the URL for a website that posts information about instances of PROPOSAL-TYPE issued by ORG.")
(comment OrganismTypeByAilment "A collection of collections.  Each #$OrganismTypeByAilment describes an animal's state of health relative to some type of #$AilmentCondition. Examples: #$Immune, #$Recovered, #$AtRisk.")
(comment stateOfAilment "The predicate #$stateOfAilment expresses the relation between an organism, a type of #$AilmentCondition that it has, and the state of the disease, which must be an instance of #$OrganismTypeByAilment. For instance, (#$stateOfAilment #$Kean #$GettingSick #$Influenza) means that Kean is comming down with the flu.")
(comment Grub "The collection of all grubs. A type of #$Beetle and #$Larva. The collection #$Grub is a #$LifeStageType and an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment Teiidae "A #$BiologicalFamily, and a sub-taxon of #$Lizard.  Teiidae is a family of lizards native to the Americas.")
(comment NewMexicoWhiptail "An all-female species of whiptails that reproduces via parthenogenesis.")
(comment Basiliscus "A #$BiologicalGenus, and a sub-taxon of #$Corytophanidae.  Basiliscus is a genus of lizards renknowed for sometimes running as a biped.")
(comment Washer-Hardware "A typically disc-shaped device used with screws and nuts.")
(comment PhonographRecord "The collection of all phonograph records. A type of #$RecordedSoundProduct and #$DiscStorageMedium. The collection #$PhonographRecord is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory. Each instance of #$PhonographRecord is a recorded sound storage device consisting of a flat disc with a very narrow spiral groove that starts at the outer edge and winds toward the middle of the disc.  Instances of this collection are intended to be played on instances of #$RecordPlayer.")
(comment Cnemidophorus "A #$BiologicalGenus, and a sub-taxon of #$Teiidae.  Cnemidophorus is a genus of lizards commonly known as \"whiptails\".")
(comment criticalPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType "<code>(#$criticalPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means any instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> must have an instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as a physical part in order to be an instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>.  See also #$criticalPhysicalPartTypeForFunctioningOfWholeType.")
(comment cellHasNumberOfChromatids "<code>(#$cellHasNumberOfChromatids CELL NUMBER)</code> identifies <code>NUMBER</code> as the number of chromatids present in <code>CELL</code>, an instance of #$EukaryoticCell.  Note that this is an instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation, as the number of chromatids may change depending on where in the cell cycle a cell is.")
(comment Explains-Prop-BinRelPropFn "(#$Explains-Prop-BinRelPropFn BIN-REL) denotes a quaternary predicate QP that relates a proposition to the binary predicate BIN-REL and two further terms T1 and T2, where (QP ?X BIN-REL T1 T2)) is equivalent to (#$explains-PropProp ?X (BIN-REL T1 T2).")
(comment explains-Prop-BinRelProp "(#$explains-Prop-BinRelProp BIN-REL QUAT-REL) means that QUAT-REL is the quaternary predicate QP that relates a proposition to the binary predicate BIN-REL and two further terms T1 and T2, where (QP ?X BIN-REL T1 T2)) is equivalent to (#$explains-PropProp ?X (BIN-REL T1 T2).")
(comment oppositeSituationTypesWRTActorType "(#$oppositeSituationTypesWRTActorType   SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 ACTOR-TYPE) means that SIT-TYPE1 is the opposite of SIT-TYPE2 with respect to what happens to an instance of ACTOR-TYPE during instances of SIT-TYPE1 and SIT-TYPE2.")
(comment BeachActivityType "A second order collection.  Instances are types of human activities, instances of which usually or often occur at a #$SandyBeach-Recreational, such as sunbathing, surfing or swimming.")
(comment SunTanning "A specialization of #$ExposureEvent and #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$SunTanning is an event in which an agent (usually a #$HomoSapiens) exposes his or her skin to direct sunlight (or a simulation thereof), intentionally or not, and in the process gets a suntan on the exposed skin.")
(comment ComputingArchitectureConstant "The collection of all #$CycLConstants which denote key concepts associated with physical computing architectures.")
(comment ControlUnit-Computational "A collection of #$ComputerHardwareComponents, each of which manages certain key components of a computing architecture.  Specifically, the #$ControlUnit reads the code for the next instruction from the cell indicated by the #$ComputerProgramCounter, decodes the numerical code for the instruction into a set of commands or signals for each of the other target systems, increments the #$ComputerProgramCounter so that it points to the next instruction, reads whatever data the instruction requires from cells in memory (or perhaps from an input device), provides the necessary data to an #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit or #$ComputerMemoryRegister, instructs the hardware to perform the specified operation (if necessary), writes the result from the #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit back to #$ComputerMemoryRegisters or an output device, and then iterates the process for the succeeding code instruction, until all instructions have been read.")
(comment Arithmetic-LogicUnit "Each instance of this collection is an #$ElectricalCircuit that is designed to perform arithmetic and/or logical operations.  The #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit (abbr. ALU) is a fundamental building block of the #$CentralProcessingUnit (CPU) of a computer. The processors inside modern CPUs accommodate very powerful and complex ALUs, and a single CPU may contain more than one ALU.")
(comment registerHasPhysicalMemoryLoc "(#$registerHasPhysicalMemoryLoc REGISTER N) means that the #$PositiveInteger N denotes the location of the #$ComputerMemoryRegister REGISTER in physical memory.")
(comment lengthOfRegister "(#$lengthOfRegister REGISTER LENGTH) means that the #$ComputerMemoryRegister REGISTER has the length LENGTH, where LENGTH is given as a #$ComputerMemoryCapacity measured, e.g., in #$Bytes.")
(comment ComputerMemoryRegister-Octet "The collection of all computer memory registers with a #$lengthOfRegister of 8 bytes.")
(comment NthRegisterInMemoryFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for referring to #$ComputerMemoryRegisters.  (#$NthRegisterInMemoryFn MEMORY N) denotes the the #$ComputerMemoryRegister at location N in the #$ComputerMemory MEMORY.")
(comment registerHasPhysicalLocationInMemory "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$NthRegisterInMemoryFn.  Where MEMORY is an instance of #$ComputerMemory and N is a #$PositiveInteger, (#$registerHasPhysicalLocationInMemory MEMORY N REGISTER) means that REGISTER is the #$ComputerMemoryRegister with location N in MEMORY.")
(comment ComputerProgramCounter "Each instance is a group of #$ComputerMemoryRegisters which keeps track of the location in memory that the next instruction is to be read from in program execution.")
(comment PointingToAMemoryRegister "The collection of all computational operations consisting of a #$ComputerProgramCounter pointing to a #$ComputerMemoryRegister.")
(comment programCounterPointing "(#$programCounterPointing POINTING COUNTER) means that the #$ComputerProgramCounter that is indicating a #$ComputerMemoryRegister in the #$PointingToAMemoryRegister instance POINTING is COUNTER.  A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that is functional in the second argument.")
(comment memoryRegisterPointedTo "(#$memoryRegisterPointedTo POINTING REGISTER) means that the #$ComputerMemoryRegister indicated by the #$ComputerProgramCounter in the #$PointingToAMemoryRegister instance POINTING is REGISTER.  A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot that is functional in the second argument.")
(comment memoryLocPointedTo "(#$memoryLocPointedTo POINTING MEMLOC) means that the numeric address in the #$ComputerMemory indicated by the #$ComputerProgramCounter in pointing is MEMLOC.")
(comment operatingSystemOfRunTimeEnvironment "Where ACTION is a #$ProgramAction, (#$operatingSystemOfRunTimeEnvironment ACTION OS) means that OS is the #$OperatingSystem of the run-time environment wherein ACTION is executed.")
(comment operatingSystemSetsCommandLineBitWidth "(#$operatingSystemSetsCommandLineBitWidth OS N) means that the #$OperatingSystem OS limits the width of command line entries to N bits.")
(comment componentTransferredTo-BinaryDataTransfer "Where TRANSFER is a #$BinaryDataTransfer, (#$componentTransferredTo-BinaryDataTransfer TRANSFER DESTINATION) means that DESTINATION is the #$ComputerStorageDevice to which the binary data is transferred in TRANSFER.")
(comment componentTransferredFrom-BinaryDataTransfer "Where TRANSFER is a #$BinaryDataTransfer, (#$componentTransferredFrom-BinaryDataTransfer TRANSFER SOURCE) means that SOURCE is the #$ComputerStorageDevice from which the binary data is transferred in TRANSFER.")
(comment valueTransferred "(#$valueTransferred TRANSFER NUMBER) means that the number encoded by the binary string transferred in the #$BinaryDataTransfer TRANSFER is NUMBER.")
(comment binaryStringOfTransfer "Where TRANSFER is a #$BinaryDataTransfer, (#$binaryStringOfTransfer TRANSFER STRING) means that STRING gives the binary form of the number whose representation is transferred from one #$ComputerStorageDevice to another in TRANSFER.")
(comment TransferringDataViaControlUnit "The collection of all #$BinaryDataTransfers wherein a #$ControlUnit-Computational transfers data from some #$ComputerStorageDevice to a #$ComputerMemoryRegister.")
(comment controlUnitReading "Where TRANSFER is a #$TransferringDataViaCPU, (#$controlUnitReading TRANSFER CONTROL-UNIT) means that CONTROL-UNIT is the #$ControlUnit-Computational which directs the tranfer of the binary data in TRANSFER.")
(comment registerTransferredTo "(#$registerTransferredTo TRANSFER REGISTER) means that REGISTER is a #$ComputerMemoryRegister to which the #$valueTransferred is transferred in TRANSFER by the #$ControlUnit-Computational that is mediating TRANSFER (#$controlUnitReading).")
(comment registerLocTransferredTo "(#$registerLocTransferredTo ?TRANSFER ?MEM-ADDRESS) means that the physical memory address of the #$ComputerMemoryRegister that is the destination (#$registerTransferredTo) in the #$TransferringDataViaControlUnit  TRANSFER is ?MEM-ADDRESS")
(comment TransferringDataFromAMemoryRegister "The collection of all instances of #$TransferringDataViaControlUnit wherein the source of the transfer (the #$componentTransferredFrom-BinaryDataTransfer) is a #$ComputerMemoryRegister.")
(comment registerLocTransferredFrom "(#$registerLocTransferredFrom ?TRANSFER ?MEM-ADDRESS) means that the physical memory address of the #$ComputerMemoryRegister that is the source (#$registerTransferredFrom) in the #$TransferringDataFromAMemoryRegister TRANSFER is ?MEM-ADDRESS.")
(comment registerTransferredFrom "(#$registerTransferredFrom TRANSFER REGISTER) means that the #$ComputerMemoryRegister REGISTER is the source of the #$TransferingDataFromAMemoryRegister TRANSFER.")
(comment aLUTransferredTo "(#$aLUTransferredTo TRANSFER ALU) means that the #$Arithmetic-LogicUnit ALU is a destination (#$componentTransferredTo-BinaryDataTransfer) of the #$TransferringDataFromAMemoryRegister TRANSFER")
(comment Parthenogenesis "Parthenogenesis is a type of #$AsexualReproductionEvent. Parthenogenesis is done by female organisms that grow embryos without fertilization by a male.")
(comment defaultAssertMt "<code>(#$defaultAssertMt SPECIFICATION MT)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, assertions of constructed groups should be made in <code>MT</code>.")
(comment cHIBLProgramFilePathname "(#$cHIBLProgramFilePathname PROGRAM PATHNAME) means that the #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS is stored in the file whose pathname is PATHNAME.")
(comment cHIBLMaximalFunctionBlockString "(#$cHIBLMaximalFunctionBlockString CHIBL-PROG STRING) means that STRING represents a 'maximal' function block within the body of CHIBL-PROG: i.e., an information structure having the form '// Function a [LOCATION] {[FUNCTION-BODY]}', where [LOCATION] specifies a program location and [FUNCTION-BODY] is the code body of the function specified.")
(comment cellTypeOfOrganType "(#$cellTypeOfOrganType CELL-TYPE ORGAN-TYPE) means that CELL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$Cell that are the basic unit for any #$Organ of type ORGAN-TYPE.")
(comment UnphosphorylatedTyrosineKinaseDimer "A #$ProteinComplex formed during the activation of tyrosine-kinase receptors that is the direct result of aggregation.  Instances of this collection may be phosphorylated, becoming instances of #$PhosphorylatedTyrosineKinaseDimer.")
(comment CappingProcess-ChemicalReaction "The process whereby a guanine 'cap' is bonded to the 5' end of an #$RNAMolecule in eukaryotic transcription.")
(comment PolyadenylationProcess "The process whereby a #$PolyATail is appended to the 3' of an #$RNAMolecule in eukaryotic transcription.")
(comment ProteinDimerization "Instances of #$ProteinDimerization are events in which two #$ProteinMolecules come together to form a #$ProteinDimer.")
(comment caeQueryLibraryDefaultAllowedModules "A binary predicate used to set default values for the #$InferenceAllowedModulesParameter
for queries constructed via the #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram, relative to a specific analyst task.")
(comment Cyclooxygenase "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule responsible for prostanoid formation.")
(disjointWith TraditionalNSAID SelectiveCOX-2Inhibitor)
(disjointWith ArrestibleProcessType CycleTypeByIterationType)
(disjointWith CyclicalProcessType CycleTypeByIterationType)
(comment CycleTypeByIterationType "A specialization of #$TemporalObjectType that facets #$Cycle-Situation.  Instances are sub-collections of #$Cycle-Situation that are characterized by being comprised of iterations through some class of event.  Examples include #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle, instances of which are series of iterations through a particular type of event that consists of the growth and division of a cell into two (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle).")
(comment SignalTransduction-CellularProcess "The second of three stages in the cell-signaling process (see #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell), this is the stage after a receptor binds with a ligand (see #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand) and consists of the \"transfer\" of the metaphorical signal to the appropriate chemical object within the cytoplasm or cell nucleus.  The completion of this event is followed by an instance of #$CellularLevelResponseToSignal, completing the cell-signaling script.")
(comment PhosphorylatingAChemicalObjectOfTypeFn "A collection denoting function used to identify important sub-collections of #$Phosphorylation by the type of organic chemical object phosphorylated.  Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$OrganicChemicalObject, (#$PhosphorylatingAChemicalObjectOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$Phosphorylation wherein the  thing which becomes bound to one or more phosphate groups is an instance of MOL-TYPE.")
(comment chemicalObjectTypePhosphorylatedInInstances "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PhosphorylatingAChemicalObjectOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$OrganicChemicalObject, (#$chemicalObjectTypePhosphorylatedInInstances MOL-TYPE PHOSPHORYLATING-TYPE) means that PHOSPHORYLATING-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$Phosphorylation wherein the chemical object which becomes bound to one or more phosphate groups is an instance of MOL-TYPE.")
(comment Dimerization "A specialization of #$PhysicalSynthesis and #$ChemicalBonding.  Each instance of #$Dimerization is a chemical reaction in which a #$DimerMolecule is produced.")
(comment ReceptorMoleculeActivationEvent "The collection of #$ChemicalInteractions in which some #$ReceptorMolecule becomes activated, so that it may initiate a signal transduction pathway (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess).  The necessary first step of receptor activation is the binding of a ligand to the receptor (see #$ReceptorBindingWithLigand).")
(comment TyrosineKinaseReceptorActivationByGrowthFactor "Instances are events in which a tyronsine-kinase receptor system becomes activated by molecules of some #$GrowthFactor.")
(comment IonChannelConformationChangeEvent "Instances of #$IonChannelConformationChangeEvent are events in which one #$IonChannel undergoes a change in shape.  Conformation changes of interest are those that open or close the channel to the passage of one or more types of #$Ion.")
(comment appAllowsArbitraryAssertionDeletion "This specifies whether an end-user application will allow a user to remove arbitrary assertions from the Cyc KB.")
(comment Herbicide "The collection of all herbicide. A type of #$Pesticide. The collection #$Pesticide is a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment WalnutFamily "The collection of all walnut trees. A type of #$DicotSubclass. #$WalnutFamily is a #$BiologicalOrder and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment TransFattyAcid "A specialization of #$UnsaturatedFattyAcid.  Each instance of #$TransFattyAcid is an unsaturated fatty acid with a trans double-bond between carbon atoms in its molecules.")
(comment ToxicSubstance "A specialization of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance.  Each instance of #$ToxicSubstance is a substance that is toxic or poisonous to humans.")
(comment Pteridophyte "Vascular plants that produce neither flowers nor seeds.")
(comment GymnospermGroup "A biological group of plant classes whose members all bear seeds which are not protected by a carpel.  The #$GymnospermGroup includes the #$Conifers and gingkos.  See also #$Seed, #$Carpel.")
(comment Spermatophyte "The collection of land plants that produce seeds.")
(comment Pterophyte "A #$BiologicalSubdivision including ferns.")
(disjointWith Pterophyte Spermatophyte)
(comment caeQueryLibraryDefaultKEIrrelevantRedundantTermsAllowed "A parameter of #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram that determines whether binding sets that contain terms tagged as #$keIrrelevantTerm are displayed. <code>(#$caeQueryLibraryDefaultKEIrrelevantRedundantTermsAllowed SPECIFICATION #$True)</code> means that in the CAE specification <code>SPECIFICATION</code>, such binding sets are displayed, whereas <code>(#$caeQueryLibraryDefaultKEIrrelevantRedundantTermsAllowed SPECIFICATION #$False)</code> means they are not.")
(comment DNAMolecularSegment "The collection of continuous subsequences of particular #$DNAMolecules, and a spec of #$MolecularComponent.  Each instance of #$DNAMolecularSegment is composed of two #$PolynucleotideStrandSegments which are part of the two #$DNAStrands that make up the larger molecule.  An important specialization of #$DNAMolecularSegment is #$Gene-HereditaryUnit, which includes those #$DNAMolecularSegments whose final product is either a type of #$PeptideMolecule or an #$RNAMolecule.")
(comment gene-GISPhysicalGeneType "(#$gene-GISPhysicalGeneType GIS PHYS-GENE-TYPE) states that the collection of physical genes, PHYS-GENE-TYPE (a specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit), instantiates the #$Gene-GIS, GIS.")
(comment codingSequenceHasInstructionsForProductType "(#$codingSequenceHasInstructionsForProductType STRAND MOL-TYPE) means that the
#$CodingSequence-MolecularSegment STRAND codes for the biochemical synthesis of MOL-TYPE, a #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies, by virtue of the nucleotide sequence that it instantiates.")
(comment carriesGeneticInstructionForType "(#$carriesGeneticInstructionForType POLY MOL-TYPE) means that POLY,
an instance of #$Polynucleotide, has a sequence that codes for
biochemical synthesis of molecules of the type MOL-TYPE, an instance of
#$MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies.   Note that POLY may contain several instances of #$CodingSequence-MolecularSegment, and thus have instructions for more than one biochemical product.  This is especially true if POLY is an entire #$DNAMolecule.")
(comment geneTypeCodesForProductType "(#$geneTypeCodesForProductType GENE-TYPE MOL-TYPE) states that instances of the #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, GENE-TYPE, are typically decoded via transcription (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and, for peptides, translation (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) to produce the biochemical product, MOL-TYPE.  MOL-TYPE is a specialization of either #$PeptideMolecule or #$RNAMolecule.")
(comment SpecifiedPartTypeCollection "An instance of second order collection.  Instances are collections that are defined intensionally as the collection of individuals that are part of some object of type, for some specified type.  Examples include #$MotorcyclePart and #$OrganismPart.")
(comment BiochemicalSignalingObject "The collection of #$ChemicalObjects ranging in complexity from #$Ions to #$Molecules that act as signals between cells or between parts of cells.  Such signals and the cellular responses to them play an essential role in the coordination of metabolic activities that allow the development and reproduction of both multicellular and single-celled organisms.")
(comment LocalBiochemicalSignalingObject "A specialization of #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject which includes those signal objects that are known to act locally, targeting cells in the vicinity of the cell which emits the signal.")
(comment NeurotransmitterMolecule "A specialization of #$LocalBiochemicalSignalingObject which includes those signal objects that typically mediate communication between #$Neurons.")
(comment PhosphorylationCascadeEndingWithTranscriptionFactorActivation "Instances are #$SignalTransductionCascades consisting of multiple #$PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule events, terminated by activation of a #$TranscriptionFactorEnzyme.")
(comment ExtracellularRegulationOfTranscription "Instances are scripts in which binding of a growth factor to a receptor in the cell membrane leads to activation of a transcription factor, thus affecting the outcome of transcription.")
(comment Dephosphorylation "A type of #$ChemicalInteraction in which a #$PhosphateIon is unbound from an organic molecule and released as a free ion. In cell biochemistry, #$Dephosphorylation is mediated by phosphatase enzymes (see #$ProteinPhosphataseMolecule).")
(disjointWith Phosphorylation Dephosphorylation)
(comment focalChemicalObject "Where CHEM is a #$ChemicalInteraction, (#$focalChemicalObject CHEM OBJ) states that OBJ plays the main, primary, or focal role in CHEM.  The identity of the focal actor in such events is not an intrinsic property of the event or the actor, but is rather determined by how the event is understood and explained by humans.")
(comment dephosphorylatedChemicalObject "<code>(#$dephosphorylatedChemicalObject DEPHOS OBJ)</code> identifies <code>OBJ</code> as the organic chemical object that is dephosphorylated (is stripped of one #$PhosphateIon) in <code>DEPHOS</code>, an instance of #$Dephosphorylation.")
(comment DephosphorylatingAProteinMolecule "The collection of all events in which a #$PhosphateIon is removed from a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex and released as a free ion.  Instances of #$DephosphorylatingAProteinMolecule are catalyzed by 'dedicated' enzymes, usually #$ProteinPhosphataseMolecules. The protein which is the #$outputsCreated of a #$DephosphorylatingAProteinMolecule is often thereby inactivated (see #$inactivatedFormOfEnzyme), and hence ready to be once again activated.  However, some proteins can be phosphorylated at multiple sites, and removing one phosphate group may not fully inactivated them.")
(disjointWith DephosphorylatingAProteinMolecule PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule)
(comment deviceTypeUsedWithDeviceType "An instance of #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate, (#$deviceTypeUsedWithDeviceType   TYPE1 TYPE2) means that instances of TYPE1 and TYPE2 are designed to interact functionally with each other.  There is no specific temporal order to the design so this relation holds between two object types that were designed to work together from the start as well as between two object types where one was designed well after the design of the first.  The only constraint along these lines is that the design is intentional.  So, this relation does not hold between Screwdriver and ViceGrip even though instances of each can be used with each other.")
(comment ExpertisePreservingThroughMacroPredicate "The collection of predicates that specify relations where expertise is transferred via rule macros such as #$relationExistsAll or #$relationAllExists through the associated technical problem concepts.  E.g. #$hasAccessory is a member of this collection because when a tech support person for an organization has some expertise in computer desktop hardware, and there is a hardware component type such that each of its instances is an accessory for some computer desktop hardware and that component type is in general supported by the organization for which the tech support person works, then at least some expertise in supporting that accessory type can be assumed.")
(comment orgTechSupportedThing "(#$orgTechSupportedThing ORG THING) means that ORG's technical support department supports uses of THING.  This is the generalization of #$orgTechSupportedProgram, #$orgTechSupportedArtifactType, and #$orgTechSupportedEventType.  Only in cases when the organization supports something that is not a member of any of those specific types should this relationship be used directly.")
(comment ComputerProgramTypeBySimilarWorkflow "A collection of types of computer programs.  Each instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeBySimilarWorkflow is a collection of programs (see #$ComputerProgram-CW) whose instances all serve a similar function and whose functions are accessed in a similar manner.  For instance, #$WordProcessingProgram-Visual is an instance of this collection because the workflow paradigms of highlighting text, dragging and dropping paragraphs and other functions are performed in a similar manner among the instances of that collection -- e.g. while there are many differences between Open Office and MS Word, the basic workflow remains similar.")
(comment JetBrainsComputerProgram "Software products made by #$JetBrains-TheCompany.")
(comment PyxisMobileComputerProgram "Software products made by #$PyxisMobileInc.")
(comment McAfeeComputerProgram "Software products made by #$McAfee-CommercialOrganization.")
(comment OpenTextConnectivitySolutionsGroupComputerProgram "Software products made by #$OpenTextConnectivitySolutionsGroup-TheCompany.")
(comment OracleComputerProgram "Software products made by #$OracleCorporation .")
(comment FoxRiverExecutionComputerProgram "Software products made by #$FoxRiverExecution-Company.")
(comment EmbarcaderoComputerProgram "Software products made by #$Embarcadero-Company.")
(comment FactsetResearchSystemsComputerProgram "Software products made by #$FactsetResearchSystemsInc.")
(comment CiscoSystemsComputerProgram "Software products made by #$CiscoSystemsInc.")
(comment AquaFoldComputerProgram "Software products made by #$AquaFold-Company.")
(comment ResearchInMotionComputerProgram "Software products made by #$ResearchinMotionLimited.")
(comment TechSupportPerson "The collection of all tech support personnel. A type of #$Person.")
(comment ConnectingInformationStoresTogether "The collection of events in which at least two different instances of #$InformationStore are linked so that information in one or the other is available for systems that use the store.  For example, linking your Facebook profile to your gmail account is an action that is an instance of this connection.")
(comment GPG-EncryptionProgram "GNU Privacy Guard (GPG) is an open-source, free, drop-in replacement for PGP cryptographic software.")
(comment TelephoneRoutingProgram-Client "the collection of dedicated client programs that allow one to make phone calls over a supported device that route the calls through a different network than the one normally used with the device.  Commonly used within corporate environments to allow employees to make phone calls to certain locations without incurring certain charges on their accounts.")
(comment Teleconference-External "The collection of teleconferences where at least some participants are not members of each other's organization -- e.g. a teleconference hosted by some company where some participants are non-employees of that company.")
(comment VideoTeleconference "The collection of all teleconferences where at least some participants are also viewing live video of participants of the teleconference.  There must be at least some cases of two-way video communication.  That is, at least one pair of participants from discrete locations must be able to see each other through the video link.  For example, if Bob, Mary and John are involved in a teleconference and each are at a discrete location, then the participants would not be video teleconferencing if Bob were viewing Mary, Mary were viewing John and John were viewing Bob.  At least one pair out of the three must be viewing each other.")
(comment Teleconference-Internal "The collection of teleconferences where all the participants are members or employees of the same organization.")
(disjointWith ScheduledAction (CollectionDifferenceFn Teleconference-Internal ScheduledAction))
(comment Teleconference "Each instance of this collection is a #$Meeting-SocialGathering whose primary compound subevent is some instance of Telecommunication-Teleconference.  That is, each instance of this collection is a meeting where the participants are essentially engaged in some #$Telecommunication-Teleconference activities.  Almost all events of this sort involve voice communication as the primary means of information exchange, but in some cases coded or purely visual teleconferences could occur.")
(comment HighDefinitionVideoTeleconferencing "The subcollection of #$VideoTeleconference where the video portion of the teleconference is presented in \"high definition\".  <i>High Definition</i> is a relative term, but at the time of the writing of this comment it typically means at a resolution of 720 horizontal lines (progressive scan) or 1080 horizontal lines (either progressive or interleaved scan) or better.")
(comment DesktopVideoTeleconferencing "The subcollection of #$VideoTeleconference where the video portion of the teleconference is enabled through standard desktop computer hardware and software.  For example, video teleconferencing conducted through a computer mounted video camera and consumer level software would be instances of this collection.  On the other hand, live 2-way briefings/news feeds accomplished via professional grade audio and video equipment run by the media department of a large corporation would not be instances of this collection.")
(comment GoogleMaps "A web-based mapping service that offers a variety of map based features such as street maps of cities and highways, satellite and street views, and driving directions.")
(comment JarFile-Java "The collection of all Java Jar files considered as abstract compiled code files.")
(comment JavaProgramLibraryOrEnvironment "The collection of all Java related entities such as particular Java programs, implementations of the Java virtual machine, code libraries -- jar files or sets of jar files distributed as units and capable of being used in a variety of programs, and other miscellanea.")
(comment QuerySearchConstraintConstant "The collection of CycL constants that constrain the CAE's query search in some specific way supported by the SubL and Java code.")
(comment BartonellaBacilliformis "A collection of all #$Bacterium in the #$BiologicalSpecies  #$BartonellaBacilliformis.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are responsible for the infection Bartonellosis.")
(comment BartonellaQuintana "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Bartonella in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment Bartonella "A collection of all the #$Bacterium in the #$BiologicalGenus #$Bartonella.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are motile with a unipolar flagella and are #$AerobicBacterium.")
(comment Bacillus "A collection of all #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$AerobicBacterium and #$SporeFormingBacterium.  Most #$BiologicalSpecies of the #$Bacillus are #$Saprophytes.")
(comment BorreliaBurgdorferi "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under the #$Borrelia in
the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells cause Lyme Disease and are
transmitted by the bite of a #$Tick.  These are microaerophilic")
(comment Borrelia "A collection of all #$Bacterium classified in the #$Borrelia. These are helical cells and cause tick-borne and lice-borne relapsing #$Fever in humans.  They are motile by means of periplasmic flagella.")
(comment ClostridiumBotulinum "A collection of #$Bacterium. A #$BiologicalSpecies formed under
the #$Clostridium genus in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells
cause #$Botulism.  They are found in soil, water
sediment, and occasionally in animal feces.  C. botulinum is divided into
seven strains, A - G, based on antigenic specificity of their individual
toxins.  All strains produce a neurotoxin of extraordinary toxicity: the
estimated lethal dose for humans is less than 1 microgram.  Spores are
highly resistant to heat.")
(comment Mycoplasma "The collection of #$Mycoplasma are widely recognized pathogens of the
respiratory and urogenital tracts and joints of animals. These are pleomorphic cells, ranging for #$CoccusBacterium to a pear-shape or ovid.  These are #$GramNegativeBacterium and usually #Bacterium-Immotile.")
(comment Mycoplasmataceae "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the #$BiologicalGenus #$Mycoplasma and #$Ureaplasma.")
(comment Ureaplasma "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom, distinguished from #$Mycoplasma by its abilty to hydrolyze urea.")
(comment Nocardia "A collection of #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These are non-motile #$BacillusBacterium with branching vegetative hyphae.  These are Gram-positive to Gram-variable #$Bacterium.  They are mesophilic and catalase-positive.  Also, these are chemoorganotrophic with an oxidative type metabolism.  #$Nocardia is often mistaken for #$Actinomyces-Genus, but these are strict #$AerobicBacterium.  These rarely cause disease in humans, predominately in immunocompromised patients.  #$BiologicalSpecies may be distinguished from one another by their patterns of proteolytic hydrolysis.")
(comment NocardiaAsteroides "A collection of #$Bacterium that is an opportunistic pathogen of humans.  These #$ProkaryoticCells cause pulmonary #$Infection after being inhaled.  The primary lesion site in the lungs shows an acute inflammation with suppuration and destruction of parenchyma.  Unlike #$Actinomyces-Genus #$Infections, these have little fibrosis and localization.")
(comment NocardiaBrasiliensis "A collection of #$Bacterium that may cause a superficial skin #$Infection in humans.  Usually, the route of infection occurs atfer some type of outdoor activity that results in a minor trauma to the skin (i.e. a thorn prick).  The infection commonly produces a localized pustule.  If they gain access to subcutaneous tissues, an infection similar to the one caused by Actinomudra Madurae may occur.")
(comment Actinomyces "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus under the #$MoneraKingdom.
#$Actinomyces are #$ProkaryoticCells that are
#$GramPositiveBacterium.  Most are free-living, particularily in
soil.   Species are either #$AnaerobicBacterium, part of the normal
flora of the mouth, or #$AerobicBacterium.")
(comment NocardiaNova "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under the #$Nocardia
in the MoneraKingdom.")
(comment NocardiaOtitidiscaviarum "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalSpecies under the #$Nocardia
in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment Pasteurellaceae "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes #$BiologicalGenus such as #$Pasteurella, Haemophilus, and Actinobacillus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are straight rigid coccoid to rod-shaped cells.  They are parasites to vertebrates.  These are #$Bacterium-Immotile and #$NonSporeFormingBacterium.  Most are #$AerobicBacterium with some species being #$AnaerobicBacterium-Facultative or microphilic.  Also, they are chemoorganotrophs with respiratory and fermentative metabolism.  Reacts positively with oxidase, catalase, and alkaline phosphatase.  They require organic nitrogen sources.")
(comment PasteurellaHemolytica "A collection of all #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under
#$Pasteurella in the #$MoneraKingdom that occurs in the upper respiratory
tracts of farm animals.  It is a prominent cause of epizootic
Pneumonia in cattle and sheep and of fowl Cholera in chickens and
turkeys.  Human infection is rare.")
(comment PasteurellaPneumotropica "This collection of a #$BiologicalSpecies under the genus 
#$Pasteurella in the #$MoneraKingdom occurs normally in the
respiratory tract of mice and rats and can cause Pneumonia when the
host-parasite balance is disturbed.  Human infection can occur
following animal bites.")
(comment PasteurellaUreae "This species under #$Pasteurella in
the #$MoneraKingdom is rarely found in animals but occurs as part of a
mixed flora in human chronic respiratory disease.")
(comment PasteurellaMultocida "This species under the genus #$Pasteurella occurs worldwide in the respiratory and gastrointestinal tract of domesticated and wild animals.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are the most
common #$Organism-Whole found in human wounds inflicted by cats and
dogs.  Infection occurs at the site of the wound usually within 24 hours.  Typically the infection takes the form of cellulitis with a well-defined erythematous border.  They also commonly cause hemorrhagic septicemia in a variety of animals.")
(comment Escherichia "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These are straight #$BacillusBacterium that occur singly or in pairs.  Either #$Bacterium-MotileByFlagellum or #$Bacterium-Immotile.  Chemoorganotrophic with both a fermentative and respiratory metabolism.  They are oxidase-negative.  May use acetate as a sole carbon source, but not citrate.  This #$BiologicalSpecies  is a pathogen for humans, responsible for food poisoning, #$UrinaryTractInfections, and neonatal meningitis (see (#$InfectionFn #$Meninges)).")
(comment Gracilicutes "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells in a #$BiologicalDivision within the #$MoneraKingdom; the #$Gracilicutes are #$ProkaryoticCells with a thin cell wall.  These cells are #$GramNegativeBacterium, with a few exceptions.  Cell shape may be spheres, oval, straight or curved rods, helices or filaments.  The majority reproduce by binary fission but some members reproduce by budding.  This group does not from endospores.  Motility varies as does respiration.")
(comment ProteusMirabilis "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Proteus-BacteriumGenus in
the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells cause
#$UrinaryTractInfections and produce bacteremia, #$Pneumonia, and focal
lesions in debilitated patients.")
(comment ProteusVulgaris "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Proteus-BacteriumGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment TreponemaPertenue "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom that causes yaws.")
(comment Treponemataceae "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells that form a
#$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the
#$BiologicalGenus #$Treponema and #$Borrelia.  This
family was once included with the #$Spirochaetaceae-Family.")
(comment TreponemaCarateum "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells of a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom. They are responsible for pinta, a
#$BacterialInfection transmitted by nonsexual means.  They are found
in Central and South America.")
(comment RickettsiaTyphi "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom that has
its reservoir in the rat, in which the infection is inapparent and
long-lasting.  Rat fleas carry it from rat to rat and sometimes to
humans, who then develop endemic typhus.")
(comment RhodococcusEqui "A collection of #$Bacterium whose instances are opportunistic pathogens for humans.")
(comment ProvidenciaAlcalifaciens "An collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Providencia
in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment Prostaglandin "#$Prostaglandins are a class of lipids found in many kinds of animals and even in some plants.  In humans (and other mammals), prostglandins are important as local signaling molecules.")
(comment ProstaglandinH2 "A type of naturally-occurring #$Prostaglandin that serves as an important precursor in the biosynthesis of other prostaglandins.")
(comment ArachidonicAcidConversionToProstaglandinH2 "Instances are #$ChemicalReactions in which a molecule of #$ArachidonicAcid is converted to a molecule of #$ProstaglandinH2.  This reaction is mediated by two isozymes, #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase1 and #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase2.")
(comment Thromboxane "#$Thromboxanes are a class of lipids found in many kinds vertebrates.  In humans (and other mammals), thromboxanes act as vasoconstrictors and promote the aggregation of #$Platelets that occurs in blood clot formation.")
(comment ThromboxaneA2 "A type of naturally-occurring #$Thromboxane that is produced by activated #$Platelets and promotes blood clotting.")
(comment ThromboxaneASynthase1 "A type of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances are able to catalyze the conversion of #$ProstaglandinH2 to #$ThromboxaneA2.  The enzyme is thus important for hemostasis, and can play a role in illness such as cardiovascular disease and stroke.")
(comment ThromboxaneABiosynthesis "Instances are #$ChemicalReactions in which a molecule of #$ProstaglandinH2 is converted to a molecule of #$ThromboxaneA2.  This reaction is mediated by the enzyme #$ThromboxaneASynthase1.")
(comment conduitAverageInteriorCrossSectionArea "(#$conduitAverageInteriorCrossSectionArea COND AREA) states that the mean interior cross section area for the conduit, COND, is AREA.  This area is the region through which fluids can flow, and can be determined by dividing the interior volume of the conduit by its length.")
(comment Vasoconstriction "Instances of #$Vasoconstriction are events in which one or more #$BloodVessels decrease their cross-sectional area.  This occurs when the smooth muscle cells in the walls of arteries (see #$Artery) and, to a lesser extent, #$Veins, contract.  If vasoconstriction occurs in the whole body, it will result in increased blood pressure; if localized, it will reduce blood flow to that tissue.  #$Vasoconstriction can be a normal response of the body, to correct for prior #$Vasodilation, to reduce blood flow to the skin to conserve heat, and in response to wounding to reduce blood loss.  Vasoconstriction can also be induced by exogenous factors such as medications.")
(comment Vasodilation "Instances of #$Vasodilation are events in which one or more #$BloodVessels increase their cross-sectional area.  This occurs when the smooth muscle cells in the walls of arteries (see #$Artery) and, to a lesser extent, #$Veins, relax.  If vasodilation occurs in the whole body, it will result in decreased blood pressure; if localized, it will increase blood flow to that tissue, as occurs during strenuous exercise when muscle demand for oxygen increases.  #$Vasodilation can be a normal response of the body, to supply tissues with greater oxygen demand, to correct for prior #$Vasoconstriction, or to increase blood flow to the skin to rid the body of excess heat.  Vasodilation can also be induced by exogenous factors such as medications.  For example, #$Vasodilators may be given to correct #$Hypertension.")
(comment ThromboxaneA2PromotionOfVascularMuscleCellContraction "Instances are scripts in which binding of #$ThromboxaneA2 to a receptor in the cell membrane leads to contraction of a vascular smooth muscle cell.  When enough of these events happen in a localized region, and they are not opposed by other forces, #$Vasoconstriction ensues.")
(comment ThromboxaneA2Receptor "A type of #$MembraneReceptorMolecule to which #$ThromboxaneA2 binds.")
(comment VascularSmoothMuscleTissue "A specialization of #$SmoothMuscle.  Vascular smooth muscle tissue forms a layer of the walls of #$BloodVessels.  It lies outside the endothelium, which is the lining of the vessels, and just inside connective tissue which forms the external walls of the vessels.")
(comment ComputerDataStorageLocation "The collection of all numerically identified fixed length data storage
locations capable of storing a number expressed in binary notation, in
either a #$ComputerMemory (see #$ComputerMemoryLocation) or a
#$CentralProcessingUnit (see #$ComputerMemoryRegister).")
(comment computerDataLocationDesignator "(Where LOC is a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation, (#$computerDataLocationDesignator LOC NUM) means that the numeric address of LOC is NUM, where NUM is a #$PositiveInteger expressed in decimal notation.")
(comment computerDataLocationDesignator-BinString "Where LOC is a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation, (#$computerDataLocationDesignator-BinString LOC BIN-STRING) means that the numeric address of LOC is represented as BIN-STRING, where BIN-STRING is a character sequence of 1's and 0's denoting a #$PositiveInteger in binary notation.")
(comment ComputerMemoryLocation "The collection of every fixed-length, numerically addressed location that is part of some computer memory.")
(comment dataLocationWrittenTo "(#$dataLocationWrittenTo WRITE LOC) means that the numeric content of the #$ComputerDataStorageLocation LOC is changed in the #$ComputerDataAlteration WRITE.")
(comment designatorOfDataLocationWrittenTo "(#$designatorOfDataLocationWrittenTo WRITE NUM) means that there is a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation that is a #$dataLocationWrittenTo in WRITE whose #$computerDataLocationDesignator is NUM.")
(comment designatorOfDataLocationWrittenTo-BinString "(#$designatorOfDataLocationWrittenTo-BinString WRITE STRING) means that there is a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation that is a #$dataLocationWrittenTo in WRITE whose #$computerDataLocationDesignator-BinString is STRING.")
(comment DataLocationAlteringFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions such that, if a piece of executable code that calls the function (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable where the function is the #$codingFunctionInvoked) is executed in a normal runtime environment, the resulting execution will be a ComputerDataAlteration: i.e., will result in a change to the content of one or more locations in computer memory.")
(comment mutableArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$DataLocationAlteringFunction, (#$mutableArgumentPosition FN N) means that, when a piece of executable code (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) for which FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked is executed in a normal run-time environment, the numeric value of the Nth argument given for FN in the execution denotes a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation whose content will be changed by the application of FN.")
(comment infoTransferConstrainingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$DataLocationAlteringFunction, (#$infoTransferConstrainingArgumentPosition FN N) means that, when a piece of executable code (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) for which FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked is executed in a normal run-time environment, the numeric value of the Nth argument given for FN in the execution constrains the bitwidth of a string involved in #$InformationTransferEvent of which the execution consists.")
(comment readArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$DataLocationAlteringFunction, (#$readArgumentPosition FN N) means that, when a piece of executable code (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) for which FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked is executed in a normal run-time environment, the numeric value of the Nth argument given for FN in the execution denotes a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation whose content will be read from by the application of FN.")
(comment argNValueAssignedFunctionCalledInExecution "Where CODE-WITH-CALL is a code block that calls a single function (a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) and EXECUTION is a #$ProgramAction, (#$argNValueAssignedFunctionCalledInExecution CODE-WITH-CALL EXECUTION N VALUE) means that the numeric value assigned to the Nth argument of the #$codingFunctionInvoked in EXECUTION is VALUE.")
(comment requiresValueConformityFromArgToArg "Where FN is an instance of #$DataLocationAlteringFunction, (#$requiresValueConformityFromArgToArg FN ARGN ARGM) means that some internally unenforced mathematical relationship is needed to hold between whatever is given in an execution as the value of the ARGNth argument of FN and whatever is given in the same executon as the value of the ARGMth argument of FN, on pain of engendering a potentially exploitable overrunning condition.")
(comment ComputerDataAlteration "The collection of all #$ProgramActions that subsume changes
to the content of at least one, and possibly more #$ComputerDataStorageLocations")
(comment GeneticMutationEvent-Organelle "Instances of #$GeneticMutationEvent-Organelle are mutation events that affect the genetic material of an #$Organelle such as a #$Mitochondrion or #$Chloroplast.")
(comment enzymeTypeInactivatedInInactivationType "The corresponding predicate of #$InactivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeInactivatedInInactivationType MOL-TYPE INACTIVATION-TYPE) means that INACTIVATION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'inactive' in the sense of becoming unable to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.  In most cases, an instance of INACTIVATION-TYPE will consist in a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent where the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically bound to an 'inactivation factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which blocks it from catalyzing the necessary reactions, preceded by a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent wherein the #$EnzymeMolecule is unbound from an 'activaton factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) for the necessary reactions.  Often, the activation and inactivation components are both #$Nucleosides.")
(comment PyramidalCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Pyramidal cells have a triangular #$Soma.")
(comment BipolarCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Each bipolar cell has two extensions or \"processes\".")
(comment PseudounipolarCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Each pseudounipolar cell cell has one axon with both a central and a peripheral branch.")
(comment MultipolarCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Each multipolar cell cell has one axon and many dendrites.")
(comment GranuleCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Granule cells are tiny neurons (typically around 10 micrometers in diameter).")
(comment PurkinjeCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Purkinje cells are large neurons located in the cerebellar cortex (specifically, in the Purkinje layer of the cerebellum).")
(comment SomaticMotorNeuron "A specialization of #$MotorNeuron.  Somatic motor neurons are motor neurons that directly innervate skeletal muscle.")
(comment MotorNeuron "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Motor neurons are cells that are part of the central nervous system but which project their axons out of the central nervous system and are thereby involved in muscle control.")
(comment BranchialMotorNeurons "A specialization of #$MotorNeuron.  Branchial motor neurons are motor neurons that directly innervate branchial muscle.")
(comment VisceralMotorNeuron "A specialization of #$MotorNeuron.  Visceral motor neurons are motor neurons that indirectly innervate cardiac muscle tissue and the smooth muscle tissue of viscera.")
(comment AlphaMotorNeuron "A specialization of #$SomaticMotorNeuron.  Alpha motor neurons innervate extrafusal muscle fibers.")
(comment GammaMotorNeuron "A specialization of #$SomaticMotorNeuron.  Gamma motor neurons innervate intrafusal muscle fibers.")
(disjointWith GammaMotorNeuron AlphaMotorNeuron)
(comment Interneuron "A specialization of #$MultipolarCell.  Each interneuron is a multipolar neuron that connects afferent neurons and efferent neurons in a neural pathway.")
(comment ReservedWord "The collection of all 'reserved words' in programming language families (see #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType).  A specialization of #$LexicalItem.")
(comment ReservedWordInFamilyFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for reasoning about instances of #$ReservedWord.  Where STRING is a #$CharacterString and FAMILY is a #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType, (#$ReservedWordInFamilyFn STRING FAMILY) denotes the reserved word expressed by STRING in programs written in languages whicha are members (hasProgrammingLanguageFamily) of FAMILY.")
(comment OutputStringFormat "The collection of all output formats employable by #$FormattedOutputConversionFunctions.  This is a #$SecondOrderCollection:  each instance being a collection of formal #$LexicalItems that jointly constitute the format.")
(comment HexadecimalOutputFormat "An #$OutputStringFormat using base 16 as the positional notation sstem.  It uses 16 distinct characters:  '0' through '9' to represent the values zero through nine, and 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', and 'F' to represent values ten to fifteen.")
(comment outputFormatConstrainingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$FormattedOutputConversionFunction, (#$outputFormatConstrainingArgument FN N) means that the value given as the Nth argument position of the function is a term that constrains the #$OutputStringFormat that the function uses.")
(comment maximumBitWidthPermittedByFormat "(#$maximumBitWidthPermittedByFormat FORMAT N) means that when the #$OutputStringFormat of a #$FormattedOutputConversionFunction is FORMAT, the maximum number of bits that can be written under fhte formatting is N.")
(comment AcuteInflammation "Instances of #$AcuteInflammation usually occur in response to infection by a pathogen or as a result of an injury such as a burn or abrasion.  After infection or injury an acute inflammatory response will usually begin almost immediately, with increased blood flow to the affected region;  migration of phagocytes to the area begins soon after, and these act to remove pathogens and clean up the remains of damaged cells.")
(comment preferredConstraintForGenTemplates "(#$preferredConstraintForGenTemplates CONSTRAINT) means that if multiple #$TermPhrasesConstraints could be used in a #$GenTemplateRecipe, CONSTRAINT is to be preferred over constraints for which this is not known.")
(comment hasExpertiseToDegreeWRT "(#$hasExpertiseToDegreeWRT EXPERT SUBJECT BASE DEGREE) means that EXPERT has some degree of expertise in SUBJECT relative to or derived from having at least DEGREE of expertise in BASE.")
(comment hasExpertiseInSimilarSoftwareWRTType "(#$hasExpertiseInSimilarSoftwareWRTType EXPERT SUBJECT TYPE) means that EXPERT has some degree of expertise in SUBJECT and the software corresponding to the problem type SUBJECT is an instance of the #$ComputerProgramTypeBySimilarWorkflow TYPE.")
(comment bitWidthOfOSArchitecture "(#$bitWidthOfOSArchitecture OS N) means that the #$OperatingSystem OS uses an N-bit architecture.")
(comment UnipolarCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Each unipolar cell has one neurite that extends from the cell body.")
(comment NeuronTypeByPolarity "The collection of collections of neurons, where each such collection is such that all of its instances have a common manner in which their axons and dendrites are arranged.")
(comment Enterobacteriaceae "A collection of a #$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes #$BiologicalGenus such as #$Escherichia, #$Yersinia and #$Salmonella.  All of which are important human pathogens.  All secrete the LPS endotoxin and are oxidase negative.  These are chemoorganotrophic with respiratory and fermentative metabolism.  These are world-wide in distribution and are found in almost every environment.")
(comment WholeBody "The entire body of an organism. The physical extent of an organism.")
(comment degreeOfConditionSeverityDiagnosed "The #$Predicate used to relate a particular #$MedicalDiagnosisOrFinding to the type of condition diagnosed (see #$hasDiagnosis).  (#$degreeOfConditionSeverityDiagnosed DIAGNOSIS DEGREE) means that, if DIAGNOSIS is accurate (see #$evaluationCorrectness), then at the time of DIAGNOSIS, the condition being diagnosed has the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition DEGREE.")
(comment DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition "A qualitative, scalar measure of 'how severe' an #$AilmentCondition is.  Although qualitative, physicians will often resort to this scale in characterizing the status of a condition.  The criteria used for deciding the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition for a given instance of #$AilmentCondition will vary with the condition type, as will the consequences that the condition has the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition that it does.")
(comment SeveritySevere "The highest degree of acuteness on the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition scale of qualitative diagnoses.")
(comment SeverityModerateToSevere "The second-highest degree of acuteness on the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition scale of qualitative diagnoses.")
(comment SeverityModerate "The medial degree of acuteness on the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition scale of qualitative diagnoses.")
(comment SeverityMild "The second-lowest degree of acuteness on the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition scale of qualitative diagnoses.")
(comment SeverityTrivial "The lowest degree of acuteness on the #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition scale of qualitative diagnoses.")
(comment severityOfCondition "(#$severityOfCondition CONDITION LEVEL) states that the #$AilmentCondition, CONDITION, has level of severity (see #$DegreeOfSeverity-AilmentCondition), LEVEL.")
(comment Neurite "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$Neurite is a projection out of a neuron.  Important specializations of #$Neurite include #$Axon and #$Dendrite.")
(comment drugTypeTypicalPhysiologicalResponseType "(#$drugTypeTypicalPhysiologicalResponseType DRUGTYPE RESPONSETYPE) states that the typical physiological response to the presence of a sufficient amount of DRUGTYPE in the body is the #$PhysiologicalProcess, RESPONSETYPE.  This predicate is agnostic as to what amount is sufficient.")
(comment ProstaglandinE2 "A type of naturally-occurring #$Prostaglandin that is biosynthesized from #$ProstaglandinH2 and plays a role in fever and inflammation.")
(comment enzymeActivityContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeType "(#$enzymeActivityContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeType ENZ-TYPE P-TYPE) states that the activity of instances of the #$EnzymeMolecule, ENZ-TYPE (typically, chemical reactions in which ENZ-TYPE acts as a catalyst) is a precursor in some chain of causality leading to an instance of the the phsiological process, P-TYPE.")
(comment enzymeInhibitionContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeType "(#$enzymeInhibitionContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeType ENZ-TYPE P-TYPE) states that the inhibition of an instance of the #$EnzymeMolecule, ENZ-TYPE, is a (perhaps neither necessary nor sufficient) precursor in some chain of causality leading to an instance of the the phsiological process, P-TYPE.")
(comment enzymeTypeCatalyzesProductionOfType "(#$enzymeTypeCatalyzesProductionOfType ?ENZ-TYPE ?CHEM-TYPE) states that the class of #$EnzymeMolecule, ?ENZ-TYPE, is capable of acting as the #$catalyst in reactions that produce molecules of the substance, ?CHEM-TYPE.  Because there may be multiple ways of producing ?CHEM-TYPE, the presence of ?ENZ-TYPE is not strictly required for its production.")
(comment ProstaglandinESynthase "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule responsible for prostanoid formation.")
(comment BacterialCellWall-GramNegative "The collection of cell walls present on most #$GramNegativeBacillusBacterium.")
(comment BacterialCellWall-GramPositive "The collection of cell walls present on most #$GramPositiveBacillusBacterium.")
(comment Peptidoglycan "A biopolymer that is found in bacterial cell walls.")
(comment Autophagosome "A specialization of #$Organelle.  Each instance of #$Autophagosome is an organelle that sequesters material for degradation.")
(disjointWith SpermCell (CollectionDifferenceFn Cell SpermCell))
(comment TroponinI "A type of organic substance. Troponin I binds to actin in thin myofilaments.")
(comment TroponinC "A type of organic substance.  Binds to calcium ions.")
(comment indexSubWordsForArg "(#$indexSubWordsForArg PRED N) means that strings that occur as the Nth argument in an assertion whose predicate is PRED should have their subwords indexed for retrieval.")
(comment programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToBlockOnOS "(#$programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToBlockOnOS PROGRAM ACTION-TYPE CODE-BLOCK OS) means that if PROGRAM is executed on OS, then, other things being equal, the execution of CODE-BLOCK that occurs in the course of that execution will trigger an action of type ACTION-TYPE.")
(comment MedicalEvaluationEvent "Instances are events in which a patient's body or parts thereof are examined and assessed by a medical professional to identify and/or characterize points of medical concern.  Specializations include both particular tests, such as an #$O2SaturationBloodTest, and more complex scripts such as a #$MedicalExaminationOfPatient wherein multiple findings may be sought and recorded.")
(comment MedicalExaminationOfPatient "Instances are events in which a single patient is examined by one or more medical professionals. Instances may have #$subEvents that include one or more instances of #$MedicalTesting.  A typical exam may result in the recording of a number of measurements, such as the patient's height and weight, the diameter of a skin blemish, or the patient's body temperature, depending on the type of examination performed.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient SortingSomethingMentally)
(disjointWith BuildingMaintenance MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith EnteringAComputerPassword MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith MediaTransferEvent MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith VisualArtActivity MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith AcademicTesting MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith PreservingFood MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith ConflictEvent MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith Remodeling MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith ProcessingRefinedOil MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith BoatMaintenance MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient (RepairingFn DurableGood))
(disjointWith DoingMath MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient)
(comment MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient "The collection of medical care events (#$MedicalCareEvent) in which exactly one individual is the subject or patient of the care event.  Examples include valve surgery, hospital visits, most clinical evaluations, etc.  Negative examples would include any event in which multiple patients are the subject of the event such as a surgery to separate conjoined twins, or a complex mass treatment event which consists of multiple cases of #$MedicalCareEvent-SinglePatient.")
(comment ProstaglandinESynthase2 "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule responsible for prostanoid formation.")
(comment ProstaglandinESynthase3 "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule responsible for prostanoid formation.")
(comment languageOfCodeType "(#$languageOfCodeType CODE-TYPE LANGUAGE) means that the #$codeLanguage of every instance of CODE-TYPE is the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage LANGUAGE.")
(comment languageFamilyOfCodeType "(#$languageFamilyOfCodeType CODE-TYPE LANGUAGE-FAMILY) means that the #$codeLanguageFamily of every instance of CODE-TYPE is LANGUAGE-FAMILY.")
(comment deficiencyLimitedToLanguage "(#$deficiencyLimitedToLanguage DEFICIENCY-TYPE LANGUAGE) means that being written in LANGUAGE is a necessary condition for a piece of #$ComputerCode having DEFICIENCY-TYPE.  More precisely, any piece of #$ComputerCode which is an instance of a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency (see #$isa spec-pred #$codeHasDeficiency) will have LANGUAGE as its #$codeLanguage.")
(comment deficiencyLimitedToLanguageFamily "(#$deficiencyLimitedToLanguageFamily DEFICIENCY-TYPE LANGUAGE-FAMILY) means that being written in a language that is a member of LANGUAGE-FAMILY is a necessary condition for a piece of #$ComputerCode having DEFICIENCY-TYPE.  More precisely, any piece of #$ComputerCode which is an instance of a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency (see #$isa spec-pred #$codeHasDeficiency will be written in an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage which belongs to the ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType LANGUAGE-FAMILY.")
(comment standardMitigationForCodeDeficiency "Where DEFICIENCY-TYPE is a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency and MITIGATION-TYPE is a #$ComputerActivityType, (#$standardMitigationForCodeDeficiency DEFICIENCY-TYPE ACTION-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, if a piece of code is an instance of DEFICIENCY-TYPE (see #$codeHasDeficiency) and a particular execution of that code (see #$codeExecuted) is an instance MITIGATION-TYPE, the execution will *not* include an instance of the event type which ordinarily characterizes the deficiency (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType).")
(comment UMLSRelation "The collection of all reified relationships, which are of type (see #$rdf-type) umls:Relation, in the Unified Medical Language System (UMLS).")
(comment ProstaglandinESynthase1 "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule responsible for prostanoid formation.")
(comment Prostacyclin "#$Prostacyclins are a class of lipids found in many kinds vertebrates.  In humans (and other mammals), prostacyclins act as vasodilators and inhibit the activation of #$Platelets that occurs in blood clot formation.")
(comment Prostanoid "#$Prostanoids are a class of lipids found in many kinds of animals and even in some plants.  Important subclasses include #$Prostaglandins, #$Thromboxanes and #$Prostacyclins.  In humans (and other mammals), prostanoids are involved in the inflammatory response.")
(comment ProstacyclinSynthase "A type of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances are able to catalyze the conversion of #$ProstaglandinH2 to #$Prostacyclin.")
(comment ProstacyclinBioynthesis "Instances are #$ChemicalReactions in which a molecule of #$ProstaglandinH2 is converted to a molecule of #$Prostacyclin.  This reaction is mediated by the enzyme #$ProstacyclinSynthase.")
(comment ChemicalInteraction "This is the class of chemical interactions, events in which molecules of two or
more types come into proximity and react in ways determined by their structure.
Note that this collection is more general than #$ChemicalReaction since these
interactions may not amount to #$PhysicalTransformationEvents.  Also, this collection is restricted to single chemical interactions: series and mass events should be represented as mass chemical interactions or as series of chemical interactions.  Cf. #$ChemicalProcess and (#$MassEventOfTypeFn #$ChemicalInteraction).")
(comment CausalSequence "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  In every instance of #$CausalSequence there are at least two distinct subsituations, CAUSE and EFFECT, for which both (#$causes-SitSit CAUSE EFFECT) and (#$startsAfterStartingOf  EFFECT CAUSE) are true.")
(comment correlatedSubSituationTypes "(#$correlatedSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUB-TYPE1 SUB-TYPE2) means that during instances of SIT-TYPE, occurrences of SUB-TYPE1 and SUB-TYPE2 are correlated.")
(comment OWLPropertyHasSpecialCaseRangeCollection "the collection of OWL properties for which the forward inference from the #$rdfs:range assertion to arg2Isa is not applicable.  For instance, an OWL data type property might implicitly reference a particular unit of measurement, but we may want to make the unit explicit in our encoding/decoding of the property.  In that case we will want to block the auto-propagation of the rdfs:range assertion to arg2Isa and instead assert the appropriate quantity-based arg2 constraint.  See the similar #$OWLPropertyHasSpecialCaseDomainCollection.")
(comment OWLPropertyHasSpecialCaseDomainCollection "the collection of OWL properties for which the forward inference from #$rdfs:domain to #$arg1Isa is not applicable.  See the similar #$OWLPropertyHasSpecialCaseRangeCollection .")
(comment LinkedLifeQueryMt "Reasoning environment for testing and demonstrating queries that access the OntoText LinkedLife data integration platform (http://www.linkedlifedata.com).  More conservative in its inclusiveness than #$LinkedLifeTestQueryMt.")
(comment InhibitionOfEnzymeOfTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used to represent the class of 'inhibitions' of a given type of enzyme.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$InhibitionOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is reduced in its ability (rendered incapable, or rendered less likely) to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.")
(comment enzymeTypeAffectedInInhibitionType "The corresponding predicate of #$InhibitionOfEnzymeOfTypeFn.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$enzymeTypeAffectedInInhibitionType MOL-TYPE INHIBITION-TYPE) means that INHIBITION-TYPE is the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is reduced in its ability (rendered incapable, or rendered less likely) to catalyze certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class of enzyme.")
(comment inhibitorMolecule "Where INHIBITION is an #$EnzymaticInhibition, (#$inhibitorMolecule INHIBITION MOL) means that MOL is the #$Molecule which binds to the affected #$EnzymeMolecule and thus prevents it from functioning or reduces its effectiveness.")
(comment ProstaglandinEBiosynthesis "Instances are #$ChemicalReactions in which a molecule of #$ProstaglandinH2 is converted to a molecule of #$ProstaglandinE2 in biological tissues.  This reaction is catalyzed by instances of the enzyme #$ProstaglandinESynthase.")
(comment enzymeSubstrateInProductionOf-TypeLevel "(#$enzymeSubstrateInProductionOf-TypeLevel ENZYME-TYPE SUBSTRATE-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE) states that, in reactions where instances of ENZYME-TYPE produce instances of PRODUCT-TYPE, the substrate acted upon is SUBSTRATE-TYPE. Furthermore, when ENZYME-TYPE acts as a catalyst in reactions involving SUBSTRATE-TYPE as an input, one of the outputs is PRODUCT-TYPE.  Note that more than one kind of enzyme may be able to mediate the conversion of SUBSTRATE-TYPE into PRODUCT-TYPE.")
(comment Fullerene "An allotrope of #$Carbon.")
(disjointWith Chondrite Achondrite)
(comment Sandstone "The collection of all sandstone. A type of #$StoneStuff. The concept #$Sandstone is an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment productOfPlant "<code>(#$productOfPlant PLANT PRODUCT)</code> means that <code>PLANT</code> is the source of <code>PRODUCT</code>.  For example <code>(#$productOfPlant MapleTree001 MapleSyrup001)</code> means that <code>MapleTree001</code> is the source of <code>MapleSyrup001</code>.")
(comment VincaAlkaloid "A collection of alkaloids that inhibit mitosis.  These alkaloids were originally derived from the #$MadagascarPeriwinkle, but are now synthetically produced.")
(comment MitoticInhibitor "A collection of chemical substances that inhibit the progress of #$Mitosis.")
(comment Terpene "A kind of #$OrganicMaterial notably present in the sap of conifers.")
(comment Taxane "A collection of terpenes that inhibit mitosis.  These terpenes were originally derived from a plant in the yew family, but many are now synthetically produced.")
(comment SpindlePoison "A collection of chemical substances that inhibit the progress of #$Mitosis by inhibiting the formation of #$MitoticSpindles.")
(comment physicalSchemaUsesLogicalSchemaFromPhyscialSchema "(#$physicalSchemaUsesLogicalSchemaFromPhyscialSchema PS1 PS2 LS) means that PS1 uses the same encoding and decoding statements as PS2 with respect to the logical fields in LS.  This is typically used in the context of SKSI mappings to triple stores.  Asserting this of a pair of physical schemas and a logical schema that corresponds to an #$SKSISupportedOWLProperty will forwardly propagate the encoding and decoding statements that involve PS2 and the subject and object field indexicals of LS into corresponding encoding and decoding statements that reference PS1 and those same logical field indexicals.  This allows us to define in a general way a relationship that appears in many different datasets -- e.g. general RDF vocabulary, SKOS vocabulary, FOAF, etc. -- and propagate its encoding and decoding statements to any KS/PS that needs to utilize that vocabulary.")
(comment substanceTypeCanInhibitEnzymeType "(#$substanceTypeCanInhibitEnzymeType SUB-TYPE ENZ-TYPE) states that molecules of SUB-TYPE can prevent or delay the chemical reactions typically catalyzed by molecules of ENZ-TYPE by interfering with the action of the enzyme.")
(comment ComputerDataAlteration-Single "The collection of all #$ProgramActions consisting in exactly one change to the content of a single #$ComputerDataStorageLocation (a #$ComputerMemoryLocation or a #$CPUMemoryRegister).")
(comment ExemptFromFactsInFictionalWorldCollector "A specialization of #$FictionalContext.  This is the collection of fictional contexts, MT,  for which (#$genlMt #$FactsInFictionalWorksMt MT) should not hold.  Typically this is because the microtheory represents a counterfactual or \"almost true\" situation whose starting assumptions (via its #$genlMt links) are incompatible with most of the fictional facts provable in #$FactsInFictionalWorksMt.")
(comment predicateForKS "(#$predicateForKS KS PRED) means that PRED can be used to access/interpret data from KS.  This entails that the corresponding logical schema for PRED is mapped to the physical schema associated with KS.")
(comment quantifiedBinaryPredicateForPredWithMacro "The corresponding predicate to #$QuantifiedVersionOfBinaryPredicateFn")
(comment AutoCreatedOWLPropertyLogicalSchema "The collection of LogicalSchemas that are auto-created by forward inference each of which is a schema for an #$SKSISupportedOWLProperty.")
(comment inhibitionOfEnzymeBySubstanceContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeLevel "(#$inhibitionOfEnzymeBySubstanceContributesToPhysiologicalProcess-TypeLevel ENZYME-TYPE SUBST-TYPE PROC-TYPE) states that the inhibition of the activity of ENZYME-TYPE by SUBST-TYPE can causally contribute to the type of physiological process, PROC-TYPE.")
(comment OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSIMappings "A subcollection of #$SKSISupportedOWLProperty.  Each instance of this collection is an OWL or RDF property that will have its needed logical schema assertions autopopulated.  The subject encodings and decodings will reference the codemapping supplied by #$hasAssociatedCMLS.  For object properties, the object encodings and decodings will also reference that reified mapping.  The object encoding and decodings for data properties are handled on a case by case basic with specific rules on subcollections of this collection for data properties whose ranges are literal strings, integers, reals, etc.")
(comment OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSI-NonQuantityScalarInterval "A subcollection of #$OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSIMappings.  Each instance of this collection is an OWL or RDF property whose range is a non-quantity scalar interval (actually, more properly, a scalar point value) like #$Integer or #$RealNumber.")
(comment OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSI-CharacterString "A subcollection of #$OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSIMappings.  Each instance of this collection is an OWL or RDF property whose range is a non-quantity scalar interval (actually, more properly, a scalar point value) like #$Integer or #$RealNumber.")
(comment OWLAutomappingConcept "The collection of concepts used to trigger the automatic generation of the SKSI mappings for OWL properties.  See the shared noted #$SharedNoteOnOWLPropertyAutogenerationofSKSIAssertions.")
(comment owlPropertyHasImplicitUnitOfMeasure "(#$owlPropertyHasImplicitUnitOfMeasure PROP UNIT) means that the owl datatype property PROP implicitly references the #$UnitOfMeasure, UNIT.  For example, consider an OWL property like example:hasLengthInMeters.  The actual asserted #$rdfs:range on this property might be #$xsd:float.  but any use of it implicitly means that the length of the subject is that number of meters.  In this case, (#$owlPropertyHasImplicitUnitOfMeasure example:hasLengthInMeters #$Meter) would be asserted.")
(comment OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSI-OWLDate "A subcollection of #$OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSIMappings.  Each instance of this collection is an OWL or RDF property whose range is implicitly some quantity typically expressed with a unit of measure function.")
(comment OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSI-Quantity "A subcollection of #$OWLProperty-AutogeneratedSKSIMappings.  Each instance of this collection is an OWL or RDF property whose range is implicitly some quantity typically expressed with a unit of measure function.  See #$foaf:age for an example of a quantity predicate with autogenerated SKSI assertions.")
(comment ProteinConformationChangeEvent "Instances of #$ProteinConformationChangeEvent are events in which one #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex changes shape.  This can occur in response to binding by a ligand, to the unbinding of a bound ligand, or to other environmental factors like changes in temperature, pH, ion concentration or phosphorylation.")
(comment activeFormOfReceptor "The corresponding predicate of #$ActiveFormOfReceptorFn. Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, (#$activeFormOfReceptor MOL-TYPE ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE) in a given context means that ACTIVE-MOL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are able to initiate the signal transduction (See #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess) typical to MOL-TYPE, usually as a result of being activated by ligand binding.")
(comment ActiveFormOfReceptorFn "Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, (#$ActiveFormOfReceptorFn MOL-TYPE) in a given context denotes the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are in a state of being able to initiate a signal transduction event (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess), usually because the receptor molecule has been activated by the binding of a ligand.  Note, however, that some receptors types may be constitutively active, possessing some level of activity without the binding of a ligand.")
(comment InactiveFormOfReceptorFn "Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, (#$InactiveFormOfReceptorFn MOL-TYPE) in a given context denotes the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are in a state of being unable to initiate a signal transduction event (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess).  For many receptor types, the inactive form is the normal state, and they require the binding of a particular ligand to activate them.  Note, however, that some receptors types may be constitutively active, possessing some level of activity without the binding of a ligand.")
(comment inactiveFormOfReceptor "The corresponding predicate of #$InactiveFormOfReceptorFn. Where MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule, (#$inactiveFormOfReceptor MOL-TYPE INACTIVE-MOL-TYPE) in a given context means that INACTIVE-MOL-TYPE is the collection of all instances of MOL-TYPE that are not able to initiate the signal transduction (See #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess) typical to MOL-TYPE, usually because they are not bound to the relevant ligand.")
(comment ReceptorMoleculeInactivationEvent "The collection of #$ChemicalInteractions in which some #$ReceptorMolecule becomes inactive, so that it no longer initiates a signal transduction pathway (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess).  For many receptor types, the necessary first step of receptor inactivation is the disassociation of the receptor from a ligand.")
(comment LigandActivatedReceptorMolecule "The collection of all #$ReceptorMolecules which are constitutively inactive, and can be transformed into their active form by binding of the appropriate ligand.")
(comment ConstitutivelyActiveReceptorMolecule "The collection of all #$ReceptorMolecules which are constitutively active.  This means that in the absence of a bound ligand, the receptor is able to initiate its typical signal transduction leading to a biological response.  Such receptors can have their activity blocked by an inverse agonist, and have their activity increased by binding with an agonist.")
(disjointWith LigandActivatedReceptorMolecule ConstitutivelyActiveReceptorMolecule)
(comment eventTypeFallsOnNthDayInMonth "(#$eventTypeFallsOnNthDayTypeInMonth EVENT MONTH NUM) is used to say that a special event falls annually on a specified Nth day during a certain month MONTH.  For example, to say that Groundhog Day falls on the second of February: (#$eventTypeFallsOnNthDayInMonth #$GroundhogDay #$February 2).")
(comment GroundhogDay "Each of these is a one-day-long annual #$Holiday celebrated on February 2nd in the United States and Canada.  Tradition dictates that if a groundhog sees its shadow when it emerges from its burrow on this day, winter will continue for six more weeks (and otherwise it will end soon).")
(comment ListOfTypeFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction from collections to collections of lists of instances of those collections.  (#$ListOfTypeFn <b>COLL</b>) is the collection of all #$Lists (i.e. ordered n-tuples) of things such that each item in the list is an instance of <b>COLL</b>.  For example, (#$ListOfTypeFn #$Integer) is the collection of lists of integers, and (#$TheList 1 2 3) is an instance of this collection. Cf. #$ListOfSpecsFn.
<p>
See the corresponding predicate #$instanceListMemberType.  And see #$SetOfTypeFn.")
(comment ListOfSpecsFn "A unary #$CollectionDenotingFunction from collections to collections of lists of specializations of those collections.  (#$ListOfSpecsFn <b>COLL</b>) is the collection of all #$Lists (i.e. ordered n-tuples) of things such that each item in the list is a specialization of <b>COLL</b>.  For example, (#$ListOfSpecsFn #$Mammal) is the collection of lists of collections of mammals, and (#$TheList #$Dog #$Cat) is an instance of this collection.  Cf. #$ListOfTypeFn.
<p>
See the corresponding predicate #$instanceListMemberGenl.")
(comment instanceListMemberGenl "A binary #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that relates types of #$Lists to the types of members they have in common.  More precisely, <code>(#$instanceListMemberType LISTTYPE COLLECTION)</code> means that every member (see #$memberOfList) of every instance (see #$isa) of <code>LISTTYPE</code> is a specialization of <code>COLLECTION</code>.  For example, the following is true:
<pre>
  (#$instanceListMemberGenl (#$ListOfSpecsFn #$Mammal) #$Mammal)
</pre>
This example involves the corresponding function #$ListOfSpecsFn, which takes a given collection to the collection of <i>all</i> lists whose members are specializations of the former.")
(comment PolysaccharideMolecule "A specialization of #$BiopolymerMolecule.  Polysaccharides are polymeric carbohydrate structures.  Notable polysaccharides include glycogen, cellulose, and chitin.")
(comment Maltodextrin "A polysaccharide derived from #$Starch and used as a food additive.")
(comment RadioactiveIsotope "The collection of all radioactive isotopes.  These are isotopes with spontaneously decaying nucleii.")
(comment AlphaDecay "A specialization of #$NuclearRadiationProcess.  Each instance of #$AlphaDecay is an event in which an alpha particle is emitted during radiation.")
(comment AlphaParticle "A specialization of #$SubAtomicParticle.  Each instance of #$AlphaParticle is identical in structure to a helium nucleus (it consists of two protons and two neutrons).  Alpha particles are produced during #$AlphaDecay.")
(comment BetaDecay "A specialization of #$NuclearRadiationProcess.  Each instance of #$BetaDecay is an event in which a beta particle is emitted during radiation.")
(disjointWith Nucleon BetaParticle)
(comment BetaParticle "A specialization of #$SubAtomicParticle.  Each instance of #$BetaParticle is a high-energy electron or positron emitted during #$BetaDecay.")
(comment PolarMolecule "The collection of molecules that have different charges at each end.")
(disjointWith NonpolarMolecule PolarMolecule)
(comment NonpolarMolecule "The collection of molecules that are non-polar, either because there is no polarity in their bonds, or because of a symmetrical distribution of their polar bonds.")
(comment MoleculeTypeByPolarity "#$MoleculeTypeByPolarity is a collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Molecule whose instances all have the same sort of polarity or lack thereof.")
(comment NewConstantWithNameFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction with an #$arity of 1 
that can be used to add new constants to the CycL language on the fly.  
Evaluating <code>(#$NewThingFn STRING)</code> will result in the creation of 
a new #$CycLConstant with a global unique identifier (GUID -- see 
#$GUIDString) named STRING that can be used to denote an object in the universe by stipluating a reference and adding CycL assertions to it.  
")
(comment ReceptorUnbindingFromLigand "The collection of events in which a #$ReceptorMolecule and its bound ligand unbind from each other. This will typically lead to a change in conformation of the receptor.  The unbinding may inactivate the receptor (if the receptor is ligand-activated), or restore its ability to be activated (if the bound ligand was an antagonist).")
(comment ReceptorLigandComplexTypeFn "Where RTYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule and LTYPE is a specialization of #$BiochemicalSignalingObject, (#$ReceptorLigandComplexTypeFn RTYPE LTYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of RTYPE that are in a state of being bound to a ligand of type LTYPE. In many cases, such a complex is in an active state and can initiate a signal transduction pathway leading to a cellular response. However, depending on the type of ligand and the type of receptor, the complex may be inactive or less active than the unbound form of the receptor.")
(comment receptorAndLigandInComplex-TypeLevel "The corresponding predicate of #$ReceptorLigandComplexTypeFn. Where RTYPE is a specialization of #$ReceptorMolecule and LTYPE is a specialization of #$BiochemicalSignalingObject, (#$receptorAndLigandInComplex-TypeLevel RTYPE LTYPE COMPLEXTYPE) means that COMPLEXTYPE is the collection of all #$ProteinComplex instances formed by a ligand of type LTYPE binding to a receptor of type RTYPE.")
(comment TripleStoreWithNameFn "(#$TripleStoreWithNameFn STRING) denotes the unique instance of #$RDFTripleStore-Physical with STRING as a name.")
(comment canonicalNameForTripleStoreKS "This relates a triple store to a canonical defining name.  This name will, in turn, be used to automatically generate the associated physical schema")
(comment ComputerDataTransfer "The collection of all #$InformationTransferEvents wherein binary numeric data is transferred from at least one #$ComputerDataStorageLocation to at least other #$ComputerDataStorageLocation")
(comment ComputerDataTransfer-Single "#$ComputerDataTransfer-Single is the collection of all #$InformationTransferEvents wherein a number encoded in binary notation is transferred from exactly one #$ComputerDataStorageLocation (the #$dataLocationReadFrom) to exactly one #$ComputerDataStorageLocation (a #$dataLocationWrittenTo.")
(comment dataLocationReadFrom "(#$dataLocationReadFrom TRANSFER LOC) means that the numeric contents of the #$ComputerDataStorageLocation LOC are transferred to a new #$ComputerDataStorageLocation in TRANSFER.")
(comment sparqlServiceEndpointForKS "related a TripleStore KS to its web URL.")
(comment RDFTripleStore-AutoGenerated "The collection of SKSI RDF triple store representations that have the bulk of their SKSI assertions auto-generated.  In general, once creating an instance of this collection one would only need to add the URL address of the triple store as shown below

<pre>
  (ist (MappingMtFn KS)
    (sparqlServiceEndpointForKS KS URL))
</pre>

and assign it a name like shown below

<pre>
  (ist SKSIMt
    (canonicalNameForTripleStoreKS KS NAME))
</pre>

It only takes a few moments for the required assertions to propagate.  The knowledge source is now ready to be assigned some OWL properties via #$hasAssociatedCMLS.")
(comment Phosphorolysis "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Each instance of #$Phosphorolysis  is a reaction in which an inorganic phosphate cleaves a compound.")
(comment Glycerophospholipid "A specialization of #$Phospholipid.  Glycerophospholipid are glycerol-based phospholipids that are the main component of biological membranes.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol "A specialization of #$Phospholipid.  Glycerophospholipids are glycerol-based phospholipids that are the main component of biological membranes.")
(comment Biolipid "Biolipid is the collection of all lipids that come from biological sources.  Thus vegetatble oil and animal fat are two kinds of biolipid.")
(comment Phosphoinositide "A specialization of #$Phosphatidylinositol.  Phosphoinositides are phosphatidylinositols that are phosphorylated.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol3Phosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns3P or PI3P.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol4Phosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns4P or PI4P.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol5Phosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns5P or PI5P.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol34Biphosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 3,4-biphosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns(3,4)P2 or PI(3,4)P2.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol35Biphosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 3,5-biphosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns(3,5)P2 or PI(3,5)P2.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol45Biphosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-biphosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns(4,5)P2 or PIP2.")
(comment Phosphatidylinositol345Triphosphate "Phosphatidylinositol 3,4,5-triphosphate is a kind of #$Phosphoinositide, also known as PtdIns(3,4,5)P3 or PIP3.")
(comment CyclicNucleotide "A specialization of #$Nucleotide.  Each instance of #$CyclicNucleotide is a nucleotide in which the phosphate group and two of  the sugar's hydroxyl groups form a ring structure.")
(comment isomers "(#$isomers CHEMTYPE1 CHEMTYPE2) means that CHEMTYPE1 and CHEMTYPE2 are types of chemicals whose instances share the same atomic constituents, but have different patterns of arrangement of those constituents.")
(comment GuanosineMonophosphate "GMP is a nucleotide  found in RNA which is an ester of phosphoric acid with a guanosine nucleotide.")
(comment IsletsOfLangerhans "A kind of pancreatic tissue (see (#$TissueTypeOfOrganTypeFn #$Pancreas)).  The islets of Langerhans are the regions of the pancreas that contain the beta cells that produce #$Insulin.")
(comment Pancreas "The collection of all pancreatic #$Organs.  Each instance of this collection is a unique #$Gland of a body attached to the #$Duodenum which is situated behind the #$Stomach beside the #$Spleen and produces #$Insulin, #$Glucagon, somatostatin, and pancreatic 'juice' essential for digestion of #$ProteinStuffs.  The #$CommonBileDuct passes through the #$Pancreas, where it normally joins with the pancreatic duct before the combined duct empties into the #$Duodenum.")
(comment GrowthHormone "A specialization of #$PeptideHormone.  Growth hormone regulates the growth of animals.")
(comment AdrenocorticotropicHormone "A #$Hormone secreted by the pituitary gland which stimulates the adrenal cortex. Sometimes used in the treatment of #$Asthma.")
(comment Glutamate "A specialization of #$Neurotransmitter, and the conjugate base of #$GlutamicAcid.  Glutamate is the most abundant excitatory neurotransmitter in vertebrates.")
(comment GABA "A specialization of #$Neurotransmitter. GABA (gamma-Aminobutyric acid) is the most abundant inhibitory neurotransmitter in the mammalian central nervous system.")
(comment PeptideHormone "A specialization of #$Hormone.  Peptide hormones are hormones that are also peptide moelcules.")
(comment Aspartate "The conjugate base of #$AsparticAcid, and a common neurotransmitter.")
(comment Octopamine "A specialization of #$Neurotransmitter.")
(comment Tyramine "A specialization of #$Neurotransmitter.")
(comment Neurotransmitter "The collection of all chemical substances released by #$Neurons to stimulate neighbouring neurons, thus allowing impulses to be passed from one cell to the next throughout the #$NervousSystem. Examples include #$Norepinephrine, #$Dopamine, #$Acetylcholine, and #$Serotonin.")
(comment drugUsedForCondition "(#$drugUsedForCondition  DRUG CONDITION) means that the drug DRUG is sometimes used by people with the intent of thereby affecting an instance of the #$PhysiologicalConditionType CONDITION.  This relationmay hold for contraindicated drugs, and for drugs that as a matter of fact do not have their intended effects.  For a stronger relation, see #$indicatedDrug.")
(comment Nephron "A specialization on #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Nephrons are the basic units of kidneys.")
(comment Chondrite "A specialization of #$Meteorite.  Chondrites are stony meteorites that have not been modified due to melting.")
(comment Achondrite "A specialization of #$Meteorite.  Achondrites are stony meteorites that lack chondrules.")
(comment Pyelonephritis "A kind of #$Nephritis and #$UrinaryTractInfection.  Pyelonephritis is a UTI that has reached up to the kidney.")
(comment DicarboxylicAcid "A specialization of #$CarboxylicAcid.  #$DicarboxylicAcid is the collection of carboxylic acids whose molecules contain at two #$CarboxylGroups.")
(comment SuccinicAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment GlutaricAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment AdipicAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment PimelicAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment SubericAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment AzelaicAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment SebacicAcid "A kind of #$DicarboxylicAcid.")
(comment TricarboxylicAcid "A specialization of #$CarboxylicAcid.  #$TricarboxylicAcid is the collection of carboxylic acids whose molecules contain three #$CarboxylGroups.")
(comment Acetaldehyde "A specialization of #$Aldehyde.  Each instance of #$Acetaldehyde is a compound with the formula CH3CHO.")
(comment Propionaldehyde "A specialization of #$Aldehyde.  Each instance of #$Propionaldehyde is a compound with the formula C3H6O. #$Propionaldehyde is a structural isomer of #$Acetone.")
(comment Acetone "C3H6O. #$Acetone is a ketone.  It is also known as 'propanone' and it is a common household solvent.  #$Acetone is a structural isomer of #$Propionaldehyde.")
(comment Aldehyde "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound.  Each instance of #$Aldehyde is a compound whose molecules include #$FormylGroups.")
(comment Butyraldehyde "A specialization of #$Aldehyde.  Each instance of #$Butyraldehyde is a compound with the formula C4H8O.")
(comment Aldose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Aldose is a monosaccharide with one #$FormylGroup per molecule.")
(comment Ketose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Ketose is a monosaccharide with one carbonyl group per molecule.")
(comment Triose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Triose is a monosaccharide with three carbon atoms per molecule.")
(comment Tetrose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Tetrose is a monosaccharide with four carbon atoms per molecule.")
(comment Pentose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Pentose is a monosaccharide with five carbon atoms per molecule.")
(comment Hexose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Hexose is a monosaccharide with six carbon atoms per molecule.")
(comment Aldohexose "A specialization of #$Aldose and #$Hexose.  Each instance of #$Aldohexose is a monosaccharide with six carbon atoms and one formyl group per molecule.")
(comment bitLengthOfComputerDataTransfer "(#$bitLengthOfComputerDataTransfer TRANSFER N) means that the number of bits transferred in the #$ComputerDataTransfer-Single is N.")
(comment MonsaccharideTypeByNumberOfCarbonAtoms "The collection of specializations of #$Monosaccharide each instance of which has molecules with a uniform number of caron atoms.")
(comment Glycine "A collection of compounds and a specialization of #$AminoAcid and #$Neurotransmitter.  Glycine molecules
are the smallest of the #$AminoAcids and occur as a constituent of
many #$ProteinMolecules.  These compounds participate in many synthetic
reactions and are also an inhibitory neurotransmitter in the central
nervous system.  Its abbreviations are \"Gly\" and \"G\".")
(comment Macromolecule "A specialization of #$Molecule.  Macromolecules are very large molecules.")
(comment Phytohormone "A specialization of #$Hormone.  Phytohormones are plant hormones.")
(comment Cytokinin "A specialization of #$Phytohormone.  Cytokinin is a kind of plant hormone that affects cell division in parts of plants.")
(comment AbscisicAcid "A specialization of #$Phytohormone.  Abscisic acid is a plant hormone that affects many plant developmental processes.")
(comment Auxin "A specialization of #$Phytohormone.  Auxin is a kind of plant hormone that affects many plant processes.")
(comment AccessoryFruit "A specialization of #$Fruit.  Each instance of #$AccessoryFruit is a fruit whose fleshy parts are not derived from a plant ovary.")
(comment Gibberellin "A specialization of #$Phytohormone.  Gibberellin is a kind of plant hormone that affects numerous plant processes.")
(comment OpticalDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$OpticalDevice is a device that affects light by either reflecting it, refracting it, causing its rays to converge or diverge, or more complicated combinations of such operations.  Examples include devices whose function is to enhance human vision (e.g., each #$Mirror, each pair of #$Eyeglasses, each set of #$Binoculars), as well as devices that manipulate light for other purposes (e.g., instances of #$OpticalComputerStorageDevice and #$LaserDiscPlayer).")
(comment Ultracentrifuge "A specialization of #$Centrifuge.  Ultracentrifuges are extremely powerful centrifuges that can apply forces of over one million times the force of gravity.")
(comment AdrenalGland "The collection of all adrenal ('suprarenal') #$Glands.  An individual #$AdrenalGland is an endocrine gland which produces #$Epinephrine and other #$Hormones.  An #$AdrenalGland is located on the cephalic end of each #$Kidney.")
(comment CellFractionation "A specialization of #$Centrifuging.  Each instance of #$CellFractionation is an event in which a tissue sample is first homogenized and then centrifugated to isolate parts of the constituent cells.")
(comment CompoundFruit "A specialization of #$Fruit.  Each instance of #$CompoundFruit is a fruit whose fleshy parts are derived from multiple plant ovaries.")
(comment AggregateFruit "A specialization of #$Fruit.  Each instance of #$CompoundFruit is a fruit whose fleshy parts are derived from multiple plant ovaries within a single flower.")
(comment MultipleFruit "A specialization of #$Fruit.  Each instance of #$CompoundFruit is a fruit whose fleshy parts are derived from multiple plant ovaries from different flowers.")
(disjointWith MultipleFruit AggregateFruit)
(comment (FruitFn PineapplePlant) "The collection of individual pineapples.")
(comment AmacrineCell "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Amacrine cells are neurons located in the retina that process visual information before it is sent to the brain.")
(comment Ketohexose "A specialization of #$Monosaccharide.  Each instance of #$Ketohexose is a monosaccharide with one carbonyl group and six carbon atoms per molecule.")
(comment AminoacyltRNASynthetase "A type of #$EnzymeMolecule whose instances catalyze esterification to form an aminoacyl-tRNA.")
(comment Amniocentesis "A specialization of #$MedicalTesting.  Each instance of #$Amniocentesis is an event in which amniotic fluid is obtained via a needle that is inserted into a uterus.")
(comment AmnioticFluid "The collection of all volumes of amniotic fluid, which is the fluid that is contained in the amniotic sac of a pregnant animal.")
(comment Amniote "A specialization of #$Vertebrate.  The amniotes are vertebrate tetrapods (including mammals, reptiles, and birds), that have amniotic eggs.")
(comment infoTransferContentSpecifyingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$FormattedOutputConversionFunction, (#$infoTransferContentSpecifyingArgumentPosition FN N) means that the #$CharacterString which is the nth argument supplied to FN in a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable specifies all or part of the character content transferred in any normal execution of that #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable.")
(comment infoTransferContentSpecifyingArgAndRest "Where FN is a #$FormattedOutputConversionFunction, (#$infoTransferContentSpecifyingArgAndRest FN N) means that if FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked by a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, the arguments of arity N and higher that are supplied to FN by the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable collectively specify the entire character content transferred in any normal execution of the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable.")
(comment basicUnit "The kind of object that this object is made of.  For instance, (#$basicUnit BrickWall001 #$Brick) states that a particular brick wall is composed of #$Bricks.")
(comment TrabecularBoneTissue "One of two types of bone tissue.  Trabecular bone, also called spongy bone or cancellous bone, is found in the interior of bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart) and is surrounded by #$CorticalBoneTissue.  In the human skeleton, trabecular bone is found at the ends of long bones.  It is softer and less dense than cortical bone, and is composed of a network of trabeculae, or small approximately cylindrical units.")
(comment CorticalBoneTissue "One of two types of bone tissue.  Cortical bone, also called compact bone, forms the dense outer layer of bones.  It is harder, denser and stronger than the #$TrabecularBoneTissue it encloses.")
(comment BoneShaft "The collection of all bone shafts. A type of #$BoneSubPart. The collection #$BoneShaft is an #$InternalAnimalBodyRegionType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and an #$AnimalBodyPartType.  The shaft of a #$LongBone is often narrower than the two ends adjacent to joints, and typically has a central cavity (the #$MedullaryCavity) containing #$BoneMarrow.")
(comment MedullaryCavity "The collection of all central cavities of bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart).  In #$LongBones, the #$MedullaryCavity fills the center of the #$BoneShaft.  In any kind of bone (#$FlatBones, #$ShortBones, etc.), the #$MedullaryCavity is a region inside the bone containing the #$BoneMarrow which is devoid of mineralized osseous tissue.")
(comment Periosteum "The surfaces of all bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart), except those surfaces at the joints of #$LongBones, are covered with the #$Periosteum, which is a thin membrane of #$ConnectiveTissue.")
(comment BinaryDataTransfer "The collection of all #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvents where a number represented with binary encoding is transferred from one #$ComputerStorageDevice, such as a #$CPUMemoryRegister, to another.")
(comment Apatite "The collection of all apatite. A type of #$Mineral. #$Apatite is an #$ExistingStuffType. Apatites are a group of calcium-phosphate minerals which may be high in concentrations of other ions, such as fluoride, chloride, bromide or hydroxyl ions. ")
(comment Hydroxyapatite "The collection of all hydroxyapatite, also called hydroxylapatite. #$Hydroxyapatite is an #$ExistingStuffType.  It is a form of #$Apatite which has a high concentration of hydroxide ions (see #$HydroxideIon). In its pure form, its chemical formula is Ca10(PO4)6(OH)2. A variant of #$Hydroxyapatite makes up the inorganic, mineral component of bone (see #$BoneTheStuff).")
(comment BoneMineral "The collection of all #$Hydroxyapatite created as part of bone (see #$BoneTheStuff).  This material varies from ''pure'' hydroxyapatite in that it contains measurable amounts of carbonate, and fewer hydroxyl groups than stoichiometry would predict.  Crystals of #$BoneMineral are very small and shaped like long, thin plates with dimensions of tens to hundreds of angstroms.")
(disjointWith CancerCell (CollectionDifferenceFn EukaryoticCell CancerCell))
(disjointWith NoncancerousCell CancerCell)
(comment summaryPredicateWRTSetOrCollection-RecommendedOrdering "(<code>#$summaryPredicateWRTSetOrCollection-RecommendedOrdering COL 
LIST-OF-PREDS)</code> means that in a summry of an instance of <code>COL</code>, the recommended order of relevant predicates is given by <code>LIST-OF-PREDS</code> (where the first element of the list should appear first, the second element should appear second, and so forth).")
(comment Cytokine "This is the collection of all (instances, not types of) cytokines.
A cytokine is a soluble peptide that acts as a chemical communicator between cells.
They are of relatively low molecular weight and are secreted by one cell for the purpose of altering either its own
functions (autocrine effect) or those of adjacent cells (paracrine effect). In many instances, individual cytokines have multiple biological activities.
Different cytokines can also have the same activity, which provides for functional redundancy within the inflammatory and immune systems.")
(comment Osteoclast "The collection of all #$Osteoclasts.  These are large cells than may contain a dozen nulclei (see #$CellNucleus) or more.  They are found in the bone tissue (see #$BoneTheStuff) of vertebrates, and are active in bone resorption.")
(comment BoneTheStuff "Hard, largely mineralized (see #$BoneMineral) connective tissue of which the adult skeleton of most vertebrates is chiefly composed.  Although bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart) are largely made up of #$BoneTheStuff, they also contain other tissue types, such as #$BoneMarrow, #$NerveTissue, and #$BloodVessels. #$BoneTheStuff refers only to the hard, mineralized portions of bones and the cells locally involved in its development, maintenance and metabolism.")
(comment Osteoblast "The collection of all #$Osteoblasts, which are cells found in the bone tissue (see #$BoneTheStuff) of vertebrates, and are active in bone building.")
(comment Osteocyte "The collection of all #$Osteocytes, which are cells found in the bone tissue (see #$BoneTheStuff) of vertebrates.  When an #$Osteoblast becomes trapped in the mineralized bone matrix (see #$BoneMineral), it becomes an #$Osteocyte.  At this point it ceases to secrete the materials for bone formation, but remains metabolically active and remains networked to neighboring cells via long extensions of its cytoplasm that pass through tiny connections in the bone mineral matrix.")
(comment HLKnowledgeBaseStore "#$HLKnowledgeBaseStore is a specialization of #$CycKB.  Each instance of #$HLKnowledgeBaseStore contains part of the information in the full Cyc knowledge base (typically constrainted syntactically to binary GAFs or similar) at the HL level of representation.")
(comment LinkedLifeQuerySimulationMt "Reasoning environment for testing and demonstrating queries that could be answered with access the OntoText LinkedLife data integration platform (http://www.linkedlifedata.com), but simulates its accessiblility when it is not actually accessible.")
(comment unknownSentenceWRTInferenceMode "<code>(#$unknownSentenceWRTInferenceMode MODE SENTENCE)</code> means that the CycL sentence <code>SENTENCE</code> is not provable in inference when asked using the cluster of inference parameters associated with <code>MODE</code>, a #$SubLKeyword used to specify one of the recognized instances of  #$InferenceModeParameter.  The legal values for <code>MODE</code> are: :SHALLOW, :MINIMAL, :MAXIMAL, and :EXTENDED.")
(comment LASIKProcedure-Surgical "A specialization of #$RefractiveEyeSurgery.  Each instance of #$LASIKProcedure-Surgical is a procedure performed using a laser to correct vision.")
(comment RefractiveEyeSurgery "A specialization of #$EyeProcedure-Surgical.  Each instance of #$RefractiveEyeSurgery is eye surgery performed with the objective of improving the refractive state of the eye.")
(comment ExcimerLaser-Device "A specialization of #$LASER-Device.  Each instance of #$ExcimerLaser-Device produces UV laser light that is well absorbed by biological tissue.")
(comment stepFollowsStepInCycleType "A predicate used to characterize orderings of steps in cycles. <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType CYCLE LATER-STEP EARLIER-STEP)</code> means that in an instance of <code>CYCLE</code>, a specialization of #$Cycle-Situation, an instance of <code>LATER-STEP</code> will be \"the next step\" to occur after an instance of <code>EARLIER-STEP</code>.  What counts as \"the next step\" is a matter of granularity.  For example, in the (eukaryotic) cell cycle, the interphase step follows the M phase step which follows another iteration of the cycle, so that <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle)</code> and both <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle)</code> hold.  However, M phase consists of two phases, Mitosis and Cytokinesis, so that in addition, <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle  #$Mitosis)</code> and <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType #$Cytokinesis #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle)</code> both hold.  However, it would does not hold that <code>(#$stepFollowsStepInCycleType #$Cytokinesis #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle)</code> since, despite the fact that cytokinesis does indeed follow interphase <i>temporally</i> (e.g., <code>(#$startsAfterStartOfInSituationType #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle #$Cytokinesis)</code> undeniably holds), it is not \"next\" in the way that #$Mitosis and #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle are.")
(comment phasesAlternateInCycleType "A predicate used to identify the two alternating \"top level\" stages in a cycle, for cycles that admit of such a description. <code>(#$phasesAlternateInCycleType CYCLE PHASE-A PHASE-B)</code> identify <code>PHASE-A</code> and <code>PHASE-B</code> as the alternating stages.  Typically, this means that <code>CYCLE</code> is a serial cycle that iterates through some class of event <code>EVENT</code> in which <code>PHASE-A</code> is followed by <code>PHASE-B</code> or vice versa.  For example, <code>(#$phasesAlternateInCycleType #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle)</code> holds by virtue of #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle denoting the class of cycling events that iterate through a series of instances of #$EukaryoticCellCycle, which is defined as a class of events that begins with an instance of #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle followed by (and ending with) an instance of #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle.")
(comment Cycle-Serial "The collection of all instances of #$Cycle-Situation in which the iterated sequence of stages of stages comprising a single repetition of the #$Cycle-Situation is instantiated in temporal series; e.g. where a given #$Cycle-Situation SIT is constituted by situation types A, B, C, and D, if SIT is a #$Cycle-Serial, then an instantiation of A is followed temporally by an instantiation of B, followed by an instantiation of C, and so on.  #$Cycle-Serial instances contrast in this respect with instances of #$Cycle-Parallel, wherein instantiated stages happen concurrently.")
(comment AdrenalCortex "The adrenal cortex is a layer of tissue along the perimeter of adrenal glands.  It is important as the location of aldosterone and cortisol production.")
(comment AdrenalMedulla "The adrenal medulla is the core of the adrenal gland.  It is important as the location of epinephrine and norepinephrine production.")
(comment Gamete-Mature "#$Gamete-Mature is a specialization of #$HaploidCell (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Gamete-Mature is a special cell that can fuses with another gamete during fertilization. Mature gametes develop from the #$Gametids produced via #$Meiosis in the reproductive tissues of organisms that reproduce sexually.  All gametes are haploid, and are produced by #$Gametogenesis-Meiotic, which is a process that subsumes #$Meiosis, and involves post-meiotic maturation of gfemetids into gametes.  In animals, gametes are the direct results of the maturation of meiotically produced gametids; in plants, meiosis produces spores (see #$Spore-PlantLifeStage), which develop into #$Gametophytes, which then produce gametes by #$Mitosis.")
(comment MesenchymalStemCell "A specialization of #$AdultStemCell. Each instance of #$MesenchymalStemCell is a multipotent stem cell with the ability to differentiate into a variety of cell types.  In vertebrates, they can differentiate into #$Osteoblasts, #$FatCells, #$Chondrocytes, and many others.  One place such cells can be found is in #$BoneMarrow.")
(comment CellularDifferentiation "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$BiologicalDevelopmentEvent. In each #$CellularDifferentiation event, one or more cells which are not yet fully specialized develop into one or more cells, some of which no longer have the ability to specialize further.  To be an input to #$CellularDifferentiation, a cell must be an instance of #$AtLeastMultipotentCell.  Differentiation may involve one or more iterations through a #$CellCycle, possibly with asymmetric divisions, in which the daughter cells receive different proportions of the parent cell's molecules or parts. It also involves changes in gene expression, which changes the way cells respond to signals received from surrounding tissues.")
(comment MultipotentCell "#$MultipotentCells normally have the ability to differentiate (see #$CellularDifferentiation) into multiple, but limited cell types.")
(comment AtLeastPluripotentCell "Individual #$EukaryoticCells which are quite undifferentiated (see #$CellularDifferentiation) are elements of this collection. #$AtLeastPluripotentCell includes both #$PluripotentCells, which can differentiate into any cell type of the adult or immature organism of a given species, but can't develop into an entire organism, and #$TotipotentCells such as the #$Zygote which can develop into an entire organism.")
(comment PluripotentCell "#$PluripotentCells are #$StemCells that can differentiate into any cell type of an adult or immature organism (of a given species), but because they lack the ability to produce structures outside the embryo proper, such as the placenta, they can't develop into an entire organism.")
(comment TotipotentCell "#$TotipotentCells can differentiate into any of the cell types of an adult or immature organism (of a given species), including tissues outside the embryo such as the placenta.  One #$TotipotentCell can develop into an entire organism, given the right conditions.")
(comment CellTypeByCellPotency "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection whose instances are collections of cells that are characterized by their ''potency,'' or capability of differentiating into more specific types of cells.")
(comment cellularInputs "(#$cellularInputs PROCESS CELL) states that the individual #$Cell, CELL, is one of the inputs to PROCESS (an instance of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel).  There may be other, non-cellular inputs to PROCESS.  CELL may or may not be destroyed by PROCESS.")
(comment AtLeastMultipotentCell "Individual #$EukaryoticCells which are not yet fully differentiated (see #$CellularDifferentiation) are elements of this collection.  #$AtLeastMultipotentCell includes cells which are multipotent (see #$MultipotentCell), meaning they are limited in which types of cells they can become, as well as #$PluripotentCells and #$TotipotentCells, which have fewer limitations.")
(comment TerminallyDifferentiatedCell "#$TerminallyDifferentiatedCells are the end result of #$CellularDifferentiation and normally cannot develop any further.  They are also typically unable to divide.")
(comment cellularOutputs "(#$cellularOutputs PROCESS CELL) states that the individual #$Cell, CELL, is one of the outputs resulting from PROCESS (an instance of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel).  There may be other, non-cellular outputs from PROCESS.  CELL may or may not have been created by PROCESS.")
(comment OsteoblastDifferentiationFromMSCs "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$OsteoblastDifferentiationFromMSCs one or more #$MesenchymalStemCells participate in cell division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), and some of the daughter cells become more specialized, ultimately becoming #$Osteoblasts (perhaps after additional cell divisions, although this is not currently understood).  Daughter cells not committing to the osteoblast cell lineage remain #$MesenchymalStemCells.")
(comment biologicalObjectTypeProducesType "<code>(#$biologicalObjectTypeProducesType BLO-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject) are sources of instances of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible).  
<p>
This is a very general relation.  For example, all of the following are true:
<p>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeProducesType #$IsletsOfLangerhans #$Insulin)<br>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeProducesType #$BananaTree (#$FruitFn #$BananaTree)) <br>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeProducesType #$Gonad #$Gamete)
<p>
Whenever it is the case that (#$biologicalObjectTypeProducesType BLO-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE), there is some type of production event (see #$BiologicalProductionEvent) in which among the outputs created (see #$outputsCreated and #$outputsCreated-TypeType) are instances of PRODUCT-TYPE, and during which instances of BLO-TYPE are important participants.")
(disjointWith Calcitonin ThyroidHormone)
(comment Triiodothyronine "A #$Hormone produced by the #$Thyroid.")
(comment productOfBLO "<code>(#$productOfPlant PLANT PRODUCT)</code> means that <code>PLANT</code> is the source of <code>PRODUCT</code>.  For example <code>(#$productOfPlant MapleTree001 MapleSyrup001)</code> means that <code>MapleTree001</code> is the source of <code>MapleSyrup001</code>.")
(comment productOfBLO "<code>(#$productOfBLO BLO PRODUCT)</code> means that <code>BLO</code> is the source of <code>PRODUCT</code>.  For example <code>(#$productOfBLO MapleTree001 MapleSyrup001)</code> means that <code>MapleTree001</code> is the source of <code>MapleSyrup001</code>.")
(comment Secretion-Bodily "The collection of all #$NaturalTangibleStuff secreted by an organism's body.  There are a wide variety of bodily secretions, including #$Hormones, #$Mucus, #$Insulin, and #$Semen.  Secretions may be deposited either within the body (e.g., #$BileTheSecretion) or outside of it (e.g., #$Sweat). 
<p>
Note: Secretions are different from #$ExcretionSubstance in that secretions are not necessarily waste products.  E.g., they may be a release of pheromones to attract a mate, a layer of sweat to cool off the organism, a layer of nectar to attract bees, etc.  Some subsets of #$Secretion-Bodily, such as #$Sweat, are also subsets of #$ExcretionSubstance (i.e., wastes).")
(comment biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType "<code>(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE)</code> means that instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject) are sources of instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible, and typically a specialization of #$Secretion-Bodily).  
<p>
For example, all of the following are true:
<p>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$IsletsOfLangerhans #$Insulin)<br>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$Thyroid #$ThyroidHormone) <br>
(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$TearDuct #$LacrimalFluid)
<p>
Whenever it is the case that (#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE), there is some type of #$SecretionEvent during which among the outputs created (see #$outputsCreated and #$outputsCreated-TypeType) are instances of SECRETION-TYPE, and during which instances of BLO-TYPE are the doers.")
(comment onlyBiologicalObjectTypeProducesType "<code>(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE)</code> means that only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject) are sources (during instances of #$BiologicalProductionEvent) of instances of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible).  
<p>
For example, all of the following are true:
<p>
(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$BananaTree (#$FruitFn #$BananaTree)) <br>
(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$Gonad #$Gamete)
<p>
Whenever it is the case that <code>(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeProducesType BLO-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE)</code>, there is some type of production event (see #$BiologicalProductionEvent) in which among the outputs created (see #$outputsCreated and #$outputsCreated-TypeType) are instances of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code>, and during which only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> are important participants.
<p>
It is often the case that instances of <code>PRODUCT-TYPE</code> can be synthesized, and thus are sometimes produced by means other than a <i>biological</i> production event.")
(comment MucousMembrane "The collection of all instances of mucus membrane.  Instances of #$MucousMembrane linesInside-Skinlike the #$DigestiveSystem, the #$ReproductiveSystem, and the #$RespiratorySystem.  #$Mucus #$covers-Paintlike each instance of #$MucousMembrane.")
(comment outputsSecreted "(#$outputsSecreted SECRETION-EVENT SECRETION) means that SECRETION is secreted during SECRETION-EVENT.")
(comment Aponeurosis "The collection of all aponeuroses. A type of #$ConnectiveTissue, #$AnimalBodyRegion, and #$InternalAnatomicalPart. The concept #$Aponeurosis is an #$AnimalBodyPartType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.  Aponeuroses are flattened tendons that connect muscles to the body parts they affect.")
(comment ConnectiveTissue "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ConnectiveTissue.  Subsets of this collection include #$Aponeurosis, #$Tendon, #$Cartilage, etc.  An important characteristic of #$ConnectiveTissue is that it is composed of a large amount of #$ExtracellularMatrix compared to other tissue types. #$Cells that inhabit the tissue and (depending on the type of cell) produce the matrix are often dispersed throughout and embedded in the matrix.  Some kinds of #$ConnectiveTissue are tough and dense, like #$Cartilage and #$BoneTheStuff.  Others, like adipose tissue (See #$FattyTissue) are loose and less desne.")
(comment Venom "The poisonous secretion of an animal, produced by specialized glands that are often associated with spines, teeth, stings, or other piercing devices. #$Venoms include a variety of types of #$BiologicalToxin, including some nerve agents, #$BloodAgentStuffs, and #$BlisterAgentStuffs.")
(comment SebaceousGland "The collection of all sebaceous #$Glands.  Each instance of this collection is a gland in the skin that produces skin oil (a.k.a. \"sebum\").")
(comment Renin "A #$PeptideHormone secreted by the kidney.")
(comment Angiotensin "A peptide that interacts significantly with #$Renin.")
(comment Adipocyte "#$Adipocytes are the primary terminally-differentiated cell type in adipose tissue (See #$FattyTissue).  They are optimized for storing fat.")
(comment FatCell "A specialization of #$SomaticCell and #$AnimalCell.  The collection of cells found in #$FattyTissue.  An important specialization is #$Adipocyte, but #$FattyTissue contains other cell types as well, such as cells that form blood vessels, fibroblasts, and #$Macrophages.")
(comment AdipocyteDifferentiationFromMSCs "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$AdipocyteDifferentiationFromMSCs one or more #$MesenchymalStemCells participate in cell division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), and some of the daughter cells become more specialized, ultimately becoming #$Adipocytes (perhaps after additional cell divisions).  Daughter cells not committing to the adipocyte cell lineage remain #$MesenchymalStemCells.  It is possible that #$Adipocytes may be able to develop from other types of precursor cells.")
(comment OsteoblastConversionToOsteocyte "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$OsteoblastConversionToOsteocyte an #$Osteoblast is transformed into an #$Osteocyte. This happens to some #$Osteoblasts, but not all, after they have participated in bone formation. One that is so transformed makes connections to existing #$Osteocytes, becomes surrounded by secreted #$Osteoid, and then is considered a mature osteocyte when the osteoid becomes mineralized.")
(comment Chondrocyte "The primary type of cell found in #$Cartilage.  Each instance of #$Chondrocyte is embedded in the cartilaginous #$ExtracellularMatrix which it helps to secrete and maintain.")
(comment AutonomicNervousSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$AutonomicNervousSystem is a part of a #$PeripheralNervousSystem that controls visceral body functions.")
(comment SympatheticNervousSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$SympatheticNervousSystem is a part of an #$AutonomicNervousSystem that controls body functions in response to stress.")
(comment ParasympatheticNervousSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$ParasympatheticNervousSystem is a part of an #$AutonomicNervousSystem that controls body functions in primarily performed when irrespective of whether the body is stressed.")
(comment EntericNervousSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$EntericNervousSystem is a part of an #$AutonomicNervousSystem that controls digestive system functions.")
(disjointWith MotorNeuron AfferentNeuron)
(disjointWith AfferentNeuron Interneuron)
(disjointWith MotorNeuron Interneuron)
(comment AfferentNeuron "A specialization of #$PseudounipolarCell.  Afferent neurons are involved in carrying signals toward the #$CentralNervousSystem from receptors.")
(comment SensoryMotorNerve "The collection of all #$Nerves with combined sensory and motor functions.  Each #$SensoryMotorNerve is a #$Nerve that both carries sensory information towards the #$Brain and innervates one or more #$Muscles.  A #$SensoryMotorNerve is neither a #$SensoryNerve nor a #$MotorNerve since these carry nerve signals in a single direction.")
(comment GlialCell "A kind cell of that, along with neurons, constitutes nervous tissue.")
(comment MicroglialCell "A kind #$GlialCell.  The microglia provide immune defence to the central nervous system.")
(disjointWith MicroglialCell MacroglialCell)
(comment MacroglialCell "A specialization of #$GlialCell. Macroglia perform a variety of functions in the nervous system.")
(comment Astrocyte "A specialization of #$MacroglialCell. Astrocytes perform a variety of functions in the nervous system.")
(comment Oligodendrocyte "A specialization of #$MacroglialCell.     Oligodendrocytes primarily serve to myelinate nerves in the central nervous system.")
(comment Ependymocyte "A specialization of #$MacroglialCell.    Ependymocyte serve a variety of functions in the central nervous system.")
(comment RadialGlia "A specialization of #$MacroglialCell.  Radial glia serve a variety of functions in the central nervous system.")
(comment SchwannCell "A specialization of #$MacroglialCell. Schwann cells serve primarily to myelinate nerve fibers in the peripheral nervous system.")
(comment Collagen-TypeI "A protein which is a type of #$Collagen.  Type-I collagen is the most frequently-occuring type of collagen in the body.  Fibers of #$Collagen-TypeI make up the non-mineral portion of the #$ExtracellularMatrix of #$BoneTheStuff, and it can be found in #$Tendons and in other tissues.")
(comment Collagen-TypeII "A protein which is a type of #$Collagen.  Type-II collagen appears as a major protein constituent of the #$ExtracellularMatrix of hyaline cartilage.  It is the only kind of #$Collagen in hyaline and elastic cartilage, and is found in fibrocartilage (which also contains #$Collagen-TypeI).")
(comment DeprecatedLibraryFunction "The collection of all instances of #$StandardLibraryFunction which are deemed to be deprecated, i.e., superseded by other functions within their respective libraries.")
(comment permittedOverlapInDataLocsGivenByArgs "(#$permittedOverlapInDataLocsGivenByArgs FN N M) means that the functionality of the #$DataLocationAlteringFunction FN is such that the function is allowed to execute even if the data locations designated by the Nth and Mth arguments with which it is called overlap.")
(comment infoTransferTerminatingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$DataLocationAlteringFunction, (infoTransferTerminatingArgumentPosition FN N) means that the functionality of FN is such that, when a piece of executable code for which FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked is executed in a normal run-time environment, the value of the Nth argument called with FN always denotes a feature whose occurrence in the information stream will terminate the execution.")
(comment MemCCopyFn "Where the number specified by the arg4 position is N, the #$MemCCpyFunction copies at most N bytes from the data location given by the arg2 position, to the data location given by the arg1 position, but stops if the character whose ID is given by the arg3 position is encountered in the copy string.  The function returns a pointer to the next character in the source buffer after the termination-triggering character, or NULL if the terminating character is not found in the first N characters of the source.")
(comment SpecifiedInferenceModeCluster "A specialization of #$InferenceMode with a completely asserted extent.  Instances are one of four modes that cluster high-value combinations of inference parameter settings with proven value against Cyc's inference regression tests (see #$KBContentRegressionTest).")
(comment InferenceMode "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameterValueObject.  Instances are values to the #$InferenceModeParameter specification in inference, which, when set, determine the values of multiple other parameters for an inference.")
(comment MemMoveFn "The #$MemMoveFunction copies the number of bytes specified by the third argument from the memory area specified by the second argument to the memory area specified by the first argument.")
(comment AcetylCoenzymeA "A specilaization of #$Thioester.  Acetyl coenzyme A is a substance that plays a significant role in iin metabolism, and in particular in the Krebs cycle.")
(comment secretionSource "(#$secretionSource SECRETION-EVENT BLO) means that during the #$SecretionEvent SECRETION-EVENT, BLO is the instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject that does the secreting.")
(comment FungalCellWall "The collection of instances of #$CellWall that are #$anatomicalParts of some (single-celled) instances of #$Fungus.")
(comment HematopoieticCell "The collection of all cells found in #$HematopoieticTissue.  This includes multipotent #$HematopoieticStemCells having the ability to differentiate into any type of #$BloodCell, as well as other types of cells that are partially or more completely differentiated (See #$CellularDifferentiation).")
(comment Lymphoblast "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Lymphoblast is a partially-differentiated cell that will differentiate further into one or more #$Lymphocytes.  #$Lymphoblasts are normally found only in the #$BoneMarrow, except in the case of certain disorders.")
(disjointWith Lymphoblast MyeloidProgenitorCell)
(disjointWith Lymphocyte Lymphoblast)
(disjointWith Myeloblast MyeloidProgenitorCell)
(disjointWith Lymphocyte Myeloblast)
(comment Myeloblast "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Myeloblast is a partially-differentiated cell that will differentiate further into one or more leucocytes (see #$WhiteBloodCell), but not into #$Lymphocytes.  #$Myeloblasts are normally found only in the #$BoneMarrow.")
(comment RedMarrow "Tissue that is found in the center of bones consisting mainly of haematopoietic cells (see #$HematopoieticCell) where the formation of the cells that make up blood occurs.")
(comment MyeloidProgenitorCell "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$MyeloidProgenitorCell is a multipotent cell with the ability to differentiate untilmately into erythrocytes (see #$RedBloodCell), thrombocytes (see #$Platelet), mast cells, and all types of #$WhiteBloodCells except those in the lymphocytic line.")
(comment UnipotentCell "Individual #$EukaryoticCells which are capable of further differentiation (see #$CellularDifferentiation), but which are fully committed to a single terminal cell type.  Naturally, each individual cell may not survive to continue this path of differentiation, but for those that do, the path does not branch.")
(comment CellCapableOfFurtherDifferentiation "Instances of #$CellCapableOfFurtherDifferentiation are able to further specialize their function, perhaps over the course of some number of rounds of cell division, ultimately developing into one or more terminally differentated cell type (see #$TerminallyDifferentiatedCell).")
(disjointWith CellCapableOfFurtherDifferentiation TerminallyDifferentiatedCell)
(disjointWith AtLeastMultipotentCell UnipotentCell)
(comment Proerythroblast "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Proerythroblast is a #$UnipotentCell that the earliest cell on a committed path of differentiation into erythroblasts (see #$RedBloodCell).  #$Proerythroblasts are normally found only in the #$BoneMarrow.")
(comment Megakaryoblast "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Megakaryoblast is a #$UnipotentCell that the earliest cell on a committed path of differentiation into #$Megakaryocytes, which in turn produce thrombocytes (see #$Platelet).  #$Megakaryoblasts are found only in the #$BoneMarrow.")
(comment Megakaryocyte "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Megakaryocyte is a #$TerminallyDifferentiatedCell that produces thrombocytes (see #$Platelet) by releasing small fragments of its cytoplasm, each enclosed by a cell membrane fragment.  #$Megakaryocytes are found in the #$BoneMarrow.")
(disjointWith Megakaryoblast Proerythroblast)
(disjointWith Megakaryoblast Myeloblast)
(comment EnzymeInactivationEvent "The collection of all #$ChemicalReactions in which an 'active' #$EnzymeMolecule (i.e., one that is capable of catalyzing a certain kind of #$ChemicalReaction that is a target for its type) undergoes some kind of configuration change which renders it 'inactive', i.e., incapable of catalyzing the aforesaid targeted type of #$ChemicalReaction.")
(comment InactivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn "A collection-denoting function used to represent the class of 'inactivations' of a given type of enzyme.  Where MOL-TYPE is a class of #$EnzymeMolecule, (#$InactivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the class of all occurrences in which an instance of MOL-TYPE is rendered 'inactive' in the sense of being disabled from catalyzing certain types of chemical reactions particular to the class.  An instance of (#$InactivationOfEnzymeOfTypeFn MOL-TYPE) may consist in a #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent, a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent, a #$ShapeChangeEvent, or some concatenation of the three.  Often, inactivation occurs  when the #$EnzymeMolecule is chemically dissociated from an 'activation factor' (see #$activationFactorForEnzyme) which otherwise enables it to catalyze the necessary reactions, followed immediately by association with an 'inactivaton factor' (see #$inactivationFactorForEnzyme) which blocks it from catalyizing the necessary reactions.")
(comment inactivationFactorForEnzyme "A type level predicate that links a class of #$EnzymeMolecule to a class of #$ChemicalObject.  (#$inactivationFactorForEnzyme FACTOR-TYPE ENZYME-TYPE) means that ordinarily, instances of FACTOR-TYPE 'inactivate' instances of ENZYME-TYPE when bonded to them chemically, in the strict sense that the bonded instance is rendedred unable to catalyze certain kinds of chemical reaction.")
(comment Basophil "A subclass of #$WhiteBloodCell.  #$Basophils play a role in various inflammatory responses.  Like #$Neutrophils and #$Eosinophils, they can enter tissues when needed.")
(comment Eosinophil "A subclass of #$WhiteBloodCell.  #$Eosinophils play a role in various immune responses.  Like #$Neutrophils and #$Basophils, they can enter tissues when needed.  #$Eosinophils can persist longer in tissues than neutrophils or basophils, providing they are not activated.")
(comment onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType "<code>(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE)</code> means that only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject) are sources (during instances of #$SecretionEvent) of instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible, and typically a specialization of #$Secretion-Bodily).  
<p>
For example, all of the following are true:
<p>
(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$IsletsOfLangerhans #$Insulin)<br>
(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$Thyroid #$ThyroidHormone) <br>
(#$onlyBiologicalObjectTypeSecretesType #$TearDuct #$LacrimalFluid)
<p>
Whenever it is the case that <code>(#$biologicalObjectTypeSecretesType BLO-TYPE SECRETION-TYPE)</code>, there is some type of #$SecretionEvent during which among the outputs created (see #$outputsCreated and #$outputsCreated-TypeType) are instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code>, and during which only instances of <code>BLO-TYPE</code> are the doers.
<p>
It is often the case that instances of <code>SECRETION-TYPE</code> can be synthesized, and thus are sometimes produced by means other than a secretion event.")
(comment Monoblast "A type of #$HematopoieticCell.  Each instance of #$Monoblast is a #$UnipotentCell that is the earliest cell on a committed path of differentiation (see #$CellularDifferentiation) into #$Monocytes and #$Macrophages.  #$Monoblasts are normally found only in the #$BoneMarrow.")
(disjointWith Monoblast Proerythroblast)
(disjointWith Megakaryoblast Monoblast)
(disjointWith BloodCell HematopoieticCell)
(comment Monocyte "A type of #$WhiteBloodCell that can play certain roles in the immune system.  #$Monocytes are produced in the #$BoneMarrow and enter the #$Bloodstream, where they circulate for a few days before entering tissues.  A large percentage are stored in the #$Spleen.  In tissues, #$Monocytes further differentiate into #$Macrophages or dendritic cells.")
(comment EnzymeActivationEvent "The collection of all #$ChemicalReactions in which an 'inactive' #$EnzymeMolecule is 'activated, i.e., rendered capabled of catalyzing a certain #$ChemicalReaction within an appropriate cellular process context, through association with some other chemical object.")
(comment DataLocationAlteringFunction-Checked "The collection of all #$DataLocationAlteringFunctions with inbuilt checks that will block execution in cases where the length of the the string being transferred is greater than the width of the destination.  It is impossible for the execution of a function call using a #$DataLocationAlteringFunction-Checked to overwrite the destination buffer, hence impossible for execution of such a function call to be the cause of a #$StackBasedBufferOverflow.")
(comment DataLocationAlteringFunction-Unchecked "The collection of all #$DataLocationAlteringFunctions whose innate functionality does not support a check of whether the memory area that is the destination of the information transfer has in fact a greater storage capacity than the length of the information being transferred.")
(comment ExtracellularMatrixTypeOfTissueTypeFn "<code>(#$ExtracellularMatrixTypeOfTissueTypeFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all portions of #$ExtracellularMatrix that are present in instances of tissue type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment tissueTypeHasExtracellularMatrixType "<code>(#$tissueTypeHasExtracellularMatrixType TISSUE-TYPE MATRIX-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>MATRIX-TYPE</code> as the collection of portions of #$ExtracellularMatrix that form the non-cellular part of portions of biological tissue of type <code>TISSUE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment forbiddenOverlapInDataLocsGivenByArgs "(#$forbiddenOverlapInDataLocsGivenByArgs FN N M) means that the functionality of the #$DataLocationAlteringFunction Fn is such that the function is not permitted to execute if the data locations designated by the Nth and Mth arguments with which it is called overlap.")
(comment StrCpyFn "#$StrCpyFunction copies the string stored in the location pointed to by the second argument to the location pointed to by the first argument.  The locations are not allowed to overlap, and the destination must be large enough to receive the copy.")
(comment StrNCpyFn "The #$StrNCpyFunction copies at most the number of bytes specified by the third argument from the data location pointed to by the second argument to the data location pointed to by the third argument.  The locations cannot overlap, and the destination location must be large enough to receive the copy.")
(comment WMemCpyFn "The #$WMemCpy function copies the number of wide characters specified in the third argument from the point in the array specified by the second argument to the point in the array specified by the third argument.  The arrays are not allowed to overlap.")
(comment properSubEventOfTypeTerminatesSit "(#$properSubEventOfTypeTerminatesSit SIT EVENT-TYPE) is true if and only if there is an instance of EVENT-TYPE, TERMINAL, such that TERMINAL is proper subsituation (#$properSubSituations) of SIT and #$temporallyCoterminal with SIT.")
(comment ProgramExecutionErrorHalt "The collection of all #$ProgramActions which halt before their intended points of completion due to error conditions.")
(comment projectTypeHasFocalActivityType "The predicate corresponding to the function #$ProjectTypeWithFocalActivityFn, <code>(#$projectTypeHasFocalActivityType PROJECT-TYPE ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>PROJECT-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Project that focally involve instances of <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment LanguageSpecificLibrary "The collection of all instances of #$StandardCodingLibrary that are specific to an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment StandardLibraryLanguage "The collection of all instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage which are associated with instances of #$StandardCodingLibrary (see #$languageOfLibrary).")
(comment FunctionLibraryForLanguageFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for referring to instances of #$LanguageSpecificLibrary.  Where LANGUAGE is an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, (#$FunctionLibraryForLanguageFn LANGUAGE) denotes the #$StandardCodingLibrary associated with LANGUAGE.")
(comment languageOfLibrary "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$FunctionLibraryForLanguageFn.  Where LANGUAGE is an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, (#$languageOfLibrary LANGUAGE LIBRARY) means that LIBRARY is the #$StandardCodingLibrary associated with LANGUAGE.")
(comment ProgrammersToolkit "The collection of all instances of #$StandardCodingLibrary that are considered programmer's toolkits.")
(comment ProgrammersToolkitForOSFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction that is used to refer to instances of #$ProgrammersToolkit based on #$OperatingSystem.  Where OS is an instance of #$OperatingSystem, (#$ProgrammersToolkitForOSFn OS) denotes the #$ProgrammersToolkit specific to OS.")
(comment toolkitOfOS "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ProgrammersToolkitForOSFn.  Where OS is an instance of #$OperatingSystem, (#$toolkitOfOS OS KIT) means that KIT is the #$ProgrammersToolkit specific to OS.")
(comment ProgrammersToolkitForReleaseOfOSFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction that is used to refer to #$ProgrammersToolkit instances based on a versioned OS.  Where OSV is an instance of #$OperatingSystem and #$VersionedSoftwareObject, (#$ProgrammersToolkitForReleaseOfOSFn OSV) denotes the #$ProgrammersToolkit specific to OSV.")
(comment toolkitOfOSRelease "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ProgrammersToolkitForReleaseOfOSFn. Where OSV is an instance of #$OperatingSystem and #$VersionedSoftwareObject, (#$toolkitOfOSRelease OSV KIT) means that KIT is the #$ProgrammersToolkit specific to OSV.")
(comment toolkitIncludesFunction "(#$functionBelongsToToolkit FN KIT) means that the #$StandardLibraryFunction FN belongs to the #$ProgrammersToolkit KIT.")
(comment FormattedOutputConversionFunction "The collection of all functions that produce output according to an #$OutputStringFormat.")
(comment ParenchymaCell "A specialization of #$BotanicalCell.  Parenchyma cells are one of the three basic plant cell types, along with #$CollenchymaCells and #$SclerenchymaCells.")
(comment CollenchymaCell "A specialization of #$BotanicalCell.  Collenchyma cells are one of the three basic plant cell types, along with #$ParenchymaCells and #$SclerenchymaCells.")
(disjointWith CollenchymaCell ParenchymaCell)
(comment SclerenchymaCell "A specialization of #$BotanicalCell.  Sclerenchyma cells are one of the three basic plant cell types, along with #$CollenchymaCells and #$ParenchymaCells.")
(disjointWith CollenchymaCell SclerenchymaCell)
(disjointWith ParenchymaCell SclerenchymaCell)
(comment BiologicalLivingObjectTypeByTaxonomicKingdom "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$BiologicalLivingObject whose instances are all of the same taxonomic kingdom.")
(comment FungusBLO "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject that includes all living fungi, parts of living fungi, and regions of living fungi.")
(comment FungusCell "The collection of #$Cells that fungi (see #$Fungus) and parts of fungi are made of.")
(comment ProtistaKingdom "An instance of #$BiologicalKingdom and a specialization of #$EukaryoticOrganism.  Each instance of #$ProtistaKingdom is a eukaryotic organism that is <i>not</i> a plant, animal, or fungus.  All unicellular eukaryotic organisms are instances of #$ProtistaKingdom, although not all instances of #$ProtistaKingdom are unicellular organisms.  Notable specializations of #$ProtistaKingdom include #$Protozoan, #$SlimeMold, and #$Algae-LikeProtist.")
(comment ProtistBLO "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject that includes all living protists (See #$ProtistaKingdom), parts of living protists, and regions of living protists.")
(comment AnaerobicBLO "Anaerobic tissues or organisms are those that can live in the absence of oxygen.")
(comment FungusTissue "The collection of all instances of #$BiologicalTissue that comes from a fungus.  Each instance of #$FungusTissue consists of cells.")
(comment PlantTissue-Dermal "A specialization of #$PlantTissue. Along with vascular tissue and ground tissue, dermal tissue is one of the three kinds of plant tissue.")
(disjointWith PlantTissue-Vascular PlantTissue-Dermal)
(disjointWith PlantTissue-Ground PlantTissue-Dermal)
(disjointWith PlantTissue-Vascular PlantTissue-Ground)
(comment PlantTissue-Vascular "A specialization of #$PlantTissue. Vascular tissue constituites the vascular networks (see #$VascularNetworkOfPlant) in plants.  Along with dermal tissue and ground tissue, it is one of the three kinds of plant tissue.")
(comment RootHair "A kind of plant part.  Root hairs are extensions of epidermal plant cells near the tips of roots.  They increase the surface area of roots, facilitating absorption of water and minerals.")
(comment PlantTissue-Ground "A specialization of #$PlantTissue. Along with dermal tissue and vascular tissue, ground tissue is one of the three kinds of plant tissue.")
(comment codingFunctionParameterStandardName "(#$codingFunctionParameterStandardName FN N NAME-STRING) means that the name ordinarily used to denote the Nth parameter or argument slot of FN is NAME-STRING.")
(comment optionalArgForCodingFunction "(#$optionalArgForCodingFunction FN N) means that a value does not need to be supplied for the Nth argument position of the #$CodingFunction FN under all conditions.")
(comment uRLReferenceForCodingFunction "(#$uRLReferenceForCodingFunction FN URL) means that a specification of the syntax and parameters for FN is found at URL.")
(comment HumanSkeletalBiologySourceDocumentsMt "A #$Microtheory containing statements about books (see #$Book-CW) and articles (see #$ScholarlyArticle) which are the sources for knowledge about human skeletal biology.")
(comment PCWRelevantToHumanSkeletalBiology "Instances are #$PropositionalConceptualWorks concerning human skeletal biology, some subtopic, or some closely related topic.")
(comment editionOfPeriodicalByIssueNumber "A #$TernaryPredicate. (#$editionOfPeriodicalByIssueNumber SERIES VOLUME-NUMBER ISSUE) means that ISSUE is the instance of #$EditionOfCWSeries-Periodic which the member of the #$PeriodicalSeries SERIES indexed by number VOLUME-NUMBER. See also #$EditionByIssueNumberFn.")
(comment codingFunctionOperationTypes "(#$codingFunctionOperationTypes FN OP-TYPE) means that the #$CodingFunction FN 'performs' instances of OP-TYPE, in the strict sense that any execution of the executable code for which FN is the #$codingFunctionInvoked will be an instance of OP-TYPE.")
(comment CodingFunctionTypeByOperationType "This #$SecondOrderCollection categorizes specs of #$CodingFunction.  Each collection instance is a type of #$CodingFunction whose instances have as a common feature the implementation of a single salient #$ProgramAction type.")
(comment codingFunctionTypeReflectedInCompendium "(#$codingFunctionTypeReflectedInCompendium FN-TYPE LIBRARY) means that at least one instance of FN-TYPE is known to belong to the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIBRARY.")
(comment codingFunctionOperationalCategory "(#$codingFunctionOperationalCategory FN OPCAT) means the #$CodingFunction FN belongs to the #$CodingFunctionTypeByOperationType OPCAT.  A typed spec pred of #$isa.")
(disjointWith DispersionEvent ConvergenceEvent)
(comment AerialDispersionEvent "The collection of all #$DistributionEvents occurring
in a gaseous medium and such that the objects distributed are solid or
liquid particles that remain in suspension in that medium for some
length of time before impinging on their target.")
(comment DispersionEvent "A specialization of #$Translation-MultiTrajectory.  Each instance of #$DispersionEvent is an event in which things move away from a common origin.")
(comment constantReservedInOperatingSystem "(#$constantReservedInOperatingSystem CONST OS) means that the name of CONST is a reserved term in the code for OS.")
(comment MemoryProtectionCodeConstant "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeConstants used in conjunction with #$MemoryManagementFunctions for specifying how allocated memory should be protected.")
(comment memoryProtectionConstantName "A typed spec-pred of #$nameString.  (#$memoryProtectionConstantName CODE-CONSTANT NAME) means that NAME is the typographic designation for the #$MemoryProtectionCodeConstant CODE-CONSTANT.")
(comment Page-Execute-WriteCopy "When the UID for this constant is given to a #$MemoryManagementFunction as the value for the #$memProtectionStatusSpecifyingArgumentPosition, the function call enables execute, read-only, or copy-on-write access to a mapped view of a file mapping object. An attempt to write to a committed copy-on-write page results in a private copy of the page being made for the process. The private page is marked as PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE, and the change is written to the new page.")
(comment MemoryAllocationCodeConstant "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeConstants used in conjunction with #$MemoryManagementFunctions for allocating real or virtual memory.")
(comment memoryAllocationConstantName "A typed spec-pred of #$nameString.  (#$memoryAllocationConstantName CODE-CONSTANT NAME) means that NAME is the typographic designation for the #$MemoryAllocationCodeConstant CODE-CONSTANT.")
(comment allocationSizeSpecifyingArgumentPosition "(#$allocationSizeSpecifyingArgumentPosition MEM-FN N) means that the Nth argument position of the #$MemoryManagementFunction MEM-FN takes a value that specifies the size in bytes of the region of memory being allocated.")
(comment allocationTypeSpecifyingArgumentPosition "(#$allocationTypeSpecifyingArgumentPosition MEM-FN N) means that the Nth argument position of the #$MemoryManagementFunction MEM-FN takes a value that specifies the type of memory allocation via the #$MemoryAllocationCodeConstant denoted.")
(comment memProtectionStatusSpecifyingArgumentPosition "(#$memProtectionStatusSpecifyingArgumentPosition MEM-FN N) means that the Nth argument position of the #$MemoryManagementFunction MEM-FN takes a value which specifies the type of memory protection via the #$MemoryProtectionCodeConstant denoted.")
(comment VirtualAllocFn "#$VirtualAllocFn reserves or commits a region of pages in the virtual address space of the call process.  The first (optional) argument specifies the starting address of the region to allocate, the second argument specifies the size of the region in bytes, the third argument specifies the type of allocation via a #$MemoryAllocationCodeConstant, and the fourth argument specifies the type of memory protection via a #$MemoryProtectionCodeConstant.")
(comment WriteFileFn "#$WriteFileFn writes data to the specified file or input/output device.  The first argument specifies a handle to a file or I/O device (which must be created with write access).  The second argument is a pointer to the buffer containing the data to be written to the file or device.  The third argument specifies the number of bytes to be written.  The fourth (optional) argument specifies a pointer to the variable that receives the number of bytes written when using a synchronous arg1 parameter (NULL should be given as the argument here if the operation is asynchronous).  The fifth, optional argument specifies a pointer to an overlapped structure.")
(comment bLOTypeLifelongProcessType "(#$bLOTypeLifelongProcessType BLO-TYPE PROC-TYPE) states that instances of the type of #$BiologicalLivingObject, BLO-TYPE, are doing (probably unconsciously) a type of #$BiologicalProcess, PROC-TYPE, throughout their existence as living things.  Given any portion of the life of such an instance of BLO-TYPE, including its entire life, there will be some instance of PROC-TYPE that is a cotemporal sub-event of that #$Living (see #$cotemporalProperSubEvents).  For example, (#$bLOTypeLifelongProcessType #$AerobicOrganism #$Respiration).")
(comment averageRateOfQuantityChange "#$averageRateOfQuantityChange relates an instance of
#$QuantityChangeEvent to the average rate at which the relevant quantity
changed during that event.  (#$averageRateOfQuantityChange <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> <code>RATE</code>) can be computed by dividing the amount of change (see #$quantityChangeAmount) by the #$duration of <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code>.  (For any given sub-interval of the time during which <code>QUANTITY-CHANGE</code> occurs, the rate of change may be lesser or greater.)  Note that for #$DecreaseEvent instances, the #$averageRateOfQuantityChange will be negative, and for #$IncreaseEvent instances, it will be positive.")
(comment in-ContClosed "(#$in-ContClosed OBJ CONT) means
that #$PartiallyTangible OBJ is completely contained within one or more cavities within #$SolidTangibleThing CONT, and that it is not possible for OBJ to leave CONT as an object without either the opening of a portal in CONT or the non-standard significant deformation of OBJ or CONT.  CONT need not have a portal.  Parts of OBJ may extend out through portals in CONT.  If OBJ can temporarily undergo (a not-too forceful) shape deformation in order to fit through a portal in CONT, then OBJ is not #$in-ContClosed with respect to CONT.  Positive examples include water in a bottle with a closed cap; King Kong in a flimsy cage; a model of a ship in a bottle (where the model must be disassembled to force it out); egg yolk in an egg shell.  Negative examples include a morsel of bread in a prison cell (morsels are small enough to leave the cell by passing in between the bars of the cell -- use #$in-ContOpen); an egg yolk in an egg -- use #$internalParts; water in an open bottle (the necessary deformation is not forceful).   A positive borderline example is a skinny person in a jail cell who could just barely manage to squeeze through the bars (the necessary deformations, although self-imposed, would be abnormal and unexpected).  A negative borderline example is a spelunker who has crawled through a narrow passage into a cave (the deformations needed to get in (and therefore out) were self-imposed and not abnormal).")
(comment ExocrineGland "The collection of all exocrine glands. A type of #$Gland. Exocrine glands secrete their products into the external environment of an organism.")
(comment Repairing "The collection of instances of #$ImprovementEvent in which an object is improve by virtue of damage to it being corrected.")
(comment equationSetOfSystem "(#$equationSetOfSystem EQ-SET SYS) means that EQ-SET is a group of equations (an instnce of #$EquationSet) that can usefully describe related aspects of the #$System, SYS.")
(comment EquationSet "A specialization of (#$GroupFn #$Equation-MathematicalStatement).  Each instance of #$EquationSet is a group of equations that together are used by people to describe related aspects of a system.")
(disjointWith Drying MakingSomethingWet)
(comment conceptOfExternalOntologyWithName "<code>(#$conceptOfExternalOntologyWithName THING ONTOLOGY NAME)</code> identifies <code>THING</code> as the element of the instance of #$AspatialInformationStore <code>ONTOLOGY</code> designated uniquely by the constant-name <code>NAME</code>.")
(comment EukaryoticCellCycle "The collection of all single iterations through #$TheCellCycle for eukaryotic cells.  Each instance consists of interphase (see #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle), which starts at the moment the cell appears and is largely period of growth and preparation for division, and the M phase (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle), during which the cell undergoes #$Mitosis and #$Cytokinesis.  For the collection of all iterations through (along a single path) events of this type (i.e., the eukaryotic cell cycle <i>as a cycle</i>, see #$TheEukaryoticCellCycle.")
(comment ConceptOfExternalOntologyWithNameFn "The function that corresponds to the predicate #$conceptOfExternalOntologyWithName, <code>(#$ConceptOfExternalOntologyWithNameFn ONTOLOGY NAME)</code> denotes the object <code>THING</code> that is designated by the constant-name <code>NAME</code> in the the instance of #$AspatialInformationStore <code>ONTOLOGY</code>.")
(comment Crista "The collection of cristae, room-like cavities inside the mitochondria (see #$Mitochondrion) formed by the mitochondrial inner and outer membranes.  The cristae are required for cellular respiration.")
(comment CentralVacuole "A specialization of #$Vacuole.  The majority of mature #$BotanicalCells have one large central vacuole.  This structure generally occupies nearly one third of the plant cell's volume.")
(comment DynamicEquilibrium "#$DynamicEquilibrium is a collection of events whose focal characteristic is an equilibrium in some measurable quantity (such as the temperature of the body, the amount of calcium in the bloodstream, or the fraction of poolgoers who are actually in the water), the value of which can be stated using some #$QuantitySlot.  The predicate #$equilibriumTypeWRTSlot relates a type of equilibrium to the #$QuantitySlot giving the value of the quantity in equilibrium.  Given an instance DYN of #$DynamicEquilibrium, the value of this slot S may remain unchanged or may shift, but the important characteristic of dynamic equilibria is that each has sub-events which oppose each other: one set of sub-events acts to increase the value of S and one set acts to decrease it.  Any instance DYN of #$DynamicEquilibrium has at least two cotemporal sub-events (see #$cotemporalProperSubEvents), one of which is an instance of INC and the other an instance of DEC, where INC is a class of increases in S (see #$IncreaseEvent) and DEC is a class of decreases in S (see #$DecreaseEvent).")
(comment equilibriumTypeWRTSlot "(#$equilibriumTypeWRTSlot EQUIL-TYPE QUANT-SLOT) means that EQUIL-TYPE is a collection of #$Equilibrium events which concern the value of QUANT-SLOT.")
(comment objectOfEquilibrium "(#$objectOfEquilibrium EQUIL THING) means that in the instance of #$Equilibrium, EQUIL, the quantity in equilibrium is a property of THING.")
(comment equilibriumWRTSlot "(#$equilibriumWRTSlot EQUIL QUANT-SLOT) means that EQUIL is an instance of #$Equilibrium with respect to the quantity whose value is given by QUANT-SLOT.")
(comment increaseSubEventType "(#$increaseSubEventType EQUIL-TYPE INC-TYPE) means that all of the #$increaseSubEvents of any instance of the #$DynamicEquilibrium type EQUIL-TYPE are of type INC-TYPE.  Furthermore, such an instance of INC-TYPE does exist.")
(comment decreaseSubEventType "(#$decreaseSubEventType EQUIL-TYPE DEC-TYPE) means that all of the #$decreaseSubEvents of any instance of the #$DynamicEquilibrium type EQUIL-TYPE are of type DEC-TYPE.  Furthermore, such an instance of DEC-TYPE does exist.")
(comment increaseSubEvents "(#$increaseSubEvents EQUIL INC) means that INC is one of the cotemporal sub-events (see #$cotemporalSubEvents) of the #$DynamicEquilibrium event, EQUIL, that is acting to increase the value of the quantity that EQUIL is an euilibrium with respect to (see #$equilibriumWRTSlot).")
(comment decreaseSubEvents "(#$decreaseSubEvents EQUIL DEC) means that DEC is one of the cotemporal sub-events (see #$cotemporalSubEvents) of the #$DynamicEquilibrium event, EQUIL, that is acting to decrease the value of the quantity that EQUIL is an euilibrium with respect to (see #$equilibriumWRTSlot).")
(comment BCopyFn "#$BCopyFn copies the number of bytes specified by the third argument position from the memory location specified by the first argument position to the memory location specified by the second argument position.")
(comment LoadModuleFn "#$LoadModuleFn loads and executes an application or creates a new instance of an existing application.  The first argument takes the file name of thhe application to be run.  The second argument takes a pointer to an application-defined LOADPARMS32 structure that defines the new application's parameter block.  If the function succeeds, it returns a numeric value greater than 31, otherwise, one of four possible values will be returned: each denotes a different error state.")
(comment GetProcAddressFn "#$GetProcAddressFn retrieves the address of an exported function or variable from the specified dynamic-link library.   The first argument takes a handle to the dynamic link library module that contains the function or variable in question, and the second argument takes the function or variable name or the function's ordinal value.  The function returns the address of the exported function or variable.")
(comment deprecatedWithRespectToCompendium "(#$deprecatedWithRespectToCompendium FN LIB) means that the #$CodingFunction FN is considered deprecated with respect to the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIB within the context of the assertion.")
(comment deprecatedWithRespectToCompendiumAsOf "(#$deprecatedWithRespectToCompendiumAsOf FN LIB DATE) means that, as of DATE (inclusive) the #$CodingFunction FN is considered deprecated with respect to the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIB.")
(comment Microvillus "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$Microvillus is a small protusion from the plasma membrane of a cell.")
(comment Cilium "A specialization of #$CellPart.  Each instance of #$Cilium is a small appendage that a cell can use (usually in concert with many other cilia) to move about.")
(comment Lipase "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Lipases are enzymes involved in the digestion of lipids.")
(comment LingualLipase "A specialization of #$Lipase.  Lingual lipases is secreted by gland on the surface of the tongue.")
(comment CeruminousGland "The collection of all ceruminous #$Glands.  Each instance of this collection is a gland in the ear that secretes ear wax.")
(comment EarWax "A specialization of #$Secretion-Bodily.  Earwax is a substance secreted by  ceruminous glands in the ear.")
(comment VonEbnersGland "A collection of #$Glands.  Von Ebner's glands produce lingual lipase.")
(comment ActiveTransport-Membrane "The collection of processes in which a substance is moved across a biological membrane against its concentration gradient.  This requires either chemical energy (see #$ActiveTransport-Primary) or an electrochemical gradient (see #$ActiveTransport-Secondary).")
(disjointWith PassiveTransport-Membrane ActiveTransport-Membrane)
(comment ActiveTransport-Primary "The collection of processes in which a substance is moved across a biological membrane against its concentration gradient.  In this form of active transport (see the generalization, #$ActiveTransport-Membrane), chemical energy such as that provided by ATP (see #$AdenosineTriphosphate) is directly used to move a substance from the low-concentration side of a membrane to the high-concentration side.")
(comment ActiveTransport-Secondary "The collection of processes in which a substance is moved across a biological membrane against its concentration gradient.  In this form of active transport (see the generalization, #$ActiveTransport-Membrane), energy to support the movement comes from a membrane potential difference created by active transport of ions, rather than a direct use of chemical energy.")
(disjointWith ActiveTransport-Secondary ActiveTransport-Primary)
(comment WhiteAdiposeTissue "A specialization of #$FattyTissue.  White adipose tissue consists of cells that store fat.")
(comment WhiteFatCell "A specialization of #$Adipocyte.  White fat cells constitute white adipose tissue (WAT).  White fat cells contain a single large droplet of fat.")
(comment BrownFatCell "A specialization of #$Adipocyte.  Brown fat cells constitute brown adipose tissue (BAT).  Brown fat cells contain multiple droplets of fat.")
(comment ChromosomeSegment "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$ChromosomeSegment is a contiguous portion of a chromatin strand.  Chromosome segments are exchanged by chromosomes during #$CrossingOver-Chromosomal.")
(comment BrownAdiposeTissue "A specialization of #$FattyTissue.  Brown adipose tissue consists of cells that store multiple droplets of fat.")
(comment RecombinantChromosome "A specialization of $EukaryoticChromosome.  Each instance of #$RecombinantChromosome is a chromosome that has swapped #$ChromosomeSegments during the crossing over that occurs as part of synapsis.")
(comment CodingFunctionParameterRolePredicate "The collection of all #$BinaryPredicates used for specifying the role that a value assigned to a particular argument position on a particular coding function plays in normal-runtime executions of function calls that call the function in question.")
(comment handleSpecifyingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$CodingFunction, (#$handleSpecifyingArgumentPosition FN N) means that the Nth argument of FN takes as its vaule a number that functions as a particular kind of smart pointer.  Instead of containing the address of the item to which it refers, a handle contains an indexical reference that is evaluated by a separate system.  This extra layer of indirection allows the referent to be relocated in memory by other operations without invalidating the handle, something which is impossible to do with direct pointers.")
(comment InterProcessSignalAdministration "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein an asynchronous notification sent from one process to another is intercepted by a call to a #$SignalHandlingFunction resulting in modification of the targeted process.")
(comment SignalHandlingFunction "An collection instance of #$CodingFunctionTypeByOperationType. Each instance is a #$CodingFunction which is engineered so as to temporarily halt or modify one computer process as the result of receiving a signal from another computer process.")
(comment DataLocationCorruption "The collection of all #$ComputerDataAlterations wherein the alteration is undesirable within the context of the stated purpose of the program being executed, i.e., where a data location acquires a value that either makes it impossible for a certain ProgramAction that is targeted for that location to achieve its purpose, or that enables an unforeseen and problematic state of affairs to be achieved by a ProgramAction using that data location.")
(comment ReentrantCodingFunction "The collection of all functions such that the function can, under ordinary circumstances, be called, interrupted, and recalled without risk of a #$DataLocationCorruption involving a local resource.")
(comment ConvergenceEvent "A specialization of #$Translation-MultiTrajectory.  Each instance of #$ConvergenceEvent is an event in which objects move to a common destination.  The objects coming together can be more or less distinct.  An example with distinct converging objects is a process involving pilgrims converging on Mecca.  An example with less obviously distinct converging objects is the wadding up of a piece of paper (in this case, the moving objects are regions of the piece of paper that get closer to one another via crumpling).")
(disjointWith ReentrantCodingFunction NonReentrantCodingFunction)
(comment NonReentrantCodingFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions which are not #$ReentrantCodingFunctions, i.e., functions whose calls cannot readily be interrupted in execution and restarted without incurring risk of #$DataLocationCorruption.")
(comment ProgramActionOfTypeDueToCallToFunctionOfTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to refer to classes of #$ProgramAction as faceted by the type of #$CodingFunction call that triggers them.  Where PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE is a class of #$ProgramAction and FN-TYPE is a sub-class of #$CodingFunction, (#$ProgramActionOfTypeDueToCallToFunctionOfTypeFn PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE FN-TYPE) denotes the subclass of instances of PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE that are caused by executions of function calls where the #$CodingFunction called (the #$codingFunctionInvoked) is an instance of FN-TYPE.")
(comment programActionOfTypeDueToCallToFunctionOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ProgramActionOfTypeDueToCallToFunctionOfTypeFn.  Where PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE is a class of #$ProgramAction and FN-TYPE is a sub-class of #$CodingFunction, (#$programActionOfTypeDueToCallToFunctionOfType PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE FN-TYPE PROGRAM-ACTION-SUBTYPE) means that PROGRAM-ACTION-SUBTYPE is the subclass of instances of PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE that are caused by executions of function calls where the #$CodingFunction called (the #$codingFunctionInvoked) is an instance of FN-TYPE.")
(disjointWith MembraneBoundRibosome FreeRibosome)
(comment Collision "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation and #$Translation-LocationChange.  Each instance of #$Collision is an event in which two or more #$PartiallyTangibles bump into each other.  Each instance of #$Collision is immediately preceded by an #$Approaching, during which at least one of the #$objectsInContact during the #$Collision is moving toward the location at which the collision takes place.  (Some of the objects in contact during the colliding may already be occupying that location immediately before contact.)  The #$Collision begins once the objects begin to be in contact, and ends once they are no longer in contact (think of two billiard balls bouncing off each other), <i>or</i> when the objects have come to rest in a stable contact position (think of an asteroid smashing into the earth and coming to rest at the bottom of the crater it has created).")
(comment libraryIncludesFunction "Where FN is a #$StandardLibraryFunction, (#$libraryIncludesFunction LIB FN) means the FN is included in LIB.")
(comment StrTokFn "#$StrTokFn parses a string (specified by the first argument) into a sequence of tokens (based on a template specified by the second argument).  Each call to #$StrTokFn returns a pointer to a null-terminated string containing the next token, minus the delimiting character.  If no more tokens are found, the function returns NULL.")
(comment StrTok-RFn "#$StrTok-RFn parses a string (specified by the first argument) into a sequence of tokens (based on a template specified by the second argument) while maintaining context through successive calls via a pointer to a char variable (specified by the third argument).  Each call to #$StrTok-RFn returns a pointer to a null-terminated string containing the next token, minus the delimiting character.  If no more tokens are found, the function returns NULL.")
(comment CodeAnalysisConstant "The collection of all constants that are highly salient for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment pointerSpecifyingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$CodingFunction, (#$pointerSpecifyingArgumentPosition FN N) means that FN takes as its nth argument a value that directly or indirectly references another #$ComputerDataStorageLocation via its #$computerDataLocationDesignator.")
(comment ReadDirFn "#$ReadDirFn takes a pointer to a directory stream as its arg1 value and returns a pointer to a dirent structure representing the next entry in the stream pointed to.")
(comment Stroma "The connective and otherwise relatively non-functional  framework of a #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(comment Carotene "Carotene is an #$OrganicMaterial synthesized by plants that has a red-orange or yellow hue.")
(comment PhotosyntheticPigment "A specialization of #$Pigment.  Every photosynthetic pigment is a pigment used by a biological living object to capture light energy to be used in photosynthesis.")
(comment Bacteriochlorophyll "Bacteriochlorophyll is a photosynthetic pigment synthesized by bacteria.")
(comment ASCTimeFn "#$ASCTimeFn takes an argument representing 'broken-down time' (a calendrical count broken down into seconds, minutes, days, months, years, etc.) and returns a #$CharacterString in a standard, date-denoting format.")
(comment ASCTime-RFn "#$ASCTime-RFn takes an argument representing 'broken-down time' (a calendrical count broken down into seconds, minutes, days, months, years, etc.) and a pointer to a buffer where the result is to be written, and returns a #$CharacterString in a standard, date-denoting format.")
(comment firstSubEventTypeWithRolePlayerOfType "(#$firstSubEventTypeWithRolePlayerOfType PROCESS STEP ROLE TYPE) means that STEP is the first proper sub-event type of PROCESS during instances of which it is typical for some instance of TYPE to play the role ROLE.")
(comment MembraneTransport-Filtration "The collection of processes in which a substance moves across a biological membrane, through pores in the membrane, due to hydrostatic pressure differences on either side of the membrane.  Pore size determines an upper limit on the size of molecules able to pass.")
(comment CalciumAbsorptionInIntestine "Instances are processes in which masses of #$CalciumIons pass from the interior of the #$AlimentaryCanal into the #$Bloodstream of a single #$Mammal.  Throughout the large and small intestine, passive transport of calcium ions does occur; active transport of dietary calcium occurs primarily in the #$Duodenum.")
(comment CalciumExitInInitialFiltrate "Instances are processes in which masses of #$CalciumIons pass from the #$Bloodstream into the #$Nephrons of the #$Kidneys of a single #$Mammal.  Calcium ions are carried along with water and other small molecules that leave the bloodstream by filtration (see #$MembraneTransport-Filtration).  As urine is processed before it leaves the kidney, much of the calcium is reabsorbed (see #$CalciumReabsorptionDuringUrineProduction).")
(comment CalciumReabsorptionDuringUrineProduction "Instances are processes in which masses of #$CalciumIons pass from the tubule of a #$Nephron back into the #$Bloodstream.  In some parts of the tubule, transport is active, but in others movement proceeds by passive transport.")
(comment FiltrationAtRenalCorpuscle "Instances are processes in which water and small molecules pass from the #$Bloodstream into the #$BowmansCapsule of a #$Nephron.  It is the first step in the production of #$Urine (see #$UrineProduction-Mammalian).  The initial filtrate generated in this way is quite dilute and contains substances that need to stay in the body, as well as substances that should be excreted.  Subsequent steps in urine production involve the reabsorption of most of the water, selective reabsorption of certain substances to be retained, active secretion of certain substances into the urine that is forming, and finally the exit of the urine from the #$Kidney.")
(comment UrineProduction-Mammalian "Instances are processes in which an animal's #$Kidneys selectively remove substances from the #$Bloodstream.  Taken together, the substances form a liquid called #$Urine.  After urine is produced by the kidneys, it is held in the bladder (see #$Bladder-Urinary) until it is released during #$Urinating.")
(comment CTimeFn "#$CTimeFn takes an #$Integer as its argument, interpreting this as number of seconds elapsed from a starting time of 00:00:00 on January 1, 1970.  It returns a #$CharacterString that represents the indicated date in a standard date-denoting format.")
(comment CTime-RFn "#$CTimeFn takes an #$Integer as its first argument, interpreting this as number of seconds elapsed from a starting time of 00:00:00 on January 1, 1970. As its second argument, it takes a pointer to a buffer where the result is to be written out. It returns a #$CharacterString that represents the indicated date in a standard date-denoting format.")
(comment relationAllExistsExistsExists "A #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to four collections and a further two binary predicates. <code>(#$relationAllExistsExistsExists BINPRED1 BINPRED2 BINPRED3 COL DEP-COL1 DEP-COL2 DEP-COL3)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST</code> of <code>COL</code>, there exists some instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>DEP-COL1</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST INST1)</code> holds, and there exists some <code>INST2</code> of <code>DEP-COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED2 INST1 INST2)</code> holds, and there exists some instance <code>INST3</code> of <code>DEP-COL3</code> such that <code>(BINPRED3 INST2 INST3)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$implies
    (#$isa ?INST COL)
    (#$thereExists ?INST1
      (#$thereExists ?INST2
      (#$and
        (#$isa ?INST1 DEP-COL1)
        (BINPRED1 ?INST ?INST1)
        (#$isa ?INST2 DEP-COL2)
        (BINPRED2 ?INST1 ?INST2)
        (#$isa ?INST3 DEP-COL3)
        (BINPRED2 ?INST2 ?INST3)))).
</pre>")
(comment relationAllExistsExists "A quintary #$RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relation to three collections and a further binary predicate. <code>(#$relationAllExistsExists BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL DEP-COL1 DEP-COL2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INST</code> of <code>COL</code>, there exists some instance <code>INST1</code> of <code>DEP-COL1</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST INST1)</code> holds, and there exists some <code>INST2</code> of <code>DEP-COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED2 INST1 INST2)</code> holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$implies
    (#$isa ?INST COL)
    (#$thereExists ?INST1
      (#$thereExists ?INST2
      (#$and
        (#$isa ?INST1 DEP-COL1)
        (BINPRED1 ?INST ?INST1)
        (#$isa ?INST2 DEP-COL2)
        (BINPRED2 ?INST1 ?INST2)))).
</pre>")
(comment GMTimeFn "#$GMTimeFn takes an #$Integer as its argument, which it interprets as the number of seconds elapsed from a starting point of 00:00:00 January 1, 1970.  It converts this date into Greenwich Mean Time and returns a character string denoting it, in standard date-denoting format.")
(comment GMTime-RFn "#$GMTime-RFn takes an #$Integer as its first argument, which it interprets as the number of seconds elapsed from a starting point of 00:00:00 January 1, 1970. As its second argument, it takes a pointer to a buffer where its result will be written.  It converts the date supplied via the first argument into Greenwich Mean Time and returns a character string denoting it, in standard date-denoting format.")
(comment RandFn "#$RandFn returns a pseudo-random integer between 0 and RAND_MAX.")
(comment Rand-RFn "#$Rand-RFn returns a pseudo-random integer between 0 and RAND_MAX.")
(comment chapterOfWork-Ordinal "(#$chapterOfWork-Ordinal CHAP WORK N) means that CHAP is the Nth chapter of the #$TextualPCW, WORK.")
(comment Alpha2-HS-GlycoproteinMolecule "A specialization of #$GlycoproteinMolecule.  A human protein found in blood serum and also in other tissues.")
(comment GlycosaminoglycanMolecule "This is the collection of chemical objects which are polysaccharides consisting of repeating disaccharide units.  The polysaccharide chain is unbranched, and the repeating units are formed of two 6 carbon sugars, one of which contains nitrogen.")
(comment ProteoglycanMolecule "A specialization of #$GlycoproteinMolecule.  Proteoglycans are a type of glycoprotein which is covalently bound to many #$GlycosaminoglycanMolecules.")
(comment LoadingAComputerFile "The collection of all #$ComputerDataTransfers wherein the #$infoTransferred is a #$ComputerFile-AIS and one of the objects acted on is a #$ComputerFileCopy.")
(comment fileReadFromDenotingArgumentPosition "Where FN is a #$FileLoadingFunction, (#$fileReadFromDenotingArgumentPosition FN N) means that the Nth argument supplied to FN is a term which denotes the #$ComputerFileCopy that execution of a call to FN will copy, and, indirectly, the #$ComputerFile-AIS that is the #$infoTransferred in the execution.")
(comment ExecutableComputerFile-AIS "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerFile-AIS that are #$ComputerCode that includes one or more instances of #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable.")
(comment ExecutableComputerFileCopy "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerFileCopy which instantiate (see #$completeAISOfIBT) instances of #$ExecutableComputerFile-AIS.")
(comment CodeInjection "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein data is transferred from a location that is not explicitly specified as an address in the program being executed.")
(comment DeleteriousCodeInjection "The collection of all #$CodeInjections where the unspecified data that is introduced by the program execution has the potential to generate an undesirable effect on being executed in turn, in terms of compromising the intended functionality of the program.  At best a #$DeleteriousCodeInjection may involve an unintended introduction of code that cuases the program to yield incorrect results, go into an infinite loop, or halt with an error condition.  At worst, it may allow an unauthorized person or application to take control of the machine state and either read from or write to an unauthorized location (or both).")
(comment FileLoadingFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions whose executions constitute #$ComputerDataTransfers where the #$infoTransferred is a #$ComputerFile-AIS that is copied from one explicitly or implicitly specified #$ComputerDataStorageLocation to another explicitly or implicitly specified #$ComputerDataStorageLocation.")
(comment FarmedFn "<code>(#$FarmedFn ANIMAL-TYPE)</code> returns the collection of instances of <code>ANIMAL-TYPE</code> that are farmed (i.e., domesticated for use of their meat, skins, or other products).  As such, <code>(#$FarmedFn ANIMAL-TYPE)</code> denotes the intersection of <code>ANIMAL-TYPE</code> and #$Livestock.")
(comment farmedAnimalType "The predicate that corresponds to #$FarmedFn, <code>(#$farmedAnimalType FARMED-SPECIALIZATION ANIMAL-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>FARMED-SPECIALIZATION</code> as the intersection of <code>ANIMAL-TYPE</code> and #$Livestock.")
(comment SigActionStructure "An abstract #$ComputerCodeExpression used in C for specifying how a psrticular #$SignalHandlingFunction should behave.")
(comment CardiovascularCirculation "A specialization of (#$CirculationFn #$Blood).  Each instance of #$CardiovascularCirculation is an event in which blood circulates within the heart, veins or arteries of an organism.")
(comment PulmonaryCirculation "A specialization of (#$CirculationFn #$Blood).  Each instance of #$PulmonaryCirculation is the part of #$CardiovascularCirculation is an event in which oxygen-depleted blood is carried from the hear to the lungs (where it is oxygenated), and then back to the heart.")
(comment SystemicCirculation "A specialization of (#$CirculationFn #$Blood).  Each instance of #$SystemicCirculation is the part of #$CardiovascularCirculation is an event in which oxygenated blood is carried from the heart to the body, and then back to the heart.")
(comment CodeAnalysisTest-FullySpecified "Each instance of #$CodeAnalysisTest-FullySpecified is a fully specified CycL query with expected results that is used in tracking performance for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment QuotedFormulaArityFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to a #$CycLFormula FORM, #$QuotedFormulaArityFn returns the number of arguments given to the relation (an instance of #$Relation (q.v.)) appearing in the initial (\"arg0\") argument place of FORM.")
(comment quotedFormulaArity "(#$quotedFormulaArity FORMULA INTEGER) means that the CycL formula FORMULA contains INTEGER arguments. See also #$QuotedFormulaArityFn and #$formulaArity.")
(comment Osteoid "Instances of #$Osteoid are non-mineral portions of the extracellular matrix of #$BoneTheStuff.  In the bone formation step of bone remodeling, #$Osteoid is secreted by #$Osteoblasts, and then is subsequently mineralized by the deposition of #$BoneMineral to form the mature extracellular matrix.")
(disjointWith PulmonaryCirculation SystemicCirculation)
(comment firstSubEventTypeOfType "(#$firstSubEventTypeOfType PROCESS EVENT-TYPE STEP) means that STEP is the first proper sub-event type of PROCESS that is a specialization of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment suggestedQueryMt "(#$suggestedQueryMt THING MT) means it is suggested that queries that are in some salient sense \"about\" THING should be asked in MT.")
(comment BiochemicalSynthesisFn "(#$BiochemicalSynthesisFn MOL-TYPE) denotes the spec of #$BiochemicalSynthesis during which instances of MOL-TYPE, a spec of
#$Molecule are being synthesized by a living organism or one of its parts. Note that this function takes a collection of molecules.  Given the current representation of chemical compounds in Cyc, one may want to use #$MoleculeFn to specify the appropriate argument when only the corresponding spec of #$MolecularStuff is reified.")
(comment Amyloplast "A specialization of #$Leucoplast.  Amyloplasts are leucoplasts specialized for storing starch.")
(comment Elaioplast "A specialization of #$Leucoplast.  Elaioplasts are leucoplasts specialized for storing lipids.")
(comment Proteinoplast "A specialization of #$Leucoplast.   Proteinoplasts are leucoplasts specialized for storing starchprotein.")
(disjointWith Amyloplast Elaioplast)
(disjointWith Proteinoplast Elaioplast)
(disjointWith Amyloplast Proteinoplast)
(comment resultServesAsPointer "(#$resultServesAsPointer FN) means that the numeric result
returned by the #$CodingFunction FN either directly or indirectly
references a #$ComputerDataStorageLocation.")
(comment resultServesAsHandle "(#$resultServesAsHandle FN) means that the numeric result
returned by the #$CodingFunction FN serves as an indexical referent
for a contextually determined #$ComputerDataStorageLocation.")
(comment resultIsBooleanSuccessIndicator "A unary predicate used to mark #$CodingFunction instances.  Where FN is a #$CodingFunction such that (#$codingFunctionOperationTypes FN OP-TYPE), (#$resultIsBooleanSuccessIndicator FN) means that, where FN-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable wherein the #$codingFunctionInvoked is FN, and EXECUTION is a #$ProgramAction where the #$codeExecuted is FN-CALL, the numeric value returned by EXECUTION (valueReturnedByProgramAction) indicates whether EXECUTION is in fact an instance of OP-TYPE, or is merely a failed attempt at such.")
(comment FunctionReturningBooleanSuccessCriterion "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions such that executions of their function calls return values which indicate whether or not the execution succeeded in carrying out the targeted operation type of the function (the #$codingFunctionOperationTypes).")
(comment resultValueDenotesSuccess "Where BOOL is a #$FunctionReturningBooleanSuccessCriterion, (#$resultValueDenotesSuccess BOOL N) means that when an execution of a call to BOOL returns the value N, the execution succeeded at implementing the targeted operation type (#$codingFunctionOperationTypes) for the input values provided to the function in the execution.")
(comment resultValueInRangeDenotesFailure "Where BOOL is a #$FunctionReturningBooleanSuccessCriterion, (#$resultValueInRangeDenotesSuccess BOOL NUMBER-COL) means that when an execution of a call to BOOL returns a numeric value that is an instance of NUMBER-COL, the execution failed at implementing the targeted operation type (#$codingFunctionOperationTypes) for the input values provided to the function in the execution.")
(comment pathNameDenotingArgumentPosition "(#$pathNameDenotingArgumentPosition FN N) means that the Nth argument supplied to FN functions as a path name to a computer file.")
(comment valueReturnedByProgramAction "(#$valueReturnedByProgramAction EXECUTION N) means that the
numeric value N is registered as a direct result of EXECUTION.")
(comment RuBisCO "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  RuBisCO is the most abundant protein in chloroplasts.  It is critically important to life on earth because it catalyzes the carbon fixation step of the Calvin cycle.")
(comment Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate "A kind of #$Ester, G3P is a product of the #$CalvinCycle.")
(comment CalvinCycle "An instance of #$CyclicalProcessType and a specialization of #$BiologicalProductionEvent and #$BiologicalDestructionEvent.  Each instance of #$CalvinCycle consists of a sequence of chemical reactions that uses ATP and NADPH to convert CO2 to G3P.")
(comment prettyString "(#$prettyString TERM STRING) means that STRING is a natural language word or expression (sequence of words) commonly used to refer to TERM.  The predicate #$prettyString is used by the code which generates CycL to NL paraphrases, but its applicability is not restricted to this use.")
(comment prettyString-Canonical "(#$prettyString-Canonical TERM STRING) means that STRING is the natural-language word or expression to use preferentially to refer to TERM.")
(comment Parenchyma "A specialization of #$PlantTissue-Ground. Parenchyma is notably the most versatile ground tissue.")
(comment Collenchyma "A specialization of #$PlantTissue-Ground.")
(comment Sclerenchyma "A specialization of #$PlantTissue-Ground.")
(comment Mesophyll "A specialization of #$Parenchyma.  Mesophyll tissue is found in the interior of plant leaves, and is the primary location of photosynthesis.")
(comment testQuestionReasonsAboutCWE "(#$testQuestionReasonsAboutCWE TQ CWE) means that answering TQ entails performing reasoning that is critical to recognizing that a piece of code belongs to CWE (has the deficiency that CWE identifies), or that is critical to establishing a workaround for code that belongs to the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CWE.")
(comment testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesCWEAsDeficiency "(#$testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesCWEAsDeficiency TQ CWE) means that TQ performs reasoning critical to establishing that some range of coding use cases have the vulnerability characterized by the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CWE.")
(comment testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesSourceOfCWE "(#$testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesSourceOfCWE TQ CWE) means that TQ performs reasoning that identifies component code that is responsible for a particular piece of code's exhibiting the vulnerability associated with the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CWE.")
(comment testQuestionReasonsAboutRunningCodeWithCWE "(#$testQuestionReasonsAboutRunningCodeWithCWE TQ CWE) reasons about executing code that exhibits the vulnerability associated with CWE.")
(comment testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesWorkaroundForCWE "(#$testQuestionAnswerIdentifiesWorkaroundForCWE TQ CWE) means that the reasoning involved in answering TQ identifies a workaround for the vulnerability associated with the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CWE for some class of use cases.")
(comment CodeAnalysisTermTrackingTest-FullySpecified "Each instance of #$CodeAnalysisTermTrackingTest-FullySpecified is a fully specified CycL query that is used in tracking vocabulary created for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment uRLReferenceForMitreCWE "(#$uRLReferenceForMitreCWE CWE URL) means that an on-line description of the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CWE is found at URL")
(comment BoneRemodeling "In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  At multiple sites throughout the #$SkeletalSystem, specialized cells called #$Osteoclasts dissolve small regions of the extracellular matrix of bone (see #$BoneResorption).  In areas where bone has been resorbed, other cells called #$Osteoblasts secrete #$Osteoid in the gaps left. This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.")
(comment BoneRemodeling-WholeBody "Instances are the spatial sum of all #$BoneRemodeling events occuring within a single organism's body, for the duration of the instance.")
(comment BoneResorption-WholeBody "Instances are the spatial sum of all #$BoneResorption events occuring within a single organism's body, for the duration of the instance.")
(comment BoneResorption "In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  #$BoneResorption is one part of this process, in which a small piece of the extracellular matrix of bone is dissolved.  This is typically done by #$Osteoclasts. In an area where bone has been resorbed, some time later (how long depends on the species) #$Osteoid will be laid down by #$Osteoblasts.  This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.")
(comment OsteoidSecretion-WholeBody "Instances are the spatial sum of all events in which #$Osteoblasts secrete #$Osteoid occuring within a single organism's body, for the duration of the instance.")
(comment BoneFormationInRemodeling "In the vertebrate skeleton, bones are constantly being remodeled.  #$BoneFormationInRemodeling is one part of this process, which occurs in an area where bone had previously been resorbed (See #$BoneResorption).  Bone formation is iniiated by #$Osteoblasts which lay down #$Osteoid (unmineralized bone matrix) in the areas which will receive the new bone.  This will become mineralized, forming new bone to replace what was removed.")
(comment BoneFormationInRemodeling-WholeBody "Instances are the spatial sum of all events in which bone (see #$BoneTheStuff) is formed in the course of #$BoneRemodeling, for the duration of the instance.")
(comment Biomineralization "Instances are process in which the tissues of living things form mineral (thus crystalline) solids.  #$Biomineralization can be a natural and beneficial process, because hard solids can protect the organism (as in the shells of #$Mollusks or of #$CoralPolyps) or give it shape and support its tissues (as in the #$SkeletalSystems of #$Vertebrates).  Mineral solids can also form as a result of disease processes, such as with #$KidneyStones.")
(comment BoneMineralization "Mineralization is the last step in the creation of bone extracellular matrix and it invovles the formation of hydroxyapatite nanocrsytals (see #$BoneMineral) within a collagenous framework.  During growth of vertebrates, the flat bones of the skull, mandibles, maxillae and clavicles are shaped first in non-cartilaginous connective tissue, while long bones are originally ''modeled'' in cartilage (see #$Cartilage).  Parts of bones which have already become mineralized are immediately subject to #$BoneRemodeling, in which old bone is dissolved and new bone is deposited.  During remodeling, collagenous #$Osteoid is deposited, which subsequently becomes hardened during #$BoneMineralization, thus completing the creation of new bone extracelllar matrix.")
(comment BoneMineralizationInRemodeling "Instances are events in which hydroxyapatite crystals (See #$BoneMineral) form within #$Osteoid previously laid down on the course of #$BoneRemodeling.")
(comment RecombinantMicroorganism "A kind of abnormal organism.  Each instance of #$RecombinantMicroorganism is a microorganism whose DNA has been artificially manipulated.")
(comment ReadFileFn "#$ReadFileFn reads data from the file or input/output device at the position specified by the file pointer if supported by the device. The first argument specifies a handle to the device being read from (the parameter must have been created with read access)  The second argument gives a pointer to the buffer that receives the data read.  The third argument specifies the maximum number of bytes to be read.  The fourth, optional argument gives a pointer to the variable that receives the number of bytes read when using a parameter that is synchronous with the arg1 position.  The fifth, optioonal argument gives a pointer to a valid and unique Overlapped structure.")
(comment NonZeroInteger "A specialization of #$Integer and the binary union of #$PositiveInteger and #$NegativeInteger.  It is #$disjointWith the singleton set of 0.")
(comment AggrecanMolecule "Instances are large proteoglycans (see #$ProteoglycanMolecule) consisting of a protein backbone with multiple chondroitin sulfate side chains (see #$ChondroitinSulfateChain).  It is a structural component of #$Cartilage.")
(comment numberAsCodingFnParameterDenotes "(#$numberAsCodingFnParameterDenotes N FN PARAM-NUM DENOTATUM) means that when the number N is assigned as the value of parameter number PARAM-NUM to FN in a function call, it denotes DENOTATUM in the context of the function call.")
(comment FileLoadingConstant "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeConstants used in conjuction with #$FileLoadingFunctions.")
(comment numberAsCodingFnResultDenotes "(#$numberAsCodingFnResultDenotes N FN THING) means that when the number N is returned as the result of executing a function call to FN, it denotes THING in the context of the execution.")
(comment IntramembranousBoneFormation "Instances are events in which bone (see #$BoneTheStuff) is formed without the prior presence of #$Cartilage.  This happens during embryonic and juvenile growth of a #$Vertebrate, for the production of the flat bones of the skeleton such as those of the skull, mandibles, etc. (see #$FlatBone), and is contrasted with #$EndochondralBoneFormation, which is the way the long bones of the skeleton (see #$LongBone) are formed.")
(comment MultipassTransmembraneProtein "A subcollection of #$TransmembraneProtein.  Multipass transmembrane proteins are proteins that are embedded in a biological membrane, and have multiple alternating hypdrophylic and hydrophobic segments along their sequence, so that the protein chain passes several times back and forth through the membrane.")
(comment SinglePassTransmembraneProtein "A subcollection of #$TransmembraneProtein.  Single pass transmembrane proteins are proteins that are embedded in a biological membrane.  They have two hydrophilic ends and a hydrophobic center,  so that they pass through the membrane once.")
(disjointWith SinglePassTransmembraneProtein MultipassTransmembraneProtein)
(comment ProteinPatchedHomolog1 "A #$MultipassTransmembraneProtein and #$MembraneReceptorMolecule which negatively regulates signaling by the Hedgehog family of proteins. It is thus involved in the patterning of developing embryos of verterates and insects.")
(comment HedgehogSignalingProteinMolecule "The Hedgehog family of proteins are cell signaling molecules involved in regulating morphogenesis in embryos, and regulate various cellular differentiation processes in adults.  They were named because fruit fly embryos lacking a functional copy of the gene producing the protein were stubby and covered with pointy projections, like a hedgehog.")
(comment SonicHedgehog-SignalingProtein "The Hedgehog family of proteins are cell signaling molecules involved in regulating morphogenesis in embryos, and regulate various cellular differentiation processes in adults.  \"Sonic Hedgehog\" is one of three homologous proteins found in #$Mammals.")
(comment IndianHedgehog-SignalingProtein "The Hedgehog family of proteins are cell signaling molecules involved in regulating morphogenesis in embryos, and regulate various cellular differentiation processes in adults.  \"Indian Hedgehog\" is one of three homologous proteins found in #$Mammals.")
(comment DesertHedgehog-SignalingProtein "The Hedgehog family of proteins are cell signaling molecules involved in regulating morphogenesis in embryos, and regulate various cellular differentiation processes in adults.  \"Desert Hedgehog\" is one of three homologous proteins found in #$Mammals.")
(comment chemicalObjectInTransport-TypeType "The corresponding predicate of #$MembraneTransportOfTypeFn.  <code>(#$chemicalObjectInTransport-TypeType OBJ-TYPE MEMBRANE-TRANS-TYPE)</code> means that in events that are instances of <code>MEMBRANE-TRANS-TYPE)</code> </code>, instances of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> are transported across a biological membrane.")
(comment SampleComputerDatabaseConcept "The collection of various concepts employed in representing the content of #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment productName-SampleDB "relates a product of some sort, a computer program, file server, etc. to its name as it appears in #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment productDescription-SampleDB "relates a product of some sort, a computer program, file server, etc. to its description as it appears in #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment productManufacturerName-SampleDB "relates a product of some sort, a computer program, file server, etc. to the name of its manufacturer as it appears in #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment SampleOrganization-SampleDB "A representation of a sample organization for use in #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment ComputerMemory-Abstract "The collection of all abstract computer memories associated with #$MachineImplementations.  Each instance is a set of tuples (#$SetOfTypeFn Tuple) whose elements consist in orderings of elements in memory together with indices.  Instances can be parsed into directly addressable sub-locations.")
(comment ComputableArithmeticFunction "The collection of all #$ComputableArithmeticFunctions.  Each instance is a #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars which is computable, in the strict sense that the values of its domain and the values of its range can be represented by machine states and a strictly mechanical process, assimilating to a Turing Machine abstraction, can transform arbitrary domain value representations to the appropriate range value representations.")
(comment UTMFunction "The collection of all computable arithmetic functions that are able to 'simulate' any computable arithmetic function in the strict sense that, if passed an encoding of a computable function f and a putative numeric input to this function i, a value o will be returned that is f(i), i.e., the value f would return on i.")
(comment uTMFunctionImplemented "(#$uTMFunctionImplemented MACHINE-IMP FN) means taht the #$MachineImplementation MACHINE-IMP implements the #$UTMFunction FN.")
(comment uTMFunctionUsedInImplementing "(#$uTMFunctionUsedInImplementing MACHINE-IMPLEMENTATION UTM-FN) means that, where MACHINE-IMPLEMENTATION is an implementation of some Turing-computable function (see #$functionImplemented), there is a wider-scoped #$MachineImplementation which causally subsumes MACHINE-IMPLEMENTATION and which is such that it implements the #$UTMFunction UTM-FN (see #$uTMFunctionImplemented) and uses it to simulate the behavior of the #$functionImplemented by MACHINE-IMPLEMENTATION.")
(comment implementationRunsOnImplementation "An inverse spec-pred of #$properSubEvents and #$causes-EventEvent.  (#$implementationRunsOnImplementation SIMULATION SIMULATING) means that SIMULATING implements an abstract machine that simulates the abstract machine implmented by SIMULATION.  More specifically, the #$uTMFunctionImplemented by SIMULATING is the #$uTMFunctionUsedInImplementing SIMULATION.")
(comment virtualMemoryOfImplementation "(#$virtualMemoryOfImplementation IMPLEMENTATION MEMORY) means that MEMORY is the memory associated with a virtual machine which is being simulated by the abstract machine implemented on IMPLEMENTATION. Specifically, the #$physicalMemoryOfImplementation of the implementation of the simulated machine is considered #$virtualMemoryOfImplementation for the implementation of the machine that is doing the simulating.")
(comment implementationDependsOnImplementation "(implementationDependsOnImplementation DEPENDENT SOURCE) means that the abstract machine implemented by DEPENDENT (#$uTMFunctionImplemented) is either directly simulated by the machine implemented by SOURCE or that it is simulated by a machine whose implementation is dependent on SOURCE.")
(comment implementationDependsOnHardware "(#$implementationDependsOnHardware IMPLEMENTATION HARDWARE) means that HARDWARE is the concrete #$ComputationalSystem that is playing the fundamental instrumental role of implementing IMPLEMENTATION.  This leaves open the possibility that the abstract machine implemented by IMPLEMENTATION is being simulated by an abstract machine in a super-implementation that is also running on HARDWARE.")
(comment implementationRunByHardware "(#$implementationRunByHardware IMPLEMENTATION HARDWARE) means that HARDWARE is the concrete #$ComputationalSystem that is 'directly running' IMPLEMENTATION, insofar as the abstract machine implemented by IMPLEMENTATION cannot meaningfully be said to be simulated by another abstract machine that is implemented by a super-implementation that also runs on HARDWARE.")
(comment ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit "#$ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit is a subset of 
#$ComputerStorageDevice.  Each instance is the complete memory storage unit of a #$Computer or, more generally, a #$ComputationalSystem.  Each #$ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit is composed of an array of indexed numeric storage devices which store #$NonNegativeIntegers as machine states, and is directly associated (via the #$hardwareMemory relation) with exactly one abstract computer memory (#$ComputerMemory-Abstract) consisting in a list or set of tuples wherein the indexed elements are the numbers stored.  Several distinct instances of #$ComputerMemory-Abstract may also be associated with a #$ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit at some remove of indirection, depending on what abstract machines the computer is implementing, and in what order of simulation.")
(comment MachineImplementation "The set of all events consisting in implementation of a computable arithmetic function by a computational hardware architecture.  More specifically, each #$MachineImplementation consists in one or possibly several uses of the aforesaid architecture in which an input token or tokens, interpreted as numbers, are supplied and an output token, also numerically interpreted, is produced.  Use of peripheral devices to convert the primary inputs (user gestures and or machine states) to numeric tokens, and to convert numeric outputs to secondary outputs may also be involved.  Every #$MachineImplementation features at least a #$functionImplemented.  Where this is a #$UTMFunction (in which case there is a #$uTMFunctionImplemented), said #$UTMFunction may be given the enumeration of another #$ComputableArithmeticFunction together with some set of putative inputs for this function, and used to return this function's outputs over this range.  This usage is a #$MachineImplementation in its own right and a #$properSubEvents of the overall #$MachineImplementation of the #$UTMFunction, which is said to be the #$uTMFunctionUsedInImplementing the simulation.  The implementation of the function being simulated is also said to run on the implementation of the function doing the simulating (#$implementationRunsOnImplementation).")
(comment functionImplemented "(#$functionImplemented MACHINE-IMP FN) means that the #$MachineImplementation MACHINE-IMP implements the #$ComputableArithmeticFunction FN.")
(comment hardwareMemory "(#$hardwareMemory STORAGE-UNIT MEMORY) means that MEMORY is the #$ComputerMemory-Abstract associated with the #$ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit STORAGE-UNIT.")
(comment OrgSpecificVersionedProgram-SampleDB "A collection of versioned #$ComputerProgram-CWs that correspond to the versions bought by a particular organization from a unique supplier.")
(comment productHasAssociatedVersion-SampleDB "links a product of some sort, a computer program, file server, etc. to an instance of #$VersionedProgram from which hang further details about that product in the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment versionedProgramHasVersionNumber-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$VersionedProgram to its version number in the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment versionHasSysReqDescription-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$VersionedProgram to its system requirements description in the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment versionHasOSDescription-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$VersionedProgram to its system requirements description in the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase")
(comment StructuredKnowledgeSource-AutoGeneratedSchemas "The subcollection of top level SKSI knowledge sources whose logical and physical schemata are automatically generated by forward rules.")
(comment ProductPricingDataSheet-SampleDB "A subcollection of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of this collection is an abstract specification of pricing details for a particular product at a particular time.")
(comment versionHasPricingDetail-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$VersionedProgram to a data node that specifies details about product pricing")
(comment pricingDetailHasEffectiveDate-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$ProductPricingDataSheet-SampleDB to an \"effective as of\" date.")
(comment pricingDetailSpecifiedPrice-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$ProductPricingDataSheet-SampleDB to a monetary value specified as the cost of the product.")
(comment OrganizationContactDetail-SampleDB "A subcollection of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of this collection is an abstract specification of contact details for a particular organization.")
(comment organizationHasContactDetails-SampleDB "relates an organization to an abstract specification of its contact details in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(comment contactDetailOrganizationName-SampleDB "relates an organization detail to the name of the detailed organization in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(disjointWith MulticellularOrganism Syncytium)
(disjointWith CellPart Syncytium)
(comment Syncytium "The collection of all large, multinuclear, cell-like structures filled with #$Cytoplasm.  A #$Syncytium may be a cell with many nuclei (see #$PolynuclearCell) which forms either by fusion of cells with fewer nuclei or by incomplete #$Cytokinesis, or may be also be structure composed of individual cells with interconnected cytoplasm, such as #$CardiacMuscle tissue.  In the latter, specialized cell to cell junctions allow free exchange of ions and allow the cells to function as one unit.  Note that syncytia may form by the fusion of cells which are genetically different, as occurs in fungi.")
(comment codingFunctionArity "A typed spec-pred of arity, specific to #$CodingFunctions.")
(comment codingFunctionHasParameter "(#$codingFunctionHasParameter FN PARAM) means that PARAM is an argument position on FN.")
(comment standardSpecificationNameForParameter "(#$standardSpecificationNameForParameter PARAM NAME-STRING) means that NAME-STRING is the standard name by which PARAM is referred to in the standard library description of the function which features PARAM as a #$CodingFunctionParameter.")
(comment CodingFunctionParameter "The collection of all argument positions of #$CodingFunctions, regarded as first-order instances of #$ComputerCodeExpression.")
(comment NthParameterOfCodingFunctionFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reference #$CodingFunctionParameters.  (#$NthParameterOfCodingFunctionFn FN N) denotes the #$ComputerCodeExpression that is the Nth argument position of the #$CodingFunction FN.")
(comment nthParameterOfCodingFunction "The corresponding predicate of #$NthParameterOfCodingFunctionFn.  Where FN is a #$CodingFunction and N is a #$PositiveInteger, (#$nthParameterOfCodingFunction FN N PARAM) means that PARAM is the #$ComputerCodeExpression that is the Nth argument position on FN.")
(comment HeterodimericProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$HeterodimerMolecule and #$ProteinMolecule.  A heterodimeric protein is formed from two subunits, each encoded by a different gene.")
(comment HomodimericProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinDimer and #$HomodimerMolecule.  A homodimeric protein is formed from two subunits of the same protein.")
(comment contactDetailOrganizationStreetAddress-SampleDB "relates an organization detail to the #$StreetAddress of the detailed organization in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(comment everyPer "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$EveryPerFn.  Where TIME-TYPE is a #$TimeParameter and N is a #$RationalNumber, (#$everyPer TIME-TYPE N FREQUENCY) means that FREQUENCY is the property of occurring once for every N occurrences of TIME-TYPE.")
(comment frequencyOfIterationOfTypeIn "(#$frequencyOfIterationOfTypeIn EVT SUBSIT-TYPE FREQUENCY) means that instances of SUBSIT-TYPE are repeated in the #$IterativeEvent EVT with a frequency of FREQUENCY.")
(comment subColWhoseInstancesSeriallyRecurWithFrequency "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$AllInstancesOfTypeWithSerialFrequencyFn.  Where SIT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Situation and FREQUENCY is a #$Frequency, (#$subColWhoseInstancesSeriallyRecurWithFrequency SIT-TYPE FREQUENCY SUB-TYPE) means that SUB-TYPE is the collection of all instances of SIT-TYPE such that each instance is part of a temporally extended series that can be parsed into an institutionally or culturally sanctioned linear sequence of events, occurring with a regularity of FREQUENCY and sharing a definitive set of features in common with the instance, including, but by no means
limited to, membership in SIT-TYPE.")
(comment nearestIndependentIntervalTypeOfFrequency "(#$nearestIndependentIntervalTypeOfFrequency FREQUENCY TIME-TYPE) means that TIME-TYPE is the #$TimeParameter used in specifying FREQUENCY.")
(comment AllInstancesOfTypeWithSerialFrequencyFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where SIT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Situation, (#$AllInstancesOfTypeWithSerialFrequencyFn SIT-TYPE FREQUENCY) denotes the collection of all instances of SIT-TYPE such that each instance is part of a temporally extended series that can be parsed into an institutionally or culturally sanctioned linear sequence of events, occurring with a regularity of FREQUENCY and sharing a definitive set of features in common with the instance, including, but by no means
limited to, membership in SIT-TYPE.  Thus, e.g., (AllInstancesOfTypeWithSerialFrequencyFn SportsEvent Yearly) denotes the set of all SportsEvents such that each instance is part of an institutionally sanctioned series of annually-occurring like events:
example instances would include the (#$AnnualEventOfYearFn #$SuperBowlGame (#$YearFn 1989), or the (#$AnnualEventOfYearFn
#$NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament (#$YearFn 2009)).")
(comment VeganDiet "An instance of #$DietProgram representing the vegan diet.  #$VeganDiet is characterized simply by a proscription (see #$dietProscribes) against eating animals and animal products (e.g., honey, eggs, and dairy products).")
(comment Osteopetrosis "Osteopetrosis is an inherited disorder that is characterized by the development of dense and brittle bones.")
(comment Rickets "A condition arising from having a vitamin D deficiency, characterized by soft bones.")
(comment Osteoarthritis "The collection of all osteoarthritis. A type of #$Arthritis. #$Osteoarthritis is a #$DiseaseType.")
(comment Narcolepsy "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition.
Each instance of this narcolepsy is a condition characterized by excessive daytime sleepiness and even falling asleep at inappropriate times.")
(comment versionedProgramHasMB_RAMRequirements-SampleDB "relates an instance of #$VersionedProgram to the free RAM required to run the program")
(comment organismTypePartIsType "See the corresponding function, #$OrganismPartTypeFn. (#$organismTypePartIsType ORG-TYPE PART-TYPE ORG-SPECIFIC-PART-TYPE) states that for every organism of type ORG-TYPE, its anatomical part of type PART-TYPE is an instance of the more specific type, ORG-SPECIFIC-PART-TYPE.  For example, (#$organismTypePartIsType #$Vertebrate #$SkeletalSystem VertebrateSkeleton).")
(comment contactDetailOrganizationCity-SampleDB "relates an organization detail to the #$City of the detailed organization in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(comment contactDetailOrganizationWebsiteURL-SampleDB "relates an organization detail to the #$UniformResourceLocator of the website of the detailed organization in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(comment supplierOfProductForOrganization-SampleDB "relates a product of some sort (a computer program, file server, etc.) to a supplier of that product in the context of the #$ComputerProgramSampleDatabase.")
(comment AmericanStyleFastFoodCuisine "The collection of instances of what many American residents (of all ethnic and subcultural backgrounds) tend to think of as \"standard\" American-style fast food.  The kinds of foods sold at Burger King, McDonalds, KFC, Arby's, TacoBell, etc. would be paradigmatic specs of this collection.")
(comment SystemSoftware "A specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  System software is software that operates computer hardware.  It includes device drivers (including BIOS programs), command interpreters and operating systems.")
(comment owlRestrictionAllValuesFrom "deprecated.")
(comment |owl:Restriction| "The collection of all OWL Restriction classes.  Each OWL restriction specifies exactly one property and one value constraint -- e.g. that every member of the class is related to some member of another class via the property, or is related via the property to only members of this other class, etc.  ")
(comment NthEditionOfWorkFn "<code>(#$NthEditionOfWorkFn WORK N)</code> denotes the Nth edition of the conceptual work WORK.")
(comment workHasNthEdition "<code>(#$workHasNthEdition WORK N EDITION)</code> identifies <code>EDITION</code> as the instance of #$StructurallySpecificWork that is the Nth edition of the conceptual work <code>WORK</code>.")
(comment |owl:NamedIndividual| "A subcollection of #$owl:Thing.  #$owl:NamedIndividual is an OWL2 entity declaration that states something or someone is an individual.")
(comment VideoController "The collection of all video controllers. A type of #$ComputerControllerBoard. The concept #$VideoController is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment IOS-Apple "Apple's iPhone operating system.")
(comment IPad "An instance of #$ProductTypeByBrand.  Each instance of #$IPad is a tablet computer manufactured by #$AppleInc.")
(comment TabletComputer "The collection of all tablet computers. A type of #$PersonalComputer, #$PortableObject, #$InformationManagementUse, and #$BatteryPoweredDevice. The collection #$TabletComputer is a #$ComputerType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and a #$ComputerHardwareDeviceType.")
(comment |owl:imports| "A predicate relating an #$owl:Ontology with another ontology that it imports.  (#$owl:imports ONTOLOGY-1 ONTOLOGY-2) means that ONTOLOGY-1 depends upon the classes and properties defined in ONTOLOGY-2.")
(comment |owl:DatatypeProperty| "A specialization of #$OWLProperty.  Each instance of #$owl:DatatypeProperty is a property that has been ontologized in an OWL ontology using OWL-Full in such a manner that it has been indicated to  relate things to data items such as integers, dates, strings, etc.  Every instance of this collection will have an #$arg2Isa constraint that is an instance of #$OwlSemanticDataType (q.v.).")
(comment |owl:ObjectProperty| "A specialization of #$OWLProperty.  Each instance of #$owl:ObjectProperty is a binary property that has been ontologized in some OWL ontology using OWL-Full in such a way that their domains and ranges have been declared to consist of certain individuals and collections.  They are distinguished from instances of #$owl:DatatypeProperty in that they do not relate things to \"data types\".")
(comment |owl:Class| "A specialization of #$Collection.  #$owl:Class is the collection of all collections that have been ontologized in at least one OWL ontology.")
(comment |owl:OntologyProperty| "A specialization of #$OntologyRelatingPredicate.   Each instance of #$owl:OntologyProperty is an #$OWLProperty that is also an #$OntologyRelatingPredicate.")
(comment ParameterOfCodingFunctionFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to reference collections of #$CodingFunctionParameters.  (#$ParameterOfCodingFunctionFn FN) denotes the collection of #$ComputerCodeExpression that are arguments of the #$CodingFunction FN.")
(comment parametersOfCodingFunction "The corresponding predicate of #$ParameterOfCodingFunctionFn.  Where FN is a #$CodingFunction, (#$parametersOfCodingFunction FN PARAM) means that PARAM is the collection of #$ComputerCodeExpressions that are the arguments of FN.")
(comment codingFunctionParameterIsa "A typed specialization of #$argIsa used to specify the argument constraints for instances of #$CodingFunction.  Where FN is a #$CodingFunction, (#$formalParameterOfCodingFunctionIsa FN N COL) means that the correct type for a value supplied as the Nth argument of FN is COL.")
(comment codingFunctionParameterName "(#$codingFunctionParameterStandardName FN PARAM NAME-STRING) means that the name ordinarily used to denote PARAM of FN is NAME-STRING.")
(comment defaultTask "(#$defaultTask TASK CYCLIST) means that not only is CYCLIST an #$allottedAgents for TASK, but in the absence of other information, it should be assumed that CYCLIST is in fact working on TASK.")
(disjointWith LaptopComputer PalmtopComputer)
(comment wingSpan "(#$wingSpan PLANE DISTANCE) indicates the total distance between the wingtips of an #$Airplane.")
(comment nextInSequence "(#$nextInSequence LIST THING) means that it seems natural to think that  a principle determines the sequence of elements N0...Nn in LIST, and that if that same principle were applied to determine the sequence in a larger list N0...Nn, Nn+1, then Nn+1 would be THING.  For example, the following are true:
<p>
<pre>
(#$nextInSequence (#$TheList 1 2 3) 4)
(#$nextInSequence (#$TheList #$G1Phase #$SPhase) #$G2Phase)
</pre>
<p>
Note that the second argument position of #$nextInSequence is not functional.  For example, both of the following are true:
<p>
<pre>
(#$nextInSequence (#$TheList 2 4) 8)
(#$nextInSequence (#$TheList 2 4) 6)
</pre>
<p>
These are both true because the principle behind the sequence 2,4 might either be \"to generate any element after the first, multiply its predecessor by 2\"  (i.e., apply (#$Lambda (?PREDECESSOR) (#$TimesFn ?PREDECESSOR 2))) or \"to generate any element after the first, add 2 to its predecessor\" (i.e., apply (#$Lambda (?PREDECESSOR) (#$PlusFn ?PREDECESSOR 2))).")
(comment enables-Generic "(#$enables-Generic X Y) says that X 
 enables Y.  This predicate serves as a generalization over many more specific  enables-* predicates. Please use one of its spec preds or axiomatically
defined specializations (i.e., spec preds of #$enablesAgentTo-Generic), whenever
possible.")
(comment UracilRibonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Uracil-Base and a phosphate group linked to #$Ribose.  Its abbreviation is U, and it pairs with #$AdenineDeoxyribonucleotide during transcription (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) or to #$AdenineRibonucleotide in the formation of the tertiary structure of #$TransferRNA.")
(comment SourceOfCodeStatementInProgramFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  Where CODE-BLOCK is a #$ComputerCodeStatement and PROGRAM is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS that contains CODE-BLOCK, (#$SourceOfCodeStatementInProgramFn CODE-BLOCK PROGRAM) denotes the source (if any) for CODE-BLOCK within PROGRAM.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that are not themselves composed of #$ComputerCodeStatements.")
(comment symbolicNameOfStatement "The most generic #$ComputerCodeParameter used for attaching a #$CharacterString to a #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic as a symbolic name.")
(comment bitWidthOfStatement "The most general computer code parameter (#$ComputerCodeParameter) for linking a #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic to its bit width.")
(comment NthTopLevelCodeStatementInFn "An individual-denoting function used for referencing instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement.  Specifically, (#$NthTopLevelCodeStatementInFn SUPER-STATEMENT N) denotes the #$ComputerCodeStatement such that it has SUPER-STATEMENT as its #$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement and such that there are N #$ComputerCodeStatements that have SUPER-STATEMENT as the #$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement and that precede it in SUPER-STATEMENT.  Intuitively, (#$NthTopLevelCodeStatementInFn SUPER-STATEMENT N) denotes the Nth 'top level' code block in SUPER-STATEMENT.")
(comment sourceOfCodeStatementInProgram "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$SourceOfCodeStatementInProgramFn.  Where CODE-STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement and PROGRAM is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS that contains CODE-STATEMENT, (#$sourceOfCodeStatementInProgram CODE-STATEMENT PROGRAM SOURCE) means that SOURCE is the CODE-SOURCE for CODE-STATEMENT within PROGRAM.")
(comment codeStatementAbstractParameter "The most general predicate linking an abstract parameter to a #$ComputerCodeStatement.")
(comment codeStatementConstrainsParameterToBitWidth "Where INVOCATION is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$codeStatementConstrainsParameterToBitWidth CODE-STATEMENT INVOCATION N WIDTH) means that the content of  #$ComputerCodeStatement CODE-STATEMENT specifies that the bitwidth of the memory location referenced by the Nth parameter of the #$codingFunctionInvoked in INVOCATION is WIDTH.")
(comment codeStatementConstrainsParameterToTransferLength "(#$codeStatementConstrainsParameterToTransferLength DIRECTIVE FN-CALL N LENGTH) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement DIRECTIVE constrains the Nth paramter in the formal argument list called with the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL to a value, LENGTH, which denotes the length of the string to be transferred by the function called with FN-CALL.")
(comment codeStatementConstrainsParameterToValue "(#$codeStatementConstrainsParameterToValue DIRECTIVE FN-CALL N VALUE) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement DIRECTIVE constrains the Nth parameter called with the 'function call' (an instance of #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) to a numeric value of VALUE.")
(comment codeStatementHasStatements "Partonomic predicate for relating one #$ComputerCodeStatement to another that it subsumes.  (#$codeStatementHasStatements STATEMENT SUB-STATEMENT) means that SUB-STATEMENT is part of the information structure of STATEMENT such that, in a normal or expected execution environment, executing STATEMENT will entail executing SUB-STATEMENT.")
(comment nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement "(#$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement SUB-STATEMENT NEAREST-SUPER-STATEMENT) means that NEAREST-SUPER-STATEMENT properly contains SUB-STATEMENT (i.e., both (#$codeStatementHasStatements NEAREST-SUPER-STATEMENT SUB-STATEMENT) and (#$different NEAREST-SUPER-STATEMENT SUB-STATEMENT) are true), and there is no other #$ComputerCodeStatement such that NEAREST-SUPER-STATEMENT contains it, and it contains SUB-STATEMENT.")
(comment uncheckedCodeStatementInProgram "(#$uncheckedCodeStatementInProgram PROGRAM CODE-STATEMENT) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement CODE-STATEMENT occurring in the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS PROGRAM lacks an appropriate code check within the context of PROGRAM.")
(comment TouchingEvent "One object spatially and temporally coming into contact with another.")
(comment ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation-Static "A collection of static physical contact situations in which two or more objects are in physical contact (see #$touches) throughout the situation's entire duration.")
(disjointWith CompoundComputerCodeStatement ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic)
(comment CompoundComputerCodeStatement "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements which can be decomposed via #$codeStatementHasStatements, into other #$ComputerCodeStatements, compound or atomic.")
(comment BracketedCodeBlock "The collection of all #$CompoundComputerCodeStatements with a syntactic structure consisting in a pair of brackets enclosing a sequence of #$ComputerCodeStatements.")
(disjointWith ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic AtomicBracketedCodeBlock)
(comment AtomicBracketedCodeBlock "The collection of all #$BracketedCodeBlocks which do not decompose via #$codeStatementHasStatement into other #$BracketedCodeBlocks.")
(disjointWith AtomicBracketedCodeBlock RecursiveBracketedCodeBlock)
(comment RecursiveBracketedCodeBlock "The collection of all #$BracketedCodeBlocks that decompose via #$codeStatementHasStatements into other #$BracketedCodeBlocks.")
(comment partSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType "(#$partSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType PARTTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of PARTTYPE produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically.  PARTTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize SUBSTANCETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions. ")
(comment partSynthesizesSubstance "(#$partSynthesizesSubstance PART SUBSTANCE) relates an #$OrganismPart, PART, to a portion of stuff, SUBSTANCE, that it biosynthetically creates.")
(comment partSynthesizesProtein-TypeType "(#$partSynthesizesProtein-TypeType PARTTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that instances of PARTTYPE produce portions of PROTEINTYPE biosynthetically.  PARTTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize PROTEINTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.  In the case where some gene directly codes for PROTEINTYPE, this means that instances of PARTTYPE express that gene.  Note that some kinds of protein are produced by post-translational modification.  In that case, such modifications are (typically) performed within instances of PARTTYPE.")
(comment partSynthesizesProtein "(#$partSynthesizesProtein PART PROTEIN) states that the #$OrganismPart PART produces  PROTEIN, a portion of #$ProteinStuff, biosynthetically.  In the case where some gene directly codes for the type of protein that PROTEIN is an instance of, this means that PART express that gene.  Alternatively, PROTEIN was produced by post-translational modification within PART.")
(comment cellTypeExpressesGene "(#$cellTypeExpressesGene CELLTYPE GENE) states that instances of CELLTYPE typically produce the products of GENE via biosynthesis.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize GENE's product.  This entails that GENE is transcribed into mRNA (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and, if GENE's ultimate product is a protein, that mRNA is translated (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) into a protein prouduct.")
(comment cellSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType "(#$cellSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType CELLTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of CELLTYPE produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize SUBSTANCETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment cellSynthesizesSubstance "(#$cellSynthesizesSubstance CELL SUBSTANCE) states that CELL produces the portion of stuff, SUBSTANCE, biosynthetically.")
(comment cellSynthesizesProtein-TypeType "(#$cellSynthesizesProtein-TypeType CELLTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that instances of CELLTYPE produce portions of PROTEINTYPE biosynthetically.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize PROTEINTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.  In the case where some gene directly codes for PROTEINTYPE, this means that instances of CELLTYPE express that gene.  Note that some kinds of protein are produced by post-translational modification.  In that case, such modifications are (typically) performed within instances of CELLTYPE.")
(comment cellSynthesizesProtein "(#$cellSynthesizesProtein CELL PROTEIN) states that CELL produces the portion of #$ProteinStuff, PROTEIN, biosynthetically.  In the case where some gene directly codes for the type of protein that PROTEIN is an instance of, this means that CELL express that gene.  Note that some kinds of protein are produced by post-translational modification.  In that case, such modifications are (typically) performed within CELL.")
(comment cellSecretesSubstance-TypeType "(#$cellSecretesSubstance-TypeType CELLTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of CELLTYPE produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically and furthermore that portions of that substance are emitted from the cell into the bloodstream or extracellular area.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize and secrete SUBSTANCETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment cellSecretesSubstance "(#$cellSecretesSubstance CELL SUBSTANCE) states that CELL produces the portion of stuff, SUBSTANCE, biosynthetically and furthermore that SUBSTANCE is emitted from CELL into the bloodstream or other extracellular area.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType "(#$tissueSynthesizesSubstance-TypeType TISSUETYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUETYPE, produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize SUBSTANCETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesSubstance "(#$tissueSynthesizesSubstance TISSUE SUBSTANCE) states that the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUE, produces the portion of stuff SUBSTANCE biosynthetically. This means that there are cells within TISSUE which synthesize SUBSTANCE.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesProtein-TypeType "(#$tissueSynthesizesProtein-TypeType TISSUETYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that instances of the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUETYPE, produce portions of PROTEINTYPE biosynthetically.  This means that some of the cells within the tisse synthesize PROTEINTYPE.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize PROTEINTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesProtein "(#$tissueSynthesizesProtein TISSUE PROTEIN) states that the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUE, produces the portion of #$ProteinStuff, PROTEIN, biosynthetically.  This means that some of the cells within TISSUE synthesize PROTEIN.")
(comment tissueSecretesSubstance-TypeType "(#$tissueSecretesSubstance-TypeType TISSUETYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of TISSUETYPE produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically and furthermore that portions of that substance are emitted from the tissue into the bloodstream or other extracellular area.  This means that some of the cells within the instance of TISSUETYPE synthesize and secrete SUBSTANCETYPE.   TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize and secrete SUBSTANCETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment tissueSecretesSubstance "(#$tissueSecretesSubstance TISSUE SUBSTANCE) states that the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUE, produces the portion of stuff SUBSTANCE biosynthetically and furthermore that SUBSTANCE is emitted from TISSUE into the bloodstream or other extracellular area.  This means that some of the cells within TISSUE synthesize and secrete SUBSTANCE.")
(comment CellularMultiplication "The collection of all events in which a single cell enlarges and then divides, to produce two or more new cells.")
(comment Telomerase "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule. Telomerase adds DNA sequence repeats to the telomeric regions of eukaryotic chromosomes.")
(comment Bioinformatics "A #$FieldOfStudy.  Bioinformatics is the application of computer science methods to the study of biology.")
(comment CodeVarTypeNamedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for referencing collection instances of #$CodeVariableType.  (#$CodeVarTypeNamedFn NAME) denotes the #$CodeVariableType referred to by NAME at the level of the compiler code.")
(comment codeVarTypeNamed "The corresponding predicate of #$CodeVarTypeNamedFn.  Where NAME is a #$CharacterString, (#$codeVarTypeNamed NAME VAR-TYPE) meanst that VAR-TYPE is the #$CodeVariableType specified via NAME at the compiler level.")
(comment typeSpecifierForVariable "(#$typeSpecifierForVariable VAR TYPE-SPECIFIER) means that TYPE-SPECIFIER is established as the #$CodeVariableType and hence the value type specifier for the #$ComputerCodeVariable VAR.")
(comment variableTypeSpecifier "(#$variableTypeSpecifier VAR-DEC SPECIFIER) means that VAR-DEC declares a variable with the type specifier SPECIFIER.")
(comment variableListSpecified "(#$variableListSpecified VAR-DEC VARS-LIST) means that the #$VariableDeclaration VAR-DEC is stated with the list of variables VARS-LIST.")
(comment setOrCollectionSignifiedForCodeVarType "(#$setOrCollectionSignifiedForCodeVarType VAR-TYPE SIGNIFIED-TYPE) means that when a variable VAR is declared with the #$CodeVariableType VAR-TYPE as the type specifier (see #$variableTypeSpecifier), and VAR appears in the argument list of a function call (#$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation), the value assigned to VAR's position in any execution of that function call (#$argNValueAssignedFunctionCalledInExecution) will be interpreted as an input of type SIGNIFIED-TYPE for purposes of executing the function.  Among other things, this means that if the function requires an input type that is in fact disjoint with SIGNFIED-TYPE, execution of the function will end in an error condition.")
(comment CodeVariableType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each collection instance of #$CodeVariableType is a collection of #$ComputerCodeVariables corresponding to a type-specifier of a programming language: for example, 'int', 'char', 'void', or 'float' in the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily.")
(comment PCWInFieldFn "(#$PCWInFieldFn FIELD) returns the collection of works that are works in the field FIELD.")
(comment transmittingCell "<code>(#$transmittingCell COMMUNICATION CELL)</code> identifies <code>cell</code> as the instance of #$Cell that is the source of the \"signal\" being sent to other cell(s) in <code>COMMUNICATION</code>, an instance of #$CellularCommunication.  Chemically, this means that <code>cell</code> is the #$secretionSource in the instance(s) of #$CellularSecretionEvent that start <code>COMMUNICATION</code>.")
(comment CellularSecretionEvent "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel-LocalizedToSingleCell, this is the subcollection of #$SecretionEvent all instances of which are such that the #$secretionSource is an instance of #$Cell.")
(comment substanceInBLOContributesToBioProcess-TypeLevel "(#$substanceInBLOContributesToBioProcess-TypeLevel ?SUBST-TYPE ?BLO-TYPE ?P-TYPE) states that the presence of some adequate amount of ?SUBST-TYPE in an instance of ?BLO-TYPE is a precursor to the occurrence of an instance of the biological process, ?P-TYPE.  The presence of ?SUBST-TYPE may not be necessary, or sufficient; however, when an instance of ?P-TYPE occurs, typically an instance of ?SUBST-TYPE has been present.")
(comment substanceInBLOTriggersBioProcess-TypeLevel "(#$substanceInBLOTriggersBioProcess-TypeLevel ?SUBST-TYPE ?BLO-TYPE ?P-TYPE) states that the presence of some adequate amount of ?SUBST-TYPE in an instance of ?BLO-TYPE is a sufficient precursor for the occurrence of an instance of the biological process, ?P-TYPE.")
(comment substanceInducesProtein-TypeType "(#$substanceInducesProtein-TypeType SUBSTANCETYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that, in some unspecified cellular environment, quantities of SUBSTANCETYPE trigger or speed up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  That is to say that there is some cellular situation in which the presence of SUBSTANCETYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment substanceInCellInducesProtein-TypeLevel "(#$substanceInCellInducesProtein-TypeLevel SUBSTANCETYPE CELLTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that when some quantity of SUBSTANCETYPE is present in an instance of CELL it triggers or speeds up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  More specifically, the presence of some quantity of SUBSTANCETYPE in and instance of CELLTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment organismTypeSynthesizesType "(#$organismTypeSynthesizesType ORGTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that instances of ORGTYPE produce portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically.  Every instance of ORGTYPE can typically be expected to synthesize SUBSTANCETYPE. ")
(comment organismSynthesizesSubstance "(#$organismSynthesizesSubstance ORG SUBSTANCE) relates an #$Organism-Whole ORG, to a portion of stuff, SUBSTANCE, that it biosynthetically creates.")
(comment onlyOrganismTypeSynthesizesType "(#$onlyOrganismTypeSynthesizesType ORGTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE) states that every instance of ORGTYPE produces portions of SUBSTANCETYPE biosynthetically, and that furthermore if a portion of SUBSTANCETYPE is naturally biosynthesized by some organism, that occurs within the body of an instance of ORGTYPE.  (Note that in laboratory settings, it may be possible to artificially synthesize SUBSTANCETYPE, or to cause cells from an instance of ORGTYPE to produce SUBSTANCETYPE, or even to genetically modify some other type of organism so that it produces SUBSTANCETYPE.) ")
(comment localRegulatorMolecules "A typed specialization of #$signalMolecules, <code>(#$localRegulatorMolecules PARACRINE-SIGNALING-EVENT MOLECULE)</code> means that the instance <code>MOLECULE</code> of #$Molecule is a signal molecule (see #$signalMolecules) in <code>PARACRINE-SIGNALING-EVENT</code>, an instance of #$ParacrineSignaling.")
(comment signalMolecules "<code>(#$signalMolecules CELL-COMMUNICATION-EVENT MOLECULE)</code> means that the instance <code>MOLECULE</code> of #$Molecule is a signal molecule in <code>CELL-COMMUNICATION-EVENT</code>, an instance of #$CellularCommunication.  A signal molecule is a molecule that is one of the #$outputsSecreted by the #$transmittingCell in a cellular communication event, and thus is the first object involved in a series of chemical interactions (possibly of length 1) that comprise the \"transmission\" of the \"message\" sent by the cell to the #$targetCells.")
(comment SynapticSignaling "A kind of #$CellularCommunication that takes place among neurons (see #$Neuron).")
(comment LocalCellularCommunication "The collection of instances of #$CellularCommunication where the #$transmittingCell and the #$targetCells are (relatively speaking) very close together and do not require the #$signalMolecules to be transported, e.g., through the bloodstream, to reach their targets.  #$LocalCellularCommunication is to be contrasted with #$LongDistanceCellularCommunication.")
(comment targetCells "<code>(#$targetCells CELL-COMMUNICATION CELL)</code> means that <code>CELL</code> is one of the instances of #$Cell that \"receives\" the \"signal\" from the #$transmittingCell in CELL-COMMUNICATION, an instance of #$CellularCommunication.  Each of the #$targetCells is the #$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell for a specific instance of #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell that starts with the reception of the signal.")
(comment ResearchinMotionLimited "A telecommunications company based in Ontario, Canada.  They are the manufacturers of the #$BlackBerry-CellPhone line of smartphones.")
(comment Gene-HereditaryUnit "A collection of the units of heredity.  Each #$Gene-HereditaryUnit is a continuous segment of a #$DNAMolecule which finds expression through transcription (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and (optionally) translation (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) in a final, functional product that is either a #$PeptideMolecule or an #$RNAMolecule.")
(comment SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType "Each instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType is a specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit (and thus a collection of segments of DNA) comprising instances that are locationally and functionally the same, more or less. If GENE-TYPE is an instance of  #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, all of its instances belong to organisms of the same species.  There may be allelic differences between the instances that render them non-identical.  More specifically, if GENE-TYPE is an instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, every instance of GENE-TYPE is found in nearly the same location along a #$DNAMolecule that is part of a chromosome in the cell in which it occurs, and each is found on the ''same-numbered'' chromosome in its cell. Also, the instances of GENE-TYPE have high similarity in their sequences of nucleotide base pairs. Finally, the biochemical product each instance of GENE-TYPE expresses (either a #$PeptideMolecule or an #$RNAMolecule) is substantially the same.  Note, however, that mutation and other chromosomal events might result in instances of GENE-TYPE which are broken in some way, thus violating some of these requirements.")
(comment onlySpeciesHasGeneType-HU "(#$onlySpeciesHasGeneType-HU ORGTYPE GENE) states that GENE is specific to organisms which are instances of ORGTYPE, where ORGTYPE is an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies.")
(comment MachineImplementationReasoningConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms that are deemed to be of particular importance for reasoning about machine implementations in computing architecture for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment CodeSyntaxRepresentationConstant "The collection of all constants deemed to be of particular importance in representing computer code syntax for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment physicalMemoryOfImplementation "(#$physicalMemoryOfImplementation IMPLEMENTATION MEMORY) means that MEMORY is the #$ComputerMemory-Abstract associated with the abstract machine implemented by IMPLEMENTATION (the #$uTMFunctionImplemented by IMPLEMENTATION).")
(disjointWith RelationshipType GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily)
(disjointWith QuantityType GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily)
(disjointWith TemporalStuffType GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily)
(comment GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily "A collection of collections of #$GeneticInformationStructures. Each instance GIS-TYPE of this collection is composed of instances of #$Gene-GIS that share these properties: 1) Each is a sequence that is instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) as a physical gene in the genetic material of members of the same #$BiologicalSpecies, and 2) Each is a sequence that, when its physical instantiation is transcribed to produce an #$RNAMolecule and optionally translated to produce a #$ProteinMolecule, will result in molecules all belonging to the same instance of #$PeptideMoleculeTypeBySourceGene.")
(comment PeptideMoleculeTypeBySourceGene "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY of #$PeptideMolecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules derived by transcribing (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and optionally translating (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) a segment of DNA (an instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit) which is a physical instantiation (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) of an instance of some #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily. Note that instances of each PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY are actual #$PeptideMolecules, but they are not necessarily all identical.  Sources of variation are as follows: a) Small differences in the genetic sequences of different DNA segments that all belong the same species of organism and code for the same product family can result in slightly different amino acid sequences being produced, which are still functionally more or less the same. Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms are one example of this type of variation. b) Alternative splicing occurs frequently.  This means that the same segment of DNA can produce RNA that is spliced (see #$RNASplicingProcess) in different ways to produce messenger RNAs that code for very different proteins.  However, each of these splice variants shares large subregions containing identical amino acid sequences.")
(comment PhysicalGeneTypeOfGene-GISTypeFn "Where GIS-TYPE is an instance of #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily, (#$PhysicalGeneTypeOfGene-GISTypeFn GIS-TYPE) denotes the collection of physical genes, i.e., specs of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit, which instantiate the instances of GIS-TYPE (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS.)")
(comment gene-GISTypePhysicalGeneType "(#$gene-GISTypePhysicalGeneType GIS-TYPE PHYS-GENE-TYPE) states that each physical gene in the collection, PHYS-GENE-TYPE (a specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit), instantiates some instance of GIS-TYPE.")
(comment ProteinFamilyType "Each instance PFAM of #$ProteinFamilyType is a collection of proteins (see #$ProteinStuff) which are considered ''related'' because of structural similarities, functional similarities, or both.  Members of PFAM need not be restricted to the same species of organism, and are probably coded for by different genes.")
(comment PhysicalGeneTypeByExactSequence "Each instance PGTBES of #$PhysicalGeneTypeByExactSequence is a specialization of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit (and thus a collection of segments of DNA) comprising instances that are locationally the same, more or less (modulo variation in surrounding DNA).  Furthermore, each instance of PGTBES possesses the same sequence of nucleotides, and each instance belongs to organisms of the same species.")
(comment initialValueGivenInDeclaration "(#$initialValueGivenInDeclaration DECLARE VALUE) means that the #$VariableDeclaration DECLARE specifies initializing the single variable that is declared to a value of THING.")
(comment TypeDefCodeStatement "The collection of all 'typedef' statements occurring in code in the C-language family.  A #$TypeDefCodeStatement creates a new rigid designator, the #$designatorMapped, in the form of a #$ComputerCodeConstant, for an existing #$ComputerCode object, the #$codeObjectMappedTo.")
(comment codeObjectMappedTo "Where TYPEDEF is a #$TypeDefCodeStatement, (#$codeObjectMappedTo TYPEDEF DATA-TYPE) means that DATA-TYPE is the data type that TYPEDEF associates with a new designator.")
(comment designatorMapped "Where TYPEDEF is a #$TypeDefCodeStatement, (#$designatorMapped TYPEDEF DESIGNATOR) means that DESIGNATOR is a new #$ComputerCodeConstant that TYPEDEF associates with a pre-existing data type.")
(comment StructureDeclaration "An important class of coding object in the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily.  A #$StructureDeclaration defines a #$List of #$ComputerCodeVariables, so ordered for purposes of convenient handling.")
(comment geneTypeCodesForPeptideType "(#$geneTypeCodesForPeptideType GENE-TYPE MOL-TYPE) states that instances of the #$SpecifiedPhysicalGeneType, GENE-TYPE, are typically decoded via transcription (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and translation (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) to produce the biochemical product, MOL-TYPE.  MOL-TYPE is a specialization of #$PeptideMolecule and an instance of #$PeptideMoleculeTypeBySourceGene.")
(comment TBXAS1-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$ThromboxaneASynthase1 class.")
(comment PTGIS-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$ProstacyclinSynthase class.")
(comment PTGS1-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase1 class.")
(comment PTGS2-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase2 class.")
(comment AVPR2-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$VasopressinV2Receptor class.")
(comment AVPR1A-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$VasopressinV1aReceptor class.")
(comment AVPR1B-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$VasopressinV1bReceptor class.")
(comment gene-GISTypeCodesForType "(#$gene-GISTypeCodesForType GIS-TYPE PEPTIDETYPE) means that instances of the nucleotide sequence collection GIS-TYPE code for peptides of the type PEPTIDETYPE when interpreted by ribsomal bodies in the process of DNA-to-peptide transcription/translation.")
(comment partExpressesGene "(#$partExpressesGene PART GENETYPE) states that the #$OrganismPart, PART, produces the products of GENETYPE via biosynthesis.  If PART is multicellular, this means that there are cells within PART which express GENETYPE.")
(comment partTypeExpressesGene "(#$partTypeExpressesGene PARTTYPE GENETYPE) states that instances of PARTTYPE typically produce the products of GENE via biosynthesis.  If PARTTYPE is multicellular, this means that there are cells within PARTTYPE which express GENETYPE.  PARTTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize one or more of GENETYPE's products.")
(comment cellExpressesGene "(#$cellExpressesGene CELL GENETYPE) states that CELL produces the products of GENETYPE via biosynthesis.  This entails that the physical instantiation of GENETYPE present in CELL is transcribed into mRNA (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and, if GENETYPE's ultimate product is a protein, that mRNA is translated (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) into a protein prouduct within CELL.")
(comment tissueTypeExpressesGene "(#$tissueTypeExpressesGene TISSUETYPE GENETYPE) states that instances of TISSUETYPE typically produce the products of GENETYPE (a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily) via biosynthesis.  This entails that GENETYPE is expressed by some of the cells in each instance of TISSUETYPE.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize one of GENETYPE's products.")
(comment tissueExpressesGene "(#$tissueExpressesGene TISSUE GENETYPE) states that the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUE, produces the products of GENETYPE (a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily) via biosynthesis.  This entails that GENETYPE is expressed by some of the cells in TISSUE.")
(disjointWith ExistingStuffType CellLifeStageType)
(disjointWith ExistingObjectType CellLifeStageType)
(comment SomaticCell "The collection of instances of #$Cell that (outside a petri-dish or having otherwise been artificially or accidentally removed from a body) make up the body (i.e., are the constituent cells of the tissues and organs) of any multi-cellular organism (and which constitute the bodies of single-celled eukaryotes).  Thus an organism's somatic cells are all of its cells aside from its sex cells (its instances of #$Gamete and #$GermCell).")
(comment SubstituteFormulaFn "A function that effects the substitution of one term for another within an EL formula.  (#$SubstituteFormulaFn NEWTERM OLDTERM FORMULA) denotes the #$CycLFormula formed by substituting NEWTERM for every occurrence (or every <i>free</i> occurrence if OLDTERM is a variable) of OLDTERM in FORMULA.  (If OLDTERM contains variables VAR1..VARN that occur free in OLDTERM, then an occurrence OLDTERM-OCC of OLDTERM is replaced with NEWTERM if and only if each occurrence of VAR1..VARN that is free in OLDTERM-OCC is also free in FORMULA.)  Note that the first two argument-places of the functor \"#$SubstituteFormulaFn\" are \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument) and thus terms occupying those places denote (not their usual denotations, but) themselves.")
(comment formulaSubstitutionFor "This predicate, which corresponds (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate) to the function #$SubstituteFormulaFn,
relates an EL formula to the result of substituting one given term for another within that formula.  (#$formulaSubstitutionFor NEWTERM OLDTERM NEWFORMULA OLDFORMULA) means that NEWFORMULA is the #$CycLFormula (q.v.) that results from substituting NEWTERM for every occurrence (or for every <i>free</i> occurrence if OLDTERM is a variable) of OLDTERM in OLDFORMULA.  (If OLDTERM contains variables VAR1..VARN that occur free in OLDTERM, then an occurrence OLDTERM-OCC of OLDTERM is replaced with NEWTERM if and only if each occurrence of VAR1..VARN that is free in OLDTERM-OCC is also free in FORMULA.)  Note that the first two argument-places of the predicate expression \"#$formulaSubstitutionFor\" are \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument), and so terms occupying those places denote (not their usual denotations, if any, but) <i>themselves</i>.")
(comment UndesirableProgramAction "The collection of all #$ProgramActions that are normally considered undesirable or infelicitous from the standpoint of generally accepted coding standards and practices.")
(comment ConvertibleTop-CarPart "The collection of all convertible tops that are designed as parts for convertible cars.")
(comment curbMassOfVehicle "The curb mass (more commonly referred to as \"curb weight\") of a vehicle is the total mass of a vehicle with all standard equipment and all fluids and other consumables -- fuel, windshield wiper fluid, etc -- topped up, but with no additional cargo including operator or passengers.")
(comment coolnessRatingOfVehicle "The totally arbitrary number assigned to a vehicle by some Cyclist for testing export of scalar properties.")
(comment FormalArgumentsStatement "The collection of all ordered sequences of #$FormalArgumentDeclarations appearing in #$FunctionDeclarations.  In the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily, every #$FunctionDeclaration has exactly one #$FormalArgumentsStatement consisting in one or mor #$FormalArgumentDeclarations.")
(comment initialValueResolvedBy "(#$initialValueResolvedBy VAR-DEC CONST) means that the #$ComputerCodeConstant CONST resolves to the initial value assigned to the variable declared by VAR-DEC.")
(comment InclusionDirective "The collection of all statementes in the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily that direct inclusion of a file in a program execution by means of an '#include' statement and a header reference.")
(comment fileHeaderNameOfInclusionDirective "(#$fileHeaderNameOfInclusionDirective DIRECTIVE FILENAME) means that FILENAME is the name of the header of the file whose inclusion DIRECTIVE specifies relative to execution of the code in which DIRECTIVE is embedded.")
(comment abstractFileTargetOfInclusion "(#$abstractFileTargetOfInclusion DIRECTIVE FILE) means that FILE is the #$ComputerFile-Abstract targeted for inclusion by DIRECTIVE with respect to execution of the code of which DIRECTIVE is a part.")
(comment ComputerCodeExpressionDefinition "The collection of every #$ComputerCodeStatement that explicitly defines a #$ComputerCodeExpression.")
(comment CodeConstantDefinition "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that define #$ComputerCodeConstants.")
(comment definiendumOfExpressionDefinition "(#$definiendumOfExpressionDefinition DEF EXPRESSION) means that EXPRESSION is the #$ComputerCodeExpression which is defined by the #$ComputerCodeExpressionDefinition DEF.")
(comment definiensOfExpressionDefinition "(#$definiensOfExpressionDefinition DEF VALUE) means that VALUE is the value associated by the #$ComputerCodeExpressionDefinition DEF with the #$ComputerCodeExpression which DEF defines.")
(comment OrganismReproductionEvent "The specialization of #$BiologicalReproductionEvent in which the #$parentActors and #$offspringActors are instance of #$Organism-Whole.")
(comment productsOfGene-GISTypesInteract "(#$productsOfGene-GISTypesInteract GIS-TYPE1 GIS-TYPE2) states that the two genes, GIS-TYPE1 and GIS-TYPE2, code for two products (types of peptide or RNA) that are thought to interact.")
(comment dataTypeSpecifierForFunctionReturn "(#$dataTypeSpecifierForFunctionReturn ?FN-DEC ?SPECIFIER) means that ?SPECIFIER is used in ?FN-DEC to state the data type of the function ")
(comment SelectionCodeStatement "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements which feature if-then-else structure.")
(comment ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement "Where SEL-STATEMENT is a #$SelectionCodeStatement, (#$ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement SEL-STATEMENT ANTECEDENT-CONDITION) means that the #$ComputerCodeExpression ANTECEDENT-CONDITION gives the antecedent condition stated in SEL-STATEMENT (i.e., ANTECEDENT-CONDITION is the 'if' part of the statement.")
(comment thenStatementOfSelectionCodeStatement "Where SEL-STATEMENT is a #$SelectionCodeStatement (#$thenStatementOfSelectionCodeStatement SEL-STATEMENT PROCEDURE-STATEMENT) means that PROCEDURE-STATEMENT is the #$ComputerCodeStatement which SEL-STATEMENT specifies as the action to be taken, provided its stated condition (the #$ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement) is met.")
(comment elseStatementOfSelectionCodeStatement "Where SEL-STATEMENT is a #$SelectionCodeStatement, (#$elseStatementOfSelectionCodeStatement SEL-STATEMENT ALT-STATEMENT) means that ALT-STATEMENT is the #$ComputerCodeStatement which SEL-STATEMENT specifies as the actiion to be taken in the event that its statemed condition (the #$ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement) is NOT met.")
(comment ConditionExpressionOfSelectionStatementFn "Where SEL-STATEMENT is a #$SelectionCodeStatement, (#$ConditionExpressionOfSelectionStatementFn SEL-STATEMENT) denotes the #$ComputerCodeExpression that stands in the relation #$ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement to SEL-STATEMENT.")
(comment statementReferencesExpression "Where STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement and EXPRESSION is a #$ComputerCodeExpression, (#$statementReferencesExpression STATEMENT EXPRESSION) means that EXPRESSSION is referred to by STATEMENT.")
(comment onlySpeciesHasGeneType-GIS "(#$onlySpeciesHasGeneType-GIS ORGTYPE GENETYPE) states that GENETYPE is specific to organisms which are instances of ORGTYPE, where ORGTYPE is an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies.")
(comment OilExtractionTypeByGeneralComplexity "A specialization of #$ConventionalClassificationType used to partition #$ExtractingPetroleum into three sub-collections -- #$PrimaryOilRecovery, #$SecondaryOilRecovery, and #$EnhancedOilRecovery -- based on the level of complexity of the techniques used to extract the oil.")
(comment SecondaryOilRecovery "A general category of #$ExtractingPetroleum in which more complex techniques that what would see in #$PrimaryOilRecovery, but less complex than those used in #$EnhancedOilRecovery, are applied to extract oil that is too difficult to extract using primary techniques.")
(comment PrimaryOilRecovery "A general category of #$ExtractingPetroleum in which \"natural\" resources, such as differences in pressure and gravity, are used to extract oil.  In a typical oil extraction operation, primary oil extraction techniques will be used first, followed by secondary techniques after the availability of 'easily extractable' oil begins to run out.")
(comment NovelWithFilmAdaptation "The collection of #$Novel-CWs for which there is also a Film-CW based on the novel.")
(comment LinkedLifeClass "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection that corresponds to one of the classes in the Linked Life Data semantic integration data source.")
(comment |entrezgene:Interaction| "A collection.  Each instance of this collection corresponds to an interaction between genes attributed to Entrez-Gene in the Linked Life Data semantic integration data source.")
(comment mitreSchemaTermName "(#$mitreSchemaTermName RELN NAME) means that RELN is the Mitre CWE schema element or sub-element whose name is NAME.")
(comment mitreSchemaElementName "(#$mitreSchemaElementName RELN NAME) means that the predicate RELN is the Mitre CWE schema element whose name is NAME.")
(comment mitreWeaknessCategoryDescription "Where CODE-TYPE is a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency, (#$mitreWeaknessCategoryDescription CODE-TYPE DESCRIPTION) means that DESCRIPTION is MITRE's dexcription of CODE-TYPE.")
(comment stageOfIntroductionForWeaknessType "Where CODE-TYPE is a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency, (#$stageOfIntroductionForWeaknessType CODE-TYPE STAGE-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE may be introduces during actions of type STAGE-TYPE in the software develepment cycle.")
(comment platformOrTechnologyTypeImplicatedInWeaknessType "If PLATFORM-OR-PLATFORM-TYPE is an #$Artifact-Generic, (#$platformOrTechnologyTypeImplicatedInWeaknessType CODE-TYPE PLATFORM-OR-PLATFORM-TYPE) means that executing code that is an instance of CODE-TYPE in a run-time environment that features PLATFORM-OR-PLATFOM-TYPE carries a nontrivial risk of realizing whatever undesirable behavior is associated with CODE-TYPE (see #$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType).  If PLATFORM-OR-PLATFORM-TYPE is a #$FirstOrderCollection, (#$platformOrTechnologyTypeImplicatedInWeaknessType CODE-TYPE PLATFORM-OR-PLATFORM-TYPE) means that executing code that is an instance of CODE-TYPE in a run-time environment that features some instance of PLATFORM-OR-PLATFOM-TYPE carries a nontrivial risk of realizing whatever undesirable behavior is associated with CODE-TYPE.")
(comment platformImplicatedInWeaknessType "(#$platformImplicatedInWeaknessType CODE-TYPE PLATFORM) means that executing code that is an instance of CODE-TYPE in a run-time environment that features PLATFORM carries a nontrivial risk of realizing whatever undesirable behavior is associated with CODE-TYPE (see #$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType).")
(comment languageImplicatedInWeaknessType "(#$languageImplicatedInWeaknessType CODE-TYPE LANGUAGE) means that code written in language is singularly at risk of being an instance of CODE-TYPE.")
(comment operatingSystemVulnerableToWeaknessType "Where CODE-TYPE is a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency, (#$operatingSystemVulnerableToWeaknessType CODE-TYPE OS) means that if an instance of CODE-TYPE is executed in a run-time environment whose operating system (#$operatingSystemOfRunTimeEnvironment) is OS, there is a risk that the undesirable activity associated with CODE-TYPE (codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType) will be realized.")
(comment computerTypeByArchitectureVulnerableToWeaknessType "(#$computerTypeByArchitectureVulnerableToWeaknessType CODE-TYPE HARDWARE-TYPE) means that, if an instance of CODE-TYPE is executed in a run-time environment where the #$deviceUsed in execution is an instance of HARDWARE-TYPE, there is a non-zero risk that an instance of the undesirable type of action associated with CODE-TYPE (see #$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType) will figure in the execution.")
(comment technologyTypeVulnerableToWeaknessType "(#$technologyTypeVulnerableToWeaknessType CODE-TYPE TECH-TYPE) means that executing code that is an instance of CODE-TYPE in a run-time environment that features some instance of TECH-TYPE in a certain instrumental role carries a nontrivial risk of realizing whatever undesirable behavior is associated with CODE-TYPE.")
(comment outcomeHazardOfWeaknessType "(#$outcomeHazardOfWeaknessType CODE-TYPE OCCURRENCE-TYPE) means that if an instance of CODE-TYPE is executed without measures being taken to mitigate the propensity with which CODE-TYPE is associated (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionType), the risk of an instance of OCCURRENCE-TYPE occurring as part of the execution is nontrivial.")
(comment likelihoodOfVulnerabilityRealizationForWeaknessType "(#$likelihoodOfVulnerabilityRealizationForWeaknessType CODE-TYPE LIKELIHOOD) means that, where (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType CODE-TYPE ACTION-TYPE),  the prior likelihood that execution of an arbitrarily selected instance of CODE-TYPE in an arbitrarily selected suitable run-time environment will include an occurrence of ACTION-TYPE is LIKELIHOOD.")
(comment salientRelationshipsForWeaknessType "(salientRelationshipsForWeaknessType CODE-TYPE ASSERTION) means that ASSERTION is a particularly salient, known relationship involving the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CODE-TYPE.")
(comment weaknessTypeHasNameInOntology "(#$weaknessTypeHasNameInOntology CODE-TYPE ONTOLOGY NAME) means the name by which the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CODE-TYPE is denoted in ONTOLOGY is NAME.")
(comment weaknessTypeTermHasEditorInMitreOntology "(#$weaknessTypeHasEditorInMitreOntology CODE-TYPE EDITOR) means that the term denoting CODE-TYPE in the #$MitreCWEOntology was added to or edited in that ontology by EDITOR.")
(comment disallowMeaningSentencesForUnboundPredicates "When this predicate is asserted of a knowledge source, the #$CycInferenceEngine will never work on meaning sentences for a literal with an unbound predicate. This has the effect of preventing conjunctive removal from applying to any unbound predicate literal.")
(comment InorganicCompound "An instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType and a specialization of #$InorganicMaterial. An instance of this collection is either composed of a single type of molecule (for example, molecular #$Nitrogen), or is an ionic compound composed of one type of #$Cation and one type of #$Anion (for example, #$AmmoniumChloride).  To be an #$InorganicCompound, the molecules or ions that make the substance up must lack carbon-hydrogen bonds.")
(comment FactSheetGenerationHeuristicsPredicate "The collection of instances of #$Predicate that are used to provide guidance to the Cyc system when it attempts to generate a fact sheet about some instance of #$Thing.")
(comment variableInitialized "(#$variableInitialized INIT VAR) means that VAR is the #$ComputerCodeVariable that INIT sets to an initial value.")
(comment expressionInitializedTo "(#$expressionInitializedTo INIT TARGET) means that in the #$InitializationStatement INIT, the value to which the #$ComputerCode TARGET resolves is what is set as the initial value for the #$variableInitialized.")
(comment InitializationStatement "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic which are independent variable initializations (i.e., initializations given separately from the #$VariableDeclaration wherein the variable is declared).")
(comment BiologicalRegulationProcess "The collection of all biological regulatory processes.  Specializations of this class might control the amount of some substance present in a biological system or the rate at which some other process, such as cell differentiation or the degradation of particular molecule, occurs.")
(comment BiologicalProcessRegulation "The collection of all biological  processes that regulate the rate, location and frequency of occurrence, duration, etc. of some other biological process.")
(comment typeRegulatedByType "(#$typeRegulatedByType BIO-PROC-TYPE REGULATION-TYPE) states that instances of the type of #$BiologicalProcess, BIO-PROC-TYPE, are regulated by instances of REGULATION-TYPE.")
(comment BiologicalProcessUpregulation "The collection of all biological  processes that positively regulate some other biological process. They cause that process to occur, cause it to occur more often, increase its rate, or otherwise increase the results of that other process.")
(comment BiologicalProcessDownregulation "The collection of all biological  processes that negatively regulate some other biological process. They prevent that process from occurring, cause it to occur less often, decrease its rate, or otherwise reduce the impact of that other process.")
(comment typeDownregulatedByType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$NegativeRegulationOfTypeFn.  <code>(#$typeDownregulatedByType BIO-PROC-TYPE DOWNREGUL-TYPE)</code> states that instances of BIO-PROC-TYPE can happen less often if at all, for shorter duration, or to a lesser spatial extent as a response to instances of DOWNREGUL-TYPE.")
(comment typeUpregulatedByType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$PositiveRegulationOfTypeFn.  <code>(#$typeUpregulatedByType BIO-PROC-TYPE UPREGUL-TYPE)</code> states that instances of BIO-PROC-TYPE can happen more often, for longer duration, or to a greater spatial extent as a response to instances of UPREGUL-TYPE.")
(comment TransformingGrowthFactorBeta1-Human "A type of #$BiochemicalSignalingObject whose instances may play an important role in regulating cell growth, cell proliferation and cell death.")
(comment classifiedWith-Uniprot "(#$classifiedWith-Uniprot PEPTIDE-MOL-TYPE COLLECTION) states that according to Uniprot, the type of peptide moleucule, PEPTIDE-MOL-TYPE, has been annotated with the collection COLLECTION.  This statement has different meanings depending on the type of thing COLLECTION represents.  For example, if COLLECTION is a type of biological process, then the statement claims that PEPTIDE-MOL-TYPE instances participate in instances of COLLECTION.")
(comment TheGeneOntology-KS "Structured knowledge source with information about genes and their sequences, proteins and their functions.")
(comment GeneOntologyEvidenceType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$GeneOntologyEvidenceType are collections of a particular type of supporting evidence, which, in #$TheGeneOntology-KS and certain other structured knowledge sources deriving part of their content from it, can be used to state the type of evidence for the association of a gene or protein with a biological process, molecular function, or cell location.")
(comment GO-ExperimentalEvidence "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from physical experiments or observations.")
(comment GO-InferredFromDirectAssay "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which takes the form of a direct assay.")
(comment GO-InferredFromPhysicalInteraction "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which takes the form of a direct assay demonstrating binding between the gene's product and a particular other molecule.")
(comment GO-InferredFromMutantPhenotype "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which observes differences in phenotype that can be attributed to mutations, polymorphism, or altered expression of the gene.")
(comment GO-InferredFromGeneticInteraction "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which observes differences in phenotype that can be attributed to mutations or alterations in a different gene that provides information about the function of this gene product.")
(comment GO-InferredFromExpressionPattern "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which consists of the timing or location of gene expression.")
(comment GO-ComputationalAnalysisEvidence "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from computational analysis of the gene's sequence.")
(comment GO-InferredFromSequenceOrStructuralSimilarity "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from a sequence-based, and manually reviewed, analysis of the gene.")
(comment GO-InferredFromSequenceAlignment "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which consists of observations of sequence alignment with a gene whose association with that process, function or location is experimentally justified.  The alignment must have been manually reviewed for length and percent match")
(comment GO-InferredFromSequenceOrthology "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which consists of an experimentally justified association to the same process, function or location for an orthologous gene/protein, i.e., a gene of a different species with strong evidence the two genes derive from a common ancestor. ")
(comment GO-InferredFromSequenceModel "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from the use of a statistical model to predict gene product function, where the results have been manually reviewed for significance.")
(comment GO-AuthorStatementEvidence "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from a published author statement.")
(comment GO-TraceableAuthorStatement "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which takes the form of a statement in an article which doesn't present original evidence, but which is supported by citation, where the cited source shows original evidence.")
(comment GO-NonTraceableAuthorStatement "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which takes the form of a statement in an article (or database) which neither presents original evidence, nor cites a source that does.")
(comment GO-CuratorStatementEvidence "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which comes from a judgement made by a curator, which does not fit into another class of evidence.")
(comment GO-InferredByCurator "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which consists of inferences made by Gene Ontology curators by combining domain knowledge with other supported associations.")
(comment GO-AutomaticallyAssignedEvidence "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location which was assigned automatically.")
(comment GO-InferredFromElectronicAnnotation "A collection of supporting evidence for a gene's (or protein's) association with a process, function or location where the association was made automatically, from sequence similarity, transfer from a database or some other automatic process, and which has not been manually reviewed.")
(comment status-Uniprot "(#$status-Uniprot STATEMENT EVIDENCE-TYPE) states that according to Uniprot, EVIDENCE-TYPE is the type of evidence supporting STATEMENT.")
(comment CollagenSynthesis "The collection of protein synthesis events that produce some type of #$Collagen.")
(comment DPT-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$Dermatopontin-Human class.")
(comment owlDataTypeSemanticCorrelation "This relation indicates the canonical OWL datatype for a given Cyc collection of Scalars.  It is leveraged by the OWL export code to determine the proper rdfs:range assertion for exported Cyc predicates.")
(comment typeTendsToIncrease "(#$typeTendsToIncrease EVT-TYPE
QUANTITY-SLOT) means that instances of EVT-TYPE tend to increase the quantity, QUANTITY-SLOT.  This does not mean that as the instance occurs, the quantity will necessarily increase, because other forces could be acting at the same time that oppose the increase.")
(comment typeTendsToDecrease "(#$typeTendsToIncrease EVT-TYPE
QUANTITY-SLOT) means that instances of EVT-TYPE tend to decrease the quantity, QUANTITY-SLOT.  This does not mean that as the instance occurs, the quantity will necessarily decrease, because other forces could be acting at the same time that oppose the decrease.")
(comment ConditionExpression "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that are used to state antecedent conditions for selection statements.")
(comment variableCitedInConditionExpression "(#$variableCitedInConditionExpression EXPRESSION VAR) means that the #$ConditionExpression EXPRESSION states an antecedent condition according to which VAR has a certain value (#$valueCitedInConditionExpression) or a value of a certain numeric type (#$valueCitedInConditionExpression).")
(comment valueCitedInConditionExpression "(#$valueCitedInConditionExpression EXPRESSION VALUE) means that the #$ConditionExpression EXPRESSION states a condition according to which a certain variable (the #$variableCitedInConditionExpression) has the value VALUE.")
(comment valueTypeCitedByConditionExpression "(#$valueTypeCitedByConditionExpression EXPRESSION VALUE-TYPE) means that the #$ConditionExpression EXPRESSION explicitly states a condition according to which a variable (the #$variableCitedInConditionExpression) has a value that belongs to the #$MeasurableScalarIntervalType VALUE-TYPE. That is, if the value of the #$variableCitedInConditionExpression is an instance of VALUE-TYPE, this is both a necessary and sufficient condition for meeting the requirement given by EXPRESSION.")
(comment valueTypeImpliedByConditionExpression "(#$valueTypeImpliedByConditionExpression EXPRESSION VALUE-TYPE) means that the condition stated by EXPRESSION can be met only if the value assigned the #$variableCitedInConditionExpression is an instance of VALUE-TYPE; i.e., the value's being an instance of VALUE-TYPE is a necessary condition for satisfying the requirement stated by EXPRESSION (but not necessarily a sufficient condition). ")
(comment leftMostExpressionCitedInConditionalQuantityComparison "(#$expressionCitedInConditionalQuantityComparison CONDITION-EXPRESSION SUB-EXPRESSION) means that CONDITION-EXPRESSION states a requirement that a certain #$NumericComparisonPredicate must hold between the values which two #$ComputerCodeExpressions resolve, the left-most of these expressions being SUB-EXPRESSION.")
(comment rightMostExpressionCitedInConditionalQuantityComparison "(#$expressionCitedInConditionalQuantityComparison CONDITION-EXPRESSION SUB-EXPRESSION) means that CONDITION-EXPRESSION states a requirement that a certain #$NumericComparisonPredicate must hold between the values which two #$ComputerCodeExpressions resolve, the right-most of these expressions being SUB-EXPRESSION.")
(comment quantityComparisonCitedByCondition "(#$quantityComparisonCitedByCondition CONDITION-EXPRESSION COMP-PRED) means that CONDITION-EXPRESSION states a requirement that that COMP-PRED should hold between the values to which two #$ComputerCodeExpressions respectively resolve.)")
(comment boneDensityTScore "(#$boneDensityTScore PATIENT SCORE) gives information about the #$BoneMineral density of PATIENT's bones.  SCORE is computed by comparing the bone density of PATIENT against the that of a reference population, usually healthy young adults of the same biological sex and ethnicity as PATIENT. SCORE is the number of standard deviations PATIENT's bone density is  away from the mean bone density of the reference population. It generally ranges from about -4.0 to about +4.0.")
(comment UnitOfAreaDensity "A collection of functions and an instance of #$InterconvertibleUnitType. Each function in this collection is used to denote instances of #$AreaDensity. Examples of quantities that are area densities (also known as surface densities) include 80 grams per square meter (a common weight of paper) and 1 gram per square centimeter (a reasonably value for bone mineral density).")
(disjointWith AreaDensity Molarity)
(disjointWith ElectricalCharge AreaDensity)
(comment AreaDensity "A #$DerivedMeasurableQuantityType and a 
specialization of #$ThreeDimensionalQuantity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$AreaDensity is a mass distributed over some area.")
(comment areaDensityOfObject "(#$areaDensityOfObject OBJ AD) means that the tangible thing OBJ has the #$AreaDensity AD.  This measure is often used to describe the weight of two dimensional things like paper (e.g., 80 grams per square meter) but is also used to express the numeric result of bone densitometry.")
(comment LowValueForFn "A #$ScalarDenotingFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$QuantitySlot and returns a #$GenericQuantity of the type required by the #$arg2Isa of the #$QuantitySlot. .   In a given context, <code>(#$LowValueForFn QUANTSLOT)</code>, where <code>QUANTTYPE</code> is the #$arg2Isa of <code>QUANTSLOT</code>, is the properly interval-like quantity that is considered a <i>low amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.
")
(comment BiologicalProcessTypeRelevantToBone "A collection of events.  Instances of #$BiologicalProcessTypeRelevantToBone are events which create, destroy, maintain, modify, or otherwise affect the skeletal system and bone tissue.")
(comment variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWith "(#$variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWith GENE-TYPE GENERIC-QUANTITY) states that some study has found that, in some population of individuals, variation in GENE-TYPE is associated with the quantitative trait, GENERIC-QUANTITY.")
(comment chemicalObjectTypesInteract "(#$chemicalObjectTypesInteract MOL-TYPE1 MOL-TYPE2) states that the two types of chemical object, MOL-TYPE1 and MOL-TYPE2 are thought to interact.")
(comment malfunctionTypeCanExplain "(#$malfunctionTypeCanExplain MAL-TYPE GENERIC-QUANTITY) states that a malfunction of type MAL-TYPE could explain the quantitiative trait expressed by GENERIC-QUANTITY.")
(comment wikipediaArticleName-Canonical "(#$wikipediaArticleName-Canonical THING NAME) means that in the English Version of #$Wikipedia-WebSite THING is described by an article with the title NAME . Note that this title is the last part of the URL, not the title that appears at the top of the rendered page.")
(comment wikipediaArticleName "(#$wikipediaArticleName THING NAME) means that in the English Version of #$Wikipedia-WebSite THING is described by an article with the title NAME . Note that this title is the last part of the URL, not the title that appears at the top of the rendered page.  This predicate differs from #$wikipediaArticleName-Canonical in that this predicate is not #$singleEntryFormatInArgs, which is to say that there may be multiple arg2 values for any given arg1 value.   Typically, this predicate will be used for redirect links, while wikipediaArticleName-Canonical should used for canonical page name.")
(comment fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType "A #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate that relates types of biological processes to other types of biological processes, where instances of the latter types are fostered by instances of the former types. <code>(#$fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType P-TYPE1 P-TYPE2)</code> means that the kind of #$Situation <code>P-TYPE1</code> fosters the kind of #$Situation <code>P-TYPE2</code>.  Fostering is a looser relation than causation: if <code>P-TYPE1</code> causes <code>P-TYPE2</code> (#$causes-SitTypeSitType), it certainly fosters it; but a situation-type can foster another without being a cause of it.  While it isn't necessarily the case when <code>(#$fosters-BioProcessTypeBioProcessType P-TYPE1 P-TYPE2)</code> that the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE1</code> is typically associated with the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE2</code>, it will be the case that the occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE1</code> is one of the most promising ways of bringing about an occurrence of an instance of <code>P-TYPE2</code>.")
(comment geneTypeMayImpactQuantitativeTrait "(#$geneTypeMayImpactQuantitativeTrait GENE-TYPE QUANTITY-SLOT) states that Cyc can demonstrate a causal relationship between GENE-TYPE and the quantitative trait, QUANTITY-SLOT.")
(comment geneTypeMayInfluenceProcessType "(#$geneTypeMayInfluenceProcessType GENE-TYPE P-TYPE) states that Cyc can demonstrate a causal relationship between GENE-TYPE and the type of #$BiologicalProcess, P-TYPE.")
(comment functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall "(#$functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall SUPER-CALL N SUB-CALL) means that SUB-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that is used to give the value which is supplied as the Nth parameter value for the function called in super-call.  More specifically, it means that the specification of SUPER-CALL is such that whatever value which is returned by the #$codingFunctionInvoked in SUB-CALL on the #$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation supplied to SUB-CALL is specified as the Nth argument value for the function called (the #$codingFunctionInvoked in SUPER-CALL.  #$functionCallYieldsNthArgumentOfFunctionCall is the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$FunctionCallForNthArgumentOfFunctionCallFn.")
(comment variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWithVariationInQuantitativeTrait "(#$variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWith GENE-TYPE QUANTITY-SLOT) states that some study has found that, in some population of individuals, variation in GENE-TYPE is associated with the quantitative trait measured by QUANTITY-SLOT.")
(comment SemiconductorDomainConstant "The collection of constants relevant to The semiconductor device fabrication domain.")
(comment SemiconductorDomainConstant-NonManufacturingSpecificNonProprietary "The collection of constants relevant to The semiconductor device fabrication domain that represent general concepts not specific to semiconductor manufacturing.  These terms may be distributed in the Cyc Knowledge Base without restriction.")
(comment SemiconductorDomainConstant-ManufacturingSpecificNonProprietary-SOW1 "The collection of constants relevant to The semiconductor device fabrication domain that represent general concepts specific to semiconductor manufacturing.  These terms may be distributed in the Cyc Knowledge Base after a restriction period.")
(comment positivelyDependsOn "(#$positivelyDependsOn SET DEP-PRED INDEP-PRED) means that the second arguments to DEP-PRED are positively dependent on those for INDEP-PRED, when elements of ?SET appear in the arg1 position.  In other words, given the range of bindings for DEP-VAL and INDEP-VAL in (#$and (#$elementOf X SET)(DEP-PRED X DEP-VAL) (INDEP-PRED X INDEP-VAL)), whenever INDEP-VAL is high for a particular X, DEP-VAL will also be high and whenever INDEP-VAL is low, DEP-VAL will be low.   Unlike the more general #$positivelyCorrelatedWith, #$positivelyDependsOn means that there is some causal link from INDEP-PRED affecting arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED.  See also #$dependsOn-Pairwise.")
(comment typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency "(#$typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency TEMP-THING-TYPE EVENT-TYPE ROLE FREQ) means that instances of TEMP-THING-TYPE play ROLE in instances of EVENT-TYPE at the rate FREQ.  For example,
<p>
(#$typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$Cheerleader #$Cheering #$performedBy #$Daily)
</p>
means that cheerleaders cheer on a daily basis.  Similarly,
<p>
(#$typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency  (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn (#$GameFn #$CollegeFootball-CW) #$competingAgents (#$CollegeFootballTeamFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin)) #$CollegeFootballSeason #$properSubEventTypes #$Weekly)
</p>
means that games involving the Texas Longhorns football team occur weekly throughout any college football season.")
(comment individualPlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency "(#$individualPlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency TEMP-THING EVENT-TYPE ROLE FREQ) means that the individual, TEMP-THING, plays ROLE in instances of EVENT-TYPE at the rate FREQ.  For example,
<p>
(#$individualPlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$BarackObama (#$GameFn #$Basketball-TheGame) #$participatingPlayers #$Weekly)
</p>
means that Barack Obama plays basketball weekly.")
(comment playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency "(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency THING EVENT-TYPE ROLE FREQ) means that THING (or instances of THING, if THING is a collection) plays ROLE in instances of EVENT-TYPE at the rate FREQ.  For example,
<p>
(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$Cheerleader #$Cheering #$performedBy #$Daily)
</p>
means that cheerleaders cheer on a daily basis.  Similarly,
<p>
(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency  (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn (#$GameFn #$CollegeFootball-CW) #$competingAgents (#$CollegeFootballTeamFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin)) #$CollegeFootballSeason #$properSubEventTypes #$Weekly)
</p>
means that games involving the Texas Longhorns football team occur weekly throughout any college football season.  Also,
<p>
(#$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency #$BarackObama (#$GameFn #$Basketball-TheGame) #$participatingPlayers #$Weekly)
</p>
means that Barack Obama plays basketball weekly.
<p>
This predicate ahs two significant typed specializations, #$playsRoleInTypeWithFrequency and #$typePlaysRoleInTypeWithFrequency (qq.v).")
(comment fnTypeHeritableThroughDecCallDependence "Where FN-TYPE is a known class of #$CodingFunction, (fnTypeHeritableThroughDecCallDependence FN-TYPE) means that a function whose #$FunctionDeclaration depends (#$codeStatementDependsOnStatement) on a call (#$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) to a function that is an instance of FN-TYPE is also an instance of FN-TYPE.")
(comment ReadFileExFn "The #$ReadFileExFn reads data from the specified file or input/output (I/O) device. It reports its completion status asynchronously, calling the specified completion routine when reading is completed or canceled and the calling thread is in an alertable wait state.")
(comment Anthracite "A specialization of #$Coal.  Anthracite is a dense variety of coal that burns with a smokeless flame.")
(comment CoalTypeByGrade "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Coal whose instances are all of the same grade.")
(comment SubBituminousCoal "The collection of all sub-bituminous coal. A #$NaturalResourceType and an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment BituminousCoal "The collection of all bituminous coal. A #$NaturalResourceType and an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment Petroleum-CrudeOilTypeByGravity "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Petroleum-CrudeOil whose instances are all of the same gravity.")
(comment OilField "A specialization of #$MineralField.  Each instance of #$OilField is a region -- developed or not -- that is naturally rich in petroleum.  For commercially developed oil fields, see the specialization #$OilField-Developed.")
(comment Wire-IntegratedCircuit "The collection of all wires in integrated circuits generically considered as conduits through which current is designed to flow.  This includes such things as contacts, resistors, etc.")
(comment SemiconductorMaterialsDataMt "A microtheory that collects information pertaining to the basic physical/electrical properties of the materials used in the manufacture of integrated circuits.")
(comment ParsingTest "Each instance of #$ParsingTest is a specification of a test that includes an NL string (see #$inputStringForParsingTest) and one or more CycL expressions (see #$cycLOutputForParsingTest).  A parser will pass the test if and only if it produces the CycL as output when given the string as input.")
(comment ParsingTestForInputStringFn "(#$ParsingTestForInputStringFn STRING) denotes the instance of #$ParsingTest in which STRING is the input (see #$inputStringForParsingTest).")
(comment cycLOutputForParsingTest "<code>(#$cycLOutputForParsingTest TEST CYCL-EXPRESSION)</code> means that <code>CYCL-EXPRESSION</code> is a CycL target for the parsing test <code>TEST</code>. Note that there may be multiple CycL expressions associated with any particular instance of #$ParsingTest.")
(comment IterationCodeStatement "The collection of all #$CompoundComputerCodeStatements which specify iterative execution relative to some specified or implicit-but-resolvable condition.")
(comment WhileStatement "A class of #$IterationCodeStatements found in programs authored using members of the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily.  A #$WhileStatement specifies that the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement be iteratively executed for as long as the value resolved by evaluating the #$conditionExpressionOfWhileStatement is nonzero at the start of loop execution.")
(comment ForStatement "A class of #$IterationCodeStatements found in programs authored using members of the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily. Every #$ForStatement features exactly three #$ConditionExpressions and one #$subStatementOfIterationStatement.  The first condition, the #$initializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement, specifies the initial settings of any relevant variables prior to entering the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement.  The #$terminationConditionExpressionOfForStatement specifies the test condition for terminating the iteration loop.  Finally, the #$reInitializingConditionExpressOfForStatement is evaluated after each iteration, and thus specifies a re-initialization for the loop.  The #$subStatementOfIterationStatement specifies the process to be iterated.")
(comment conditionExpressionOfForStatement "A predicate which links a given #$ForStatement to each of its three #$ConditionExpressions.  Its key spec-preds are #$initializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement, #$terminationConditionExpressionOfForStatement, and #$reInitializingConditionExpressOfForStatement.")
(comment initializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement "(#$initializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement FOR-STATE INIT) means that INIT gives the initializing values for the relevant variables to be used in the iterative loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of FOR-STATE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$InitializingConditionOfForStatementFn")
(comment InitializingConditionOfForStatementFn "A #$ReifiableFunction for referencing the initializing expression of a given #$ForStatement.  Where FOR-STATE is a #$ForStatement, (#$InitializingConditionOfForStatementFn FOR-STATE) denotes the #$ConditionExpression that specifies the initial settings of any relevant variables prior to entering the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of FOR-STATE.  See also the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical), #$initializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement.")
(comment terminationConditionExpressionOfForStatement "(#$terminationConditionExpressionOfForStatement FOR-STATE TERM) means that TERM states the test condition for terminating the iterative loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of FOR-STATE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$TerminationConditionOfForStatementFn.")
(comment TerminationConditionOfForStatementFn "A #$ReifiableFunction for referencing the statement of the termination condition for a given #$ForStatement.  Where FOR-STATE is a #$ForStatement, (#$TerminationConditionOfForStatementFn FOR-STATE) denotes the #$ConditionExpression that specifies the test condition for terminating the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of FOR-STATE.  See also the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) #$terminationConditionExpressionOfForStatement.")
(comment reInitializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement "(#$reinitializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement FOR-STATE RE-INIT) means that RE-INIT specifies relevant variable settings for re-entrance into the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of FOR-STATE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of $ReInitializingConditionOfForStatementFn.")
(comment ReInitializingConditionOfForStatementFn "A #$ReifiableFunction for referencing the specification of the re-entrant settings of the relevant variables relative to the iteration loop given by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of a #$ForStatement.  Where FOR-STATE is a #$ForStatement, (#$ReInitializingConditionOfForStatementFn FOR-STATE) denotes the #$ConditionExpression that states the internal initialization settings for the variables prior to each successive execution of the iteration loop.  See also the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) #$reInitializingConditionExpressionOfForStatement.")
(comment conditionExpressionOfWhileStatement "(#$conditionExpressionOfWhileStatement WHILE-STATE TEST) means that TEST states the test condition that must return a nonzero value prior to re-entering the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of WHILE-STATE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of ConditionExpressionOfWhileStatementFn.")
(comment ConditionExpressionOfWhileStatementFn "A #$ReifiableFunction for specifying the expression of the test condition for a given #$WhileStatement.  (#$ConditionExpressionOfWhileStatementFn WHILE-STATE) denotes the #$ConditionExpression which states a test that must return a non-zero value in order for a program execution to re-enter the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of WHILE-STATE.  See also the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical), #$conditionExpressionOfWhileStatement.")
(comment conditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatement "(#$conditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatement WHILE-STATE TEST) means that TEST states the test condition that must return a nonzero value after executing the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of WHILE-STATE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of ConditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatementFn.")
(comment ConditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatementFn "A #$ReifiableFunction for specifying the expression of the test condition for a given #$DoWhileStatement.  (#$ConditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatementFn WHILE-STATE) denotes the #$ConditionExpression which states a test that must return a non-zero value after a program execution has executed the iteration loop specified by the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement of WHILE-STATE, in order for execution to continue.  See also the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical), #$conditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatement.")
(comment conditionExpressionOfIterationStatement "A predicate for linking instances of #$IterationStatement to the #$ConditionExpressions stating initialization settings or test conditions for execution of the #$IterationStatement's iteration loop (#$subStatementOfIterationStatement).  Important specializations are #$conditionExpressionOfForStatement, #$conditionExpressionOfWhileStatement, and #$conditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatement.")
(comment conditionExpressionOfStatement "The most general predicate for linking a #$ComputerCodeStatement to a #$ComputerCodeExpression that is used to give execution parameters or conditions for the statement.  Important specializations are #$ifExpressionOfSelectionCodeStatement and #$conditionExpressionOfIterationStatement.")
(comment subStatementOfIterationStatement "(#$subStatementOfIterationStatement ITER-STATE LOOP-STATE) means that LOOP-STATE is the subordinate #$ComputerCodeStatement which specifies the iterated procedure of ITER-STATE.  In the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily, every #$IterationStatement contains exactly one #$subStatementOfIterationStatement, and one or more #$conditionExpressionOfIterationStatements.  See the #$IterationCodeStatement specs #$ForStatement, #$WhileStatement and #$DoWhileStatement and their relata for additional restrictions concerning the condition expressions.")
(comment SubStatementOfIterationStatementFn "Where ITER-STATE is an #$IterationCodeStatement (more specifically, a #$ForStatement, a #$WhileStatemetn, or a #$DoWhileStatement), (#$SubStatementOfIterationStatementFn ITER-STATE) denotes the subordinate #$ComputerCodeStatement that specifies the procedure to be iterated in association with the execution of ITER-STATE.  See also the #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical, #$subStatementOfIterationStatement")
(comment functionCallOfConditionExpression "(#$functionCallOfConditionExpression CONDEX FN-CALL) means that CONDEX is a #$ConditionExpression whose condition is that the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL does not result in an error, more specifically, that the #$codingFunctionInvoked in FN-CALL does not fail on the arguments which FN-CALL assigns to it.  The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical of #$FunctionCallOfConditionExpressionFn.")
(comment FunctionCallOfConditionExpressionFn "Where CONDEX is a #$ConditionExpression whose test condition is set via a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$FunctionCallOfConditionExpressionFn CONDEX) denotes the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that is used to give the test condition of CONDEX:  specifically, the requirement set by CONDEX is that the #$codingFunctionInvoked in (#$FunctionCallOfConditionExpressionFn CONDEX) does not fail on the arguments assigned to it by (#$FunctionCallOfConditionExpressionFn CONDEX).  See also #$functionCallOfConditionExpression.")
(comment nthArgAssignedInFunctionCall "Where FN-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$nthArgAssignedInFunctionCall FN-CALL N ARG) means that ARG is the Nth argument assigned to the #$codingFunctionInvoked by FN-CALL.")
(comment JumpCodeStatement "The collection of all 'jump statements' in #$ComputerCode.  Execution of a #$JumpCodeStatement terminates execution of the nearest subsuming embedded process and transfers control unconditionally to the #$CodeStatement which it specifies.")
(comment ReturnStatement "The collection of all 'return statements in #$ComputerCode.  When a #$ReturnStatement specifies a #$ComputerCodeExpression, this expression is passed to the caller of the #$CodingFunction in whose definition the #$ReturnStatement appears.")
(comment EnhancedOilRecovery "A general category of #$ExtractingPetroleum in which more complex techniques than one would see in #$PrimaryOilRecovery or #$SecondaryOilRecovery are used to extract oil that is too difficult to extract using techniques associated with the other two general categories.")
(comment isAPieceOf "(#$isAPieceOf OBJ STUFF) means that the partially tangible OBJ is composed entirely of the material STUFF in such a way that entails it is an instance of the #$TangibleStuffCompositionType STUFF.")
(comment ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery "A specialization of #$EnhancedOilRecovery.  Each instance of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery is an event in which crude oil is heated in order to make it possible to extract the crude more efficiently.")
(comment CyclicSteamStimulation "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamInjection.  Cyclic steam stimulation is a technique for extracting crude oil which involves injecting steam into a well, allowing it to soak in the well, and then proceeding with oil production from the same well.")
(comment ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamInjection "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery. Steam injection techniques include SAGD and cyclic steam stimulation.")
(comment ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamFlooding "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamInjection.  In steam flooding, steam is injected into one or more wells to enable oil to flow more freely into other production wells.")
(comment WellDrilling "A specialization of #$DrillingSomething.  Each instance of #$WellDrilling is an event in which a well is drilled.")
(comment DirectionalDrilling "A specialization of #$WellDrilling.  Each instance of #$DirectionalDrilling is an event in which a non-vertical well is drilled.")
(comment VerticalWell "A specialization of #$Well.  Each instance of #$VerticalWell is a well that is drilled from the surface more or less directly toward the center of the Earth.")
(disjointWith NonVerticalWell VerticalWell)
(comment TBXAS1-Human-GIS "The collection of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS instances that code for proteins of the #$ThromboxaneASynthase1 class.")
(comment PhysicalGeneTypeOfGene-GISFn "Where GIS is a genetic information structure that is an instance of #$Gene-GIS, (#$PhysicalGeneTypeOfGene-GISFn GIS) denotes the collection of physical genes, i.e., specs of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit, which instantiate GIS (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS.)  Note each instance of #$Gene-GIS represents a single, specific sequence of nucleotides, and does not admit variation that may occur between two individuals for the same gene, or even between a single individual's two chromosomes.  Therefore, the instances of (#$PhysicalGeneTypeOfGene-GISFn GIS) are physical genes instantiating the same specific sequence of nucleotides.")
(comment PTGS1-Human-GIS "The collection of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS instances that code for proteins of the #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase1 class.")
(comment PTGS2-Human-GIS "The collection of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS that code for proteins of the #$ProstaglandinG-HSynthase2 class.")
(comment AVPR2-Human-GIS "The collection of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS that code for proteins of the #$VasopressinV2Receptor class. (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com)")
(comment AVPR1A-Human-GIS "The #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS that codes for proteins of the #$VasopressinV1aReceptor class. (LinkedLife data: http://www.linkedlifedata.com)")
(disjointWith Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil (CollectionDifferenceFn Petroleum-HeavyCrudeOil Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil))
(comment Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil "A specialization of #$Petroleum-HeavyCrudeOil.  Extra heavy crude oil is a kind of oil with an API gravity of less than 10.0.  It is called \"bitumen\", and is found in the oil sands deposits in Alberta, Canada.  Extra heavy crude oil, unlike most other crude, is solid under normal ambient conditions.")
(comment VaporExtractionProcess "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery.  As in #$SteamAssistedGravityDrainage, each instance of #$VaporExtractionProcess involves drilling two horizontal wells, one a few meters below the other.  Hydrocarbon solvents are injected into the upper well.  The solvents dilute bitumen and lower its viscosity, causing it to flow via the force of gravity into the lower well.")
(comment InSituCombustion "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery.  During each instance of #$InSituCombustion, air is injected to the oil reservoir to ignite it and thereby to reduce the viscosity of the oil. The air is injected into a vertical well and the oil is then produced from a horizontal well.")
(comment WellInjection "A specialization of #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomething and #$FluidFlowEvent.  In each instance of #$WellInjection, some fluid is injected into a #$Well.")
(disjointWith ProductionWell InjectorWell)
(comment ElectricalResistanceOfObjectFn "<code>(#$ElectricalResistanceOfObjectFn  OBJ)</code> represents the quantity of #$Ohms of resistance of OBJ.  This is the corresponding function to #$electricalResistanceOfObject.")
(comment SemiconductorManufacturingConceptsMt "A microtheory that collects information pertaining to the basic semiconductor manufacturing concepts and device descriptions.")
(comment SemiconductorQueryMt "A microtheory used for querying about semiconductor devices, processes, etc.")
(comment SystemForFn "<code>(#$SystemForFn ACTIVITY)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$FunctionalSystem that are systems for implementing instances of <code>ACTIVITY<code>, a collection of events.")
(comment systemTypeForEventType "The predicate that corresponds to #$SystemForFn, <code>(#$systemTypeForEventType SYSTEM-TYPE ACTIVITY)</code> identifies <code>SYSTEM-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$FunctionalSystem that are systems for implementing instances of <code>ACTIVITY<code>, a collection of events.")
(comment SemiconductorWaferLayer "The collection of all deposited layers of some substance or other over a (usually) silicon base in semiconductor device manufacturing.")
(comment MetalLayer-SemiconductorDevice "The collection of all deposited layers of metal based substances on a semiconductor device during the fabrication stage.")
(comment InsulatingLayer-SemiconductorDevice "The collection of all deposited layers of non-conductive materials on a semiconductor device during the fabrication stage.")
(comment DielectricLayer-SemiconductorDevice "The collection of all deposited layers of dielectric materials on a semiconductor device during the fabrication stage.")
(comment Contact-IntegratedCircuit "The collection of contacts in integrated circuits defined as a vertical wire between two layers that bridges the connection between a wire on each layer.")
(comment collRelationUnique "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that relates a predicate to a pair of collections such that each instance of the first (second) collection is related by the predicate to (from) exactly one instance of the second (first) collection.  Thus, <code>(#$collRelationUnique PRED COL1 COL2)</code> is true if and only if both of these are true:
<pre>
  (#$relationAllExistsUnique PRED COL1 COL2)

  (#$relationExistsUniqueAll PRED COL1 COL2)
</pre>
For example,
<pre>
  (#$collRelationUnique #$internalParts #$Thigh #$Femur)
</pre>
means that (i) every thigh has or had a unique femur inside it and (ii) every
femur is or was inside a unique thigh.")
(comment AirPathThroughSolid "A collection of paths; a subset of #$PathThroughSolid.  Each element of #$AirPathThroughSolid is a region of open space extending from at least one portal on the surface of a solid, into the interior.  The portal may be open to surrounding air (as with a highway tunnel), or it may be covered.  Some elements of #$AirPathThroughSolid go `all the way through' the solid; such paths have at least two portals.  See also #$Portal and #$Cavity.")
(comment Wellbore "A specialization of #$PathThroughSolid and #$PathArtifact.  Wellbores are holes drilled to be critical parts of wells (see #$Well).  Generally, as part of a well, a wellbore will be used either to inject fluid material into the Earth, or to extract fluid material from the Earth.")
(comment VerticalWellbore "A specialization of #$Wellbore.  Horizontal wellbores are wellbores that run at least roughly perpendicular to the surface of the Earth.")
(comment HorizontalWell "A specialization of #$NonVerticalWell.  Each instance of #$HorizontalWell is a well that significantly utilizes a #$HorizontalWellbore.")
(comment NonVerticalWellbore "A specialization of #$Wellbore.  Non-vertical wellbores are wellbores that do not run at least roughly perpendicular to the surface of the Earth.")
(comment SAGDUpperHorizontalWellbore "A specialization of #$HorizontalWellbore.  SAGD horizontal wellbores are wellbores parts of #$SAGDUpperWells.  They run parallel to and a few meters above #$SAGDLowerHorizontalWellbores.")
(comment SAGDLowerHorizontalWellbore "A specialization of #$HorizontalWellbore.  SAGD horizontal wellbores are wellbores parts of #$SAGDLowerWells.  They run parallel to and a few meters below #$SAGDUpperHorizontalWellbores.")
(disjointWith VerticalWellbore NonVerticalWellbore)
(comment NonVerticalWell "A specialization of #$Well.  Each instance of #$NonVerticalWell is a well with a #$Wellbore that is created via #$DirectionalDrilling, and which is therefore non-vertical.")
(comment VolatileOrganicCompound "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound.  Volitale organic compounds are organic chemical compounds which evaporate at ordinary ambient conditions, and which can have a negative effect on human health.")
(comment Ethylbenzene "The collection of all ethylbenzene. A #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment HorizontalWellbore "A specialization of #$NonVerticalWellbore.  Horizontal wellbores are wellbores that run at least roughly parallel to the surface of the Earth.")
(comment UsingSteamToHeatHeavyOil-ExtractionTechnique "The collection of instances of #$HeatingOfHeavyOil-ExtractionTechnique in which the heavy oil is heated with steam.")
(comment HeatingOfHeavyOil-ExtractionTechnique "The step in #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery in which the oil is heated to enable its extraction.")
(comment heatTransferDestination "A typed specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$energyTransferredTo, <code>(#$heatTransferDestination TRANSFER TANGIBLE)</code> means that in the instance <code>TRANSFER</code> of #$TemperatureChangingProcess, heat (see #$ThermalEnergy) is transferred to <code>TANGIBLE</code>, an instance of #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment heatTransferSource "A typed specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$energyTransferredFrom, <code>(#$heatTransferSource TRANSFER TANGIBLE)</code> means that in the instance <code>TRANSFER</code> of #$TemperatureChangingProcess, heat (see #$ThermalEnergy) is transferred from <code>TANGIBLE</code>, an instance of #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment energyTransferred "<code>(#$energyTransferred TRANSFER ENERGY)</code> means that <code>ENERGY</code> is some of the #$EnergyStuff that is transfered in <code>TRANSFER</code>, an instance of #$EnergyTransferEvent.")
(comment UsingGravityToMoveAnObject "The collection of events in which, as part of some larger process, gravity is applied as a means to move an object.")
(comment UsingGravityToMovePetroleumIntoAProductionWell "The specialization of #$UsingGravityToMoveAnObject wherein gravity is used to move petroleum into a production well.")
(comment MovingPetroleumIntoAProductionWell "A specialization of #$ForceAffectingAnObjectsMovement, this is the collection of events in which petroleum is moved from some location into a production well so that it can be retrieved.")
(comment CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn "#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn is a collection denoting function that takes an individual denoting function, a collection, TYPE, and an integer representing an arg position of the function, ARG-NUM, to the collection of values returned by FUNCTION by the instances of TYPE in ARG-NUM.  For instance, (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$GovernmentFn  #$City  1) denotes the subcollection of the range of #$GovernmentFn such that each corresponding element in the domain is an instance of #$City -- i.e. the collection of city governments.  For binary or higher arity functions, the other argument places are not restricted.  E.g.,  (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$StreetNamedFn #$MetropolitanArea  1) refers to the collection of streets in instances of #$MetropolitanArea  while (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn #$StreetNamedFn (StringOfMaximumLengthFn 6) 2) is the collection of streets that can be referred to by strings with a maximum length of 6.  In set-theoretic terms, for any FUNCTION, COLL, NUM (#$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn FUNCTION COLL NUM) denotes the maximal subcollection of the range of COLL such that every NUMth element in the domain of FUNCTION is an instance of COLL.")
(comment collectionOfValuesFromFnApplicationToArg "This is the corresponding predicate to #$CollectionOfValuesForFunctionFn.  (#$collectionOfValuesFromFnApplicationToArg FUNCTION COLL NUM VALUE-COLL) menas that VALUE-COLL is the collection of values achieved by applying FUNCTION to each instance of COLL (A subcollection of the NUMth argument position of FUNCTION) along with any other arguments (if FUNCTION is binary or higher).  That is, VALUE-COLL is that subset of the range of FUNCTION such that each NUMth element in its domain is an instance of COLL.")
(comment ICContactCoupling "The collection of all complex objects that consists in a #$Contact-IntegratedCircuit that is connected to wires at the top and bottom in an integrated circuit.")
(comment programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToStatement "(#$programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToStatement PROGRAM CODE-BLOCK ACTION-TYPE) means that if PROGRAM is executed on a computing architecture in typical run-time conditions, there is a non-trivial potential of the architecture exhibiting #$ComputerActivity of type ACTION-TYPE due to the presence of CODE-BLOCK within PROGRAM")
(comment CartilageTypeByCompositionType "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$Cartilage into subcollections based on their protein composition and organization at the microscopic level.")
(comment HyalineCartilage "Instances are portions of #$Cartilage tissue which are elastic and translucent, with an #$ExtracellularMatrix composed mostly of #$Collagen-TypeII and chondroitin sulfate (see #$ChondroitinSulfateChain).")
(comment ElasticCartilage "Instances are portions of #$Cartilage tissue which are elastic and similar to #$HyalineCartilage, with an #$ExtracellularMatrix composed of #$Collagen-TypeII and elastic fibers.")
(comment Fibrocartilage "Instances are portions of #$Cartilage tissue which are composed of thick bundles of #$Collagen fibers.  Both #$Collagen-TypeI and #$Collagen-TypeII are present.")
(comment ArticularCartilageStructure "Each instance of #$ArticularCartilageStructure is the entire contiguous piece of #$HyalineCartilage that covers the end of a bone which participates in a #$SynovialJoint with another bone.  Typically all bones in a #$SynovialJoint have an #$ArticularCartilageStructure covering their surfaces that might rub against another bone in the joint.")
(comment ArticularCartilage "Instances are any portion of the #$HyalineCartilage tissue covering the surface of a bone where it can contact another bone in a #$SynovialJoint, This includes every #$ArticularCartilageStructure as well as any sub-portion thereof.")
(comment Contact-WireJointCrossSection "The collection of 2-dimensional cross-sections of the joints or connection points between a #$Contact-IntegratedCircuit and a wire it is connected to in the context of an #$ICContactCoupling.  the contact resistance is inversely related to the area of this cross-section -- i.e. as the area increases, the contact resistance decreases.")
(comment ICContact-WireJoint "The collection of joints between a #$Contact-IntegratedCircuit and a #$Wire-IntegratedCircuit in a integrated circuit device.")
(comment ConcentrationSlotFn "<code>(#$ConcentrationSlotFn STUFFTYPE)</code> denotes the #$BinaryPredicate, PRED, such that (PRED OBJ CONCENTRATION) states that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ has a #$constituents of type STUFFTYPE at CONCETRATION.")
(comment concentrationSlotFor "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for #$ConcentrationSlotFn, <code>(#$concentrationSlotFor CONCENTRATION-SLOT STUFFTYPE)</code> identifies <code>CONCENTRATION-SLOT</code> as the binary predicate which relates a thing to its concentration of <code>STUFFTYPE</code>")
(comment BloodstreamPlasma "An instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType.  Instances are the total physical extent of blood plasma (See #$BloodPlasma) in an individual animal.")
(comment HighValueForFn "A #$ScalarDenotingFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$QuantitySlot and returns a #$GenericQuantity of the type required by the #$arg2Isa of the #$QuantitySlot. .   In a given context, <code>(#$HighValueForFn QUANTSLOT)</code>, where <code>QUANTTYPE</code> is the #$arg2Isa of <code>QUANTSLOT</code>, is the properly interval-like quantity that is considered a <i>high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.
")
(comment ResistanceOfAConductor-UsingCrossSection-DCFormula "The formula to determine resistance in Ohms of a conductor (for DC).  The formula is R = (p * L)/A where R = resistance in Ohms, p = the bulk conductivity of the substance of which the conductor is composed in Ohms-meters, L = the length of the conductor in meters, and A = the YZ cross-section area of the conductor or (for conductors embedded into a device) the area of the smallest cross-section where it connects to the source or drain in square meters.")
(comment HighLevelTalks "A specialization of #$DiplomaticEvent-Intergovernmental.  High-level talks are communications between top envoys of national governments.")
(comment PascalSecond "A unit of dynamic viscosity.")
(disjointWith BulkResistance Molarity)
(disjointWith Temperature BulkResistance)
(disjointWith AngularDistance BulkResistance)
(disjointWith Voltage BulkResistance)
(disjointWith Volume BulkResistance)
(disjointWith Pressure BulkResistance)
(disjointWith ElectricalCharge BulkResistance)
(disjointWith Mass BulkResistance)
(comment bulkResistivityOfStuffType "<code>(#$bulkResistivityOfStuffType STUFF-TYPE OHMS-M)</code> means that instances of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> have this <code>OHMS-M</code> of #$ElectricalResistance measured in Ohms-meters ((#$UnitProductFn #$Ohm #$Meter)).")
(comment BulkResistance "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$BulkResistance is a measure of the intrinsic resistance to electrical flow through a type of stuff.  Its SI unit of measure is the ohm-meter --(#$UnitProductFn #$Meter #$Ohm)  .")
(comment slotsUsedInFormula "(#$slotsUsedInFormula REIFIED-FORMULA PRED-COLL) means that PRED-COLL is the collection of quantity slots used to attribute the quantites involved in REIFIED-FORMULA.")
(comment SlotCollectionForFormulaFn "(#$SlotCollectionForFormulaFn REIFIED-FORMULA) refers the collection of quantity slots used to attribute the quantites involved in REIFIED-FORMULA.")
(comment unitSlotsForFormula "(#$unitSlotsForFormula QBF QUANTITY SLOT) means that the QUANTITY as it is used in QBF is measured using SLOT.")
(comment conventionalUnitsForFormula "(#$conventionalUnitsForFormula QBF QUANTITY UNIT means that the QUANTITY as it is used in QBF is conventionally expressed in UNIT.  This means that when answers to queries that employ this formula should be converted into the conventional unit for that quantity.")
(comment Endosteum "The inner surfaces of the #$MedullaryCavity of bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart) is lined with the #$Endosteum, which is a thin membrane of #$ConnectiveTissue.")
(comment BoneFormationDuringGrowth "The collection of events in which mineralized bone tissue is formed during the growth and development of #$Vertebrates.")
(comment BoneFormation "The collection of events in which bone (hard, mineralized tissue) is formed.  Bone can be formed during the growth and development of #$Vertebrates (see #$BoneFormationDuringGrowth).  It also forms during healing of injuries to bones (see #$BoneFormationInFractureRepair).  Bone forms during the ongoing process of skeletal remodeling (see #$BoneFormationInRemodeling). Finally, bone can form in places where it shouldn't, in response to disease or injury (see #$EctopicBoneFormation).
<p>
Bone formation is one part of a complex process resulting in the production of a mature instance of #$Bone-BodyPart, such as a particular #$Femur or #$Clavicle.  For that process, see #$BoneBodyPartGrowthAndDevelopment.")
(comment BoneBodyPartGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a bone (see #$Bone-BodyPart) is created, grows, and matures into its adult form.")
(comment VertebrateGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a #$Vertebrate organism is created, grows, and matures into its adult form.")
(comment SkeletalSystemGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a #$VertebrateSkeleton is created, grows, and matures into its adult form.")
(comment Perichondrium "The surfaces of body parts made of #$ElasticCartilage and #$HyalineCartilage, including the cartilage portions of developing bone, are covered with the #$Perichondrium, which is a dense layer of irregular, fibrous connective tissue.  #$ArticularCartilage and #$Fibrocartilage do not have a #$Perichondrium covering.")
(comment EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a bone (see #$Bone-BodyPart) is created, grows, and matures into its adult form, via a process in which the bone is initially shaped in #$HyalineCartilage that is eventually replaced with bone (see #$BoneTheStuff).")
(comment DevelopingBone-BodyPart "Instances of #$DevelopingBone-BodyPart are body parts of a young #$Vertebrate organism which will grow and develop into mature instances of #$Bone-BodyPart. In the early stage of this process, before bone mineral has begun to accumulate, these parts can't be called bones.")
(comment DevelopingBone-Precartilage "Instances are tight aggregation of cells in a #$Vertebrate which are committed to becoming the #$Chondrocytes. These cells will produce the cartilage model on which #$EndochondralBoneFormation will occur.")
(comment OsteochondralProgenitorCell "A specialization of #$AdultStemCell. Each instance of #$OsteochondralProgenitorCell is a multipotent stem cell with the ability to differentiate into #$Osteoblasts or #$Chondrocytes,")
(comment DevelopingBone-CartilageModel "Instances are #$HyalineCartilage structures which are in the process of growing and developing into bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart.  In this type of structure, ossification (deposition of #$BoneMineral) has not yet begun.")
(comment Osteoporosis "Osteoporsosis is bone disease characterized by a low  bone mineral density.")
(comment variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWithConditionType "<code>(#$variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWith GENE-TYPE CONDITION-TYPE)</code> means that a study has found that, in some population of individuals, variation in <code>GENE-TYPE</code> is associated with the physiological condition type <code>CONDITION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typicalFocalIsaForFormula "(#$typicalFocalIsaForFormula QBF COLL) means that the things that are typically involved with QBF are instances of COLL.")
(comment onLineURLReferenceForMicrofabTerm "(#$onLineURLReferenceForMicrofabTerm TERM URL) means that URL is a public domain #$UniformResourceLocator which includes a description of TERM or salient information concerning TERM.")
(comment MicrofabricationProcess "The collection of all instances of the intersection of #$Manufacturing and #$ConfiguringEvent wherein there is at least one #$objectConfiguredDuring which is a #$MicroscopicScaleObject (defined, for semiconductor processing purposes, as a 'micron-scaled' object (#$SpatialScaleComparableIndividualsFn #$Micron) or smaller.")
(comment MicrofabricationProcessType "The collection of all kinds of #$MicrofabricationProcess, i.e., all specializations of #$MicrofabricationProcess via #$genls.")
(comment PositiveQuantityFormula "The collection of mathematical formulas that express some physical principle #$PhysicalPrinciple via values on some quantity slots where the quantity values are assumed to be positive.")
(comment criticalDimensionOfTypeFor "(#$criticalDimensionOfTypeFor COLL1 QUANT-TYPE COLL2) means that the values of QUANT-TYPE associated with instances of COLL2 play a large role in the properties or functionality of suitably related instances of COLL1.  For example, the spark plug gap for a gasoline internal combustion engine is a critical dimension for the ignition systems for such vehicles -- (#$criticalDimensionOfTypeFor #$Automobile-GasolineEngine DistanceBetweenGroundAndCentralElectrode #$SparkPlug) .")
(comment XChromosome-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$SexChromosome.  Normally, male humans have one unduplicated copy of the \"X\"chromosome in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes, whereas normally female humans have two unduplicated copies of the \"X\"chromosome in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment geneTypeFoundOnChromosomeType "(#$geneTypeFoundOnChromosomeType GENE-GIS-TYPE CHROMOSOME-TYPE) means that instantiations of instances of GENE-GIS-TYPE are on instances of CHROMOSOME-TYPE.")
(comment GeneTypeOfTaxonFn "Where TAXON is a #$BiologicalTaxon, (#$GeneTypeOfTaxonFn TAXON) denotes the collection of genetic information structures, i.e., specs of #$Gene-GIS, which are instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) in the DNA of some individual organism belonging to TAXON. For example, (#$GeneTypeOfTaxonFn #$Mammal) denotes the collection of all mammalian genetic information structures.")
(comment GeneTypeByTaxon "A collection of collections of #$GeneticInformationStructures. Each instance GIS-TYPE of this collection is composed of instances of #$Gene-GIS such that each is a sequence that is instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) as a physical gene in the genetic material of members of the same #$BiologicalTaxon. Examples include (#$GeneTypeOfTaxonFn #$Mammal).")
(comment GeneTypeBySpecies "A collection of collections of #$GeneticInformationStructures. Each instance GIS-TYPE of this collection is composed of instances of #$Gene-GIS such that each is a sequence that is instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) as a physical gene in the genetic material of members of the same #$BiologicalSpecies. Examples include (#$GeneTypeOfSpeciesFn #$HomoSapiens).")
(comment geneTypeForSpecies "(#$geneTypeForSpecies GIS-TYPE SPECIES) states that the collection, GIS-TYPE (a specialization of #$Gene-GIS), is the collection of all genetic information structures which are instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) in the DNA of individual organisms which are members of SPECIES.")
(comment GeneTypeOfSpeciesFn "Where SPECIES is a #$BiologicalSpecies, (#$GeneTypeOfSpeciesFn SPECIES) denotes the collection of genetic information structures, i.e., specs of #$Gene-GIS, which are instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) in the DNA of some individual organism belonging to SPECIES. For example, (#$GeneTypeOfSpeciesFn #$HomoSapiens) denotes the collection of all human genetic information structures.")
(comment geneTypeForTaxon "(#$geneTypeForTaxon GIS-TYPE TAXON) states that the collection, GIS-TYPE (a specialization of #$Gene-GIS), is the collection of all genetic information structures which are instantiated (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) in the DNA of individual organisms which are members of TAXON.")
(comment variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWithConditionTypeInPopulation "<code>(#$variationInGeneTypeAssociatedWithConditionTypeInPopulation GENE-TYPE CONDITION-TYPE ORGANISM-TYPE)</code> means that a study has found that, in a population of individuals of type <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code>, variation in <code>GENE-TYPE</code> is associated with the physiological condition type <code>CONDITION-TYPE</code>.")
(comment criticalDimensionRepresentedViaSlot "(#$criticalDimensionRepresentedViaSlot    COLL QUANT-TYPE SLOT) means that QUANT-TYPE is a critical dimension for instances of COLL and that the relationship between COLL and the QUANT-TYPE is represented with SLOT.")
(comment DrainingProcess " A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$DrainingProcess is an event in which a fluid is drained from a reservoir.")
(comment WellOutflow-Natural "A specialization of #$WellOutflow.  In each instance of #$WellOutflow-Natural, a fluid flows out of a #$Well naturally, without the aid of artificial lift devices.")
(comment WellOutflow-ArtificiallyLifted "A specialization of #$WellOutflow.  In each instance of #$WellOutflow-ArtificiallyLifted, a fluid flows out of a #$Well with the aid of artificial lift devices.")
(comment ElectricalSubmersiblePump "A specialization of #$ArtificialLiftDevice.  Each instance of #$ElectricalSubmersiblePump is a pump used to increase the outflow rate of a well.  ESPs are submersed into a well, and are supplied powered from the surface.")
(comment ProgressingCavityPump "A specialization of #$ArtificialLiftDevice.  Each instance of #$ProgressingCavityPump is a device used to increase the outflow rate of a well.  A PCP transfers fluid by means of causing fluid to move through the sequence of small cavities within the pump.")
(comment PositiveDisplacementPump "A specialization of #$Pump-Mechanical.  Positive displacement pumps cause fluid to move by trapping a fixed amount of it then forcing it to move in the desired direction.")
(comment Pump-MechanicalTypeByStuffPumped "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Pump-Mechanical whose instances are all of the same stuff pumped.")
(comment Pump-MechanicalTypeByGeneralPumpingMechinism "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Pump-Mechanical whose instances are all of the same general pumping mechinism.")
(comment VelocityPump "A specialization of #$Pump-Mechanical.  Velocity  pumps cause fluid to move by adding kinetic energy to the fluid flow.")
(comment DarcysLaw "An instance of #$PhysicalPrinciple (q.v.).  Darcy's law describes the flow of fluid through a porous medium.")
(comment CartilageGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a bone (see #$Bone-BodyPart) is created, grows, and matures into its adult form.")
(comment CartilageGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which #$Cartilage is created, grows, and develops in the body of an organism.  Instances include events in which body parts made of #$Cartilage are produced, as well as events in which some portion of cartilage, which might be a sub-part of another body part, is produced.")
(comment FormationOfCartilageModel "Instances of #$FormationOfCartilageModel are events in which the #$OsteochondralProgenitorCells in a #$DevelopingBone-Precartilage differentiate into #$Chondrocytes and begin secreting #$ExtracellularMatrix.  An event of this type is one step in the growth and development of a #$Bone-BodyPart via #$EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment.")
(comment CartilageGrowthAndDevelopmentInEndochondralBoneDevelopment "Instances are events in which #$Cartilage is created, grows and develops as part of #$EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment.")
(comment ChondrocyteDifferentiation-MSCToChondrocyte "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$ChondrocyteDifferentiation-MSCToChondrocyte one or more #$MesenchymalStemCells participate in cell division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), and some of the daughter cells become more specialized, ultimately becoming #$Chondrocytes (perhaps after additional cell divisions).  Daughter cells not committing to the chondrocyte cell lineage remain #$MesenchymalStemCells.")
(comment ChondrocyteDifferentiation "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$ChondrocyteDifferentiation one or more cells in the chondroblastic lineage participate in cell division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), and some of the daughter cells become more specialized in the direction of becoming #$Chondrocytes.")
(comment ChondrocyteDifferentiation-OsteochondralProgenitorToChondrocyte "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$ChondrocyteDifferentiation-OsteochondralProgenitorToChondrocyte one or more #$OsteochondralProgenitorCells participate in cell division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle), and some of the daughter cells become more specialized, ultimately becoming #$Chondrocytes (perhaps after additional cell divisions).  Daughter cells not committing to the chondrocyte cell lineage remain #$OsteochondralProgenitorCells.")
(comment Metaphysis-BoneSubPart "The collection of all metaphyses. Each is a region of a #$LongBone between the diaphysis (see #$BoneShaft) and the two epiphyses (see #$BoneExtremity) and is a type of #$BoneSubPart.  Each long bone has two.")
(comment EpiphysealPlate "Instances are regions of #$HyalineCartilage tissue at each metaphysis (see #$Metaphysis-BoneSubPart) of #$LongBones in immature #$Vertebrates that are still growing. This is a region of proliferating #$Chondrocytes responsible for the increase in the length of bone as the organism grows. Older chondorcytes are pushed away from the plate, where they degenerate.  #$Osteoblasts replace this tissue with bone. ")
(comment EndochondralBoneFormation "Instances are events in which bone (see #$BoneTheStuff) is formed upon a cartilaginous \"model\" by the replacement of #$Cartilage with bone. This happens during embryonic and juvenile growth of a #$Vertebrate, for the production of the long bones of the skeleton (see #$LongBone), and is contrasted with #$IntramembranousBoneFormation, which is the way the flat bones of the #$Skull (see #$FlatBone) are formed.  Bone also forms endochondrally in the course of fracture healing.")
(comment LamellarBoneTissue "A type of bone tissue based on the organization of its collagen fibers.  In #$LamellarBoneTissue, #$Collagen fibers are organized in a regular parallel arrangement, resulting in bone that is mechanically stronger than #$WovenBoneTissue.  #$WovenBoneTissue is produced as the first kind of bone in fetal development, and after #$BoneFractures.  It is later remodeled into #$LamellarBoneTissue.")
(comment WovenBoneTissue "A type of bone tissue based on the organization of its collagen fibers.  In #$WovenBoneTissue, #$Collagen fibers are organized haphazardly, resulting in bone that is mechanically weaker than #$LamellarBoneTissue.  #$WovenBoneTissue is produced as the first kind of bone in fetal development, and after #$BoneFractures.  It is later remodeled into #$LamellarBoneTissue.")
(comment BoneFractureHealing "A collection of events in which a bone (see #$Bone-BodyPart) heals after a #$BoneFracture. Instances of #$BoneFractureHealing are triggered in normal #$Vertebrate individuals by a #$BoneFracture.")
(comment CartilageFormationInFractureRepair "Instances are events in which #$Cartilage is created, grows and develops as part of #$EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment.")
(comment WovenBoneFormationInFractureRepair "Instances are sub-events of some #$BoneFractureHealing process, in which #$WovenBoneTissue is the first kind of new bone tissue to be generated at the repair site.")
(comment BoneUnionInFractureRepair "Instances are events during #$BoneFractureHealing in which the formerly separated parts of a #$Bone-BodyPart become connected.")
(comment SoftCallus-Bone "#$SoftCallus-Bone is a #$HyalineCartilage structure formed in response to a #$BoneFracture.  It is a temporary body part that will eventually be replaced by bone.")
(comment HardCallus-Bone "#$HardCallus-Bone is a structure made of #$WovenBoneTissue formed in response to a #$BoneFracture.  It is a temporary body part that will eventually be remodeled into #$LamellarBoneTissue.")
(disjointWith WellInflow WellOutflow)
(comment inputStringForParsingTest "<code>(#$inputStringForParsingTest TEST STRING)</code> means that <code>STRING</code> is the input string for the parsing test <code>TEST</code>.")
(comment WellInflow "A specialization of #$DrainingProcess.  In each instance of #$WellInflow, a fluid flows into a #$Well from the reservoir into which it is inserted.")
(comment River-Underground "A specialization of #$River.  Each instance of #$River-Underground is a river that flows wholly or partly beneath the ground.")
(comment River "A specialization of #$Stream.  Each instance of #$River is a natural stream of water, normally of a large volume.  Instances of #$River include the #$ColoradoRiverOfArizona, the #$AmazonRiver, the #$YangtzeRiver, and the #$ThamesRiver.
<p>
For smaller streams, see #$Creek.")
(comment allProperSubSitTypesOf "(#$allProperSubSitTypesOf SIT-COL COL-TYPE) means that COL-TYPE is a collection of collections such that every collection instance of COL-TYPE is a #$properSubSituationTypes of SIT-COL.  That is, (#$allProperSubSitTypesOf SIT-COL COL-TYPE) means that a collection COL is an instance of COL-TYPE if and only if every instance of SIT-COL has some instance of COL as a #$properSubSituations.  This is the corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$AllProperSubSitTypesOfFn.")
(comment quantSlotAllInInterval "A #$TypeTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate.  (#$quantSlotAllInInterval SLOT COL RANGE) means that any value assumed by any instance of COL on the #$MeasurableQuantitySlot SLOT must be subsumed within RANGE:  that is, if (isa INST COL) and (SLOT INST VALUE), then (#$quantitySubsumes RANGE VALUE).")
(comment AllProperSubSitTypesOfFn "Where SIT-COL is a collection, each of whose instances is subject to characteristic subdivision into temporal parts that are not themselves instances of SIT-COL, (#$AllProperSubSitTypesOfFn SIT-COL) denotes the #$CollectionType consisting of every collection SUBSIT-COL such that every instance of SIT-COL has some instance of SUBSIT-COL as a #$properSubSituations, or equivalently, such that (#$properSubSituationTypes SIT-COL SUBSIT-COL)")
(comment Aquifer "The collection of all aquifers. An aquifer is an underground layer of water-bearing permeable rock, gravel, sand, or silt from which groundwater can be usefully extracted (e.g., by using a water well).")
(comment GeologicalFormation "A specialization of #$Region and #$PartiallyTangible.  The geological formation is the fundamental unit of lithostratigraphy. Each instance of #$GeologicalFormation is a layer composed of one or more geological strata (see #$GeologicalStratum) with similar properties.")
(comment GeologicalStratum "A specialization of #$Region and #$PartiallyTangible.  A geological stratum is single distinct layer of rock with homogeneous characteristics.")
(comment layerOf "(#$layerOf LAYER OBJ) means that LAYER is a #$Layer of OBJ.")
(comment inRooted-PassesThrough "Assume for the sake of explanation that the orientation of OBJ1 is vertical.  Given that, (#$inRooted-PassesThrough OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 in is embedded into OBJ2 in such a way so that the top of OBJ1 is sticks out from the top surface of OBJ2 and the bottom of OBJ1 is sticks out from the bottom surface of OBJ2.  If OBJ1 were to be removed from OBJ2, a hole that goes completely through OBJ2 would be present.  This entails that the length of OBJ1 is greater than the thickness or height of OBJ2.  For example, consider a nail that is put completely through a board.  In that case, the nail would be #$inRooted-PassesThrough the board.")
(comment in-RootedCompletelyFlush "Assume for the sake of explanation that the orientation of OBJ1 is vertical.  Given that, (#$in-RootedCompletelyFlush OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 in is embedded into OBJ2 in such a way so that the top of OBJ1 is flush with the top surface of OBJ2 and the bottom of OBJ1 is flush with the bottom surface of OBJ2.  If OBJ1 were to be removed from OBJ2, a hole that goes completely through OBJ2 would be present.  If (#$connectedPerpendicularlyTo OBJ1 OBJ2) also holds, then the length of OBJ1 is equal to the thickness or height of OBJ2.  For example, consider a nail that is put completely through a board.  If you were to snip the bottom and the top of the nail flush with the bottom and the top of the board, respectively, then the resulting nail portion would be #$in-RootedCompletelyFlush in the board.")
(comment insignificantVarietyOfType "(#$insignificantVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE) means that AB-TYPE is the collection of all insignificant or \"minor\" instances of TYPE.")
(comment significantVarietyOfType "(#$significantVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE) means that AB-TYPE is the collection of all significant or \"major\" instances of TYPE.")
(comment Chromosome12-Human "A specialization of #$HumanChromosome and #$Autosome.  Normally, humans have two unduplicated copies of chromosome 12 in diploid cells without duplicated chromosomes.")
(comment SignificantFn "(#$SignificantFn TYPE) denotes the collection of significant or \"major\" things that are instances of TYPE (a specialization of #$Individual).")
(comment InsignificantFn "(#$InsignificantFn TYPE) denotes the collection of insignificant or \"minor\" things that are instances of TYPE (a specialization of #$Individual).")
(comment relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes "(#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 BIN-PRED SLOT-1 COMP-PRED-1 SLOT-2 COMP-PRED-2 ) means that when INST-1 and INST-2 (instances of OBJ-TYPE1 and OBJ-TYPE2 respectively) stand in BIN-PRED such that (BIN-PRED INST-1 INST-2), then when the values for SLOT-1 for INST-1 COMP-PRED-1 (are greater, less, etc.) then the values for SLOT-2 for INST-2 will be COMP-PRED-1 (greater, less, etc.).  For example if a wing of an airplane is rigidly connected to the fuselage (#$connectedTo-Rigidly), then if the altitude of the fuselage goes up, then the altitude of the wing will go up -- (#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForObjectTypes #$AirplaneFuselage  #$AirplaneWing #$connectedTo-Rigidly #$altitudeAboveGround #$greaterThan #$altitudeAboveGround #$greaterThan).")
(comment in-RootedCompletelyFlushPerpendicular "(#$in-RootedCompletelyFlushPerpendicular OBJ1 OBJ2) means (#$connectedPerpendicularlyTo OBJ1 OBJ2) and (#$in-RootedCompletelyFlush OBJ1 OBJ2).")
(comment cruelVarietyOfType "(#$cruelVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE AB-EVT-TYPE) means that AB-EVT-TYPE is the collection of all particularly cruel instances of EVT-TYPE.")
(comment MercifulFn "(#$MercifulFn EVENT-TYPE) denotes the specialization of EVENT-TYPE whose instances are particularly merciful relative to ordinary instances of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment mercifulVarietyOfType "(#$mercifulVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE AB-EVT-TYPE) means that AB-EVT-TYPE is the collection of all merciful instances of EVT-TYPE.")
(comment CruelFn "(#$CruelFn EVENT-TYPE) denotes the specialization of EVENT-TYPE whose instances are particularly cruel relative to ordinary instances of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment CourageousFn "(#$CourageousFn EVENT-TYPE) denotes the specialization of EVENT-TYPE whose instances are particularly courageous relative to ordinary instances of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment courageousVarietyOfType "(#$courageousVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE AB-EVT-TYPE) means that AB-EVT-TYPE is the collection of all courageous instances of EVT-TYPE.")
(comment OfficeOfPublicOfficial "A specialization of #$GovernmentalOrganization.  Each instance of #$OfficeOfPublicOfficial is an organization that consists of a #$PublicOfficial and his or her staff #$PublicOfficial.  This staf can perform many functions, including trhe issuance of statements.")
(comment OfficeOfPublicOfficialFn "(#$OfficeOfPublicOfficialFn OFFICIAL) denotes the instance of #$OfficeOfPublicOfficial that is the office of OFFICIAL.")
(comment officialHasPublicOffice "(#$officialHasPublicOffice OFFICIAL OFFICE) means that OFFICE is the instance of #$OfficeOfPublicOfficial that is the office of the #$PublicOffical OFFICIAL.")
(comment ThinFilmDeposition "The collection of #$MicrofabricationProcess instances wherein a so-called #$ThinFilm of material is deposited onto a substrate or previously depositied #$ThinFilm layers.  Here, 'thin' has the technical sense of a layer whose thickness is measurable in nanometers (#$Nano #$Meter) or at most micrometers (#$Micron) and usually controlled to within tens of nanometers.  #$ThinFilmDeposition is a widely-applied step in #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer, also in the application of optical coatings.")
(comment ThinFilm "The collection of all so called 'thin films' generated in in #$Manufacturing, usually for purposes of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer or optical coating.  A #$ThinFilm is a solid layer of substance, with thickness between several micrometers at the most and a single atomic radius at the least, deposited via #$ThinFilmDeposition onto a target surface.")
(comment thinFilmDeposited "Where DEPOSITING is a #$ThinFilmDeposition, (#$thinFilmDeposited DEPOSITING FILM) means that FILM is the #$ThinFilm that is deposited on some surface (a substrate or a previously deposited #$ThinFilm as the result of DEPOSITING.")
(comment Stratigraphy "A #$FieldOfStudy.  Stratigraphy is the sub-field of geology that involves the study of layers of rock (i.e., instances of #$GeologicalStratum).")
(comment ThicknessFn "(#$ThicknessFn OBJ) denotes the thickness of OBJ.")
(comment CarbonateRock "The collection of all carbonate. A specialization of of #$SedimentaryRock. Carbonate rocks are formed by precipitation of CaCO3.")
(comment ClasticSedimentaryRock "The collection of all clastic sedimentary rock. A specialization of of #$SedimentaryRock. Clastic sedimentary rocks are formed by weathering, transport and deposition of debris from pre-existing rocks.")
(comment Porosity "A specialization of #$TangiblePhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Porosity is a specific porosity of some physical object.  Different porosities may be represented using #$GenericValueFunctions.  Porosities of objects are indicated with the predicate #$porosityOfObject (q.v.).")
(comment porosityOfObject-Percent "(#$porosityOfObject-Percent OBJ PERCENTAGE) means that the tangible object OBJ has PERCENTAGE #$Porosity.")
(comment Chalk "A kind of #$Limestone.")
(disjointWith MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation SinglePhaseFluidFlow-Translation)
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation "A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation is an event in which the fluid in motion is in multiple phases (i.e.,it is partly gaseous and partly liquid).")
(comment SinglePhaseFluidFlow-Translation "A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$SinglePhaseFluidFlow-Translation is an event in which the fluid in motion is in a single phase (i.e., either it is all gaseous or it is all liquid).")
(disjointWith LiquidFlow-Translation GasFlow-Translation)
(comment LiquidFlow-Translation "A specialization of #$SinglePhaseFluidFlow-Translation and #$LiquidFlowEvent.  Each instance of #$LiquidFlow-Translation is a translation event in which the fluid in motion is entirely liquid.")
(comment GasFlowEvent "The collection of instances of #$FluidFlowEvent in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is some instance(s) of #$GaseousTangibleThing.")
(disjointWith GasFlowEvent LiquidFlowEvent)
(comment GasFlow-Translation "A specialization of #$GasFlowEvent and #$SinglePhaseFluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$LiquidFlow-Translation is an event in which the fluid in motion is entirely liquid.")
(comment WealthyFn "<code>(#$WealthyFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are wealthier than ordinary.")
(comment PoorFn "<code>(#$PoorFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are more financially impoverished than ordinary.")
(comment poorVarietyOfType "<code>(#$poorVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually financially impoverished instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment wealthyVarietyOfType "<code>(#$wealthyVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all wealthy instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment YoungFn "<code>(#$YoungFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are younger than ordinary.")
(comment OldFn "<code>(#$OldFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are older than ordinary.")
(comment oldVarietyOfType "<code>(#$oldVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all old instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment youngVarietyOfType "<code>(#$youngVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all young instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment WiseFn-Agent "<code>(#$WiseFn-Agent AGENT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>AGENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$IntelligentAgent) that are wiser than ordinary.")
(comment FoolishFn-Agent "<code>(#$FoolishFn-Agent AGENT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>AGENT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$IntelligentAgent) that are more foolish than ordinary.")
(comment wiseVarietyOfType-Agent "<code>(#$oldVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all old instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment foolishVarietyOfType-Agent "<code>(#$foolishVarietyOfType-Agent AG-TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all foolish instances of <code>AG-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$IntelligentAgent).")
(disjointWith Genius (FoolishFn-Agent Person))
(comment SectarianStrife "A specialization of #$CivilUnrest and #$ConflictEvent.  Sectarian strife involves conflict between sects.")
(comment Bloodshed "A #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent.  Each instance of #$Bloodshed is an act violent enough to result in the drawing of blood.  It involves wounding and sometimes killing.")
(comment ArabCountry "The collection of nation-states that have very large Arab populations.")
(comment CivilUnrest "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$CivilUnrest is an event in which large numbers of people act out in response to major socio-political problems.  Extreme forms of civil unrest are classed as civil wars, whereas milder forms are riots and public protests.")
(comment Mating "The collection of all events in which two reproductively compatible instances of #$EukaryoticOrganism join (either literally, as in the case of single-celled eukaryotes, or figuratively, as in the case of sexual copulation (see #$SexualCopulation)) in a way that -- barring artificial obstacles to the process -- will make reproduction possible.  \"Reproductively compatible\" has a technical sense here: the participants must be instances of a shared #$OrganismClassificationType for which reproduction is possible, and they must be either a) of opposite sexes (see #$hasBiologicalSex), b) of opposite mating types (which applies to single-celled organisms -- see #$organismMatingType), or they must be hermaphroditic (e.g., worms).")
(comment MatingOfSCerevisiae "The collection of instances of #$Mating done by cells belonging to the yeast <i>saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>.")
(comment MatingOfHaploids "The collection of instances of #$Mating done by single-celled haploid organisms.")
(comment CreationOfDiploidSCerevisiaeThroughFusion "A specialization of #$BiologicalFusionEvent.  Instances are events in which a diploid yeast <i>S. cerevisiae</i> cell is created as the result of two haploid cells mating.")
(comment SCerevisiaeMatingScript "A three-stage script in which <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells \"communicate\" by secreting mating factors, causing them to physically move toward one another to a point where they begin to merge (the \"mating\") until a new cell that combines the DNA from the original cells emerges.")
(comment DiploidSCerevisiae "The collection of <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells that are diploid.")
(comment HaploidSCerevisiae "The collection of <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells that are haploid.")
(comment SCerevisiaeMatingType "A sub-collection of #$MatingType, this is a collection that facets the collection of haploid <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells into \"A\" cells and \"Alpha\" cells.")
(comment MatingType "The collection of mating types.  These are classes of single-celled haploid organisms that are reproductive \"complements\" to some other class of organisms.  This is analogous to the #$AnimalTypeBySex faceting of animals.")
(comment organismTypeHasMatingTypes "<code>(#$organismTypeHasMatingTypes ORG-TYPE M-TYPE)</code> relates a class <code>ORG-TYPE</code> of single-celled eukaryotic organisms to the mating types <code>M-TYPE</code> (see #$MatingType) defined for that organism.")
(comment SingleCellDiploidOrganism "The collection of #$SingleCellOrganism that are diploid.")
(comment SingleCellHaploidOrganism "The collection of #$SingleCellOrganism that are haploid.")
(disjointWith MatingFactor GrowthFactor)
(disjointWith SecretionOfMatingFactor EndocrinalSecretionOfHormones)
(comment SecretionOfMatingFactor "The collection of instances of #$CellularSecretionEvent in which a haploid single-celled organism secretes mating factor (see #$MatingFactor), a chemical that causes other nearby haploid cells (of the same species and of a \"complementary\" mating type, to move toward the secreting cell and begin mating.")
(comment MatingFactor "A collection of chemicals that are secreted by haploid single-celled organisms to promote mating.")
(comment SCerevisiae-AMatingType "This is the collection of all \"A\"-type haploid <i>S. cerevisiae</i> cells, one of two mating types for that type of yeast.  A-type cells can mate with Alpha-type yeast cells (see #$SCerevisiae-AlphaMatingType.")
(comment SecretionOfMatingFactorA "The specialization of #$SecretionOfMatingFactor consisting of events in which A-type <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells secrete the A mating factor.")
(comment SecretionOfMatingFactorAlpha "The specialization of #$SecretionOfMatingFactor consisting of events in which Alpha-type <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells secrete the Alpha mating factor.")
(disjointWith SecretionOfMatingFactorAlpha SecretionOfMatingFactorA)
(disjointWith SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromAlpha SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromA)
(comment SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromAlpha "The collection of instances of #$SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent in which an Alpha-type yeast cell signals an A-type cell.")
(comment SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromA "The collection of instances of #$SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent in which an A-type yeast cell signals an Alpha-type cell.")
(comment SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent "The collection of instances of #$CellularCommunication in which a yeast cell signals another yeast cell of the opposite mating type.")
(comment SCerevisiae-AlphaMatingType "This is the collection of all \"Alpha\"-type haploid <i>S. cerevisiae</i> cells, one of two mating types for that type of yeast.  Alpha-type cells can mate with A-type yeast cells (see #$SCerevisiae-AMatingType.")
(comment AFactorReceptor "The sub-collection of #$ReceptorMolecule whose instances are receptors for the a mating factor (see #$MatingFactorA).")
(comment AlphaFactorReceptor "The sub-collection of #$ReceptorMolecule whose instances are receptors for the alpha mating factor (see #$MatingFactorAlpha).")
(comment MatingFactorAlpha "A subcollection of #$MatingFactor used by instances of the #$SCerevisiae-AlphaMatingType yeast to \"attract\" a mate.")
(comment MatingFactorA "A subcollection of #$MatingFactor used by instances of the #$SCerevisiae-AMatingType yeast to \"attract\" a mate.")
(comment organismMatingType "A spec-pred (see #$genlPreds) of #$isa, <code>(#$organismMatingType ORG M-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>M-TYPE</code> as the unique instance of #$MatingType that <code>ORG</code>, an instance of #$SingleCellHaploidOrganism, belongs to.")
(comment CommunicationBetweenMatingSCerevisiaeCells "A collection of events comprised of instances of #$SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent that take place as part of the yeast mating script.")
(comment AlphaTypeCellMovesToATypeCell "The complete movement of an alpha-type yeast cell to to join up with a signaling a-type yeast cell.")
(comment AlphaAndAYeastCellsMoveToEachOther "The complete movement of Alpha-type and A-type yeast cells to one another prior to mating.")
(comment ATypeCellMovesToAlphaTypeCell "The complete movement of an a-type yeast cell to to join up with a signaling alpha-type yeast cell.")
(comment MovementOfATypeCellTowardAlphaTypeCell "The collection of individual movement events of an Alpha-type yeast cell toward (see #$towardLocation) a signlaing A-Type cell.  Each such movement is a response by the cell to a signal from that cell (see #$SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromAlpha).")
(comment MovementOfAlphaTypeCellTowardATypeCell "The collection of individual movement events of an Alpha-type yeast cell toward (see #$towardLocation) a signlaing A-Type cell.  Each such movement is a response by the cell to a signal from that cell (see #$SCerevisiaeSignalingEvent-FromA).")
(comment AlphaAndATypeCellsMakeContact "The event in the Yeast cell mating script in which the Alpha and A cells make contact.")
(comment MergingOfAlphaAndATypeCellNuclei "The collection of events in which the nuclei of Alpha and A <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells merge, combining the DNA from both cells.")
(comment MergingOfCellNuclei "The collection of events in which the nuclei of two (haploid) cells merge, combining the DNA from both cells.")
(comment CreationOfDiploidOrganismThroughFusion "A specialization of #$BiologicalFusionEvent, in which two haploid cells fuse to form a diploid organism.  There are two general cases of this: the haploid cells may be gametes (see #$Gamete) that merge in a #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent  to form a #$Zygote, or the haploid cells may be single-celled organisms, in which case the resultant organism is a single-celled diploid organism of the same species as the original haploids.")
(comment MergingOfAlphaAndATypeCellCytoplasm "The collection of events in which the cytoplasm of Alpha and A <i>S. cerevisiae</i> yeast cells merge.")
(comment MergingOfCellCytoplasm "The collection of events in which two cell cytoplasms merge.")
(comment AlphaTypeCellReceivesAMatingFactor "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent that takes place as part of the yeast mating script.  Instances are the binding of A mating factor molecules with A receptor molecules located on the membrane of an Alpha-type cell, causing it to move towards the source of the mating factor.")
(comment ATypeCellReceivesAlphaMatingFactor "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent that takes place as part of the yeast mating script.  Instances are the binding of Alpha mating factor molecules with Alpha receptor molecules located on the membrane of an A-type cell, causing it to move towards the source of the mating factor.")
(disjointWith ExtrudedBodyPart EndocrineSystem)
(comment EndocrineSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$EndocrineSystem is a system of body parts which function together  to enable its owner (an instance of #$Animal) to have a suitable supply of endocrine hormones.")
(comment UnitedKingdomGovernmentDepartment "A collection of government organizations.  Each instance of #$UnitedKingdomGovernmentDepartment is an organization that is part of the national government of the United Kingdom.")
(comment ForeignAndCommonwealthOffice-UK "The FCO is the British government department responsible for promoting the interests of the United Kingdom overseas.")
(comment UnitedKingdomGovernmentDepartment-Ministerial "A collection of British government organizations.  Each instance of #$UnitedKingdomGovernmentDepartment-Ministerial is a ministerial organization that is part of the national government of the United Kingdom.")
(comment HomeOffice-UK "The Home Office is the department of the British government department responsible for immigration control, security, and order.")
(comment MinistryOfDefence-UK "The British Ministry of Defence is the defense department of the British government.")
(comment componentsInSeriesInNetwork "<code>(#$componentsInSeriesInNetwork LIST NETWORK )</code> means that the #$ElectricalNetwork, NETWORK consists of the members of LIST connected in series.")
(comment ElectricalComponentsInParallelFn "<code>(#$ElectricalComponentsInParallelFn  LIST)</code> denotes the instance of #$ElectricalNetwork that consists of the members of list connected in parallel.")
(comment ElectricalComponentsInSeriesFn "<code>(#$ElectricalComponentsInSeriesFn   LIST)</code> denotes the instance of #$ElectricalNetwork that consists of the members of list connected in series.")
(comment componentsInParallelInNetwork "<code>(#$componentsInParallelInNetwork LIST NETWORK )</code> means that the #$ElectricalNetwork, NETWORK consists of the members of LIST connected in parallel.")
(comment OwnerFn-Type "<code>(#$OwnerFn-Type OBJ-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all owners of instances of OBJ-TYPE.  For example, (#$OwnerFn-Type #$Gun) denotes the collection of gun owners.")
(comment ownerOfType "<code>(#$ownerOfType OBJ-TYPE OWNER-TYPE)</code> means that <code>OWNER-TYPE</code> is the collection of owners of instances of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code>.")
(comment diploidOrganismHasGeneotypeForGene "(#$diploidOrganismHasGeneotypeForGene ORG GIS-TYPE GENE1 GENE2) states that the individual diploid organism, ORG, has the specific genetic sequences GENE1 and GENE2 as its alleles for the type of gene, GIS-TYPE.")
(comment organismHasAlleleForGene "(#$organismHasAlleleForGene ORG GENE GIS-TYPE) states that the individual organism, ORG, has the specific genetic sequence GENE as one of its alleles for the type of gene, GIS-TYPE.")
(comment geneticDeletionOf "(#$geneticDeletionOf DELETION-COL GIS-TYPE) states DELETION-COL is the collection of abstract genetic sequences of type GIS-TYPE in which part or all of the typical sequence is mission.")
(comment TheNullGeneSequence "#$TheNullGeneSequence denotes the degenerate case of an empty #$Gene-GIS.  I.e., the physical instantiation of this is in a #$Genome is one in which the #$Gene-HereditaryUnit instantiating (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) a particular #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily is simply missing on one of both chromosomes.")
(comment protestAgainst "<code>(#$protestAgainst PROTEST THING)</code> means that <code>PROTEST</code> is a protest against <code>THING</code>.")
(disjointWith Molarity ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith Temperature ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith AngularDistance ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith Voltage ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith Volume ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith Pressure ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith ElectricalCharge ElectricalConductance)
(disjointWith Mass ElectricalConductance)
(comment ElectricalConductance "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$ElectricalResistance is a measure of the resistance to electrical flow through an object.  Instances of #$ElectricalResistance include #$InsulatorResistance, #$ConductorResistance, #$SemiconductorResistance, and #$SuperconductorResistance.")
(comment ElectricalConductance "A specialization of #$ElectricalQuantity.  Each instance of #$ElectricalConductance is a measure of the ability for electricity to flow through an object.  #$ElectricalConductance is the reciprocal of #$ElectricalResistance -- that is, if the resistance = R, then the conductance is 1/R.")
(comment Siemens "  #$Siemens is the standard unit of electrical conductance.  Conductance is the reciprocal of resistance.")
(comment Vasopressin "An antidiuretic #$Hormone secreted in the hypothalamus which elevates blood pressure.")
(comment chemicalSubstanceTypeOfDeposition "(#$chemicalSubstanceTypeOfDeposition DEPOSITING SUBST-TYPE) means that the #$ThinFilm which is deposited in DEPOSITING (#$thinFilmDeposited) is an instance of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType SUBST-TYPE.")
(comment thinFilmChemicalSubstanceType "(#$thinFilmChemicalSubstanceType FILM SUBST-TYPE) means that the #$ThinFilm FILM belongs to the #$ChemicalSubstanceType SUBST-TYPE.  A typed specialization of #$isa.")
(comment thicknessOfDeposition "(#$thicknessOfDeposition DEPOSITING INTERVAL) means that the thickness of the #$ThinFilm laid down in DEPOSITING (the #$thinFilmDeposited) is given by INTERVAL.")
(comment thicknessRangeOfDeposition "(#$thicknessRangeOfDeposition DEPOSITION DIFF) means that DIFF is the difference between the largest thickness measurable for the #$ThinFilm laid down in DEPOSITION and the smallest thickness measurable for that same #$ThinFilm. ")
(comment jointTypeBetween "(#$jointTypeBetween TYPE-1 TYPE-2 COLL) means that COLL is the collection of #$Joint-Physicals where the joint is between an instance of TYPE-1 and TYPE-2.  See the corresponding function #$JointTypeBetweenFn.")
(comment GeneticDeletionFn "(#$GeneticDeletionFn GIS-TYPE) denotes the collection of abstract genetic sequences of type GIS-TYPE in which some or all of the sequence is missing.  #$TheNullGeneSequence, denoting the most degenerate case of complete deletion, is an instance of every collection denoted by this function applied to its argument.")
(comment ParietalCell "#$ParietalCells are the cells in the stomach that produce #$GastricJuices.")
(comment GastricJuice "A specialization of #$Secretion-Bodily. Gastric juices are secreted by the #$ParietalCells in the stomach to break down ingested food.")
(disjointWith MuscleTissue EpithelialTissue)
(comment EpithelialTissue "A specialization of #$AnimalTissue.  Epithelium is one of the four basic kinds of animal tissue (along with #$ConnectiveTissue, #$MuscleTissue and #$NerveTissue.")
(disjointWith NerveTissue EpithelialTissue)
(disjointWith ConnectiveTissue EpithelialTissue)
(comment IntegratedCircuitPhysicsMt "A microtheory that collects information pertaining to the basic physical laws surrounding the operation of integrated circuits along with a fixed frame of reference for referring to the length, width, and thickness of these objects.")
(comment ParsingTestType "Each instance of #$ParsingTestType is a collection whose instances are individual parsing test definitions.  Instances of #$ParsingTestType represent categories of tests grouped together because they are usefully viewed or run as a unit.")
(comment Cheerleader "The collection of all cheerleaders. Instances need not be instances of #$YoungHuman, for example, cheerleaders for professional sports teams.")
(comment ParsingTestTypeByContent "Each instance of #$ParsingTestTypeByContent represents a category of tests grouped together because they are usefully considered, viewed or run as a unit.")
(comment ParsingTest-UnderDevelopment "A specialization of #$ParsingTest, and an instance of #$ParsingTestTypeByDevelopmentStatus.  Each instance of #$ParsingTest-UnderDevelopment is a parsing test that is currently under development.")
(comment ParsingTestTypeByDevelopmentStatus "Each instance of #$ParsingTestTypeByDevelopmentStatus is a collection whose instances are individual parsing test definitions with a status such as \"has succeeded\" (see #$ParsingTest-HasSucceeded),  \"has never succeeded\" (see #$ParsingTest-NeverSucceeded), and \"under development\" (see #$ParsingTest-UnderDevelopment).")
(comment ParsingTest-NeverSucceeded "A specialization of #$ParsingTest, and an instance of #$ParsingTestTypeByDevelopmentStatus.  Each instance of #$ParsingTest-NeverSucceeded is a parsing test that has never fully parsed.")
(comment ParsingTest-HasSucceeded "A specialization of #$ParsingTest, and an instance of #$ParsingTestTypeByDevelopmentStatus.  Each instance of #$ParsingTest-HasSucceeded is a parsing test that has at least sometime in the past fully parsed.")
(comment ThinFilmDepositionTypeByChemicalSubstanceTypeDeposited "A #$FacetingCollectionType on #$ThinFilmDeposition.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ThinFilmDeposition whose instances all share a common #$chemicalSubstanceTypeOfDeposition, i.e., wherein all of the instances deposit films of a common #$ChemicalSubstanceType.")
(comment ThinFilmDepositionTypeByChemicalSubstanceTypeDepositedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to reify collection instances of #$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByChemicalSubstanceTypeDeposited.  Where SUBST-TYPE is a #$ChemicalSubstanceType, (#$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByChemicalSubstanceTypeDepositedFn SUBST-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$ThinFilmDepositions wherein a #$ThinFilm of SUBST-TYPE (#$chemicalSubstanceTypeOfDeposition) is deposited.")
(comment chemSubstanceTypeOfFilmsDeposited "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByChemicalSubstanceTypeDepositedFn.  Where SUBST-TYPE is a #$ChemicalSubstanceType, (#$chemSubstanceTypeOfFilmsDeposited SUBST-TYPE DEPOSIT-TYPE) means that DEPOSIT-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ThinFilmDeposition wherein the #$ThinFilm deposited is of type SUBST-TYPE.")
(comment ThinFilmDepositionTypeByResistanceOfFilmDeposited "A #$FacetingCollectionType that forms a #$covering on #$ThinFilmDeposition.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ThinFilmDeposition whose instances all deposit #$ThinFilms with a common #$ElectricalResistance (#$SemiconductorResistance, #$InsulatorResistance, #$ConductorResistance, #$SuperconductorResistance).")
(comment ThinFilmDepositionTypeByResistanceOfFilmDepositedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to reify instances of #$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByResistanceOfFilmDeposited.  (#$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByResistanceOfFilmDepositedFn RESISTANCE) denotes the collection of every #$ThinFilmDeposition wherein the #$ThinFilm deposited (#$thinFilmDeposited) has an #$electricalResistanceOfObject of RESISTANCE.")
(comment resistanceOfFilmsDeposited "(#$resistanceOfFilmsDeposited RESISTANCE DEPOSITING-TYPE) means that DEPOSITING-TYPE is the collection of all #$ThinFilmDepositions wherein the #$ThinFilm deposited (#$thinFilmDeposited) has an #$electricalResistanceOfObject of RESISTANCE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ThinFilmDepositionTypeByResistanceOfFilmDepositedFn.")
(comment IntrinsicFactor "A type of glycoprotein excreted by #$ParietalCells.")
(comment Pylorus "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$Pylorus is the distal section of a #$Stomach, next to the #$PyloricValve.")
(comment Fundus "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$Fundus is a section of a #$Stomach.")
(comment PyloricValve "The collection of all pyloric #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection is a #$Portal from the #$Pylorus of a #$Stomach to the #$Duodenum (part of the #$SmallIntestine).")
(comment BodyOfStomach "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$BodyOfStomach is a section of a #$Stomach.")
(comment Cardia "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$Cardia is a section of a #$Stomach.")
(comment UpperEsophagealSphincter "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$UpperEsophagealSphincter is a section of an #$Esophagus.")
(comment LowerEsophagealSphincter "An instance of #$OrganSubPartType   Each instance of #$LowerEsophagealSphincter is a section of an #$Esophagus.")
(disjointWith Organization InsulatingMedium)
(comment InsulatingMedium "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$InsulatingMedium is a partially tangible object that can serve as a insulator, e.g., for heat or electricity.  Specializations include #$ElectricalInsulator.")
(comment ElectricalInsulator "The collection of objects which can serve as electrical insulators.  These objects have a high resistance to the flow of electricity with the resistance of the ideal insulator approaching infinity.")
(comment LoopOfHenle "A specialization on #$InternalAnatomicalPart.  Loops of Henle are parts of nephrons.")
(comment OilSands "A specialization of #$PetroleumReservoir.  Each instance of #$OilSands is a petroleum deposit wherin a mixture of sand, clay, water, and #$Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil are found.  Very large oil sands deposits are in Venezuela and Canada.")
(comment AthabascaOilSands "The Athabasca oil sands are large bitumen deposits in northeastern Alberta.")
(comment BitumenUpgrading "A specializaton of #$ProcessingEvent.  Bitumen upgrading is the process of transforming #$Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil into #$SyntheticCrude.")
(comment SyntheticCrude "A specialization of #$PetroleumProduct.  Each instance of #$SyntheticCrude is the product of #$BitumenUpgrading.  Synthetic crude is a petroleum product that can be transported for further processing to an #$OilRefinery.")
(comment Movie-Silent "The collection of all #$Movie-CW that have no recorded  #$MovieSoundtracks.")
(comment OrinocoOilSands "The Orinoco oil sands are large bitumen deposits in Venezuela.")
(comment WellOutflow "A specialization of #$DrainingProcess.  In each instance of #$WellOutflow, a fluid flows out of a #$Well.  Sometimes this flow is natural (see #$WellOutflow-Natural), but often it requires the use of an artificial lift (see #$WellOutflow-ArtificiallyLifted).")
(comment StuffTypeByResistanceFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for reifying instances of #$ExistingStuffTypeByElectricalResistance.  Where RESISTIVITY is an #$ElectricalResistance, (#$StuffTypeByResistanceFn RESISTIVITY) denotes the #$ExistingStuffType whose instances all have RESISTIVITY as #$electricalResistanceOfObject under 'normal' conditions.")
(comment definingResistanceOfStuffType "(#$definingResistanceOfStuffType RESISTIVITY STUFF-TYPE) means that STUFF-TYPE is the #$ExistingStuffType whose instances all feature an #$electricalResistanceOfObject of RESISTIVITY under some normal conditions.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$StuffTypeByResistanceFn.")
(comment ExistingStuffTypeByElectricalResistance "A #$FacetingCollectionType and a specialization of #$ExistingStuffType.  Each collection instance is an #$ExistingStuffType defined by a common electrical resistance exhibited by all of its instances under familiar conditions.")
(comment ChurnFlow-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation. Each instance of #$ChurnFlow-VerticalUpward involves a highly turbulent flow pattern and dispersion of both gas and liquid phase.  Churn flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than slug flow (see #$SlugFlow-VerticalUpward).")
(comment SlugFlow-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation. Each instance of #$SlugFlow-VerticalUpward involves coalescing bubbles, some of which can expand across the entire flow pathway. Slug flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than bubble flow (see #$BubbleFlow-VerticalUpward).")
(comment AnnularFlow-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation. Each instance of #$AnnularFlow-VerticalUpward involves a mist of liquid droplets in a moving gas. Annular flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than churn flow (see #$ChurnFlow-VerticalUpward). Indeed, annular flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than all other instances of #$MultiphaseVerticalUpwardFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-VerticalUpward is a multiphase flow in which the flowing fluid is moving upward in a direction roughly aligned with the direction of the force of gravity.")
(comment MultiphaseVerticalUpwardFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio "The collection of multiphase vertical upward flow regime types, which are differentiated by the gas-to-liquid ratios.")
(comment BubbleFlow-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation. Each instance of #$BubbleFlow-VerticalUpward involves dispersed bubbles of gas within a moving volume of a continuous liquid phase moving substance. Bubble flow involves a higher liquid-to-gas ratio than all other instances of #$MultiphaseVerticalUpwardFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal is a multiphase flow in which the flowing fluid is moving in a direction roughly perpendicular to the direction of the force of gravity.")
(comment MultiphaseHorizontalFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio "The collection of multiphase horizontal flow regime types, which are differentiated by the gas-to-liquid ratios.")
(comment AnnularFlow-Horizontal "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal. Each instance of #$AnnularFlow-Horizontal involves a mist of liquid droplets in a moving gas. Annular flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than stratified flow (see #$StratifiedFlow-Horizontal).")
(comment BubbleFlow-Horizontal "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal. Each instance of #$BubbleFlow-Horizontal involves dispersed bubbles of gas within a moving volume of a continuous liquid phase moving substance. Bubble flow involves a higher liquid-to-gas ration than all other instances of #$MultiphaseHorizontalFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio.")
(comment StratifiedFlow-Horizontal "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal. Each instance of #$StratifiedFlow-Horizontal involves a flow pattern wherein liquid flows beneath an annular flow.  Stratified flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than slug flow (see #$SlugFlow-Horizontal).")
(comment SlugFlow-Horizontal "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal. Each instance of #$SlugFlow-Horizontal involves an intermittent flow of dispersed bubbles of gas within a moving volume of continuous liquid phase  substance, and large coalesced bubbles on of top moving liquid. Slug flow involves a higher gas-to-liquid ratio than bubble flow (see #$BubbleFlow-Horizontal).")
(comment audioPortionOfWork "<code>(#$audioPortionOfWork WORK AUDIO)</code> means that <code>AUDIO</code> is the audio portion of <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$AudioVisualWork.  #$audioPortionOfWork is neutral with respect to whether <code>AUDIO</code> stands on its own as a conceptual work (an instance of #$AudioConceptualWork) in its own right, in which case it is also a #$subWorks of <code>WORK</code>.")
(comment AudioVisualWork "The collection of works that are intended to be experienced both visually and audibly, and so has an audio component (see #$audioPortionOfWork) and visual component (see #$visualPortionOfWork).  These components may or may not qualify as full-blown conceptual works in their own right.")
(comment visualPortionOfWork "<code>(#$visualPortionOfWork WORK VISUAL)</code> means that <code>VISUAL</code> is the visual portion of <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$AudioVisualWork.  #$visualPortionOfWork is neutral with respect to whether <code>AUDIO</code> stands on its own as a conceptual work (an instance of #$VisualWork) in its own right, in which case it is also a #$subWorks of <code>WORK</code>.")
(disjointWith AudioConceptualWork AudioVisualWork)
(disjointWith Movie-Silent AudioVisualWork)
(comment AudioVisualIBT "The collection of all instances of #$InformationBearingThing that consist of audio (#$SoundInformationBearingThing) and visual (#$VisualInformationBearingThing) elements.")
(comment ibtInstantiatesArtifact "<code>(#$ibtInstantiatesArtifact IBT ARTIFACT)</code> means that the instance <code>IBT</code> is a complete instantiation of <code>ARTIFACT</code>, and instance of #$Artifact-Intangible and #$AspatialInformationStore.  Where <code>ARTIFACT</code> is an instance of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork, use the the specialization #$instantiationOfWork.")
(comment MultiMediaAnalysisMt "An instance of #$ApplicationContext that contains knowledge useful for applying Cyc to multi-media analysis and retrieval problems.")
(comment IntramembranousBoneGrowthAndDevelopment "A collection of events in which a bone (see #$Bone-BodyPart) is created, grows, and matures into its adult form.  Unlike #$EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment, in which the bone is initially shaped in #$HyalineCartilage that is eventually replaced with bone, in intramembranous bone growth and development, #$OsteochondralProgenitorCells develop into #$Osteoblasts, and secrete #$Osteoid which becomes mineralized, without the presence of a cartilage model.")
(comment slotsDirectlyProportionalViaConstantToSlotForRelatedTypes "(#$slotsDirectlyProportionalViaConstantToSlotForRelatedTypes  OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 BIN-PRED SLOT-1 SLOT-2 CONSTANT) means that when INST-1 and INST-2 (instances of OBJ-TYPE1 and OBJ-TYPE2 respectively) stand in BIN-PRED such that (BIN-PRED INST-1 INST-2), then the values for SLOT-2 for INST-2 are directly proportional to the values for SLOT-1 for INST-1 via CONSTANT -- i.e SLOT-VAL-OBJ2 = CONSTANT-VAL * SLOT-VAL-OBJ1.")
(comment slotsInverselyProportionalViaConstantToSlotForRelatedTypes "(#$slotsInverselyProportionalViaConstantToSlotForRelatedTypes   OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 BIN-PRED SLOT-1 SLOT-2 CONSTANT) means that when INST-1 and INST-2 (instances of OBJ-TYPE1 and OBJ-TYPE2 respectively) stand in BIN-PRED such that (BIN-PRED INST-1 INST-2), then the values for SLOT-2 for INST-2 are inversely proportional to the values for SLOT-1 for INST-1 via CONSTANT -- i.e SLOT-VAL-OBJ2 = CONSTANT-VAL / SLOT-VAL-OBJ1.")
(comment ConcentrationOfGasInFluidByVolume "A specialization of #$ConcentrationStrength (q.v.) statable in terms of the ratio of the volume of gas relative to the volume of liquid in a continuous volume of fluid.")
(comment QPQuantityFn "<code>(#$QPQuantityFn SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE)</code> is a
function-denoting function which returns a temporally qualifiable function when given a specialization of #$ScalarQuantity as an argument. <code>((#$QPQuantityFn SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE) THING)</code> is the quantity of <code>SCALAR-QUANT-TYPE</code> that <code>THING</code> has, whether or not that quantity is measured or even measurable.  For example, ((#$QPQuantityFn #$Mass) #$EiffelTower) denotes a mass: namely, the mass of the Eiffel Tower.  Functions denoted by #$QPQuantityFn are typically used in conjunction with #$valueOf (q.v.). For example, (#$valueOf ((#$QPQuantityFn #$Mass) #$EiffelTower) (#$MetricTon 10100)) is true.")
(comment hasConcentrationOfGasInFluidByVolume "(#$hasConcentrationOfGasInFluidByVolume OBJ CONC) means that OBJ has the #$ConcentrationOfGasInFluidByVolume CONC.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-BubbleFlow "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-BubbleFlow is the collection of all \"bubble flow\" multiphase fluid translations. Each instance of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-BubbleFlow involves dispersed bubbles of gas within a moving volume of a continuous liquid phase moving substance.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-AnnularFlow "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-AnnularFlow is the collection of all \"annular flow\" multiphase fluid translations. Annular flow involves a mist of liquid droplets in a moving gas.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-SlugFlow "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-SlugFlow is the collection of all \"slug flow\" multiphase fluid translations. Slug flow involves intermittent flow of dispersed coalescing bubbles of gas within a moving volume of continuous liquid phase substance.")
(comment MultiphaseFlowTypeByGasToLiquidRatio "The collection of multiphase flow regime types, which are differentiated by the gas-to-liquid ratios.")
(comment typeEntirePortionOfTypeForType "(#$typeEntirePortionOfTypeForType OBTYPE STUFFTYPE PORTION-TYPE) means PORTION-TYPE is the specialization of STUFFTYPE whose instances are the entire physical extent of instances of STUFFTYPE that are physical parts of instances of OBJECTTYPE. For example, (#$typeEntirePortionOfTypeForType #$Chimpanzee #$Blood EntirePortionOfBloodOfAnyChimp) means EntirePortionOfBloodOfAnyChimp is the collection of instances of #$Blood, each of which is the total portion of blood in some chimpanzee.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidTangibleThing "A subcollection of #$FluidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$MultiphaseFluidTangibleThing is a fluid that is part gas and part liquid.")
(comment MultiphaseFluidFlow-ChurnOrStratifiedFlow "A specialization of #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-Translation.  #$MultiphaseFluidFlow-ChurnOrStratifiedFlow is the collection of all churn (in the vertical upward case) or stratified (in the horizontal case) multiphase fluid translations.")
(comment Beer "The collection of all beer. A type of #$CarbonatedBeverage and #$AlcoholicBeverage. The collection #$Beer is a #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType and a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$Beer is a portion of the carbonated alcoholic beverage produced from the fermentation of barley (or, less often, corn or wheat).")
(comment MovementInDirectionFn "(#$MovementInDirectionFn DIRECTION) denotes the collection of translation events (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) in which the primary object moving has a velocity with a vector direction of DIRECTION.")
(comment movementInDirection "(#$movementInDirection MOVE-TYPE DIRECTION) means MOVE-TYPE is the collection of translation events (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) in which the primary object moving has a velocity with a vector direction of DIRECTION.")
(comment FluidFlow-Translation-VerticalUpward "A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  #$FluidFlow-Translation-VerticalUpward is the collection of events in which a fluid moves upward.")
(comment FluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal "A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  #$FluidFlow-Translation-Horizontal is the collection of events in which a fluid moves horizontally.")
(comment Whaling "The #$Hunting of whales by humans.")
(disjointWith Hunting Lobstering)
(disjointWith TillingSoil (AttemptingFn HarvestingAquaticAnimals))
(comment HarvestingAquaticAnimals "A specialization of #$HumanActivity, this is the collection of events in which one or more aquatic animals is caught or killed and removed from the water.")
(comment CatchingFish "The purpose of #$Fishing -- this is the collection of events in which one or more #$Fish are secured (i.e., 'hooked' or 'netted') then successfully removed from the water.")
(comment SpecifiedMultimediaDetectionTargetEventType "A collection of collections, instances are types of #$PhysicalEvent that have been specifically identified as targets for event-recognition from some media, as part of a specific event-recognition program or project.")
(comment HarvestingLobster "A specialization of #$HarvestingAquaticAnimals, this is the collection of events in which humans successfully trap and remove lobsters from the water.")
(comment Lobstering "The collection of events in which humans attempt to trap and extract lobster from the water.")
(comment seriesCoMembers "This predicate relates a pair of things together just in case they are members of the same series.  It is equivalent to (#$Kappa (?X ?Y) (#$thereExists ?SERIES (#$and (#$seriesMembers ?SERIES ?X) (#$seriesMembers ?SERIES ?Y))))")
(comment InsulatorContactInsulator-Series "A specialization of #$ContactInsulatingLayerSeries in which a single contact is flanked by an insulating layer on both sides.")
(comment GeneOntology "An instance of #$Ontology.  The Gene Ontology is developed and maintained by the Gene Ontology Consortium, and includes sub-ontologies about biological processes that gene products may act in, molecular functions that gene products may have, and cellular components to which they may be localized.")
(comment wellboreMeasuredDepth "(#$wellboreMeasuredDepth WB MD) means that the measured depth of the #$Wellbore WB is the #$Distance MD.  This is not truly a measure of depth, except in the case of strictly vertical wells.  Rather, this is a measure of the length of the wellbore. The wellbore measured depth is used to determine how much pipe will fit in the wellbore.  Almost always, due to curves in the wellbore, the #$wellboreMeasuredDepth will be longer than the #$depthOfObject (or \"true measured depth\").")
(comment BlowoutPreventer "A specialization of #$Valve-Mechanical.  Each instance of #$BlowoutPreventer is large valve used to control oil and gas wells.  Blowout preventers are critical in enabling control of formation kick.")
(comment DrillingFluid "A specialization of #$FluidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$DrillingFluid is a fluid (or a mixtures of fluids and solids) used to facilitate the drilling of boreholes into the Earth.")
(comment Blowout-WellDrilling "Blowouts are uncontrolled releases of oil or gas from oil wells or gas wells, respectively.")
(comment OffshoreOilPlatform "The collection of all off-shore oil platforms. All instances are physical devices meant for drilling an oil well and subsequently regulating the flow of #$Petroleum-CrudeOil through this #$OilWell from underground reservoirs.")
(comment OffshoreDrillingRig "A specialization of #$DrillingRig.  Each instance of #$OffshoreDrillingRig is a drilling rig used in offshore drilling.")
(comment MidgetSubmarine "The collection of submarines under 150 tons, typically operated by a crew of from 1 to 6 persons.")
(comment WellCasing "The collection of all pipes cemented in place during the construction of a well to stabilize the wellbore.")
(comment ConductorCasing "Conductor casing is the widest casing in a casing string, and it is used closed to the surface of a well.")
(comment SurfaceCasing "Surface casing protects fresh-water aquifers so they are not contaminated by well activites.  It also provides structural strength so that the remaining casing may used.")
(comment ProductionCasing "Production casing is the smallest casing used in a well.")
(comment slotsForTypeSatisfyEquation "(#$slotsForTypeSatisfyEquation COLL BIN-PRED SLOT FORMULA) means that instance of COLL have values for SLOT that vary according to FORMULA which represents the right hand side of an equation.")
(comment WidthOfAContactDependentOnWidthOfFlankedInsulators "The formula to determine the width of a contact given the width of the insulating layers on each side of it relative to instances of #$InsulatorContactInsulator-Series.  The width of the contact between the two insulators = Width of the series - ( The sum of the widths of the flanking insulators).")
(comment QuantityBasedFormula "The collection of reified mathematical formulas that express some physical principle #$PhysicalPrinciple via values on some quantity slots.")
(comment SingleFocalObjectFormula "The collection of mathematical formulas that express some physical principle #$PhysicalPrinciple via values on some quantity slots where the subject of each of the slots is assumed to be the same object.  This entails the same conditions of applicability as asserting (#$constraintForQuantityBasedFormula FORMULA QUANT1 QUANT2 #$equals) for each pair of quantities involved in FORMULA.  For example, the area of a rectangle is a function of the length and height of the rectangle -- it is assumed the values for length and height are from the same rectangle.  Contrast this with a formula to determine the combined area of two rectangles where the area of one is added to the area of the other.")
(comment constraintForQuantityBasedFormula "(#$constraintForQuantityBasedFormula QBF QUANTITY1 QUANTITY2 BIN-PRED) means that for the formula to be applicable, the thing with QUANTITY1 must stand in BIN-PRED to the thing with QUANTITY2.  So, if SLOT-1 and SLOT-2 are the slots associated with those quantities via #$unitSlotsForFormula, then the following must be true for the formula to be applicable to INS-1 or INS-2 (#$and (SLOT-1 INS-1 QUANTITY1) (SLOT-2 INS-2 QUANTITY2) (BIN-PRED INS-1 INS-2)).  Note that this expresses a necessary condition of the formula's application.  A sufficient condition is that all relevant constraints for the formula are satisfied.")
(comment DigitalCamera "An instance of #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a specialization of #$ElectronicDevice.  Each instance of #$DigitalCamera is a #$Camera that records images using a #$ComputerHardwareMemoryStorageUnit   rather than (e.g.) some #$PhotographicFilm.  Specializations include #$StillCamera-Digital and #$DigitalCamcorder.")
(comment Photosensor "A collection of electronic sensor devices. Photosensors detect the presense of light.")
(comment SolarCell "The collection of all solar cells. A type of #$CurrentSource, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$ElectricalComponent. The collection #$SolarCell is a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment Photodiode "A collection of diodes. Photosensors can convert light into current or voltage.")
(comment OpticalFiber "An optical fiber is a thin, flexible, and transparent fiber made of glass or plastic.  Optical fibers are used as waveguides to transmit light from one end of the fiber to the other.")
(comment FiberOpticCable "A specialization of #$Path-InfoTransfer, #$CordlikeObject and #$PhysicalDevice, #$FiberOpticCable is the collection of cords made of #$OpticalFibers (thin fibers of glass that guide the light of transmitting lasers without significant loss even though these cords are not always straight at the time of transmission).  Instances of the collection #$FiberOpticCable enable very high-speed networking (approximately 100 Mbps).")
(comment Transparent "#$Transparent is the collection of transparent objects.  Transparent objects transmit enough light to see clear images through them.  See also #$transparencyOfObject.")
(comment OpticalSensorFiber "A specialization of #$OpticalFiber.  Optical sensor fibers are used to detect light along their length.")
(comment OptoelectronicDevice "A specialization of #$ElectronicDevice.  Optoelectronic devices are electronic devices that operate by detecting or controlling  light.")
(comment isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot "(#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF QUANTITY COLL) means that the thing standing in arg1 of the slot associated with quantity when applying QBF must be an instance of COLL.  If the quantity is implictly restricted to certain types of entities, then COLL = that type.  E.g. If (#$unitSlotsForFormula QBF (#$AreaFn (#$The #$RightTriangle)) #$areaOfObject), then (#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF (#$AreaFn (#$The #$RightTriangle)) #$RightTriangle).  If the quantity type is unrestricted, then the thing standing in arg1 of the associated slot must satisfy the relevant #$arg1Isa constraints of that slot --  e.g. if (#$unitSlotsForFormula QBF (#$The #$Area) #$areaOfObject), then (#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot QBF (#$The #$Area) #$PolyDimensionalThing).")
(comment DistributedTemperatureSurvey "A specialization of #$StructuredInformationSource.  Each instance of #$DistributedTemperatureSurvey is a continuous temperature profile produced by a #$DistributedTemperatureSensor, for the length of its #$OpticalSensorFiber.")
(comment DistributedTemperatureSensor "A specialization of #$OptoelectronicDevice and #$TemperatureMeasuringDevice.  Each instance of #$DistributedTemperatureSensor is a system that uses #$OpticalSensorFiber as a linear sensor detect temperatures as a continuous profile, often over large distances (see #$DistributedTemperatureSurvey).")
(comment DistributedTemperatureSensing "A specialization of (#$MassEventOfTypeFn (#$MeasuringFn #$Temperature)).  Each instance of #$DistributedTemperatureSensing is an event in which temperatures are measured one or more across a distributed space (to produce #$DistributedTemperatureSurveys), using a #$DistributedTemperatureSensor.  Each instance of #$DistributedTemperatureSensing involves multiple #$DistributedTemperatureSensing-SingleSurveyProduction sub-events, each of which results in the production of one #$DistributedTemperatureSurvey.")
(comment DistributedTemperatureSensing-SingleSurveyProduction "A specialization of (#$MassEventOfTypeFn (#$MeasuringFn #$Temperature)).  Each instance of #$DistributedTemperatureSensing-SingleSurveyProduction is an event in which temperatures are measured across a distributed space to produce one #$DistributedTemperatureSurvey.")
(comment BoneResorptionByBMU "#$BoneResorption done as part of #$BoneRemodeling is performed by a group of #$Osteoclasts that proceed along the surface of trabecular bone (see #$TrabecularBoneTissue) forming a channel, or tunnel through cortical bone (see #$CorticalBoneTissue).  Trailing this group of #$Osteoclasts is a group of #$Osteoblasts, which secrete #$Osteoid that subsequently becomes mineralized.  The entire assemblage is called a Basic Multicellular Unit (see #$BoneBMU) or BMU.  #$BoneResorptionByBMU is the collection of instances of #$BoneResorption which are performed by the osteoclasts of a single BMU.")
(comment ProliferationOfCellTypeFn "A function that yields a collection of events in which a certain type of #$Cell proliferates. (#$ProliferationOfCellTypeFn CELL-TYPE) denotes the collection of all cell proliferation events in which a population of cells of type CELL-TYPE undergoes many #$CellDivision events, increasing the size of the cell population.")
(comment cellTypeProliferationType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$ProliferationOfCellTypeFn.  (#$cellTypeProliferationType CELL-TYPE P-TYPE) states that P-TYPE is a collection of #$CellProliferation events in which cells of type CELL-TYPE proliferate.")
(comment geothermalGradient "<code>(#$geothermalGradient OBJ RATE)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has a geothermal gradient of RATE.")
(comment TemperaturePerDistanceRatio "How much temperature changes over a linear distance. For example, in a geothermal gradient (see #$geothermalGradient) temperature increases with depth.")
(comment DegreesCelsiusPerMeter "The temperature of something (in degrees celcius) per linear meter.")
(comment SignificantPetroleumProductionEventType "The collection of collections of events that are generally deemed to be unusual enough to attend to during normal well operation.")
(comment LayerDeposition "The collection of all vaporous deposition process in manufacturing wherein a layer of substance is laid down atom-by-atom or molecule-by-moleculew on a solid surface.")
(disjointWith ThinFilmDeposition CoatingDeposition)
(comment CoatingDeposition "")
(comment pressureOfDeposition "(#$pressureOfDeposition DEPOSITING PRESSURE) means that the #$thinFilmDeposited in DEPOSITING is deposited in a chamber maintained at the #$Pressure PRESSURE.")
(comment atmosphericPressureRangeOfDepositionType "Where DEPOSITING-TYPE is a specialization of #$ThinFilmDeposition, (#$atmosphericPressureRangeOfDepositionType DEPOSITING-TYPE PRESSURE-RANGE) means that in every instance of DEPOSITING-TYPE, the #$ThinFilm instance that is deposited is deposited in a chamber maintained at an atmospheric pressure whose value is quantitatively subsumed by PRESSURE-RANGE.")
(comment VacuumDeposition "The collection of all vaporous deposition process in manufacturing wherein a layer of substance is laid down atom-by-atom or molecule-by-moleculew on a solid surface at sub-atmospheric pressure.")
(comment VacuumDeposition-ThinFilm "The collection of all deposition processes wherein a #$ThinFilm is deposited atom-by-atom or molecule-by-molecule at sub-atmospheric pressures on a solid surface.")
(comment CVDTypeByPressureAtApplication "A #$FacetingCollectionType that facets #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm whose instances all share a common #$pressureOfDeposition.")
(comment volatilePrecursorChemSubstTypeOfCVD "(#$volatilePrecursorChemSubstTypeOfCVD CVD SUBST-TYPE) means that some instance of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType SUBST-TYPE plays the role of a chemical precursor (#$inputsDestroyed) in CVD that reacts or decomposes to generate the #$ThinFilm that is #$thinFilmDeposited in CVD.")
(comment volatilePrecursorChemSubstTypeOfCVDType "A #$RuleMacroPredicate.  (#$volatilePrecursorChemSubstTypeOfCVDType CVD-TYPE SUBST-TYPE) means that every #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm that is an instance of CVD-TYPE features SUBST-TYPE as its #$volatilePrecursorChemSubstTypeOfCVD - that is, that every #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm that is an instance of CVD-TYPE has an instance of SUBST-TYPE as a chemical precursor (#$inputsDestroyed) that reacts or decomposes to generate the #$ThinFilm that is #$thinFilmDeposited in the CVD-TYPE instance.")
(comment AtmosphericPressureCVD "The collection of all CVD processes (instances of #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm) that run at atmospheric pressure.")
(comment LowPressureCVD "The collection of all CVD processes (instances of #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm) that run at subatmospheric pressures.")
(comment UltraHighVacuumCVD "The collection of all CVD processes (instances of #$ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm) that run at near-vacuum pressures.")
(comment ChemicalVaporDeposition-ThinFilm "The collection of all #$ThinFilmDeposition instances wherein the #$ThinFilm that is deposited is produced by exposing the substrate or target layer (see #$thinFilmDepositionOnSurfaceOf) to one or more volatile precursors which react to produce the #$thinFilmDeposited.")
(comment CowardlyFn "(#$CowardlyFn ACT-TYPE) denotes the specialization of ACT-TYPE whose instances are particularly cowardly relative to ordinary instances of ACT-TYPE.")
(comment cowardlyVarietyOfActionType "(#$cowardlyVarietyOfActionType ACT-TYPE AB-ACT-TYPE) means that AB-ACT-TYPE is the collection of all particularly cowardly instances of ACT-TYPE.")
(comment chemicalObjectTypeParticipatesInBioProcessType "(#$chemicalObjectTypeParticipatesInBioProcessType OBJ-TYPE PROC-TYPE) states that in some unspecified circumstance, instances of OBJ-TYPE can be actors in instances of PROC-TYPE. Not every instance of OBJ-TYPE necessarily acts in such a way, but instances of PROC-TYPE are typically observed to have some instance of OBJ-TYPE participating.")
(comment substanceTypeParticipatesInBioProcessType "(#$substanceTypeParticipatesInBioProcessType SUBST-TYPE PROC-TYPE) states that in some unspecified circumstance, instances of SUBST-TYPE can be actors in instances of PROC-TYPE. Not every instance of SUBST-TYPE necessarily acts in such a way, but instances of PROC-TYPE are typically observed to have some instance of SUBST-TYPE participating.")
(comment processTypeInvolvesChemicalObjectTypeWithStatus "(#$processTypeInvolvesChemicalObjectTypeWithStatus PROC-TYPE OBJ-TYPE STATUS) states that there is evidence of type STATUS that instances of OBJ-TYPE can be actors in instances of PROC-TYPE. Not every instance of OBJ-TYPE necessarily acts in such a way, but instances of PROC-TYPE are typically observed to have some instance of OBJ-TYPE participating.")
(comment VectorOrQuantitySlot "A generalization of #$VectorIntervalSlot and #$QuantitySlot.  Each instance of this collection is a binary predicate that attributes some vector interval, scalar interval or quantity to an object.")
(comment FallingStockMarket "A specialization of #$Market and #$DecreaseInMonetaryValue.  Each instance of #$FallingMarket is an event in which the things bought and sold in/on a particular #$Market decrease in overall monetary value.  See also #$RisingMarket")
(comment StockMarketCrash "A specialization of #$MarketCrash and #$FallingStockMarket.  Each instance of #$StockMarketCrash is an event in which the things bought and sold in/on a particular #$StockMarket decrease rapidly in overall monetary value.")
(comment MarketCrash "A specialization of #$FallingMarket.  Each instance of #$MarketCrash is an event in which the things bought and sold in/on a particular #$Market decrease rapidly in overall monetary value.")
(comment Figurehead "A collection of people (a subset of #$Person). A #$Figurehead is a person who in some way appears to be a leader of an organization, but actually has no real power in that organization.")
(comment figureheadOf "(#$figureheadOf GROUP AGENT) means that #$IntelligentAgent AGENT is a #$Figurehead of GROUP.")
(comment 2010FlashCrash "The 2010 flash crash.  A #$StockMarketCrash in which the Dow Jones Industrial Average plunged nine percent and then recovered those losses within minutes.")
(comment WallStreetCrashOf1929 "The 1929 US stock market crash.  The most devastating #$StockMarketCrash in US history.")
(disjointWith Hunting Trawling)
(disjointWith Angling Hunting)
(comment HookingAFish "The collection of events in which a fish is hooked to a fishook.")
(comment FishingWithANet "The collection of instances of #$Fishing in which one attempts to catch fish with a net (see #$FishingNet).")
(comment CatchingFishWithANet "The collection of instances of #$CatchingFish in which fish are caught with a net.")
(comment CatchingFishWithRodAndReel "The collection of instances of #$CatchingFish in which fish are caught with a fishing rod.")
(comment UnderwaterEvent "The collection of events that take place (see #$eventOccursAt) under water.")
(comment ReelingInAHookedFish "The subcollection of #$ReelingInAFishingLine in which an actual fish is attached to the end of the line.")
(comment hookedObject "<code>(#$hookedObject HOOK-EVENT HOOKED)</code> means that in the instance <code>HOOK-EVENT</code> of #$Hooking-AttachmentEvent, <code>HOOKED</code> is the object that is physically hooked by a hook.")
(comment NettingFish "The stage in #$CatchingFishWithANet in which the fish is initially \"snared\" by the net, prior to retrieval.")
(comment ReelingInAFishingLine "The collection of events in which someone reels (see #$Reeling) in a fishing line (see #$FishingLine).")
(comment propellingTypeSubsequentProjectileMotionType "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$ProjectileTypeSubsequentMotionTypeFn, <code>#$propellingTypeSubsequentProjectileMotionType PROPELLING MOTION)</code> identifies <code>MOTION</code> as the collection of instances of #$ProjectileMotion that are the result of <code>PROPELLING</code>, which, as an instance of #$ProjectilePropellingTypeByProjectileType, is the collection of all instances of #$ProjectilePropelling in which an object of a given type is propelled.")
(comment ProjectilePropellingTypeByProjectileType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$ProjectilePropelling into sub-collections based on what type of object is propelled.")
(comment ProjectileTypeSubsequentMotionTypeFn "<code>(#$ProjectileTypeSubsequentMotionTypeFn PROPELLING-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ProjectileMotion that are the result of an instance of <code>PROPELLING-TYPE</code>, which, as an instance of #$ProjectilePropellingTypeByProjectileType, is the collection of all instances of #$ProjectilePropelling in which an object of a given type is propelled.")
(comment objectPropelled "<code>(#$objectPropelled PROPELLING OBJECT)</code> identifies <code>OBJECT</code> as the projectile propelled in <code>PROPELLING</code>, an instance of #$ProjectilePropelling.  See also the specialization #$objectThrown.")
(comment Spearfishing "A primitive method of #$Fishing in which people hunt fish with spears.")
(comment RetrievingACatchFromTheWater "The stage is #$HarvestingAquaticAnimals in which the \"catch\" is finally pulled from the water.")
(comment SecuringAPotentialCatch-AquaticHarvesting "The first step in #$HarvestingAquaticAnimals in which the \"catch\" is initially secured (hooked, netted, speared, trapped, etc.), allowing it to be subsequently retrieved.")
(comment ThrowingASpear "The collection of #$ThrowingAnObject events in which the #$objectThrown is a spear (see #$Spear).")
(comment PropellingOfProjectileTypeFn "<code>(#$PropellingOfProjectileType PROJECTILE-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ProjectilePropelling in which the #$objectPropelled is an instance of <code>PROJECTILE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment propellingTypeOfProjectileType "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$PropellingOfProjectileTypeFn, <code>(#$propellingTypeOfProjectileType PROPELLING-TYPE PROJECTILE-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>PROPELLING-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$ProjectilePropelling in which the #$objectPropelled is an instance of <code>PROJECTILE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment RemovingSomethingFromStuff "The collection of events in which an object is removed from some stuff-like substance in which it was contained or embedded.  Typically, the object is of a different type than the stuff it was in.")
(comment RemovalFromStuffTypeFn "<code>(#$RemovalFromStuffTypeFn STUFF-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of events in which an object is removed from some stuff-like substance of the type <code>STUFF-TYPE</code>.")
(comment removalTypeFromStuffType "The predicate that corresponds to #$RemovalFromStuffTypeFn, <code>(#$removalTypeFromStuffType REMOVAL-TYPE STUFF-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>REMOVAL-TYPE</code> as the collection of removal events such that an object is removed from some stuff-like substance of type <code>STUFF-TYPE</code>.")
(comment RemovingSomethingFromAGenericContainer "The collection of instances of #$RemovingSomething-Translational in which the removal is a removal of something out of a container-like environment.  Positive examples include removing a marble from a jar, a sore tooth from a mouth, and a toy from the bottom of a pool.  Counter-examples include removing a mole from skin, removing rust from a metal surface, and removing oneself from a situation.")
(comment RemovalFromGenericContainterTypeFn "<code>(#$RemovalFromGenericContainterTypeFn CONTAINER-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of removal events where what is removed is removed from (see #$removalFrom) a container-like object of type <code>CONTAINER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment removalTypeFromGenericContainerType "The predicate that corresponds to #$RemovalFromGenericContainterTypeFn, <code>(#$removalTypeFromGenericContainerType REMOVAL-TYPE CONTAINER-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>REMOVAL-TYPE</code> as the collection of removals where what is removed is removed from (see #$removalFrom) a container-like object of type <code>CONTAINER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment removalFrom "An instance of #$ActorSlot that specializes #$objectRemaining and #$fromLocation, #$removalFrom relates an instance of #$RemovingSomething-Translational to the object or place from which something is removed.")
(comment WellTubing "The collection of pipes run within #$WellCasing to transport fluids.")
(comment ProductionTubing "A specialization of #$WellTubing.  Production tubing is used to bring well fluids out of the well.")
(comment ProductionWell "A specialization of #$Well.  Each instance of #$ProductionWell is a well used specifically to extract fluid stuff from the Earth.")
(comment ChristmasTree-Well "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$ChristmasTree-Well is a system of valves and fittings installed at the top of a well to control and direct the flow of well fluids.")
(comment GasLift "A specialization of #$ArtificialLiftDevice.  Each instance of #$GasLift is a device used to increase the outflow rate of a well by injecting gas into the liquid flowing out of the well.  The injection of the gas makes the fluid flowing out of the well lighter (less dense), so it permits the well to flow faster.")
(comment Pumpjack "A specialization of #$ArtificialLiftDevice and #$Pump-Mechanical.  Pumpjacks are commonly used mechanisms for causing #$WellOutflow-ArtificiallyLifted.")
(comment Casinghead "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$Casinghead is a system of heavy fittings installed at the surface, which the well casing is attached to.")
(comment Wellhead "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$Wellhead is a system of devices, valves, and pipes that sits at the top of a #$Wellbore.  It has various significant parts, such as the #$Casinghead and the #$Tubinghead and the #$ChristmasTree-Well.")
(comment TubingCorrosion "The oxidation of an iron-based #$WellTubing.")
(comment SubsurfacePump "A specialization of #$Pump-Mechanical.  Subsurface pumps are pumps that are used in wells below the surface of the earth.")
(comment SubsurfacePumpFailure "The failure of a #$SubsurfacePump.")
(comment ValveFailure "The failure of a #$Valve-Mechanical.")
(comment WellboreSanding "The accumulation of instances of #$SandParticle at the bottom of a well.")
(comment FormationDamage "The collection of events in which the geological formation near the wellbore is damaged, slowing oil production.")
(comment Waterflooding "A specialization of #$SecondaryOilRecovery.  IN each instance of #$Waterflooding, water is injected into a producing reservoir to flush tapped oil from the formation to increase recovery.")
(comment PumpFailure "The failure of a #$Pump-Mechanical.")
(comment StockTankBarrelsPerDay "This is a unit of volume movement equaling one #$StockTankBarrel-UnitOfVolume (i.e. 158.97 #$Liters, or 42 U.S. gallons) in one #$DaysDuration.")
(comment BarrelsPerDay "This is a unit of volume movement equaling one #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume or 158.97 #$Liters in one #$DaysDuration.")
(comment ConcentrationStrength "A general #$QuantityType whose instance are used to state how much of something there is in a particular sample of something else.  Specializations of #$ConcentrationStrength include #$Concentration-PartsPerNumber and #$Molarity.")
(comment StockTankBarrelsPerDayPerPoundsPerSquareInch "A unit used to express the productivity index or \"PI\" (see #$productivityIndex) of a well.")
(comment ProductivityIndex-InflowFormula "An expression of the ability of a reservoir to deliver fluids to the wellbore.")
(comment DoWhileStatement "A class of #$IterationCodeStatements found in programs authored using members of the #$C-ProgrammingLanguageFamily.  A #$DoWhileStatement specifies that the #$subStatementOfIterationStatement be iteratively executed for as long as the value resolved by evaluating the #$conditionExpressionOfDoWhileStatement is nonzero at the end of loop execution.")
(comment exampleInstanceForQuantityForFormula "(#$exampleInstanceForQuantityForFormula QBF QUANTITY THING) means that thing is an example or characteristic instance of the type of thing having QUANTITY in the context of QBF.  It will be denoted with either a #$The expression or , if there is more than one of a certain type involved in a formula, with a #$TheNthFn expression.  E.g. (#$exampleInstanceForQuantityForFormula #$NewtonsSecondLaw (#$The #$Mass) (#$The #$PartiallyTangible)) holds because  (#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot #$NewtonsSecondLaw
       (#$The #$Mass) #$PartiallyTangible) holds.  Note that since #$NewtonsSecondLaw is a #$SingleFocalObjectFormula we'll know that if we get different #$isa constraints we should be able to generate a single example to represent them all.")
(comment StockTankBarrel-UnitOfVolume "A function which returns an instance of #$Volume. A stock tank barrel is similar to a barrel (see #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume).  Like a barrel, a stock tank barrel is 42 U.S. gallons or about 158.987 liters, but the oil is required to be at a temperature of 60 degrees F (15.556  degrees C).")
(comment WellInflow-Water "A specialization of #$WellInflow.  In each instance of #$WellInflow-Water, water flows into a #$Well .")
(comment WellInflow-Oil "A specialization of #$WellInflow.  In each instance of #$WellInflow-Water, petroleum flows into a #$Well.")
(comment rateOfFlow "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot that a movement event to its flow rate.")
(comment FlowPressure "A specialization of #$Pressure.  The pressure a fluid exerts when it is flowing.")
(comment ProductivityIndexValue "#$ProductivityIndexValue is the collection of quantities that express the productivity index of a well.")
(comment OilAndGasIndustryKBContentTest "A collection of KB content regression tests that exercise Cyc's knowledge of the Oil and Gas industry.")
(comment SemanticConstructionGrammarTemplate "A specialization of #$Template.   Each instance of #$SemanticConstructionGrammarTemplate specifies a pattern and program parameters for using a semantic construction grammar template parser to translate natural language into CycL.")
(comment SCGIndexicalConcept "A specialization of #$IndexicalConcept.  Each instance of #$SCGIndexicalConcept is a term that can be used to establish links between the #$nlPattern and the #$cycLPattern for a #$SemanticConstructionGrammarTemplate.")
(comment PatternTermFn "(#$PatternTermFn TERM N) denotes the Nth #$SCGIndexicalConcept for TERM.")
(comment termOfTypeWithIndex "(#$patternTerm TERM N INDEXICAL) means INDEXICAL is the Nth #$SCGIndexicalConcept for TERM.")
(comment scgTemplateVariable "(#$scgTemplateVariable TEMPLATE TERM) means that TERM is the variable associated with TEMPLATE.")
(comment templateResultType "(#$templateResultType TEMPLATE THING) means that when NL is ampped into the CycL for template, the result will be an instance or specialization of THING.")
(comment templateMt "(#$templateMt TEMPLATE MT) means that MT is the proper reasoning context within which to apply TEMPLATE.")
(comment templateInferenceMode "(#$templateInferenceMode TEMPLATE MODE) means that MODE is the proper inference mode to use for TEMPLATE.")
(comment cycLPattern "(#$cycLPattern TEMPLATE EXPR) means that EXPR specifies the CycL form into which #$SemanticConstructionGrammarTemplate maps NL.  Usually, some of the terms in EXPR will be instances of #$SCGIndexicalConcept (q.v.).")
(comment exampleConstraintSentenceForQuantityBasedFormula "(#$exampleConstraintSentenceForQuantityBasedFormula QBF EXAMPLE-SENTENCE) means that EXAMPLE-SENTENCE is a sentence that captures (at the example level) an operative constraint on the applicability of a #$QuantityBasedFormula.  This relationship is a function of the values for #$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot, #$constraintForQuantityBasedFormula,  and #$unitSlotsForFormula and utilizes the mappings to example instances via #$exampleInstanceForQuantityForFormula.")
(comment ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn "(#$ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn QBF QUANTITY) denotes a characteristic sentence that objects mapped to the example instances involved must meet in order for the equation to be applicable in the context of QBF an instance of #$QuantityBasedFormula.  The QUANTITY argument denotes the quantity on the left hand side of the equation (a lone quantity that is the first argument to a #$numericallyEquals formula) that acts as a filter to filter out the quantity attribution which would end up in the consequent of a rule constructed with the resulting formula.  For example, the result of evaluating (#$ExampleAntecedentFormulaForEquationFn QBF (#$The #$Area)) where the equation associated with QBF is (#$The #$Area) = (#$The #$Length) x (#$The #$Width), would be the following conjunction (#$and (#$lengthOfObject (#$The #$SpatialThing) (#$The #$Length)) (#$widthOfObject (#$The #$SpatialThing) (#$The #$Width))).")
(comment couldImpact "(#$couldImpact AFFECTOR AFFECTED) says that there is at least weak evidence that AFFECTOR, in some underspecified way, has an impact on AFFECTED. This predicate is neutral with respect to whether AFFECTOR and AFFECTED are agents, propositions, situations, or classes  of situations.")
(comment InsulatorResistance "An instance of #$ElectricalResistance.  #$InsulatorResistance is a very high level of electrical resistance; objects having #$InsulatorResistance conduct no electricity at all.  See also #$electricalResistanceOfObject.")
(comment ConductorResistance "An instance of #$ElectricalResistance.  #$ConductorResistance is a very low level of electrical resistance; any object having #$ConductorResistance readily conducts electricity.  See also #$electricalResistanceOfObject.")
(comment ThinFilmDepositionTypeByDepositionMethodType "A #$FacetingCollectionType covering #$ThinFilmDeposition.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ThinFilmDeposition whose instances all feature instances of a common situation type as #$properSubSituations, or sequences of propersubsituations instantiating a distinctive sequence of situation types.")
(comment UnconventionalPetroleumDeposit "A specialization of #$PetroleumReservoir. Unconventional petroleum deposits are areas in geological formations that contain a significant amount of unconventional petroleum (such as #$Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil.")
(comment OsteoblastDifferentiation "A collection of events and a specialization of CellularDifferentiation. In each instance of #$OsteoblastDifferentiation one or more cells become more specialized in the direction of becoming #$Osteoblasts.")
(comment BiologicalHomeostasis "The collection of all biological regulatory processes that serve to maintain an organism's internal environment.  Processes that regulate an organism's body temperature, energy reserves, blood pressure, blood glucose level, etc., are all homeostatic regulatory processes.")
(comment ChemicalHomeostaticRegulation "The collection of all biological regulatory processes that serve to maintain the \"correct\" levels of substance in an organism (or in a part of an organism).")
(comment CalciumIonHomeostasis "Instances of #$CalciumIonHomeostasis are processes in which the concentration of #$CalciumIons in an organism or part of an organism such as a cell, is maintained.")
(comment RenalAbsorptionFromGlomerularFiltrate "Instances are processes in which substances are selectively re-absorbed from the pro-urine, or initial filtrate, during urine production.  Urine production is a two stage process: first, fluid is removed from the #$Bloodstream via simple filtration (see #$FiltrationAtRenalCorpuscle).  This step is not very selective; essentially all molecules below a certain size are allowed to enter the kidney.  As the pro-urine moves through the #$Nephron and collecting ducts, various substances are absorbed back into the #$Bloodstream through a variety of means, some active and some passive.")
(comment applicableRuleTemplateForFormula "(#$applicableRuleTemplateForFormula  QBF TEMPLATE) means that rules derived from the formula using #$trueRule should use TEMPLATE, an instance of #$RuleTemplate. Typically the arg2 will be one of either (#$PredicateRuleTemplateFn #$theorem-Forward) -- for forward rules, or (#$PredicateRuleTemplateFn theorem) for backwards rules.")
(disjointWith UnitOfRate UnitOfPermeability)
(comment UnitOfPermeability "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure.  Each instance of #$UnitOfPermeability is a function that returns an instance of #$Permeability (q.v.) when applied to a real number (or a pair of real numbers).")
(comment Darcy "An instance of #$UnitOfPermeability.  #$Darcy is a function that returns an instance of #$Permeability.  Darcy units are widely used in petroleum engineering.")
(comment permeabilityOfObject "(#$permeabilityOfObject OBJ PERM) means that OBJ has the #$Permeability PERM.")
(comment viscosityOfSubstance "(#$viscosityOfSubstance F VISC) means that the #$FluidTangibleThing F has the #$Viscosity VISC.")
(comment Viscosity "Each instance of #$Viscosity represents a specific viscosity (i.e., \"runniness\") of some substance. The lower the viscosity of a substance, the more easily it flows or spreads out. Vicosities of objects are indicated with the predicate #$viscosityOfSubstance.")
(comment ExampleConsequentFormulaForEquationFn "(#$ExampleConsequentFormulaForEquationFn  QBF QUOTED-EQA) denotes a characteristic mathematical sentence that the quantities must satisfy to be equal to the quantity on the left hand side in EQA.  For example, (in pseudo CycL) the result of evaluating (#$ExampleConsequentFormulaForEquationFn QBF (#$Quote (#$The #$Area) = (#$The #$Length) x (#$The #$Width))) would be the following (#$areaOfObject (#$The #$SpatialThing) (#$TimesFn (#$The #$Length) (#$The #$Width))).  Note that the equation in arg2 of this function should be a quoted CycL sentence.")
(comment AverageReservoirPressure "A specialization of #$Pressure.  The average reservoir pressure of a well.")
(comment canonicalVariableNameForExampleInstance "(#$canonicalVariableNameForExampleInstance QBF THING VAR) means that VAR is the canonical variable assigned to THING for use in rules generated by QBF.")
(disjointWith ActorSlot SetOrCollectionPredicate)
(comment sceneTypeDependencies "<code>(#$sceneTypeDependencies SCRIPT PRED1 SCENE1 PRED2 SCENE2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INS</code> of the situation-type <code>SCRIPT</code>, if <code>(PRED1 INS SCENE1)</code> holds, then <code>(PRED2 INS SCENE2)</code> follows.  Like <code>SCRIPT</code>, <code>SCENE1</code> and <code>SCENE2</code> are specializations of #$Situation, hence <code>PRED1</code> and <code>PRED2</code> must be capable of relating an individual (such as <code>INS</code> to a collection -- see #$KindLevelPredicate.")
(comment ExtremeContactWireMisalignment "The collection of events or situations in which a #$Contact-IntegratedCircuit and a #$Wire-IntegratedCircuit that are arranged in a perpendicular coupling (are associated with an appropriate instance of #$ICContact-WireJoint) are misaligned in that neither of the surface areas in contact spatially subsume each other.  This situation can result in a reduced value for the corresponding #$Contact-WireJointCrossSectionArea.")
(comment KCNH8-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for proteins of the #$IonChannel class named ''potassium voltage-gated channel subfamily H member 8''.")
(comment RBMS3-Human-GIS "The collection of human #$NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''RNA binding motif, single stranded interacting protein 3''.")
(comment ERC2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''ELKS/RAB6-interacting/CAST family member 2p''.")
(comment ZNF366-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''zinc finger protein 366''.")
(comment GPR98-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''G protein-coupled receptor 98''.")
(comment PHACTR1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''phosphatase and actin regulator 1''.")
(comment CNTNAP2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''contactin associated protein-like 2''.")
(comment NRG1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''neuregulin 1''.")
(comment VAMP1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''vesicle-associated membrane protein 1''.")
(comment CTNNBL1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''catenin, beta like 1''.")
(comment LMX1A-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''LIM homeobox transcription factor 1, alpha''.")
(comment NR5A2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''nuclear receptor subfamily 5, group A, member 2''.")
(comment FMN2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''formin 2''.")
(comment CACNA2D3-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for the #$IonChannel component protein named ''calcium channel, voltage-dependent, alpha 2/delta subunit 3''.")
(comment IFT57-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''intraflagellar transport 57 homolog''.")
(comment HHLA2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''HERV-H LTR-associating 2''.")
(comment FSTL1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''follistatin-like 1''.")
(comment PRR16-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''proline-rich 16''.")
(comment FunctionCallForNthArgumentOfFunctionCallFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used to denote a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable with a certain use.  Where SUPER-CALL is itself a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$FunctionCallForNthArgumentOfFunctionCallFn SUPER-CALL N) denotes the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable such that whatever value is returned by its #$codingFunctionInvoked on its #$actualArgumentListOfFunctionInvocation is specified as the value supplied to the Nth argument of the #$codingFunctionInvoked in SUPER-CALL.")
(comment FunctionCallSetsInitializationValueForVariableFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used to reference function calls (instances of #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) which are used to set the initialization values of #$InitializationStatements.  Specifically, where INIT is an #$InitializationStatement and VAR is a #$ComputerCodeVariable such that INIT sets the initialization value for VAR by means of a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$FunctionCallSetsInitializationValueFn INIT VAR) denotes the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that INIT uses to set the initialization value for VAR.")
(comment functionCallSetsInitializationValueForVariable "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$FunctionCallSetsInitializationValueForVariableFn.  Where INIT is an #$InitializationStatement and VAR is a #$ComputerCodeVariable such that INIT sets the initialization value for VAR by means of a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$functionCallSetsInitializationValueForVariable INIT VAR CALL) means that INIT uses CALL to set the initialization value for VAR.")
(comment predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf "<code>(#$predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf 
 COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> means that the binary predicate <code>COMP-PRED</code> is the composition of the binary predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code>. If <code>(#$predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf 
 COMP-PRED PRED-1 PRED-2)</code>, then <code>(COMP-PRED X Z)</code> if and only if there is something, <code>Y</code>, such that <code>(PRED-1 X Y)</code> and <code>(PRED-2 Y Z)</code>. 
<p>
Suppose, for example, that (#$predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf #$mothersName #$mother #$nameString). Then it follows from (#$mother #$GeorgeWBush #$BarbaraBush ) and (#$nameString #$BarbaraBush \"Barbara Bush\") that (mothersName
#$GeorgeWBush \"Barbara Bush\"). The function corresponding to this
predicate is #$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn.")
(comment unfocusedWikipediaArticleName "(#$unfocusedWikipediaArticleName TITLE) holds when the #$Wikipedia-WebSite article with the title TITLE is not tightly focused around a single clear concept.  Thus, articles with such assertions are not good targets for automatic concept learning/creation, because the resulting concept will end up being quite muddled.")
(comment averageReservoirPressureForWell "<code>(#$averageReservoirPressureForWell WELL RATE)</code> means that the #$ProductionWell <code>WELL</code> is in a producing reservoir with an average pressure of <code>RATE</code>.")
(comment PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid "A specialization of #$CarboxylicAcid.  Each instance of #$PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid is an organic acid with containing one or more nitrogen atoms connected through carbon atoms to one or more carboxyl (-COOH) groups.")
(comment PenteticAcid "A specialization of #$PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid. Pentetic acid (DTPA) is an acid, like EDTA, commonly used to dissolve limescale.")
(comment Fura-2 "A specialization of #$PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid. Fura-2 is used in calcium imaging.")
(comment NitrilotriaceticAcid "A specialization of #$PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid.")
(comment GradualAccumulation "A specialization of #$IncreaseEvent and #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$GradualAccumulation  is an event in which a physical stuff gradually accumulates somewhere. Examples include the accumulation of #$PlaqueStuff and #$Limescale.")
(comment PlaqueBuildup "A specialization of #$GradualAccumulation.  Each instance of #$PlaqueBuildup is an event in which a #$PlaqueStuff builds up on teeth.")
(comment DescalingAgent "A specialization of #$CleaningSubstance.  Descaling agents are used to prevent or reduce the buildup of scale.")
(comment EthylenediaminetetraaceticAcid "A specialization of #$PolyaminoCarboxylicAcid. Ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) is an acid commonly used to dissolve #$Limescale.")
(comment SlottedLiner "Slotted liners are used to line the producing portions of wellbores.")
(comment LimescaleBuildup "A specialization of #$GradualAccumulation.  Each instance of #$LimescaleBuildup is an event in which #$Limescale builds up on something (such as a kettle, a water heater, a bathtub or a pipe).")
(comment ScaleBuildupOnSlottedLiner "The collection of events in which scale accumulates on a #$SlottedLiner.")
(comment Descaling "The activity of removing scale, usually with a #$DescalingAgent.")
(comment Limescale "The collection of all limescale, a hard chalky deposit created when calcium and possibly other minerals come out of liquid solution.")
(comment SteamAssistedGravityDrainage "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamFlooding.  Each instance of #$SteamAssistedGravityDrainage involves using two horizontal wells, one a few meters below the other.  Steam is injected into the upper well.  The steam heats bitumen and lowers its viscosity, whereupon the force of gravity causes it to flow into the lower well.")
(comment ReverseSteamAssistedGravityDrainage "A specialization of #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamFlooding.  Each instance of #$SteamAssistedGravityDrainage injecting steam into the production well of a pair of wells typically used for SAGD, and then letting melted bitumen flow into that same well.")
(comment BinaryCompositionPredicateFn "<code>(#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn PRED-1 PRED-2)</code> designates the binary predicate that is the composition of the binary predicates <code>PRED-1</code> and <code>PRED-2</code>. 
<p>
<code>((#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn PRED-1 PRED-2) X Z)</code> is true if and only if there is something, <code>Y</code>, such that <code>(PRED-1 X Y)</code> and <code>(PRED-2 Y Z)</code>. For example, ((#$BinaryCompositionPredicateFn #$mother #$nameString) #$GeorgeWBush \"Barbara Bush\"), since (#$mother #$GeorgeWBush #$BarbaraBush) and (#$nameString #$BarbaraBush \"Barbara Bush\"). The function corresponding to this predicate is #$predicateIsPredicateCompositionOf.")
(comment DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseType "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of #$PhysicalDevices (a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice) whose instances all have use in a common kind of manufacturing as an intended primary function.")
(comment allInstancesDedicatedToManufacturingProcessType "(#$allInstancesDedicatedToManufacturingProcessType DEV-TYPE PROC-TYPE) means that DEV-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$PhysicalDevice which have performing the role of #$deviceUsed in instances of PROC-TYPE as an #$intendedPrimaryFunction.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseTypeFn")
(comment llGeneImpactBoneTest "The predicate that corresponds to #$LLGeneImpactBoneTestFn, <code>(#$llGeneImpactBoneTest GENE N TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the instance of #$KBContentTest that queries for a #$couldImpact chain of <code>N</code> steps between <code>GENE</code>, a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily, and the amount of bone present in the body, denoted by (#$QuantitySlotForArg2Fn #$BoneTheStuff #$amountPresentAt).")
(comment LLGeneImpactBoneTestFn "A function that returns an instance of #$KBContentTest.  (#$LLGeneImpactBoneTestFn GENE N) is the KB Content Test that queries for a #$couldImpact chain of length N between GENE and the amount of bone present in the body, represented by the quantity slot (#$QuantitySlotForArg2Fn #$BoneTheStuff #$amountPresentAt).")
(comment relationAllInstanceInstance-Conditional "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate used to tersely express a common rule pattern. <code>(#$relationAllInstanceInstance-Conditional TYPE PRED1 THING1 PRED2 THING2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INS</code> of the collection <code>TYPE</code>, if <code>(PRED1 INS THING1)</code> holds, then <code>(PRED2 INS THING2)</code> follows.")
(comment OilAndGasIndustryMt "A general theory context used to represent knowledge specifically relevant to the oil and gas industry.")
(comment RateOfFlowFn "(#$RateOfFlowFn MOV) denotes the rate of flow of the movement event MOV.")
(comment reservoirOfWell "<code>(#$reservoirOfWell WELL RES)</code> means that <code>RES</code> is the reservoir from which <code>WELL</code> draws down resources.")
(comment ReservoirOfWellFn "<code>(#$ReservoirOfWellFn WELL)</code> denotes the reservoir from which <code>WELL</code> draws down resources.")
(comment skinFactor "<code>(#$skinFactor WELL FACTOR)</code> means that the #$ProductionWell <code>WELL</code> has a skin factor of <code>FACTOR</code>.  A positive skin factor means something is impeding inflow, and a negative skin factor means inflow is happening faster than otherwise expected.")
(comment SkinFactorFn "<code>(#$SkinFactorFn WELL)</code> denotes the skin factor of the #$ProductionWell <code>WELL</code>.  A positive skin factor means something is impeding inflow, and a negative skin factor means inflow is happening faster than otherwise expected.")
(comment SteadyStateMultiphaseInflowWithSkinFormula "An expression used to calculate expected multiphase steady state flow in terms of average reservoir pressure, incorporating \"skin\".")
(comment NKX3-1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''NK3 homeobox 1''.")
(comment MED30-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''mediator complex subunit 30''.  This gene is also named ''THRAP6''.")
(comment PHF20L1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''PHD finger protein 20-like 1''.")
(comment FREM1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''FRAS1 related extracellular matrix 1''.")
(comment C9orf138-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''family with sequence similarity 154, member A''.")
(comment ZCCHC6-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''zinc finger, CCHC domain containing 6''.")
(comment C9orf126-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''suppressor of cancer cell invasion''.")
(comment PARD3-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''par-3 partitioning defective 3 homolog''.")
(comment PLEKHA1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''pleckstrin homology domain containing, family A (phosphoinositide binding specific) member 1''.")
(comment FGF14-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''fibroblast growth factor 14''.")
(comment HTRA1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''HtrA serine peptidase 1''.")
(comment ETS2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''v-ets erythroblastosis virus E26 oncogene homolog 2''.")
(comment IL1RL1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''interleukin 1 receptor-like 1''.")
(comment MTHFR-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase (NAD(P)H)''.")
(comment ESR1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''estrogen receptor 1''.")
(comment LRP5-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''low density lipoprotein receptor-related protein 5''.")
(comment VDR-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''vitamin D (1,25- dihydroxyvitamin D3) receptor''.")
(comment CYP19A1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''cytochrome P450, family 19, subfamily A, polypeptide 1''. Also known as ''CYP19''.")
(comment COL1A1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''collagen, type I, alpha 1''.")
(comment XPR1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''xenotropic and polytropic retrovirus receptor 1''.")
(comment CDH9-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''cadherin 9, type 2 (T1-cadherin)''.")
(comment ARL15-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''ADP-ribosylation factor-like 15''.")
(comment CSMD3-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''CUB and Sushi multiple domains 3''.")
(comment MTMR2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''myotubularin related protein 2''.")
(comment CHST11-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''carbohydrate (chondroitin 4) sulfotransferase 11''.")
(comment DCC-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''deleted in colorectal carcinoma'', which is a netrin 1 receptor.")
(comment ZNF569-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''zinc finger protein 569''.")
(comment CD2AP-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''CD2-associated protein''.")
(comment TBX20-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''T-box 20''.")
(comment MLLT3-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''myeloid/lymphoid or mixed-lineage leukemia (trithorax homolog, Drosophila); translocated to, 3''.")
(comment ALDH1A2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''aldehyde dehydrogenase 1 family, member A2''.")
(comment RestrictionOnSlotFn "<code>(#$RestrictionOnSlotFn TYPE SLOT)</code> denotes the predicate <code>PRED</code> that is a restriction on the possible arg1 values of <code>SLOT</code> to instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment directlyRelatedSlotsForFormula "<code>(#$directlyRelatedSlotsForFormula FORM SLOT1 COL1 SLOT2 COL2)</code> means that <i>ceteris paribus</i>, relative to a system <code>SYS</code> described by the formula <code>FORM</code>, if <code>(#$isa INS1 COL1)</code> and <code>(#$isa INS2 COL2)</code>, and <code>INS1</code> and <code>INS2</code> are suitably related within <code>SYS</code>, then values of <code>?X</code> for <code>(SLOT1 INS1 ?X)</code> will vary directly with values of <code>?Y</code> for <code>(SLOT2 INS2 ?Y)</code> and <i>vice versa</i>.")
(comment inverselyRelatedSlotsForFormula "<code>(#$inverselyRelatedSlotsForFormula FORM SLOT1 COL1 SLOT2 COL2)</code> means that <i>ceteris paribus</i>, relative to a system <code>SYS</code> described by the formula <code>FORM</code>, if <code>(#$isa INS1 COL1)</code> and <code>(#$isa INS2 COL2)</code>, and <code>INS1</code> and <code>INS2</code> are suitably related within <code>SYS</code>, then values of <code>?X</code> for <code>(SLOT1 INS1 ?X)</code> will vary inversely with values of <code>?Y</code> for <code>(SLOT2 INS2 ?Y)</code> and <i>vice versa</i>.")
(comment inflowRate "<code>(#$inflowRate WELL-INFLOW RATE)</code> means that the inflow <code>WELL-INFLOW</code> flows at the rate <code>RATE</code>.")
(comment ProportionalityPredicate "The collection of predicates that pertain to mathematical proportionalities (e.g., they are used to declare that certain quantities are directly or inversely related).")
(comment ContactInsulatingLayerSeries "A type of physical series and system of devices.  Each instance of this collection is a physical series of contacts and portions of insulating material consisting of some number of contacts surrounded by some portion of an insulating layer.  Just enough of the insulating layer is included in each insulating series member (#$seriesMembers) so that, assuming the contact is vertically embedded into the insulating layer, the length of the Z axis of the contact is equal to the length of the Z axis of any adjacent insulating member of the series.  Typical instances will involve at least one contact situated between a pair of insulating series members.  The length of the Y axis of the entire chunk is the sum of the lengths of the Y axis of each contact plus the sum of the lengths of the Y axis for each separating insulating member.")
(comment Acceleration "Acceleration is the change in speed of an object per unit time.  It is a measurable physical quantity, measured in units such as #$MetersPerSecondPerSecond.")
(comment CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeConstants that are reserved for purposes of specifying alternate response values for #$CodingFunctions whose range of possible return values is finite.")
(comment codeFunctionCodeConstantValueString "(#$codeFunctionCodeConstantValueString CONST STRING) means that STRING denotes the numeric value associaated with the #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant CONST.")
(comment codeFunctionCodeConstantValue "(#$codeFunctionCodeConstantValue CONST INT) means that INT is the value associated with CONST.")
(comment codeFunctionHasCaseConstant "(#$codeFunctionHasCaseConstant FN CONSTANT) means that CONSTANT is a #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant used to reference one of several possible alternate return values of FN.")
(comment CaseConstantNamedInLibraryFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for referencing #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstants.  (#$CaseConstantNamedInLibraryFn NAME LIB) denotes the #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant named NAME in the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIB.")
(comment caseConstantHasNameInLibrary "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CaseConstantNamedInLibraryFn.  (#$caseConstantHasNameInLibrary CONST NAME LIB) means that NAME is the name supplied for the #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant CONST by the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIB.")
(comment RateOfChangeInQuantityFn "<code>(#$RateOfChangeInQuantityFn QUANT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment rateOfChangeInQuantityRelativeToRateOfChangeInQuantity "<code>(#$rateOfChangeInQuantityRelativeToRateOfChangeInQuantity QUANT-TYPE1 QUANT-TYPE2 RATE)</code> means that <code>RATE</code> is the collection of rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE1</code> relative to the rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE2</code>.")
(comment rateOfChangeInQuantity "<code>(#$rateOfChangeInQuantity QUANT-TYPE RATE)</code> means <code>RATE</code> is the collection of rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Raccoon-Common "The collection of all common raccoons. A type of #$CarnivoreOrder. #$Raccoon-Common constitutes a #$BiologicalSpecies.")
(comment ClassicalMechanics "Classical mechanics: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment Joule "The joule is an energy quantity or work in the International System of Units. One joule is equal to the energy expended in applying a force of one #$Newton through a distance of one #$Meter.")
(comment Newton "The newton is the basic unit of force in the MKS system.  It is the force that gives to a mass of one kilogram an acceleration of one meter per second per second.")
(comment Rheology "A field devoted to the study of the flow of liquids and soft solids.")
(comment enthalpyOfSystem "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$System to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$enthalpyOfSystem SYS QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy had by <code>SYS</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.  In general, the enthalpy of a system is expresed as H, where H=U+pV and U is the internal energy of the system, p is the pressure at the boundary of the system and its environment, and V is the volume of the system.")
(comment Viscometer "A device used for measuring the viscosity of a fluid.")
(comment specificGravity "<code>(#$specificGravity SUBSTANCE S)</code> means that the specific density of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> is <code>S</code>.  <code>S</code> is the ratio of the density of <code>SUBST</code> to the density of water.  It is assumed that the density measurements are taken at 1 atmosphere of pressure.")
(comment specificWeight "<code>(#$specificWeight SUBSTANCE GAMMA TEMP)</code> means that the specific weight of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> at the temperature <code>TEMP</code> and standard sea-level atmospheric pressure is <code>GAMMA</code>.  <code>GAMMA</code> is the weight per unit volume of <code>SUBSTANCE</code>.")
(comment Hydraulics "Hydraulics: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment HenryDarcy "Henry Darcy was a French engineer who made significant contributions to #$Hydraulics.")
(comment DijonMustard "A specialization of #$Mustard-ThePreparation.  Dijon style mustard usually contains both red and white wine.")
(comment YellowMustard "A specialization of #$Mustard-ThePreparation.  Yellow mustard is the most common mustard in the US.  It is smooth and bright yellow.")
(comment SpicyBrownMustard "A specialization of #$Mustard-ThePreparation.  Spicy brown mustard is a common mustard used in the US.  It has coarsely-ground brown mustard seeds as its main ingredient.  It has a speckled brown color.")
(comment SpeckledPattern "The collection of all instances of speckled patterns, consisting of speckles (small spots of contrasting colors).")
(comment HoneyMustard "A specialization of #$Mustard-ThePreparation.  Honey  mustard is a blend of honey and mustard.")
(comment EcolePolytechnique "A major university in France.")
(comment CollegeDeFrance "A major university in France.")
(comment PantheonAssasUniversity "A major university in France.")
(comment NewSorbonneUniversity "A major university in France.")
(comment ParisSorbonneUniversity "A major university in France.")
(comment PierreAndMarieCurieUniversity "A major university in France.")
(comment ParisDiderotUniversity "A major university in France.")
(comment ParisSud11University "A major university in France.")
(comment Paris13University "A major university in France.")
(disjointWith StressVector Molarity)
(disjointWith Mass StressVector)
(disjointWith Temperature StressVector)
(disjointWith ElectricalCharge StressVector)
(disjointWith AngularDistance StressVector)
(disjointWith Volume StressVector)
(disjointWith Voltage StressVector)
(disjointWith Pressure StressVector)
(disjointWith Volatility-Physical StressVector)
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance StressVector)
(comment StressVector "A specialization of #$RatioQuantity.  Each instance of #$StressVector is a force vector divided by the area upon which is acts.")
(comment NormalStress "A specialization of #$StressVector.  Each instance of #$NormalStress is a stress vector perpindicular to the area of a substance.")
(comment ShearStress "A specialization of #$StressVector.  Each instance of #$ShearStress is a stress vector tangent to the area of a substance.")
(comment ShearStrength "A specialization of #$TangiblePhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$ShearStrength is a specific capacity of some physical object to resist the slipping of one segment in relation to another (see #$StressVector).  Shear strengths are designated using a #$GenericValueFunction; higher value means more resistance to slippage.  Shear strengths of objects are indicated with the predicate #$shearStrengthOfObject.")
(comment Ant "The collection of all ants. A apecialization of #$Hymenoptera. #$Ant is an #$OrganismClassificationType.  Each instance of #$Ant is a small insect of a family known for organizing into large colonies.")
(comment SimpleEye "A specialization of #$Eye.  Simple eyes are non-compound eyes.  Simple eyes, in contrast with #$CompoundEyes, have one concave photoreceptive surface.  Some simple eyes have a single lens (see #$SingleLensEye).")
(disjointWith SimpleEye CompoundEye)
(comment CompoundEye "A specialization of #$Eye.  Each instance of #$CompoundEye is an eye, in contrast with instances of #$SimpleEye, that has multiple concave photoreceptive surfaces.")
(comment RateOfChangeRelativeToRateOfChangeFn "<code>(#$RateOfChangeRelativeToRateOfChangeFn QUANT-TYPE1 QUANT-TYPE2)</code> denotes the collection of rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE1</code> relative to the rates of change in <code>QUANT-TYPE2</code>.  For example, the rates of change in pressure relative to the rates of change in height (which might be expressed as \"dp/dh\") would be denoted with (#$RateOfChangeRelativeToRateOfChangeFn  #$Pressure #$Height).")
(comment MultiphaseOilVerticalOutflowFormula "An expression used to calculate multiphase oil outflow from a well.")
(comment coefficientOfFriction-Kinetic "When two surfaces are in contact and relative motion, the frictional resistance is almost uniform over a wide range of low speeds.  This resistance is characterized by the kinetic coefficient of friction.  The kinetic coefficient is typically less than the coefficient of static friction (see #$coefficientOfFriction-Static). <code>(#$coefficientOfFriction-Kinetic OBJ1 OBJ2 NUM)</code> means that <code>NUM</code> is the ratio of the frictional resistance force (see #$FrictionVector) to the normal force which presses the surfaces of <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> together.  See also #$coefficientOfFriction")
(comment FrictionFactorOfFluidFlowFn "<code>(#$FrictionFactorOfFluidFlowFn FLOW)</code> denotes the friction factor <code>f</code> for <code>FLOW</code>.")
(comment DiameterOfCylinderFn "<code>(#$DiameterOfCylinderFn CYL)</code> denotes the diameter <code>D</code> of the cylinder <code>CYL</code>.")
(comment diameterOfCylinder "<code>(#$DiameterOfCylinderFn CYL)</code> denotes the diameter <code>D</code> of the cylinder <code>CYL</code>.")
(comment CPQuestionSuggestionTemplate "The collection of all instances of #$FormulaTemplate that are used to suggest questions from content in a selected portion of text from a cellular biology source.")
(comment femoralNeckLength "(#$femoralNeckLength ORG L) relates an organism, ORG, to a measure of hip geometry, L.  Specifically, L is the length of the necks of ORG's femurs.")
(comment femoralNeck-ShaftAngle "(#$femoralNeck-ShaftAngle ORG A) relates an organism, ORG, to a measure of hip geometry, A.  Specifically, A is the angle at which the neck of the #$Femur (the portion that participates in the #$HipJoint) joins the shaft of the #$Femur.")
(comment femoralNeckWidth "(#$femoralNeckWidth ORG W) relates an organism, ORG, to a measure of hip geometry, W.  Specifically, W is the width of the necks of ORG's femurs, at their narrowest point.")
(comment OrderOfMagnitudeInterval "#$OrderOfMagnitudeInterval, a specialization of #$ScalarInterval, is the collection of intervals which represent significant differences in quantity, for the various types of measurable properties.  The most familiar case is for numbers, in which orders of magnitudes typically correspond with powers of 10; thus, in any given numerical quantity, the 100's dominate the 10's or the units, which are negligible with respect to the hundreds.  Similar scales could be identified for any measurable property.  For example, for #$Time-Quantity, some intervals which represent orders of magnitude are: #$AFewSecondsDuration, #$AFewMinutesDuration, #$AFewHoursDuration, #$AFewDaysDuration, #$AFewWeeksDuration, etc.  Note that orders of magnitude for the same measurable property may differ between microtheories; e.g., the orders of magnitude for #$Time-Quantity in a `GeologicalTimeMt' would be much larger than those listed above, which are relevant for human perceptions and activities.
<p>
<p>
<p>
Any two attributes which represent amounts of the same kind of property (e.g., time, distance) and which are also instances of #$OrderOfMagnitudeInterval will be assumed to differ so substantially in size that the smaller one (and values associated with it) will be insignificant compared to the larger interval (and values associated with it).  That is, in general and as a default, if ORD1 and ORD2 are two different instances of #$OrderOfMagnitudeInterval which are also instances of the same type of quantity (e.g., #$Speed, #$Mass, #$Density), then one is negligible with respect to the other.  To know which dominates the other, we need additional knowledge about their relative size, e.g., that ORD2 is a #$followingValue of (i.e., 'bigger' than) ORD1.  See also #$negligibleWRT, #$followingValue.  The predicate #$orderOfMagnitude (q.v.) is used to relate particular quantities to the appropriate instance of #$OrderOfMagnitudeInterval.  For example, two days -- in Cyc, (#$DaysDuration 2) -- has the #$orderOfMagnitude #$AFewDaysDuration.")
(comment subExpressionForFactor "<code>(#$subExpressionForFactor PRINCIPLE EXPR QUANTITY-TYPE)</code> means that in the formula for <code>PRINCIPLE</code>, the sub-expression <code>EXPR</code> is a way of expressing the relevance of <code>QUANTITY-TYPE</code> within the principle.")
(comment industryTypeProducingProductType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ProductionIndustryTypeFn.  Where PRODUCT-TYPE is a product type, (#$industryTypeProducingProductType PRODUCT-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE) means that INDUSTRY-TYPE is the collection of all and only those instances of #$Industry-Localized which produce instances of PRODUCT-TYPE.")
(comment ManufacturingMetrologyProcess "The collection of all instances of #$MeasuringSomething that are performed in support of some manufacturing process (#$Manufacturing).")
(comment MetrologyProcessTypeByIndustryType "A faceting collection on #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess whose instances are all carried out in support of manufacturing in a common industry.")
(comment MetrologyProcessesOfIndustryTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used in reifying collection instances of #$MetrologyProcessTypeByIndustryType.  Where INDUSTRY-TYPE is an #$IndustryType, (#$MetrologyProcessesOfIndustryTypeFn INDUSTRY-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$MeasuringSomething that occur as #$properSubEvents of instances of #$Manufacturing supporting INDUSTRY-TYPE, or more exactly, instances of #$Manufacturing that are themselves #$properSubEvents of instances of #$Industry-Localized that are instances INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment allMetrologyProcessesOfIndustryType "Where INDUSTRY-TYPE is an #$IndustryType, (#$allMetrologyProcessesOfIndustryType INDUSTRY-TYPE METROLOGY-TYPE) means that METROLOGY-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$MeasuringSomething that occur as #$properSubEvents of instances of #$Manufacturing supporting INDUSTRY-TYPE, or more exactly, instances of #$Manufacturing that are themselves #$properSubEvents of instances of #$Industry-Localized that are instances INDUSTRY-TYPE.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$MetrologyProcessesOfIndustryTypeFn.")
(comment factorTypicallyAccountsFor "<code>(#$factorTypicallyAccountsFor PRINCIPLE QUANTITY-TYPE EXPR PERCENTAGE)</code> means that typical applications of the formula for <code>PRINCIPLE</code>, the factor <code>QUANTITY-TYPE</code> typically accounts for <code>PERCENTAGE</code> amount of the value described by the sub-expression <code>EXPR</code>.")
(comment TNFRSF11B-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily, member 11b''.")
(comment WLS-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''wntless homolog''.  The gene is also known as ''GPR177''.")
(comment SOX6-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''SRY (sex determining region Y)-box 6''.")
(comment RAP1A-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''RAP1A, member of RAS oncogene family''.")
(comment TBC1D8-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''TBC1 domain family, member 8 (with GRAM domain)''.")
(comment OSBPL1A-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''oxysterol binding protein-like 1A''.")
(comment PPAP2B-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''phosphatidic acid phosphatase type 2B''.")
(comment HECW2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''HECT, C2 and WW domain containing E3 ubiquitin protein ligase 2''.")
(comment CASR-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''calcium-sensing receptor''.")
(comment MMRN1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''multimerin 1''.")
(comment IRX2X-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''iroquois homeobox 2''.")
(comment PDZD2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''PDZ domain containing 2''.")
(comment TGFB1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''transforming growth factor, beta 1''.")
(comment CACNB2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''calcium channel, voltage-dependent, beta 2 subunitp''.")
(comment DOCK1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''dedicator of cytokinesis 1''.")
(comment PDGFD-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''platelet derived growth factor D''.")
(comment RAD51l1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''RAD51-like 1''.")
(comment SALL1-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''RNA binding motif, single stranded interacting protein 3''.")
(comment FBXO31-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''F-box protein 31''.")
(comment CDH2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''cadherin 2, type 1, N-cadherin (neuronal)''.")
(comment formulaCompleteInputFactorsForOutputQuantity "<code>(#$formulaCompleteInputFactorsForOutputQuantity QBF SET-OF-FACTORS OUTPUT-QUANTITY)</code> means that inputting values to <code>QBF</code> for all of the factors in <code>SET-OF-FACTORS</code> will provide sufficient information for using <code>QBF</code> to calculate a value for <code>OUTPUT-QUANTITY</code>.")
(comment transistorThresholdVoltage "(#$transistorThresholdVoltage TRANSISTOR VOLTAGE) means that VOLTAGE is the voltage required to \"open\" the gate.  Depending on whether it is a n-channel or p-channel transistor, this threshold will be either a positive or negative voltage, respectively.  For negative thresholds, voltages that are less negative will close the gate.  For positive thresholds higher positive voltages will open the gate.")
(comment N-TypeSemiconductorStuff "The collection of all N-type semiconductor stuff.  N-type semiconductors are made by a \"doping\" process that adds atoms capable of providing extra conduction electrons to the semiconductor substrate.")
(comment P-TypeSemiconductorStuff "The collection of all P-type semiconductor stuff.  P-type semiconductors are made by a \"doping\" process that takes away weakly bound electrons from the semiconductor substrate.")
(comment N-Region-Transistor "The collection of all areas in a transistor that are n-regions.")
(comment P-Region-Transistor "The collection of all areas in a transistor that are p-regions.")
(comment N-Channel-Transistor "The collection of all N-regions in transistors that are embedded in p-regions.")
(comment P-Channel-Transistor "The collection of all P-regions in transistors that are embedded in N-regions.")
(comment NorPRegion-Semiconductor "The collection of all areas made of semiconductor stuff that are processed to be either N or P regions.")
(comment Scalpel "The collection of all scalpels. A type of #$Knife, #$ManufacturedGoods, and #$MedicalDevice. The collection #$Scalpel is a  a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment WellTypeByDirection "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Well whose instances are all of the same direction.")
(comment WellTypeByIntendedDirectionOfFlow "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Well whose instances are all of the same intended direction of flow.")
(comment WellTypeByResource "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Well whose instances are all used to extract the same kind of resource.")
(comment SourceWire-Transistor "The collection of source terminals in transistors.  Typically current flows from the source to the drain portion of the terminal.  The signal is regulated or modified by the current from the gate.")
(comment DrainWire-Transistor "The collection of drain terminals in transistors.  Typically current flows from the source to the drain portion of the terminal.  The signal is regulated or modified by the current from the gate.")
(comment TransisitorTypeByPolarity "A specialization of #$SecondOrderCollection. Each instance of this collection is a spec of #$Transistor, instances of which share composition and functionality based on the polarity of the regions under the gate, source, and drain.")
(comment N-MOSFET-Transistor "The collection of MOSFET transistors that have an <i>n</i> source and drain region on top of a <i>p</i> substrate.  An n-channel (see #$N-Channel-Transistor) is formed when the positive voltage hits a certain threshold.  Voltages less than the threshold result in a closed gate.")
(comment P-MOSFET-Transistor "The collection of MOSFET transistors that have a <i>p</i> source and drain region on top of an <i>n</i> substrate.  A p-channel (see #$P-Channel-Transistor) is formed when the negative voltage hits a certain negative threshold.  Voltages greater than the threshold result in a closed gate.")
(comment FieldEffectTransistor "A specialization of #$Transistor.  Each instance of #$FieldEffectTransistor (also called a <i>unipolar transistor</i>) is a transistor that operates by creating a conductive channel between two terminals of the same polarity via either holes (p-channel) or electrons (n-channel).")
(comment DepletionModeFieldEffectTransistor "The collection of instances of #$FieldEffectTransistor that naturally have a conductive channel and whose gate narrows current (closes) or widens (opens) that channel.  Contrast this with an #$EnhancementModeFieldEffectTransistor where some current from gate to source is required to open the channel in the first place.")
(comment MetrologyTaskTypeBySubsumingProcessingEventType "A #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess whose instances all figure in a common type of #$ProcessingEvent.")
(comment MetrologyTaskTypeBySubsumingProcessingEventTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used in reifying instances of #$MetrologyTaskTypeBySubsumingProcessingEventType.  Where PROCESSING-TYPE is a specialization of #$ProcessingEvent, (#$MetrologyTaskTypeBySubsumingProcessingEventTypeFn PROCESSING-TYPE) denotes the class of all instances of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess that occur as #$properSubEvents of instances of PROCESSING-TYPE.")
(comment allMetrologyInInstancesOfProcessingType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$MetrologyTaskTypeBySubsumingProcessingEventTypeFn.  Where PROCESSING-TYPE is a specialization of #$ProcessingEvent, (#$allMetrologyInInstancesOfProcessingType PROCESSING-TYPE METROLOGY-TYPE) means that METROLOGY-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess that occur as #$properSubEvents in instances of PROCESSING-TYPE.")
(comment MetrologyTool "The collection of every instance of #$MeasuringDevice which has use (#$deviceUsed in some type of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess as its #$intendedPrimaryFunction.")
(comment MetrologyToolTypeByMetrologyType "A collection of collections.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$MetrologyTool whose instances are intended to be used (see #$deviceUsed, #$intendedPrimaryFunction) in instances of some common type of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess.")
(comment DeviceTypeUsedForMetrologyTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used in reifying collection instances of #$MetrologyToolTypeByMetrologyType.  Where METROLOGY-TYPE is a specialization of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess, (#$DeviceTypeUsedForMetrologyTypeFn METROLOGY-TYPE) is the collection of all #$MetrologyTool instances which have as their #$intendedPrimaryFunction use (#$deviceUsed) in instances of METROLOGY-TYPE. ")
(comment allDevicesUsedForMetrologyType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$DeviceTypeUsedForMetrologyTypeFn.  Where METROLOGY-TYPE isa a specialization of #$ManufacturingMetrologyProcess, (#$allDevicesUsedForMetrologyType METROLOGY-TYPE TOOL-TYPE) means that TOOL-TYPE is the collection of every #$MetrologyTool that has playing the role of #$deviceUsed in instances of METROLOGY-TYPE as its #$intendedPrimaryFunction.")
(comment PrePerforatedLiner "Pre-perforated liners are used to line the producing portions of wellbores.")
(comment NorPChannel-Semiconductor "The collection of all areas in a transistor that are either N or P channels -- that is, each instance of this collection is either an n-region embedded within a p-region or vice versa.  Depending on whether the transistor is a depletion mode or enhancement mode device, this channel will either intrinsically exist between the source and drain of a transistor, or it will not be an intrinsic feature and instead be created by the gate current.")
(comment SubstrateRegion-Transistor "The collection of all chunks of semiconductor material that are the substrate or body of a (typically FET) transistor.")
(comment SourceRegion-Transistor "The collection of all areas in a transistor that are either n-regions or p-regions that are, conceptually, the source of the current flow through the transistor.  They are defined by their location directly below the source wire that provides the current.")
(comment DrainRegion-Transistor "The collection of all areas in a transistor that are either n-regions or p-regions that are, conceptually, the destination of the current flow through the transistor.  They are defined by their location directly below the drain wire that provides the current.")
(comment MetalOxideSemiconductorFET "A type of #$FieldEffectTransistor where, originally (and now increasingly) a metal gate contact was insulated from the source and drain layers by an insulating layer of some sort of oxide.  The traditional silicon dioxide gate insulator is now increasingly being replaced by high-K dielectrics due to leakages of the silicon dioxide at thicknesses below 2 nanometers.")
(comment EnhancementModeFieldEffectTransistor "The collection of instances of #$FieldEffectTransistor that do not naturally have a conductive channel and some current from gate to source is required to create or open the channel.  Contrast this with a #$DepletionModeFieldEffectTransistor where the channel is instrinsically open and the gate voltage closes or reopens it.")
(comment Tubinghead "A specialization of #$SystemOfDevices.  Each instance of #$Tubinghead is a system of fittings installed at the surface, which the well tubing is attached to.  The #$Tubinghead is supported by the #$Casinghead.")
(comment sentenceLocationInParagraph "The predicate that corresponds to #$ParagraphSentenceFn, <code>(#$sentenceLocationInParagraph SENTENCE PARAGRAPH INDICATOR)</code> identifies <code>SENTENCE</code> as the instance of #$NLSentence that is uniquely identified via the #$SentenceLocator <code>INDICATOR</code> within <code>PARAGRAPH</code>, an instance of #$NLParagraph.")
(comment ChokeValve "A specialization of #$Valve-Mechanical.  Choke valves are used to create choked flow.")
(comment EngineChoke "A specialization of #$ChokeValve.  Engine chokes are sometimes used in internal combustion engines to restrict the flow of air into the carburetor.")
(disjointWith EngineChoke IndustrialChoke)
(comment AdjustibleChoke "A specialization of #$IndustrialChoke.  Adjustible chokes are valves designed to be used at the surface to control downhole pressure by means of introducing a restriction to flow.")
(comment FixedChoke "A specialization of #$IndustrialChoke.  Fixed chokes create choked flow by directing flow through a restriction with a fixed size.")
(comment genomicsPreferredName "(#$genomicsPreferredName THING STRING) means that the string STRING is a preferred name for #$Cyc to use when referring to THING in the context of reasoning about genes, proteins and their roles in living systems.")
(comment CellularCommunicationTypeByOrganismType "A second order collection that facets #$CellularCommunication into sub-collections based on the kind of organism involved.")
(comment CellularCommunicationInPlants "The collection of cellular communication events that take place in plants.")
(comment CellularCommunicationInAnimals "The collection of cellular communication events that take place in animals.")
(comment SemiconductorRegionTypeByPolarity "This collection facets chunks of semiconductor stuff into N or P regions.")
(comment semiconductorRegionPolarity "(#$semiconductorRegionPolarity SEMICONDUCTOR-REGION POLARITY) means that the semiconductor region is of the type given by POLARITY.")
(comment SwitchStatement "The collection of all #$SelectionCodeStatements which specify choice points between multiple options as defined by the possible return values of a called #$CodingFunction.")
(comment switchVariableOfSwitchStatement "(#$switchVariableOfSwitchStatement STATEMENT VAR) means that VAR is the cited #$ComputerCodeVariable whose value (as evaluated via an independent function call) will determine which one of several possible cases to pursue in the #$CaseListingStatement of the #$SwitchStatement STATEMENT.")
(comment CaseListingStatement "The collection of all #$BracketedCodeBlocks with immediately subsuming statements that are #$SwitchStatements, and that list the possible cases of the subsuming #$SwitchStatement.")
(comment CaseListingStatementOfSwitchStatementFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used in reifying instances of #$CaseListingStatement.  Where SWITCH is a #$SwitchStatement, (#$CaseListingStatementOfSwitchStatementFn SWITCH) denotes the bracketed #$CaseListingStatement of SWITCH.")
(comment caseListingStatementOfSwitchStatement "(#$caseListingStatementOfSwitchStatement SWITCH CASE-LISTING) means that CASE-LISTING is the bracketed #$CaseListingStatement of the #$SwitchStatement SWITCH.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CaseListingStatementOfSwitchStatementFn.")
(comment CaseStatement "The collection of all statements stating individual alternative cases within a #$CaseListingStatement of a #$SwitchStatement.  #$CaseStatements are ordinarily individuated by #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstants where the executable statements embedded within the #$CaseStatement will be executed in case the case constants value is returned by the #$switchVariableOfSwitchStatement for the #$SwitchStatement that immediately subsumes the #$CaseListingStatement that subsumes the #$CaseStatement.")
(comment caseListingHasCaseStatement "(#$caseListingHasCaseStatement CASE-LISTING CASE-STATEMENT) means that CASE-STATEMENT specifies one of the alternative cases in the #$CaseListingStatement CASE-LISTING.")
(comment CaseStatementForCaseConstantFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for reifying instances of #$CaseStatement.  Where LISTING is a #$CaseListingStatement and CASE-CONST is a #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant used to specify a possible return value for the #$CodingFunction used to establish the value of the #$switchVariableOfSwitchStatement for the #$SwitchStatement that subsumes LISTING, (#$CaseStatementForCaseConstantFn LISTING CASE-CONSTANT) denotes the #$CaseStatement which is individuated in LISTING by the reserved constant CASE-CONSTANT.")
(comment listingHasCaseStatementForConstant "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CaseStatementForCaseConstantFn.  Where LISTING is a #$CaseListingStatement and CASE-CONST is a #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant used to specify a possible return value for the #$CodingFunction used to establish the value of the #$switchVariableOfSwitchStatement for the #$SwitchStatement that subsumes LISTING, (listingHasCaseStatementForConstant LISTING CASE-CONST CASE-STATE) means that CASE-STATE is the #$CaseConstant individuated in isting by CASE-CONSTANT.")
(comment conditionedStatementOfCaseStatement "(#$conditionedStatementOfCaseStatement CASE-STATEMENT EXECUTABLE) means that EXECUTABLE is the executable #$ComputerCodeStatement within CASE-STATE that will be executed if the value of the #$CodeFunctionDedicatedCaseConstant that is the #$conditionExpressionOfStatement for CASE-STATE is returned.  The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ConditionedStatementOfCaseStatementFn.")
(comment Asparagus-Foodstuff "Asparagus in any of its edible forms, whether raw or cooked.")
(comment ImmediateCausalSlotTrendPredicate "Instances of #$ImmediateCausalSlotTrendPredicate are used to describe immediate causal trends of some quantity.")
(comment ConstrictionEvent "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$ConstrictionEvent is an event in which some object is constricted (i.e., it is made narrower).")
(comment Bottomhole "A specialization of #$Underground.  Each instance of #$Bottomhole is the part of a #$Wellbore at the deepest true vertical depth.")
(comment OpeningAValve "A specialization of #$ConstrictionEvent.  Each instance of #OpeningAValve is an event in which a #$Valve is made less restrictive of flow through a conduit.")
(comment ClosingAValve "A specialization of #$ConstrictionEvent.  Each instance of #$ClosingAValve is an event in which a #$Valve is made more restrictive of flow through a conduit.")
(disjointWith OpeningAValve ClosingAValve)
(comment downstreamFrom "<code>(#$downstreamFrom FLOW-PATH LOC1 LOC2)</code> means that some portion of the #$objectMoving during a typical #$FluidFlow-Translation <code>FLOW</code> that occurs in <code>FLOW-PATH</code> is found at <code>LOC1</code> before it it flows to <code>LOC2</code>.")
(comment upstreamFrom "<code>(#$upstreamFrom FLOW-PATH LOC1 LOC2)</code> means that some portion of the #$objectMoving during a typical #$FluidFlow-Translation <code>FLOW</code> that occurs in <code>FLOW-PATH</code> is found at <code>LOC1</code> after it it flows to <code>LOC2</code>.")
(comment pipeSegments "<code>(#$pipeSegments PIPE SEG)</code> means that <code>SEG</code> is a segment of <code>PIPE</code>.  Segments of pipes are pipe conduits that are parts of large pipe conduits.")
(disjointWith WideningAConduit ConstrictionEvent)
(comment WideningAConduit "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$WideningAConduit is an event in which a conduit is widened.")
(comment transistorGateStatus "(#$transistorGateStatus  TRANSISTOR STATUS) means that the gate in TRANSISTOR has STATUS -- is either open or closed according to whether the voltage threshold (see #$transistorThresholdVoltage) at the gate terminal is reached.")
(comment AdjustingAValve "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$AdjustingAValve is an event in which some valve is either opened or closed.")
(disjointWith SinglePhaseHydrocarbonFluid MultiphaseFluidTangibleThing)
(comment HydrocarbonFluid "Hydrocarbon in fluid form.")
(comment MultiHydrocarbonFluid "The collection of all instances of #$HydrocarbonFluid that contain distinct types of #$Hydrocarbon, whether they be in a mixture (see #$HydrocarbonMixture) or simply occurring together as gas and liquid in a #$MultiphaseHydrocarbonFluid.  \"Types of #$Hydrocarbon\" here mean that distinct instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies are represented.")
(comment MultiphaseHydrocarbonFluid "The collection of instances of #$MultiphaseFluidTangibleThing comprised entirely of hydrocarbons. This would include, e.g., all of the oil/gas portion of a fluid flowing from a well, but not the entire fluid, which also includes water.")
(comment gasOilRatio "An instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot, <code>(#$gasOilRatio HYDROCARBON SCALAR)</code> means that <code>SCALAR</code> is the result of calculating the ratio (see #$ratioOfTo) of the volume of gas in a sample  of #$MultiHydrocarbonFluid <code>HYDROCARBON</code> to the volume of oil in the sample.")
(comment SinglePhaseHydrocarbonFluid "The collection of all instances of #$HydrocarbonFluid whose constituent hydrocarbon(s) are in a consistent state of matter (e.g., all liquid, all gaseous).")
(comment ProductionTubingAndBottomholeSystem "A specialization of #$Artifact and #$Pipe-GenericConduit.  The production tubing and bottomhole system is the generically pipe-like system in a well consisting of the production tubing and the bottomhole into which the reservoir drains.")
(comment bottomholeFlowingPressure "<code>(#$bottomholeFlowingPressure WELL PRESS)</code> means that the #$ProductionTubingAndBottomholeSystem <code>WELL</code> has a fluid flowing at #$Pressure <code>PRESS</code> in the vicinity of the #$Bottomhole.")
(comment productivityIndex "<code>(#$productivityIndex WELL QUANT)</code> means that the #$ProductionTubingAndBottomholeSystem <code>WELL</code> has a productivity index of <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment Gas-LightHydrocarbon "The collection of all instances of #$Hydrocarbon whose molecules are \"short\" or simple enough that in pressure/atmospheric/temperature conditions akin to those on the surface of the earth, are in a gaseous state.")
(comment gasOilRatio-InSolution "An instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot, <code>(#$gasOilRatio-InSolution HYDROCARBON SCALAR)</code> means that <code>SCALAR</code> is the result of calculating the ratio (see #$ratioOfTo) of the volume of #$Gas-LightHydrocarbon in a sample  of #$MultiHydrocarbonFluid <code>HYDROCARBON</code> to the volume of #$Petroleum-CrudeOil in the sample, <i>were it the case</i> that <code>HYDROCARBON</code> is in a single phase (liquid) form.  Hence, where <code>HYDROCARBON</code> is entirely liquid, #$gasOilRatio-InSolution becomes equivalent to #$gasOilRatio, which measures the actual gas/oil ratio, regardless of state.")
(comment wellInflowRate "<code>(#$wellInflowRate WELL RATE)</code> means that the well  <code>WELL</code> has an inflow that flows at the rate <code>RATE</code>.")
(comment LotProcessingStep "The collection of all industrial #$ProcessingEvents wherein a delimited 'step' or 'stage' in an industry fabrication process model is instantiated as a subevent for every element of a processed 'lot' (#$ProcessingAllotment), with as many such subevents obtaining as there are elements in the #$ProcessingAllotment.  The subevents may occur sequentially (#$LotProcessingStep-Serial) or simultaneously (#$LotProcessingStep-Parallel):  that is, the elements of the #$ProcessingAllotment being processed in the #$LotProcessingStep may be processed one after the other, or all together.")
(comment LotProcessingStepTypeByIterationStructure "A #$CollectionType which partitions #$LotProcessingStep. It has two collection instances: #$LotProcessingStep-Serial and #$LotProcessingStep-Parallel.  The former is the collection of all #$LotProcessingSteps wherein all of the elements of the #$ProcessingAllotment or 'lot' being processed are processed simultaneously; the latter is the collection of all #$LotProcessingSteps wherein all of the elements of the #$ProcessingAllotment are processed sequentially.")
(disjointWith LotProcessingStep-Parallel LotProcessingStep-Serial)
(comment MassProcessingInIncrementsTool "The collection of all #$PhysicalDevices which are designed for use in instances of (#$MassEventOfTypeFn #$ProcessingEvent), i.e., events wherein a procedurally delimited number of like #$ProcessingEvents are respectively executed, in sequence or in parallel, on items or sets of items.")
(comment LotProcessingTool "The collection of all #$PhysicalDevices designed to carry out delimited sets of operations on the elements of #$ProcessingAllotments ('lots') either in series or in parallel.")
(comment lotProcessIterationSchemeOfTool "A predicate which distinguishes whether a given #$LotProcessingTool executes instances of #$LotProcessingStep-Serial or #$LotProcessingStep-Parallel.   (#$lotProcessIterationSchemeOfTool TOOL PROCESSING-TYPE) means that TOOL is designed to execute exclusively #$LotProcessingSteps of the #$LotProcessingStepTypeByIterationStructure PROCESSING-TYPE.")
(comment lotProcessIterationSchemeOfToolType "A predicate which distinguishes whether all of the instances of a given class of #$LotProcessingTool execute #$LotProcessingSteps that are either exclusively #$LotProcessingStep-Serial or exclusively #$LotProcessingStep-Parallel.  (#$lotProcessIterationSchemeOfToolType TOOL-TYPE PROCESSING-TYPE) means that every instance of TOOL-TYPE s designed to execute exclusively #$LotProcessingSteps of the #$LotProcessingStepTypeByIterationStructure PROCESSING-TYPE.")
(comment LotProcessingStep-Parallel "The collection of all industrial #$ProcessingEvents wherein a delimited 'step' or 'stage' in an industry fabrication process model is simultaneously instantiated as a subevent for every element of a processed 'lot' (#$ProcessingAllotment), with as many instantiations as there are elements in the #$ProcessingAllotment.")
(comment DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to reify instances of #$DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseType.  Where PROC-TYPE is a specialization of #$Manufacturing, (#$DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseTypeFn PROC-TYPE) denotes the collection of every instance INST of PhysicalDevice such that (#$intendedPrimaryFunction INST PROC-TYPE deviceUsed) holds, i.e., the collection of all #$PhysicalDevices that have use in instances of PROC-TYPE as an intended primary function.")
(comment AthabascaOilSandsBitumen "The extra heavy crude oil (i.e. bitumen) derived from the Athabasca oil sands in the Alberta, Canada region.")
(comment Liquid-LightHydrocarbon "A specialization of #$Hydrocarbon.  Each instance of #$Liquid-LightHydrocarbon is a substance consisting of very light hydrocarbon molecules.  The hydrocarbon molecules in question are just heavy enough to remain in liquid form under normal terrestrial surface conditions.")
(comment Petroleum-CrudeOil "A specialization of #$FossilFuel and #$HydrocarbonMixture, and a #$TangibleStuffCompositionType, crude oil is usually pumped from the ground and used to make gasoline, petrochemicals, plastics, etc.  See also #$PetroleumProduct and #$PetroleumProduct-Refined.  Most crude oil is liquid under ordinary ambient conditions, but heavier crudes such as bitumen (see #$Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil) are solid under normal ambient conditions.")
(comment MultiHydrocarbonSubstance "A specialization of #$Hydrocarbon. Each instance of #$MultiHydrocarbonSubstance isa a substance consisting of different types of #$Hydrocarbon, whether in a mixture, or in a liquid, gas or solid form.")
(comment HydrocarbonMixture "A specialization of #$MultiHydrocarbonSubstance.  Each instance of #$HydrocarbonMixture is a substance consisting of different hydrocarbons wherein the different hydrocarbons occur together in a mixture (versus, e.g., separated in a #$MultiphaseHydrocarbonFluid).")
(comment DilutingHydrocarbonWithLightHydrocarbon "A specialization of #$Diluting.  Each instance of #$DilutingHydrocarbonWithLightHydrocarbon is an event in which some portion of #$Hydrocarbon is diluted by mixing some lighter hydrocarbon in with it.")
(comment dilutingAgent "<code>(#$dilutingAgent DILUTING SUBST)</code> means that <code>SUBST</code> is a diluent in the event <code>DILUTING</code>.  Cf. #$dilutedSubstance.")
(comment dilutedSubstance "<code>(#$dilutedSubstance DILUTING SUBST)</code> means that <code>SUBST</code> is diluted in the event <code>DILUTING</code>.  Cf. #$dilutingAgent.")
(comment Naphtha "A specialization of #$HydrocarbonMixture, #$Liquid-LightHydrocarbon, and #$PetroleumProduct.  Naphtha is an intermediate product produced during the refining of crude oil or coal tar.  It is a volatile mixture of light liquid hydrocarbons.")
(comment Dilbit "A specialization of #$PetroleumProduct.  Dilbit is bitumen  (see #$Petroleum-ExtraHeavyCrudeOil) diluted with #$Naphtha.")
(comment PetroleumEngineering "Petroleum engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment DepletionRegion-Semiconductor "The collection of all areas within a doped semiconductor that is devoid of any mobile charge carriers.")
(comment ElectronHole "Instances of this collection are spatial regions in atoms or atomic lattice that lack an electron where one could exist or is normally present.  In integrated circuit manufacturing, it typically refers to a lack of an electron in an otherwise full electron shell.")
(comment concentrationOfElectronsInRegion "(#$concentrationOfElectronsInRegion REGION CONCENTRATION) means that REGION (typically a region on some piece of semiconductor) has the concentration of free electrons CONCENTRATION.")
(comment concentrationOfElectronHolesInRegion "(#$concentrationOfElectronHolesInRegion REGION CONCENTRATION) means that REGION (typically a region on some piece of semiconductor) has the concentration of #$ElectronHoles CONCENTRATION.")
(comment N-ChannelCreation "The collection of all events in which an N channel is created in a FET transistor")
(comment POrNChannelCreation "The collection of all events in which a P or N channel is created in a FET transistor")
(comment P-ChannelCreation "The collection of all events in which an P channel is created in a FET transistor")
(disjointWith P-ChannelCreation N-ChannelCreation)
(comment NChannelRemoval "The collection of all events in which an N channel is removed/destroyed in an FET transistor")
(comment POrNChannelRemoval "The collection of all events in which a P or N channel is removed/destroyed in an FET transistor")
(comment PChannelRemoval "The collection of all events in which an P channel is removed/destroyed in an FET transistor")
(comment InversionLayerRegion-Semiconductor "The collection of all areas within a doped semiconductor that have an appreciable concentration of mobile charge carriers.")
(comment CreationFn "A function which takes a #$FirstOrderCollection as its argument and returns a collection of #$CreationEvents in each of which some member of the input collection is an #$outputsCreated in that event.")
(comment DestructionFn "A function which takes a #$FirstOrderCollection as its argument and returns a collection of #$DestructionEvents in each of which some member of the input collection is an #$inputsDestroyed in that event.  See also #$PhysicalDestructionOfIndividualFn.")
(comment SituationTypeForTypeFn "(#$SituationTypeForTypeFn TYPE COLL) refers to the collection of situations in which instances of TYPE are instances of COLL.  The collection of situations returned are characterized as situations in which the criteria for membership in COLL are satisfied.  For example, (#$SituationTypeForTypeFn #$Marble-Ball  #$BlueColor) is the collection of situations in which some instance of #$Marble-Ball, INS, satisfies (#$mainColorOfObject INS #$BlueColor).  This holds because #$mainColorOfObject is the defining relationship for colors.  For collections specified via a scoping relation (like #$TheCollectionOf or subcollection functions used with #$TheSetOf), the membership condition is given by any constraints imposed by the scoping expression.")
(comment situationTypeForType "The corresponding predicate for #$SituationTypeForTypeFn.")
(comment boilingPointAt1ATM "A predicate that relates an object to its so-called \"normal\" boiling point, or the temperature at which it boils at one Atmosphere of pressure.")
(comment boilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$boilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that the instance #$PartiallyTangible will boil when its temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant.")
(comment meltingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$meltingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that the instance #$PartiallyTangible will reach the equilibrium between solid and liquid when its temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant.")
(comment Petrophysics "Petrophysics: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment Geophysicist "Scientist engaged in the development and application of Geophysics.")
(comment Petrophysicist "Scientist engaged in the development and application of Petrophysics.")
(comment ReservoirEngineering "Reservoir engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment DrillingEngineering "Drilling engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment PetroleumProductionEngineering "Petroleum production engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment DrillingEngineer "The collection of engineers who specialize in #$DrillingEngineering.")
(comment ReservoirEngineer "The collection of engineers who specialize in #$ReservoirEngineering.")
(comment PetroleumProductionEngineer "The collection of engineers who specialize in #$PetroleumProductionEngineering.")
(comment BarnesAndNobleNook "A specialization of #$EBookReader.  Each instance of #$BarnesAndNobleNook is a Nook e-book reader.")
(comment EBookReader "A specialization of #$PortableObject and #$BatteryPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$EBookReader is a portable device designed to be used for reading e-books.")
(comment BiologicalEngineering "Biological engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment BiologicalEngineer "The collection of engineers involved bioengineering.")
(comment BiochemicalEngineer "The collection of engineers involved biochemical engineering.")
(comment AutomotiveEngineering "Automotive engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment ComputerEngineering "Computer engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy focused on the design and building of computers.")
(comment NookColor "A specialization of #$EBookReader.  Each instance of #$NookColor is a color Nook e-book reader.")
(comment AerospaceEngineering "Aerospace engineering: a #$ScientificFieldOfStudy.")
(comment criticalPoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$criticalPoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that the instance #$PartiallyTangible will reach the equilibrium between gas and liquid when its temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant.  <code>TEMP</code> is the so-called \"critical temperature\" above which point <code>OBJ</code>, if in a gaseous state, cannot be liquified, regarless of the pressure.  <code>PRESSURE</code> is similarly the critical pressure, above which point <code>OBJ</code>, if in liquid form, cannot be transition into a gaseous state, regardless of the temperature.  At any point above the critical point, <code>OBJ</code> will be in a plasma state.")
(comment dewPoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$dewPoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that the instance #$PartiallyTangible will, if in a gaseous state, form its first droplet of dew when its temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant. For chemically pure substances, #$dewPoint-TemperatureAtPressure is identical to #$boilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure (and hence to #$bubblePoint-TemperatureAtPressure).  Dew point is useful to distinguish from boiling point when studying substances that are mixtures of other substances with different boiling points. In such circumstances, it used in conjunction with bubble point to calculate a multi-phase \"envelope\" in which a substance has both gas and liquid present.")
(comment bubblePoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$bubblePoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that the instance #$PartiallyTangible will form its first bubble of gas when its temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant. For chemically pure substances, #$bubblePoint-TemperatureAtPressure is identical to #$boilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure.  bubble point is useful to distinguish from boiling point when studying substances that are mixtures of other substances with different boiling points. In such circumstances, it used in conjunction with dew point (see #$dewPoint-TemperatureAtPressure) to calculate a multi-phase \"envelope\" in which a substance has both gas and liquid present.")
(comment PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary "A collection of predicates that define phase transitions of a substance (e.g., from solid into liquid) in terms of convergences of temperature and pressure.")
(comment VectorMagnitudeFn "<code>(#$VectorMagnitudeFn VECTOR)</code> denotes the scalar interval which is the magnitude of <code>VECTOR</code>.")
(comment PetroleumReservoir "A specialization of #$Region and #$PartiallyTangible.  Petroleum reservoirs are areas in geological formations that contain a significant amount of crude petroleum.")
(comment GasReservoir "A specialization of #$HydrocarbonReservoir.  Gas reservoirs are areas in geological formations that contain a significant amount of light hydrocarbon (hydrocarbon that is gaseous under surface conditions) and little-to-no heavy hydrocarbon (petroleum).")
(comment HydrocarbonReservoir "A specialization of #$Region and #$PartiallyTangible.  Hydrocarbon reservoirs are areas in geological formations that contain a significant amount of hydrocarbons.")
(comment NaturalReservoir "A collection of underground deposits of natural resources that typically occur as fluids under normal conditions.")
(comment reservoirPayload "A temporally qualifiable relation that relates an instance of #$NaturalReservoir to its entire contents.  As a reservoir is drained, the amount of those contents is reduced. If a reservoir is drained entirely (which almost never happens in reality), the reservoir ceases to exist as a reservoir.")
(comment UndergroundWaterSource "A specialization of #$NaturalReservoir, this is the collection of all naturally-occuring sources of water.")
(comment determinantColRelnToTypicalArgIsaForFormula "<code>(#$determinantColRelnToTypicalArgIsaForFormula FORM SLOT COL1 QUANT RELN)</code> means that in systems properly described by the #$QuantityBasedFormula <code>FORM</code>, if a components of that system include instances <code>INS1</code> and <code>INS2</code> of <code>COL1</code> and <code>COL2</code> respectively, and it is true that <code>(#$unitSlotsForFormula FORM QUANT SLOT)</code>, <code>(#$isaConstraintForQuantityBasedFormulaSlot FORM QUANT COL1)</code> and <code>(#$typicalFocalIsaForFormula FORM COL2)</code>, then <code>(RELN INS1 INS2)</code> is true.")
(comment factorExpectedToAccountFor "<code>(#$factorExpectedToAccountFor IND FACTOR-QUANTITY-TYPE QUANTITY PERCENTAGE)</code> means that <i>ceteris paribus</i>, the factor <code>FACTOR-QUANTITY-TYPE</code> will account for <code>PERCENTAGE</code> amount of the quantity <code>QUANTITY<code> had by <code>IND</code>.")
(comment proportionalityTypeForSlotsInFormula "<code>(#$proportionalityTypeForSlotsInFormula QBF SLOT1 SLOT2 PROPORTIONALITY)</code> means that 
<i>ceteris paribus</i>, the values of <code>SLOT1</code> and <code>SLOT2</code> as calculated using <code>QBF</code> bear the proportionality relation <code>PROPORTIONALITY</code to one another.")
(comment formulaFactorDependsOnSlotValue "<code>(#$formulaFactorDependsOnSlotValue QBF QUANT SLOT)</code> means that value of <code>FACTOR</code> as calculated with <code>QBF</code>, depends in part on the value of the slot, <code>SLOT</code>, when that value is input to <code>QBF</code>. ")
(comment ReservoirTypeByPhaseProperties "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$HydrocarbonReservoir into sub-collections based on the phase qualities (e.g., liquid, gas, multi-phase, etc.) of the hydrocarbon (see #$reservoirPayload) in the reservoir.")
(comment MultiPhaseFluidHydrocarbonReservoir "The collection of instances of #$HydrocarbonReservoir whose constituent hydrocarbon (see #$reservoirPayload) has portions (see #$physicalPortions) that of distinct states of matter, e.g., some liquid, some gas.")
(comment SinglePhaseFluidHydrocarbonReservoir "The collection of instances of #$HydrocarbonReservoir whose constituent hydrocarbon (see #$reservoirPayload) is of a uniform state of matter, e.g., all liquid.")
(comment HydrocarbonReservoir-AllLiquid "A subcollection of #$SinglePhaseFluidHydrocarbonReservoir.  Each instance is a hydrocarbon reservoir whose constituent hydrocarbon (see #$reservoirPayload) is entirely in a liquid state.")
(comment DryGasReservoir "A subcollection of #$SinglePhaseFluidHydrocarbonReservoir.  Each instance is a hydrocarbon reservoir whose constituent hydrocarbon (see #$reservoirPayload) is entirely in a gaseous state, and is light enough that it remains gaseous from the time it flows into the well to the time it reaches the surface.")
(comment WetGasReservoir "A specialization of #$SinglePhaseFluidHydrocarbonReservoir. #$WetGasReservoir is similar to #$DryGasReservoir in that both are collections of light hydrocarbon reservoirs in which all the hydrocarbon in those reservoirs is in a gaseous state. However, unlike a dry gas reservoir, in which the hydrocarbon remains in a gaseous state as it is brought to the surface, in a wet gas reservoir, some of the gas takes on a liquid form as it is extracted.")
(comment substanceAtPhaseTransitionPoint "<code>(#$substanceAtPhaseTransitionPoint SUBSTANCE PRED)</code> means that the pressure and temperature of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> are such that they are identical to those of the transition point indicated by <code>PRED</code>, an instance of #$PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary.")
(comment substanceAtOrAbovePhaseTransitionPoint "<code>(#$substanceAtOrAbovePhaseTransitionPoint SUBSTANCE PRED)</code> means that the pressure and temperature of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> are such that it at or has moved below the transition point indicated by <code>PRED</code>, an instance of #$PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary.")
(comment substanceAbovePhaseTransitionPoint "<code>(#$substanceAbovePhaseTransitionPoint SUBSTANCE PRED)</code> means that the pressure and temperature of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> are such that it has moved above the transition point indicated by <code>PRED</code>, an instance of #$PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary.")
(comment substanceAtOrBelowPhaseTransitionPoint "<code>(#$substanceAtOrBelowPhaseTransitionPoint SUBSTANCE PRED)</code> means that the pressure and temperature of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> are such that it has either arrived at or has dropped below the transition point indicated by <code>PRED</code>, an instance of #$PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary.")
(comment substanceBelowPhaseTransitionPoint "<code>(#$substanceBelowPhaseTransitionPoint SUBSTANCE PRED)</code> means that the pressure and temperature of <code>SUBSTANCE</code> are such that it has dropped below the transition point indicated by <code>PRED</code>, an instance of #$PhaseBehaviorPredicate-Ternary.")
(comment formationVolumeFactor "An instance of #$FunctionalPredicate and #$TernaryPredicate, <code>(#$formationVolumeFactor SOURCE STUFF SCALAR)</code> means that <code>SCALAR</code> is the result of calculating the ratio (see #$ratioOfTo) of the volume of <code>STUFF</code> at the conditions (specifically #$ambientPressure and #$temperatureOfObject) in <code>SOURCE</code>, an instance of #$NaturalReservoir, to its volume at \"standard conditions\".")
(comment OilFormationVolumeFactorFn "<code>(#$OilFormationVolumeFactorFn RESERVOIR)</code> denotes the oil formation volume factor of the #$ProductionWell <code>RESERVOIR</code>.  This factor is the oil and dissolved gas volume at reservoir conditions divided by oil volume at standard conditions.")
(comment bottomholeStaticPressure "<code>(#$bottomholeStaticPressure WELL PRESS)</code> means that the #$ProductionWell <code>WELL</code> has a static fluid at #$Pressure <code>PRESS</code> at its bottomhole.")
(comment fluidPressureInPipe "(#$fluidPressureInPipe PIPE PRESS) means that the #$FluidTangibleThing in PIPE exerts the #$Pressure PRESS.")
(comment fluidPressure "(#$fluidPressureInPipe FLUID PRESS) means that the #$FluidTangibleThing FLUID exerts the #$Pressure PRESS at its surface.")
(comment NeoclassicArchitecturalStyle "The collection of instances of 
#$ConstructionArtifact in the Neoclassical style.  The #$NeoclassicArchitecturalStyle is a neo-Greek-Roman style of building design developed in Europe that became popular in the 17th through 20th Centuries, especially after the end of the heyday of the #$BaroqueArchitecturalStyle and the #$RococoArchitecturalStyle. It is characterized by the use of symmetric arrangements of columns, pediments, limited  embellishments, and Greek and Roman style details.")
(comment objectHasSlotValueAtConditions "A predicate used to describe the effects of different environmental conditions (most notably temperature and pressure) on a sample of tangible stuff.  <code>(#$objectHasSlotValueAtConditions OBJ SLOT VALUE PLACE)</code> means that were <code>OBJ</code> to have its temperature and pressure approach the approximate temperature and pressure of the instance <code>PLACE</code> of #$Place, <code>(SLOT OBJ VALUE)</code> would obtain.  <code>SLOT</code> here is a #$MeasurableQuantitySlot, such as #$massOfObject, and <code>VALUE</code> is constrained to be an appropriate arg2 value for <code>SLOT</code>.")
(comment aboveGroundRegion "the predicate that corresponds to #$AboveGroundRegionFn, <code>(#$aboveGroundRegion UNDERGROUND ABOVETGROUND)</code> identifies <code>ABOVEGROUND</code> as the above-ground region, including the earth's surface and surrounding air, within to a few meters above the ground, that is, intuitively, \"the surface region\" above <code>UNDERGROUND</code> an underground location.")
(comment AboveGroundRegionFn "<code>(#$AboveGroundRegionFn UNDERGROUND)</code> denotes the above-ground region, including the earth's surface and surrounding air, within to a few meters above the ground, that is, intuitively, \"the surface region\" above <code>UNDERGROUND</code> an underground location.")
(comment waterFormationVolumeFactor "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, <code>(#$waterFormationVolumeFactor SOURCE SCALAR)</code> means that 
<code>(#$formationVolumeFactor SOURCE WATER SCALAR)</code> holds for any instance <code>WATER</code> of #$Water found in the #$NaturalReservoir <code>SOURCE</code>.")
(comment gasFormationVolumeFactor "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, <code>(#$gasFormationVolumeFactor SOURCE SCALAR)</code> means that 
<code>(#$formationVolumeFactor SOURCE GAS SCALAR)</code> holds for any representative portion <code>GAS</code> of #$Gas-LightHydrocarbon from the payload (see #$reservoirPayload) of the #$HydrocarbonReservoir <code>SOURCE</code>.")
(comment oilFormationVolumeFactor "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, <code>(#$oilFormationVolumeFactor SOURCE SCALAR)</code> means that 
<code>(#$formationVolumeFactor SOURCE OIL SCALAR)</code> holds for any representative portion <code>OIL</code> of #$Petroleum-CrudeOil from the payload (see #$reservoirPayload) of the #$HydrocarbonReservoir <code>SOURCE</code>.")
(comment PipeSegment-GenericConduit "A specialization of #$Pipe-GenericConduit.  Each instance #$PipeSegment-GenericConduit is a pipe that stands in the #$pipeSegments relation to a larger segment of pipe.")
(comment DensityFn "<code>(#$DensityFn OBJ)</code> denotes the density of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment semiconductorWaferIDString "(#$semiconductorWaferIDString WAFER ID-STRING) means that ID-STRING gives the unique identifier string that is laser-etched on WAFER as WAFER's permanent ID for processing.")
(comment SpeedFn "<code>(#$SpeedFn OBJ)</code> denotes the speed of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment semiconductorWaferLotIDString "(#$semiconductorWaferLotIDString WAFER-LOT LOT-ID) means that LOT-ID is the unique identifier used in referencing the semiconductor wafer lot WAFER-LOT for processing purposes.")
(comment SemiconductorRegionTypeByMobileCarrierPresence "A faceting of semiconductor stuff by the presence or absence of mobile charge carriers.")
(comment InclinationFn "<code>(#$InclinationFn OBJ)</code> denotes the anglular distance of the angle of inclination of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment FluidPressureInPipeFn "<code>(#$FluidPressureInPipeFn PIPE)</code> denotes the pressure of the fluid in <code>PIPE</code>.")
(comment formulaEntailsSlotValueDependsOnFactor "(#$formulaEntailsSlotValueDependsOnFactor TYPE SLOT QBF FACTOR) means that QBF entails that FACTOR is relevant to the value of SLOT for instances of TYPE.")
(comment WellPartType "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$WellPartType is a kind of device used in the practice of extracting resources from a well.")
(comment gasOilRatio-Produced "An instance of #$ScalarIntervalSlot, <code>(#$gasOilRatio-Produced HYDROCARBON SCALAR)</code> means that <code>SCALAR</code> is the result of calculating the ratio (see #$ratioOfTo) of the volume of (#$GaseousFn #$Gas-LightHydrocarbon) in a sample  of #$MultiHydrocarbonFluid <code>HYDROCARBON</code> to the volume of #$Petroleum-CrudeOil in the sample, <i>were it the case</i> that <code>HYDROCARBON</code> is at \"normal\" or \"surface\" conditions (temperature and pressure).  Hence, where <code>HYDROCARBON</code> is at normal conditions, #$gasOilRatio-Produced becomes equivalent to #$gasOilRatio, which measures the actual gas/oil ratio, regardless of state.")
(comment IndustrialChoke "A specialization of #$ChokeValve.  Industrial chokes are heavy-duty valves used to regulate flowing pressures and flow rates.  For example, industrial chokes are used at the surface of oil wells to regulated flow rates by controlling downhole pressure.")
(comment PhysicalAccelerationEvent "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$PhysicalAccelerationEvent is an event in which the #$primaryObjectMoving accelerates.")
(comment LinearAccelerationEvent "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$LinearAccelerationEvent is an event in which the #$primaryObjectMoving has a positive linear acceleration.")
(comment AngularAccelerationEvent "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$AngularAccelerationEvent is an event in which the #$primaryObjectMoving has a positive angular acceleration.")
(comment parameterAdjustedToExecuteCapability "(#$parameterAdjustedToExecuteCapability OBJ-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE SLOT) means that it is by manifesting various values of SLOT that instances of OBJ-TYPE are able to effectively play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE.  For example, (#$parameterAdjustedToExecuteCapability #$PartiallyTangible #$LinearAccelerationEvent #$primaryObjectMoving #$speedOfObject-Translation) means that objects accelerate by increasing their speed.")
(comment controllingParameterOfObjectType "(#$controllingParameterOfObjectType TYPE SLOT EVENT-TYPE) means EVENT-TYPE is the collection of events in which the values of SLOT for TYPE are controlled.")
(comment ControllingParameterOfObjectTypeFn "(#$ControllingParameterOfObjectTypeFn TYPE SLOT) denotes the collection of events in which the values of SLOT for TYPE are controlled.")
(comment typicalIngredientTypes "(typicalIngredientTypes FOOD-TYPE EDIBLE-TYPE) indicates that EDIBLE-TYPE is frequently an ingredient of FOOD-TYPE, though not necessarily or exclusively.")
(comment ArtificialLiftDevice "A specialization of #$MechanicalDevice.  Each instance of #$ArtificialLiftDevice is a device such as a pump or a gas lift that is used to accelerate to outflow of fluid from a well.")
(comment ReticleDie "A physical instantiation of the smallest repeated element in a #$MaskingReticle pattern.")
(comment WaferDie "The collection of all physical parts of #$SemiconductorWafer instances which will eventually be laser-sawed into separate #$IntegratedCircuit instances.")
(comment precursorDieOfIC "(#$precursorDieOfIC DIE IC) means that the #$WaferDie DIE is the #$SemiconductorWafer die that will eventually be cut into a self-contained #$IntegratedCircuit.")
(comment WaferDieTypeByResultantICType "A type-level collection.  Each instance is a collection of #$WaferDie instances which all share the property that they will eventually result in a common type of #$IntegratedCircuit.")
(comment WaferDieTypeByResultantICTypeFn "A function used in reifying sub-classes of #$WaferDie by the type of #$IntegratedCircuit that will eventually be produced from the sub-class.  Where IC-TYPE is a kind of #$IntegratedCircuit, (#$WaferDieTypeByResultantICTypeFn IC-TYPE) denotes the class of all #$WaferDie instances that will eventually yield (be #$transformedInto)  instances of IC-TYPE.")
(comment precursorDieTypeForICType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$WaferDieTypeByResultantICTypeFn.  Where IC-TYPE is a kind of #$IntegratedCircuit, (#$precursorDieTypeForICType IC-TYPE DIE-TYPE) means that DIE-TYPE is the class of all #$WaferDie instances that will eventually yield (be #$transformedInto)  instances of IC-TYPE")
(comment diePositionOnWaferXCoord "(#$diePositionOnWaferXCoord DIE INTEGER) means that INTEGER gives the x-coordinate of the #$WaferDie DIE on a #$SemiconductorWafer as measured from the origin point on the wafer.")
(comment diePositionOnWaferYCoord "(#$diePositionOnWaferYCoord DIE INTEGER) means that INTEGER gives the y-coordinate of the #$WaferDie DIE on a #$SemiconductorWafer as measured from the origin point on the wafer.")
(comment waferDieFuseProgrammedIDString "(#$waferDieFuseProgrammedIDString DIE ID-STRING) means that ID-STRING is the unique identifier assigned to the #$WaferDie DIE via 16 bit eletrical fuse programming.")
(comment iCFuseProgrammedIDString "(#$iCFuseProgrammedIDString IC ID-STRING) means that ID-STRING is the unique identifier assigned to the #$IntegratedCircuit IC via 16-bit electronic fuse programming.")
(comment intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType "<code>(#$intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE ROLE1 INTENDED-EVENT-TYPE ROLE2)</code> means that during an instance <code>EVENT</code> of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, if an instance <code>SUB-EVENT</code> of <code>SUB-EVENT-TYPE</code> is a sub-event of <code>EVENT</code>, whatever plays <code>ROLE1</code> in <code>SUB-EVENT</code> is indended to play the role <code>ROLE2</code> in an instance of <code>INTENDED-EVENT-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$intendedConsequenceTypeOfSubEventType #$KillingThroughPoisoning #$Poisoning #$bodilyDoer #$Dying #$doneBy) means that during a killing by poisoning event, whoever is poisoned is also intended to die.")
(comment WellCompletion "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject.  Each instance of #$WellCompletion is an event in which a well is prepared for production (in the case of #$ProductionWells) or injection (in the case of #$InjectionWells).  Objectives of well completion include protecting the casing, ensuring emergency reservoir isolation is possible, running the proper production or injection tubing, and so on.")
(comment ProductionPacker "A specialization of #$ManMadeObstacle.  Production packers are used to create a seal between the outside of the production tubing and the inside of the cylinder that contains the production tubing.")
(comment Packer-Well "A specialization of #$ManMadeObstacle.  Packers are used to create a seal between the outside of the production or injection tubing and the inside of the cylinder that contains the tubing.")
(comment InjectionPacker "A specialization of #$ManMadeObstacle.  Production packers are used to create a seal between the outside of the production tubing and the inside of the cylinder that contains the production tubing.")
(comment PeanutButterAndJellySandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Each instance of #$PeanutButterAndJellySandwich is a sandwich whose main ingredients include #$PeanutButter and #$Jelly-Foodstuff.")
(comment PackerEmplacement "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject.  Each instance of #$PackerEmplacement is an event in which instances of #$Packer-Well are placed in a well to create a seal between either the production or injection tubing and the surrounding cylinder.")
(comment IsolationOfArea "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$IsolationOfArea is an event in which one area is isolated from another.")
(comment IsolationOfAnnulus "A specialization of #$IsolationOfArea.  Each instance of #$IsolationOfAnnulus is an event in which the annulus between the tubing and the inner casing is isolated.")
(comment sceneTypeDependencies-CeterisParibus "A generalzation of #$sceneTypeDependencies, <code>(#$sceneTypeDependencies-CeterisParibus SCRIPT PRED1 SCENE1 PRED2 SCENE2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INS</code> of the situation-type <code>SCRIPT</code>, if <code>(PRED1 INS SCENE1)</code> holds, then, all other things normally true of <code>INS</code> are assumed to hold, <code>(PRED2 INS SCENE2)</code> follows.")
(comment InjectionTubing "A specialization of #$WellTubing.  Injection tubing is used to inject well fluids into the well.")
(comment effectOfConditionsOnObject "<code>(#$effectOfConditionsOnObject OBJ CONDITIONS SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that were the tangible thing <code>OBJ</code> to be put into the environmental conditions of <code>CONDITIONS</code>, a consequence would be that <code>OBJ</code> would play the role <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment GasEscapingFromLiquid "The collection of events in which gas separates from a liquid.")
(comment AnnularSafetyValve "A specialization of #$Valve-Mechanical.  Annular safety valves are installed to regulate backflow of gas in wells that use gas injection.")
(comment DownholeSafetyValve "A specialization of #$Valve-Mechanical.  Downhole safety valves are installed inside wellbores as a measure to help prevent the uncontrolled release of reservoir fluids in the event of a worst case scenario surface disaster.")
(comment SurfaceControlledSubsurfaceSafetyValve "A specialization of #$DownholeSafetyValve.  SCSSVs are downhole valves that are surface-controlled.")
(comment ClosingInAWell "A specialization of #$ShuttingOffSomething and #$ChangingDeviceState.  Each instance of #$ClosingInAWell is an event in which a well is closed in (i.e., shut down for a period of time, usually for repairs).")
(comment EmergencyFn "<code>(#$EmergencyFn EVENT-TYPE)</code> denotes the specialization of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> whose instances are performed in response to an emergency.")
(comment emergencyVarietyOfType "<code>(#$emergencyVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE AB-EVT-TYPE)<code> means that <code>AB-EVT-TYPE</code> is the collection of all emergency instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment carrierMobilityInRegion "(#$carrierMobilityInRegion REG CARRIER-MOBILITY) states that the rate of possible movement of charge carriers through region is CARRIER-MOBILITY
")
(comment ReticlePattern "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure as well as #$AspatialInformationStore.  #$ReticlePattern is an abstract 2-dimensional structure that is transferred to a #$ResistLayer during #$PhotoResistExposure by means of a #$MaskingReticle or #$MaskingReticle subsection.  A chemical change in the #$ResistLayer records the pattern:  either this chemically altered portion of the resist, or all but the chemically altered portion, is then ablated during the removal stage, prior to template-based deposition, etching, or implantation.")
(comment reticlePartSubsumesPattern "(#$reticlePartSubsumesPattern RETICLE-PART PATTERN) means that the #$MaskingReticle part RETICLE-PART physically instantiates the #$ReticlePattern PATTERN in a way that facilitates the transfer of PATTERN to the #$ResistLayer during #$PhotoResistExposure.")
(comment reticlePartHasPattern "(#$reticlePartHasPattern RETICLE-PART PATTERN) means that the #$MaskingReticle part RETICLE-PART physically instantiates exactly the #$ReticlePattern PATTERN in a way that facilitates the transfer of PATTERN to the #$ResistLayer during #$PhotoResistExposure.")
(comment ReticlePattern-Maximal "The collection of all #$ReticlePatterns such that each instance is the largest pattern instantiated by some entire #$MaskingReticle.")
(comment reticleHasPattern "(#$reticleHasPattern RETICLE PATTERN) means that the entire #$MaskingReticle instance RETICLE instantiates exactly the #$ReticlePattern PATTERN in a way that facilitates the transfer of PATTERN to the #$ResistLayer during #$PhotoResistExposure.")
(comment subReticlePatterns "A specialization of #$subInfoStructures.  (#$subReticlePattern SUPER SUB) means that the #$ReticlePattern SUB is a component of the #$ReticlePattern SUPER.")
(comment ReticleDiePattern "The smallest repeated pattern in any complete #$ReticlePattern of a #$MaskingReticle.")
(comment ProductionTubingString "Each instance of #$ProductionTubingString consists of all of the components of the #$ProductionTubing in a well, from the bottomhole to the wellhead.")
(comment CompletionString "Each instance of #$CompletionString is a complete system of artifacts installed during completion to ensure that the well flows properly and safely.")
(comment SlidingSleeve "A specialization of #$Pipe-GenericConduit and #$Artifact-NonAgentive. Sliding sleaves liding sleeve is a standard component for the completion of an oil or gas well. Their main uses are to control from what zones fluids flow into well tubing.")
(comment WellFlowing "A specialization of #$DrainingProcess.  In each instance of #$WellFlowing, well inflow and outflow occur.")
(comment OptimalWellFlowing "A specialization of #$WellFlowing.  In each instance of #$OptimalWellFlowing, well inflow and outflow occur optimally in terms of safety and productivity.")
(comment OilProductionPlant "A specializaton of #$HeavyIndustryFacility.  Oil production plants process production fluids from oil wells.")
(comment BitumenUpgrader "A specialization of #$HeavyIndustryFacility.  Bitumen upgraders are used to perform #$BitumenUpgrading (q.v.).")
(comment FlowBetweenWellAndProductionPlant "Each instance of #$FlowBetweenWellAndProductionPlant is a conveyance of fluid between a well and a production plant.")
(comment ColdLakeOilSands "The Cold Lake oil sands are large bitumen deposits in northeastern Alberta.")
(comment ColdLakeOilSandsBitumen "The extra heavy crude oil (i.e. bitumen) derived from the Cold Lake oil sands in the Alberta, Canada region.")
(comment PeaceRiverOilSands "The Peace River oil sands are large bitumen deposits in northeastern Alberta.")
(comment reservoirInFormation "<code>(#$reservoirInFormation RES FORM)</code> means that the #$NaturalReservoir <code>RES</code> is located at and is part of the #$GeologicalFormation <code>FORM</code>.")
(comment conformablyOverlays "<code>(#$conformablyOverlays ABOVE-FORM BELOW-FORM)</code> means that the #$GeologicalFormation <code>ABOVE-FORM</code> conformably overlays the #$GeologicalFormation <code>BELOW-FORM</code>.")
(comment ruleGivesFormulaForCalculatingSlotValue "A specialization of #$salientAssertions that relates a #$VectorOrQuantitySlot to the rule or rules whose antecedents give algorithm(s) for calculating the value of that slot.")
(comment SandMitigation "The collection of attempts to mitigate the influence of sand in clogging a fluid conduit.")
(comment PetroleumProductionActionType "A collection of specializations of #$Event.  Each instance of #$PetroleumProductionActionType is a collection of purposeful actions, instances of which are significantly performed during instances of (#$ProductionOfFn #$PetroleumProduct).")
(comment PartonomicRatioSlot "A specialization of #$QuantitySlot (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PartonomicRatioSlot is a binary predicate that is used to relate an individual to a #$RatioQuantity based on the proportion of some part of some type of that individual to a part of of some other type of that individual.  To tersely state the types of parts being compared, the dimension along which they are compared (e.g., #$massOfObject), and the dividend/divisor roles, use #$slotCalculatesRatioOfPartTypeToPartTypeForTypeAlongDimension.")
(comment slotCalculatesRatioOfPartTypeToPartTypeForTypeAlongDimension "A predicate used to tersely describe the semantics of an instance of #$PartonomicRatioSlot.
<code>(#$slotCalculatesRatioOfPartTypeToPartTypeForTypeAlongDimension SLOT ARG-1-TYPE PART-TYPE-1 PART-TYPE-2 DIMENSION)</code> means that <code>SLOT</code> relates an instance of <code>ARG-1-TYPE</code> to the ratio of the <code>DIMENSION</code> -- an instance of #$MeasurableQuantitySlot, e.g., #$massOfObject -- of the part of it that is of type <code>PART-TYPE-1</code> to the <code>DIMENSION</code> of the part of it that is of type <code>PART-TYPE-2</code>.")
(comment causes-SitTypeRolePlayingSitTypeRolePlaying "An instance of #$CausationPredicate, <code>(#$causes-SitTypeRolePlayingSitTypeRolePlaying CAUSE-TYPE CAUSAL-ROLE EFFECT-TYPE EFFECT-ROLE)</code> means that events of type <code>CAUSE-TYPE</code> cause events of type <code>EFFECT-TYPE</code> such that objects that play the role <code>CAUSAL-ROLE</code> in the causal event play the <code>EFFECT-ROLE</code> in the resulting event.")
(comment causes-SubSitTypeRolePlayingSubSitTypeRolePlaying "(#$causes-SitTypeRolePlayingSitTypeRolePlaying SCRIPT SCENE1 ROLE1 SCENE2 ROLE2) means that in any instance of SCRIPT, something's playing ROLE1 in SCENE1 causes something's playing ROLE2 in SCENE2.")
(comment mostGeneralCoveringOfEventType "A specialization of #$coveringOfEventType, <code>(#$mostGeneralCoveringOfEventType EVT-TYPE LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES)</code> that adds the additional restriction that the breakdown of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> via the list of event-types <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> is, in the current context, the most general, accepted way of decomposing <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.  Specifically, if #$coveringOfEventType holds, not only of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> and <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> but of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> and a <i>different</i> list <code>ALTERANTIVE-LIST</code>, then it must be the case that #$coveringOfEventType holds of at least one element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> and some sub-list of <code>ALTERNATIVE-LIST</code>.  For example, in the context of American sports, <code>(#$coveringOfEventType #$NFLSeason (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason))</code> and <code>(#$coveringOfEventType #$NFLSeason (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason #$SuperBowlGame))</code> are both true (both are complete decompositions of #$NFLSeason in correct temporal order); however, #$mostGeneralCoveringOfEventType only holds of #$NFLSeason and the former list, not the latter, as the latter replaces the more general #$NFLPostSeason with its decomposition into #$NFLPostSeason and #$SuperBowlGame.
<p>
Note the additional requirement that #$mostGeneralCoveringOfEventType hold of an event-type and the most general decomposition for which there is consensus in the current context.  This notion of consensus is intended to impose a \"naturalness\" requirement on the decomposition, so as to block arbitary decompositions into list of event-types that aren't particularly meaningful or salient in the relevant context. For example, one could introduce into the reified collection hierarchy an arbitrary collection, #$NFLPreseasonFollowedByNFLRegularSeason, which decomposes into #$NFLPreseason and #$NFLRegularSeason, and use it as a counterexample to the above claim that the most general decomposition of #$NFLSeason is the one that divides it into the three event-types.  However, in the context of American football, there is no generally recognized event-type that the constant #$NFLPreseasonFollowedByNFLRegularSeason denotes (despite the fact that it is a metaphysically \"real\" event-type) -- in the context in question, the world just isn't \"carved up\" that way.")
(comment Shale "The collection of all shale. A specialization of #$ClasticSedimentaryRock.")
(comment eventYieldsImmediateCausalTrend "<code>(#$eventYieldsImmediateCausalTrend SIT THING SLOT TREND)</code> means that the value for the predicate <code>SLOT</code> applied to <code>THING</code> (in the first argument position) trends as indicated by <code>TREND</code> after (#$STIF q.v.) <code>EVENT</code> than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) <code>EVENT</code>. In addition, it means <code>EVENT</code> is the cause of that trend.")
(comment typeHasCriticalFactorForSlot "<code>(#$typeHasCriticalFactorForSlot  TYPE SLOT FACTOR)</code> means that <code>FACTOR</code> is critical for determining the value of <code>SLOT</code> for any instance of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment formulaFactorDependsOnQuantity "<code>(#$formulaFactorDependsOnQuantity QBF QUANT-TYPE QUANT)</code> means that the factor  <code>QUANT-TYPE</code> as calculated with <code>QBF</code>, depends in part on the value of the quantity, <code>QUANT</code>, when that value is input to <code>QBF</code>. ")
(comment InjectingSteamIntoAWell "A specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$InjectingSteamIntoAWell is an event in which steam is injected into a well.")
(comment TemperatureFn "<code>(#$TemperatureFn OBJ)</code> denotes the temperature of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment SaturatedSteamTemperatureFn "<code>(#$SaturatedSteamTemperatureFn OBJ)</code> denotes the temperature of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment dateOfTermRelease "(#$dateOfTermRelease TERM DATE) means that terms tagged with the KBSubset term TERM will be available for non-prop releases at DATE.

")
(comment IdealSubCool "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent. Ideal sub-cool is a phenomenon that can occur at a SAGD well system.  During ideal sub-cool at a region of the bottomhole, the actual bottomhole temperature is less than the saturated steam temperature. During ideal sub-cool, a liquid column is maintained above the producion well.")
(comment HighSubCool "An instance of #$NegativePetroleumProductionEventType. High sub-cool is a phenomenon that can occur at a SAGD well system.  During high sub-cool at a region of the bottomhole, the actual bottomhole temperature is much less than the saturated steam temperature. During high sub-cool, there is an inefficiently large accumulation of liquids that may prevent steam in the steam chamber from uniformly distributing.")
(comment SubCoolPhenomenonType "The collection of all collections of significant sub-cool events.  These include #$ZeroSubCool, IdealSubCool, and #$HighSubCool.")
(comment PartTypeEntirePortionFn "(#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn OBTYPE STUFFTYPE) yields the collection of instances of STUFFTYPE that are the entire physical extent of STUFFTYPE that are physical parts of instances of OBJECTTYPE.  For example, (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Chimpanzee #$Blood) is the collection of instances of #$Blood, each of which is the total portion of blood in some chimpanzee.")
(comment outflowRate "<code>(#$outflowRate WELL-OUTFLOW RATE)</code> means that the outflow <code>WELL-OUTFLOW</code> flows at the rate <code>RATE</code>.")
(comment greaterValueThanOrEqualTo "A version of #$greaterThanOrEqualTo that has the same semantics of #$greaterThanOrEqualTo, but is not evaluatable, so can be used to reason with a broader range of arguments.")
(comment greaterValueThan "A version of #$greaterThan that has the same semantics of #$greaterThan, but is not evaluatable, so can be used to reason with a broader range of arguments.")
(comment relationAllInstanceInstance-Conditional-CeterisParibus "A generalzation of #$relationAllInstanceInstance-Conditional, <code>(#$relationAllInstanceInstance-Conditional TYPE PRED1 THING1 PRED2 THING2)</code> means that for any instance <code>INS</code> of the collection <code>TYPE</code>, if <code>(PRED1 INS THING1)</code> holds, then, all other things normally true of <code>INS</code> are assumed to hold, <code>(PRED2 INS THING2)</code> follows.")
(comment SiliconDioxideRegion-Semiconductor "The collection of all silicon dioxide regions appearing in integrated circuits
")
(comment ElectricalPath "A specialization of #$ElectricalNetwork.  Each instance of #$ElectricalPath is a path within an electrical circuit from some point of origin to some destination
")
(comment voltageAcrossPath "(#$voltageAcrossPath PATH V) means that the difference between the voltage at the start and ending of PATH is V
.")
(comment currentInPath "(#$currentInPath P I) means that I is the total current in the #$ElectricalPath P
.")
(comment ElectricalPathBetweenFn "An instance of #$BinaryFunction.  When applied to a starting location and an ending location in an electrical circuit or network it denotes the path an electrical signal would take from that start to that finish.  The path may take any number of branches, but, by definition, they must either merge back into a subpath that leads to the end or they will not be part of the path denoted by this function.

")
(comment electricalPathBetween "This is the corresponding predicate for the function #$ElectricalPathBetweenFn.")
(comment gateVoltageToSource "(#$gateVoltageToSource GATE V) means that the difference between the voltage at the gate and the source is V.
")
(disjointWith CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent)
(disjointWith SingleUnitOperationComponentTool-SemiconductorProcessing MultiUnitOperationComponentTool-SemiconductorProcessing)
(comment PathBetweenSourceAndDrain "A specialization of #$ElectricalPath.  Each instance of #$PathBetweenSourceAndDrain is an electrical path from the source region to the drain region of a transistor.


")
(comment PathBetweenGateAndSource "A specialization of #$ElectricalPath.  Each instance of #$PathBetweenGateAndSource is an electical path from the gate contact to the source region of a transistor.

")
(comment PathBetweenDrainAndSource "A specialization of #$ElectricalPath.  Each instance of #$PathBetweenDrainAndSource is an electrical path from the drain region to the source region of a transistor.")
(comment EpitaxialProcess "The collection of all #$ThinFilmDepositions wherein the #$ThinFilm that is deposited is a crystalline structure that is grown on the substrate, using the substrate as a seed crystal.")
(comment Homoepitaxy-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all instances of #$EpitaxialProcess-SemiconductorManufacture wherein the #$thinFilmDeposited belongs to the same class of material as the substrate it is deposited on.")
(disjointWith Heteroepitaxy-SemiconductorManufacture Homoepitaxy-SemiconductorManufacture)
(comment Heteroepitaxy-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all instances of #$EpitaxialProcess-SemiconductorManufacture wherein the #$thinFilmDeposited is of a different chemical substance type than the substrate it is deposited on.")
(comment coreToolHasUnitOperationComponent "(#$coreToolHasUnitOperationComponent TOOL CHAMBER) means that the #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent CHAMBER is a physical component in the #$CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing instance TOOL.")
(comment lotProcesIterationSchemeOfUnitOperationComponentType "(#$ lotProcesIterationSchemeOfUnitOperationComponentType CHAMBER-TYPE ITER-SCHEME) means that every instance of the #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent type CHAMBER-TYPE processes #$SemiconductorWafer elements of a given #$ProcessingAllotment according to the iteration scheme given by ITER-SCHEME:  simultaneously if the value of ITER-SCHEME is #$LotProcessingStep-Parallel, and one at a time if the value of ITER-SCHEME is #$LotProcessingStep-Serial.")
(comment lotProcessIterationSchemeOfUnitOperationComponent "(#$lotProcessIterationSchemeOfUnitOperationComponent CHAMBER ITER-SCHEME) means that the #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent CHAMBER processes #$SemiconductorWafer elements of a given #$ProcessingAllotment according to the iteration scheme given by ITER-SCHEME:  simultaneously if the value of ITER-SCHEME is #$LotProcessingStep-Parallel, and one at a time if the value of ITER-SCHEME is #$LotProcessingStep-Serial.")
(comment CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing "The collection of all wafer processing tools (instances of (#$DeviceTypeByManufacturingProcessOfUseTypeFn #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer)) that are fitted with one or more instances of #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent.")
(comment MultiUnitOperationComponentTool-SemiconductorProcessing "The collection of all instances of #$CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing that are configured with more than one #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent.")
(comment SingleUnitOperationComponentTool-SemiconductorProcessing "The collection of all instances of #$CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing that have exactly one #$SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent as a subcomponent.")
(comment WellPad "A sp[ecialization of #$Facility-Generic.  Each instance of #$WellPad is a facility at which a well has a wellhead.   Every verical well requires its own pad, but directional drilling allows multiple horizontal wells to share a #$MultiWellPad.")
(comment SAGDProducerWell "A specialization of #$HorizontalWell, #$OilWell and #$ProductionWell.  Each instance of #$SAGDProducerWell is a horizontal well used to extract oil during #$SteamAssistedGravityDrainage. Cf. #$SAGDInjectorWell.")
(comment horizontalSectionLength "<code>(#$horizontalSectionLength WELL LENGTH)</code> means <code>LENGTH</code> is the length of the horizontal section of the #$HorizontalWell <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment surfaceCasingThickness "<code>(#$surfaceCasingThickness WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the thickness of the surface casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment surfaceCasingTVD "<code>(#$surfaceCasingTVD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the true vertical depth of the deepest end of the surface casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment intermediateCasingThickness "<code>(#$intermediateCasingThickness WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the thickness of the intermediate casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment intermediateCasingTVD "<code>(#$intermediateCasingTVD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the true vertical depth of the deepest end of the intermediate casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment intermediateCasingMD "<code>(#$intermediateCasingMD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the measured depth of the deepest end of the intermediate casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment sagdLinerEndMD "<code>(#$sagdLinerEndMD SAGD-WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the measured depth of the deepest end of the liner in the #$SAGDProducerWell <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment sagdLinerEndTVD "<code>(#$sagdLinerEndTVD SAGD-WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the true vertical depth of the deepest end of the liner in the #$SAGDProducerWell <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment IntermediateCasing "Intermediate casing is set in place in a well after the #$SurfaceCasing (if any) and before the #$ProductionCasing (if any) to provide additional structural integrity.")
(comment areaOfSmallestFlowXZCrosssection "(#$areaOfSmallestFlowXZCrosssection OBJ AREA) means that AREA is the area of the smallest XZ cross-section area associated with OBJ that would impede the flow of something (e.g. a fluid, a signal, etc.).  For objects not connected to other objects whose length from side to side at each point along the X, Y, or Z axes is the same, this is equivalent to the area of the XZ crosssection of the object itself.  For objects connected to another object at the top or bottom (along the Y axis) of the XZ axes, this area is the area of the smallest XZ crossection of the associated joint of the connected objects.  For the purposes of this relation the X axis is defined as the width of an object when the length is the vertical Y axis.  The Z axis would then be its depth.  For objects with no intrinsic orientation (e.g. a portion of rubber tubing), by fiat the Y axis is the axis associated with its longest side.")
(comment maxMeasuredDepthOfObject "(#$maxMeasuredDepthOfObject OBJ MD) means that the measured depth of OBJ is the #$Distance MD.  This is not truly a measure of depth, except in the case of objects that are strictly vertically embedded in the ground.  Rather, this is a measure of the length from a point on the surface surface, to where the \"end\" of OBJ is, somewhere underground.")
(comment ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation "The collection of all so-called 'unit operations' that occur as delimited processes within end-to-end instances of #$Manufacturing as specified by process thread 'scripts'.")
(comment ManufacturingProcessUnitOperationType "A collection of collections that is a #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance is a collection of events which is specified as a characteristic 'step' or 'stage' within a manufacturing process thread by an industry standard specification.")
(comment UnitOperationsOfTypeFn "A unary, collection-denoting function used for reifying collection instances of #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperationType.  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of manufacturing process (a specialization of (#$ProcessFn #$Manufacturing), (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn PROCESS-TYPE) denotes the specialization of PROCESS-TYPE consisting in all and only those instances of PROCESS-TYPE which are 'unit operations', i.e., which are considered self-contained instantiations of stages of a pre-specified manufacturing process thread.")
(comment allUnitOperationInstancesOf "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicateicate-Canonical) of #$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn. Where PROCESS-TYPE is a kind of manufacturing process (a specialization of (#$ProcessFn #$Manufacturing), (#$allUnitOperationInstancesOf PROCESS-TYPE PROCESS-TYPE-UNIT-OPS) means that UNIT-OPS is the unique collection consisting in all and only those instances of PROCESS-TYPE which are 'unit operations', i.e., which are considered self-contained instantiations of stages of a pre-specified manufacturing process thread.")
(comment UnitOperationsOfInIndustryTypeFn "A unary, collection-denoting function used for reifying collections of instances of #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation (collection instances of #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperationType).  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a specialization of manufacturing process (#$ProcessFn #$Manufacturing) and INDUSTRY-TYPE is an #$IndustryType, (#$UnitOperationsOfInIndustryTypeFn PROCESS-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of PROCESS-TYPE which are considered self-contained instantiations of stages of a pre-specified process thread regarding manufacturing in INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment allUnitOperationsOfTypeInIndustryType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$UnitOperationsOfInIndustryTypeFn.  Where PROCESS-TYPE is a specialization of manufacturing process (#$ProcessFn #$Manufacturing) and INDUSTRY-TYPE is an #$IndustryType, (#$allUnitOperationsOfTypeInIndustryType PROCESS-TYPE INDUSTRY-TYPE ALL-UNIT-OPS) means that ALL-UNIT-OPS is the unique collection of all instances of PROCESS-TYPE which are considered self-contained instantiations of stages of a pre-specified process thread regarding manufacturing in INDUSTRY-TYPE.")
(comment UnitOperation-SemiconductorWaferProcessing "The collection of all instances of #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation that are instances of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer.")
(comment SemiconductorProcessingUnitOperationComponent "The collection of all processing components which are used exclusively in instances of #$UnitOperation-SemiconductorWaferProcessing and which may be associated with semiconductor processing core tools (instances of #$CoreTool-SemiconductorProcessing)")
(comment zAxis "A binary predicate that relates a 3-dimensional Cartesian coordinate system to its z-axis.")
(comment FBIAgent "The collection of law-enforcement agents who work for the Federal Bureau of Investigation.")
(comment TreasuryEnforcementAgent "The collection of law-enforcement agents who work for the Treasury Department.")
(comment DEAAgent "The collection of law-enforcement agents who work for the Drug Enforcement Administration.")
(comment ATFAgent "The collection of law-enforcement agents who work for the Bureau of Alcohol Tobacco and Firearms   .")
(comment CIAAgent "The collection of agents who work for the Central Intelligence Agency.")
(comment MI5Agent "The collection of agents who work for the British Security Service.")
(comment InternationalMilitaryAlliance "An alliance of nations which are allied for military purposes.")
(comment CubicPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 3.")
(comment PolynomialFunction "The collection of all polynomal functions, considered as abstract entities independent of a particular syntactic formulation (i.e., choice of variables).")
(comment CurvedLine "A specialization of #$Line.  Each instance of #$CurvedLine is a line that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLine-Planar "A specialization of #$Line-Planar.  Each instance of #$CurvedLine is a planar line that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLine-NonPlanar "A specialization of #$Line-Planar.  Each instance of #$CurvedLine-NonPlanar is a non-planar line that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLineSegment "A specialization of #$LineSegment and #$CurvedLinearObject.  Each instance of #$CurvedLineSegment is a line segment that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLineSegment-Planar "A specialization of #$LineSegment-Planar and #$CurvedLineSegment.  Each instance of #$CurvedLineSegment-Planar is a planar line segment that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLineSegment-NonPlanar "A specialization of #$Line-Planar.  Each instance of #$CurvedLineSegment- is a non-planar line segment that is not straight.")
(comment CurvedLinearObject "A specialization of #$LinearObject. Each instance of #$CurvedLinearObject is a linear object that has at least some portions that are neither straight nor sharp angles.")
(disjointWith CurvedLine-Planar CurvedLine-NonPlanar)
(disjointWith Line-Straight CurvedLine)
(comment Parabola "A specialization of #$CurvedLine-Planar.  Each instance of #$Parabola is a curved line that can be obtained by intersecting a cone with a plane parallel to a straight line on the cone's surface.")
(comment QuarticPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 4.")
(comment PolynomialFunctionTypeByDegree "A collection of collections that is a specialization of #$FunctionType.  Each instance of #$PolynomialFunctionTypeByDegree is a collection of polynomial functions, each of which are of the same degree.")
(comment QuinticPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 5.")
(comment SexticPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 6.")
(comment SepticPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 7.")
(comment HecticPolynomialFunction "A sub-collection of #$PolynomialFunction, each of which has a degree of 100.")
(comment polynomialDegree "<code>(#$polynomialDegree FUNC DEG)</code> means that the degree of the #$PolynomialFunction <code>FUNC</code> is <code>DEG</code>.")
(comment Spline "The collection of all splines, which are piecewise-polynomial functions that are useful for interpolation.")
(comment RemovalProcess-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all so-called 'removal' processes in #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer, inclusive of 'removals' at both the single wafer (#$SemiconductorWafer) level and the level of processing 'lots' (#$ProcessingAllotment).  In every instance, one or more layers of #$ThinFilm are removed from one or more #$SemiconductorWafers.")
(comment RemovalProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all semiconductor manufacturing industry 'removal' processes ((#$RemovalProcess-SemiconductorManufacture) wherein one or more instances of #$ThinFilm are removed from a single #$SemiconductorWafer.")
(comment RemovalProcess-SemiconductorProcessingAllotment "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SemiconductorManufacture wherein a common removal agent removes or is brought to the point of removing #$ThinFilms sharing a common #$ChemicalSubstanceType from all of the wafers (#$SemiconductorWafer instances) in a #$ProcessingAllotment.")
(comment (UnitOperationsOfTypeFn RemovalProcess-SingleWafer) "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer that are self-contained unit operations #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation within instantiations of #$SemiconductorWafer manufacturing process threads.  'Self contained' here means, among other things, that all and only the entirety of the #$ThinFilm that the process thread specification indicates *should* be removed from the wafer for the process 'step' *is* removed from the wafer by the end of the (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer) instance, within acceptable margins of error.")
(comment (UnitOperationsOfTypeFn PhotoresistStrippingProcess-SingleWafer) "The collection of all events wherein a previously deposited and developed photoresist template is completely removed (within acceptable margins of error) from a #$SemiconductorWafer instance using physical or chemical means, as an instantiation of a designed stage within an instantiation of a process thread specification that includes the stage.")
(comment PhotoresistStrippingProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all processes wherein a #$ResistLayer instance that has already been used in a #$PhotolithographyProcess-SingleIteration and a subsequent #$WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer is removed from the wafer surface by exposure to a general solvent.")
(comment (UnitOperationsOfTypeFn WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer) "The collection of all events wherein selected portions of a #$ThinFilm that is not an instance of #$ResistLayer are completely removed (to within acceptable fault tolerances or margins of error) by exposure to either an acid solvent or ion plasma.")
(disjointWith ElementStuff Nitride)
(disjointWith Agent-Generic Nitride)
(comment SiliconNitride "#$SiliconNitride (Si3N4) is a chemical compound of #$Silicon and #$Nitrogen.  It is a hard #$Ceramic having high strength over a broad temperature range, moderate thermal conductivity, low coefficient of thermal expansion, moderately high elastic modulus, and unusually high fracture toughness for a ceramic (Wikipedia).")
(comment saturationSteamTemperature "<code>(#$saturationSteamTemperature OBJ TEMP)</code> means <code>TEMP</code> is the saturation steam temperature at <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment fiberInWell "<code>(#$fiberInWell DTS WELL)</code> means the #$DistributedTemperatureSensor <code>DTS</code> is in the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment Nitride "A collection instance of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies and a specialization of #$InanimateObject.  Each instance of #$Nitride is a portion of stuff wherein each molecule is a compound of #$Nitrogen with a formal oxidation state of -3 (Wikipedia).")
(comment TetraethylOrthosilicate "#$TetraethylOrthosilicate is the collection of all portions of stuff composed of molecules consisting in four ethyl groups attached to an SiO4 4- ion called orthosilicate.  Often abbreviated 'TEOS', the compound is used in instances of (#$ProductionIndustryTypeFn #$SemiconductorDevice) as a crosslinking agent and a precursor to #$SiliconDioxide, which it readily converts to in the presence of water (Wikipedia).")
(disjointWith TransportInvolvingADriver RecreationalBoardRidingActivity)
(comment adjFormIsOfOrPertainsTo "A predicate used to assign general, dictionary-like semantics for adjectives.  <code>(#$adjFormIsOfOrPertainsTo WORD THING)</code> means that, generally speaking, uses of the adjective form of the word <code>WORD</code> denote something about, originating from, or otherwise related to <code>THING</code>.")
(comment RecreationalBoardRidingActivity "A kind of #$RecreationalActivity in which people ride boards along some surface, often leaving the surface temporarily to perform acrobatic maneuvers, or \"board tricks.\"")
(comment RecreationalBoardRidingActivityTypeBySurface "An instance of #$DisjointCollectionType that facets #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity into subcollections based on the type of surface used to do the board riding.")
(comment RecreationalBoardRidingActivity-OnWater "An instance of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivityTypeBySurface, this is the collection of instances of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity that take place primarily on the water.")
(comment RecreationalBoardRidingActivity-OnSnow "An instance of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivityTypeBySurface, this is the collection of instances of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity that take place primarily on the snow.")
(comment SnowSurfaceTransportation "The collection of transportation events in which something is transported along a snowy surface.")
(comment OverSnowTransportationDevice "The collection of transportation devices that are intended to facilitate travel over snow-covered terrain.")
(comment BoardSport "The collection of all sports that involve riding on and performing tricks with a board.")
(comment dontMapWikipediaArticle "(#$dontMapWikipediaArticle TITLE) holds when the #$Wikipedia-WebSite article with the title TITLE is not appropriate for mapping to a Cyc concept.")
(comment GasExplosion "A specialization of #$Explosion.  Each instance of #$GasExplosion is an explosion resulting from a the ignition of gas from a gas leak.")
(comment GasLeak "A specialization of #$Leaking-EmittingAnObject.  Each instance of #$GasLeak is an event in which an explosive gas such as enatural gas, methane, propane or butane leaks from a pipe or container.")
(comment ModificationProcess-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all events wherein one or more #$SemiconductorWafers are subjected to a #$PhysicalTransformationEvent that transforms selected portions of either the wafer substrate itself, or of a #$SemiconductorWaferLayer deposited on the substrate.")
(comment ModificationProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$ModificationProcess-SemiconductorManufacture in which selected portions of a single wafer, and possibly some of its appurtenances (deposited #$ThinFilm layers, etc.) are operated on in a process involving #$ChemicalReaction.")
(comment (UnitOperationsOfTypeFn ModificationProcess-SingleWafer) "The collection of all instances of #$ModificationProcess-SingleWafer wherein a complete 'recipe' for modifying a #$SemiconductorWafer instance or selected portion thereof is carried out end-to-end (to designed completion) as an instantiation of a specified stage in a specified semiconductor manufacturing process thread.")
(comment WaferPadOxidation-UnitOperation "The collection of all wafer modification unit operations (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn #$ModificationProcess-SingleWafer) wherein a 'pad' layer of oxide is deliberately formed over all or selected portions of a #$SemiconductorWafer in an end-to-end process that instantiates a specified 'stage' or 'step' in an IC manufacturing process thread specification.")
(comment PadOxideLayer "The collection of all oxidation layers formed on instances of #$SemiconductorWafer in the course of wafer processing (instances of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer).")
(comment IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation "A #$MicrofabricationProcessType:  the collection of all instances of #$UnitOperation-SemiconductorWaferProcessing wherein the resistivity of an array of areas on a #$SemiconductorWafer instance is changed by bombarding these zones with ions of a given type that have been accelerated by means of an eletrical field.")
(comment NWellImplantation-UnitOperation "The collection of all instances of #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation wherein the culmination of the operation is the creation of multiple 'n-wells', regions of negative charge, via ionic bombardment that leaves an excess of electrons insinuated through the crystalline structure of the target areas.")
(disjointWith NWellImplantation-UnitOperation PWellImplantation-UnitOperation)
(comment ionTypeEmployedInImplantation "Where IMPLANT-OP is an #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation and ION-TYPE is an #$IonTypeByChemicalSpecies, (#$ionTypeEmployedInImplantation IMPLANT-OP ION-TYPE) means that IMPLANT-OP accomplishes it's purpose by bombarding its target (ordinarily, a portion of a #$SemiconductorWafer instance) with ions of type ION-TYPE.")
(comment PWellImplantation-UnitOperation "The collection of all instances of #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation wherein the culmination of the operation is the creation of multiple 'p-wells', regions of positive charge, via ionic bombardment that leaves an excess of 'electron holes' insinuated through the crystalline structure of the target areas.")
(comment ModificationProcess-SemiconductorProcessingAllotment "The collection of all 'lot level' instances of #$ModificationProcess-SemiconductorManufacture.  In each instance of #$ModificationProcess-SemiconductorProcessingAllotment, a #$PhysicalTransformationEvent involving a #$ChemicalReaction takes place involving all of the #$SemiconductorWafer instances in a wafer processing 'lot' (an instance of (#$StandardIndustryProcessingLotTypeFn (#$ProductionIndustryTypeFn #$SemiconductorDevice) #$SemiconductorWafer)).")
(comment BoardTrick "The collection of all tricks (scripted patterns of maneuvers) to be performed on a board.  Board tricks are instantiated as #$PerformingABoardTrick events.")
(comment GraphicArtist "Graphic artists (also known as \"graphic designers\") are professional visual artists who assemble visual art.")
(comment AlbumCoverArtwork "A specialization of #$Graphic-VisualIBT.  Album covers are graphic art designed to appear on the cover of the packaging of a music album.")
(comment SketchComedyTVShow "The collection of television shows that consist at least in large part of various comedy sketches.")
(comment GenericCausationPredicate "The subcollection of #$CausationPredicate whose instances serve to relate causes (or cause-types) to effects (or effect-types) without any further semantic entailment as to how the causation comes about, whether it is indirect or direct, how likely the effect-type is to come about as a consequence of a cause (or cause-type), etc.  A canonical example is #$causes-SitTypeSitType, which relates to situation-types in a generic cause/effect way.  A canonical counter-example is #$pathogenCausesCondition, which relates a physiological condition to a pathogen that is responsible for that condition by virtue of how it interacts with its host.  #$GenericCausationPredicate is a #$completelyAssertedCollection.")
(comment IndirectlyCausalFn "(#$IndirectlyCausalFn PRED) denotes the specialization SPEC-PRED of the #$GenericCausationPredicate PRED such that when SPEC holds truly of its arguments, an indirect causal relationship holds of its arguments.  See also #$DirectlyCausalFn.")
(comment DirectlyCausalFn "(#$DirectlyCausalFn PRED) denotes the specialization SPEC-PRED of the #$GenericCausationPredicate PRED such that when SPEC holds truly of its arguments, an direct causal relationship holds of its arguments.  See also #$IndirectlyCausalFn.")
(comment indirectlyCausalSpecializationPred "The predicate that corresponds to #$IndirectlyCausalFn, <code>(#$indirectlyCausalSpecializationPred PRED SPEC-PRED)</code> denotes the specialization <code>SPEC-PRED</code> of the #$GenericCausationPredicate PRED such that when <code>SPEC-PRED</code> holds truly of its arguments, an indirect causal relationship holds of its arguments.  See also #$directlyCausalSpecializationPred.")
(comment directlyCausalSpecializationPred "The predicate that corresponds to #$DirectlyCausalFn, <code>(#$directlyCausalSpecializationPred PRED SPEC-PRED)</code> denotes the specialization <code>SPEC-PRED</code> of the #$GenericCausationPredicate <code>PRED</code> such that when <code>SPEC-PRED</code> holds truly of its arguments, an direct causal relationship holds of its arguments.  See also #$indirectlyCausalSpecializationPred.")
(comment PhysicalVaporDeposition "#$PhysicalVaporDeposition is a variety of #$VacuumDeposition-ThinFilm whose instances involve using purely physical processes such as high-temperature vacuum evaporation or plasma sputter bombardment to deposit #$ThinFilm instances by condensation of a vaporized form of the material onto a surface.")
(comment etchantUsed "Where ENGRAVE is an #$EngravingEvent, (#$etchantUsed ENGRAVE IND) means IND is the #$PartiallyTangible instance that is the focal agent that actually etches the surface being engraved.")
(comment WaferEtching-Dry "The collection of all instances of #$WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer wherein the #$etchantUsed is a gas in a plasmatic state, i.e., an instance of #$Plasma-StateOfMatter.")
(comment WaferEtching-Wet "The collection of all instances of #$WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer wherein the etching instrument")
(comment SplineTypeByDegree "A collection of collections that is a specialization of #$FunctionType.  Each instance of #$SplineTypeByDegree is a collection of #$Splines each of which are of the same degree, or \"order\".  The order of a spline is the order of its highest-degree polynomial.")
(comment QuadraticSpline "A specialization of#$Spline.  Each instance of #$QuadraticSpline is a spline of degree 2 (i.e. it is a spline the highest-degree polynomial of which is of degree 2).")
(comment CubicSpline "A specialization of#$Spline.  Each instance of #$CubicSpline is a spline of degree 3 (i.e. it is a spline the highest-degree polynomial of which is of degree 3).")
(comment QuarticSpline "A specialization of#$Spline.  Each instance of #$QuarticSpline is a spline of degree 4 (i.e. it is a spline the highest-degree polynomial of which is of degree 4).")
(comment QuinticSpline "A specialization of#$Spline.  Each instance of #$QuinticSpline is a spline of degree 5 (i.e. it is a spline the highest-degree polynomial of which is of degree 5).")
(comment SexticSpline "A specialization of#$Spline.  Each instance of #$SexticSpline is a spline of degree 6 (i.e. it is a spline the highest-degree polynomial of which is of degree 6).")
(comment splineDegree "<code>(#$splineDegree FUNC DEG)</code> means that the degree of the #$Spline <code>FUNC</code> is <deg>DEG</code>. The degree of a spline is the degree of its highest-degree polynomial")
(comment splineHasPolynomialFunction "<code>(#$splineHasPolynomialFunction SPLINE POLY)</code> means that <code>POLY</code> is one of the polynomials that is a piecewise component of <code>SPLINE</code>.")
(comment SanskritLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Sanskrit.")
(comment LiteratureTypeByHistoricalPeriod "A collection of specializations of #$LiteraryWork-CW .  Each instance of #$LiteratureTypeByHistoricalPeriod is a collection of literary works originally written during a certain historical period.  Instances include #$BronzeAgeLiterature and #$ClassicalLiterature.")
(comment BronzeAgeLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$BronzeAgeLiterature is a literary work written during the Bronze Age.")
(comment AncientEgyptianLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Ancient Egyptian.")
(comment SumerianLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Sumerian.")
(comment AkkadianLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Akkadian.")
(comment EgyptianLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Egyptian.")
(comment LiteratureTypeByLanguage "A collection of specializations of #$LiteraryWork-CW .  Each instance of #$LiteratureTypeByLanguage is a collection of literary works originally written in a certain language.  Instances include #$AncientEgyptianLiterature and #$MiddleEnglishLiterature.")
(comment MedievalLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$MedievalLiterature is a literary work written during the Medieval era.")
(comment MiddleEnglishLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Middle English.")
(comment ClassicalLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$ClassicalLiterature is a literary work written during the Classical era.")
(comment AncientGreekLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Ancient Greek.")
(comment LatinLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Latin.")
(comment RenaissanceLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$RenaissanceLiterature is a literary work written during the Renaissance.")
(comment EarlyModernLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$EarlyModernLiterature is a literary work written during the Early Modern era.")
(comment BaroqueLiterature "A specialization of #$LiteraryWork-CW.  Each instance of #$BaroqueLiterature is a literary work written during the Baroque era.")
(comment PapyrusScroll "A specialization of #$Scroll.  Each instance of #$PapyrusScroll is a scroll made of a #$PapyrusSheet.")
(comment SingleGateTransistor "The collection of transistors with a single gate.  Multiple gate transistors are currently in the prototype or research stage and currently single gate transistors are the only types of transistors in mass production.")
(comment GateLength-Transistor "The length of the gate in a transistor when the gate is in the \"open\" or \"on\" state.  It is the distance between the source and drain region in a transistor.")
(comment RussianLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Russian.")
(comment FrenchLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in French.")
(comment GermanLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in German.")
(comment SpanishLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Spanish.")
(comment JapaneseLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Japanese.")
(comment ArabicLiterature "A sub-collection of #$LiteraryWork-CW. Each instance is a literary work written in Arabic.")
(comment PlatonicDialogue "The Platonic dialogues are the works written by Plato.")
(comment CarrierMobility "A specialization of #$Rate.  A type of quantity whose instances are the rate at which a charge carrier can move though a material when pulled by an electric field.  The two main sub-quantities are electron mobility and hole mobility.  This quantity is typically specified in units of square centimeters per volt-seconds (cm^2 / V * S).")
(comment equationPermutations "(#$equationPermutations EQUATION PERMUTATION) means that PERMUTATION is an equivalent form of EQUATION that consists of an equality statement (using #$numericallyEquals) that has some term involved in EQUATION in the \"left hand side\".  For example, if EQUATION = (#$numericallyEquals AREA (#$TimesFn LENGTH WIDTH)), then values for PERMUTATION would include (#$numericallyEquals LENGTH (#$QuotientFn AREA WIDTH)), (#$numericallyEquals WIDTH (#$QuotientFn AREA LENGTH)).  Note that when EQUATION is itself an equality statement with exactly one term in the \"left hand side\", EQUATION is itself a valid value for PERMUTATION.")
(comment GateRegion-Transitor "The collection of all areas in a transistor in which a N or P channel forms when the transistor is on.  Located between the source and drain regions, an N or P channel forms when the voltage between the gate wire and source exceeds the transistor threshold voltage (either more positive or more negative depending on the type of transistor).")
(comment transistorSourceToDrainCurrent "(#$transistorSourceToDrainCurrent T I) means that I is the total source to drain current in the transistor, T.  In N-type transistors this is the flow of electrons from source to drain (and, of course, of holes from drain to source).  In P-type transistors the flow of electrons is in the opposite direction.")
(comment Funicular "A specialization of #$CableDrivenConveyance. Each #$Funicular is a cable railway with two cars: the ascending and descending vehicles counterbalance.")
(disjointWith CartographicFeatureType PersonTypeByActivity)
(disjointWith MoneyTenderType PersonTypeByActivity)
(disjointWith EntertainmentEventType PersonTypeByActivity)
(comment VisualImageTypeByMotionStatus "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$VisualImage whose instances are all of the same motion status.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity VisualImageTypeByMotionStatus)
(comment Poem-CWTypeByTheme "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Poem-CW whose instances are all of the same theme.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity Poem-CWTypeByTheme)
(comment StudioTypeByActivity "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Studio whose instances are all of the same activity.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity StudioTypeByActivity)
(disjointWith OrganizationType PersonTypeByActivity)
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity TVShowTypeByGenre)
(comment PragmaDirective "Each implementation of C and C++ supports some features unique to its host machine or operating system. Some programs, for instance, need to exercise precise control over the memory areas where data is placed or to control the way certain functions receive parameters. The #pragma directives offer a way for each compiler to offer machine- and operating system-specific features while retaining overall compatibility with the C and C++ languages. Pragmas are machine- or operating system-specific by definition, and are usually different for every compiler.  Pragmas can also be used in conditional statements, to provide new preprocessor functionality, or to provide implementation-defined information to the compiler.")
(comment WarningPragmaDirective "A #$WarningPragmaDirective is a #$ComputerCodeStatement that specifies a selective modification of a compiler warning message.")
(comment WarningPragmaSpecifier "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeConstants which are used by #$WarningPragmaDirectives to specify selective modifications in compiler warning messages.")
(comment WarningLevelSpecifier "A specialization of #$WarningPragmaSpecifier.  A #$WarningLevelSpecifier is a #$ComputerCodeConstant which is used by a #$WarningPragmaDirective to set a particular warning level for a certain type of compiler warning (see #$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction).")
(comment WarningLevelFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for referencing #$ComputerCodeConstants used by #$WarningPragmaDirectives to specify warning levels for particular classes of #$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction.  Where N is a #$PositiveInteger and LN is a #$ProgrammingLanguage, (#$WarningLevelFn LN N) denotes the #$ComputerCodeConstant in LN used in #$WarningPragmaDirectives in LN to specify a warning level of N.")
(comment numberSpecifiedByWarningLevelSpecifier "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$WarningLevelFn.  Where N is a #$PositiveInteger and LN is a #$ProgrammingLanguage, (#$numberSpecifiedByWarningLevelSpecifier LN N SPCFR) means that SPCFR is the #$ComputerCodeConstant in LN used in #$WarningPragmaDirectives in LN to specify a warning level of N.")
(comment warningSpecifier "Where DIRECTIVE is a #$WarningPragmaDirective, (#$warningSpecifier DIRECTIVE SPECIFIER) means that SPECIFIER is the #$WarningPragmaSpecifier used by DIRECTIVE to specify the behavior for some class of #$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction.")
(comment CompilerWarning-ProgramAction "The class of all #$ProgramActions wherein warning signals are issues by compilers.")
(comment WarningTypeNumberFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where PL is a #$ProgrammingLanguage and N is a #$NonNegativeInteger, (#$WarningTypeNumberFn PL N) denotes the class of all compiler warnings (all instances of #$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction) denoted by the number N in PL.")
(comment compilerWarningTypeHasNumber "The corresponding predicate of #$WarningTypeNumberFn. Where PL is a #$ProgrammingLanguage and N is a #$NonNegativeInteger, (#$compilerWarningTypeHasNumber PL N WARN-TYPE) means that WARN-TYPE is the class of all compiler warnings (all instances of #$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction) denoted by the number N in PL.")
(comment warningClassAffected "Where DIRECTIVE is a #$WarningPragmaDirective, (#$warningClassAffected DIRECTIVE WARN-TYPE) means that DIRECTIVE specifies special compiler handling for compiler warnings (#$CompilerWarning-ProgramAction instances) of type WARN-TYPE for the context where the program in which DIRECTIVE appears is being compiled.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory)
(comment electricalConductanceOfObject "<code>(#$electricalConductanceOfObject   OBJ DEGREE)</code> means that the tangible object <code>OBJ</code> has this <code>DEGREE</code> of #$ElectricalConductance.  A higher value of <code>DEGREE</code> indicates <code>OBJ</code> is a better conductor, i.e., one that conducts with less energy lost to heat.")
(comment arrayValueOfVariableDeclaration "Where DECLARE is a #$VariableDeclaration, (#$arrayValueOfVariableDeclaration DECLARE N) means that DECLARE specifies the variable being declared to be an array of N instances of whatever data type is specified by the #$variableTypeSpecifier assertion or assertions.")
(comment BeachingFish "A specialization of #$CatchingFishWithRodAndReel.  In each instance of #$BeachingFish, fish are landed on a beach with a fishing rod.  A special technique is required for beaching fish on a beach with high surf.")
(comment BarblessFishhook "The collection of fishhooks that do not have barbs.")
(comment BarbedFishhook "The collection of fishhooks that have barbs.")
(disjointWith BarblessFishhook BarbedFishhook)
(comment FishhookBarb "The collection of barbs at the end of fishhooks. Not all fishhooks have barbs, in particular #$BarblessFishhooks do not.")
(comment subcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCount "<code>(#$subcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCount TYPE ROLE RP-TYPE NUMBER SPEC)</code> means that <code>SPEC</code> is the specialization of <code>TYPE</code> which is distinct from more general instances of <code>TYPE</code> in that its instances involve exactly <code>NUMBER</code> instance of <code>RP-TYPE</code> playing the role <code>ROLE</code>.  For example (#$subcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCount #$SmokingCigarettes  #$deviceUsed #$Cigarette 1 #$SmokingACigarette) means #$SmokingACigarette is the specialization of #$SmokingCigarettes in which exactly one instance of #$Cigarette is a #$deviceUsed.")
(comment SubcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCountFn "<code>(#$SubcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCountFn TYPE ROLE RP-TYPE NUMBER)</code> denotes the specialization of <code>TYPE</code> which is distinct from more general instances of <code>TYPE</code> in that its instances involve exactly <code>NUMBER</code> instances of <code>RP-TYPE</code> playing the role <code>ROLE</code>.  For example (#$SubcollectionWithRolePlayerOfTypeCountFn #$CatchingFish #$agentCaptured #$Fish 1) denotes the specialization of #$CatchingFish in which exactly one instance of #$Fish is the #$agentCaptured.")
(comment uRLReferenceForComputerCodeType "(uRLReferenceForComputerCodeType CODE-TYPE URL) means that URL is deemed a relevant web source for the #$ComputerCode specialization CODE-TYPE.")
(comment Queen "The collection of all queens. Cf. the specializations #$Queen-HeadOfState and #$QueenConsort.")
(comment QueenConsort "The collection of wives of kings who do not have the authority of instances of #$Queen-HeadOfState.")
(comment shortStringMD "<code>(#$shortStringMD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the measured depth of the deepest end of the short string of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment longStringMD "<code>(#$longStringMD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the measured depth of the deepest end of the long string of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment productionStringMD "<code>(#$productionStringMD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the measured depth of the deepest end of the production string of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment productionStringTVD "<code>(#$productionStringTVD WELL DIST)</code> means <code>DIST</code> is the true vertical depth of the deepest end of the production string of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment QuantityBasedFormula-ForwardDeriveRules "The collection of quantity based formulas for which #$equationPermutations of the sentence in #$equationFormFor are used to generate rules.")
(comment speedOfCPU "<code>(#$speedOfCPU CPU SPEED)</code> means that the #$CentralProcessingUnit  <code>CPU</code> has the speed <code>SPEED</code>.")
(comment projectsValueToInstanceViaRelnWithPred "<code>(#$projectsValueToInstanceViaRelnWithPred COL-A PRED-A PROJ-RELN COL-B PRED-B)</code> means that if <code>(PRED-A INST-A VALUE)</code> is true where <code>INST-A</code> is an instance of <code>COL-A</code>, then there exists at least one instance <code>INST-B</code> of <code>COL-B</code> such that <code>(PROJ-RELN INST-A INST-B)</code> is true and <code>(PRED-B INST-B VALUE)</code> is true.
<p>
For example, (#$projectsValueToInstanceViaRelnWithPred  #$Computer #$computerSpeed #$properPhysicalParts #$CentralProcessingUnit #$speedOfCPU) means that if <code>(#$computerSpeed COMPUTER-212 (#$MegaHertz 2009.302))</code>, then there is some instance <code>CPU</code> of #$CentralProcessingUnit <code>CPU</code> such that <code>(#$properPhysicalParts COMPUTER-212 CPU)</code> and <code>(#$speedOfCPU CPU (#$MegaHertz 2009.302))</code>.")
(comment projectsValueToInstanceViaRelnWithPred-Unique "<code>(#$projectsValueToInstanceViaRelnWithPred-Unique COL-A PRED-A PROJ-RELN COL-B PRED-B)</code> means that if <code>(PRED-A INST-A VALUE)</code> is true where <code>INST-A</code> is an instance of <code>COL-A</code>, then there exists exactly one instance <code>INST-B</code> of <code>COL-B</code> such that <code>(PROJ-RELN INST-A INST-B)</code> is true and <code>(PRED-B INST-B VALUE)</code> is true.")
(comment DevisedStructuredActivityWithFocalDevice "The collection of all tricks (scripted patterns of maneuvers) to be performed on or using a specific type of device, specified via #$structuredActivityFocalDeviceType.")
(comment structuredActivityFocalDeviceType "<code>(#$structuredActivityFocalDeviceType ACTIVITY DEVICE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>DEVICE-TYPE</code> is the focal device used in performances of <code>ACTIVITY</code> an instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivityWithFocalDevice.")
(comment EntrezGene-SKS "#$EntrezGene-SKS is the National Center For Biotechnology Information's web-accessible database of gene information.")
(comment UniProt-SKS "#$UniProt-SKS is web-accessible database of information about proteins.")
(comment AtomicLayerDeposition "A class of self-limiting sequential surface #$ThinFilmDeposition that deposites conformal #$ThinFilm instances onto substrates of varying compositions.  Due to the characteristics of self-limiting surface reactions, #$AtomicLayerDeposition makes atomic-scale deposition control possible.")
(comment ReactiveIonEtch "A form of #$WaferEtching-Dry in which chemically reactive plasma is generated under low pressure by an electromagnetic field:  high-energy ions within the plasma react with the reactant layer on the wafer and remove it.")
(comment PubMed-SKS "#$PubMed-SKS is the National Center For Biotechnology Information's web-accessible citation database for biomedical literature.")
(comment ThermalModificationProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$ModificationProcess-SingleWafer wherein the modification is imparted wholly or partially through the application of controlled heating to the target layer or substrate.")
(comment LLGeneImpactBoneTest2Fn "Version 2 of a function that returns an instance of #$KBContentTest.  (#$LLGeneImpactBoneTest2Fn GENE N) is the KB Content Test that queries for a #$couldImpact chain of length N between GENE and the amount of bone present in the body, represented by the quantity slot (#$QuantitySlotForArg2Fn #$BoneTheStuff #$amountPresentAt).")
(comment llGeneImpactBoneTest2 "The predicate that corresponds to #$LLGeneImpactBoneTest2Fn, <code>(#$llGeneImpactBoneTest2 GENE N TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the ''version 2'' instance of #$KBContentTest that queries for a #$couldImpact chain of <code>N</code> steps between <code>GENE</code>, a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily, and the amount of bone present in the body, denoted by (#$QuantitySlotForArg2Fn #$BoneTheStuff #$amountPresentAt).")
(comment geneProductParticipatesInBioProcessType "(#$chemicalObjectTypeParticipatesInBioProcessType OBJ-TYPE PROC-TYPE) states that in some unspecified circumstance, instances of OBJ-TYPE can be actors in instances of PROC-TYPE. Not every instance of OBJ-TYPE necessarily acts in such a way, but instances of PROC-TYPE are typically observed to have some instance of OBJ-TYPE participating.")
(comment ChemicalMechanicalPlanarization-SemiconductorWafer "The collection of all instances in semiconductor wafer processing where excess material from a #$ThinFilmDeposition or fill is ground down to a planar surface at specified depth by a combination of chemical and mechanical means.")
(comment substanceTypeUsedForCMP "Where CMP is an instance of #$ChemicalMechanicalPlanarization-SemiconductorWafer and SUBST-TYPE is a #$ChemicalSubstanceType, (#$substanceTypeUsedForCMP CMP SUBST-TYPE) means that some instance of SUBST-TYPE is used to facilitate the planarization process CMP.")
(comment SiliconWafer-Bulk "The collection of all 'bulk' #$SemiconductorWafers used in 28 nm bulk wafer processing.")
(comment SiliconOnInsulatorWafer "The collection of all preprocessed 'SOI' (silicon-on-insulator) wafers used in 32 nm SOI wafer processing.")
(comment EpitaxialLayer-SOIWafer "The collection of all silicon layers that are epitaxially grown directly on the substrate in #$SiliconOnInsulatorWafers.")
(comment BuriedOxideLayer-SOIWafer "The collection of all buried oxide (BOX) layers in #$SiliconOnInsulatorWafers.")
(comment P-TypeSiliconSOIWaferLayer "The collection of all P-Type silicon layers deposited on the box layers (#$BuriedOxideLayer-SOIWafer) of #$SiliconOnInsulatorWafers.")
(comment ThermalModificationProcess-Lot "The collection of all 'lot level' processes wherein all of the members of a semiconductor wafer lot (#$MEProcessingWaferLot) are simultaneously heated in order to effect some #$ModificationProcess-SemiconductorManufacture uniforml accross the lot.")
(comment ThermalDiffusionProcess-Lot "The collection of all 'lot level' thermal diffusion processes in which thermal diffusion (see #$ThermalModificationProcess-SingleWafer) is effected accross all of the wafers in an #$MEProcessingWaferLot.")
(comment llGeneImpactBoneTest-Generic "<code>(#$llGeneImpactBoneTest-Generic GENE N TEST)</code> identifies <code>TEST</code> as the #$KBContentTest that queries for a #$couldImpact chain of <code>N</code> steps between <code>GENE</code>, a #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily, and the amount of bone present in the body, denoted by (#$QuantitySlotForArg2Fn #$BoneTheStuff #$amountPresentAt).")
(comment personTypeWithHeritageFromRegion "<code>(#$personTypeWithHeritageFromRegion PERSON-TYPE REGION PERSON-TYPE-WITH-HERITAGE)</code> means that <code>PERSON-TYPE-WITH-HERITAGE</code> is the specialization <code>PRSON-TYPE</code> who have heritage from <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment PersonTypeWithHeritageFromRegionFn "<code>(#$PersonTypeWithHeritageFromRegionFn PERSON-TYPE REGION)</code> denotes the specialization <code>PRSON-TYPE</code> who have heritage from <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment hasHeritageFromRegion "<code>(#$hasHeritageFromRegion PERSON REGION)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> has heritage from <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment CanadianAmerican "A specialization of #$UnitedStatesPerson.  Each instance of #$CanadianAmerican is an American who either immigrated to the United States from Canada, or whose ancestry prominently features persons of Canadian origin.")
(comment SelfImmolation "A specialization of #$Suicide.  Self-immolation involves burning oneself to death.")
(comment PetroleumProduct "An #$ExistingStuffType; a specialization of #$PetroleumBasedProduct. #$PetroleumProducts include substances derived from  #$Petroleum-CrudeOil through #$Refining (specs of the collection #$PetroleumProduct-Refined) and other products, such as #$Naphtha. Note: This collection is NOT coextensive with #$Oil;  #$Oil includes substances, such as #$EdibleOil, that are not petroleum, and #$PetroleumProduct includes substances, such as #$GasolineFuel, that are not #$Oils.")
(comment producerTypeOfType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$ProducerFn. (#$producerTypeOfType X (ProducerFn X)) will always be true for X meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment AluminumCompany "A specialization of both #$SellingOrganization and #$CommercialOrganization.  Each instance of #$AluminumCompany is a commercial organization whose primary business consists in mining or refining aluminum and marketing the resultant product.")
(comment ProducerFn "<code>(#$ProducerFn COL)</code> denotes the specialization of #$IntelligentAgent whose instances produce instances of <code>COL</code>. For example, (#$ProducerFn #$PetroleumProduct) returns the collection of all agents who produce petroleum products.  In terms of natural resources, the \"production\" involved may include mining or refining or harvesting from the wild.")
(comment annualProductionVolume "<code>(#$annualProductionVolume AGENT COL VOL)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> produces <code>VOL</code> volume of <code>COL</code> per year.")
(comment BidOnPurchase "A proposal formulated by a potential buyer, communicated to a potential seller.  If accepted by both, may turn into a contract.")
(comment prospectiveRole "<code>(#$prospectiveRole ROLE PROSP-ROLE)</code> identifies <code>PROSP-ROLE</code> as a generalization of the #$BinaryRolePredicate <code>ROLE</code> such that <code>(PROSP-ROLE EVENT ROLE-PLAYER)</code> means that <code>ROLE-PLAYER</code> is prospectively a player of <code>ROLE</code> in <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment ProspectiveRoleFn "<code>(#$ProspectiveRoleFn ROLE)</code> denotes the generalization <code>GENL-PRED</code> of the #$BinaryRolePredicate <code>ROLE</code> such that <code>(GENL-PRED EVENT ROLE-PLAYER)</code> means that <code>ROLE-PLAYER</code> is prospectively a player of <code>ROLE</code> in <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment purchaseOfferValue "<code>(#$purchaseOfferValue OFFER VALUE)</code> identifies <code>VALUE</code> as the instance of #$MonetaryValue for which the #$communicatorOfInfo of the instance <code>OFFER</code> of #$RequestingToMakeAPurchase has indicated that he/she/it is offering to pay for the <code>(#$ProspectiveRoleFn #$objectPaidFor)</code>.")
(comment OrganizationTypeWithFocalActivitiesOfPersonTypeFn "<code>(#$OrganizationTypeWithFocalActivitiesOfPersonTypeFn PERSON-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of organizations that perform the charateristic actions of instances of <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment organizationTypeWithFocalActivitiesOfPersonType "<code>(#$organizationTypeWithFocalActivitiesOfPersonType PERSON-TYPE ORG0TYPE)</code> means that <code>ORG-TYPE</code> is the collection of organizations that perform the charateristic actions of instances of <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment purchaseOfferValue-PerShare "An instance of rule macro predicate relating an offer to purchase a company or stock in a company or mutual fund in terms of units of monetary value per share. <code>(#$purchaseOfferValue-PerShare OFFER VALUE)</code> is equivalent to <code>(#$purchaseOfferValue OFFER ((#$PerFn VALUE-UNIT (#$UnitOfCountFn #$Stock) N))</code> where <code>VALUE</code> is expressible as <code>(VALUE-UNIT N)</code>.")
(comment desiredEndStateOfPlanSpecification "(#$desiredEndStateOfPlan PLAN PROP) says that if an instantiation EXECUTION of the #$Plan-ExpectedSituationType PLAN is successful (see #$successfulForAgents), then PROP will be true at the end of EXECUTION.")
(comment BiddingToMakeAPurchaseOrSale "A specialization of #$Proposing-CommunicationAct. Each instance of this collection is an act of communicating a bid wither from a prospective seller to a prospective buyer or <i>vice versa</i>.")
(comment BiddingToMakeASale "A specialization of #$RequestingToMakeASale and #$BiddingToMakeAPurchaseOrSale. Each instance of this collection is an act of communicating a #$BidOnSale to a potential buyer. See also #$GettingBids.")
(comment BiddingToMakeAPurchase "A specialization of #$RequestingToMakeAPurchase and #$BiddingToMakeAPurchaseOrSale. Each instance of this collection is an act of communicating a bid to a potential seller.")
(comment competingProposals "<code>(#$competingProposals P1 P2)</code> means that <code>P1</code> and <code>P2</code> are proposals that are at least <i>prima facie</i> at least partially mutually exclusive and pertaining to a similar set of objectives or resources.")
(comment maximalWithRespectToType "<code>(#$maximalWithRespectToType THING PRED  COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> means that relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, the #$Thing <code>THING</code> is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MaximalWithRespectToDurationFn "<code>(#$MaximalWithRespectToDurationFn PRED DURATION)</code> denotes the temporal thing which, relative to other things during in <code>DURATION</code>, is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MaximalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistoryFn "<code>(#$MaximalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistoryFn T-THING SIT-TYPE ROLE SLOT)</code> denotes the individual <code>IND</code> which is such that during the temporal extent of <code>T-THING</code> from its inception until the present, <code>T-THING</code> has done (see #$doneBy) one or more instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and <code>IND</code> played the role <code>ROLE</code> in at least one such instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> and is maximal with regard to its value for <code>SLOT</code> compared to all other things that have played the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> done by <code>IND</code>.
<p>
This function is useful for denoting the largest fish someone has ever caught, or the highest mountain someone has ever climbed.")
(comment maximalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistory "<code>(#$maximalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistory IND T-THING SIT-TYPE ROLE SLOT)</code> means that during the temporal extent of <code>T-THING</code> from its inception until the present, <code>T-THING</code> has done (see #$doneBy) one or more instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and <code>IND</code> played the role <code>ROLE</code> in at least one such instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> and is maximal with regard to its value for <code>SLOT</code> compared to all other things that have played the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> done by <code>IND</code>.
<p>
This predicate is useful for indicating the largest fish someone has ever caught, or the highest mountain someone has ever climbed.")
(comment MaximalWithRespectToPlaceFn "<code>(#$MaximalWithRespectToPlaceFn PRED PLACE)</code> denotes the object which, relative to other things found in <code>PLACE</code>, is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment maximalWithRespectToPlace "<code>(#$maximalWithRespectToPlace ST PRED PLACE)</code> means that relative to other things found in <code>PLACE</code>, the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>ST</code> is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ PLACE)</code>, and <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code>, and if <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any other #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>OTHER-OBJ</code> found in <code>PLACE</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-OBJ OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment Monocrystalline "A #$Monocrystalline solid is a material wherein a single crystal lattice is continuous to the edges of the sample, with no grain boundaries.")
(disjointWith Monocrystalline Polycrystalline)
(comment Polycrystalline "#$Polycrystalline materials are solids that are composed of many #$Monocrystalline subregions ('grains') of varying size and orientation.")
(comment P-TypeSilicon "The collection of all instances of monocrystalline (#$Monocrystalline) #$Silicon where the lattice structure has been 'doped' in such a way that #$Cations (usually #$Boron ions) chemically bound within the lattice maintain a deficit of electrons, hence a net positive (P) charge.")
(comment N-TypeSilicon "The collection of all instances of monocrystalline (#$Monocrystalline) #$Silicon where the lattice structure has been 'doped' in such a way that #$Anions (often #$Phosphorus or #$Arsenic ions) chemically bound within the lattice maintain a surplus of electrons, hence a net negative (N) charge.")
(comment PolycrystallineSilicon "Each instance of #$PolycrystallineSilicon (also known in microfabrication as 'polysilicon' or just 'poly' is a sample of chemically pure #$Silicon composed of microscopic #$Monocrystalline structures, or 'grains with random orientation of the crystal lattice structure within each grain.")
(comment AnnealingProcess-SemiconductorModification "Instances of #$AnnealingProcess-SemiconductorModification are high temperature processes that are used to permeate a target layer or substrate with molecules of some type of chemical dopant (see #$dopantTypeDiffused).  Resultant structures are characterized by low resistivity.")
(comment LanthanumIIIOxide "The collection of all substances with the chemical formula La2O3, containing the rare earth element #$Lanthanum + #$Oxygen.  Instances are used in developing ferroelectric and optical materials.")
(comment MaximalWithRespectToTypeFn "<code>(#$MaximalWithRespectToTypeFn PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> denotes the #$Thing <code>THING</code> which, relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MaximalTypeWithRespectToTypeFn "<code>(#$MaximalTypeWithRespectToTypeFn PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> denotes the #$Collection <code>COL</code> such that any thing Thing <code>THING</code> that is an instance of <code>COL</code>, relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment minimalWithRespectToType "<code>(#$minimalWithRespectToType THING PRED  COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> means that relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, the #$Thing <code>THING</code> is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MinimalWithRespectToTypeFn "<code>(#$MinimalWithRespectToTypeFn PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> denotes the #$Thing <code>THING</code> which, relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment minimalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistory "<code>(#$minimalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistory IND T-THING SIT-TYPE ROLE SLOT)</code> means that during the temporal extent of <code>T-THING</code> from its inception until the present, <code>T-THING</code> has done (see #$doneBy) one or more instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and <code>IND</code> played the role <code>ROLE</code> in at least one such instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> and is minimal with regard to its value for <code>SLOT</code> compared to all other things that have played the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> done by <code>IND</code>.
<p>
This predicate is useful for indicating the smallest puppy someone has ever seen, or the smallest apartment someone has ever lived in.")
(comment MinimalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistoryFn "<code>(#$MinimalRolePlayerWRTSlotDuringIndividualHistoryFn T-THING SIT-TYPE ROLE SLOT)</code> denotes the individual <code>IND</code> which is such that during the temporal extent of <code>T-THING</code> from its inception until the present, <code>T-THING</code> has done (see #$doneBy) one or more instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and <code>IND</code> played the role <code>ROLE</code> in at least one such instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> and is minimal with regard to its value for <code>SLOT</code> compared to all other things that have played the role <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> done by <code>IND</code>.
<p>
This function is useful for denoting the shortest letter someone has ever read, or the smallest apartment someone has ever lived in.")
(comment minimalTypeWithRespectToType "<code>(#$minimalTypeWithRespectToType COLLECTION PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> means that relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, any thing #$Thing <code>THING</code> that is an instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code> that is not also an instnace of <code>COLLECTION</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment maximalTypeWithRespectToType "<code>(#$maximalTypeWithRespectToType COLLECTION PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> means that relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, any thing #$Thing <code>THING</code> that is an instance of <code>COLLECTION</code> is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code> that is not also an instnace of <code>COLLECTION</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment minimalWithRespectToPlace "<code>(#$minimalWithRespectToPlace ST PRED PLACE)</code> means that relative to other things found in <code>PLACE</code>, the #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>ST</code> is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(#$objectFoundInLocation OBJ PLACE)</code>, and <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code>, and if <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any other #$SpatialThing-Localized <code>OTHER-OBJ</code> found in <code>PLACE</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-OBJ OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MinimalWithRespectToPlaceFn "<code>(#$MinimalWithRespectToPlaceFn PRED PLACE)</code> denotes the object which, relative to other things found in <code>PLACE</code>, is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment minimalWithRespectToDuration "<code>(#$minimalWithRespectToDuration TT PRED DURATION)</code> means that relative to other things during time <code>PLACE</code>, the #$TemporalThing <code>ST</code> is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MinimalTypeWithRespectToTypeFn "<code>(#$MinimalTypeWithRespectToTypeFn PRED COMPARISON-COLLECTION)</code> denotes the #$Collection <code>COL</code> such that any thing Thing <code>THING</code> that is an instance of <code>COL</code>, relative to other things in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.  I.e. it is true that <code>(PRED THING QUANT)</code> and for any #$Thing <code>OTHER-THING</code> in <code>COMPARISON-CLASS</code>, if there is some other #$Quantity <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> of such that <code>(PRED OTHER-THING OTHER-QUANT)</code>, <code>OTHER-QUANT</code> is less than <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment MinimalWithRespectToDurationFn "<code>(#$MinimalWithRespectToDurationFn PRED DURATION)</code> denotes the temporal thing which, relative to other things during in <code>DURATION</code>, is minimal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment AssetsFn "<code>(#$AssetsFn AGENT)</code> denotes the entire group of tangible and intangible assets of <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment groupOfAssetsOfAgent "<code>(#$groupOfAssetsOfAgent AGENT GROUP)</code> means that <code>GROUP</code> is the entire group of tangible and intangible assets of <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment CourtRecord "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$CourtRecord is a record pertaining to the proceedings of a legal court.")
(comment BankruptcyAuction "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding and #$Auction-Event.  Each instance of #$BankruptcyAuction is a n auction that occurs as part of a #$BankruptcyProceeding..")
(comment TitaniumNitride "The collection of all substances with the chemical formula TiN.  Instances are extremely hard ceramics, often used as coatings on #$Titanium alloys, steel, carbide, and #$Aluminum components to improve the subtrate's surface properties.")
(comment bidForObjectFromFor "(#$bidForObjectFromFor BID BIDDER TARGET) means that there is a #$BiddingToMakeAPurchaseOrSale, BID, in which the potential buyer or seller is offering some amount of money via #$purchaseOfferValue on BID for TARGET -- the object of the bid.")
(comment BuyingAnOrganization "The collection of events in which an organization is the object purchased.")
(comment attemptToGainControlhasAssociatedProposal "(#$attemptToGainControlhasAssociatedProposal ATTEMPT PROP) means that in ATTEMPT there was an associated proposal, PROP, communicated that involved the offer, bid, conditions, etc.")
(disjointWith SemiconductorStuff DielectricStuff)
(comment DielectricStuff "The collection of all materials that exhibit the properties of electrical insulators in virtue of being polarized by an applied electric field.  When an instance of #$DielectricStuff is placed in an electric field, charges shift from their average equilibrium positions so that positive charges are displaced toward the field and negative charges are displaced in the opposite direction, creating an internal, secondary electric field within the dielectric counter to the external field.")
(comment SilicateGlass "#$Glass composed primarily of #$SiliconDioxide, with other materials added to either support ease of processing, or to effect some desirable property.")
(comment FluorosilicateGlass "A dialectric material (#$DielectricStuff) used as an insulator between metal layers in #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer.")
(comment Glass "A specialization of #$InorganicMaterial.  Each instance of #$Glass is a solid substance with an amorphous, i.e., non-crystalline molecular structure that exhibits an aphasic glass transition from solid to liquid form on heating.")
(comment BorophosphosilicateGlass "A type of #$SilicateGlass whose instances include instance of both #$Boron and #$Phosphorus as additives.  Instances are commonly used in #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer for insulating layers between metal or conducting layers.")
(disjointWith ElementStuff Silicide)
(disjointWith Agent-Generic Silicide)
(comment Silicide "The collection of all substances which are chemical compounds of #$Silicon and some other element.")
(comment functionTypePredictsPairBasedOnInitialValues "<code>(#$functionTypePredictsPairBasedOnInitialValues FUNC-TYPE XLIST YLIST X Y)</code> means that a function of type <code>FUNC-TYPE</code> predicts the pair <code><X, Y></code> given the set of pairs that would be created by associating the first member of <code>XLIST</code> (call it \"<code>X1</code>\") with the first member of <code>YLIST</code> (call it \"<code>Y1</code>\") to produce the pair <code><X1, Y1></code>, and associating the second member of <code>XLIST</code> (call it \"<code>X2</code>\") with the first member of <code>YLIST</code> (call it \"<code>Y2</code>\") to produce the pair <code><X2, Y2></code>, and so on. 
<p>
This predicate is not functional in general. It behaves like a functional predicate in both the arg4 and arg5 positions when the instance of the function type referenced in the arg1 position is 1-1.  Similarly, it behaves like a functional predicate in the arg4 position when the instance of the function type referenced in the arg1 position is 1-many, and it behaves like a functional predicate in the arg5 position when the instance of the function type referenced in the arg1 position is many-1.
<p>
This predicate is agnostic as to whether it is doing interpolation or extrapolation.")
(comment MetrologyTestStructure-Wafer "The collection of all #$SemiconductorDevices constructed on #$SemiconductorWafer instances solely for purposes of metrology testing.")
(comment WaferMetrologyOpticalTestStructure "The collection of all instances of #$MetrologyTestStructure-Wafer designed to aid in measurement testing (#$WaferTest-Metric) involving, e.g., overlay alignment or critical dimension.")
(comment WaferMetrologyElectricalTestStructure "The collection of all #$MetrologyTestStructure-Wafer designed to aid in electrical testing.")
(comment WaferMetrologyElectricalTestStructure-SingleDevice "The collection of all electrical test structures that are self-contained 'atomic components' (e.g. CMOS devices) within wafer die, and that are constructed solely for the purpose of electrical testing.")
(comment WaferMetrologyElectricalTestCircuit "The collection of all complete #$ElectricalCircuits constructed solely to be used in instances of #$WaferTest-Electrical.")
(comment MetrologyWaferSiteTest "The collection of all semiconductor industry metrology tests (#$MetrologyProcessesOfIndustryTypeFn (#$ProductionIndustryTypeFn #$SemiconductorDevice)) conducted on particular #$MetrologyTestStructure-Wafer instances on particular wafers.")
(comment testStructureTested "Where SITE-TEST is a #$MetrologyWaferSiteTest and TEST-STRUCTURE is a #$MetrologyTestStructure-Wafer, (#$testStructureTested SITE-TEST TEST-STRUCTURE) means that SITE-TEST occurs at TEST-STRUCTURE and evaluates TEST-STRUCTURE in some way.")
(comment WaferTest-Physical "The collection of all #$MetrologyWaferSiteTests which measure physical properties or dimensions of #$WaferDie components.")
(comment WaferTest-Defect "The collection of all #$MetrologyWaferSiteTests which try to identify defective residuals from instances of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer.")
(comment WaferTest-Electrical "The collection of all #$MetrologyWaferSiteTests which measure electrical properties or performance of #$SemiconductorWafer components.")
(comment FinalWaferElectricalTest "The collection of all instances of #$WaferTest-Electrical which occur at the end of wafer processing preparatory to wafer sectioning.")
(comment SampledWaferElectricalTest "The collection of all instances of #$WaferTest-Electrical performed on sampled wafers in the cource of wafer processing.")
(comment WaferTest-Metric "The collection of all instances of #$WaferTest-Physical where either a measurement of component dimension or proportionality (#$CriticalDimensionTest-WaferMetrology) or of deposition alignment (#$OverlayTest-WaferMetrology) is taken.")
(comment CriticalDimensionTest-WaferMetrology "All instances of #$WaferTest-Metric wherein what is measured is the width of a critical line feature deriving from the photomask, used as a dimensional control metric.")
(disjointWith CriticalDimensionTest-WaferMetrology OverlayTest-WaferMetrology)
(comment OverlayTest-WaferMetrology "The collection of all instances of #$WaferTest-Metric wherein the alignment of a certain #$ThinFilmDeposition is measured relative to a previously deposited #$SemiconductorWaferLayer.")
(comment FinalWaferElectricalTesting-LotLevel "The collection of all final rounds of electrical testing carried out on all of the members of an #$MEProcessingWaferLot prior to the sectionin of those members.  Each instance of #$FinalWaferElectricalTesting-LotLevel is comprised of instances of #$FinalWaferElectricalTest carried out in series or in parallel on each wafer that is a member of the affected lot.")
(comment TissueFormationFn "<code>(#$TissueFormationFn TISSUE-TYPE)</code> denotes a subcollection of #$BiologicalProductionEvent. In each instance of this collection there is an instance of <code>TISSUE-TYPE</code> that is a #$outputsCreated.")
(comment chemicalObjectInBLOContributesToBioProcess-TypeLevel "(#$chemicalObjectInBLOContributesToBioProcess-TypeLevel ?SUBST-TYPE ?BLO-TYPE ?P-TYPE) states that the presence of some adequate amount of ?SUBST-TYPE in an instance of ?BLO-TYPE is a precursor to the occurrence of an instance of the biological process, ?P-TYPE.  The presence of ?SUBST-TYPE may not be necessary, or sufficient; however, when an instance of ?P-TYPE occurs, typically an instance of ?SUBST-TYPE has been present.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesObject-TypeType "(#$tissueSynthesizesObject-TypeType TISSUETYPE OBJECTTYPE) states that instances of the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUETYPE, produce portions of OBJECTTYPE biosynthetically.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize OBJECTTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment objectInducesProtein-TypeType "(#$objectInducesProtein-TypeType OBJECTTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that, in some unspecified cellular environment, quantities of OBJECTTYPE trigger or speed up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  That is to say that there is some cellular situation in which the presence of OBJECTTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment objectInCellInducesProtein-TypeLevel "(#$objectInCellInducesProtein-TypeLevel OBJECTTYPE CELLTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that when some quantity of OBJECTTYPE is present in an instance of CELL it triggers or speeds up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  More specifically, the presence of some quantity of OBJECTTYPE in and instance of CELLTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment cellSynthesizesObject-TypeType "(#$cellSynthesizesObject-TypeType CELLTYPE OBJECTTYPE) states that instances of CELLTYPE produce portions of OBJECTTYPE biosynthetically.  CELLTYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, cell lineage, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize OBJECTTYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment TranscriptionCoactivatorMolecule "The collection of all #$ProteinMolecules which are capable of increasing the transcription of some gene or genes, but which do not bind directly to DNA. They do so by binding to some transcription factor, typically.\"")
(comment gene-GISTypeTranscribedInType "(#$gene-GISTypeTranscribedInType GIS-TYPE TRANSCRIP-TYPE) states that TRANSCRIP-TYPE is the class of events, each of which are Transcription-DNAToRNA, in which some instance of the GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily, GIS-TYPE, is transcribed.")
(comment GeneProductTypeFn "(#$GeneProductTypeFn GIS-TYPE) denotes an instance of #$PeptideMoleculeTypeBySourceGene which is the class of peptide molecules produced from DNA corresponding to GIS-TYPE.")
(comment tissueSynthesizesProteinMolecule-TypeType "(#$tissueSynthesizesProteinMolecule-TypeType TISSUETYPE MOLECULETYPE) states that instances of the #$BiologicalTissue, TISSUETYPE, produce portions of MOLECULETYPE biosynthetically.  This means that some of the cells within the tisse synthesize MOLECULETYPE.  TISSUETYPE must be specific enough with respect to its species, stage of development, etc. so that every instance can typically be expected to synthesize MOLECULETYPE, but exceptions can apply in unusual conditions.")
(comment objectTypeCorrelateOf "(#$objectTypeCorrelateOf OBJECT-PRED SUBSTANCE-TYPE-PRED OBJECT-ARG-NUM SUBSTANCE-ARG-NUM) means that OBJECT-PRED is the same relationship as SUBSTANCE-TYPE-PRED except that it takes a type of chemical object in OBJECT-ARG-NUM instead of the chemical substance type that the substance-type pred has in SUBSTANCe-ARG-NUM.")
(comment SeptenaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 7).  Each instance of #$SeptenaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 7.")
(comment NovenaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 9).  Each instance of #$NovenaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 9.")
(comment DenaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 10).  Each instance of #$DenaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 10.")
(comment OctonaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 8).  Each instance of #$OctonaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 8.")
(comment substanceInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType "(#$substanceInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType SUBSTANCETYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that, in some unspecified cellular environment, quantities of SUBSTANCETYPE trigger or speed up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  That is to say that there is some cellular situation in which the presence of SUBSTANCETYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment arg8Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg8Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the eighth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG8 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg9Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg9Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the ninth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ARG9 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG9 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment objectInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType "(#$objectInducesProteinMolecule-TypeType SUBSTANCETYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that, in some unspecified cellular environment, quantities of OBJECTTYPE trigger or speed up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  That is to say that there is some cellular situation in which the presence of OBJECTTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment substanceInCellInducesProteinMolecule-TypeLevel "(#$substanceInCellInducesProteinMolecule-TypeLevel SUBSTANCETYPE CELLTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that when some quantity of SUBSTANCETYPE is present in an instance of CELL it triggers or speeds up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  More specifically, the presence of some quantity of SUBSTANCETYPE in and instance of CELLTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment objectInCellInducesProteinMolecule-TypeLevel "(#$objectInCellInducesProteinMolecule-TypeLevel OBJECTTYPE CELLTYPE PROTEINTYPE) states that when some quantity of OBJECTTYPE is present in an instance of CELL it triggers or speeds up the biosynthesis of PROTEINTYPE.  More specifically, the presence of some quantity of OBJECTTYPE in and instance of CELLTYPE causes the initiation or the increase in transcription of the gene or genes coding for PROTEINTYPE and the subsequent translation of mRNA to produce PROTEINTYPE, or to produce a precursor of the protein that is then post-translationally modified to result in PROTEINTYPE.")
(comment functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints "(#$functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints   FUNC-TYPE THING DEP-VALUE1 INDEP-VALUE1 DEP-VALUE2 INDEP-VALUE2 DEP-VALUE3 INDEP-VALUE3) means that a function of type FUNC-TYPE predicts that, given that that the quantitative value of something is the dependent DEP-VALUE1 when it has the corresponding independent value INDEP-VALUE1, and is VALUE2 when it has the corresponding INDEP-VALUE2, the quantitative value will be VALUE3 when it has the corresponding INDEP-VALUE3.
<p>
For example, the independent values might be dates, and the dependent values might be stock prices.  In that case, (#$functionTypePredictsPointFromPoints FUNC-TYPE STOCK VALUE1 DATE1 VALUE2 DATE2 VALUE3 DATE3) would mean that a function of type FUNC-TYPE predicts that the value of STOCK will be VALUE3 on DATE3, given that it is  VALUE1 on DATE1 and VALUE2 on DATE2.")
(comment ThinFilmDeposition-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all instances of #$ThinFilmDeposition that are carried out in the course of semiconductor manufacturing.")
(comment CopperElectroplating-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all instances of #$ElectroChemicalDeposition-SemiconductorManufacture wherein the #$thinFilmDeposited is an instance of #$Copper.")
(comment ElectroChemicalIndustrialThinFilmDeposition "The collection of all instances of #$ElectroPlating carried out in the course of instances of #$Manufacturing.  We consider this collection to be roughly coextensive with 'industrial electroplating'.")
(comment functionTypePredictsValueAtDateFromValuesAtDates "(#$functionTypePredictsValueAtDateFromValuesAtDates FUNC-TYPE THING VALUE1 DATE1 VALUE2 DATE2 VALUE3 DATE3) means that a function of type FUNC-TYPE predicts that, given that the value of THING onis VALUE1 on DATE1 and VALUE2 on DATE2, the value of thing is VALUE3 on DATE3.")
(comment setOfTermsHasConceptFilterStatus "(#$setOfTermsHasConceptFilterStatus SET STATUS-COLL) means that each member of SET is a quoted instance (#$quotedIsa) of the concept filter status collection STATUS-COLL.  (E.g. (#$setOfTermsHasConceptFilterStatus (#$TheSet #$Action #$Event) #$TermUnacceptableForQueryStringMapping) means that #$Action and #$Event are both unacceptable for query string mapping in CAE/Cure tasks whose guidance Mts can see that assertion.")
(comment ElectroChemicalDeposition-SemiconductorManufacture "The collection of all instances of #$ElectroChemicalIndustrialThinFilmDeposition that are carried out in the course of semiconductor manufacture (#$MEWaferFabricationProcess-SingleWafer).")
(comment layerSectionRemoved "Where REMOVING is a #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer and LAYER is a #$SemiconductorWaferLayer, (#$layerSectionRemoved REMOVING LAYER) means that one or more sections of LAYER are removed from the wafer substrate that is the #$objectRemaining after REMOVING.")
(comment layerCompletelyRemoved "(#$layerCompletelyRemoved REMOVING LAYER) means that the #$SemiconductorWaferLayer LAYER is entirely removed from the wafer construct that is the #$objectRemaining in REMOVING, modulo negligible quantities.")
(comment layerHaltedAt "(#$layerHaltedAt REMOVING LAYER) means that the #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer REMOVING 'stops' at LAYER, in the sense that LAYER is the first #$SemiconductorWaferLayer substantively unaffected by REMOVING.")
(comment chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerAffected "(chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerAffect PROCESSING SUBST-TYPE) just in case there is a #$SemiconductorWaferLayer LAYER such that LAYER is an #$objectActedOn in PROCESSING and the #$thinFilmChemicalSubstanceType of LAYER is SUBST-TYPE.")
(comment chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerRemoved "(#$chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerRemoved REMOVING SUBST-TYPE) means that there is a #$SemiconductorWaferLayer whose #$thinFilmChemicalSubstanceType is SUBST-TYPE, and which is at least partially removed (#$layerSectionRemoved) in REMOVING.")
(comment chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerHaltedAt "(#$chemicalSubstanceTypeOfLayerHaltedAt REMOVING SUBST-TYPE) means that there is #$SemiconductorWaferLayer LAYER such that (#$layerHaltedAt REMOVING LAYER) and such that (#$thinFilmChemicalSubstanceType LAYER SUBST-TYPE).")
(comment PiecewiseMathematicalFunction "The collection of all piecewise mathematical functions, which are functions that are defined differently for disjoint portions of their ranges.")
(comment LinearPolynomialFunction-Piecewise "A sub-collection of #$PiecewiseMathematicalFunction, each of which is is polynomial with a degree of 1.")
(comment ClosingOfAStockMarket "The collection of events which are the termination of the day's trading in some stock market or other.")
(comment OpeningOfAStockMarket "The collection of events which are the opening of the day's trading in some stock market or other.")
(comment dopantTypeDiffused "Where DIFFUSION is a #$AnnealingProcess-SemiconductorModification and SUBST-TYPE is a #$ChemicalSubstanceType, (#$dopantTypeDiffused DIFFUSION SUBST-TYPE) means that an instance of SUBST-TYPE is chemically diffused through a target layer or substrate in DIFFUSION.")
(comment MallocFn "A #$MemoryManagementFunction.  Where BYTESIZE is a #$NonNegativeInteger, (#$MallocFn BYTESIZE) allocates BYTESIZE bytes and returns a pointer to the allocated memory.")
(comment CallocFn "Where N is a #$PositiveInteger and BYTESIZE is a #$NonNegativeInteger, (#$CallocFn N BYTESIZE) allocates memory for an array of N elements of BYTESIZE bytes each and returns a pointer to the allocated memory.")
(comment The2DPoint "<code>(#$The2DPoint INTERVAL1 INTERVAL2)</code> is the ordered tuple whose elements are <code>INTERVAL1</code> and <code>INTERVAL2</code>.  This function is useful for denoting points in dimensioned conceptual spaces, such as a space used to conceptualize how one value of a system depends on other values of a system.")
(comment point-2D "<code>(#$point-2D INTERVAL1 INTERVAL2 2DPOINT)</code> means that <code>2DPOINT</code> is the ordered tuple (specifically, the #$2DPoint) whose elements are <code>INTERVAL1</code> and <code>INTERVAL2</code>.  This predicate is useful for describing points in dimensioned conceptual spaces, such as a space used to conceptualize how one value of a system depends on other values of a system.")
(comment extrapolationWithSimpleLinearRegression "<code>(#$extrapolationWithSimpleLinearRegression SET-OF-2DPOINTS 2DPOINT)</code> means that a simple linear regression extrapolates the #$2DPoint <code>2DPOINT</code> given the set of other #$2DPoints in <code>SET-OF-2DPOINTS</code>.")
(comment interpolationWithPiecewiseLinearPolynomial "<code>(#$interpolationWithPiecewiseLinearPolynomial SET-OF-2DPOINTS 2DPOINT)</code> means that an instance of #$LinearPolynomialFunction-Piecewise interpolates the #$2DPoint <code>2DPOINT</code> given the set of other #$2DPoints in <code>SET-OF-2DPOINTS</code>.")
(comment amountPaidToDuring "(#$amountPaidToDuring AGT1 AGT2 MONETARY-AMOUNT INTERVAL) means that AGT1 payed a total of MONETARY-AMOUNT to AGT2 during INTERVAL.  This could have been one lump sum or it could have been in multiple payments spread out through INTERVAL.")
(comment Silicon-GermaniumAlloy "The collection of all #$MetalAlloy instances which consist of any molar ratio of #$Silicon and Germanium.  Instances are commonly used in microfabrication of instances of #$SemiconductorDevice.")
(comment suppliesPercentageFor "(#$suppliesPercentageFor AGENT1 AGENT2 PERCENT INTERVAL) means that AGENT2 supplies AGENT1 with goods or services and PERCENT is the percent of AGENT1's total expenditures that are served by AGENT2 during interval.")
(comment CommercialAssetTransaction "Buying events involving commercial organizations buying and selling significant assets, such as factories, companies, etc.")
(comment assetPurchased "(#$assetPurchased EVENT OBJECT) means that in the #$CommercialAssetTransaction EVENT, the ownership rights for the significant asset OBJECT are transferred from one #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to another.  OBJ is not the #$objectTendered but the asset that is bought/sold.")
(comment assetSalePrice-Event "The predicate #$assetSalePrice-Event is used to relate an asset transaction (that is, an instance of #$CommercialAssetTransaction) to the total amount of money paid by the buyer in that event. (#$assetSalePrice-Event BUYING MONEY) means that the sum total charge for all assets and taxes, as well as any ancillary charges (e.g. shipping and handling, delivery charges, discounts, etc.) in the BUYING is the #$MonetaryValue MONEY. This predicate is not to be confused with the predicate.")
(comment dateOfAssetTransaction "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a specialization of both #$startingDate and #$endingDate (qq.v.).  #$dateOfEvent relates a CommercialAssetTransaction to a #$Date on or in which it transpired.  <code>(#$dateOfAssetTransaction TRANS DATE)</code> means that <code>TRANS</code> both starts and ends during <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment coactivatesTranscriptionOfTypeInitiatedByType "(#$coactivatesTranscriptionOfTypeInitiatedByType COACT-TYPE GIS-TYPE FACTOR-TYPE) states that the molecule COACT-TYPE acts as a #$TranscriptionCoactivatorMolecule to upregulate the initiation of transcription of GENE-GIS by FACTOR-TYPE.")
(comment ManufacturingTypeSpecifiedByThread "A collection of #$Collections.  Each collection instance is a #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$ManufacturingASingleObject whose instances share a common workflow process thread specification.")
(comment SemiconductorWaferProcessing-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$SemiconductorProcessing-Wafer wherein exactly one #$SemiconductorWafer is the locus of the action.")
(comment 28NMBulkWaferFabrication "The collection of all end-to-end instances of #$MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer that successfully follow the 28 nanometer bulk wafer fabrication thread specification.")
(comment 32NMSOIWaferFabrication "The collection of all end-to-end instances of #$MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer that successfully follow the 32 nanometer silicon-on-insulator (SOI) process thread.")
(comment scheduleDataSentence "A binary #$SummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a #$Place to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$scheduleDataSentence PLACE SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact that is considered by the salient audience to constitute scheduling information about PLACE in the current context.")
(comment SummitCrater "A specialization of #$Crater.  Each instance of #$SummitCrater is a crater near the summit of a #$Volcano.")
(comment AustralianGovernmentDepartment "A collection of government organizations.  Each instance of #$UnitedKingdomGovernmentDepartment is an organization that is part of the national government of the United Kingdom.")
(comment DepartmentOfDefence-Australia "The Australian Department of Defence is the defense department of the Australian government.")
(comment DepartmentOfNationalDefence-Canada "The Canadian Department of National Defence is the defense department of the Canadian government.")
(comment sectionHeader-CIS "<code>(#$sectionHeader-CIS WORK HEADER)</code> identifies the #$TextStringOccurrence <code>HEADER</code> as the header of <code>WORK</code> an instance of #$TextualPCW.")
(disjointWith NWellCreation-Mass PWellCreation-Mass)
(comment Goldsmith "The collection of all goldsmiths, who are workers who create objects made of gold. #$Goldsmith is a #$PersonTypeByActivity.")
(comment Metalworker "The collection of all metalworkers, who are people who create, alter or repair objects made of metal. #$Metalworker is a #$PersonTypeByActivity.")
(comment Silversmith "The collection of all silversmiths, who are workers who create objects made of silver. #$Silversmith is a #$PersonTypeByActivity.")
(comment Metalworking "The collection of events whose intended output are #$Artifacts made out of #$Metal, typically using #$MetalworkingTools.")
(comment Metalwork "The collection of #$Metal #$Artifacts.")
(comment corporateCompetitors-Generic "(#$corporateCompetitors-Generic COMPANY-1 COMPANY-2) means that COMPANY-1 and COMPANY-2 are direct competitors.")
(comment corporateCompetitors-Hoovers "(#$corporateCompetitors-Hoovers COMPANY-1 COMPANY-2) means that COMPANY-1 and COMPANY-2 are direct competitors.")
(comment interpolated2DPointComponentsFromPeicewiseLinearPolynomial "<code>(#$interpolated2DPointComponentsFromPeicewiseLinearPolynomial SET-OF-TUPLES X-PARAM Y-PARAM)</code> means that a #$LinearPolynomialFunction-Piecewise  interpolates a #$2DPoint determined by the tuple <code><X-PARAM, Y-PARAM></code> when applied to <code>SET-OF-TUPLES</code>.")
(comment setOf2DPointsIncludesPointWithComponents "<code>(#$setOf2DPointsIncludesPointWithComponents SET-OF-TUPLES X-PARAM Y-PARAM)</code> means that <code>X-PARAM</code> and <code>Y-PARAM</code> are components of a 2D point that is a member of <code>SET-OF-TUPLES</code>.")
(comment HooversThing "A thing represented in the Hoover's database.")
(comment HooversCompany "A #$LegalCorporation represented in the Hoover's database.")
(comment hooversValue "(#$hooversValue THING FIELD VALUE) means that one FIELD value (perhaps of many) for THING in the Hoover's database is VALUE.")
(comment GateStack-Transistor "The collection of gate stacks in transistors.  These \"gates\" are the source of a current that, in field effect transistors, opens or closes some p or n channel at some positive or negative threshold of voltage (see #$transistorThresholdVoltage) and this allows current to pass between the source and drain regions of the transistor.")
(comment AreaOfObjectFn "<code>(#$AreaOfObjectFn OBJ)</code> denotes the 2-dimensional area of <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment AreaOfRegionFn "<code>(#$AreaOfObjectFn REGION)</code> denotes the 2-dimensional area of <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment nthLargestElement "(#$nthLargestElement X N SET FUNCTION) means that X is an element of SET that has precisely N-1 other elements with a larger value for FUNCTION. For example, (#$nthLargestElement #$Alaska-State 1 #$State-UnitedStates #$AreaOfRegionFn) means that Alaska is the largest state (no elements have a larger #$areaOfRegion). Yet there may be more #$nthLargestElements. For example, (#$nthLargestElement ?X 1 (#$TheSet 1 2 3 -3) #$AbsoluteValueFn) is true for both 3 and -3 ; when the elements in the set are ordered according to their absolute value both 3 and -3 are largest elements. See also #$nthSmallestElement.")
(comment bottomholeFlowingPressureOfWell "<code>(#$bottomholeFlowingPressureOfWell WELL PRESS)</code> means that the #$Well <code>WELL</code> has a fluid flowing at #$Pressure <code>PRESS</code> in the vicinity of the #$Bottomhole.  I.e., <code>WELL</code> has a #$ProductionTubingAndBottomholeSystem <code>SYS</code> such that <code>(#$bottomholeFlowingPressure SYS ?PRESS</code>.")
(comment FabricationOfByInTimeIntervalFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where ARTIFACT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Artifact, ORG is an instance of #$ManufacturingOrganization, and TIME-INT is a #$TimeInterval, (#$FabricationOfByInTimeIntervalFn ARTIFACT-TYPE ORG TIME-INT) denote the collection of all instances of #$ManufacturingASingleObject such that an instance of ARTIFACT-TYPE is the #$objectProcessed, ORG is the #$directingAgent, and such that the #$ManufacturingASingleObject #$occursDuring INT.")
(comment allFabricationOfByInTimeInterval "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$FabricationOfByInTimeIntervalFn.  Where ARTIFACT-TYPE is a specialization of #$Artifact, ORG is an instance of #$ManufacturingOrganization, and TIME-INT is a #$TimeInterval, (#$allFabricationOfByInTimeInterval ARTIFACT-TYPE ORG TIME-INT MANUFACTURE-TYPE) means that MANUFACTURE-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ManufacturingASingleObject such that an instance of ARTIFACT-TYPE is the #$objectProcessed, ORG is the #$directingAgent, and such that the #$ManufacturingASingleObject #$occursDuring INT.")
(comment TropicalRainForest "A specialization of #$Rainforest. Each #$TropicalRainForest is an area of dense forest located in the tropics and characterized by high annual rainfall and continuous high temperature. Up to three tree layers grow above a variable shrub layer. Source: <i>The Times Atlas of the World (1995).</i>")
(comment Rainforest "A specialization of #$Forest. Each #$Rainforest is an area of dense forest characterized by high annual rainfall.")
(comment TemperateRainforest "A specialization of #$Rainforest. Each #$TemperateRainforest is an area of dense forest located in a temperate climate zone and characterized by high annual rainfall.")
(comment MediumSizedFn "<code>(#$MediumSizedFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are medium-sized as compared to other instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment mediumSizedVarietyOfType "<code>(#$mediumSizedVarietyOfType TYPE MED-TYPE)</code> means that <code>MED-TYPE</code> is the collection of all medium-sized instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment Dichlorodiphenyltrichloroethane "A type of #$Insecticide, commonly called \"DDT\".")
(comment ClosingPrice "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue. ")
(comment OpeningPrice "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue. ")
(comment weaknessTypeReference-CW "Where CW is a #$ConceptualWork, (#$weaknessTypeReference-CW WEAKNESS-TYPE CW) means that CW is a reference which provides further reading and insight into the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency WEAKNESS-TYPE.")
(comment weaknessTypeMitigationReference-CW "Where CW is a #$ConceptualWork, (#$weaknessTypeReference-CW WEAKNESS-TYPE CW) means that CW is a reference which provides further reading and insight into mitigations and workarounds for the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency WEAKNESS-TYPE.")
(comment HighThreshholdVoltage-FET "A specialization of #$FieldEffectTransistor.  Each instance of This collection is a field effect transistor with a higher threshold voltage than RVT transistors.  Typically these are used when low leakage (at the cost of slower switching speeds) is desired.")
(comment RegularThreshholdVoltage-FET "A specialization of #$FieldEffectTransistor.  Each instance of This collection is a field effect transistor with a higher threshold voltage than LVT transistors and a lower threshold voltage than HVT transistors. ")
(comment LowThreshholdVoltage-FET "A specialization of #$FieldEffectTransistor.  Each instance of This collection is a field effect transistor with a lower threshold voltage than RVT transistors.  Typically used in critical paths where speed is essential. ")
(comment GateOxideLayer-Transistor "The collection of gate oxide layers in transistors.  Each instance of this collection is a thin layer of an insulating material (silicon dioxide, silicon oxynitride, or high-k dielectric materials) between the gate stack and the region when the n or p channel will form when the gate is open.")
(comment gateDelay-Transistor "(#$gateDelay-Transistor TRANSISTOR VELOCITY) relates a transistor to the time interval it takes for the transistor to turn on (the time it takes for a n or P channel to form allowing the current to pass through the gate area).")
(comment lengthOfGate-Transistor "(#$lengthOfGate-Transistor TRANSISTOR LENGTH) relates a transistor to the length of the n or p channel that forms in the transistor's \"on\" state. ")
(comment widthOfGate-Transistor "(#$widthOfGate-Transistor TRANSISTOR LENGTH) relates a transistor to the width of the n or p channel that forms in the transistor's \"on\" state. ")
(comment areaOfGate-Transistor "(#$areaOfGate-Transistor TRANSISTOR LENGTH) relates a transistor to the area of the n or p channel that forms in the transistor's \"on\" state. ")
(comment NaturalFlowWell "A specialization of #$ProductionWell.  Each instance of #$NaturalFlowWell is a well that has outflow but does not use any kind of #$ArtificialLiftDevice to enhance its outflow.")
(disjointWith NaturalFlowWell ArtificialLiftWell)
(comment ArtificialLiftWell "A specialization of #$ProductionWell.  Each instance of #$ArtificialLiftWell is a well that uses some sort of #$ArtificialLiftDevice to enhance outflow.")
(comment 2DPoint "A specialization of #$Point.  Each instance of #$2DPoint can be defined by an ordered tuple with exactly two elements, each of which is a #$ScalarInterval.")
(comment pointDefinedByList "<code>(#$pointDefinedByList POINT LIST)</code> means that the #$Point <code>POINT</code> is completely described by the list <code>LIST</code>.")
(comment Glucose6PhosphateMolecule "The collection of all glucose 6-phosphate molecules, also known as Robinson ester.  Instances are characterized by the presence of a phosphate group on the 6' carbon.  Instances can have many roles within cells, for example, as an input to #$Glycolysis or to the pentose phosphate pathway.")
(comment chemicalObjectsCreated-TypeType "(#$chemicalObjectsCreated-TypeType REACTION-TYPE CHEM-OBJ-TYPE) means that instances of CHEM-OBJ-TYPE are produced in instances of REACTION-TYPE. The products are those #$Molecules, #$Ions etc. that are formed by the reaction.")
(comment chemicalObjectsDestroyed-TypeType "(#$chemicalObjectsDestroyed-TypeType REACTION-TYPE CHEM-OBJ-TYPE) states that in instances of REACTION-TYPE, some instance of CHEM-OBJ-TYPE is destroyed.")
(comment G1PConversionToG6P "Instances are #$ChemicalReactions in which a #$Glucose1PhosphateMolecule is converted to a #$Glucose6PhosphateMolecule.  This reaction is mediated by the enzyme #$Phosphoglucomutase.")
(comment SkeletalMyocyte "#$SkeletalMyocytes are a type of cell found in #$StriatedMuscle, also known as skeletal muscle.  These are long, multinucleated cells which contract when excited, to result in overall contraction of the muscle.")
(comment HafniumIVOxide "One of the most common and stable compounds of #$Hafnium.  Instances are electrical insulators with a band gap of approximately 6 electron volts.  Its high dielectric constant (25) makes it a good dielectric insulator.")
(comment slopeOfRegressionLineForSetOfPoints "<code>(#$slopeOfRegressionLineForSetOfPoints   SET-OF-POINTS SLOPE)</code> means that <code>SLOPE</code> is the slope of the regression line determined by the points in <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code>.")
(comment CellLifeStageTypeByProcessType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType instances of which are all and only those specializations of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel that are significant steps in the propagation of cells by mitotic division (see #$EukaryoticCellCycle) or in the production of gametes by meiotic division (see #$Gametogenesis-Meiotic).")
(comment oppositeSubsituationTypesWRTActorType "(#$oppositeSubsituationTypesWRTActorType SUPER SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 ACTOR-TYPE) means that when SIT-TYPE1 and SIT-TYPE2 occur as part of SUPER, they behave as opposites with respect to what happens to instances of ACTOR-TYPE.")
(comment extractedRelnWeight "<code>(#$extractedRelnWeight EXTRACTION WEIGHT)</code> identifies the number <code>WEIGHT</code> as the weight assigned to the EXTRACTION by its producer.  This is intended to approximate the reliability of the extraction.")
(comment structuredKnowledgeSourceNamespace "(#$structuredKnowledgeSourceNamespace SK-SOURCE NAMESPACE) indicates that the structured knowledge source SK-SOURCE uses the namespace NAMESPACE. This assumes a maximum of one namespace per knowledge source.")
(comment DateToSecondsSince1970Fn "#$DateToSecondsSince1970Fn is an evaluatable function that takes a date and returns a positive integer equal to the number of seconds from the start of 1970 to (the start of) the specified date.  For instance, (#$DateToSecondsSince1970Fn  (#$MinuteFn 21 (#$HourFn 0 (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1970)))))) evaluates to 1260.")
(comment secondsSince1970ToDate "<code>(#$secondsSince1970ToDate NUM DATE)</code> holds just in case <code>DATE</code> is the date that is <code>NUM</code> seconds since the start of 1970.  The is the corresponding predicate to #$SecondsSince1970ToDateFn.")
(comment typeHasBoilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure "<code>(#$typeHasBoilingPoint-TemperatureAtPressure OBJ-TYPE TEMP PRESSURE)</code> means that instances of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> (a specialization of  #$PartiallyTangible) will boil when their temperature (#$temperatureOfObject) and ambient pressure (see #$ambientPressure) converge at <code>TEMP</code> and <code>PRESSURE</code>, respectively, all other variables held constant.")
(comment Coenzyme "A #$Coenzyme is a small, non-protein organic molecule that can become bound to a protein, particularly an #$EnzymeMolecule, thus enabling its biological activity.  Some molecules classified as coenzymes can have additional functions.")
(comment NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide "The collection of NAD+  molecules. Such molecules are found in all #$Cells, and have important roles in electron transfer, able to become reduced (transformed into #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide) by accepting an electron, and then able to act to reduce other molecules by giving that electron up.")
(comment ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide "The collection of NADH molecules. These are the reduced form of #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide. Such molecules are found in all #$Cells, and have important roles in electron transfer, able to become reduced (transformed into #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide) by accepting an electron, and then able to act to reduce other molecules by giving that electron up.")
(comment implantationTargetsWaferStructuresOfType "(#$implantationTargetsWaferStructuresOfType IMPLANTATION STRUCTURE-TYPE) means that the #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation IMPLANTATION targets structures of type STRUCTURE-TYPE on the wafer being implanted.")
(comment antoineEquationParametersForTypeAndInterval "<code>(#$antoineEquationParametersForTypeAndInterval SUBSTANCE-TYPE A-PARAM B-PARAM C-PARAM RANGE)</code> means that the parameters A, B and C, for the Antoine Equation for the substance <code>SUBSTANCE-TYPE</code> are the numbers <code>A-PARAM</code>, <code>B-PARAM</code>, and <code>C-PARAM</code>, respectively, for the temperature range <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtPoint "<code>(#$regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtPoint SET1 SET2 POINT)</code> means that the lines determined by linear regression on <code>SET1</code> and <code>SET2</code> intersect at <code>POINT</code>.")
(disjointWith DephosphorylationOfGlucose6Phosphate PhosphorylatingAProteinMolecule)
(comment DephosphorylationOfGlucose6Phosphate "The collection of all events in which a #$PhosphateIon is removed from a #$Glucose6PhosphateMolecule and released as a free ion.  Instances of #$DephosphorylationOfGlucose6Phosphate are catalyzed by the enzyme glucose 6-phosphatase.  The reaction, which occurs in #$Hepatocytes, produces free glucose, which is able to pass the cell membrane, enter the bloodstream, and be taken up by other cells.")
(disjointWith DephosphorylatingAProteinMolecule DephosphorylationOfGlucose6Phosphate)
(comment MembraneTransport "The collection of processes in which chemical objects move or are moved across a biological membrane.  Movement from low concentration to high concentration requires energy.  This is refered to as active transport (see #$ActiveTransport-Membrane).  Passive transport (#$PassiveTransport-Membrane) is movement across a membrane not requiring energy.")
(comment PassiveTransport-Membrane "The collection of processes in which chemical objects move across a biological membrane from a region of high concentration to a region of lower concentration.  This movement can occur without an expenditure of energy.")
(comment MembraneTransport-SimpleDiffusion "The collection of processes in which chemical objects move across a biological membrane from an area of high concentration to one of low concentration, without the assistance of pores or transport proteins. Molecules and ions able to move in this way are typically small, uncharged chemical objects.")
(comment MembraneTransport-FacilitatedDiffusion "The collection of processes in which chemical objects move across a biological membrane from an area of high concentration to one of low concentration, with the assistance of transport proteins.")
(comment NormativeSpecification "The common sub-collection of both #$Specification and #$Criterion.  Each instance of #$NormativeSpecification is a conceptual work that describes how something should be.  The instances can refer to instances or whole sub-collections of #$Situation or #$SomethingExisting.  Thus, the conceptual work associated with an instance of #$Blueprint is an instance of #$NormativeSpecification because it describes what the properties of the resultant building should be.  Familiar specializations of #$NormativeSpecification include #$Agreement, #$Obligation, and #$Instructions.")
(comment ContextOfPCWMeetingThresholdFn "(#$ContextOfPCWMeetingThresholdFn WORK THRESHOLD) denotes the #$PropositionalInformationThing associated with WORK that meets THRESHOLD.  Typically, this is used with tools that automatically extract information from a document (WORK) and provide some measure of confidence.  The context resulting from this function contains a subset of the assertions that would be seen in (#$ContextOfPCWFn WORK).")
(comment CausalPrecursorTypeForTypeFn "<code>(#$CausalPrecursorTypeForTypeFn EFFECT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of events which, <i>ceteris paribus</i>, when instantiated cause instances of <code>EFFECT-TYPE</code> to occur.")
(comment MolecularBeamEpitaxy "A form of #$PhysicalVaporDeposition that takes place in vacuum or ultra-high vacuum with a slow deposition rate.")
(comment extractionReaderName "<code>(#$extractionReaderName EXTRACTION STRING)</code> identifies the program that performed the #$RelationExtraction <code>EXTRACTION</code> by the name <code>STRING</code>.")
(comment Hubcap "The collection of hubcaps -- decorative discs used to cover the wheel (or at least the center of the wheel) on an automobile.")
(comment objectRaised "This predicate is used in connection with particular instances of #$LiftingAnObject, to identify the object that is lifted during the event.  <code>(#$objectRaised LIFT OBJ)</code>.")
(disjointWith ChangingATireScript-Roadside ChangingATireScript-Garage)
(comment AttachmentOfWheelToAutomobile "A connection which necessarily has a nut and a bolt. May or may not join to other objects.")
(comment DParagraph-TextualPCW "A specialization of #$StructurallySpecificWork and #$TextualPCW.  An instance of #$DParagraph-TextualPCW is a propositional work whose informational structure (see #$infoStructureOfCW) has a unique header and whose body is a bulleted list of phrases or sentences.")
(comment EliteIceHockeyLeague "A professional ice hockey league in the United Kingdom.")
(comment extractedRelnUnweighted "<code>(#$extractedRelnUnweighted EXTRACTION)</code> identifies EXTRACTION as an extraction that was not provided with a weight by its producer. See also #$extractedRelnWeight.")
(comment wellHasDepthsWithinLiner "<code>(#$wellHasDepthsWithinLiner WELL DEPTH)</code> means that <code>DEPTH</code> is a measured depth within the liner of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment bottomholeFlowingPressureOfWellOnDate "<code>(#$bottomholeFlowingPressureOfWellOnDate WELL DATE PRESS)</code> means that the #$Well <code>WELL</code> has a fluid flowing at #$Pressure <code>PRESS</code> in the vicinity of the #$Bottomhole on the date <code>DATE</code>.  I.e., <code>WELL</code> has a #$ProductionTubingAndBottomholeSystem <code>SYS</code> such that <code>(#$bottomholeFlowingPressure SYS PRESS)</code>.")
(comment objectHasPressureOnDate "<code>(#$objectHasPressureOnDate OBJ DATE PRESS)</code> means that the #$PartiallyTangible <code>OBJ</code> has a #$Pressure <code>PRESS</code> on the date <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment slotTypicallyDirectlyProportionalToSlotForType "(#$slotTypicallyDirectlyProportionalToSlotForType  COLL SLOT-1 SLOT-2) means that it is typically the case that the values for SLOT-1 (for instances of COLL) have a directly proportional relationship to the values for SLOT-2.  For example, as mass increases, weight increases, or as square footage increases, the house value increases.  This is meant to capture common sense cases of the relationships between slots, but allows exceptional situations to trump the relationship -- e.g. as the diameter of a hose increases, throughput increases -- except if there is some sort of blockage.")
(comment percentageYieldOfWaferFabrication "(#$percentageYieldOfWaferFabrication MANUFACTURING PERCENT) means that the percentage ratio of the number of integrated circuits (#$IntegratedCircuit) that are cut from the wafer (#$SemiconductorWafer) that is #$objectProcessed in MANUFACTURING and that are considered functional within acceptable performance margins to the overall number of integrated circuits cut from the wafer is given by PERCENT.")
(comment drainRegionResistanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$drainRegionResistanceOfTransistor   OBJ OHMS)</code> means that the drain region of OBJ, an FET, has the electrical resistance OHMS.")
(comment sourceRegionResistanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$sourceRegionResistanceOfTransistor   OBJ OHMS)</code> means that the source region of OBJ, an FET, has the electrical resistance OHMS.")
(comment gateRegionResistanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$gateRegionResistanceOfTransistor   OBJ OHMS)</code> means that the gate region of OBJ, an FET, has the electrical resistance OHMS.")
(comment bodyRegionResistanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$bodyRegionResistanceOfTransistor   OBJ OHMS)</code> means that the body region of OBJ, an FET, has the electrical resistance OHMS.")
(comment objectHasApplicableSheetResistance "<code>(#$objectHasApplicableSheetResistance OBJ OHMS)</code> means that the sheet resistance of OBJ, a sheet of some material in which a current passes through perpendicularly, has the electrical resistance OHMS.")
(comment objectHasPressure "(#$objectHasPressure OBJ PRESS) means that the #$PartiallyTangible <code>OBJ</code> exerts the Pressure <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment saturationSteamTemperatureOnDate "(#$saturationSteamTemperatureOnDate OBJ TEMP DATE) means TEMP is the saturation steam temperature at OBJ on DATE.")
(comment discreteMeterDepthsWithinLiner "<code>(#$discreteMeterDepthsWithinLiner WELL DEPTH)</code> means that <code>DEPTH</code> is a discrete meter interval within the liner of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment averageTemperatureAtLinerDepthsForTimeInterval "<code>(#$averageTemperatureAtLinerDepthsForTimeInterval WELL  DEPTH TEMP TIME-INTERVAL)</code> means that during <code>TIME-INTERVAL</code> the average temperature at the depth <code>DEPTH</code> in <code>WELL</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment averageTemperatureAtDepthForTimeInterval "<code>(#$averageTemperatureAtDepthForTimeInterval  OBJ DEPTH TEMP TIME-INTERVAL)</code> means that during <code>TIME-INTERVAL</code> the average temperature at the measured depth <code>DEPTH</code> in <code>OBJ</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment Compressor "The collection of all compressors. A type of #$PoweredDevice. Compressors are devices used to compress fluids.")
(comment ReciprocatingPump "A specialization of #$PositiveDisplacementPump.  Each instance of #$ReciprocatingPump is a pump that causes one or more cavities to be filled and emptied by the motion of a piston, plunger or diapragm.")
(comment RotaryPump "A specialization of #$PositiveDisplacementPump.  Each instance of #$RotaryPump  is a pup that causes a one or more cavities to be filled and emptied through the rotary motion of a gear or screw.")
(comment GearPump "A specialization of #$RotaryPump.  Each instance of #$GearPump is a pump that causes displacement by the motion of two or more impellers such as gears or cams.")
(comment CentrifugalPump "A specialization of #$Pump-Mechanical.  Centrifugal pumps cause fluid to move by rotating the blades of an impeller to cause a reduction of pressure at the entrance to the impeller.")
(comment thinFilmDepositionOnSurfaceOf "A specialization of #$objectActedOn and #$toLocation. Where DEPOSITION is a #$ThinFilmDeposition (#$thinFilmDepositionOnSurfaceOf DEPOSITION OBJECT) means that the #$ThinFilm that is the #$thinFilmDeposited in DEPOSITION is deposited on a surface of object.")
(comment specifiesArgumentTakesPointer "Where ARG-DEC is a #$FormalArgumentDeclaration, (#$specifiesArgumentTakesPointer ARG-DEC) means that ARG-DEC specifies that the #$argumentSpecified takes a value that should be interpreted as a pointer to another data address.")
(comment returnExpression "(#$returnExpression RETURN-STATMENT EXPRESSION) means that the #$ReturnStatement STATEMENT specifies that the value of the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION should be returned.")
(comment attribution-Uniprot "(#$attribution-Uniprot STATEMENT ATTRIB) states that according to Uniprot, ATTRIB gives attribution information that support STATEMENT.")
(comment arraySizeOfVariableResolvedBy "(#$arraySizeOfVariableResolvedBy VAR-DEC EXPRESSION) means that the variable declared in VAR-DEC is declared to be an array of a size given by the value of EXPRESSION.")
(comment CodePointerDeclaration "The collection of all #$VariableDeclarations that declare the expressions they introduce to be pointers.")
(comment energyOfIonImplantation "(#$energyOfIonImplantation IMPLANT ENERGY-QUANT) means that the #$EnergyQuantity ENERGY-QUANT quantifies the energy with which #$Ions directed in IMPLANT are implanted in the target layer or substrate.  Frequently measured in (#$Kilo #$ElectronVolt).")
(comment IonImplantationDosage "A #$UnitOfMeasureConcept and a specialization of #$RaditionDose.  Each #$IonImplantationDosage is a quantitative measure of number of ions per unit are used to characterize an #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation.")
(comment dosageOfIonImplantation "(#$dosageOfIonImplantation IMPLANT DOSAGE) means that the #$IonImplantationDosage DOSAGE characterizes the #$IonImplantation-WaferProcessingUnitOperation IMPLANT in terms of #$Ions implanted per unit area.  Frequently measured in (#$PerFn (#$UnitOfCountFn #$Ion) #$SquareCentimeter).")
(comment evidence-Uniprot "(#$evidence-Uniprot ATTRIBUTION EVIDENCE-TYPE) states that according to Uniprot, EVIDENCE-TYPE is the type of evidence provided by ATTRIBUTION.")
(comment eventSlotChange "(#$eventSlotChange EVT SLOT COMP) says that as a result of EVT, the corresponding change in SLOT to some object, OBJ, such that (#$decreasesSlotFor EVT OBJ SLOT) or (#$increasesSlotFor EVT OBJ SLOT) is COMP a numeric comparison predicate (typically #$lessThan, or #$greaterThan).")
(comment AntiTankArtilleryGun "Artillery for anti-tank operations.")
(comment HEATShell "A specialization of #$ProjectileShellAssembly and #$ExplosiveDevice.  Each instance of #$HEATShell is a projectile containing explosive material and is constructed to be effective in piercing the armor of tanks.")
(disjointWith IndirectAllocationFunction DirectAllocationFunction)
(comment ShallowTrenchIsolationSubProcessType-32NM "The collection of all sub-processes of the Shallow Trench Isolation stage of
32NM semiconductor wafer processing.")
(comment CarbonTetrachloride "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound.  Each instance of #$CarbonTetrachloride is a sample of the compound CCl4.")
(comment CarbonDisulfide "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound.  Each instance of #$CarbonDisulfide is a sample of the compound CS2.")
(comment sidewallCapacitanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$sidewallCapacitanceOfTransistor  OBJ
C)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> has sidewall capacitance
<code>C</code>.")
(comment AnimalHormone "A specialization of #$Hormone.  #$AnimalHormones are substances which play a role in inter-cell communication in #$Animals.")
(comment drainVoltageToSource "(#$gateVoltageToSource TRAN V) means that
the difference between the voltage at the drain and the source in TRAN is V.")
(comment oxideLayerCapacitanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$oxideLayerCapacitanceOfTransistor  OBJ C)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code>'s oxide layer has a  capacitance of <code>C</code>.")
(comment depletionLayerCapacitanceOfTransistor "<code>(#$depletionLayerCapacitanceOfTransistor  OBJ C)</code> means that
<code>OBJ</code>'s depletion layer that forms when the transistor is \"off\"
has a  capacitance of <code>C</code>.")
(comment unitOperationDuration "(#$unitOperationDuration UNIT-OP TIME-QUANT) means that the #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation UNIT-OP has a duration of TIME-QUANT.")
(comment unitOperationEntryTime "(#$unitOperationEntryTime UNIT-OP START-TIME) means that the entry time for the #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation UNIT-OP is given by START-TIME.")
(comment unitOperationExitTime "(#$unitOperationExitTime UNIT-OP END-TIME) means that the exit time for the #$ManufacturingProcessUnitOperation UNIT-OP is given by END-TIME.")
(comment objIndicationWRTRoleInType "<code>(#$objIndicationWRTRoleInType OBJ ROLE SIT-TYPE TV)</code> means that the evidence available in the current context supports judging <code>(relationExistsInstance ROLE SIT-TYPE OBJ)</code> as having the truth value <code>TV</code>.")
(comment objectDiffersFromPopulationOfTypeQualitatively "An instance of #$VariableArityPredicate used to describe the qualitative differences of an object against objects from a population of objects of that type, <code>(objectDiffersFromPopulationOfTypeQualitatively OBJ POP-TYPE QS NCP)</code> means that <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> differs from the other objects making up the population of type <code>POP-TYPE</code> in that its value of <code>QS</code> stands in the relation <code>NCP</code> to each other member's value of <code>QS</code>.  To specify a factor by which the values differ, one can add the optional fifth argument, constrained to be an instance of #$ScalarInterval.")
(comment typeChangesQuantityInDirection "<code>(#$typeChangesQuantityByFactor EVT-TYPE ROLE ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE QUANTITY-SLOT FACTOR)</code> means that during instances <code>I</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, where <code>(#$and (ROLE I PLAYER) (#$isa PLAYER ROLE-PLAYER-TYPE))</code>, the value of <code>?X</code> in <code>(QUANTITY-SLOT I ?X)</code> changes from a given value at the start of <code>I</code> to a value arrived at by multiplying <code>?X</code> by <code>FACTOR</code>.")
(comment CriticalTransistorSlot "A specialization of #$PhysicalAmountSlot.  
This collection is a collection of quantity slots that characterize important
physical and electrical properties of transistors")
(comment OffMode-Transistor "The collection of transistors (particularly
MOSFET) whose gate to source voltage is less than the threshold voltage of the
device.  The gate will be off and the only current passing to the drain region
will be subthreshold current.")
(comment SaturationMode-Transistor "The collection of transistors (particularlyMOSFET) whose gate to source voltage is more than the threshold voltage of the device and the difference between the gate source voltage and the threshold voltage is less than the drain to source voltage.  The gate will be on and a broad conductive channel formed.")
(comment LinearRegionMode-Transistor "The collection of transistors
(particularlyMOSFET) whose gate to source voltage is more than the threshold
voltage of the device but where the difference between the gate source voltage
and the threshold voltage is greater than or equal to the drain to source
voltage.  The gate will be on and the device is acting as a resistor controlled 
by the gate voltage relative to both drain and source voltages.")
(comment transistorOhmicModeCurrent "(#$transistorOhmicModeCurrent T I)
means that I is the current from source to drain while the transistor is in
linear region or ohmic mode averaged under two conditions: when Gate voltage =
supply voltage and drain voltage is supply voltage / 2  and when drain voltage
= supply voltage and gate voltage = supply voltage / 2.")
(comment transistorSaturationCurrent "(#$transistorSaturationCurrent T I)
means that I is the current from source to drain while the transistor is in
saturation mode and the voltage from gate to source = voltage from drain to
source = supply voltage.")
(comment transistorSubthresholdCurrent "(#$transistorSubthresholdCurrent T
I) means that I is the total subthreshold leakage current that is flowing while 
the transistor is in the off state and when (for normally off transistors) gate 
to source voltage = 0 and drain to source voltage = supply voltage.")
(comment transistorSupplyVoltage "(#$transistorSupplyVoltage T V)means that V is the voltage supplied to the transistor from elsewhere in the circuit.  Typcially a constant for a particular transistor technology.")
(comment transistorModeOfOperation "(#$transistorModeOfOperation TRAN MODE) 
means that the transistor TRAN is operating in MODE -- an instance of
#$TransistorTypeByMode.")
(comment pegMoreSpecificContents-CycL "<code>(#$pegMoreSpecificContents-CycL PEG CYCL)</code> means that <code>CYCL</code> is a CycL representation that is more specific than (part of) the content of the instance <code>PEG</code> of #$LinguisticExpressionPeg.")
(comment ratioGeneratingRule "(#$ratioGeneratingRule RULE QBF) means that in the context of the assumptions provided by QBF, a reified formula, rule should be used to general qualitative relationships between the associated quantity slots involved in the rule.")
(comment SaturationModeCurrent-Transistor "This reified formula expresses the relationship between the supply voltage, gate to source voltage, drain to source voltage, and the Ids when the transistor is in saturation mode and the gate and drain voltage are equal to the supply voltage")
(comment SubQuantityFromSlotFn "<code>(#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn SLOT)</code> denotes the collection of quantities that are the quantities measured by SLOT.  The resulting quantity type will be a subcollection of the #$arg2Isa of the quantity slot in arg1 of this function.  Note that although the results of this function are often extensionally equivalent to the #$arg2Isa quantity type of the slot, these collection are useful ways to distinguish collections of quantities based on intensional features such as the relationship used to attribute the quantity.  E.g. it is useful to distinguish the gate voltage (#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn #$gateVoltageToSource) from the drain voltage (#$SubQuantityFromSlotFn  drainVoltageToSource).")
(comment slotAttributesSubQuantity "<code>(#$slotAttributesSubQuantity SLOT SUB)</code> means that the quantities that SLOT attributes are instances of SUB.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$SubQuantityFromSlotFn.")
(comment slotTypicallyInverselyProportionalToSlotForType "(#$slotTypicallyInverselyProportionalToSlotForType COLL SLOT-1 SLOT-2) means
that it is typically the case that the values for SLOT-1 (for instances of
COLL) have an inversely proportional relationship to the values for SLOT-2. 
For example, as the weight of an automobile increases, its gas mileage
decreases.  See #$slotTypicallyDirectlyProportionalToSlotForType for the
directly proportional version of this predicate.")
(comment Kahlua "The collection of all Kahlua. A type of #$CoffeeLiqueur.")
(comment PrehensileTail "A specialization of #$Tail-BodyPart.  Each instance of #$PrehensileTail is a tail that can be controlled by the organism of which it is a part to hold onto other objects.")
(comment transistorOverdriveVoltage "(#$transistorOverdriveVoltage TRAN V) means that the difference between the gate to source voltage and the threshold voltage when the transitor is on saturation mode is V.")
(comment antoineEquationParametersForTypeAndPressureInterval "<code>(#$antoineEquationParametersForTypeAndPressureInterval SUBSTANCE-TYPE A-PARAM B-PARAM C-PARAM RANGE)</code> means that the parameters A, B and C, for the Antoine Equation for the substance <code>SUBSTANCE-TYPE</code> are the numbers <code>A-PARAM</code>, <code>B-PARAM</code>, and <code>C-PARAM</code>, respectively, for the pressure range <code>RANGE</code>.")
(comment temperatureInMEUnitOperation "A very general predicate for associating #$Temperatures with instances of #$UnitOperation-SemiconductorWaferProcessing.  (#$temperatureInMEUnitOperation OP TEMP) means that sometime during the execution of OP, TEMP was a measurable, relevant #$Temperature associated with one or more of the components in OP.")
(comment maxTemperatureOfUnitOperation "(#$maxTemperatureOfUnitOperation OP TEMP) means that TEMP is the maximum #$Temperature registered at the locus of operations in the course of OP.")
(comment maxTemperatureInUOThermalMod "A typed spec-pred of #$maxTemperatureOfUnitOperation.  Where THERMAL-MOD is a unit operation thermal modification - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn #$ThermalModificationProcess-SingleWafer) -, (#$maxTemperatureInUOThermalMod THERMAL-MOD MAX-TEMP) means that MAX-TEMP is the highest temperature registered in the annealing chamber or furnace during the course of THERMAL-MOD.  Usually measured in #$DegreeCelsius.")
(comment maxTemperatureInMEUODeposition "A typed spec-pred of #$maxTemperatureOfUnitOperation.  Where DEP is a thin film deposition unit operation in the semiconductor industry - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn #$ThinFilmDeposition-SemiconductorManufacture) - (#$maxTemperatureInMEUODeposition DEP MAX-TEMP) means that MAX-TEMP is the maximum temperature registered for the deposition substance (#$thinFilmDeposited) during the course of DEP. Usually measured in #$DegreeCelsius.")
(comment criticalDimensionOfUORemoval "Where REMOVAL is a unit operation consisting in a removal process - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn RemovalProcess-SingleWafer) - (#$criticalDimensionOfUORemoval REMOVAL CD) means that CD is the critical dimension that figures in REMOVAl.  Usually measured in #$Angstroms or (#$Nano #$Meter)s.")
(comment depthOfUORemoval "Where REMOVAL is a unit operation consisting in a removal process - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn RemovalProcess-SingleWafer) - (#$depthOfUORemoval REMOVAL DEPTH) means that REMOVAL is carried out to a depth of DEPTH in the affected area.  Usually measured in #$Angstroms or (#$Nano #$Meter)s.")
(comment criticalDimensionOfUOEtch "Where ETCH is a unit operation consisting in a wafer etch - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer) - (#$criticalDimensionOfUOEtch ETCH CD) means that CD is the critical dimension associated with ETCH.  Usually measured in #$Angstroms or (#$Nano #$Meter)s.")
(comment depthOfUOEtch "Where ETCH is a unit operation consisting in a wafer etch - see (#$UnitOperationsOfTypeFn WaferEtchingProcess-SingleWafer) - (#$depthOfUOEtch ETCH DEPTH) means that ETCH is carried out to a depth of DEPTH in the material being etched.  Usually measured in #$Angstroms or (#$Nano #$Meter)s.")
(disjointWith Stampede CoordinatedGroupActivity)
(comment OpenGate-Transistor "The collection of all transistor gates whose state is \"open\" meaning current is not able to pass.")
(comment ClosedGate-Transistor "The collection of all transistor gates whose state is \"closed\" meaning current is able to pass.")
(comment WetRemovalProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer in which the #$stuffUsed to effect the removal is an instance of #$LiquidTangibleThing.")
(disjointWith WetRemovalProcess-SingleWafer DryRemovalProcess-SingleWafer)
(comment DryRemovalProcess-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer in which the #$stuffUsed to effect the removal is an instance of #$GaseousTangibleThing.")
(comment ChemicalCleaning-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer wherein some contaminant is partially or completely removed from a wafer by chemical means in the course of a #$MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer.")
(comment WetChemicalCleaning-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalCleaning-SingleWafer where liquid means are used to remove contamination from a #$SemiconductorWafer in the course of a #$MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer.  See #$WetRemovalProcess-SingleWafer.")
(comment DryChemicalCleaning-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalCleaning-SingleWafer where gaseous means are used to remove contamination from a #$SemiconductorWafer in the course of a #$MEWaferFabrication-SingleWafer.  See #$WetRemovalProcess-SingleWafer.")
(comment relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl "(#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl  COLL QUANT-PRED-1 COMP-PRED-1 QUANT-PRED-2 COMP-PRED-2 THING) means that instances of COLL whose values for QUANT-PRED-1 are COMP-PRED-1 (more, less, etc.) than those values for other instances of COLL are associated with correspondingly COMP-PRED-2 (more, less, etc.) values for QUANT-PRED-2 relative to THING.  THING is often a collection of slots that must remain constant for the relationship to hold (Note these slots may be filled by the same or a different object).  For example, a rectangle with a greater length than another rectangle has a greater area all other things being equal (#$relationBetweenQuantitySlotsForColl  #$Rectangle #$lengthOfObject #$greaterThan #$areaOfObject #$greaterThan (#$TheCollection #$lengthOfObject #$areaOfObject #$heightOfObject))")
(comment TransconductanceOfTransistor-QBF "This reified formula expresses the relationship between the transconductance of a transistor, the gate to source voltage, source to drain current, and the threshold voltage.")
(comment FlashMobScript "A specialization of #$CoordinatedGroupActivity.  Each instance of #$FlashMobScript is a three-stage event in which members of the group (the prospective #$FlashMob) slowly and inconspicuously occupy a public area, mixing with other, unsuspecting occupants of that area (see #$FlashMobSetup); then, at a prearranged time or in response to a signal, break out into a scripted routine, such as a choreographed dance or some other activity unusual for a public area (see #$FlashMobPerformance); then, at the conclusion of the routine, dissipate into the crowd (see #$FlashMobDispersal).")
(comment FlashMobPerformance "A specialization of #$ChoreographedGroupActivity.  Each instance of #$FlashMobPerformance is a a spontaneous-looking (to the audience) performance of a scripted routine by a #$FlashMob -- a group of individuals who inconspicuously gather in a public area, mixing with other, unsuspecting occupants of that area (see #$FlashMobSetup); then, at a prearranged time or in response to a signal, break out into the performance.")
(comment FlashMobSetup "A specialization of #$CoordinatedGroupActivity, #$FlashMobSetup is the first step in the #$FlashMobScript, immediately prior to a #$FlashMobPerformance.  During a #$FlashMobSetup, the individuals involved gather inconspicuously in a public area, mixing with other, unsuspecting occupants of that area, so as to maximize the surprise factor when the performance begins.")
(comment BioPAXLevel3Ontology "An instance of #$Ontology.  The BioPAX Level 3 Ontology is an open-source, collaboratively-developed language for describing metabolic pathways, signaling pathways, gene regulatory networks, molecular interactions and genetic interactions.  ")
(comment BiochemicalPathway "This is the collection of biochemical pathways. A biochemical pathway is a series of chemical reactions in which one or more of the outputs of one reaction are one of the inputs to the next reaction. Examples include #$MetabolicPathways such as #$Glycolysis, in which glucose is converted to pyruvate releasing energy that can be used to fuel other cell processes, and signal transduction (see #$SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-MultiStageReaction) pathways, in which a biochemical signal is converted into a cellular response.")
(comment regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtXValue "<code>(#$regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtXValue SET1 SET2 INTERVAL)</code>
means that the lines determined by linear regression on <code>SET1</code> and
<code>SET2</code> intersect at a point whose \"x\" value is
<code>INTERVAL</code>.")
(comment regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtYValue "<code>(#$regressionLinesForSetsIntersectAtYValue SET1 SET2 INTERVAL)</code>
means that the lines determined by linear regression on <code>SET1</code> and
<code>SET2</code> intersect at a point whose \"y\" value is
<code>INTERVAL</code>.")
(comment Polishing-SingleWafer "The collection of all instances of #$RemovalProcess-SingleWafer where the wafer is mechanically polished to remove impurities.")
(comment nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement "(#$nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement BLOCK
SUB-BLOCK N) means that, first, SUB-BLOCK is contained in BLOCK and there is no 
other #$ComputerCodeStatement such that BLOCK contains it and it contains
SUB-BLOCK 
(i.e., (#$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement SUB-BLOCK BLOCK)), and second,
that
there are exactly N #$ComputerCodeStatement that have BLOCK as the
#$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement, and that precede SUB-BLOCK within BLOCK. 
Intuitively, SUB-BLOCK is the Nth 'top-level' #$ComputerCodeStatement appearing 
in
BLOCK.")
(comment focalProteinMoleculeRegulated "Where REGULATION is an #$ProteinMoleculeActivityRegulationEvent, (#$focalProteinMoleculeRegulated REGULATION MOL) means that MOL is the #$ProteinMolecule whose cabability to act in its typical role is altered in REGULATION.")
(comment ProteinMoleculeActivityRegulationEvent "Instances are #$ChemicalInteractions in which, by virtue of being bound to or unbound from some other #$ChemicalObject, an #$ProteinMolecule has its 'activity' altered.  By 'activity', we mean the ability of the molecule to act in the typical kinds of #$ChemicalReactions it normally participates in.  These might include catalyzing certain reactions, activating some other protein, or, in the case of ion channels, opening or closing to change the flow of ions across a membrane.")
(comment AllostericProteinMoleculeRegulation "Instances are #$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is altered by a regulatory molecule that binds to a site OTHER than the protein molecule's normal active site.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to bind to a target molecule at its active site, thereby causing a change in that target molecule - by catalyzing a chemical reaction, or activating it for some other purpose.")
(comment NonallostericProteinMoleculeRegulation "Instances are
#$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is altered by
a regulatory molecule that binds to the protein molecule's
normal active site.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to
bind to a target molecule at its active site, thereby causing a change in that
target molecule - by catalyzing a chemical reaction, or activating it for some
other purpose.")
(disjointWith AllostericProteinMoleculeRegulation NonallostericProteinMoleculeRegulation)
(comment AllostericProteinMoleculeInhibition "Instances are
#$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is reduced by
a regulatory molecule that binds to a site OTHER than the protein molecule's
normal active site.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to
bind to a target molecule at its active site, thereby causing a change in that
target molecule - by catalyzing a chemical reaction, or activating it for some
other purpose.")
(comment AllostericProteinMoleculeActivation "Instances are
#$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is increased by
a regulatory molecule that binds to a site OTHER than the protein molecule's
normal active site.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to
bind to a target molecule at its active site, thereby causing a change in that
target molecule - by catalyzing a chemical reaction, or activating it for some
other purpose.")
(disjointWith AllostericProteinMoleculeInhibition AllostericProteinMoleculeActivation)
(disjointWith NonallostericProteinMoleculeInhibition NonallostericProteinMoleculeActivation)
(comment NonallostericProteinMoleculeActivation "Instances
are #$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is
increased by means other than #$AllostericProteinMoleculeActivation.")
(disjointWith AllostericProteinMoleculeActivation NonallostericProteinMoleculeActivation)
(comment NonallostericProteinMoleculeInhibition "Instances
are#$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is reduced
by means other than #$AllostericProteinMoleculeInhibition.")
(disjointWith AllostericProteinMoleculeInhibition NonallostericProteinMoleculeInhibition)
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition "Instances are #$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is reduced.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to catalyze a reaction, receive a chemical signal, activate some other protein, pass ions (in the case of an ion channel), etc.\"")
(comment ProteinMoleculeActivation "Instances are #$ChemicalInteractions in which a #$ProteinMolecule's 'activity' is increased.  By 'activity', we mean the protein molecule's ability to catalyze a reaction, receive a chemical signal, activate some other protein, pass ions (in the case of an ion channel), etc.\"")
(disjointWith ProteinMoleculeActivation ProteinMoleculeInhibition)
(comment CPUMemoryRegister "A collection of specialized units associated
with instances of #$ComputerMemory-Abstract.  Each #$CPUMemoryRegister is a
specialized
memory cell that is part of a #$CentralProcessingUnit, which can be read from
and written to faster than the main memory area.  There are typically between
one and two hundred registers depending on the CPU type.")
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Irreversible "A subcollection of #$ProteinMoleculeInhibition, each instance of which permanently blocks the activity of the affected molecule.  Irreversible inihibition often, but not always, occurs via covalent modification of the protein molecule's structure.\"")
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Reversible "A subcollection of #$ProteinMoleculeInhibition, each instance of which permanently blocks the activity of the affected molecule.  Irreversible inihibition often, but not always, occurs via covalent modification of the protein molecule's structure.")
(disjointWith ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Reversible ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Irreversible)
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Competitive "A subcollection of #$ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Reversible, instances of which have the property that the regulatory molecule and the normal target molecule or substrate of the protein cannot bind to the protein at the same time, because they bind to the same location.  This type of inhibition is so named because the regulatory molecule and the target molecule 'compete' for the same binding site.")
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Uncompetitive "A subcollection of #$ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Reversible, instances of which have the property that the regulatory molecule only binds to the protein/substrate complex, not to affected molecule by itself.  With the inhibitor bound to the protein/substrate complex, the normal action of the protein (catalyzing a reaction, activating the substrate, etc.) can't proceed.")
(comment ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Noncompetitive "A subcollection of #$ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Reversible, instances of which have the property that the inhibiting regulatory molecule may bind to the unbound protein molecule, or to the protein/substrate complex.  With the inhibitor bound, the normal action of the protein (catalyzing a reaction, activating the substrate, etc.) can't proceed.")
(disjointWith ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Uncompetitive ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Noncompetitive)
(disjointWith ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Uncompetitive ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Competitive)
(disjointWith ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Competitive ProteinMoleculeInhibition-Noncompetitive)
(comment regulatoryChemicalObject "Where REG is
a #$ProteinMoleculeActivityRegulationEvent, (#$regulatoryChemicalObject REG
OBJ) states that OBJ plays a regulatory role in REG. It does so by binding with
the focal protein molecule (see #$focalProteinMoleculeRegulated) and increasing 
or decreasing its activity - i.e., its ability to bind to a substrate and
activate it, catalyze a reaction, or otherwise do what the focal protein
typically does.")
(comment CPUMemoryRegisterType "A #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance is a class of #$CPUMemoryRegisters characterized by a common programming designation.")
(comment EAXRegister "The collection of all EAX registers.")
(comment statementLoadsTheRegisterOfType "Where STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement, (#$statementLoadsTheRegisterOfType STATEMENT REGISTER-TYPE) means that STATEMENT is a specification such that any #$ProgramAction that executes it in a 'normal' run-time environment will write to the unique #$CPUMemoryRegister of type REG-TYPE on the physical machine implementing the program.")
(comment statementOverwritesTheRegisterOfType "(#$statementOverwritesTheRegisterOfType STATEMENT REG-TYPE) means that when STATEMENT is executed in a normal runtime environment, the #$ProgramAction which executes it will write a result to the unique #$CPUMemoryRegister of type REG-TYPE in the operating platform executing the program of which STATEMENT is a part, where this register already holds some previous value inserted there as a result of executing a prior statement (a statement on which STATEMENT depends) in the program:  as a result of the new write operation, the previous value stored in the register will be lost.")
(comment functionCallReturnsInTheRegisterOfType "(#$functionCallReturnsInTheRegisterOfType FN-CALL REG-TYPE) means that when
the function call (#$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) FN-CALL is
executed in a 'normal' run-time environment, the result will be written to the
unique register of type REG-TYPE in the physical platform implementing the
program in which FN-CALL appears.")
(comment expressionHolderOfValueReturnedByFunctionCallIn "(#$expressionHolderOfValueReturnedByFunctionCallIn EXPRESSION FN-CALL STATEMENT) means that within a scope given by STATEMENT, the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION is interpreted as a pointer to whatever value is returned by FN-CALL.")
(comment expressionSoleHolderOfValueReturnedByFunctionCallIn "(#$expressionHolderOfValueReturnedByFunctionCallIn EXPRESSION FN-CALL STATEMENT) means that within a scope given by STATEMENT, the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION is interpreted as a pointer to whatever value is returned by FN-CALL.")
(comment expressionAssignedValue "(#$expressionAssignedValue STATEMENT EXPRESSION) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement STATEMENT assigns a value to the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION.")
(comment transconductanceOfTransistorAtPointOnCurve "<code>(#$transconductanceOfTransistorAtPointOnCurve TRANS SIEMENS)</code> means that the transistor <code>OBJ</code> has <code>SIEMENS</code> of transconductance at a given drain current and gate to source voltage that define a point on the operating curve in the \"on\" region.  For DC field effect transistors, this is the ratio of 2 x drain current at that bias point over the difference between the gate voltage and the threshold voltage (effective or overdrive voltage).")
(comment GroupMarching "The collection of events in which a group of people march together.")
(comment Sterol "A specialization of #$Steroid.  Sterols are also known as \"steroid alcohols\". They are a subgroup of steroids with a hydroxyl group at the 3-position of the A-ring.")
(comment Phytosterol "A specialization of #$Sterol.  Each instance of #$Phytosterol is a sterol produced by a plant.")
(comment Zoosterol "A specialization of #$Sterol.  Each instance of #$Zoosterol is a sterol produced by an animal.")
(comment Cholesterol "The collection of all cholesterol. A type of #$Sterol.")
(comment DrugTargetType "A type level collection. Each instance is a type of molecule, usually a protein molecule type, targeted by some drug.")
(disjointWith FreeingAVehicleStuckOnAPatchOfIce FreeingAVehicleStuckInMud)
(disjointWith SurfaceConstrainedRotation TireSpinningInPlace)
(disjointWith PrecipitationParticle PatchOfIce)
(comment FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle "The collection of events in which a stuck or otherwise confined vehicle is freed from its confinement, usually by pushing, pulling, or careful maneuvering.")
(comment FreeingAStuckVehicleByTowing "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle that accomplishes the \"liberation\" of the vehicle by towing it until it is in a place where it can act again as a #$vehicle.")
(comment FreeingAStuckVehicleByPushing "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle that accomplishes the \"liberation\" of the vehicle by having people push it until it is in a place where it can act again as a #$vehicle.")
(comment FreeingAVehicleFromATractionlessSurface "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle in which the vehicle that is the #$objectFreed starts out as stuck (rather than confined) by virtue of being on or partially in a substance (e.g., mud, snow, ice) that prevents it from gaining sufficient traction to move away from its location.")
(comment FreeingAStuckOrConfinedAnimal "The collection of events in which a stuck or otherwise confined animal is freed from its confinement.")
(comment FreeingAStuckOrConfinedObject "A collection of events in which an object that is stuck or in some way trapped in close confinement is freed or removed.")
(comment objectFreed "(#$objectFreed FREEING OBJ) means OBJ is removed or able to be maneuvered from its previouslocation where it had been stuck or confined.")
(comment FacingObstacles "The collection of situations in which some agent is confronted with obstacles that impede that agent's goals.")
(comment FreeingAWatercraftStuckOnASandBar "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle in which a watercraft is freed from a #$Bar-Topographical.")
(comment FreeingAVehicleStuckInSnow "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle in which a vehicle is freed from a large area of snow.")
(comment SnowBank "The collection of snow banks.")
(comment FreeingAVehicleStuckOnAPatchOfIce "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle in which a vehicle is pushed or pulled from a patch of ice that prevented it from gaining sufficient traction to move.")
(comment FreeingAVehicleStuckInMud "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle in which a vehicle is pushed or pulled from some mud that prevented it from gaining sufficient traction to move.")
(comment StuckOrConfinedAnimalSituation "The collection of situations in which an animal is stuck or confined in some way that prevents it from making any significant translational motion.")
(comment StuckOrConfinedSituation "A specialization of #$Configuration.  Instances of this collection are situations in which objects are configured in such a way that one or more of the objects is considered \"stuck\" or, if otherwise capable of translational motion, hindered.")
(disjointWith StuckOrConfinedVehicleSituation StuckOrConfinedAnimalSituation)
(comment StuckOrConfinedVehicleSituation "The collection of situations in which a vehicle is stuck or confined in some way that prevents it from making any significant translational motion.")
(comment PatchOfIce "The collection of all patches of ice -- layers of ice on some surface.")
(comment FreeingAStuckAutomobileByTowing "The specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle that accomplishes the \"liberation\" of an instance of #$Automobile by towing it until it is in a place where it can act again as a #$vehicle.")
(comment TireSpinningInPlace "The collection of instances of #$TireRotation in which the tire spins with no surface pressure that would allow it to roll along a surface.")
(comment TireRotation "The collection of events in which a tire rotates along an axis.")
(comment ManueveringAVehicleFromAConfinedSpace "A specialization of #$FreeingAStuckOrConfinedVehicle, in which a vehicle is freed from a hindering configuration of objects by slow and careful maneuvering of the vehicle by the driver.")
(comment StatementWithCodeHawkDesignationFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for reifying and representing instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement based on their designations in codehawk output renderings.  Where BLOCK-NAME is a character string used in CodeHawk to designate a given program section, (#$StatementWithCodeHawkDesignationFn BLOCK-NAME) denotes the section so designated.")
(comment codehawkDesignationOfStatementInProgram "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$StatementWithCodeHawkDesignationFn.  (#$codehawkDesignationOfStatementInProgram PROGRAM STRING STATEMENT) means that STATEMENT is the #$ComputerCodeStatement with the designation STRING in the CodeHawk output representation of PROGRAM.")
(comment candidateLocationTypeReferencedByExpression "(#$candidateLocationTypeReferencedByExpression EXPRESSION MEM-TYPE STATEMENT) means that, within the scope of STATEMENT, it is possible/feasible that the value of EXPRESSION functions as a pointer to an address in whatever is the local instantiation of #$ComputerMemoryType MEM-TYPE for the execution of the program (#$ComputerProgram-CWIS) in which STATEMENT occurs.")
(comment pointerOffsetFromCandidateLocationInStack "(#$pointerOffsetFromCandidateLocationInStack EXPRESSION N STATEMENT) means that, within the scope of STATEMENT, it is possible/feasible that the value of EXPRESSION is computed in such a way that EXPRESSION serves as a pointer to a location with some nonzero offset from position N in the local instantiation of #$StackBasedMemory-Entire for the #$ComputerProcessRunning that executes the program in which STATEMENT occurs.")
(comment determinesExpressionValueViaInput "(#$determinesExpressionValueViaInput STATEMENT INPUT OUTPUT) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement STATEMENT determines the value of OUTPUT using the value that the expression INPUT has within the scope of STATEMENT.")
(comment candidatePointerReference "(#$candidatePointerReference EXPRESSION N STATEMENT) means that, within the scope of STATEMENT, EXPRESSION could be a pointer with a value of N.")
(comment expressionCompared "(#$expressionCompared CHECK EXP) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK directs that the value of EXP should be quantitatively compared to some specified value (the #$valueComparedAgainst).")
(comment valueComparedAgainst "(#$valueComparedAgainst CHECK VALUE) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK directs that the value of a #$ComputerCodeExpression (the #$expressionCompared) should be compared to VALUE.")
(comment relationCompared-ExpressionToValue "(#$relationCompared-ExpressionToValue CHECK COMPARISON-RELN) means that the #$CodingCheckSpecification CHECK specifies that a check should be made to see if a certain expression (the #$expressionCompared) has the numeric comparison relation COMPARISON-RELN to a certain value (the #$valueComparedAgainst).")
(comment BoneMorphogeneticProtein "A family of protein molecules which are classified as #$Cytokines and #$GrowthFactors.   Subcollections of this group have instances which play a variety of important roles in the early development of mammalian embryos, regulating the development of bone, cartilage, kidneys, and other tissues, and continuing to be important in adults.")
(comment TransformingGrowthFactorBetaSuperfamily "A large family of protein molecules which are similar in structure.  They are regulatory proteins and are classified as #$Cytokines.")
(comment RUNX2-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''runt-related transcription factor 2''.")
(comment RuntRelatedTranscriptionFactor2 "A type of #$TranscriptionFactorEnzyme molecule whose instances play an important role in the development of #$Osteoblasts and in the activation of genes which control #$BoneMineralization.")
(comment ImmatureOsteoblast "The collection of all #$Cells which are in a cell line committed to differentiating into #$Osteoblasts.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAfter "(#$closestEventOfTypeAfter  EVT1 EVT2 TYPE) means that EVT1 is the nearest event of TYPE after EVT2.  In medical contexts it is assumed that both events involve the same patient.")
(comment SerineProtease "A specialization of #$Protease.  Each instance of #$SerineProtease is protease in which one of the amino acids in the active site of the enzyme is #$Serine.")
(comment Chymotrypsin "A specialization of #$SerineProtease and a kind of digestive enzyme.")
(comment Trypsin "A specialization of #$SerineProtease and a kind of digestive enzyme.")
(comment Elastase "A specialization of #$SerineProtease and a kind of digestive enzyme.")
(comment Subtilisin "A specialization of #$SerineProtease and a kind of digestive enzyme.")
(comment ThreonineProtease "A specialization of #$Protease.  Each instance of #$ThreonineProtease is protease with a threonine residue in the active site.")
(comment CysteineProtease "A specialization of #$Protease.  Each instance of #$CysteineProtease is protease with cysteine residue at the active site.")
(comment Actinidain "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Papain "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Bromelain "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Ficain "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Caspase "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.  Caspases play significant roles in apoptosis.")
(comment Caspase1 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase2 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase3 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase4 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase5 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase6 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase7 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase8 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase9 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase10 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase12 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase13 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Caspase14 "A specialization of #$Caspase.")
(comment Calpain "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Cathepsin "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment Separase "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease. Separase triggers the onset of #$Anaphase.")
(comment Autophagin "A specialization of #$CysteineProtease.")
(comment AspartateProtease "A specialization of #$Protease.  Each instance of #$AspartateProtease is protease with aspartate residue at the active site.")
(comment Pepsin "A specialization of #$AspartateProtease. Pepsin is a kind of digestive enzyme.")
(comment Chymosin "A specialization of #$AspartateProtease.")
(comment Nepenthesin "A specialization of #$AspartateProtease.")
(comment dielectricConstantOfStuffType "<code>(#$dielectricConstantOfStuffType STUFF-TYPE K)</code> means that instances of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> have this <code>K</code> of relative permittivity.  Because it is a ratio of capacitances, the actual constant is a dimensionless number.")
(comment objectHasApplicableDielectricConstant "<code>(#$objectHasApplicableDielectricConstant OBJ K) means that object is composed of STUFF-TYPE to some percent (#$constituentPercentByMass) and (#$dielectricConstantOfStuffType STUFF-TYPE K*)</code> holds where K is some function of K*, the percentage of STUFF-TYPE in OBJ and the other constituents of OBJ.")
(comment objectHasApplicableBulkResistivity "<code>(#$objectHasApplicableBulkResistivity OBJ OHMS-M) means that object is composed of STUFF-TYPE to some percentage (#$constituentPercentByMass) and (#$bulkResistivityOfStuffType STUFF-TYPE OHMS-M*)</code> holds where OHMS-M is some function of OHMS-M*, the percentage of STUFF-TYPE in OBJ, and the remaining constituents in OBJ.")
(comment ArbitraryCodeExecution "The collection of all #$UndesirableProgramActions wherein an input by an unauthorized user manipulates a #$ComputerProcessRunning that is executing a program into executing arbitrary code at the privilege level of the program.")
(comment typeRepressesTranscriptionOfType "(#$typeRepressesTranscriptionOfType FACTOR-TYPE GIS-TYPE) means that instances of the transcription factor, FACTOR-TYPE, can suppress the transcription of GIS-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ChangingDeviceState Grooming)
(disjointWith MakingWrittenMaterial Grooming)
(disjointWith StrictlyMentalEvent Grooming)
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure Grooming)
(disjointWith PerformanceTesting Grooming)
(disjointWith Manufacturing Grooming)
(disjointWith PersonalGrooming GroomingAnother)
(comment HumansGroomingANonHumanAnimal "The collection of instances of #$GroomingAnother in which the performer is a human and the beneficiary is an instance of #$NonHumanAnimal.")
(disjointWith HumansGroomingALargeNonHumanAnimal HumansGroomingASmallNonHumanAnimal)
(comment HumansGroomingASmallNonHumanAnimal "The collection of instances of #$HumansGroomingANonHumanAnimal in which the beneficiary is a small animal, such as a duck, cat, or dog.")
(comment HumansGroomingALargeNonHumanAnimal "The collection of instances of #$GroomingAnother in which the beneficiary is a large animal, such as a horse, camel, or elephant.")
(comment PetSalon "A localized (one site) commercial organization that performs #$Grooming for pets.")
(comment DeviceForCuttingHair "The collection of devices designed for cutting hair.")
(comment BathingOneself "The collection of #$Bathing events in which the bather bathes him or herself.")
(comment Grooming "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction, this is the collection of events in which an animal cleans or improves the hygiene or appearance of an animal (which may or may not be itself).")
(comment GroomingAnother "The specialization of #$Grooming in which one animal grooms another.")
(comment taskAssociatedWith-SharedScripts "A reflexive specialization of #$taskAssociatedWith, <code>(#$taskAssociatedWith-SharedScripts TASK-A TASK-B)</code> means that instances of <code>TASK-A</code> are frequently associated with instances of <code>TASK-B</code> due to both being instantiated as part of some third event.")
(comment ResistanceOfAConductor-UsingSheetResistDCFormula "The formula to determine resistance in Ohms of a conductor (for DC) using sheet resistance and width of the conductor -- instead of bulk resistance and cross-section area.  The formula is R = Rs(L/W) where R = resistance in Ohms, Rs = the sheet resistivity of the object given a particular thickness measured in Ohms, L = the length of the conductor in meters, and W = the width of the conductor in meters.")
(disjointWith ApplyingSomethingToSurface PlacingSomethingOnARaisedSurface)
(comment PlacingSomethingOnARaisedSurface "A collection of events.  In each #$ApplyingSomethingToSurface event, something is placed atop an object sufficient to support it, typically to make it easier for the performer to handle or inspect it.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAtLocationBeforeDate "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypeAtLocationBeforeDate EVT LOCATION TYPE DATE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> before <code>DATE</code> that occurs at <code>LOCATION</code>.")
(comment closestEventOfTypeAtLocationAfterDate "<code>(#$closestEventOfTypeAtLocationAfterDate EVT LOCATION TYPE DATE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the nearest event of <code>TYPE</code> after <code>DATE</code> that occurs at <code>LOCATION</code>.")
(comment RooftopJumping "The collection of events in which some animal jumps from one rooftop to another.")
(comment silkNAF "A unary #$KBDependentRelation (q.v.) that takes instances of #$CycLSentence as arguments.  <code>(#$silkNAF SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is not currently \"known\" by the Cyc system to be true.  More precisely, the inference engine cannot prove <code>SENTENCE</code> using all possible inference capabilities and the current state of the knowledge base.  This predicate corresponds to the \"naf\" operator in the SILK langage. <code>SENTENCE</code> might actually be known to be false, or its truth-value might be simply unknown in the present sense.  <p>Note that, as a KB dependent relation, #$silkNAF is #$notAssertible (q.v.).")
(comment Metalloprotease "A specialization of #$Protease.  Each instance of #$Metalloprotease is protease whose catalytic mechanism involves a metal.")
(comment Hypercholesterolemia "A specialization of #$Dyslipidemia.  #$Hypercholesterolemia involves abnormally high quantities of cholesterol in the bloodstream.")
(comment rHsOfFormulasHasOperatorAtDepth "(#$rHsOfFormulasHasOperatorAtDepth QBF RHS LHS OPERATOR DEPTH DEPTH-ARG DEPTH-ARG-NUM) means that the quantity based formula QBF has the RHS and LHS associated with its #$equationFormFor (either a directly asserted formula or a permutation -- #$equationPermutations).  Furthermore, the RHS has OPERATOR at DEPTH and DEPTH-ARG is one of the non-operator arguments at that depth in DEPTH-ARG-NUM place.  DEPTH is represented as an integer.  A DEPTH of 1 means that the argument and associated operator are direct arguments of the RHS.  A DEPTH of 2 means that that OPERATOR and DEPTH-ARG are arguments to an argument of the RHS.  Note that by convention the LHS is always a single depth term.")
(comment Cercopithecidae "A specialization of #$Monkey.  The Cercopithecidae are the \"old world monkeys\", native to Africa and Asia.")
(comment BinaryBackEndForCHIBLProgramFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for referring to certain programs.  Where CHIBL-PROG is a #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS, (#$BinaryBackEndForCHIBLProgramFn #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS) denotes the binary program from which CHIBL-PROG was generated.")
(comment cHIBLGeneratedFrom "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of BinaryBackEndForCHIBLProgramFn. Where CHIBL-PROG is a #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS,(#$cHIBLGeneratedFrom CHIBL-PROG BIN-PROG) means that BIN-PROG is the binary program from which CHIBL-PROG was generated.")
(comment CompilingAComputerProgram "The collection of all computational processes devoted to compiling one #$ComputerProgram-CWIS (the #$sourceCompiled) into another (the #$outputCompiledTo) by means of a #$Compiler (the #$compilerUsed).")
(comment sourceCompiled "(#$sourceCompiled COMPILING SOURCE-PROG) means that SOURCE-PROG is the source program (#$ComputerProgram-CWIS) which is compiled into a new specification by COMPILING.")
(comment outputCompiledTo "(#$outputCompiledTo COMPILING OUTPUT-PROG) means that OUTPUT-PROG is the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS whose syntax informs the output of COMPILING (in the vernacular, the program that 'results' from carrying through COMPILING.")
(comment compilationFlag "A ternary predicate used for tracking compilation settings. Where OP-TYPE is a kind of #$ComputerProcessRunning, (#$compilationFlag COMPILING OP-TYPE TV) means that operations of type OP-TYPE are explicitly allowed or disallowed in COMPILING depending on the value of TV.  I.e., (#$compilationFlag COMPILING OP-TYPE #$True) means that actions of type OP-TYPE are explicitly allowed in COMPILING while (#$compilationFlag COMPILING OP-TYPE #$False) means that actions of type OP-TYPE are explicitly disallowed in COMPILING.")
(comment compilationAttRelevantForProgram "(#$compilationAttRelevantForProgram OP-TYPE PROGRAM) means that having instances of OP-TYPE explicitly enabled or disabled in the #$CompilingAComputerProgram that produced the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS PROGRAM is a necessary condition and partial explanation for the fact that PROGRAM has the form that it does")
(comment compilationAttSettingForProgram "(#$compilationAttSettingForProgram OP-TYPE TV PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM is the result of a compilation process wherein instances of OP-TYPE were/are explicitly enabled or disabled, depending on the value of TV.  I.e.,  (#$compilationAttSettingForBinaryProgram OP-TYPE #$True PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM results from a compilation process wherein instances of OP-TYPE are explicitly enabled, and (#$compilationAttSettingForBinaryProgram OP-TYPE #$False PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM results from a compilation process whereing instances of OP-TYPE are explicitly disabled.")
(comment compilerUsed "(#$compilerUsed COMPILING COMPILER) means that COMPILER is the #$Compiler used to execute the #$CompilingAComputerProgram instance COMPILING.")
(comment Cytokinesis-MeiosisI "The fourth stage #$FirstMeioticCellDivision.")
(comment GoldCoin "A specialization of #$Coin-Currency.  Each instance of #$GoldCoin is a coin made of gold.")
(comment SilverCoin "A specialization of #$Coin-Currency.  Each instance of #$SilverCoin is a coin made of silver.")
(comment OptimizationOfCode "The process of modifying a program during compilation to make some aspect of it work more efficiently or use fewer resources, to the extent the compiler can predict.")
(comment compilerOptimizes "(#$compilerOptimizes OPTIMIZATION COMPILER) means the COMPILER is the #$Compiler used in the #$OptimizationOfCode OPTIMIZATION.")
(comment CompilerCodeTemplate "Each instance is an abstract #$SoftwareObject which completely specifies the compilation settings to be used in one or more instances of #$CompilingAComputerProgram; i.e., each instance specifies which #$CompilationStageTypes are allowed and which are disallowed for a putative #$CompilingAComputerProgram instance.")
(comment compilationTemplate "(#$compilationTemplate COMPILING TEMPLATE) means that TEMPLATE is the #$CompilerCodeTemplate used in the #$CompilingAComputerProgram COMPILING")
(comment compilerTemplateEnables "(#$compilerTemplateEnables TEMPLATE STAGE-TYPE) means that TEMPLATE specifies that operations of type (#$CompilationStageType) STAGE-TYPE be allowed in compilations of which TEMPLATE is a #$compilationTemplate.")
(comment compilerTemplateDisables "(#$compilerTemplateDisables TEMPLATE STAGE-TYPE) means that TEMPLATE specifies that operations of type (#$CompilationStageType) STAGE-TYPE not be allowed in compilations of which TEMPLATE is a #$compilationTemplate.")
(comment templateAssumesPointerWidth "(#$templateAssumesPointerWidth TEMPLATE N) means that TEMPLATE presupposes a pointer with of N bits.")
(comment templateAssumesArchitecture "(#$templateAssumesArchitecture TEMPLATE SYSTEM-TYPE) means that TEMPLATE presupposes a a computing architecture (#$ComputerTypeByArchitecture) of SYSTEM-TYPE.")
(comment CodeTemplateNamedFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for representing particular instances of #$CompilerCodeTemplate. (#$CodeTemplateNamedFn NAMESTRING) denotes the #$CompilerCodeTemplate with the unique name string NAMESTRING.")
(comment nameOfCodeTemplate "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of CodeTemplateNamedFn.  (#$nameOfCodeTemplate TEMPLATE NAME) means that NAME is the name of the #$CompilerCodeTemplate TEMPLATE.")
(comment templateUsedInCompilingBinarySourceFor "(#$templateUsedInCompilingBinarySourceFor TEMPLATE CHIBL) means that TEMPLATE is a #$CompilerCodeTemplate used in compiling the binary program that was the source for the #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS CHIBL.")
(comment Eyrie-librarycall-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-librarycall-KS.")
(comment configEventHasChangeInSlotAndEffectOnRelatedSlot "(#$configEventHasChangeInSlotAndEffectOnRelatedSlot   EVT RELATED-OBJECT-TYPE CHANGE-SLOT  CHANGE-DIRECTION CONFIG-OBJ-TYPE CONFIG-SLOT CONFIG-DIRECTION) says that as a result of the configuration event, EVT, there is a change on CHANGE-SLOT in CHANGE DIRECTION for some instance of RELATED-OBJECT-TYPE that is suitably related to the configured object in EVT and the configured object is CONFIG-OBJ-TYPE and has a corresponding change in CONFIG-SLOT in CONFIG-DIRECTION .")
(disjointWith HealthCare SewingFabric)
(comment SewingFabric "The most common form of #$Sewing, in which fabric is the material sewn.")
(comment MedicalFieldOfStudy "This is a collection of scientific disciplines having to do primarily with topics directly related to medical practice.")
(comment dateOfPressureMeasurement "<code>(#$dateOfPressureMeasurement PM DATE)</code> means that <code>PM</code> is a (#$MeasuringFn #$Pressure) performed on <code>DATE</code>/.")
(comment wellHasTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthBasedOnTrace "<code>(#$wellHasTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthBasedOnTrace WELL DATE SET-OF-DEPTHS-AND-TEMPS DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that on <code>DATE</code> the well <code>WELL</code> (according to some normalization process applied to <code>SET-OF-DEPTHS-AND-TEMPS</code>), has the temperature <code>TEMP</code> at the depth <code>DEPTH</code>.")
(comment stressOfDeposition "Where SILICIDE-DEP is a #$UnitOperation-SemiconductorWaferProcessing, (#$stressOfDeposition DEP PRESSURE) means that PRESSURE is the measure of the tensile or compressive stress to which the #$thinFilmDeposited is subjected.  Usual measured in (#$Giga #$Pascal-UnitOfPressure).")
(comment OilAndGasIndustryGeneralKnowledgeTest "A collection of KB content regression tests that exercise queries relevant to general knowledge about the oil and gas industry.")
(comment BiopolymerMolecule-GeneticallyCoded "The collection of macromolecules which are produced by and can be found within living things and whose repeating subunits form a sequence of varying types that is genetically coded. This class includes proteins (essentially polymers of amino acids and nucleic acids (such as DNA or RNA).")
(comment immediatelyAfterInList "<code>(#$immediatelyAfterInList LIST ELEMENT-N ELEMENT-N-PLUS-1)</code> means that <code>ELEMENT-N-PLUS-1</code> is immediately after <code>ELEMENT-N</code> in <code>LIST</code>.")
(comment proteinProducts-TypeType "(#$proteinProducts-TypeType REACTION-TYPE PROTEIN-MOL-TYPE) says that instances of REACTION-TYPE (a specialization of #$ChemicalReaction), generate an instance of PROTEIN-MOL-TYPE (a specialization of #$ProteinMolecule).  ")
(comment complexProducts-TypeType "(#$complexProducts-TypeType REACTION-TYPE COMPLEX-TYPE) says that instances of REACTION-TYPE (a specialization of #$ChemicalReaction), generate one or more instances of COMPLEX-TYPE (a specialization of #$MacromolecularComplex\").")
(comment maximumPumpDepth "<code>(#$maximumPumpDepth WELL DIST)</code> means that <code>DIST</code> is the maximum measured depth of the pump used in teh #$ArtificialLiftWell <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment coactivatesTranscriptionOfTypeInitiatedByType-GeneLevel "(#$coactivatesTranscriptionOfTypeInitiatedByType-GeneLevel COACT-GIS GIS-TYPE FACTOR-GIS) states that the gene GOACT-GIS codes for a molecule which acts as a #$TranscriptionCoactivatorMolecule to upregulate the initiation of transcription of GENE-GIS by a transcription factor coded for by FACTOR-GIS.")
(comment traceur "A strictly functional slot used to relate a #$ParkourActivity event to its performer.")
(comment geneProductTypeRepressesTranscriptionOfType "(#$geneProductTypeRepressesTranscriptionOfType GIS-TYPE1 GIS-TYPE2) means that GIS-TYPE1 codes for a factor that can repress or inhibit transcription of GIS-TYPE2.")
(comment wellHasTVDAtMD "<code>(#$wellHasTVDAtMD WELL MD TVD)</code> means that the measured depth of <code>WELL</code> is <code>MD</code> at the true verticalDepth <code>TVD</code>.")
(comment formationTopDepthInLocation "<code>(#$formationTopDepthInLocation FORMATION LOCATION DEPTH)</code> means that under <code>LOCATION</code>, the formation <code>FORMATION</code> has its top at a true vertical depth of the distance <code>DEPTH</code>.")
(comment nonComplexNonProteinProducts-TypeType "(#$nonComplexNonProteinProducts-TypeType REACTION-TYPE MOL-TYPE) says that instances of REACTION-TYPE (a specialization of #$ChemicalReaction), generate one or more instances of MOL-TYPE, where MOL-TYPE is neither a #$ProteinMolecule, nor a MacromolecularComplex.")
(comment moleculeTypeModulatesCatalysisOfReactionTypeWithEffect "(#$moleculeTypeModulatesCatalysisOfReactionTypeWithEffect MOL-TYPE RXN-TYPE EFFECT-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE has the effect EFFECT-TYPE (usually some form of activation or inhibition) on the reaction type, RXN-TYPE, by modulating the behavior of the catalyst that facilitates the reaction.")
(comment activatesCatalystInProductionOf-TypeLevel "(#$activatesCatalystInProductionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE PROD-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE activates (increases the activity of) the catalyst, ?CATALYST-TYPE, for facilitating reactions that produce instances of ?PROD-TYPE.")
(comment inhibitsCatalystInProductionOf-TypeLevel "(#$inhibitsCatalystInProductionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE PROD-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE inhibits, blocks or decreases the ability of CATALYST-TYPE to facilitate reactions that produce instances of PROD-TYPE.")
(comment interpolationWithCubicSpline "<code>(#$interpolationWithCubicSpline SET-OF-2DPOINTS 2DPOINT)</code> means that an instance of #$CubicSpline interpolates the #$2DPoint <code>2DPOINT</code> given the set of other #$2DPoints in <code>SET-OF-2DPOINTS</code>.")
(comment wellCasingStartAndEndDepths "<code>(#$wellCasingStartAndEndDepths WELL START-DIST END-DIST)</code> means that the casing in <code>WELL</code> starts at the measured depth <code>START-DIST</code> and ends at the measured depth <code>END-DIST</code>.")
(comment wellPassesThroughFormation "<code>(#$wellPassesThroughFormation WELL FORMATION LOC)</code> means that beneath <code>LOC</code>, <code>WELL</code> passes through some portion of the geological formation <code>FORM</code>.")
(comment enzymeTypeCatalyzesDestructionOfType "(#$enzymeTypeCatalyzesDestructionOfType ?ENZ-TYPE ?CHEM-TYPE) states that the class of #$EnzymeMolecule, ?ENZ-TYPE, is capable of acting as the #$catalyst in reactions that alter molecules of the substance, ?CHEM-TYPE, thus destroying them.  Because there may be multiple ways of producing ?CHEM-TYPE, the presence of ?ENZ-TYPE is not strictly required for its destruction.")
(comment enzymeTypeCatalyzesProductionOrDestructionOfType "(#$enzymeTypeCatalyzesProductionOrDestructionOfType ?ENZ-TYPE ?CHEM-TYPE) states that the class of #$EnzymeMolecule, ?ENZ-TYPE, is capable of acting as the #$catalyst in reactions that affect molecules of the substance, ?CHEM-TYPE. This relation is agnostic as to whether molecules of ?CHEM-TYPE are outputs or inputs in such reactions. Because there may be multiple ways of producing or degrading ?CHEM-TYPE, the presence of ?ENZ-TYPE is not strictly required for ?CHEM-TYPE to be altered.")
(comment DXABoneDensityScan "The collection of all dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry tests to assess bone mineral density.  A type of #$XRayTest. ")
(comment PostmenopausalWoman "The collection of #$AdultFemaleHumans who have reached an age, typically around 50, at which ovulation, and thus menstrual cycles, have stopped and the woman is no longer able to bear children.")
(comment supplementalSlotsForFormula "(#$supplementalSlotsForFormula QUANTITY SLOT) means that there is some quantity used in formula that is a function of SLOT.  This holds if the quantity is used directly in the formula (see #$unitSlotsForFormula) or if the quantity determines some quantity that is used in the formula.  E.g. If a formula uses (#$The #$Area), then since area is a function of length x width, both (#$The #$Length) and (#$The #$Width) and their associated slots are supplemental units in the formula.  The exact relationship to the other slots can be spelled out via other attributes of the formula.")
(comment Eyrie-functionblock-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-functionblock-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-nearestcfg-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-nearestcfg-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-reachablecfg-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-reachablecfg-KS.")
(comment discreteMeterDepthsAboveProducingFormationTop "<code>(#$discreteMeterDepthsAboveProducingFormationTop WELL DEPTH)</code> means that <code>DEPTH</code> is a discrete meter interval within the casing of the #$Well <code>WELL</code> above the producing formation top.")
(comment FunctionCallImplementationStatement "The class of top-level statements in Codehawk output directly under CHIBL programs (#$CHIBLProgram-CWIS).  Each instance is an ordered list of statements relating to implementation of a particular function call.")
(comment FunctionCallImplementationSubBlock "The collection of all designated sub-blocks of code comprising #$FunctionCallImplementationStatements in CHIBL output.  Each #$FunctionCallImplementationStatement has one or typically more #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlocks as its top-level substatements.")
(comment successorStatements "(#$successorStatements SUCCESSOR PREDECESSOR) means that SUCCESSOR is a later statement than PREDECESSOR within the linear ordering of statements within the program within which both SUCCESSOR and PREDECESSOR appear.  More specifically, (successorStatements SUCCESSOR PREDECESSOR) means that either there is a superstatement SUPER such that (nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement SUPER SUCCESSOR N) and (nthCodeStatementOfStatment SUPER PREDECESSOR M) and (greaterThan N M) (i.e., (#$sameLevelSuccessorStatements SUCCESSOR PREDECESSOR)), or there are statements SUPER-SUCCESSOR and SUPER-PREDECESSOR such that (#$codeStatementHasStatements SUPER-SUCCESSOR SUCCESSOR) and (#$codeStatementHasStatements SUPER-PREDECESSOR PREDECESSOR), and (#$sameLevelSuccessorStatements SUPER-SUCCESSOR SUPER-PREDECESSOR.")
(comment sameLevelSuccessorStatements "(#$sameLevelSuccessorStatements SUCCESSOR PREDECESSOR) means that there is an immediately subsuming statement SUPER such that (#$nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement SUPER SUCCESSOR N) for some integer N (SUCCESSOR is the nth 'top-level' substatement under SUPER) and (#$nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement SUPER PREDECESSOR M) for some integer M (PREDECESSOR is the mth 'top-level' substatement under SUPER) and (#$greaterThan N M).")
(comment directSuccessorStatements "The 'direct' or anti-transitive version of #$sameLevelSuccessorStatements.  (#$directSuccessorStatements SUCCESSOR PREDECSSOR) means that SUCCESSOR directly follows PREDECESSOR in the linear ordering of top-level substatements under some #$ComputerCodeStatement that subsumes them both - i.e., that there is a statement SUPER such that (nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement SUPER PREDECESSOR N) for some non-negative integer M, and such that (nthCodeStatementOfCodeStatement SUPER SUCCESSOR N) where N=M+1.")
(comment expressionDeterminesQuantityForFormula "<code>(#$expressionDeterminesQuantityForFormula QBF EXPRESSION QUANT)</code> means that in the context of the constraints of QBF, EXPRESSION is one way of determining the value of QUANT.  For example, this predicate can be used to state that the area quantity in the formula can be decomposed into an expression of (length X width) subject to the other constraints placed on the formula.  The slots used to attribute the quantities used in the expression are associated with the formula via supplementalSlotsForFormula.")
(comment controlFlowGraphDependency "(#$controlFlowGraphDependency DEPENDENT PROVIDER) means that there is a control flow graph dependency between DEPENDENT and PROVIDER, such that DEPENDENT depends on PROVIDER.")
(comment directControlFlowGraphDependency "The 'direct', anti-transitive version of #$controlFlowGraphDependency.  (#$directControlFlowGraphDependency DEPENDENT PROVIDER) means that there is a direct, directed link from PROVIDER to DEPENDENT in the program control flow graph.")
(comment optionalConstraintPattern "A binary predicate used to associate a template for building CycL sentences with optional clauses that can be added via #$and.")
(comment metaTemplate "<code>(#$metaTemplate TEMPLATE META-TEMPLATE)</code> means that <code>META-TEMPLATE</code> is a more general template than <code>TEMPLATE</code> -- i.e., that instantiations of <code>TEMPLATE</code> are thereby instantiations of <code>META-TEMPLATE</code>.")
(comment uninterestingProportionForFormula "(#$uninterestingProportionForFormula QBF QUANTITY-1 QUANTITY-2) means that proportionality statements involving QUANTITY-1 and QUANTITY-2 are uninteresting.")
(disjointWith Mountain BoardingRamp)
(comment Eyrie-nullptrarith-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-nullptrarith-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-pointerarg-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-pointerarg-KS.")
(comment CodeHawkTableConstant "The quoted collection of all CycL constants used in directly mapping and ingesting Codehawk table information.")
(comment libraryCall "(#$libraryCall FUNCTION-BLOCK INSTRUCTION METHOD) means that INSTRUCTION in FUNCTION-BLOCK calls the #$StandardLibraryFunction METHOD.")
(comment nullPointerArithmetic "(#$nullPointerArithmetic FUNCTION-BLOCK ADD-OP-INST POSS-NULLPOINT-INST) means that ADD-OP-INST in FUNCTION-BLOCK performs an additive arithmetic operation on a possible null pointer value supplied by POSS-NULLPOINT-INST.")
(comment passesOutputAsNthArgument "(#$passesOutputAsNthArgument FUNCTION-BLOCK HAND-OFF-INST SOURCE-INST STACK-PLACE-INST FN N) means that HAND-OFF-INST in FUNCTION-BLOCK hands the output of SOURCE-INST which was placed on the stack by STACK-PLACE-INST to the #$StandardLibraryFunction FN as its Nth argument.")
(comment Skatepark "A specialization of #$Park.  Each instance of #$Skatepark is a park designed for people to ride #$Skateboards, #$RollerSkates, etc. in.")
(disjointWith DurableGood ShredOfPaper)
(comment ShredOfPaper "The collection of individual shreds, or small cut or torn pieces of #$Paper.")
(disjointWith TransportFacility FixedStructurePlatform)
(comment nLPattern "(#$nLPattern TEMPLATE PATTERN) means that PATTERN is the pattern of natural language to which TEMPLATE corresponds.")
(comment FormulaArgPositionParaphraseFn "(#$FormulaArgPositionParaphraseFn ARG-POSITION) denotes the #$AtomicParaphrase of the argument at ARG-POSITION.")
(disjointWith ChemicalObjectExtraCellularToIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent ChemicalObjectIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent)
(comment ChemicalObjectExtraCellularToIntraCellularSignalTransmissionEvent "An important specialization of #$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent.  Each instance is a case of#$ChemicalObjectSignalTransmissionEvent in which the information transfer is from the extracellular environment to the internal environment of a cell.  Instances of this type of signal tranmission are often parts of some #$ChemicalObjectInterCellularSignalTransmissionEvent.   One or more #$ChemicalObjects (individual atoms, ions, molecules) serve as the #$meansOfInfoTransfer, and often the transmission is mediated by a #$MembraneReceptorMolecule . ")
(comment GProteinMolecule "A important specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  A #$GProteinMolecule functions as a molecular implementation of a boolean, which is either 'on' or 'off' depending on whether it is bound to a #$GuanosineDiphosphate (GDP) or a #$GuanosineTriphosphate (GTP) (hence the name 'G-Protein').  If it is 'on', i.e., activated, a #$GProteinMolecule is able to in turn catalyze additional reactions of a particular class in a cellular transduction pathway.  #$GProteinMolecules play important roles in human vision and olfactory systems.")
(comment CentrosomalDuplication "The process wherein an instance of #$Centrosome replicates during Interphase, producing a second centrosome.  During mitosis, each centrosome independently produces a series of microtubule \"chains\" that began to force the two centrosomes to opposite ends of the cell. Together, the two sets of chains form a mitotic spindle, which are responsible, first, for pushing the cells (duplicated) chromosomes to the center of the cell, then breaking them apart to form two sets of (unduplicated) chromosomes in #$Anaphase.")
(comment G-Protein-MediatedCellSignalingProcess "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that begin with the reception of a signal by a #$GProteinLinkedReceptor, leading the activation of a #$GProteinMolecule, which then interacts with molecules further downstream until the cell responds.")
(disjointWith BiocatalyticMolecule AlphaHelix)
(disjointWith SystemOfDevices MicrobiologicalSystem)
(comment averageTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthBetweenDates "<code>(#$averageTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthBetweenDates WELL DEPTH TEMP START END)</code> means that during the time interval between <code>START</code> and the later date <code>END</code>, the average temperature at the normalized depth <code>DEPTH</code> in <code>WELL</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment ChemicalObjectTypeUninterestingForCausalReasoning "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects such that its instances are so commonly reactants or products in biochemical interactions that they are unremarkable as such.  In other words, if a type of reaction is known to produce or consume chemical objects from one of these collections, so many other types of reaction produce or consume that type of thing that it is not particularly interesting, and we should not produce causal chains that use an instance of this collection as a node in a chain. ")
(comment Proton-Hydron "The most common isotopic form of cationic #$Hydrogen, having a single positive charge.  This form is essentially a bare #$Proton.  Other isotopic forms are the #$Deuteron and the #$Triton-Hydron.    #$Hydrons have no electrons, so they are essentially a bare #$AtomicNucleus.")
(comment Deuteron "An isotopic form of cationic #$Hydrogen (specifically, of #$Deuterium), having a single positive charge.  The atomic nucleus contains one #$Proton and one #$Neutron.  #$Deuterons have no electrons, so they are essentially a bare #$AtomicNucleus.")
(comment CellSignalingProcessWithTyrosineKinaseReceptor "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that begin with the reception of a signal by a #$ReceptorTyrosineKinaseMolecule, leading to the activation of multiple relay proteins, which then interacts with molecules further downstream until the cell responds.")
(comment DeepSeaOilDrilling "The subcollection of #$OffshoreOilDrilling whose instances occur in bodies of water that are 500 feet or greater in depth")
(comment situationTypeHasPermitType "the corresponding predicate to #$PermitForSitTypeFn")
(comment PermitForSitTypeFn "A collection denoting function that takes a type of situation and returns the collection of permits that are credentials that allows that situation to take place under certain conditions according to some set of laws or rules.")
(comment IssuingAPermit "A specialization of #$GrantingPermission.  Each instance of #$IssuingAPermit is the action of authorizing the issuing of a permit to perform some activity or other.  E.g. issuing a hunting permit or license.")
(comment IssuingCredentialTypeFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction that takes for its value a specialization of #$Credential and returns the collection of actions which are the issuings of that kind of credential.")
(comment permissionTypeGrantsCredentialType "(#$permissionTypeGrantsCredentialType GRANTING-TYPE CREDENTIAL-TYPE)means that GRANTING-TYPE is the collection of issuings of CREDENTIAL-TYPE.")
(comment moratoriumLength "A binary predicate that relates a #$Moratorium to the time quantity that the moratorium lasts.")
(comment moratoriumImposedBy "A binary predicate that relates a #$Moratorium to the individuals who were legally responsible or instrumental in bringing about the existence of the moratorium.")
(comment EquipmentForEventTypeFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes a type of event and returns the collection of equipment used in instances of that collection.  ")
(comment inhibitsCatalystInConsumptionOf-TypeLevel "(#$inhibitsCatalystInConsumptionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE INPUT-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE inhibits, blocks or decreases the ability of CATALYST-TYPE to facilitate reactions that consume or degrade instances of INPUT-TYPE.")
(comment inhibitsCatalystInProductionOrConsumptionOf-TypeLevel "(#$inhibitsCatalystInProductionOrConsumptionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE AFFECTED-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE inhibits, blocks or decreases the ability of CATALYST-TYPE to facilitate reactions that produce or consume instances of AFFECTED-TYPE.")
(comment activatesCatalystInProductionOrConsumptionOf-TypeLevel "(#$activatesCatalystInProductionOrConsumptionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE AFFECTED-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE increases the activity of the catalyst, CATALYST-TYPE, in its facilitation of reactions that produce or consume instances of AFFECTED-TYPE.")
(comment activatesCatalystInConsumptionOf-TypeLevel "(#$activatesCatalystInConsumptionOf-TypeLevel MOL-TYPE CATALYST-TYPE INPUT-TYPE) states that the molecule MOL-TYPE activates (increases the activity of) the catalyst, ?CATALYST-TYPE, in its facilitation of reactions that consume instances of ?PROD-TYPE.")
(comment statementExecutionValue "(#$statementExecutionValue STATEMENT PROG-ACTION VAL) means that in the #$ProgramAction PROG-ACTION the integer value VAL is in some way involved with the execution of STATEMENT.")
(comment statementInputValue "(#$statementInputValue STATEMENT PROG-ACTION VAL) means that in the #$ProgramAction PROG-ACTION the integer value VAL is given as an input to the process executing STATEMENT.")
(comment statementOutputValue "(#$statementOutputValue STATEMENT PROG-ACTION VAL) means that in the #$ProgramAction PROG-ACTION the integer value VAL is given as an output by the process executing STATEMENT.")
(comment ExecutionOfStatementWithVariantValueFn "A collection-denoting function used to reify #$ProgramAction types, primarily for purposes of workarounds reasoning.  Where STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement, VAL-PRED is a spec-pred of #$statementExecutionValue, and COMP-PRED is a #$NumericComparisonPredicate, (#$ExecutionOfStatementWithVariantValueFn STATEMENT VAL-PRED COMP-PRED) denotes the class of all #$ProgramActions that are executions of STATEMENT in which the value indicated by VAL-PRED which STATEMENT would otherwise get as a result of the specifications of the program in which STATEMENT appears is replaced by another value bearing the same relation to STATEMENT in execution, and bearing the relation COMP-PRED to the dispreferred value.")
(comment instancesExecuteWithVariantValueModulo "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ExecutionOfStatementWithVariantValueFn.  Where STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement, VAL-PRED is a spec-pred of #$statementExecutionValue, and COMP-PRED is a #$NumericComparisonPredicate, (#$instancesExecuteWithVariantValueModulo STATEMENT VAL-PRED COMP-PRED EXEC-COL) means that EXEC-COL is the class of all #$ProgramActions that are executions of STATEMENT in which the value indicated by VAL-PRED which STATEMENT would otherwise get as a result of the specifications of the program in which STATEMENT appears is replaced by another value bearing the same relation to STATEMENT in execution, and bearing the relation COMP-PRED to the dispreferred value.")
(comment indicatedMitigationForProgram "(#$indicatedMitigationForProgram PROGRAM ACTION-TYPE) means that, in the context of the assertion, static analysis indicates that at least one of the weakness types exhibited by PROGRAM might be mitigated during execution if an action of type ACT-TYPE is taken during execution.")
(comment CodeStatementValueAssignmentPredicate "The collection of all predicates used to specify numeric values associated with given code statements in particular program executions.")
(comment indicatedStatementMitigationForProgram "Where PROG is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS, STATEMENT is a #$ComputerCodeStatement within PROG, VALUE-PRED is a #$CodeStatementValueAssignmentPredicate, and COMP-PRED is a #$NumericComparisonPredicate, (#$indicatedStatementMitigationForProgram PROG STATEMENT VALUE-PRED COMP-PRED) means that at least one of the weakness types exhibited by PROG can possibly be ameliorated in execution if the value indicated by VAL-PRED that STATEMENT would otherwise be given as a result of the specifications of PROG is replaced by another value bearing the same relation to STATEMENT in execution, and bearing the relation COMP-PRED to the dispreferred value.")
(comment AutoEngine-FourCycle "The intersection of #$AutoEngine and #$FourCycleEngine.")
(comment AutoEngine-Electric "The intersection of #$AutoEngine and #$ElectricalMotor.")
(comment ElectricCar "A specialization of #$Automobile.  Each instance of #$ElectricCar is a car that has an #$AutoEngine-Electric.")
(comment LithiumIonPolymerBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$LithiumIonPolymerBattery is a rechargeable battery made with lithium.")
(comment LithiumSulfurBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$LithiumSulfurBattery is a rechargeable battery made with lithium and sulfur.")
(comment LithiumTitanateBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$LithiumTitanateBattery  is a rechargeable battery made with lithium-titanate nanocrystals.")
(comment LithiumIronPhosphateBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$LithiumIronPhosphateBattery  is a rechargeable battery made with LiFePO4.")
(comment NickelMetalHydrideBattery "A specialization of #$RechargeableBattery.  Each instance of #$NickelMetalHydrideBattery  is a rechargeable battery made with nickel oxide hydroxide and a hydrogen-absorbing alloy.")
(comment situationAffectsThingInWay "(#$situationAffectsThingInWay  SIT OBJ EVT-TYPE) says that as a result of OBJ's participation in SIT, there is a good likelihood that there will be events of EVT-TYPE (denoted by #$IncreaseOnSlotFn or #$DecreaseOnSlotFn) in which the associated quantity slot will increase or decrease, accordingly, for OBJ.  E.g. (#$situationAffectsThingInWay SIT OBJ (#$IncreaseOnSlotFn #$massOfObject)) means that as a result of SIT there is good chance that the mass of OBJ will increase.")
(comment averageTemperatureAtNormalizedLinerDepthsBetweenDates "<code>(#$averageTemperatureAtNormalizedLinerDepthsBetweenDates WELL  DISCRETE-METER-DEPTH TEMP START-DATE END-DATE)</code> means that between <code>START-DATE</code> and the later date <code>END--DATE</code>, the average temperature at the normalized depth <code>DEPTH</code> in <code>WELL</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment MilitaryForceFn "<code>(#$MilitaryForceFn ORG)</code> denotes the collection of deployable military units that are sub-organizations of the armed forces of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment militaryForceType "<code>(#$militaryForceType ORG FORCE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>FORCE-TYPE</code> is the collection of deployable military units that are sub-organizations of the armed forces of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment relationInstanceAll "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that is used to state that a given binary predicate holds between a given thing and all instances of a given collection. (#$relationInstanceAll BINPRED THING COL) means every instance INST of COL is such that (BINPRED THING INST) holds.  It is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:
<p>
(#$implies
(#$isa ?INST COL)
(BINPRED THING ?INST)) .
<p>
For example, `(#$relationInstanceAll #$geopoliticalSubdivision #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$State-UnitedStates)' means that each State in the Union is a subdivision of the United States.  Cf. #$relationAllInstance, and see #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
(comment lastSubEvents "A #$SubEventPredicate that is a specialization of both #$properSubEvents and  #$lastProperSubSituations (qq.v.).  (#$lastSubEvents EVENT END) means that  END is a final part of EVENT.  That is, END is a proper subevent of EVENT that starts after EVENT starts and ends exactly when EVENT ends.  Also,  END should be something that it would seem intuitively correct (in the  context in question) to describe as \"the last part\" of EVENT.  Typically,  END doesn't start until at least halfway through (i.e. the temporal  mid-point of) the occurring of EVENT.  Note that more than one event might  be considered a last part of a given event; for example, either the ninth  inning or the last play of the ninth inning could be considered the last  subevent of a baseball game.  See also #$firstSubEvents.")
(comment internalSubEvents "A SubEventPredicate that is a specialization of both #$properSubEvents and a negation predicate of both #$firstSubEvents and #$lastSubEvents. (#$internalSubEvents EVENT SUB) means that SUB is a proper part of EVENT, but is neither a final nor initial part of EVENT.  That is, SUB starts after EVENT starts and ends before EVENT ends.  It is very often the case that an event will have many parts that are related to it via #$internalSubEvents.")
(comment internalSubEventTypes "A #$FirstOrderCollectionPredicate that is a specialization of #$properSubEventTypes and a type-level correlate of #$internalSubEvents (q.v.). This predicate is used to state that events of one given type always have events of another given type as proper internal (i.e., neither first nor last subevents). (#$internalSubEventTypes EVENTTYPE SUBEVENTTYPE) means that EVENTTYPE (a specialization of #$Event) has the specialization of #$Event SUBEVENTTYPE as a proper sub-event type, but not as a first sub-event type or as a last sub-event type.")
(comment fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING AREA DATE)</code> means that the long-string FCV values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> indicate <code>AREA</code> (an area by which an FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes) means that <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING PRESSURE DATE)</code> means that the long-string THP value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>PRESSURE</code> (a pressure differential over 2 hours measured by a THP gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING AREA DATE)</code> means that the short-string FCV values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> indicate <code>AREA</code> (an area by which an FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes) means that <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING TEMP DATE)</code> means that the short-string THT value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>TEMP</code> (a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING PRESSURE DATE)</code> means that the short-string THP value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>PRESSURE</code> (a pressure differential over 2 hours measured by a THP gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment thtToeValueAtDate "<code>(#$thtToeValueAtDate WELL DATE TEMP)</code> means that the temperature recorded by the of long-string THT gauge on <code>DATE</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING TEMPERATURE DATE)</code> means that the short-string THT value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>TEMPERATURE</code> (a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING TEMPERATURE DATE)</code> means that the long-string THT value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>TEMPERATURE</code> (a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING AREA DATE)</code> means that the value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>AREA</code> (an area by which a short-string FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment thpShortStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING PRESSURE DATE)</code> means that the short-string THP value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>PRESSURE</code> (a pressure differential over 2 hours measured by a THP gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvShortStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thtShortStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING PRESSURE DATE)</code> means that the long-string THP value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>PRESSURE</code> (a pressure differential over 2 hours measured by a THP gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate "<code>(#$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE STRING AREA DATE)</code> means that the value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>AREA</code> (an area by which a long-string FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate and #$thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesProductionStartsAtDate).")
(comment nearNarrowSpecs "<code>(#$nearNarrowSpecs COL NEAR-SPEC)</code> relates any collection <code>COL</code> to the nearest \"narrow\" collections <code>NEAR-SPEC</code> which are both subsets of <code>COL</code> and are \"narrow\" in the sense that they are not overly general (upper ontology) collections.  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the genls hierarchy.  #$nearNarrowSpecs is supported by code.")
(comment BLIntegrationConstant "The collection of all #$CycLConstants introduced in the final 2011 integration phase of the #$BootstrappedLearningProject.")
(comment mitigationForSoftwareDevelopmentStage "(#$mitigationForSoftwareDevelopmentStage WEAKNESS-TYPE MITIGATION-TYPE STAGE-TYPE) means that including an instance of MITIGATION-TYPE at the stage in the software development cycle given by STAGE-TYPE is a possible mitigation for code instantiating WEAKNESS-TYPE.")
(comment preventativeForWeaknessTypeInDevelopmentStage "(#$preventativeForWeaknessTypeInDevelopmentStage WEAKNESS-TYPE PREVENTATIVE-TYPE STAGE-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, a computer program (#$ComputerProgram-CWIS) that is the 'output' (strictly speaking, the #$contentOfCreatedIBO-AIS) of an instance of #$SoftwareDevelopmentProcess-Complete will not instantiate WEAKNESS-TYPE if the instance of STAGE-TYPE that is subsumed by the #$SoftwareDevelopmentProcess-Complete includes (properly subsumes) an instance of PREVENTATIVE-TYPE.")
(comment palliativeForWeaknessTypeInDevelopmentStage "(#$palliativeForWeaknessTypeInDevelopmentStage WEAKNESS-TYPE PALLIATIVE-TYPE STAGE-TYPE) means that if CODE is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS instantiates WEAKNESS-TYPE and is the product (the #$contentOfCreatedIBO-AIS) of a certain #$SoftwareDevelopmentProcess-Complete, then the likelihood that execution of CODE will include an unwanted action of the type associated with WEAKNESS-TYPE (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType) is much reduced if the STAGE-TYPE stage of the development process includes (properly subsumes as a subsituation) an instance of PALLIATIVE-TYPE.")
(comment candidateMitigationForWeaknessType "Where CODE-TYPE is a #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency such that (#$codeTypeHasPropensityForActionOfType CODE-TYPE ACTION-TYPE), (#$candidateMitigationForWeaknessType CODE-TYPE MITIGATION-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, if an execution of an instance of CODE-TYPE is an instance of MITIGATION-TYPE, the likelihood that the execution will feature an instance of ACTION-TYPE will be greatly reduced or eliminated, compared with the prior likelihood of an instance of ACTION-TYPE occurring as part of an execution of the same instance of CODE-TYPE that is not known to be an instance of MITIGATION-TYPE.")
(comment moratoriumDelaysActType "A binary predicate that relates a #$Moratorium to the type of activities or events which are are delayed or prohibited during the moratorium period (#$moratoriumPeriod).")
(comment typeCanActivateTranscriptionOfType "(#$typeCanActivateTranscriptionOfType FACTOR-TYPE GIS-TYPE) means that instances of the transcription factor, FACTOR-TYPE, can initiate transcription of GIS-TYPE.")
(comment geneProductTypeCanActivateTranscriptionOfType "(#$geneProductTypeCanActivateTranscriptionOfType GIS-TYPE1 GIS-TYPE2) means that GIS-TYPE1 codes for a factor that can initiate transcription of GIS-TYPE2.")
(comment InjectorWell "A specialization of #$Well.  Each instance of #$InjectorWell is a well used specifically to inject stuff into the Earth.")
(comment SAGDInjectorWell "A specialization of #$HorizontalWell and #$InjectorWell.  Each instance of #$SAGDInjectorWell is a horizontal well used to inject steam during #$SteamAssistedGravityDrainage. Cf. #$SAGDProducerWell.")
(comment injectorWellServesProducerWell "<code>(#$injectorWellServesProducerWell INJ PROD)</code> means that the injector well <code>INJ</code> injects substances into the Earth to facillitate the performance of the producer well, <code>PROD</code>.")
(comment CycloneAsEvent "The collection of all cyclone events. A type of #$StormAsEvent.")
(comment TropicalStormAsEvent "A powerful cyclone, though not as powerful as a #$HurricaneAsEvent.")
(comment TropicalStormAsObject "A powerful cyclone, though not as powerful as a #$HurricaneAsObject.")
(comment stormStrength "<code>(#$stormStrength STORM STRENGTH)</code> means that the strength of <code>STORM</code> is <code>STRENGTH</code>.")
(comment maximalWithRespectToDuration "<code>(#$maximalWithRespectToDuration TT PRED DURATION)</code> means that relative to other things during time <code>DURATION</code>, the #$TemporalThing <code>TT</code> is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment stormTrack "<code>(#$stormTrack S T)</code> means that the storm <code>S</code> is moving in the translocation event <code>T</code>.  The translocation event <code>T</code> is a motion distinct from any of the internal movement events involved in <code>S</code>, such as cyclonic wind processes.")
(comment batters "<code>(#$batters EVT OBJ)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> is acted on in </code>EVT</code> in such a way as to be likely to end up damaged. Whether in fact <code>OBJ</code> is damaged is in part dependent upon how well <code>OBJ</code> can withstand the kind of battering in question.  The battering need not be intentional, but may be done, for example, by waves striking a seashore, or heavy winds in a storm blowing against buildings.")
(comment maximalWithRespectToDurationAndPlace "<code>(#$maximalWithRespectToDuration TT PRED DURATION PLACE)</code> means that relative to other things during time <code>DURATION</code> at <code>PLACE</code>, the #$TemporalThing <code>TT</code> is maximal with regard to the manner in which it stands in the relation <code>PRED</code> to some #$ScalarQuantity <code>QUANT</code>.")
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue Synapse)
(disjointWith Cell Synapse)
(comment Synapse "The collection of specialized junctions which link two cells, often #$Neurons, and which function to pass chemical or electrical signals from one cell to the other. The signaling cell is always a #$Neuron, and the signal is passed from its #$Axon to the second cell, which might be another #$Neuron or a muscle cell (see #$Myocyte) or a cell of a #$Gland.")
(comment SynapticSignaling-Electrical "A kind of #$CellularCommunication that takes place among neurons (see #$Neuron) connected at gap junctions, in which a voltage change of one cell rapidly results in a voltage change in the other.")
(comment cellularCommunicationPath "<code>(#$cellularCommunicationPath CELL-COMMUNICATION PATH)</code> means that the \"signal\" released from the #$transmittingCell and received by one of the #$targetCells in <code>CELL-COMMUNICATION</code> moves through or along <code>PATH</code>.  Where communication occurs between cells of a #$MulticellularOrganism, <code>PATH</code> is part of that organism.  However, in the case of #$SingleCellOrganism instances, <code>PATH</code> is through some medium outside the individual organisms.")
(comment Synapse-Chemical "The collection of specialized junctions through which a #$Neuron passes chemical, neuronal signals (see #$Neurotransmitter) to another cell, either a #$Neuron, or a muscle cell or cell in a #$Gland.")
(comment Synapse-Electrical "The collection of specialized junctions through which a #$Neuron directly passes electrical signals to another #$Neuron.")
(comment rateOfInflation "<code>(#$rateOfInflation GEO RATE)</code> means <code>RATE</code> is the rate of inflation for the geopolitical entity <code>GEO</code> over a given period of time or relative to a given date. For example, in 1996 it is estimated that (#$rateOfInflation #$Iran (#$PerFn (#$Percent 35.6) #$YearsDuration)). ")
(comment SynapticSignaling-Chemical "A kind of #$CellularCommunication in which a #$Neuron passes a signal, in the form of #$NeurotransmitterMolecules to another cell, which may be a #$Neuron, a muscle cell, or a cell in a #$Gland.")
(comment SecretoryCell "A specialization of #$SomaticCell.  Each instance of #$SecretoryCell is a cell which has, as one of its functions, the secretion of some hormone, protein or other substance which is released into the bloodstream, extracellular fluid, or other extracellular environment.")
(comment MilitaryAdvance "A specialization of #$MilitaryEvent.  Each instance of #$MilitaryAdvance is an event in which a military force advances its position into or toward enemy-controlled territory.")
(comment wellHasShutInAtStartDateAccordingToParameterChanges "<code>(#$wellHasShutInAtStartDateAccordingToParameterChanges WELL CURRENT-DATE FCV-VALUE THT-VALUE THP-VALUE DATE)</code> means that values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>FCV-VALUE</code> (an area by which an FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes), <code>THT-VALUE</code> (a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge) and <code>THP-VALUE</code> (a pressure differential over 2 hours measured by a THP gauge) indicate <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasShutInStartDate "<code>(#$wellHasShutInStartDate WELL DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has a shut in beginning on <code>DATE</code>.  Cf. #$wellHasProductionStartDate.")
(comment wellHasProductionStartDate "<code>(#$wellHasProductionStartDate WELL DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has a shut in ending and production starting on <code>DATE</code>.  Cf. #$wellHasShutInStartDate.")
(comment wellIsShutInDuringDate "<code>(#$wellIsShutInDuringDate WELL DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has a shut in that starts before <code>DATE</code> and ends after <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellIsInProductionDuringDate "<code>(#$wellIsInProductionDuringDate WELL DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has been in production since some date before <code>DATE</code> and will be in production until some date after <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasClosestProductionStartDateBeforeDate "<code>(#$wellHasClosestProductionStartDateBeforeDate WELL START-DATE DATE)</code> means that <code>START-DATE</code> is the most recent production start date for <code>WELL</code> prior to <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasBeenInProductionForDurationAsOfDate "<code>(#$wellHasBeenInProductionForDurationAsOfDate WELL TQ)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has been in production for at least the time quantity <code>TQ</code>.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementClassificationType "The collection consisting of every specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement that serves as a conventional classifier for #$ComputerCodeStatements.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByPropensityForEventType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose every instance is such that executing it under normal run-time conditions has a high likelihood of realizing an instance of a certain kind of event, either as a causal consequence of the execution, or as a subsituation of the execution itself. ")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExecutionActionType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose every instance is such that executing it under normal run-time conditions has a high likelihood of situationally subsuming an instance of a certain kind of event.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByOutcomeType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType.  Each collection instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose every instance is such that executing it under normal run-time conditions has a high likelihood of causing an instance of a certain kind of outcome as a temporally subsequent event.")
(comment CodeTypeWithPropensityForOutcomeTypeFn "A #$ReifiableFunction and a #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for referencing instances of #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeByOutcomeType.  Where SIT-TYPE is a kind of #$Situation, (#$CodeTypeWithPropensityForOutcomeTypeFn SIT-TYPE) is the collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements whose executions in normal run-time conditions have a high likelihood of causing an instance of SIT-TYPE to occur as a consequence of the execution.")
(comment allInstancesHavePropensityForOutcomeOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$CodeTypeWithPropensityForOutcomeTypeFn.  Where SIT-TYPE is a kind of #$Situation, (#$allInstancesHavePropensityForOutcomeOfType CODE-TYPE SIT-TYPE means that CODE-TYPE is the collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements whose executions in normal run-time conditions have a high likelihood of causing an instance of SIT-TYPE to occur as a consequence of the execution.")
(comment codeHasPropensityForOutcomeOfType "Where SIT-TYPE is a type of #$Situation, (#$codeHasPropensityForOutcomeOfType CODE SIT-TYPE) means that executing CODE in normal run-time conditions is likely to cause an instance of SIT-TYPE as a temporally subsequent outcome.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByIncludedStatementOfType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType. Every instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose instances have in common the fact that they all subsume at least one instance of a given kind of #$ComputerCodeStatement.")
(comment ComputerCodeWithIncludedStatementOfTypeFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for referencing collection instances of #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeByIncludedStatementOfType.  Where STATEMENT-TYPE is a kind of #$ComputerCodeStatement, (#$ComputerCodeWithIncludedStatementOfTypeFn STATEMENT-TYPE) denotes the class of every #$ComputerCodeStatement that subsumes (#$codeStatementHasStatements) an instance of STATEMENT-TYPE.")
(comment allInstancesIncludeStatementOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ComputerCodeWithIncludedStatementOfTypeFn. Where INCL-STATEMENT-TYPE is a kind of #$ComputerCodeStatement, (#$allInstancesIncludeStatementOfType STATEMENT-TYPE INCL-STATEMENT-TYPE) means that STATEMENT-TYPE is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement which subsume one or more instances of INCL-STATEMENT-TYPE.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExcludedStatementOfType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType. Every instance is a specialization of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose instances have in common the fact that each subsumes *no* instance of a certain type of #$ComputerCodeStatement.")
(comment ComputerCodeThatExcludesStatementsOfTypeFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for referencing collection instances of #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExcludedStatementOfType.  Where EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE is a class of #$ComputerCodeStatement, (#$ComputerCodeThatExcludesStatementsOfTypeFn EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE) denotes the class of every #$ComputerCodeStatement that does not include any instance of EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE.")
(comment allInstancesExcludeStatementsOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of ComputerCodeThatExcludesStatementsOfTypeFn.  Where EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE is a class of #$ComputerCodeStatement, (#$allInstancesExcludeStatementsOfType STATEMENT-TYPE EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE) means that STATEMENT-TYPE is the class of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement which contain no instances of EXCL-STATEMENT-TYPE.")
(comment statementExplicitlyReferencesProcedureOfType "(#$statementExplicitlyReferencesProcedureOfType STATEMENT PROCEDURE-TYPE) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement STATEMENT explicitly mentions PROCEDURE-TYPE using a rigid designator.")
(comment statementExplicitlyMandatesProcedureOfType "(#$statementExplicitlyMandatesProcedureOfType STATEMENT PROCEDURE-TYPE) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement STATEMENT either is or subsumes an imperative statement that specifies that PROCEDURE-TYPE be instantiated and that references PROCEDURE-TYPE directly by means of a rigid designator.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExcludedSpecForActionOfType "A collection of collections and an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType. #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExcludedSpecForActionOfType is the collection of all specializations of #$ComputerCodeStatement such that all instances of each collection instance all exclude explicit reference to the same kind of #$ProgramAction.")
(comment ComputerCodeStatementTypeLackingExplicitSpecForActionOfTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for referencing instances of #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeByExcludedSpecForActionOfType.  Where ACTION-TYPE is a class of #$ProgramAction, (#$ComputerCodeStatementTypeLackingExplicitSpecForActionOfTypeFn ACTION-TYPE) denotes the class of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that lack explicit mandates for an instance of ACTION-TYPE; i.e., the class of every #$ComputerCodeStatement that does not contain any statement which explicitly refers to ACTION-TYPE in a way that will cause an instance of ACTION-TYPE to occur in execution.")
(comment noInstanceExplicitlySpecifiesActionOfType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ComputerCodeStatementTypeLackingExplicitSpecForActionOfTypeFn.  Where ACTION-TYPE is a class of #$ProgramAction, (#$noInstanceExplicitlySpecifiesActionOfType CODE-TYPE ACTION-TYPE) means that CODE-TYPE is the class of all #$ComputerCodeStatements that lack any statement which explicitly refers to ACTION-TYPE in a way that will cause an instance of ACTION-TYPE to occur in execution.")
(comment typeSeparatesStuffTypeIntoNEqualPortions "<code>(#$typeSeparatesStuffTypeIntoNEqualPortions SEPARATION STUFF-TYPE N)</code> means that every instance of the type of #$Separation-Complete-ObjectDestroyed is such that its input is an instance of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> that is#$separatedIntoPortions such that the result is <code>N</code> instances of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> of (approximately) equal size and shape.")
(comment massEventStartingPlace "<code>(#$massEventStartingPlace M-E START-PLACE)</code> means that <code>M-E</code> has its first proper sub-event (see #$firstSubEvents) at <code>START-PLACE</code>.  It may then spread to other places (see #$massEventSpreadsToPlace).")
(comment massEventSpreadsToPlace "<code>(#$massEventSpreadsToPlace M-E LATE-PLACE)</code> mea that <code>M-E</code> has sub-events events other than the first sub-event (see #$firstSubEvents) at <code>LATE-PLACE</code>.  <code>LATE-PLACE</code> will not be the same place as <code>START-PLACE</code> where <code>(#$massEventStartingPlace M-E START-PLACE)</code>.")
(comment massEventSpreadsFromPlaceToPlace "<code>(#$massEventSpreadsFromPlaceToPlace ME P1 P2)</code> means that the mass event <code>ME</code> has one subevent at <code>P1</code> and some of its subsequent subevents at <code>P2</code>.  The subevent of <code>ME</code> that occurs at <code>P1</code> need not be the first subevent of<code>ME</code>; it need only be some proper sub event that occurs prior to other proper subevents of <code>ME</code>  that occur at <code>P2</code>.")
(comment many "An instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.  <code>(#$many SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2)</code> means that many things are instances of both <code>SETORCOL1</code> and <code>SETORCOL2</code>.  What counts as \"many\" can vary greatly with context; thus it is difficult to give this quantifier a precise definition.  However, we can pin down certain of its logical features, e.g.:
<pre>
(#$transitiveViaArg #$many #$subsetOf 2).
</pre>
It is also important to note that #$many is the contradictory predicate (see #$contradictoryPreds) of #$few (q.v.).")
(comment pressureMeasured "<code>(#$pressureMeasured M P)</code> means that during the (#$MeasuringFn #$Pressure) <code>M</code>, the pressure measured is <code>P</code>.")
(comment predominantResidentType "<code>(#$predominantResidentType PLACE PERSON-TYPE)</code> means that a predominant resident type of <code>PLACE</code> is <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.  Thus it is usually true that <code>PLACE</code> is characterized by the mode of living of <code>PERSON-TYPE</code>.")
(comment RegionCharacterizedByResidentTypeFn "<code>(#$RegionCharacterizedByResidentTypeFn RES-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of populated places characterized by the presence of residents that are instances of <code>RES-TYPE</code>. For example (#$RegionCharacterizedByResidentTypeFn #$BlueCollarWorker) is the collection of working class areas.")
(comment regionTypeCharacterizedByResidentType "<code>(#$regionTypeCharacterizedByResidentType RES-TYPE REG-TYPE)</code> means that <code>REG-TYPE</code> is the collection of populated places characterized by the presence of residents that are instances of <code>RES-TYPE</code>.")
(comment EthnicallyDiverseRegion "A specilization of #$PopulatedPlace.  Each instance of #$EthnicallyDiverseRegion is a region in which significant fractions of the population are from different ethnic backgrounds.")
(comment SingleCellEukaryoticOrganism "The intersection of #$SingleCellOrganism and #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment Eumetazoa "A biological subkingdom, and a specialization of #$Animal.")
(comment Cnidaria "A biological phylum, and a specialization of #$Eumetazoa.")
(comment Hydra "A biological genus, and a specialization of #$Cnidaria.")
(comment CellReplacement-Renewal "A kind of #$CellReplacement, distinguished from tissue repair, where dead or damaged cells not associated with a particular portion of tissue (e.g., blood cells) are replaced by the body through cell division.")
(comment CellReplacement "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Instances are events in which dead or damaged cells are replaced by the body through cell division.")
(comment Tubulin "A type of globular protein that is the primary constituent of #$Microtubules.")
(comment getMeasurementAtTime "<code>(#$getMeasurementAtTime GAUGE DATE NUMBER)</code> means that on <code>DATE</code> the gauge <code>GAUGE</code> provides the reading <code>NUMBER</code>.")
(comment BoardRidingWhileStanding "An instance of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivityTypeBySurface, this is the collection of instances of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity that take place primarily on the water.")
(comment BoardRidingWhileSitting "An instance of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivityTypeBySurface, this is the collection of instances of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity that take place primarily on the water.")
(disjointWith BoardRidingWhileStanding BoardRidingWhileSitting)
(comment minimalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType "(#$minimalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N) means that every instance of SIT-TYPE features at least N situations SUBSIT such that (#$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUBSIT). That is, (#$minimalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N) holds if and only if every instance SIT of SIT-TYPE properly subsumes at least N instances of SUBSIT-TYPE, none of which is properly subsumed by another instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that SIT subsumes.")
(comment maximalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType "(#$maximalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N) means that every instance of SIT-TYPE features at most N situations SUBSIT such that (#$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUBSIT).  That is, (#$maximalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N) holds just in case every instance SIT of SIT-TYPE properly subsumes at most N instances of SUBSIT-TYPE, none of which is properly subsumed by another instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that SIT subsumes.")
(comment instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType "(#$instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType SIT SUBSIT-TYPE) means that SIT properly subsumes as many 'unembedded' instances of SUBSIT-TYPE as the situation context allows (where 'unembedded' means that for each instance of SUBSIT-TYPE subsumed, there is not other instance of SUBSIT-TYPE that subsumes it and that SIT in turn subsumes - see #$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit).  Specifically, if SIT is an instance of SIT-TYPE, and it is known that (#$maximalNumberOfTopLevelInstancesOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE N), then from (#$instanceMaximizedWithRespectToTopLevelInstancesOfType SIT SUBSIT-TYPE) it follows that there are exactly N instances SUBSIT of SUBSIT-TYPE such that (#$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUBSIT).")
(comment topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit "(#$topLevelInstanceOfTypeInSit SIT SUBSIT-TYPE SUBSIT) means that 1) SUBSIT is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE, 2) SUBSIT is a #$properSubSituations OF SIT and 3) there is no other situation OTR-SIT such that i) OTR-SIT is an instance of SIT-TYPE and ii) SIT properly subsumes OTR-SIT and OTR-SIT properly subsumes SUBSIT.")
(comment signatureTestForCodeType "(#$signatureTestForCodeType CODE-TYPE TEST) means that in any context where the #$testQuery of TEST returns bindings or returns #$True, there is a high likelihood that an instance of CODE-TYPE exists.")
(comment signatureFormulaForCodeType "(#$signatureFormulaForCodeType CODE-TYPE FORMULA) means that the #$CycLSentence FORMULA states a logical condition whose satisfaction in context is ordinarily sufficient to justify inferring the existence of an instance of CODE-TYPE.")
(comment thresholdSpecs "<code>(#$thresholdSpecs COL SPEC)</code> relates any collection <code>COL</code> to its spec collections <code>SPEC</code> but only for collections <code>COL</code> that are below a threshold as defined by the predicates #$excludeFromThresholdSpecs and #$includeInThresholdSpecs.  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the genls hierarchy and the extents of the include/exclude predicates.  #$thresholdSpecs is supported by code.")
(comment excludeFromThresholdSpecs "<code>(#$excludeFromThresholdSpecs COL)</code> is used to control the inference removal module for the predicate #$thresholdSpecs.  It prevents (#$thresholdSpecs <code>COL</code>) from returning bindings.  See also #$includeInThresholdSpecs")
(comment includeInThresholdSpecs "<code>(#$includeInThresholdSpecs COL)</code> is used to control the inference removal module for the predicate #$thresholdSpecs.  It forces (#$thresholdSpecs <code>COL</code>) to returning bindings.  See also #$excludeFromThresholdSpecs")
(comment CodeTypeSignatureTest "The collection of all fully specified KB content tests (#$KBContentTest-FullySpecified) where the saved query is considered the 'signature' for a #$ComputerCodeStatementClassificationType in the sense that a domain wherein the query is satisfied is one which probably includes an instance of the #$ComputerCodeStatementClassificationType in question, with a degree of likelihood approaching certainty.")
(comment BottomHolePressureGauge "The collection of all devices made to measure bottomhole pressure. A type of #$Gauge.")
(comment TubingheadPressureGauge "The collection of all devices made to measure tubinghead pressure. A type of #$Gauge.")
(comment ValvePositionGauge "The collection of all devices made to measure valve position. A type of #$Gauge.")
(comment OilPressureGauge "The collection of all oil pressure gauges. A type 
of #$Gauge, #$ManufacturedGoods, #$NewAutoDealerPartsMarketCategory, and 
#$VehiclePart. The collection #$OilPressureGauge is a 
#$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType and an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory.")
(comment PressureGauge "The collection of all pressure gauges. A type of #$Gauge.")
(comment ValvePositionGauge-ShortString "The collection of all devices made to measure valve position for a flow control valve in the short string of a well. A type of #$ValvePositionGauge.")
(comment ValvePositionGauge-LongString "The collection of all devices made to measure valve position for a flow control valve in the long string of a well. A type of #$ValvePositionGauge.")
(comment TubingheadPressureGauge-LongString "The collection of all devices made to measure tubinghead pressure in the long string of a well. A type of #$TubingheadPressureGauge.")
(comment TubingheadTemperatureGauge-LongString "The collection of all devices made to measure tubinghead temperature for the long string of a well. A type of #$TubingheadTemperatureGauge.")
(comment TubingheadTemperatureGauge "The collection of all devices made to 
measure tubinghead temperature. A type of #$Gauge.")
(comment TubingheadTemperatureGauge-ShortString "The collection of all devices made to measure tubinghead temperature for the short string of a well. A type of #$TubingheadTemperatureGauge.")
(comment WellGaugeType "The collection of gauge types instances of which are frequently used in wells.")
(comment GaugeOfTypeInWellFn "(#$GaugeOfTypeInWellFn G-TYPE WELL) denotes the gauge of type G-TYPE that is in WELL.")
(comment gaugeOfTypeInWell "(#$gaugeOfTypeInWell G-TYPE WELL G) means G is the gauge of type G-TYPE that is in WELL.")
(comment TubingheadPressureGauge-ShortString "The collection of all devices 
made to measure tubinghead pressure in the short string of a well. A type of 
#$TubingheadPressureGauge.")
(comment DNAPolymer "The collection of all #$Polynucleotides whose
#$polymericSubComponents are the #$NitrogenBases #$Adenine-Base,
#$Guanine-Base, #$Cytosine-Base, and #$Thymine-Base, joined in ester
linkages to a #$Deoxyribose moiety: i.e., deoxyribonucleic acid
polymers.")
(comment FunctionWithAutoGeneratedCorrespondingPredicate "A specialization of #$Function-Denotational.  This is the collection of functions whose corresponding predicates are functionally denoted and automatically generated.")
(comment autoGeneratedCorrespondingPredicateForFunction "(autoGeneratedCorrespondingPredicateForFunction FUNC PRED) means that PRED is the automatically generated corresponding predicate to FUNC.")
(comment TestFunctionFn " This is only a test")
(comment PlantCellTelophase "The collection of instances of #$Telophase that take place in an instance of #$BotanicalCell.")
(comment ProgrammingLanguageMt "The #$TheoryMicrotheory containing background knowledge required for reasoning about instances and types of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment ProgrammingLanguageDataMt "The #$DataMicrotheory containing information about particular instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment moodOfSentence "(#$moodOfSentence SENTENCE MOOD) means that SENTENCE expresses a proposition int the linguistic mood (#$InformationBearingObjectMood) MOOD, in virtue of syntactic features of SENTENCE which are sufficient conditions for determining the mood expressed.")
(comment moodCharacterizesFormalLanguageTypeStatements "Where LANGUAGE-TYPE is a #$LanguageFamilyType and a specialization of #$ArtificialLanguage-Formal, (#$moodCharacterizesFormalLanguageTypeStatements MOOD LANGUAGE-TYPE) means that every complete sentence in every language that is an instance of LANGUAGE-TYPE has the #$InformationBearingObjectMood (#$moodOfSentence) MOOD.")
(comment moodCharacterizesSomeFormalLanguageTypeStatements "Where LANGUAGE-TYPE is a #$LanguageFamilyType and a specialization of #$ArtificialLanguage-Formal, (#$moodCharacterizesSomeFormalLanguageTypeStatements MOOD LANGUAGE-TYPE) is true if there are one or more formal languages containing one or more complete sentences whose #$moodOfSentence is MOOD.")
(comment interpretationTypeOfProgrammingLanguageType-SomeLanguagesAndStatements "Where LANGUAGE-TYPE is a #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType and SIT-TYPE is a class of #$Situation, (#$interpretationTypeOfProgrammingLanguageType-SomeLanguagesAndStatements LANGUAGE-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means, literally, that there is at least one language belonging to LANGUAGE-TYPE that contains at least one statement signifying an instance of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment functionEvaluated "(#$functionEvaluated EVALUATING FN) means that FN is the #$Function-Denotational evaluated in the #$DeterminingTheValueOfASlot EVALUATING.")
(comment CodingFunctionTypeByPurityOfFunction "A faceting collection that partitions #$CodingFunction.  There are two collection instances: #$PurelyFunctionalCodingFunction and #$ImpureCodingFunction.  The former is the collection of all #$CodingFunctions which carry out mathematical operations without otherwise perturbing the machine state:  the latter is the collection of all #$CodingFunctions whose execution results in discernable 'side effects' in the machine state that have to be taken account of in subsequent operations.")
(comment PurelyFunctionalCodingFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions such that i) the function always evaluates the same output given the same input (i.e., the output does not depend on any hidden machine state that can change over the execution of a program or an input from a peripheral device) and ii) evaluation of the function does not cause any semantically significant side effect in data structures or output to peripherals.")
(comment ImpureCodingFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions where either the output on a given input can vary as a contingent feature of the run-time environment, or where evaluating the function results in a semantically significant change in machine state that is unrelated to the range of the function.")
(comment statementsExpressedInFormalismsOfField "(#$statementsExpressedInFormalismsOfField LANGUAGE-TYPE FIELD) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatements of every #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage that belongs to LANGUAGE-TYPE are expressed using conventional notational formalisms developed to implement reasoning in FIELD.")
(comment ProceduralProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages which express computations to be performed in terms of directives specifying changes to the machine state.")
(comment HybridProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage that display characteristic features of distinct instances of #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType.")
(comment LogicalProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages that use propositional logic or a first- or higher-order predicate calculus as a purely or mostly declarative representation language with a theorem-prover or model-generator serving as the problem solver that targets efficient methods for generating results.")
(comment PredicateLogicProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$LogicalProgrammingLanguages that use a first or higher-order predicate calculus as a representation language.")
(comment HigherOrderLogicProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$PredicateLogicProgrammingLanguages where the predicate calculus that is as a representation language is 'higher order', in at least the sense of permitting quantification over predicates, and possibly over sentences as well.")
(comment FunctionalProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$DeclarativeProgrammingLanguages that express computation in terms of evaluating mathematical functions without reference to state or mutable data.")
(comment PurelyFunctionalProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$FunctionalProgrammingLanguages such that the only type of method called by any well-formed statement of the language is a #$PurelyFunctionalCodingFunction.")
(disjointWith PurelyFunctionalProgrammingLanguage (CollectionDifferenceFn FunctionalProgrammingLanguage PurelyFunctionalProgrammingLanguage))
(comment TypeSafeProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages that enforce data type requirements on function calls in some degree.")
(comment BoundsCheckedProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$AbstractProgrammingLanguages that support automated checking of whether a variable value is within the upper and lower bounds of a candidate storage location.")
(comment CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell-MultiplePathways "The collection of instances of CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell that involve a signaling molecule binding with a  receptor molecule, triggering more than one transduction pathway (instances of SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-MultiStageReaction).  Thus one signal can influence several cellular responses.")
(comment interpretationTypeOfProgrammingLanguageType "Where LANGUAGE-TYPE is a #$ProgrammingLanguageFamilyType and SIT-TYPE is a class of #$Situation, (#$interpretationTypeOfProgrammingLanguageType LANGUAGE-TYPE SIT-TYPE) means that every statement (#$ComputerCodeStatement) of language (#$codeLanguage) #$signifies an instance of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment ImpureFunctionalProgrammingLanguage "The collection of all #$FunctionalProgrammingLanguages that allow calls (instances of #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable) to #$CodingFunctions which are instances of #$ImpureCodingFunction.")
(comment HomologousChromosomePair "The collection of all homologous pairs of chromosomes.  Each #$HomologousChromosomePair consists of two #$EukaryoticChromosomes that are parts of the same #$Cell, contain genes for the same proteins, and whose DNA sequences are, though not identical, substantially similar to each other.  The members of a #$HomologousChromosomePair, like any chromosome in a eukaryotic cell, will be #$UnduplicatedChromosomes at the beginning of #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle, and #$DuplicatedChromosomes at the end of #$InterphaseOfEukaryoticCellCycle. During #$ProphaseI of #$Meiosis, the two members of the pair will join together to form a #$Tetrad-Chromosomal.")
(comment arg7Genl "A binary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg7Genl RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the seventh argument to <code>RELN</code> must be a subcollection of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$genls ARG7 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argGenl for a  similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg8Genl "A binary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg8Genl RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the eighth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be a subcollection of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$genls ARG8 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argGenl for a  similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg10Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg10Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the tenth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ARG9 ARG10...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG10 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg11Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg11Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the eleventh argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ARG9 ARG10 ARG11 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG11 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg12Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg12Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the twelfth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ARG9 ARG10 ARG11 ARG12 ...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG12 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(comment arg13Isa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(#$arg13Isa RELN COL)</code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the thirteenth argument to <code>RELN</code> must be an instance of <code>COL</code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ARG6 ARG7 ARG8 ARG9 ARG10 ARG11 ARG12 ARG13...)</code> is semantically well-formed only if <code>(#$isa ARG13 COL)</code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See #$argIsa for a similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
(disjointWith WoodworkingTool FoodUtensil)
(comment objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDate "
<code>(#$objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDate OBJ DATE 
DURATION SLOT QUANT SET)</code> means <code>SET</code> is a set of points 
defined as tuples of <code>QUANT</code> and a quantity of seconds, where the 
quantity of seconds is seconds since 1970 corresponding to dates that fall 
between <code>DATE</code> and an earlier date <code>DURATION</code> prior to 
<code>DATE</code>, and the value <code>QUANT</code> is such that <code>(SLOT OBJ 
QUANT)</code> holds at the date denoted by the corresponding quantity of 
seconds.")
(comment objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDateAtParameterizedPart "
<code>
(#$objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDateAtParameterizedPart  
OBJ DATE DURATION SLOT QUANT PART-SLOT PART-QUANT SET)</code> means 
<code>SET</code> is a set of points defined as tuples <code>QUANT</code> and 
quantities of seconds, where the quantities of seconds are seconds since 1970 
corresponding to dates that fall between <code>DATE</code> and an earlier date 
<code>DURATION</code> prior, and <code>QUANT</code> is the value 
<code>SLOT</code> such that there exists a part <code>PART</code> of 
<code>OBJ</code> such that at the date specified by the corresponding quantity 
of seconds <code>(SLOT PART QUANT)</code> where <code>PART</code> is the 
part of <code>OBJ</code> such such that  <code>(PART-SLOT PART PART-QUANT)
</code>  is true.")
(comment objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDate-SecondOffsets "<code>(#$objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDate-SecondOffsets OBJ DATE DURATION SLOT QUANT SET)</code> means <code>SET</code> is a set of points defined as tuples of <code>QUANT</code> and a quantity of seconds, where the quantity of seconds is duration in seconds before or after <code>DATE</code>, and the value <code>QUANT</code> is such that <code>(SLOT OBJ QUANT)</code> holds at the date denoted by the corresponding quantity of seconds.")
(comment objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDateAtParameterizedPart-SecondOffsets "(#$objHasSlotValueTimePointSetForPreviousDurationFromDateAtParameterizedPart-SecondOffsets OBJ DATE DURATION SLOT QUANT PART-SLOT PART-QUANT SET) means SET is a set of points defined as tuples of QUANT and a quantity of seconds,  where the quantity of seconds is duration in seconds before or after DATE, and QUANT is the value SLOT such that there exists a part PART of OBJ such that at the date specified by the corresponding quantity of seconds (SLOT PART QUANT) where PART is the part of OBJ such such that (PART-SLOT PART PART-QUANT) is true.")
(comment EntireSurfaceTypeFn "(#$EntireSurfaceTypeFn COL) returns the collection of contiguous #$EntireSurfaceLayer instances that cover instances of COL, a specialization of #$SpatialThing.  We remain agnostic about whether or not it is the case that such surface layers are parts of the the objects they are the surface of.")
(disjointWith CerealFood Spread-Food)
(disjointWith Preservative-Food Spread-Food)
(comment Spread-Food "A specialization of #$FoodIngredientOnly.  Each instance of #$Spread-Food is a substance used as an integral part of a food (as oppoed to #$Condiments which are optional) that is applied with a knife (as opposed to #$Dip-Food.  Commonly used spreads are butter, jam, and mayonaise  Instances of #$Spread-Food are not eaten by themselves.  Note that depending on the dish, a food may be a spread, a condiment, or an ingredient.")
(comment bottomholePressureAtDate "<code>(#$bottomholePressureAtDate WELL DATE AREA)</code> means that the bottomhole pressure of <code>WELL</code> is <code>PRESS</code> on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment UndenaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 11).  Each instance of #$UndenaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 11.")
(comment DuodenaryPredicate "A #$PredicateTypeByArity and specialization of (#$ArityRelationFn 12).  Each instance of #$DuodenaryPredicate is a #$Predicate whose #$arity is 12.")
(disjointWith Jumping JumpingOverSomethingWithATransporter)
(comment fiberName "<code>(#$fiberName FIBER NAME)</code> means that <code>FIBER</code> has the name string <code>NAME</code>.")
(comment SAGDProducerWell-Observation "A specialization of #$HorizontalWell aand #$OilWell.  SAGD observation wells do not actually produce oil, but are used to study SAGD oil production.")
(comment BufferBoundingViolation "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein an operation which the controlling code (#$codeExecuted) directly or implicitly specifies should be a #$ComputerDataTransfer from or a #$ComputerDataAlteration affecting a particular buffer in fact transfers information from or alters information in a region outside the bounds of the buffer that is targeted.")
(comment BufferOutOfBoundsRead "The collection of all #$ComputerDataTransfers wherein the #$dataLocationReadFrom overlaps one or both boundaries (upper and lower) of the buffer implicitly or explicitly targeted for the transfer by the #$codeExecuted.")
(comment BufferOverread "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerDataTransfer wherein the upper (higher) bound of a targeted buffer is overlapped in the transfer.")
(comment BufferUnderwrite "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerDataAlteration wherein the lower bound of a targeted buffer is overlapped by the data-altering operation.")
(comment BufferUnderread "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerDataTransfer wherein the lower bound of a targeted buffer is overlapped by the data transfer.")
(comment BufferOutOfBoundsWrite "A specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  Each instance of #$BufferOutOfBoundsWrite is an event in which data is input to a running process that pushes commands into the execution stack of the computer on which the program is running.  As a consequence, the program may crash, or the the return address may be overwritten so that it points back into the buffer.  Buffer overflows involve supplying the program a data string that is too large for the the buffer of the program to handle, via a function in the program that does not perform bounds checking. In the standard C library there are a number of functions that copy or append strings without bounds checking: strcat(), strcpy(), sprintf(), vsprintf(), gets(). See #$VulnerableToBufferOverflow,  #$BufferOverflowFault-ProgramCrashing, and #$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution.")
(comment DistributionOfChromosomes-Eukaryotic-CellularProcess "A cellular process common to both #$Mitosis and #$Meiosis, in which genetically similar chromosomal structures within a dividing cell (e.g., #$chromatids in a #$DuplicatedChromosome or homologous #$DuplicatedChromosome instances in a #$Tetrad-Chromosomal) are separated and \"pushed\" to opposite \"poles\" of the cell, where they will wind up being the total chromosomal content of the cells that result from the impending division.")
(comment DataTypeTransformation "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein a value is converted from one data type to another.")
(comment dataTypeConvertedFrom "(#$dataTypeConvertedFrom CONVERSION TYPE) means that TYPE is the #$ComputerDatatypeType that a value is converted from in the #$DataTypeTransformation CONVERSION.")
(comment dataTypeConvertedTo "(#$dataTypeConvertedTo CONVERSION TYPE) means that TYPE is the #$ComputerDatatypeType that a value is converted to in the #$DataTypeTransformation CONVERSION.")
(comment ImproperDataTypeConversion "The collection of all #$DataTypeTransformations that are undesirable in the sense of causing some undesirable behavior or outcome in the execution, such as nonterminating looping.  More specifically, #$ImproperDataTypeConversion is the collection of all program executions wherein a value is converted from one #$ComputerDatatypeType to another in a way such that the result has the potential for causing a dangerous program behavior if passed to the appropriate context.")
(comment UnintendedSignExtension "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein the data type of a value is transformed into a larger data type in such a way that the value becomes sign extended.")
(comment SignedToUnsignedDataConversionError "The collection of all #$DataTypeTransformations where a signed primitive is converted to an unsigned value.")
(comment UnsignedToSignedDataConversionError "The collection of all #$DataTypeTransformations where an unsigned primitive is converted to a signed value.")
(comment NumericTruncationError "The collection of all #$DataTypeTransformations wherein a primitive is cast to a primitive of smaller size in such a way that data is lost in the conversion.")
(comment CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseOne "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created in part to support the #$CodeAnalysisProject in Phase One.")
(comment Desalination "The collection of events in which salt is removed from #$Water-Saline to render it suitable for drinking or for use in irrigation.")
(comment SeawaterDesalination "A specialization of #$Desalination.  #$SeawaterDesalination is The collection of events in which salt is removed from #$SeaWater to render it suitable for drinking or for use in irrigation.")
(comment DisjointMedicalSituationType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  This is the collection of medical situation types that are sibling disjoint with each other.  Note: this collection should not include all surgical procedure types even those thought to be \"natural\" kinds because some procedure types share instances with others even though they don't stand in a genls relationship.  E.g.

<pre>
   (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$HeartValveProcedure-Surgical #$objectActedOn #$AorticValve)</pre> 

is not a specialization of #$HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure   -- there are aortic valve procedures that are not repairs.  but clearly the two collections are not disjoint.<br><br>

In cases like the example above, one should assert as instances of DisjointSurgicalProcedureType those collections which will give the greatest coverage without falsehood and assert individual disjointness assertions to cover any gaps.")
(comment eventOccursAtWell "<code>(#$eventOccursAtWell EVENT WELL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> occurs at the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment eventOccursAtDepth "<code>(#$eventOccursAtDepth EVT DIST)</code> means <code>EVT</code> occurs at <code>DEPTH</code>.")
(comment atLeastNthSubSitTypeOfTypeInSitType "(#$atLeastNthSubSitTypeOfTypeInSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE FRAMING-TYPE N) means that any instance SIT of SIT-TYPE will properly subsume an instance SUBSIT of SUBSIT-TYPE such that 1) SUBSIT is also an instance of FRAMING-TYPE; 2) there is no instance of FRAMING-TYPE that properly subsumes SUBSIT and that SIT in turn properly subsumes; and 3) there are at least N-1 other instances OTR-INST of FRAMING-TYPE such that i) SIT properly subsumes OTR-INST; ii) there is no other instance of FRAMING-TYPE that properly subsumes OTR-INST and that SIT properly subsumes; and iii) SUBSIT starts after the ending of OTR-INST.")
(comment nthPossibleSubSitTypeOfTypeInMaxedSitType "(#$nthPossibleSubSitTypeOfTypeInMaxedSitType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE FRAMING-TYPE N) means that any instance SIT of SIT-TYPE will properly subsume an instance SUBSIT of SUBSIT-TYPE such that 1) SUBSIT is also an instance of FRAMING-TYPE; 2) there is no instance of FRAMING-TYPE that properly subsumes SUBSIT and that SIT in turn properly subsumes; and 3) there are at most N-1 other instances OTR-INST of FRAMING-TYPE such that i) SIT properly subsumes OTR-INST; ii) there is no other instance of FRAMING-TYPE that properly subsumes OTR-INST and that SIT properly subsumes; and iii) SUBSIT starts after the ending of OTR-INST.")
(comment eventHasDownholeProfile "<code>(#$eventHasDownholeProfile EVENT SET)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> has a downhole profile specified by <code>SET</code>.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro "A predicate used to generate plausible questions from text. <code>
(#$plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro BINARY-PRED BINARY-PRED-ARG-POSITION RULE-MACRO)</code> means that in the question-suggestion context at hand, it is reasonable to suggest a query of the form <code>(RULE-MACRO BINARY-PRED ARG3 ARG4)</code>, where <code>PRED-ARG-POSITION</code> designates, by reference to the argument-positions defined for <code>BINARY-PRED</code>, the argument position in which a variable appears.  For example, <code>
(#$plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPositionWithMacro #$likesAsFriend 1 #$relationAllExists)</code> means that <code>(#$relationAllExists #$likesAsFriend ?WHO #$BillClinton)</code> is a plausible question in the question-suggestion context at hand.")
(disjointWith SubEventPredicate NonPartonomicBinaryRolePredicate)
(comment NonPartonomicBinaryRolePredicate "The collection of instances of #$BinaryRolePredicate that hold of events and some role-player that is not a part (i.e., #$subEvents) of that event.")
(comment underlyingProcessBehindSubSitType "<code>(#$underlyingProcessBehindSubSitType SCRIPT UNDERLYING-PROCESS SCENE)</code> means that in any instantiation of <code>SCRIPT</code>, one of the #$properSubEventTypes that comprises <code>SCENE</code> is <code>UNDERLYING-PROCESS</code> which contributes causally to <code>SCENE</code>'s instantiation.")
(comment eventHasSignalMeasurement "<code>(#$eventHasSignalMeasurement EVENT SET)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> has a signal measurement specified by <code>SET</code>.")
(comment TemperatureGauge "The collection of all temperature gauges. A specialization of #$TemperatureMeasuringDevice.")
(comment Thermocouple "The collection of all thermocouples. A specialization of #$TemperatureMeasuringDevice.")
(comment thtHeelValueAtDate "<code>(#$thtHeelValueAtDate WELL DATE TEMP)</code> means that the temperature recorded by the short-string THT gauge on <code>DATE</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment thermocoupleTemperatureReadingAtDate "<code>(#$thermocoupleTemperatureReadingAtDate TC DATE TEMP)</code> means that the temperature recorded by the #$Thermocouple <code>TC</code> on <code>DATE</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment WellShutIn "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$WellShutIn is an event during which a #$Well is shut-in (i.e. taken out of production) for at least a short while, usually in order to perform some required maintenance before going back on production.")
(comment WellProduction "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$WellProduction is an event during which a #$Well is producing.  For the contrasting sort of event (during which a well is out of production), see #$WellShutIn.")
(disjointWith WellShutIn WellProduction)
(comment wellHasProductionEventWithStartDate "<code>(#$wellHasProductionEventWithStartDate WELL START-DATE PROD)</code> means that <code>PROD</code> is the well production event that began at <code>START-DATE</code> at the well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment wellHasShutInEventWithStartDate "<code>(#$wellHasShutInEventWithStartDate WELL START-DATE S-IN)</code> means that <code>S-IN</code> is the well shut-in event that began at <code>START-DATE</code> at the well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment wellHasShutInEndDate "<code>(#$wellHasShutInEndDate WELL DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL</code> has a shut in ending on <code>DATE</code>.  Cf. #$wellHasProductionStartDate.")
(comment wellHasShutInEventWithEndDate "<code>(#$wellHasShutInEventWithEndDate WELL END-DATE S-IN)</code> means that <code>S-IN</code> is the well shut-in event that ends at <code>START-DATE</code> at the well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment normContravened "(#$normContravened SIT NORM-SPEC) means that SIT suffices to make true a sentence which contradicts which contradicts a specification that is part of NORM-SPEC.")
(comment SecurityPolicy "The collection of all instances of #$OrganizationPolicy that define what constitutes a #$SecurityBreach for the organization in the sense of stating conditions whose violation constitutes such a breach.")
(comment securityPolicyViolated "(#$securityPolicyViolated BREACH POLICY) means that POLICY is a #$SecurityPolicy which is violated as a result of the #$SecurityBreach BREACH.")
(comment securityPolicyOfNetwork "(#$securityPolicyOfNetwork POLICY NETWORK) means that POLICY is an enforced security policy for machines on NETWORK and for users of those machines.")
(comment securityPolicyOfSoftwareObject "(#$securityPolicyOfSoftwareObject POLICY SOFTWARE) means that POLICY is a #$SecurityPolicy enforced for execution of SOFTWARE and, by extension, for users of SOFTWARE.")
(comment securityPolicyOfProgram "(#$securityPolicyOfProgram POLICY PROGRAM) means that POLICY is a #$SecurityPolicy enforced in execution of PROGRAM and, by extension, for users of PROGRAM.")
(comment securityPolicyOfOperatingSystem "(#$securityPolicyOfOperatingSystem POLICY OS) means that POLICY is a #$SecurityPolicy that is enforced in operation of OS and, by extension, for users of OS.")
(comment ProgramExecutionSecurityPolicyViolation "The collection of every #$SecurityBreach that is a causal result of some #$ProgramAction, and in which a specified #$SecurityPolicy can be identified as the #$securityPolicyViolated.")
(comment ProgramInternalSecurityPolicyViolation "The collection of all #$SecurityBreaches that are caused by #$ProgramActions and such taht the #$securityPolicyViolated is a policy of the program being executed (#$securityPolicyOfProgram)")
(comment normContravened "(#$normContravened SIT NORM-SPEC) means that SIT suffices to make true a sentence which contradicts a specification that is part of NORM-SPEC.")
(comment ProgramActionWithoutInternalTerminationProvision "The collection of all iterative #$ProgramActions wherein the #$codeExecuted lacks either an implicit or an explicit semantic provision for terminating the action in question, so that an external intervention in the apparatus implementing the program is required to make the action terminate.")
(comment DataCorruption-ProgramAction "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein data is altered in ways not commensurate with best standards and practices in computer programming.")
(comment DataDegradation-ProgramAction "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein data that one or more users have an interest in preserving is lost.")
(comment Calibration "A specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$ActionOnObject.  Each instance of #$Calibration is an event in which the measurements produced by one device (the standard) are compared with the measurements produced by another device (the unit under test).")
(comment unitUnderTestInCalibration "<code>(#$unitUnderTestInCalibration CAL DEV)</code> measn that in the #$Calibration event <code>CAL</code>, the unit under test is <code>DEV</code>.")
(comment SaturationSteamTemperatureInLiner "Each instance of #$SaturationSteamTemperatureInLiner is an event in which the actual temperature in the liner is greater than or equal to the saturation steam temperature.")
(comment ClawedLobster "A #$BiologicalFamily.  A specialization of #$Crustacean.")
(comment Homarus "A #$BiologicalGenus. A specialization of #$ClawedLobster. The two significant immediate specializations of #$Homarus are #$AmericanLobster and #$EuropeanLobster.")
(comment employerLeft "<code>(#$employerLeft ENDING EMPLOYER)</code> means that during <code>ENDING</code>, an instance of #$EmploymentTermination, <code>EMPLOYER</code> is the agent that one or more employees is leaving.")
(comment departingEmployee "<code>(#$departingEmployee ENDING PERSON)</code> means that during <code>ENDING</code>, an instance of #$EmploymentTermination, <code>PERSON</code> is one of the employees is that is leaving the employer.")
(comment unitAbsoluteScaleOffset "A ternary #$MetaFunction predicate that relates two interconvertible #$UnitOfMeasures (q.v.) to the real number by which the units are offset when the measurements are absolute (not relative to some other value.)  <code>(#$unitAbsoluteScaleOffset UNIT1 UNIT2 N)</code> and a corresponding <code>(#$unitMultiplicationFactor UNIT1 UNIT2 M)</code> means that when converting from <code>UNIT1</code> to <code>UNIT2</code>, after multiplying the <code>UNIT1</code> value by <code>M</code> we add <code>N</code>.  This is primarily useful for temperature conversions.")
(comment AbsoluteQuantityConversionFn "<code>(#$AbsoluteQuantityConversionFn UNIT QUANTITY)</code> converts the absolute <code>QUANTITY</code> into an equivalent absolute quantity expressed using <code>UNIT</code> as the unit of measure. For example, (#$AbsoluteQuantityConversionFn #$Kelvin (#$DegreeCelsius -273.15)) denotes the absolute quantity (#$Kelvin 0).  Contrast this with the relative qualtity conversion function, #$QuantityConversionFn. (#$QuantityConversionFn #$Kelvin (#$DegreeCelsius -273.15) denotes (#$Kelvin -273.15).  For units on scales that do not involve an offset, both <code>(#$AbsoluteQuantityConversionFn UNIT QUANTITY)</code> and <code>(#$QuantityConversionFn UNIT QUANTITY)</code> denote the same thing.")
(comment resigningEmployee "<code>(#$resigningEmployee RESIGNATION PERSON)</code> means that during <code>ENDING</code>, an instance of #$ResigningFromEmployment, <code>PERSON</code> is the employee is that is leaving the employer.")
(comment firedEmployee "<code>(#$firedEmployee DISCHARGE PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> was discharged with prejudice during <code>DISCHARGE</code>.")
(comment laidOffEmployee "<code>(#$laidOffEmployee  DISCHARGE PERSON)</code> means that <code>PERSON</code> was laid off during <code>DISCHARGE</code>.")
(comment positionResignedFromInOrg "<code>(#$positionResignedFromInOrg RESIGN PERSON ORG POS-TYPE)</code> means that during the #$ResigningFromEmployment <code>RESIGN</code>, the #$resigningEmployee is <code>PERSON</code>, and who is resigning from the position <code>POS-TYPE</code> in <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment hiredPerson "<code>(#$hiredPerson HIRING PERSON)</code> means that the #$Person <code>PERSON</code> was hired during the #$HiringSomeoneToDoSomething <code>HIRING</code>.")
(comment hirer "<code>(#$hirer HIRING AGENT)</code> means that the #$Agent-Generic <code>AGENT</code> was the hirer during the #$HiringSomeoneToDoSomething <code>HIRING</code>.")
(comment positionHiredToInOrg "<code>(#$positionHiredToInOrg HIRING PERSON ORG POS-TYPE)</code> means that during the #$HiringSomeoneToDoSomething <code>HIRING</code>, the #$hiredPerson is <code>PERSON</code>, and who is hired to fill the position <code>POS-TYPE</code> in <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment positionResignedFrom "This predicate is used to specify the type of position that a person undergoing a resignation in some organization is resigning from.")
(comment promotedPerson "<code>(#$promotedPerson PROMOTION PERSON)</code> means the person <code>PERSON</code> is the person promoted in <code>PROMOTION</code>.")
(comment ExpansionSlot "The collection of expansion slots for computers and computer related hardware -- e.g. slots in the mother board of a computer where #$ExpansionCards plug in.")
(comment ExpansionCard "The collection of peripheral printed circuit boards in computers and computer related devices.")
(comment ComputerPort "#$ComputerPort is the collection of all physical connections through which peripherals can communicate with the CPU of a particular computer or computer related device.  Note that this collection is distinct from the collection of network ports, which are integers assigned to communication protocols (see #$NetworkPortNumber).")
(comment KVMSwitch "The collection of all computer interface switch boxes designed to switch keyboard (K) or video (V) or mouse (M) from one computer to another.")
(comment RemoteAccessUnit "The collection of remote access units.")
(comment EncryptionDevice "A specialization of #$Computer.  Each instance of this collection is a dedicated hardware machine capable of processing encryption requests.")
(comment DiskArray-Computer "A type of disk storage system composed of multiple harddrives, disk controllers, power supply and an onboard memory cache.")
(comment VoiceLoggingDevice "The collection of all information recording devices used to log audio/voice communication.")
(comment VPNNetworkAccessDevice "The collection of remote access devices designed to provide access/authentication/etc. to VPN networks.")
(comment VideoSwitch-Computer "The collection of all computer interface switch boxes designed to switch a video monitor from one computer to another.")
(comment NetworkTrafficUnit "An network computer network device that typically support a wide range of advanced traffic routing functionality and protocols.")
(comment MediaControlUnit-WithTouchInterface "An media control device used for office meetings, home entertainment, etc.")
(comment AVMediaInternetGatewayDevice "A kind of #$ComputerHardwareItem.  Instances are devices that control the transmission of media data over IP networks and often can integrate those transmissions with voice transmissions over a traditional phone network.")
(comment ExpansionSlot-LocationSpecific "The collection of expansion slots for computers that are specific to a particular location on the device -- e.g. Cisco 4506 EXP in slot location 2.")
(comment ComputerPort-LocationSpecific "The collection of port on computers and computer hardware that are specific as to location -- e.g. RJ-45 port with port id 2.")
(comment localizedExpansionSlotTypeHasType "(#$localizedExpansionSlotTypeHasType SPEC GENL) means that SPEC is a location specific specialization of GENL.  E.g. (#$localizedExpansionSlotTypeHasType CISCO-PCI-SUPERVISOR-720-at-SLOT-7 CISCO-PCI-SUPERVISOR-720) holds because CISCO-PCI-SUPERVISOR-720-at-SLOT-7 is the location specific (slot 7) version of the slot type CISCO-PCI-SUPERVISOR-720.")
(comment ComputerPort-NonCardDevice "The collection of ports on devices that are not expansion cards.")
(comment ComputerPort-ExpansionCard "The collection of ports on expansion cards.")
(comment WirelessAccessPoint-Device "Electronic devices which allow connection to a wireless network.  These may be dedicated access point devices or combination devices that allow a variety of connections.")
(comment ExpansionCard-Daughter "The collection of all \"daughter\" card. A type of #$ExpansionCard. Each instance of this collection is a expansion card that is designed as an extension to a mother board -- hence the alternate name \"daughter board\" or as an extension to another expansion card.")
(comment CarrierCard "The collection of all \"carrier\" cards. A type of #$ExpansionCard. Each instance of this collection is a expansion card that has a slot for another expansion (\"daughter\") card.")
(comment TeleprocessingControlUnit "The collection of all control units for teleprocessing.")
(comment NetworkAccessServer "An network computer network device that typically support a wide range of advanced traffic routing functionality and protocols.")
(comment TelephoneInterface "The collection of hardware devices designed to interface telephones with other devices such as sound recorders, etc.")
(comment MediaControlUnit "An media control device used for office meetings, home entertainment, etc.")
(comment WavelengthDivisionMultiplexingSystem-CommunicationDevice "The collection of communication devices capable of transmitting or receiving fiber-optic signals that have a plurality of signals on a single optical fiber.")
(comment WirelessRouter "The collection of all routers designed for use with WiFi or other wireless systems.")
(comment ComputerPort-Logical "#$ComputerPort-Logical is the collection of all computer (and device) ports abstracted from their physical realization.")
(comment ComputerPort-Generic "#$ComputerPort-Generic is the collection of all computer or computer device ports whether considered as purely physical devices or considered in terms of their abstract logical functionality.  See the immediate specializations #$ComputerPort and #$ComputerPort-Logical")
(comment hasParentProductComponent "A very general relation that relates a more specialized product type to a more general entity.  For example, this might relate a type of expansion slot to the types of devices that have those slots or it could relate a logical expansion port to a hardware component port.  In most cases, the actual information will be stored on the various specializations of this predicate.  E.g. card_type_compatible_with_slot_type, port_type_for_device_type, port_type_for_card_type, etc.")
(comment 120VoltDevice "The collection of electrical devices that are designed to work exclusively with 120 volts (The actual acceptable voltage varies somewhat but is close to the 120 volt standard).")
(comment voltageSuppliedFromSource "(#$voltageSuppliedFromSource DEVICE V) means that the power supply for DEVICE (either internal or external) supplies V voltage to DEVICE.")
(comment 240VoltDevice "The collection of electrical devices that are designed to work exclusively with 240 volts (The actual acceptable voltage varies somewhat but is close to the 240 volt standard).")
(comment DeviceTypeByVoltageRequirement "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection and a specialization of #$ArtifactType.  Each instance of DeviceTypeByVoltageRequirement is a collection of devices grouped together according to their voltage requirements.")
(comment ComputerHardwareDeviceConnector "The collection of physical connectors that connect electronic devices together.  This collection covers all types of these connectors male or female.  Note that this collection is orthogonal to the collection of computer/device ports or the associated cabling.  The port itself is associated with a particular connector type -- e.g. RS 232, but the connector type does not necessarily define the port type.  In addition both the port and the connection cable have connectors of a particular type which, if compatible with each other, have the opposite sexes.")
(comment AttachmentUnitInterface "A 15 pin connector from an ethernet source to a signal transciever.")
(comment Firewire-IEEE1394-6CircuitConnector "The collection of 6 circuit (4 data + 2 power) connectors to firewire ports.")
(comment TypeNConnector-50Ohm "The collection of 50 ohm Type N connectors.")
(comment Mini-DB50Connector "The collection of Mini DB-50 connectors.")
(comment DB-50Connector "The collection of DB-50 connectors.")
(comment SCSI-25-Connector "The collection of SCSI-25 connectors.")
(comment ST2-Type-Connector "The collection of ST2 Type connectors.")
(comment SFP-Plus_2pr-Connector "The collection of SFP+_2pr connectors")
(comment V-dot-35-Connector "The collection of V.35 connectors")
(comment SFP-Plus_4pr-Connector "The collection of SFP+_4pr connectors")
(comment HardwareDeviceConnector-Female "The collection of device connectors that are \"female\".")
(comment HardwareDeviceConnector-Male "The collection of device connectors that are \"male\".")
(comment ADTRANInc "ADTRAN Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  ADTRAN, Inc. is a global provider of networking and communications equipment for use in the last mile of telecommunications networks. ADTRAN networking equipment solutions enable voice, data, video, and Internet communications across copper, fiber, and wireless network infrastructures. ADTRAN is headquartered in Huntsville, Alabama.")
(comment EvertzLtd "Evertz Ltd is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Founded in 1966, Evertz is headquartered in Burlington, Canada, and is a broadcast equipment designer.")
(comment BluecoatSystemsInc "BluecoatSystemsInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  (NASDAQ: BCSI) is a network security and network management company based in Sunnyvale, California.")
(comment TransitionNetworksInc "Transition Networks Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Transition Networks, Inc. develops, manufactures, and distributes hardware-based connectivity solutions in the European market.")
(comment ShunraInc "Shunra Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  A pioneer in WAN emulation, Shunra is also a leader in APE.")
(comment FoundryInc "Foundry Networks, Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  It was a networking hardware vendor selling high-end Ethernet switches and routers. The company was founded in 1996 by Bobby R. Johnson.")
(comment ArubaInc "Aruba Networks, Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Aruba Networks, Inc in Sunnyvale, CA is a public company categorized under Mobile Communication Equipment.")
(comment MellanoxInc "Mellanox is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Founded in 1999, Mellanox Technologies is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California and Yokneam, Israel.")
(comment NetscoutInc "NetscoutInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  NetScout Systems, Inc. is a provider of end-to-end network and application assurance.")
(comment AzulInc "AzulInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Azul Networks L.L.C. Azul Networks L.L.C. has a location in The Woodlands, TX.")
(comment NiksunInc "NiksunInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  he company was founded in 1997 by CEO Parag Pruthi.")
(comment CeloxicaInc "CeloxicaInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Provides the unique Accelerator Card by Celoxica and our development of function-specific, optimised firmware which plugs into an industry standard server.  Began as a technology spin-out from Oxford University in 1996, satisfying processor-intensive and performance-hungry tasks for a wide range of industries including oil, gas and the life sciences.")
(comment AxisCommunications "AxisInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Axis is an IT company offering network video solutions for professional installations.")
(comment NetOpticInc "NetOpticInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Founded in April 1996 by Eldad Matityahu, Net Optics is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.")
(comment CanaryInc "CanaryInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.")
(comment APCONInc "APCONInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  APCON, Inc. develops and provides packet aggregation switching solutions. The company offers IntellaPatch, a data aggregation and filtering system for enterprise networks. ")
(comment RADInc "RADInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Founded in 1981, RAD Data Communications is an industry leader in access solutions for data and telecommunications applications.")
(comment ScannexInc "ScannexInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Manufacturer was Feet Computer Systems, Germany, c. 1993")
(comment ArborInc "ArborInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Arbor Networks is a global provider of DDoS attack protection, network security and visibility solutions.")
(comment 3PARInc "3PARInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  3PAR Inc. is a manufacturer of systems and software for data storage and information management headquartered in Fremont, California, USA.")
(comment RiverbedInc "RiverbedInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  WAN optimization, Application acceleration, WAN bandwidth optimization, and IT consolidation.")
(comment AmuletInc "AmuletInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Amulet invented the Graphical Operating System in Silicon.")
(comment CycladesInc "CycladesInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Cyclades Corporation in Fremont, CA is a private company categorized under Integrated Circuits, Semiconductor Networks, Etc.")
(comment AlliedTelesisInc "AlliedTelesisInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Allied Telesis delivers IP/Ethernet network solutions.")
(comment InternetSecuritySystemsInc "InternetSecuritySystemsInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  On 23 August 2006, IBM announced its intention to acquire Internet Security Systems for $1.3 billion.")
(comment Force10Inc "Force10 Inc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Force10 Networks virtualizes Ethernet networks.  Force10's world headquarters is located in San Jose, California.")
(comment AcopiaInc "AcopiaInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Data Solutions (formerly Acopia) switch.")
(comment AristaInc "AristaInc is a company that is associated with Network Interface cards.  Arista Networks (formerly Arastra) builds and sells 10 Gigabit Ethernet switches for cloud-computing data centers. At the core of Arista's platform is the Extensible Operating System (EOS), a software architecture with self-healing and live in-service software upgrade capabilities.")
(comment AudioVisualDevice-InternetTelephony "The collection of all consumer electronic products with the ability to transmit and or receive digital audio or video signals that are transmitted via IP (#$InternetProtocol).  Many of these devices can also handle analog audio and visual data.")
(disjointWith HardwareDeviceConnector-Male HardwareDeviceConnector-Female)
(comment ComputerPort-Logical-IndexNotFixed "The collection of all collections of logical hardware ports in which all the configurable parameters are fixed except for their various index numbers.")
(comment hardwareGroupGroupModelPosition "relates a #$ComputerHardwareGroupType to a reified model position.")
(comment AutoDuplex-CommunicationCapability "A type device.  Each instance of this collection is a device that is able to communication via the \"auto-duplex\" communication mode for network communication.  In auto-duplex mode the device determines the best or most appropriate duplex mode to operate via negotiation with its communication partner.")
(comment HalfDuplex-CommunicationCapability "A type device.  Each instance of this collection is a device that is able to communication via the \"half-duplex\" communication mode for network communication.  In half-duplex mode a device can send and receive, but not at the same time.")
(comment FullDuplex-CommunicationCapability "A type device.  Each instance of this collection is a device that is able to communication via the \"full-duplex\" communication mode for network communication.  In full-duplex mode a device can send and receive data at the same time.")
(comment DeviceTypeByDuplexMode "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of devices that share a particular communication mode -- full duplex, half duplex, or auto.")
(comment DeviceTypeByDataTransferSpeed "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of devices that share a particular data speed capability -- 10 mbits/sec, 100 mbits/sec, 1000 mbits/sec, etc.")
(comment 10Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that operate at 10 mbits/sec.")
(comment 100Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that operate at 100 mbits/sec.")
(comment 1000Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that operate at 1000 mbits/sec.")
(comment DeviceTypeByPurpose "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of devices that share a particular networking purpose such as \"Host\" or \"Span\" (Switched Port Analyzer).")
(comment Span-SwitchedPortAnalyzer "A collection of devices that use the Cisco method of port mirroring called \"Switched Port Analyzer\".")
(comment Host-NetworkDevicePurpose "A collection of devices that use the Cisco method of port mirroring called \"Switched Port Analyzer\".")
(comment GigabitEthernetPort "The collection of all gigabit ethernet ports. A type of #$EthernetPort.")
(comment PortTypeByFamily "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports that share a particular class of attributes.")
(comment PortTypeByEncapsulation "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports that share a particular type of encapsulation.")
(comment Dot1Q-Encapsulation "the collection of device ports running the industry standard Dot1Q trunking protocol.")
(comment NoNetworkEncapsulation "the collection of device ports setup without any encapsulation.")
(comment ComputerPortConnectorType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of connectors for computer ports.")
(comment PortTypeByProtocol "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports that share a particular protocol -- e.g. ethernet.")
(comment PortTypeByAdministrativeStatus "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports that share a particular class of attributes.")
(comment Down-PortAdministrativeStatus "The collection of computer ports in the \"down\" administrative state.")
(comment Up-PortAdministrativeStatus "The collection of computer ports in the \"up\" administrative state.")
(comment PortTypeByInferfaceType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports instantiated via a particular type of interface.")
(comment PhysicalInterface-ComputerPort "The collection of computer ports realized via physical interfaces (e.g. as opposed to virtual or sub-interfaces).")
(comment VirtualInterface-ComputerPort "The collection of computer ports realized via virtual interfaces.")
(comment Sub-Interface-ComputerPort "The collection of computer ports realized via sub-interfaces.")
(comment AggregateInterface-ComputerPort "The collection of computer ports realized via aggregate interfaces.")
(comment Management-NetworkDevicePurpose "A collection of devices whose networking purpose is management.")
(comment AutoNegotiate-10mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that are setup to operate at 10 mb/sec and auto-negotiate the connection speed.")
(comment AutoNegotiate-100mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that are setup to operate at 100 mb/sec and auto-negotiate the connection speed.")
(comment AutoNegotiate-1000mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that are setup to operate at 1000 mb/sec and auto-negotiate the connection speed.")
(comment AutoNegotiate_10-100Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that are set up to operate at either 10 or 100 Mb/sec and are set to auto-negotiate the connection speed.")
(comment AutoNegotiate_10-100-1000Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that are set up to operate at either 10, 100, or 1000 Mb/sec and are set to auto-negotiate the speed of data exchange.")
(comment 10000Mb-sec "The collection of networking devices that operate at 10000 mbits/sec.")
(comment specificationForTypeWithID "This is the corresponding predicate to #$SpecificationForTypeFn.")
(comment Proc3 "Stub for model building purposes")
(comment Proc4 "Stub for model building purposes")
(comment Proc5 "Stub for model building purposes")
(comment Stor2 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment PS3 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment IO3 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment IO4 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment IO5 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment IO6 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice ComputerStorageDevice-NonMemory)
(comment ComputerStorageDevice-NonMemory "The collection of devices used by computers to store information other than internal computer memory, e.g., floppy disks, direct access storage devices (DASD), optical disk devices, microfilm libraries, and 5.25 inch hard drives.")
(comment PS4 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment PS5 "Stub for modeling purposes")
(comment portRangeUnused "relates a logical port specification to an integer range of ports that are unused or not specified.  Note that this only needs to be used if the unused port numbers lie between used port numbers.  E.g. If the #$maxNumberForPortSpec = 48 and #$minNumberForPortSpec = 1, but ports 32-40 are unassigned, then (#$portRangeUnused SPEC (#$IntervalRangeFn 32 40)) holds.")
(comment NetworkPort-Physical "The collection of all physical network ports.  Each instance of this collection is a port on a device that is intended to connect the device to a network of some sort.")
(comment ThalesInc "Thales e-Security is a company that is associated with encryption devices and data security.")
(comment Device-Logical "Each instance of this collection is an artifact or a system of artifacts essentially associated with a specification of how it is configured and used.")
(comment modelPositionComponentHasNoUserConfigurableOptions "relates a #$HardwareGroupModelPosition to a component that has no user choices or configuration options.")
(comment PortTypeByAbstraction "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer ports that share a particular abstraction  -- physical, logical, etc.")
(comment numberOfInputCordsetsForProductType "relates a type of artifact to the number of input cordsets found in instances of that artifact.")
(comment numberOfCordsForProductType "relates a type of artifact to the number of cords found in instances of that artifact.")
(comment electricalInputDrawForType "relates a type of electrical device to the amount of electrical current instances of that type draw.")
(comment specificationHasRequiredChoiceSet "(#$specificationHasRequiredChoiceSet SPEC SET) means that each member of SET is a sub-specification of SPEC (see #$specificationHasAssociatedSubSpec), each of them is \"optional\", but any build of SPEC must include the components specified by at least one member of SET.")
(comment specificationHasMutuallyExclusiveChoiceSet "(#$specificationHasMutuallyExclusiveChoiceSet SPEC SET) means that each member of SET is a sub-specification of SPEC (see #$specificationHasAssociatedSubSpec), each is \"Optional\", but any build of SPEC must include the components specified by exactly one member of SET.")
(comment developerNotes "A #$DocumentationPredicate (q.v.) that is used to relate additional information about the CycL concept above and beyond what is appropriate for #$comments.")
(comment AtLeastOne "A positive integer range that denotes the range of integers from 1 to #$PlusInfinity.")
(comment ExactlyOne "A positive integer range that denotes the range of integers from 1 to #$PlusInfinity.")
(comment CardinalityQuantType "A collection of reified scalar intervals that are used to display cardinality constraints for various purposes.")
(comment NetworkDevice-Composite "A configured network device type associated with policies with additional configuration details not specified by the #$ComputerHardwareGroupType.")
(comment networkDeviceTypeUtilizesHardwareGroupType "Relates a #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType to an instance of #$ComputerHardwareGroupType.")
(comment LogicalPortSpecification "A subcollection of #$DeviceConfigurationSpecification.  Each instance of This collection is a specification of a set of logical ports associated with a component in a #$HardwareComponentSpecification.")
(comment OtherNetworkDevice "A context dependent collection of network devices whose extent is typically determined by UI menu choices.")
(comment electricalInputDraw "relates an electrical device to the amount of electrical current it draws.")
(comment minimumPowerCordRatingForDevice "relates an electrical device to the lower bound of the power rating for its cord.")
(comment powerCordRatingMinimumForType "relates an electrical device type to the lower bound of the power rating for its cord.")
(comment maxBandwidthOfDevice "relates an electrical device to the lower bound of the power rating for its cord.")
(comment maxBandwidthOfDevice "relates an artifact to its maximum communication bandwidth rate.")
(comment measuredAveragePowerOfDevice "relates an electrical device to its measured average power.")
(comment measuredMaximumPowerOfDevice "relates an electrical device to its measured maximum power.")
(comment wattageRatingForPowerSupplyOfDevice "relates an electrical device to the wattage rating of its power supply.")
(comment rackUnits "relates a rack-mounted device to the number of \"rack-units\" it requires.")
(comment Vershok "A #$UnitOfDistance.  One vershok = 1.75 inches.  This is equivalent to one \"rack unit\".")
(comment ComponentCardSpecification "A subcollection of #$DeviceConfigurationSpecification.  Each instance of This collection is a specification of a hardware component card and is linked to a #$HardwareComponentSlotPosition.")
(comment specificationHasConditionalSpecification "(#$specificationHasConditionalSpecification INDEPENDENT DEPENDENT) means that if INDEPENDENT is selected as an option for the build, then DEPENDENT must also be selected.  This is a (trivially) reflexive and transitive relation.  Note that either INDEPENDENT or DEPENDENT can be associated with a single or multiple hardware components (or cards).")
(comment conditionallyExcludedSpecification "(#$conditionallyExcludedSpecification SPEC-1 SPEC-2) means that if SPEC-1 is chosen, then SPEC-2 cannot be chosen.  This imposes an additional constraint on model builds above and beyond those given by other conditional associations and mutually exclusive choice sets.")
(comment compatibleSpecifications "(#$compatibleSpecifications SPEC-1 SPEC-2) means that SPEC-1 and SPEC-2 are associated with the same hardware group model and that using both specifications in the build is consistent will all model constraints -- i.e. it is not the case that #$incompatibleSpecifications holds of SPEC-1 and SPEC-2.")
(comment specificationHasUnusableSubSpecification "relates a DeviceConfigurationSpecification to a reified specification that, because of various constraints asserted about the model, is unsatisfiable or unusable as a subspecification of that specification.")
(comment specificationForPositionHasIncompatibleComponent "holds of a component position and a device specification when the specification has an associated hardware component (see #$specificationHasHardwareComponentOption) that is incompatible with that position  -- e.g. the position is associated with a slot on a device and the associated card that the specification configures is not known to be compatible with that slot type (See #$card_type_compatible_with_slot_type).")
(comment incompatibleSpecifications "(#$incompatibleSpecifications SPEC-1 SPEC-2) means that given the constraints present in the model SPEC-1 and SPEC-2 cannot be used together in any build.  The most common constraint violation would be when a particular choice would require-- because of other choices and conditional relations (see #$specificationHasConditionalSpecification) a selection of more or less than one specification from the mutually exclusive choice set (#$specificationHasMutuallyExclusiveChoiceSet).")
(comment modelEntityLinkedToModelEntity "a very general predicate that is the common generalization of any binary predicate that links \"nodes\" together in a graph.")
(comment GraphConstraintConcept "The collection of concepts that are part of a generic graph constraint checking system implemented via rules in #$GenericGraphConstraintMt.")
(comment setOfConstraintViolationPairsRecursivelyDown "(#$setOfConstraintViolationPairsRecursivelyDown NODE SET) means that SET is the set of things that stand in the arg2 of #$graphConstraintViolated to some entity linked downward from NODE.")
(comment ConstraintConditionPredicate "The collection of #$GraphConstraintConcepts that are predicates designed to state some constraint of the graph -- e.g. that to be a valid link requires some condition hold.")
(comment CardinalityGraphConstraintPredicate "The collection of #$GraphConstraintConcepts that are predicates designed to state some cardinality constraint on the number of entities standing in certain model relations.")
(comment constraintVersionOf "(#$constraintVersionOf KNOWLEDGE-PRED CONSTRAINT-PRED) means that CONSTRAINT-PRED is the \"constraint\" correlate to KNOWLEDGE-PRED in the operative context.  This means that unlike KNOWLEDGE-PRED whose assertion in a context means that the described relationship holds, the assertions of CONSTRAINT-PRED in a context means that it a condition of model validity or model goodness, etc. that the described relationship holds, but there is no assumption that it in fact holds.  This predicate faciliates the conversion of KNOWLEDGE-PRED assertions in some strong assumptions Mt -- an Mt that describes an ideal situation or model, to the domain Mt where they are interpreted as constraints on the model as opposed to a description of how the model actually is.")
(comment idealWorldMicrotheoryMt "(#$idealWorldMicrotheoryMt IDEAL-MT CONSTRAINT-MT) means that IDEAL-MT has declarative statements that describe an ideal situation, model, or graph in the sense that its statements describe relationships that would hold in the \"best case\" or only in valid models, etc. CONSTRAINT-MT is a real world/model constraint MT where the ideal statements in IDEAL-MT have been converted into constraints in the model via #$constraintVersionOf.  E.g. if (#$constraintVersionOf PRED CONSTRAINT-PRED) holds in CONSTRAINT-MT and (#$idealWorldMicrotheoryMt IDEAL-MT CONSTRAINT-MT), then assertions of the form (ist IDEAL-MT (PRED ARG1, ... ARGN)) can be automatically converted into assertions of the form (ist CONSTRAINT-MT (CONSTRAINT-PRED ARG1, ... ARGN)).")
(comment (SpecificationForTypeFn Switch-Network "Linked LP Spec has no min/max port numbers") "Tests that specifications with a linked LP spec with no max port number assertion are returned as violations.")
(comment LogicalPortOrSpecification "This is the common generalization of #$ComputerPort-Logical and #$LogicalPortSpecification.")
(comment LogicalPortForSpecFn "(#$LogicalPortForSpecFn SPEC NUM NAME) denotes the logical port associated with SPEC numbered NUM with NAME.")
(comment slotTypeForComponentType "A generalization of #$slot_type_for_device_type and #$slot_type_for_card_type")
(comment Winemaking "The activity of producing wine.")
(comment Snifter "Distinctively-shaped glass used for drinking aged brown spirits.")
(comment Myxococcales "A #$BiologicalOrder, commonly known as \"myxobacteria\" or \"slime bacteria\".")
(comment Hallux "The innermost toe, commonly called the \"big toe\".")
(comment plausibleQueriesJustified "<code>(#$plausibleQueriesJustified 
ABSTRACT-STRUCTURE QUERY-SPEC JUSTIFICATION)</code> means that when testing 
knowledge of <code>ABSTRACT-STRUCTURE</code> it makes sense to ask <code>QUERY-
SPEC</code> because <code>JUSTIFICATION</code> is part of the answer.")
(comment DegreeRankine "The standard unit of temperature in the Rankine scale.")
(comment nthThermalCycleForReportingPurposes "(#$nthThermalCycleForReportingPurposes WELL EVENT N) means that EVENT is the Nth warming stage of a thermal cycle in the well WELL, since the last time a series of 5 cycles terminated.")
(comment LogicalSchemaMappedToMultipleKSs "The collection of all #$LogicalSchemas that are mapped to more than one knowledge source, usually because each mapped KS is a #$subKS of a primary knowledge source to which the logical schema belongs.")
(comment InheritingGene "Each instance of #$InheritingGene is an event in which the biological offspring of an organism inherits a gene from one of its parents.  From the perspective of the parent, such events are considered to be the passing on of genes to their offspring.")
(comment CausationWithinCellSignalingProcesses "The collection of chemical processes in which the causation occurs within Cell Signaling processes.")
(comment EnzymaticActivity-Muscle-LiverCellLocus "The collection of instances of #$EnzymaticActivity in which the locus of the process is some #$SkeletalMyocyte or #$Hepatocyte)) ")
(comment cycLHasTopicVia "<code>(#$cycLHasTopicVia CYCL TOPIC CONCEPT) means that the content of the CycL expression (a sentence, assertion, term, etc.) strongly relates to TOPIC by virtue of CONCEPT.")
(comment QuestionCategorizationTopic-Intermediate "The collection of situation types that are used to classify CycL content as relating at least to some non-trivial degree to that situation.")
(comment QuestionCategorizationTopicConcept "The collection of concepts that relate to categorizing CycL concepts and assertions in the context of query suggestion")
(comment QuestionCategorizationTopic "The collection of situation types that are used to classify CycL content as strongly relating to that situation.")
(comment SituationPredTopicFn "(#$SituationPredTopicFn SIT-TYPE PRED) denotes the situation type in which the instances are \"about\" (in some strong sense) the things that stand in PRED to some instance of SIT-TYPE.  This is used in classifying CycL assertions and concepts as being \"about\", in some strong sense, the returned situation type.  E.g. (#$SituationPredTopicFn #$BowlingActivity #$eventOccursAt) denotes, by definition, the collection of situations that are about places where bowling occurs.")
(comment EarlyMitoticSpindle "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$SpindleApparatus is an assembly of #$Microtubules and proteins that facilitates chromosome movement during either #$Mitosis of #$Meiosis.")
(comment ChangeInValueReturnedByFn "Where <code>FN</code> is a parametric function whose value for admitted
argument <code>ARG</code> changes over time, <code>(#$ChangeInValueReturnedByFn FN ARG COMPARE)</code>
denotes the collection of all events in which the
<code>#$NumericComparisonPredicate COMPARE</code> holds between the value returned
by <code>FN</code> for <code>ARG</code> at the start of the event and the value returned by <code>FN</code>
for <code>ARG</code> at the end of the event.  E.g. where 
<p>
<pre>
(#$FunctionToArg 2
(#$Kappa (?X ?Y) (#$priceChargedFor ?X Petroleum-CrudeOil ?Y)))</pre></p> is
used to represent the function that denotes the price of oil in a
given region in a temporal context,

<p>
<pre>
(#$ChangeInValueReturnedByFn                                                                                  
(#$FunctionToArg 2                                                                                  
(#$Kappa (?X ?Y) (#$priceChargedFor ?X Petroleum-CrudeOil ?Y)))                                    
#$Bahrain #$greaterThan)                                                                            
</pre>
</p>

denotes the collection of all events in which the price of oil in Bahrain                            
is greater at the end of the event than at the start.")
(comment statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement "(#$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement OUTPUTS and the #$ComputerCodeStatement INPUTS are both subsumed in a a common program with a control flow structure such that OUTPUTS specifies an operation on the value of an expression, which in turn is referenced by INPUTS in a way that specifies an operation to be carried out on this value as the very next step in the execution of the program.")
(comment statementOutputsIndirectlyToStatement "(#$statementOutputsIndirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS) is true if and only if (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) is true and (#$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS) is false.  That is, (#$statementOutputsIndirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS) holds just in case OUTPUTS and INPUTS are part of common program whose control flow entails a chain of operations between OUTPUTS and INPUTS, each link of which involves passing a value to the next statement to be executed via an expression, where a value given to INPUTS is determined by this chain, and where this value and the expression used to convey it do not pass directly from OUTPUTS to INPUTS in the sequence of statements.")
(comment statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack-Transitive "(#$statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) and that at least one of the specificatory links in the chain of operation specifications between OUTPUTS and INPUTS in the program control flow involves an input-output statement pair A, B, such that (#$statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack A B).")
(comment statementOutputsToStatementExclusivelyThroughStack-Transitive "(#$statementOutputsToStatementExclusivelyThroughStack-Transitve OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) and, for every pair of statements A, B, such that (#$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement A B) in the chain between OUTPUTS and INPUTS, it is true that (statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack A B).  That is, the specification of INPUTS uses an input value that results from a chain of 'hand-off' specifications in which OUTPUTS is involved, and where every specification specifies that a certain value be placed in an expression on the stack which the next specification in the chain uses.")
(comment statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack "(#$statementOutputsToStatementThroughStack OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that (#$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS), and that this is done by means of OUTPUTS specifying placement of a certain value into a certain stack expression where INPUTS specifies retrieval of this value from the same stack expression.")
(comment statementTransmitsValueToStatementThroughIntermediates "(#$statementTransmitsValueToStatementThroughIntermediates OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that (#$statementOutputsIndirectlyToStatement OUTPUTS INPUTS) and that a value that is operated on in some way by OUTPUTS (e.g., by initializing an expression to have that value) is eventually specified to be passed to INPUTS as an input via the chain of operation specifications between OUTPUTS and INPUTS in the program control flow.")
(comment statementTransmitsValueToStatementViaExpression "(#$statementTransmitsValueToStatementViaExpression means that (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS), and that a value which is associated with a certain expression by OUTPUTS is eventually given as an input to INPUTS using that same expression, via the chain of operation specifications between OUTPUTS and INPUTS in the program control flow.")
(comment suppliesValueFromStatementToMethodInNthArg "(#$suppliesValueFromStatementToMethodInNthArg FN-CALL OUTPUT METHOD N) means that the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL calls METHOD (#$codingFunctionInvoked) and that it uses an expression to supply the Nth argument of METHOD that is directly assigned its value by OUTPUT.")
(comment IncapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel "This is the subcollection of those #$IncapabilityPredicates whose first argument is a specialization of #$Individual.  These predicates are 'type-level' because they assert something about the capabilities of a type of thing, rather than an individual.  Contrast #$IncapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel.")
(comment IncapabilityPredicate "This is a collection of #$TernaryPredicates which assert <i>lack of</i> capabilities of different sorts, and all of which can be generalized in the same way on their second and third argument places..")
(comment IncapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel "This is the subcollection of those #$IncapabilityPredicates whose first argument #$isa #$Individual.")
(comment topicHasFocalConcept "(#$topicHasFocalConcept TOPIC CONCEPT) means that TOPIC -- a specialization of #$Situation has CONCEPT as one of its major role players.\"")
(comment 2DPointXValueFn "<code>(#$2DPointXValueFn POINT)</code> denotes the \"x\" value of the 2D point <code>POINT</code>. Thus <code>(#$2DPointXValueFn (#$The2DPoint 5 7))</code> denotes 5. ")
(comment 2DPointYValueFn "<code>(#$2DPointYValueFn POINT)</code> denotes the \"Y\" value of the 2D point <code>POINT</code>.  Thus <code>(#$2DPointYValueFn (#$The2DPoint 5 7))</code> denotes 7.")
(comment behaviorCapable-DoneBy "This predicate relates objects to the kinds of activites instances of which they are capable of playing the #$doneBy role.  See also #$behaviorCapable.")
(comment behaviorIncapable-DoneBy "This predicate relates objects to the kinds of activites instances of which they are incapable of playing the #$doneBy role.  See also #$behaviorIncapable.")
(comment ProgramExecution-Complete "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein the #$codeExecuted is a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS.")
(disjointWith AllocationOfResources DeallocationOfResources)
(comment DeallocationOfResources "The collection of all events in which a resources or a set or collection of resources, that had been committed for use in a specific task, is freed up for usage in other tasking.")
(comment DeallocationOfComputerMemory "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein one or more #$ComputerMemoryLocations that had been allocated for use in a particular program task are freed from commitment to that task.")
(comment DeallocationOfComputerStorage "The collection of all instances of #$DeallocationOfComputerMemory that involve a measurable decrease in #$computerAccountStorageShare for some #$ComputerAccount.")
(comment AllocationOfComputerMemory "The collection of all #$ProgramActions wherein one or more #$ComputerMemoryLocations are commited for use for a particular program task.")
(comment resourceAllocated "(#$resourceAllocated ALLOCATION ITEM) means that in ALLOCATION, ITEM is committed, and possibly configured, for playing an 'input' role of some kind in a task that has yet to be performed relative to ALLOCATION (and that may or may not ever be performed).")
(comment resourceDeallocated "(#$resourceDeallocated DEALLOCATION ITEM) means that in DEALLOCATION, ITEM is freed from being committed to (and possibly configured for) a task to which it was previously committed.")
(comment memoryAllocated "(#$memoryAllocated MEM-ALLOC LOC) means that the #$ComputerMemoryLocation LOC is committed for a program execution-related task in MEM-ALLOC.")
(comment memoryDeallocated "(#$memoryDeallocated MEM-DEALLOC LOC) means that the #$ComputerMemoryLocation LOC, having previously been committed for a program execution-related task in some #$AllocationOfComputerMemory, is deallocated for that task in the #$DeallocationOfComputerMemory MEM-DEALLOC.")
(comment AttemptingToReturnAMemoryResourceWithAnIncompatibleFunction "The collection of all unsuccessful attempts to deallocate computer memory wherein the failure comes about because the #$MemoryDeallocationFunction used in the attempted deallocation is incompatible with the #$MemoryAllocationFunction that was originally used in committing the #$ComputerMemoryLocation or locations involved.")
(comment MemoryAllocationFunction "The collection of all #$MemoryManagementFunctions that serve to allocate #$ComputerMemoryLocations for tasks.")
(comment MemoryDeallocationFunction "The collection of all #$MemoryManagementFunctions that serve to deallocate #$ComputerMemoryLocations from tasks to which they have been committed.")
(comment complementaryMemoryManagementFunctions "#$complementaryMemoryManagementFunctions is the predicate that holds by definiiton of any pair of #$MemoryManagementFunctions such that one member of the pair is a #$MemoryDeallocationFunction and the other is a #$MemoryAllocationFunction, regardless of order.")
(comment compatibleMemoryManagementFunctions "Where FN and COMP-FN are #$complementaryMemoryManagementFunctions, (#$compatibleMemoryManagementFunctions FN COMP-FN) is true just in case the member of the pair which is a #$MemoryDeallocationFunction can be used to deallocate the same block of memory allocated by the member of the pair which is a #$MemoryAllocationFunction in a given program, without #$UndesirableProgramActions resulting from the specification in executions of that program.")
(comment incompatibleMemoryManagementFunctions "Where FN and COMP-FN are #$complementaryMemoryManagementFunctions, (#$incompatibleMemoryManagementFunctions FN COMP-FN) means that if the member of the pair which is a #$MemoryAllocationFunction is used in a program to allocate a block of memory, using the complementary member of the pair (the #$MemoryDeallocationFunction) to deallocate that same block of memory in the same program will create a specification such that executions of the program will be liable to a number of #$UndesirableProgramActions, with types including #$ProgramActionWitoutInternalTerminationProvision, #$DataCorruption-ProgramAction, and #$ArbitraryCodeExecution.")
(comment deallocatesSameMemBlockAsAllocated "(#$deallocatesSameMemBlockAsAllocated DEALLOCATION-CALL ALLOCATION-CALL) means that DEALLOCATION-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that calls a #$MemoryDeallocationFunction on the same block of memory that the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable ALLOCATION-CALL calls a #$MemoryAllocationFunction on.")
(comment wellHasDistanceTemperaturePointSetOnDate "<code>(#$wellHasDistanceTemperaturePointSetOnDate WELL SET DATE)</code> means that a set <code>SET</code> measurements that are represented as the set of points that are ordered depth (#$Distance) and temperature (#$Temperature) tuples apply to the well <code>WELL</code> on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment GeneticVariation "#$GeneticVariation is the amount of variation in the genes in a population of organisms.  A population of clones has a low amount of #$GeneticVariation.  Sexual reproduction and mutation lead to increases in genetic variation.")
(comment populationHasGeneticVariation "(#$populationHasGeneticVariation POP VAR) means that the population of organisms <code>POP</code> has the genetic variation <code>VAR</code>.")
(comment EarlySpindle "A specialization of #$SpindleStructure, this is the collection of all such structures that are in early stages of development in the #$SpindleApparatusAssembly process, prior to undergoing sufficent state change (see #$objectOfStateChange) to count as a full-blown #$SpindleApparatus.")
(comment biologicallyResponsibleFor "A specialization of #$biologicalFunction, <code>(#$biologicallyResponsibleFor BLO-TYPE EVENT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that not only is it a #$biologicalFunction of objects of type ?BLO-TYPE to play the role <code>ROLE</code> in events of type <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, <i>only</i> objects of type <code>BLO-TYPE</code> can play this role. So while small esophagus, small intestine, and stomach all have as biological functions the moving of food through the digestive tract, only the heart has the biological function of, and thus is responsible for, pumping blood.")
(comment setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints "<code>(#$setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints SET-OF-POINTS FUNCTION-TYPE SET-OF-DERIVATIVE-POINTS)</code> means that if one takes <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code> and generates a curve <code>C</code> from it using an instance of <code>FUNCTION-TYPE</code>, then <code>SET-OF-DERIVATIVE-POINTS</code> is the set of points on the first derivative of <code>C</code> with respect to the values of the points in <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code>.  For example, <code>(#$setOfFirstDerivativePointsBasedOnSetOfPoints (#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint A B) (#$The2DPoint C D)) #$CubicSpline 2  (#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint P B) (#$The2DPoint Q D)))</code> would mean <code>(#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint P B) (#$The2DPoint Q D))</code> are points on the line defined by the equation for the first derivative with respect to Y (i.e. the arg 2 value of #$The2DPoint) of the curve produced by cubic spline interpolation on <code>(#$TheSet (#$The2DPoint A B) (#$The2DPoint C D))</code>.")
(comment cycLHasTopicVia-Candidate "(#$cycLHasTopicVia-Candidate CYCL TOPIC CONCEPT) means that the content of the CycL expression (a sentence, assertion, term, etc.) is a candidate for being strongly related to TOPIC by virtue of CONCEPT.")
(comment cycLHasTopic "(#$cycLHasTopic CYCL TOPIC) means that the content of the CycL expression (a sentence, assertion, term, etc.) strongly relates to TOPIC.\"")
(comment The-Unreifiable "An ureifiable version of #$The.")
(comment ShorteningOfKinetochoreMicrotubule "The collection of events in which instances of #$Microtubule that are part of a #$SpindleApparatus and are connected to (see #$connectedTo) a #$Kinetochore shorten.")
(comment MotorProteinMovementAlongStructure "The collection of events in which a motor protein moves along the surface of a chemical object.")
(comment MotorProteinMovementAlongMicrotubule "The collection of events in which a motor protein moves along the surface of a #$Microtubule that is attached to a #$Kinetochore.")
(comment SpindleElongation "The collection of events in which a #$SpindleStructure grows until a full-blows #$SpindleApparatus is formed.")
(comment ElongationOfSpindleMicrotubule "The collection of events in which a #$Microtubule attached to a #$Centrosome elongates, through  #$IncorporationOfTubulinIntoMicrotubule events.")
(comment IncorporationOfTubulinIntoMicrotubule "The collection of events in which a #$Microtubule combines with a #$TubulinMolecule.")
(comment wellHasAverageTemperatureInLinerAtDate "<code>(#$wellHasAverageTemperatureInLinerAtDate WELL TEMP DATE)</code> means the average teperature in the well <code>WELL</code> at <code>DATE</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment MapFunctionOverListUntilResult "This function applies a unary (evaluatable) function <code>F</code> to each element in a given list <code>L</code> until the result satisfies a certain test condition, at which point the list of results (up to and including the result of the succesfull input) is returned.  If no element of <code>L</code> is such that applying <code>F</code> to it results in something that satisfies the test condition, no value is returned.
<p>
For example, asking 
<pre>
  (#$evaluate ?VAR 
       (#$MapFunctionOverListUntilResult #$SquaredFn (#$TheList 1 2 3 4 5)
                                   (#$Kappa (?X) (#$greaterThan ?X 7))))
</pre>
will return the binding (#$TheList 1 4 9) for <code>?VAR</code>, because applying #$SquaredFn to 1 yields 1, which is less than 7, applying $SquaredFn to 2 yields 4, which is also less than 7, but applying #$SquaredFn to 3 yields 9, which is greater than 7.  Since applying #$SquaredFn to 3  yields a result that satisfies the test condition, it is not necessary to calculate the result of applying #$SquaredFn to 4 or 5.  Instead, upon applying #$SquaredFn to 3 and determining that the result passes the test condition, the function evaluation halts and returns (#$TheList 1 4 9) as a binding for <code>?VAR</code>.
<p>
C.f. the similar function #$MapFunctionOverListUntil.")
(comment MapFunctionOverListUntil "This function applies a unary (evaluatable) function <code>F</code> to each element in a given list <code>L</code> until the input satisfies a certain test condition, at which point the list of results (up to and including the result of the succesfull input) is returned.  If no element of <code>L</code> satisfies the test condition, no value is returned.<p>
For example, asking:
<pre>  
  (#$evaluate ?VAR        
     (#$MapFunctionOverListUntil #$SquaredFn (#$TheList 1 2 3 4 5)                                   
                                 (#$Kappa (?X) (#$greaterThan (#$SquaredFn ?X) 7))))
</pre>
will return the binding (#$TheList 1 4 9) for <code>?VAR</code>, because applying #$SquaredFn to 1 yields 1, which is less than 7, applying $SquaredFn to 2 yields 4, which is also less than 7, but applying #$SquaredFn to 3 yields 9, which is greater than 7.  Since applying #$SquaredFn to 3  yields a result that satisfies the test condition, it is not necessary to calculate the result of applying #$SquaredFn to 4 or 5.  Instead, upon applying #$SquaredFn to 3 and determining that the result passes the test condition, the function evaluation halts and returns (#$TheList 1 4 9) as a binding for <code>?VAR</code>.
<p>
C.f. the similar function #$MapFunctionOverListUntilResult.")
(comment CodeHawkAtomicInstruction "The collection of all designated sub-blocks of code comprising #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlocks in CHIBL output.  Each #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlock in a CHIBL program is composed of one and ordinarily many #$CodeHawkAtomicInstructions.")
(comment wellHasDepthTemperaturePointsInLinerAtDate "<code>(#$wellHasDepthTemperaturePointsInLinerAtDate WELL POINT DATE)</code> means <code>POINT</code> is a depth/temperature point in the liner of well <code>WELL</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasDepthTemperatureSlopesInLinerAtDate "<code>(#$wellHasDepthTemperatureSlopesInLinerAtDate WELL POINT DATE)</code> means <code>POINT</code> is a depth/temperature slope in the liner of well <code>WELL</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment sksiModulesDoomedUnlessArgBound "<code>(#$sksiModulesDoomedUnlessArgBound LOGICAL-FIELD-VALUE-FN MEANING-SENT-ASSERTION)</code> means that any SKSI module for the meaning sentence predicate in <code>MEANING-SENT-ASSERTION</code> that allows the argument position occupied by <code>LOGICAL-FIELD-VALUE-FN</code> in <code>MEANING-SENT-ASSERTION</code>to be unbound is doomed.")
(comment sksDoesNotAllowConjunctiveRemoval "<code>(#$sksDoesNotAllowConjunctiveRemoval SKS)</code> means that no conjunctive removals should be sent to <code>SKS</code> to be solved.")
(comment CodeHawkHierarchicalStatementType "A #$DisjointCollectionType.  Each instance is a type of #$ComputerCodeStatement corresponding to an organizational level in CHIBL output.")
(comment blockSubsumesInstruction "A typed specialization of #$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement. #$blockSubsumesInstruction is the relation that holds by definition between a #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlock and a #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction which it subsumes.")
(comment functionStatementSubsumesBlock "A typed specicalization of #$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement.  #$functionStatementSubsumesBlock is the relation that holds by definition bewteen a #$FunctionCallImplementationStatement and a #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlock that it subsumes.")
(comment programSubsumesFunctionStatement "A typed specialization of #$nearestProperSubsumingCodeStatement.  #$programSubsumesFunctionStatement is the relation that holds by definition between a #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS and a #$FunctionCallImplementationStatement that it subsumes.")
(comment functionStatementComputesFunction "A typed specializationof #$codingFunctionDefined.  (#$functionStatementComputesFunction FN-STATMENT FN) means that the #$FunctionCallImplementationStatement FN-STATEMENT is a specification of how to compute FN.")
(comment ClimbingOverSomething "A specialization of #$GoingOverSomething and #$LocomotionProcess-Animal (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$ClimbingOverSomething is an event in which an agent deliberately climbs over something, e.g. a #$ChainLinkFence.  In each instance of #$ClimbingOverSomething there is a proper sub-event which is a #$ClimbingUp and another proper sub-event which is a #$ClimbingDown. The agent performing the the entire \"climbing over\" action performs the cimbing on one side of the object climbed over (see #$objectClimbedOver) and performs the climbing down on the other side of the object.")
(comment Climbing "A specialization of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal.  Each instance of #$Climbing is a locomotion process, by which an animal moves upward along some steep surface through its own effort.  Notable specializations include #$ClimbingUp, #$ClimbingOverSomething and #$ClimbingDown.")
(disjointWith NursingYoung FeedingByHand)
(comment PlasmaMembraneReceptorMolecule "The collection of all #$ReceptorMolecules typically embedded in the outer membrane of cells (see #$CellMembrane).")
(comment MembraneReceptorMolecule "The collection of all #$ReceptorMolecules embedded in internal or external cellular membranes.  For those typically embedded in the plasma membrane itself, see #$PlasmaMembraneReceptorMolecule.")
(comment CellMembraneCytosolicSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of #$CellMembranes. Each #$CellMembraneCytosolicSurface is adjacent to and completely surrounds the #$Protoplasm.")
(comment NucleotideEnzymeActivationProcess "The collection of chemical processes in which some nucleotide activated or inactivated some enzyme")
(comment topicHasRelevantTestSuite "(#$topicHasRelevantTestSuite TOPIC TEST-TYPE) means that the instances of TEST-TYPE are good candidates for being closely related to TOPIC.  This, by itself, is not sufficient to infer #$cycLHasTopicVia-Candidate, but it serves as a first pass filter.")
(comment topicHasFocalPredicate "(#$topicHasFocalPredicate TOPIC PRED) means that some specPred of PRED plays a large role in describing some important feature of TOPIC -- a specialization of #$Situation.  Often one of the Topic's other focal concepts (or one of its instances) stands in PRED (or one of its specPreds).")
(disjointWith UprightPosture BentOverPosture)
(disjointWith LyingOnBackPosture BentOverPosture)
(comment PreparingFoodItemFn "<code>(#$PreparingFoodItemFn FOOD-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of events in which instances of <code>FOOD-TYPE</code> are prepared.  For example, (#$PreparingFoodItemFn #$SpaghettiMarinara) denotes the collection of events in which instances of #$SpaghettiMarinara are prepared.")
(comment preparationTypeOfFoodItemType "<code>(#$preparationTypeOfFoodItemType PREP-EVT-TYPE FOOD-TYPE)</code> means <code>PREP-EVT-TYPE</code> is the collection of events in which instances of <code>FOOD-TYPE</code> are prepared.")
(comment IntegralMonotopicProtein "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule.  Integral monotopic proteins are proteins that are permanently attached to membranes at one side.")
(disjointWith Ingesting Meiosis)
(comment genlTemplates "<code>(#$metaTemplate TEMPLATE META-TEMPLATE)</code> means that <code>META-TEMPLATE</code> is a more general template than <code>TEMPLATE</code> -- i.e., that instantiations of <code>TEMPLATE</code> are thereby instantiations of <code>META-TEMPLATE</code>.")
(comment GTPaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of hydrolyzing a #$GuanosineTriphosphate molecule to release a #$PhosphateIon and a #$GuanosineDiphosphate molecule.")
(comment MiracleWhip "The collection of all Miracle Whip. A type of #$Spread-Food and #$Emulsion. Miracle Whip is a sandwich spread manufactured and sold by Kraft.")
(comment SimpleAcrobaticMotion "A specialization of #$SimpleWholeBodyMovement, Simple acrobatic motions include whole-body movements such as cartwheels, backflips and somersaults.")
(comment Somersault "A specialization of #$SimpleAcrobaticMotion.  Each instance of #$Somersault is an acrobatic motion in which the doer completes one full forward rolling motion, beginning and ending with feet on the ground.")
(comment Cartwheel "A specialization of #$SimpleAcrobaticMotion.  Each instance of #$Cartwheel is an acrobatic motion in which the doer completes one full sideways rolling motion beginning with feet on the ground, proceeding to a state in which the hands are providing support (in the case of #$StandardCartwheels, or without hand support in the case of #$AerialCartwheels) and then ending with the feet once again on the ground.")
(comment StandardCartwheel "A specialization of #$Cartwheel.  In standard cartwheels, there is a point at which the performer is supporting himself or herself with hands on the ground (contrast this collection with #$AerialCartwheel).")
(comment BackwardRoll "A specialization of #$SimpleAcrobaticMotion.  Each instance of #$BackwardRoll is an acrobatic motion in which the performer completes one full backward rolling motion, beginning and ending with feet on the ground.")
(comment Flip "A specialization of #$SimpleAcrobaticMotion.  Each instance of #$Flip is an acrobatic motion in which the performer completes one full flipping motion.  Flips are similar to rolls in that both involve a full rotation.  However, flips also involve a period of time during which the performer is not in contact with the ground.")
(comment Backflip "A specialization of #$Flip.  In backflips, the performer flips backward from a standing position and then lands with his feet on the ground.).")
(comment AerialCartwheel "A specialization of #$Cartwheel.  In aerial cartwheels, at no point does the performer support himself or herself with hands on the ground (contrast this collection with #$StandardCartwheel).")
(comment BridalBouquet "A specialization of #$FlowerArrangement and #$PortableObject.  Bridal bouquets are floral arrangements intended to be held by brides during weddings.  There is a also a tradition involving throwing these bouquets after a wedding ceremony.")
(comment ThrowingABridalBouquet "A specialization of #$ThrowingFlowers.  Each instance of #$ThrowingABridalBouquet is an event in which a bride throws her #$BridalBouquet shortly after her wedding ceremony.")
(comment WalkingDownTheAisle "A specialization of #$SocialRitual.  Each instance of #$WalkingDownTheAisle is an event in which a bride walks down the aisle during a #$WeddingCeremony.")
(comment CellDivisionAndDistributionOfChromosonesToDaughterCells "The collection of biological processes in which DNA is replicated in the context of cell division")
(disjointWith UprightPosture SquattingPosture)
(disjointWith LyingOnBackPosture SquattingPosture)
(comment NonKinetochoreMicrotubule "A specialization of #$Microtubule, membership in which is dependent on where in a cell division process the cell that contains the microtubule is.  A #$NonKinetochoreMicrotubule is one that is \"left over\" after all of the #$MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore events take place in the relevant mitotic or meiotic event.  Such microtubules continue to grow, stretching the cell into an oblong shape, while those connected to kinetochores begin to retract.")
(disjointWith PavingARoad (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn SpreadingStuffOntoSurface stuffUsed Cream-Generic))
(comment ruleUsedInEruditeForwardInference "The collection of rules used in forward inference by the Erudite system.  If a forward rule does is not a quoted instance of this collection, it will not be run forward when processing ERUDITE documents.")
(comment VoteCounting "A specialization of #$Counting.  Each instance of #$VoteCounting is an event that occurs as part of an election.  During each instance of #$VoteCounting, votes cast during the subsuming election are counted.")
(comment earlyVoteCount "<code>(#$earlyVoteCount ELEC COUNT)</code> means that the #$VoteCounting <code>COUNT</code> is an early vote count in the #$Election <code>ELEC</code>.")
(comment finalVoteCount "<code>(#$finalVoteCount ELEC COUNT)</code> means that the #$VoteCounting <code>COUNT</code> is the final vote count in the #$Election <code>ELEC</code>.")
(comment candidateHasPercentageOfVotesInVoteCount "<code>(#$candidateHasPercentageOfVotesInVoteCount COUNT AGENT N)</code> means that according to the #$VoteCounting event <code>COUNT</code>, the candidate <code>AGENT</code> has <code>N</code> percent of the votes in the subsumiong election.")
(comment candidateRankInVoteCount "<code>(#$candidateRankInVoteCount COUNT AGENT N)</code> means that according to the #$VoteCounting event <code>COUNT</code>, the candidate <code>AGENT</code> ranks <code>N</code>th among the candidates in term sof the number of votes tallied in his favor.")
(comment ChromatidsAndChromosomeDuplication "The collection situations in where a chromatid is involved in the biological processes in which a chromosome duplicates")
(comment ArmyGeneral "A specialization of #$General-Rank.   Each instance of #$ArmyGeneral is a person who holds the rank of general in an army.")
(comment MRTimePointComparisonProperty "An object property that compares a time point to another time point or to a time interval.  Also known as a time point constraint.")
(comment KinetochoreAtTugOfWarEnd "The collection of situations that result after kinethochore microtubule tug of wars")
(comment EmbryoDevelopmentEvent "The collection of events in which a multicellular (see #$MulticellularOrganism), diploid (see #$DiploidOrganism) eukaryote (see #$EukaryoticOrganism) develops, starting from the #$Zygote stage and continuing until the new individual germinates, hatches, is born, or (in the case of humans after eight weeks of development) becomes a #$Fetus.  During embryogenesis, cells divide and differentiate as the #$Embryo forms the characteristic internal (organs) and external parts (limbs, etc.) that it will have as a juvenile and adult.")
(disjointWith PlacingSandwichFillingsOnBread AdministrationOfStuffToTissue)
(comment sandwichFillings "<code>(#$sandwichFillings SANDWICH FILLINGS)</code> means that <code>FILLINGS</code> is the instance of #$Food that comprises the \"stuff\" that makes up (i.e., that is inside the slices of bread) <code>SANDWICH</code>, an instance of #$Sandwich.")
(comment PouringLiquid "The collection of events in which some liquid is poured from a container.")
(disjointWith Gear Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite)
(disjointWith WindPoweredDevice Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite)
(disjointWith Flywheel Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite)
(disjointWith Inflated Deflated)
(comment Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite "The collection of instances of #$Wheel that are comprised, at a minimum, of a #$LandTransportationWheel fitted inside a #$Tire.")
(comment Wheel-WheelTubeAndTireComposite "The most common type of #$Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite, instances of this collection have as an #$internalParts an #$InnerTube, which, when inflated, makes the object a functional wheel.")
(comment EnzymeSubstrateBindingSite "The collection of #$ChemicalBindingSites that are subcomponents of #$EnzymeMolecules, at which a substrate molecule may bind to be acted upon by the enzyme.")
(comment TyrosineKinaseDomain "The collection of #$ChemicalBindingSites that are subcomponents of #$TyrosineKinaseMolecules, at which a #$ProteinMolecule containing #$Tyrosine may bind and receive a phosphate transferred from ATP to the tyrosine.")
(comment SignalBindingSite "The collection of #$ChemicalBindingSites that are subcomponents of #$ReceptorMolecules, at which a #$BiochemicalSignalingObject may bind, thus initiating a signal transduction process.")
(comment in-PassesThrough "(#$in-PassesThrough OBJ1 OBJ2) means that a portion of OBJ1 is surrounded by OBJ2, but two or more regions of OBJ1 extend out from OBJ2.  Furthermore, one such region extends out from one side of OBJ2 , and another extends out from a different side of OBJ2.  For example, each instance of #$IntegralTransmembraneProtein has a central region surrounded by the #$Membrane-Biological in which it is embedded, as well as regions which stick out from either side of the membrane.")
(comment IntracellularDomain "The collection of parts of large molecules, usually #$IntegralMembraneProteins, that are exposed on the cytosolic side of a #$CellMembrane (see #$CellMembraneCytosolicSurface) or protrude into the #$Cytosol.")
(comment ExtracellularDomain "The collection of parts of large molecules, usually #$IntegralMembraneProteins, that are exposed on the outer side of a #$CellMembrane (see #$CellMembraneOuterSurface).")
(comment TransmembraneDomain "The collection of parts of #$IntegralMembraneProteins that are completely embedded in and surrounded by a #$CellMembrane.  #$TransmembraneDomains are hydrophobic; typically, #$AlphaHelix instances are #$TransmembraneDomains.")
(comment MRTimeIntervalComparisonProperty "An object property that compares a time point to another time point or to a time interval.  Also known as a time point constraint.")
(comment IntervalBetweenCalendarDays "The collection of continuous time intervals whose beginning and ending points are both calendar days.")
(comment ChromosonesDuplicationAndDistributionDuringMitosis "The collection of biological processes in which chromosomes are duplicated and distributed during mitosis")
(comment ProteinDimer "Instances of #$ProteinDimer are #$MultiProteinComplexes formed of two #$ProteinMolecules through the process of #$ProteinDimerization.")
(comment TyrosineKinaseDimer "A #$MultiProteinComplex formed during the activation of tyrosine-kinase receptors, consisting of two such #$ReceptorTyrosineKinaseMolecules which have aggregated.")
(comment BindingSiteActivationEvent "The collection of all #$ChemicalReactions in which an 'inactive' #$ChemicalBindingSite is 'activated, i.e., rendered capable of participating in a #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent with some appropriate #$ChemicalObject.")
(comment ReceptorTyrosineKinaseDomainActivationEvent "The collection of all events in which the #$TyrosineKinaseDomain of an 'inactive' #$ReceptorTyrosineKinaseMolecule is 'activated, i.e., rendered capable of acting in phosphorylation.")
(comment wffConstraintMt "(#$wffConstraintMt <code>MT</code>) means that all WFF constraints in <code>MT</code> (that is, GAF assertions in MT whose predicates are instances of #$WFFConstraintPredicate) are to be interpreted as constraints rather than as supports for deduced conclusions. This also applies to microtheories whose #$mtMonad is MT.")
(comment PhosphorylatedTyrosineKinaseDimer "A #$MultiProteinComplex formed during the activation of tyrosine-kinase receptors.")
(comment relayMolecules "A specialization of #$instrument-Generic, <code>(#$relayMolecules TRANSDUCTION MOLECULE)</code> identifies <code>MOLECULE</code> as one of the instances of #$ChemicalObject, often a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex, which is acted on (see #$objectActedOn) in one of the #$catalyticSteps of <code>TRANSDUCTION</code>.")
(disjointWith SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-SingleReaction SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-MultiStageReaction)
(comment GroundMeat "The collection of all ground meat. A type of #$Meat, #$Artifact, and #$HomogeneousStructure. The collection #$GroundMeat is a #$MeatCutType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment GroundTurkey "Turkey meat, ground.")
(comment MeatGrinding "A specialization of #$Grinding. In each instance of #$MeatGrinding, a portion of #$Meat is ground and some form of #$GroundMeat is thereby produced.")
(comment GroundFn "(#$GroundFn TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances (groups of pieces) that are the result of taking 1 or more instances of TYPE and grinding them (in a #$Grinding event) so that they are ground up.")
(comment groundFormOf "<code>(#$groundFormOf TYPE GROUND-FORM-OF-TYPE)</code> means that <code>GROUND-FORM-OF-TYPE</code> is the ground form og <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment Burger "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Each instance of #$Burger is a sandwich made with a patty (e.g. a ground beef patty, or a ground turkey patty) and a burger bun.")
(comment SloppyJoeSandwich "A type of #$Sandwich consisting of loose ground meat in a generous quantity of sauce on a bread or a burger bun.")
(comment LigandGatedIonChannelCellSignalingProcess "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that begin with the reception of a signal by a #$LigandGatedIonChannel, leading to a #$ChangeInCellIonConcentration.")
(comment MeatballSandwich "A type of #$Sandwich the main ingredient of which is meatballs.")
(comment Meatball "A specialization of #$MeatMixture.  Each instance of #$Meatball is a round ball-shapped portion of meat and other food ingredients.  Instances of #$Meatball are often served with pasta or in a #$MeatballSandwich.")
(comment MeatballSub "A type of #$SubmarineSandwich the main ingreadient of whcih is meatballs.")
(comment WarmCheeseSandwich "A specialization of #$CheeseSandwich.  Each instance of #$WarmCheeseSandwich is a cheese sandwich that is prepared in a way that causes the cheese to melt.")
(comment ColdCheeseSandwich "A specialization of #$CheeseSandwich.  Each instance of #$ColdCheeseSandwich is a cheese sandwich that is without warming it.  The cheese in a cold cheese sandwich is unmelted.")
(comment FoodOrDrink-Cold "This is the collection of foods and beverages usually served at room temperature or slightly colder.")
(comment FoodOrDrink-Chilled "This is the collection of foods and beverages usually served much colder than room temperature.")
(comment SituationTopicSetFn "(#$SituationTopicSetFn SET PRED-SET) denotes the situation type in which all of the members of SET stand in some relationship (or an instance of the member does) to some predicate in PRED-SET and the corresponding situations are importantly linked to each other (often by one of the preds in PRED-SET).  For example, (#$SituationTopicSetFn (#$TheSet #$Horse #$Person) (#$TheSet #$transporter #$on-Physical)), strictly speaking, denotes the collection of situations in which a horse plays some role either on something or being ridden or as the transporter in an event and a person is either a transporter or either on something or something is on him and these individuals and the situations they are in are linked in some important but unspecified way.  There typically will be a useful subset of that collection of situations as many will be highly unlikely --  A man being the transporter in an event where the horse is riding him is one of those unlikely instances of this -- that can be generated through additional assertions on the collection.")
(comment LooseMeatSandwich "A type of #$Sandwich the main ingreadient of which is loose meat.")
(comment ReubenSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Reubens include layered corned beef or pastrami, sauerkraut and Swiss cheese, with a dressing Russian or Thousand Island dressing.")
(comment DeliSlice-MeatCut "The collection of all deli sliced cut pieces of meat. A type of #$Meat and #$Food-ReadyToEat. #$DeliSlice-MeatCut is an #$ExistingStuffType.")
(comment CheeseSlice "The collection of all slices of cheese.")
(comment SwissCheeseSlice "The collection of all slices of Swiss cheese.")
(comment ClubSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Club sandwiches include two layers of fillings between 3 slices of toasted bread. The traditional club ingredients (see #$ClubSandwich-Traditional) are turkey on the bottom layer, and bacon, lettuce, and tomato on the top layer.")
(comment ClubSandwich-Traditional "A specialization of #$ClubSandwich.  Traditional club sandwiches include 3 slices of toasted bread, with turkey between the bottom two slices and bacon, lettuce, and tomato between the top two slices.")
(comment BreakfastSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Breakfast sandwiches typically include breakfast meats, breads, eggs and cheese as ingredients.")
(comment EggSandwich "A specialization of #$BreakfastSandwich.  Egg sandwiches include eggs as an ingredient.")
(comment BaconLettuceAndTomatoSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Bacon lettuce and tomato sandwiches include bacon, lettuce and tomato as an ingredient, usually with toasted bread.")
(comment HamAndCheeseSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Ham and cheese sandwiches include ham and cheese as ingredients.")
(comment BaconEggAndCheeseSandwich "A specialization of #$BreakfastSandwich.  Bacon egg and cheese sandwiches include bacon, eggs and cheese as ingredients.")
(comment LobsterRoll "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Lobster rolls are sandwiches in which lobster meat is the main ingredient.")
(comment NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithPredicate "#$NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithPredicate is the collection of #$TextStringOccurrences with #$cisIsAnOccurrenceOfStructureType of #$NLSentence that directly contain (#$structureContainsCIS) some #$TextStringOccurrence whoe #$referent is a property or relation (#$Predicate).")
(comment eventLocale "(#$eventLocale EVENT REGION) means that REGION is the #$GeographicalRegion within whose boundaries EVENT occurs.")
(comment getTemperatureTrend-Set "<code>(#$getTemperatureTrend-Set  FIBER DATE TQ SET)</code> means that at the #$Date <code>DATE</code> (within the \"time-window\" duration specified by #$Time-Quantity <code>TQ</code>) the #$DistributedTemperatureSensor <code>FIBER</code> measured the temperatures at the depths indicated by the depth/temperature points in  <code>SET</code>.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-argumentdetail-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-argumentdetail-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-imagecall-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-imagecall-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-instruction-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-instruction-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-librarycall-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-librarycall-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-nearestcfg-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-nearestcfg-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-operandaddressmode-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-operandaddressmode-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-operandreadmode-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-operandreadmode-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-operandregister-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-operandregister-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-operandtype-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-operandtype-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-operandwritemode-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-operandwritemode-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-rhsresultinvariant-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-rhsresultinvariant-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-valuerangeinvariant-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-valuerangeinvariant-KS.")
(comment characteristicSoundTypeFromActionType "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$CharacteristicSoundTypeFromActionTypeFn, <code>(#$characteristicSoundTypeFromActionType SOUND-TYPE EVENT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>SOUND-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$AudibleSound that are characteristic of instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Event.")
(comment CharacteristicSoundTypeFromActionTypeFn "<code>(#$CharacteristicSoundTypeFromActionTypeFn EVENT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$AudibleSound that are characteristic of instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$Event.")
(comment CheeseSandwich "A type of #$Sandwich consisting of bread and cheese, possibly also with meat or spreads or condiments.")
(comment TunaSaladSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Tuna salad sandwiches are sandwiches in which tuna salad is the main ingredient.")
(comment TunaSalad "The collection of all instances of #$Salad whose main ingredient is tuna meat.")
(comment EggSaladSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Egg salad sandwiches are sandwiches in which egg salad is the main ingredient.")
(comment ChickenSaladSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Chicken salad sandwiches are sandwiches in which chicken salad is the main ingredient.")
(comment ChickenSalad "The collection of all instances of #$Salad whose main ingredient is chicken meat.")
(comment SaladSandwich "A specialization of #$Sandwich.  Salad sandwiches are sandwiches in which salad of some sort (e.g. #$ChickenSalad, #$EggSalad or #$TunaSalad) is the main ingredient.")
(comment SKSIDescriptionVocabularyConstant "All the vocabulary used to describe SKSI schemata and knowledge sources, rather than any particular content of any of these things.")
(disjointWith PlasmaMembraneReceptorMolecule IntracellularReceptorMolecule)
(comment IntracellularReceptorMolecule "The collection of all instances of #$ReceptorMolecule that are located within a #$Cell.  This includes #$CytoplasmicReceptorMolecules, #$NuclearReceptors, and receptors that may be present on membranes of subcellular structures.")
(comment AndrogenReceptor "A class of #$ReceptorMolecule that is activated by binding with #$Testosterone or dihydrotestosterone in the #$Cytosol.  This complex then moves into the #$Nucleus, where it regulates gene expression.")
(comment CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing important specializations of #$CellularCommunication.  Where SIGNAL-TYPE is a specialization of an 'organism-wide' dispersal of a substance composed of instances of some kind of signal molecule such as #$EpinephrineMolecule (said dispersal type will often be represented using #$IntercellularMediumReleaseOfChemicalObjectTypeFn) and RESPONSE-TYPE is a kind of cellular level response (a specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel), (#$CellularSignalToResponseProcessTypeFn SIGNAL-TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$CellularCommunication which begin with an instance of SIGNAL-TYPE and conclude with many cells undergoing a response of RESPONSE-TYPE.")
(comment AndrogenReceptorSignalingProcess "The collection of all signal transduction pathways that begin with the reception of a signal by an #$AndrogenReceptor, leading to gene regulation.")
(comment codeStatementDependsOnStatement-AllExecutions "(#$codeStatementDependsOnStatement-AllExecutions DEPENDENT DEPENDED-ON) means that, in any possible execution of a program containing both DEPENDENT and DEPENDED-ON, DEPENDENT will not be executed unless DEPENDED-ON is executed.")
(comment codeStatementDependsOnStatement-SomeExecutions "(#$codeStatementDependsOnStatement-SomeExecutions DEPENDENT DEPENDED-ON) means that in some executions (at least one execution) of the program which subsumes both DEPENDENT and DEPENDED-ON, DEPENDENT cannot be executed without executing DEPENDED-ON as part of the same execution.")
(comment codeStatementCandidateDependency "(#$codeStatementCandidateDependency CAND-DEPENDENT CAND-DEPENDED-ON) means that, within the substructure of a certain #$ComputerProgram-CWIS, it is possible to identify a linear of #$ComputerCodeStatements between CAND-DEPENDENT and CAND-DEPENDED-ON (possibly consisting of just CAND-DEPENDENT and CAND-DEPENDED-ON, but possibly not) such that #$codeStatementDependsOnStatement-SomeExecutions holds between any two immediate successors within the order.")
(comment statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive "This is the transitive generalization of #$statementOutputsDirectlyToStatement.  (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that OUTPUTS and INPUTS are both part of a common #$ComputerProgram-CWIS with a control structure such that between OUTPUTS and INPUTS there is discernable one or more specified 'hand-offs' in which a value is passed from one statement to the next in virtue of the outputting statement specifying an operation that ends with the value being attached to a certain expression, while the inputting statement specifies some use of that value via a reference to the same expression.  In other words, (#$statementOutputsToStatement-Transitive OUTPUTS INPUTS) means that OUTPUTS and INPUTS are both part of a program with at least one possible execution thread such that executing INPUTS will involve using a value determined by a chain of operations, one of which is specified by OUTPUTS.  Note that this does not entail that the same expression is used throughout the chain of operations, or that a single value is transmitted as a constant through the chain, or that the dependency obtains for every possible execution of the program.")
(disjointWith MovementOfActivatedAndrogenReceptorIntoNucleus (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(disjointWith LocatingInIntendedPosition MovementOfActivatedAndrogenReceptorIntoNucleus)
(disjointWith LocomotionEvent MovementOfActivatedAndrogenReceptorIntoNucleus)
(comment MovementOfActivatedAndrogenReceptorIntoNucleus "A specialization of #$Translation-Complete in which an instance of (#$ActivatedFormOfEnzymeFn #$AndrogenReceptor) moves from the #$Cytosol into the #$Nucleus of a #$Cell.")
(comment GeneRegulationEvent "Instances are types of #$BiologicalRegulationProcess in which the rate of production of the product of some gene is either increased or decreased.  Genes may be regulated by modifying their ability to be transcribed, or the rate at which they are transcribed (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA), or by modifying how much of the #$MessengerRNA is translated into proteins (see Translation-RNAToProtein). ")
(comment TranscriptionRegulationEvent "Instances are #$GeneRegulationEvents in which the rate of production of the product of some gene is either increased or decreased, by modifying the ability of the gene to be transcribed, or the rate at which is is transcribed (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA)")
(comment getTraceValuesBelowTemperatureThreshold "<code>(#$getTraceValuesBelowTemperatureThreshold FIBER DATE THRESH-TEMP DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> for temperatures below <code>THRESH-TEMP</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment getTraceValuesAboveTemperatureThreshold "<code>(#$getTraceValuesAboveTemperatureThreshold FIBER DATE THRESH-TEMP DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> for temperatures above <code>THRESH-TEMP</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment getTraceValuesInTemperatureRange "<code>(#$getTraceValuesAboveTemperatureThreshold FIBER DATE LOW-TEMP HIGH-TEMP DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> for temperatures in the interval bounded by <code>LOW-TEMP</code> and <code>HIGH-TEMP</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment getTraceAtDateByDepthRange "<code>(#$getTraceValuesAboveTemperatureThreshold FIBER DATE LOW-DIST HIGH-DIST DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> for temperatures in the interval bounded by <code>LOW-DIST</code> and <code>HIGH-DIST</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment getTraceTimeStampsByFiberID "<code>(#$getTraceTimeStampsByFiberID FIBER START-DATE END-DATE DATE)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> produced a trace at <code>DATE</code>, which is a date between <code>START-DATE</code> and <code>END-DATE</code>.")
(comment getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepth "<code>(#$getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepth FIBER DATE DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the temperature <code>TEMP</code> at the (possibly interpolated) depth <code>DEPTH</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepthByTempRange "<code>(#$getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepthByTempRange FIBER DATE DEPTH MIN-TEMP MAX-TEMP TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the temperature <code>TEMP</code> at the (possibly interpolated) depth <code>DEPTH</code> at <code>DATE</code>, where <code>TEMP</code> is in the interval bounded by <code>MIN-TEMP</code> and <code>MAX-TEMP</code>.")
(comment getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRange "<code>(#$getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRange FIBER DATE N MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> at regular internals of <code>N</code> meters <code>DATE</code>, where <code>DEPTH</code> is in the interval bounded by <code>MIN-DEPTH</code> and <code>MAX-DEPTH</code>.")
(comment queryHasQuotedLiteral "(#$queryHasQuotedLiteral QUERY QUOTE) means that QUERY has the content of QUOTE as a literal in its query sentence.")
(comment CytoplasmicProteinKinaseMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinKinaseMolecule.  Each instance of #$CytoplasmicProteinKinaseMolecule is a protein kinase that is typically found in the #$Cytoplasm of a #$Cell, in contrast to membrane-bound protein kinases such as a #$ReceptorTyrosineKinaseMolecule.")
(comment ProteinKinaseActivity "The collection of all events in which a #$ProteinKinaseMolecule is involved, including events in which it is activated, inactivated, or in which it acts as a #$catalyst.")
(comment DifferenceMagnitudeFn "#$DifferenceMagnitudeFn is the function that takes two scalars and returns the magnitude of their difference. (#$DifferenceMagnitudeFn A B) is thus equivalent to (#$AbsoluteValueFn (#$DifferenceFn A B)).")
(comment setHasPointsWithYValueRelnToMatchingXValuePointsInSet "<code>(#$setHasPointsWithYValueRelnToMatchingXValuePointsInSet SET1 SET2 OP COMP QUANT NEWSET)</code> means that the points in <code>NEWSET</code> are each point <code>P1</code> in <code>SET1</code> such that if the X value of <code>P1</code> matches the X value of any point <code>P2</code> in <code>SET2</code>, then for the corresponding Y values <code>Y1</code> and <code>Y2</code> of <code>P1</code> and <code>P2</code>, <code>(COMP (OP Y1 Y2) QUANT)</code> is true.")
(comment BindingOfEpinephrineToLiverCellMembrane "The collection of all #$ConnectingTogether events in which en #$EpinephrineMolecule binds to a #$CellMembrane.")
(comment MatureNeuron "A specialization of #$Neuron.  Each instance of #$MatureNeuron is a nerve cell that is mature.")
(comment MatureMyocyte "#$MatureMyocytes are mature muscle cells.")
(comment Fibroblast "Fibroblasts are animal cells that synthesize extracellular matrix and collagen.")
(comment TranscriptionUpregulation-AndrogenReceptorSignaling "Instances are #$TranscriptionRegulationEvents in which, as a result of #$Testosterone signaling to the #$AndrogenReceptor system, the transcription of certain genes coding for male characteristics is increased.")
(comment grower "<code>(#$grower EVT OBJ)</code> means that <code>OBJ</code> grows in the #$GrowthEvent <code>EVT</code>.")
(disjointWith SterileEnvironment EnvironmentSuitableForBiochemicalInteractions)
(comment SolubleGuanylylCyclase-Receptor "A class of #$IntracellularReceptorMolecule that is activated by binding with #$NitricOxide in the #$Cytosol.  It is involved in smooth muscle relaxation, such as that that occurs with #$Vasodilation.  Each molecule is composed of two different subunits, and those subunits can each be derived from two different genes.")
(comment SituationConceptSetFn "(#$SituationConceptSetFn SET) denotes the situation type in which all of the members of SET stand in some unspecified relationship with each other.")
(comment NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithoutPredicate "#$NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithPredicate is the collection of #$TextStringOccurrences with #$cisIsAnOccurrenceOfStructureType of #$NLSentence that directly contain (#$structureContainsCIS) some #$TextStringOccurrence with a #$referent to some concept and that do not contain any with a referent that is a predicate .")
(disjointWith NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithoutPredicate NLSentenceStructTypeWithSubsumedTextstringAssociatedWithPredicate)
(comment UnorganizedPersonGroup "A group of persons without an organizational structure, group name, or (frequently/usually) member names.")
(comment fcvHeelValueAtDate "<code>(#$fcvHeelValueAtDate WELL DATE PERCENT)</code> means that the short-string FCV on <code>DATE</code> is <code>PERCENT</code> open.")
(comment fcvToeValueAtDate "<code>(#$fcvToeValueAtDate WELL DATE PERCENT)</code> means that the area of the long-string FCV on <code>DATE</code> is <code>PERCENT</code> .")
(comment PoliticalRally "The collection of instances of #$Rally intended to reinforce or increase awareness of or drum up support for some political cause, such as a person's candidacy for some elected position or some ballot initiative.  Note that #$PoliticalRally and #$ProtestRally are not disjoint, but neither is a subset of the other.")
(comment ProtestRally "A (usually large) gathering of people who gather to protest something.  Like other kinds of #$Rally, there are likely to be speakers who speak with the intent of increasing the passion that the participants feel about thing being protested.  Note that #$PoliticalRally and #$ProtestRally are not disjoint, but neither is a subset of the other.")
(disjointWith (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Picketing ProtestMarch ProtestRally)) (CollectionDifferenceFn PublicProtesting (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Picketing ProtestMarch ProtestRally))))
(comment kShasLogicalSchema "This predicate relates an SKSI knowledge source with a logical schema.")
(comment Election-SingleIssue "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Election.  Each instance of #$Election-SingleIssue is an event in which members of an #$Organization cast votes to determine the answer to one issue.  Important specializations include #$ElectionForOffice, where voters are asked what individual should serve in a particular office or what political party should get seats on a governing body, and #$Referendum, in which the voters are asked to accept or reject a single proposal.  #$Election-SingleIssue is contrasted with #$Election-MultipleIssue, instances of which consist of several, #$cotemporal instances of #$Election-SingleIssue.  ")
(comment Election-MultipleIssue "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Election.  Each instance of #$Election-MultipleIssue is an event in which members of an #$Organization cast votes on several questions during a single voting session. For example, in one instance of #$Election-MultipleIssue, voters might cast ballots stating their choice for state governor, state representatives and senators, county commissioner, and several #$Referendums.")
(comment Referendum "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Election-SingleIssue.  Referendums - also called ballot initiatives or plebiscites - are a type of election in which voters are asked to accept or reject a particular proposal.  A #$Referendum may be binding, resulting in direct effect (change in law or constitution, recall of previous election, etc.) in the polity in which it occurs, or non-binding, in which case it offers advice to the legislature.  Depending on the geopolitical entity holding the vote, it may be referred to by different names depending on various characteristics. ''Referendum'' in the USA usually means a direct vote originating in a #$LegislativeOrganization, which other direct votes are called ''initiatives'' or ''ballot initiatives.'' This collection is intended to represent all direct votes, plebiscites, initiatives and referendums in which voters express acceptance or rejection of a single proposal.")
(disjointWith Election-MultipleIssue Election-SingleIssue)
(comment componentElections "Where ELECTION is an #$Election-MultipleIssue held under the auspices of some polity, (#$componentElections ELECTION SUB-ELECTION) means that SUB-ELECTION is one of the instances of #$Election-SingleIssue that is a #$cotemporalSubEvents of ELECTION, in which voters make a choice for a single #$Referendum, for a single #$PoliticalParty to fill seats in a governing body of the polity, or for a single individual (or pair of individuals, if they are running mates) to fill an elected position in the polity.")
(comment ephemeralTermDescriptionCollection "A predicate for autolexifying ephemeral terms. If (#$ephemeralTermDescriptionCollection TYPE LEXICAL-MT) is asserted in the query mt for an inference, then ephemeral terms denoting instances of TYPE hypothesized for that inference will receive lexifications of the form 'the TYPE' in LEXICAL-MT.")
(comment organizationMembershipSoughtInElection "(#$organizationMembershipSoughtInElection ELECTION ORGANIZATION) means that ELECTION is held in order to choose people to serve as members of ORGANIZATION during a statutory term following ELECTION.  In some polities, elections do not identify individual candidates to fill single positions, but rather identify groups of people (usually political parties) to fill seats in an organization.  For example, in elections whose results are determined under a party-list proportional representation scheme, parties provide an ordered list of candidates, and get a number of seats proportional to their share of the votes, which will be filled by the first N candidates on their list.")
(comment organizationToBeFilledByElectoralProcess "(#$organizationToBeFilledByElectoralProcess PROCESS ORGANIZATION) means that ORGANIZATION is the organization, usually a governing body, that PROCESS is supposed to fill.  Thus, e.g., it is true that (organizationToBeFilledByElectoralProcess (ProcessToElectFn Austria AustrianNationalCouncil (YearFn 2008)) AustrianNationalCoucil).")
(comment mrContestedEntityInElection "(contestedEntityInElection ELECTION ENTITY): The ELECTION event has as its ContestedEntity ENTITY.")
(comment electionCandidates "A #$BinaryRolePredicate used to identify the contestants in an #$Election.  (#$electionCandidates ELECTION CANDIDATE) means that CANDIDATE is (in the 'timeless' sense of 'is' one of the declared candidates running in ELECTION. Note that the candidates in an election can be individual people, but they instead might be instances of #$PoliticalParty.")
(comment PoliticalElectionCampaign "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$PoliticalEvent and #$AdvertisingCampaign.  Each instance of #$PoliticalElectionCampaign is an event in which a group tries to secure elected office for the candidate of its choice.  Where the candidate is a #$PoliticalParty, the goal of the campaign is to fill the organization whose
membership is sought in the election (see #$organizationMembershipSoughtInElection) with as many party members as possible. Note that while every #$PoliticalElectionCampaign is coterminal with some #$ElectionForOffice, #$PoliticalElectionCampaign is disjoint with #$Election.")
(comment politicalCampaignOf "<code>(#$politicalCampaignOf CAMPAIGN CANDIDATE)</code> means that <code>CAMPAIGN</code>, an instance of #$PoliticalElectionCampaign, is a campaign that promotes <code>CANDIDATE</code> for election to the relevant office in contest in the relevant election.  Note that <code>CANDIDATE</code> can be an individual #$Person or a #$PoliticalParty.")
(comment campaignEventPerformer "<code>(#$campaignEventPerformer CAMPAIGN-EVT CAMPAIGNER)</code> means that <code>CAMPAIGN-EVT</code>, an instance of #$PoliticalElectionCampaignEvent, is performed by <code>CAMPAIGNER</code>.  Sometimes <code>CAMPAIGNER</code> is also the candidate benefiting from the campaign, but often it is a different, yet affiliated, person or organization.")
(comment CampaignOrganization "A sub-collection of #$PoliticalOrganization. Each instance is a team of people who work to maximize the success of one #$PoliticalElectionCampaign.  The goal of each such organization is to convince voters to vote for the candidate of the campaign (see #$politicalCampaignOf).")
(comment campaignHasOrganization "<code>(#$campaignHasOrganization CAMPAIGN ORGANIZATION)</code> means that <code>CAMPAIGN</code>, an instance of #$PoliticalElectionCampaign, is directed by the instance of #$CampaignOrganization, <code>ORGANIZATION</code>. ")
(disjointWith ElectionForOffice Referendum)
(disjointWith CHIBLInternalCodingFunction StandardLibraryFunction)
(comment setHasPointsWithAveragedYValuesOfSetsOfPoints "<code>(#$setHasPointsWithAveragedYValuesOfSetsOfPoints SET-OF-SETS-OF-POINTS SET-OF-POINTS)</code> means that <code>SET-OF-POINTS</code> is the set of points whose X values match all of the X values of the points in each of the sets in <code>SET-OF-SETS-OF-POINTS</code>, and whose Y values are the average of the Y values of the points in each of the sets in <code>SET-OF-SETS-OF-POINTS</code>.")
(comment setHasPointsWithYValueRelnTo "<code>(#$setHasPointsWithYValueRelnTo SET OP COMP QUANT1 QUANT2 NEWSET)</code> means that the points in <code>NEWSET</code> are each point <code>P</code> in <code>SET</code> such that for the Y values <code>Y</code> of <code>P</code> , <code>(COMP (OP Y QUANT1) QUANT2)</code> is true.")
(comment thpHeelValueAtDate "<code>(#$thpHeelValueAtDate WELL DATE PRESSURE)</code> means that the pressure recorded by the short-string THP gauge on <code>DATE</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment thpToeValueAtDate "<code>(#$thpToeValueAtDate WELL DATE PRESSURE)</code> means that the pressure recorded by the long-string THP gauge on <code>DATE</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment bhpValueAtDate "<code>(#$bhpValueAtDate WELL DATE PRESSURE)</code> means that the pressure recorded by the BHP gauge on <code>DATE</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment averageSaturationSteamTemperatureForTimeInterval "<code>(#$averageSaturationSteamTemperatureForTimeInterval OBJ TEMP START-DATE END-DATE)</code> means that during the interval between <code>START-DATE</code> and <code>END-DATE</code> the average saturation steam temperature at #$PartiallyTangible <code>OBJ</code> is <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment kShasPhysicalSchema "This predicate relates an SKSI knowledge source with a physical schema.")
(comment lifeCycleElementaryFlowInputs "A predicate for something with the inputs required for its production")
(comment getTraceTimeStampByFiberID "<code>(#$getTraceTimeStampByFiberID FIBER START-DATE END-DATE N DATE)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> produced a trace at <code>DATE</code>, which is a date between <code>START-DATE</code> and <code>END-DATE</code>.  If <code>N</code> = 0, <code>DATE</code> is the earliest date of a DTS using <code>FIBER</code> in that date range,  and if <code>N</code> = 1, <code>DATE</code> is the latest date of a DTS using <code>FIBER</code> in that date range.")
(disjointWith CoolingIndicativeOfThermalCycling WarmingIndicativeOfThermalCycling)
(comment wellHasThermocouple "<code>(#$wellHasThermocouple WELL TC)</code> means that the #$Thermocouple <code>TC</code> is in <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment WinningPositionInElection "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$WinningAConflict.  In each instance of #$WinningPositionInElection, one candidate (either an individual person or a pair of running mates) is declared the winner of the election.")
(comment numberOfSeatsWon "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$WinningSeatsInElection to an #$NonNegativeInteger denoting the number of seats won.  (#$numberOfSeatsWon WINNING INTEGER) means that the winning party won INTEGER seats in WINNING.")
(comment winningCandidate "A #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates a #$WinningPositionInElection to the candidate winning it.  (#$winningCandidate WINNING INDIVIDUAL) means that INDIVIDUAL is the winner in WINNING.")
(comment winningParty "(#$winningParty WINNING PARTY) means that in the #$WinningSeatsInElection, WINNING, PARTY is the #$PoliticalParty securing the seats.")
(comment seatsWonInOrganization "(#$seatsWonInOrganization WINNING ORGANIZATION) means that in the #$WinningSeatsInElection, WINNING, the seats secured are in ORGANIZATION.")
(comment IntroducingABill "A specialization of #$LegalProceeding.  Each instance of #$IntroducingABill is an event in which one or more members of a #$LegislativeOrganization introduces a bill for consideration as a potential law by the members of that organization.  The person or persons who introduce the bill are the sponsors or cosponsors of the bill.  In many legislative bodies, this is the first step of the process of #$Legislating.")
(comment Legislating "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$LegalProceeding and #$GroupActivity.  Each instance of #$Legislating is an event in which #$Legislators introduce legislation (see #$IntroducingABill), deliberate (see #$LegislativeDeliberation), and decide the fate of proposed legislation (see #$AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill and its specializations.).  Depending on the procedures followed by the particular legislative body performing a #$Legislating, other events might be included, but these three steps are the most fundamental steps followed in all cases.")
(comment LegislativeActivity "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$LegalProceeding and #$GroupActivity.  Each instance of #$LegislativeActivity is an event performed by a #$Legislator or #$LegislativeOrganization in the course of #$Legislating.  This includes instances of #$Legislating itself, as well as instances of #$IntroducingABill, #$Filibuster, #$PassingALaw, and other actions done as the work of the legislature.")
(comment LegislativeDeliberation "A specialization of #$LegislativeActivity.  Each instance of #$LegislativeDeliberation is an event in which the members of a #$LegislativeOrganization and their staff consider a proposed piece of legislation.  They perform research, hold #$Debates, and otherwise undertake all the actions that must occur  before the legislative body accepts or rejects the proposed bill. ")
(comment RejectingProposedBill "The collection of all events in which a governing body with legislative powers rejects a proposed bill, and fails to pass it.")
(disjointWith IntroducingABill AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill)
(disjointWith LegislativeDeliberation IntroducingABill)
(disjointWith LegislativeDeliberation AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill)
(disjointWith RejectingProposedBill PassingALaw)
(comment billSponsor "<code>(#$billSponsor BILL SPONSOR)</code> means that <code>SPONSOR</code> is one sponsors of the legislation <code>BILL</code>, an instance of #$Bill-ProposedLaw.")
(comment AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill "A specialization of #$LegislativeActivity.  Each instance of #$AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill is an event in which the members of a #$LegislativeOrganization collectively decide the fate of a proposed bill.  Successful bills are passed into law (see #$PassingALaw), while unsuccessful ones can be rejected outright (see #$RejectingProposedBill) or allowed to die without coming to a vote.")
(comment legislativeBody "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$LegislativeActivity to the #$LegislativeOrganization in the context of which the activity occurs.  ")
(comment ApprovingProposedBill "The collection of all events in which a governing body with legislative powers accepts a proposed bill.  This is a necessary step, though not always a sufficient one, for the bill to become law.  The #$Bill-ProposedLaw may still need to be approved by a second legislative body, or by a monarch or president, depending on the rules of the nation where the billis being considered.")
(disjointWith ApprovingProposedBill RejectingProposedBill)
(disjointWith LegislativeDeliberation LegislativeVote)
(disjointWith IntroducingABill LegislativeVote)
(disjointWith Election LegislativeVote)
(comment LegislativeVote "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Vote-CollectiveDecision.  Each instance of #$LegislativeVote is an event in which members of a #$LegislativeOrganization cast votes in favor of or against proposed legislation.  The rules of the #$LegislativeOrganization determine how the vote count will determine approval or rejection of the #$Bill-ProposedLaw.")
(comment Deciding-Collectively-AmongChoices "A specialization of #$Deciding-Collectively and of #$SelectingSomething.  Each instance of #$Deciding-Collectively-AmongChoices is an event in which a group of agents selects one choice from a set of options, either informally (as when a group of friends decides where to eat lunch together) or formally (as when an #$ElectionForOffice is held to choose who will serve in some elected position.)  This collection is contrasted with #$Deciding-Collectively-YesOrNo, in which a group of agents accept or reject a proposal.")
(comment Deciding-Collectively-YesOrNo "A specialization of #$Deciding-Collectively.  Each instance of #$Deciding-Collectively-YesOrNo is an event in which a group of agents accepts or rejects a particular proposal.  This collection includes instances in which the decision-making is informal, such as when a pair of friends decides whether or not to enter a bridge tournament, and instances involving formal yes or no decision making, such as a #$Referendum or an instance of #$AcceptingOrRejectingProposedBill done in a legislature. This collection is contrasted with #$Deciding-Collectively-AmongChoices, in which a group of agents selects one choice from a set of options.")
(disjointWith Deciding-Collectively-YesOrNo Deciding-Collectively-AmongChoices)
(comment proposalConsidered "(#$proposalConsidered DECISION PROPOSAL) identifies the instance of #$NormativeSpecification PROPOSAL as the thing being decided in DECISION, which is an instance of #$Deciding-Collectively-YesOrNo.  Note that this predicate is an instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, so PROPOSAL must be a complete specification of the issues being considered and decided in DECISION.")
(comment totalVotes "(#$totalVotes VOTING NUMBER) means that the total number of votes cast in VOTING is NUMBER.")
(comment votesInFavor "(#$votesInFavor VOTING NUMBER) means that the number of votes cast in favor of the #$proposalConsidered in VOTING is NUMBER.")
(comment votesAgainst "(#$votesAgainst VOTING NUMBER) means that the number of votes cast against the #$proposalConsidered in VOTING is NUMBER.")
(comment hasIntroducingLegislationSponsor "(#$hasIntroducingLegislationSponsor INTRO SPONSOR) identifies SPONSOR, usually an instance of #$Legislator, as the sponsor of the billl being introduced in INTRO, an instance of #$IntroducingABill.\"")
(comment ThermocouplesHealTemp "A type of thermocouple.")
(comment ThermocouplesMotorTemp "A type of thermocouple.")
(comment ThermocouplesPumpTemp "A type of thermocouple.")
(comment ThermocouplesToeTemp "A type of thermocouple.")
(comment HypotheticalForVariableFn "(#$HypotheticalForVariableFn VAR) denotes the thing hypothesized in a conditional query to instantiate the variable VAR. This is useful for specifying #$testAnswersCycL-Wanted for hypothetical queries.")
(comment extractionIDSourceText "<code>(#$extractionIDSourceText EXTRACTION-ID TEXT)</code> identifies the string <code>TEXT</code> as the source of the unique instance of #$RelationExtraction with ID <code>EXTRACTION-ID</code>.")
(comment extractionIDSourceOffsetStart "<code>(#$extractionIDSourceOffsetStart EXTRACTION-ID OFFSET-START)</code> identifies the integer <code>OFFSET-START</code> as the starting point of the offset of the unique instance of #$RelationExtraction with ID <code>EXTRACTION-ID</code>.")
(comment extractionIDSourceOffsetEnd "<code>(#$extractionIDSourceOffsetEnd EXTRACTION-ID OFFSET-END)</code> identifies the integer <code>OFFSET-END</code> as the ending point of the offset of the unique instance of #$RelationExtraction with ID <code>EXTRACTION-ID</code>.")
(comment ProgramExecutionTrackingPredicate "The collection of all predicates used for tracking the dynamic use of values and expressions in actual and hypothesized instances of #$ProgramExecution-Complete.")
(comment ScopedExecutionRolePredicate "Instances of this collection are used to track the semantic roles of particular values in particular program executions (instances of #$ProgramExecution-Complete) within scopes determined by #$ComputerCodeStatements in the program being executed.")
(comment pointerToLocation "(#$pointerToLocation STATEMENT EXECUTION NUM LOC) means that while STATEMENT is being executed during the particular program execution (#$ProgramExecution-Complete) EXECUTION, the #$PositiveInteger NUM serves as a pointer to the #$ComputerDataStorageLocation LOC.")
(comment handleForLocation "(#$handleForLocation STATEMENT EXECUTION NUM LOC) means that while STATEMENT is being executed in the #$ProgramExecution-Complete EXECUTION, NUM serves as a handle for the #$ComputerDataStorageLocation LOC.")
(comment numberTypeOfArg "(#$numberTypeOfArg CODE-FN N NUMBER-TYPE) means that the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN as a computable mathematical function over a set of input-output tuples, takes a number of type NUMBER-TYPE in its Nth argument position.")
(comment numberTypeOfResult "(#$numberTypeOfResult CODE-FN NUMBER-TYPE) means that, considered as a computable mathematical function over a set of input-output tuples, CODE-FN is expected to return a number of the type NUMBER-TYPE.")
(comment dataStorageTypeOfArg "(#$dataStorageTypeOfArg CODE-FN N STORAGE-TYPE) means that the implementation of #$CodingFunction CODE-FN assumes that the Nth argument input to CODE-FN is stored in memory via a convention indicated by the #$CodeVariableType STORAGE-TYPE (where this is a conventional programming data type such as 'char', 'int', 'float', etc.")
(comment dataStorageTypeOfResult "(#$dataStorageTypeOfResult CODE-FN STORAGE-TYPE) means that the implementation of the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN assumes that the result returned by CODE-FN is stored in memory via a convention indicated by the #$CodeVariableType STORAGE-TYPE.")
(comment semanticInterpretationTypeOfArg "(#$semanticInterpretationTypeOfArg CODE-FN ARGN INTERPRET-COL) means that, in the 'peripheral interpretation' of the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN, the numeric input to the ARGNth argument of CODE-FN encodes an instance of COL.")
(comment semanticInterpretationTypeOfResult "(#$semanticInterpretationTypeOfResult CODE-FN COL) means that, in the 'peripheral interpretation' of the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN, the numeric output returned by the function encodes an instance of COL.")
(comment selfEncodingArg "(#$selfEncodingArg CODE-FN N) means that relative to the peripheral semantic interpretation of the inputs and outputs of the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN, the numeric input to the Nth argument position of CODE-FN is to be interpreted as encoding exactly the number that is entered.")
(comment selfEncodingResult "(#$selfEncodingResult CODE-FN) means that the numeric result returned by the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN should be interpreted as just that number: i.e., there is no secondary or peripheral interpretation in which the number is an encoding or an address for anything else.")
(comment operationalRoleOfResult "(#$operationalRoleOfResult CODE-FN EXECUTION-ROLE) means that the semancit role in program exectuion of the numeric output from the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN is given by the #$ScopedExecutionRolePredicate EXECUTION-ROLE.")
(comment operationalRoleOfArg "(#$operationalRoleOfArg CODE-FN ARG-N EXECUTION-ROLE) means that the semantic role in program execution of the numeric input to the ARG-Nth argument of the #$CodingFunction CODE-FN is given by the #$ScopedExecutionRolePredicate EXECUTION-ROLE.")
(comment isolatedFrom-Uniprot "(#$isolatedFrom-Uniprot PEPTIDE-MOL-TYPE BLO-TYPE) states that according to Uniprot, the type of peptide moleucule, PEPTIDE-MOL-TYPE, has been isolated from the type of #$BiologicalLivingObject, BLO-TYPE.")
(comment BoneMarrowStroma "Instances of #$BoneMarrowStroma are portions of #$BoneMarrow that are not directly involved in the production of blood cells.  Of the marrow inside one #$LongBone, #$YellowMarrow makes up most of the stroma, and other non-blood-producing cells make up the rest. ")
(comment Person-DummyNamedEntity "This term is solely for use inside NL processing components.  It does not correspond to any real people.")
(comment Organization-DummyNamedEntity "This term is solely for use inside NL processing components.  It does not correspond to any real people.")
(comment Place-DummyNamedEntity "This term is solely for use inside NL processing components.  It does not correspond to any real people.")
(comment SOX9-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''SRY (sex determining region Y)-box 9''.")
(comment PrecartilageCondensationEvent "Instances of #$PrecartilageCondensationEvent are events in which #$MesenchymalStemCells produce a tight aggregation of cells which are committed to becoming mostly #$Chondrocytes, with some becoming #$Osteoblasts.  An event of this type is the first step in the growth and development of a #$Bone-BodyPart via #$EndochondralBoneGrowthAndDevelopment.")
(comment GeneExpressionTypeFn "(#$GeneExpressionTypeFn GIS-TYPE) denotes the collection of #$GeneExpression events in which a gene that is an instance of GIS-TYPE (an instance of #$GeneTypeBySpeciesAndProductFamily) is expressed.")
(comment geneTypeExpressionType "(#$geneTypeExpressionType GIS-TYPE EXPRESSION-TYPE) states that EXPRESSION-TYPE is the collection of gene expression events in which some instance of GIS-TYPE is expressed.")
(comment PTH-Human-GIS "The collection of human NucleicAcidSequence-GISes that code for protein named ''Parathyroid Hormone''.")
(comment ExperimentalRAPSGenerationConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms used for generating experimental reactive action plans.")
(comment ExperimentalRAPSGenerationScriptConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms used in representing elements of scripts where the script structure is targeted for leveraging reactive action plans.")
(comment ExperimentalRAPSGenerationMetaConstant "The collection of all #$CycLTerms used in leveraging script structures to generate reactive action plans.")
(comment UAVSurveillanceTheoryMt "The #$TheoryMicrotheory containing the CycL theory associated with #$AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV")
(comment AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV "The collection of all events wherein a UAV in flight attempts to view a so-called 'hot suspicious' target on the ground.  Normally, such attempts involve five canonical stages: #$PositioningUAVForObservation, #$PoweringOnAUAVCamera, #$EnablingUAVCameraTrackingCapability, a #$UAVObservationPassSeries (consisting in one or more observation passes at the intended target) and #$UAVCameraShutdown.")
(comment intendedObservationTargets "Where OBS-ATTEMPT is an (#$AttemptingFn Observing), (#$intendedObservationTargets OBS-ATTEMPT TARGET) means that whoever or whatever is performing (#$performedBy) OBS-ATTEMPT intends to observe TARGET for the duration of OBS-ATTEMPT.")
(comment intendedTarget-UAVObservation "(#$intendedTarget-UAVObservation VIEW-ATTEMPT TARGET) means that TARGET is the intended target of the attempted observation by UAV (#$AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV) VIEW-ATTEMPT.")
(comment uAVUsedInObservation "(#$uAVUsedInObservation VIEW-ATTEMPT UAV) means that UAV is the #$UnmannedAerialVehicle used to carry out the #$AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV VIEW-ATTEMPT.")
(comment UAVCamera "The collection of all cameras carried by instances of #$UnmannedAerialVehicle.")
(comment cameraUsedInAttemptedViewingOfTargetViaUAV "(#$cameraUsedInAttemptedViewingOfTargetViaUAV VIEW-ATTEMPT CAMERA) means that the #$UAVCamera CAMERA is one of the cameras used in #$AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV.")
(comment PositioningUAVForObservation "The collection of all #$FlyingViaAirTransportationDevice wherein a #$UnmannedAerialVehicle is positioned for a #$UAVObservationPassSeries")
(comment PoweringOnAUAVCamera "The collection of all events consisting in turning on power to a #$UAVCamera.")
(comment uAVCameraActivated "(#$uAVCameraActivated POWER-ON CAMERA) means that CAMERA is the #$UAVCamera turned on in the #$PoweringOnAUAVCamera CAMERA-ON.")
(comment TrackingViaUAVCamera "The collection of all instances of #$TrackingAnObject where a #$UAVCamera is a #$deviceUsed.")
(comment EnablingUAVCameraTrackingCapability "The collection of all events wherein #$TrackingViaUAVCamera in an activated #$UAVCamera is enabled.")
(comment uAVCameraTrackingEnabled "(#$uAVCameraTrackingEnabled ENABLE-TRACKING CAMERA-ENABLED) means that the #$UAVCamera CAMERA has its tracking capability enabled in the #$EnablingUAVCameraTrackingCapability ENABLE-TRACKING.")
(comment UAVObservationPass "The class of every observation pass made by an instance of #$UnmannedAerialVehicle in an #$AttemptedViewingOfSuspiciousTargetViaUAV.")
(comment UAVObservationPassType "A type level collection.  Each collection instance is a collection of #$UAVObservationPass instances characterized by some common feature.")
(comment UAVObservationPass-Overflight "The class of all #$UAVObservationPass instances wherein the UAV flys a straight-line trajectory over the observing target (the #$observationPassTarget).")
(comment UAVObservationPass-Circular "The class of all #$UAVObservationPass instances wherein the UAV flies a circular trajectory around the target.")
(comment UAVObservationPassSeries "The class of all events consisting in one or more instances of #$UAVObservationPass against a single observation target (the #$passSeriesTarget).")
(comment passSeriesTarget "(#$passSeriesTarget PASS-SERIES TARGET) means that TARGET is the common observation target (the #$observationPassTarget of every #$UAVObservationPass in the #$UAVObservationPassSeries PASS-SERIES.")
(comment observationPassTarget "(#$observationPassTarget PASS TARGET) means that TARGET is the unique #$intendedObservationTargets of the $UAVObservationPass PASS.")
(comment cameraUsedInObservationPass "(#$cameraUsedInObservationPass PASS CAMERA) means that CAMERA is the #$UAVCamera used in the #$UAVObservationPass PASS.")
(comment UAVCameraShutdown "The collection of all events wherein the power supply to a #$UAVCamera is turned off.")
(comment uAVCameraDeactivated "(#$uAVCameraDeactivated SHUTDOWN CAMERA) means that CAMERA is the #$UAVCamera whose power supply is turned off in the #$UAVCameraShutdown SHUTDOWN.")
(comment CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell "This is the collection of cell-signaling events that take place at the granularity of a single cell, i.e., events that begin when a cell has received an extra-cellular signal, and end with the response evoked. This collection is what  \"cell signaling\" refers to in most biology textbooks, in the sense of the three-step process of reception, transduction, and response.")
(disjointWith SignalTransduction-CellularProcess-SingleReaction CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell)
(comment CDKActivity "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$CyclinDependentKinaseMolecule is involved, including events in which it is activated, inactivated, or in which it acts as a #$catalyst.")
(comment getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepth-InUnit "<code>(#$getInterpolatedTemperatureAtDepth FIBER DATE DEPTH TEMPUNIT)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the temperature <code>TEMP</code> in the units <code>UNIT</code> at the (possibly interpolated) depth <code>DEPTH</code> at <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment assertionRequiredForJustificationParaphrase "<code>(#$assertionRequiredForJustificationParaphrase ASSERTION)</code> means that when <code>ASSERTION</code> is used in a proof, a paraphrase of that proof should explicitly mention <code>ASSERTION</code>.).")
(disjointWith CellMembrane EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembrane EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith Tonoplast EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith NuclearEnvelope EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(comment EndoplasmicReticulumLumen "The interior of the #$EndoplasmicReticulum, enclosed by the #$EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane. ")
(comment IonChannel "Each instance of #$IonChannel is a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex that naturally occurs as part of the membranes living cells and is involved in regulating the voltage gradient across the plasma membrane.  Ion channels form aqueous pores through lipid, hydrophobic biological membranes (the #$CellMembrane as well as those of certain #$Organelles), through which various #$Ions can pass.  #$IonChannels are usually specific for particular types of ions.  Some #$IonChannels are open all the time, while others can open and close in response to stimuli such as a change in cell potential (see #$VoltageGatedIonChannel), the binding of a signal molecule (see #$LigandGatedIonChannel), temperature changes, and other stimuli.")
(comment LigandGatedIonChannel "Instances of #$LigandGatedIonChannel are #$IonChannels in a #$Membrane-Biological that open or close when a specific ligand (see #$ExtracellularSignalingChemicalObject) binds to a receptor site on the extracellular side of the channel.")
(comment VoltageGatedIonChannel "Instances of #$VoltageGatedIonChannel are #$IonChannels in #$Membrane-Biological that open or close depending on the cell's membrane potential, i.e. the difference in #$Voltage between the #$Cytosol and the #$ExtracellularFluid.")
(comment preferredUnitForQuantityType "<code<(#$preferredUnitForQuantityType QT UNIT)</code> means that <code>UNIT</code> is the preferred unit for measuring the quantity type <code>QT</code> in the current context.")
(comment SteamBreakthrough-Rapid "A specialization of #$SteamBreakthrough.  Each instance of #$SteamBreakthrough-Rapid is a steam breakthrough that develops relatively rapidly.")
(comment SteamBreakthrough-Gradual "A specialization of #$SteamBreakthrough.  Each instance of #$SteamBreakthrough-Gradual is a steam breakthrough that develops relatively gradually.")
(disjointWith SteamBreakthrough-Rapid SteamBreakthrough-Gradual)
(comment rapidlyDevelopingVarietyOfType "<code>(#$rapidlyDevelopingVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE R-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that <code>R-EVT-TYPE</code> is the collection of all particularly rapidly developing instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment graduallyDevelopingVarietyOfType "<code>(#$graduallyDevelopingVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE R-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that <code>R-EVT-TYPE</code> is the collection of all gradually developing instances of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment HeatingOfSlottedLiner "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$HeatingOfSlottedLiner is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is heated.")
(comment HeatingOfSlottedLiner-Gradual "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$HeatingOfSlottedLiner is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is heated gradually.")
(comment HeatingOfSlottedLiner-Rapid "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$HeatingOfSlottedLiner is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is heated rapidly.")
(comment SteamChamber "#$SteamChamber is the collection of regions in which steam is present underground, having been injected there, typically by an #$InjectorWell.")
(comment SteamChamberGrowth "A specialization of #$GrowthEvent.  Each instance of #4SteamChamberGrowth is an event in which a  steam chamber grows.")
(comment SteamChamberGrowthTowardLiner "A specialization of #$SteamChamberGrowth.  Each instance of #$SteamChamberGrowthTowardLiner is an event in which a steam chamber grows toward a #$SlottedLiner.")
(comment GlycogenBreakdown-CellularSignalingScript "The collection of all #$CellSignalingProcess-LocalizedToSingleCell instances which begin with the binding of an epinephrine molecule to a G-Protein-Linked receptor site in the membrane of a liver cell, and which end in (comparatively) large-scale liberation of glucose in the cytosol as the result of glycogen breakdown, following a cascade of molecular reactions instantiating characteristic types.")
(comment ZeroSubCool "Zero sub-cool is a phenomenon that can occur at a SAGD well system.  At zero sub-cool at a region of the bottomhole, the actual bottomhole temperature is equal to or greater than the saturated steam temperature. During zero sub-cool, injected steam is short circuited into the producing well due to low bottomhole pressure.")
(comment SteamGettingCloserToProducer "The general collection of events that occur during thermally enhanced oil recovery using steam during which steam gets increasingly close to the producer.")
(comment ReducingSubCool "The collection of events in which sub-cool level reduction occurs.")
(comment underlyingProcessBehindSitType "<code>(#$underlyingProcessBehindSitType CAUSE-PROCESS EFFECT-PROCESS)</code> means that <code>CAUSE-PROCESS</code> is an underlying process behind <code>EFFECT-PROCESS</code>.")
(comment increasesLikelihood-SitSitType "(#$increasesLikelihood-SitSitType SIT SIT-TYPE) means that the occurrence of SIT increases the likelihood that instances of SIT-TYPE will occur.  SIT may or may not end up being a direct cause of that instance of SIT-TYPE.  ")
(comment Kankuamo-EthnicGroupOfNewWorldNatives "A sub-collection of #$EthnicGroupOfNewWorldNatives. Each instance is a member of the Kankuamo people.  They are based predominantly in Columbia. ")
(comment TribeOfIndigenousPeople "The collection of tribal organizations whose members are indigenous peoples of the area where the tribe is based.")
(comment partTypesAttenuated "<code>(#$partTypesAttenuated INDIVIDUAL PART-TYPE)</code> means that the instance of #$Individual <code>INDIVIDUAL</code> is unusual with respect to other instances of some collection of which it is an instance, in that the instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> it has as a part is less forceful in its effects than is normal.")
(comment causalPrecursorTypeForType "<code>(#$causalPrecursorTypeForType CAUSE-TYPE EFFECT-TYPE)</code> means <code>CAUSE-TYPE</code> is the collection of events which, <i>ceteris paribus</i>, when instantiated cause instances of <code>EFFECT-TYPE</code> to occur.   Unlike the more general predicate #$causes-SitTypeSitType (q.v.), this predicate is functional in the first argument position (the corresponding function is #$CausalPrecursorTypeForTypeFn).")
(comment inhibitedVarietyOfType "(#$inhibitedVarietyOfType EVT-TYPE AB-EVT-TYPE) means that AB-EVT-TYPE is the collection of all inhibited instances of EVT-TYPE.")
(comment InhibitedFn "(#$InhibitedFn EVENT-TYPE) denotes the specialization of EVENT-TYPE whose instances are inhibited relative to ordinary instances of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment MajorPetroleumProductionEventType "The collection of collections of events that are generally deemed to be extremely important to attend to during normal well operation.")
(comment SAGDProductionWellOutflow "A specialization of #$WellOutflow.  Each instance of #$SAGDProductionWellOutflow is an event in which fluid flows from a #$SAGDProducerWell.")
(comment WellOutflow-WithOptimalOilToWaterRatio "The collection of all well outflow events wherein the oil/water ratio is within the optimal range.")
(comment WellInflow-WithOptimalOilToWaterRatio "The collection of all well inflow events wherein the oil/water ratio is within the optimal range.")
(comment SteamResidesInSteamChamber "The collection of events which occur during thermally enhanced oil recovery using steam, wherein the steam resides in the steam chamber.")
(comment ReductionOfSteamInjectionPressureOrRate "The collection of events in which steam injection rate or steaminjection pressure is reduced.")
(comment appropriateCorrectiveActionType "<code>(#$appropriateCorrectiveActionType EVENT-TYPE SCRIPT CORRECTIVE-TYPE)</code> means that if <code>SCRIPT</code> is proceeding sub-optimally because an instance of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> has occurred during it, an appropriate means of re-optimizing the process is to perform an instance of <code>CORRECTIVE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment candidateRemedialActionTypeDuringType "<code>(#$candidateRemedialActionTypeDuringType C-TYPE SUPERTYPE)</code> means <code>C-TYPE</code> is a candidate remedial action during <code>SUPERTYPE</code>.")
(comment hasStrongCulturalTiesTo "(#$hasStrongCulturalTiesTo AGT1 GEO-AGENT) means that AGT1 has strong cultural ties to GEO-AGENT.  ")
(comment eventTypeVideoClassificationExpansionRole "<code>(#$eventTypeVideoClassificationExpansionRole ROLE)</code> means that <code>ROLE</code>, an instance of #$BinarySituationPredicate, is used to generate additional features from specified features used in multi-media classification systems.")
(comment MonitoringTemperaturesInSystemWithDTSAndThermocouples "A specialization of #$Monitoring.  Each instance of #$MonitoringTemperaturesInSystemWithDTSAndThermocouples is an event in which the temperatures in a system are monitored with both #$Thermocouples and #$DistributedTemperatureSensors.")
(comment DiscrepantReadingsOfObjectTypeFromDevicesOfTypeFn "(#$DiscrepantReadingsOfObjectTypeFromDevicesOfTypeFn OBJ-TYPE DEVTYPE1 DEVTYPE2) denoted the collection of situations in which an instance of DEVTYPE1 and and instance of DEVTYPE2 are providing discrepant information about an instance of OBJ-TYPE.")
(comment ActiveTransportProtein "Each instance of #$ActiveTransportProtein is a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex that naturally occurs as part of the membranes living cells and uses chemical energy to transport ions or molecules - usually a specific type, depending on the type of transporter - across the biological membrane of which it is a part. ")
(comment TransportATPase "Each instance of #$TransportATPase is a #$MembraneTransportProtein that actively transports ions or molecules - usually a specific type - against its concentration gradient across the biological membrane of which it is a part.  To do so, it uses chemical energy derived from hydrolyzing #$AdenosineTriphosphate to remove one #$PhosphateIon.
")
(comment MeasuringDeviceProducingInaccurateReadingsFn "(#$MeasuringDeviceProducingInaccurateReadingsFn  GAUGE-TYPE) denotes the collection of events in which an instance of GAUGE-TYPE produces inaccurate readings.")
(comment CellularCommunicationByDirectContact "The collection of instances of #$CellularCommunication where the #$transmittingCell and the #$targetCells are directly adjacent, so that signals can be transferred either by molecules on the surface of the cells, or by signal molecules dissolved in the cytosol when the cells are connected by cell-cell junctions.")
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue Cell-CellConnection)
(disjointWith Cell Cell-CellConnection)
(comment Cell-CellConnection "The collection of specialized connections which link two cells and which function to pass molecules from one cell to the other.  Two notable specs exist: #$GapJunction, instances of which occur between animal cells, and #$Plasmodesma, instances of which occur between plant cells.")
(comment GapJunction "The collection of specialized connections which link the #$Cytoplasm of two adjacent #$AnimalCells.  They form hydrophilic channels along which molecules and ions can pass, coupling the cells chemically and electrically.")
(comment Plasmodesma "The collection of specialized connections which link the #$Cytoplasm of two adjacent #$BotanicalCells.  They form hydrophilic channels along which molecules and ions can pass, coupling the cells chemically.")
(disjointWith GapJunction Plasmodesma)
(comment seriousMaleficiary "An #$ActorSlot and a specialization of #$maleficiary .  <code>(#$seriousMaleficiary EVENT AGENT)</code> means that AGENT's interests, life, health, or well being were seriously impacted in a negative fashion by EVENT.")
(comment WellSurveillance "The collection of events in which the condition of a well is monitored over a period of time.")
(comment SAGDWellSurveillance "The collection of events in which the condition of a SAGD well is monitored over a period of time.")
(comment StoppingActionOfOthers "An instance of #$TemporalObjectType and a specialization of #$Interfering.  Each instance of #$StoppingActionOfOthers is an event in which one or more intelligent agents interferes with an event, already underway, being undertaken by one or more different intelligent agents, with the result that the event is prematurely terminated.")
(comment RAPStatementClassificationType "The type-level collection of every kind of #$ComputerCodeStatement whose instances appear in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS (including #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS).")
(comment RAPMappingPredicate "The collection of all instances of #$BinaryPredicate used in mapping #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatements to the conditions that they specify.")
(comment RAPStructurePredicate "The collection of all predicates used in specifying the syntactic structure of instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.")
(comment RAPSpecificationStatement "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeStatements used in specifying reactive action packages (instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS).")
(comment ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS "The collection of all completely specified reactive action packages (RAPs), considered as syntactic information structures.")
(comment ReactiveActionPackageIndex "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that serve as identifying indices for instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS (RAPs).  Each RAP has exactly one index which serves as its unique identifiers.  The index name frequently denotes an action type which is implemented by the RAP.")
(comment RAPIndexFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction used for reifying and referencing instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageIndex.  Where RAP is an instance of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS, (#$RAPIndexFn RAP) denotes the unique identifier used for referencing RAP in other instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.")
(comment rAPIndexName "(#$rAPIndexName INDEX STRING) means that STRING is the #$CharacterString which INDEX attaches to INDEX's reactive action package (#$indexOfRAP) as a unique identifier.")
(comment rAPIndexSituationType "Frequently, the indices used by reactive action packages (see #$ReactiveActionPackageIndex) indicate the class of situation which the RAP specification is intended to implement.  (#$rAPIndexSituationType INDEX SIT-TYPE) means that SIT-TYPE is the class of #$Situation specified by the #$ReactiveActionPackageIndex INDEX.")
(comment indexOfRAP "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$RAPIndexFn.  Where RAP is an instance of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS, (#$indexOfRAP RAP INDEX) means that INDEX is a #$ComputerCodeExpression which serves as the unique identifier used for referencing RAP in other instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.")
(comment RAPClauseSpecificationStatement "The collection of all clauses which appear in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.")
(comment reactiveActionPackageHasClause "Where RAP is a #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS and CLAUSE isa #$RAPClauseSpecificationStatement, (#$reactiveActionPackageHasClause RAP CLAUSE) means that CLAUSE is a clause that appears as a proper sub-statement in RAP.")
(comment rAPClauseTypeTag "Where CLAUSE-TYPE is a specialization of #$RAPClauseSpecificationStatement, (#$rAPClauseTypeTag CLAUSE-TYPE ID-STRING) means that ID-STRING is the #$CharacterString conventionally used to identify instances of CLAUSE-TYPE in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.")
(comment RAPConditionSpecificationStatement "#$RAPConditionSpecificationStatement is the collection of all clauses which appear in RAP specifications and which are used to state conditions for the process being specified.")
(comment rAPStatementConditionCode "Where COND-STATEMENT is a #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatement, (#$rAPStatementConditionCode COND-STATEMENT COND-CODE-STRING) means that COND-CODE-STRING is a #$CharacterString which gives the form of the code in which the condition specified by COND-STATEMENT is expressed.")
(comment rAPStatementCode "Where STATEMENT is any #$RAPSpecificationStatement, (#$rAPStatementCode STATEMENT CODE-STRING) means that CODE-STRING is a #$CharacterString giving the form of the code in which STATEMENT is expressed.")
(comment PredicateMonitoringRAPStatement "The collection of all 'MONITOR-STATE' clauses that appear in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.  Instances allow a #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS to synchronize itself with conditions in the world by either waiting or looping until a certain predicate (which could be expressed as as a complex logical formula with open variables) is satisfied.")
(comment stateMonitored-RAP "(stateMonitored-RAP MONITOR-STATE CONTENT-TEST) means that the #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified gives the predicate (query) and context such that the #$PredicateMonitoringRAPStatement monitors for whether said predicate is true in said context.")
(comment TimeMonitoringRAPStatement "The collection of all 'MONITOR-TIME' clauses that appear in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.  Such clauses cause the RAP to suspend for a specified period of time, which may be given either in absolues terms (see #$referenceDelayDeadlineAbsolute-RAP) or relative terms (see #$referenceDelayDeadlineRelative-RAP).")
(comment referenceDelayDeadlineRelative-RAP "(#$referenceDelayDeadlineRelative-RAP MONITOR-TIME WAIT-DUR DUR-UNTIL-SUSPEND) means that the #$TimeMonitoringRAPStatement MONITOR-TIME says that the task specified by the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS in which MONITOR-TIME appears must suspend when the #$Time-Quantity DUR-UNTIL-SUSPEND has elapsed, and must at that point wait for a duration of WAIT-DUR until resuming.")
(comment referenceDelayDeadlineAbsolute-RAP "(#$referenceDelayDeadlineAbsolute-RAP MONITOR-TIME INTERVAL) means that the #$TimeMonitoringRAPStatement MONITOR-TIME says that the task specified by the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS in which MONITOR-TIME appears must suspend at the start of the #$TimeInterval INTERVAL, and remain suspended until INTERVAL ends.")
(comment SitTypeMonitoringRAPStatement "The collection of all 'MONITOR-EVENT' clauses that appear in instances of #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS.  Such clauses cause the RAP to suspend until a situation of a specified type is instantiated.")
(comment waitForEventType-RAP "(#$waitForEventType-RAP MONITOR-EVENT SIT-TYPE) means that execution of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS in which MONITOR-EVENT appears is instructed to suspend until an event of type SIT-TYPE occurs.")
(comment RepeatWhileConditionRAPStatement "The RAP language uses REPEAT-WHILE clauses to explicitly declare looping RAPS.  See #$repeatWhileCondition-RAP.")
(comment repeatWhileCondition-RAP "Where REPEAT-WHILE is a #$RepeatWhileConditionRAPStatement, (#$repeatWhileCondition-RAP REPEAT-WHILE TEST) means that REPEAT-WHILE specifies that the execution of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS that includes REPEAT-WHILE should iterate for as long as as the query stored with TEST continues to return true in context.")
(comment SuccessCriterionForRAPStatement "In a  #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS or RAP, a #$SuccessCriterionForRAPStatement clause says that an execution of the RAP cannot succeed unless a specified condition (see #$successCriterion-RAP) is true.")
(comment successCriterion-RAP "Where SUCCEED is a #$SuccessCriterionForRAPStatement, (#$successCriterion-RAP SUCCEED TEST) means that SUCCEED states that executions of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which it is a part cannot succeed unless the query saved with TEST is true in the context that TEST specifies.")
(comment FailureCriterionForRAPStatement "Instances of #$FailureCriterionForRAPStatement are used in circumstances where a programmer wants to specify conditions under which execution of a #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS will fail.  A  #$FailureCriterionForRAPStatement states that executions of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which it is a part will fail if the condition that the  #$FailureCriterionForRAPStatement (#$failureCriterion-RAP) specifies becomes true.")
(comment failureCriterion-RAP "Where FAIL is a #$FailureCriterionForRAPStatement, (#$failureCriterion-RAP FAIL TEST) means that FAIL states that executions of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which FAIL is a component will fail if the query stored with TEST returns true in the context TEST specifies.")
(comment PreconditionCriterionForRAPStatement "The collection of all #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatements that state preconditions for executing RAPS.  More specifically, each instance of #$PreconditionCriterionForRAPStatement is a clause which states that the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which it is a component should not be executed unless a specified condition (see #$precondition-RAP) is met.")
(comment precondition-RAP "Where PRECONDITIONS is a #$PreconditionCriterionForRAPStatement, (#$precondition-RAP PRECONDITIONS TEST) means that PRECONDITIONS states that the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which it is a part should be executed only if the query saved with TEST returns true in the context TEST specifies immediately prior to the start of execution.")
(comment ConstraintCriterionForRAPStatement "The collection of all #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatements specifying perdurant constraints for the executions of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS instances they are part of.  That is, each instance of #$ConstraintCriterionForRAPStatement states a condition that must remain true for the entirety of each execution of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which it is a part if said execution is to succeed.")
(comment constraint-RAP "Where CONSTRAINTS is a #$ConstraintCriterionForRAPStatement, (#$constraint-RAP CONSTRAINTS TEST) means that CONSTRAINTS states that the query saved with TEST must be true in the context saved for the duration of an execution of the #$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS of which CONSTRAINTS is a part, in order for that execution to count as successful.")
(comment standardDeviceInCalibration "<code>(#$standardDeviceInCalibration CAL DEV)</code> means that in the #$Calibration event <code>CAL</code>, the device used as the standard is <code>DEV</code>.")
(comment DurationEstimateRAPStatement "A collection of #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatements.  Each instance specifies the expected duration of executions of the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) in which it is embedded.")
(comment estimatedExecutionTime-RAP "Where DURATION-SPEC is a #$DurationEstimateRAPStatement, (#$estimatedExecutionTime-RAP DURATION-SPEC DUR) means that DURATION-SPEC specifies that DUR is the estimated completion time for executions of the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) of which DURATION-SPEC is a part.")
(comment TimeOutInstructionRAPStatement "The collection of every #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatement that specifies a maximum duration deadline for executions of the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) of which it is a part.")
(comment maxDelayDuration-RAP "Where TIMEOUT-SPEC is a #$TimeOutInstructionRAPStatement, (#$maxDelayDuration-RAP TIMEOUT-SPEC DURATION) means that TIMEOUT-SPEC specifies that any execution of the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) of which it is a part should error out if it takes longer than DURATION to succeed.")
(comment FutilityThresholdSpecifyingRAPStatement "The collection of all #$RAPConditionSpecificationStatements that override the default futile loop detector thresholds for executions of the RAPs in which they appear.  More specifically, each instance of #$FutilityThresholdSpecifyingRAPStatement either specifies a number which is the maximum number of times any method in the enclosing RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) should be tried (see #$futilityThresholdIterationCount-RAP), or specifies that futile loop detection should be turned off (see #$futilityLoopDetectionTurnedOff-RAP).")
(comment futilityThresholdIterationCount-RAP "Where FUTILITY-LIMIT is a #$FutilityThresholdSpecifyingRAPStatement, (#$futilityThresholdIterationCount-RAP FUTILITY-LIMIT COUNT) means that FUTILITY-LIMIT states that COUNT is the maximum number of times any method can be tried in executing the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) of which FUTILITY-LIMIT is a part.")
(comment futilityLoopDetectionTurnedOff-RAP "Where FUTILITY-LIMIT is a #$FutilityThresholdSpecifyingRAPStatement, (#$futilityLoopDetectionTurnedOff-RAP FUTILITY-LIMIT) means that FUTILITY-LIMIT turns off futility loop detection for the RAP (#$ReactiveActionPackageSpecification-CWIS) of which FUTILITY-LIMIT is a part.")
(comment TypeTypeQuaternaryRuleMacroPredicate "A specialization of #$RuleMacroPredicate and #$QuaternaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$TypeTypeQuaternaryRuleMacroPredicate relates a count in its fourth argument place and a collection in its third argument place to a #$Collection in its second argument place via an instance of #$BinaryPredicate in its first argument place.  One example of instances of this collection is #$relationAllExistsCount.")
(comment relationPercentExists "A quaternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that some percentage of a collection's instances stand in a particular binary relationship to some instance of another class.  <code>(#$relationPercentExists BINPRED COL1 COL2 PERCENT)</code> states that, for <code>PERCENT</code> of the instances <code>INS1</code>of <code>COL1</code>, there exists some instance <code>INS2</code> of <code>COL2</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INS1 INS2)</code>.  For example, <code>(#$relationPercentExists #$owns #$HumanAdult #$Automobile 0.05)</code> means that five percent of #$HumanAdults own a car.")
(comment relationExistsPercent "A quaternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that some percentage of a collection's instances stand in a particular binary relationship to some instance of another class.  <code>(#$relationExistsPercent BINPRED COL1 COL2 PERCENT)</code> states that, for <code>PERCENT</code> of the instances <code>INS2</code>of <code>COL2</code>, there exists some instance <code>INS1</code> of <code>COL1</code> such that <code>(BINPRED INS1 INS2)</code>.  For example, <code>(#$relationExistsPercent #$politicalPartyMembers #$PoliticalParty (#$AdultFn #$UnitedStatesPerson) .3) states that 30 percent of adult #$UnitedStatesPersons are members of a political party.")
(comment relationInstancePercent "A quaternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that some percentage of a collection's instances stand in a given binary relationship to a particular thing.  <code>(#$relationInstancePercent BINPRED THING COL2 PERCENT)</code> states that, for <code>PERCENT</code> of the instances <code>INS2</code>of <code>COL2</code>, <code>(BINPRED THING INS2)</code> holds.  For example, (#$relationInstancePercent #$ailmentTypeAffects #$SickleCellAnemia #$EthnicGroupOfBlacksOfTheUS .002) states that 1 in 500 American Blacks suffer from #$SickleCellAnemia.")
(comment CalibrationOfTypeFn "(#$CalibrationOfTypeFn TYPE) denote the collection of calibrations of instances of TYPE.")
(comment calibrationOfType "(#$calibrationOfType TYPE CALIB-TYPE) means CALIB-TYPE is the collection of calibrations of instances of TYPE.")
(comment ReplacingFn "A collection-forming function.  Takes a class of object, and returns the class of scripts in which that type of object is replaced.")
(comment relationPercentInstance "A quaternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can be used to state that some percentage of a collection's instances stand in a given binary relationship to a particular thing.  <code>(#$relationPercentInstance BINPRED COL1 THING PERCENT)</code> states that, for <code>PERCENT</code> of the instances <code>INS1</code> of <code>COL1</code>, <code>(BINPRED INS1 THING)</code> holds.  For example, (#$relationPercentInstance #$providesServiceType #$UsedAutoDealership (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile) .1) states that ten percent of used car dealerships offer auto repair services.")
(comment CandidateAgent "Instances of #$CandidateAgent are persons, political parties or pairs of running mates who are engaged in running for office.")
(comment WellSaturatedWithSteam "The collection of events in which a producer well used during #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamFlooding becomes saturated with steam.")
(comment dataFromDateAtDepthEvincesEventType-FromSource "(#$dataFromDateAtDepthEvincesEventType-FromSource NEG-EVENT-TYPE WELL DATE DEPTH AGENT) means that, according to the criteria dictated by AGENT, the significant well event type NEG-EVENT-TYPE occurs at WELL on DATE at the measured depth DEPTH.")
(comment ExtractingPetroleumUsingArtificialLift "A specialization of #$ExtractingPetroleum.  Each instance of #$ExtractingPetroleumUsingArtificialLift is an event in which petroleum is extracted using an #$ArtificialLiftDevice.")
(comment ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamInjectionAndArtificialLift "The collection of events in which both stam injection and artificial lifts are used to extract petroleum.")
(comment hasWinningPositionInElectionOrganization "(#$hasWinningPositionInElectionOrganization WINNING ORGANIZATION) means that in the WinningPositionInElection, WINNING, a position in ORGANIZATION was won.")
(comment MultiMediaClassificationPredicate "the most general class of predicates used specifically to enumerate features useful for multimedia classification tasks.")
(disjointWith (PartTypeFn HomoSapiens Head-Vertebrate) (CollectionDifferenceFn Head-Vertebrate (PartTypeFn HomoSapiens Head-Vertebrate)))
(comment eventTypeInferredFeatures "<code>(#$eventTypeInferredFeatures EVT-TYPE FEATURE)</code> means that <code>FEATURE</code>, which can be any #$Thing useful for classifying multi-media works as containing depictions of events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, is a classification feature that has been inferred, or derived from the KB (or through some other processing), rather than stipluated.")
(comment genlMultiMediaFeatures "An instance of #$MultiMediaClassificationPredicate, <code>(#$genlMultiMediaFeatures FEATURE GENL-FEATURE)</code> means that <code>GENL-FEATURE</code> is a more general classification feature than <code>FEATURE</code>; specifically, any time <code>FEATURE</code> is present, <code>GENL-FEATURE</code> is also present.")
(comment MRSharedAttackType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$AttackOnTangible which are means of attack recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment MRSharedKillingOrInjuryType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$AttackOnTangible which are means of killing or injury recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment MRSharedPropertyDamageType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$AttackOnTangible which are means of damaging property recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment MRSharedDemonstrationFormType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$PublicProtesting which are forms of demonstration recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment MRSharedJudicialSentenceType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$PurposefulAction and #$SocialOccurrence which are types of judicial sentence recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment effectArg "(#$effectArg PRED N) means #$Predicate PRED incorporates a cause/effect relation between two of its arguments, and the Nth argument to PRED is the effect argument.  Cf. #$causeArg.")
(comment causeArg "(#$causeArg PRED N) means #$Predicate PRED incorporates a cause/effect relation between two of its arguments, and the Nth argument to PRED is the cause argument.  Cf. #$effectArg.")
(comment DemolitionOfStructure "A collection of events.  In a #$DemolitionOfStructure event, some #$FixedStructure is physically destroyed on purpose.  Such events can occur with the permission of the owner of the structure, as when an old building is torn down to make way for new construction, or they can occur as part of an attack.")
(disjointWith (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet KidnappingSomeone ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing PhysicalAttackOnPersonWithoutConsent DemolitionOfStructure)) (CollectionDifferenceFn AttackOnTangible (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet KidnappingSomeone ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing PhysicalAttackOnPersonWithoutConsent DemolitionOfStructure))))
(disjointWith (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing PhysicalAttackOnPersonWithoutConsent)) (CollectionDifferenceFn AttackOnTangible (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing PhysicalAttackOnPersonWithoutConsent))))
(disjointWith (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing DemolitionOfStructure)) (CollectionDifferenceFn AttackOnTangible (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet ShootingAndHittingSomething StabbingSomething Bombing DemolitionOfStructure))))
(comment MRSharedCrimeType "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal which are types of crime recognized in the #$MRSharedOntology.")
(comment AdjustingAnIndustrialChoke "A specialization of #$AdjustingAValve. Each instance of #$AdjustingAnIdustrialChoke is an event in which some industrial choke is either opened or closed.")
(comment ClosingAnIndustrialChoke "A specialization of #$ClosingAValve. Each instance of #$ClosingAnIndustrialChoke is an event in which an #$IndustrialChoke is made more restrictive of flow through a conduit.")
(comment OpeningAnIndustrialChoke "A specialization of #$OpeningAValve. Each instance of #$OpeningAnIndustrialChoke is an event in which an #$IndustrialChoke is made less restrictive of flow through a conduit.")
(comment ConstrictingDownstreamPipeSegment "The collection of events in which a relatively downstream portion of a pipe system is constricted.")
(comment IncreasingPressureInUpstreamPipeSegment "The collection of events in which the pressure in a relatively upstream portion of a pipe system increases.")
(comment semanticReferenceTypeOfParameter "(#$semanticReferenceTypeOfParameter PARAM COL) means that values specified for the #$CodingFunctionParameter PARAM denote instances of COL in the extended semantic interpretation of the standard library function which has PARAM as a #$CodingFunctionParameter.")
(comment dataStorageTypeOfParameter "Where NTHPARAMOFFN is a reified argument position of some #$CodingFunction, (#$dataStorageTypeOfParameter NTHPARAMOFFN STORAGE-TYPE) means that the normative pragmatics of the language which includes the #$CodingFunction require that values of NTHPARAMOFFN be stored using a method indicated by the #$CodeVariableType STORAGE-TYPE.")
(comment operationalRoleOfParameter "Where NTHPARAMOFFN is a reified argument position of a #$CodingFunction (i.e., where NTHPARAMOFFN is an instance of #$CodingFunctionParameter), (#$operationalRoleOfParameter NTHPARAMOFFN ROLE) means that the pragmatics of the language that includes the function featuring NTHPARAMOFFN mandate that the numeric values play the role indicated by the #$ScopedExecutionRolePredicate ROLE.")
(comment numberTypeOfParameter "Where NTHPARAMOFFN is a the reified nth argument position of a certain #$CodingFunction, (#$numberTypeOfParameter NTHPARAMOFFN NUM-TYPE) means that in the normative specification of the language of which the #$CodingFunction is a part, numeric inputs to NTHPARAMOFFN are expected to be numbers of type NUM-TYPE.")
(comment numberTypeOfParameter "Where NTHPARAMOFFN is a the reified nth argument position of a certain #$CodingFunction, (#$numberTypeOfParameter NTHPARAMOFFN NUM-TYPE) means that in the normative specification of the language of which the #$CodingFuncition is a part, numeric inputs to NTHPARAMOFFN are expected to be numbers of type NUM-TYPE.")
(comment WastingDuringFn "(#$WastingFn WASTED-TYPE PROCESS) denotes the collection of events during which some quantity of WASTED-TYPE is wasted during an instance of PROCESS.")
(comment wastedDuring "(#$wastedDuring WASTED-TYPE PROCESS WASTING-PROCESS) means WASTING-PROCESS is the collection of events during which some quantity of WASTED-TYPE is wasted during an instance of PROCESS.")
(comment wastedResource "(#$wastedResource EVT R) means some non-trivial amount of resourse R is wasted during EVT.")
(comment ComputerHardwareExpansionCardType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer expansion cards of a certain sort.")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-Maintained "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that are, in the appropriate context, being currently maintained.")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-Recommended "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that are, in the appropriate context, currently recommended for use.")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-Passive "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that have, in the appropriate context, the product lifecycle phase status of \"passive\".")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-EndOfLife "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that, in the appropriate context, are being phased out or depricated.")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-Demise "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that, in the appropriate context, have been retired from use.")
(comment ProductLifeCyclePhase-Unknown "The collection of instances of #$Artifact-Generic that lack, in the appropriate context, a product Lifecycle phase status.")
(comment slotNumber "Relates a type of slot to an integer representing its location.")
(disjointWith OperatingSystem-Hypervisor SmartPhoneOS)
(comment OperatingSystem-Hypervisor "A type of #$OperatingSystem. Each instance of this collection is an operating system program whose program copies are typically associcated with hypervisor (virtual machine manager) functionality.  Instances of this collection act as virtual bios that can host guest operating systems.  They either run directly on the hardware -- Type 1 \"bare metal\", or the run on the top of the native OS running on the machine  -- Type 2 \"hosted\".")
(comment ProvisionedSoftwareProduct "Instances of this collection are composite entities that consist of a instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW (versioned or not) and some information pertaining to their configuration in a particular environment.  For example the composite entity that is a particular version of Linux SuSE together with data regarding the default settings it needs to have to run on Bob's network would be an instance of this collection.")
(comment softwarePortionOfProduct "This predicate relates an instance of ProvisionedSoftwareProduct to the #$ComputerProgram-CW that is configured in that product")
(comment ComponentConfigurationSpecification "Each instance of this collection is a specification of the allowable ways a particular component can be configured.")
(comment modelPositionHasSpecification "relates a ComponentPosition-Generic (typically either a model position or slot position) to a specification that is allowed in that position.")
(comment ConfiguredServerCabinet "The collection of server cabinets and configuration accessories (patch cables, fittings, etc.) that are bundled together into a configured \"kit\" that is ready for the installation of the server hardware and associated components")
(comment ComputerServerCabinet-BladeServer "The collection of computer server cabinets designed to hold multiple blade-style server machines")
(comment BladeServerCabinet-Rittal-47RU "The collection of Rittal computer server cabinets with 47 rack units")
(comment PatchPanel-Network "A device that routes connections from one jack to another -- typically from a jack on the front to a jack on the back. ")
(comment LevitonPatchPanel-24Port "The collection of 24 port patch panels by Leviton.")
(comment CopperCable-Network "The collection of #$ComputerNetworkingCables whose primary component in the non-insulation part of the wire is copper.")
(comment FiberOpticCable-MultiMode "The collection of instances of #$FiberOpticCable that support more than one light propagation path.  Typically used in shorter cable runs than single-mode fibers.")
(comment FiberOpticCable-SingleMode "The collection of instances of #$FiberOpticCable that support exactly one light propagation path.  Typically used in longer cable runs than multi-mode fibers.")
(comment FiberCableJunctionBox "The collection of boxes which enclose junctions of Fiber Optic cables.  These operate as a patch panel for fiber optic connections")
(comment VMNetworkByAccessibility "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of VM networks configured to operate in a certain way with respect to how it behaves or is accessible on the local intranet")
(comment ReinstantiateVMOnNewHardware "The collection of service events which involve bringing up a new virtual machine on a new portion of hardware after some hardware failure.")
(comment ComputerHardwareFailure "The collection of computer hardware failures.")
(comment ResourcePoolComponentFailure "The collection of events in which some component of a resource pool has failed.")
(comment intervalTypeBetween-Inclusive "This is the corresponding predicate to #$IntervalTypeBetweenFn-Inclusive.  (intervalTypeBetween-Inclusive INT-TYPE-1 INT-TYPE-2 INT-TYPE-BETWEEN-INCLUSIVE) means that INT-TYPE-BETWEEN-INCLUSIVE is the collection of continuous time intervals that run from the start of an instance of the first argument until the end of the next occurring instance of the second argument. ")
(comment SystemDependentMaxInteger "An indeterminate term that denotes a non-negative integer that represents the maximum number of something allowed by the system involved.  The actual integer denoted depends on the context of the assertion in which this appears (both the #$Microtheory context and the context of the predicate in which it serves as argument are relevant).")
(comment ComputerServerWithChassisFn "(#$ComputerServerWithChassisFn CHASSIS-TYPE) denotes the collection of computer blade or rack servers that utilize CHASSIS-TYPE.")
(comment ComputerProcessorTypeByMicroArchitecture "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a type of computer processor that share the same CPU micro-architecture.")
(comment Nehalem-CPUMicroArchitecture "The collection of computer processors that utilize Intel's Nehalem CPU microarchitecture.  Processors with this microarchitecture are built using the 45 nanometer technology tier.")
(comment Westmere-CPUMicroArchitecture "The collection of computer processors that utilize Intel's Westmere CPU microarchitecture.  These processors were based on shrinking Nehalem architrecture.  Processors with this microarchitecture are built using the 32 nanometer technology tier.")
(comment computerHasProcessor "(#$computerHasProcessor COMPUTER PROCESSOR) means that PROCESSOR is one of the #$ComputerProcessors in COMPUTER.")
(comment Nehalem-WestmereArchitectureBasedComputerProcessor "The collection of computer processors that utilize Intel's Nehalem architecture.  Instances of this collection include Nehalem 45nm and Westmere 32nm.")
(comment CardPort12-NDCardPortStrategy "stub")
(comment AccessBlockModelType "A collection of types of access blocks.")
(comment ComputerHardwareComponentType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a type of hardware computer component including such non-electronic components as rack chassis.  An important specialization of this is #$ComputerHardwareDeviceType.")
(comment TransferRate-ComputerData "A specialization of #$ComputerQuantity, #$Rate, and #$PhysicalQuantity (qq.v.). Each instance of this collection is some particular measure of the data transfer rate of some component of a computer system.  Measured in transfers per second, or, more commonly, as gigatransfers per second.")
(comment TransfersPerSecond "(#$TransfersPerSecond REAL) denotes the rate at which data is transferred when REAL number of transfers are performed per second.  Note that this measurement is neutral to the size of the data package transferred (word length).  So this number alone does not allow you to determine the actual bit rate.  In general, word length (bits/transfer unit) x transfers/second = bits/second")
(comment quickPathInterconnect_BusSpeed "(#$quickPathInterconnect_BusSpeed PROC GTS) means that the QPI (an Intel interconnect protocol) rate is GTS -- typically recorded in gigatransfers/second")
(comment processorClockSpeed "(#$processorClockSpeed PROC FREQ) means that the clock speed of the CPU associated with PROC is FREQ.")
(comment VendorNeutralSoftwareSpecification "Instances of this collection are functional specifications of a type of software and various properties or requirements that a piece of software must satisfy to be an acceptable component in some system or other.  Typically these serve as placeholders in various complex models of systems or devices and are linked to the acceptable configured software packages that satisfy the requirements ")
(comment PowerStrip-54Receptacle "The collection of power strips with 54 sockets or receptacles.")
(comment PowerStrip-48Receptacle "The collection of power strips with 48 sockets or receptacles.")
(comment DeviceWithDualVoltagePowerSupply "The collection of electrical devices whose power supplies can work within either the 120 or 240 voltage ranges.")
(comment DualVoltage-Device "The collection of electrical devices that can work within either the 120 or 240 voltage ranges.")
(comment PCIExpress-ExpansionSlotStandard "The collection of computer expansion slots that conform to the PCIExpress protocol.")
(comment ComputerExpansionConnectionTypeByProtocol "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer expansion slots or port that share an official protocol or standard.")
(comment expansionDeviceInterfaceType "relates a type of electonic device that can serve as a computer peripheral or add-on module to the interface type by which it is connected to the computer.")
(comment manufacturerAssignedDesignation "relates an artifact type to one of its manufacturer assigned identification strings.  This is the common generalization of things such as part numbers, model numbers, model name, etc.  It is often best to utilize a more specific relation when representing knowledge as these strings may not be completely context free even within the scope of the same manufacturer.")
(comment SerialAttachedSCSI-Bus "The collection of computer buses that conform to the SAS protocol.")
(comment interfaceTypeSpeed "relates a device type to the rate at which it can communicate via its interface.")
(comment SerialAttachedSCSI-Bus-3GBperSecond "The collection of computer buses that conform to the SAS protocol and operate at 3 gigabits/s.")
(comment SerialAttachedSCSI-Bus-6GBperSecond "The collection of computer buses that conform to the SAS protocol and operate at 6 gigabits/s.")
(comment ComputerComponentTypeByFormFactor "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer components that share a \"form factor\" -- a set of standards that define various physical dimensions.")
(comment 2_point_5_Inch_SFF-DiskDrive "The collection of computer disk drives whose disks are 2.5 inches and are designed for small form factor (SFF) computers.")
(comment HotSwappableComputerComponent "The collection of all computer components that can be switched out without requiring a restart of the system.")
(comment PowerSupplyCouplerByInternationalStandard "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of power supply couplers that conform to a certain set of international standards (e.g IEC60320-C12)\"")
(comment IEC60320-1-C14 "The collection of power supply couplers that conform to the IEC 60320-1 C13/C14 standard that are female connectors.")
(comment IEC60320-1-C13 "The collection of power supply couplers that conform to the IEC 60320-1 C13/C14 standard that are male connectors.")
(comment IEC60320-1-C13_C14 "The collection of power supply couplers that conform to the IEC 60320-1 C13/C14 standard -- C13 refers to the male coupler located on the appliance and C14 refers to the female coupler that supplies the power to the appliance from the power supply.")
(comment processorTypeHasCPUMicroarchitecture "relates a type of processor to its CPU microarchitecture")
(comment SubNetwork-Network "A logical subdivision of an IP network.  All computers on the same subnet share a common most significant bit in their IP address.")
(comment ProvisionedNetworkProduct "A general collection whose instances range from provisioned software specifications, access blocks, compute appliances, etc., to logical entities like subnets.  The essential component is that the instances of this collection are \"provisionable\" versions of procurable products in that they are associated with some configuration details not universally true of the products themselves.")
(comment provisionableHasComponent "This predicate relates an instance of #$ProvisionedNetworkProduct to an entity that is a concrete (in some sense) instantiation of some portion (perhaps all) of the provisioned product.  E.g. this can related a provisionable software product to its #$ComputerProgram-CW correlate or a provisionable piece of equipment to its specific procurable versions.")
(comment instantiatedSubnet "This predicate relates an instance of #$SubnetComponentType to the instance of #$SubNetwork-Network that is its concrete instantiation")
(comment modelEntityUtilizesModelEntity "(#$modelEntityUtilizesModelEntity ENTITY1 ENTITY2) means that ENTITY1, in some general sense, utilizes ENTITY2 in the context of the model to which they both belong.  Note that this is not a symmetric (though not necessarily asymmetric) relationship")
(comment componentTypeHasPositionType "Relates a type of model components to the type of position it occupies in the model")
(comment NetworkDeviceFromHWGFn "A binary function that takes an instance of #$ComputerHardwareGroupType and a name string and returns an instance of #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType.")
(comment deviceAssociatedWithHWGAndName "Relates an instance of #$ComputerHardwareGroupType and a name string to the corresponding instance of #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType.")
(comment DeviceSet-Composite "The collection of composite devices consisting of one or more instances of #$Device-Composite configured to work together as a group.  ")
(comment deviceSetModelID "relates a type of device set (composite) to its assigned ID.")
(comment DeviceSetTypeWithNameFn "A binary function that takes an instance of #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType and a name/ID string and returns an instance of #$DeviceSet-CompositeType.")
(comment deviceSetAssociatedWithDeviceAndName "Relates an instance of #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType and a name string to the corresponding instance of #$DeviceSet-CompositeType.")
(comment numberOfDevicesInDeviceSet "relates a type of device set to the number of devices that comprise the set")
(comment deviceSetTypeUtilizesDeviceType "Relates an instance of #$DeviceSet-CompositeType the its corresponding instance of #$NetworkDevice-CompositeType.")
(comment hardwareGroupHasSpecification "deprecated.  Do not use.")
(comment NthDeviceInDeviceSetFn "A reifiable function that allows you to refer to the Nth device in a device set")
(comment nthDeviceInDeviceSet "The corresponding predicate to #$NthDeviceInDeviceSetFn")
(comment deviceInDeviceSet "Relates a device set type to an (indeterminate) instance of one of its members.")
(comment deviceSetAssociatedWithAccessPortProduct "Relates an instance of #$DeviceSet-CompositeType the an instance of #$AccessPortProductType in the context of some provisioned network product like a resource pool or access block.")
(comment IntervalTypeBetweenFn-Inclusive "A binary function that takes two instances of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries and returns the collection of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries whose instances are the continuous time intervals between the starting point of instances of the first argument to the ending point of the next occurring instance of the second argument.  E.g. (#$IntervalTypeBetweenFn-Inclusive (#$TimeOfWeekFn #$Monday #$TimeOfDay-10AM) (#$TimeOfWeekFn #$Tuesday #$TimeOfDay-11AM)) denotes the collection of continuous time intervals that start on the first moment of a Monday at 10am and run through the last moment of the 11th hour of the next occurring Tuesday.  Note that if all instances of one interval type of either argument subsume some instance of the interval type of the other, the result is reduced to the subsuming type E.g. if the first argument is #$Monday and the second is #$TimeOfDay-11AM, the result is equivalent to #$Monday since every Monday subsumes some instance of #$TimeOfDay-11AM.  This is required by the intended interpretation that the instances of each returned interval type are all the same length and subsume some instance of each of the arguments.  The function is undefined for arguments for which there is no corresponding continuous interval type calculable according this definition.")
(comment VendorHardwareModel-Specification "A subcollection of #$ComponentConfigurationSpecification.  Each instance of This collection is a specification that outlines the allowable components and configurations of a particular procurable component  -- that is, it provides the legal builds that you can specify from the vendor.  Typically these are provided by the vendor.  For example, some instances of #$VendorHardwareModel-Specification provide the legal builds for certain computer servers.  In that case, the fully specified server that is procured from the vendor is an instantiation of one of these specifications.  This is disjoint with #$HardwareComponentSpecification which are specifications that specify additional configuration details that are post vendor delivery and relate to the particular role the component will play in the system in which it is installed.")
(disjointWith VendorHardwareModel-Specification HardwareComponentSpecification)
(comment HardwareComponentSpecification "A subcollection of #$ComponentConfigurationSpecification.  Each instance of #$HardwareComponentSpecification is a specification of additional attributes of a procurable component.  Contrast this with #$VendorHardwareModel-Specification which is the collection of specifications of the various ways in which you can order a procurable component.")
(comment instantiatesSpecification "relates a #$ComponentConfigurationSpecification to an artifact type that represent the class of instantiations of that specification.")
(comment typeInstancesHaveValue "(#$typeInstancesHaveValue COL VALUE) means that every instance of COL has VALUE as the value of some property attribution.")
(comment typeHasNumberOfProcessors "(#$typeHasNumberOfProcessors COMP-TYPE NUM) means that every instance of COMP-TYPE has NUM processors.")
(comment typePredHasInstanceLevelCorrelate "(#$typePredHasInstanceLevelCorrelate TYPE-PRED INSTANCE-PRED) means that INSTANCE-PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate that is the instance level correlate to TYPE-PRED. In general, (TYPE-PRED ARG1 VALUE) will entail (#$relationAllInstance INSTANCE-PRED ARG1 VALUE).")
(comment typeHasProcessorType "(#$typeHasProcessorType COMP-TYPE TYPE) means that the processors in every instance of COMP-TYPE are members of TYPE.")
(comment computerTypeUsesChassisType "(#$computerTypeUsesChassisType COMP-TYPE CHASSIS-TYPE) relates a type of computer type to the type of computer chassis it employs.")
(comment computerServerWithChassisType "(#$computerServerWithChassisType CHASSIS-TYPE SERVER-TYPE) relates a type of computer server chassis to the canonical collection of computer servers that use that chassis.")
(comment typeHasMemoryTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasMemoryTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList MEM-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes NUM instances of MEM-TYPE.")
(comment typeHasIOExpansionTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasIOExpansionTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList IO-CARD NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes NUM instances of IO-CARD.")
(comment typeHasHDDTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasHDDTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList HDD-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes NUM instances of HDD-TYPE.")
(comment typeHasPowerSupplyTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasPowerSupplyTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList PS-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes NUM instances of PS-TYPE.")
(comment rackModuleUnits "relates a type of #$ComputerHardwareItem to the number of \"rack units\" it occupies.")
(comment MRFluentProperty "The following comment is from #$MRSharedOntology as defined in OWL. 

<blockquote> A fluent property (e.g., hasSpouse) is a function that when applied to appropriate arguments results in a term that is a fluent.  For example, the fluent property hasSpouse is a function that when applied to arguments of type person results in a fluent, e.g., has Spouse(PersonA, PersonB). 
<p>         
Informally, one often talks about a fluent property as a predicate that when applied to arguments results in a sentence with a truth value.  Such common usage is, strictly speaking, incorrect.  Nevertheless, this usage is reflected in our making Fluent a subclass of GeneralizedStatement and FluentProperty a subclass of GeneralizedProperty, which facilitates using such tools as the Protege ontology browser.</blockquote>

")
(comment positionAppointedToInOrg "<code>(#$positionAppointedToInOrg APPOINTMENT PERSON ORG POS-TYPE)</code> means that during the #$AppointingSomeoneToAPosition <code>APPOINTMENT</code>, the #$appointee is <code>PERSON</code>, who is hired to fill the position <code>POS-TYPE</code> in <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment ReachingSaturationSteamTemperature "The collection of events in which the actual temperature reaches the saturation steam temperature.")
(comment ReachingSaturationSteamTemperatureInLiner "The collection of events in which the actual temperature in the liner reaches the saturation steam temperature.")
(comment HeatingOfSlottedLiner-AfterShutIn "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$HeatingOfSlottedLiner-AfterShutIn is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is heated after a well is shut in.")
(comment HumansTouching "The collection of instances of #$PhysicalContactSituation <code>S</code> in which two or more instances of #$HomoSapiens <code>H1</code> and <code>H2</code> are such that <code>(#$objectsInMutualContact S H1 H2)</code>.")
(disjointWith (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn Movement-TranslationEvent directionOfTranslation-Avg Down-Generally) (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn Movement-TranslationEvent directionOfTranslation-Avg Up-Generally))
(comment predNotAllowedInGeneralizedQueryForTheSetOf "(#$predNotAllowedInGeneralizedQueryForTheSetOf PREDICATE) means that is a generalized version of a query for a #$TheSetOf problem is created during inference and it includes a use of PREDICATE, then the restricted form of the query is executed instead of the generalized form.")
(comment wellHasBeenShutInForDuration "(#$wellHasBeenShutInForDuration WELL TQ) means that the #$Well WELL has been shut in for TQ amount of time.")
(comment deviceHasBeenDeactivatedForDuration "(#$deviceHasBeenDeactivatedForDuration DEV TQ) means that the #$PhysicalDevice DEV has been deactivated for TQ amount of time.")
(comment greatestGaugeValueBetweenDates "(#$greatestGaugeValueBetweenDates WELL GAUGE-TYPE DATE1 DATE2 NUMBER) means that NUMBER is the greatest value produced by the gauge of type GAUGE-TYPE in WELL between the dates DATE1 and DATE2, where DATE1 is the early bound and DATE2 is the late bound.")
(comment leastGaugeValueBetweenDates "(#$leastGaugeValueBetweenDates WELL GAUGE-TYPE DATE1 DATE2 NUMBER) means that NUMBER is the least value produced by the gauge of type GAUGE-TYPE in WELL between the dates DATE1 and DATE2, where DATE1 is the early bound and DATE2 is the late bound.")
(comment leastThpToeValueBetweenDates "<code>(#$leastThpToeValueBetweenDates WELL DATE1 DATE2 PRESSURE)</code> means that the least pressure recorded by the long-string THP gauge between <code>DATE1</code> and <code>DATE2</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment greatestThpHeelValueBetweenDates "<code>(#$greatestThpHeelValueBetweenDates WELL DATE1 DATE2 PRESSURE)</code> means that the greatest pressure recorded by the short-string THP gauge between <code>DATE1</code> and <code>DATE2</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment greatestThpToeValueBetweenDates "<code>(#$greatestThpToeValueBetweenDates WELL DATE1 DATE2 PRESSURE)</code> means that the greatest pressure recorded by the long-string THP gauge between <code>DATE1</code> and <code>DATE2</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment SteamBreakthrough "A specialization of #$PenetrationEvent and #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$SteamBreakthrough is an event in which steam breaks through into an area where it is not desired from an area in which it is being used.")
(comment SteamBreakthrough-InThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery "A specialization of #$SteamBreakthrough.  Each instance of #$SteamBreakthrough-InThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery is an event in which steam breaks through into a #$ProductionWell.  The source of such steam is typically an adjacent injection well.")
(comment relevantDateForWellEvent "<code>(#$relevantDateForWellEvent WELL-EVENT DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL-EVENT</code> is detected to have the relevant date <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment dateOfDetectionOfWellEvent "<code>(#$dateOfDetectionOfWellEvent WELL-EVENT DATE)</code> means that <code>WELL-EVENT</code> is detected to have occurred at the date <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment AttenuationOfBarrier "A specialization of #$WeakeningEvent.  Each instance of #$AttenuationOfBarrier is an event in which a barrier is reduced in its effectiveness.")
(comment AttenuationOfBarrierBetweenInjectedSteamAndProductionLiner "A specialization of #$AttenuationOfBarrier.  Each instance of #$AttenuationOfBarrierBetweenInjectedSteamAndProductionLiner  is an event in which a barrier between the injected steam and the production liner is weakened during #$ThermallyEnhancedOilRecovery-SteamInjection.")
(comment independentVariableInFormula "(#$independentVariableInFormula QBF SLOT TYPE) means that in the formula QBF, the SLOT value of TYPE is an independent variable.")
(comment dependentVariableInFormula "(#$dependentVariableInFormula QBF SLOT TYPE) means that in the formula QBF, the SLOT value of TYPE is a dependent variable.")
(comment CodeAnalysisConstant-CodingFunctionKnowledgeAcquisition "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created to support knowledge capture of features of instances of #$CodingFunction for the #$CodeAnalysisProject.")
(comment SteamMovingTowardWellThroughFractureInReservoir "The collection of events in which steam moves through either a natural or induced fracture or channel in the reservoir, toward the producer well.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-rhsexpression-PS "The physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-rhsexpression-KS. ")
(comment lHSCoordinateOfNodeInTree "(#$lHSCoordinateOfNodeInTree NODE LHS DAG) means that LHS is
the left-hand side coordinate of the #$AbstractThing NODE in the
operational tree qua #$DirectedAcyclicGraph, DAG.")
(comment rHSCoordinateOfNodeInTree "(#$rHSCoordinateOfNodeInTree NODE RHS DAG) means that RHS is
the right-hand side coordinate of the #$AbstractThing NODE in the
operational tree qua #$DirectedAcyclicGraph, DAG.")
(comment DefinedCodeVariableType "A #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each collection insantce of #$DefinedCodeVariableType is a collection of #$ComputerCodeVariables corresponding to a defined data-type specifier of a programming language, e.g. 'SIZE_T'.")
(comment CodeVarTypeDefNamedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for referencing collection instances of #$DefinedCodeVariableType. Where NAME is a #$CharacterString, (#$CodeVarTypeDefNamedFn NAME) denotes the #$DefinedCodeVariableType specified by NAME.")
(comment codeVarTypeDefNamed "The corresponding predicate of #$CodeVarTypeDefNamedFn.  Where NAME is a #$CharacterString, (#$codeVarTypeNamed NAME VAR-DEFTYPE) means that VAR-DEFTYPE is the #$DefinedCodeVariableType specified by NAME.")
(comment Handle-CodeVariable "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeVariables which serve as handles that reference addresses for #$DataStorageLocations within a scoped context in a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS.")
(comment PointerToDataTypeNamedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where DATA-TYPE is a #$CodeVariableType, (#$PointerToDataTypeNamedFn DATA-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that serve as pointers to locations that are constrained to store data of type DATA-TYPE.")
(comment allPointersToDataType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PointerToDataTypeNamedFn.  Where DATA-TYPE is a #$CodeVariableType, (#$allPointersToDataType DATA-TYPE POINTERS) means that POINTERS is the collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that serve as pointers to locations that are constrained to store data of type DATA-TYPE.")
(comment HandleForDataTypeNamedFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where DATA-TYPE is a #$CodeVariableType, (#$HandleForDataTypeNamedFn DATA-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that serve as handles to locations that are constrained to store data of type DATA-TYPE.")
(comment allHandlesForDataType "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$HandleForDataTypeNamedFn.  Where DATA-TYPE is a #$CodeVariableType, (#$allHandlesForDataType DATA-TYPE HANDLES) means that HANDLES is the collection of all #$ComputerCodeExpressions that serve as handles to locations that are constrained to store data of type DATA-TYPE.")
(comment Pointer-CodeVariable "The collection of all #$ComputerCodeVariables which serve as pointers that specify addresses for #$ComputerDataStorageLocations within a scoped context in a #$ComputerProgram-CWIS.")
(comment MR2011Ontology "The #$subWorks of #$MRSharedOntology that comprises the ontology (see #$Ontology) used for the #$MachineReadingProject's 2011 problem set.")
(comment studentAtInstitution "A #$CoexistingObjectsPredicate that relates a #$Person to an #$EducationalOrganization.  (#$studentAtInstitution STUDENT INSTITUTION) holds when STUDENT is a student at the #$EducationalOrganization, INSTITUTION.")
(comment thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate "<code>(#$thtLongStringTemperatureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate WELL CURRENT-DATE TEMP DATE)</code> means that the longs-string THT value available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of <code>TEMP</code> (a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge) indicates <code>WELL</code> was shut-in at <code>DATE</code>. This measurement in isolation is not sufficient to indicate a shut-in (see also #$fcvLongStringAreaChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate and #$thpLongStringPressureChangeIndicatesShutInAtDate).")
(comment relevantDateForShutInPressureCheckRelativeToDate "(#$relevantDateForShutInPressureCheckRelativeToDate DATE RELEVANT-DATE) means that when checking for a shut-in at DATE, the date RELEVANT-DATE is a relevant date on which to check the pressure.")
(comment leastThpHeelValueBetweenDates "<code>(#$leastThpHeelValueBetweenDates WELL DATE1 DATE2 PRESSURE)</code> means that the least pressure recorded by the short-string THP gauge between <code>DATE1</code> and <code>DATE2</code> is <code>PRESSURE</code>.")
(comment MRFluentTransitionEvent "Instances of #$MRFluentTransitionEvent are events that occur at a time point and in which some fluent property (see #$MRFluentProperty) begins to hold, or ceases to hold, among a set of things.")
(comment MRFluentTransitionEventTypeFn "(#$MRFluentTransitionEventTypeFn FLUENT-PROPERTY) denotes the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true, or stops being true, for some appropriate X and Y.  For example, (#$MRFluentTransitionEventTypeFn #$spouse) is the collection of events in which marriages start or stop.")
(comment mrFluentTransitionEventType "A predicate corresponding to #$MRFluentTransitionEventTypeFn.  (#$mrFluentTransitionEventType FLUENT-PROPERTY EVENT-TYPE) states that EVENT-TYPE is the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true, or stops being true, for some appropriate X and Y.")
(comment MRFluentInitiationEventTypeFn "(#$MRFluentInitiationEventTypeFn FLUENT-PROPERTY) denotes the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true for some appropriate X and Y.  For example, (#$MRFluentInitiationEventTypeFn #$spouse) is the collection of events in which marriages begin.")
(comment mrFluentInitiationEventType "A predicate corresponding to #$MRFluentInitiationEventTypeFn.  (#$mrFluentInitiationEventType FLUENT-PROPERTY EVENT-TYPE) states that EVENT-TYPE is the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true for some appropriate X and Y.")
(comment MRFluentTerminationEventTypeFn "(#$MRFluentTerminationEventTypeFn FLUENT-PROPERTY) denotes the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true for some appropriate X and Y.  For example, (#$MRFluentTerminationEventTypeFn #$spouse) is the collection of events in which marriages begin.")
(comment mrFluentTerminationEventType "A predicate corresponding to #$MRFluentTerminationEventTypeFn.  (#$mrFluentTerminationEventType FLUENT-PROPERTY EVENT-TYPE) states that EVENT-TYPE is the collection of events in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) begins to be true for some appropriate X and Y.")
(comment eventHasDepthTemperaturePair "<code>(#$eventHasDepthTemperaturePair  EVENT 2DPOINT)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> is an underground event characterized by <code>2DPOINT</code>. <code>2DPOINT</code> is the distance degree pair <code>DEPTH</code>, <code>TEMP</code> indicating <code>EVENT</code> involves a temperature in its focal actor at <code>DEPTH</code> of <code>TEMP</code>.")
(comment MRFluentTransitionObjectPredFn "(#$MRFluentTransitionObjectPredFn FLUENT-PROPERTY) denotes the #$BinaryPredicate that relates any #$MRFluentTransitionEvent instance, in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) starts or stops being true about a particular X and Y, to the Y involved in the transition event.")
(comment mrFluentTransitionObjectPred "A predicate corresponding to #$MRFluentTransitionObjectPredFn.  (#$mrFluentTransitionObjectPred FLUENT-PROPERTY OBJ-PRED) states that OBJ-PRED is the #$BinaryPredicate that relates any #$MRFluentTransitionEvent instance, in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) starts or stops being true about a particular X and Y, to the Y (the object of the fluent property) involved in the transition event.")
(comment MRFluentTransitionSubjectPredFn "(#$MRFluentTransitionObjectPredFn FLUENT-PROPERTY) denotes a #$BinaryPredicate that relates an #$MRFluentTransitionEvent instance, in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) starts or stops being true about a particular X and Y, to the X involved in the transition event.")
(comment mrFluentTransitionSubjectPred "A predicate corresponding to #$MRFluentTransitionSubjectPredFn.  (#$mrFluentTransitionSubjectPred FLUENT-PROPERTY SUBJ-PRED) states that SUBJ-PRED is the #$BinaryPredicate that relates any #$MRFluentTransitionEvent instance, in which (FLUENT-PROPERTY X Y) starts or stops being true about a particular X and Y, to the X (the subject of the fluent property) involved in the transition event.")
(comment rootNodeOfOperandTreeIsSubtraction "(#$rootNodeOfOperandTreeIsSubtraction INSTRUCTION N) means that the root node of the operational tree of the Nth operand of INSTRUCTION (#$operationalTreeOfOpNumOfInstruction) is a type of #$ExecutableAritmeticOperation wherein the function used is subtraction (#$DifferenceFn).")
(comment permittedNullResult "Where INSTRUCTION is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$permittedNullResult INSTRUCTION) means that, in the program context in which it is embedded, there are possible program executions wherein executing INSTRUCTION may return a null value on the function being called.")
(comment mrHoldsAt "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true at some #$TimePoint.  <code>(#$mrHoldsAt SENT TIME-POINT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true at <code>TIME-POINT</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, holdsAt, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimePoint as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrHoldsThroughout "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true at every moment during some #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$mrHoldsThroughout SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true all thoughout <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, holdsThroughout, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrHoldsWithin "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true during at least part of some #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$mrHoldsWithin SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true during a period contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, holdsWithin, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrMaximallyHoldsThroughout "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true at every moment during some #$TimeInterval, but not true throughout any other larger, containing time interval.  <code>(#$mrMaximallyHoldsThroughout SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true all throughout <code>INTERVAL</code>, and for any other interval <code>LARGER-INTERVAL</code> that properly contains <code>INTERVAL</code>, <code>SENT</code> is not true throughout it. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, maximallyHoldsThroughout, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrClippedBackward "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true all throughout some #$TimeInterval, but was not true before it.  <code>(#$mrClippedBackward SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true throughout <code>INTERVAL</code>, but is not true at the time point immediately preceding <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, clippedBackward, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrClippedForward "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true all throughout some #$TimeInterval, but will not be true after it.  <code>(#$mrClippedForward SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true throughout <code>INTERVAL</code>, but is not true at the time point immediately following <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, clippedForward, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrMinimallyHoldsWithin "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate and #$ModalPredicate that is used to state that a given sentence is true during at least part of some #$TimeInterval, but not true during part of some smaller, contained interval. <code>(#$mrMinimallyHoldsWithin SENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true during a period contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>, and for any other smaller interval, <code>SMALL-INTERVAL</code>, if it is properly contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>, <code>SENT</code> is not true during at least some part of <code>SMALL-INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, minimallyHoldsWithin, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$ContinuousTimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrOccursAt "An instance of both #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state that a given event occurs at some #$TimePoint.  <code>(#$mrOccursAt EVENT TIME-POINT)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> happens at <code>TIME-POINT</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, occursAt, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimePoint as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrOccursOver "An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state that a given event occurs during some #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$mrOccursOver EVENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> happens thoughout <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, occursOver, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.
<p>
The comment from the OWL ontology file follows: 
<p>
occursOver(Event, TimeInterval) is true if Event occurs over TimeInterval.  When Event is solid, this means that Event occurs over no interval I such that I properly contains TimeInterval.  When Event is liquid, Event may also occur over such an interval I.")
(comment mrOccursWithin "An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state that a given event occurs at some point during a #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$mrOccursWithin EVENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> occurs over (see #$mrOccursOver) some interval contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, occursWithin, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrMinimallyOccursWithin "An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that is used to give the smallest #$TimeInterval within which (see #$mrOccursWithin) an event occurs. <code>(#$mrMinimallyOccursWithin EVENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> occurs within (see #$mrOccursWithin) <code>INTERVAL</code>, but does not occur within any time interval properly contained by <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, minimallyOccursWithin, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrMaximallyOccursOver "An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that is used to state that a given event occurs over the course of some #$TimeInterval, but not over any larger containing interval.  <code>(#$mrMaximallyOccursOver EVENT INTERVAL)</code> means that <code>EVENT</code> occurs over (see #$mrOccursOver) <code>INTERVAL</code>, and there is no other interval over which <code>EVENT</code> occurs and which properly contains <code>INTERVAL</code>. This predicate is a mirror of the #$owl:ObjectProperty, maximallyOccursOver, in the #$MR2011Ontology.  Although the intent of this predicate is to have instances of #$TimeInterval as arg2, the digested document content we will need to import may have other sorts of things in that argument position, so the second argument is left lightly constrained.")
(comment mrHoldsSometime "An instance of #$TemporalPredicate that holds between a given sentence and a #$TimeInterval when the sentence is true throughout or at sometime during the time interval.  This is a very general predicate and does not mirror any instances of #$owl:ObjectProperty from the #$MR2011Ontology, but is intended to provide a way to ask Cyc ''Can we find bindings for the variables in this sentence, and some time interval with respect to which the sentence has some truth status?''.")
(comment getTraceAtDate "<code>(#$getTraceAtDate  FIBER DATE TQ DEPTH TEMP)</code> means that at the #$Date <code>DATE</code> (within the \"time-window\" duration specified by #$Time-Quantity <code>TQ</code>) the #$DistributedTemperatureSensor <code>FIBER</code> measured a #$Temperature <code>TEMP</code> at the measured depth <code>DEPTH</code>.")
(comment getTemperatureTrend "<code>(#$getTemperatureTrend FIBER DEPTH START-DATE END-DATE SENSING-DATE TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> at the measured depth <code>DEPTH</code> measured the temperature <code>TEMP</code> on <code>SENSING-DATE</code>, which occurred between <code>START-DATE</code> and the later <code>END-DATE</code>.")
(comment MRTemporalQualifierPredicate "An instance of #$PredicateType, and a spec of #$TemporalPredicate, #$BinaryPredicate and #$ModalPredicate.  Instances of #$MRTemporalQualifierPredicate are binary predicates which serve to state the temporal conditions under which statements made with instances of #$MRFluentProperty are true.  #$MRTemporalQualifierPredicate does not mirror a class that is present in #$MR2011Ontology.  Rather, this collection has been introduced as a convenience.")
(disjointWith VisualMark SpindleStructure)
(disjointWith VisualMark CellPart)
(comment wellHasProductionStartDateAsEvidentOnDate "<code>(#$wellHasProductionStartDateAsEvidentOnDate  WELL CURRENT-DATE  DATE)</code> means that values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> of the area by which an FCV valve has changed over the course of 30 minutes, a temperature differential over 2 hours measured by a THT gauge, and a pressure differential over 3 hours measured by a THP gauge indicate <code>WELL</code> began production at <code>DATE</code>.")
(disjointWith RAPSetVariable RAPCounterVariable)
(comment contextOfPCWMeetingThreshold "(#$contextOfPCWMeetingThreshold WORK THRESHOLD CONTEXT) means that CONTEXT is the portion of the context of WORK that meets THRESHOLD.")
(comment unknownThatOutputIsNonNull "Where INST is a #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction and , (#$unknownThatOutputIsNonNull INST) means that there is no data available that shows a possible value range for the output of the function invoked by INST such that the low end of the range is non-negative. I.e., no #$valueRangeOfOperand data that disproves the hypothesis that INST returns a null value in some execution environments.")
(comment MREventInTimePredicate "An instance of #$PredicateType, and a spec of #$TemporalPredicate and #$BinaryPredicate.  Instances of #$MREventInTimePredicate are binary predicates which relate an instance of #$Event to a #$TimeInterval over which or within which it occurs.")
(comment heelSteamInjectionRateAtDate "<code>(#$heelSteamInjectionRateAtDate WELL DATE RATE)</code> means that the rate of steam production in the heel of <code>WELL</code> at <code>DATE</code> is <code>RATE</code> .")
(comment toeSteamInjectionRateAtDate "<code>(#$toeSteamInjectionRateAtDate WELL DATE RATE)</code> means that the rate of steam production at the toe of <code>WELL</code> at <code>DATE</code> is <code>RATE</code> .")
(comment dateAtDurationAfter "(#$dateAtDurationAfter EARLY DURATION LATE) means that LATE is the date exactly DURATION amount of time after EARLY.")
(comment dateAtDurationBefore "(#$dateAtDurationBefore LATE DURATION EARLY) means that EARLY is the date exactly DURATION amount of time before LATE.")
(comment rootNodeOfOperandTreeIsAddition "(#$rootNodeOfOperandTreeIsAddition INSTRUCTION N) means that the root node of the operational tree of the Nth operand of INSTRUCTION (#$operationalTreeOfOpNumOfInstruction) is a type of #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation wherein the function used is addition (#$PlusFn).")
(comment ProductionTubingString-Long "The longest production tubing string in a well.")
(comment ProductionTubingString-Short "The shortest production tubing string in a well.")
(comment shutInOccursInStringType "(#$shutInOccursInStringType SU STRING-TYPE) means that the shut-in SU occurs in a string of type STRING-TYPE).")
(comment HeatingAboveFormationTop-Rapid "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$HeatingOfSlottedLiner is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is heated rapidly.")
(comment getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRange-Set "<code>(#$getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRange-Set FIBER DATE N MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH SET)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs in <code>SET</code> at regular internals of <code>N</code> meters at <code>DATE</code>, at depths  in the interval bounded by <code>MIN-DEPTH</code> and <code>MAX-DEPTH</code>.")
(comment TranslationalMotionTypeByDirection "A collection that facets #$Movement-TranslationEvent into subcollections based on the general direction (see #$directionOfTranslation-Avg) of the movement event-instances.")
(comment multiMediaClassificationExpansionFacetingCollection "<code>(#$multiMediaClassificationExpansionFacetingCollection FACET)</code> means that <code>FACET</code>, an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType, is used to generate additional features from specified features used in multi-media classification systems. Specifically, instances <code>COLL</code> of <code>FACET</code> are derivable as micro-features of their specializations or of events that decompose into a sequence of events involving instances of <code>COLL</code>.")
(comment parameterValueInSpecification "(#$parameterValueInSpecification PARAM VAL SPEC) states that, according to the #$Specification SPEC, the #$Parameter PARAM has the value VAL.")
(comment withinNDegreesOfSaturationSteamTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthOnDate "<code>(#$withinNDegreesOfSaturationSteamTemperatureAtNormalizedDepthOnDate WELL DEPTH TEMP SAT-TEMP DEGREES DATE)</code> means that based on average temperatures over <code>DURATION</code>, the temperature <code>TEMP</code> in <code>WELL</code> is approaching (i.e. is within <code>DEGREES</code>) of the saturation steam temperature <code>SAT-TEMP</code> at <code>DEPTH</code> on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasMostRecentShutInEventWithStartDatePriorToDate "<code>(#$wellHasMostRecentShutInEventWithStartDatePriorToDate WELL START-DATE S-IN DATE)</code> means that <code>S-IN</code> is most recent well shut-in event prior to <code>DATE</code>, and it began at <code>START-DATE</code> at the well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment significantWellEventTypeOccursOnDateAfterEvent "<code>(#$significantWellEventTypeOccursOnDateAfterEvent NEG-EVENT-TYPE WELLDATE EVENT)</code> means that the significant well event type <code>NEG-EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>WELL</code> on <code>DATE</code> after the event <code>EVENT</code>.")
(comment callClosureOfFunctionStatement "(#$callClosureOfFunctionStatement FN-DEF CALLED-FN-DEF) means that either FN-DEF contains a #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction that calls the function defined by CALLED-FN-DEF, or that FN-DEF contains an instruction that calls some function defined by a #$FunctionCallImplementation MID-FN-DEF, and (#$callClosureOfFunctionStatement MID-FN-DEF CALLED-FN-DEF).")
(comment nearestCallClosureOfFunctionStatement "(#$nearestCallClosureOfFunctionStatement FN-DEF CALLED-FN-DEF) means that FN-DEF contains a #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction that calls the function defined by CALLED-FN-DEF.")
(comment visualDepictionsOfContain "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>(#$visualDepictionsOfContain X Y)</code> means that, as a default, for any instance <code>VISUAL</code> of #$VisualInformationBearingThing, if <code>(#$visuallyDepicts VISUAL X)</code>, then <code>(#$visuallyDepicts VISUAL Y)</code>. For example, <code>(#$visualDepictionsOfContain WashingtonCrossingTheDelaware GeorgeWashington)</code> means that if a visual information bearing thing depicts the event of George Washington crossing the Delaware, it also depicts George Washington.")
(comment classificationFeatures "<code>(#$classificationFeatures THING FEATURE)</code> means that <code>FEATURE</code> is a feature used to build classifiers for <code>THING</code>.")
(comment visualDepictionsOfTypeContainType-CeterisParibus "An  instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate, <code>#$visualDepictionsOfTypeContainType-CeterisParibus TYPE OTHER-TYPE)</code> means that if an instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing <code>VIBT</code> is such that it depicts an instance of <code>TYPE</code> (i.e., <code>(#$relationInstanceExists #$visuallyDepicts VIBT TYPE)</code>), then, all other things being equal, it also depicts an instance of <code>OTHER</code> (<code>(#$relationInstanceExists #$visuallyDepicts VIBT OTHER-TYPE)</code>).")
(comment StringToListOfIntegersFn "(#$StringToListOfIntegersFn NUMSTRING) denotes the list of integers (if any) that is represented by NUMSTRING in the Arabic numeral system. That is: if NUMSTRING consists entirely of #$ArabicNumerals separated by spaces, then the above non-atomic term denotes whichever list of integers NUMSTRING represents in the Arabic system, otherwise the term is #$undefined (q.v.).")
(comment StringifyFn "(#$StringifyFn THING) denotes the canonical string representation of THING. Note that this representation may not be unique; for example, the integer 2 and the string \"2\" both have a canonical string representation of \"2\".")
(comment MRStatementClass "Supporting vocabulary for Erudite's Machine Reading project. The following comment is from nary.owl. <blockquote>A metaclass for (n-ary) GeneralizedStatements [see #$MRGeneralizedStatement].</blockquote> ")
(comment MRGeneralizedStatement "Supporting vocabulary for Erudite's Machine Reading project. The following comment is from nary.owl. <blockquote> A logical statement with a predicate and one or more arguments.  Only the subclasses of GeneralizedStatement are intended to be instantiated. Every subclass C of GeneralizedStatement should (in a conforming implementation) be an instance of the metaclass StatementClass [see #$MRStatementClass].  The predicate of an instance of C is accessible via nary:predicate or (when all instances of C are intended to share a common predicate) via C's property hasStatementClassPredicate.  Each subclass C is to have an arity (greater than zero) determined by the number of hasStatementClassArgumentAccessor property values specified for C.  The arguments of an instance of any given GeneralizedStatement subclass C may be accessed via C's hasStatementClassArgumentAccessor property.  A given GeneralizedProperty P should have at least one argument. In contrast to rdf:Statement (and rdf:Property), any argument may be literal-valued (e.g., string-valued).</blockquote>")
(comment MRStatementTypeFn "<code>(#$MRStatementTypeFn PROPERTY)</code> denotes the collection of logical statements (see #$MRGeneralizedStatement) having <code>PROPERTY</code> in the predicate position.")
(comment mrStatementType "A predicate corresponding to #$MRStatementTypeFn.  (#$mrStatementType PROPERTY STATEMENT-TYPE) states that STATEMENT-TYPE is the collection of logical statements having PROPERTY in the predicate position.")
(comment MRArgumentAccessorFn "<code>(#$MRArgumentAccessorFn PROPERTY ARG)</code> denotes a #$BinaryPredicate which relates instances of <code>(#$MRStatementTypeFn PROPERTY)</code> to terms which would fill the argument position, <code>ARG</code>, in literals having <code>PROPERTY</code> in the predicate position. ")
(comment mrArgumentAccessor "A predicate corresponding to #$MRArgumentAccessorFn.  <code>(#$mrArgumentAccessor PROPERTY ARG-POS PRED)</code> states that <code>PRED</code> is the #$BinaryPredicate which relates <code>(MRStatementTypeFn PROPERTY)</code> instances (reified versions of logical statements having <code>PROPERTY</code> in the predicate position) to the thing that would fill the <code>ARG-POS</code> place in a simple literal made with <code>PROPERTY</code>.")
(comment MRGeneralizedProperty "Supporting vocabulary for Erudite's Machine Reading project. The following comment is from nary.owl.  <blockquote> A property that may be associated with a GeneralizedStatement </blockquote>
")
(comment mrNAryDefinitionMt "The Erudite machine reading ontology, #$MR2011Ontology, introduces a layer of representation in which logical statements are reified (see #$MRGeneralizedStatement) so that non-binary relationships (such as a ternary relationship between an organization, a person, and their role in the organization, or a temporal qualification on a binary statement) can be stated only with binary relationships.  This predicate states the microtheory in which conclusions defining terms that are part of this ''binarized'' layer are to be stored.")
(comment codeHasWeaknessTypeDueToInstructionAt "(#$codeHasWeaknessTypeDueToInstructionAt CODE DEF-TYPE ADDRESS) means that the #$ComputerCodeStatement CODE belongs to the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency DEF-TYPE because it contains the binary instruction with ADDRESS.")
(comment XMLSchema-W3C-2001 "An XML schema language (see #$XML-BasedLanguage) that, like all such schemas, expresses a set of rules that determine whether a document is valid.  This schema was published as a W3C recommendation. ")
(comment wikipediaArticleURL-Expansion "(#$wikipediaArticleURL-Expansion THING URL) means that in #$Wikipedia-WebSite THING is described by an article located at URL")
(comment Eyrie-V2-termreturnvaluedetail-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-termreturnvaluedetail-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-termvaluerangeinvariant-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-termvaluerangeinvariant-KS.")
(comment DocumentationPageExternalURLPredicate "The collection of predicates from which focal term external documentation URLs can be generated.  Instances of this collection are queried when the \"Documentation\" tab is opened for some concept and any links found by the predicates in this collection are displayed in an \"External Documentation Links\" section of that page. ")
(comment externalURLPredicateDiplayString "associates an instance of #$DocumentationPageExternalURLPredicate with a string that serves as its label for UI display purposes.")
(comment externalURLPredicateQueryMt "This associates a microtheory used to query for relevant values with an instance of #$DocumentationPageExternalURLPredicate")
(comment terminalDateForTypeAtLocation "(#$mostRecentSOPEventOfTypeAtLocation DATE TYPE PLACE) means DATE is a terminal date for an occurance of TYPE at PLACE.  In other words, the last time anyone checked prior to DATE, an occurance of TYPE was happening at PLACE but no evidence at DATE indicates that an instance of TY{E is still happening at PLACE.")
(comment mostRecentTerminalDateForTypeAtLocationBeforeDate "(#$mostRecentTerminalDateForTypeAtLocationBeforeDate DATE TYPE PLACE LATER) means DATE is the most recent terminal date for an occurance of TYPE in WELL prior to the date LATER.")
(comment pertinentIndexicalQuery-WithDate "(#$pertinentIndexicalQuery-WithDate THING Q-SPEC DATE) means that in the current context, relevant to THING a pertinent indexical query specification is Q-SPEC.  Specifically, in the current conext it is appropriate to ask a version of Q-SPEC wherein the non-date indexical term in Q-SPEC is replaced with THING and any indexical date in the query is replaced with DATE.")
(comment physicalSchemasNeeded "(#$physicalSchemasNeeded QUERY-SPEC SCHEMA-SET) means the query described by the #$CycLQuerySpecification QUERY-SPEC uses interpretation of content in the physical schemas in SCHEMA-SET when running.")
(comment testQuestionNeedsPhysicalSchemas "(#$testQuestionNeedsPhysicalSchemas CONTENT-TEST SCHEMA-SET) means that the query saved with the #$KBContentTest-FullySpecified CONTENT-TEST draws on interpretation of the information in the physical schemas in SCHEMA-SET when running.")
(comment termPermittedNullInputValueToStatement "(#$termPermittedNullInputValueToStatement TERM STATEMENT) means that in the program context of statement, the value denoted by TERM is directed to be input to STATEMENT, with no check made as to whether or not the value of TERM is null.")
(comment mainArithmeticFunctionOfExecutableArithOperation "(#$mainArithmeticFunctionOfExecutableArithOperation OP MAIN-FUNC) means that the main operator called by the #$ExecutableArithmeticOperation OP is the #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars MAIN-FUNC.")
(comment mrPersonTitleInOrganization "(#$mrPersonTitleInOrganization PERSON ORGANIZATION TITLE) states that PERSON has the title TITLE at ORGANIZATION.  TITLE may be an official title, such as ''CEO'' or ''Senator'', or a less official one like ''accountant''.")
(comment mrOfficeWon "(#$mrOfficeWon WINNING POSITION) means that in the WinningPositionInElection, WINNING, POSITION (an instance of #$Title) is the position won.")
(comment mrContestedEntityCampaignedFor "(contestedEntityCampaignedFor CAMPAIGN ENTITY): The CAMPAIGN event has as its ContestedEntity ENTITY.")
(comment inflowLengthsWithStartingDepths "(#$inflowLengthsWithStartingDepths WELL DEPTH-TEMP-POINTS-IN-LINER DEPTH-LENGTH-PAIRS) means that the #$Well WELL has liner inflow sections described by the list of lists, DEPTH-LENGTH-PAIRS, as evinced by the depth/temperature pairs in DEPTH-TEMP-POINTS-IN-LINER (the set of depth/temperature points from the liner of WELL from a single DTS trace taken during a shut-in).  DEPTH-LENGTH-PAIRS is a list of lists; it's sub-lists are pairs of distances D1 and D2.  Each D1 indicates the start of a liner inflow section and each D2 indicates the length of the liner inflow section started at D1.")
(comment shutInOngoingAtDate "(#$shutInOngoingAtDate SU DATE) measn that the #$WellShutIn SU temporally subsumes the #$Date DATE.")
(comment termInOperandOfInstructionHasValRange "(#$termInOperandOfInstructionHasValRange INSTR OPNUM LHC LOW-END HI-END) means that the term that has the left-hand coordinate LHC in the operational subtree of operand number OPNUM in the #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INSTR is constrained to have a value between LOW-END and HI-END in the execution of INSTR.")
(comment termInOperandOfInstructionHasLoVal "(#$termInOperandOfInstructionHasLoVal INSTR OPNUM LHC LOW-END) means that the lowest value that the term with left-hand coordinate LHC in the operational subtree of operand number OPNUM in the CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INSTR can have in the execution of  INSTR is LOW-END.")
(comment termInOperandOfInstructionHasHiVal "(#$termInOperandOfInstructionHasLoVal INSTR OPNUM LHC HI-END) means that the highest value that the term with left-hand coordinate LHC in the operational subtree of operand number OPNUM in the CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INSTR can have in the execution of INSTR is LOW-END.")
(comment termOfInstructionHasLHCoordinateInTree "(#$termOfInstructionHasLHCoordinateInTree INST NODE LHC DAG) means that the term NODE, which specifies a value for some operand of INST, has the left-hand coordinate LHC in the operational subtree DAG.")
(comment termOfInstructionHasRHCoordinateInTree "(#$termOfInstructionHasRHCoordinateInTree INST NODE RHC DAG) means that the term NODE, which specifies a value for some operand of INST, has the left-hand coordinate LHC in the operational subtree DAG.")
(comment codeHawkInstructionHasAddressInProgram "(#$codeHawkInstructionHasAddressInProgram PROG INSTR ADDRESS) means that the address of INSTR in the #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS PROG is given by ADDRESS.")
(comment programSubsumesInstruction "(#$programSubsumesInstruction CHIBL-PROG INSTRUCTION) means that INSTRUCTION is an instructions contained in some block of some function statement of the #$CHIBLProgram-CWIS CHIBL-PROG.")
(comment wellHasLinerLength "<code>(#$wellHasLinerLength WELL DISTANCE)</code> means that <code>DISTANCE</code> is the length of the liner of the #$Well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment listOfNthMembersOfSublists "(#$listOfNthMembersOfSublists LIST-OF-LISTS N NEWLIST) means that NEWLIST is the list of the Nth elements of the sublists in LIST-OF-LISTS.  For example, (#$listOfNthMembersOfSublists (#$TheList (#$TheList 1 2) (#$TheList 3 4))) (#$TheList 2 4)) is true.")
(comment occursDuringMajorStepsOf "<code>(#$occursDuringMajorStepsOf SUB-EVENT SUPER-EVENT)</code> means that <code>(#$properSubEventTypes EVENT-TYPE ?SUB-EVENT)</code> where <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> is one of the major steps of <code>SUPER-EVENT</code>, in the sense that <code>(#$coveringOfEventType SUPER-EVENT LIST)</code> and <code>(#$memberOfList EVENT-TYPE LIST)</code>.")
(comment CellularSubStructureTypeByFunction "A collection that facets #$CellPart into subcollections based (solely) on the function that those part-types play.")
(comment getMeasurementAtTraceTimeStamps "(#$getMeasurementAtTraceTimeStamps GAUGE FIBER START-DATE END-DATE DATE NUMBER) means that the gauge GAUGE measures NUMBER at a date DATE between START-DATE and END-DATE (inclusive), where DATE is a date on which a DTS trace was produced by FIBER.  The gauge GAUGE and the fiber FIBER are assumed to be in the same well.")
(comment operationalTreeOfOpNumOfInstruction "(#$operationalTreeOfOpNumOfInstruction INST OP-NUM DAG)
means that DAG is the operational history, qua #$DirectedAcyclicGraph,
of the value supplied for operand number OP-NUM in the
#$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INST.")
(comment statementOperatesOnTerm "(#$statementOperatesOnTerm STATEMENT TERM) means that STATEMENT mandates that a logical or arithmetic operation be carried out on whatever value is denoted by TERM.")
(comment averageOfListElements "<code>(#$averageOfListElements LIST AVG)</code> means that <code>AVG</code> is the arithmetic mean of the elements in the list <code?LIST</code>.")
(comment getMeasurementAtTraceTimeStamps-List "(#$getMeasurementAtTraceTimeStamps GAUGE FIBER START-DATE END-DATE LIST) means that the gauge GAUGE measures the list of DATE number pairs between START-DATE and END-DATE (inclusive), where DATE is a date on which a DTS trace was produced by FIBER, and NUMBER is the number produced by GAUGE on DATE. The gauge GAUGE and the fiber FIBER are assumed to be in the same well.")
(comment bhpValuesAtTraceTimeStamps-List "(#$bhpValuesAtTraceTimeStamps-List WELL START-DATE END-DATE LIST) means that the the BHP gauge in WELL  measures the list of DATE PRESSURE pairs between START-DATE and END-DATE (inclusive), where DATE is a date on which a DTS trace was produced by the DTD fiber FIBER in WELL, and NUMBER is the number produced by GAUGE on DATE.")
(comment functionStatementSubsumesInstruction "(functionStatementSubsumesInstruction FN-DEF INSTR) means that the #$FunctionCallImplementationStatement FN-DEF includes a #$FunctionCallImplementationSubBlock that in turn includes the #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INSTR.")
(comment cWEHeuristic-CHIBLLevel "A documentation predicate used for keeping track of the primary heuristics referencing CHIBL output that are used in detecting instantiation of MITRE code weakness enumeratonns.")
(comment mrBinarizedSentence "#$mrBinarizedSentence is part of the query conversion support for Erudite's Machine Reading project.  <code>(#$mrBinarizedSentence BINARIZED SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is the non-binarized (converted) form of the Erudite query sentence, <code>BINARIZED</code>.")
(comment getMeanTemperatureAtDepthBetweenDates "<code>(#$getMeanTemperatureAtDepthBetweenDates FIBER DEPTH START END AVG-TEMP)</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> at the measured depth <code>DEPTH</code> measured temperatures that average <code>AVG-TEMP</code> between <code>START</code> and the later date <code>END</code>.")
(comment withinNDegreesOfSaturationSteamTemperatureAtDepthsInRangeOnDate-Set "(#$withinNDegreesOfSaturationSteamTemperatureAtDepthsInRangeOnDate-Set  WELL SET SAT-TEMP DEGREES DATE DURATION MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH) means that SET is the set of depth/average temperature pairs over DURATION where the temperature in the pair at the depth is within DEGREES of the saturation steam temperature SAT-TEMP at DATE, and the depths in the pair are between MIN-DEPTH and MAX-DEPTH.")
(comment highestTemperaturePointInSetOfDepthTemperaturePoints "(#$highestTemperaturePointInSetOfDepthTemperaturePoints SET POINT) means that in the set of 2-D depth/temperature points, SET, the highest temperature point is POINT.")
(comment saturationSteamTemperaturesAtTraceTimeStamps-List "(#$saturationSteamTemperaturesAtTraceTimeStamps-List WELL START-DATE END-DATE LIST) means that the list of DATE TEMPERATURE pairs between START-DATE and END-DATE are such that  DATE is a date on which a DTS trace was produced by the DTS fiber FIBER in WELL, and TEMPERATURE is saturation steam temperature in WELL on DATE.")
(comment nodeFreeOfConstraintViolations "(#$nodeFreeOfConstraintViolations ENTITY TRUTH-VALUE) means that it is TRUTH-VALUE (#$True or #$False) that ENTITY (a node in some graph) is linked downwards (via #$modelEntityLinkedToModelEntity) to something that has a constraint violated or is otherwise unsound.  The actual operative constraints depend on the context")
(comment getMeanTemperatureAtDepthRangeBetweenDates-Set "<code>(#$getMeanTemperatureAtDepthRangeBetweenDates-Set  FIBER MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH START END SET)</code> means <code>SET</code> is the set of depth/average temperature pairs that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured at <code>N</code>-interval depths between <code>MIN-DEPTH</code> and <code>MAX-DEPTH</code> between <code>START</code> and the later date <code>END</code>.")
(comment mrTerminates "A #$BinaryPredicate that is used in Erudite's #$MR2011Ontology to state that a given sentence stops being true at the end of an #$MRFluentTransitionEvent .  <code>(#$mrTerminates FTE SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is true before <code>FTE</code>, an instance of #$MRFluentTransitionEvent, occurs, and ceases to be true at the next point in time after <code>FTE</code>.")
(comment mrInitiates "A #$BinaryPredicate that is used in Erudite's #$MR2011Ontology to state that a given sentence starts being true at the end of an #$MRFluentTransitionEvent .  <code>(#$mrInitiates FTE SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is not true before <code>FTE</code>, an instance of #$MRFluentTransitionEvent, occurs, and begins to be true at the next point in time after <code>FTE</code>.")
(comment CoolingOfSlottedLiner-Rapid "A specialization of #$CoolingProcess.  Each instance of #$CoolingOfSlottedLiner-Rapid is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is cooled rapidly.")
(comment CoolingOfSlottedLiner "A specialization of #$CoolingProcess.  Each instance of #$CoolingOfSlottedLiner is an event in which a #$SlottedLiner is cooled.")
(comment startingDay " (#$startingDay INTERVAL DAY) means that INTERVAL  and DAY begin at the same time point (see  #$startingPoint) and that INTERVAL ends (see #$endingPoint) no earlier than DAY ends.  For example, INTERVAL might be a (#$YearFn 1999), so DAY would be January 1, 1999.")
(comment endingDay " (#$endingDay INTERVAL DAY) means that INTERVAL and DAY end at the same time point (see  #$endingPoint) and that INTERVAL starts (see #$startingPoint) no later than DAY starts.  For example, INTERVAL might be a (#$YearFn 1999), so DAY would be December 31, 1999.")
(comment dayLaterThan "#$dayLaterThan is similar to #$laterThan, but is restricted to #$CalendarDays. <code>(#$dayLaterThan LATE-DAY EARLY-DAY)</code> is true when <code>LATE-DAY</code> and <code>EARLY-DAY</code> are #$CalendarDays, and <code>LATE-DAY</code> starts after <code>EARLY-DAY</code> is over.")
(comment dayEarlierThan "#$dayEarlierThan is the inverse of #$dayLaterThan. <code>(#$dayEarlierThan EARLY-DAY LATE-DAY)</code> is true when <code>LATE-DAY</code> and <code>EARLY-DAY</code> are #$CalendarDays, and <code>LATE-DAY</code> starts after <code>EARLY-DAY</code> is over.")
(comment mrDaysEqual "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a specialization of #$cotemporal restricted to #$CalendarDays, motivated by the task of mapping to the Erudite Machine Reading Project's ontology (see #$MR2011Ontology).  <code>(#$mrDaysEqual DAY1 DAY2)</code> means that <code>DAY1</code> is the same day as <code>DAY2</code>.")
(comment WellInflowAssessment "A specialization of #$Evaluating.  Each instance of #$WellInflowAssessment is an event in which a well's inflow is evaluated.")
(comment WellInflowAssessment-10HoursAfterShutIn "A specialization of #$WellInflowAssessment.  Each instance of #$WellInflowAssessment-10HoursAfterShutIn is an event in which a well's inflow is evaluated 10 hours after a shut-in.")
(comment HeadOfNationStateTitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  #$PrimeMinister-Title, #$Emperor-Title, etc. which are titles held by people in their capacity as the leaders of countries.")
(comment HeadOfGPETitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  #$PrimeMinister-Title, #$Mayor-Title, etc. which are titles held by people in their capacity as the leaders of #$GeopoliticalEntity instances.")
(comment HeadOfCityTownOrVillageTitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  #$Mayor-Title, etc. which are titles held by people in their capacity as the leaders of instances of #$City.")
(comment MinisterTitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  #$ForeignMinister-Title, #$EnergyMinister-Title, etc. which are titles held by people in their capacity as ministers in a government.")
(comment HeadOfCompanyTitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  #$TopExecutive-Title, #$President-Title, etc. which are titles held by people in their capacity as the leaders of companies.")
(comment WellShutInTrendCompilation "A specialization of #$Evaluating.  Each instance of #$WellShutInTrendCompilation is an event in which a well's shut in trends are compiled.")
(comment suggestedConstantName "(#$suggestedConstantName CONSTANT STRING) means that the #$SubLString STRING is the suggested \"name\" for the #$CycLConstant CONSTANT. When possible, CONSTANT is then automatically renamed to have STRING as its #$constantName.")
(comment codingFunctionsDefCallsCodingFunction "(#$codingFunctionsDefCallsCodingFunction CALLING-FN CALLED-FN) means that the standard or canonical specification of how to execute CALLING-FN includes a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable where the #$codingFunctionInvoked is CALLED-FN.")
(comment objectDecorated "<code>(#$objectDecorated DECORATING OBJECT)</code> means that the physical object <code>OBJECT</code> is the object being decorated in <code>DECORATING</code>, an instance of #$Decorating.")
(comment PuttingSomethingIntoSomethingPartWay "The collection of instances of #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomething in which the primaryObjectMoving is put only part-way into something else, i.e., the object is not entirely enclosed (see #$enclosedObject), though some part of it is.")
(comment DecoratingCakeWithCandles "The collection of instances of #$DecoratingWithObjects in which the #$objectDecorated is an instance of #$Cake that is decorated with (see #$decorativeObjectsApplied) with candles.")
(comment CelebratoryEatingOfTheCake "A specialization of #$SocialRitual in which the #$socialParticipants in a #$Party-Celebration partake in cake.  This is a common practice in birthday parties and other anniversary celebrations and in wedding receptions.")
(comment ApplaudingTheBlowingOutOfBirthdayCakeCandles "A specialization of #$SocialRitual consisting of #$Applauding-Clapping events done by the non-honoree participants of a #$BirthdayParty event in response to a successful #$BlowingOutTheCandlesOnABirthdayCake event done by the #$honoree of the birthday party.")
(comment LightingTheCandlesOnABirthdayCake "The collection of events, made up of #$LightingACandle events, in which the candles on a birthday cake are lit.  This is typically done immediately prior to presenting the cake to the #$honoree (see #$PresentationOfTheBirthdayCake).")
(comment objectInserted-Unenclosed "<code>(#$objectInserted-Unenclosed INSERTION OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible that has been inserted part-way into something in <code>INSERTION</code>, a #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomethingPartWay event.")
(comment objectInserted "<code>(#$objectInserted INSERTION OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible that has been inserted into something in <code>INSERTION</code>, a #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomething event. If <code>OBJECT</code> is inserted sufficiently fully that it also plays an #$enclosedObject role, then it plays the more specific #$objectInserted-Enclosed role.  If not, and the event in question is a #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomethingPartWay event, then it plays the more specific #$objectInserted-Unenclosed role.")
(comment objectInserted-Enclosed "<code>(#$objectInserted-Enclosed INSERTION OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible that has been inserted into something in <code>INSERTION</code>, a #$PuttingSomethingIntoSomething event, so as to be enclosed by that object.")
(comment decorativeObjectsApplied "<code>(#$decorativeObjectsApplied DECORATING DECORATIONS)</code> means that <code>DECORATIONS</code> are the objects being used to decorate some other object in <code>DECORATIONS</code>, an instance of #$DecoratingWithObjects.")
(comment ServingTheCakeToGuests "A specialization of #$SocialRitual that is part of any type of #$Party-Celebration, such as a #$BirthdayParty event or a #$WeddingReception event, in which a cake is a central part of the proceedings.")
(comment significantEventTypeOccursOnDate "<code>(#$significantEventTypeOccursOnDate SIG-EVENT-TYPE OBJ
DATE)</code> means that the significant well event type <code>SIG-EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>OBJ</code> on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment significantEventTypeOccursOnDateAtDepth "<code>(#$significantEventTypeOccursOnDateAtDepth NEG-EVENT-TYPE OBJ
DATE DISTANCE)</code> means that the significant event type <code>NEG-
EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>OBJ</code> on <code>DATE</code> at the 
measured depth <code>DISTANCE</code>.")
(comment datapointSetEvincesEventTypeAtLocationOnDates-FromSource "(#$datapointSetEvincesEventTypeAtLocationOnDates-FromSource EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE1 DATE2 DATE3 SET AGENT) means that, according to the criteria dictated by AGENT, the significant event type EVENT-TYPE occurs at OBJ on DATE according to the datapoints in SET, and data retrieved at DATE1, DATE2 and DATE3 are pertinent to the evidence.")
(comment dataFromDateAtDepthWithSetEvincesEventType-FromSource "(#$dataFromDateAtDepthWithSetEvincesEventType-FromSource EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE DEPTH SET AGENT) means that, according to the criteria dictated by AGENT, the significant event type EVENT-TYPE occurs at OBJ on DATE at the depth DEPTH.")
(comment dataOfDepthAndCriticalTemperatureEvincesEventType-FromSource "(#$datapointSetEvincesEventTypeAtLocationOnDates-FromSource EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE DEPTH LIST AGENT) means that, according to the criteria dictated by AGENT, the significant well event type NEG-EVENT-TYPE occurs at OBJ on DATE at the measured depth DEPTH, with the critical reportable temperatures in the list LIST-OF-TEMP.")
(comment indicatedFunctionMitigationForProgram "(#$indicatedFunctionMitigationForProgram
?PROGRAM ACTION-TYPE STATEMENT-ADDRESS FUNCTION REPLACEMENT-FUNCTION) means that one way of mitigating the fact that PROGRAM is prone to ACTION-TYPE due to a function call to FUNCTION at STATEMENT-ADDRESS is to replace the instruction at STATEMENT-ADDRESS with an instruction that calls REPLACEMENT-FUNCTION.")
(comment mrSubTimeInterval "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is part of the Erudite Machine Reading Project's temporal calculus. <code>(#$mrSubTimeInterval CONTAINER CONTAINED)</code> means that all the moments of time that are part of <code>CONTAINED</code> are also part of <code>CONTAINER</code>.  This implies that <code>CONTAINED</code> does not start before, or end after, <code>CONTAINER</code>.  #$mrSubTimeInterval is basically #$temporallySubsumes restricted to instances of #$IntervalBetweenCalendarDays.")
(comment getMeasurementAtTimes "(#$getMeasurementAtTimes GAUGE LIST DATE NUMBER) means that the gauge GAUGE measures NUMBER at a date DATE where DATE is a date in the list of dates LIST.")
(comment |ListOfDatesToCSVDateListFn-YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS| "(#$ListOfDatesToCSVDateListFn-YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS #$EvaluatableFunction LIST-OF-CYCL-DATES) evaluates to a string constructed generating dates in the form YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS by comma-separating the dates in LIST-OF-CYCL-DATES.")
(comment |DateEncodeStringFn-YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS| "(#$DateEncodeStringFn-YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS DATE) returns a string encoding of DATE (an instance of #$Date) in the format YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.")
(comment BotanicalCellWallFormation "The biological process by which a dividing plant cell forms a new cell wall.")
(disjointWith CellPlateMembrane EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(comment CellPlateFormation "The process by which a #$CellPlate forms within an instance of #$BotanicalCell, as part of cell division.")
(comment CellPlateMembraneMergesWithExistingCellWallMembrane "A specialization of
#$PhysicalTransformationEvent, this is the final step in the #$BotanicalCellWallFormation process, where the membrane surrounding the #$CellPlate merges with the dividing plant cell's existing plasma membrane, marking the completion of #$Cytokinesis.")
(comment MovementOfVesicleToCenterOfBotanicalCell "The collection of events in which a single #$CellularVesicle in an instance of #$BotanicalCell moves from the #$GolgiApparatus to the center of the cell.  The totality of such events is a prerequisite for #$BotanicalCellWallFormation in botanical #$CellDivision.")
(comment stepInProcessAnalogousToStepInProcess "<code>(#$stepInProcessAnalogousToStepInProcess PROCESS1 STEP1 PROCESS2 STEP2)</code> means that <code>STEP1</code> and <code>STEP2</code> play analogous roles (fulfill similar functions) within <code>PROCESS1</code> and <code>PROCESS2</code>, respectively.")
(comment cWEMitigationHeuristic-CHIBLLevel "A documentation predicate used for keeping track of the primary heuristics referencing CHIBL output that are used in detecting instantiation of MITRE code weakness enumations.")
(comment wellHasMostRecentThermalCyclingEventAtDatePriorToDate "<code>(#$wellHasMostRecentThermalCyclingEventAtDatePriorToDate WELL TC-DATE EVT DATE)</code> means that <code>EVT</code> is the most recent thermal cycling event at the well <code>WELL</code> prior to <code>DATE</code>, and it occurred at <code>TC-DATE</code> at the well <code>WELL</code>.")
(comment MultiWellPad "A specialization of #$WellPad.  Each instance of #$MultiWellPad is a facility at which multiple horizontal wells have their wellheads.")
(comment mrHasSubGPE "#$mrHasSubGPE is an SKSI-supported OWL property that states geographic subregion relationships in Erudite Machine Reading project's gazetteer.  (#$mrHasSubGPE SUPER SUB) means that SUPER is a geographic super-region of SUB.")
(comment CorrespondingPredicateForFunctionFn "(#$CorrespondingPredicateForFunctionFn FUNC) denotes the canonical predicate version of FUNC.  When FUNC is an n-ary #$Function-Denotational, (#$CorrespondingPredicateForFunctionFn FUNC) will be an n + 1-ary predicate whose 1st through nth arguments constraints will mirror the arg1 - argN argument constraints of FUNC and whose nth + 1 argument place is constrained to be the resultIsa/Genl of FUNC.")
(comment CodeDeficiencyFacetingType "A #$CollectionTypeType and a specialization of ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency.  Each instance is a collection of collections of instances of #$ComputerCode.  Every code type in the instance has the property that all of its instances are prone to a common type #$UndesirableProgramAction at run-time, and the #$UndesirableProgramAction types associated with the code types in the #$CodeDeficiencyFacetingType instance reflect a common theme that justifies reifying the #$CodeDeficiencyFacetingType instance and grouping the code types in terms of it.")
(comment mitreWeaknessClassDesignation "(#$mitreWeaknessClassDesignation FACETING-TYPE NAME) means that MITRE corporation designates the #$CodeDeficiencyFacetingType FACETING TYPE by the name NAME.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByNumberHandlingDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency that are related to the improper handling, conversion and calculation of numbers. More specifically, these weakness types deal with code used to manipulate a number during a calculation, but in the process make a mistake related to the allowable range of values or related to the understanding of how the number is stored in memory. This in-turn causes an unintended resultant value to be calculated.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByInputValidationDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the associated type of #$UndesirableProgramAction pertains to failure to validate or incorrect validation of input. The focus here is on input that is used to create / access resources or to control operation of the application.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByErrorHandlingDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the subsumed code handles errors incorrectly, where this includes but is not limited to, failure to specify generation of correct return or status codes, and failure to accommodate all possible return/status codes that could be generated by a function at run-time.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByResourceDrainDeficiency "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the defining defect relates to the improper allocation and release of resources in a way that allows for resource exhaustion and possibly denial-of-service.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeBySQLCommandInjectionDeficiency "The class of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the defining deficiency pertains to software that constructs all or part of a command or SQL statement using externally-influenced input from an upstream component, but it does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes special elements that could modify how it is parsed or interpreted when it is sent to a downstream component.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByConcurrencyHandlingDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the defining deficiency is related to concurrent use of shared resources such as system resources (e.g. files, memory, processes) and app-layer resources (e.g. signal handlers).")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByDataLocationCorruptionDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the defining deficiency pertains to license to perform operations on a memory buffer in a way that the programmer does not intended, including buffer overflows and underflows, out of bounds accesses, and memory safety errors.")
(comment ComputerCodeTypeByNullPointerErrorDeficiency "The collection of all collection instances of #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency where the defining deficiency involves dereference of a pointer that the programmer did not intend or accommodate.")
(comment MR2011AgentOntologyTerm "The collection of all terms in the #$MR2011Ontology 'agent' namespace.")
(comment MR2011TimeOntologyTerm "The collection of all terms in the #$MR2011Ontology 'time' namespace.")
(comment mrHoldsThroughout-BackchainRequired "An backchain-supported version of #$mrHoldsThroughout (cf.).")
(comment InstanceOfFromExtractionFn "(#$InstanceOfFromExtractionFn COLLECTION EXTRACTION) denotes an instance of COLLECTION mentioned in the #$RelationExtraction, EXTRACTION.")
(comment TimeIntervalWithDurationFn "A binary function that takes a #$TimeInterval and a #$Time-Quantity, and returns an instance of #$TimeInterval.  <code>(#$TimeIntervalWithDurationFn INTERVAL DURATION)</code> is an instance of #$TimeInterval with the same temporal bounds as INTERVAL, and having a #$duration of DURATION.  Usually INTERVAL has uncertain bounds.  ")
(comment TimeIntervalOfSpecStringFn "One of the corresponding functions for #$hasTimeIntervalSpecString.  (#$TimeIntevalOfSpecStringFn STR) is the time interval specified by STR.  See #$hasTimeIntervalSpecString for more details on the format of the string ARG1s of this function.")
(comment mrHoldsThroughout-Query "A removal-module-supported version of #$mrHoldsThroughout that should be used at query time.")
(disjointWith CellLifeStageType CellLifeStageSubcollectionTypeByCellType)
(comment minMeasuredDepthOfObject "(#$minMeasuredDepthOfObject OBJ MD) means 
that the minimum measured depth of OBJ is the #$Distance MD.  This is not truly 
a measure of depth, except in the case of objects that are strictly vertically 
embedded in the ground.  Rather, this is a measure of the length from a point on 
the surface, to where the \"top\" of OBJ is, somewhere underground.")
(comment InsufficientReductionOfSteamInjectionAfterShutIn "A specialization of 
#$InjectingSteamIntoAWell.  Each instance of #$InsufficientReductionOfSteamInjectionAfterShutIn occurs when 
some steam (or too much steam) is injected into a well when it should not be after a shut-in.")
(comment bodilyOccursIn "An #$ActorSlot and a specialization of #$eventOccursAt and #$nonDeliberateActors (qq.v.).  <code>(#$bodilyOccursIn EVENT ORGANISM)</code> means that the physical event <code>EVENT</code> occurs at or within the body of <code>ORGANISM</code>, an instance of #$Organism-Whole.  As such, #$bodilyOccursIn in is similar to and has overlap with #$bodilyDoer, the difference being an issue of the granularity of the event in question, where the granularity determines whether it makes sense to say that the organism is meaningfully the doer (#$doneBy) of the event.  At the \"coarsest\" end of the spectrum, where the entire body of <code>ORGANISM</code> is the doer of <code>EVENT</code> (e.g., #$Sleeping, #$HavingASeizure), <code>(#$bodilyDoer EVENT ORGANISM)</code> holds but <code>(#$bodilyOccursIn EVENT ORGANISM)</code> does not.  At the other end of the spectrum, from the level of cellular processes, down to chemical interactions that comprise them (e.g., #$Mitosis, #$CDKActivity (when it occurs in a body)), <code>(#$bodilyOccursIn EVENT ORGANISM)</code> holds but <code>(#$bodilyDoer EVENT ORGANISM)</code> does not.  In the middle are events, such as heart attacks, suffering from an infection, and event mass-events comprised of individual cell-level events in sufficiently massive quantities (e.g., #$Sweating), where both relations hold.")
(comment OutOfRangePointerOffsetWrite "The class of all #$UndesirableProgramActions wherein pointer arithmetic is performed on a (possibly unintentionally) valid pointer in a way that gives rise to an offset that points outside the intended range of memory locations fro the resulting pointer.")
(comment WellInflowAssessment-24HoursAfterShutIn "A specialization of #$WellInflowAssessment.  Each instance of #$WellInflowAssessment-24HoursAfterShutIn is an event in which a well's inflow is evaluated 24 hours after a shut-in.")
(comment Kinetochore-PreMicrotubuleAttachment "An instance of #$SituatedObjectType, this is the specialization of #$Kinetochore whose instances are connected to the centromere of one of two sister chromatids, but have yet to attach to a #$Microtubule.")
(comment Drunk "An instance of #$AnimalTypeByMentalState and a specialization of #$Intoxicated.  Each instance of #$Drunk is an #$Animal who has ingested enough #$Ethanol to significantly alter its mental state and impair its motor skills.  An important specialization is #$LegallyDrunk (q.v.).")
(comment AnucleatedEukaryoticCell "A specialization of #$Cell.  Each instance of #$AnucleatedCell is a cell without a nucleus.")
(disjointWith RelationshipType DurativeEventType)
(disjointWith IntraCellularSignalingProcess ExternallyOriginatingCellularSignalingProcess)
(comment ExternallyOriginatingCellularSignalingProcess "The collection of all instances of #$BiochemicalSignalingProcess that originate outside the cell that executes the response.")
(comment typeDeterminesValueOfArgInReln "(#$typeDeterminesValueOfArgInReln TYPE N PRED) identifies TYPE as the process of determining the value of the Nth argument in any formula FORMULA of the form (PRED . ARGS) where all of the argument-places in FORMULA are bound but for the Nth.  For example, (#$typeDeterminesValueOfArgInReln #$CalculatingTheAPROnALoan 2 #$annualPercentageRate) identifies #$CalculatingTheAPROnALoan as the collection of instances of #$EpistemicallyDeterminingTheValueOfASlot in which one determines the value of ?X in (#$annualPercentageRate LOAN ?X) for some LOAN.")
(comment inhibitionOfSitTypeAffectsSlot "<code>(#$inhibitionOfSitTypeAffectsSlot EVT-TYPE SLOT)</code> means that inhibiting, or interfering with events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> will affect the value of <code>SLOT</code> where <code>SLOT</code> holds of of an event that is a sub-event or super-event of the instance of <code>EVT-TYPE</code> that is inhibited.")
(comment CanadianTerritory "The collection of all the #$FirstOrderAdministrativeDivisions of #$Canada which are instances of #$Territory.")
(comment NorthwestTerritories-Canada "Northwest Territories: a #$CanadianTerritory.")
(comment Nunavut-TerritoryCanada "Nunavut: a #$CanadianTerritory.")
(comment Yukon-TerritoryCanada "Yukon Territories: a #$CanadianTerritory.")
(comment SinglyHeldTitle "The collection of #$Titles such that, given a particular #$Organization, only one individual may hold that title in the organization at one time.  For example, only one person may be #$Emperor-Title of #$Japan at one time. ")
(comment durationOfLifeInYears "(#$durationOfLifeInYears ORGANISM YEARS-DURATION) means that YEARS-DURATION have passed (rounding down to whole years) between ORGANISM's birth date (#$birthDate) and their death (#$dateOfDeath).")
(comment ageInYearsAtDeathEvent "(#$ageInYearsAtDeathEvent PERSON INTEGER) means that INTEGER number of complete years have passed between PERSON's birth date (#$birthDate) and their death (#$dateOfDeath).  See #$durationOfLifeInYears for a similar predicate that relates an organism to the quantity of (whole) years that elapsed from its birth to death.")
(comment operationTypeOfCodingFunctionCategory "(#$operationTypeOfCodingFunctionCategory FN-TYPE OP-TYPE) means that every instance of FN-TYPE is a #$CodingFunction such that an execution of a function call for which it is the #$codingFunctionInvoked will implement an instance of OP-TYPE under normal run-time conditions.  I.e., if (#$operationTypeOfCodingFunctionCategory FN-TYPE OP-TYPE) and  (#$codingFunctionOperationalCategory FN FN-TYPE), then (#$codingFunctionOperationTypes FN OP-TYPE) is true.")
(comment MemoryAllocationAndDeallocationFunction "The collection of all #$MemoryManagementFunctions that both allocate and deallocate memory in the course of their application.")
(comment resultValueDenotesFailure "Where BOOL is a #$FunctionReturningBooleanSuccessCriterion, (#$resultValueDenotesFailure BOOL N) means that when an execution of a call to BOOL returns the value N, the execution failed at implementing the targeted operation type (#$codingFunctionOperationTypes) for the input values provided to the function in the execution.")
(comment resultValueDenotesSuccessOrFailureForFunction "(#$resultValueDenotesSuccessOrFailureForFunction FN VAL) means that the integer value VAL as returned by the #$CodingFunction FN means either that FN has failed in its application, or that it has succeeded.")
(comment PointerReturningFunction "The class of all #$CodingFunctions which return values that serve to address #$ComputerDataStorageLocations.")
(comment functionDefPermitsNullPointerReturn "(#$functionDefPermitsNullPointerReturn FN) means that the #$CodingFunction FN returns a pointer (i.e., that (#$operationalRoleOfResult FN #$pointerToLocation)), and moreover, that FN is defined in such a way that a null (non-referencing or dereferenced) pointer can be returned under certain conditions.")
(comment causes-SitTypeSitTypeInSitsOfType "(#$causes-SitTypeSitTypeInSitsOfType CAUSAL-TYPE CAUSED-TYPE SUBSUMING-TYPE) means that, in any instance of SUBSUMING-TYPE, an instance of CAUSAL-TYPE (occurring as a proper subsituation of the subsuming instance) will cause an instance of CAUSED-TYPE.")
(comment sitsOfTypeRiskSitsOfTypeInSitsOfTypeModulo "(#$sitsOfTypeRiskSitsOfTypeInSitsOfTypeModulo CAUSAL-TYPE CAUSED-TYPE SUBSUMING-TYPE EXCEPTION-TYPE) means that, in any instance of SUBSUMING-TYPE in which an instance of EXCEPTION-TYPE does not occur, occurrence of an instance of CAUSAL-TYPE has a medium-to-high risk of causing an instance of CAUSED-TYPE to OCCUR.")
(comment sitsOfTypeCauseSitsOfTypeInSitsOfTypeModulo "(#$sitsOfTypeCauseSitsOfTypeInSitsOfTypeModulo CAUSAL-TYPE CAUSED-TYPE SUBSUMING-TYPE EXCEPTION-TYPE) means that, in any instance of SUBSUMING-TYPE in which an instance of EXCEPTION-TYPE does not occur, occurrence of an instance of CAUSAL-TYPE will cause an instance of CAUSED-TYPE to OCCUR.")
(comment causes-SitTypeSitTypeIfNoInstanceOfIncluded "(#$causes-SitTypeSitTypeIfNoInstanceOfIncluded CAUSAL-TYPE CAUSED-TYPE EXCEPTION-TYPE) means that if a situation instance of CAUSAL-TYPE does not subsume an instance of EXCEPTION-TYPE as a proper subsituation, it will cause an instance of CAUSED-TYPE to occur.")
(comment Evolution "Every instance of #$Evolution is a #$BiologicalProcess and an #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent in which there is change across successive generations in the genetic material of individuals belonging to a group capable of interbreeding (a population within a #$BiologicalSpecies), resulting in changes in the inherited characteristics displayed by those individuals.  Although change from one generation to the next can be small, taken together over time these changes add to genetic diversity and can result in new forms of life arising.")
(comment evolutionarySuccessor-SitType "<code>(#$evolutionarySuccessor-SitType SITTYPE1 SITTYPE2)</code> states that the type of #$Situation, <code>SITTYPE2</code>, arose through the process of evolution from the type of #$Situation, <code>SITTYPE1</code>.  For example, some surmise that #$EukaryoticCellDivision evolved from #$ProkaryoticCellDivision.   Any  relationship between instances of <code>SITTYPE1</code> and instances of <code>SITTYPE2</code> is indirect and separated by long periods of time, so that e.g., today's prokaryotic cell divisions have no evolutionary relationship to today's eukaryotic cell divisions.  Rather, if that hypothesis is correct, prokaryotic cell divisions occurring a very long time ago changed gradually over many generation as genetic material of those organisms changed, eventually taking on the characteristics of eukaryotic cell division.")
(comment Hypothesis "Each instance of #$Hypothesis is a theory (see #$PhilosophicalTheory) which provides an explanation for some observation.  An hypothesis can be used to make predictions. For an hypothesis to be a scientific hypothesis, it must be falsifiable - it must be possible to devise an experiment that has the potential to disprove the hypothesis.")
(comment HypothesisThatFn "(#$HypothesisThatFn SENTENCE) denotes the instance of #$Hypothesis which purports that SENTENCE is true.")
(comment sentenceHypothesis "(#$sentenceHyopothesis SENTENCE HYP) states that HYP is the #$Hypothesis in which SENTENCE is true.")
(comment criticalRelnWithTypeForFunctioningOfWholeType "<code>(#$criticalRelnWithTypeForFunctioningOfWholeType WHOLE-TYPE TYPE PRED)</code> means that in order to serve its primary function (see #$primaryFunction) as a device (see #$deviceUsed), any instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> must have a working instance of <code>TYPE</code> related to the instance of WHOLE-TYPE via PRED.  E.g. if X is an instance of WHOLE-TYPE, then for X for function properly, there must be an instance, Y, of TYPE such that (PRED X Y).")
(comment BicycleWheel-WheelTubeAndTireComposite "The most common type of #$Wheel-WheelAndTireComposite used in Bicycles.  Instances of this collection have as an #$internalParts an #$InnerTube, which, when inflated, makes the object a functional  bicycle wheel.")
(comment WholeTypeForPartTypeFn "(#$WholeTypeForPartTypeFn PART-TYPE WHOLE-TYPE) denotes the collection of instances of WHOLE-TYPE that have instances of PART-TYPE as a #$properPhysicalParts.")
(comment AutomobileWheelAndTireComposite "The collection of wheel and tire composite objects that are designed for use on automobiles.")
(disjointWith EukaryoticChromosome BacterialChromosome)
(comment BacterialChromosome "A specialization of #$Chromosome and #$ProkaryoticChromosome.  Each instance of #$BacterialChromosome consists of a single structured strand of DNA located within a bacterial cell (a #$Bacterium).")
(comment ProkaryoticCellGrowthDuringDivision "During #$ProkaryoticCellDivision, as the genetic material is replicating, the cell increases in size.")
(comment ChromosomalDuplication-Eukaryotic "The collection of all events in which a eukaryotic chromosome is duplicated, resulting in an instance of #$DuplicatedChromosome.")
(comment ChromosomalDuplication "The collection of all events in which a chromosome is duplicated. In the case of eukaryotes, this results in a #$DuplicatedChromosome (see #$ChromosomalDuplication-Eukaryotic).  In prokaryotes, as the genetic material is duplicated, the chromosome separates into two. ")
(comment ChromosomeReplication-Prokaryotic "The collection of all events in which a prokaryotic chromosome is duplicated, resulting in two identical #$ProkaryoticChromosomes.")
(comment inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep "(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType  SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 ROLE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2 ROLE2 TYPE) means that if SIT-TYPE is such that (#$properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1) and (#$properSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE2), and (#$isa SIT SIT-TYPE), and (#$isa SUB1 SUBSIT-TYPE1) and (#$isa SUB2 SUBSIT-TYPE2) and (#$subSituations SIT SUB1) and (#$subSituations SIT SUB2), then for any INST such that (#$isa INST TYPE) and such that (ROLE1 SUB1 INST), (ROLE2 SUB2 INST).  The vernacular sense of the predicate is that, in a situtation type featuring SUBSIT-TYPE1 and SUBSIT-TYPE2 as #$properSubSituationTypes, whatever instance of TYPE plays ROLE1 in the sub-situation that is an instance of SUBSIT-TYPE1 in an instance of the situation type also plays the role ROLE2 in the instance of SUBSIT-TYPE2.")
(comment OriginOfReplication-DNA "A collection of #$DNAMolecularSegments.  Each #$OriginOfReplication-DNA is a continuous segment of a #$DNAMolecule which is a location at which #$ChromosomalDuplication can begin.  #$Bacterium instances typically have one circular chromosome with a single origin of replication.  #$EukaryoticOrganisms have multiple sites on each chromosome at which DNA copying begins.")
(comment DuplicationOfOriginOfReplication "A specialization of #$IBTCopying.  Each instance of #$DuplicationOfOriginOfReplication is an event in which an origin of replication (see #$OriginOfReplication-DNA) on a is duplicated, as an early step in duplicating the entire #$Chromosome.")
(comment SeparationOfTheOriginsOfReplication "A specialization of #$SeparationEvent.  Each inastance of #$SeparationOfTheOriginsOfReplication is an event in which the origins of replication rapidly move apart during bacterial cell division.")
(comment BacterialChromosome-PartiallyDuplicated "A specialization of #$BacterialChromosome. Each instance of #$BacterialChromosome-PartiallyDuplicated consists of a branched strand of DNA, part of which is not yet duplicated.  The remaining part consists of two duplicate segments, resulting from ongoing duplication.")
(comment DistributionOfGeneticMaterial-CellularProcess "A cellular process common to various forms of cell division, including #$BinaryFission, #$Mitosis and #$Meiosis, in which chromosomal structures within a dividing cell are separated and  move to opposite \"poles\" of the cell, where they will wind up being the total chromosomal content of the cells that result from the impending division.  ")
(comment DistributionOfChromosomes-Bacterial "The process that occurs during the division of bacterial cells in which each of the two copies of the bacterial chromosome move to opposite \"poles\" of the cell prior to cytokinesis, where they will wind up being the total chromosomal content of the cells that result from the impending division.")
(disjointWith DistributionOfChromosomes-Eukaryotic-CellularProcess DistributionOfChromosomes-Bacterial)
(comment CellMembraneInwardGrowthAndSeparationOfCells "An instance of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  In each instance, the #$CellMembrane and #$ProkaryoticCellWall of a dividing #$ProkaryoticCell grows inward between the already-separated duplicated genetic material, finally dividing the #$Cytoplasm and producing two separate daughter cells.")
(comment inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep "An instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate used to tersely represent/reason about role-inheritance relations at a high-level of description.
<code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP ROLE2 TYPE)</code> means that objects of type <code>TYPE</code> that play the role <code>ROLE1</code> in events of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that are scenes in an instance of <code>SCRIPT</code> will also play the role <code>ROLE2</code> in some #$subEvents of <code>MAJOR-STEP</code>, a \"major step\" of <code>SCRIPT</code>.  To be a major step in this context is to be part of a specified decomposition of <code>SCRIPT</code> into stages, via the #$coveringOfEventType relation.  As such, <code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSomeStepOfMajorStep SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP ROLE2 TYPE)</code> is equivalent to 
<code>(#$inheritRolePlayersOfType-SubSitTypeToSubSitType  SCRIPT SIT-TYPE ROLE1 MAJOR-STEP SUB-EVENT-ROLE2 TYPE)</code> with the additional constraints that <code>(#$roleHasSubEventsVersion ROLE2 SUB-EVENT-ROLE2)</code> and <code>(#$thereExists ?DECOMPOSITION (#$and (#$coveringOfEventType SCRIPT ?DECOMPOSITION) (#$memberOfList MAJOR-STEP ?DECOMPOSITION)))</code>.")
(comment operationResultComparison "<code>(#$operationResultComparison OP A B COMP QUANT)</code> means that the result of evaluating <code>(OP A B)</code> is a value <code>VALUE</code> that stands in the relation <code>(COMP VALUE QUANT)</code>.")
(comment significantEventTypeOccursOnDatePerDataSet "<code>(#$significantEventTypeOccursOnDatePerDataSet  NEG-EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE SET)</code> means that the significant well event type <code>NEG-EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>OBJ</code> on <code>DATE</code> according to the data points in <code>DISTANCE</code>.")
(comment significantEventTypeOccursOnDatesPerDataSet "<code>(#$significantEventTypeOccursOnDatesPerDataSet  NEG-EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE1 DATE2 DATE3 SET)</code> means that the significant well event type <code>NEG-EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>OBJ</code> on <code>DATE1</code> according to the data points in <code>SET</code>, based on evidence from <code>DATE2</code> and <code>DATE3</code>.")
(comment HexStringToIntegerFn "Where HEX-STRING is an alphanumeric character string denoting a number in hexadecimal format, (#$HexStringToIntegerFn HEX-STRING) returns the #$Integer denoted by HEX-STRING.")
(comment successorInstructionsInBlock "")
(comment wellHasMostRecentPreviousFinalThermalCycleDate "(#$wellHasMostRecentPreviousFinalThermalCycleDate WELL DATE PRIOR-DATE)  Means that prior to DATE, the last date of a series of 5 thermal cycles occured in WELL on PRIOR-DATE.")
(comment significantEventTypeOccursOnDateWithSignificantDate "<code>(#$significantEventTypeOccursOnDate SIG-EVENT-TYPE OBJ DATE SIG-DATE)</code> means that the significant well event type <code>SIG-EVENT-TYPE</code> occurs at <code>OBJ</code> on <code>DATE</code> and <code>SIG-DATE</code> is also significant.")
(comment inflowLengthsArePercentageOfWellLinerLength "(#$inflowLengthsArePercentageOfWellLinerLength WELL LIST N) means that based on the inflow lengths specified in LIST, WELL had a  calculated inflow length percentage N.")
(comment NewGUIDStringFn-Lazy "A zero-arity evaluatable function that produces a GUID string when evaluated.  Unlike #$NewGUIDStringFn-Immediate, which is evaluated at the EL level and will immediately result in the generation of a GUID, (#$NewGUIDStringFn-Lazy) will be evaluated later, such as when an #$evaluate literal is processed in the application of a rule.")
(comment NewGUIDStringFn-Immediate "(#$NewGUIDStringFn-Immediate is a 0 arity function that returns a unique GUID string.  The expression '(#$NewGUIDStringFn-Immediate)' evaluates at assert time into a GUID.  Its primary usefullness is with certain functions that take a GUID string argument (c.f. #$SomeTimeInIntervalFn).")
(comment partTypesFactsForType-Specs "<code>(#$partTypesFactsForType-Specs TYPE CONSTRAINT SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is a sentence that expresses a salient parts-related fact about some specializaton of <code>TYPE</code> that is an instance of <code>CONSTRAINT</code>.")
(comment wellObservedToBeInProductionOnDate "(#$wellObservedToBeInProductionOnDate WELL DATE) means that WELL was observed to be in production on DATE.")
(comment wellObservedToBeShutInOnDate "(#$wellObservedToBeShutInOnDate WELL DATE) means that WELL was observed to be shut in on DATE.")
(comment Population-Ecological "The collection of naturally-occurring groups of organisms, such that each group consists of members of a single species, and all group members live more or less in the same location at a given time.  This notion of population is of importance to population geneticists and those who study the dynamics of individual naturally occurring populations, i.e. age and gender distributions, age at reproduction, fecundity, etc. Animal populations may be migratory like some birds and butterflies. Plant populations travel less, but populations of waterborne plants like algae may move great distances as water flows. Populations of different species will differ in their size and in the range that they cover, depending on the typical behaviors or habits of the particular type of organism.  Members of a #$Population-Ecological have at least the possibility, modulo gender compatibility and maturity, of interbreeding.  Physical barriers to breeding keep populations separate; for example, a river separating populations of mice.")
(comment PopulationOfBLOs "The collection of groups of #$BiologicalLivingObjects, such that each group consists of members of a single species, and all group members live in the same location and interact to breed (if they do so), to communicate (e.g., via chemical signaling or language), and to compete for nutrients and space.  This collection includes naturally occurring populations as well as artificial ones such as cell cultures or ant farms. ")
(comment PopulationOfTypeFn "(#$PopulationOfTypeFn TYPE) is the collection of all #$PopulationOfBLOs whose
#$groupMemberType is the #$BiologicalLivingObject TYPE.")
(comment CellCulture "The collection of all cell cultures,  which are populations of cells, usually all of the same species and type, maintained under artificial laboratory conditions.  Cell cultures might be grown to see how they react to new pharmaceuticals, to perform other kinds of experiments, or to grow enough of them so that a pathogen can be identified.")
(comment iterationCardinalityMax "<code>(#$iterationCardinalityMax EVENT N)</code> identifies <code>N</code> as the maximum number of iterations through events of the type <code>TYPE</code> for which <code>EVENT</code> is an instance of #$IteratedEventScene.  <code>(#$iterationCardinalityMax EVENT N)</code> thus entails <code>(#$relationInstanceExistsMax #$properSubEvents EVENT TYPE N)</code> for the requisite type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment iterationCardinalityMin "<code>(#$iterationCardinalityMin EVENT N)</code> identifies <code>N</code> as the minimum number of iterations through events of the type <code>TYPE</code> for which <code>EVENT</code> is an instance of #$IteratedEventScene.  <code>(#$iterationCardinalityMin EVENT N)</code> thus entails <code>(#$relationInstanceExistsMin #$properSubEvents EVENT TYPE N)</code> for the requisite type <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment CellDeath "This is the collection of events in which cells die.  This could occur for a variety of reasons, including #$Apoptosis (programmed cell death), a lack of crucial resources, or when targeted by the #$ImmuneSystem of the multicellular organism of which they are a part. ")
(comment eyrieDataType "The data typing predicate specific to #$Eyrie-V2-KS.")
(comment programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToStatement-Derivative "(#$programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToStatement-Derivative PROG STATEMENT DERIV-ACT-TYPE) means that there is some collection instance of #$ComputerActivity ACT-TYPE such that (#$programHasPropensityForActionOfTypeDueToStatement PROG STATEMENT ACT-TYPE) and either DERIV-ACT-TYPE is a proper generalization of ACT-TYPE, or a proper subsituation type of ACT-TYPE.")
(comment functionCalledInProgram "(functionCalledInProgram PROG FN) means that the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS contains a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable that calls the #$CodingFunction FN.")
(comment libraryFunctionCalledByProgram "(#$libraryFunctionCalledByProgram PROGRAM FN) means that FN is a #$StandardLibraryFunction which is called by a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable (a 'function call') specified within PROGRAM.")
(comment definitionOfFunctionCalledByProgram "A specialization of #$codeStatementHasStatements.  (#$definitionOfFunctionCalledByProgram PROG FN-DEF) means that the #$ComputerProgram-CWIS PROG contains a #$ComputerCodeStatement FN-DEF specifying how to execute a certain #$CodingFunction.")
(comment DynamicallyLinkedLibraryFunction "The collection of all dynamically linked library functions.")
(comment StaticallyLinkedLibraryFunction "The collection of all statically linked library functions.")
(comment libraryLinkingTypeOfFunction "A typed specialization of #$isa.  (#$libraryLinkingTypeOfFunction FN LINK-TYPE) means that LINK-TYPE is the #$LibraryFunctionTypeByLinkingMethodology of the #$StandardLibraryFunction FN.")
(comment dynamicFileNameOfLibrary "(#$dynamicFileNameOfLibrary LIB FILENAME) means that FILENAME is the dynamic file name of the #$StandardCodingLibrary LIB.")
(comment wellLinerStartAndEndDepths-WithValidFiber "<code>(#$wellLinerStartAndEndDepths-WithValidFiber WELL START-DIST END-DIST)</code> means that the liner with valid fiber in <code>WELL</code> starts at the measured depth <code>START-DIST</code> and ends at the measured depth <code>END-DIST</code>.")
(disjointWith VocabularyMicrotheory UniquifyingDescriptionContext)
(comment UniquifyingDescriptionContext "The collection of microtheories that are of sufficiently narrow scope in their focus that descriptions of objects that occur within them are assumed to uniquely identify those objects.")
(comment extractedType "<code>(#$extractedType OBJECT TYPE)</code> means that Cyc has typed <code>OBJECT</code> as being an instance of the collection <code>TYPE</code> via some automated means.")
(comment extractedTypeFromDescriptionString "<code>(#$extractedTypeFromDescriptionString OBJECT TYPE STRING)</code> means that Cyc has typed <code>OBJECT</code> as being an instance of the collection <code>TYPE</code> via analysis of the string <code>STRING</code>, which is a description of <code>OBJECT</code>.")
(comment aVAnalysisContext "The predicate that corresponds to the function  #$AVAnalysisContextFn, <code>(#$aVAnalysisContext VISUAL-IBT MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$AVWorkAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions used in the analysis of <code>VISUAL-IBT</code>, an instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.")
(comment aVWorkWithID "The predicate that corresponds to #$AVWorkWithIDFn, <code>(#$aVWorkWithID VISUAL-IBT ID)</code> means that ID is the unique identifier for <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.")
(comment objectDescriptionInContext "<code>(#$objectDescriptionInContext THING MT STRING)</code> means that in the context <code>MT</code>, the string <code>STRING</code> is a description of <code>THING</code>.")
(comment ObjectFromDescriptionInContextFn "<code>(#$ObjectFromDescriptionInContextFn CONTEXT STRING)</code> refers to the object that is referred to by the description <code>STRING</code> in <code>CONTEXT</code>, an instance of
#$UniquifyingDescriptionContext.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-functiontype-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-functiontype-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-functiontypecode-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-functiontypecode-KS.")
(comment codeAnalysisPrimingQuery "(#$codeAnalysisPrimingQuery QUERY PRIMER) means that the #$CodeAnalysisTest-FullySpecified PRIMER is a priming query used to cache important data store information to be used in answering QUERY.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-programfunctionmap-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-programfunctionmap-KS.")
(comment Eyrie-V2-termglobalvaluedetail-PS "A physical schema for #$Eyrie-V2-termglobalvaluedetail-KS.")
(comment eyrieFunctionHasTypeID "(#$eyrieFunctionHasTypeID FN ID) means that the #$StandardLibraryFunction FN is linked with the numeric type id ID in the Eyrie functiontype table (#$Eyrie-V2-functiontype-PS).")
(comment termTargetsOperandOfInstruction "(#$termTargetsOperandOfInstruction INSTR OP-NUM GLOBAL-VAL) means that the global value designated by the term GLOBAL-VAL is supplied to operand number OP-NUM of the function called by INSTR.")
(comment eyrieTermStringDesignation "(#$eyrieTermStringDesignation GV-TERM STRING) means that STRING is the #$CharacterString designation assigned to the global value term GV-TERM by CodeHawk.")
(comment arrestingOfficer "The predicate #$arrestingOfficer relates an instance of #$ArrestingSomeone to the law enforcement officer performing the arrest.  (#$arrestingOfficer EVENT PERSON) means that PERSON was the person doing the arresting.")
(comment mrArrestForCrimeType "The predicate #$mrArrestForCrimeType relates an arrest to a type of crime.  (#$mrArrestForCrimeType ARREST CRIME-TYPE) states that CRIME-TYPE is the basis for the arresting event, ARREST.  Either the arrested person is suspected of having perpetrated an instance of CRIME-TYPE, or is expected to perform one in the future.")
(comment accuser "A #$BinaryRolePredicate and a specialization of #$senderOfInfo.  #$accuser relates an instance of #$Accusing to the instance of #$Agent-Generic which performs the accusing.  <code>(#$accuser ACCUSING AGT)</code> means that <code>AGT</code> is the agent issuing the accusation in <code>ACCUSING</code>.")
(comment trialProsecution "An instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate.  (#$trialProsecution TRIAL AGT) means that AGT is an individual or organization representing the state in a criminal trial TRIAL (see #$Trial-Criminal) of an agent charged with a crime.")
(comment defendants "(#$defendants ARG1 ARG2) means that the agent ARG2 is the accused party in the court case ARG1.")
(comment trialDefendants "An instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate. (#$trialDefendants TRIAL AGT) states that AGT is an agent who is suspected of a crime (in a #$Trial-Criminal) or against whom a lawsuit has been brought (in a civil trial).")
(comment mrTrialCrimeType "(#$mrTrialCrimeType TRIAL CRIME-TYPE) states that in the #$Trial-Criminal TRIAL, the defendant is suspected of having performed an instance of CRIME-TYPE.")
(comment mrHasTradeAgreementNationState "\"From the Erudite Machine Reading Project's agent.owl ontology: The class of event in which NationState undertakes a trade agreement with content class Content and status class Status.\"")
(comment MRTradeAgreementTypeByStatus "Instances of this collection are specializations of #$TradeAgreement. Each represents some state of implementation of a trade agreement.")
(comment MRTradeAgreement-Agreement "TradeAgreements which have the status \"Agreement\" as specified in agent.owl of the #$MR2011Ontology.")
(comment MRTradeAgreement-InNegotiation "TradeAgreements which have the status \"NegotiatingAgreement\" as specified in agent.owl of the #$MR2011Ontology.")
(comment MRTradeAgreement-Signed "TradeAgreements which have the status \"SignedAgreement\" as specified in agent.owl of the #$MR2011Ontology.")
(comment MRTradeAgreement-Effected "TradeAgreements which have the status \"EffectedAgreement\" as specified in agent.owl of the #$MR2011Ontology.")
(comment eyrieFunctionType "The function typing predicate specific to #$Eyrie-V2-KS.")
(comment BotanicalCellWithCellPlate "A subset of #$BotanicalCell.  #$BotanicalCellWithCellPlate is the collection of plant cells which possess a #$CellPlate.  This structure forms in cells that are undergoing the final steps of the #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle, of the #$FirstMeioticCellDivision, and of the #$SecondMeioticCellDivision.  It is deposited at the metaphase plate between two groups of chromosomes which have separated, and grows toward the cell walls, merging with them to result in two separate cells.")
(comment codeHawkInstructionID "(#$codeHawkInstructionID INST ID) means that ID is the unique identifier for the #$CodeHawkAtomicInstruction INST.")
(comment interArgIsaGenl1-2 "<code>(#$interArgIsaGenl1-2 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL)</code> means that, when an instance of <code>INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code> appears as the first argument to <code>REL</code>, the second argument is constrained to be a spec of <code>DEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code>.")
(comment TransporterTrickTypeByTransporterType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$TransporterStunt into sub-collections based on the kind of transporter used.")
(comment TransporterStunt "A specialization of #$DevisedStructuredActivityWithFocalDevice, this is the collection of tricks or maneuvers that are executed as part of riding a transportation device.")
(comment stuntTypeWithTransporterType "<code>(#$stuntTypeWithTransporterType  TRICK-TYPE TRANSPORTER-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TRICK-TYPE</code> as the specialization of #$TransporterStunt such that each instance is a trick that focally involves maneuvering a transportation device of type <code>TRANSPORTER</code>.")
(comment TransporterStuntFn "<code>(#$TransporterStuntFn TRANSPORTER-TYPE)</code> denotes the specialization of #$TransporterStunt where each instance is a trick that focally involves maneuvering a transportation device of type <code>TRANSPORTER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment foodItemPrepared "<code>(#$foodItemPrepared PREPARATION FOOD)</code> means that <code>FOOD</code> an instance of #$Food is prepared in <code>PREPARATION</code>, an instance of #$PreparingFoodItem.")
(comment nearestRequiredActorSlots "<code>(#$nearestRequiredActorSlots EVT-TYPE ACTOR-SLOT)</code> means that the instance <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> of #$ActorSlot has a value for every instance of the event-type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> (hence, <code>(#$requiredActorSlots EVT-TYPE ACTOR-SLOT)</code> holds), but that it is a \"nearest\" such actor slot -- i.e., though there may be a proper generalization of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> that is also required for <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there are no proper specializations of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> that are required.  Hence querying for the values of <code>ACTOR-SLOT</code> will result in a list of actor-slots that, given Cyc's current state of understanding, will be sufficient for specifying all of the actors in a given instance of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment visuallyDepicts-Type-Precise "A specialization of #$visuallyDepicts-Type that is not transitive via #$genls in the second argument position. <code>(#$visuallyDepicts-Type-Precise VISUAL-IBT TYPE)</code> thus means that the instance of  #$VisualInformationBearingThing <code>VISUAL-IBT</code> depicts an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, but that there is no specialization of <code>TYPE</code> that <code>VISUAL-IBT</code> that is known to be depicted.")
(comment assemblyInputs "<code>(#$assemblyInputs ASSEMBLING INPUT)</code> means that <code>INPUT</code> is an isntance of #$PartiallyTangible that is one of the pieces assembled to form an object in <code>ASSEMBLING</code>, an instance of #$Assembling.")
(disjointWith RuleMacroPredicate PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate)
(disjointWith DocumentationPredicate PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate)
(comment PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate "The collection of instances of #$Predicate that are used to specify how to build queries for purposes of question-suggestion.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateAssociatedInferenceMode "<code>(#$plausibleQueryPredicateAssociatedInferenceMode PREDICATE MODE)</code> means that suggested queries built from the predicate <code>PREDICATE</code> should be asked with the inference mode set to <code>MODE</code>, an instance of #$SpecifiedInferenceModeCluster.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPosition "An instance of #$PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate, <code>(#$plausibleQueryPredicateVariablizedArgPosition PREDICATE N)</code> means that plausible queries should be constructed from the predicate <code>PREDICATE</code> by inserting an open variable in the <code>N</code>nth argument-place.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateWithMacroAssociatedInferenceMode "An instance of #$PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate,  <code>
(#$plausibleQueryPredicateWithMacroAssociatedInferenceMode BINARY-PRED RULE-MACRO MODE)</code> means that in the question-suggestion context at hand, it is reasonable to suggest a query with a sentence of the form <code>(RULE-MACRO BINARY-PRED ...)</code>, where the inference mode for the query is set to <code>MODE</code>.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateAssociatedTextGranularity "An instance of #$PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate, <code>(#$plausibleQueryPredicateAssociatedTextGranularity PREDICATE LINGUISTIC-OBJECT-TYPE)</code> means that for purposes of question-suggestion from some target text, queries built from the predicate <code>PREDICATE</code> should apply most generally at the level of text-objects of the granularity of type <code>LINGUISTIC-OBJECT-TYPE</code>, e.g., #$NLSentence, #$NLParagraph, etc.")
(comment Sclera "The collection of all sclera. A type of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart and #$AnimalBodyPart. The collection #$Sclera is an #$OrganSubPartType, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, and a #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType.  Instances are the whitish-colored, outer surface of the vertebrate #$Eye, not including the transparent #$Cornea.")
(comment AdministeringADrugViaEyeAbsorption "The collection of events in which some quantity of a #$DrugSubstance, possibly in combination with inactive ingredients, is placed on the #$Sclera of the #$Eye, and is from there absorbed into the tissues and bloodstream.")
(comment SkinAbsorption "Each instance of #$SkinAbsorption is a bodily event in which an animal absorbs something into its tissues and/or bloodstream via (a portion of) its #$Skin.")
(comment AdministeringADrug "The act of administering to oneself or to another animal one dose of a drug or other pharmacy product, usually as part of medical treatment.  The result of each #$AdministeringADrug instance is that some portion of the drug substance administered is in the tissues and/or bloodstream of the body.  Therefore, instances cover the action taken to provide the drug to the body as well as any additional passive events that may need to occur so that the drug enters the body's tissues and/or bloodstream.")
(comment TopicalDrugAdministration "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$AdministeringADrug.  Instances of #$TopicalDrugAdministration are events in which a drug substance (possibly also including inactive ingredients) is applied to the surface of an animal's body.  This collection includes both self-administration and administration by another agent.")
(comment TransdermalAdministration "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$AdministeringADrug. Instances of #$TransdermalAdministration are events in which some portion of a drug substance is allowed to contact the skin, and is absorbed through the skin into the bloodstream.")
(comment TransdermalAdministration "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$AdministeringADrug. Instances of #$TransdermalAdministration are events in which some portion of a drug substance is made to contact the skin, and is absorbed through the skin into the bloodstream.")
(comment BodySurfaceApplication "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType.  Instances are events in which a substance or object is applied to the external surface of the body.  Specializations include (#$ApplyingStuffFn #$Makeup), #$ApplyingSoapToBody, and #$ApplyingTransdermalPatch.  Instances may be performed by the #$Animal which is #$bodilyActedOn in the event, or by a separate agent.")
(comment Capsule-Ingestible "The collection of all #$Pills in capsule form.  An instance of #$Capsule-Ingestible is a portion of a #$ConsumableProduct, such as a #$DrugSubstance or a #$DietarySupplement, in powdered or granular form, contained in a capsule that is typically made out of #$Gelatin or some other substance which will dissolve when swallowed so that the product is released and can be absorbed.")
(comment constituentTypes-Active "<code>(#$constituentTypes-Active ?OBJ ?TYPE)</code> states that <code>OBJ</code> contains some portion of the type of stuff, <code>TYPE</code>, as an active ingredient.  In other words, that portion is a constituent of this product which would actually produce the effects intended by the product if it were used as intended.  Other ingredients, such as colorings, flavorings, binding agents, etc. are usually not included.")
(comment Self-AdministrationOfDrug "The act of administering one dose of a drug or other pharmacy product (see #$AdministeringADrug) to oneself, usually as part of medical treatment. Instances cover the action taken to provide the drug to the body as well as any additional passive events that may need to occur so that the drug enters the body's tissues and/or bloodstream.")
(disjointWith InVitroAdministration Self-AdministrationOfDrug)
(disjointWith Injecting-Intrathecal Self-AdministrationOfDrug)
(disjointWith IntracoronaryInjectionOfThrombolyticAgent Self-AdministrationOfDrug)
(comment TransdermalAdministration-Patch "The collection of events in which a #$TransdermalPatch is applied to the skin of an animal (See #$ApplyingTransdermalPatch), contained substances are exposed to the skin of the animal, and the therapuetic agent absorbs through the skin and into the bloodstream of the animal.")
(comment ComponentTypeAndNumberSpecificationAttribute "The collection of attributes used to specify components of larger constructs where the attribute can be used to understand how many of a certain type of component are specified to be in instantiations of the build.")
(comment typeHasProcessorTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasProcessorTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList PROC-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes NUM instances of PROC-TYPE.")
(comment DeviceOrPowerSupplyIsDualVoltage "The collection of electrical devices whose power supplies can utilize either ~110 or ~220 volts or that can directly utilize either voltage range.")
(comment StandardElectricalCurrentType "The collection of canonical types of electical currents.  #$DirectCurrent and #$AlternatingCurrent are the current instances of this collection.")
(comment deviceTypeUsesCurrentType "(#$deviceTypeUsesCurrentType TYPE CURRENT-TYPE) means that every instance of TYPE utilizes the #$StandardElectricalCurrentType CURRENT-TYPE.")
(comment numberOfMainSpecifiedComponentTypeInSystemType "(#$numberOfMainSpecifiedComponentTypeInSystemType TYPE1 TYPE2 NUM)</code> means that there is a specification relevant in the context of assertion in which it was specified that there are NUM instances of TYPE2 as main functional components in instances of TYPE1.  This relationship does not hold of unspecified components (even if they play large functional roles in instances of TYPE1).  For example, an assertion about a certain type of server farm may specify that there are 6 computer servers of a certain sort as specified components, but it would not follow that there are thereby 6 motherboards as specified components even though each computer server has a motherboard as a main functional component.")
(comment typeHasNICConnectorTypeAndNumber "(#$typeHasNICConnectorTypeAndNumber COMP-TYPE (TheList CONN-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of COMP-TYPE includes a network interface card with NUM instances of the connector type CONN-TYPE.")
(comment ProductTypeTypeByOrderability "The collection of collections of product \"types\" (note that instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW or their corresponding provisioned correlates can be instances of instances of this collection) that are organized by \"orderability\" -- orderable, procurable, or provisionable.")
(comment systemComponentTypeHasRelnToInstance "(#$systemComponentTypeHasRelnToInstance SYS-TYPE TYPE RELN INSTANCE) means that if an instance, X, of TYPE is a component (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole) in some instance of SYS-TYPE, then (RELN X INSTANCE).")
(comment componentInSystem-ComponentUtilizesComponent "(#$componentInSystem-ComponentUtilizesComponent COM-1 COM-2) means that there is some #$FunctionalSystem to which both COM-1 and COM-2 belong and, in some general sense, COM-1 utilizes COM-2 within that system.  E.g. in a modern internal combustion engine, one might say that the ECU (Engine control unit) utilizes the fuel injection system to modify fuel air mixture.")
(comment ConnectingNetworkDevices "The collection of events in which network devices are connected together.")
(comment ProtectingADeviceFromAPowerSurge "The collection of situations in which an electrical device is being protected from a power surge.")
(comment HousingOfASystemOfDevices "The collection of instances of #$ContainingSomething where the thing contained is an integrated system of devices.")
(comment HousingAComputer "The collection if instances of #$HousingASystemOfDevices where the devices house constitute a computer.")
(comment portComponentTypeAndNumber "(#$portComponentTypeAndNumber TYPE (TheList PORT-TYPE NUM) means that the every instance of TYPE has as a component NUM network ports of PORT-TYPE.")
(comment storageCapacity "Relates a type of computer hardware component to the amount of storage it includes.")
(comment HardwareComponentConnectorTypeBySex "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection and a specialization of #$ArtifactType.  Each instance of #$HardwareComponentConnectorTypeBySex is a collection of component couplers that are the same sex.")
(comment SFP_SFP-Plus-Connector "The collection of SFP/SFP+ connectors")
(comment ArtifactTypeOrAbstractProduct "This collection is a subcollection of the union of #$ConceptualWork, #$AbstractInformationStructure and various specializations of #$Artifact-Generic.  It serves as a useful generalization of various product \"types\".  While most \"types\" are represented as collections, some of the more abstract products -- specifications, computer software, etc. are individuals.  In a clear sense they are analogous to collections as the actual things that people interact with will be their instantiations  -- e.g., #$programCopies, #$instantiationOfAIS, etc.")
(comment deviceHasInterfaceSpeedOption "relates a device to a rate at which it can communicate via its interface.")
(comment deviceCanAutoNegotiateInterfaceSpeedOption "relates a device to #$True or #$False according to whether it can autonegotiate its interface speed.")
(comment intendedUseTypeCategory "relates a type of artifact or specification to the category of things that represent the intended use of its instances.  This does not entail that those instances are members of that collection as the artifact in question may be only a functional part of instances of the use collection -- E.g. (#$intendedUseTypeCategory HondaCivicChassis ConsumerPassengerAutomobile)")
(comment componentChoiceInSystem-FunctionalRoleTypeType "(#$componentChoiceInSystem-FunctionalRoleTypeType SYSTEM-TYPE TYPE) means that instances of SYSTEM-TYPE can have TYPE as a component.  Specifically, TYPE is one of the component choices for builds of SYSTEM-TYPE.  This does not entail that for any given component, it could be absent from the build -- sometimes a choice is a choice of one.  Nor does this entail that any particular set of values for \"TYPE\" can be jointly instantiated into any particular build.")
(comment resourcePoolHasVirtualMemorySize "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$ResourcePool-Computational to computer memory. (#$resourcePoolHasVirtualMemorySize POOL SIZE) means that POOL can supply SIZE to one of its virtual machines.")
(comment resourcePoolHasVirtualDiskSize "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$ResourcePool-Computational to the amount of disk space that it can supply to virtual machines.")
(comment Vent-Artifact "The collection of portals in systems that are designed to carry gas either out of or into the system.  See the specializations #$IntakeVent, and #$OuttakeVent.")
(comment IntakeVent "The collection of instances of #$Vent-Artifact that are currently serving the purpose of allowing gas to enter the system.")
(comment OuttakeVent "The collection of instances of #$Vent-Artifact that are currently serving the purpose of allowing gas to exit the system.")
(comment systemComponentTypeHasRelnToType "(#$systemComponentTypeHasRelnToType SYS-TYPE TYPE RELN RELATED-TYPE) means that every instance of SYS-TYPE has some instance, X, of TYPE as a component (#$componentInSystem-FunctionalRole) and there is some instance, Y, of RELATED-TYPE such that (RELN X Y).")
(comment Computer-Generic "A specialization of #$System and an immediate generalization of #$Computer.  Each instance of #$Computer-Generic is either a physical computer (#$Computer) or a virtual computer (#$VirtualComputerInstance).")
(comment VirtualComputerInstance "A specialization of #$InformationBearingThing and #$Artifact-Intangible.  Each instance of #$VirtualComputerInstance is a currently executing virtual machine that acts as a computer .")
(comment computer-Generic-IPAddress "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Computer-Generic with instances of #$IPAddress. (#$computer-Generic-IPAddress COMP IP) means that COMP has the IP address IP. (Note that a given computer might have different IP addresses at different times.)")
(comment ipAssignedViaProtocol "(#$ipAssignedViaProtocol COMP IP PROTOCOL) means that the #$IPAddress, IP, was assigned to COMP via PROTOCOL (e.g. DCHP).")
(comment computer-Generic-DNSSubdomain "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Computer-Generic to a string that characterizes its DNS subdomain.")
(comment computer-Generic-NetworkZone "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Computer-Generic to a string that characterizes its network zone.")
(comment RequestingAVMFromThePool "Each instance of this collection is an official request to instantiate a VM (#$VirtualComputerInstance) from some instance of #$ResourcePool-Computational.")
(comment InstantiatingAVMFromThePool "Each instance of this collection is a service event whereby a new instance of #$VirtualComputerInstance is instantiated from some #$ResourcePool-Computational.")
(comment actionExpectedEffects "(#$actionExpectedEffects ACTION-TYPE SITUATION-TYPE) states that if some instance of ACTION-TYPE is executed and the #$actionPreconditions hold,then we can expect that some instance of SITUATION-TYPE will arise. Note that unlike #$actionEffects, it is not necessarily the case that the situation will occur immediately after the action.")
(comment SCSIController "The collection of all SCSI controllers. A type of #$ElectronicDevice.  Each instance of this collection is a Small Computer System Interface (SCSI).  A SCSI controller is device that allows the CPU in a computer to communicate with a disk drive of some sort.  In the past disk controllers were separate from the disk drive.  In modern implementation the controller is integrated into the disk drive and is not a separate expansion board.  #$SCSIController is an instance of #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment ComputerProcessor-Logical " Each instance of this collection is a logical processor.  A logical processor is a processor either physical or virtual that is able to execute a CPU instruction.  E.g. a modern quad core CPU with hyper-threading has up to eight logical processors available -- two for each core.")
(comment computerHasLogicalProcessor "(#$computerHasLogicalProcessor COMPUTER PROCESSOR) means that PROCESSOR is one of the logical processors in COMPUTER.")
(comment computerHasOSAccessibleRAM "(#$computerHasOSAccessibleRAM COMPUTER RAM) means that COMPUTER, either physical or virtual, has RAM amount of memory available to the OS -- this is often referred to as \"total physical memory\".")
(comment computerHasAvailableLocalStorage "(#$computerHasAvailableStorage COMPUTER AMOUNT) means that COMPUTER, either physical or virtual, has AMOUNT amount of storage available to it.\"")
(comment runsOS-Generic "<code>(#$runsOS-Generic COMPUTER-GENERIC OS)</code> means that the individual #$Computer-Generic <code>COMPUTER-GENERIC</code> is running the #$OperatingSystem <code>OS</code>.")
(comment resourcePoolTypeGroupMembersRunOS "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates types of #$ResourcePool-Computational to an #$OperatingSystem. (#$resourcePoolTypeGroupMembersRunOS POOL-TYPE OS) means that, by default, any #$groupMembers of an instance of POOL-TYPE will be running (#$runsOS) OS.")
(comment valuesConstrainValuesForReln "(#$valuesConstrainValuesForReln PRED1 PRED2 RELN COMP) means that the arg2 values for PRED1 for X are constrained to be COMP the arg2 values for PRED2 for Y when (RELN X Y).  E.g. (#$valuesConstrainValuesForReln #$vMemoryOption    #$hypervisorSupportedMemoryAllocation #$resourcePoolTypeGroupMembersRunOS #$lessThanOrEqualTo) means that the values for #$vMemoryOption for some X, cannot be greater than the #$hypervisorSupportedMemoryAllocation for some Y when (#$resourcePoolTypeGroupMembersRunOS X Y)")
(comment InternetAppliance-Enterprise "The collection of special purpose internet connectivity devices for networks.  These devices are configured to be easy to setup and optimize internet connectivity to the user's network often with dedicated caching, bandwidth management and special features designed to optimize for internet-like content -- audio/video streaming, etc.")
(comment InternetAppliance-Consumer "The collection of personal computers (in the broad sense) designed to access the internet for a specific purpose like webbrowsing or email activities. Typically easy to setup and configure their range of functionality is more limited than most personal computers, laptops, etc.  This should not be confused with #$InternetAppliance-Enterprise.")
(comment HumanMachineInterface "The collection of #$ControlDevices used to interface humans with various types of machines.  While a single button or lever would not be an instance of this collection, a system of such designed to control, e.g., a printing machine would.")
(comment TouchInterfaceControlUnit "The collection of devices used to interact with machines via touch.  Note that the key feature of such devices are their ability to recognize the presence of one or more points of direct contact caused by the user touching the control portion of the device (either directly or with a stylus in some cases).  Hence a traditional computer keyboard would not be an instance of this collection as those rely on the key presses to register the signal and do not directly recognize the user input.")
(comment TabletopDevice "The collection of devices designed to sit on the table (either freestanding or inside of a mount or dock) during normal usage.")
(comment FloorPlacedDevice "The collection of devices designed to be placed on the floor during normal operation.")
(comment PhysicalDeviceTypeByPlacement "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a type of physical device characterized by its location during normal usage -- wall mounted, tabletop, floor mounted, etc.")
(comment WallMountedDevice "The collection of devices that are mounted on a wall during normal usage -- E.g. your typical thermostat. ")
(comment TeleconferencingEquipment "A collection of electronic devices.  Each instance of #$TeleconferencingEquipment is a device dedicated to various teleconferencing functions such as streaming video or bridging multiple audio steams.")
(comment MultiMediaConferenceBridge "The collection of devices used as bridges for teleconferencing.  These include bridge-style telephones as well as dedicated teleconferencing media servers and such that are used with telephones but require external phones to display or capture the audio/video signals.")
(comment Antenna-WiFi-Broadcast "A specialization of #$Antenna.  Each instance of this collection is an antenna attached to a WiFi access point that allows broadcast of the WiFi signal over a larger area.")
(comment RemoteMonitoringDevice "The collection of remote network monitoring devices.  Each instance of this collection is a device designed to support monitoring and protocol analysis of computer networks.")
(comment TerminalServer "A computer server for local area networks typically used to connect peripherals like printers, etc. to the network.  They can be simple devices with no advanced functions like encryption or authentication.  often they are used as intermediaries by allowing access to console functions of the connected devices.")
(comment NetworkSercuritySystem-Device "The collection of network computer devices designed to monitor the network for threats and defend against them.  ")
(comment TemporalSynchronizationServer "the collection of computer servers used in a network to provide accurate time and synchronize compatible connected devices and systems")
(comment MediaConvergenceServer "The collection of proprietary server machines sold by Cisco designed to be the standard platform for various Cisco products such as \"Cisco Unity\".")
(comment NetworkAppliance "A computer that is specialized for use on a network.  Instances of this collection are typically optimized for better throughput of network data and include dedicated functions for common network tasks that are often typically performed by multiple machines.")
(comment Codec-Software "The collection of computer programs used to encode/decode a data stream or signal -- typically from one format to another or from an analog signal to digital or vice-versa.")
(comment Multiplexer "A specialization of #$ElectronicComponent.  Each instance of #$Multiplexer is a device used for multiplexing electromagnetic signals.  In general, a multiplexor takes one of several analog or digital signals as input and forwards them into another single signal as output.")
(comment Provisioning "The collection of provisioning events.  Each instance of this collection is an act of getting together the necessary equipment or supplies in response to some need or request.")
(comment rPChoiceDeterminesVMAttribute "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a POD attribute to an instance level attribute of a virtual machine just in case the POD attribute states a configuration detail that provides the options for or determines that attribute of the VM. ")
(comment computerHasNumberOfLogicalProcessors "(#$computerHasNumberOfLogicalProcessors COMPUTER NUM) means that COMPUTER has NUM logical processors available to it.")
(comment RackComputerChassis "This is the collection of #$ComputerChassis that hold rack computers/servers.")
(comment BladeComputerChassis "This is the collection of chassis for blade servers.  A subcollection of #$RackComputerChassis, instances of this collection are even more streamlined than the typical rack chassis.  These chassis are designed to fit into \"blade enclosures\" that provided dedicated power and cooling to all units.")
(comment BladeServerCabinet-47RU "The collection of computer blade server enclosures with 47 rack units")
(comment BladeServer-Computer "The collection of ComputerServers that are thin but deep and designed to fit within a larger \"blade enclosures\"  (See #$ComputerServerCabinet-BladeServer).  Typically multiple blade servers are mounted into a single cabinet which is typically provided with a dedicated cooling and power supply system.")
(comment StoringComputerServersForUse "each instance of this collection is an instance of #$StorageOfSomethingInAContainer where multiple computer servers are housed in some sort of rack and made available for use.  This does not include events such as storing the servers in a box or closet if they are powered off and not ready for use.")
(comment typicallyOccurDuringPeriodType "(#$typicallyOccurDuringPeriodType SIT-TYPE PERIOD-TYPE) means that instances of SIT-TYPE are usually (typically, in most cases, etc.) temporally subsumed by instances of PERIOD-TYPE.")
(comment satisfiesRequest "(#$satisfiesRequest REQUEST SITUATION)' means that SITUATION arises as a response to request and is sufficient to have satisfied the request.  For example, if I request a particular service like having my lawn mowed, and the situation of having a mowed lawn arises as a result of this request, then (#$satisfiesRequest RequestingLawnBeMowed LawnIsMowed) holds.")
(comment expectedDelayBetween "(#$expectedDelayBetween ACTION-TYPE SITUATION-TYPE PRED DURATION) states that an instance, A,  of ACTION-TYPE occurs and an instance SITUATION-TYPE, S, follows it, such that (PRED A S), then it is reasonable or expected that there be DURATION time elapsed between the end of the action and the start of the situation.  For example, if you are cooking eggs for breakfast, then it would be expected that the eggs are cooked within 2-3 minutes.  So, (#$expectedDelayBetween CrackingEggsIntoAHeatedPan EnjoyingOverMediumEggs #$actionExpectedEffects (#$MinutesDuration 2-3))")
(comment MeinbergInc "MeinbergInc is a company that is associated with network time servers.  www.meinberg.de produces PCI-X cards.")
(comment TandbergInc "TANDBERG is a global provider of telepresence and high-definition video conferencing solutions for unified communications.")
(comment NTTInc "NTTInc provides wireless telecommunications services, packet communications services, and satellite mobile communications services in Japan.")
(comment NetScalerInc "NetScalerInc is a company that was associated with network virtualization.  It was acquired by Citrix Systems in 2005.")
(comment JuniperNetworks "Juniper Networks, a publicly traded corporation information technology company founded in 1996.")
(comment LucentTechnologies "Lucent Technologies was a publicly traded technology corporation.  Acquired by Alcatel in 2006 the resulting company is called Alcatel-Lucent USA, Inc.")
(comment CienaCorp "Ciena Corp., a publicly traded corporation specializing in telecommunications networking equipment.")
(comment AvayaInc "Avaya Inc., a publicly traded corporation.  Founded in 2000, Avaya specializes in computer networking and telecommunications.")
(comment CrestronInc "CrestronInc was founded in 1968.  It specializes in systems for audio/video control and automation.")
(comment BayNetworksInc "Bay Networks specialized in network hardware.  It was founded in 1994 and acquired by Nortel in 1998.")
(comment AdicInc "AdicInc is a subsidiary of Quantum Corp.  They specialize in tape backup systems and storage management software.")
(comment EndaceLtd "Endace Ltd is a New Zealand company that specialized in Network monitoring and analysis technology.")
(comment ExpansionCardTypeBySpecificFunction "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of computer expansion cards whose instances provide similar functionality.")
(comment WideAreaNetwork-InterfaceCard "The collection of network interface cards (#$EthernetControllerBoard) used in network devices (such as routers) that are designed to allow date to be transmitted ever a Wide Area Network.")
(comment NetworkSwitchingModule-ExpansionCard "The collection of expansion cards with some of the functions of a network switch.")
(comment FiberMediaConverter "The collection of expansion cards that allow conversion from one type of cabling to another.")
(comment SharedPortAdapter-Network "A collection of expansion cards.  Shared Port Adapters are a Cisco proprietary card type. ")
(comment AudioCompressionModule-Network "A collection of expansion cards.  Each instance of this collection if a expansion card that is used to compress audio signals in VoIP networks. ")
(comment VariableMultiplexer-ExpansionCard "A collection of expansion cards.  Each instance of this collection is a #$VariableMultiplexer that is also an expansion card.")
(comment VariableMultiplexer "The collection of devices that perform signal equalization and multiplexing.")
(comment NetworkTappingModule-ExpansionCard "A collection of expansion cards.  Each instance of this collection is a expansion card designed to extract a signal from some carrier connection without breaking or disturbing the connection.  Often used in passive monitoring of computer networks. ")
(comment VoiceModule-ExpansionCard "A collection of expansion cards.  Each instance of this collection is a expansion card designed carry and process audio signals over a network.")
(comment FiberChannelAdapter-ExpansionCard "The collection of expansion cards used for routing signals in a Fiber Channel network.")
(comment FICONModule-ExpansionCard "The collection of expansion cards used for routing signals via the FICON protocol.")
(comment TransceiverModule-ExpansionCard "The collection of transceivers used in data communications that are designed to fit into device slots. ")
(comment VirtualTapeServerInterface-ExpansionCard "The collection of expansion cards used for interfacing with virtual tape servers.")
(comment StorageAreaNetworkAccessModule-ExpansionCard "The collection of expansion cards used for interfacing with storage area networks.")
(comment ExpansionCard-PCI "The collection of expansion cards that utilize the \"Peripheral Component Interconnect\" bus standard.  The PCI standard specifies the size and shape of the physical bus and communication protocols, but it does not otherwise specify the functionality of the card or circuit.")
(disjointWith UsingADevice DrugTreatment-SingleDose)
(disjointWith GroupActivity DrugTreatment-SingleDose)
(comment DrugTreatment-SingleDose "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent: a collection of medical care events in which a single dose of a drug is administered (see #$AdministeringADrug) and has a resulting physiological and/or mental effect (see #$DrugTherapy).")
(disjointWith UsingADevice DrugTreatmentSequence)
(disjointWith GroupActivity DrugTreatmentSequence)
(comment DrugTreatmentSequence "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent: a collection of medical care events in which a sequence of drug doses are administered, each resulting in a physiological and/or mental effect on the patient.  Instances of #$DrugTreatmentSequence are often described by physicians in prescriptions (see #$DrugPrescription-Specification), which specify what dosage of which drug is taken, how many doses and on what schedule, etc.")
(comment DrugTreatmentSequence-Continuous "A specialization of #$DrugTreatmentSequence: a collection of medical care events in which some substance is continuously provided to the patient - for example, a drug in an intravenous drip, or oxygen supplementation. This collection is in contrast with #$DrugTreatmentSequence-DiscreteDoses, instances of which consist of a series of #$DrugTreatment-SingleDose instances.")
(disjointWith DrugTreatmentSequence-DiscreteDoses DrugTreatmentSequence-Continuous)
(comment DrugTreatmentSequence-DiscreteDoses "A specialization of #$DrugTreatmentSequence: a collection of medical care events in which a sequence of discrete drug doses are administered, each resulting in some physiological and/or mental effect on the patient.  This collection is in contrast with #$DrugTreatmentSequence-Continuous, in which some substance is continuously provided to the patient - for example, a drug in an intravenous drip, or oxygen supplementation.")
(comment DrugAddictionRehabilitation "A collection of events in which a person is assisted to recover from addiction to some drug substance.  Each #$DrugAddictionRehabilitation event is likely to have numerous #$subEvents, typically including repeated psychological counseling and/or behavioral modification techniques.")
(disjointWith DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose DrugTreatmentSequence-SameDose)
(comment DrugTreatmentSequence-SameDose "A specialization of #$DrugTreatmentSequence-DiscreteDoses: a collection of medical care events in which a sequence of discrete drug doses are administered, all at the same dosage, each resulting in some physiological and/or mental effect on the patient.  This collection is in contrast with #$DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose, in which the dosage is varied according to some specified pattern. ")
(comment DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose "A specialization of #$DrugTreatmentSequence-DiscreteDoses: a collection of medical care events in which a sequence of discrete drug doses is administered, in which the dosage is varied according to some specified pattern, and each dose exerts its physiological and/or mental effect on the patient.  Instances of #$DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose would include corticosteroid regimens in which the dosage is tapered off over several days, or courses of antibiotics which have a larger first dose than the subsequent ones. This collection is in contrast with #$DrugTreatmentSequence-SameDose, in which each dose given or taken is the same size.")
(comment PharmacyProductTypeByName "The collection of types of drug products that are specified as to their brand or generic name (which indicates what type or types of compounds are contained in their instances), but are not specified as to dosage form, administration route, strength or packaging.  For example, #$ZoloftProduct is an instance of #$PharmacyProductTypeByName, but 'Zoloft tablets' would not be.")
(disjointWith UsingADevice DrugTreatment)
(disjointWith GroupActivity DrugTreatment)
(comment DrugTreatment "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent: a collection of medical care events in which one or more doses of a drug is administered (see #$AdministeringADrug) each having a resulting physiological and/or mental effect (see #$DrugTherapy).")
(comment drugTypeOfTreatment "This predicate relates a #$DrugTreatment event to an instance of #$PharmacyProductType.  (#$drugTypeOfTreatment TRT DRUG-TYPE) states that DRUG-TYPE is the type of drug used in TRT.")
(comment Slipway "The collection of instances of #$Ramp that are or can be safely used to load watercraft into or extract watercraft from the water.")
(disjointWith PathThroughAir Slipway)
(comment VertRamp "The collection of instances of #$HalfPipe that are sufficiently large that the rider is able to propell him or herself vertically into the air, and thus land on the ramp, rather than being propelled out of the ramp, as is typically the case with a #$MiniRamp.")
(disjointWith HalfPipe QuarterPipe)
(disjointWith MiniRamp VertRamp)
(comment MiniRamp "The collection of instances of #$HalfPipe that are relatively small and portable.")
(comment executionTypeOfManeuverType "The predicate that corresponds to #$ExecutionOfManeuverTypeFn, <code>(#$executionTypeOfManeuverType EXECUTION-TYPE MANEUVER-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>EXECUTION-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of an instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalManeuver of type <code>MANEUVER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ExecutionOfManeuverTypeFn "<code>(#$ExecutionOfManeuverTypeFn MANEUVER-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of an instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalManeuver of type <code>MANEUVER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment PathTypeByPathMediumType "A facet on #$Path-Spatial, instances are specializations of that collection whose instances are all paths through a common type of medium.")
(comment SolidSurfacePath "The collection of all instances of #$Path-Spatials that have a solid surface.")
(comment instructionDeterminesProgramActionType "(#$instructionDeterminesProgramActionType INSTRUCTION TYPE) means that a successful execution of the code instruction INSTRUCTION in a running program will result, other things being equal, in a #$ProgramAction that is an instance of TYPE.")
(comment SittingOnSomething "This is the collection of situations in which an animal is sitting on some supporting object.")
(comment seat "<code>(#$seat SITTING SEATING-DEVICE)</code> identifies <code>SITTING-DEVICE</code> as the instance of #$SeatingDevice that being used normally as a seat in <code>SITTING</code>, an instance of #$SittingOnSomething.  That is, not only is <code>SEATING-DEVICE</code> the #$supportingObject, but the #$SeatingDeviceSeat of <code>SEATING-DEVICE</code> is occupied by the animal sitting.  Not that not every instance of #$SittingOnSomething will have a #$seat, though it will have a #$supportingObject (e.g., sitting on the floor, sitting on the arm of a chair, etc.).")
(comment seated "<code>(#$seated SITTING SEATED)</code> identifies <code>SEATED</code> as the animal sitting in <code>SITTING</code>, an instance of #$SittingOnSomething.")
(comment objectRepaired "<code>(#$objectRepaired REPAIR OBJECT)</code> means that <code>OBJECT</code> is repaired in <code>REPAIR</code>, an instance of #$SimpleRepairing.")
(comment eventFocalLocation "<code>(#$eventFocalLocation EVENT LOCATION)</code> means that the event <code>EVENT</code> is focally located at <code>LOCATION</code>, an instance of #$EnduringThing-Localized.  #$eventFocalLocation is more restrictive than its generalization, #$eventOccursAt, which applies to all instances of #$EnduringThing-Localized that spatially subsume every object to which it applies.  I.e., given a dancing-on-the-table event <code>DancingOnTheTable-13926</code> that takes place on a table <code>Table-43</code>, #$eventOccursAt will not only hold of <code>DancingOnTheTable-13926</code> and <code>Table-43</code>, it will hold of <code>DancingOnTheTable-13926</code> and the room in which <code>Table-43</code> resides, the floor of the building where the room is, the building itself, the city block of the building, the city, the country of the city, the planet Earth, and the entire physical universe.  However, #$eventFocalLocation holds only of <code>DancingOnTheTable-13926</code> and <code>Table-43</code>.  This is not to say that #$eventFocalLocation is functional or single-entry in its second argument place; depending on the granularity of the context, it might be that the #$eventFocalLocation of an event might include a range of locations.  For example, the operations of a land rover on Mars might, in the context of naive discussions about what's newsworthy, be such that the #$eventFocalLocation is the surface of Mars (or Mars itself), while in the context of NASA operations tracking the rover, the #$eventFocalLocation might be particular regions on the surface of Mars.  But in neither context is it likely that the solar system would count as the #$eventFocalLocation, even though it does fall under the extent of #$eventOccursAt.")
(comment fieldOfPlay "<code>(#$fieldOfPlay COMPETITION AREA)</code> identifies <code>AREA</code> as the designated instance of #$SportsPlayingArea where <code>COMPETITION</code>, an instance of #$SportsCompetition, is played.")
(disjointWith GameWalkthrough-Instructions MedicalPrescription-Specification)
(disjointWith MedicalPrescription-Specification MachineCodeInstruction)
(disjointWith Recipe-CW MedicalPrescription-Specification)
(disjointWith CheatingInstructionsForGameProgram MedicalPrescription-Specification)
(disjointWith DirectionsToGetSomewhere MedicalPrescription-Specification)
(disjointWith InvestmentGuide MedicalPrescription-Specification)
(comment MedicalPrescription-Specification "A collection of #$ConceptualWorks, each of which is also an instance of #$Instructions.  Each instance of #$MedicalPrescription-Specification is a set of formal instructions given by a medical care giver (an instance of #$Prescriber) in their professional capacity to a patient in their care, typically concerning the use of a drug or a medical device.")
(comment DrugProductFn "<code>(#$DrugProductFn PHARM-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of products which have the drug, <code>PHARM-TYPE</code>, as their focal ingredient.  Instances of <code>(#$DrugProductFn PHARM-TYPE)</code> are products intended to deliver one or more doses of <code>PHARM-TYPE</code> to individuals who use them.")
(comment TherapeuticClassType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections of drugs characterized by their ability to address some symptom (e.g., #$CoughSuppressant or #$AntidiureticAgent), to have some effect on the body (e.g., #$Anorectic or #$Expectorant), or to have an effect through a particular mechanism (e.g., #$BetaBlocker or #$GlycoproteinIIbIIIaInhibitor).  Particular drug substances are rarely instances of #$TherapeuticClassType.")
(disjointWith Microtheory PrescriptionParameter)
(disjointWith SoftwareParameter PrescriptionParameter)
(comment PrescriptionParameter "The collection of all parameters typically given a value in instances of #$MedicalPrescription-Specification.  In many legal jurisdictions, there exist laws that require each prescription to fully specify certain parameters.")
(comment connectedByFactSet "<code>(#$connectedByFactSet SET-OF-THINGS SET-OF-SENTENCES)</code> means that the facts (represented as CycLSentences) in <code>SET-OF-SENTENCES</code> jointly serve to relate the elements of <code>SET-OF-THINGS</code>.  For example, <code>(#$connectedByFactSet (#$TheSet #$KevinBacon #$HerbertRoss) (#$TheSet (#$movieActors #$Footloose-TheMovie #$KevinBacon) (#$movieDirectors #$Footloose-TheMovie #$HerbertRoss)))</code> means that Kevin Bacon and Herbert Ross are connected by the chain: Kevin Bacon acted in <i>Footloose</i>, which Ross directed.  See also #$relatedToVia.")
(comment nodesDerivedFromSourceConnectedByFactSet "<code>(#$nodesDerivedFromSourceConnectedByFactSet NODE-SET OBJECT PREDICATE FACT-SET)</code> means that <code>(#$connectedByFactSet NODE-SET FACT-SET)</code> where <code>NODE-SET</code> is a subset all values of <code>ARG2 ... ARGN</code> where <code>(PREDICATE OBJECT ARG2 ... ARGN)</code>.  For example, <code>(#$nodesDerivedFromSourceConnectedByFactSet 
  (#$TheSet #$Dog #$LandStuff 
    (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$DiggingAHole #$doneBy #$Dog)) 
  (#$AVWorkWithIDFn 181361) #$visuallyDepicts-Type-Precise 
  (#$TheSet 
    (#$relationAllExists #$objectActedOn 
      (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$DiggingAHole #$doneBy #$Dog) #$LandStuff) 
    (#$relationAllExists #$doneBy 
      (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$DiggingAHole #$doneBy #$Dog) #$Dog)))</code> means that the set of facts in the arg4 connect the nodes in the arg1, where each element of the arg1 is a value for <code>DEPICTED</code> such that <code>(#$visuallyDepicts-Type-Precise (#$AVWorkWithIDFn 181361) DEPICTED)</code>.")
(comment prescriptionForPatient "Identifies the animal that a prescription is for.  <code>(#$prescriptionForPatient SCRIP ANIMAL)</code> states that <code>SCRIP</code> is a doctor's prescription which authorizes (and recommends) that the drug or medical device identified in <code>SCRIP</code> (see #$prescribedType) be purchased for the named patient, <code>ANIMAL</code>, and that it be be used by that patient in the manner specified.")
(comment prescriptionFilled "(#$prescriptionFilled FILL PRESCRIPTION) means that in the #$FillingAPrescription event FILL, the medical prescription (see #$MedicalPrescription-Specification), PRESCRIPTION, was filled.")
(comment prescribedType "Identifies the drug or medical device that a prescription is for.  <code>(#$prescribedType SCRIP TYPE)</code> states that <code>SCRIP</code> is a doctor's prescription which authorizes (and recommends) that the drug or medical device, <code>TYPE</code>, be purchased for the patient named in the prescription (see #$prescriptionForPatient), and that it be be used by that patient in the manner specified.")
(comment DrugPrescription "A specialization of #$OfficialDocument. Each instance of this collection is a document in which a doctor (#$Doctor-Medical) authorizes a patient to purchase a certain amount of a #$PrescriptionDrug and take it according to some specified schedule. For the actual instructions that make up a prescription, see #$DrugPrescription-Specification.")
(comment numberOfRefills "(#$numberOfRefills SCRIP N) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP is a doctor's prescription which authorizes the named patient to purchase a refill of the specified drug in the specified amount up to N times.  For example, if the initial prescription is for a 30-day supply, and 5 refills are allowed, the patient may obtain up to a 6-month supply of the medication on authority of that one prescription.")
(comment DevicePrescription-Specification "A collection of #$ConceptualWorks, each of which is also an instance of #$Instructions.  Each instance of #$DevicePrescription-Specification is a set of formal instructions given by a medical care giver (an instance of #$Prescriber) in their professional capacity  with regard to a patient in their care, concerning the use of a #$MedicalDevice.  Often, such devices are deployed or installed in events performed by a prescribing physician (e.g., installation of a #$Pacemaker or #$CardiacValveProsthesis).  If the patient is to acquire and use the device (e.g., #$HypodermicSyringes for the injection of prescribed medicines), the prescription instructs and authorizes the patient to acquire the specified device or devices, and gives instructions for how it is to be used. ")
(comment prescriptionFromPrescriber "Identifies the medical professional that issues a prescription.  <code>(#$prescriptionFromPrescriber SCRIP PRO)</code> states that <code>SCRIP</code> is issued by the #$Prescriber, <code>PRO</code>.\")")
(comment numberOfDoses "(#$numberOfDoses SCRIP N) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP is a doctor's prescription which authorizes and instructs the named patient to acquire N doses of the specified drug type each time the prescription is filled.  For example, if (#$numberOfDoses SCRIP 30), and (#$numberOfRefills SCRIP 2), the total number of doses the patient is authorized by SCRIP to acquire is 90 (because the first filling doesn't count as a refill).\")")
(comment prescriptionSpecifiesDosage "(#$prescriptionSpecifiesDosage SCRIP QUANT) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP asks that each dose taken in the #$DrugTreatmentSequence-SameDose specified by the prescription be in the amount of QUANT.  Quite frequently, QUANT will be an instance of #$Mass, however some medication dosages may be specified with a different type of quantity.  For prescriptions which specify a #$DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose, use this predicate instead: #$prescriptionSpecifiesDosageForNthDose.")
(comment prescriptionSpecifiesDosageForNthDose "(#$prescriptionSpecifiesDosageForNthDose SCRIP QUANT N) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP asks that the Nth dose taken in the #$DrugTreatmentSequence-VariableDose specified by the prescription be in the amount of QUANT.  Quite frequently, QUANT will be an instance of #$Mass, however some medication dosages may be specified with a different type of quantity.  For prescriptions which specify a #$DrugTreatmentSequence-SameDose, use this predicate instead: #$prescriptionSpecifiesDosage.")
(comment prescriptionSpecifiesTreatmentStartTime "(#$prescriptionSpecifiesDosageForNthDose SCRIP DATE) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP asks that first dose of the specified #$DrugTreatmentSequence be taken/administered at DATE.")
(comment prescriptionSpecifiesAdministrationRouteType "(#$prescriptionSpecifiesAdministrationRouteType SCRIP ADMIN-TYPE) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP asks that the drug administered in the specified #$DrugTreatmentSequence be taken/administered in events of ADMIN-TYPE.")
(comment prescriptionDescribesDrugTreatmentType "The predicate #$prescriptionDescribesDrugTreatmentType is used to associate instances of #$DrugPrescription-Specification with a specialization of DrugTreatment which are their focal content.  <code>(#$prescriptionDescribesDrugTreatmentType SPEC TYPE)</code> means that the content of #$DrugPrescription-Specification <code>SPEC</code> is directed at the occurrence of an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment DrugPrescription-Specification "A collection of #$ConceptualWorks, each of which is also an instance of #$Instructions.  Each instance of #$DrugPrescription-Specification is a set of formal instructions given by a medical care giver (an instance of #$Prescriber) in their professional capacity, concerning the use of a drug by or for a patient in their care.  Situations that conform to this kind of specification (see #$situationConformsToSpecification) are thus instances of #$DrugTreatment.  In the event that the patient or their guardian is to administer the drug (i.e., it is not being provided as part of medical services such as care in a hospital or clinic), the prescription also authorizes the patient or their agent to purchase the specified amount of the drug.")
(comment MedicalPrescription-NonInstitutional "A specialization of #$MedicalPrescription-Specification.  Each instance of #$MedicalPrescription-NonInstitutional is a set of formal instructions given by a medical care giver (an instance of #$Prescriber) in their professional capacity, to a patient in their care (or to the patient's guardian).   Situations that conform to this kind of specification (see #$situationConformsToSpecification) are instances of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent in which the administering of the prescribed drug or the deployment of the prescribed device is done by the patient herself or by a family member or other helper.  A necessary precondition of this treatment, authorized by the prescription, is that the patient or their agent purchases the specified medical device or amount of the drug.")
(comment MedicalPrescription-Institutional "A specialization of #$MedicalPrescription-Specification.  Each instance of #$MedicalPrescription-Institutional is a set of formal instructions given by a medical care giver (an instance of #$Prescriber) in their professional capacity, regarding the medical treatment of a patient in their care.   Situations that conform to this kind of specification (see #$situationConformsToSpecification) are instances of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent in which the providing of the prescribed drug or the deployment of the prescribed device is done by health care workers at the institution caring for the patient.")
(comment bhpValuesAtTraceTimeStamps "(#$bhpValuesAtTraceTimeStamps-List WELL START-DATE END-DATE (#$TheList DATE PRESSURE)) means that the the BHP gauge in WELL  measures PRESSUE on DATE, between START-DATE and END-DATE (inclusive), where DATE is a date on which a DTS trace was produced by the DTD fiber FIBER in WELL.")
(comment FillingAPrescription "The collection of all events in which a #$MedicalPrescription-Specification is filled.  This involves #$BuyingAnObject, which is an instance of some #$PharmacyProductType as specified in the prescription.  Some important subsets of #$FillingAPrescription are #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, in which the purchaser obtains the prescribed drug or device directly from a retailer such as a #$Pharmacy or #$OpticalRetailer, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, in which the #$Pharmacy which fills the prescription is a #$MailOrderPharmacy, and #$FillingAPrescription-Institutional, in which a #$MedicalCareInstitution which is caring for a patient fills an in-house #$Prescriber's prescription without any action by the patient.")
(comment drugAdministrationSubEvents "<code>(#$drugAdministrationSubEvents TREAT ADMINISTER)</code> identifies <code>ADMINISTER</code> as an instance of #$AdministeringADrug that is a #$properSubEvents of the treatment with a drug (see #$DrugTreatment),  <code>TREAT</code>.")
(comment DoseOfDrug "A collection of measured portions of #$DrugSubstances.  Instances are quantities of some #$DrugSubstance that are each introduced into the body during an instance of #$AdministeringADrug.  Note that the pill swallowed, the cream applied, the spray inhaled etc. is quite often composed of other, inactive ingredients in addition to the #$DrugSubstance; these composite objects are not instances of #$DoseOfDrug, and play some role other than #$drugAdministered in instances of #$AdministeringADrug.")
(comment sizeOfDose "(#$sizeOfDose DOSE QUANT) states that the #$DoseOfDrug, DOSE, has the amount QUANT.  Quite frequently, QUANT will be an instance of #$Mass, however some medication dosages may be measured with a different type of quantity.")
(comment getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRangeTempRange "<code>(#$getNormalizedTraceAtDateByDepthRange FIBER DATE N MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH MIN-TEMP MAX-TEMP (#$The2DPoint DEPTH TEMP))</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code> measured the depth/temperature pairs <code>DEPTH</code>/<code>TEMP</code> at regular internals of <code>N</code> meters <code>DATE</code>, where <code>DEPTH</code> is in the interval bounded by <code>MIN-DEPTH</code> and <code>MAX-DEPTH</code> and where <code>TEMP</code> is in the interval bounded by <code>MIN-TEMP</code> and <code>MAX-TEMP</code>.")
(comment getNormalizedTraceBetweenDatesByDepthRange "<code>(#$getNormalizedTraceBetweenDatesByDepthRange  FIBER MIN-DEPTH MAX-DEPTH N START END (The2DPoint DEPTH AVG-TEMP))</code> means that the DTS fiber <code>FIBER</code>  normalized to <code>N</code>-meter interval depths between <code>MIN-DEPTH</code> and <code>MAX-DEPTH</code> measured temperatures that average <code>AVG-TEMP</code> between <code>START</code> and the later date <code>END</code>.")
(comment ListOfSetElementsFn "The function #$ListOfSetElementsFn, applied to a #$SetOrCollection SET, results in an extensional list of all the elements of SET in an arbitrary order.  For example, supports that SET = (#$TheSet A B). The (#$ListOfSetElementsFn SET) = (#$TheList A B).  Note that although the order is arbitrary, it is determinate in that evaluating this with the same set on different occasions will always result in the same list.")
(comment prescriptionSubstitutionOfTherapueticEquivalentAllowed "A #$UnaryPredicate.  If (#$prescriptionSubstitutionOfTherapueticEquivalentAllowed SCRIP), the #$DrugPrescription-Specification,  SCRIP, is such that the patient may be treated with a drug that is therapeutically equivalent to the prescribed drug (see #$prescribedDrugType), and that treatment will still conform to the specfication of the prescription.")
(comment prescriptionDosageRateNotToExceed "(#$prescriptionDosageRateNotToExceed SCRIP QUANT TIME) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification SCRIP asks that no more than QUANT of the prescribed drug be administered to the patient within any period of time of length TIME.  Not all drug prescriptions will specify a value for this parameter, however a value is often given when a medication is prescribed to be taken as needed to control some kind of symptom.")
(comment AscendingAlongSurface "Any process in which an object moves upward along some surface.")
(comment ProgramActionRecord "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic that have a standard interpretation as records of program actions, as recorded in #$LogFile instances.")
(comment programActionRecorded "(#$programActionRecorded ACTION RECORD) means that RECORD is a #$ProgramActionRecord which records the occurrence of the #$ProgramAction ACTION.")
(comment timeStampStringOfProgramActionRecord "(#$timeStampStringOfProgramActionRecord RECORD STRING) means that STRING is a #$CharacterString denoting the unique timestamp of the #$ProgramActionRecord RECORD.")
(comment timeStampOfProgramActionRecord "(#$timeStampOfProgramActionRecord RECORD DATE) means that DATE is the unique #$Date which serves as the timestamp of the #$ProgramActionRecord RECORD.")
(comment LogFile "The collection of all log files recording the temporal executions of #$ProgramActions.  A #$LogFile is itself a special kind of #$ComputerCodeStatement consisting in a sequential list of records ostensibly of #$ProgramActions, i.e., a list of #$ProgramActionRecords.  In an accurate #$LogFile, the list of #$ProgramActionRecords corresponds to a temporal sequence of actions taken by a system in the course of executing a program.")
(comment logFileMembers "(#$logFileMembers LOG-FILE RECORD) means that the #$ProgramActionRecord RECORD is a sub-statement of the #$LogFile LOG-FILE.")
(comment executionHasLogFile "(#$executionHasLogFile EXECUTION FILE) means that the #$LogFile FILE records the entirety of EXECUTION (a #$ProgramExecution-Complete) and nothing else.")
(comment executionInLogFile "(#$executionInLogFile PROG-ACTION LOG) means that the #$ProgramAction PROG-ACTION is recorded somewhere in the #$LogFile LOG, either as an individual #$ProgramActionRecord or as a sequence of such.")
(comment RecordingAProgramActionInALogFile "A specialization of #$ProgramAction and of #$InformationRecordingProcess.  Each instance is a #$ProgramAction wherein an ostensible distinct #$ProgramAction is recorded in a #$LogFile (the #$logFileRecordedTo) via a #$ProgramActionRecord (the #$logFileEntryCreated).")
(comment logFileEntryCreated "(#$logFileEntryCreated RECORDING RECORD) means that RECORD is the #$ProgramActionRecord (qua syntactic entity) that is recorded in some #$LogFile in RECORDING (a #$RecordingAProgramActionInALogFile)")
(comment logFileRecordedTo "(#$logFileRecordedTo RECORDING FILE) means that FILE is the #$LogFile (a #$ComputerFile-AIS) that is written to in RECORDING.")
(comment MountableTransporterDevice "The collection of instances of #$MountableTransporter that are also instances of #$PhysicalDevice.")
(comment RampSurface "A specialization of #$PathArtifact and #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible, this is the collection of top-side surfaces of ramps -- the part of the ramp that actually makes it a ramp.")
(comment IontophoreticTransdermalAdministration "The collection of events in which a drug is administered by using a small electric charge to drive its molecules through the skin and into the bloodstream. A device including a chamber containing the drug and a solvent is placed against the skin.  If the drug molecules are positively charged, a positive charge will force it across the skin.  If they are negatively charged, a negative charge is used in that chamber. ")
(comment PathSurface "The collection of all path surfaces, the part of a #$Path-Customary where the actual movement along the path ordinarily or is intended to take place, and by virtue of which the path is considered to be a path.  For example a given #$Highway may have any number of parts, such as layers of concrete, dirt, and gravel, or steel beams and support columns in places where the highway is raised.  But only the road surface of the highway is where one would customarily travel when using the highway as a path.  Similarly, a blood vessel is a path, but it is the inner surface of the vessel where the flow of blood normally takes place, not the outer surface.")
(comment motionFocallyInvolvesPathSurfacesOf "<code>(#$motionFocallyInvolvesPathSurfacesOf MOVEMENT OBJECT)</code> means that <code>MOVEMENT</code>, an instance of #$Movement-TranslationEvent, is a movement focally involving the use of <code>OBJECT</code>, an instance of #$PathArtifact, as a #$motionPathway-Partial, where that use consists, in large part, of sub-events in which one or more instances of #$PathSurface that are a physical part of <code>OBJECT</code> play the role of #$motionPathway-Complete.  Positive examples include the use of a ramp to perform a bicycle or skateboard jump, which involves riding up the ramp surface; and walking up a staircase, which requires stepping on the top-surface of one or more steps.  A negative example would be jumping down from the top of a ramp or from the top of a staircase.")
(comment RoadSurface "The collection of road surfaces -- the part of the road one rides or drives on.")
(comment RampArtifact "The collection of instances of #$Ramp that are construction artifacts, and suitable for #$Movement-TranslationEvent instances involving vehicles or large-ish animals.  Counterexamples include natural ramp formations and toy ramps.")
(comment conventionalPathSurfaceAreas "<code>(#$conventionalPathSurfaceAreas PATH-ARTIFACT PATH-SURFACE)</code> means that <code>PATH-SURFACE</code> is an instance of #$PathSurface that helps comprise the conventional area for traversal along <code>PATH-ARTIFACT</code>, an instance of #$Path-Customary.")
(comment TransportationDevice-RemotelyControlled "The collection of #$TransportationDevices that operate under the control of a driver (see #$driverActor) who is not in or on the device.  Examples include drone aircraft operated by remote control and remotely controlled vehicles that perform dangerous tasks or visit dangerous places (e.g., deep water explorers).  Note that not every instance of #$TransportationDevice-RemotelyControlled is also an instance of #$TransportationDevice-Unmanned, as there exist passenger vehicles that can be controlled remotely - for example, some trains that carry people between buildings at airports.")
(comment expectedDenotationTypeOfArg "(#$expectedDenotationTypeOfArg FN ARGN TYPE) means that the input to the ARGNth argument of the #$CodingFunction FN is expected to be some value (string or pointer) that denotes an instance of TYPE.")
(comment functionSafeChecksForCodeVariableType "(#$functionSafeChecksForCodeVariableType FN VAR-TYPE) means that FN performs a series of standard well-formedness checks on its output when this output conforms to the standard syntactic data format given by the #$CodeVariableType VAR-TYPE.")
(comment functionSafeChecksForSemanticDataType "(#$functionSafeChecksForSemanticDataType FN TYPE) means that the #$CodingFunction FN safe-checks its output in cases where the semantic interpretation of the output maps it to an instance of the #$Collection TYPE.")
(comment functionSafeChecksForStringType "(#$functionSafeChecksForStringType FN STRING-TYPE) means that the #$CodingFunction FN safe-checks its output where this output consists in (has a standard interpretation as) a character string of type STRING-TYPE.")
(comment functionSafeChecksForValuesDenoting "(#$functionSafeChecksForValuesDenoting FN COL) means that it is reasonably certain that when a term denoting an instance of COL is returned as a value by FN, that input has been checked for 'unsafe' typographic characters.")
(comment movementCoordinatedWith "<code>(#$movementCoordinatedWith MOVEMENT EVENT-OR-SEQUENCE)</code> means that the instance of #$MovementEvent <code>MOVEMENT</code> is comprised of subEvents whose timing (and perhaps duration, trajectory and path) are coordinated with discernible events that comprise <code>EVENT-OR-SEQUENCE)</code> an instance of #$Event or #$EventSeries.")
(comment theBeat "<code>(#$theBeat MUSIC BEAT)</code> identifies <code>BEAT</code> as the instance of #$AudibleBeat that is the entire beat of <code>MUSIC</code>, an instance of #$Music.")
(comment AudibleBeat "The collection of all instances of #$AudibleSoundSequence that are discernable as forming a rhythmic beat.")
(comment AudibleSoundOrSoundSequence "The collection of audible sounds and discernible sequences of audible sounds.")
(comment PeriodicEventSeries-HumanScale "The collection of instances of #$PeriodicEventSeries that are discernible by humans under ordinary circumstances.  Positive examples include the rhythmic tapping of a pencil on a desk and the rising and setting of the sun each day.  Negative examples include the periodic passing of haley's comet through our region of space and the sequence of base-matching steps that go into replicating DNA.")
(comment TankerTruck "The collection of all tanker trucks. A type of #$Truck and #$MaterialTransporter designed to carry relatively large quantities (thousands of gallons) of some liquid, such as water, milk, or petroleum products. #$TankerTruck is a #$RoadVehicleTypeByBodyStyle, a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType, a #$VehicleTypeByIntendedUse, and a #$RoadVehicleTypeByUse.")
(comment MusicTypeByArtist "A collection that facets #$Music into sub-collections based on the artist.  \"based on the artist\" is defined broadly here, so as to include: a) performers of the music (including live performances as well as music played from a recording of a performance), so that the music generated from a recording of Jimi Hendrix playing \"All Along the Watchtower\" counts as the music of Jimi Hendrix in the relevant sense; b) authors of the work that the music instantiates, so that the same music in the example above would also count as the music of Bob Dylan; and, in some contexts, c) the music closely associated with an artist, so that, for example, a Jimi Hendrix tribute band's performance of \"All Along the Watchtower\" counts, not only as Bob Dylan's music (due to the criterion in b)), but as Jimi Hendrix music, due to his having made the song into a hit.")
(comment MusicOfFn "<code>(#$MusicOfFn ARTIST)</code> denotes all the music of <code>ARITST</code>, in the most general sense in which an instance of #$Music might be \"of\" an artist.  For a more thorough description, see #$MusicTypeByArtist.")
(comment musicOf "The predicate that corresponds to #$MusicOfFn, <code>(#$musicOf MUSIC-TYPE ARTIST)</code> identifies the instance <code>MUSIC-TYPE</code> of #$MusicTypeByArtist as the collection of all the music of <code>ARITST</code>, in the most general sense in which an instance of #$Music might be \"of\" an artist.  For a more thorough description, see #$MusicTypeByArtist.")
(comment termInOperationalHistoryOfParameter "(#$termInOperationalHistoryOfParameter TERM FN-CALL ARG-NUM) means that, in the program in which the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL appears, TERM appears somewhere in the operational history that generates whatever value is supplied in the program to the ARG-NUMth parameter of the function called in FN-CALL.")
(comment functionInOperationalHistoryOfParameter "(#$functionInOperationalHistoryOfParameter FN FN-CALL ARG-NUM) means that, in the program in which the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL appears, the #$CodingFunction FN is called somewhere in the operational history that generates whatever value is supplied in the program to the ARG-NUMth parameter of the function called in FN-CALL.")
(comment expressionInOperationalHistoryOfParameter "(#$expressionInOperationalHistoryOfParameter EXPRESSION FN-CALL ARG-NUM) means that, in the program in which the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable FN-CALL appears, the #$ComputerCodeExpression EXPRESSION is referenced somewhere in the operational history that generates whatever value is supplied in the program to the ARG-NUMth parameter of the function called in FN-CALL.")
(comment typeAbsentFromOperationalHistoryOfParameter "(#$typeAbsentFromOperationalHistoryOfParameter TYPE INSTR ARG-NUM) means that, in the program where the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable INSTR appears, no #$AbstractIndividual of the type TYPE is referenced in the operational history that generates the value supplied to the ARG-NUMth parameter of the #$CodingFunction called by INSTR.")
(comment URIParsingSafeCheckFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions that are used to safe-check instances of #$UniformResourceIdentifier for typographically problematic or dangerous substrings.")
(comment Standing "The collection of events in which the #$bodilyDoer is an animal that is supporting its own weight by standing on at least one extended leg. To count as standing, the event must be a continuous standing, and not a translocation via ambulation, nor an event in which one remains in place but moves ones legs so as to temporarily remove support (such as hopping up and down and jogging in place).  A borderline case of standing would be a gradual replacement of one leg (or set of legs) in the supporting role with another leg (or set of legs), while support is constantly maintained and while remaining in place.  One can still be standing with assistance, (such as using a cane or holding a rail), so long as the assistance does not entirely replace the support provided by the legs.  To represent a non-supporting \"standing,\" such as an astronaut in zero-gravity who appears to be standing, use the more general (#$InPositionFn #$UprightPosture).  To represent a motionless standing, use the more specific #$StandingStill.")
(comment SittingStill "The collection of events in which an animal holds still while sitting.")
(comment HoldingStill "The collection of instances of #$Posture-Configuration in which the #$bodilyDoer willfully maintains his or her posture without additional external body movement for some non-trivial #$duration of time.")
(comment BeingStill "The collection of instances of #$Posture-Configuration in which the doer (see #$doneBy) remains in a posture without additional external body movement for some non-trivial #$duration of time.  If this is done intentionally, the event counts as an instance of #$HoldingStill.")
(comment prescriptionTakeAsNeededForSymptomType "(#$prescriptionTakeAsNeededForSymptomType SCRIP SYMPTOM-TYPE) states that the #$DrugPrescription-Specification, SCRIP, instructs the patient to take a dose of the specified drug when the patient is troubled by instances of SYMPTOM-TYPE. The effect of this instruction is to remove the necessity that the patient take each dose on schedule, up to and including finishing all doses, in order for their treatment to conform to the prescription.  This instruction is usually accompanied by a dosage limit (#$prescriptionDosageRateNotToExceed).")
(comment medicalProductPurchased "(#$medicalProductPurchased FILL MED-PROD) means that in the #$FillingAPrescription event FILL, MED-PROD was purchased.  MED-PROD is an instance of some PharmacyFormalProductType, and may be a bottle of pills, a spray bottle containing some number of metered doses, a splint for immobilizing some body part, ")
(comment PharmaceuticalSalesItem "Instances of #$PharmaceuticalSalesItem are objects that can be available for sale at a #$Pharmacy or by a #$MedicalCareInstitution, and contain one or more doses of a #$DrugSubstance.  These include bottles of #$Pills, packages of #$TransdermalPatches, single-dose ampules of some #$InjectableLiquid-Medical, etc.  Note that this collection is not a spec of #$DrugSubstance.   Also note that, while a significant portion of an instance might be some naturally-occuring substance that can't be considered to be an artifact, the instance itself, by virtue of being created (assembled, packaged) by an agent, is an instance of #$Artifact-Generic.")
(comment potentialRolePlayerTypeInScriptType "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for querying for all the roles that instances of a given actortype can play in instances of a certain script type.")
(comment ComputationalResourceManagementFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunction instances concerned with the sequestration, release, and apportionment of computational resources, including, but not limited to, memory.")
(comment ComputationalResourceAllocationFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunction instances that are specifically concerned with the sequestration of computational resources without concerning deallocation or release of resources.")
(comment ComputationalResourceDeallocationFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunction instances that are specifically concerned with the release (deallocation) of computational resources, without concerning allocation of resources.")
(comment ComputationalResourceAllocationAndDeallocationFunction "The collection of all #$CodingFunctions which both allocate and deallocate computational resources such as memeory.")
(comment complementaryResourceManagementFunctions "#$complementaryResourceManagementFunctions is the predicate which holds, by definition, between any two distinct  #$ComputationalResourceManagementFunctions if and only if one is a #$ComputationalResourceAllocationFunction and the other is a  #$ComputationalResourceDeallocationFunction.")
(comment incompatibleResourceManagementFunctions "(#$incompatibleResourceManagementFunctions FN-1 FN-2) means that (#$complementaryResourceManagementFunctions FN-1 FN-2), but that the member of the pair devoted to resource deallocation should not be used to free resources sequestered by the member of the pair devoted to resource allocation, for reasons pertaining to computational security.")
(comment compatibleResourceManagementFunctions "#$compatibleResourceManagementFunctions FN-1 FN-2 means that (#$complementaryResourceManagementFunctions FN-1 FN-2) and that the member of the pair devoted to resource deallocation can be safely used to free resources sequestered by the member of the pair devoted to resource allocation.")
(comment functionSafeChecksFunctionForTypeReferenced "(#$functionSafeChecksFunctionForTypeReferenced CHECK-FN CHECKED-FN TYPE) means that CHECK-FN can be used in programmatic control flow to safe-check values that are interpreted as instances of TYPE as referenced by handle or pointer arguments in the inputs to CHECKED-FN, so that CHECKED-FN may safely be used with these arguments.")
(comment functionSafeChecksFunctionForTypeReferencedInArg "(#$functionSafeChecksFunctionForTypeReferencedInArg CHECK-FN CHECKED-FN ARG-NUM TYPE) means that CHECK-FN can be used in programmatic control flow to safe-check values that are interpreted as instances of TYPE as referenced by a handle or pointer argument in the ARG-NUMth argument position of CHECKED-FN, so that CHECKED-FN may safely be used with such an argument.")
(comment Couple-Romantic "The collection of pairs of people that are in a romantic relationship with one another.")
(comment MarriedCouple "The collection of all pairs of people who are married to each other. A type of #$Couple-Romantic.")
(comment Couple-SameSex "The collection of all instances of #$Couple-Romantic where both #$groupMembers are of the same sex.")
(comment VintageFn "#$VintageFn is a variable-arity subcollection-denoting function that takes a type of #$DurableGood and returns a subcollection of that good whose instances are all characteristic of the best of that type of good from some historical period during which those instances were produced.  The addition of a second #$TimeInterval argument, say the 1920's, will further refine the specialization of that type of good, by indicating an aforementioned historical period.  For example, <code>(#$VintageFn #$CoffeeTable-PieceOfFurniture)</code> denotes the collection of vintage coffee tables, and <code>(#$VintageFn #$CoffeeTable-PieceOfFurniture (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn (#$YearFn 1920) (#$YearFn 1929)))</code> denotes the collection of vintage 1920-1929 coffee tables.  The latter collection is a specialization of the former.")
(comment VintageArtifact "The collection of vintage artifacts, instances of #$DurableGood that were manufactured during some time period earlier than that of the given context, and are characteristic of the best of that time period. For example, vintage clothing is clothing from a particular time period, say the 1920's")
(comment vintageSpecs "A variable-arity predicate, and the predicate that corresponds to the function #$VintageFn.  <code>(#$vintageSpecs X VINTAGE-X)</code> identifies <code>VINTAGE-X</code> as the collection of all vintage instances of <code>X</code>.  <code>(#$vintageSpecs X VINTAGE-X-BY-PERIOD PERIOD)</code> identifies <code>VINTAGE-X-BY-PERIOD</code> as the collection of all instances of <code>X</code> that are vintage instances of <code>X</code> produced in the period <code>PERIOD</code>, an instance of #$TimeInterval.  As such, <code>VINTAGE-X-BY-PERIOD</code> is a specialization of <code>VINTAGE-X</code>.")
(comment arityOfFunctionCalled "Where FN-CALL is a #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable, (#$arityOfFunctionCalled FN-CALL ARITY) means that the #$arity of the #$CodingFunction called by FN-CALL is ARITY.")
(comment functionAbsentFromOperationalHistoryOfParameter "(#$functionAbsentFromOperationalHistoryOfParameter FN INSTR ARGN) means that ARGN is a positive integer less than or equal to the arity of the function called by INSTR (see #$arityOfFunctionCalled) and there is no operational history associated with that parameter of INSTR that involves a call to FN.")
(comment extentPermutations "<code>(#$extentPermutations SET LIST)</code> 
maps between an extensional set and extensional lists that are
permutations of its elements in either direction.")
(comment ShapingSubtractively "A collection of #$PurposefulActions; a subcollection of #$ShapingSomething. In each #$ShapingSubtractively, an agent intentionally forms some piece of solid material into a different shape by removing one or more #$physicalPortions of the #$objectActedOn.  The intended product may be a new kind of thing (as when, during sewing, one cuts out a sleeve piece from a piece of fabric), or it may merely be shorter (as when one cuts off the bottom of a flower stem when arranging a bouquet) or smoother (as when one sands a piece of furniture) than the original.  In all cases the final product will be less massive than, but made out of the same material as, the original.")
(comment CuttingInPieces "The collection of all cutting events [#$CuttingSomething] which are composed of repeated cuttings in which there is a complete separation [#$Separation-Complete].  As a result, several (or many more) distinct connected objects are created.  The pieces may be of similar or vastly dissimilar size.  For example, instances of #$DrillingSomething and #$SawingSomething have important subevents which are instances of #$CuttingInPieces, since small pieces (e.g. sawdust) are removed from the larger piece.")
(comment HandTool "A specialization of both #$Tool and #$PortableObject.  Each instance of #$HandTool is a portable tool which is hand-held, hand-supported and hand-guided throughout its operation.  Typically the work piece (the object being acted on when the tool is used) remains stationary.  Members of this collection can be contrasted with #$StationaryTools, which remain in a fixed location while the work piece is moved (although in some cases the tool has moving parts that are operated by hand, e.g. a #$Chopsaw.  Specializations of #$HandTool include the collections #$Screwdriver, #$ManualDrill, and #$BlowDryer.")
(disjointWith HandTool StationaryTool)
(comment HorseShaped "#$HorseShaped is the instance of #$AnimalBodyShapeType defined by the typical shape of a horse.")
(comment GroupActivityFn "<code>(#$GroupActivityFn SINGLE-DOER-ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$GroupActivity characterized by the individual participants doing instances of <code>SINGLE-DOER-ACTIVITY</code>, a specialization of #$SingleDoerAction.  For example, <code>(#$GroupActivityFn #$Singing-SingleDoerAction)</code> is the collection of group singing events.")
(comment groupActivityTypeOfType "The predicate that corresponds to #$GroupActivityFn, <code>(#$groupActivityTypeOfType SINGLE-DOER-ACTIVITY-TYPE GROUP-ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>GROUP-ACTIVITY-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$GroupActivity characterized by the individual participants doing instances of <code>SINGLE-DOER-ACTIVITY</code>, a specialization of #$SingleDoerAction.")
(comment essentialPartTypes "<code>(#$essentialPartTypes WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that <code>PART-TYPE</code> is an essential type of part for every instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> -- i.e., there can be no instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> such that it lacks an instance of <code>PART-TYPE</code> as a part; accordingly, an event that removes all instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> from an instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> would destroy that instance.")
(comment essentialProperParts "The intersection of #$essentialParts and #$properParts.")
(comment essentialParts "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$parts, #$essentialParts relates an object to those parts of it that are essential to its existence.  Specifically, the removal of an essential part will be or cause an instance of #$DestructionEvent in which the original object plays the role of #$inputsDestroyed.")
(comment characteristicEssentialSubEventTypes "<code>(#$characteristicEssentialSubEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUB-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by and require the occurrence of sub-events of type <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment characteristicEssentialProperSubEventTypes "<code>(#$characteristicEssentialProperSubEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUB-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by and require the occurrence of proper sub-events of type <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment characteristicProperSubEventTypes "A specialization of #$properSubEventTypes, <code>(#$characteristicProperSubEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUB-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by sub-events of type <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code>.  That is, a common-sense characterization or description of an event of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> would (as a default) involve mentioning its <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code> sub-events.  For example, while both of the following sentences are true,<p><code>(#$properSubEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Swallowing)</code></p> <p><code>(#$properSubEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Event-Localized)</code></p>
only #$Swallowing is such that it is characteristic of #$EatingEvent in the relevant sense, and so can be strengthened to
<p><code>(#$characteristicProperSubEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Swallowing)</code>.</p>")
(comment characteristicSubEventTypes "A specialization of #$subEventTypes, <code>(#$characteristicSubEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUB-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by sub-events of type <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code>.  That is, a common-sense characterization or description of an event of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> would (as a default) involve mentioning its <code>SUB-EVT-TYPE</code> sub-events.  For example, while the following three sentences are all true,<p>
<code>(#$subEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$EatingEvent)</code></p> <p><code>(#$subEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Swallowing)</code></p> <p><code>(#$subEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Event-Localized)</code></p>
only #$Swallowing is such that it is characteristic of #$EatingEvent in the relevant sense, and so can be strengthened to
<p><code>(#$characteristicSubEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Swallowing)</code>.</p> Indeed, since <code>(#$properSubEventTypes #$EatingEvent #$Swallowing)</code> holds, this can be further strengthened, using #$characteristicProperSubEventTypes.")
(comment DrillPress "A type of #$Drill and #$StationaryTool.  Instances of #$DrillPress typically have a platform on which the work piece is placed, and a mechanism that allows an operator (or perhaps a computer program) to move a rotating #$DrillBit in a straight line perpendicular to the platform in order to bore a hole in the work piece.")
(comment StationaryTool "A specialization of #$Tool.  Each instance of #$StationaryTool is a #$Tool which is more or less stationary during its use.  Unlike #$HandTools, a #$StationaryTool is not supported by the hand and moved by hand to alter a stationary workpiece.  Instead, the tool (which likely has moving parts, and may be controlled to some extent by the hand of the user, and may also be portable), remains mostly in one place and the work piece is moved.")
(comment activityTypeHasProjectType "<code>(#$activityTypeHasProjectType ACTIVITY-TYPE PROJECT-TYPE)</code> states that <code>PROJECT-TYPE</code> is the collection of actions in which a complete project composed primarily of subevents which are instances of <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code> is finished.")
(comment Woodworking "A specialization of #$CraftActivity and an instance of #$SkilledActivityType.  Instances are activities in which portions of #$Wood are shaped, or assembled, or otherwise manipulated in the course of making some #$Artifact.  Instances of #$Woodworking need not have an output which is a completed artifact.  For the collection of events which have wooden artifacts as their intended output, see (#$ProjectTypeFn #$Woodworking).")
(comment ProjectTypeFn "<code>(#$ProjectTypeFn ACTIVITY-TYPE)</code> denotes a class of actions, each instance of which is a complete project composed primarily of subevents which are instances of <code>ACTIVITY-TYPE</code>.  For example, (#$ProjectTypeFn #$Sewing) is the class of actions in which a whole sewing project is finished.  Instances of #$Sewing might merely be steps in some larger #$MakingSomething event, and have no finished product as their #$outputsCreated.  Instances of (#$ProjectTypeFn #$Sewing), however, typically have an (intended) output which is a completed garment, a finished surgical suture, a completed quilt, or some other final artifact created mostly by sewing.")
(comment Woodcarving "The collection of events in which a piece of #$Wood is shaped by #$Carving.")
(comment Chisel "The collection of all chisels, #$HandTools used to remove material from a piece of material which is often made of #$Wood or #$StoneStuff, but sometimes made of #$Plastic or even #$Metal.")
(comment WoodworkingChisel "The collection of all #$Chisels designed to cut #$Wood, but also suitable for shaping materials of similar or lesser hardness, such as many types of #$Plastic.")
(comment SawingSomething "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$ShapingSomething.  Each instance of #$SawingSomething is an event in which an agent cuts at least partially through some hard object by making a more-or-less continuous series of small cuts.  The #$CuttingDevice used in an instance of #$SawingSomething is often a saw (e.g. a #$HandSaw or #$PowerSaw), but it need not be; for example, one might saw through a tree branch with a #$Knife. Often the material being cut is #$Wood, but other materials can be cut this way, e.g., #$Plastic.")
(disjointWith DrillingSomething JointingSomething)
(disjointWith SlicingSomething JointingSomething)
(disjointWith ChoppingSomething JointingSomething)
(disjointWith StabbingSomething JointingSomething)
(disjointWith Piercing JointingSomething)
(comment JointingSomething "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$ShapingSomething.  Often, the #$objectActedOn is an instance of #$Board-PieceOfWood.  Each instance of #$JointingSomething is an event in which an agent smooths a narrow edge or a face of a (probably #$Beam shaped) piece of material, making it into a flat plane.   In #$Woodworking, for example, #$JointingSomething is performed in the course of turning a rough piece of lumber into a board that more closely approaches the shape of a #$RectangularParallelepiped.  A tool commonly used to perform #$JointingSomething is a #$Jointer.")
(comment ThreeDimensionalShapeType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$GeometricShapeType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType is a specialization of #$ThreeDimensionalGeometricThing (q.v.) all of whose own instances have something in common as regards their shape.  Instances include the collections #$Cylinder and #$Cube.  Cf. #$TwoDimensionalShapeType.")
(comment ThicknessPlaner "The collection of all thickness planers. A type of #$Tool-PowerTool and #$WoodworkingTool. The concept #$ThicknessPlaner is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment TruingAPieceOfLumber "The collection of events in which a #$Board-PieceOfWood is shaped to make opposite faces parallel and planar, and to make adjacent faces (except not necessarily the end faces) perpendicular.")
(comment JointingABoardFace "An instance of #$SkilledActivityType and a specialization of #$JointingSomething.  Each instance of #$JointingABoardFace is an event in which an agent smooths one face of a #$Board-PieceOfWood, making it into a flat plane.  This corrects shape defects typical of rough lumber (see #$RoughSawnBoard) such as cupping, bowing and twisting.")
(comment PlaningABoard "An instance of #$SkilledActivityType and a specialization of #$Woodworking.  Each instance of #$PlaningABoard is an event in which an agent runs a #$Board-PieceOfWood through a #$ThicknessPlaner.  This has the effect of making the affected surface of the board (usually the top surface) equidistant to its opposite surface at all points affected by the cutting knives of the planer.  If the opposite surface was a planar surface, the two surfaces will be parallel after this operation if the entire extent of the affected face was cut. ")
(comment RippingABoard "Instances are events in which an agent cuts a #$Board-PieceOfWood lengthwise and parallel to the grain of the wood. #$TableSaws are among the tools best suited to make this kind of cut.")
(comment JointingABoardFacePerpendicularToAdjacentFace "Instances are events in which an agent smooths one face of a board to create a face that is perpendicular to the adjacent face of that board.  If the adjacent face was planar, the resulting new face will also be planar.  A #$Jointer is one of the best tools to use in this kind of shaping event.")
(comment MiterSaw "A type of #$Saw.  Instances of #$MiterSaw are designed for crosscutting linear pieces of material, such as boards (see #$Board-PieceOfWood) or small-gauge metal rod or bar at precise angles.  For wood, there exist both manual and powered miter saws.  Metal-cutting miter saws are almost always electric.  All miter saws have a cutting table with a fence, which is a vertical surface against which the work piece can be placed to keep it in a fixed position while it is cut.  This table can be rotated to adjust the angle of the cut.")
(comment PoweredMiterSaw-CarpentryTool "A type of #$MiterSaw.  Instances of #$PoweredMiterSaw-CarpentryTool are designed for crosscutting pieces of wood (see #$Board-PieceOfWood) or linear materials of similar density.  Each has a rotating cutting table with a fence.  Each has an arm on which the cutting blade is mounted.  The operator lowers this arm, bringing the blade through the work piece to cut it.  In the simplest type, only the angle of the rotating table can be adjusted, and the blade is always perpendicular to the cutting table.  In a compound miter saw, the arm/blade can be tilted too, allowing cuts to be made that are angled in two axes.")
(comment WoodCuttingCircularSawBlade "The collection of blades for many types of #$PowerSaws.   Each is relatively flat, circular in shape, and with teeth all around the edge.  A hole at the center allows the blade to be mounted on the arbor of the saw, which transmits the spinning force from the motor to the blade when the saw is turned on. ")
(comment CircularSaw "A type of #$Saw.  Instances of #$CircularSaw are hand-held, hand-guided and hand-supported powered saws designed for cutting wood, but they can also be used to cut plastic, fiber-cement planks or sheet, and other materials with the substitution of an appropriate blade.  In use, instances of #$CircularSaw are held in one hand and moved to pass the spinning blade through the material to be cut.  Usually the work piece is immobilized.  When cutting sheets of material, often a straight edge is affixed to the material with clamps to provide a fence so the cut can be made straight. ")
(comment CircularSawBlade "The collection of blades for many types of #$PowerSaws.   Each is relatively flat and circular in shape.  A hole at the center allows the blade to be mounted on the arbor of the saw, which transmits the spinning force from the motor to the blade when the saw is turned on.  When optimized for cutting wood or plastic, blades will be made of #$Steel and have teeth all around the perimeter.  Blades optimized for cutting metal may be made of an abrasive composite material that is gradually worn away as the blade is used.  Blades optimized for cutting masonry may be made of steel, but have an abrasive coating at the cutting edge.  Many configurations of rotary blades exist. ")
(disjointWith MiterSaw CircularSaw)
(disjointWith TableSaw MiterSaw)
(disjointWith TableSaw CircularSaw)
(comment CrosscuttingABoard "Instances are events in which an agent cuts a #$Board-PieceOfWood crosswise and perpendicular to the grain of the wood.")
(comment Backsaw "A type of #$HandSaw.  The teeth of a #$Backsaw are angled back toward the handle of the saw, so that the saw cuts on the pull stroke.  The blades of #$Backsaws are typically thinner and stiffer than blades of other #$HandSaws, because the tension created when pulling on the blade keeps it straight and unbent.  Backsaws may have a stiffening spine of thicker metal opposite the cutting edge, but not all do; some have cutting teeth on both edges.")
(disjointWith TableSaw Bandsaw)
(disjointWith Bandsaw MiterSaw)
(comment Bandsaw "A type of #$Saw.  Instances of #$Bandsaw have a blade which is a continuous loop of thin metal with teeth along one narrow edge.  The thickness of the blade, its width, and the configuration of the teeth can be adjusted to optimize it for cutting various materials.  Various configurations exist.  Large metal-cutting bandsaws often keep the work piece stationary, and automatically lower the moving blade through the metal to cut it, while the area of the cut is bathed in coolant.  Smaller wood-cutting and meat-cutting bandsaws often have a horizontal cutting table and a vertically-oriented blade that is pulled down through an opening in the table by wheels above and below the table.  The operator manually moves the work piece past the blade.   Large bandsaws in sawmills may have the blade at various orientations, and often automatically move the timber to be cut through the blade, either via gravity or with an active feed system. ")
(comment BandsawBlade "The collection of blades for #$Bandsaws.   Each is a continuous loop formed from a strip of steel which is much thinner than it is wide, with cutting teeth along one narrow edge.  Blades can be optimized for cutting wood, metal or meat.  Small bandsaws may use a blade that has a perimeter of a few feet; large ones may need blades with a perimeter of several yards.")
(disjointWith ChainSaw Bandsaw)
(disjointWith ChainSaw TableSaw)
(disjointWith ChainSaw CircularSaw)
(disjointWith ChainSaw MiterSaw)
(disjointWith Bandsaw CircularSaw)
(comment GrilledCheeseSandwich "A specialization of #$CheeseSandwich.  Each instance of #$GrilledCheeseSandwich is a cheese sandwich that is fried or toasted.")
(comment sandwichTypeDefiningFillingTypes "(#$sandwichTypeDefiningFillingTypes SANDWICH-TYPE FILLINGS) means that SANDWICH-TYPE is the collection of all and only those #$Sandwiches whose fillings (see #$sandwichFillings) include all elements of FILLINGS.")
(comment ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn "(#$ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn ARTIFACT-TYPE STUFF-TYPE) specifies the collection of all instances of ARTIFACT-TYPE fashioned out of some portion of STUFF-TYPE, such that that portion is a #$mainConstituents of the artifact instance.   Thus (#$ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn #$Pants #$SilkCloth) would be the collection of all silk pants. ")
(comment artifactTypeMadeMainlyOfType "<code>(#$artifactTypeMadeMainlyOfType ARTIFACT-TYPE STUFF-TYPE ARTIFACT-SUBTYPE)</code> means that <code>ARTIFACT-SUBTYPE</code> is the collection of all instances <code>INSTANCE</code> of <code>ARTIFACT-TYPE</code> which are composed chiefly (see #$mainConstituents) of some portion of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code>. See the function that corresponds to this predicate, #$ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn.")
(comment DenimJacket "The collection of jackets made primarily of #$DenimCloth.")
(comment FoilSheet "The collection of all #$FreeSheets (unattached along their surfaces) which are made of extremely thin, flexible pieces of #$Metal. Exemplars include #$AluminumFoil and gold leaf.")
(comment Jointer "The collection of all jointers, also called edge jointers. A type of #$Tool-PowerTool and #$WoodworkingTool.  #$Jointers have a rotating cutter head and flat infeed and outfeed surfaces, and are designed so that when a piece of #$Wood is moved from the infeed surface over the cutting head to the outfeed surface, material is removed causing the affected face of the piece to become more like a flat plane with each pass through the tool.")
(comment PlaningABoard "An instance of #$SkilledActivityType and a specialization of #$Woodworking.  Each instance of #$PlaningABoard is an event in which an agent flattens one surface of a board.  This can be accomplished by running a #$Board-PieceOfWood through a #$ThicknessPlaner.  This will make the affected surface equidistant to its opposite surface at all points affected by the cutting knives of the planer.  If the opposite surface was a truly planar surface, the two surfaces will be parallel after this operation if the entire extent of the affected face was cut.")
(disjointWith TableSaw Lathe)
(disjointWith ChainSaw Lathe)
(disjointWith Lathe MiterSaw)
(disjointWith Lathe CircularSaw)
(comment Lathe "A type of #$StationaryTool used for #$ShapingSubtractively in a manner that is symmetric about an axis of rotation.  Instances of #$Lathe allow the workpiece to be mounted and spun at relatively high speed, while a cutting tool removes material from it.  Wood cutting lathes (see #$WoodLathe) usually have a tool rest so an operator can more easily control hand-held cutting tools, and may have either one or two points at which the workpiece may be fixed.  Metalworking lathes usually provide a way to mount hardened cutting tools, which are operated either by handwheels or by computer.")
(comment WoodLathe "A type of #$StationaryTool used for shaping pieces of #$Wood subtractively in a manner that is symmetric about an axis of rotation.  Instances of #$WoodLathe allow the workpiece to be mounted and spun at relatively high speed, while a (typically) hand-held cutting tool is controlled by an operator to remove material from the workpiece.  Wood cutting lathes usually have a tool rest to make it easier to control hand-held cutting tools.  ")
(comment Woodturning "Instances of #$Woodturning are events in which an agent shapes a piece of wood by holding a cutting tool against its surface as it spins in a #$WoodLathe.")
(comment SandingSomething "Using #$Sandpaper or a #$PowerSander to smooth the surface of an object, or to remove paint or other substances from the object's surface.")
(comment BeltSander "Instances of #$BeltSander are power tools which may be stationary or hand-held, and which have an abrasive belt which moves on two or more powered rollers.  Either the workpiece is brought against this abrasive belt, or the tool is moved across the surface of the workpiece, to remove material and smooth the surface.")
(comment HandheldBeltSander "Instances of #$HandheldBeltSander are handheld #$BeltSanders typically used to shape or smooth #$Wood.  ")
(comment candidateUnsafecheckedReturnInputTo "(#$candidateUnsafecheckedReturnInputTo OUTPUT-CALL INPUT-CALL) means that there is some positive evidence that the value returned by OUTPUT-CALL is not safe-checked in the operational history of INPUT-CALL in a way that it could/should be.")
(comment termHasValueAsInputTo-SomeExecutions "(#$termHasValueAsInputTo-SomeExecutions TERM INSTR VAL) means that the control flow of the program of which INSTR is a part allows the #$ComputerCodeExpression TERM to have the value VAL in at least one execution path.")
(comment inputMayBeUnsafechecked "(#$inputMayBeUnsafechecked TERM INSTRUCTION) means that there is some positive evidence that TERM is not safe-checked in the operational history of INSTRUCTION in a way that it could/should be")
(disjointWith TemperatureChangingProcess AssemblingPartsDuringMaking)
(disjointWith Stirring AssemblingPartsDuringMaking)
(comment AssemblingPartsDuringMaking "Instances are events in which the parts of a physical object are assembled together, intentionally by an agent, in the course of making the whole.  Note that the making event, an instance of #$MakingSomething, may also include other steps which are not assembly steps - for example, the fabrication of the parts to be assembled, or a finishing step such as painting.")
(comment Finish "Each #$Finish is a type of #$CoatingMaterial which may be applied to the surface of an object in order to protect it, decorate it, or otherwise improve its aesthetics and/or durability.  Specializations include #$RustproofingPaint and #$Varnish.")
(comment Varnish "Transparent liquid applied to wood and other materials in order to seal and protect it.  After application, #$Varnish will dry and harden.  Many types of varnish exist, including those made with polyurethane, epoxies, lacquer, acrylic polymers and more.")
(comment UnfinishedWoodenFurniture "This is the collection of instances of #$FurniturePiece which are made of wood and which are devoid of #$Finish.  Some stores sell furniture in this state for customers to purchase and complete by sanding and finishing; other instances of this collection are an intermediate step in the making of a completed piece of furniture. ")
(disjointWith (ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn FurniturePiece Wood) (ArtifactTypeMadeMainlyOfTypeFn FurniturePiece Metal))
(comment returnedExpressionOfTypeDenotesFailure "(#$returnedExpressionOfTypeDenotesFailure FN EXPRESSION-TYPE) means that when a function call to FN returns a value whose standard interpretation is as a #$ComputerCodeExpression of the type EXPRESSION-TYPE, it indicates the function call has not succeeded.")
(comment generateIsaRuleForSubcollectionInvolving "(#$generateIsaRuleForSubcollectionInvolving  PRED) means that when PRED occurs in arg2 of one of the four main ternary subcollection functions (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn), an expansion rule concluding to #$isa and that function term and the appropriate collection backchain required meta information should be asserted onto the subcollection.  Typically this is only asserted onto binary predicates that cannot be solved by removal only -- e.g. require SKSI or transformation.")
(comment MakingSomething "A collection of creation events -- a specialization of both #$CreatingAnArtifact and #$PhysicalCreationEvent (qq.v.).  Each instance of this collection involves some #$PartiallyTangible thing being made (by some #$Agent-PartiallyTangible) from raw materials or from parts. The end result (see #$productsCreated) might or might not be a #$Product or even a completed artifact (it could be an intermediate form, or a component of a completed artifact). Examples include baking a loaf of bread, assembling a high-fidelity audio component and fabricating a part for a chair. See also the more specialized #$Constructing.")
(comment workpieceOut "<code>(#$workpieceOut ACTION OBJECT)</code> means that the physical object <code>OBJECT</code> is that part of the thing being acted on that is the intended result of <code>ACTION</code>, an instance of #$CraftActivity or #$ShapingSomething.  If <code>ACTION</code> is one in which material is removed from the object acted on, that which is not the #$workpieceOut is #$scrap.  For example, when drilling a hole in a piece of #$Metal so that it can be bolted to something else, the resulting metal-with-a-hole is the #$workpieceOut and metal shavings produced are #$scrap.  When cutting a short board off a long board because the short one is needed, it is the #$workpieceOut and the remainder, which might be a useful piece of wood for some other purpose, is #$scrap.")
(comment scrap "<code>(#$scrap ACTION OBJECT)</code> means that the physical object <code>OBJECT</code> is one of the parts of the thing being acted on that is NOT the intended result of <code>ACTION</code>, an instance of #$CraftActivity or #$ShapingSomething.  If <code>ACTION</code> is one in which material is removed from the object acted on, that which is not the #$workpieceOut is #$scrap.  For example, when drilling a hole in a piece of #$Metal so that it can be bolted to something else, the resulting metal-with-a-hole is the #$workpieceOut and metal shavings produced are #$scrap.  They are also #$wasteProducts.  When cutting a short board off a long board because the short one is needed, it is the #$workpieceOut and the remainder, which might be a useful piece of wood for some other purpose, is #$scrap.")
(comment workpieceIn "<code>(#$workpieceIn ACTION OBJECT)</code> means that the physical object <code>OBJECT</code> is an intended input to <code>ACTION</code> (an instance of #$CraftActivity or #$ShapingSomething), and is the input that is transformed or destroyed to produce the intended result, the #$workpieceOut.  The matter that makes up the intended result of <code>ACTION</code> was part of <code>OBJECT</code> before <code>ACTION</code> occured.")
(comment JointingABroadFaceOfRoughLumber "Instances are events in which an agent smooths the first face of a #$RoughSawnBoard to make it planar.  This is the first step to #$TruingAPieceOfLumber.  A #$Jointer is one of the best tools to use in this kind of shaping event, and the broad face which is mostly concave (as opposed to a narrow edge, or a mostly convex face) is the best face to start with.")
(comment WoodturningTool "The collection of all #$HandTools designed to be used with a #$WoodLathe to shape #$Wood.  Example specializations include the roughing gouge, the skew chisel and the parting tool.  ")
(disjointWith Saw ClawHammer)
(comment ClawHammer "A hand tool used primarily for pounding (of nails) and also for prying.  Comprised of a handle and a heavy head with one blunt end for pounding; the other end of the head is forked and wedged for prying.")
(comment Hammer "A hand tool used for pounding and possibly for prying.  Comprised of a handle and a heavy head with one blunt end for pounding; the other end of the head may be different and designed for cutting, prying or applying some other type of force.")
(disjointWith Sledgehammer ClawHammer)
(comment Sledgehammer "A hand tool used for pounding, e.g., of stakes into the ground, or to break up rocks, or to flatten hot metal, or for many other uses where concentrated force is desired.  Composed of a handle and a heavy, symmetrical head with two blunt ends.")
(comment OrganophosphorusCompoundType "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType that have at least one carbon-phosphorus bond.")
(comment SingleCovalentBond "A specialization of #$CovalentBond in which a single electron is shared.")
(comment DoubleCovalentBond "A specialization of #$CovalentBond in which a two electrons are shared.")
(disjointWith DoubleCovalentBond SingleCovalentBond)
(disjointWith SnowSurfaceTransportation Jibbing)
(disjointWith RecreationalBoardRidingActivity-OnSnow Jibbing)
(comment Jibbing "A specialization of  
  (#$TransportViaFn #$Snowboard), this is the collection of events in which someone rides a snowboard on a non-snow-covered surface.")
(comment ExecutionOfManeuverFn "<code>(#$ExecutionOfManeuverFn MANEUVER)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of the instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalManeuver <code>MANEUVER</code>.")
(comment executionTypeOfManeuver "The predicate that corresponds to #$ExecutionOfManeuverFn, <code>(#$executionTypeOfManeuver EXECUTION-TYPE MANEUVER)</code> identifies <code>EXECUTION-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of an <code>MANEUVER</code>, an instance of #$SpecifiedPhysicalManeuver.")
(comment ExecutionOfStuntOnTransporterTypeFn "<code>(#$ExecutionOfStuntOnTransporterTypeFn MANEUVER TRANPORTER-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of an instance of the instance <code>MANEUVER</code> of #$TransporterStunt done on a transporter of type <code>TRANSPORTER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment executionTypeOfStuntOnTransporterType "The predicate corresonding to to #$ExecutionOfStuntOnTransporterTypeFn, <code>(#$executionTypeOfStuntOnTransporterType ACTION-TYPE MANEUVER TRANSPORTER-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction that are successful instantiations of the #$TransporterStunt <code>MANEUVER</code> performed on a transporter of type <code>TRANSPORTER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Ollie-BoardTrick "The ollie -- a board-riding trick used in skateboarding and snowboarding where the rider lifts the nose of the board and travels briefly through the air in a forward direction while maintaining contact with the board with his or her feet, without holding the board with his or her hands.")
(comment Nollie-BoardTrick "The nollie -- a board-riding trick based on the ollie, but where the rider lifts the rear of the board and travels backward through the air.")
(comment Sandboarding "A kind of #$RecreationalBoardRidingActivity where one rides a board along a sand dune.")
(comment Sandboard "A kind of #$SportBoard designed for use in #$Sandboarding.")
(comment PresentationOfTheBirthdayCake "A specialization of #$SocialRitual in which a birthday cake is officially presented to the #$eventHonors of a #$BirthdayParty event, often accompanied by the singing of #$HappyBirthdayToYou-TheSong.")
(comment Screwdriver "A hand tool used for driving screws and bolts, for UNscrewing, or for prying.  Comprised of a handle, a long shank, and a head specifically shaped to fit into cavities on the heads of screws and bolts so that rotary force may be transferred.")
(comment forceAppliedTo "<code>(#$forceAppliedTo APPLY OBJ)</code> states that in the #$ApplyingAForce event, <code>APPLY</code>, the force is applied to <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment RotaryDrivingImplement "A specialization of #$HandTool.  Instances of RotaryDrivingImplement are used to apply rotational force to fasteners like screws or to nuts on bolts.  This collection includes user-powered devices such as #$Screwdrivers and #$Wrenches, as well as electrically- or air-powered tools like impact drivers.")
(comment TurningWorkpieceOnLathe "A specialization of #$ApplyingATorque.  In each instance of #$TurningWorkpieceOnLathe, a piece of material (often #$Wood or #$Metal) is rotated while attached to one or both centers of a #$Lathe.  Such events are a necessary subevent of using a lathe for shaping the material.")
(comment CuttingOffPiecesToShapeSomething "Instances of this class are events in which small pieces of a rigid whole are repeatedly cut off.  The resulting workpiece (see #$workpieceOut) is thus smaller than the #$workpieceIn.  In such events, the whole is not completely chopped up.  The smaller, shaped object is the intended goal of the performer, and the pieces cut off are #$scrap.")
(comment RemovingWoodWithWoodturningTool "Instances of this class are events in which an agent uses a #$WoodturningTool to repeatedly remove small pieces of #$Wood from a wooden workpiece, as it rotates on a lathe.  Such events are an essential subevent of #$Woodturning. ")
(comment holdsInHand "<code>(#$holdsInHand AGENT OBJ)</code> states that the #$EmbodiedAgent, <code>AGENT</code>, and the #$PartiallyTangible, <code>OBJ</code>, are in physical contact and that furthermore force is applied by <code>AGENT</code> to restrain the motion of <code>OBJ</code>.  Additionaly, the part of <code>AGENT</code> in contact with <code>OBJ</code> is one or more of <code>AGENT</code>'s parts which is a #$HolderGripper - e.g., the #$Hand of a #$HomoSapiens or the #$Pincer of some insect.  This relation is agnostic as to which of potentially several appendages is applying the force, and what sort of motion is prevented. ")
(comment Screw-Connector "The collection of all connectors which  have threads that either bite into some base material to connect one or more objects to it, or which fit into a threaded nut to hold objects together between the nut and the head of the screw.  A type of #$ScrewShapedObject, #$RigidPortableObject, #$Connector, and #$Shaft. The collection #$Screw-Connector is an #$ArtifactTypeByGenericCategory and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(disjointWith Bolt WoodScrew)
(comment WoodScrew "The collection of all screws which are #$PointyEnded and have threads designed to bite into #$Wood. ")
(comment Wakeboarding "The collection of all wakeboarding events.
  wakeboarding is a lot like #$WaterSkiing, only one kneels on a board instead of standing on skis.  Keep in mind that not all instances of #$Wakeboarding
 are performances of #$Wakeboarding-CW, an organized sport, though certainly all performances of #$Wakeboarding-CW are instances of #$Wakeboarding.")
(comment wellHasShutInAtStartDateAccordingToFCVChange "<code>(#$wellHasShutInAtStartDateAccordingToFCVChange WELL CURRENT-DATE DATE)</code> means that values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> indicate <code>WELL</code> was shut-in on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasStartupAtStartDateAccordingToFCVChange "<code>(#$wellHasStartUpAtStartDateAccordingToFCVChange WELL CURRENT-DATE DATE)</code> means that values available at <code>CURRENT-DATE</code> indicate <code>WELL</code> resumed production on <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment rolePlayersInSitTypeStandInRelation "<code>(#$rolePlayersInSitTypeStandInRelation ROLE1 ROLE2 SIT-TYPE RELN)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE1 SIT ROLEPLAYER1)</code> and <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER2)</code>, then <code>(RELN ROLEPLAYER1 ROLEPLAYER2)</code> holds.  See also #$rolePlayersOfTypesInSitTypeStandInRelation.")
(comment rolePlayersOfTypesInSitTypeStandInRelation "<code>(#$rolePlayersOfTypesInSitTypeStandInRelation ROLE1 TYPE1 ROLE2 TYPE2 SIT-TYPE RELN)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE1 SIT ROLEPLAYER1)</code> and <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER2)</code>, if <code>ROLEPLAYER1</code> and <code>ROLEPLAYER2</code> are instances of <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code>, respectively, then <code>(RELN ROLEPLAYER1 ROLEPLAYER2)</code> holds.")
(comment rolePlayersInSitTypeDoNotStandInRelation "<code>(#$rolePlayersInSitTypeDoNotStandInRelation ROLE1 ROLE2 SIT-TYPE RELN)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE1 SIT ROLEPLAYER1)</code> and <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER2)</code>, then <code>(#$not (RELN ROLEPLAYER1 ROLEPLAYER2))</code> holds.")
(comment rolePlayersOfTypesInSitTypeDoNotStandInRelation "<code>(#$rolePlayersOfTypesInSitTypeDoNotStandInRelation ROLE1 TYPE1 ROLE2 TYPE2 SIT-TYPE RELN)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE1 SIT ROLEPLAYER1)</code> and <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER2)</code>, if <code>ROLEPLAYER1</code> and <code>ROLEPLAYER2</code> are instances of <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code>, respectively, then <code>(#$not (RELN ROLEPLAYER1 ROLEPLAYER2))</code> holds.")
(comment wellHasClosestShutInStartDateBeforeDate "<code>(#$wellHasClosestShutInStartDateBeforeDate WELL START-DATE DATE)</code> means that <code>START-DATE</code> is the most recent shut-in start date for <code>WELL</code> prior to <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasClosestObservedProductionDateBeforeDate "<code>(#$wellHasClosestObservedProductionDateBeforeDate WELL OBS-DATE DATE)</code> means that <code>OBS-DATE</code> is the most recent date <code>WELL</code> was observed to be in production prior to <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment wellHasClosestObservedShutInDateBeforeDate "<code>(#$wellHasClosestObservedShutInDateBeforeDate WELL OBS-DATE DATE)</code> means that <code>OBS-DATE</code> is the most recent date <code>WELL</code> was observed to be shut in prior to <code>DATE</code>.")
(comment returnFromHasValueAsInputTo-SomeExecutions "(#$returnFromHasValueAsInputTo-SomeExecutions FN-CALL INSTR VAL) means that the control flow of the program subsuming both FN-CALL and INSTR allows the term returned by FN-CALL to have the value VAL as an input determining the value of some operand position in the function call INSTR in at least one execution path.")
(comment DemonstrationTypeOfActivityTypeFn "<code>(#$DemonstrationTypeOfActivityTypeFn ACTIVITY)</code> denotes the collection of all demonstrations of <code>ACTIVITY</code>, a specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction.")
(comment demonstrationTypeOfActivityType "The predicate that corresponds to #$DemonstrationTypeOfActivityTypeFn, <code>(#$demonstrationTypeOfActivityType DEMONSTRATION ACTIVITY)</code> identifies <code>DEMONSTRATION</code> as the collection of all demonstrations of <code>ACTIVITY</code>, a specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction.")
(comment TechnologyDemonstration "The collection of all demonstrations of a piece of technology working.")
(comment activityTypeDemonstrated "<code>(#$activityTypeDemonstrated DEMONSTRATION ACTIVITY)</code> means that the specialization <code>ACTIVITY</code> of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction is the activity demonstrated in <code>DEMONSTRATION</code>, an instance of #$GivingADemonstration.")
(comment DemonstrationTypeOfTechnologyTypeFn "<code>(#$DemonstrationTypeOfTechnologyTypeFn TECHNOLOGY)</code> denotes the collection of all demonstrations of <code>TECHNOLOGY</code>, a specialization of #$Technology-Artifact.")
(comment demonstrationTypeOfTechnologyType "The predicate that corresponds to #$DemonstrationTypeOfTechnologyTypeFn, <code>(#$demonstrationTypeOfTechnologyType DEMONSTRATION TECHNOLOGY)</code> identifies <code>DEMONSTRATION</code> as the collection of all demonstrations of <code>TECHNOLOGY</code>, a specialization of #$Technology-Artifact.")
(comment technologyTypeDemonstrated "<code>(#$technologyTypeDemonstrated DEMONSTRATION TECHNOLOGY-TYPE)</code> means that the type of #$Technology-Artifact demonstrated in the instance <code>DEMONSTRATION</code> of #$TechnologyDemonstration is <code>TECHNOLOGY-TYPE</code>.")
(comment GivingADemonstration "The collection of all events in which one agent demonstrates a capability or technology to another.")
(comment characteristicSuperEventTypes "A specialization of #$superEventTypes, <code>(#$characteristicSuperEventTypes EVT-TYPE SUPER-EVT-TYPE)</code> means that events of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> are characterized by virtue of being sub-events of an overarching instance of <code>SUPER-EVT-TYPE</code>.  That is, a common-sense characterization or description of an event of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> would (as a default) involve mentioning its belonging to <code>SUPER-EVT-TYPE</code> sub-events.  For example, while both of the following sentences are true,<p><code>(#$superEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$Brewing)</code></p> <p><code>(#$superEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$IntelligentAgentActivity)</code></p> only #$Brewing is such that it is characteristic of #$ConditioningBeer in the relevant sense, and so <p><code>(#$characteristicSuperEventTypes #$ConditioningBeer #$Brewing)</code>.</p> holds.")
(disjointWith CodeAnalysisConstant-Extant CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseTwo)
(disjointWith CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseOne CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseTwo)
(comment CodeAnalysisConstant-NewInPhaseTwo "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created in part to support the #$CodeAnalysisProject in Phase Two.")
(comment allocationAddressSpecifyingArgumentPosition "(#$allocationAddressSpecifyingArgumentPosition ALLOC-FN N) means that the Nth argument position of the #$ComputationalResourceAllocationFunction ALLOC-FN takes a value that specifies the starting address of the resource to allocate.")
(comment PhysicalTemplate "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Instances of #$PhysicalTemplate are devices intended to serve as patterns or templates for the creation and/or shaping of other #$PartiallyTangibles. Examples specializations include #$SewingPattern and #$ShellForCasting.")
(comment SewingPattern "Instances of this collection are groups of outlines and other information, typically printed on tissue paper, that show the shape of the parts that can be cut out of sheet-like material, such as fabric, and assembled to make a completed textile artifact.  The user of the pattern lays out each pattern piece on the fabric to be used, affixing them with pins, and uses them as a guide to cut each piece out of the fabric with scissors. Additional information may be present on a pattern piece, such as fold lines, stitching lines, button locations, center line of the body, etc. ")
(comment instanceSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase "(#$instanceSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase COL) means that sentences of the for (#$isa TERM COL), for any closed term TERM, are trivial for justification paraphrase.")
(comment specSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase "(#$specSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase COL) means that sentences of the for (#$genls TERM COL), for any closed term TERM, are trivial for justification paraphrase.")
(comment instanceAndSpecSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase "(#$instanceAndSpecSentencesTrivialForJustificationParaphrase COL) means that sentences of the for (#$isa TERM COL) or (#$genls TERM COL), for any closed term TERM, are trivial for justification paraphrase.")
(comment termDeterminesValueOfInputToArgNumInCall "(#$termDeterminesValueOfInputToArgNumInCall TERM ARGN FN-CALL) means that TERM plays a role in determining the value that is supplied to the ARGNth argument of the function called in FN-CALL in the control flow of the program wherein FN-CALL appears.")
(disjointWith Person (CollectionDifferenceFn Thing Person))
(comment SewingPin "Instances of #$SewingPin are #$Pins which have a straight, thin, sharp and pointy #$Steel #$Shaft and a head made of #$Plastic, #$Glass, or #$Metal.  They are between one inch and 1.5 inches long.")
(comment SewingPatternPiece "Each instance of this collection is the outline, typically printed on tissue paper, of one type of part that can be cut out of sheet-like material, such as fabric, and assembled with other parts to make a completed textile artifact.  Given a particular pattern piece of a particular design, that piece may be used to cut several parts that will make up the whole.  For example, a collar piece may be used to cut the top surface of the collar, the bottom surface, and the interfacing.  Additional information may be present on a pattern piece, such as fold lines, stitching lines, button locations, center line of the body, etc. ")
(comment FusibleInterfacing "The collection of all #$Interfacing-Cloth which has a heat-activated adhesive on one side.  This type of interfacing is intended to be ironed onto the back side of a piece of fabric during the construction of a textile product.")
(comment Interfacing-Cloth "The collection of all cloth that is either a) intended to be used as interfacing, or b) is serving as interfacing.  Interfacing is used to stiffen parts of textile products, such as the collars and waistbands of garments. It is generally hidden, sandwiched between layers of the main fabric the item is made of.  Although often an interfacing piece is created from fabric intended to be used for that purpose, it is possible to use any stiff fabric as interfacing.")
(comment Lining-Cloth "The collection of all cloth that is either a) intended to be used as lining, or b) is serving as lining.  Lining is used to cover the inside surface of textile products, such as garments.  Although often a lining piece is created from fabric intended to be used for that purpose, it is possible to use almost any fabric or even non-fabrics sheets of material like leather or plastic as linings.")
(disjointWith Helmet Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Crown Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Earmuffs Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic PocketProtector)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic BootSpur)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic Condom)
(disjointWith SupportBrace-SomethingToWear Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic Holster)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic CastForBrokenBone)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic Splint)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic Saddle)
(disjointWith Backpack Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic EarPlug)
(disjointWith Wristwatch Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Stethoscope Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic ScubaDivingTank)
(comment Tassel "The collection of decorative bunches of dangling thread or yarn used to decorate clothing, pillows, furniture, window coverings, etc.")
(comment UnfinishedGarment "A specialization of #$Garment.  Each instance of #$UnfinishedGarment is a #$Garment in the process of being constructed.  Therefore, it may have physical parts that are not connected to the whole.")
(comment ClothingItemPart-SingleSheet "Instances of #$ClothingItemPart-SingleSheet are #$physicalParts of an instance of #$ClothingItem which consist of a single piece of fabric, leather or some other sheetlike material.  Examples include the interfacing of a collar, the left front panel of a pair of pants, and the right front lining of a jacket.  This collection is agnostic about whether its instances are connected parts of some #$ClothingItem or whether they are unconnected because the clothing is being made or being altered. ")
(comment LayingOutPiecesOnSheetMaterial "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$ArrangingObjects. In each #$LayingOutPiecesOnSheetMaterial, a performer decides how a set of pieces should be cut out of a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, and marks the location of each by drawing the outline, placing a template, or some other method.")
(comment LayingOutSewingPatternPieces "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$LayingOutPiecesOnSheetMaterial.  In each instance of #$LayingOutSewingPatternPieces, a performer places #$SewingPatternPieces on a piece of #$Cloth or Leather so that all pieces can be cut without interfering with others, and so that each piece is oriented correctly with the grain of the fabric (if fabric is used) and with any #$VisualPattern that may be present on the sheet goods.")
(comment AcrylicPlastic "A specialization of #$Thermoplastic.  Each instance of #$AcrylicPlastic is a polymer ")
(disjointWith AdministeringADrug PlacingSewingPatternPiece)
(comment IBTWithAudioElements "The collection of all instances of #$InformationBearingThing that have at least one instance of #$SoundInformationBearingThing as a part.")
(comment IBTWithVisualElements "The collection of all instances of #$InformationBearingThing that have at least one instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing as a part.")
(comment ibtContainsAudibleType "<code>(#$ibtContainsAudibleType IBT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>IBT</code> of #$IBTWithAudioElements contains the type of <code>#$AudibleSoundOrSoundSequence</code> <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ibtContainsAudibleType-Precise "<code>(#$ibtContainsAudibleType-Precise IBT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>IBT</code> of #$IBTWithAudioElements contains the type of <code>#$AudibleSoundOrSoundSequence</code> <code>TYPE</code>, where <code>TYPE</code> is the most specific type of sound or sound-sequence detectible in the current context.")
(comment termTargetsArgNumOfInstruction "(#$termTargetsArgNumOfInstruction TERM ARGN INSTR) means that within the control flow of the program containing the function call INSTR, the global value denoted by TERM is supplied to the ARGNth argument of the function called by INSTR.")
(comment CuttingOutASewingPatternPiece "Instances of this collection are events in which four or fewer pieces of the same shape are cut out of a sheet of cloth or leather by cutting around the perimeter of the shape with scissors.  The number of pieces so created is determined by the number of layers of sheet material that are present in the layout. The location of the cutting is provided by a #$SewingPatternPiece.")
(disjointWith Metalworking SewingActivity)
(disjointWith CookingFood SewingActivity)
(disjointWith Woodworking SewingActivity)
(comment SewingActivity "Instances of #$SewingActivity are events which are associated with a sewing project.  This includes actually making stiches (see #$Sewing) as well as other events such as cutting out the parts of a garment (#$CuttingOutASewingPatternPiece), transferring pattern markings to the cut pieces (#$MarkingSewingProjectPiece), etc.")
(comment CuttingOutASewingPattern "Instances of this collection are events in which all the pieces of cloth or leather required for a sewing project are cut out.  The number of pieces so created is determined by the number of #$SewingPatternPieces in the #$SewingPattern used, and the number of each individual piece that is needed. ")
(comment CuttingOutA2DPiece "Instances of this class are events in which a piece in the desired shape and size is cut free of a sheet of material (the #$workpieceIn), by cutting around its perimeter with a suitable tool, such as scissors, a sharp knife or a laser cutter, or by cutting the desired shape in one operation with a blanking punch and die. The #$objectRemoved is the resulting workpiece (see #$workpieceOut), and the remaining material is #$scrap   In such events, the whole is not completely chopped up.  The #$scrap that remains often will become the #$workpieceIn for another instance of #$CuttingOutA2DPiece.")
(comment (TransportViaFn Horse-Domesticated) "The collection of all event in which someone or something is transported via a domesticated horse.  This is to be distinguished from the more specific #$HorsebackRiding, which is a type #$RecreationalActivity.")
(comment sameValueToCallPairInArg "(#$sameValueToCallPairInArg TERM INSTR1 INSTR2 ARGN) means that within the control flow of the program of which INSTR1 and INSTR2 are both a part, TERM supplies the same value to the function (or distinct functions) called by INSTR1 and INSTR2 in the ARGNth argument position.")
(comment sameValueToCallsInArg "Where SET-OF-CALLS is a set of function calls within the same program, (#$sameValueToCallsInArg TERM SET-OF-CALLS ARGN) means that within the control flow of the program subsuming all of the calls in SET-OF-CALLS, the value denoted by TERM is supplied to the ARGNth argument position of the function or functions called by each call in SET-OF-CALLS.")
(comment MarkingSewingProjectPiece "A collection of events.  #$MarkingSewingProjectPiece is a specialization of #$MarkingOnASurface, instances of which involve an agent making or placing marks on an instance of #$ClothingItemPart-SingleSheet as directed by the #$SewingPatternPiece from which it was cut.  Such markings show darts, fold lines, locations that must line up when two pieces are sewn together, locations where stitching must start or stop, and other features that should be heeded when the project is assembled. ")
(comment Seam-SewnConnection "A specialization of #$Connection-Physical.  Each instance of #$Seam-SewnConnection is a group consisting of parts of at least two instances of #$PartiallyTangible that are mechanically connected by a series of #$Stitches, all of which are part of the same length of #$Thread.")
(comment Dart-SewnConnection "A specialization of #$Seam-SewnConnection.  Each instance of #$Dart-SewnConnection is a seam which joins one piece of #$Foldable material to itself in such a way that it no longer lays flat, but can assume the shape of a #$ConicalSurface-WithoutBase.  Darts are created in instances of #$ClothingItemPart-SingleSheet to make the piece of material follow the shape of the body on which it will be worn.")
(comment MakingASeam-Sewing "Instances of this collection are events in which flexible sheet material (usually #$Cloth or #$Leather) is correctly positioned, held in place if necessary by pinning, and then stitched.  Seams are made that hold two or more pieces together, that hem a raw fabric edge, that create a #$Dart-SewnConnection, that merely mark a location on the affected material, and for a variety of other functions. ")
(comment MakingADart-Sewing "Instances of this collection are events in which a #$ClothingItemPart-SingleSheet is folded, held in place if necessary by pinning, and then stitched from the point of the dart to the edge of the fabric, so as to create a #$Dart-SewnConnection.")
(comment PinningClothInPlace "Instances of #$PinningClothInPlace are events in which an instance of #$Cloth is pinned to another instance of #$Cloth, or to another location on the same piece of #$Cloth, with one or more #$SewingPins.  This is most often done prior to actually making the stitches in #$MakingASeam-Sewing.")
(comment SewingTwoPiecesTogether "Instances are events in which two previously unattached pieces of #$Foldable, sheetlike material are sewn together by making a series of #$Stitches. ")
(comment SewingAThingToItself "Instances are events in which a seam is made that connects one region of one instance of #$Foldable, sheetlike material to another region on the same piece.")
(disjointWith SewingTwoPiecesTogether SewingAThingToItself)
(comment Avitaminosis "A specialization of #$DietaryDeficiencyCondition.  Each instance of #$Avitaminosis is a nutritional disorder involving a dietary vitamin deficiency.")
(comment MineralDeficiencyCondition "A specialization of #$DietaryDeficiencyCondition.  Each instance of #$MineralDeficiencyCondition is a nutritional disorder involving a dietary mineral deficiency.")
(comment Hyponatremia "A specialization of #$MineralDeficiencyCondition.  Each instance of #$Hyponatremia is a condition involving a sodium deficiency.")
(comment IronDeficiency "A specialization of #MineralDeficiencyCondition.  Each instance of #$IronDeficiency is a nutritional disorder involving a dietary iron deficiency.")
(comment conditionInvolvesDeficiencyOfType "(#$conditionInvolvesDeficiencyOfType COND-TYPE TYPE) means that COND-TYPE involves a deficiency of TYPE.")
(comment Pellagra "A specialization of #$Avitaminosis.  Each instance of #$Pellagra is a nutritional disorder involving a dietary niacin deficiency.")
(comment deficientInNutrient "(#$deficientInNutrient ORGANISM TYPE) means that ORGANISM is deficient in the nutrient TYPE.")
(comment NutritionDisorder "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$NutritionDisorder is a physiological condition involving a lack or an excess of nutrients.")
(comment visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInScene "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInScene VIS-IBT OBJ-TYPE ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements depicts an event that contains a sub-event of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> in which an object of type <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is seen playing the role <code>ROLE</code> in that sub-event.")
(comment AmphiphilicChemicalObject "The collection of nanoscopic entities (primarily molecules, ions, atoms) which exhibit both hydrophilic and lipophilic properties.  CF. #$HydrophilicChemicalObject and #$HydrophobicChemicalObject.")
(comment PotentialEnergy "Potential energy is stored energy. It is the energy embodied in an object or system by virtue of its position or arrangement of its parts. In mechanical terms, the potential energy of an object is a measure of the work that had to be expended to bring the object from a ground state to another state. For example, the work performed to raise a block with mass, <code>m</code>, a fixed height, <code>h</code>, above the ground increases the potential energy of the block by the quantity <code>m*g*h</code>, where <code>g</code> is the acceleration due to gravity. See also #$PotentialEnergyFunction.")
(disjointWith Light-Stuff ChemicalEnergy)
(comment ChemicalEnergy "#$ChemicalEnergy is energy embodied in an object or system by virtue of of the arrangement of its #$Molecules, #$Atoms, #$Electrons, etc.  #$ChemicalReactions change these arrangements, and may absorb or release energy in another form, such as light or heat.  ")
(comment EnergyConversion-ElectromagneticToChemical "A specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-ElectromagneticToChemical are events powered by #$ElectromagneticRadiation which increase the #$ChemicalEnergy of a system or object.  #$Photosynthesis-Plant is a notable specialization.")
(comment HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation "A specialization of #$BiologicalEnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation is a process in which a single organism acquires energy and carbon in the form of organic compounds made by some other organism.  There are a variety of ways of doing so.  Heterotrophic micro-organisms may live in the bodies of hosts and absorb some of the host's organic molecules, or they may acquire such molecules from dead organisms or shed parts.  #$Animals may eat and then digest the entire bodies of other organisms, or their parts (e.g., instances of #$Leaf) or their products (e.g., #$Milk). ")
(comment AutotrophicNutrientAssimilation "A specialization of #$BiologicalEnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$AutotrophicNutrientAssimilation is a process in which a single organism acquires energy and converts it into energy-containing organic molecules needed for life, doing so NOT by assimilating similar molecules from the bodies or products of another organism, but by getting the raw materials and energy from its environment.  In this form of nutrition, #$Carbon comes from the #$CarbonDioxide in the atmosphere.")
(comment numberOfInputsToFunctionCall "(#$numberOfInputsToFunctionCall INSTR N) means that N distinct inputs are supplied to the #$ComputerFunctionInvocation-Executable INSTR in the program control flow.")
(comment ExecutingAFunctionCallWithAnIncorrectNumberOfArguments "The collection of all events in which a function call is executed with a number of inputs that is different from the funciton arity, potentially leading to undefined behavior.")
(disjointWith HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation AutotrophicNutrientAssimilation)
(comment SaprotrophicNutrientAssimilation "A specialization of #$HeterotrophicNutrientAssimilation.  Each instance of #$SaprotrophicNutrientAssimilation is a process in which a single organism acquires energy and carbon in the form of organic compounds made by some other organism, doing so by secreting enzymes that break down the remains of an organism or its shed parts into smaller molecules.  It then takes these smaller molecules into its cells.")
(comment PhotosyntheticPlant "An instance of #$OrganismTypeByCellularPhysiology and a specialization of #$Plant. Each instance of #$PhotosyntheticPlant is a plant which, in the presence of (#$GaseousFn #$CarbonDioxide), (#$LiquidFn #$Water) and the correct wavelengths of light, is able to do #$Photosynthesis-Plant.")
(comment Photoautotroph "The collection of organisms that use energy from #$Sunlight to manufacture organic nutrients from inorganic raw materials.  ")
(comment Photolithoautotroph "The collection of organisms which use energy from #$Sunlight to manufacture organic nutrients from inorganic raw materials, using #$CarbonDioxide from the atmosphere and using an inorganic electron donor such as #$Water or #$HydrogenSulfide.")
(comment Phototroph "The collection of organisms which obtain their energy from #$Sunlight.")
(comment Photolithotroph "The collection of organisms that use inorganic electron donors in #$Photosynthesis-Generic.  Such donors include water, sulpher, and hydrogen.")
(comment visuallyDepictsTypeFocally-Precise "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsTypeFocally-Precise VIS-IBT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements is primarily a depiction of <code>TYPE</code>, where <code>TYPE</code> is the most specific type generated from the inputs used to determine <code>TYPE</code>..")
(disjointWith BlueGreenAlgae Algae)
(comment PurpleSulfurBacterium "A collection of bacteria and a specialization of #$Proteobacterium.  These bacteria are able to perform  photosynthesis and are #$Photolithoautotrophs.  Rather than using #$Water as their electron donor, they use #$HydrogenSulfide and thus produce #$Sulfur as a byproduct, not #$Oxygen.")
(comment visuallyDepictsScenes "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsScenes VIS-IBT SCENE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements is such that it depcits an event of type <code>SCENE</code> that is part of a larger event that the <code>VIS-IBT</code> is focally about.")
(comment visuallyDepictsTypeFocally "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsTypeFocally VIS-IBT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements is primarily a depiction of <code>TYPE</code>.  So which <code>VIS-IBT</code> may visually depict many things (e.g., the parts of the instance of <code>TYPE</code>, objects in the foreground or background, etc.) it is nevertheless focally a depiction of an instance of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment visuallyDepictsTypeFocally-Refined "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsTypeFocally-Refined VIS-IBT TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements is primarily a depiction of an instance <code>INS</code> of <code>TYPE</code>, where <code>TYPE</code> has been determined via analysis to be at a level of description of <code>INS</code> suitable for describing or recounting the contents of <code>VIS-IBT</code> to a human audience.")
(comment visuallyDepictsSuperEventTypes "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsSuperEventTypes VIS-IBT EVT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements is such that it depcits an event of type <code>EVT-TYPE</code> by virtue of it depicting, focally, an event of type <code>FOCAL-TYPE</code> for which <code>EVT-TYPE</code> is a #$characteristicSuperEventTypes.")
(comment RemainsFn "<code>(#$RemainsFn IND)</code> denotes the remains of the #$Individual <code>IND</code>.  For every <code>(#$RemainsFn IND)</code>, it is the case that <code>IND</code> was an individual and its remains are <code>(#$RemainsFn IND)</code>.  See also the corresponding predicate, #$remainsOf.")
(disjointWith ChemicalEnergy SolarEnergy)
(comment AnaerobicDecompositionProcess "The collection of processes wherein microoganisms decompose the remains of organisms (dead bodies, shed parts, feces) into simpler chemical components in anoxic conditions. ")
(comment OrganismNutrientAssimilation "A specialization of #$BiologicalEnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$OrganismNutrientAssimilation is the process in which a single organism acquires energy and converts it into energy-containing organic molecules needed for life.  Every organism is doing this, either continuously or repeatedly throughout its life.  Some organisms (#$Autotrophs) are able to create energy-containing molecules from inorganic raw materials through the use of #$SolarEnergy or #$ChemicalEnergy.  Others (#$Heterotrophs) must consume energy-containing carbon compounds created by another organism.  There may be periods in an organism's life when it gets energy from stored reserves, such as the seed and early seedling stages of a #$PhotosyntheticPlant, before it is able to perform photosynthesis.")
(comment distributionSource "A binary predicate relating an event in which things are distributed to the source from which the distribution takes place. For example, in an event of spraying an aerosol from a can, the can is the source of the dispersion: (#$distributionSource Spraying001 Can001). Similarly, if the explosion of a bomb, Bomb001, causes the distribution-of-shrapnel event, Dist001, then (#$distributionSource Dist001 Bomb001) is true. Despite the lack of rules to enforce this, not every pair of an instance of PhysicalDistributionEvent and the instance of PartiallyTangible where the distribution intuitively originates will satisfy #$distributionSource. For example, although Lake Itasca is the headwaters of the Missippi, and therefore in a sense the source of the (very long duration) event in which the Mississippi flows into the Gulf of Mexico, it is not true that (distributionSource FlowOfTheMississippi Itasca), and not just because there are tributaries of the Mississippi that themselves have source this is not the right kind of distribution event to have a distributionSource. Finally, note that #$distributionSource is interesting primarily not for its own sake, but rather for the sake of enabling interesting restrictions to be put on kinds of instances of PhysicalDistributionEvent.")
(comment typeDiffused "(#$typeDiffused EVENT TYPE) means that during the #$DiffusionEvent EVENT the kind of thing diffused is TYPE.")
(comment interArgIsaGenl2-1 "<code>(#$interArgIsaGenl2-1 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL)</code> means that, when an instance of <code>INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code> appears as the second argument to <code>REL</code>, the first argument is constrained to be a specialization of <code>DEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code>.")
(comment TheoryAboutBiology "The collection of #$ScientificTheory[ies] that concern aspects of #$Biology.  For example, the theory of island biogeography attempts to predict patterns of species richness on islands; the #$EndosymbiontTheory explains the origin of #$Plastids, #$Mitochondrion[ia] and maybe other #$Organelles by postulating that the ancestors of cells with these organelles took in #$ProkaryoticCells as endosymbionts.")
(comment TheoryAboutEvolution "The collection of #$ScientificTheory[ies] that concern aspects of #$Evolution.  For example, the #$EndosymbiontTheory explains the origin of #$Plastids, #$Mitochondrion[ia] and maybe other #$Organelles by postulating that the ancestors of cells with these organelles took in #$ProkaryoticCells as endosymbionts.")
(comment PectoralFin "Fin located symmetrically on either side of fish and sea mammals, used for stabilizing and steering. Homologous to the forelimbs of terrestrial tetrapods.")
(comment standardRegisterClassDesignation "(#$standardRegisterClassDesignation REGISTER-TYPE CLASS-NAME) means that CLASS-NAME is the standard designator used in the computer industry for referring to the register class REGISTER-TYPE.")
(comment WesternCulture "The collection of all cultures of instances of #$WesternCountry.")
(comment servingServed "An instance of #$ActorSlot, <code>(#$servingServed SERVICE SERVING)</code> means that <code>SERVING</code> is the #$FoodOrDrink served in <code>SERVICE</code>, an instance of #$ServingFoodOrDrink.")
(comment LeafEpidermis "The outer-most cell layer of leaves. Given an instance of #$Leaf, there is a unique instance of #$LeafEpidermis which covers it.")
(comment MesophyllCell "A specialization of #$BotanicalCell.  #$MesophyllCells are a type of #$ParenchymaCell that make up #$Mesophyll, the tissue which forms the central part of #$Leaf[ves] that is sandwiched between the upper and lower layers of #$PlantTissue-Dermal that covers a leaf.  #$MesophyllCells typically contain a group of #$Chloroplasts.")
(comment AreaFrequencyOfObjects "A #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType (q.v.) and a specialization of #$RatioQuantity (q.v.).  Quantities that are instances of #$AreaFrequencyOfObjects apply to (see #$quantityRange) #$SpatialThings, and measure the number of some type of object per some (specified or unspecified) unit of area (e.g. #$SquareMile).<p>One sample specialization of #$AreaFrequencyOfObjects is the collection, #$DensityOfPopulation. ")
(comment frequencyOfPartTypePerArea "A predicate for stating the frequency or density with which a type of #$PartiallyTangible is present as a part of some other #$PartiallyTangible, as a function of its area. Specifically, <code>(#$frequencyOfPartTypePerArea OBJ PARTTYPE AREAFREQUENCY)</code> states that <code>OBJ</code> has instances of <code>PARTTYPE</code> as parts, and they are distributed over the surface of <code>OBJ</code> at a frequency of <code>AREAFREQUENCY</code>.  For example, (#$frequencyOfPartTypePerArea Leaf001 #$Chloroplast ((#$PerFn (#$UnitOfCountFn #$Chloroplast) (#$UnitProductFn (#$Milli #$Meter) (#$Milli #$Meter))) 1000) states that Leaf001 has 1000 #$Chloroplasts for each square millimeter of its area.")
(comment StackBasedMemory-Entire "A given instance of #$StackBasedMemory-Entire is an #$AbstractIndividual that is best thought of as a reified functional role within a computational architecture.  At any given time in processing operations, a #$StackBasedMemory-Entire is associated with a list of positive integers that serve as memory addresses. The identity of this list changes over time in predictable ways based on the operations executed on the #$Computer whose stack-based memory it is.")
(comment machineStack-Entire "A #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot.  (#$machineStack-Entire COMPUTER STACK) means that STACK is the entire stack of the abstract memory of the #$Computer COMPUTER.")
(comment stackAddressListAtOperationStart "(#$stackAddressListAtOperationStart STACK ADDRESSES OP) means that the memory stack STACK has allocated the list of addresses ADDRESSES at the start of the #$ProgramAction OP.")
(comment stackTopAddressAtOperationStart "(#$stackTopAddressAtOperationStart STACK TOP OP) means that at the start of the #$ProgramAction OP, TOP is the address at the 'top' of the memory stack STACK")
(comment StackAllocation "The collection of all memory allocations (#$AllocationOfComputerMemory) wherein some portion of machine memory is allocated to the stack (#$StackBasedMemory-Entire).")
(comment addressListAllocated "(#$addressListAllocated ALLOCATION ADDRESS-LIST) means that ADDRESS-LIST is precisely the list of addresses in memory allocated by the #$AllocationOfComputerMemory ALLOCATION.")
(comment memoryAllocatedTo "(#$memoryAllocatedTo ALLOCATION MEMORY) means that MEMORY is the #$ComputerMemory-Abstract to which a list of memory addresses is allocated in yhr #$AllocationOfComputerMemory ALLOCATION.")
(comment pointerReturnedByAllocation "(#$pointerReturnedByAllocation ALLOCATION ADDRESS) means that the #$AllocationOfComputerMemory operation ALLOCATION returns the memory location address ADDRESS as the return value of the function being called in ALLOCATION.")
(comment StackDeallocation "The collection of all memory deallocations (#$DeallocationOfComputerMemory) wherein some portion of the address list of the extant stack (the #$StackBasedMemory-Entire) is deallocated from said stack memory.")
(comment addressListDeallocated "(#$addressListDeallocated DEALLOCATION ADDRESS-LIST) means that ADDRESS-LIST is the list of memory location addresses deallocated from memory in the #$DeallocationOfComputerMemory DEALLOCATION.")
(comment memoryDeallocatedFrom "(#$memoryDeallocatedFrom DEALLOCATION MEMORY) means that MEMORY is the #$ComputerMemory-Abstract from which memory locations are deallocated from in the #$DeallocationOfComputerMemory DEALLOCATION.")
(comment pointerInputToDeallocation "(#$pointerInputToDeallocation DEALLOCATION ADDRESS) means that ADDRESS is the point in the extant memory from which the #$DeallocationOfComputerMemory DEALLOCATION starts in deallocating space from some portion of machine memory.")
(comment PlantEpidermis "The outermost cell layer covering a plant or part of a plant.  For each entire #$Plant, there is a unique instance of #$PlantEpidermis which is its outermost layer of #$Cells.")
(disjointWith Culture-Bacterial OuterChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Organism-Whole OuterChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue OuterChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane EndomembraneSystem)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue Organelle)
(disjointWith Organelle OuterChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Cell OuterChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Culture-Bacterial InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Organism-Whole InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Organelle InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith Cell InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerChloroplastMembrane EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerChloroplastMembrane EndomembraneSystem)
(disjointWith InnerChloroplastMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith VisualMark OrganellePart)
(disjointWith Culture-Bacterial OrganellePart)
(disjointWith OrganellePart Cleavage_Furrow)
(disjointWith Molecule OrganellePart)
(disjointWith Organism-Whole OrganellePart)
(disjointWith Organ OrganellePart)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue OrganellePart)
(disjointWith Cell OrganellePart)
(disjointWith Organelle OrganellePart)
(comment OrganellePart "The collection of structures which are found and formed as parts of #$Organelles.")
(comment IntermembraneSpace "Instances of #$IntermembraneSpace are regions within a #$Chloroplast or a #$Mitochondrion that lie between their inner and outer membrane.")
(comment IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion "Instances of #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion are regions within a #$Mitochondrion that lie between its #$OuterMitochondrialMembrane and its #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane. ")
(comment IntermembraneSpace-Chloroplast "Instances of #$IntermembraneSpace-Chloroplast are regions within a #$Chloroplast that lie between its #$OuterChloroplastMembrane and its #$InnerChloroplastMembrane. ")
(comment ChloroplastStroma "Instances of #$ChloroplastStroma are portions of dense fluid within the #$InnerChloroplastMembrane within which #$Thylakoids are suspended. ")
(comment Thylakoid "A specialization of #$OrganellePart.  Thylakoids are small flattened sacs found inside of #$Chloroplasts. The membrane of thylakoids divides the interior of a chloroplast into the thylakoid space and the stroma.")
(disjointWith NuclearEnvelope ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic)
(disjointWith CellMembrane ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic InnerChloroplastMembrane)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic EndomembraneSystem)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(comment ThylakoidSpace "Instances of #$ThylakoidSpace are regions inside #$Thylakoids. Within a #$Chloroplast, all portions of #$ThylakoidSpace are a single connected region separated from the #$ChloroplastStroma by the thylakoid membrane system.")
(disjointWith Chloroplast Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith Mitochondrion Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith CellNucleus Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith Organism-Whole Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith Cell Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(disjointWith Granum-ThylakoidStack Thylakoid)
(disjointWith BiologicalMembrane Granum-ThylakoidStack)
(comment Granum-ThylakoidStack "A specialization of #$OrganellePart.  Instances of #$Granum-ThylakoidStack are structures often found inside #$Chloroplasts, consisting of stacks of #$Thylakoid sacs.  #$Thylakoids are approximately disk-shaped, so grana are approximately cylindrical. ")
(comment birthdayPartyFor "<code>(#$birthdayPartyFor PARTY AGENT)</code> means that the instance <code>PARTY</code> of #$BirthdayParty is a birthday party for <code>AGENT</code>.")
(comment visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInPostEventType "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInPostEventType VIS-IBT OBJ-TYPE ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements depicts an event that is part of a larger super-event  with a scene of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that takes place after or prior to the end of that event, and in which an object of type <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is seen playing the role <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInPrecursor "<code>(#$visuallyDepictsObjectTypePlayingRoleInPrecursor VIS-IBT OBJ-TYPE ROLE SIT-TYPE)</code> means that the instance <code>VIS-IBT</code> of #$IBTWithVisualElements depicts an event that is part of a larger super-event with a scene of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> that starts prior to that event, and in which an object of type <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is seen playing the role <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment OxygenicPhotosynthesis "A collection of events in which organisms, including #$Algae, higher #$Plants and #$BlueGreenAlgae, use energy
captured from sunlight to create sugars and molecular #$Oxygen from #$CarbonDioxide and #$Water.")
(comment AnoxygenicPhotosynthesis "A collection of events in which a #$Phototroph uses energy
from sunlight to form energy molecules.  In this process, #$Oxygen is
not used or released as a by-product, see instead
#$OxygenicPhotosynthesis.")
(comment Photosynthesis-Bacterial "A collection of events in which a #$Bacterium forms energy-containing molecules from raw materials and the energy in sunlight.  Different types of photosynthetic #$Bacterium[ia] exhibit different forms of photosynthesis, including both #$OxygenicPhotosynthesis and
#$AnoxygenicPhotosynthesis.")
(comment RollingOnASurface "A specialization of #$Motion-SolidAgainstSolid (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RollingOnASurface is a process of moving along a surface in which the #$objectMoving rotates while it translates.   For example, what a car's tires do when the car is being driven is an instance of #$RollingOnASurface.  Points on the #$objectMoving become flush with (see #$flushSurfaces) the #$motionPathway-Complete for a brief period (depending on speed, diameter, surface rolled on, deformability of roller, and pressure) and then move perpendicularly away as the object moves along.  The #$objectMoving in a #$RollingOnASurface moves along the surface without #$Sliding-Generic.")
(comment Weaving-Movement "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Movement-TranslationEvent. In each #$Weaving-Movement, something moves in a sinuous, spiral, or circular course.")
(comment PeripheralProtein "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule.  Peripheral proteins are proteins that are loosely bound to the surface of a membrane.")
(disjointWith Animal (CollectionDifferenceFn Organism-Whole Animal))
(comment EndergonicReaction "Instances are chemical reactions which require energy.")
(comment ExergonicReaction "Instances are chemical reactions which release energy.")
(comment chemicalEnergyOfObject "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$chemicalEnergyOfObject OBJ QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of chemical energy had by <code>OBJ</code> (i.e. the amount of energy contained in its chemical bonds) is <code>QUANT</code>.  In general, assertions made with this predicate should be temporally qualified.")
(comment gravitationalPotentialEnergyOfObject "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$gravitationalPotentialEnergyOfObject OBJ QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of potential energy had by <code>OBJ</code> by virtue of its relative position inside a gravitational field is <code>QUANT</code>.  If <code>OBJ</code> is allowed to fall, some of this potential energy is converted into kinetic energy and its resulting gravitational potential energy will be less.  In general, assertions made with this predicate should be temporally qualified.")
(comment potentialEnergyOfObject "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$potentialEnergyOfObject OBJ QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of potential energy had by <code>OBJ</code> (i.e. the amount of energy contained in its chemical bonds plus the amount of energy it possesses due to its relative position in gravity, due to its elastic state, due to its electrical charge and due to other static factors) is <code>QUANT</code>.  In general, assertions made with this predicate should be temporally qualified.")
(comment EnergyOfObjectPredicate "A specialization of #$PhysicalAmountSlot, #$TangibleObjectPredicate and #$FunctionalSlot.   Each instance of #$EnergyOfObjectPredicate is a binary predicate that is used to state the amount of some type of energy, such as kinetic energy or gravitational potential energy, possessed by or contained in some #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment Photophore "A specialization of #$Organ present in many species of #$Cephalopod and #$Fish that allows the animal to produce bioluminescent light.")
(comment SodiumChannel "A specialization of #$IonChannel.  Each instance of #$SodiumChannel is an integral transmembrane protein that channel conducts sodium through a #$CellMembrane.")
(comment IonChannelTypeByTypeConducted "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$IonChannel whose instances are all of the same type conducted.")
(comment IonChannelTypeByGateType "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$IonChannel whose instances are all of the same gate type.")
(comment biologicalFunction "(#$biologicalFunction OBJ-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that each instance of OBJ-TYPE, is able to play ROLE in a situation of type SIT-TYPE, and such situations naturally occur for some #$BiologicalLivingObject.  In a creationist microtheory, this would be a subset of #$intendedBehaviorCapable.  Roles which are possible due to learning by the organism are not included.  Thus (#$biologicalFunction #$Heart #$CardiovascularCirculation #$providerOfMotiveForce) but not (#$biologicalFunction #$Hand #$Swimming-Generic #$providerOfMotiveForce) even though a hand can be used this way.")
(comment SodiumChannel-VoltageGated "A specialization of #$SodiumChannel and #$VoltageGatedIonChannel .  Each instance of #$SodiumChannel-VoltageGated is a voltage-gated sodium channel.")
(comment SodiumChannel-LigandGated "A specialization of #$SodiumChannel and #$LigandGatedIonChannel .  Each instance of #$SodiumChannel-LigandGated is a ligand-gated sodium channel.")
(comment CalciumChannel "A specialization of #$IonChannel .  Each instance of #$CalciumChannel is an ion channel through which calcium ions can pass.")
(comment PotassiumChannel "A specialization of #$IonChannel .  Each instance of #$PotassiumChannel is an ion channel through which potassium ions can pass.")
(comment PotassiumChannel-VoltageGated "A specialization of #$PotassiumChannel and #$VoltageGatedIonChannel .  Each instance of #$PotassiumChannel-VoltageGated is a voltage-gated ion channel through which potassium ions can pass.")
(comment Endocytosis "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel.  Each instance of #$Endocytosis is an event in which a cell takes in a molecule by engulfing it.")
(comment Pinocytosis "A specialization of #$Endocytosis.  Each instance of #$Pinocytosis is an event in which a cell engulfs a droplet of extracellular fluid that contains useful molecules.")
(comment ReceptorMediatedEndocytosis "A specialization of #$Endocytosis.  Each instance of #$ReceptorMediatedEndocytosis is an event in which a cell engulfs a portion of its plasma membrame to ingest receptors with bound ligands.")
(comment TestForQueryBindingFn "(#$TestForQueryBindingFn QUERY VAR BINDING) denotes the #$KBContentTest defined by running QUERY and verifying that BINDING is returned as a binding for VAR. Bindings for other variables, or other bindings for VAR, are by definition irrelevant to the success or failure of the test.")
(comment AnabolicPathway "The collection of all instances of #$MetabolicPathway that are constructive -- i.e., that form a chemical object from simpler components.")
(comment CatabolicPathway "The collection of all instances of #$MetabolicPathway that are degradative -- i.e., that break a molecule down into simpler components.")
(comment MetabolismComponentTypeByPathwayType "The collection whose two instances, #$Catabolism and #$Anabolism, comprise the to major components of #$Metabolism.")
(comment Metabolism "The collection of all groups of instances of #$MetabolicPathway that take place in a #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(comment Catabolism "The collection of all groups of instances of #$CatabolicPathway that take place in a #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(comment Anabolism "The collection of all groups of instances of #$AnabolicPathway that take place in a #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(comment CatabolicPathwayTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, instances are specializations of #$CatabolicPathway that are distinguished by the constituent reactions that comprise their instances.")
(comment AnabolicPathwayTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, instances are specializations of #$AnabolicPathway that are distinguished by the constituent reactions that comprise their instances.")
(comment MetabolicPathwayTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, instances are specializations of #$MetabolicPathway that are distinguished by the constituent reactions that comprise their instances.")
(comment DegradativeBiochemicalPathway "The collection of all instances of #$BiochemicalPathway, regardless of whether they are metabolic in nature, that culminate in the decomposition of a complex chemical object into simpler ones.")
(comment ConstructiveBiochemicalPathway "The collection of all instances of #$BiochemicalPathway, regardless of whether they are metabolic in nature, that culminate in the construction of a more complex chemical object from simpler ones.")
(disjointWith ConstructiveBiochemicalPathway DegradativeBiochemicalPathway)
(comment Diphosphate "The collection of all chemical objects consisting in two phosphorus atoms linked together by an oxygen atom, and linked to three other oxygen atoms apiece.")
(comment Triphosphate "The collection of all chemical objects consisting in three phosphorus atoms linked together by two oxygen atoms; the middle phosphorus is linked to two additional oxygen atoms, while the end phosphorus atoms are linked to three additional oxygens apiece - hence, each phosphorus in the group links to a total of four oxygen atoms.")
(comment Bioenergetics "The study of how living things make and use energy.")
(comment etymologicallyDerivedFrom "<code>(#$etymologicallyDerivedFrom WORD . ORIGINS)</code> means that the word <code>WORD</code> is etymologically derived from the word or words that comprise <code>. ORIGINS</code>, with the order of combination determined by the order in which those words occur.")
(comment EntropyQuantity "Entropy is a measure of energetic disorder of a physical system.  Systems in which energy is evenly distributed throughout the system have higher entropy than systems in which energy is irregularly distributed. ")
(comment entropyOfSystem "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EntropyQuantity.  <code>(#$entropyOfSystem OBJ ENT)</code> means that <code>ENT</code> is amount of entropy had by <code>OBJ</code>, a thermodynamic system. ")
(comment ThermodynamicsMt "The most general microtheory for representing the propositions of #$Thermodynamics.")
(comment BioenergeticsMt "The most general microtheory for representing the propositions of #$Bioenergetics.")
(comment mtForField "<code>(#$mtForField MT FIELD)</code> means that <code>MT</code>, an instance of #$TheoryMicrotheory and #$GeneralMicrotheory, is the most general microtheory appropriate for representing the propositions distinctive to <code>FIELD</code>, a #$FieldOfStudy.  A field may have many sub-fields, and the distinctive propositions of those sub-fields (which may be mutually inconsistent or incommensurable) should not go in the #$mtForField for the \"parent\" field, but in more specialized #$mtForField microtheories for the specific sub-fields.")
(comment Thermodynamics "The study of energy transfer within and between systems of matter and/or radiation, and its effects on those systems.")
(comment MetabolicPathway "This is the collection of metabolic pathways. A metabolic pathway is a series of chemical reactions that take place in a biological living object, to break down molecules to generate energy (see #$CatabolicPathway) or to use energy to generate complex molecules (see #$AnabolicPathway).  The complete set of metabolic pathways in a biological living object is its #$Metabolism.")
(comment partwiseDisjoint "<code>(#$partwiseDisjoint I1 I2)</code> means that <code>I1</code> and <code>I2</code> do not share any parts. I.e., there are no individuals <code>I</code> such that <code>(#$parts I1 I)</code> and <code>(#$parts I2 I)</code>.  For example (#$partwiseDisjoint #$Alaska-State #$Italy) is true because there is no instance of #$Individual that is a #$parts of both #$Alaska-State and #$Italy.  Similarly, an event during which Barack Obama brushes his teeth is #$partwiseDisjoint with an event during which John McCain brushes his teeth, even if they occur simultaneously: neither of these #$BrushingOnesTeeth events shares a part with the other.")
(comment totalInternalEnergyOfObject "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$totalInternalEnergyOfObject OBJ QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy had by <code>OBJ</code> (i.e. its potential energy plus its kinetic energy) is <code>QUANT</code>. In general, assertions made with this predicate should be temporally qualified.")
(comment gibbsFreeEnergyOfSystem "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$gibbsFreeEnergyOfSystem OBJ QUANT)</code> means that <code>QUANT</code> is amount of energy had by <code>OBJ</code>, a thermodynamic system at constant pressure and temperature, that is available to do work.  A change in the Gibbs free energy of a system is equivalent to its change in enthalpy (see #$enthalpyOfSystem) minus the product of its absolute temperature and its change in entropy (see #$entropyOfSystem). ")
(comment keyConcepts "<code>(#$keyConcepts WORK THING)</code> means that <code>THING</code> is a key, or highly focal, subject of <code>WORK</code>, an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Many expository works will explicitly identify key concepts by having initial references to them appear in <b>bold</b> or <i>italics</i>, or even by enumerating them via a glossary or a special section entitled \"key concepts.\"")
(comment JWillardGibbs "J. Willard Gibbs, father of physical chemistry and chemical thermodynamics, one of the greatest scientists of the late 19th century.")
(comment enrolledAtSchool "<code>(#$enrolledAtSchool PERSON SCHOOL)</code> means that the instance <code>PERSON</code> of #$Person is enrolled as a student at <code>SCHOOL</code>, an instance of #$EducationalOrganization.")
(comment undergraduateAt "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$enrolledAtSchool, <code>(#$undergraduateAt PERSON SCHOOL)</code> means that the instance <code>PERSON</code> of #$Person is enrolled as an ungraduate student at <code>SCHOOL</code>, an instance of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution.")
(comment graduateStudentAt "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$enrolledAtSchool, <code>(#$graduateStudentAt PERSON SCHOOL)</code> means that the instance <code>PERSON</code> of #$Person is enrolled as a graduate student at <code>SCHOOL</code>, an instance of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution.")
(comment uRLReferenceForMitreSchemaComponent "(#$uRLReferenceForMitreSchemaComponent PRED URL) means that URL is the resource identifier for MITRE's schema specification for the schema component or sub-component given by PRED.")
(comment cWEDescriptionSummary "(#$cWEDescriptionSummary DEFICIENCY-TYPE DESCRIPTION) means that DESCRIPTION is a short description of DEFICIENCY-TYPE limited to describing the key definitional points.")
(comment cWEExtendedDescription "(#$cWEExtendedDescription DEFICIENCY-TYPE DESCRIPTION) means that DESCRIPTION is a natural language descriptionof DEFICIENCY-TYPE with important details that are nevertheless unnecessary for conveying the fundamental concept behind the entry.")
(comment cWEExample "(#$cWEExample DEFICIENCY-TYPE EXAMPLE) means that EXAMPLE is a natural-language example showing code that instantiates DEFICIENCY-TYPE.")
(comment cWEWhiteboxDefinition "(#$cWEWhiteboxDefinition DEFICIENCY-TYPE DEFINITION) means that DEFINITION is a natural language description of DEFICIENCY-TYPE from a 'white box' perspective, i.e., one that includes the knowledge control flow, data flow, and all other inner workings of the software instantiating DEFICIENCY-TYPE.")
(comment cWEBlackboxDefinition "(#$cWEBlackboxDefinitions DEFICIENCY-TYPE DEFINITION) means that DEFINITION is a natural language description of DEFICIENCY-TYPE from an external or 'black box' perspective, meaning that the view includes no reference to how the softare is processing data other than what can be inferred from observing the software's behavior.")
(comment QSSingleVariableTernaryQueryFn "(#$QSSingleVariableTernaryQueryFn PRED ARG-N ARG-M VARPOS) denotes the Query Suggestor query for bindings for the VARPOS-th argument of a ternary CycL sentence where the arg0 is PRED, and the other two arguments, in order of argument number, are ARG-N and ARG-M. For example (#$QSSingleVariableTernaryQueryFn #$behaviorCapable (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Cello) #$performedBy 1) specifies the Query Suggestor query for individuals capable of playing the cello.")
(comment HydrophobicInteraction "The collection of events in which nonpolar substances tend to aggregate in aqueous solution.")
(comment HydrophobicAggregate "The collection of aggregates that are the result of #$HydrophobicInteraction events.")
(comment NonpolarChemicalObject "A specialization of #$HydrophobicChemicalObject.  Each instance of #$NonpolarChemicalObject is a chemical object that is non-polar, either because there is no polarity in its bonds, or because of a symmetrical distribution of its polar bonds.")
(comment PolarChemicalObject "A specialization of #$HydrophilicChemicalObject.  Each instance of #$PolarChemicalObject is a chemical object that is polar, either because there is polarity in its bonds, or because of an asymmetrical distribution of its polar bonds.")
(comment Food "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$FoodOrDrink.  Each instance of #$Food is a particular portion of food of a type which can be, and habitually is, eaten by humans or other animals.  Here the notion of <i>eating</i> is important; eating an instance of #$Food will generally require biting or chewing, but if placed into the mouth (e.g. with a utensil) in a manner not considered to be drinking, it is still considered eating.  Thus, edible stuff normally taken in via drinking, inhalation, or osmosis is excluded from this collection.  A borderline example is a bowl of bouillon, which, although it can be drunk from the bowl is normally \"eaten\" with a spoon; a borderline non-example is a very thick milkshake, which may be eaten with a spoon, but is normally drunk (possibly using a straw) from a glass.  Instances of #$Food provide calories and/or nutrients that humans or animals need. Living animals are generally not considered to be food.")
(disjointWith Food AnimalBLO)
(disjointWith PerceptualAgent (CollectionDifferenceFn Thing PerceptualAgent))
(comment deportee "(#$deportee DEP PERSON) means that PERSON was deported during DEP.")
(comment computationalResourceAffected "The most general predicate for linking a computational resource (a #$ComputerStorageDevice or an #$AbstractIndividual such as a #$StackBasedMemory-Entire) to a #$ProgramAction wherein it is 'utilized'.  It has (at least) three important specializations: #$computationalResourceUsed, #$computationalResourceCommitted, and #$computationalResourceReleased.")
(comment computationalResourceUsed "(#$computationalResourceUsed PROGRAM-ACTION RESOURCE) means that RESOURCE is a computational resource (a #$ComputerStorageDevice or an #$AbstractIndividual) whose state is altered by PROGRAM-ACTION.")
(comment computationalResourceCommitted "(#$computationalResourceCommitted ACTION RESOURCE) means that the computational resource RESOURCE (an instance of either #$ComputerStorageDevice or #$AbstractIndividual) is allocated for future use by ACTION.")
(comment computationalResourceReleased "(#$computationalResourceReleased ACTION RESOURCE means that the resource RESOURCE (an instance of either #$ComputerStorageDevice or #$AbstractIndividual) is deallocated from use by ACTION.)")
(comment computationalResourceTypeAffectedInActionType "(#$computationalResourceTypeAffectedInActionType PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE RESOURCE-TYPE) means that every instance of PROGRAM-ACTION-TYPE ordinarily 'utilizes' an instance of RESOURCE-TYPE (where the actual details of the utilization involved will vary depending on the type of resource.")
(comment computationalResourceTypeImplicatedInDeficiencyType "(#$computationalResourceTypeImplicatedInDeficiencyType CODE-TYPE RESOURCE-TYPE) means that executions of instances of the #$ComputerCodeTypeByDeficiency CODE-TYPE will involve some use of an instance of RESOURCE-TYPE.")
(comment SecondLawOfThermodynamicsMt "An instance of #$LawOfNatureMicrotheory (q.v.).  #$SecondLawOfThermodynamicsMt contains propositional information to the effect that heat from a lower temperature system cannot flow into a higher temperature system spontaneously, and entails, famously, that a #$PerpetualMotionMachine is impossible.")
(comment lawContents "<code>(#$lawContents LAW SENTENCE)</code> means that the CycL sentence <code>SENTENCE</code> captures part or all of the propositional content of <code>LAW</code>, an instance of #$LawOfNature.")
(comment articulationOfLaw-CycL "<code>(articulationOfLaw-CycL LAW CYCL)</code> identifies <code>CYCL</code> as a comprehensive CycL representation of <code>LAW</code>, an instance of #$LawOfNature.")
(comment ProcessRequiringNoEnergyInput "A central concept of #$Thermodynamics, this is the collection of physical events that occur without any input of energy, described within the field of #$Thermodynamics as \"spontaneous\" processes.  Every instance of #$PhysicalEvent falls under this collection or its counterpart, #$ProcessRequiringEnergyInput.")
(comment ProcessRequiringEnergyInput "This is the collection of physical events that required an input of energy in order to transpire, described within the field of #$Thermodynamics as \"non-spontaneous\" processes.  Every instance of #$PhysicalEvent falls under this collection or its counterpart, #$ProcessRequiringNoEnergyInput.")
(comment ChemicalThermodynamics "A scientific field of study that applies the principles of #$Thermodynamics to #$Chemistry.")
(comment ChemicalThermodynamicsMt "The most general microtheory for representing the propositions of #$ChemicalThermodynamics.")
(comment MembraneTransport-Diffusion "A specialization of #$PassiveTransport-Membrane.  Each instance of  #$MembraneTransport-Diffusion is an event in which particles spread through random motion from regions of high concentration to regions of low concentration across a membrane, without being facilitated by proteins.")
(comment LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis "Photosynthesis - events in which organisms convert energy captured from sunlight into chemical energy usable for their metabolic needs (and for the needs of other, heterotrophic organisms that may eat them) - proceeds in two steps.  In instances of #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis (called \"light reactions\" or \"light-dependent reactions\"), the energy in sunlight is captured and trapped in short-lived molecules.  In the second step, chemical energy in these molecules is used to drive the #$CalvinCycle, which uses #$CarbonDioxide to create energy-containing carbohydrates.")
(comment Osmosis "A specialization of #$DiffusionEvent.  Each instance of #$Osmosis is an event in which water molecules diffuse across a semipermeable membrane.")
(comment DiffusionEvent "A specialization of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Each instance of #$DiffusionEvent is an event in which particles spread through random motion from regions of high concentration to regions of low concentration.")
(comment MembraneTransport-Osmosis "A specialization of #$Osmosis and #$MembraneTransport-SimpleDiffusion. Each instance of #$MembraneTransport-Osmosis is an event in which a water molecule diffuses across a biological membrane.")
(comment hydrolysisOfSubstanceType "<code>(#$hydrolysisOfSubstanceType HYDROLYSIS-TYPE SUBSTANCE-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>HYDROLYSIS-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$Hydrolysis-ChemicalReaction in which <code>SUBSTANCE-TYPE</code> is, along with #$Water, a chemical reactant.")
(comment HydrolysisOfTypeFn "<code>(#$HydrolysisOfTypeFn SUBSTANCE-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$Hydrolysis-ChemicalReaction in which <code>SUBSTANCE-TYPE</code> is, along with #$Water, a chemical reactant.")
(comment AssemblerProgram-CW "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW that when executed generate #$ComputerCodeStatements (including programs) in assembly code from #$ComputerCodeStatements provided as inputs.")
(comment AssemblerProgramTypeByFormat "A type-level collection.  Each collection instance is a class of assembler programs (instances of #$AssemblerProgram-CW) which produce output in a common assembler format.")
(comment assemblerSharesFormat "(#$assemblerSharesFormat ASSEMBLER ASSEMBLER-TYPE) means that the #$AssemblerProgram-CW belongs to the #$AssemblerProgramTypeByFormat ASSEMBLER-TYPE.")
(comment assemblerTypeFormatOriginatesWith "(assemblerTypeFormatOriginatesWith ASSEMBLER-FORMAT ORG) means that ORG is the #$Organization (usually, but not always, a #$CommercialOrganization), with which the #$AssemblerProgramTypeByFormat FORMAT originates, in the sense that personnel employed by the organization are authors of the specification of FORMAT.")
(comment assemblerTypeFormatStandardAcronym "(#$assemblerTypeFormatStandardAcronym ASSEMBLER-FORMAT ACRONYM-STRING) means that ACRONYM-STRING is the standard acronym used to denot the #$SAssemblerProgramTypeByFormat ASSEMBLER-FORMAT.")
(comment GNUAssemblerATAndTFormat "The GNU AT&T assembler format.")
(comment MicrosoftAssemblerFormat "The Microsoft assembler format.")
(comment BorlandIDEALAssemblerFormat "The Borland IDEAL assembler format.")
(comment binaryFormatStringOfInstruction "(#$binaryFormatStringOfInstruction INSTR STRING) means that the binary hexadecimal format of the #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic INSTR is given by the #$CharacterString STRING.")
(comment symbolicFormatStringOfInstruction "(#$symbolicFormatStringOfInstruction INSTR STRING ASSEMBLER-TYPE-BY-FORMAT) means that the atomic instruction (an instance of #$ComputerCodeStatement-Atomic) INSTR is given the symbolic format string STRING by assemblers (instances of #$AssemblerProgram-CW) with the #$AssemblerProgramTypeByFormat ASSEMBLER-TYPE-BY-FORMAT.")
(comment ChemicalEquilibrium "A physical situation (concerning a thermodynamic system) is a chemical equilibrium when each chemical reaction occurring in the system is opposed by the reverse reaction, and both occur at the same rate, so that there is no net change in the concentrations of the reactants or products over time.")
(comment situationConcernsThermodynamicSystem "The predicate #$situationConcernsThermodynamicSystem is used to identify a portion of matter with a role in a #$PhysicalSituation as one that is of interest in a thermodynamic analysis.  <code>(#$situationConcernsThermodynamicSystem SIT SYSTEM)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> is a group of #$PartiallyTangible things likely each with a role in the #$PhysicalSituation, <code>SIT</code>, about which it is meaningful to ask a variety of questions, such as \"What is the change in the Gibbs free energy of this system over <code>SIT</code>?\" Because actors can be created and destroyed over the course of an instance of #$PhysicalSituation,  membership in <code>SYSTEM</code> may change over <code>SIT</code>.")
(disjointWith Atom ElementaryParticle)
(disjointWith Proton ElementaryParticle)
(comment ElementaryParticle "A specialization #$TemporalThing and #$SpatialThing-Localized, although various models of #$Physics may think otherwise.  Each instance of #$ElementaryParticle is a particle in the physical universe which is not divisible, i.e., not made up of smaller particles.  #$ElementaryParticles are the basic building blocks out of which the physical universe is made. ")
(disjointWith Lepton Photon)
(comment Photon "A specialization of #$ElementaryParticle.  Each #$Photon is a quantum of #$ElectromagneticRadiation (including of #$VisibleLight), and carries electromagnetic force.  #$Photons are thought to be massless and have no charge. ")
(comment CatalystReactantsComplex "The collection of chemical objects that consist of a #$BiocatalyticMolecule and the chemical reactants involved in a reaction for which that molecule is the #$catalyst.  Such objects are intermediate outputs of catalytic reactions -- the catalyst binds to the reactants, resulting in the complex, which then breaks apart, freeing the catalyist and the products of the reaction.")
(comment EnzymeSubstrateComplex "The collection of chemical objects that consist of a #$EnzymeMolecule and the chemical reactants involved in a reaction for which that molecule is the #$catalyst.  Such objects are intermediate outputs of catalytic reactions -- the catalyst binds to the reactants, resulting in the complex, which then breaks apart, freeing the catalyist and the products of the reaction.")
(comment RibozymeReactantsComplex "The collection of chemical objects that consist of a #$RibozymeMolecule and the chemical reactants involved in a reaction for which that molecule is the #$catalyst.  Such objects are intermediate outputs of catalytic reactions -- the catalyst binds to the reactants, resulting in the complex, which then breaks apart, freeing the catalyist and the products of the reaction.")
(comment CatalysisOutputTypeByCatalystType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets CatalystReactantsComplex into sub-collections based on the type of catalyst.")
(comment CatalyticBindingEvent "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectBindingEvent, this is the first step of #$Catalysis, wherein the #$catalyst of the over-arching chemical reaction binds to the objects that are the #$chemicalReactants in that reaction, producing an instance of #$CatalystReactantsComplex.")
(comment RibozymeBindsToReactants "One of two main classes of #$CatalyticBindingEvent.  Instances are bindings in which the #$catalyst of the over-arching chemical reaction is an instance of #$RibozymeMolecule.")
(comment EnzymeBindsToSubstrate "One of two main classes of #$CatalyticBindingEvent.  Instances are bindings in which the #$catalyst of the over-arching chemical reaction is an instance of #$EnzymeMolecule.")
(comment CatalyticBindingEventTypeByCatalystType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$CatalyticBindingEvent into sub-collections based on the type of catalist.")
(comment CatalystReleaseOfChemicalProducts "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectUnbindingEvent, this is the final step of #$Catalysis, where the #$CatalystReactantsComplex breaks apart into the the products of the over-arching #$ChemicalReaction and the #$catalyst of that reaction.")
(comment CatalyticReaction "The sub-collection of #$ChemicalReaction whose instances involve a #$catalyst.")
(comment Sucrase "A collection of enzymes capable of acting as a catalyst in the hydrolysis of #$Sucrose.")
(comment CatalysisTypeByCatalystType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$Catalysis into sub-collections based on the type of catalist.")
(comment EnzymaticCatalysis "An instance of #$CatalysisTypeByCatalystType, this is the sub-collection of #$Catalysis where the catalyst of the over-arching reaction is an instance of #$EnzymeMolecule.")
(comment RibozymalCatalysis "An instance of #$CatalysisTypeByCatalystType, this is the sub-collection of #$Catalysis where the catalyst of the over-arching reaction is an instance of #$RibozymeMolecule.")
(comment Catalysis "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction in which an instance of #$BiocatalyticMolecule facilitates a chemical reaction by binding to the prospective reactants, forcing them to be in close proximity.  The biocatalytic molecule that \"hosts\" the reaction is said to be the #$catalyst in that reaction, and the reaction is thus an instance of #$CatalyticReaction.")
(comment FullSpectrumElectromagneticEmission "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmittingAWave.  Each instance is an event in which #$ElectromagneticRadiation is emitted, and furthermore, radiation of all or very nearly all #$wavelengths are emitted.  For example, #$TheSun does so constantly (at least from the human temporal perspective).")
(comment radiationEmitted "A #$BinarySituationPredicate that relates an instance of (#$WaveEmissionFn #$ElectromagneticRadiation) to all #$ElectromagneticRadiation emitted therein.  <code>(#$radiationEmitted EMISSION RADIATION)</code> means that <code>RADIATION</code> is an event that is caused by (i.e. set into motion) in <code>EMISSION</code>.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationTransmission "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.  Instances of #$ElectromagneticRadiationTransmission are events in which EM radiation propagates through matter. ")
(comment FluidAbsorptionEvent "A specialization of #$AbsorptionEvent.  Instances are events in which some quantity of fluid enters some #$PartiallyTangible thing.   For example, events in which gaseous #$Oxygen is absorbed into an animla's bloodstream, and events in which a #$Sponge-CleaningImplement absorbs (#$LiquidFn #$Water).")
(comment AbsorptionEvent "A specialization of #$TransferIn. Instances are events in which things are taken into some #$PartiallyTangible thing.  The thing taken in may be another #$PartiallyTangible, such as a liquid or gas, or a non-tangible thing such as a quantity of energy.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption "A specialization of #$AbsorptionEvent.  Instances are events in which some quantity #$ElectromagneticRadiation enters some #$PartiallyTangible thing.  When a quantity of energy - say, a #$Photon - is absorbed by matter, that bit of radiation is missing from what is reflected or transmitted as the radiation strikes the matter.  Rather than being destroyed, the energy is converted to a different form: often, an increase in the excitation state of electrons in the matter. ")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationReflection "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Instances are events in which some quantity #$ElectromagneticRadiation, after traveling in a particular direction so as to strike some piece of matter, \"bounces\" off the surface of that matter (or off irregularities below the surface of the matter) in a new direction.  When the matter encountered forms a smooth reflective surface, reflecting can occur in a specular fashion, so that all of the outgoing radiation travels in the same, predictable direction.  This allows patterns of intensity and wavelength present in the incoming radiation to be preserved in the outgoing radiation, as when an image is reflected in a mirror.  When the surface is rough, or when features below the surface are reflective and oriented in a variety of directions (e.g., edges of cells in organic matter, or edges of crystals, etc.), radiation will be reflected in a diffuse fashion.")
(comment SpecularReflection "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationReflection.  Instances are events in which some quantity of #$ElectromagneticRadiation, after traveling in a single direction so as to strike some piece of matter having a smooth, reflective surface, \"bounces\" off the surface of that matter. All of the outgoing radiation travels in the same, predictable direction.  This allows patterns of intensity and wavelength present in the incoming radiation to be preserved in the outgoing radiation, as when an image is reflected in a mirror.  In this type of reflection, the angle that the incident (incoming) radiation makes to the surface is the same as the angle that the reflected radiation makes to the surface, except it is on the other side of the \"surface normal\" (a vector exactly perpendicular to the surface).  The surface normal, the vector of the incident radiation and the vector of the outgoing radiation are all in the same plane.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationStrikingMatter "This is the collection of physical events in which some quantity of #$ElectromagneticRadiation meets with matter.  When this occurs, the EM radiation is either transmitted (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationTransmission), reflected (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationReflection) or absorbed (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption).  It is common for a given sample of physical stuff to transmit part of the radiation, reflect part of it, and absorb part of it all at the same time, unless the radiation under consideration is an indivisible amount (a #$Photon).")
(comment electromagneticEnergyAmount "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiation to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$electromagneticEnergyAmount EM QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy had by <code>EM</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment AbsorptionSpectrum "A specialization of #$Spectrum.  Each instance of #$AbsorptionSpectrum is a distribution over the frequencies of the #$ElectromagneticSpectrum of the fraction, at each frequency, of incident radiation absorbed by a material.  An instance of #$AbsorptionSpectrum may be a characteristic of a particular sample of material.  It may also be characteristic of a collection of samples, all of which have the same chemical makeup.")
(comment ChlorophyllA "Instances are portions of #$ChlorophyllA, a #$PhotosyntheticPigment produced by #$PhotosyntheticPlants, #$BlueGreenAlgae, and #$Algae.  Molecules of Chlorophyll A differ from those of #$ChlorophyllB in having a #$FormylGroup where molecules of #$ChlorophyllB have a #$MethylGroup attached to their #$PorphyrinRing.")
(comment PorphyrinRing "Instances of #$PorphyrinRing are #$MolecularComponents of many biochemically important compounds.  Four #$Nitrogen atoms appear near the center of the ring, and can bond metal ions. ")
(comment ChlorophyllB "Instances are portions of #$ChlorophyllB, a #$PhotosyntheticPigment produced mostly by #$PhotosyntheticPlants.  Molecules of Chlorophyll B differ from those of #$ChlorophyllA in having a #$MethylGroup where molecules of #$ChlorophyllA have a #$FormylGroup attached to their #$PorphyrinRing.")
(comment AbsorptionSpectrumFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction, used to refer to the #$AbsorptionSpectrum of a type of chemical species or chemical mixture.  (#$AbsorptionSpectrumFn CHEM-TYPE) denotes the instance of #$AbsorptionSpectrum which describes the fraction of incident #$ElectromagneticRadiation that a sample of CHEM-TYPE will absorb (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption) for each #$wavelength of radiation in the ElectromagneticSpectrum.")
(comment absorptionMaxima "(#$absorptionMaxima SPECT WAVELEN) states that a peak in absorptance occurs in SPECT at the wavelength WAVELEN. ")
(comment EnergyCouplingProcess "A specialization of #$BiochemicalProcess, this is the collection of events in which an instance of #$ExergonicReaction provides energy for an instance of #$EndergonicReaction.")
(comment NLSectionHeader "The collection of all headers of sections in textual works.")
(comment someTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithMinCardinality "<code>(#$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithCardinality SIT-TYPE COL ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves <code>N</code> or more instances of <code>COL</code> playing <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment someTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithCardinality "<code>(#$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithCardinality SIT-TYPE COL ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves <code>N</code> instances of <code>COL</code> playing <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment SituationTypeRelation-Actors-TypeCardinalityAndRoles "The specialization of #$SituationTypeRelation-Actors-TypeAndRoles whose instances are predicates that can be used to represent the cardinalities of types of role-players in a given situation-type.")
(comment ChemicalObjectTypeBySharedStructuralFeature "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules that share some structural feature.  Collections such that all instances have the same chemical formula and structure are one special case, and they will be instances of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies, a spec of #$ChemicalObjectTypeBySharedStructuralFeature.  Other instance of this class include #$PorphyrinMolecule, all instance of which have a #$PorphyrinRing, and (#$MoleculeFn #$Aldehyde), all instances of which contain a #$FormylGroup.")
(disjointWith EnzymeMolecule PorphyrinMolecule)
(comment PorphyrinMolecule "A collection of #$Molecules.  An instance of #$PorphyrinMolecule is an organic molecule having as a #$molecularSubComponents at least one #$PorphyrinRing.  Heme, the pigment in #$RedBloodCells, is one example of a #$PorphyrinMolecule.")
(comment PeptideMoleculeTypeByPeptideFamily "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY of #$PeptideMolecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules derived by transcribing (see #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and optionally translating (see #$Translation-RNAToProtein) a segment of DNA (an instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit) which is a physical instantiation (see #$instantiationOfGene-GIS) of an instance of some #$GeneTypeByProductFamily. Note that instances of each PEPTIDE-MOL-FAMILY are actual #$PeptideMolecules, but they are not necessarily all identical.  Sources of variation are as follows: a) Instances of this collection are collections of molecules created in the cells of organisms belonging to different species.  They are grouped together because they share most of their amino acid sequences and are presumably descended from common \"ancestor peptides\". b) Alternative splicing occurs frequently.  This means that the same segment of DNA can produce RNA that is spliced (see #$RNASplicingProcess) in different ways to produce messenger RNAs that code for very different proteins.  However, even within a single species, each of these splice variants shares large subregions containing identical amino acid sequences.")
(comment GeneTypeByProductFamily "A collection of collections of #$GeneticInformationStructures. Each instance GIS-TYPE of this collection is often called a \"gene family.\"  Genes that share nucelotide sequences are often grouped into families, and these familes can and do cross species lines.  If the genes in an instance of #$GeneTypeByProductFamily encode peptides, there will be a corresponding instance of #$PeptideMoleculeTypeByPeptideFamily that those peptide molecules are instances of.  ")
(comment InducedFit-MolecularConfiguration "A specialization of #$Enclosing-Configuration, this is the collection of configurations of molecules in which an #$EnzymeMolecule has enclosed its substrates as a result of a #$ProteinConformationChangeEvent that takes place as a part of #$Catalysis.")
(comment someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithCardinality "<code>(#$someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSituationTypeWithCardinality SIT-TYPE COL ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves <code>N</code> instances of <code>COL</code> playing <code>ROLE</code>, and nothing other than instances of <code>COL</code> play that role.")
(comment Xanthophyll "#$Xanthophylls are a group of photosynthetic accessory pigments synthesized by plants that have a yellow hue.")
(comment PhotosyntheticAccessoryPigment "A specialization of #$PhotosyntheticPigment.  Accessory pigments help to capture the energy of light to drive the light reactions (see #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis), but they do not participate directly in the splitting of water that #$ChlorophyllA permits.")
(comment Carotenoid "Instances are portions of #$Carotenoid, a #$PhotosyntheticAccessoryPigment produced mostly by #$PhotosyntheticPlants, #$Algae, some #$Bacterium[a], and some #$Fungus[i].  Carotenoids are not a single chemical compound, but a family of compounds that tend to have a yellow or orange color.")
(comment EnzymeFoldingAroundSubstrate "The subcollection of #$ProteinConformationChangeEvent whose instances are events in which an instance of #$EnzymeMolecule changes shape so as to envelop it substrate into its #$bindingSite.  The result (see #$eventOutcomes) is an induced fit (see #$InducedFit-MolecularConfiguration) that provides optimal conditions for the substrate components to react.")
(comment someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithCardinality "<code>(#$someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithCardinality SIT-TYPE COL SUB-SIT-TYPE ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves sub-situations of type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> such that <code>N</code> instances of <code>COL</code> playing <code>ROLE</code>, and nothing other than instances of <code>COL</code> play that role.")
(comment someTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithCardinality "<code>(#$someAndOnlyTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithCardinality SIT-TYPE COL SUB-SIT-TYPE ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves sub-situations of type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> such that <code>N</code> instances of <code>COL</code> playing <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment someTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithMinCardinality "<code>(#$someTypePlaysRoleInSubSituationTypeWithMinCardinality SIT-TYPE COL SUB-SIT-TYPE ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves sub-situations of type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> such that <code>N</code> or more instances of <code>COL</code> play <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment conditionTypeAffectsOrganismsOfType "This predicate relates kinds of physiological conditions to the kinds of organisms that it can affect.  (#$conditionTypeAffectsOrganismsOfType COND-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that instances of ORG-TYPE are capable of being the bodily doers in conditions of type COND-TYPE.")
(comment conditionTypeOnlyAffectsOrganismsOfType "(#$conditionTypeOnlyAffectsOrganismsOfType COND-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that instances of the #$PhysiologicalConditionType COND-TYPE *only* affect instances of the #$OrganismClassificationType ORG-TYPE: i.e., if (#$isa COND COND-TYPE) and (#$bodilyDoer COND DOER) it follows that (isa DOER ORG-TYPE).")
(comment narrowestTypeOfOrganismExclusivelyAffected "(#$narrowestTypeOfOrganismExclusivelyAffected COND-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that ORG-TYPE is the narrowest collection (collection with the smallest extension) for which (#$conditionTypeOnlyAffectsOrganismsOfType COND-TYPE ORG-TYPE) is true.")
(comment Fuel "The collection of things that serve primarily to store energy, for use in work.  This is a highly context-sensitive notion of \"fuel\" -- ATP might be considered a fuel in the context of #$Biochemistry, but in the context of the the automotive industry only combustable fuels, such as gasoline, might count as fuels.")
(comment RedLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 620 to 740 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be red but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment SpectralColor "The collection of all colors, the perception of which is triggered by light of a single #$wavelength.")
(comment NonSpectralColor "The collection of all colors, the perception of which is triggered by light of a mixture of wavelengths.")
(disjointWith NonSpectralColor SpectralColor)
(comment SpectralColorFn "A #$UnaryFunction.  (#$SpectralColorFn WAVELENGTH) denotes the pure, #$SpectralColor, the perception of which is triggered by light of the single #$wavelength, WAVELENGTH.")
(comment wavelengthCorrespondsToColor "(#$wavelengthCorrespondsToColor WAVELEN COLOR) states that quantities of #$VisibleLight consisting of the pure #$wavelength WAVELEN will be perceived as the #$SpectralColor, COLOR.")
(disjointWith SpectralColor (CollectionDifferenceFn Color SpectralColor))
(comment OrangeLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 590 to 620 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be orange but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment YellowLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 570 to 590 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be yellow but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment BlueLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 450 to 490 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be blue but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment GreenLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 490 to 560 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be green but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment VioletLight "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight with a wavelength in the range of 400 to 450 nanometers.  Instances which comprise a single wavelength have a #$SpectralColor, but instances which comprise a mix of wavelengths in this range will still appear to be violet but have a #$NonSpectralColor.")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationInteractingWithMatter "This is the collection of physical event scripts in which some quantity of #$ElectromagneticRadiation propagates, meets with a portion matter, and variously leaves that sample or is absorbed.")
(disjointWith Living Metabolism)
(disjointWith ChemicalInteraction Living)
(comment physiologicallyDoneBy "<code>(#$physiologicallyDoneBy EVT BLO)</code> means that the instance <code>BLO</code> of #$BiologicalLivingObject is the non-deliberate doer of the event <code>EVT</code>, a biological process.")
(comment metabolismOf "An instance of #$ActorSlot that relates an instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject to its #$Metabolism.")
(comment TheATPCycle "The cycle in which hydrolysis of ATP leads to the release of energy, sufficient to power the phosphorylation of ADP, which results in ATP that is available for hydrolysis.")
(comment IncidentRadiationIsSumOfTransmitted-Reflected-Absorbed "In an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationInteractingWithMatter, all incident radiation is either transmitted, reflected, or absorbed. Therefore the amount of energy incident in the event is equal to the sum of that transmitted, reflected, and absorbed. ")
(comment SingleIndirectFocalObjectFormula "The collection of mathematical formulas that express some physical principle #$PhysicalPrinciple via values on some quantity slots where each subject of each of the slots is related to a single object that is not directly mentioned in the formula.  For example, the amount of energy released in an #$ExergonicReaction is equal to the amount used in an #$EndergonicReaction plus that lost as heat.  In this formula, it is assumed the values for the energy quantities are from events that are all subevents of the same #$EnergyCouplingProcess.  ")
(comment incidentEnergyAmount "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationStrikingMatter to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$incidentEnergyAmount STRIKE QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy striking an object in <code>STRIKE</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment IncidentEnergyAmountFn "(#$IncidentEnergyAmountFn STRIKE) denotes the amount of energy incident on the object in STRIKE, an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationStrikingMatter.")
(comment reflectedEnergyAmount "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationReflection to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$reflectedEnergyAmount REF QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy reflected in <code>REF</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment ReflectedEnergyAmountFn "(#$ReflectedEnergyAmountFn REF) denotes the amount of energy reflected in REF, an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationReflection.")
(comment absorbedEnergyAmount "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$absorbedEnergyAmount ABS QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy absorbed in <code>ABS</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment AbsorbedEnergyAmountFn "(#$AbsorbedEnergyAmountFn ABS) denotes the amount of energy reflected in ABS, an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption.")
(comment transmittedEnergyAmount "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationTransmission to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$transmittedEnergyAmount TRANS QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy transmitted through an object in <code>trans</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.")
(comment TransmittedEnergyAmountFn "(#$TransmittedEnergyAmountFn TRANS) denotes the amount of energy transmitted through the object in TRANS, an instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationTransmission.")
(comment indirectInstanceForQuantityBasedFormula "<code>(#$indirectInstanceForQuantityBasedFormula QBF INSTANCE)</code> means that <code>INSTANCE</code> is a term that, while not being mentioned in the formula <code>QBF</code>, is an import part of its context.  Specifically, for <code>QBF</code> to hold of a set of quantities in the world, those quantities must bear some relation to <code>INSTANCE</code>.  If these constraints are binary, they can be stated with the predicates #$formulaTermRelationFromIndirectInstance and #$formulaTermRelationToIndirectInstance.")
(comment formulaTermRelationFromIndirectInstance "#$formulaTermRelationFromIndirectInstance is used to state additional constraints on #$QuantityBasedFormulas which are #$SingleIndirectFocalObjectFormulas.  <code>(#$formulaTermRelationFromIndirectInstance QBF THING SLOT)</code> means that, where <code>X</code> is the indirect focal object of <code>QBF</code> (given by <code>(#$indirectInstanceForQuantityBasedFormula QBF X)</code>), <code>(SLOT X THING)</code> is a constraint that must be true for the formula to hold of a set of quantities.")
(comment formulaTermRelationToIndirectInstance "#$formulaTermRelationToIndirectInstance is used to state additional constraints on #$QuantityBasedFormulas which are #$SingleIndirectFocalObjectFormulas.  <code>(#$formulaTermRelationToIndirectInstance QBF THING SLOT)</code> means that, where <code>X</code> is the indirect focal object of <code>QBF</code> (given by <code>(#$indirectInstanceForQuantityBasedFormula QBF X)</code>), <code>(SLOT THING X)</code> is a constraint that must be true for the formula to hold of a set of quantities.")
(comment wavelength "(#$wavelength WAVE LENGTH) means that the #$WavePropagation WAVE consists only of waves having the length LENGTH.  LENGTH is a #$Distance measuring one complete wave in a #$WavePropagation event.")
(comment COITypeDerivedFromFn "<code>(#$COITypeDerivedFromFn COI)</code> denotes the collection of COIs that are near-variants of <code>COI</code>, including <code>COI</code> itself.")
(comment cOITypeDerivedFrom "<code>(#$cOITypeDerivedFrom COI COI-TYPE)</code> means that <code>COI-TYPE</code> is the collection of COIs that are near-variants of <code>COI</code>, including <code>COI</code> itself.")
(disjointWith Section-PCW TableOfContents-PCW)
(comment TableOfContents-PCW "The collection of all instances of #$TextualPCW that are tables of contents.")
(comment IrradianceDistribution "Each instance of #$IrradianceDistribution is a function from wavelengths (instances of #$Distance) to amounts of energy per unit time per unit area (instances of #$Irradiance).  Each such function describes, for some source of #$ElectromagneticRadiation and some surface, the amount of energy per area per time of each wavelength that impinges upon the surface.  ")
(comment Irradiance "A specialization #$Rate and #$PhysicalQuantity (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Irradiance is an amount of energy per some unit of time, per unit area.  #$Irradiances are usually characterized for a particular #$wavelength of #$ElectromagneticRadiation, coming from some source and incident on a surface.")
(disjointWith Distance Irradiance)
(disjointWith Speed Irradiance)
(disjointWith Power Irradiance)
(disjointWith Voltage Irradiance)
(disjointWith Area Voltage)
(disjointWith Frequency Irradiance)
(disjointWith FlowRate Irradiance)
(disjointWith AngularAccelerationRate Irradiance)
(disjointWith Acceleration Irradiance)
(comment Distribution "This represents the most general statistical distribution.")
(comment IrradianceDistributionFn "An #$FunctionDenotingFunction.  <code>(#$IrradianceDistributionFn SOURCE SURFACE) </code> denotes a function that maps from wavelengths to the #$Irradiance of that wavelength of radiation coming from <code>SOURCE</code> and indident on <code>SURFACE</code>.  For example, the value of ((#$IrradianceDistributionFn #$TheSun #$Mesopause-PlanetEarth) ((#$Nano #$Meter) 550)) - the #$Irradiance from the sun to an area in the upper reaches of the earth's atmosphere, of light at a wavelength of 550 nm - is about ((#$PerFn #$Watt #$SquareMeter) 1000).")
(comment irradianceByWavelengthFromSourceToDestinationFunction "A predicate corresponding to the function #$IrradianceDistributionFn.  <code>(#$irradianceByWavelengthFromSourceToDestinationFunction SOURCE DESTINATION FUNCTION</code> states that <code>FUNCTION</code> is a function from wavelength to #$Irradiance, and describes how much energy per unit time, per unit area is emitted from <code>SOURCE</code> and is incident on <code>DESTINATION</code>.")
(comment resultArgIsa "(#$resultArgIsa FUNCTION INTEGER COLLECTION) means that the result of applying the instance of #$RelationDenotingFunction FUNCTION to a series of arguments for which FUNCTION is defined will result in an instance REL of #$Relation such that (#$argIsa REL INTEGER COLLECTION).")
(comment irradianceFromSourceToDestinationAtWavelength "<code>(#$irradianceFromSourceToDestinationAtWavelength SOURCE DESTINATION WAVELENGTH IRRADIANCE)</code> states that <code>IRRADIANCE</code> is the amount of energy of <code>WAVELENGTH</code> emitted from <code>SOURCE</code> which is incident on <code>DESTINATION</code> per unit time, per unit area.  ")
(comment Sunlight "The collection of all sunlight. #$Sunlight is #$VisibleLight emitted by #$TheSun.")
(comment SunShining "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$EmittingAWave.  Each instance is an event in which #$ElectromagneticRadiation is emitted by #$TheSun.  Given any time interval subsumed by the existince of #$TheSun, exactly one such event exists and is #$cotemporal with the interval.  Each such event is one of the #$subEvents of #$SunShining-CompleteDuration.")
(comment waveEmitted "This predicate, a specialization of causes-EventEvent (qq.v.), relates a wave emission to the wave emitted.  <code>(#$waveEmitted EMIT WAVE)</code> means that <code>WAVE</code> begins because of <code>EMIT</code>.")
(comment PreparingABiologicalSampleForStudy "The collection of events in which a sample of biological material is prepared for study.  Examples include gram-staining bacteria and freezing cells for analysis.")
(comment FreezeFracture "A specialization of #$PreparingABiologicalSampleForStudy in which a biological sample is subjected to #$Cryofixation then cracked open, so that its internal structure can be observed.")
(comment PhotonEmission "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Emission.  Each instance is an event in which a #$Photon is emitted as a result of an #$Atom or #$Molecule transitioning from a higher energy state to a lower energy state.  The difference between the two states determines the energy (and thus frequency and #$wavelength) of the #$Photon so produced.  Because each type of chemical species can assume only particular energy states, each species has a characteristic set of frequencies it emits.")
(disjointWith Sunlight ArtificialLighting)
(comment SeymourJonathanSinger "A famous cell biologist and recipient of the 1959 Guggenheim Fellowship for Molecular and Cellular Biology.")
(comment GarthLNicolson "A famous chemist and molecular biologist, honored by the United States military for his work with veterans.")
(comment CellBiologist "The collection of instances of #$Biologist who focus on #$CellBiology.")
(comment HughDavson "A famous biologist known for his work with #$JamesFredericDanielli, with whom he developed the Davson-Danielli model of cellular membranes (see #$Davson-DanielliModel).")
(comment JamesFredericDanielli "A famous biologist known for his work with #$HughDavson, with whom he developed the Davson-Danielli model of cellular membranes (see #$Davson-DanielliModel).")
(comment WavePropagationTypeByEmitterType "A collection of collections.  Each instance WP of  #$WavePropagationTypeByEmitterType is a specialization of #$WavePropagation such that instances of WP are all emitted by an instance of some type of emitter with consistent emission characteristics (e.g., an A440 tuning fork, an #$Atom of #$Iron, or a specific model of #$LightEmittingDiode).")
(comment waveTypeOfEmitterType "<code>(#$waveTypeOfEmitterType WAVE-TYPE EMITTER-TYPE)</code> states that <code>WAVE-TYPE</code> is the collection to which all instances of #$WavePropagation emitted by instances of <code>EMITTER-TYPE</code> belong.")
(comment SolarRadiation "Instances of #$SolarRadiation are wave propagation events and include any #$ElectromagneticRadiation emitted by #$TheSun, whether those events are the propagation of a subset of the wavelengths the sun emits, or are instances that include all wavelengths emitted.")
(comment FullMixtureRadiationTypeByEmitterType "A collection of collections.  Each instance <code>FMRT</code> of  #$FullMixtureRadiationTypeByEmitterType is a specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation such that instances of <code>FMRT</code> are all emitted by the same type of emitter (and are thus specializations of some instance of #$WavePropagationTypeByEmitterType), and that furthermore each instance of <code>FMRT</code> consists of the complete mixture of wavelengths so emitted.  The quantity of each wavelength included in <code>FMRT</code> is described by <code>FMRT</code>'s emission spectrum (see #$EmissionDistribution).")
(comment FullMixtureRadiationTypeByEmitterType "A collection of collections.  Each instance <code>FMRT</code> of  #$FullMixtureRadiationTypeByEmitterType is a specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation such that instances of <code>FMRT</code> are all emitted by the same type of emitter (and are thus specializations of some instance of #$WavePropagationTypeByEmitterType), and that furthermore each instance of <code>FMRT</code> consists of the complete mixture of wavelengths so emitted.  Collections of radiation filtered by passing through matter (e.g., the atmosphere) are typically excluded from this collection.  The quantity of each wavelength included in <code>FMRT</code> is described by <code>FMRT</code>'s emission spectrum (see #$EmissionDistribution).")
(comment FullMixtureOfWavelengthsFn "<code>(#$FullMixtureOfWavelengthsFn WAVE-TYPE)</code> denotes the specialization of <code>WAVE-TYPE</code> such that each instance of (#$FullMixtureOfWavelengthsFn WAVE-TYPE) consists of the full range of wavelengths possible given the medium through which propagation has hitherto occurred.  For radiation propagating through a vacuum, originating from a particular emitter, the distribution of wavelengths present will be unchanged and (#$FullMixtureOfWavelengthsFn WAVE-TYPE) will be an instance of #$FullMixtureRadiationTypeByEmitterType.  ")
(comment fullMixtureOfWavelengths "<code>(#$fullMixtureOfWavelengths WAVE-TYPE MIXTURE-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>MIXTURE-TYPE</code> as the specialization of <code>WAVE-TYPE</code> that includes all wavelengths that are possible given the makeup of the originally emitted radiation and the medium through which the radiation has hitherto passed.")
(comment resultIsaWhenArgIsa "<code>(#$resultIsaWhenArgIsa FN COLL NUM TYPE)</code> means that when the <code>NUM</code>th argument to a well-formed application of the function <code>FN</code> is an instance of the collection <code>TYPE</code>, that application of <code>FN</code> will denote an instance of <code>COLL</code>.")
(comment TheoryAboutTheStructureOfThePlasmaMembrane "A specialization of #$TheoryAboutBiology, this is the collection of all theories about the structure of the #$CellMembrane.")
(comment theoryIterations "<code>(#$theoryIterations THEORY VERSION)</code> means that <code>VERSION</code> is a version of the instance <code>THEORY</code> of #$EvolvingTheory.")
(comment currentTheoryIteration "<code>(#$currentTheoryIteration THEORY VERSION)</code> identifies <code>VERSION</code> as the current, up-to-date version of the instance <code>THEORY</code> of #$EvolvingTheory.")
(comment TheoryAboutTheStructureOfTheAtom "An instance of #$StructuralHypothesisTypeByStructureType, this is the collection of theories describing the structure of the #$Atom.")
(comment StructuralHypothesisTypeByStructureType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$ScientificTheory into sub-collections, each of which is a collection of (potentially conflicting) theories that purport to describe the structure of some hard to observe object-type or phenomenon.")
(comment theoryPrecursors "<code>(#$theoryPrecursors NEW-THEORY OLD-THEORY)</code> means that the instance <code>OLD-THEORY</code> of #$PhilosophicalTheory is a \"theory of X\" that was under consideration in the relevant field of study prior to the introduction of <code>NEW-THEORY</code> a newer \"theory of X.\"")
(comment Davson-DanielliModel "An instance of #$TheoryAboutTheStructureOfThePlasmaMembrane, predominant from about 1935 to 1972.")
(comment theoryTypeImpactsMt "A predicate used to adjust the Microtheory hierarchy on the fly, in response to advances in world knowledge.  <code>(#$theoryTypeImpactsMt TYPE MT)</code> means that theories of type <code>TYPE</code>, if true, would extend the knowledge in <code>MT</code>, an instance of #$Microtheory.  From this, knowledge that the #$hypothesisAcceptanceStatus of a theory is currently #$AcceptedHypothesis can support the forward derivation of a #$genlMt link from <code>MT</code> to that theory.")
(comment commonSubEventTypes "(#$commonSubEventTypes EVENT-TYPE-1 EVENT-TYPE-2) means that events of EVENT-TYPE-1 often or commonly have EVENT-TYPE-2 as subevents (#$subEvents).")
(comment commonDeviceTypeUsed "(#$commonDeviceTypeUsed EVENT-TYPE DEVICE-TYPE) means that events of EVENT-TYPE-1 often or commonly have instances of DEVICE-TYPE as an #$instrument-Generic.
")
(comment constituentWavelengths "<code>(#$constituentWavelengths WAVE LENGTH)</code> means that the #$WavePropagation <code>WAVE</code> includes waves having the length <code>LENGTH</code>.  <code>LENGTH</code>is a #$Distance measuring one complete wave in a #$WavePropagation event.  Where <code>WAVE</code> has only one wavelength, (#$wavelength WAVE LENGTH) also holds.")
(comment missingWavelengths "<code>(#$missingWavelengths WAVE LENGTH)</code> means that the #$WavePropagation <code>WAVE</code> does not include waves having the length <code>LENGTH</code>.  ")
(comment eventTypeObjectRoleSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an event type to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$eventTypeObjectRoleSentence EVENT-TYPE SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact about the role players in EVENT-TYPE. ")
(comment eventTypeSubEventTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an event type to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$eventTypeSubEventTypeSentence EVENT-TYPE SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact about the sub-event types in EVENT-TYPE. ")
(comment commonLocationTypeOfEventType "<code>(#$commonLocationTypeOfEventType EVENT-TYPE LOC-TYPE)</code> means that it is common to find events of EVENT-TYPE occurring (#$eventOccursAt) at instances of LOC-TYPE.")
(comment eventTypeLocationTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates an event type to a #$CycLSentence-Assertible.  (#$eventTypeSubEventTypeSentence EVENT-TYPE SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a fact about the the locations types at which instances of EVENT-TYPE occur. ")
(comment eventTypePlannedFor "(#$eventTypePlannedFor PLANNING EVENT-TYPE) means that during the planning event PLANNING, the planners are developing plans that will, if successful, result in an instance of EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment planningEventFullySuccessfulForAgent "(#$planningEventFullySuccessfulForAgent PLANNING AGENT) holds just in case PLANNING was an instance of #$Planning that was fully successful for agent (i.e. it resulted in a #$Plan that was successfully executed).")
(comment planProduced "(#$planProduced PLANNING PLAN) means that during PLANNING, the plan PLAN was produced.")
(comment theoryNthIteration "<code>(#$theoryNthIteration THEORY ITERATION N)</code> identifies <code>ITERATION</code> as the <code>N</code>th iteration of <code>THEORY</code>, an instance of #$EvolvingTheory.")
(comment EvolvingTheory "The collection of all instances of #$PhilosophicalTheory whose propositional contents change over time, in response to new data.")
(comment AnalysisOfTypeFn "<code>(#$AnalysisOfTypeFn COLL)</code> denotes the specialization of #$AnalyzingSomething in which instances of <code>COLL</code> are studied.")
(comment analysisTypeOfType "The predicate that corresponds to #$AnalysisOfTypeFn, <code>(#$analysisTypeOfType ANALYSIS-TYPE COLL)</code> identifies <code>ANALYSIS-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$AnalyzingSomething in which the thing studied is an instance of <code>COLL</code>.")
(comment evidentiallySupportsTheory "<code>(#$evidentiallySupportsTheory EVIDENCE THEORY)</code> means that <code>EVIDENCE</code> is evidence in favor of <code>THEORY</code>, an instance of #$PhilosophicalTheory.")
(comment functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType "<code>(#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> there are, by default, instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> that are #$properPhysicalParts of the whole and play an important role in the proper functioning of that whole.  <code>(#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code> does not entail <code>(#$essentialPartTypes WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE)</code>, but is entailed by it (via #$criticalPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType).")
(comment evidentiallyConsistentWithTheory "<code>(#$evidentiallyConsistentWithTheory EVIDENCE THEORY)</code> means that <code>EVIDENCE</code> is evidence that does not conflict with <code>THEORY</code>, an instance of #$PhilosophicalTheory.")
(comment GenQuantFromRealFn "A function from a #$Real0-1 to an instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional, <code>(#$GenQuantFromRealFn REAL)</code> denotes the generalized quantifier <code>QUANT</code> such that <code>(QUANT COL1 COL2)</code> holds if and only if the percentage of COL1 are also COL2 is <code>REAL</code>.")
(comment genQuantRealBasis "The predicate that corresponds to the function #$GenQuantFromRealFn, <code>(#$genQuantRealBasis QUANTIFIER REAL)</code> identifies <code>QUANTIFIER</code> as the instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier-Proportional such that<code>(QUANTIFIER COL1 COL2)</code> holds if and only if the percentage of COL1 are also COL2 is <code>REAL</code>.")
(comment objectRelativeComposition "<code>(#$objectRelativeComposition OBJECT TYPE SPEC QUANTIFIER)</code> means that the relative composition of <code>OBJECT</code> with respect to instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are also instances of <code>SPEC</code> is expressible in terms of <code>QUANTIFIER</code>.")
(comment Cryofixation "A method of rapidly freezing biological samples by subjecting them to temperatures in at or below that of the boiling point of nitrogen.")
(comment GorterAndGrendel "The research team of #$EvertGorter and #$FrancoisGrendel who posited the theory that cell membranes are phospholipid bilayers.")
(comment FrancoisGrendel "The famous dutch biochemist who, along with  #$EvertGorter hypothesized that cell membranes are phospholipid bilayers.")
(comment EvertGorter "The famous dutch biochemist who, along with #$FrancoisGrendel hypothesized that cell membranes are phospholipid bilayers.")
(comment primaryDeveloperOfTheory "A specialization of #$contributorToTheory, <code>(#$primaryDeveloperOfTheory AGENT THEORY)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is the main contributer to <code>THEORY</code>, a scientific theory.")
(comment DavsonAndDanielli "The research team consisting of #$HughDavson and #$JamesFredericDanielli that proposed the so-called \"sandwich\" model of the cell membrane as a phospholipid bilayer surrounded by a layer of globular proteins (see #$GlobularProteinMolecule) on each side (see #$Davson-DanielliModel).")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiationFilteringProcess "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$Filtering-Generic.  Each instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationFilteringProcess is an event in which #$ElectromagneticRadiation passes through a #$PartiallyTangible.  Radiation that exits on the other side will typically have a different #$IrradianceDistribution than the entering radiation, because some #$wavelengths have been absorbed (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption) by the filter.  This collection includes both intentional filtering, as might be done to produce particular colors of light to illuminate actors on stage, or to project an image on a screen, as well as filtering that happens as a result of natural processes such as the filtering of #$Sunlight by #$TheEarthsAtmosphere.")
(comment AtmosphericLightPath "Instances are portions of a planet's atmosphere relative to some region on a #$Planet's surface, such that light incident on that region and coming from (one of) the planet's #$Sun had to pass through that portion of atmosphere.  Where an #$Atmosphere consists of multiple #$AtmosphericLayers, each instance of #$AtmosphericLightPath will include a portion of each layer. ")
(comment FilteringOfSolarRadiationByEarthsAtmosphere "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiationFilteringProcess.  Each instance of #$FilteringOfSolarRadiationByEarthsAtmosphere is an event in which some instance of #$SolarRadiation passes through a portion of #$TheEarthsAtmosphere.  Radiation that penetrates will typically have a different #$IrradianceDistribution than the entering radiation, because some #$wavelengths have been absorbed (see #$ElectromagneticRadiationAbsorption) by the molecules that make up the atmosphere.  The deeper radiation penetrates, the more is absorbed. ")
(comment filteringInput "The predicate #$filteringInput relates an instance of #$Filtering-Generic to the input to the filtering process.  <code>(#$filteringInput EVENT THING)</code> means that in the instance of #$Filtering-Generic, <code>EVENT</code>, <code>THING</code> is the portion of stuff to be filtered.")
(comment filteringOutput "The predicate #$filteringOutput relates an instance of #$Filtering-Generic to the output of the filtering process.  <code>(#$filteringOutput EVENT THING)</code> means that in the instance of #$Filtering-Generic, <code>EVENT</code>, <code>THING</code> is the portion of stuff remaining after something has been filtered out. ")
(comment eventProvidesEnergyThatDrivesEvent "A specialization of #$facilitates-EventEvent. <code>(#$eventProvidesEnergyThatDrivesEvent EVENT1 EVENT2)</code> means that the event <code>EVENT1</code> provides energy that is required for the ocurrence of <code>EVENT2</code>.")
(comment absorbsFractionAtWavelength "<code>(#$absorbsFractionAtWavelength CHEM-TYPE WAVELENGTH FRACTION)</code> states that <code>FRACTION</code> is the proportion of incident  #$ElectromagneticRadiation of <code>WAVELENGTH</code> that is absorbed by samples of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>.")
(comment absorptionSpectrumOfStuffFunction "A predicate corresponding to the function #$AbsorptionSpectrumFn.  <code>(#$absorptionSpectrumOfStuffFunction CHEM-TYPE FUNCTION)</code> states that <code>FUNCTION</code> is a function on wavelengths which gives the proportion of incident #$ElectromagneticRadiation of each wavelength that is absorbed by samples of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>.")
(comment SaladOil "The collection of instances of #$VegetableOil that are suitable for using as or as an ingredient in salad dressing.")
(comment OilAndVinegarSaladDressing "The collection of instances of #$SaladDressing comprised of #$SaladOil and #$Vinegar.")
(comment essentialIngredientTypes "The intersection (c.f., #$predicateIntersection) of #$typeIngredientTypes and #$essentialPartTypes.")
(comment TheodorWilhelmEngelmann "A physiologist from Germany who also worked as a botanist, and first demonstrated the action spectrum for #$Photosynthesis-Plant in 1883.")
(comment PhotonAbsorption "A specialization of #$AbsorptionEvent.  Instances are events in which a single quantum of #$ElectromagneticRadiation (a #$Photon) is absorbed by a #$ChemicalObject.  Rather than being destroyed, the energy is converted to a different form, depending on the #$wavelength (and thus energy embodied) of the #$Photon.  For example, #$Photons of #$VisibleLight typically are captured as an increase in the excitation state of an electron in the #$ChemicalObject. ")
(comment GroundStateFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  #$GroundStateFn takes an instance CHEM of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies and returns the specialization of CHEM such that all of its instances are at their lowest possible energy level. For example, (#$GroundStateFn (#$MoleculeFn #$ChlorophyllA)) is the collection of ground-state chlorophyll A molecules. An instance of this class is able to be transformed into an excited-state molecule by absorbing a photon of light at the right wavelength. ")
(comment ExcitedStateFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  #$ExcitedStateFn takes an instance CHEM of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies and returns the specialization of CHEM such that each of its instances exhibit an energy level which is ABOVE the lowest possible energy level for that type of chemical object. For example, (#$ExcitedStateFn (#$MoleculeFn #$ChlorophyllA)) is the collection of excited-state chlorophyll A molecules. An instance of this class is typically short-lived, and able to return to a ground-state molecule by emitting a photon, emitting heat, or transferring its excitation energy to a neighboring chemical object. ")
(comment COIDefinitionalPredicate "#$COIDefinitionalPredicate is the collection of predicates that are used to define COIs.")
(comment adjustableParameterForSpecificationVariantsWithIncrementValue "(#$adjustableParameterForSpecificationVariantsWithIncrementValue PARAM SPECIFICATION THING) means that it makes sense to create variants of SPECIFICATION by adjusting it values for PARAM.")
(comment centralMetaphorOfTheory "<code>(#$centralMetaphorOfTheory METAPHOR THEORY)</code> means that in commonly-occuring articulations of the instance <code>THEORY</code> of #$PhilosophicalTheory, the instance of #$Metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> is appealed to.")
(comment outerLayerOf "(#$outerLayerOf LAYER OBJ) means that LAYER is the outermost #$Layer of OBJ, or if OBJ is a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, LAYER may be the outermost #$Layer of one side of OBJ.")
(comment completeOuterLayerOf "(#$completeOuterLayerOf LAYER OBJ) means that LAYER is the complete outermost #$Layer of the object OBJ.  Each #$externalParts of LAYER #$spatiallyIntersects OBJ.")
(comment quantumEnergyLevel "<code>(#$quantumEnergyLevel OBJ ENERGY)</code> states that the quantum mechanical particle or system <code>OBJ</code> has the energy value, <code>ENERGY</code>.  In practice it may usually be impossible to measure this value, and where it can be predicted, <code>OBJ</code> will never assume a particular value of <code>ENERGY</code> for a significant duration (more than a fraction of a second unless it's at a ground state or metastable state.  A given particle or system can only assume certain values for <code>ENERGY</code>; thus these levels are said to be quantized.")
(comment GroundStateChemicalObject "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject.  Each instance of #$GroundStateChemicalObject is a chemical object exhibiting the lowest #$quantumEnergyLevel possible for a chemical object in its configuration. ")
(comment groundState-TypeType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$GroundStateFn.  <code>(#$groundState-TypeType CHEM-TYPE GROUND-STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>GROUND-STATE-TYPE</code> is the specialization of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>, an instance of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies, which includes all instances of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> that are at their lowest possible energy level. ")
(comment ExcitedStateChemicalObject "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject.  Each instance of #$ExcitedStateChemicalObject is a chemical object exhibiting a #$quantumEnergyLevel which is above the lowest possible for a chemical object in its configuration. ")
(disjointWith GroundStateChemicalObject ExcitedStateChemicalObject)
(comment complementaryPreds-Incapability "(#$complementaryPreds-Incapability INST-CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that INST-CAP-PRED is the #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel that complements the #$IncapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel TYPE-INCAP-PRED.  An instance-level capability predicate restricts its first argument to #$Individuals, whereas a type-level incapability predicate restricts its first argument to #$Collections.  What makes the two predicates complementary is that the second predicate is a way of stating incapacity for types such that the capacity involved is expressed at the instance level using the first.")
(comment TypeIncapableFn "TypeIncapableFn takes an instance-level #$CapabilityPredicate and returns a type-level predicate that is used to state the corresponding INcapability for selected collections.  That is, where CAP-PRED is a #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel, and SIT-TYPE and ROLE are, respectively, a situation type and role that are admitted arg2 and adimitted arg 3 for CAP-PRED, ((#$TypeIncapableFn CAP-PRED) AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that there is NO instance INST of AGENT-TYPE such that (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE).  Thus, for example, ((#$TypeIncapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$FlightlessBird #$Flying #$bodilyDoer) means that no #$FlightlessBird is #$behaviorCapable of playing the role of #$bodilyDoer in #$Flying events.")
(comment typeIncapable "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$TypeIncapableFn.  (#$typeIncapable CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that TYPE-INCAP-PRED is a type-level predicate that is used to state the INcapability complementing CAP-PRED for selected collections.  That is, where CAP-PRED is a #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel, and SIT-TYPE and ROLE are, respectively, a situation type and role that are admitted arg2 and adimitted arg 3 for CAP-PRED, (typeIncapable CAP-PRED TYPE-INCAP-PRED) means that TYPE-INCAP-PRED is a predicate such that (TYPE-INCAP-PRED AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means there is NO instance INST of AGENT-TYPE such that (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE).")
(comment membraneBilayer "<code>(#$membraneBilayer MEMBRANE BILAYER)</code> identifies <code>BILAYER</code> as the #$LipidBilayer component of <code>MEMBRANE</code>, an instance of #$Membrane-Biological.")
(comment innerLayerOf "An instance of #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate that relates a layered object with its inner layers.")
(comment relevantPredicateForMetaphoricalMapping "(#$relevantPredicateForMetaphoricalMapping PREDICATE) means that the predicate PREDICATE is relevant for interpreting metaphors. ")
(comment ElectronStateTransition "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ElectronStateTransition, an #$Electron that is part of an #$Atom or #$Molecule moves from one orbital to another and the #$quantumEnergyLevel of the system changes.  The energy levels that such systems can assume are discrete and determined by the bound state of all the particles in the system. For example, in photoexcitation of a pigment molecule (see #$PigmentMoleculePhotoexcitation), when a pigment molecule absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light, the energy of that photon is used to boost an electron in the molecule to a higher-energy molecular orbital.")
(comment EnergyLevelTransition "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$EnergyLevelTransition, a quantum  system such as an #$Atom, #$Molecule, #$Electron, or #$AtomicNucleus moves from one #$quantumEnergyLevel to another.  For example, in photoexcitation of a pigment molecule (see #$PigmentMoleculeExcitation), when a pigment molecule absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light, the energy of that photon is used to boost an electron in the molecule to a higher-energy molecular orbital.   <p>The energy levels that such systems can assume are discrete and determined by the bound state of all the particles in the system.")
(comment Gulping "A specialization of #$Swallowing.  Each instance of #$Gulping is an event in which an #$Animal rapidly swallows a solid or a liquid from its #$Mouth to its #$Stomach.")
(comment matchableQueries "A generalization of #$plausibleQueries, used to expand the space of queries Cyc can suggest into a larger spec of queries to match against typed (or spoken) questions from a user.")
(comment partTypeSupportsCapability "Where TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapability PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that, for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapability PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that PART-TYPE supports the ability to play ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE in any type of system where instances of PART-TYPE are important functional components. Thus, e.g., (#$partTypeSupportsCapability Heart behaviorCapable (CirculationFn Blood) bodilyDoer) means that #$Hearts support systems that include them as important functional components (e.g. Vertebrates) in being #$bodilyDoer of (#$CirculationFn Blood), and logically entails that ((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Vertebrate (#$CirculationFn #$Blood) #$bodilyDoer), provided (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType #$Vertebrate #$Heart) is known or provable.")
(comment partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType "Where TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE AGT-TYPE) means that, if there is systemtype SYSTEM-TYPE such that (#$functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE) and (#$genls AGT-TYPE SYSTEM-TYPE), then (TYPE-CAP-PRED AGT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE).Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED SIT-TYPE ROLE AGT-TYPE) means that instances of PART-TYPE are functionally integrated into all instances of some parent class of AGT-TYPE, but that instances of PART-TYPE support an ability in instances of AGT-TYPE to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE that is not necessarily shared by all instances of the parent class.")
(disjointWith HumanInfant (CollectionDifferenceFn HomoSapiens HumanInfant))
(comment ElectronExcitation "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ElectronExcitation, an #$Electron that is part of an #$Atom or #$Molecule moves from one orbital to a higher-energy orbital.  If the electron is part of a #$Molecule, this is associated with molecular excitation.  Because electrons can occupy only certain orbitals, the energy levels that such systems can assume are discrete.")
(comment ElectronExcitedStateDecay "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ElectronExcitedStateDecay, an #$Electron that is part of an #$Atom or #$Molecule moves from a higher-energy orbital to a lower-energy, orbital (usually? to its normal, ground-state orbital).  If the electron is part of a #$Molecule, this is associated with decay of the molecule's excited state. ")
(disjointWith ChemicalObjectExcitedStateDecay ChemicalObjectExcitation)
(disjointWith ElectronExcitedStateDecay ElectronExcitation)
(comment EnergyConversion-InAnInternalCombustionEngine "A specialization of #$EnergyConversion-ChemicalToKinetic. It is the set of all energy conversions in an #$InternalCombustionEngine.")
(comment EnergyConversion-InAnAutomobileGasolineEngine "A specialization of #$EnergyConversion-InAnInternalCombustionEngine. It is the collection of energy conversions in an #$InternalCombustionEngine of an #$Automobile-GasolineEngine.")
(comment MultiProteinComplex "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject. Each instance of #$MultiProteinComplex consists of two or more proteins linked by non-covalent protein-protein interactions.")
(comment MacromolecularComplex "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject. Each instance of #$MacromolecularComplex consists of two or more #$ChemicalObjects linked by covalent or non-covalent interactions, at least one of which is a macromolecule such as a #$ProteinMolecule, #$RNAMolecule, or #$DNAMolecule.  Other chemical objects in the complex may be these types of things or smaller molecules and ions.  ")
(comment PrimaryElectronAcceptor-Photosynthesis "A collection of #$Molecules.  An instance of #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-Photosynthesis is an organic molecule associated with a #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter, which, in its unreduced state, is able to take an excited #$Electron transferred from one of the #$ChlorophyllA molecules of the reaction center and become reduced.  This is the first chemical reaction in the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.")
(comment LightHarvestingComplex "A specialization of #$MacromolecularComplex. Each instance of #$LightHarvestingComplex is a complex including several protein molecules in association with several #$PhotosyntheticPigment molecules.  Several #$LightHarvestingComplexes are typically part of each #$Photosystem, and surround the #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter that is part of that #$Photosystem.  Because a #$LightHarvestingComplex includes a variety of pigments, it is able to absorb a broader range of light wavelengths than the #$ChlorophyllA molecules in the #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter. The energy of light thus absorbed is passed from pigment molecule to pigment molecule and eventually to a chlorophyll in the reaction center by #$ResonanceEnergyTransfer.")
(comment Photosystem "A specialization of #$MacromolecularComplex. Each instance of #$Photosystem is a super-complex including one #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter and several #$LightHarvestingComplexes in close association.  #$Photosystems are the molecular-scale sites of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.  Green plants (those able to perform #$OxygenicPhotosynthesis) possess two kinds of photosystem, #$PhotosystemI and #$PhotosystemII, which differ in the wavelength of light absorbed by their central #$ChlorophyllA molecules, and play different roles in the photosynthetic light reactions. ")
(comment P700ReactionCenter "A specialization of #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter, called \"P700\" because the #$ChlorophyllA molecules at its core are best at absorbing light with a wavelength of 700 nanometers, due to their location relative to the surrounding molecules. ")
(comment P680ReactionCenter "A specialization of #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter, called \"P680\" because the #$ChlorophyllA molecules at its core are best at absorbing light with a wavelength of 680 nanometers, due to their location relative to the surrounding molecules. ")
(comment ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic "A specialization of #$Membrane-Biological.  Instances of #$ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic partition the interior space of #$Chloroplasts into the #$ChloroplastStroma and the #$ThylakoidSpace. The thylakoid membrane contains many membrane-bound complexes called #$Photosystems that are the molecular-scale sites of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.")
(comment PhotosystemII "A specialization of #$Photosystem. Each instance of #$PhotosystemII is a super-complex including one #$P680ReactionCenter and several #$LightHarvestingComplexes in close association.  #$PhotosystemII instances are found bound to the thylakoid membranes of #$Chloroplasts (see #$ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic) and to the photosynthetic membranes of #$BlueGreenAlgae.  There is variation between species in the exact structure, type and numbers of photosynthetic pigment molecules, and exact composition of protein subunits of #$PhotosystemII instances.  ")
(comment PhotosystemI "A specialization of #$Photosystem. Each instance of #$PhotosystemI is a super-complex including one #$P700ReactionCenter and several #$LightHarvestingComplexes in close association.  #$PhotosystemI instances are found bound to the thylakoid membranes of #$Chloroplasts (see #$ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic) and to the photosynthetic membranes of #$BlueGreenAlgae.  There is variation between species in the exact structure, type and numbers of photosynthetic pigment molecules, and exact composition of protein subunits of #$PhotosystemI instances.  ")
(disjointWith ElectronTransportChain SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(comment NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate "The collection of NADP   molecules. Such molecules are found in both plants and animals, and have important roles in electron transfer, able to become reduced (transformed into #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate) by accepting an electron, and then able to act to reduce other molecules by giving that electron up.")
(comment ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate "The collection of NADPH molecules. These are the reduced form of #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate. Such molecules are found in both plants and animals, and have important roles in electron transfer, able to act to reduce other molecules by giving up an #$Electron (being transformed into #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate), then able to become reduced (transformed back into this form) by accepting an electron.")
(comment reducingAgent "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$reducingAgent REDOX REACTANT) means that during REDOX, an instance of #$RedoxReaction, REACTANT, an instance of #$ChemicalObject, acts as a reducing agent and is oxidized as a result. I.e., one of the #$Atoms of REACTANT loses one or more #$Electrons and thus has its oxidation state increased.")
(comment oxidizingAgent "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$oxidizingAgent REDOX REACTANT) means that during REDOX, an instance of #$RedoxReaction, REACTANT, an instance of #$ChemicalObject, acts as an oxidizing agent and is reduced as a result. I.e., one of the #$Atoms of REACTANT gains one or more #$Electrons and thus has its oxidation state decreased.")
(comment NaiveQuantumPhysicsMt "#$NaiveQuantumPhysicsMt is a #$Microtheory which attempts to capture aspects of non-Newtonian physics such as the wave nature of particles, the quantization of electromagnetic radiation, electron excitation and other phenomena to the extent necessary to understand and explain processes in chemistry and biology, for example photosynthesis.  A correct and modern Quantum Physics Microtheory, if fully developed, would express the mathematical framework of quantum mechanics (describing physical interactions in terms of Hilbert spaces and operators thereon) and describe its fundamental concepts, such as wave/particle duality, the Uncertainty Principle, quantum states of matter, quantum entanglement, etc.")
(disjointWith TelevisionCrew DebateTeam)
(disjointWith SupportGroup DebateTeam)
(disjointWith FanClub DebateTeam)
(disjointWith CriminalOrganization DebateTeam)
(disjointWith Carpool DebateTeam)
(disjointWith Cell-Organization DebateTeam)
(comment DebateTeam "#$DebateTeam is a specialization of #$Team. Each instance of #$DebateTeam is a group of people who participate in a debate.")
(comment debateTeamMembers "(#$debateTeamMembers TEAM MEMBER) means that MEMBER is a player on TEAM in the temporal context of the assertion.")
(comment SelectivelyPermeableThing "The collection of #$PartiallyTangibles which are differentially permeable to substances. That is, for every instance of #$SelectivelyPermeableThing, there are at least two substances such that it is permeable to them, and such that the degree of permeability with respect to these substances is different.")
(comment ChemicalObjectExcitation "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ChemicalObjectExcitation, a #$ChemicalObject absorbs energy, which boosts an electron in the molecule or atom to a higher-energy molecular orbital.  This can occur because the object absorbs a #$Photon, or because it absorbs the energy of a neighboring chemical object that is in an excited state. ")
(comment ChemicalObjectExcitationByPhoton "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ChemicalObjectExcitationByPhoton, a #$Molecule, #$Atom or other #$ChemicalObject absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light and the energy of that photon boosts an electron in the object to a higher-energy molecular orbital.  For example, the excitation of #$Chlorophyll molecules by light is the first step in #$Photosynthesis-Plant, the process that converts energy from #$Sunlight into energy-containing chemical compounds.")
(comment ChemicalObjectEnergyLevelTransition "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ChemicalObjectEnergyLevelTransition, the #$quantumEnergyLevel of a #$ChemicalObject changes to one of the other discrete values it can assume, as a result of one of its #$Electrons moving from one orbital to another.  For example, in photoexcitation of a pigment molecule (see #$PigmentMoleculePhotoexcitation), when a pigment molecule absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light, the energy of that photon is used to boost an electron in the molecule to a higher-energy molecular orbital.")
(comment ChemicalObjectExcitedStateDecay "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$ChemicalObjectExcitedStateDecay, a #$Molecule, #$Atom, #$Ion, etc. which has an electron in a higher-energy-than-normal orbital returns to its ground state.  This may result in the emission of a photon of light (fluorescence), generation of heat, or the transfer of the energy to a neighboring electron in a neighboring #$ChemicalObject. ")
(comment ResonanceEnergyTransfer "A specialization of #$EnergyTransferEvent.  In each instance of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfer, an #$ExcitedStateChemicalObject returns to its ground state (becomes a #$GroundStateChemicalObject), and a neighboring chemical object enters an excited state. The #$quantumEnergyLevel of the first object drops by some amount, and that of the second object rises by that amount.")
(comment paulingElectronegativityOfType "<code>(#$paulingElectronegativityOfType ELEMENT-TYPE POSNUM)</code> states that the type of element, <code>ELEMENT-TYPE</code>, has an electronegativity of <code>POSNUM</code> on the Pauling scale (a unitless scale).  This value is a measure of how strongly atoms of that type attract #$Electrons (or electron density). In a #$ChemicalInteractions between atoms of differing electronegativities, typically the one that is an instance of the type with the higher value will attract electrons more strongly.  However, for a particular #$Atom, actual electronegativity increases at higher oxidation states (when the atom has partially or completely donated electron(s) to a neighboring chemical object).")
(comment PhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Instances of  #$PhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow occur during #$Photosynthesis-Plant. Unlike #$PhotosyntheticLightReactions-CyclicElectronFlow, which can also occur during photosynthesis in green plants, instances of this class involve both #$PhotosystemI and #$PhotosystemII, split molecules of #$Water, and produce ATP.")
(disjointWith PhotosyntheticLightReactions-CyclicElectronFlow PhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow)
(comment PhotosyntheticLightReactions-CyclicElectronFlow "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Instances of  #$PhotosyntheticLightReactions-CyclicElectronFlow occur during #$OxygenicPhotosynthesis and also during some types of #$AnoxygenicPhotosynthesis. Unlike #$PhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow, which can also occur during photosynthesis in green plants, instances of this class involve only #$PhotosystemI, do not split molecules of #$Water, and do not produce NADPH. However, ATP is produced.  ")
(comment PhotosyntheticReactionCenter "A specialization of #$MacromolecularComplex. Each instance of #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter is a complex including several protein molecules, two molecules of #$ChlorophyllA, and a #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-Photosynthesis.  One #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter is part of each #$Photosystem, instances of which are embedded in the #$ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic of #$Chloroplasts, and are the molecular-scale sites of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.")
(comment Pheophytin "#$Pheophytin is a photosynthetic pigment synthesized by plants.  It shares the structure of #$ChlorophyllA, except that it lack the #$Magnesium ion.  It is believed to be the primary electron acceptor in #$PhotosystemII.")
(comment EnergyTransferFromLHCToReactionCenter "A specialization of #$EnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToReactionCenter begins when a pigment molecule in a #$LightHarvestingComplex becomes excited by the absorption of a #$Photon. The energy in that molecule's excited electron is passed from pigment molecule to pigment molecule in a series of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfers until finally one of the core #$ChlorophyllA molecules in the #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter becomes excited.")
(comment EventSeries-Noncontinuous "The collection of #$Series, instances of  which are #$Groups of #$Events, each member of which  is separated from the other by a non-trivial #$Time-Quantity.  Instances of #$EventSeries-Noncontinuous are #$Events in their own right.  Examples include Major League Baseball's World Series, which is also a #$Series of  (at most) seven distinct events with many hours between  them.  Non-examples include breathing events,   which are generally continuous strings of breathing subevents.")
(disjointWith EventSeries-Noncontinuous EventSeries-ContinuousNonoverlapping)
(comment EventSeries-ContinuousNonoverlapping "The collection of #$Series, instances of  which are #$Groups of #$Events, each member of which  is directly followed by the next.  Instances of #$EventSeries-ContinuousNonoverlapping are #$Events in their own right.  Examples include  #$Breathing events, which are generally continuous strings of taking a breath, and #$Rotation-Periodic, instances of which consist of revolutions in sequence.")
(disjointWith PhysicalSeries EventSeries)
(comment EventSeries "The collection of #$Series, instances of  which are #$Groups of #$Events  Instances of #$EventSeries are #$Events in their own right.  Examples include Major League Baseball's World Series, which is also a #$Series of  (at most) seven distinct events with many hours between  them, and #$Breathing events,   which are generally continuous strings of #$TakingABreath subevents.")
(comment P700ChlorophyllAMolecule "Instances are molecules of #$ChlorophyllA which are part of an instance of #$P700ReactionCenter.  These molecules are special because, in an excited state, they have the ability to donate their excited electron, which begins the chemical portion of the light reactions of photosynthesis.")
(comment ReactionCenterChlorophyllAMolecule "Instances are molecules of #$ChlorophyllA which are part of an instance of #$PhotosyntheticReactionCenter.  These molecules are special because, in an excited state, they have the ability to donate their excited electron, which begins the chemical portion of the light reactions of photosynthesis.")
(comment P680ChlorophyllAMolecule "Instances are molecules of #$ChlorophyllA which are part of an instance of #$P680ReactionCenter.  These molecules are special because, in an excited state, they have the ability to donate their excited electron, which begins the chemical portion of the light reactions of photosynthesis.")
(comment EnergyTransferToReactionCenterChlorophyll "A specialization of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfer, instances of which occur in a #$Photosystem.  In each instance of #$EnergyTransferToReactionCenterChlorophyll, an excited-state molecule of a #$PhotosyntheticPigment in a #$LightHarvestingComplex returns to its ground state (becomes a #$GroundStateChemicalObject), and one of the #$ReactionCenterChlorophyllAMolecules in the photosystem's reaction center enters an excited state.  Instances of this class are the terminal events in instances of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToReactionCenter.")
(comment EnergyTransferToP700Chlorophyll "A specialization of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfer, instances of which occur in an instance of #$PhotosystemI.  In each instance of #$EnergyTransferToP700Chlorophyll, an excited-state molecule of a #$PhotosyntheticPigment in a #$LightHarvestingComplex returns to its ground state (becomes a #$GroundStateChemicalObject), and one of the #$P700ChlorophyllAMolecules in the photosystem's reaction center enters an excited state.  Instances of this class are the terminal events in instances of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToP700ReactionCenter.")
(comment EnergyTransferFromLHCToP700ReactionCenter "A specialization of #$EnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToP700ReactionCenter is caused when a pigment molecule in a #$LightHarvestingComplex of an instance of #$PhotosystemI becomes excited by the absorption of a #$Photon. The transfer begins when the energy in that molecule's excited electron is passed from pigment molecule to pigment molecule in a series of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfers until finally one of the core #$ChlorophyllA molecules in the #$P700ReactionCenter becomes excited.")
(comment energyTransferredFrom "A typed specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$fromLocation, <code>(#$energyTransferredFrom TRANSFER OBJ)</code> means that in the instance <code>TRANSFER</code> of #$EnergyTransferEvent, energy is transferred from <code>OBJ</code>, an instance of #$SpatialThing and #$TemporalThing.")
(comment energyTransferredTo "A typed specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$toLocation, <code>(#$energyTransferredTo TRANSFER OBJ)</code> means that in the instance <code>TRANSFER</code> of #$EnergyTransferEvent, energy is transferred to <code>OBJ</code>, an instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized and #$SomethingExisting.")
(comment EnergyTransferToP680Chlorophyll "A specialization of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfer, instances of which occur in an instance of #$PhotosystemII.  In each instance of #$EnergyTransferToP680Chlorophyll, an excited-state molecule of a #$PhotosyntheticPigment in a #$LightHarvestingComplex returns to its ground state (becomes a #$GroundStateChemicalObject), and one of the #$P680ChlorophyllAMolecules in the photosystem's reaction center enters an excited state.  Instances of this class are the terminal events in instances of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToP680ReactionCenter.")
(comment EnergyTransferFromLHCToP680ReactionCenter "A specialization of #$EnergyTransferEvent.  Each instance of #$EnergyTransferFromLHCToP680ReactionCenter is caused when a pigment molecule in a #$LightHarvestingComplex of an instance of #$PhotosystemII becomes excited by the absorption of a #$Photon. The transfer begins when the energy in that molecule's excited electron is passed from pigment molecule to pigment molecule in a series of #$ResonanceEnergyTransfers until finally one of the core #$ChlorophyllA molecules in the #$P680ReactionCenter becomes excited.")
(comment directlyPrecedesInSeries "(#$directlyPrecedesInSeries ITEM1 ITEM2 SERIES) means that ITEM1 comes immediately before ITEM2 in the series, SERIES.")
(comment NLWorkWithIDFn "<code>(#$NLWorkWithIDFn ID)</code> identifies the instance of #$InformationBearingThing that has the unique identifier ID.")
(comment MetaphorAnalysisContext "The collection of microtheories that are used for analyzing metaphors.")
(comment inputStringForMetaphorTest "<code>(#$inputStringForMetaphorTest TEST STRING)</code> means that <code>STRING</code> is the input string for metaphor interpretation <code>TEST</code>.")
(comment nonMetaphoricalInterpretation "<code>(#$nonMetaphoricalInterpretation IBT SENT)</code> means that <code>SENT</code> is the non metaphorical interpretation of <code>IBT</code>.")
(comment ParsingOutputContextFn "<code>(#$ParsingOutputContextFn IBT)</code> identifies the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions produced by the parser. ")
(disjointWith ChlorophyllA ChlorophyllB)
(disjointWith ChlorophyllA PhotosyntheticAccessoryPigment)
(disjointWith Chlorophyll Bacteriochlorophyll)
(disjointWith Chlorophyll Carotenoid)
(disjointWith ChlorophyllB Carotenoid)
(disjointWith ReactionCenterChlorophyllAMolecule LightHarvestingComplexPigmentMolecule)
(disjointWith PhotosyntheticReactionCenter LightHarvestingComplex)
(disjointWith PhotosystemI PhotosystemII)
(disjointWith Photosystem LightHarvestingComplex)
(disjointWith PhotosyntheticReactionCenter Photosystem)
(disjointWith P680ReactionCenter P700ReactionCenter)
(disjointWith P700ChlorophyllAMolecule P680ChlorophyllAMolecule)
(disjointWith EnergyTransferToP700Chlorophyll EnergyTransferToP680Chlorophyll)
(disjointWith EnergyTransferFromLHCToP680ReactionCenter EnergyTransferFromLHCToP700ReactionCenter)
(comment transformationResultType "An #$BinaryRoleTypePredicate that relates #$PhysicalTransformationEvents to types of things -- types of tangible objects or other \"enduring\" things (see #$SomethingExisting) -- that are the results of those transformations. <code>(#$transformationResultType EVENT OBJECT-TYPE)</code> means that as a consequence of <code>EVENT</code>, the object that is the #$transformedObject in <code>EVENT</code> is an instance of <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment transformationInputType "An #$BinaryRoleTypePredicate that relates #$PhysicalTransformationEvents to types of things -- types of tangible objects or other \"enduring\" things (see #$SomethingExisting) -- that are the inputs of those transformations. <code>(#$transformationInputType EVENT OBJECT-TYPE)</code> means that as a precondition for <code>EVENT</code>, the object that is the #$transformedObject in <code>EVENT</code> is, going into <code>EVENT</code> an instance of <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code>, and, as a result of <code>EVEN</code>, that object is no longer an instance of <code>OBJECT-TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith AligningOfChromosomes Telophase-Generic)
(comment Telophase-Generic "#$Telophase-Generic is a specialization of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent whose instances take place as part of cell division, either mitotic (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle) and thus as an instance of #$Telophase, or meiotic (see #$Meiosis) and thus as an instance of #$TelophaseI or #$TelophaseII. #$Telophase-Generic events are essentially characterized by the formation of two nuclear envelopes around the two sets of chromosomes defined by a previous #$Anaphase-Generic event.")
(disjointWith AligningOfChromosomes Anaphase-Generic)
(disjointWith Telophase-Generic Anaphase-Generic)
(comment Anaphase-Generic "#$Anaphase-Generic is a specialization of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent whose instances take place as part of cell division, either mitotic (see #$MitoticPhaseOfCellCycle) and thus as an instance of #$Anaphase, or meiotic (see #$Meiosis) and thus as an instance of #$AnaphaseI or #$AnaphaseII. #$Anaphase-Generic events are essentially characterized by the movement of chromosomes away from the #$metaphasePlateOfCell to opposite sides of the cytoplasm, in preparation for a #$Telophase-Generic event.")
(comment LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton, a #$LightHarvestingComplexPigmentMolecule absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light and the energy of that photon boosts an electron in the object to a higher-energy molecular orbital.  Events of this type provide the energy required to perform photosynthesis (see #$Photosynthesis-Plant). ")
(comment PhotosystemI-LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$PhotosystemI-LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton, a #$LightHarvestingComplexPigmentMolecule that is part of an instance of #$PhotosystemI absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light and the energy of that photon boosts an electron in the object to a higher-energy molecular orbital.  Events of this type provide the energy required to perform photosynthesis (see #$Photosynthesis-Plant). ")
(disjointWith EnergyTransferToReactionCenterChlorophyll EnergyTransferFromLHCToReactionCenter)
(comment PhotosystemII-LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$PhotosystemII-LHCPigmentMoleculeExcitationByPhoton, a #$LightHarvestingComplexPigmentMolecule that is part of an instance of #$PhotosystemII absorbs a photon of the correct wavelength of light and the energy of that photon boosts an electron in the object to a higher-energy molecular orbital.  Events of this type provide energy required to perform photosynthesis (see #$Photosynthesis-Plant). ")
(comment PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemI "A collection of #$Molecules.  An instance of #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemI is an organic molecule associated with a the #$P700ReactionCenter of #$PhotosystemI, which, in its unreduced state, is able to take an excited #$Electron transferred from one of the #$ChlorophyllA molecules of the reaction center and become reduced.")
(comment PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII "A collection of #$Molecules.  An instance of #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII is an organic molecule associated with a the #$P680ReactionCenter of #$PhotosystemII, which, in its unreduced state, is able to take an excited #$Electron transferred from one of the #$ChlorophyllA molecules of the reaction center and become reduced.")
(comment userGeneratedKEMt "The predicate that corresponds to #$UserGeneratedKEMtFn.")
(comment userAnalysisContextOf "The predicate that corresponds to #$UserAnalysisContextOfThingFn, <code>(#$userAnalysisContextOf MT USER THING)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the microtheory whose asserted contents are judgments made by the user <code>USER</code> of the thing <code>THING</code>.")
(comment UserAnalysisContextOfThingFn "<code>(#$UserAnalysisContextOfThingFn USER THING)</code> denotes the microtheory whose asserted contents are judgments made by the user <code>USER</code> of the thing <code>THING</code>.")
(comment genlMtForMetaphorInterpretation "A specialization of #$genlMt. Use this predicate for asserting relations between metaphor interpretation microtheories")
(comment MetaphoricalTransformationOfFn "(#$MetaphoricalTransformationOfFn THING COLLECTION) returns the metaphorical image of THING that is of type COLLECTION.")
(comment metaphoricalTransformationOfEntity "'(#$metaphoricalTransformationOfEntity THING COLLECTION IMAGE)' means that IMAGE is the metaphorical image of THING. Here THING must be an instance of COLLECTION.")
(comment in-ContOrPartonomic-Generic "<code>(#$in-ContOrPartonomic-Generic IN OBJ)</code> means that the two tangible objects, <code>IN</code> and <code>OBJ</code> are such that <code>IN</code> is physically inside </code>OBJ</code>, either by virtue of being an #$internalParts of </code>OBJ</code>, or by virtue of being contained (#$in-ContGeneric) in <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment approximateQuantityForInstance "(#$approximateQuantityForInstance PRED INST QUANT) means that #$ScalarQuantity QUANT is an approximation of the actual #$ScalarPointValue of INST with respect to #$MeasurableQuantitySlot PRED. The use of #$approximateQuantityForInstance rather than (PRED INST QUANT) is taken to indicate some error in measurement, rounding, or both. When (#$approximateQuantityForInstance PRED INST QUANT) is asserted, a corresponding (#$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified PRED INST QUANT-POINT ERROR) will be forward concluded. If QUANT is a #$ScalarProperInterval, QUANT-POINT will be the midpoint #$ScalarPointValue of the interval, and the error will be the distance from the endpoints to this midpoint. If QUANT is a #$ScalarPointValue, QUANT-POINT = QUANT, and the estimated error will be equal to one half of the order magnitude of the smallest significant digit of QUANT (that is, if the trailing significant digit is .000X, it has a magnitude of -4, and thus the assumed maximum error is .5*10^-4, resulting in a range of .000X -.00005 to .000X + .00005). This is intended to capture the assumptions that a.) if the error was expected to be greater than this value, either a less precise value would have been provided (or #$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified would have been used) and b.) rounding affects, at most, the terminal digit, and at most by one half of the magnitude of that digit. For example, the assertion (#$approximateQuantityForInstance #$thicknessOfObject #$CellMembrane007 (#$Nano #$Meter 8)) will result in the corresponding assertion (#$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified #$thicknessOfObject #$CellMembrane007 (#$Nano #$Meter 8) (#$Nano #$Meter .5)) in the KB.  (#$approximateQuantityForInstance #$thicknessOfObject #$CellMembrane008 (#$Nano #$Meter 8 10)) would result in (#$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified #$thicknessOfObject #$CellMembrane008 (#$Nano #$Meter 9) (#$Nano #$Meter 1)). When error is known, use #$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified instead.")
(comment approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified "(#$approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified PRED INST QUANT ERROR) means that QUANT is an approximation of the actual value of PRED for INST, to within ERROR. ERROR is either a known error value, supplied at assertion time, or it is estimated as a consequence of an #$approximateQuantityForInstance assertion (in which case it will have been foward concluded). For example, (approximateQuantityForInstance-ErrorSpecified objectLength Surfboard0001 (Meters 3.5) (Meters .05)) means that the actual length of Surfboard0001 is within .05 meters of 3.5 meters. The error is primarily useful in inference regarding metric comparison between individuals.")
(comment approximateQuantityForType "(#$approximateQuantityForType PRED COL QUANT) means that #$ScalarQuantity QUANT is the approximate scalar quantity for the #$Collection COL with respect to #$MeasurableQuantitySlot PRED. The use of #$approximateQuantityForType rather than #$relationAllInstance is taken to indicate variance with respect to the actual values of individuals. If QUANT is a #$ScalarPointValue, it is taken to represent the median value of the distribution of values for instances of the collection. It would be false to infer that all instances have this value, even approximately (q.v. approximateQuantityForInstance), and in fact none of them might have this value. When QUANT is a #$ScalarProperInterval, the range specified by QUANT is taken to be the range from one standard deviation above and below the mean of the actual values of the instances. Thus, is should be expected that at least 68% of instances have values within this range. When (#$approximateQuantityForType PRED COL QUANT) is asserted, a corresponding (approximateQuantityForType-SigmaSpecified PRED COL QUANT-POINT SIGMA)  assertion is forward concluded, according to the following rules:

1.) When QUANT is a #$ProperScalarInterval, QUANT-POINT is the midpoint of QUANT and SIGMA is the distance from QUANT-POINT to either end of the interval.

2.) When QUANT is fractional (not an integer) or if more than half of QUANT's digits are significant, QUANT-POINT = QUANT and  SIGMA is equal to 2 times the order of magnitude of the trailing significant digit. For example, if QUANT is (Meter 2.3943), SIGMA will be (Meter .0002). If QUANT is (Meter 594380), SIGMA will be (Meter 20).

3.) When QUANT is an integer with fewer than half of its digits significant, QUANT-POINT = QUANT and  SIGMA is equal to 2 times one order of magnitude lower than the trailing significant digit. For example, if QUANT is (Kilometer 1243000000), SIGMA will be (Kilometer 200000).

In all cases, SIGMA is an estimated standard deviation for the actual distribution of values over the population of COL. Obviously, it is highly unlikely that estimated SIGMAs are the *actual* standard deviations. It is hoped that these estimates are conservative enough that *AT LEAST* 95% of instances fall within (#$TimesFn SIGMA 2) of QUANT, while at the same time being narrow enough to permit metric comparisons, inferences concluding (not (isa ?X ?Y)), etc. The reason for separating cases (2) and (3) above is that integer values with few significant digits are taken to be specific up to the trailing digit. In the limiting case of a single significant digit, e.g., (Mile 1000), it would not do for SIGMA to be (Mile 2000), so we instead use (Mile 200) (still a very conservative estimate).")
(comment approximateQuantityForType-SigmaSpecified "(#$approximateQuantityForType PRED COL QUANT SIGMA) means that #$ScalarQuantity QUANT is the approximate scalar quantity for the #$Collection COL with respect to #$MeasurableQuantitySlot PRED. That is, QUANT is taken to be the mean of the distribution of values related to instances of COL via PRED, and SIGMA is taken to be the standard deviation of this distribution (and may have been estimated via a #$approximateQuantityForType assertion). This facilitates reasoning that requires comparison between types that admit of variance. For example, if (#$approximateQuantityForType-SigmaSpecified PRED COL1 QUANT1 SIGMA1) and (approximateQuantityForType-SigmaSpecified PRED COL2 QUANT2 SIGMA2), and the difference between QUANT1 and QUANT2 is greater than (#$PlusFn (#$TimesFn SIGMA1 3) (#$TimesFn SIGMA2 3)), it is safe to concluded that (disjointWith COL1 COL2).")
(comment NonSquareRectangle "A specialization of #$Rectangle.  Each instance of #$NonSquareRectangle is a rectangle with two sides of one length and two sides of a different length.")
(comment RomanNumeral "The collection of all Roman #$Numerals.  The Roman numeral system uses combinations of letters from the Latin alphabet to signify values. ")
(comment coveringOfEventType "<code>(#$coveringOfEventType EVT-TYPE LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES)</code> means that:  <p> (1) for each instance <code>EVT</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there exists some instance of each element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a proper sub-situation of <code>EVT</code>;  <p> (2) there is no further sub-situation of <code>EVT</code> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>; <p> (3) an instance of the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> starts at the starting of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (4) after the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>, each subsequent element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> is such that the instance of it that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code> starts after the start of the instance of the prior element in <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code>.   <p> Thus, for example, consider the claim (#$coveringOfEventType #$NFLSeason (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  This means that (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPreSeason), (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLRegularSeason and (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPostSeason).  Further, for any instance of #$NFLSeason <b>NFL-Season-001</b>, there is no sub-event of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  It also entails that there is an instance of #$NFLPreSeason, <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, that is the first proper sub-situation of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> .  Finally, it entails that some instance  <b>NFLRegularSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLRegularSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the start of <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, and  some instance  <b>NFLPostSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLPostSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the end of <b>NLRegularSeason-001</b>.")
(disjointWith ArabicNumeral RomanNumeral)
(comment characterizeEventTypeCompositionally "A specialization (see #$genlPreds) of #$partTypesFactsForType, <code>#$characterizeEventTypeCompositionally EVENT-TYPE SENTENCE)</code> means that the #$CycLSentence <code>SENTENCE</code> contributes to a description of how the event type <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> decomposes into sub-event-types.")
(disjointWith Phospholipid (CollectionDifferenceFn (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn Lipid parts CellMembrane) Phospholipid))
(comment LipidBilayer-Configuration "The collecion of #$ConfigurationOfComplexObjects in which lpid molecules (primarily #$Phospholipids) are configured in a bilayer (usually a membrane of some sort).")
(comment MitoticGameteProduction "The process of producing gametes through mitosis.")
(comment MetaphorApplicationContextFn "<code>(#$MetaphorApplicationContextFn  MetaphorAnalysisContext METAPHOR)</code> identifies the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions produced when METAPHOR is used in the analysis of facts in <code>MetaphorAnalysisContext</code>.")
(comment MetaphorTransferContextFn "<code>(#$MetaphorTransferContextFn   MetaphorAnalysisContext)</code> identifies the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions transferred from the source to the target during the interpretation process. ")
(comment QSInfrastructureQuery "A specialization of #$CycLQuerySpecification, instances of which are used to do reasoning about the properties of queries to be used to improve suggestion in response to UI gesturing or matching against user-specified (NL) questions.")
(comment qsDefaultQuestionCategory "<code>(#$qsDefaultQuestionCategory CATEGORY)</code> means that the #$QuestionSuggestionCategory <code>CATEGORY</code> is the category for any #$matchableQueries not otherwise explicitly specified as having a category in the given question-suggestion context.")
(comment QSDefaultParameterValuesSpecifierPredicate "The collection of instances of #$UnaryPredicate that are used to set default values for the parameters of queries for the purposes of question-suggestion or question-matching.")
(comment qsDefaultMicrotheory "<code>(#$qsDefaultMicrotheory MT)</code> means that, sans any explicit specification to the contrary, the #$microtheoryParameterValueInSpecification for a query suggested or matched in the relevant Question Suggestion context is <code>MT</code>.")
(comment qSInfrastructureQueryForQueryParameter "<code>(#$qSInfrastructureQueryForQueryParameter QUERY PARAMETER)</code> identifies <code>QUERY</code> as the instance of #$QSInfrastructureQuery that is used to identify the value of <code>PARAMETER</code>, a binary predicate that describes the properties of CycL queries.")
(comment nlWorkWithID "The predicate that corresponds to #$NLWorkWithIDFn, <code>(#$nlWorkWithID IBT ID)</code> means that ID is the unique identifier for <code>IBT</code>, an instance of #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment necessaryConditionFor-InSitType "<code>(#$necessaryConditionFor-InSitType SITUATION-TYPE STEP-TYPE1 STEP-TYPE2)</code> means that in the type of #$Situation,  <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>, <code>STEP-TYPE1</code> is a necessary condition for <code>STEP-TYPE2</code>. This means that if an instance INS2 of <code>STEP-TYPE2</code> is part of an instantiation S of <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>, then INS2 will start after INS1 -- an instance of <code>STEP-TYPE1</code> that is also part of S.")
(comment preconditionFor-InSitType "<code>(#$preconditionFor-InSitType SITUATION-TYPE SCENE1 SCENE2)</code> means that <code>SCENE1</code> and <code>SCENE2</code> are both scenes in <code>SITUATION-TYPE</code>, and that <code>SCENE1</code> is a precondition for <code>SCENE2</code>.  This means both that <code>SCENE1</code> comes before, and is a necessary condition for <code>SCENE2</code>.  Cf. #$necessaryConditionFor-InSitType.")
(comment slotsPositivelyCorrelatedWithSlotForRelatedTypes "(#$slotsPositivelyCorrelatedWithSlotForRelatedTypes  OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 BIN-PRED SLOT-1 SLOT-2) means that when INST-1 and INST-2 (instances of OBJ-TYPE1 and OBJ-TYPE2 respectively) stand in BIN-PRED such that (BIN-PRED INST-1 INST-2), then the values for SLOT-2 for INST-2 are positively correlated with the values for SLOT-1 for INST-1. ")
(comment MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore-Prometaphase "A specialization of #$MicrotubuleConnectsToKinetochore.  The collection of events in which microtubules connect to kinetochores during #$Prometaphase.")
(comment stepPreparesForFollowingStepBySatisfyingPrerequisite "<code>(#$stepPreparesForFollowingStepBySatisfyingPrerequisite SITTYPE NEXT-SITTYPE PRECOND ENABLED)</code> states that <code>PRECOND</code>, a #$subSituationTypes of <code>SITTYPE</code>, is a precondition for <code>ENABLED</code>, a #$subSituationTypes of <code>NEXT-SITTYPE</code>, and thus the completion of an instance of <code>SITTYPE</code> prepares the actors invovled to perform an instance of <code>NEXT-SITTYPE</code>.")
(comment parsingOutputContext "The predicate that corresponds to the function  #$ParsingOutputContextFn, <code>(#$parsingOutputContext IBT MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions used in the analysis of <code>IBT</code>, an instance of #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment metaphorTransferContext "The predicate that corresponds to the function  #$MetaphorTransferContextFn, <code>(#$metaphorTransferContext MetaphorAnalysisContext MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions transferred from the source to the target during the interpretation process. ")
(comment metaphorApplicationContext "The predicate that corresponds to the function  #$MetaphorApplicationContextFn, <code>(#$metaphorApplicationContext IBT METAPHOR MT)</code> identifies <code>MT</code> as the instance of #$MetaphorAnalysisContext that is the microtheory that contains assertions when METAPHOR is used in the interpretation of IBT. ")
(comment QSSingleVariableQuaternaryQueryFn "<code>(#$QSSingleVariableQuaternaryQueryFn PRED ARG-L ARG-M ARG-N VARPOS)</code> denotes the Query Suggestor query for bindings for the <code>VARPOS</code>-th argument of a quaternary CycL sentence where the arg0 is <code>PRED</code>, and the other three arguments, in order of argument number, are <code>ARG-L</code>, <code>ARG-M</code> and <code>ARG-N</code>. For example <code>(#$QSSingleVariableQuaternaryQueryFn #$travelTime #$CityOfLondonEngland #$CityOfParisFrance    (#$TravelingByMeansOfFn #$EurostarChunnelTrain) 4)</code> specifies the Query Suggestor query for the amount of time it takes to travel from London to Paris by means of the Eurostar Chunnel tran.")
(comment qsSingleVariableQuaternaryQuery "The predicate that corresponds to #$QSSingleVariableQuaternaryQueryFn, <code>(#$qsSingleVariableQuaternaryQuery PRED ARG-L ARG-M ARG-N VARPOS QUERY)</code> identifies <code>QUERY</code> as the Query Suggestor query for bindings for the <code>VARPOS</code>-th argument of a quaternary CycL sentence where the arg0 is <code>PRED</code>, and the other three arguments, in order of argument number, are <code>ARG-L</code>, <code>ARG-M</code> and <code>ARG-N</code>. For example <code>(#$qsSingleVariableQuaternaryQuery #$travelTime #$CityOfLondonEngland #$CityOfParisFrance (#$TravelingByMeansOfFn #$EurostarChunnelTrain) 4 QUERY-52)</code> identifies <code>QUERY-52</code> as the Query Suggestor query for the amount of time it takes to travel from London to Paris by means of the Eurostar Chunnel tran.")
(comment genStringAssertion-Constrained "<code>(#$genStringAssertion-Constrained THING CONSTRAINT ASSERTION)</code> means that when paraphrasing <code>THING</code> into natural language in contexts where the paraphrase is constrained by <code>CONSTRAINT</code>, the assertion <code>ASSERTION</code> is to be used.  For example, <code>(#$genStringAssertion #$CreationEvent #$Noun (#$ist #$GeneralEnglishMt (#$multiWordString (#$TheList \"creation\") #$Event-TheWord #$CountNoun #$CreationEvent)))</code> means that in contexts requiring generation as a noun, <code>#$CreationEvent</code> should be generated as \"creation event(s)\".")
(comment characterizeEffectsOfProcessOnType "<code>#$characterizeEffectsOfProcessOnType EVENT-TYPE COLL SENTENCE)</code> means that the #$CycLSentence <code>SENTENCE</code> contributes to a description of how the event type <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> affects instances of <code>COLL</code>.")
(comment PumpingGasolineInAnAutomobile "A specialization of #$PumpingGasEvent. It is the collection of all events in which gasoline is pumped from a pump into the gas tank of an automobile.")
(comment FlowOfGasolineInAnAutomobileEngine "An instance of #$TemporalStuffType and a specialization of #$FluidFlow-Translation. Each instance of #$FlowOfGasolineInAnAutomobileEngine is an event in which some #$GasolineFuel flows into an automobile's engine.")
(comment CombustionOfGasolineInAnAutomobile "A collection of events, and a specialization of #$InternalCombustionProcess. Each instance of #$CombustionOfGasolineInAnAutomobile is an event in which combustion of gasoline in an automobile engine converts chemical energy into useful kinetic energy.")
(comment specifiedPartTypeCollectionForType "An instance of #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot, <code>(#$specifiedPartTypeCollectionForType PART-TYPE WHOLE-TYPE)</code> relates the instance <code>PART-TYPE</code> of #$SpecifiedPartTypeCollection to the precise specialization <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code> of #$PartiallyTangible such that which <code>(#$normalWholeTypeForPartType PART-TYPE WHOLE-TYPE)</code>.")
(comment CUREUserModelFn "#$CUREUserModelFn is a binary function from a #$Cyclist and a task (i.e. an #$Allotment) to the user model of that user working on that task.")
(comment cureUserModel "(#$cureUserModel USER TASK MODEL) indicates that MODEL is a model of USER working on TASK.  It is the predicate that corresponds to #$CUREUserModelFn, and is used in the CURE to associate a user with that user's current task.")
(comment CellPartTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$CellPart into sub-collections based on the #$biologicalFunction of their instances.")
(comment precomputedPlausibleQueryForPred "<code>(#$precomputedPlausibleQueryForPred QUERY PREDICATE)</code> means that 1) the instance <code>QUERY</code> of #$CycLQuerySpecification has been pre-computed as a candidate for suggestion, prior to any analysis of a particular text against which to do the suggestion, and that 2) the suggestion of query will depend on the question-suggestion features specified on <code>PREDICATE</code>, which is the arg0 of the #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification of <code>QUERY</code>.")
(comment GenomeTypeOfOrgTypeGenInfoFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used for representing collections of #$Genome-GenInfo.  Where ORG-TYPE is an #$OrganismClassificationType, (#$GenomeTypeOfOrgTypeGenInfoFn ORG-TYPE) denotes the class of all instances of #$Genome-GenInfo that belong (#$genomeOfBLO-GenInfo) to instances of ORG-TYPE.  The corresponding function (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$genomeTypeOfOrgType-GenInfo.")
(comment genomeTypeOfOrgType-GenInfo "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical  of #$GenomeTypeOfOrgTypeGenInfoFn.  Where ORG-TYPE is an #$OrganismClassificationType, (#$genomeTypeOfOrgType-GenInfo ORG-TYPE GENOME-TYPE) means that GENOME-TYPE is the class of all instances of Genome-GenInfo that belong (#$genomeOfBLO-GenInfo) to instances of ORG-TYPE.")
(comment hypothesizedSentenceForMetaphorInterpretation "(#$hypothesizedSentenceForMetaphorInterpretation THING PROP) means that PROP has been hypothesized based on inferences drawn from THING. ")
(comment MembraneReceptorMoleculeTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$MembraneReceptorMolecule into subcollections based on the role those molecules play in various signaling pathways.")
(comment MembraneProteinTypeByFunction "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$MembraneProtein into subcollections of molecules based on the role those molecules play in various signaling pathways.")
(comment perRatioCol "The corresponding predicate
(#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$PerRatioColFn.  Where NUMERATOR-TYPE and DENOMINATOR-TYPE are both instances of
#$InterconvertibleUnitType, (#$perRatioCol NUMERATOR-TYPE
DENOMINATOR-TYPE COL) means that COL is the collection of all scalar quantities that can be represented as a
ratio where the numerator is measured by units of the first type and
the denominator is measured by units of the second type.  Thus,
e.g. (#$PerRatioColFn #$UnitOfMoney #$UnitOfVolume) would represent
the collection of all quantities measuring a unit of money per unit
volume, such as ((#$PerFn #$Dollar-UnitedStates #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume) 108),
((#$PerFn #$Ruble-Russia #$Liter) 100), ((#$PerFn #$Rupee-Nepal
#$Gallon-Imperial) 52.8), and so on. ")
(comment ClothesWasherControlSystem "The collection of all control devices of automatic clothes washers.")
(comment interArgIsaGenl2-3 "<code>(#$interArgIsaGenl2-3 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL)</code> means that, when an instance of <code>INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code> appears as the second argument to <code>REL</code>, the third argument is constrained to be a spec of <code>DEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code>.")
(comment interArgIsaGenl3-2 "<code>(#$interArgIsaGenl3-2 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL)</code> means that, when an instance of <code>INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code> appears as the third argument to <code>REL</code>, the second argument is constrained to be a specialization of <code>DEPENDENT-ARG-COL</code>.")
(comment ControlSystemCheckpoint "A specialization of #$ConfigurationOfComplexObject.  Each instance of #$ControlSystemCheckpoint is a checkpoint at which a control system regulates the behavior of that which it controls.")
(comment RegulationAtCheckpoint "A specialization of #$ControllingSomething.  In each instance of #$RegulationAtCheckpointViaInternalControl, the functioning or behavior of something is regulated at a checkpoint (see #$ControlSystemCheckpoint).")
(comment RegulationAtCheckpointViaInternalControl "A specialization of #$ControllingSomething.  In each instance of #$RegulationAtCheckpointViaInternalControl, the functioning or behavior of something is regulated at a checkpoint (see #$ControlSystemCheckpoint) via internal controls (see #$systemExternalControls.")
(comment RegulationAtCheckpointViaExternalControl "A specialization of #$ControllingSomething.  In each instance of #$RegulationAtCheckpointViaExternalControl, the functioning or behavior of something is regulated at a checkpoint (see #$ControlSystemCheckpoint) via external controls (see #$systemExternalControls).")
(comment systemControlOperatesViaControlType "<code>(#$systemControlOperatesViaControlType SYSTEM CONTROL-TYPE)</code> means that <code>SYSTEM</code> exterts control over that which it controls via the kind of controlling, <code>CONTROL-TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDeviceControlSystemCheckpoint ChemicalSignalingCheckpoint)
(comment ClothesWasherWashCycle "The cycle of events involved in running a clothese washer.  Typical sub-event types include the wash tub filling, agitation of the wash tub, and draining of the wash tub.")
(comment PhysicalDeviceControlSystemCheckpoint "A specialization of #$ControlSystemCheckpoint.  Each instance of #$PhysicalDeviceControlSystemCheckpoint is a checkpoint that affects the how the control system of a physical device regulates the behavior of that device.")
(comment PoliticalIndoctrination "A specialization of #$Indoctrination-Script. Each instance of this collection is the entire series of events in which an agent learns a political ideology without critically examining it.")
(comment SocialistIndoctrination "A specialization of #$PoliticalIndoctrination. Each instance of this collection is the entire series of events in which an agent learns socialist ideology without critically examining it.")
(comment metaphorSalientBasisBinPred "<code>(#$metaphorSalientBasisBinPred  METAPHOR PRED N)</code> means that if, for the basis <code>BASIS</code> of <code>METAPHOR</code>,  <code>PRED</code> is a binary predicate that holds of <code>BASIS</code> and some further thing <code>THING</code> where <code>BASIS</code> is the Nth argument to <code>PRED</code>, then when <code>METAPHOR</code> is applied to something <code>FOO</code>, <code>PRED</code> holds of <code>FOO</code> and some further thing <code>THING</code> where <code>BASIS</code> is the Nth argument to <code>PRED</code>.")
(comment metaphorRelnMappingFromTo "A predicate used to generate semantics from metaphorical uses of language, by mapping relations that are invoked on a literal reading to those that apply when the the language is understood as instantiating a particular metaphor. <code>(#$metaphorRelnMappingFromTo METAPHOR BASIS-RELN TARGET-RELN)</code> means that where <code>(BASIS-RELN ARG-1, ..., ARG-N)</code> results from a literal interpretation of some natural language utterance <code>NLU</code>, an interpretation according to which <code>NLU</code> instantiates the metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> would instead result in <code>(TARGET-RELN ARG-1, ..., ARG-N)</code>.<p>For example, a literal reading of \"Gerry caught the flu,\" would require that the #$objectCaught relation be made to hold between some event and #$Influenza.  However, when interpreted as instantiating a particular metaphor (the \"catching\" metaphor for #$InfectingEvent), the #$infectionTypeTransmittedDuring relation would be used instead.")
(comment systemTypeControlType "#$systemTypeControlType relates a type of system to a type of control that it has.")
(comment systemTypeInternalControlType "#$systemTypeInternalControlType relates a type of system to a type of internal control that it has.")
(comment systemTypeExternalControlType "#$systemTypeExternalControlType relates a type of system to a type of external control that it has.")
(comment metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity "<code>(#$metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity METAPHOR  BASIS-SENTENCE THING-SENTENCE)</code> means that the metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable because of the the similarity between the basis and that to which the metaphor applies that is expressed by the pair of sentences <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code>.  In general, <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> will differ only in that <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code>mentions the metaphor's basis where <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> mentions that to which <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable.  Cf. #$metaphorGroundsOutInFacts.")
(comment metaphorGroundsOutInFacts "<code>(#$metaphorGroundsOutInFacts METAPHOR BASIS-SENTENCE THING-SENTENCE1 ... )</code> means that the metaphor <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable because of a similarity between the basis and that to which the metaphor applies that is based on the truth of <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code>. In general, <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> (about the basis) and <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> differ in more ways than that just <code>BASIS-SENTENCE</code> mentions the metaphor's basis where <code>EXTENDED-SENTENCE</code> mentions that to which <code>METAPHOR</code> is applicable. Cf. #$metaphorFoundedOnSimilarity.")
(comment WashingMachineExternalWaterFaucetCoupling "A specialization of #$PhysicalConnection-Configuration.  Each instance of #$WashingMachineExternalWaterFaucetCoupling is a connection of a clothes washing machine to an external water supply regulated by a faucet.")
(comment FaucetsControllingWaterSupplyToWashingMachine "A specialization of #$Tap-PlumbingFixture.  Each instance of #$FaucetsControllingWaterSupplyToWashingMachine is a faucet that controls the water supply to the washing machine.")
(comment ClothesWasherFullWashTubCheckpoint "The checkpoint in the #$ClothesWasherWashCycle at which the #$ClothesWasherControlSystem should detect that the wash tub is full.")
(comment BiologicalFunctionTwoVariableQueryFn "(#$BiologicalFunctionTwoVariableQueryFn TYPE) denotes the Query Suggestor query about the biological function of TYPE.  For example (#$BiologicalFunctionTwoVariableQueryFn #$CellNucleus) specifies the Query Suggestor query for what roles, and in what types of processes, cell nuclei act in when fulfilling their biological functions.")
(comment UnicellularProtist "A specialization of #$ProtistaKingdom.  Each instance of #$UnicellularProtist is a protist that consists of only one cell.")
(comment Euglena "A specialization of #$UnicellularProtist. Each instance of #$Euglena is a unicellular flagellate protist.")
(comment GreenAlgae "The collection of all green algae. They contain chlorophylls a and b, which gives them a bright green color.")
(comment UnicellularAlgae "The collection of all algae that consist of only one cell.")
(comment MulticellularAlgae "The collection of all algae that consist of more than one cell.")
(comment Bioethanol "#$Bioethanol refers to ethanol liquid that can be made from common crops such as sugarcane, potato and corn.")
(comment MulticellularProtist "A specialization of #$ProtistaKingdom.  Each instance of #$MulticellularProtist is a protist that consists of more than one cell.")
(comment Prophase-Traditional "A specialization of #$Prophase-Generic. In the history of biology, before prophase and prometaphase were recognized as distinct processes, everything that transpires during prometaphase was considered to be part of prophase.")
(comment differenceFactsForTypes "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate used to query for salient facts about the similarities between types of things. <code>(#$differenceFactsForTypes TYPE1 TYPE2 SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is a true statement about the difference between <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment Kelp "A specialization of #$BrownAlgae.  Kelps require nutrient-rich water and grow in shallow oceans.")
(comment Esterification "The type of #$ChemicalReaction in which esters are made from alcohols and carboxylic acids.")
(comment ProductionOfBiodieselFromFats "The type of #$ChemicalReaction in which #$Triglyceride is converted into #$Biodiesel.")
(comment EthanolGasolineFuelMixture "A specialization of #$LiquidFuel. A mixture of ethanol and gasoline is used in many internal combustion engines.  ")
(comment Biodiesel "A specialization of #$Biofuel. It is an alternative fuel produced from renewable resources such as vegetable oil and animal fat.     ")
(comment BiodieselFuelMixture "A specialization of #$LiquidFuel and #$Mixture. A mixture of biodiesel and petroleum diesel is used in many standard diesel engines. ")
(comment AlgalOil "A specialization of #$Oil. The instances of #$AlgalOil are produced by algae.  ")
(comment ProductionOfBiodieselFromAlgalOil "A specialization of #$Transesterification. In this reaction, algal oil is converted into biodiesel. ")
(comment QSSingleVariableBinaryQueryFn "<code>(#$QSSingleVariableBinaryQueryFn PRED ARG VARPOS)</code> denotes the Query Suggestor query for bindings for the <code>VARPOS</code>-th argument of a binary CycL sentence where the arg0 is <code>PRED</code> with the argument <code>ARG</code>, which is the argument position that is not the <code>VARPOS</code>-th. For example <code>(#$QSSingleVariableBinaryQueryFn #$performedBy #$Event-702 2)</code> specifies the Query Suggestor query for the performer of event 702.")
(comment qsSingleVariableBinaryQuery "The predicate that corresponds to #$QSSingleVariableBinaryQueryFn, <code>(#$qsSingleVariableBinaryQuery PRED ARG VARPOS QUERY)</code> identifies <code>QUERY</code> as the Query Suggestor query for bindings for the <code>VARPOS</code>-th argument of a binary CycL sentence where the arg0 is <code>PRED</code> with the argument <code>ARG</code>, which is the argument position that is not the <code>VARPOS</code>-th. For example <code>(#$qsSingleVariableBinaryQuery #$performedBy #$Event-702 2 QUERY)</code> identifies <code>QUERY</code> as the Query Suggestor query for the performer of event 702.")
(comment checkSentence "A #$KBDependentRelation (q.v.) and specialization of #$knownSentence (q.v.) that pragmatically delays attempting to prove its sentence argument until it has no free variables. More precisely, (#$checkSentence SENT) means that SENT is provable by the Cyc inference engine from sentences currently in the Knowledge Base. #$checkSentence is a non-assertible predicate (see #$notAssertible). Note that this predicate is not to be confused  with #$assertedSentence, which is used to state that a given  sentence is explicitly asserted in the KB.")
(comment CellMembrane-Stuff "The collection of #$LipidBilayers out of which #$CellMembranes are constituted. Note that (#$rewriteOf #$CellMembrane (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Cell #$CellMembrane-Stuff)). #$CellMembrane-Stuff should be used for representing the qualities of the membrane material which constitutes cell membranes (e.g., the presence of receptor proteins) and #$CellMembrane should be used for representing qualities of complete cell membranes that cannot be asserted of #$CellMembrane-Stuff (e.g., containment of cytoplasm). ")
(comment SubcellularMembrane "This is the collection of #$CellularMembranes that are internal parts of #$Cells. It consists of all #$CellularMembranes except for #$CellMembranes.")
(disjointWith Photophosphorylation-Chloroplast SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(disjointWith SignalTransduction-CellularProcess ElectronTransfer)
(comment Ferredoxin "A specialization of #$ProteinStuff. #$Ferredoxin is an iron-sulfur protein that plays an important role in #$ElectronTransfer events in chemical reactions.")
(comment ElectronDonorType "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects that can donate an electron to another compound in a chemical reaction. They frequently play the role of #$reducingAgent in #$RedoxReaction.   ")
(comment ElectronAcceptorType "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects that can accept an electron from another compound in a chemical reaction. They frequently play the role of #$oxidizingAgent in #$RedoxReaction.   ")
(comment typeAcceptsSubatomicTypeInEventType "(#$typeAcceptsSubatomicTypeInEventType EVENT-TYPE CHEM-TYPE PARTICLE-TYPE) means that instances of CHEM-TYPE accept instances of PARTICLE-TYPE in events of type EVENT-TYPE.  ")
(comment typeDonatesSubatomicTypeInEventType "(#$typeDonatesSubatomicTypeInEventType EVENT-TYPE CHEM-TYPE PARTICLE-TYPE) means that instances of CHEM-TYPE donate instances of PARTICLE-TYPE in events of type EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment focalStepTypeForStepAtWhichTypeActsInTypeTest "<code>(#$focalStepTypeForStepAtWhichTypeActsInTypeTest TEST STEP-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>STEP-TYPE</code> as the type of process-step that should be considered when suggesting the query associated with <code>TEST</code>, an instance of #$CPTStepAtWhichTypeActsInTypeTest.")
(comment evidenceContraryToTheory "<code>(#$evidenceContraryToTheory EVIDENCE THEORY)</code> means that <code>EVIDENCE</code> is evidence that conflicts with <code>THEORY</code>, an instance of #$PhilosophicalTheory.")
(comment PerRatioColFn "A CollectionDenotingFunction that returns collection instances of QuantityType that are specializations of RatioQuantity. Specifically, where NUMERATOR-TYPE and DENOMINATOR-TYPE are both instances of #$InterconvertibleUnitType, (#$PerRatioColFn NUMERATOR-TYPE DENOMINATOR-TYPE) denotes all scalar quantities that can be represented as a ratio where the numerator is measured by units of the first type and the denominator is measured by units of the second type.  Thus, e.g. (#$PerRatioColFn #$UnitOfMoney #$UnitOfVolume) would represent the collection of all quantities measuring a unit of money per unit volume, such as ((#$PerFn #$Dollar-UnitedStates #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume) 108), ((#$PerFn #$Ruble-Russia #$Liter) 100), ((#$PerFn #$Rupee-Nepal #$Gallon-Imperial) 52.8), and so on. ")
(comment HydrophobicInteriorOfLipidBilayer "The collection of hydrophic interior regions of #$LipidBilayers that result from the hydrophobic aggregation of the #$HydrophobicTailOfPhospholipids.")
(comment in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix "A #$ConnectionPredicate and specialization of #$sticksInto (q.v.) that relates #$PartiallyTangibles to the #$FluidTangibleThing matrices in which they are embedded. Note that <code>(#$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix OBJ MATRIX)</code> does not mean that OBJ is #$in-ImmersedGeneric in <code>MATRIX</code>, nor that it is wet in any appreciable way. Such embeddings have many of the properties associated with #$in-Rooted, except that one of the associated objects is technically a fluid. Most instances of #$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix relations occur at the molecular level (e.g., #$Molecules and #$MacromolecularComplexes embedded in #$CellularMembranes), but probably not all (e.g. #$Cells in an #$ExtracellularMatrix).")
(comment in-EmbeddedInAndPassesThroughFluidMatrix "A #$ConnectionPredicate and specialization of #$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix (q.v.) that relates #$PartiallyTangibles to the #$FluidTangibleThing matrices in which they are embedded in and pass through. Note that <code>(#$in-EmbeddedInFluidMatrix OBJ MATRIX)</code> does not mean that OBJ is #$in-ImmersedGeneric in <code>MATRIX</code>, nor that it is wet in any appreciable way. Such embeddings have many of the properties associated with #$inRooted-PassesThrough, except that one of the associated objects is technically a fluid. Most instances of #$in-EmbeddedInAndPassesThroughFluidMatrix relations occur at the molecular level (e.g., #$Molecules and #$MacromolecularComplexes embedded in #$CellularMembranes).")
(comment agentTypeRoleStateRequirement "(#$agentTypeRoleStateRequirement AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE FEATURE) means that an instance AGT of type AGENT-TYPE plays ROLE in a situation SIT of type SIT-TYPE only if (#$physicalStructuralFeatures AGT REQ-FEATURE) holds for the duration of SIT.")
(comment agentTypeCapabilityStateRequirement "(#$agentTypeCapabilityStateRequirement AGENT-TYPE CAPABILITY REQ-FEATURE) means that an instance AGT of type AGT-TYPE has the capability CAPABILITY only if REQ-FEATURE is a #$physicalStructuralFeatures of AGT.")
(comment agentTypeFunctionalRoleStateRequirement "(#$agentTypeFunctionalRoleStateRequirement AGENT-TYPE SYSTEM-TYPE SYSTEM-ROLE FEATURE) means that an instance of AGENT-TYPE, AGENT, plays the functional role SYSTEM-ROLE in a #$FunctionalSystem of type SYSTEM-TYPE only if (#$physicalStructuralFeatures AGENT FEATURE) holds in the context of the role-playing.")
(comment ElectronTransferFromExcitedP680ToPrimaryElectronAcceptor "A specialization of #$ElectronTransfer and #$ChemicalReaction.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransferFromExcitedP680ToPrimaryElectronAcceptor is an event in which an electron is transferred from the excited P680 to the primary electron acceptor. It results in the formation of P680+. ")
(comment OxygenEvolvingComplex "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of catalyzing water splitting reaction in photosynthesis events.")
(comment SugarMolecule "The collection of all sugar molecules, that is, molecules of #$Disaccharides and #$Monosaccharides.  These typically have the empirical formula (CH2O)n, where n means there can be any multiple up to 12 of (CH2O).")
(comment Sugar "Instances are portions of sugar, i.e., a piece of a substance made up of sugar molecules.  #$Sugars include #$Monosaccharides and #$Disaccharides.")
(comment geopoliticalTargetOfInvasion "(#$geopoliticalTargetOfInvasion INVASION MAX-TARGET) means that MAX-TARGET is the broadest #$GeographicalRegion that may justifiably be said to be the 'target' of INVASION, in the sense that whomever is conducting INVASION has the immediate goal of achieving political and military control over the inhabitants and government of MAX-TARGET.")
(comment Polymerization-Biosynthesis "A specialization of #$Polymerization and #$BiochemicalSynthesis.  Each instance of #$Polymerization-Biosynthesis is a chemical reaction in which polymers are produced by biochemical processes inside the bodies of living organisms.")
(comment quantityOfEnergyStuff "A #$FunctionalSlot and specialization of #$hasPhysicalQuantity that relates a portion of #$EnergyStuff to an #$EnergyQuantity.  <code>(#$quantityOfEnergyStuff E-STUFF QUANT)</code> means that the total quantity of energy represented by <code>E-STUFF</code> is <code>QUANT</code>.  ")
(comment entireChemicalEnergyPortion "A #$FunctionalSlot that relates a #$PartiallyTangible to a portion of #$ChemicalEnergy.  For example, (#$entireChemicalEnergyPortion ChocolateBar37 (#$EntireChemicalEnergyPortionFn ChocolateBar37)) states that (#$EntireChemicalEnergyPortionFn ChocolateBar37) is all the #$ChemicalEnergy contained in ChocolateBar37.\"")
(comment EntireChemicalEnergyPortionFn "A function, applied to a #$PartiallyTangible (such as a #$Doughnut, a #$Plant or a #$Molecule), returns a portion of #$ChemicalEnergy that is the entire portion of chemical energy that is \"in\" or \"possessed by\" that #$PartiallyTangible.  For example, in a particular temporal context, (#$EntireChemicalEnergyPortionFn Plant37) denotes the whole portion of chemical energy embodied in Plant37.  This is a time-dependent quantity, because the size of the portion can change as the plant respires or photosynthesizes.")
(comment AbsorptionInAlimentaryCanal "Each instance of #$AbsorptionInAlimentaryCanal is a bodily event in which an animal absorbs small #$Molecules into its #$Cells via the walls of its #$AlimentaryCanal. ")
(comment Biofuel "A specialization of #$Fuel. It is a type of fuel whose energy is derived from biological carbon fixation. #$FossilFuels are not considered instances of this collection.")
(comment EthanolFermentationProcess "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess and #$ChemicalProcess. An instance of #$EthanolFermentationProcess is a process in which yeasts convert sugars such as #$Glucose and #$Fructose into #$Ethanol and #$CarbonDioxide.\" ")
(comment IndustrialProduction-Generic "A specialization of #$Production-Generic. In each instance of #$IndustrialProduction-Generic, some goods or services are produced at an industrial facility. ")
(comment ProductionOfBiodiesel-ChemicalReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances are chemical reactions in which biodiesel is produced. ")
(comment IndustrialEthanolProduction "A specialization of #$IndustrialProduction-Generic. In each instance of #$IndustrialEthanolProduction, ethanol is produced at a large scale in a factory. ")
(comment IndustrialBiodieselProduction "A specialization of #$IndustrialProduction-Generic. In each instance of #$IndustrialBiodieselProduction, biodiesel is produced at a large scale in a factory. ")
(comment TranslationOfSubAtomicParticles "A specialization of #$Translation-LocationChange. In an instance of #$TranslationOfSubAtomicParticles, the moving object is a  #$SubAtomicParticle .")
(comment Quinone "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound.  It is a class of compounds that is derived from aromatic compounds such as #$Benzene and naphthalene. They are used in the production of hydrogen peroxide.")
(comment Plastoquinone "A specialization of #$Quinone.  Instances are involved in the electron transfer chain from #$PhotosystemII to #$PhotosystemI. ")
(comment BiodieselProductionProcess "A specialization of #$ChemicalProcess. An instance of #$BiodieselProductionProcess is a process in which biodiesel is produced through #$Esterification and transesterification. ")
(comment electronDonor "An #$ActorSlot that is a specialization of #$fromLocation (q.v.).  This predicate is used to identify the #$ChemicalObject which donates an #$Electron (or a fraction of an electron) in an #$ElectronTransfer event.  <code>(#$electronDonor TRANFSER DONOR)</code> means that in <code>TRANSFER</code>, an electron moves away from <code>DONOR</code> and toward the chemical object playing the role of #$electronAcceptor.  ")
(comment electronAcceptor "An #$ActorSlot that is a specialization of #$toLocation (q.v.).  This predicate is used to identify the #$ChemicalObject which receives an #$Electron (or a fraction of an electron) in an #$ElectronTransfer event.  <code>(#$electronAcceptor TRANFSER ACC)</code> means that in <code>TRANSFER</code>, an electron moves away from the chemical object playing the role of #$electronDonor and toward <code>ACC</code>.")
(comment CytochromeB6FComplex "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule. Instances play an important role in transferring electrons from #$PhotosystemII to #$PhotosystemI. ")
(comment subAtomicParticleCarrier "<code>(#$subAtomicParticleCarrier EVENT CARRIER)</code> means that <code>CARRIER</code> carries an instance of #$SubAtomicParticle in EVENT. ")
(comment ElectronTransfer "A specialization of #$ChemicalInteraction.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransfer is an event in which an electron (or a fraction of an electron) is transferred from one #$ChemicalObject to another.  #$ElectronTransfer events are always part of some #$RedoxReaction.")
(comment ElectronTransferFromTypeToTypeFn "<code>(#$ElectronTransferFromTypeToTypeFn TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ElectronTransfer in which an #$Electron or fraction of an electron is transferred from an instance of <code>TYPE1</code> to an instance of <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment electronTransferFromTypeToType "<code>(#$electronTransferFromTypeToType TYPE1 TYPE2 TRANSFER-TYPE)</code> means that <code>TRANSFER-TYPE</code> is the collection of #$ElectronTransfer events in which an #$Electron, or a fraction of an electron, is transferred from an instance of the #$ChemicalObject <code>TYPE1</code> to an instance of the #$ChemicalObject <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment electronCarrier "<code>(#$electronCarrier ET-CHAIN CARRIER)</code> means that <code>CARRIER</code> carries an electron during part of the #$ElectronTransportChain, <code>ET-CHAIN</code>.  Specifically, the #$ChemicalObject <code>CARRIER</code> is the #$electronAcceptor in one #$ElectronTransfer in <code>ET-CHAIN</code>, and is the #$electronDonor in the subsequent step in the chain.")
(comment chemicalObjectsInElectronTransportChain "<code>(#$chemicalObjectsInElectronTransportChain CHAIN-TYPE LIST-OF-OBJ-TYPES)</code> means that: <p>(1) for each instance <code>ETC</code> of <code>CHAIN-TYPE</code>, there exists some instance of each element of <code>LIST-OF-OBJ-TYPES</code>. The first in the list is the #$fromLocation for the chain of transfers as a whole, the last in the list is the #$toLocation, and each intermediate element plays the role of #$electronCarrier in the #$ElectronTransportChain <code>ETC</code>; <p>(2) there are no further chemical objects playing those roles in <code>ECT</code> that are not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of <code>LIST-OF-OBJ-TYPES</code>;<p>(3) for each pair of #$ChemicalObject types <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code> adjacent in ?LIST, there exists an instance <code>TRANS</code> of #$ElectronTransfer which is a #$properSubEvents of <code>ECT</code>, and in which an instance of <code>TYPE1</code> is the #$electronDonor, and <code>TYPE2</code> is the #$electronAcceptor; <p>(4) the #$firstSubEvents of <code>ETC</code> will be an instance of #$ElectronTransfer between instances of the first two elements of ?LIST; <p>and (5) the #$lastSubEvents of <code>ETC</code> will be an instance of #$ElectronTransfer between instances of the last two elements of ?LIST;   <p>For example, (#$chemicalObjectsInElectronTransportChain #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSII-To-PSI  (#$TheList #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII (#$MoleculeFn #$Plastoquinone) #$CytochromeB6FComplex #$PlastocyaninMolecule #$P700ChlorophyllAMolecule)).  This means that, for example, (#$properSubEventTypes #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSII-To-PSI (ElectronTransferFromTypeToTypeFn #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII (#$MoleculeFn #$Plastoquinone)).  Further, for any instance of #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSII-To-PSI <b>PSIIToPSIChain-001</b>, there is no sub-event of <b>PSIIToPSIChain-001</b> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of (#$TheList #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII (#$MoleculeFn #$Plastoquinone) #$CytochromeB6FComplex #$PlastocyaninMolecule #$P700ChlorophyllAMolecule)).  Other things are entailed as described in 3 - 5 above.")
(disjointWith MembraneTransportOfHydrogenPlusIon ElectronTransfer)
(comment concentrationOfHydroniumIonsInRegion "(#$concentrationOfHydroniumIonsInRegion REGION CONCENTRATION) means that REGION  has the concentration of H+ ions CONCENTRATION.")
(comment ConcentrationofHydroniumIons "A specialization of #$Molarity (q.v.). Each instance of #$ConcentrationofHydroniumIons is the number of moles (see #$Mole-ChemicalCountUnit) of #$HydrogenPlusIons per unit volume of some solution.")
(comment TranslationOfAtomicAndSubAtomicParticles "A specialization of #$Translation-LocationChange. In an instance of #$TranslationOfAtomicAndSubAtomicParticles, the moving object is an  #$Atom, #$Ion or a #$SubAtomicParticle .")
(comment TranslationOfIon "A specialization of #$TranslationOfAtomicAndSubAtomicParticles. In an instance of #$TranslationOfIons, the moving object is an  #$Ion .")
(comment ElectronTransferFromExcitedP700ToPrimaryElectronAcceptor "A specialization of #$ElectronTransfer and #$ChemicalReaction.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransferFromExcitedP700ToPrimaryElectronAcceptor is an event in which an electron is transferred from the excited P700 to the primary electron acceptor. It results in the formation of P700 . ")
(comment agentRoleMetricRequirement "(#$agentRoleMetricRequirement AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE METRIC-SLOT RANGE) means that an instance of AGENT-TYPE, AGENT, plays the role ROLE in an instance of SIT-TYPE, SIT, only if the #$MeasurableQuantitySlot METRIC-SLOT has the value RANGE on AGENT throughout the course of SIT.")
(comment agentFunctionalRoleMetricRequirement "Where QUANT-SLOT is a #$MeasurableQuantitySlot, (#$agentFunctionalRoleMetricRequirement AGENT-TYPE SYSTEM-TYPE SYSTEM-ROLE QUANT-SLOT VAL) means that an instance of AGENT-TYPE, AGENT, plays the #$SystemRole SYSTEM-ROLE in an instance of SYSTEM-TYPE only if (QUANT-SLOT AGENT VAL) holds in the temporal context of the role-playing.")
(comment agentCapabilityMetricRequirement "Where QUANT-SLOT is a #$MeasurableQuantitySlot, (#$agentCapabilityMetricRequirement AGENT-TYPE CAPABILITY QUANT-SLOT VAL) means that if AGENT is an instance of AGENT-TYPE, (hasCapability AGENT CAPABILITY) is true only if (QUANT-SLOT AGENT VAL) is true.")
(comment columnValueInDBDecodedVia "(#$columnValueInDBDecodedVia COLUMN FUNCTION) means that FUNCTION is either an evaluatable or an unreifiable unary function and the the raw values that appear in COLUMN are assigned their logical values by an application of FUNCTION.")
(comment AminoAcidTypeBySideChainProperties "This type level collection (see #$CollectionType) is a partition of #$AminoAcid. Each instance of #$AminoAcidTypeBySideChainProperties is an equivalence class of #$AminoAcids grouped according to the characteristic properties of their side chains (R groups). I.e, #$NonpolarAminoAcids, #$UnchargedPolarAminoAcids, #$AcidicAminoAcids, and #$BasicAminoAcids.")
(comment NonpolarAminoAcid "The collection of #$AminoAcids which are nonpolar, and consequently #$HydrophobicChemicalObjects.")
(comment UnchargedPolarAminoAcid "The collection of #$AminoAcids which are polar but uncharged, and consequently #$HydrophilicChemicalObjects.")
(comment PositivelyChargedAminoAcid "The collection of #$AminoAcids which are negatively charged, and consequently slightly basic.")
(comment NegativelyChargedAminoAcid "The collection of #$AminoAcids which are nonpolar, and consequently slightly acidic.")
(comment ChannelProtein "Each instance of #$ChannelProtein is a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex and #$MembraneTransportProtein that has as part of its structure a hydrophilic channel through which hydrophilic substances may pass. #$IonChannels are a specialization which permit the passage of certain charged particles. #$Aquaporins permit the pasage of water, but screen out charged particles.")
(comment connectedTo-Loosely "A specialization of #$connectedTo, <code>(#$connectedTo-Loosely OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> are #$connectedTo one another, but in such a way that not much energy, effort, etc. would be required to break the relationship.")
(disjointWith BiologicalMembrane (CollectionDifferenceFn LipidBilayer BiologicalMembrane))
(comment Bacteriorhodopsin "A type of #$TransmembraneProtein found in the
#$CellMembranes of some types of #$Archaea. #$Bacteriorhodopsin is a
photoactivated proton pump.")
(comment PeptideN-Terminus "The collection of N-termini of
#$PeptideMolecules. #$PeptideMolecules of any length have an amine
group at one end and a carboxyl group at the other. This
\"terminal\" amine group is the N-terminus.")
(comment PeptideC-Terminus "The collection of C-termini of
#$PeptideMolecules. #$PeptideMolecules of any length have an amine
group at one end and a carboxyl group at the other. This
\"terminal\" carboxyl group is the C-terminus.")
(comment Cell-CellRecognitionProtein "The specialization of #$MembraneProteins which enable the
cell to recognize other cells and/or for other cells to recognize the
cell. Note that, although this function may involve brief attachment,
it is distinct from #$IntercellularJoiningProtein.")
(comment IntercellularJoiningProtein "The specialization of #$MembraneProteins which enable cells
to attach to one another in various ways, for purposes other than cell
recognition (q.v. #$Cell-CellRecognitionProtein).")
(comment AttachmentProtein "The specialization of #$MembraneProteins which are attached
to the cytoskeleton or extracellular matrix.")
(comment PlastocyaninMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  #$PlastocyaninMolecules are an important participant in electron transfer which occurs as part of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.")
(comment LawOfThermodynamics "The 4 laws of thermodynamics.")
(comment awayFromLocation "The predicate #$awayFromLocation is used to indicate a location away from which something moves in a particular movement.  <code>(#$awayFromLocation MOVE LOC)</code> means that, when movement ends, each #$objectMoving in <code>MOVE</code> (a #$Movement-TranslationEvent) is found further from <code>LOC</code> than it was when the event <code>MOVE</code> started. <code>LOC</code> may be, but is not necessarily, the starting location of each #$objectMoving in that event.  For that stronger meaning, see the spec-predicate #$fromLocation.  See also #$motionPathway-Complete, #$pathConnects.")
(comment towardLocation "The predicate #$towardLocation is used to indicate a location toward which something moves in a particular movement.  <code>(#$towardLocation MOVE LOC)</code> means that, when movement ends, each #$objectMoving in <code>MOVE</code> (a #$Movement-TranslationEvent) is found closer to <code>LOC</code> than it was when the event <code>MOVE</code> started. <code>LOC</code> may be, but is not necessarily, the final location of each #$objectMoving in that event. For that stronger meaning, see the spec-predicate #$toLocation See also #$motionPathway-Complete, #$pathConnects.")
(comment OrganicFuelMolecule "A collection of #$Molecules.  Instances of #$OrganicFuelMolecule are molecules of #$OrganicCompounds that are rich in bonds between #$Carbon and #$Hydrogen #$Atoms. When these molecules are oxidized, the high potential energy of the electrons in the C-H bonds is set free when new, lower-energy bonds form, and can be harnessed to do work or released as heat.  Examples include molecules of substances used as fuels for machines or industrial processes, like (#$MoleculeFn #$Propane), as well as molecules used by living cells to do work, such as (#$MoleculeFn #$CarbohydrateStuff) and (#$MoleculeFn #$Lipid). ")
(comment facilitates-SitTypeSitType "<code>(#$facilitates-SitTypeSitType FOSTERING FOSTERED)</code> means that in general, instances of <code>FOSTERING</code> tend to facilitate (i.e., aid in the occurrence of) instances of <code>FOSTERED</code>.")
(comment fieldPrinciples "<code>(#$fieldPrinciples FIELD PROPOSITION)</code> means that the instance <code>PROPOSITION</code> of #$Proposition is one of the principles of <code>FIELD</code>, an instance of #$FieldOfStudy.  #$fieldPrinciples holds not of just any proposition that the practitioners of <code>FIELD</code> are likely to assent to (e.g., That Paris is a city in France, does not qualify as a principle of any field; it's just something everybody knows.); rather a principle is held up by the practitioners as an established truth that explains some aspect of the phenomena of interest to the field.  The body of such principles for a field (plus its corollaries) in some loose sense comprises \"the prevalent theory\" of a field.")
(comment situationConsistentWithPrinciples "<code>(#$situationConsistentWithPrinciples SITUATION PRINCIPLE)</code> means that the instance <code>SITUAITON</code> of #$Situation adheres to, or is consistent with, <code>PRINCIPLE</code> an instance of #$Proposition.  Specifically, the set of all true sentences that describe <code>SITUATION</code> is #$consistent with the sentence of <code>PRINCIPLE</code>.")
(comment lawTypeExplainsPhenomena "<code>(#$lawTypeExplainsPhenomena LAW-TYPE EVENT-TYPE)</code> means that the class of event <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> falls under the scope of things explained by <code>LAW-TYPE</code>, an instance of #$LawOfNatureTypeByDomain.")
(comment LawOfNatureTypeByDomain "A collection that facets #$LawOfNature into subcollections based on the aspect of physical reality that they explain.")
(comment HydrogenBond "The collection of configurations in which an (#$AtomFn #$Hydrogen), covalently bonded in some #$ChemicalObject, is attracted to an electronegative #$Atom in some other instance of #$ChemicalObject, or within the same molecule if it is a large one.  Thus a weak bond exists between the two chemical objects, or between different parts of the same large molecule.")
(comment CarbonHydrogenBond "The collection of configurations in which an (#$AtomFn #$Hydrogen) is covalently bonded to an (#$AtomFn #$Carbon), most likely as part of a larger #$Molecule.  Such bonds are NOT a specialization of #$HydrogenBond.")
(comment internalChemicalBonds "This predicate relates a #$PolyAtomicChemicalObject to the #$ChemicalBonds that cause its component #$Atoms to stay together.  <code>(#$internalChemicalBonds CHEMICAL-OBJECT BOND)</code> states that <code>BOND</code> is one of the bonds between two of the atoms that <code>CHEMICAL-OBJECT</code> comprises.")
(comment sitTypeIsSpecWithTypeRestrictionOnRolePlayer "<code>(sitTypeIsSpecWithTypeRestrictionOnRolePlayer SPEC SIT-TYPE ROLE TYPE)</code> identifies <code>SPEC</code> as the unique specialization of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, a specializaton of #$Situation, such that all objects that play <code>ROLE </code> in instances of <code>SPEC</code> are, at the appropriate temporal span of actively playing that role, instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment Metabolism-SingleCellOrganism "The collection of instances of Metabolism done at by single-celled organisms.")
(comment Metabolism-MulticellularOrganism "The collection of instances of Metabolism done by multi-cellular organisms.")
(comment Metabolism-EntireOrganism "The collection of instances of Metabolism done by an entire organism.")
(comment Metabolism-Cellular "The collection of instances of Metabolism done at the cellular level.")
(comment TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn "<code>(#$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of #$IteratedEventScenes that are #$properSubEventTypes of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> that satisfy the following conditions <pre> Assume TOTALITY = (#$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE) <br><br>   1.  <b>Maximality</b>: If EVENT is an instance of EVENT-TYPE and TOTAL-01 is a proper sub-event of<br> EVENT and an instance of TOTALITY, then for any SUB such that SUB is a<br> sub-event of EVENT and an instance of SUB-EVENT-TYPE, SUB is a sub-event<br> of TOTAL-01  <br> <br> 2.  <b>Exclusion</b>: Any sub-event of an instance of the totality collection is a sub-event of<br> some instance of SUB-EVENT-TYPE or some temporal sum of them -- i.e. every part of<br> it is a sub-event of some instance of SUB-EVENT-TYPE.  </pre>  For example, assume DrawingWaterFromAManualPump is a complex event type in which a bucket or other container is placed under a manual water pump, optionally some water is poured into the pump to prime it, then a number of iterations of MovingTheHandleOfAManualPumpUpAndDown are performed until water begins to flow into the container.  Given that, (#$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn DrawingWaterFromAManualPump MovingTheHandleOfAManualPumpUpAndDown) is the collection of the proper sub-events of instances of DrawingWaterFromAManualPump that consist of repeated instances of MovingTheHandleOfAManualPumpUpAndDown.  It is easy to see that any sub-event of an instance of (#$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn DrawingWaterFromAManualPump MovingTheHandleOfAManualPumpUpAndDown) is itself a sub-event of some instance of MovingTheHandleOfAManualPumpUpAndDown -- e.g. the first time the handle is moved upwards, or is a sub-event of some sum -- e.g. the arbitrary sub-event that consists of moving the handle down during the second iteration and moving the handle up during the third iteration is a sub-event of the sum of the second and third iterations.  <br><br>Note that the instances of the returned collection need not be temporally contiguous (cf. contiguousAfter).  E.g. each instance of (#$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn #$BaseballGame #$BaseballInning) consists of a series of temporally non-contiguous baseball innings.  Given that the events between the innings are not sub-events of the innings, it is easy to see how those portions of the baseball game fail to be subevents of instances of this collection -- the Exclusion condition rules them out because no part of any break between the innings is a part of a baseball inning. This is the function that corresponds to the third argument of the predicate #$iterativeSubEventTypesTotality.")
(comment BiologicalMembrane "This is the collection of membranes which grow as parts of living #$Cells. It not only includes the outermost CellMembrane, but also the NuclearEnvelope, inner and outer mitocondrial membranes, etc. Note that this is the constant to use when representing facts that hold of #$BiologicalMembranes qua objects and not of the membrane stuff out of which they consist. To represent facts about the later, use BiologicalMembrane-Stuff.")
(comment BiologicalMembrane-Stuff "This is the collection of all LipidBilayers that are parts of Cells, making up the various membrane structures therein. The corresponding \"objectual\" constant is #$BiologicalMembrane")
(comment TissueMembrane "The collection of #$Membranes which are #$BiologicalTissues. It does not include #$BiologicalMembranes, which are parts of #$Cells.")
(comment iterativeSubEventTypesTotality "<code>(#$iterativeSubEventTypesTotality EVENT-TYPE SUB-SUB-EVENT-TYPE SUB-EVENT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>SUB-EVENT-TYPE</code> as the collection of all instances of #$IteratedEventScene that are iterations through instances of <code>SUB-SUB-EVENT-TYPE</code> as part of the unfolding of some event of type <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$TotalityOfSubEventsOfTypeFn.  See that term for a more formal definition of the meaning of this relation.")
(comment electronAffinityOfType "(#$electronAffinityOfType ELEMENT KJ_PER_MOLE) means that the amount of energy needed for adding electrons to atoms of ELEMENT is the specified amount (normally expressed in kiloJoules per mole).  Electron affinity has often been expressed with the opposite sign -- indicating energy released when an electron is added")
(comment electronegativityOfType "(#$electronegativityOfType ELEMENT VALUE) indicates the ability of an atom in a molecule to attract electrons to itself.  The relative electronegativities of two atoms sharing a bond indicate whether that bond would be non-polar, polar covalent, or ionic.  An atom with high #$ionizationEnergy and very negative #$electronAffinityOfType would be very electronegative.  Values of #$electronegativityOfType range from 0.7 to 4.0.")
(comment ReductionOfNADPPlusToNADPH "The type of #$Reduction-ChemicalReaction in which #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate is reduced to #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate.")
(comment SituationFn "#$SituationFn is a Cyc function.  (#$SituationFn VAR FORM) denotes a collection of situations, whose instances satisfy VAR as used in the #$CycLSentence-Assertible FORM.  FORM will contain ?VAR as a free variable, and may contain other variables.  For now (11/97), quantification of all other variables must be explicit, and we do not allow variables bound outside of #$SituationFn to appear within FORM.  For example, FORM might describe the general situation in which a person speaks to their boss:  (#$SituationFn ?SPK (#$thereExists ?PER (#$thereExists ?BOSS (#$and (#$isa ?SPK #$Speaking) (#$senderOfInfo ?SPK ?PER) (#$communicationTarget ?SPK ?BOSS) (#$boss ?PER ?BOSS))))).")
(comment CCR5Protein "The collection of C-C chemokine receptors of type 5 (CCR5)
proteins which occur primarily on the surface of human white blood
cells. It is a chemokine receptor that also serves as a co-receptor
for (#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus).")
(comment ViralInvasionOfCell "The collection of events in which an instance of #$Virus (a
virion) invades a living #$Cell. A spec of #$ActionOnObject.")
(comment viralInvader "An #$ActorSlot relating an instance of #$Virus (a virion) to
a #$ViralInvasionOfCell. <code>(#$viralInvader INV VIR)</code> means
that VIR is the virion that invaded a cell in event INV.")
(comment invadedCell "An #$ActorSlot relating a #$Cell to a
#$ViralInvasionOfCell. <code>(#$invadedCell INV CELL)</code> means
that CELL is the cell that invade by a virion in the event INV.")
(comment invasionOfCellByVirusType "The predicate that corresponds to
#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn. <code>(#$invasionOfCellByVirusType
VIRUS-TYPE (#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn VIRUS-TYPE))</code> will
always be true when <code>VIRUS-TYPE</code> is a type of #$Virus.")
(comment InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn "<code>(#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn VIRUS-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ViralInvasionOfCell in which an individual cell is invaded by a virus of type <code>VIRUS-TYPE</code>. Thus, <code>(#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus)</code> denotes the collection of events in which an individual cell is invaded by an instance of the #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus. Note that, although a cell may be invaded/infected by a particular virus, it usually does not have the associated #$ViralInfection, this is something contracted by a host organism as a whole, and it usually involves many millions of #$ViralInvasionOfCell subevents (except when the host is itself a microorganism).")
(comment EndergonicChemicalInteraction "Instances are chemical interactions (see #$ChemicalInteraction) which require energy.")
(comment ExergonicChemicalInteraction "Instances are chemical interactions (see #$ChemicalInteraction) which release energy.")
(comment SimpleRedoxReaction "A specialization of #$RedoxReaction and an instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Instances of #$SimpleRedoxReaction are #$ChemicalReactions in which #$Electrons are transferred from one #$ChemicalObject to another.  The object providing the electrons is oxidized (see #$Oxidation-HalfReaction), while the one gaining the electrons is reduced (see #$Reduction-HalfReaction).  
<p>In some cases entire electrons change ownership. For example, when #$Sodium reacts with #$Chlorine to form #$Salt-NaCl, an #$Electron from #$Sodium is transferred wholly to the atom of #$Chlorine.   In other cases the degree of electron sharing between atoms changes. For example, in the #$Carbon to #$Hydrogen bonds in #$Methane, a pair of electrons is shared about equally; the same is true of molecular #$Oxygen (O2).  After methane and oxygen react to form CO2 and water, electrons move closer to the oxygen atoms, but they don't entirely leave the carbon atom (now part of CO2) or the hydrogen atom (now part of H2O).
<p>#$SimpleRedoxReaction instances complete in a single step, having one #$Reduction-HalfReaction, one #$Oxidation-HalfReaction and one #$ElectronTransfer as subevents.  Complex redox reactions needing muliple steps to complete, such as the oxidation of organic molecules in #$CellularRespiration, are not included in this collection.")
(comment Oxidation-HalfReaction "A specialization of #$OxidationProcess and an instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Instances of #$Oxidation-HalfReaction are #$ChemicalInteractions which are one part of a #$RedoxReaction R, and in which the #$reducingAgent of R becomes oxidized by beciming less closely associated with electrons.")
(comment Reduction-HalfReaction "A specialization of #$Reduction-ChemicalReaction and an instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Instances of #$Reduction-HalfReaction are #$ChemicalInteractions which are one part of a #$RedoxReaction R, and in which the #$oxidizingAgent of R becomes reduced by becoming more closely associated with electrons.")
(disjointWith ExergonicChemicalInteraction EndergonicChemicalInteraction)
(disjointWith Reduction-HalfReaction Oxidation-HalfReaction)
(disjointWith CyclicPhotophosphorylation SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(comment CyclicPhotophosphorylation "A specialization of #$Photophosphorylation. Instances occur during cyclic electron flow in #$PhotosystemI.")
(comment Fermenting-Brewing "The stage of #$Brewing durung which yeast operats on the sugars in wort to produce #$Ethanol and carbon dioxide, converting the wort into beer.")
(comment EthanolFermentationReaction "A specialization of #$Fermenting-Cellular. In this chemical reaction, sugars such as glucose, fructose, and sucrose are converted into #$Ethanol and #$CarbonDioxide.")
(comment AnaerobicBiochemicalProcess "The collection of all groups of instances of #$BiochemicalProcess in which #$Oxygen does not play a role.  This includes both biochemical processes that can occur in the presence of oxygen and simply don't use it, as well as those biochemical process that can only occur when oxygen is absent.")
(comment CellularRespiration "The breakdown of energy-containing organic molecules such as sugars, which releases energy used to make ATP.  Some form of this process occurs in the cells of all living things.  The most common type of cellular respiration is #$CellularRespiration-Aerobic; however, some prokaryotes (see #$ProkaryoticCell) perform #$AnaerobicCellularRespiration. ")
(comment AnaerobicCellularRespiration "The breakdown by prokaryotes (see #$ProkaryoticCell) of energy-containing organic molecules (see #$OrganicFuelMolecule), which releases energy used to make ATP, without the use of #$Oxygen.  This collection includes instances that have a variety of chemical reaction formulas, because processes have evolved to use 10 or so different molecules, other than oxygen, as the electron acceptor. ")
(disjointWith CellularRespiration-Aerobic AnaerobicCellularRespiration)
(disjointWith MolarEnergy ElectricalConductance)
(comment MolarEnergy "A specialization of #$RatioQuantity (q.v.). Each instance of #$MolarEnergy is a ratio of an amount of energy (#$EnergyQuantity) to the number of moles (see #$Mole-ChemicalCountUnit) of some chemical species, and is often measured in (#$PerFn #$Kilocalorie #$Mole-ChemicalCountUnit) or (#$PerFn (#$Kilo #$Joule) #$Mole-ChemicalCountUnit).  Instances of #$MolarEnergy can be used to talk about the concentration of chemical energy in a type of substance, or the rate of energy released when a type of compound is catabolized.")
(comment Vesicle "A specialization of #$LipidBilayer.  Each instance of #$Vesicle is a lipid bilayer enclosing a small area.")
(comment Liposome "A specialization of #$Vesicle.  Each instance of #$Liposome is an artificially constructed vesicle.")
(disjointWith CellMembrane Vesicle)
(disjointWith OuterNuclearMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerNuclearMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith Vesicle InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith Vesicle OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterNuclearMembrane Vesicle)
(disjointWith InnerNuclearMembrane Vesicle)
(comment SurfactantMoleculeStructure "The collection of all structures that surfactant molecules form in aqueous solution.")
(disjointWith OuterNuclearMembrane CellPlateMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerNuclearMembrane CellPlateMembrane)
(comment UnilamellarVesicle "A specialization of #$LipidBilayer and #$Vesicle.  Each instance of #$UnilamellarVesicle is a vesicle with one bilayer.")
(comment Micelle "A specialization of #$SurfactantMoleculeStructure.  Each instance of #$Micelle is a roughly spherical aggregate of surfactant molecules wherein the hydrophilic heads of the molecules are in contact with the surrounding solution and the hydrophobic heads are pointed inward toward each other.")
(disjointWith Micelle Vesicle)
(disjointWith LipidBilayer Micelle)
(comment MultilamellarVesicle "A specialization of #$Vesicle.  Each instance of #$MultilamellarVesicle is a vesicle with more than one lipid bilayer.")
(disjointWith UnilamellarVesicle MultilamellarVesicle)
(comment systemicMetricRequirement "(#$systemicMetricRequirement SYSTEM QUANT-SLOT VAL SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that the #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEM requires a subcomponent to play the situational role ROLE in a #$Situation of type SIT-TYPE that is a sub-situation of its implementing process, and that a component of SYSTEM which does play the role ROLE in a sub-process of type SIT-TYPE is of a type AGENT-TYPE such that (#$agentRoleMetricRequirement AGENT-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE QUANT-SLOT VAL).  Intuitively, it means that SYSTEM depends on a subcomponent playing the role ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE, and that the subcomponent of SYSTEM which does play ROLE in a sub-process of type SIT-TYPE is of a type that necessitates its having the value VAL on QUANT-SLOT for the duration of the time that it plays ROLE in an instance of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment systemExemptedFromMetricConstraint "(#$systemExemptedFromMetricConstraint SYSTEM QUANT-SLOT VAL SIT-TYPE ROLE) holds just in case SYSTEM has a requirement (#$systemRequirement) for a subcomponent to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE, and a subcomponent which in fact plays ROLE in an instance of SIT-TYPE which is a subsituation of SYSTEM's implementation does *not* have to register a value of VAL on QUANT-SLOT in order to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment systemTypeMetricRequirement "(#$systemTypeMetricRequirement SYSTEM-TYPE QUANT-SLOT VALUE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that any normal instance of SYSTEM-TYPE features a component playing the required role ROLE in a required situation of type SIT-TYPE (subsumed by the systems implementing process) such that this component is only capable of playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE if it maintains VALUE on QUANT-SLOT throughout the duration of the role-playing (#$agentRoleMetricRequirement).")
(comment AmbientClimateSituation "The collection of all instances of #$WeatherEvent that may be correctly characterized as 'climates' or 'climate situation'.  The exact requirements for a #$WeatherEvent's meeting this criterion are vague, but it seems relatively safe to say that duration is a key feature:  that is, a 'climate' is a weather situation with distinguishing features that persist for more than hours, days, or probably weeks or months.  A year may be the minimum granularity (the collection of #$AnnualClimateCycles is precisely the collection of all #$AmbientClimateSituations of a duration of exactly one year). A given #$AmbientClimateSituation is characterized by certain metric ranges of temperature, humidity, pressure, and maybe other #$MeasurableQuantitySlots (e.g., pH level) that are never contravened for the duration of the #$AmbientClimateSituation in question. Every #$AmbientClimateSituation is an important situational subcomponent (#$subSituations) of the implementing process (#$autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem) of some #$Ecosystem:  we do not foreclose on the possibility that, in some cases at least, the #$AmbientClimateSituation *is* the implementing process, i.e., the process whereby the #$Ecosystem is realized.")
(comment ambientClimateTypeOfRegion "(#$ambientClimateTypeOfRegion REGION CLIMATE-TYPE) means that #$GeographicalRegion REGION is a constituent in (#$situationConstituents) in some #$AmbientClimateSituation that is an instance of they type CLIMATE-TYPE and whose temporal extent subsumes the time at which (#$ambientClimateTypeOfRegion REGION CLIMATE-TYPE) is true.")
(comment ambientClimateOfRegion "(#$ambientClimateOfRegion REGION CLIMATE) means that CLIMATE is an #$AmbientClimateSituation that occurs at the #$GeographicalRegion REGION.")
(comment ambientClimateOfEcosystem "(#$ambientClimateOfEcosystem ECOSYSTEM CLIMATE) means that CLIMATE is an #$AmbientClimateSituation which is a proper sub-situation (#$properSubSituations) of the implementing process (#$autocatalyticProcessImplementsSystem) of ECOSYSTEM.")
(comment climateEntailsValueOnSlot "Where CLIMATE-SIT is an #$AmbientClimateSituation, (#$climateEntailsValueOnSlot CLIMATE-SIT QUANT-SLOT VALUE) means that the exigencies of CLIMATE-SIT are such that some (at least one) #$situationConstituents have a value somewhere in the range given by VALUE on the #$MeasurableQuantitySlot QUANT-SLOT at every time point covered by CLIMATE-SIT.  Thus, e.g., (#$climateEntailsValueOnSlot AntarticClimate-PresentDay #$temperatureOfObject (#$IntervalRangeFn (#$DegreeCelsius -80)(#$DegreeCelsius 5))) means that, at  every time point in the present-day Antarctic climate (the #$AmbientClimateSituation that has obtained in Antarctica since probably the Eocene), there is some #$situationConstituents that has a temperature between -80 and 5 degrees celsius.")
(comment Ecosystem-Extreme "The class of all #$Ecosystems whose ambient climates feature some metric or metrics that contravene the ordinary systemic requirements of normal instances of #$Cell.  More specifically, an #$Ecosystem is considered an instance of #$Ecosystem-Extreme if its ambient climate (#$ambientClimateOfEcosystem) entails a value on the #$MeasurableQuantitySlot SLOT (#$climateEntailsValueOnSlot) that is greater than or less than a value that is a #$systemicMetricRequirement of #$Cells on the same #$MeasurableQuantitySlot SLOT, owing to cellular functional requirements and the limitations of the subcellular agents that ordinarily fill those requirements.")
(disjointWith Phosphorylation SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(disjointWith OxidativePhosphorylation SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(comment NonCyclicPhotophosphorylation "A specialization of #$Photophosphorylation. Instances occur during noncyclic electron flow in #$PhotosystemI and #$PhotosystemII. ")
(comment C3CarbonFixationInCalvinCycle "An instance of #$ChemicalReaction. It is one of three steps of #$CalvinCycle. In this step,  #$CarbonDioxide molecules are attached to a five-carbon sugar named ribulose bisphosphate. ")
(comment RegenerationOfRuBPInCalvinCycle "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. It is one of three steps of #$CalvinCycle. In this step,  #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate is converted into #$Ribulose-1-5-Bisphosphate.")
(disjointWith PassingThroughAnInitiallyObstructedPortal CarbonDioxideIntakeInPlants)
(comment MultiStepRedoxReaction "A specialization of #$RedoxReaction and an instance of #$TemporalObjectType.  Instances of #$MultiStepRedoxReaction are #$ChemicalReactions in which #$Electrons are transferred between #$ChemicalObjects in two more more steps, each of which are an instance of #$SimpleRedoxReaction.  The objects providing  electrons are oxidized while those gaining electrons are reduced.    <p>Examples of #$MultiStepRedoxReaction include the oxidation of organic molecules in #$CellularRespiration, and sequences of electron transfers that occur in an #$ElectronTransportChain. ")
(comment NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide-Generic "The collection of NAD  and NADH  molecules. Such molecules are found in all #$Cells, and have important roles in electron transfer.  The oxidized form, NAD  (#$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide) is able to become reduced (transformed into #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide) by accepting an electron, and then able to act to reduce other molecules by giving that electron up.")
(comment SurfactantMolecule "A specialization of #$AmphiphilicChemicalObject. Each instance of #$SurfactantMolecule is a molecule is an amphiphilic molecule (e.g. a phospholipid or a protein) that may form a bulk aggregate in water (see #$SurfactantMoleculeStructure).")
(comment hasState "A #$BinaryPredicate and #$TimeDependentRelation that relates an instance of #$EnduringThing-Localized to an instance of #$ObjectTypeByIntrinsicState.  <code>(#$hasState THING STATE)</code> means that, in the particular temporal context in which the formula is stated, <code>THING</code> is in the state, <code>STATE</code>.  Since #$hasState is a specialization of #$isa, this also means that, at that time, <code>THING</code> is an element of the collection, <code>STATE</code>. ")
(comment ChemicalObjectTypeByOxidationReductionState "A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects, all of the same #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies or #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType, characterized by the fact that each of its instances are in the same state of oxidation or reduction.  Membership in this collection shifts over time.  For example,  #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide, an instance of this collection, is the class of #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide-Generic molecules which are, in a given temporal context, in their reduced state.  <p>Note that \"oxidation state\" is a formal chemistry term that is a property of #$Atoms, but where an atom in a chemical object is in an oxidized state relative to some other form that atom and chemical object can be in, it is not uncommon for the chemical object as a whole to be referred to as \"oxidized.\"")
(comment typeHasOxidationReductionState "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a type of chemical object to oxidized and reduced forms it can occur in.  <code>(#$typeHasOxidationReductionState CHEM-TYPE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>STATE-TYPE</code> is a specialization of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> such that all of the instances of <code>STATE-TYPE</code> in a given temporal context exhibit the same degree of oxidation or reduction. <p>Note that \"oxidation state\" is a formal chemistry term that is a property of #$Atoms, but where an atom in a chemical object is in an oxidized state relative to some other form that atom and chemical object can be in, it is not uncommon for the chemical object as a whole to be referred to as \"oxidized.\"")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE ROLE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER)</code> and if <code>ROLEPLAYER</code> is an instance of TYPE</code>, then immediately before <code>SIT</code> begins, <code>(#$hasState ROLEPLAYER STATE-TYPE)</code> holds.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE ROLE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE SIT ROLEPLAYER)</code> and if <code>ROLEPLAYER</code> is an instance of TYPE</code>, then immediately after <code>SIT</code> begins, <code>(#$hasState ROLEPLAYER STATE-TYPE)</code> holds.")
(comment ChemicalObjectTypeByExcitationState "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects, all of the same #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies or #$MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType, characterized by whether the instances are at their ground state or at some excited state.  For example, given a temporal context, (#$ExcitedStateFn (#$MoleculeFn #$ChlorophyllA)) is the collection of #$ChlorophyllA molecules which are at that time in some excited state.")
(comment typeHasExcitationState "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates a type of chemical object to excited and ground states it can occur in.  <code>(#$typeHasExcitationState CHEM-TYPE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>STATE-TYPE</code> is a specialization of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> such that all of the instances of <code>STATE-TYPE</code> are either in their ground state or are in one of perhaps many possible excited states - that is, they are at an energy level which is above the baseline (= ground state) for that type of chemical object.")
(comment excitedState-TypeType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$ExcitedStateFn.  <code>(#$excitedState-TypeType CHEM-TYPE EXCITED-STATE-TYPE)</code> means that <code>EXCITED-STATE-TYPE</code> is the specialization of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>, an instance of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies, which includes all instances of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> that exhibit an energy level which is ABOVE the lowest possible level for instances of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>.")
(comment TheCurrentDocument "#$TheCurrentDocument is an #$IndexicalConcept that refers to the document that Cyc is currently engaged in understanding.")
(comment DogShow "The collection of dog shows.  Instances are #$JudgedCompetition in dogs act as #$competingAgents and are compared against one another along various standards, such as behavior (see #$DogObedienceTrial), physical skill (see #$DogAgilityTrial) or whether a dog instantiates an abstract aesthetic standard for that dog's breed (see #$DogBreedShow).  #$DogShow is defined so as to be disjoint with not-primarily-judged dog competitions, such as dog-fighting events or dog racing events.")
(comment JudgedCompetition "The collection of instances of #$Competition whose outcomes are, be design, determined by judging.")
(comment DogShowTypeByFocus "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$DogShow into specializations based on the standards by which the #$competingAgents in that type of show are judged.")
(comment TheNationalDogShow "One of three major types of #$DogBreedShow held in the United States, the National Dog Show is sanctioned by the American Kennel Club (see #$AmericanKennelClub).")
(comment DogBreedShow "The collection of instances of #$DogShow in which each competing dog is judged based on how well they instantiate an abstract aesthetic ideal for that dog's particular breed (see #$DogTypeByBreed).")
(comment DogObedienceCompetition "The collection of instances of #$DogShow in which dogs are judged on how well they follow a handler's set of commands.")
(comment coveringOfEventType-Nonoverlapping "<code>(#$coveringOfEventType-Nonoverlapping EVT-TYPE LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES)</code> means that:  <p> (1) for each instance <code>EVT</code> of <code>EVT-TYPE</code>, there exists some instance of each element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a proper sub-situation of <code>EVT</code>;  <p> (2) there are no further sub-situations of <code>EVT</code> that are not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>; <p> (3) an instance of the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> starts at the starting of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (4) after the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code>, each subsequent element of <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> is such that the instance of it that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code> starts after the end of the instance of the prior element in <code>LIST-OF-EVT-TYPES</code> that is a sub-event of <code>EVT</code>.   <p> Thus, for example, consider the claim (#$coveringOfEventType-Nonoverlapping #$NFLSeason (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  This means that (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPreSeason), (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLRegularSeason and (#$properSubEventTypes #$NFLSeason #$NFLPostSeason).  Further, for any instance of #$NFLSeason <b>NFL-Season-001</b>, there is no sub-event of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some instance of some element of (#$TheList #$NFLPreSeason #$NFLRegularSeason #$NFLPostSeason)).  It also entails that there is an instance of #$NFLPreSeason, <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, that is the first proper sub-situation of <b>NFLSeason-001</b> .  Finally, it entails that some instance  <b>NFLRegularSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLRegularSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the end of <b>NFLPreSeason-001</b>, and  some instance  <b>NFLPostSeason-001</b> of  #$NFLPostSeason is a proper sub-event of  <b>NFLSeason-001</b> which starts after the end of <b>NLRegularSeason-001</b>.")
(comment ClosingOfStomata "The collection of events in which plants close their #$Stomate to conserve water.")
(comment C4Plant "A specialization of #$Plant. Instances survive solely on #$C4-CarbonFixationInPlants. ")
(comment Photorespiration "A collection of events in which  #$Ribulose-1-5-Bisphosphate has #$Oxygen added to it by #$RuBisCO instead of #$CarbonDioxide during #$Photosynthesis-Plant. ")
(comment scarcityOfTypeInRegion "(#$scarcityOfTypeInRegion TYPE REGION LEVEL) means that the level of scarcity of TYPE in REGION is LEVEL.")
(comment BundleSheathCell "A specialization of #$Cell. Instances of #$BundleSheathCell are photosynthetic cells arranged into tightly packed layers around the veins of the leaf. ")
(disjointWith EukaryoticCell BundleSheathCell)
(comment PEPCarboxylaseMolecule "A specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of catalyzing carbon fixation in #$C4Plant. ")
(comment C4CarbonFixation "An instance of #$ChemicalReaction. It is one of three biochemical mechanisms used in carbon fixation. A 4-carbon molecule is the first product of this reaction.")
(comment PhosphorylationPathway "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway. Instances are complex pathways in which a phosphate group is added to an organic compound.")
(comment emergentPartType "<code>(#$emergentPartType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE EMERGENT-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>EMERGENT-PART</code> (an instance of <code>EMERGENT-PART</code>) is also part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i> and <i>depend on</i> (in a non-causal sense of \"dependence\") instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more specific predicate, #$supervenientPartType.")
(comment supervenientPartType "<code>(#$supervenientPartType WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE SV-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>SV-PART</code> (an instance of <code>SV-PART</code>) is also part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>, and, further: <code>WHOLE</code> is not reducible to <code>PART</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>SV-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i>, <i>depend on</i> (in a non-causal sense of \"dependence\") and <i>are not reducible to</i> instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>SV-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentPartType.")
(comment objectDisplayed "<code>(#$objectDisplayed DISPLAYING DISPLAYED)</code> means that the object <code>DISPLAYED</code> is on display in <code>DISPLAYING</code>, an instance of #$DisplayingSomething.")
(comment HandStacking-PreparingShowDogForJudging "A specialization of #$HandlingAnAnimal, this is the collection of events in a dog show, prior to judging, in which the handler of an animal physically postures his or her dog to prepare for presentation of the dog to the judges.")
(comment animalHandled "<code>(#$animalHandled HANDLING ANIMAL)</code> means that <code>ANIMAL</code> is the animal controlled during <code>HANDLING</code>, an instance of #$HandlingAnAnimal.")
(comment ParadingAShowDog "The collection of events that take place as part of a #$DogShow in which a dog's handler walks the dog around an open space in front of an audience.")
(comment animalHandler "<code>(#$animalHandler HANDLING AGENT)</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is handling, or controlling, the #$animalHandled in <code>HANDLING</code>, an instance of #$HandlingAnAnimal.")
(comment PresentationOfShowDogForJudging "The collection of events during a dog show in which a dog is officially presented for judging.")
(comment DocumentOfTextStringFn "(#$DocumentOfTextStringFn TEXT) denotes the document whose contents are exactly the contents of TEXT.")
(comment documentOfTextString "A predicate corresponding to the function #$DocumentOfTextStringFn.  <code>(#$documentOfTextString X (#$DocumentOfTextStringFn X))</code> will always be true for <code>X</code> meeting the relevant arg constraints.")
(comment NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate-Generic "The collection of NADP  and NADPH  molecules. Such molecules are found in both plants and animals, and have important roles in electron transfer.  The oxidized form, NADP  (#$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate) is able to become reduced (transformed into #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate) by accepting an electron, and then able to act to reduce other molecules by giving that electron up.")
(comment EnzymeMoleculeTypeByReactionType "A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of #$EnzymeMolecules  such that its instances are characteristically capable of catalyzing some instance of #$SpecifiedChemicalInteractionType. For example, #$ProteinKinaseMolecule, the collection of enzyme molecules that can catalyze phosphorylation of protein molecules, is an instance.  It is not necessary that instances of instances resemble each other in their chemical formula or structure. There are many different types of #$ProteinKinaseMolecule that occur in different organisms or have different roles within the same organism.  Other instances of #$EnzymeMoleculeTypeByReactionType may be more consistent in the structure of their instances; in those cases, they should also be instances of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType or #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies.  For example, #$AdenylylCyclaseMolecule has ten known variants in mammals that differ in their sequence of anmino acids and are coded for by different genes, but they all share similarities in structure.  It is therefore also an instance of #$ProteinMoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType.")
(comment EventTypeGrainFn "A #$ReifiableFunction and #$GenlsPreservingSubcollectionDenotingFunction, which maps from specializations of #$Event which are #$TemporalStuffType to the \"grain\" or \"granule\" of that type of event. <code>(#$EventTypeGrainFn EVENT-TYPE)</code> denotes a specialization of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> whose instances can't be spatiotemporally subdivided without rendering them no longer instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>. For example, (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis) is the class of #$Glycolysis reactions which are \"one pass\" all the way through the event, and in which the actors are individual #$ChemicalObjects, not masses of them. ")
(comment eventTypeGrain "<code>(#$eventTypeGrain EVENT-TYPE GRAIN-TYPE)</code> states that <code>GRAIN-TYPE</code> is the specialization of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> whose instances are the instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code> which can't be spatiotemporally subdivided without rendering the subdivisions no longer instances of <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>. For example, (#$eventTypeGrain #$Glycolysis (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis)) states that (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis) is the specialization of #$Glycolysis reactions which are \"one pass\" all the way through the event, and in which the actors are individual #$ChemicalObjects, not masses of them.")
(comment ChemicalReactionTypeCharacterizedByChemicalObjectParticipants "Each instance of this collection is a specialization of#$ChemicalReaction which describes the reaction in terms of the individual #$ChemicalObjects participating.  Instances of #$ChemicalReactionTypeCharacterizedByChemicalObjectParticipants can be constrasted with instances of #$ChemicalReactionTypeByEquationFormula, which describe reactions in terms of substances (masses of chemical objects) interacting.")
(comment HexokinaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of phosphorylating 6-carbon sugars (see #$Hexose). One important role of (at least some) hexokinases is in facilitating the phosphorylation of #$Glucose molecules in the first reaction of #$Glycolysis.")
(comment BiologicalFusionEvent "A collection of #$FusionEvents in which #$OrganicMaterials, generally parts of #$BiologicalLivingObjects or the objects themselves, fuse to form a single #$OrganicMaterial.")
(comment GP120Protein "The collection of GP120 molecules. These glycoproteins are
parts of #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus that are responsible for binding to
host cell's #$CD4Protein and #$CCR5Protein receptor molecules.")
(comment GP41Protein "The collection of GP41 molecules. These glycoproteins are
parts of retroviruses, and in the case of
#$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus, they enable the second stage
of (#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus)
events.")
(comment GP160Protein "The collection of GP160 molecules, which are all parts of
#$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus virions, and consist entirely of one
GP120Protein and one GP41Protein, non-covalently bonded.")
(comment ViralEnvelope "The collection of envelopes surrounding the capsids of some
viruses. These envelopes consist of #$CellMembrane-Stuff from the host
cell, but as they are no longer surround cell, they are not
#$CellMembranes.")
(disjointWith CellMembrane ViralEnvelope)
(comment HIVCellInvasion "The collection of #$ViralInvasionOfCells in which the
#$viralInvader is #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus. A rewrite
of (#$InvasionOfCellByVirusTypeFn #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus).")
(disjointWith ReceptorBindingWithLigand ReceptorBindingWithViralProtein)
(comment ReceptorBindingWithViralProtein "The collection of all chemical binding events in which a
#$ReceptorMolecule binds with a viral protein. Usually subevents of
[attempted] #$ViralInvasionOfCell events.")
(comment BiologicalMembraneFusionEvent "The collection of #$BiologicalFusionEvents in which two
#$BiologicalMembranes fuse to form a single membrane. This include the
fusing of vesicles with a cellular membrane, as well as the fusion of
a #$ViralEnvelope with a #$CellMembrane.")
(comment PharmacyProductType-Level0 "The collection of types of drug products that may be specified as to their brand or generic name (which indicates what type or types of compounds are contained in their instances), but are not specified as to dosage form, administration route, strength or packaging.  For example, #$ZoloftProduct and #$Antidepressant are instances of #$PharmacyProductType-Level0, but 'Zoloft tablets' would not be.")
(comment GenericPharmacyProductType-NameOnly "Instances are types of generic drugs, specific as to name only.  For example, (#$GenericFormFn #$Nifedipine) would be an instance, but 'Nifedipine capsules' would not be an instance of #$GenericPharmacyProductType-NameOnly since it excludes all types of nifedipine which are not in capsule form.")
(comment Oxycodone "Oxycodone is an opioid analgesic.")
(comment PurduePharma "Purdue Pharma is a pharmaceutical company.")
(comment AdditionOfCarbonDioxideToPEPInC4CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances of #$AdditionOfCarbonDioxideToPEPInC4CarbonFixation involve addition of #$CarbonDioxide to #$PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion. #$OxaloacetateAnion is one of the products of this reaction. ")
(comment MalateProductionInC4CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances of #$MalateProductionInC4CarbonFixation produce #$MalateAnion during #$C4CarbonFixationInPlants.")
(comment concentrationOfCarbonDioxideInRegion "(#$concentrationOfCarbonDioxideInRegion REGION CONCENTRATION) means that REGION  has the concentration of #$CarbonDioxide  CONCENTRATION.")
(comment ProductionOfATPDuringPhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances of #$ProductionOfATPDuringPhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow lead to the production of #$AdenosineTriphosphate during #$PhotosyntheticLightReactions-LinearElectronFlow.")
(comment TransferOfMalateToBundleSheathCellsInC4CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Instances involve transfer of #$MalateAnion to #$BundleSheathCell through #$Plasmodesma . ")
(comment DecarboxylationReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. One of the products of these reactions is #$CarbonDioxide.")
(comment DecarboxylationOfMalateInBundleSheathCellsInC4CarbonFixation " A specialization of #$DecarboxylationReaction. Instances involve conversion of #$MalateAnion to #$CarbonDioxide and #$PyruvateIon.")
(comment ConversionOfPyruvateIonToPEPInC4CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances involve conversion of #$PyruvateIon to #$PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion during #$C4CarbonFixationInPlants .")
(comment emergentPartType-Causal "<code>(#$emergentPartType-Causal WHOLE-TYPE PART-TYPE EMERGENT-PART-TYPE)</code> means that whenever any instance <code>PART</code> of <code>PART-TYPE</code> is part of any instance <code>WHOLE</code> of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, then some <code>EMERGENT-PART</code> (an instance of <code>EMERGENT-PART</code>) is also caused to be part of <code>WHOLE</code> because <code>PART</code> is <code>PART</code> of <code>WHOLE</code>.  In other words, as parts of instances of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>, instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code> <i>covary with</i> and are <i>caused by</i> instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> (although instances of <code>PART-TYPE</code> are not necessary for instances of <code>EMERGENT-PART-TYPE</code>, even as parts of <code>WHOLE-TYPE</code>) Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentPartType.")
(comment subSitTypeMakesTypeAvailableForParticipationInSitType "<code>(#$subSitTypeMakesTypeAvailableForParticipationInSitType SCRIPT SCENE-1 TYPE SCENE-2)</code> means that in events of type <code>SCRIPT</code>, sub-events of type <code>SCENE-1</code> are such that they make objects of type <code>TYPE</code> available for playing a role \"downstream\" in events of type <code>SCENE-2</code>.  <code>SCENE-1</code> can make <code>TYPE</code> available by creating instances of <code>TYPE</code> or generally having instance of <code>TYPE</code> play an #$outputs role, or by transforming an object so that it becomes of type <code>TYPE</code>, or by changing some property of an object of type <code>TYPE</code> so that it is suitable for playing the appropriate role in <code>SCENE-2</code>.")
(comment emergentProperty-AllExistsExists-Causal "(#$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists-Causal TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), that causes INS to also beas the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true).  In other words, the truth of:  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> <i>causes</i> the truth of  <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code>  Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists.")
(comment emergentProperty-AllExistsExists "(#$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), then INS also bears the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true) because (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true.  In other words, the truth of: <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code><p> <i>covaries</i> with and <i>depends</i> on (in a possibly non-causal sense of \"dependence\") the truth of  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> However, the truth of the latter need not be necessary for the truth of the former.   Cf. the more specific predicate, #$supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists.")
(comment supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists "(#$supervenientProperty-AllExistsExists TYPE BASE-PRED BASE-COL E-PRED E-COL) means that whenever any instance INS of TYPE bears the relation BASE-PRED to some instance B-INS of BASE-COL (i.e. (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true), then INS also bears the relation E-PRED to some instance E-INS of E-COL (i.e. for some instance E-INS of E-COL (E-PRED INS E-INS) is true) because (BASE-PRED INS B-INS) is true.  Further: the property INS has in virtue bearing E-PRED to E-INS is not reducible to the property INS has in virtue bearing BASE-PRED to B-INS.  In other words, the truth of: <p> <code>   (thereExists ?X  <br>   (and <br>      (isa ?X E-COL)   <br>   (E-PRED INS ?X))) </code><p> is <i>irreducible to</i>, <i>covaries</i> with, and <i>depends</i> on (in a possibly non-causal sense of \"dependence\") the truth of  <p> <code> (thereExists ?Y <br> (and <br> (isa ?Y BASE-COL) <br> (B-PRED INS ?Y)))   </code><p> However, the truth of the latter need not be necessary for the truth of the former. Cf. the more general predicate, #$emergentProperty-AllExistsExists.")
(disjointWith Phosphorylation IsomerizationReaction)
(disjointWith IsomerizationReaction Dephosphorylation)
(disjointWith Catalysis IsomerizationReaction)
(disjointWith IsomerizationReaction DecarboxylationReaction)
(disjointWith BinaryChemicalReaction IsomerizationReaction)
(disjointWith Hydrolysis-ChemicalReaction IsomerizationReaction)
(comment nothingOfTypePlaysRoleInSituationType "<code>(#$nothingOfTypePlaysRoleInSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE ROLE)</code> means that there are no instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> such that an instance of <code>TYPE</code> plays the role <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment CD4Protein "The collection of CD4 receptor protein molecules, which occur primarily on the surface of white blood cells, but not exclusively. CD4 proteins are an important accessory protein to the antigen receptors of Helper T cells, and is a primary receptor used by #$HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus to enter a cell.")
(comment MembraneGlycoproteinMolecule "The collection of #$GlycoproteinMolecules which are embedded in #$CellMembranes.")
(comment transformedObject "(#$transformedObject EVT OBJ) identifies OBJ as the instance of #$SomethingExisting which undergoes a transformation in the #$PhysicalTransformationEvent EVT. Example: (#$transformedObject SallyTurnsFredIntoAFrog2345 #$Fred) means that the thing which undergoes a transformation in the #$PhysicalTransformationEvent SallyTurnsFredIntoAFrog2345 is #$Fred. See also #$transformedInto.")
(comment entailsRoleInEventOfType "The purpose of this predicate is to relate #$SystemRolePredicates (i.e., relations representing functional roles) to their corresponding #$BinaryRolePredicates (i.e., relations representing the roles that agents play in events).  (#$entailsRoleInEventOfType SYS-SLOT EVENT-TYPE SYS-ACT-SLOT AGT-ACT-SLOT) means that if an agent plays the functional role SYS-SLOT in a particular functional system, and that system in turn plays the role SYS-ACT-SLOT in an event of type EVENT-TYPE, then the agent will play the role AGT-ACT-SLOT in that same event.")
(comment IsomerizationReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  In an #$IsomerizationReaction, a substance is transformed into one of its #$isomers.  Each #$ChemicalObject in the portion of stuff reacting has exactly the same #$Atoms as before, but some of the chemical bonds have been rearranged. ")
(comment IsomeraseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of catalyzing some type of isomerization (see #$IsomerizationReaction), the rearrangement of a #$PolyAtomicChemicalObject's constituent #$Atoms into one of its #$isomers.  Isomerase enzymes are usually specific to a particular type of substrate, and perform a particular type of rearrangement.")
(comment Fructose6PhosphateMolecule "The collection of all fructose 6-phosphate molecules, also known as Neuberg ester.  Instances are characterized by the presence of a phosphate group on the 6' carbon.  Instances are very common within cells,  and occu as an  intermediary in #$Glycolysis")
(comment PhosphoglucoisomeraseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that catalyze the transformation of #$Glucose6PhosphateMolecules into #$Fructose6PhosphateMolecules or vice-versa.  The glucose-6-phophate to fructose-6-phosphate direction is a step during #$Glycolysis.")
(comment IsomerizationReaction-EnzymeMediated "A specialization of #$IsomerizationReaction, including those #$IsomerizationReactions that are catalyzed by #$EnzymeMolecules.")
(comment ConversionOfTypeToTypeByEnzymeFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction used for representing #$ChemicalReactions that are types of #$EnzymaticActivity.  (#$ConversionOfTypeToTypeByEnzymeFn FROM-TYPE TO-TYPE ENZYME-TYPE) denotes a collection which is an instance of #$SpecifiedChemicalInteractionType and specialization of #$EnzymaticActivity in which instances of FROM-TYPE are converted to instances of TO-TYPE with an instance of ENZYME-TYPE serving as the #$catalyst.  For any given type of reaction denoted by a use of this function, instances may involve other chemical reactants or chemical objects besides FROM-TYPE and TO-TYPE, but FROM-TYPE and TO-TYPE are in some sense the focal inputs and products for the type of reaction.")
(comment processConvertsTypeToTypeViaEnzyme "(#$processConvertsTypeToTypeViaEnzyme REACT-TYPE FROM-TYPE TO-TYPE ENZYME-TYPE) means that instances of REACT-TYPE are chemical reactions in which FROM-TYPE gets converted to TO-TYPE as facilitated by ENZYME-TYPE.")
(comment PhotosynthesisInCAMPlants "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway. It is a mode of carbon fixation that evolved in some plants as an adaptation to arid conditions. ")
(comment OpeningOfStomata "The collection of events in which plants open their #$Stomate to take up #$CarbonDioxide. ")
(comment CAMPlant "A specialization of #$Plant. Instances adapt to arid conditions by a mode of carbon fixation called #$CAMPhotosynthesis . ")
(comment CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances of #$CarbonFixation involve the reduction of #$CarbonDioxide to an #$OrganicCompound.  ")
(comment CarbonFixationInCAMPlants "A specialization of #$CarbonFixation.  Instances of #$CarbonFixationInCAMPlants involve #$CarbonFixation in #$CAMPlant. ")
(comment MalateStorageInCAMPhotosynthesis "A specialization of #$StorageOfSomething.  Instances of #$MalateStorageInCAMPhotosynthesis involve storage of #$MalateAnion in #$MesophyllCell during the night. ")
(comment ElectronTransportChainFromPSIToNADPPlusCation "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSIToNADPPlusCation, photoexcited electrons pass from the #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemI through the protein #$Ferredoxin to NADP  reductase which leads to the production of #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate.")
(comment Photosynthesis-ElectronFlowCycleInPhotosystemI "A specialization of #$Cycle-Situation.  Each instance of #$Photosynthesis-ElectronFlowCycleInPhotosystemI is a process through which photoexcited electrons use #$PhotosystemI but not #$PhotosystemII during photosynthesis light reactions. ")
(comment TransferaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are capable of catalyzing a type of #$ChemicalReaction in which a functional group is transferred from one #$Molecule to another.  Like all enzymes, each #$TransferaseMolecule is usually specific to a particular type of substrate, and facilitates a particular type of reaction.")
(comment PhosphofructokinaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of phosphorylating #$Fructose6PhosphateMolecules, and important step in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment CellularRecognitionEvent "The collection of events in which cells \"recognize\" one
another by means of binding #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules, usually
#$MembraneGlycoproteinsMolecules. Instances always have as subevents
one or more instance of (#$ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn
#$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules
#$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecule). In some sense this recognition
occurs at a type level, although it is not the case that any cell
recognizes any other as belonging to a certain type, per se, as cells
lack intentionality. Rather, specific surface molecules of one cell
bind selectively to specific surface receptorsmolecules of another
cell, \"recognizing\" it as \"a match\", so to speak, and responding
differentially. Since any other cell with similar surface molecules
would likewise be a \"match\", this can be thought of as a type-level
recognition event, despite that it consists, strictly speaking,
entirely of #$ChemicalBindingEvents.")
(comment recognizerInCellularRecognitionEvent "This predicate relates an instance of #$Cell
<code>CELL</code> to an instance of #$CellularRecognitionEvent in
which specific #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules of the
<code>CELL</code> bind to #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules on another
#$Cell, resulting in a possibly differential response from
<code>CELL</code>. A cell may be both
#$recognizerInCellularRecognitionEvent and also
#$recognizedInCellularRecognitionEvent, provided that
<code>CELL</code> both responds and is responded to as a result of the
#$CellularRecognitionEvent.")
(comment recognizedInCellularRecognitionEvent "This predicate relates an instance of #$Cell
<code>CELL</code> to an instance of #$CellularRecognitionEvent in
which specific #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules of the
<code>CELL</code> bind to #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules on another
#$Cell, resulting in a possibly differential response from the other
cell. A cell may be both #$recognizedInCellularRecognitionEvent and
also #$recognizerInCellularRecognitionEvent, provided that
<code>CELL</code> both responds and is responded to as a result of the
#$CellularRecognitionEvent.")
(comment cellRecognizedAsTypeInRecognitionEvent "<code>(cellRecognizedAsTypeInRecognitionEvent RECOG CELL
CELL-TYPE)</code> means that in #$CellularRecognitionEvent
<code>RECOG</code>, #$Cell <code>CELL</code> was \"recognized\" as
being of type <code>CELL-TYPE</code>, in the sense that the
\"recognizing\" cell(s) respond(s) to the cell differentially and in
the same manner that they would respond to all other instances of
<code>CELL-TYPE</code>. Thus, <code>CELL-TYPE</code> should generally
be specified as the most general collection of #$Cells with respect to
whose instances the differential response of the recognizing #$Cell
would be invariant.")
(comment RejectionOfForeignCell "The collection of #$CellularImmuneResponse events in which a
non-self cell is rejected by the immune system.")
(comment cellPresentsAntigenType "<code>(#$cellPresentsAntigenType CELL ANT-TYPE)</code> means
that <code>CELL</code> has instances of antigen <code>ANT-TYPE</code>
displayed on it's #$CellMembrane.")
(comment cellTypePresentsAntigenType "<code>(#$cellTypePresentsAntigenType CELL-TYPE ANT-TYPE)</code> means
that instances of <code>CELL-TYPE</code> have instances of antigen <code>ANT-TYPE</code>
displayed on their #$CellMembranes.")
(comment A-Antigen "The collection of antigens which prototypically occur on the #$RedBloodCells of humans and some other mammalian species with #$BloodTypeA and #$BloodTypeAB. They may also occur on epithelial cells.")
(comment B-Antigen "The collection of antigens which prototypically occur on the #$RedBloodCells of humans and some other mammalian species with #$BloodTypeB and #$BloodTypeAB. They may also occur on epithelial cells.")
(comment MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecule "The collection of #$GlycoconjugateMolecules which are embedded in #$CellMembranes. They play important roles in #$CellularRecognitionEvents and #$BiochemicalSignalingProcesses.")
(comment CellularMembraneTransport "The collection of instances of #$MembraneTransport in which the #$objectPenetrated is an instance of #$CellMembrane.")
(disjointWith MembraneTransport-Outward MembraneTransport-Inward)
(comment holdsMetaphorically "<code>(#$holdsMetaphorically SENTENCE)</code> means that <code>SENTENCE</code> is metaphorically true.")
(comment PhosphorylatingWithATP "The collection of all events in which a phosphate group is transferred from a molecule of #$AdenosineTriphosphate to another #$Molecule.  Instances of #$PhosphorylatingWithATP are often catalyzed by some #$KinaseMolecule that is specific to the job and specific to the molecule so phosphorylated.  ")
(comment Fructose1-6-BisphosphateMolecule "The collection of all fructose 1,6-phosphate molecules, also known as Harden-Young ester.  Instances are characterized by the presence of phosphate groups on carbons 1 and 6.  Instances are very common within cells,  and occurs as an  intermediary in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment MonophosphateGroup "The collection of all #$PhosphateOrPolyphosphateGroups consisting of a single phosphorus atom surrounded by four oxygen atoms with three negative charges.  When bonded as part of a larger molecule, the negative charges may not be present.")
(comment PhosphateIon " The collection of phosphate ions (PO4(-3)).  In aqueous solution, this ion can exist in several forms because it associates with #$HydrogenPlusIons in the solution to various degrees, neutralizing one or more of its negative charges.")
(comment MolecularComponent "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjects which, notwithstanding the fact that they are conventionally regarded as #$ChemicalObjects in their own right, may exist as #$molecularSubComponents of larger 'molecular' structures (#$Molecules or #$PolyatomicIons) in the sense that instances are attached by at least one covalent bond to an atom that is not part of the instance.  The collection includes the individual #$Atoms, instances of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular, and any covalently bonded group of atoms that sometimes occurs as part of a larger molecule or ion but which does not, in that situation, contain all the atoms in that molecule or ion.")
(comment AminoGroup "The collection of all amino (NH2-) groups. A type of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular. #$AminoGroup is a #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment FunctionalGroup-Molecular "A collection of microscopic-scale objects; a subset of #$ChemicalObject.  Every instance of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular is a microscopic object whose component atoms are all chemically bonded to each other, and which tend to \"travel as a unit\" when the group is bonded to other atoms to form a complete molecule.   A #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular often acts as a unit in chemical reactions and is of a chemical species whose instances form a standard part of numerous different types chemicals.  Examples: individual #$Nucleotides in a #$DNAMolecule, or phosphate groups (see #$MonophosphateGroup) as part of ATP or in solution.  Counterexample: an ionized molecule.  ")
(disjointWith Atom FunctionalGroup-Molecular)
(comment MethylGroup "Chemical group (see #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular) that is hydrophobic, and derived from molecules of #$Methane.")
(comment SulfhydrylGroup "A specialization of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular.  Each instance of #$SulfhydrylGroup is a functional group with the structure SH.")
(comment FormylGroup "A specialization of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular.  Each instance of #$FormylGroup is a functional group with the structure CHO.")
(comment CarboxylGroup "A specialization of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular.  Each instance of #$CarboxylGroup is a sample of #$Oxygen double-bonded to a #$Carbon atom that is also bonded to an -OH group.")
(comment CarbonylGroup "A specialization of #$FunctionalGroup-Molecular.  Each instance of #$CarbonylGroup is an atom of #$Carbon double bonded with #$Oxygen. This collection includes instances of CO when bonded as part of a molecule.")
(comment MolecularRadical "A collection of microscopic-scale objects; a subset of #$ChemicalObject.  Every instance of #$MolecularRadical is a chemical object having unpaired #$Electrons or an incompletely filled outer shell. This property tends to make radicals (sometimes called \"free radicals\") highly reactive and short-lived.")
(comment HydroxylGroup "The collection of all hydroxyl groups (-OH), including #$HydroxideIons and those covalently bonded in a larger #$PolyAtomicChemicalObject.\"")
(comment HydroxideRadical "The collection of all hydroxide radicals (OH), which are the neutral form of the #$HydroxideIon, having an unpaired electron.")
(comment partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance "Where CAPABILITY is an instance of #$Capability, and TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY) means that, where (#$capabilityToRoleSitType ROLE SIT-TYPE CAPABILITY) and for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that ($#functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstance PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY) means that, where CAPABILITY is a #$Capability such that the relevant capability relation is underspecified, (i.e., we don't know that CAPABILITY is a fiscal capability, a behavioral capability, an anatomic capability, etc.), instances of PART-TYPE support CAPABILITY in systems that include them as components, so that where CAPABILITY is associated with playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE, (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE) ordinarily holds for any instance that has an instance of PART-TYPE as a functional part.")
(comment partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType "Where CAPABILITY is an instance of #$Capability, and TYPE-CAP-PRED is the type-level #$correspondingPreds-Capability of CAP-PRED, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY AGT-TYPE) means that, where (#$capabilityToRoleSitType ROLE SIT-TYPE CAPABILITY) and for any type of system SYSTEM-TYPE such that (genls SYSTEM-TYPE AGT-TYPE) and such that ($#functionallyImportantPhysicalPartTypeOfWholeType SYSTEM-TYPE PART-TYPE), (TYPE-CAP-PRED SYSTEM-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE). Intuitively, (#$partTypeSupportsCapabilityInstanceInType PART-TYPE CAP-PRED CAPABILITY AGT-TYPE) means that, where CAPABILITY is a #$Capability such that the relevant capability relation is underspecified, (i.e., we don't know that CAPABILITY is a fiscal capability, a behavioral capability, an anatomic capability, etc.), instances of PART-TYPE support CAPABILITY in instances of AGT-TYPE that include them as components, so that where CAPABILITY is associated with playing ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE, (CAP-PRED INST SIT-TYPE ROLE) ordinarily holds for any instance of AGT-TYPE that has an instance of PART-TYPE as a functional part.")
(comment LightProductionProcess "The process of generating #$VisibleLight.")
(comment Chemiluminescence "The production of light through chemical means.")
(comment ElectronTransportChainFromPSIIToPSI "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSIIToPSI, photoexcited electrons pass from the #$PrimaryElectronAcceptor-PhotosystemII to #$PhotosystemI. ")
(comment ChemotrophicBacterium "A Specialization of #$Microorganism and #$Bacterium.. Instances obtain their energy by #$OxidationProcess of electron donors.")
(comment BlueGreenAlgae "The collection of (mostly dark blue-green in bulk) aquatic organisms called \"blue-green algae\" or sometimes \"cyanobacteria\".  The elements of #$BlueGreenAlgae are also elements of #$Autotroph and of #$ProkaryoticCell, and they carry out processes of #$Photosynthesis-Bacterial.  The class of #$BlueGreenAlgae, also called Cyanophyta, is one of the #$BiologicalDivisions of the #$MoneraKingdom.  (Compare with #$Bacterium.)")
(comment ConversionOfStarchToGlucose "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances of #$ConversionOfStarchToGlucose involve conversion of #$Starch to #$Glucose. It is an important step in #$IndustrialEthanolProduction.  ")
(comment Transesterification "A specialization of #$Esterification in which the organic group of an acid is exchanged with the organic group of an acid.")
(comment Fat "A specialization of #$Lipid. #$Fats consist of a wide variety of compounds that are chemically triglycerides, triesters of glycerol and fatty acids.")
(comment AnimalFat "A specialization of #$Fat. Instances are derived from animals.")
(comment TransferOfWaterFromRootToLeaf "The collection of events in which #$Water is transferred from #$Root of a plant to one of its #$Leaf. ")
(comment OxyContin "#$OxyContin is the collection of #$Oxycodone time-release formula produced by #$PurduePharma.")
(comment chemicalProducts "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$chemicalProducts REACTION PRODUCT) means that PRODUCT, an instance of #$ChemicalObject, is one of the outputs of REACTION, an instance of #$ChemicalReaction. The products are those chemicals (instances of #$Molecule or #$Ion) that are the result of a reaction. See the type level #$chemicalProducts-TypeType and #$chemicalReactants.")
(comment chemicalProducts-Macroscopic "An instance of #$ActorSlot.  (#$chemicalProducts-Macroscopic REACTION PRODUCT) means that PRODUCT, an instance of a single #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies is the complete amount of that type of chemical substance that is a result of REACTION.")
(comment chemicalReactants "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$chemicalReactants REACTION REACTANT) means that during REACTION, an instance of #$ChemicalReaction, REACTANT, an instance of #$ChemicalObject, plays a reactant role. The reactants are those chemicals that react with other reactants to form the products of the reaction. See the type level #$chemicalReactants-TypeType and also #$chemicalProducts.")
(comment chemicalReactants-Macroscopic "An instance of #$ActorSlot.  (#$chemicalReactants-Macroscopic REACTION REACTANT) means that REACTANT, an instance of a single #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies is the complete amount of that type of chemical substance reacting in REACTION.")
(comment chemicalObjectParticipants-TypeType "(#$chemicalObjectParticipants-TypeType REACTION-TYPE CHEM-OBJ-TYPE) means that, in each instance of REACTION-TYPE, some instance of CHEM-OBJ-TYPE is one of the #$chemicalReactants, #$chemicalProducts, #$catalysts, or other participant.")
(comment chemicalObjectsDestroyed "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$chemicalObjectsDestroyed REACT REACTANT) means that during REACT, the instance of #$ChemicalObject, REACTANT, is destroyed. ")
(comment chemicalObjectsCreated "An instance of #$ActorSlot. (#$chemicalObjectsCreated REACT CREATED) means that during REACT, the instance of #$ChemicalObject, CREATED, comes into existence. ")
(disjointWith TransferOfPhosphateFromOneMoleculeToAnother (ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn AdenosineTriphosphate PhosphateIon))
(disjointWith (ChemicalUnbindingEventTypeWithTypesFn AdenosineTriphosphate PhosphateIon) (ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn OrganicChemicalObject PhosphateIon))
(disjointWith TransferOfPhosphateFromOneMoleculeToAnother (ChemicalBindingEventTypeWithTypesFn OrganicChemicalObject PhosphateIon))
(comment DihydroxyacetonePhosphateMolecule "The collection of all dihydroxyacetone phosphate molecules.   Instances occur as an  intermediary in #$Glycolysis")
(comment Fructose-BisphosphateAldolaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of cleaving #$Fructose1-6-BisphosphateMolecules into two 3-carbon molecules, which is an important step in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment LyaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes which catalyze reactions in which one molecule is broken into two, or two are combined into one, by some mechanism other than oxidation or hydrolysis.")
(comment CleavageOfFructose1-6-BisphosphateInGlycolysis "The collection of all events in which a #$Fructose1-6-BisphosphateMolecule is split into two smaller molecules by an aldolase (see Fructose-BisphosphateAldolaseMolecule).  ")
(comment TriosephosphateIsomeraseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that catalyze the transformation of #$DihydroxyAcetonePhosphateMolecules (DHAP) into #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate (GADP) and vice versa.   DHAP to GDAP is a step during #$Glycolysis.")
(comment OxidoreductaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes which catalyze redox reactions.")
(comment GlyceraldehydePhosphateDehydrogenase "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzyme molecules which are able to catalyze the conversion of #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate to #$1-3-Bisphosphoglycerate as part of #$Glycolysis.")
(comment 1-3-BisphosphoglycerateMolecule "A type of organic molecule (see (#$MoleculeFn #$OrganicCompound)). 1,3-Bisphosphoglycerate is an intermediate in #$Glycolysis and in the #$CalvinCycle.")
(comment Ritonavir "The collection of all ritonavir. #$Ritonavir is a #$ProteaseInhibitor, a #$PharmaceuticalType, and a #$GenericPharmacyProductType-NameOnly.")
(comment Benzodiazepine "The collection of all #$Benzodiazepines. There exist many different kinds of #$Benzodiazepines; #$XanaxProduct and #$ValiumProduct are two examples.")
(comment DrugSubstance "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$DrugSubstance is something that can be introduced into an organism's body to produce certain physiological effects.  This collection includes naturally-occurring substances, as well as manufactured substances.")
(comment Lovastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Simvastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Atorvastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Cerivastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Fluvastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Mevastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Pitavastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Pravastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Rosuvastatin "A specialization of #$Statin.")
(comment Tizanidine "A specialization of #$MuscleRelaxant.")
(comment Norvir "The collection of all norvir. #$Norvir is a #$ProteaseInhibitor and a #$BrandNamePharmacyProductType.")
(comment Kaletra "#$Kaletra is a #$ProteaseInhibitor and a #$BrandNamePharmacyProductType.")
(comment IntegraseInhibitor "The collection of all types of drugs that block retroviral integrase from working.  This blocks a step in viral reproduction.")
(comment Integrase "Integrase is a collection of enzymes produced by retroviruses (such as HIV) that enables the genetic material of the virus to be integrated into the DNA of the infected cell.")
(comment SplittingOfWaterAndProductionOfOxygenInPhotosynthesis "A Specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In #$SplittingOfWaterAndProductionOfOxygenInPhotosynthesis , water is separated into electrons, protons and oxygen. ")
(comment concentrationOfOxygenMoleculeInRegion "(#$concentrationOfOxygenMoleculeInRegion REGION CONCENTRATION) means that REGION  has the concentration of #$Oxygen  CONCENTRATION.")
(comment TransferOfSugarInPlants "The collection of events in which #$Sugar is transferred from the leaves to other parts of the plant.")
(comment CellMembraneExtracellularSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of #$CellMembranes. In a plant cell, the #$CellMembraneExtracellularSurface will be adjacent to and enclosed by the #$CellWall.  In an animal cell, the #$CellMembraneExtracellularSurface may be adjacent to #$ExtracellularFluid and/or portions of #$ExtracellularMatrix.")
(comment EndoplasmicReticulumMembraneLumenalSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of #$EndoplasmicReticulumMembranes.")
(comment Opiate "A collection of drugs.  Each instance of #$Opiate is a natural opiate alkaloid found in the resin of the opium poppy,")
(comment CodeinePhosphate "The collection of all codeine.  #$CodeinePhosphate is a #$PharmaceuticalType and a #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment OpioidReceptor "A type of G protein-linked receptor to which #$OpioidDrug molecules bind.")
(comment Endorphin "A sub-collection of #$EndogenousOpioidPeptide.  #$Endorphin is produced in the pituitary gland and the hypothalamus of vertebrates.")
(comment Enkephalin "A sub-collection of #$EndogenousOpioidPeptide.  These are peptides that are produced in the peripheral nervous system and the medulla of vertebrates.")
(comment Opioid "The collection of opioids.  Each instance of #$Opioid is a psychoactive chemical with an effect achieved by binding to #$OpioidReceptors.")
(comment OpioidDrug "A collection of drugs.  Each instance of #$OpioidDrug is a drug with a psychopharmacological effect achieved by binding to #$OpioidReceptors.")
(comment ReductionHalfReactionTypeFn "<code>(#$ReductionHalfReactionTypeFn REDOX-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$Reduction-HalfReaction which are sub-events of instances of <code>REDOX-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction.")
(comment typeHasReductionHalf "<code>(#$typeHasReductionHalf REDOX-TYPE REDUCT-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the type of #$SimpleRedoxReaction, <code>REDOX-TYPE</code> have, as their reduction subevents, instances of <code>REDUCT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typeHasOxidationHalf "<code>(#$typeHasOxidationHalf REDOX-TYPE OXID-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the type of #$SimpleRedoxReaction, <code>REDOX-TYPE</code> have, as their oxidation subevents, instances of <code>OXID-TYPE</code>.")
(comment OxidationHalfReactionTypeFn "<code>(#$OxidationHalfReactionTypeFn REDOX-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$Oxidation-HalfReaction which are sub-events of instances of <code>REDOX-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction.")
(comment RedoxAndPhosphorylationOfGlyceraldehyde3PhosphateInGlycolysis "Instances are reactions that are steps in #$Glycolysis, mediated by #$GlyceraldehydePhosphateDehydrogenase.")
(comment OxidizedFn "<code>(#$OxidizedFn CHEM-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChemicalObject which are oxidized forms of instances of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$ChemicalObject.  Note that there may be more than one way to oxidize a particular type of #$ChemicalObject.")
(comment oxidizedForm "<code>(#$oxidizedForm CHEM-TYPE OXID-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the type of #$ChemicalObject, <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> can be transformed through being oxidized into instances of <code>OXID-TYPE</code>.  Also, <code>OXID-TYPE</code> is the collection of all chemical objects that can be derived from an instance of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> by oxidation.  Since large complex molecules may be oxidized in many different ways, <code>OXID-TYPE</code> is not an instance of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment ReducedFn "<code>(#$ReducedFn CHEM-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ChemicalObject which are reduced forms of instances of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$ChemicalObject.  Note that there may be more than one way to reduce a particular type of #$ChemicalObject.")
(comment reducedForm "<code>(#$reducedForm CHEM-TYPE RED-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the type of #$ChemicalObject, <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> can be transformed through being reduceded into instances of <code>RED-TYPE</code>.  Also, <code>RED-TYPE</code> is the collection of all chemical objects that can be derived from an instance of <code>CHEM-TYPE</code> by reduction.  Since large complex molecules may be reduced in many different ways, <code>RED-TYPE</code> is not an instance of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment EndogenousOpioidPeptide "A sub-collection of #$PeptideMolecule and #$Analgesic. Instances of these substances are characterized by their ability to relieve pain.")
(comment Endomorphin "A sub-collection of #$EndogenousOpioidPeptide.")
(comment Methadone "The collection of all methadone. #$Methadone is a #$PharmaceuticalType and a #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment Heroin "A white, #$Crystalline, narcotic #$Powder, derived from #$Morphine, formerly used as an #$Analgesic and sedative.")
(comment Dynorphin "A sub-collection of #$EndogenousOpioidPeptide.")
(comment Lignin "The collection of lignin polymers, most of which occur as
constituents of plant #$CellWallMaterials.")
(comment CellWallMaterial "The collection of mixtures of #$CarbohydrateStuff, #$Lignin, #$Peptidoglycans, #$ProteinStuff, and other molecules that make up #$CellPlates and #$CellWalls in plants, fungi, and protists.")
(comment ClimbingRope "The collection of instances of #$Rope that are also instances of    (#$EquipmentForEventTypeFn #$RockClimbing).")
(comment WebbingStrip "The collection of all strips of #$Webbing, a strong woven material used in seatbelts and in other safety equipment.")
(comment Webbing "A strong woven material used in seatbelts and in other safety equipment.")
(comment WebbingLoop "The collecton of all instances of #$WebbingStrip that have been woven into a loop.")
(comment ClimbingHarness "Harnesses used for #$RockClimbing.")
(comment Quickdraw "A device consisting of two instances of #$Carabiner joined by a single instance of #$WebbingLoop, used in rock and ice climbing to connect a rope to another object, typically a bolts or another rope.")
(comment CarabinerGate "The piece on a #$Carabiner that opens or closes.")
(comment EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane "The collection of #$BiologicalMembranes which are parts of #$EndoplasmicReticulum #$Organelles.")
(comment GolgiCisternaStack "The collection of stacks of #$GolgiCisterna membranes which
are parts of the #$GolgiAparatus organelles of #$Cells.")
(comment GolgiCisCisterna "The collection of #$GolgiCisterna which are located at one
face of a #$GolgiCisternaStack (opposite face from a
#$GolgiTransCisterna) and function as a receiving site for
#$TransportVesicles.")
(comment GolgiTransCisterna "The collection of #$GolgiCisterna which are located at one
face of a #$GolgiCisternaStack (opposite face from a
#$GolgiCisCisterna) and function as a formation and departure site for
#$TransportVesicles.")
(comment GolgiMedialCisterna "The collection of #$GolgiCisterna which are located between the #$GolgiCisCisterna and the #$GolgiTransCisterna in a #$GolgiCisternaStack and fuction as sites of molecule modification and synthesis.")
(comment P680ChlorophyllACation "A specialization of #$PolyatomicCation. Instances of #$P680ChlorophyllACation  are P680  ions. They are formed in #$PhotosystemII when an electron is transferred from an excited P680 to a primary electron acceptor.")
(comment CyclicElectronTransportChainInPhotosystemI "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$CyclicElectronTransportChainInPhotosystemI, photoexcited electrons cycle back from #$Ferredoxin to #$CytochromeB6FComplex. ")
(comment P700ChlorophyllACation "A specialization of #$PolyatomicCation. Instances of #$P700ChlorophyllACation  are P700   ions. They are formed in #$PhotosystemI when an electron is transferred from an excited P700 to a primary electron acceptor.")
(comment CyclicElectronTransportChainInPhotosystemI-InPurpleSulfurBacterium "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$CyclicElectronTransportChainInPhotosystemI-InPurpleSulfurBacterium, photoexcited electrons cycle back from #$Ferredoxin to #$CytochromeB6FComplex in #$PurpleSulfurBacterium. ")
(comment ElectronTransportChainFromPSIIToNADPCation "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  Instances are entire electron transport chains from #$PhotosystemII to #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate. Important #$properSubEvents include #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSIIToPSI and  #$ElectronTransportChainFromPSIToNADPPlusCation. ")
(comment ConversionOfG3PToGlucose "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Instances involve conversion of #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate  to #$Glucose.")
(comment DeflectingSomething "The collection of all #$PhysicalEvents wherein a directed translation ends and the primary object moving in that translation begins a new directed translation with a vector whose direction differs from the original vector as measured from the point of terminus, via a direct transfer of energy to the primary object moving.")
(comment itemDeflected "Where DEFLECTING is a #$DeflectingSomething,  (#$itemDeflected DEFLECTING DEFLECTED) means that DEFLECTED is the #$primaryObjectMoving in a directed translation shortly before DEFLECTING occurs, and the #$primaryObjectMoving in another directed translation shortly after DEFLECTING occurs such that the direction of motion of DEFLECTED in the posterior translation differs measurably from the direction of motion of DEFLECTED in the anterior translation, and such that the energy applied in DEFLECTING directly causes the change in direction of motion.")
(comment BoundarySituation "The collection of all events wherein one or more motile objects are precluded from entering or leaving a spatial region by the presence of a boundary.")
(comment boundaryInSituation "(#$boundaryInSituation SIT BOUNDARY) means that BOUNDARY functions as the boundary in the #$BoundarySituation SIT.  This entails that some object, and often the instances of a class of object, are not permitted to cross BOUNDARY for the temporal duration of SIT.")
(comment passagePrevented "(#$passagePrevented BOUNDARY-SIT AGENT) means that AGENT is prevented from crossing the #$boundaryInSituation in the #$BoundarySituation BOUNDARY-SIT.")
(comment itemAdmitted "Where TRANSPORT is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation, (#$itemAdmitted TRANSPORT ITEM) means that ITEM crosses whatever is the #$transportBoundarySystem in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT")
(comment itemPermittedEntry "Where TRANSPORT is a RegulatedTransportSituation such that BOUNDARY is the #$transportBoundarySystem in TRANSPORT and REGION is the largest region that BOUNDARY can be said to completely surround (see (#$PredicateIntersection2Fn #$touches-Directly #$surroundsCompletely)), (#$itemPermittedEntry TRANSPORT ITEM) means that there is a #$CrossingABorder which occurs at BOUNDARY, where ITEM is the #$primaryObjectMoving, and such that the #$toLocation is REGION.")
(comment itemInterdicted "(#$itemInterdicted TRANSPORT ITEM) means that in the course of the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT, there exists a #$BoundarySituation wherein the #$passagePrevented is ITEM.")
(comment itemContained "Where TRANSPORT is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation with the #$transportBoundarySystem BOUNDARY such that REGION is the largest region completely enclosed by BOUNDARY, (#$itemContained TRANSPORT ITEM) means that TRANSPORT includes a #$BoundarySituation wherein ITEM is within REGION and prevented from crossing BOUNDARY.")
(comment itemExcluded "Where TRANSPORT is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation with the #$transportBoundarySystem BOUNDARY such that REGION is the largest region completely enclosed by BOUNDARY, (#$itemExcluded TRANSPORT ITEM) means that TRANSPORT includes a #$BoundarySituation wherein ITEM is outside of REGION and prevented from crossing BOUNDARY.")
(comment stuffTypeFlowRegulated "(#$stuffTypeFlowRegulated TRANSPORT-SIT STUFF-TYPE) means that a 'stuff-like' instance of the #$ExistingStuffType STUFF-TYPE is selectively permitted to cross, or selectively prevented from crossing, the #$transportBoundarySystem in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT-SIT.")
(comment stuffTypeAdmitted "(#$stuffTypeAdmitted TRANSPORT-SIT STUFF-TYPE) means that a 'stuff-like' instance of the #$ExistingStuffType STUFF-TYPE is selectively permitted to cross the #$transportBoundarySystem in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT-SIT (#$itemAdmitted).")
(comment stuffTypeInterdicted "(#$stuffTypeInterdicted TRANSPORT-SIT STUFF-TYPE) means that a 'stuff-like' instance of the #$ExistingStuffType STUFF-TYPE is selectively prevented from crossing the #$transportBoundarySystem in TRANSPORT-SIT (#$itemInterdicted).")
(comment objectTypeFlowRegulated "(#$objectTypeFlowRegulated TRANSPORT-SIT OBJECT-TYPE) means that an 'object-like' instance of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE is selectively permitted to cross, or selectively prevented from crossing, the #$transportBoundarySystem in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT-SIT.")
(comment objectTypeAdmitted "(#$objectTypeAdmitted TRANSPORT-SIT OBJECT-TYPE) means that an 'object-like' instance of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE is selectively permitted to cross the #$transportBoundarySystem in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT-SIT (#$itemAdmitted).")
(comment objectTypeInterdicted "(#$objectTypeInterdicted TRANSPORT-SIT OBJECT-TYPE) means that an 'object-like' instance of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE is selectively prevented from crossing the #$transportBoundarySystem in TRANSPORT-SIT (#$itemInterdicted).")
(comment objectTypeRateOfTransport-Entry "Where TRANSPORT-SIT is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation in which the #$transportBoundarySystem encloses a region, (#$objectTypeRateOfTransport-Entry TRANSPORT-SIT OBJ-TYPE N DUR) means that the rate at which instances of OBJ-TYPE are crossing the boundary into the enclosed region is N instances per DUR for the whole duration of TRANSPORT-SIT.")
(comment stuffTypeRateOfTransport-Entry "Where TRANSPORT-SIT Is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation in which the #$transportBoundarySystem encloses a region, (#$stuffTypeRateOfTransport-Entry TRANSPORT-SIT STUFF-TYPE FLOW-RATE) means that, for the duration of TRANSPORT-SIT, a 'stuff-like' instance of the #$ExistingStuffType STUFF-TYPE is flowing into the region across the boundary at a volumetric flow rate given by FLOW-RATE.")
(comment stuffTypeRateOfTransport-Exit "Where TRANSPORT-SIT Is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation in which the #$transportBoundarySystem encloses a region, (#$stuffTypeRateOfTransport-Entry TRANSPORT-SIT STUFF-TYPE FLOW-RATE) means that, for the duration of TRANSPORT-SIT, a 'stuff-like' instance of the #$ExistingStuffType STUFF-TYPE is flowing into the region across the boundary at a volumetric flow rate given by FLOW-RATE.")
(comment objectTypeRateOfTransport-Exit "Where TRANSPORT-SIT Is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation in which the #$transportBoundarySystem encloses a region, (#$objectTypeRateOfTransport-Exit TRANSPORT-SIT OBJ-TYPE N DUR) means that the rate at which instances of OBJ-TYPE are exiting the enclosed region across the boundary is N instances per DUR for the whole duration of TRANSPORT-SIT.")
(comment itemPermittedExit "Where TRANSPORT is a RegulatedTransportSituation such that BOUNDARY is the #$transportBoundarySystem in TRANSPORT and REGION is the largest region that BOUNDARY can be said to completely surround (see (#$PredicateIntersection2Fn #$touches-Directly #$surroundsCompletely)), (#$itemPermittedExit TRANSPORT ITEM) means that there is a #$CrossingABorder which occurs at BOUNDARY, where ITEM is the #$primaryObjectMoving, and such that the #$fromLocation is REGION.")
(comment RegulatedTransportSituation "The collection of all situations in which flows or tranlations of objects or stuffs across a demarcated boundary are preferential, i.e., non-random, relative to type.  Every #$RegulatedTransportSituation features exactly one #$PartiallyTangible object as a #$transportBoundarySystem:  this may consist in a physical barrier that prevents individuals of a certain type from entering or leaving an area, or in a more complex system that effects interdiction partially through signals and information processing on the part of the agents being interdicted.  Every #$RegulatedTransportSituation also features some item or number of items that are permitted to pass through the boundary in question (#$itemAdmitted), and another item or number of items which are not permitted to pass through the boundary in question (#$itemInterdicted).  Assuming the boudary forms an enclosed region the things that are interdicted may be confined within the enclosed area (#$itemContained), or they may be prevented from entering the enclosed area (#$itemExcluded):  likewise instances that are #$itemAdmitted may be #$itemPermittedEntry or #$itemPermittedExit.  Some cases of #$RegulatedTransportSituation are such that some interdicted items may be #$itemContained while others are #$itemExcluded.  Some instances of #$RegulatedTransportSituation may also be such that all instances that are #$itemAdmitted and all instances that are #$itemInterdicted have all salient features in common, i.e., what is being regulated is exclusively the rate of flow of things of a certain type.  It may also be the case that there are two or several types of things such that instances are both admitted and interdicted (contained or excluded) throughout the course of the situation, but at different rates depending on the type.  In the extreme (but not necessarily uncommon) case, a type of thing may be exclusively admitted while another type of thing is exclusively interdicted. It is not out of the question that one and the same object may be both #$itemAdmitted and #$itemInterdicted at different times in the same #$RegulatedTransportSituation:  #$itemAdmitted and #$itemInterdicted are not negation preds.  Situationally, every #$RegulatedTransportSituation includes a (#$GroupFn #$CrossingABorder) that is the situational sum of all the boundary-crossings that happen as part of the situation; likewise a mass #$BoundarySituation that is also a (#$GroupFn #$BoundarySituation):  the situational sum of all interdictions that occur in the course of the #$RegulatedTransportSituation.")
(comment Arginine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These compounds are essential for protein synthesis and supplies the amidine group for the synthesis of creatine.  Its abbreviations are Arg and R.")
(comment GolgiCisterna "The collection of cisterna which are parts of the #$GolgiApparatus organelles of #$Cells.")
(comment GolgiCisternaMembrane-Stuff "The collection of membranous material (#$LipidBilayers) which make up #$GolgiCisterna.")
(comment EndoplasmicReticulumMembrane-Stuff "The collection of #$BiologicalMembrane-Stuffs out of which #$EndoplasmicReticulum #$Organelles are made.")
(comment GolgiCisternaMembrane "The collection of #$BiologicalMembranes which are parts of #$GolgiCisterna structures.")
(comment EndoplasmicReticulumMembraneCytosolicSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of #$EndoplasmicReticulum organelles. Each #$EndoplasmicReticulumMembraneCytosolicSurface is adjacent to, in contact with, and completely surrounded by the #$Cytosol.")
(comment GolgiCisternaMembraneCytosolicSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of #$GolgiCisterna structures. Each #$GolgiCisternaMembraneCytosolicSurface is adjacent to, in contact with, the #$Cytosol.")
(comment GolgiCisternaMembraneLumenalSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of #$GolgiCisternaMembranes.")
(comment GolgiCisternaLumen "The interior of the #$GolgiCisterna, enclosed by the #$GolgiCisternaMembrane. ")
(comment exceptForInArg "A meta-predicate used to state exceptions to rules encoded as ground atomic formulae via rule macro predicates, <code>(#$exceptFor THING N ASSERTION)</code> means that substituting <code>THING</code> in for the <code>N</code>th argument to the #$assertionSentence <code>SENT</code> of <code>ASSERTION</code> yields a sentence <code>EXCEPTIONAL</code> that is not true, despite the fact that <code>SENT</code> encodes a rule from which <code>EXCEPTIONAL</code> logically follows.  For example, where <code>ASSERTION</code> is an assertion of the sentence, <p><code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$anatomicallyCapableOf) #$Flying-FlappingWings #$Bird #$doneBy)</code>, <p>the assertion, <p><code>(#$exceptForInArg #$Ostrich 2 ASSERTION)</code> <p>means that ostriches are an exception to this rule, i.e., that <p><code>((#$TypeCapableFn #$anatomicallyCapableOf) #$Flying-FlappingWings #$Ostrich #$doneBy)</code> <p>is not true.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceTypeBySchedule "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$USControlledSubstanceTypeBySchedule is a collection of substances regulated by the Controlled Substances Act listed on a particular schedule of US Code.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceScheduleI "The Schedule I list of substances according to US Code.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceScheduleII "The Schedule II list of substances according to US Code.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceScheduleIII "The Schedule III list of substances according to US Code.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceScheduleIV "The Schedule IV list of substances according to US Code.")
(comment USControlledSubstanceScheduleV "The Schedule V list of substances according to US Code.")
(comment substanceRegulatedOnSchedule "<code>(#$substanceRegulatedOnSchedule SUBSTANCE SCHED)</code> means that <code>SUBSTANCE</code> is on the schedule <code>SCHED</code>, which indicates how <code>SUBSTANCE</code> is regulated.")
(comment 3-PhosphoglycerateMolecule "A biochemically important molecule that is formed in the first step of #$CalvinCycle and is also an intermediate in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment SubstrateLevelPhosphorylation "The collection of all events in which a phosphate group is directly, enzymatically transferred from an organic molecule to #$AdenosineDiphosphate, forming #$AdenosineTriphosphate.")
(comment PhosphoglyceromutaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that catalyze the transformation of #$3-PhosphoglycerateMolecules into #$2-PhosphoglycerateMolecules or vice-versa.  The 3-phospho- to 2-phospho- direction is a step during #$Glycolysis.")
(comment PhosphoglycerokinaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of performing #$SubstrateLevelPhosphorylation of ADP (see #$AdenosineDiphosphate) to produce ATP by transforming a #$1-3-BisphosphoglycerateMolecule to a #$3-PhosphoglycerateMolecule as a step in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment 2-PhosphoglycerateMolecule "A biochemically important molecule that is an intermediate in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are used in #$C4CarbonFixationInPlants and are an intermediate in #$Glycolysis.")
(comment EnolaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that catalyze the conversion of #$2-PhosphoglycerateMolecules to #$PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion. ")
(comment PyruvateKinaseMolecule "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of performing #$SubstrateLevelPhosphorylation of ADP (see #$AdenosineDiphosphate) to produce ATP by transforming a #$PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion into a #$PyruvateIon.")
(comment PhosphateTransferFrom1-3Bisphospoglycerate "The collection of all events in which a phosphate group is directly, enzymatically transferred from a #$1-3-BisphosphoglycerateMolecule to #$AdenosineDiphosphate, forming #$AdenosineTriphosphate and a #$3-PhosphoglycerateMolecule.")
(comment PhosphateTransferFromPhosphoenolpyruvate "The collection of all events in which a phosphate group is directly, enzymatically transferred from a #$PhosphoenolpyruvateAnion to #$AdenosineDiphosphate, forming #$AdenosineTriphosphate and a #$PyruvateIon.")
(comment ApplicationSpecificQuestionSuggestionMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories that support question-suggestion for a specific application, and thus are the target of rules that conclude #$plausibleQueries and #$matchableQueries for a given source of data.")
(comment CellMembraneGrowth "Instances of #$CellMembraneGrowth are events in which portions of #$BiologicalMembrane are created and added to the #$CellMembrane of a particular cell, resulting in its increase in size.")
(comment drugIsFocalIngredientOfProduct "A predicate corresponding to the function #$DrugProductFn.  <code>(#$drugIsFocalIngredientOfProduct DRUG PRODUCT</code> states that <code>PRODUCT</code> is a #$PharmacyProductType intended to be used to deliver one or more doses of <code>DRUG</code> to the individual that uses it.")
(comment concentration "<code>(#$concentration OBJ STUFF-TYPE CON)</code> states that the concentration of <code>STUFF-TYPE</code> within <code>OBJ</code> is <code>CON</code>.")
(comment EnergyInvestmentPhaseOfGlycolysis "Instances are #$MetabolicPathways which are part of the larger #$Glycolysis pathway, and consist of the first five chemical reactions of glycolysis (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis), in which there is a net use of #$AdenosineTriphosphate.  The products of this stage are thus of higher energy than the inputs, so this portion of #$Glycolysis could be said to be an #$AnabolicPathway.")
(comment EnergyPayoffPhaseOfGlycolysis "Instances are #$MetabolicPathways which are part of the larger #$Glycolysis pathway, and consist of the final five chemical reactions of glycolysis (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis), in which there is a net gain of #$AdenosineTriphosphate.  The products of this stage are thus of lower energy than the inputs, so this portion of #$Glycolysis is a #$CatabolicPathway.")
(comment LastFiveReactionsOfGlycolysis "Instances are #$MetabolicPathways which are sequences of the final five chemical reactions of glycolysis (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis).  Two such reaction sequences make up an instance of #$EnergyPayoffPhaseOfGlycolysis.")
(comment elaborateVarietyOfType "<code>(#$elaborateVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually elaborate instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment ElaborateFn "<code>(#$ElaborateFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are more elaborate than ordinary.")
(comment SimpleFn "<code>(#$SimpleFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>TYPE</code> that are more simple than ordinary.")
(comment simpleVarietyOfType "<code>(#$simpleVarietyOfType TYPE AB-TYPE)</code> means that <code>AB-TYPE</code> is the collection of all unusually simple instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment TheKrebsCycle "A specialization of #$Cycle-Serial.  Instances are multiple complete iterations through a sequence of chemical reactions in living cells which fully oxidizes the organic molecules that result from oxidizing #$PyruvateIon as part of cellular respiration.  For the event which represents one pass through the cycle, see #$KrebsCycle. ")
(comment TheEukaryoticCellCycle "A specialization of #$Cycle-Serial and #$EventSeries.  Instances are chains of individual growth and division periods for eukaryotic cells, such that any input (see #$parentCell) to a given iteration is the output (see #$daughterCells) of the previous iteration, and at least one of the outputs of the given iteration is an input to the next iteration.  For the collection of all single iterations (i.e., the eukaryotic cell cycle as a localized process in which a single eukaryotic cell grows and divides), see #$EukaryoticCellCycle.")
(disjointWith ProcessRequiringNoEnergyInput ProcessRequiringEnergyInput)
(comment transportBoundarySystem "(#$transportBoundarySystem RTS BOUNDARY) means that BOUNDARY is the boundary across which traffic flows of certain kinds are regulated in the #$RegulatedTransportSituation RTS.")
(comment conservativeViaArgWRTTypes "This is a type-restricted version of #$conservativeViaArg.  (#$conservativeViaArgWRTTypes PRED BIN-PRED ARGN TYPE1 TYPE2) means that if PRED is the arg0 operator of a known sentence SENTENCE, and FROM-ARG is known to be the ARGNth argument of SENTENCE, and (BIN-PRED FROM-ARG TO-ARG) is true, then the sentence that results from substituting TO-ARG for FROM-ARG in SENTENCE is also true, provided FROM-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE1, and TO-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE2.")
(comment conservativeViaArgInverseWRTTypes "This is a type-restricted version of #$conservativeViaArgInverse.  (#$conservativeViaArgInverseWRTTypes PRED BIN-PRED ARGN TYPE1 TYPE2) means that if PRED is the arg0 operator of a known sentence SENTENCE, and TO-ARG is known to be the ARGNth argument of SENTENCE, and (BIN-PRED FROM-ARG TO-ARG) is true, then the sentence that results from substituting FROM-ARG for TO-ARG in SENTENCE is also true, provided FROM-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE1, and TO-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE2.")
(comment transitiveViaArgWRTTypes "This is a type-restricted version of #$transitiveViaArg.  (#$transitiveViaArgWRTTypes PRED TRANS-BIN-PRED ARGN TYPE1 TYPE2) means that if PRED is the arg0 operator of a known sentence SENTENCE, and FROM-ARG is known to be the ARGNth argument of SENTENCE, and (TRANS-BIN-PRED FROM-ARG TO-ARG) is true, then the sentence that results from substituting TO-ARG for FROM-ARG in SENTENCE is also true, provided FROM-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE1, and TO-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE2.")
(comment transitiveViaArgInverseWRTTypes "This is a type-restricted version of #$transitiveViaArgInverse.  (#$transitiveViaArgInverseWRTTypes PRED TRANS-BIN-PRED ARGN TYPE1 TYPE2) means that if PRED is the arg0 operator of a known sentence SENTENCE, and TO-ARG is known to be the ARGNth argument of SENTENCE, and (TRANS-BIN-PRED FROM-ARG TO-ARG) is true, then the sentence that results from substituting FROM-ARG for TO-ARG in SENTENCE is also true, provided FROM-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE1, and TO-ARG is known to be an instance of TYPE2.")
(comment ReductionInCalvinCycle "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. This is one of three steps of #$CalvinCycle. In this step, each molecule of #$3-PhosphoglycerateMolecule is reduced to #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate .")
(comment PhotosyntheticLightReactionsCyclicElectronFlowInPurpleSulfurBacteria "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Instances of  #$PhotosyntheticLightReactionsCyclicElectronFlowInPurpleSulfurBacteria occur in #$PurpleSulfurBacterium. ")
(comment chromosomeSets "<code>(#$chromosomeSets CELL SET)</code> means that <code>SET</code> is one of <code>CELL</code>'s sets of chromosomes.")
(comment matchableQueryWithDefaultCategory "<code>(#$matchableQueryWithDefaultCategory THING QUERY CATEGORY)</code> means that the #$CycLQuerySpecification <code>QUERY</code> is a #$matchableQueries for <code>THING</code> that falls into the category <code>CATEGORY</code>.")
(comment JunctionBetweenGlycolysisAndKrebsCycle "Instances are events in which #$PyruvateIons are oxidized into #$AcetylCoenzymeA as part of #$Glycolysis. Such events serve as the junction between #$Glycolysis and the #$KrebsCycle in #$CellularRespiration.")
(comment CoenzymeAMolecule "The collection of coenzyme A molecules. Instances are metabolically important, and may be involved in fatty acid metabolism or #$Glycolysis. ")
(comment DecarboxylationOfPyruvateInGlycolysis " A specialization of #$DecarboxylationReaction. Instances involve conversion of #$PyruvateIon to #$CarbonDioxide and an intermediate.  This is one step of a three-step reaction (see #$JunctionBetweenGlycolysisAndKrebsCycle) that is sometimes called \"pyruvate decarboxylation\" and sometimes called \"pyruvate oxidation\".")
(comment ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject. Each instance of #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex is either a single #$ProteinMolecule or is a group of #$ProteinMolecules linked into a #$MultiProteinComplex.")
(comment AnaphasePromotingComplex "A specialization of #$MultiProteinComplex. Each instance of #$AnaphasePromotingComplex is a protein complex that can be activated during mitosis to initiate anaphase.")
(comment MultiEnzymeComplex "This is the collection of enzyme complexes, which are #$MultiProteinComplexes consisting of two or more individual #$EnzymeMolecules.  ")
(disjointWith RibozymeMolecule MultiEnzymeComplex)
(disjointWith SugarMolecule MultiEnzymeComplex)
(comment PyruvateDehydrogenaseComplex "An specialization of #$MultiEnzymeComplex.  Instances are enzymes that are capable of performing the reactions that transform #$PyruvateIon into #$AcetylCoenzymeA (see #$JunctionBetweenGlycolysisAndKrebsCycle).")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateQueryMt "An instance of #$PlausibleQuerySpecificationPredicate, <code>(#$plausibleQueryPredicateQueryMt PREDICATE MT)</code> means that plausible queries constructed from the predicate <code>PREDICATE</code> should be asked from the microtheory <code>MT</code>.")
(comment qsQueryPredicate "<code>(#$qsQueryPredicate QUERY PRED)</code> identifies <code>PRED</code> as the instance of #$Predicate that is the #$operatorFormulas for the #$sentenceParameterValueInSpecification for the instance <code>QUERY</code> of #$CycLQuerySpecification.")
(comment maximalTypeWRTSlotInSitType "<code>(#$maximalTypeWRTSlotInSitType TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE COLLECTION SLOT)</code> means that relative to other things in COLLECTION anything <code>THING</code> that is an instance of TYPE is maximal with regard to its value for SLOT when it plays the role ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE. ")
(comment exclusiveSubSituationTypes "(#$exclusiveSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE EITHER-TYPE XOR-TYPE) means that every instance of SIT-TYPE has as #$properSubSituations an instance of either EITHER-TYPE or XOR-TYPE, but no instance of SIT-TYPE ever has an instance of both collections as #$properSubSituations.")
(comment DecarboxylatedIntermediateInPyruvateOxidation "The collection of chemical objects with the formula CH3CO which are the result of the first, decarboxylation step of the transformation of #$PyruvateIon into #$AcetylCoenzymeA.  After this initial decarboxylation step, the atoms of the #$PyruvateIon reactant may be bound to a cofactor in the reaction, hence we neither claim the intermediate is an #$Ion or a #$Molecule.")
(comment OxidationToAcetateInGlycolysis " A specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction. Instances involve conversion of the #$DecarboxylatedIntermediateInPyruvateOxidation to #$AcetateIon and the generation of NADH from NAD .  This is the second step of a three-step reaction (see #$JunctionBetweenGlycolysisAndKrebsCycle) that is sometimes called \"pyruvate decarboxylation\" and sometimes called \"pyruvate oxidation\".")
(comment AcetylCoAProductionInGlycolysis " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve attachment of an #$AcetateIon to a #$CoenzymeAMolecule.  This is the third and final step of a three-step reaction (see #$JunctionBetweenGlycolysisAndKrebsCycle) that is sometimes called \"pyruvate decarboxylation\" and sometimes called \"pyruvate oxidation\".")
(comment HansAdolfKrebs "A German biochemist and physician known for determining the steps of the #$KrebsCycle, also known as the citric acid cycle or the tricarboxylic pathway, and for similar work on the #$Urea cycle.")
(comment CitrateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are an intermediate in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)). ")
(comment OxaloacetateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are produced in the first step of #$C4CarbonFixation, and are produced as the final product in a single iteration through the Krebs Cycle (See (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle).")
(comment IsocitrateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are an intermediate substrate in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)).")
(comment AlphaKetoglutarateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are an intermediate substrate in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)).")
(comment SuccinateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are an intermediate substrate in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)).")
(comment TransportVesicle "The collection of #$Vesicles whose primary purpose is the
transportation of objects, particularly molecules, either within the
interior space of the vesicle or within the #$BiologicalMembrane-Stuff
out of which the #$TransportVesicle consists.")
(comment VesicularBudding "The collection of events in which a #$Vesicle is formed and
separates from an existing #$BiologicalMembrane.")
(comment VesicularTransportEvent "The collection of #$TransportationEvents in which an object, often a molecule, is transported from one location to another by means of a #$TransportVesicle. #$VesicularTransportEvents involve three distinct stages: #$VesicularBudding, a #$TransportationEvent, and a #$BiologicalMembraneFusionEvent.")
(comment SuccinylCoenzymeA "A specilaization of #$Thioester.  Acetyl coenzyme A is a substance that plays a significant role in iin metabolism, and in particular in the Krebs cycle.")
(comment FumarateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are an intermediate substrate in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)).")
(comment MalateAnion "A specialization of #$PolyatomicAnion.  Instances are produced in the second step of #$C4CarbonFixation. Other instances are intermediate substrates in the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment CondensationReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  In a #$CondensationReaction, most of the atoms in two #$Molecules combine to form a single #$Molecule, and one small molecule, such as water or acetic acid, is lost.")
(disjointWith CondensationReaction DecarboxylationReaction)
(disjointWith IsomerizationReaction CondensationReaction)
(disjointWith Hydrolysis-ChemicalReaction CondensationReaction)
(disjointWith Phosphorylation CondensationReaction)
(disjointWith (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet (MoleculeFn Water) (MoleculeFn MethylAlcohol) (MoleculeFn AceticAcid) (MoleculeFn HydrogenChloride))) (CollectionDifferenceFn Molecule (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet (MoleculeFn Water) (MoleculeFn MethylAlcohol) (MoleculeFn AceticAcid) (MoleculeFn HydrogenChloride)))))
(comment CitrateFormationInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$CondensationReaction. Instances involve combination of the acetyl group from #$AcetylCoenzymeA to #$OxaloacetateAnion to form #$CitrateAnion.  A  #$CoenzymeAMolecule is freed. This is the first step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment IsocitrateFormationInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$IsomerizationReaction. Instances involve conversion of a #$CitrateAnion into an #$IsocitrateAnion.  This is the second step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment OxidationOfIsocitrateInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$RedoxReaction. Instances involve oxidation then decarboxylation of an #$IsocitrateAnion to produce an #$AlphaKetoglutarateAnion and a molecule of #$CarbonDioxide, while reducing NAD  to NADH.  This is the third step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment TransferOfPyruvateIonToMesophyllCellsInC4CarbonFixation "A specialization of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Instances involve transfer of #$PyruvateIon to #$MesophyllCell during #$C4CarbonFixation .")
(comment CBvanNiel "An American microbiologist known for explaining the chemistry of #$Photosynthesis-Generic.")
(comment CBvanNielsFirstExperimentWithTracerIsotopes "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In this reaction, #$CarbonDioxide was reacted with #$Water with an isotope of #$Oxygen to understand the mechanism of #$Photosynthesis-Plant.")
(comment WaterWithOxygen18Atom "A specialization of #$Water. Instances contain O-18, an isotope of #$Oxygen.  ")
(comment O2MoleculeWithOxygen18Atom "A specialization of #$O2Molecule. Instances contain O-18, an isotope of #$Oxygen.")
(comment CarbonDioxideWithOxygen16Atoms "A specialization of #$CarbonDioxide. Instances contain O-16, an isotope of #$Oxygen.")
(comment CBvanNielsSecondExperimentWithTracerIsotopes "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In this reaction, #$CarbonDioxide containing O-18 isotopes was used to understand the mechanism of #$Photosynthesis-Plant.")
(comment CarbonDioxideWithOxygen18Atoms "A specialization of #$CarbonDioxide. Instances contain O-18, an isotope of #$Oxygen.")
(comment O2MoleculeWithOxygen16Atom "A specialization of #$O2Molecule. Instances contain O-16, an isotope of #$Oxygen.")
(comment particleTransferredInEventTypeFromTo "(#$particleTransferredInEventTypeFromTo EVENT-TYPE PARTICLE-TYPE SOURCE-TYPE DESTINATION-TYPE) means that instances of PARTICLE-TYPE are transferred from instances of SOURCE-TYPE to instances of DESTINATION-TYPE in events of type EVENT-TYPE. ")
(comment accelerationOfObject-Angular "This predicate relates an object to its magnitude of angular acceleration. <code>(#$accelerationOfObject-Angular OBJECT ACCELERATION)</code> means that the angular acceleration of <code>OBJECT</code> has magnitude <code>ACCELERATION</code>. Note that physically, angular acceleration is a vector valued quantity, possessing both a direction and a magnitude. This predicate is intended to relate only the magnitude of angular acceleration to the object, irrespective of the directional component of angular acceleration.")
(disjointWith MitochondrialMatrix IntermembraneSpace)
(disjointWith MitochondrialMatrix Cytosol)
(disjointWith Cytosol IntermembraneSpace)
(comment Glycosylation "A process that occurs primarily in the #$RoughEndoplasmicReticulum and #$GolgiApparatus, but may also occur in the #$Cytoplasm, in which a carbohydrate is joined to a protein or lipid.")
(comment N-LinkedGlycosylation "A process that occurs in the #$EndoplasmicReticulum and in which a carbohydrate is joined to a nitrogen atom of an asparagine or arginine side-chain of a protein.")
(comment GlycosylationTypeByLocusOfCellularProcess-CellPart "A second order collection faceting #$Glycolization by
#$locusOfCellularProcess-CellPart. Note that since #$Glycolization is
site-specific, it is limited to four #$CellPart locations:
#$EndoplasmicReticulum, #$GolgiApparatus, #$Cytoplasm, and
#$Nucleus. Its complete extent is therefore asserted.")
(comment Glycosylation-CellNucleus "The collection of #$Glycosylation events that occur at the
#$CellNucleus.")
(comment NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn "#$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn is an instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.   #$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn, when applied to  specializations of #$Situation SIT-TYPE and SUB-SIT-TYPE, and a #$PositiveInteger N, returns the N-th sub-situation of type SUB-SIT-TYPE in SIT-TYPE.  For example, (#$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn DogControl (#$GainingControlOfFn #$Dog) 1) and (#$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn DogControl (#$GainingControlOfFn #$Dog) 2) would represent distinct (#$GainingControlOfFn #$Dog) sub-situations in a DogControl script.  Also, (#$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn DogControl (#$GainingControlOfFn #$Dog) 1) and (#$NthSubSituationTypeOfTypeFn DogControl #$GainingControl 2)) would represent distinct #$GainingControl sub-situations in a DogControl situation type.")
(comment biologicalFunctionOfProcessInBLOType "<code>(#$biologicalFunctionOfProcessInBLOType EVENT FUNCTION BLO-TYPE)</code> means that in instances of biological living objects of type events of type <code>BLO-TYPE</code> that are #$physiologicallyDoneBy those objects serve the purpose of bringing about or fostering events of type <code>FUNCTION</code>.")
(comment WaterWithOxygen16Atom "A specialization of #$Water. Instances contain O-16, an isotope of #$Oxygen.  ")
(comment Epidermis-Plant "A specialization of #$Epidermis and #$PlantPart.  Each instance of #$Epidermis is the outermost layer of leaves, roots, stems or flowers in a plant.")
(comment Epidermis-Leaf "A specialization of #$Epidermis-Plant. Each instance of #$Epidermis-Leaf is the outermost layer of a #$Leaf in a #$Plant.")
(comment priorLikelihoodOfPassiveTransport "(#$priorLikelihoodOfPassiveTransport GRANULE-TYPE FILTER-TYPE LIKELIHOOD) means that if all that is known about a particular #$Filtering-Transport is that the #$filterer is an instance of type FILTER-TYPE, the #$likelihood of an instance of GRANULE-TYPE being #$itemAdmitted in the #$Filtering-Transport is LIKELIHOOD.")
(comment SuccinylCoAProductionInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$RedoxReaction. Instances involve decarboxylation then oxidation of an #$AlphaKetoglutarateAnion to produce a molecule of #$CarbonDioxide and a molecule of #$SuccinylCoenzymeA, while reducing NAD  to NADH.  This is the fourth step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment NucleosideDiphosphate "A collection of nucleotides. They consist of a #$NitrogenBase, such as #$Adenine-Base, linked with a sugar and two phosphates.")
(comment FlavinAdenineDinucleotide "The collection of FAD  molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have and important role in electron transfer, able to exist in a partially reduced state (FADH) and a fully reduced state (FADH2).  ")
(comment FlavinAdenineDinucleotide-FullyReduced "The collection of FADH2  molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have and important role in electron transfer, able to exist in a fully oxidized state (FAD), a partially reduced state (FADH) and a fully reduced state (FADH2).  ")
(comment FlavinAdenineDinucleotide-PartiallyReduced "The collection of FADH  molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have and important role in electron transfer, able to exist in a fully oxidized state (FAD), a partially reduced state (FADH) and a fully reduced state (FADH2).  ")
(comment FlavinAdenineDinucleotide-Generic "The collection including molecules of FAD, FADH and FADH2. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have and important role in electron transfer, able to exist in a fully oxidized state (FAD), a partially reduced state (FADH) and a fully reduced state (FADH2).  ")
(comment SuccinateProductionInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve removal of a #$CoenzymeAMolecule then phosphorylation of a #$NucleosideDiphosphate to produce a molecule of #$GuanosineTriphosphate and a #$SuccinateAnion.  This is the fifth step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment OxidationOfSuccinateInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$RedoxReaction. Instances involve oxidation  of an #$SuccinateAnion to produce an #$FumarateAnion, while reducing FAD  to FADH2.  This is the sixth step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment MalateProductionInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve reaction of a #$FumarateAnion with a molecule of water to produce an #$MalateAnion.  This is the seventh step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment OxidationOfMalateInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction. Instances involve oxidation  of an #$MalateAnion to produce an #$OxaloacetateAnion, while reducing NAD  to NADH.  This is the eigth and last step in one complete iteration through the #$KrebsCycle.")
(comment ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex "A specialization of #$MacromolecularComplex. Each instance of #$ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex is an assemblage of molecules that act together to couple the passing of electrons from an electron donor to an electron acceptor with the puming of #$HydrogenPlusIons across a biological membrane.  The resulting differential in the concentration of hydrogen ions is used to power the synthesis of ATP, which can then be used to do work within a cell. ")
(disjointWith Photosystem ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex)
(disjointWith ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex LightHarvestingComplex)
(disjointWith PhotosyntheticReactionCenter ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex)
(comment MolecularElectronTransportChainFn "<code>(#$MolecularElectronTransportChainFn CHAIN-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex whose molecular parts are the electron donors and acceptors for instances of the type of #$ElectronTransportChain, <code>CHAIN-TYPE</code>.")
(comment electronTransportChainTypeHasMolecularComplexType "<code>(#$electronTransportChainTypeHasMolecularComplexType CHAIN-TYPE COMPLEX-TYPE)</code> means that <code>COMPLEX-TYPE</code> is the collection of #$ElectronTransportChain-MolecularComplex objects which engage in instances of <code>CHAIN-TYPE</code>.")
(comment FlavinMononucleotide-Generic "The collection including molecules of FMN, FMNH and FMNH2. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have a role in electron transfer, able to exist in a fully oxidized state (FMN), a partially reduced state (FMNH) and a fully reduced state (FMNH2).  ")
(comment FlavinMononucleotide "The collection of FMN molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have a role in electron transfer, able to exist in a partially reduced state (FMNH) and a fully reduced state (FMNH2).  ")
(comment FlavinMononucleotide-PartiallyReduced "The collection of FMNH molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have a role in electron transfer, able to exist in an oxidized state (FMN), a partially reduced state (FMNH) and a fully reduced state (FMNH2).  ")
(comment FlavinMononucleotide-FullyReduced "The collection of FMNH2 molecules. Such molecules are found in #$EukaryoticCells, where they have a role in electron transfer, able to exist in an oxidized state (FMN), a partially reduced state (FMNH) and a fully reduced state (FMNH2).  ")
(comment Cofactor "A #$Cofactor is a small molecule that can become bound to a protein, particularly an #$EnzymeMolecule, thus enabling its biological activity.  When a cofactor is an organic molecule, it is usually called a #$Coenzyme.  Some proteins require multiple cofactors to enable their activity. ")
(comment FlavoproteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  #$FlavoproteinMolecules are #$ProteinMolecules which have either a #$FlavinMononucleotide or a #$FlavinAdenineDinucleotide as a #$prostheticGroup.")
(comment prostheticGroup "(#$prostheticGroup PROTEIN-MOL MOLECULAR_COMPONENT) means that MOLECULAR_COMPONENT is a connected part of PROTEIN-MOL (either an instance of #$Molecule or a larger part of a molecule).  #$prostheticGroups are non-protein molecules bound to protein molecules, in particular to #$EnzymeMolecules, that are required for the functionality of the protein. ")
(comment Iron-SulfurCluster "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjects consisting of multiple #$Iron and #$Sulfur atoms in which the #$Iron atoms occur as #$Ions linked by sulfide ions.  Such objects occur as #$prostheticGroups of #$Iron-SulfurProteinMolecules. ")
(comment Iron-SulfurProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  #$Iron-SulfurProteinMolecules are #$ProteinMolecules which have an #$Iron-SulfurCluster as a #$prostheticGroup.")
(comment ConcentrationGradient "A specialization of #$Configuration and #$AbundanceGradient. Instances include situations in which there is a difference in concentration of a constituent between two regions.")
(disjointWith AbundanceGradientAlongASurface ConcentrationGradient)
(comment frequencyOfTypePerUnitArea "<code>(#$frequencyOfTypePerUnitArea OBJ TYPE AREAFREQUENCY)</code> means that the population per unit area of instances of <code>TYPE</code> over the surface of <code>OBJ</code> is <code>AREAFREQUENCY</code>.  ")
(comment ProtonGradientBetweenStromaAndThylakoidSpace "A specialization of #$ConcentrationGradient. Instances include situations in which there is a difference in concentration of #$HydrogenPlusIons between #$ChloroplastStroma and #$ThylakoidSpace. ")
(comment minimalTypeWRTSlotInSitType "<code>(#$minimalTypeWRTSlotInSitType TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE COLLECTION SLOT)</code> means that relative to other things in COLLECTION anything <code>THING</code> that is an instance of TYPE is minimal with regard to the value for SLOT in SIT-TYPE when it plays the role ROLE in SIT-TYPE. ")
(comment AbundanceGradientAlongASurface "A specialization of #$AbundanceGradient. Instances include situations in which the numbers of a constituent change across a given two-dimensional surface.")
(comment AbundanceGradient "A specialization of #$Configuration. Instances include situations in which the numbers of a constituent change across a given two or three dimensional region. ")
(comment portalTypeAdmitsObjectType "(#$portalTypeAdmitsObjectType PORTAL-TYPE OBJECT-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, a given instance of type OBJECT-TYPE is able to pass through (#$canPassThroughPortal) a given instances of the #$Portal specialization PORTAL-TYPE.")
(comment MoleculeOrientationEvent "The collection of #$Movement-Rotations where the focal
object rotating is a #$Molecule, there is a #$providerOfMotiveForce,
and a specific orientation is the result of the event (e.g. a molecule
rotation resulting from brownian motion would not be an instance of
#$MoleculeOrientationEvent.")
(comment CellularMoleculeOrientationEvent "The collection of #$MoleculeOrientationEvents in which the
#$Molecule oriented is part of a #$Cell.")
(comment Flippase "The collection of #$IntegralMembraneProteins responsible for
the orientation of other #$Phospholipids in a #$BiologicalMembrane.")
(comment Translocon "A collection of #$MultiProteinComplexes that are responsible
for movement of polypeptides through membranes and also the location
and orientation of #$MembraneProteins.")
(comment BiologicalMembraneMoleculeOrientationEvent "The collection of #$MoleculeOrientationEvents in which the
#$Molecule oriented is part of #$BiologicalMembrane-Stuff, and where the
location is a #$BiologicalMembrane.")
(comment MembraneProteinOrientationEvent "The collection of
BiologicalMembraneMoleculeOrientationEvents in which the oriented
#$Molecule is a #$MembraneProtein.")
(comment MembranePhospholipidOrientationEvent "The collection of
BiologicalMembraneMoleculeOrientationEvents in which the oriented
#$Molecule is a #$Phospholipid.")
(comment filterHasPoresOfType "(#$filterHasPoresOfType BARRIER PORTAL-TYPE) means that BARRIER contains many #$Portals (#$containsPortals) of type PORTAL-TYPE.")
(comment ElectronTransferInRedoxTypeFn "<code>(#$ElectronTransferInRedoxTypeFn REDOX-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of #$ElectronTransfers that occur as part of instances of <code>REDOX-TYPE</code>, a specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction.  In such a reaction, the chemical object from which electrons are transferred becomes oxidized, and the chemicalobject to which electrons are transferred becomes reduced.")
(comment typeHasElectronTransfer "<code>(#$typeHasElectronTransfer REDOX-TYPE TrANS-TYPE)</code> means that instances of the type of #$SimpleRedoxReaction, <code>REDOX-TYPE</code> have, as their #$ElectronTransfer subevents, instances of <code>OXID-TYPE</code>.")
(comment RedoxOfTypeAndTypeFn "<code>(#$RedoxOfTypeAndTypeFn REDUCED-TYPE OXIDIZED-TYPE)</code> denotes a type of #$SimpleRedoxReaction in which <code>REDUCED-TYPE</code> is the chemical object that is reduced, and <code>OXIDIZED-TYPE</code> is the chemical object that is oxidized")
(comment redoxOfTypeAndType "<code>(#$redoxOfTypeAndType REDUCED-TYPE OXIDIZED-TYPE REDOX-TYPE)</code> means that <code>REDOX-TYPE</code> is the collection of #$SimpleRedoxReaction events in which an instance of the type of #$ChemicalObject, <code>REDUCED-TYPE</code>, is reduced, and an instance of the type of #$ChemicalObject, <code>OXIDIZED-TYPE</code>, is oxidized.")
(comment ElectronTransportChain "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportChain is a sequence of exergonic #$SimpleRedoxReactions in which #$Electrons are passed from a donor to a molecule that is more  electronegative, then from that molecule to the next in the chain (yet more electronegative), until the final electron acceptor receives the electron.  Instead of passing the electron directly to the final acceptor, which would lead to a large release of energy, an #$ElectronTransportChain releases energy in controlled steps, often generating energy containing molecules like #$AdenosineTriphosphate along the way.  #$ElectronTransportChains occur as part of #$CellularRespiration and as part of the #$LightDependentStepOfPhotosynthesis.")
(comment MitochondrialComplexIFlavoproteinMolecule "A specialization of #$FlavoproteinMolecule.  #$MitochondrialComplexIFlavoproteinMolecule are #$ProteinMolecules which are part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexI.")
(comment MitochondrialComplexIIronSulfurProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$Iron-SulfurProteinMolecule.  #$MitochondrialComplexIIronSulfurProteinMolecule are #$ProteinMolecules which are part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexI.")
(comment HemeGroup "The collection of all #$ChemicalObjects consisting of an #$Iron #$Atom bound in the center of #$PorphyrinRing.  Such objects occur as #$prostheticGroups of #$HemoproteinMolecules. ")
(comment HemoproteinMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule.  #$HemoproteinMolecules are #$ProteinMolecules which have a #$HemeGroup as a #$prostheticGroup.")
(comment CytochromeMolecule "A specialization of #$ProteinMolecule. Cytochromes are iron-containing proteins that can participate in #$ElectronTransportChains.")
(comment CytochromeCMolecule "A specialization of #$CytochromeMolecule. Cytochrome C is a small, water-soluble #$HemoproteinMolecule loosely bound to the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane.  It transfers electrons between #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII and #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIV.")
(comment CytochromeC1Molecule "A specialization of #$CytochromeMolecule. Cytochrome C1 is a #$HemoproteinMolecule that is part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII. ")
(comment CytochromeBMolecule "A specialization of #$CytochromeMolecule. Cytochrome B is a #$HemoproteinMolecule.  Some instance is part of each #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII and of each #$CytochromeB6FComplex.")
(comment MitochondrialComplexIII-IronSulfurProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$Iron-SulfurProteinMolecule.  #$MitochondrialComplexIII-IronSulfurProteinMolecules are #$ProteinMolecules which are part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII.")
(comment CytochromeAMolecule "A specialization of #$CytochromeMolecule. Cytochrome A is a #$HemoproteinMolecule that is part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIV. ")
(comment CytochromeA3Molecule "A specialization of #$CytochromeMolecule. Cytochrome A3 is a #$HemoproteinMolecule that is part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIV. ")
(comment GolgiApparatusProcess-BiologicalMembraneStuff "The collection of processes which portions of
#$CellMembrane-Stuff undergo in the #$GolgiApparatus.")
(comment GlycoconjugateMoleculeModification "The collection of events in which a #$GlycoconjugateMolecule
undergoes a chemical reaction which alters the structure of its
hydrocarbon component. The output of any such modification is another
#$GlycoconjugateMolecule.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen, electrons pass from the FADH2 generated in the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)) to molecular #$Oxygen.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  In each instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen, electrons pass from the NADH and FADH2 generated in #$Glycolysis (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$Glycolysis)) and the #$KrebsCycle (see (#$EventTypeGrainFn #$KrebsCycle)) to molecular #$Oxygen.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexII "An specialization of #$MultiEnzymeComplex.  Instances are macromolecular complexes located on the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane that function to transfer electrons from FADH2 to #$CoenzymeQ10 as part of the sequence of reactions in the #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen.")
(comment MitochondrialComplexII-IronSulfurProteinMolecule "A specialization of #$Iron-SulfurProteinMolecule.  #$MitochondrialComplexII-IronSulfurProteinMolecules are #$ProteinMolecules which are part of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexII.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIV "An specialization of #$MultiEnzymeComplex.  Instances are large macromolecular complexes located on the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane and in instances of #$Bacterium that function to transfer electrons from a #$CytochromeCMolecule to an #$Oxygen molecule as part of the sequence of reactions in the #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen and in #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexI "An specialization of #$MultiEnzymeComplex.  Instances are large macromolecular complexes located on the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane that function to transfer electrons from NADH (see #$ReducedNicotinamideAdenineDinucleotide) to #$CoenzymeQ10 as part of the sequence of reactions in the #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen.")
(comment MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII "An specialization of #$MultiEnzymeComplex.  Instances are large macromolecular complexes located on the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane that function to transfer electrons from #$CoenzymeQ10 to a #$CytochromeCMolecule as part of the sequence of reactions in the #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen and in #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen.")
(comment MembraneProtein "A subcollection of #$ProteinMolecule. Membrane proteins are proteins closely associated with a biological membrane. Those which are permanently attached to or embedded in the membrane are #$IntegralMembraneProteins. Those with a looser relationship are #$PeripheralProteins.")
(comment doingWhile "The predicate that corresponds to #$DoingWhileFn, <code>(#$doingWhile DOING-WHILE-TYPE DOING-TYPE WHILE-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>DOING-WHILE-TYPE</code> as the subcollection of instance of the event-type <code>DOING-TYPE</code> such that the doer of the event is simultaneously the doer of an instance of <code>WHILE-TYPE</code>.  See also #$doneWhile.")
(comment DoingWhileFn "<code>(#$DoingWhileFn DOING-TYPE WHILE-TYPE)</code> denotes the subcollection of instance of the event-type <code>DOING-TYPE</code> such that the doer of the event is simultaneously the doer of an instance of <code>WHILE-TYPE</code>.  For example, <p> <code>(#$DoingWhileFn #$AnimalWalkingProcess #$Sleeping)</code> <p>is the collection of events in which an animal sleepwalks (walks while sleeping). See also #$doneWhile.")
(comment AttendingVisuallyToLocusOfOnesOwnActivity "A specialization of #$WatchingSomething, this is the collection of events in which one watches his or her own actions while doing them. Typically this means focusing one's eyes on what one's hands are doing; in other cases, this might involve viewing real-time visual projection of ones actions, such as when a surgeon watches a television screen that is displaying his or her manipulations of a device inside the patient.")
(comment doneWhile "<code>(#$doneWhile EVENT-1 EVENT-2)</code> means that the doer (see #$doneBy) of <code>EVENT-1</code> is simultaneoulsy the doer of <code>EVENT-2</code>.")
(comment HandlingFoodOrDrink "A specialization of #$ManipulatingFoodOrDrink and #$HandlingAnObject, instances are events in which an agent directly handles #$FoodOrDrink, versus, e.g., the manipulations of food or drink by a machine, such as the operations of a blender.")
(comment LookingTypeByDirection "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$WatchingSomething into subcollections based on the general direction, relative to the orientation of the agent doing the watching, of the watcher's gaze.")
(comment HandlingAnObjectOnAReadilyAccessibleSurface "The collection of instances of #$HandlingAnObject in which the object is, at least initially, and often frequently, being supported on the surface of an object within easy reach of the handler, so as not to require the handler to move into a stretched or extended reach position.  For humans, canonical examples include activities in which a person works with his or her hands on a table, workbench, stovetop, or other surface designed to facilitate such work by minimizing the amount of extra-hand-involved exertion required.")
(comment OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of #$OuterMitochondrialMembranes. Each #$OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface is adjacent to and completely surrounded by the cell's #$Cytosol (see (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Cell #$Cytosol)).")
(disjointWith OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface CellMembraneSurface)
(comment OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of #$OuterMitochondrialMembranes. Each #$OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface is adjacent to and completely surrounds the #$Mitochondrion's intermembrane space (see (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Mitochondrion #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion)).")
(disjointWith OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface CellMembraneSurface)
(comment InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of #$InnerMitochondrialMembranes. Each #$InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface is adjacent to and completely surrounds the #$MitochondrialMatrix (see (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Mitochondrion #$MitochondrialMatrix)).")
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface CellMembraneSurface)
(comment InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of #$InnerMitochondrialMembranes. Each #$InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface is adjacent to and completely surrounded by the mitochondrion's intermembrane space (see (#$PartTypeEntirePortionFn #$Mitochondrion #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion)).")
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface CellMembraneSurface)
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface)
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface)
(disjointWith OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface InnerMitochondrialMembraneIntermembraneSurface)
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface)
(disjointWith OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface InnerMitochondrialMembraneMatrixSurface)
(disjointWith OuterMitochondrialMembraneCytosolicSurface OuterMitochondrialMembraneInnerSurface)
(disjointWith InnerMitochondrialMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith CellMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith CellMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerChloroplastMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith BiologicalMembrane SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(disjointWith Cell SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(disjointWith Organelle SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(disjointWith Organ SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(disjointWith Organism-Whole SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(comment SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion "A collection of #$CellParts. Each instance of #$SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion is some entire connected region within a #$Cell or #$Organelle, delineated by a #$BiologicalMembrane, exclusive of any other membrane-delineated compartments that may be surrounded by or floating in the region.  So, for example, #$Cytosol is a specialization of #$SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion, because it is that portion of the #$Cytoplasm that does not include #$Organelles as parts.  Because #$Cytoplasm instances include as parts other membrane-bound regions such as instances of #$Mitochondrion, it is not a specialization of this class.")
(comment membraneBoundsCompartment "An instance of #$RelativeLocationalPredicate.  <code>(#$membraneBoundsCompartment MEMBRANE SPACE)</code> means that <code>MEMBRANE</code> completely surrounds and directly touches <code>SPACE</code>.  For example, #$membraneBoundsCompartment would hold between an #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane and the #$MitochondrialMatrix within it. Note that <code>MEMBRANE</code> and <code>SPACE</code> are spatially disjoint. ")
(comment MembraneTransportOfTypeFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used to denote collections of events in which a type of chemical object is transported across a membrane. <code>(#$MembraneTransportOfTypeFn OBJ-TYPE)</code> is the subcollection of #$MembraneTransport events in each instance of which the type of object being transported across a membrane is <code>OBJ-TYPE</code>, which is an instance of #$ExistingObjectType and a specialization of #$ChemicalObject. For instance, '(#$MembraneTransportOfTypeFn #$HydrogenPlusIon)' denotes the collection of events in which protons are moved across a biological membrane.")
(comment MembraneTransport-Outward "The collection of instances of #$MembraneTransport in which chemical objects move out of a subcellular region (see #$SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion) through the membrane that surrounds it (see #$membraneBoundsCompartment).")
(comment MembraneTransport-Inward "The collection of instances of #$MembraneTransport in which chemical objects move into a subcellular compartment (see #$SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion) through the membrane that surrounds it (see #$membraneBoundsCompartment.)")
(comment BiologicalMembraneSurfaceTypeBySide "The collection of collections of
#$BiologicalMembraneSurfaces that partitions these into the side of
the #$BiologicalMembrane on which they are located. The only two
instances are #$BiologicalMembraneInteriorSurface and
#$BiologicalMembraneExteriorSurface.")
(comment BiologicalMembraneInteriorSurface "The collection of #$BiologicalMembraneSurfaces which
completely surround and are in contact with the interior region of the
#$BiologicalMembranes to which they belong.")
(comment BiologicalMembraneExteriorSurface "The collection of #$BiologicalMembraneSurfaces which are
extiorior to the #$BiologicalMembranes to which they
belong. #$BiologicalMembraneExteriorSurfaces, but definition,
completely surround their complimentary
#$BiologicalMembraneInteriorSurfaces.")
(comment exteriorMembraneSurface "<code>(#$exteriorMembraneSurface MEM SURF)</code> means that
<code>SURF</code> is the exterior surface of <code>MEM</code>.")
(comment sentenceJustifications-Simple "<code>(#$sentenceJustifications-Simple SENTENCE JUSTIFICATION)</code> means that one justification of <code>SENTENCE</code> is the instance <code>JUSTIFICATION</code> of #$Justification, and that <code>JUSTIFICATION</code> consists of a simplified list of supports, corresponding to leaf nodes and rules in a proof tree.")
(comment Justification "The collection of all justifications of some sentence, position, or action.")
(comment justificationOfWithSupports "The predicate that corresponds to #$JustificationFn, <code>(#$justificationOfWithSupports JUSTIFICATION SENTENCE SET-OF-SUPPORTS)</code> identifies <code>JUSTIFICATION</code> as the instance of #$Justification that is a logical justification of the CycL sentence <code>SENTENCE</code> whose supports are the sentences given in <code>LIST-OF-SUPPORTS</code>.")
(comment JustificationFn "<code>(#$JustificationFn SENTENCE SET-OF-SUPPORTS)</code> denotes the instance of #$Justification that is a logical justification of the CycL sentence <code>SENTENCE</code> whose supports are the sentences given in <code>SET-OF-SUPPORTS</code>.")
(comment ElectronTransportThroughComplexI "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportThroughComplexI is a sequence of redox reactions involving an instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexI as the #$catalyst.  In addition to these reactions, protons (instances of #$HydrogenPlusIon) are transported out of the #$MitochondrialMatrix and into the mitochondrial intermembrane space.")
(comment ElectronTransportThroughComplexII "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportThroughComplexII is a sequence of redox reactions involving an instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexII as the #$catalyst. Unlike electron transport through the other respiratory complexes, this complex does not move protons across the membrane.")
(comment ElectronTransportThroughComplexIII "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportThroughComplexIII is a sequence of redox reactions involving an instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIII as the #$catalyst.  In addition to these reactions, protons (instances of #$HydrogenPlusIon) are transported out of the #$MitochondrialMatrix and into the mitochondrial intermembrane space.")
(comment ElectronTransportThroughComplexIV "A specialization of #$ElectronTransportChain.  Each instance of #$ElectronTransportThroughComplexIII is a sequence of redox reactions involving an instance of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportComplexIV as the #$catalyst.  In addition to these reactions, protons (instances of #$HydrogenPlusIon) are transported out of the #$MitochondrialMatrix and into the mitochondrial intermembrane space.")
(comment TransportOfHydrogenPlusIonFromMitochondrialMatrixToIntermembraneSpace "A type of #$ActiveTransport-Membrane.  In each instance, a #$HydrogenPlusIon is moved across the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane from the #$MitochondrialMatrix to the #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion.  Energy to do so comes from the redox reactions of electron transport.")
(comment supportingSurfaceUsedInHandling "<code>(#$supportingSurfaceUsedInHandling HANDLING SUPPORTING-SURFACE)</code> means that <code>SUPPORTING-SURFACE</code> is the #$SurfaceRegion-Tangible on which the #$objectActedOn is supported in <code>HANDLING</code>, an instance of #$HandlingAnObjectOnAReadilyAccessibleSurface.")
(disjointWith ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Range ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Precise)
(comment ComparativeAltitudePredicate "A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate and #$SpatialPredicate, instances are predicates that relate two spatial objects in terms of their relative altitudes.")
(comment ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Precise "The collection of instances of  #$ComparativeAltitudePredicate that specify exactly where along the vertical axis of an object another object's altitude lies.")
(comment ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Range "The collection of instances of  #$ComparativeAltitudePredicate that specify some range along the vertical axis of an object within which another object's altitude lies.")
(comment situationFocalLocation "<code>(#$situationFocalLocation SIT LOCATION)</code> means that the #$Situation, <code>SIT</code>, is focally located at <code>LOCATION</code>, an instance of #$EnduringThing-Localized.  #$situationFocalLocation is more restrictive than its generalization, #$situationLocation, which applies to all instances of #$EnduringThing-Localized that spatially subsume every object to which it applies.  I.e., given an instance of #$ScrewedConnection, <code>ScrewedConnection-13926</code> that occurs within a piece of furniture, <code>Table-43</code>, #$situationLocation will not only hold between <code>ScrewedConnection-13926</code> and <code>Table-43</code>, it will hold of <code>ScrewedConnection-13926</code> and the room in which <code>Table-43</code> resides, the floor of the building where the room is, the building itself, ..., the planet Earth, and the entire physical universe.  However, #$situationFocalLocation holds only of <code>ScrewedConnection-13926</code> and <code>Table-43</code>.  This is not to say that #$situationFocalLocation is functional or single-entry in its second argument place; depending on the granularity of the context, it might be that the #$situationFocalLocation of a situation might include a range of locations.  However, unlike #$situationLocation, #$situationFocalLocation does not propagate to spatially-subsuming locations of its second argument. ")
(comment testTypeForWork "A predicate used to organize instances of #$KBContentTest into classes based on their relevance to exercising Cyc's representation of the claims of an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork, <code>(#$testTypeForWork TEST-TYPE WORK)</code> means that all of the instances of <code>TEST-TYPE</code> are relevant to <code>WORK</code> in the way suggested.")
(comment ConcentrationDifferentialAcrossBiologicalMembrane "A specialization of #$ConcentrationGradient. In each instance of #$ConcentrationDifferentialAcrossBiologicalMembrane, there is some #$BiologicalMembrane separating two regions such that the concentration of some #$TangibleStuffCompositionType is different in the two regions. ")
(comment CellularCompartment "A collection of #$MicroscopicScaleObjects. Each instance of #$CellularCompartment is some entire connected region defined in some sense by a #$BiologicalMembrane.  Such instances are either #$SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegions, which are connected regions within a #$Cell or #$Organelle, delineated by a #$BiologicalMembrane, exclusive of any other membrane-delineated compartments that may be surrounded by or floating in the region.  Or, instances are a microscopic-scale region immediately outside a single #$Cell. ")
(disjointWith Organism-Whole CellularCompartment)
(disjointWith BiologicalTissue CellularCompartment)
(disjointWith Organelle CellularCompartment)
(disjointWith Cell CellularCompartment)
(disjointWith BiologicalMembrane CellularCompartment)
(comment ExtracellularRegion-Immediate "A collection of #$MicroscopicScaleObjects. Each instance of #$ExtracellularRegion-Immediate is the region just outside a single #$Cell, shaped approximately like a hollow sphere.  The cell occupies the hollow of said sphere, and is not part of it. ")
(disjointWith ExtracellularRegion-Immediate SubcellularMembrane-EnclosedRegion)
(comment regionSurroundsMembrane "An instance of #$RelativeLocationalPredicate.  <code>(#$regionSurroundsMembrane REGION  MEMBRANE)</code> means that <code>REGION</code> completely surrounds and directly touches <code>MEMBRANE</code>.  For example, #$regionSurroundsMembrane would hold between a #$Cell's #$Cytosol and the #$OuterMitochondrialMembrane  of a #$Mitochondrion within that cell.  Note that <code>MEMBRANE</code> and <code>REGION</code> are spatially disjoint. ")
(comment VesicleMembrane "The collection of #$BiologicalMembranes which are parts of
#$Vesicles. This collection does not include the #$LipidBilayers that
are parts of #$Liposomes, as these are artificial.")
(disjointWith VesicleMembrane OuterMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith ThylakoidMembrane-Eukaryotic VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith InnerChloroplastMembrane VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith OuterChloroplastMembrane VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith CellPlateMembrane VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith NuclearEnvelope VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith Tonoplast VesicleMembrane)
(disjointWith VesicleMembrane InnerMitochondrialMembrane)
(disjointWith CellMembrane VesicleMembrane)
(comment VesicleMembraneLumenalSurface "The collection of all complete inner surfaces of
#$VesicleMembranes.")
(comment VesicleMembraneCytosolicSurface "The collection of all complete outer surfaces of
#$VesicleMembranes.")
(comment quantityChangesInSituationType "<code>(#$quantityChangesInSituationType SIT-TYPE SLOT)</code> means that in situations of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, the value on <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot, changes.  ")
(comment RelationshipBetweenConcentrationOfPollutantsAndDistanceFromSource "This formula represents the fact that the concentration of pollutants decreases with the distance from the pollution source.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSubSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance <code>SUBSIT</code> of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> which is a subsituation of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE SUBSIT ROLEPLAYER)</code> and if <code>ROLEPLAYER</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then immediately after <code>SIT</code> ends, <code>(#$hasState ROLEPLAYER STATE-TYPE)</code> holds.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSubSituationType SIT-TYPE TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE STATE-TYPE)</code> means that for any instance <code>SUBSIT</code> of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> which is a subsituation of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, if <code>(ROLE SUBSIT ROLEPLAYER)</code> and if <code>ROLEPLAYER</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then immediately sit <code>SIT</code> begins, <code>(#$hasState ROLEPLAYER STATE-TYPE)</code> holds.")
(comment transmembranePotential "(#$transmembranePotential MEMBRANE VOLTS) states that the voltage difference across the #$BiologicalMembrane, MEMBRANE, is the #$Voltage VOLTS.  Membrane potential is determined by subtracting the voltage of the environment that surrounds the membrane (see #$regionSurroundsMembrane) from the voltage of region bounded by the membrane (see #$membraneBoundsCompartment). ")
(comment ElectricalPotentialDifference "A specialization of #$Configuration. Instances are physical situations in which there is a difference in electrical charges between two regions.  ")
(comment ElectrochemicalGradient "A specialization of #$Configuration. Instances are situations in which there is both a difference in the concentration of a type of substance between two regions, and a difference in electrical charge between those two regions.")
(comment gradientConcernsType "<code>(#$gradientConcernsType GRADIENT TYPE)</code> identifies <code>TYPE</code> as the kind of substance or object whose abundance differs between regions in <code>GRADIENT</code>, an instance of #$AbundanceGradient.")
(comment regionOfHighConcentration "<code>(#$regionOfHighConcentration GRAD REGION)</code> states that in the instance of #$ConcentrationGradient, <code>GRAD</code>, the region having the higher concentration of the type in question (see #$gradientConcernsType) is <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment regionOfLowConcentration "<code>(#$regionOfLowConcentration GRAD REGION)</code> states that in the instance of #$ConcentrationGradient, <code>GRAD</code>, the region having the lower concentration of the type in question (see #$gradientConcernsType) is <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment optimalTemperatureForEnzyme "(#$optimalTemperatureForEnzyme MOL TEMP) means that TEMP (usually a range of temperatures) is the optimal temperature for the functioning of the #$EnzymeMolecule MOL.")
(comment optimalpHForEnzyme "(#$optimalpHForEnzyme MOL TEMP) means that TEMP (usually a range of pH values) is the optimal pH for the functioning of the #$EnzymeMolecule MOL.")
(comment RibozymeMolecule "This is the collection of (individual) ribosyme molecules, which are RNA molecules that can catalyze biochemical reactions.")
(comment Metabolism-Human "The collection of instances of #$Metabolism done by humans.")
(comment HumanDNAMolecule "The collection of DNA molecules found in the cells of humans.")
(comment HumanEnzymeMolecule "The collection of enzyme molecules coded for by instances of #$HumanDNAMolecule.")
(comment EnzymeMoleculeTypeBySourceOrganismType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$EnzymeMoleculeTypeBySourceOrganismType is collection of enzyme molecules coded for by the DNA of a particular type of organism.")
(comment ThermophilicBacteriumEnzymeMolecule "The collection of enzyme molecules coded for by instances of #$HumanDNAMolecule.")
(comment enzymeTypeOfOrganismType "(#$enzymeTypeOfOrganismType ORG-TYPE ENZ-TYPE) means ENZ-TYPE is the collection of enzymes coded for by the DNA of organisms that are instances of ORG-TYPE.")
(comment ElectricalPotentialAcrossBiologicalMembrane "A specialization of #$ElectricalPotentialDifference. Instances are physical situations in which there is a difference in electrical charges between two regions separated by a #$BiologicalMembrane.  ")
(comment SelectiveBarrierTransport "The collection of all instances of #$RegulatedTransportSituation wherein the #$transportBoundarySystem in question is a physical surface such that whatever is admitted (#$itemAdmitted) is admitted in virtue of the surface's physical structure, either jointly or individually, and such that whatever is excluded is excluded because some physical feature will not allow it ingress (in the simplest case, the structure lacks pores for admitting what is excluded, but more complex situations are allowed, e.g., the pores might feature sensors which close portals when a certain type of agent is detected, a la Maxwell's demon).  Every #$SelectiveBarrierTransport includes a (#$GroupFn PassingThroughPortal) which is the situational sum of all 'admissions' that occur during the filtration, and a (#$GroupFn BarrierSituation) (which is also a #$BarrierSituation in its own right) which is the situational sum of all the 'interdictions' that occur during the filtration.")
(comment selectiveBarrier "Where TRANSPORT is a #$RegulatedTransportSituation where BOUNDARY serves as the #$transportBoundarySystem, if BOUNDARY is a porous surface whose physical structure is the primary cause of what is transported across the boundary getting transported, and the primary cause of what is interdicted getting interdicted, then TRANSPORT is said to be a #$SelectiveBarrierTransport and BOUNDARY is said to be the #$selectiveBarrier in TRANSPORT.")
(comment O-LinkedGlycosylation "A process that occurs in #$GolgiApparatus and in which a (#$MoleculeFn #$CarbohydrateStuff) is joined to an oxygen atom which is part of an amino acid (#$Serine, #$Threonine, #$Tyrosine, #$Hydroxylysine, #$Hydroxyproline) or lipid (e.g #$Ceramide).")
(comment MembraneGlycolipidMolecule "The collection of #$GlycolipidMolecules which are embedded in #$CellMembranes.")
(comment MembraneMoleculeGlycosylation "The collection of #$Glycosylation events whose outputs are #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules.")
(comment MembraneMoleculeO-LinkedGlycosylation "The intersection of #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules and #$O-LinkedGlycosylation.")
(comment MembraneMoleculeN-LinkedGlycosylation "The collection of #$MembraneGlycoconjugateMolecules and #$N-LinkedGlycosylationn.")
(comment interiorMembraneSurface "<code>(#$interiorMembraneSurface MEM SURF)</code> means that surface <code>SURF</code> is the interior surface of #$BiologicalMembrane <code>MEM</code>.")
(comment AdditionOfMembraneMoleculeToCellMembrane "The collection of events in which a membrane
#$Molecule (usually a #$MembraneProtein or #$Phospholipid) is added to
a #$CellMembrane).")
(comment AdditionOfMembraneProteinToCellMembrane "The collection of events in which a #$MembraneProtein is
added to a #$CellMembrane. A #$properSubEvents of
#$CellMembraneGrowth.")
(comment GolgiApparatusProcess "The collection of processes which portions of CellMembrane-Stuff undergo in the GolgiApparatus.")
(comment MembraneSidedness-Configuration "The collection of #$LipidBilayer-Configuration such that one layer of the #$LipidBilayer is recognizably the inward surface (q.v. #$inwardMembraneSurface-Role) and the other the outward surface (q.v. #$outwardMembraneSurface-Role). In many cases, the #$primaryObjectConfigured will be a #$BiologicalMembrane or some other finite but unbounded bilayer containing a connected space.")
(comment AirPollutionCausedByAutomobiles "A specialization of #$AirPollutionProcess. Instances include events in which automobiles emit harmful gases like #$CarbonDioxide,#$SulfurDioxide and #$CarbonMonoxide into the atmosphere. ")
(comment Prism "A specialization of #$LaboratoryEquipment.  Each instance of #$Prism is a #$Transparent device with flat, polished optical surfaces that refract light. ")
(comment SeparationIntoConstituentParts "A specialization of #$Separation-Complete. Instances include events in which an object is separated into its constituent parts. ")
(comment PhotoelectricTube "A specialization of #$Tube-Tangible and #$LaboratoryEquipment. Instances are extremely sensitive to some wavelengths of light, and are often used in photoelectric experiments.")
(comment EnergyConversion-ElectromagneticToElectric "A specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-ElectromagneticToElectric are events which convert the energy contained in  #$ElectromagneticRadiation to electric energy.  ")
(comment EnergyConversion-LightToElectric "A specialization of #$EnergyConversion-ElectromagneticToElectric. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-LightToElectric are events in which light energy is converted to electric energy.")
(comment EnergyConversionInSpectrophotometer "A specialization of #$EnergyConversion-LightToElectric. Instances of #$EnergyConversionInSpectrophotometer are events in which light energy is converted to electric energy in a #$Spectrophotometer. ")
(comment VisualIBTTransitionTypeByVisualEffect "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType that facets #$VisualIBTTransition into specializations based on the kind of visual effect instantiated.")
(comment VisualIBTTransition "A specialization of #$VisualInformationBearingThing, #$VisualIBTTransition is the collection of visual transitions within a visual IBT.  Transitions are (usually) deliberately authored changes from one visual IBT to another visual IBT, introduced as part of video or film-editing process or in other visual-ibt-production processes, such as slide presentations.")
(comment DissolveTransition "A kind of #$VisualIBTTransition in which the prior IBT appears to dissolve into, and is eventually replaced by, the subsequent IBT.")
(comment FadeTransition "A kind of #$VisualIBTTransition in which one IBT begins to blur or fade into another IBT.  Often one of the IBTs is a blank or uniformly colored \"shot\"; when the prior IBT is, the fade is a \"fade in\" (see #$FadeInTransition), and when the subsequent IBT is, the fade is a \"fade out\" (see #$FadeOutTransition).")
(comment WipeTransition "A kind of #$VisualIBTTransition in which the prior IBT appears to be pushed off or wiped away from the viewing area, to be replaced with another.")
(comment FadeToBlackTransition "An extremely common class of #$FadeOutTransition, in which a visually rich IBT fades away and is replaced by a uniformly black IBT.")
(comment FadeOutTransition "The collection of instances of #$VisualIBTTransition in which a visually rich IBT fades away and is replaced by a visually poorer  IBT.  The first IBT is said to \"fade out.\"")
(comment FadeInTransition "The collection of instances of #$VisualIBTTransition in which a relatively visually poor IBT fades away and is replaced by a visually rich IBT, which is said to \"fade in.\"")
(comment EnzymeMoleculeActivityRegulationEvent "Instances are #$ChemicalInteractions in which, by virtue of being bound to or unbound from some other #$ChemicalObject, an #$EnzymeMolecule has its 'activity' altered.  By 'activity', we mean the #$EnzymeMolecule's ability to act as the #$catalyst in the typical kinds of #$ChemicalReactions it normally participates in (see, e.g., #$enzymeTypeCatalyzesProductionOfType).  Specializations of this collection include the activation of enzymes (see #$EnzymeActivationEvent), their inactivation (see #$EnzymeInactivationEvent) and their inhibition (see #$EnzymaticInhibition).")
(comment GradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane "A specialization of #$Configuration. Instances are physical situations in which there is a difference in conditions on two sides of a #$BiologicalMembrane.  The condition in question could be the concentration of a substance or the electrical potential of the region. ")
(comment gradientAcrossMembrane "<code>(#$gradientAcrossMembrane GRAD MEMBRANE)</code> states that in the instance of #$GradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane, <code>GRAD</code>, the #$BiologicalMembrane serving to divide the two regions is <code>MEMBRANE</code>.")
(comment ElectrochemicalGradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane "A specialization of #$ElectrochemicalGradient. In each instance of #$ElectrochemicalGradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane, there is some #$BiologicalMembrane separating two regions such that the concentration of some type of substance is different in the two regions, and there is a difference in electrical charge in the two regions. ")
(comment ProtonGradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane "A specialization of #$ConcentrationDifferentialAcrossBiologicalMembrane. In each instance, the concentration of #$HydrogenPlusIons differs in the regions separated by a #$BiologicalMembrane.")
(comment ProtonGradientAcrossInnerMitochondrialMembrane "A specialization of #$ProtonGradientAcrossBiologicalMembrane. In each instance, the concentration of #$HydrogenPlusIons is greater in the intermembrane space (see #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion) than in the #$MitochondrialMatrix.  This gradient is established and maintained by events in the electron transport chain, and powers the sythesis of ATP in chemiosmosis (see #$Chemiosmosis-Mitochondrial).")
(comment Chemiosmosis "A specialization of #$ChemicalInteraction.  In  instances of #$Chemiosmosis, the movement of #$HydrogenPlusIons down their concentration gradient across a #$BiologicalMembrane powers the synthesis of ATP (#$AdenosineTriphosphate).")
(comment Chemiosmosis-Mitochondrial "A specialization of #$Chemiosmosis.  In  instances of #$Chemiosmosis-Mitochondrial, the movement of #$HydrogenPlusIons down their concentration gradient from the #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion to the #$MitochondrialMatrix across the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane powers the synthesis of ATP (#$AdenosineTriphosphate).")
(comment MitochondrialMassElectronTransport "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway.  Instances are events consisting of many instances of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-FADH2ToOxygen and many instances of #$MitochondrialElectronTransportChain-NADHToOxygen occuring simultaneously and sequentially in a single #$Mitochondrion. ")
(disjointWith ElectronTransportChain MitochondrialMassElectronTransport)
(disjointWith Chemiosmosis MitochondrialMassElectronTransport)
(disjointWith MitochondrialMassElectronTransport SignalTransduction-CellularProcess)
(comment OxidativePhosphorylation "A type of #$PhosphorylationPathway in which electron transport establishes and maintains a proton gradient across a membrane, allowing ATP to be synthesized in #$Chemiosmosis.  This pathway occurs in the metabolism of all aerobic organisms.")
(comment CompoundTypeByProportionalCompositionFn "<code>(#$CompoundTypeByProportionalCompositionFn ELEMENT-LIST INTEGER-LIST)</code> denotes the instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType whose instances are any various compounds whose atomic composition is such that their molecules contain the atoms of the type designated in <code>ELEMENT-LIST</code>, in proportion given by <code>INTEGER-LIST</code>.")
(comment OxidativePhosphorylation-Mitochondrial "A type of #$OxidativePhosphorylation that occurs in instances of #$Mitochondrion, in which electron transport establishes and maintains a proton gradient across the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane, which powers the synthesis of ATP (#$AdenosineTriphosphate) in #$Chemiosmosis. ")
(comment ATPSynthaseMolecule "A subcollection of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are found embedded in the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane of eukaryotes, and in the #$CellMembrane of prokaryotes.  By providing a path for #$HydrogenPlusIons to move down a concentration gradient, ATP synthase is able to use the energy so released to synthesize ATP (#$AdenosineTriphosphate).")
(comment Poikilotherm "A specialization of #$Animal and an instance of #$OrganismClassificationType.  Each instance of #$Poikilotherm is a \"cold-blooded\" animal whose body temperature varies considerably because it is determined mainly by its surrounding environmental temperature.  Cf. #$Homeotherm.")
(comment Ectotherm "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$Ectotherm is an organism that controls its temperature via external means (e.g. by basking in the sun, or congregating around a hot spring).")
(comment Denaturation "A specialization of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.  Each instance of #$Denaturation is an event in which a protein or a nucleic acid loses its  tertiary and secondary structure.")
(comment ProteinDenaturation "A specialization of #$Denaturation.  Each instance of #$ProteinDenaturation is an event in which a protein loses its tertiary and secondary structure.")
(disjointWith ProteinDenaturation NucleicAcidDenaturation)
(comment DNADenaturation "A specialization of #$NucleicAcidDenaturation.  Each instance of #$DNADenaturation is an event in which DNA separates into single strands.")
(comment NucleicAcidDenaturation "A specialization of #$Denaturation.  Each instance of #$NucleicAcidDenaturation is an event in which a double-strand nucleic acid separates into single strands.")
(comment MethodType "A specialization of #$LearnedActivityType, #$MethodType is the the collection of types of purposeful actions that decompose into a common pattern of sub-event-types and/or role-player types (e.g., instruments) used in the course of the event.  #$MethodType is an instance of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType, which means that ordinarily, an instance of #$MethodType is such by virtue of being a <i>method of</i> doing some class of #$PurposefulAction.  When an instance <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> of #$MethodType requires a high level of skill on the part of the performer, or its sub-event/role-player-type structure is so rigid that minor deviations from that structure would entail a failure to actualize an instance of <code>ACTION-TYPE</code>, then <code>ACTION-TYPE</code> is likely to be an instance of the more specialized #$TechniqueType.")
(disjointWith FacetingCollectionType FacetingBasisCollectionType)
(comment FacetingBasisCollectionType "An instance of #$CollectionType.  Each instance <code>COLL-TYPE</code> of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType is a collection of second order or higher (most of) whose instances <code>COLL</code> are also instances of some instance <code>FACET</code> of #$FacetingCollectionType such that <code>(#$genls FACET COLL-TYPE)</code>.  It is by virtue of this faceting that these <code>COLL</code> collections are instances of <code>COLL-TYPE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$isa #$TechniqueType #$FacetingBasisCollectionType)</code>, because to be an instance of #$TechniqueType (i.e., to be a technique), is to be a collection of events that follow a certain pattern for instantiating some kind of purposeful action, where that pattern requires a certain amount of skill.  More concisely, to be a  technique is to be a technique relative to (a technique <i>for doing</i>) some kind of purposeful action or other. Thus the instances of #$TechniqueType are techniques <i>for</i> sewing, <i>for</i> solving puzzles, <i>for</i> training, etc, and thus, in addition to instantiating #$TehcniqueType, these instances will instantiate a collection that facets sewing, solving puzzles, etc., into distinct techniques.")
(comment facetingBasisCollectionTypeAppliesToType "A specialization of #$typeGenls, <code>(#$facetingBasisCollectionTypeAppliesToType FACETING-BASIS-TYPE COLL)</code> means that <code>FACETING-BASIS-TYPE</code> is an instance of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType whose instances are all (or mostly) instances of #$FacetingCollectionType that facet specializations of <code>COLL</code>.")
(comment AbsorptionSpectrumMeasurement "A specialization of #$MeasuringSomething. Instances include events in which #$AbsorptionSpectrum is measured by using a #$Spectrophotometer. ")
(comment SeparationOfLightIntoItsConstituentColors "A specialization of #$SeparationIntoConstituentParts. Instances include events in which #$Light is separated into its constituent colors.")
(comment LightPropagationThroughLiquid "A specialization of #$Locomotion-LiquidImmersed. Instances include events in which #$Light is passed through a container containing some #$LiquidTangibleThing  ")
(comment LightPropagationThroughChlorophyllSolution "A specialization of #$LightPropagationThroughLiquid. Instances include events in which #$Light is passed through a container containing #$Chlorophyll . ")
(comment ActionSpectrum "A specialization of #$Spectrum.  Each instance of #$ActionSpectrum is a function which maps wavelengths of electromagnetic radiations to the rate of photosynthesis caused by them. ")
(comment actionSpectrumOfStuffFunction "A predicate corresponding to the function #$ActionSpectrumFn.  <code>(#$actionSpectrumOfStuffFunction CHEM-TYPE FUNCTION)</code> states that <code>FUNCTION</code> is a function on wavelengths which gives the rate of chemical reaction when instances of CHEM-TYPE are used to power the reaction.")
(comment ActionSpectrumFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction, used to refer to the #$ActionSpectrum of a type of chemical species or chemical mixture.  (#$AbsorptionSpectrumFn CHEM-TYPE) denotes the instance of #$ActionSpectrum which describes the rate of progress of a chemical reaction caused by  a sample of CHEM-TYPE. ")
(comment Photoprotection "A specialization of #$ProtectionSituation.  Each instance of #$Photoprotection is a situation in which an organism takes some steps to protect itself from excessive light energy.  ")
(comment PhotoprotectionInPlants "A specialization of #$Photoprotection.  Each instance of #$PhotoprotectionInPlants is a situation in which a #$Plant takes some steps to protect itself from  excessive light energy.  ")
(comment Fluorescence "A specialization of #$EmittingAWave. Instances are events in which #$VisibleLight is emitted by a substance that has absorbed light or other electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment Acidification "A specialization of #$IncreaseEvent.  Each instance of #$Acidification is an event in which there is a buildup of #$HydrogenPlusIons (or #$Protons) in a given spatial region.  ")
(comment OceanAcidification "A specialization of #$Acidification.  Each instance of #$OceanAcidification is an event in which there is a buildup of #$HydrogenPlusIons (or #$Protons) in an ocean.")
(comment SoilAcidification "A specialization of #$Acidification.  Each instance of #$OceanAcidification is an event in which there is a buildup of #$HydrogenPlusIons (or #$Protons) in soil. ")
(comment FreshWaterAcidification "A specialization of #$Acidification.  Each instance of #$FreshWaterAcidification is an event in which there is a buildup of #$HydrogenPlusIons (or #$Protons) in a body of water containing fresh water. ")
(comment Cuttlefish "The collection of all cuttlefish (order Sepiida). A type of #$Cephalopod.")
(comment rolePlayerStatesConservedOverSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerStatesConservedOverSituationType SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that if an individual plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, any state true of the individual before the situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType) will be true after the situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType). i.e., the situation leaves the role player unchanged.")
(comment rolePlayerStatesConservedOverSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerStatesConservedOverSubSituationType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that if an individual plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> which is a subsituation of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, any state true of the individual before the subsituation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType) will be true after the subsituation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType). i.e., the subsituation leaves the role player unchanged.")
(comment outwardMembraneSurface-Role "<code>#$outwardMembraneSurface-Role CONF MEM-SIDE)</code> means that in the #$MembraneSidedness-Configuration <code>CONF</code> is the outward side of the bilayer configuration.")
(comment inwardMembraneSurface-Role "<code>#$inwardMembraneSurface-Role CONF MEM-SIDE)</code> means that in the #$MembraneSidedness-Configuration <code>CONF</code> is the inward side of the bilayer configuration.")
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(disjointWith ExistingStuffType AnimalCapabilityType-Restricted)
(comment CiliaryBeating "A specialization of #$LocomotionProcess.  Each instance of #$CiliaryBeating is an event in which a cell moves by beating its cilia.")
(comment Bouldering "A method of #$RockClimbing.  Instances are done by climbing support-free at low altitudes (relative to the nearest safe surface).")
(comment isaFacetingOfVia "<code>(#$isaFacetingOfVia FACET COLL BASIS)</code> means that <code>FACET</code> is an instance of #$FacetingCollectionType that facets (see #$facets-Generic) <code>COLL</code> into sub-collections by virtue of being a specialization of <code>BASIS</code>, an instance of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType.  For example, <p> <code>(#$isaFacetingOfVia #$ScoringPointsByMethod #$ScoringPoints #$MethodType)</code> <p>means that #$ScoringPointsByMethod facets #$ScoringPoints into sub-collections that are instances of #$MethodType.")
(comment FacetingOfViaTypeFn "<code>(#$FacetingOfViaTypeFn COLL BASIS)</code> denotes the instance <code>FACET</code> of #$FacetingCollectionType that facets (see #$facets-Generic) <code>COLL</code> into sub-collections by virtue of being a specialization of <code>BASIS</code>, an instance of #$FacetingBasisCollectionType.  For example, <p> <code>(#$FacetingOfViaTypeFn #$ScoringPoints #$MethodType)</code> <p>denotes the collection that facets #$ScoringPoints into sub-collections that are instances of #$MethodType.")
(comment rolePlayerStatesTransformedOverSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerStatesTransformedOverSituationType
SIT-TYPE ROLE FROMSTATE TOSTATE)</code> means that if an individual
plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and
prior to playing that role has state
<code>FROMSTATE</code> (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType),
after the
situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType) the
role player will have state <code>TOSTATE</code> and will not have
state <code>FROMSTATE</code>.")
(comment rolePlayerStatesTransformedOverSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerStatesTransformedOverSubSituationType
SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE FROMSTATE TOSTATE)</code> means that if an
individual plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of
<code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> that is a subsituation of an instance of
<code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and prior to playing that role has state
<code>FROMSTATE</code> (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType),
after the
situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType) the role
player will have state <code>TOSTATE</code> and will not have state
<code>FROMSTATE</code>.")
(comment C3Plant "A specialization of #$Plant. Instances survive solely on #$C3CarbonFixationInCalvinCycle. ")
(comment HealthImprovementEvent-Plant "A specialization of #$ImprovementEvent.  In an instance of #$HealthImprovementEvent-Plant, some member of #$Plant improves the general state of its health (see #$stateOfHealth and #$BLOTypeByGenericHealthStatus). ")
(disjointWith DevelopingAilment HealthImprovementEvent-Plant)
(comment Adaptation "A Specialization of #$PhysicalEvent. Instances include events in which there is an alteration in the structure or function of an organism or any of its parts by which the organism becomes better fitted to survive and multiply in its environment. ")
(comment PlatformInstanceFromFn "#$PlatformInstanceFromFn takes a specialization of #$ResourcePool-Computational and returns the collection of instantiations of that particular type of resource pool.  The returned value will be a specialization of #$InstantiatingAVMFromThePool.")
(comment platformInstanceTypeFrom "(#$platformInstanceTypeFrom RP-TYPE VM-TYPE) relates a specialization of #$ResourcePool-Computational to the collection of service events that are the maintained instantiations of that particular type of resource pool.")
(comment ResourcePoolCostCategory "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of certain services, components, etc. that share a major feature with respect to how it contributes to the cost of software deployment.")
(comment ComputeServiceSizeType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a coolection of \"compute units\" or virtual machines whose instances share a particular \"size\" -- a particular memory and processor model.")
(comment GridComputingMachineType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of reference machines that have a certain configuration that serves as the index for compute units for a particular memory model for a configured Compute Farm Scope.")
(comment ComputerTypeByCoreAndMemoryFn "An binary function that takes an integer and an amount of RAM and returns the collection of computers -- either virtual or physical, that have that core/memory configuration.")
(comment computerTypeByCoreAndMemory "An ternary predicate that takes an integer and an amount of RAM and relates it to the collection of computers -- either virtual or physical, that have that core/memory configuration.")
(comment ComputerTypeByCoreAndMemoryConfig "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$Computer-Generic whose instances share a particular \"shape\" -- share the same number of processor cores and amount of RAM.")
(comment sharedComputingServiceOfferingTermType "(#$sharedComputingServiceOfferingTermType PRODUCT-TYPE SERVICE-TERMS) means that the service provided by PRODUCT-TYPE is offered via the term type indicated by SERVICE-TERMS.")
(comment costRelevantSubcomponentOrService "A #$BinaryPredicate.  (#$costRelevantSubcomponentOrService THING-1 THING-2) means that THING-2 is a sub-component, or an associated service or component type of THING-1 that directly contributes to the total cost of instances of THING-1.  Note that this relationship is not always a \"part\" or \"subsumption\" relation.  This would hold between a retail organization and a temp service that provides staffing on a regular basis.")
(comment ProductCostCategoryType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of certain services, components, etc. that share a major feature with respect to how it contributes to the cost of a product's deployment, maintenance, etc.")
(comment InfrastructureServiceOrProduct "The collection of products or services which add directly to the infrastructure of some place.")
(comment SoftwareInfrastructureProduct "The collection of products and services which directly add to the infrastructure for software product sales and deployment.")
(comment SubscriptionServicesProduct "The collection of subscription services which directly add to the infrastructure cost for some product type")
(comment DataCenterSubscriptionProductsAndServices "The collection of data center products and services which directly add to the deployment costs of the Compute Farm product.")
(comment BreakFixServices "The collection of data center services related to maintenance and repair of various compute components.")
(comment utilizesComponentOrServiceCategory "(#$utilizesComponentOrServiceCategory PROD-TYPE CAT) means that the service provided by PROD-TYPE utilizes (either in its infrastructure or in the course of product delivery or maintenance) services or components classified as CAT.")
(comment ColocationServices "The collection of data center services related to the colocation space.")
(comment subCostCategory "(#$subCostCategory CAT SUB) means that products or services classified under SUB are also associated with the more general cost category CAT.")
(comment Non-CapitalDataCenterServices "The collection of non-capital data center services.")
(comment DataCenterInstallServices "The collection of data center install services.")
(comment DataCenterCabling-ProductsAndServices "The collection of data center cabling products and services.")
(comment HardwareProductOrService "The collection of products or services relating to hardware.")
(comment DataCenterHardwareProductOrService "The collection of Data Center products or services relating to hardware.")
(comment DataCenter-Cabinet-PowerStripProductsAndServices "The collection of data center services relating to power strips and cabinets.")
(comment ProductsAndServicesMisc-CostCategory "The collection of subscription products and services which are classified as contributing to the misc. cost category.")
(comment costCategoryLevel "Relates a cost category to its generality level.  Used for generating labels for UIs")
(comment DedicatedNetwork-WAN-CostCategory "The collection of subscription services relating to dedicated WAN network products and services.")
(comment DedicatedNetwork-Assets-CostCategory "The collection of subscription services relating to dedicated network product assets.")
(comment OperationalSupportServicesProduct "The collection of products and services contributing to operational support costs")
(comment EngineeringAndOperationalStaffingServices "The collection of engineering and operations staffing services relating operational support.")
(comment TechnicalPlatform-HardwareProductOrService "The collection of hardware products or services relating to technical platform.")
(comment HardwareWriteDown-TechnicalPlatformServices "The collection of technical platform services relating to hardware write-down")
(comment Non-Capital-TechnicalPlatformProductsAndServices "The collection of technical platform services that are non-capital")
(comment Storage-TechnicalPlatformProductsAndServices "The collection of technical platform services that are storage related")
(comment TechnicalPlatform-SubscriptionServices "The collection of subscription services relating to technical platform.")
(comment Servers-TechnicalPlatformServices "The collection of technical platform services relating to hardware servers")
(comment Peripherals-TechnicalPlatformServices "The collection of technical platform services relating to hardware peripherals")
(comment VoiceProducts-CostCategory "The collection of subscription products or services relating to voice services.")
(comment UserPhoneProductsAndServices-Voice-CostCategory "The collection of subscription services relating to Voice - user phone products and services")
(comment HardwareOrSoftwareProductOrService-CostCategory "The collection of hardware or software products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized under some particular enterprise cost category.  This would include installation services, the cost of software licensing, etc.  But would not include products or services whose costs are not directly associated with providing that enterprise service  -- e.g. a tech support service whose costs are built into a licensing fee and not broken out into its own line item for purposes of provisioning or billing.")
(comment TopLevelCostCategory-SharedComputing "The collection of hardware or software products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized under some particular enterprise cost category.  This would include installation services, the cost of software licensing, etc.  But would not include products or services whose costs are not directly associated with providing that enterprise service  -- e.g. a tech support service whose costs are built into a licensing fee and not broken out into its own line item for purposes of provisioning or billing.")
(comment TechnologyInfrastructure-General-CostCategory "The collection of hardware or software products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"technology infrastructure\" costs.")
(comment ApplicationDevelopment-CostCategory "The collection of application products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as application development costs.")
(comment TI-Infrastructure-CostCategory "The collection of Technology Infrastructure products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"infrastructure\" costs.")
(comment ServiceSubscriptions-CostCategory "The collection of Technology Infrastructure products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"operational services\" costs.")
(comment ProductSubscriptions-CostCategory "The collection of Technology Infrastructure products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"core subscription\" costs.")
(comment SoftwareAndDirectTech-CostCategory "The collection of application products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as software and direct tech costs.")
(comment CoreSupport-Software-CostCategory "The collection of application products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"core support\" costs.")
(comment Projects-Software-CostCategory "The collection of application products and services whose costs either in whole or part can be categorized as \"project\" costs.")
(comment NetworkProductOrService-CostCategory "The collection of network products or services relating to TI infrastructure.")
(comment DedicatedNetwork-General-CostCategory "The collection of network products and services relating to TI infrastructure.")
(comment StaffingServices-Infrastructure-CostCategory "The collection of staffing services associated with infrastructure support.")
(comment AppDev-NIL-CostCategory "A placeholder for a subcategory for categories with no current reified subcategories")
(comment StaffingServices-OperationalServices-CostCategory "The collection of staffing services associated with operational services.")
(comment TechnicalPlatform-OperationalServices-CostCategory "The collection of technical platform services associated with operational services.")
(comment Storage-TechnicalPlatform-OperationalServices-CostCategory "The collection of operational services technical platform services that are storage related")
(comment CoreSubscriptions-Level2CostCategory "The collection of core subscription services -- used as a placeholder for a more detailed level 2 category.")
(comment CoreSubscriptions-Level3CostCategory "Placeholder for more specific level 3 core subscription subcategory")
(comment AppDev-NIL-LEV3-CostCategory "A placeholder for a subcategory for categories with no current reified subcategories")
(comment ResidentialMortgage-BackedSecurity "A specialization of #$Morgage-BackedSecurity. Each instance of #$ResidentialMortgage-BackedSecurity is a security backed by commercial mortgages.")
(comment Mortgage-BackedSecurity "A specialization of #$DebtSecurity. Each instance of #$Mortgage-BackedSecurity is a security backed by mortgages.")
(comment CommericalMortgage-BackedSecurity "A specialization of #$Mortgage-BackedSecurity. Each instance of #$CommericalMortgage-BackedSecurity is a security backed by commercial mortgages.")
(comment MarketDataProductRegardingFn "(#$MarketDataProductRegardingFn SECURITY-TYPE) denotes the collection of market data products associated with SECURITY-TYPE.  E.g. (#$MarketDataProductRegardingFn #$Mortgage-BackedSecurity) denotes the collection of market data products that contain information primarily about instances of #$Mortgage-BackedSecurity.")
(comment MarketDataProductVendor "A collection of businesses. Each #$MarketDataProductVendor is a firm  that produces , compiles, or otherwise makes available information artifacts relating to financial products.")
(comment Trepp-Organization "A supplier of market data products and analytics.  A subsidiary of Daily Mail and General Trust Plc.")
(comment MarketDataProduct-PIT "The collection of market data products whose main component is propositional information.  A typical market data product might have many instances of #$MarketData-PIT as its propositional content -- e.g. the content of a Bloomberg data feed.")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various aspects of market data products. ")
(comment Trepp-CMBSAnalytics "The collection of instantiations of Trepp's CMBS Analytics market data product")
(comment vendorOfProductType "(#$vendorOfProductType VENDOR PROD-TYPE) means that VENDOR offers instances of PROD-TYPE for sale in some offical capacity.  VENDOR may be the manufacturer or it may be a third party distributor.  ")
(comment subProductType "(#$subProductType SUB PROD-TYPE) means that SUB is a type of product based on PROD-TYPE but enhanced, restricted, or otherwise altered from PROD-TYPE so as to constitute a unique offering.  ")
(comment Trepp-CMBSAnalytics-FICC "The collection of instantiations of Trepp's CMBS Analytics market data product licensed for use by GS FICC.")
(comment Trepp-CMBSAnalytics-GSAM "The collection of instantiations of Trepp's CMBS Analytics market data product licensed for use by GSAM.")
(comment licensedUserForAgreementType "(#$licensedUserForAgreementType AGREE-TYPE PARTY)</code> means that AGREE-TYPE is a type of #$LegalAgreement such that each in each instance of it, PARTY is a licensed user of the products or services described by the AGREE-TYPE.  ")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-LicensedUser "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various market data products based on their licensed users -- a particular group at an organization, a particular user of a piece of software, etc.")
(comment MarketDataProductTypeForUserFn "(#$MarketDataProductTypeForUserFn PROD-TYPE USER) denotes the collection of market data products that are instance of PRED-TYPE where USER is a licensed user.  For example, (#$MarketDataProductTypeForUserFn #$BloombergProfessionalService-Agreement FredTheTrader) is the collection of instances of the Bloomberg Professional Services agreement in which FredTheTrader is a licensed user.  Typically this is used to specify a type of agreement that, for the most part, is the same for different users, but where different contracts are drawn up for different users.")
(comment DataProduct-PIT "The collection of data products whose main component is propositional information.  A typical data product might have many instances of #$PropositionalInformationThing as its propositional content -- e.g. the content of a Bloomberg data feed, a magazine copy.")
(comment MarketDataProductOrService "The collection of products or services associated with market data.")
(comment Asset-BackedSecurity "A specialization of #$TradeableSecurity.  Each instance of #$Asset-BackedSecurity is a tradable security where the value and income to investors is derived from a specified pool of assets.  These pools of assets often consist of individual assets that cannot themselves be easily sold or traded.")
(comment CollateralizedDebtObligation "A specialization of #$Asset-BackedSecurity.  Each instance of #$CollateralizedDebtObligation is a structured (has \"tranches\") asset-backed security whose collateral are debt obligations like loans and bonds. ")
(comment MarketDataProduct-DataFeed "The collection of FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that involve access to dynamic data feeds of various sorts.")
(comment MarketDataProduct-AuthoredData "The collection of instances #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their clients with authored documents.  Typically subscription based, these agreements provide summaries of other sources of data and provide authored opinion or analysis.  ")
(comment MarketDataProduct-AnalysisTools "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their clients with software tools and data to enable data analysis.  This may include access to databases, specialized algorithms and the software that implements them as well as integration with other tools and services ")
(comment MarketDataProduct-BuyersServices "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their clients with software and data that list acquirement opportunities and help their users identify investment opportunities.")
(comment MarketDataProduct-DatebaseAccess "The collection of FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that involve access to complied databases of financial data.")
(comment MarketDataProduct-ResearchTools "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their clients with software and data that enable data research.  The data and tools provided with these services provide methods to focus on trends of historical data.")
(comment MarketDataProduct-ReferenceVerification "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide verified reference data or other data verification services.")
(comment ComputingService-ServiceType "Each instance of this collection is a collection of service events that constitute a top-level service type for Shared Computing.")
(comment equipmentTypeForProduct "(#$equipmentTypeForProduct PROD DEVICE-TYPE) means that DEVICE-TYPE is a collection of devices or components typically closely associated with the product PROD.  For instance, a document shredding service type would be associated with document shredders.  ")
(comment productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory "(#$productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory INDEP-PROD-TYPE DEP-PROD-TYPE CAT) means that expenses incurred during the provisioning of INDEP-PROD-TYPE involve DEP-PROD-TYPE and are categorized under the cost category CAT.  E.g. Bob's Flower Shop's \"BurstOfColor\" flower product has expenses relating to \"CrystalVase-Product\" which they classify under the\"ContainersAndWrapping\" cost category.  So, when characterizing Bob's expenses you assert 
<pre>
<code>
  (productOrServiceTypeAssignedCategory BurstOfColor CrystalVase-Product ContainersAndWrapping)</code></pre>

Note that this representation assumes either a context exclusive to Bob's use of the BurstOfColor product or that BurstOfColor is itself a vendor/provider specific product type.  The relationship is undefined if neither of those contexts of use obtain.")
(comment VariableExpense "the collection of situations involving expenses (#$ExpenseFigure) classified as \"variable costs\".  A variable cost is a cost that is dependent on the quantity of good or services produced by an organization or by the amount of their activities -- e.g. costs of raw materials for products, costs for hourly employees, etc.")
(comment Variable40-Fixed60-Expense "The collection of situations that involve expenses/costs classified as \"40% Variable / 60% Fixed\".")
(comment SalesTax-CostCategory "The collection of tax expense situations related to misc infrastructure expenses.")
(comment CourierServices-CostCategory "The collection of services relating to courier services.")
(comment Misc-Misc-CostCategory "Miscellaneous product and services expenses.")
(comment EngineeringStaffingServices-CostCategory "The collection of engineering staffing services that contribute to infrastructure costs.")
(comment securityTypeHasFeatureType "Relates a type of security to a collection such that it is typically the case that an instance of that security type has some important relationship to some instance of the collection in arg2.  For example, most securities are assigned a credit rating.  Hence, (#$securityTypeHasFeatureType #$TradeableSecurity #$CreditRating-TradeableSecurity) means that it is typically the case that an instance of #$TradeableSecurity is related in some important way to some instance of #$CreditRating-TradeableSecurity.  This is a general relation as the exact relationship between the two concepts is not explicit.  In essence, this is a financial product specific analogue of #$instanceInvolveType.")
(comment CreditRating-Moodys "The collection of types of credit ratings by Moody's Investors Service (each type of credit rating is a collection of securities given a particular rating).")
(comment CreditRating-SandP "The collection of types of credit ratings by Standard & Poor's (each type of credit rating is a collection of securities given a particular rating).")
(comment CreditRating-TradeableSecurity "The collection of types of credit ratings issued by credit rating agencies (each type of credit rating is a collection of securities given a particular rating) where the thing rated is a tradeable security.")
(comment CreditRating-Fitch "The collection of types of credit ratings by Fitch Ratings (each type of credit rating is a collection of securities given a particular rating).")
(comment StandardStatelessComputeType-Service "The collection of top-level service products that are the deployment of some number of units of \"stateless computing\" either via the \"grid computing\" paradigm or through instantiation of individual virtual machines.  In all cases the resulting computing units are stateless in the sense that there is minimal storage of data on the machines implementing the computing units.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-1Core8GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with 1 core and 8GB memory.")
(comment StandardStatelessComputing-Service "Each instance of this collection is a service event whereby some instance of #$VirtualComputerInstance or some unit of grid computing is deployed and made available to a user.  The \"stateless\" refers to the fact that the user's settings and files are not permanently stored on the physical machines involved in the computing.")
(comment ClassicStatefulComputeType-Service "The collection of top-level service products that are the deployment of some number of units of compute either via the \"grid computing\" paradigm or through instantiation of individual virtual machines.  In all cases the resulting computing units are stateful in the sense that there is storage of user data and configuration on the machines implementing the computing units.")
(comment CreditRatingTypeByRatingAgency "A collection of credit rating types.  Each instance of this collection is the collection of types of credit ratings by a particular rating agency.")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-AssetType "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various market data products based on the focal subject type of the data -- e.g. data about bonds, stocks, etc. ")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-ContentType "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various market data products based on the type of content the data product includes-- e.g. includes Moody's ratings, coupon rate, losses, etc. ")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-LicenseTerms "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various market data products based on broad types of license terms.  See #$SituationTypeByDataUseRights")
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-ProductType "The collection of specializations of #$MarketDataProduct-PIT that characterize various different sorts of market data products based on the type of service they provide -- e.g. data feed, access to analysis software, authored documents, etc.")
(comment FinancialInstrumentTransaction "The collection of buying events in which the objects bought are financial instruments (e.g. stocks, mutual funds, etc.) or other forms of financial transactions such as mortgages.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-1Core2GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM from VMi with 1 core and 2GB memory.")
(comment StandardStatefulComputeType-Service "The GS standard top-level service products that are the deployment of some number of units of compute either via the \"grid computing\" paradigm or through instantiation of individual virtual machines.  In all cases the resulting computing units are stateful in the sense that there is storage of user data and configuration on the machines implementing the computing units.")
(comment StandardStatefulComputing-Service "Each instance of this collection is a service event whereby some instance of #$VirtualComputerInstance or some unit of grid computing is deployed and made available to a user.  The \"stateful\" refers to the fact that the user's settings and files are permanently stored on the physical machines involved in the computing.")
(comment EnvironmentalSocialAndCorporateGovernance-Policy "The collection of organizational policies which deal with concerns relevant to  Environmental, Social and Corporate Governance (ESG) criteria for socially responsible investment.  See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_Social_and_Corporate_Governance.")
(comment expenseVariabilityPercentageForCategory "Relates a product type, a cost category and a number between 0 and 100 to an instance of #$ExpenseVariabilityType which categorizes the percentage of costs associated with that category to some group and cost class attribute -- e.g. (#$expenseVariabilityPercentageForCategory PROD CATEGORY 75 #$ConsumerFixedExpense-CostClass) means that 75% of the costs associated with CATEGORY relative to PROD are classified as \"fixed consumer expenses\".")
(comment OperatingSystem-NetworkComponent "A type of #$OperatingSystem. Each instance of this collection is an operating system program whose program copies are typically associcated with network devices such as routers and switches.  Often these are proprietary operating systems designed by the manufacturer or designer of the device.  These operating systems typically control many aspects of the routing, switching, and other network functions performed by the device.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-2Core16GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-4Core32GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-4Core64GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-6Core48GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-6Core96GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-1Core4GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-1Core8GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-2Core12GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-2Core16GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-2Core24GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-2Core4GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-2Core8GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core16GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core24GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core32GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core48GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core64GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-6Core48GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-6Core96GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-8Core48GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-8Core96GB "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment ClassicStatefulComputing-Service "Each instance of this collection is a service event whereby some amount of computing power is deployed and made available to a user.  The \"stateful\" refers to the fact that storage is made available for the persistence of user files and settings.")
(comment GridComputeFacilitiesKit "The collection of Grid Compute server install kits.")
(comment serviceTypeProvidesType "(#$serviceTypeProvidesType PROD TYPE) means that the service product PROD provides TYPE to its customers to satisfy their orders.  This is a general relation and the exact relation to instances of TYPE is underspecified.  E.g. a virtual machine service provides instances of #$VirtualComputerInstance, while a grid computing service might provide units of computing power that are quantified by reference to machines of TYPE.")
(comment CorporateActivity "A specialization of #$CommercialActivity.  Each instance of this collection is an major or important action performed by some corporation.  Typically these require board or stockholder approval.  Examples include major acquisitions, stock splits, mergers, etc.  Negative examples are things like buying stationery supplies and other such minor events.  ")
(comment MarketDataProduct-WebApplicationBased "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their service via a web-based application.")
(comment agreementTypeInvolvesType "(#$agreementTypeInvolvesType AGREE-TYPE TYPE) means that some instance of TYPE is required for the #$agreeingServiceProvider to provide the agreed upon service.  Often instances of TYPE are provided or made available to the service receiver.  When TYPE is some infrastructure concept or system type required for the provider to provide the service use the more specific #$agreementTypeRequiresSystemType ")
(comment specificProductType "A #$BinaryPredicate.  (#$specificProductType PROD SPEC) means that PROD is a generic version of a product or service and that SPEC is a more specific version of PROD.  There may or may not be a #$genlInverse relationship between PROD and SPEC.")
(comment contractForTypeWithID "A ternary predicate.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$ContractForTypeWithIDFn.  See the comment on that term for details.")
(comment agreementLicensesProductType "(#$agreementLicensesProductType AGREE PROD-TYPE)</code> means that AGREE is a #$LegalAgreement such that some primary use rights for some instance of PROD-TYPE are transferred to the licensee according to the terms of the agreement.  ")
(comment ContractWithVendorWithIDFn "A binary reifiable function.  This function takes a vendor and an ID string and denotes the instance of #$Contract that is the contract with that vendor that has that ID as an identifier.  Note that uses of this function are highly context dependent.  The source of the ID string should be made clear.  E.g. in the context of a particular business's representation of their contracts, it may be an assumption of their application microtheory that the ID is provided by the licensee assigned ID provided by some customer system.  In other contexts it may be provided by the vendor.")
(comment InternalDataUseLicense "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that gives someone or some organization the right to use some set of licensed data internally within their organization (subject to license restrictions -- e.g. only within licensed groups).")
(comment DataUseLicense "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants some use rights with respect to the use of some set of data to someone or some organization.")
(comment ExternalDataDistributionLicense "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some rights to distribute some set of licensed data externally -- outside their organization (subject to certain license restrictions -- e.g. limited amounts, etc.).")
(comment DerivedDataDistributionLicense-ClientReportOnly "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some rights to distribute some set of derived data subject to the constraints that the derived data is distributed as part of the product offerings of the licensee and not resold as a data product.  E.g. the derived data may be included in presentations or summary documents pertaining to the licensee's business offerings, but not repackaged and sold by itself.")
(comment ExternalDataDistributionLicense-Limited "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some limited rights to distribute some set of licensed data externally -- outside their organization.")
(comment PerAccessFee-License "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that specifies a \"per seat\" or \"per access\" charge for use of the licensed data or software.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Site "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that licenses someone or some organization the right to use some set of licensed data, or software at a particular physical site -- subject to any further restrictions imposed by the license.  This differs from an enterprise license in cases where the licensee is a multi-site organization -- e.g. A large university with multiple campuses, a multinational, etc.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Enterprise "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that licenses someone or some organization the right to use some licensed product throughout their enterprise -- subject to any further restrictions imposed by the license.")
(comment DerivedDataDistributionLicense-SomeRights "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some rights to distribute some set of derived data subject to any further license restrictions.")
(comment DerivedDataDistributionLicense-NoDistributionRights "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that specifically denies the licensed user any rights to distribute data derived from the licensed data product.")
(disjointWith DerivedDataDistributionLicense-NoDistributionRights DerivedDataDistributionLicense-SomeRights)
(comment MarketDataProductClassificationType-Delivery "The collection of concepts that are used to classify various market data products based on their schedule of delivery -- e.g. real time, monthly, etc. ")
(comment MarketDataProduct-DesktopSuite "The collection of instances of #$FinancialServicesAgreement-Ongoing that provide their clients with an integrated suite of software tools, feeds, etc. This can be in the form of a suite that is run from a client's desktop or via the use of dedicated equipment (see #$ElectronicTradingPlatform).")
(comment DerivedDataDistributionLicense-InternalDistribution "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some rights to distribute some set of derived data internally within the licensed user's organization -- subject to any further license restrictions.")
(comment DerivedDataDistributionLicense-ExternalDistribution "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some rights to distribute some set of derived data to recipients external to the licensed user's organization  -- subject to any further license restrictions.")
(comment DerivedDataDisallowed-License "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that specifically denies the right to create derived data based on the licensed data in the product.")
(disjointWith DerivedDataDisallowed-License DerivedDataLicense)
(comment ExternalDataDistributionDisallowed-License "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that prohibits the distribution of licensed data to someone outside the organization of the licensed user.")
(disjointWith ExternalDataDistributionLicense ExternalDataDistributionDisallowed-License)
(comment DerivedDataLicense "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that specifies what rights there are to with respect to some set of derived data -- new data based on calculations or analysis of the licensed data, etc.  This is the broadest license type that entails the right to create derived data.  Note the specification of the rights could indicate that there are no derived data distribution rights.")
(comment ExternalDataDistributionLicense-Limited-ClientReports "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some limited rights to distribute some set of licensed data externally -- outside their organization -- provided it is distributed as part of the licensee's normal offerings to clients in reports, etc. and not sold outright as a data product.")
(comment ExternalDataDistributionLicense-Limited-Publications "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that grants someone or some organization some limited rights to distribute some set of licensed data externally -- outside their organization -- provided it is distributed as part of a publication by the licensee where the data serves to provide evidence or support for the assertions made in the publication.")
(comment FinancialOrganizationScheduledHolidayOrClosure "A specialization of #$ScheduledAction.  Each instance of this collection is a scheduled closure of some financial institution or organization -- e.g. a bank or an exchange.")
(comment CorporateEarnings-Dividends "The collection of earnings (#$EarningsFigure) that are related to corporations -- e.g. earnings per share, dividends, profits, etc.")
(comment CorporateRevenueEstimate "The collection of instances of #$Estimate that are estimates or forecasts of the future earnings of some company or financial organization.")
(comment marketDataProductAboutAssetType "(#$marketDataProductAboutAssetType PRODUCT ASSET-TYPE) means that the market data product PRODUCT has instances of ASSET-TYPE as one of its focal topics.  E.g. a data feed product that concentrates on residential mortgage securities would be related via this predicate to #$ResidentialMortgage-BackedSecurity.")
(comment marketDataProductWithContentType "this is the corresponding predicate to #$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn.  It relates a market data product type, PRODUCT-TYPE, to some type of thing, TYPE such that the instances of PRODUCT-TYPE include information about the instances TYPE as attributes of some focal entity type that the product is about.  See the comment on #$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn for more detail.")
(comment marketDataProductHasInformationOfType "(#$marketDataProductHasInformationOfType PRODUCT TYPE) means that the market data product PRODUCT includes information about instances of TYPE where that information is used to characterize some focal entity of PRODUCT.  E.g. (#$marketDataProductHasInformationOfType PRODUCT #$CorporateRevenueEstimate) means that PRODUCT includes data fields that express or report instances of #$CorporateRevenueEstimate as attributes of the focal entities of the product.")
(comment MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn "(#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL) denotes the collection of market data products whose data fields include information pertaining to instances of COLL characterized as attributes of the focal entities of the product (cf. #$marketDataProductAboutAssetType).  More formally, for any COLL, each instance of (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL), PRODUCT, is such that it has some propositional content type, PROP-TYPE associated with it such that 
<pre>
   (#$relationAllExists #$propositionalInfoAbout PROP-TYPE COLL)
</pre>

Furthermore this propositional content characterizes (attributes some properties to) the focal entities -- either directly or indirectly -- of the product.  To put it another way, each instance of (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn COLL) is a data product that includes information about instances of COLL where that information is used to characterize another entity.
<br><br>
For example, (#$MarketDataProductWithContentTypeFn #$FinancialInstrumentTransaction) is the collection of instances of #$MarketDataProduct-PIT whose instances include information about financial instrument transactions -- e.g. stock and bond sales -- as attributes of particular tradeable securities.  An example of an instance of this collection would be a daily summary from an exchange showing volumes of sales for each ticker symbol.  A negative example would be a simple list of dates of sales with no information linking the sales to particular products or deals. ")
(comment DesktopSuite-FinancialSoftware "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are suites of financial programs and subprograms run from an integrated \"desktop\" environment.")
(comment InvestmentOpportunitySoftware "Software that provides potential buyers with information and details about potenial investment opportunities.")
(comment HistoricalData-ReferenceSoftware "A collection of software designed to maintain and present historical data for reference and research purposes.")
(comment FinancialAnalysisSoftware "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are written as utilities to help analyze financial data.  These programs often run models that allow them to simulate financial trends and forecast future behavior.")
(comment FinancialEvaluation "The collection of all financial evaluations. A type of #$FollowingAStandardProcedure and #$Evaluating. #$FinancialRiskEvaluation is a prominent subcollection.")
(comment FinancialRiskEvaluation "The collection of all financial risk evaluations. A type of #$FinancialEvaluation.")
(comment FinancialDataFeed-System "A subcollection of #$DataFeed-System and #$FinancialDataCommunicationSystem.  Each instance of this collection is a data feed considered as an information transfer system.  A financial data feed service implements one of these in order to deliver their service to their clients.")
(comment DataFeed-System "The collection of instances of #$FunctionalSystem designed and configured to dynamically stream information from one place to another -- often continuously. While the access is dynamic, the latency is independent of the method of data transfer.  E.g. a system that transmits information dynamically from a system with a two-hour offset may still be a data feed, but it wouldn't be real-time.  Characteristic properties of a data feed include incremental and (typically) regular updates and the dynamic access aspect -- typically information is pushed directly to the data consumers.")
(comment Analysis-Report "The collection of instances of #$TextualPCW that report on the results of some analysis.")
(comment FinancialAnalysis-Report "The collection of instances of #$Analysis-Report that report on the results of some financial analysis.")
(comment InternalDataUseLicense-Limited "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that gives someone or some organization the right to use some set of licensed data in a limited fashion internally within their organization (subject to license restrictions -- e.g. only within licensed groups).")
(comment AccessingADatabase "The collection of actions that involve accessing, running queries, etc. some database.")
(comment ApptioExportPredicate "A specialization of #$Predicate.  Each instance of this collection is a predicate that captures an Apptio Exportable relation.")
(comment ApptioExportEntity "The collection of entities that will be exported to Apptio along with their relations")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-2Core8GB-Legacy "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-4Core16GB-Legacy "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment DynamicCompute-Product-4Core48GB-Legacy "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment MiscApptioExportEntity "Each instance of this collection is some concept or other that needs to be included in the apptio exports but is not part of some other collection of exported terms")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-8Core96GB-1500GBDisk "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment VMiCompute-Product-4Core16GB-60GBDisk "Each instance of this collection is the deployment and maintenance of a VM with the configuration indicated by its #$computeProductHasSizeConfig value.")
(comment Product-SubOrderable "The collection of products that are pre-configured versions of orderable products.  Typically the value of #$orderableProductHasOption, but it may include any legacy configurations that are not current offerings.")
(comment computeProductHasDiskSize "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates types of #$GSComputeService to the amount of disk space that it can supply to virtual machines.")
(comment virtualMachineInstantiatedViaProduct "A #$BinaryPredicate which relates an instance of #$VirtualComputerInstance to the instance of GSComputeService that instantiated it.")
(comment instantiatedVM "A #$BinaryPredicate which relates instances of #$VirtualComputerInstance to instances of #$ResourcePool-Computational.  (#$instantiatedVM VM POOL) means that VM is a virtual machine instantiated from POOL and is currently up and running.  Note:  This relates a virtual machine to the physical machine it is running on.  For the relationship between a virtual machine and the service product that is responsible for its instantiation see #$virtualMachineInstantiatedViaProduct.")
(comment computeProductHasMemorySize "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates types of #$GSComputeService to the amount of memory that it can supply to virtual machines.")
(comment computeProductHasNumberOfLogicalProcessors "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates types of #$GSComputeService to the amount of logical processors that it can supply to virtual machines.")
(comment ResourcePool-Unit "A specialization of both #$InformationBearingThing and #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject.  Each instance of this collection is a complex entity consisting of computer servers, operating systems, storage disks, and other physical assets organized into a computing resource that can be assigned as a functional component of a computing resource pool.")
(comment ResourcePool-Product "A specialization of both #$InformationBearingThing and #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject.  Each instance of this collection is a complex entity consisting of one or more #$ResourcePool-Units and associated products, services, etc, that serve as the provisionable infrastructure for compute products -- grid computing, virtual machine services, etc.")
(comment BladeServerCabinet-Wrightline-44RU "The collection of Wrightline computer server cabinets with 44 rack units")
(comment DataUseLicense-Department "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product of some sort to a particular department of an organization.")
(comment DataUseLicense-BusinessUnit "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product to a particular business unit of an organization.")
(comment licenseTypeMoreRestrictiveInScopeThan "(#$licenseTypeMoreRestrictiveInScopeThan LICENSE-TYPE1 LICENSE-TYPE2) means that the class of licensed users given by the terms of the instances of LICENSE-TYPE2 is more restricted than that of LICENSE-TYPE1.  This does not entail that any given instance of LICENSE-TYPE2 has less licensed users than some (or indeed any) instance of LICENSE-TYPE1.  Rather, this indicates a dispositional relation to the effect that for a given organization, they will have fewer licensed users if they were to license under LICENSE-TYPE2 vs. LICENSE-TYPE1 -- e.g. were they to purchase a department wide license vs a enterprise wide license.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Division "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product to a particular division of an organization.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Campus "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product to a particular campus of an organization.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Building-Location "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product to a specific building, address or location of an organization.")
(comment DataUseLicense-Region "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that, subject to the conditions of the license, licenses a data product to a specific region for a multi-region organization.")
(comment contractVendor-Licensor "(#$contractVendor-Licensor CONTRACT VENDOR) means that VENDOR is the licensor of the product licensed via CONTRACT.  This may be different from both the carrier/distributor and billing vendor.  ")
(comment contractVendor-Carrier "(#$contractVendor-Carrier CONTRACT PRODUCT CARRIER) means that CARRIER is the carrier or distributor of the product type, PRODUCT licensed via CONTRACT.  This may be different from both the licensor and billing vendor.  ")
(comment contractVendor-Billing "(#$contractVendor-Billing CONTRACT PRODUCT BILLER) means that CONTRACT stipulates that with respect to the fee schedule established for the licensed use of PRODUCT, payment is to be made to BILLER.  ")
(comment TieredFee-License "A collection of instances of #$License-LegalAgreement.  Each instance of this collection is a license that establishes different fees depending on various tiers of service or access -- typically the number of licensed users in a particular scope.")
(comment contractLicensee "(#$contractLicensee CONTRACT LICENSEE) means that LICENSEE is the receiver of the goods or services provided for in CONTRACT.  Note this does not mean that the whole of LICENSEE (if an organization or group) has the rights to utilize the product or service -- the license terms may restrict usage to some subgroup of LICENSEE.")
(comment agreementEndDate "A specialization of #$objectEndingDate.  (#$agreementEndDate AGREE DATE) means that AGREE ends on DATE.  Often the actual end of the agreement will be the ending point of DATE, but this is not necessarily so.")
(comment agreementStartDate "A specialization of #$objectStartingDate.  (#$agreementStartDate AGREE DATE) means that AGREE starts on DATE.  Often the actual start of the agreement will be the starting point of DATE, but this is not necessarily so.")
(comment licensedByContractForProductType "(#$licensedByContractForProductType CONTRACT PRODUCT PARTY) means that a licensed user for PRODUCT as specified by CONTRACT is PARTY.  Note that PARTY may be an organization or group or an individual.  if a group, then each #$groupMembers is also licensed provided any other conditions in the contract related to licensed users is also satisfied.  For example, a license may specify that a particular group in an organization is the pool of licensed users, but specify certain fees for each member that uses the product.")
(comment FunctionAppliesToArgsPredicate "A subcollection #$Predicate.  Each instance <code>PRED</code> is of the form <code>(PRED FUNCTION . ARGS)</code> where <code>FUNCTION</code> is an instance of #$ReifiableFunction, #$Function-Denotational, and #$PartialFunction, and the argument list <code>. ARGS</code> is of the right length and constitutes objects of the right type and inter-arg constraints for <code>FUNCTION</code> such that <code>(FUNCTION . ARGS)</code> is a well-formed expression that potentially denotes an object of the return-type for <code>FUNCTION</code>.  Because <code>FUNCTION</code> is a partial function, there is no guarantee that it is defined for all objects in its range; <code>(PRED FUNCTION . ARGS)</code> means that <code>FUNCTION</code> does indeed return a value for this sequence of arguments.")
(comment functionAppliesToArgs-Binary "An instance of #$FunctionAppliesToArgsPredicate, <code>(#$functionAppliesToArgs-Binary FUNCTION ARG-1 ARG-2)</code> means that the instance <code>FUNCTION</code> of #$PartialFunction and #$Function-Denotational is defined for the arguments <code>ARG-1</code> and <code>ARG-2</code> and does indeed return a value (i.e., denotes a unique object of the type defined by its #$resultIsa) for this sequence of arguments.")
(comment functionAppliesToArg "An instance of #$FunctionAppliesToArgsPredicate, <code>(#$functionAppliesToArg FUNCTION ARG)</code> means that the instance <code>FUNCTION</code> of #$PartialFunction and #$Function-Denotational is defined for the argument <code>ARG</code> and so does indeed return a value (i.e., <code>(FUNCTION ARG)</code> denotes a unique object of the type defined by its #$resultIsa).")
(comment functionAppliesToArgs-Ternary "An instance of #$FunctionAppliesToArgsPredicate, <code>(#$functionAppliesToArgs-Ternary FUNCTION ARG-1 ARG-2 ARG-3)</code> means that the instance <code>FUNCTION</code> of #$PartialFunction and #$Function-Denotational is defined for the sequence of arguments <code>ARG-1</code>, <code>ARG-2</code> and <code>ARG-3</code> and does indeed return a value (i.e., <code>(FUNCTION ARG-1 ARG-2 ARG-3)</code> denotes a unique object of the type defined by its #$resultIsa).")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeStatesConservedOverSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeStatesConservedUnderSituationType SIT-TYPE ROLE TYPE)</code> means that if an instance of <code>TYPE</code> plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, any state true of the instance before the situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType) will be true after the situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType). i.e., the situation leaves the role player unchanged.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeStatesConservedOverSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerStatesInvariantOverSituationType SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE TYPE)</code> means that if an instance of <code>TYPE</code> plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> which is a subsituation of an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, any state true of the instance before the subsituation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSubSituationType) will be true after the subsituation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSubSituationType). i.e., the subsituation leaves the role player unchanged.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeStatesTransformedOverSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeStatesTransformedOverSituationType
SIT-TYPE ROLE TYPE FROMSTATE TOSTATE)</code> means that if an instance
of <code>TYPE</code> plays <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of
<code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and prior to playing that role has state
<code>FROMSTATE</code> (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType),
after the
situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType) the role
player will have state <code>TOSTATE</code> and will not have state
<code>FROMSTATE</code>.")
(comment rolePlayerOfTypeStatesTransformedOverSubSituationType "<code>(#$rolePlayerOfTypeStatesTransformedOverSubSituationType
SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE ROLE TYPE FROMSTATE TOSTATE)</code> means that if
an instance of <code>TYPE</code> plays <code>ROLE</code> in an
instance of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE</code> that is a subsituation of an
instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, and prior to playing that role has
state
<code>FROMSTATE</code> (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateBeforeSituationType),
after the
situation (q.v. #$rolePlayerOfTypeHasStateAfterSituationType) the role
player will have state <code>TOSTATE</code> and will not have state
<code>FROMSTATE</code>.")
(comment membraneSurfacePart-Role "<code>(#$membraneSurfacePart-Role CONF MOL)</code> means
that molecule <code>MOL</code> playes the role of surface part of a
membrane in a #$MembraneSidedness-Configuration situation.")
(comment InteriorMembraneSurfacePart "A state which denotes the collection of molecules which are
a surface part of an #$InteriorMembraneSurface.")
(comment ExteriorMembraneSurfacePart "A state which denotes the collection of molecules which are
a surface part of an #$ExteriorMembraneSurface.")
(comment CesareanSection-SurgicalProcedure "The collection of surgical procedures which are the specific procedure employed to remove the child from the womb during an instance of #$CesareanBirth")
(comment similarInValueOnFunctionalSlot "This predicate relates two things in terms of some BinaryPredicate that relates them to similar instances of a given collection of collections. (#$similarInValueOnRelation T1 T2 BINPRED) means that there are similar collections COL1 and COL2, such that (BINPRED T1 COL1) and (BINPRED T2 COL2).  The minimum notion of similarity is that COL1 and COL2 be instances of the same \"faceting\" sort of collection.  For instance, #$HighMountainousRegion and #$HillyRegion are both instances of the collection #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  Furthermore, if the collection type to which they belong is ordered (see #$CollectionWithAnEventLikeOrder), then COL1 and COL2 should be \"close\" together in the ordering.  For instance #$HillyRegion is closer to #$HighMountainousRegion than #$FlatRegion in the ordering on #$RegionTypeByHilliness.  So, it is likely that a region, REG1, such that (#$terrainType REG1 #$HighMountainousRegion) stands in #$similarInValueOnRelation via #$terrainType to a region, REG2, such that (#$terrainType REG2 #$HillyRegion).  But not likely that it stands in such a relation to an instance of #$FlatRegion.  See also #$resemblesInValue.")
(comment typesSimilarInValueOnRelation "This predicate relates two collections in terms of some #$BinaryPredicate that relates them to similar instances of a given collection. (#$typesSimilarInValueOnRelation T1 T2 BINPRED) means that for all instances <code>INS1</code> of <code>T1</code> and <code>INS2</code> of <code>T2</code>, if <code>(BINPRED INS1 VAL1)</code> and <code>(BINPRED INS2 VAL2)</code>, then <code>(#$similarTo VAL1 VAL2)</code>.")
(comment TransBarrierGradient "#$TransBarrierGradient is the collection of all #$TransBoundaryGradients where the boundary in question that the gradient is 'across' (#$gradientAcrossBoundary) is a physical structure that physically constrains the likelihood with which at least some of the instances of the population of interest may cross from one side to the other.")
(comment regulatedTransportMaintainsGradient "(#$regulatedTransportMaintainsGradient TRANSPORT GRADIENT) means that the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT acts to maintain the #$TransBoundaryGradient  GRADIENT.")
(comment gradientAcrossBoundary "(#$gradientAcrossMembrane GRAD BOUNDARY) states that in the #$TransBoundaryGradient GRAD, the boundary between the region of high concentration (#$regionOfHighConcentration) and the region of low concentration (#$regionOfLowConcentration) is BOUNDARY.")
(comment transportedUpAGradientIn "(#$transportedUpAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that there is a #$TransBoundaryGradient with a #$regionOfHighConcentration HIGH-CON and a #$regionOfLowConcentration LOW-CON such that there is a #$MovementEvent that is a #$properSubEvents of TRANSPORT where ITEM is the #$primaryObjectMoving and where the #$fromLocation is LOW-CON and the #$toLocation is HIGH-CON. Intuitively, (#$transportedUpAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that at some point in TRANSPORT, ITEM moves from the low-concentration region to the high-concentration region of a #$TransBoundaryGradient that temporally intersects TRANSPORT.")
(comment transportedDownAGradientIn "(#$transportedDownAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that there is a #$TransBoundaryGradient with a #$regionOfHighConcentration HIGH-CON and a #$regionOfLowConcentration LOW-CON such that there is a #$MovementEvent that is a #$properSubEvents of TRANSPORT where ITEM is the #$primaryObjectMoving and where the #$fromLocation is HIGH-CON and the #$toLocation is LOW-CON. Intuitively, (#$transportedUpAGradientIn TRANSPORT ITEM) means that at some point in TRANSPORT, ITEM moves from the high-concentration region to the low-concentration region of a #$TransBoundaryGradient that temporally intersects TRANSPORT.")
(comment transportedUpTheGradient "(#$transportedUpTheGradient TRANSPORT ITEM GRADIENT) means that ITEM moves from the #$regionOfLowConcentration of the #$TransBoundaryGradient GRADIENT to the #$regionOfHighConcentration of GRADIENT during the course of (as a #$subEvents of) the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT.")
(comment transportedDownTheGradient "(#$transportedDownTheGradient TRANSPORT ITEM GRADIENT) means that ITEM moves from the #$regionOfHighConcentration of the #$TransBoundaryGradient GRADIENT to the #$regionOfLowConcentration of GRADIENT during the course of (as a #$subEvents of) the #$RegulatedTransportSituation TRANSPORT.")
(comment gradientAcrossBarrier "(#$gradientAcrossBarrier GRADIENT-SIT BARRIER) means that in the #$TransBarrierGradient configuration GRADIENT-SIT, BARRIER acts to physically regulate the flow between the segregated regions of GRADIENT-SIT in a way that maintains GRADIENT-SIT.")
(comment distinctButSimilar "<code>(#$distinctButSimilar OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that <code>(#$similarTo OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>, but falling short of <code>(#$equals OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>.  This is an extremely general relation, but nevertheless useful in that it can indicate the need for future KE work to flesh out the similarity.")
(comment similarTo "<code>(#$similarTo OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that the things <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> are similar along some dimension(s) of comparision; where the similarity is context-independent -- i.e., along any possible dimension -- <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> are identical (i.e.,  <code>(#$equals OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>.")
(comment relativeAbundanceOfType "<code>(#$relativeAbundanceOfType TYPE REGION PERCENT)</code> means that   the number of organisms of <code> TYPE </code> as a percentage of the total number of organisms in <code> REGION </code> is <code> PERCENT </code>. ")
(comment TranspirationInPlants "A specialization of #$Transpiring-ExudingSomething. In each #$TranspirationInPlants , plants lose water vapor from leaves, stems, flowers and roots. ")
(comment MetabolicAdaptation "A Specialization of #$Adaptation. Instances include events in which there is an alteration in the metabolic pathway of an organism  by which the organism becomes better fitted to survive and multiply in its environment. ")
(comment AdditionOfRuBPToOxygenInPhotorespiration " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve addition of RuBP to Oxygen in #$Photorespiration.")
(comment ConversionOfPhosphoglycolateToGlycerateInPhotorespiration " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve conversion of #$Phosphoglycolate to glycerate during #$Photorespiration. ")
(comment Glycerate "A specialization of #$OrganicCompound. Instances are salts or esters of #$GlycericAcid.  ")
(comment typeChangesInAdaptationType "(#$typeChangesInAdaptationType ADAPTATION-TYPE  TYPE) means that instances of ADAPTATION-TYPE tend to bring about changes in instances of TYPE. Some examples include physiological transformations and changes in pathways of chemical reactions. ")
(comment AdditionOfN-LinkedMembraneGlycoproteinToCellMembrane "The collection of events in which a #$MembraneGlycoprotein is added
to a #$CellMembrane, where #$N-LinkedGlycosylation occurs. A
#$properSubEvents of #$CellMembraneGrowth.")
(comment GradientSituation "A specialization of #$Configuration. Instances include situations in which the value of a #$QuantitySlot changes across a given two or three dimensional region. ")
(comment regionOfHighSlotValue "<code>(#$regionOfHighSlotValue GRAD REGION)</code> states that in the instance of #$GradientSituation, <code>GRAD</code>, the region having the higher slot value of relevant #$QuantitySlot is <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment regionOfLowSlotValue "<code>(#$regionOfLowSlotValue GRAD REGION)</code> states that in the instance of #$GradientSituation, <code>GRAD</code>, the region having the lower slot value of relevant #$QuantitySlot is <code>REGION</code>.")
(comment TemperatureGradient "A specialization of #$GradientSituation. Instances include situations in which there is a temperature difference between two points or regions. ")
(disjointWith AbundanceGradient TemperatureGradient)
(comment HydrolysisTypeByChemicalHydrolysized "A specialization of #$SpecifiedChemicalInteractionType that facets #$Hydrolysis-ChemicalReaction into sub-collections based on which instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType is hydrolysized (that is the chemical, other than #$Water, that is a #$chemicalReactants-TypeType for each sub-collection).")
(comment quantityChangesInGradientType "<code>(#$quantityChangesInGradientType GRADIENT-TYPE SLOT)</code> means that in gradients of type <code>GRADIENT-TYPE</code>, the value on <code>SLOT</code>, an instance of #$QuantitySlot, changes across a two or three-dimensional region.")
(comment BundleSheathCellLayer "A specialization of #$Layer and #$PlantPart.  Each instance of #$BundleSheathCellLayer is a layer of #$BundleSheathCell found in the #$Leaf.")
(comment PhotosynthesisInC4Plants "A specialization of #$Photosynthesis-Plant. Instances are events which occur in #$C4Plant.")
(comment sqlAppendedToTableAtImport "This predicate is used to state an arbitrary constraint that should be appended to the SELECT statement used when the RDB reflector imports a data from a table. That is, if the sentence <code>(#$sqlAppendedToTableAtImport TABLE SQL)</code> is asserted in the mapping microtheory for the database table <code>TABLE</code> then when the RDB Reflector imports the data from <code>TABLE</code>, it should append the string <code>SQL</code>, separated by a single space, to the end of the SELECT statement that is generated to fetch the table data. Cyc need not do anything to ensure that the resulting SELECT statement is well-formed. If the result of appending <code>SQL</code> leads to a malformed SELECT statement, or otherwise leads to an error when fetching the data, Cyc should exit with an error message.")
(comment sentenceJustifications-ProofViewSummary "<code>(#$sentenceJustifications-ProofViewSummary SENTENCE JUSTIFICATIONS)</code> means that one justification of <code>SENTENCE</code> as provided by the Proof View summary code is the list of sentences <code>JUSTIFICATIONS</code>.")
(comment MovementOfHydrogenPlusIonFromIntermembraneSpaceToMitochondrialMatrix "A type of #$PassiveTransport-Membrane.  In each instance, a #$HydrogenPlusIon moves down a #$ConcentrationGradient (the #$ProtonGradientAcrossInnerMitochondrialMembrane) from the #$IntermembraneSpace-Mitochondrion to the #$MitochondrialMatrix.  The portals that allow this motion are formed by #$ATPSynthaseMolecules embedded in the #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane.")
(comment MembraneTransportOfHydrogenPlusIon "A specialization of #$TranslationOfIon.  Each instance of #$MembraneTransportOfHydrogenPlusIon is an event in which a H+ ion is moved across a biological membrane.")
(comment TransBoundaryGradient "#$TransBoundaryGradient is the collection of all #$GradientSituations where the uniform concentration or distribution of individuals of a given type is higher on one side of an identifiable boundary than on the other.")
(comment ATPSynthaseHPlusChannel "The collection of all channels formed by #$ATPSynthaseMolecules, taken as #$DirectedPath-Generics through the protein, and consequently the membrane in which the protein is embedded (usually an #$InnerMitochondrialMembrane or a thylakoid membrane in a #$Chloroplast).")
(comment AllergicReactionTypeToTypeFn "(#$AllergicReactionTypeToTypeFn TANGIBLE-TYPE) denotes the class of #$AllergicReactions that occur when sensitive individuals are exposed to instances of TANGIBLE-TYPE.")
(comment typeCanCauseAllergicReactionType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$AllergicReactionTypeToTypeFn.  <code>(#$typeCanCauseAllergicReactionType TANGIBLE-TYPE REACTION-TYPE)</code> states that <code>REACTION-TYPE</code> is the collection of #$AllergicReactions that may occur upon exposure of sensitive persons to <code>TANGIBLE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Allergy-Condition "A collection of long-lasting physiological states. An instance of #$Allergy-Condition is an event, usually lasting for several years or an entire lifetime, in which an organism is sensitive to a type of substance such that, when exposed to the substance, there is a high likelihood of an #$AllergicReaction occuring.  ")
(comment AllergyToTypeFn "<code>(#$AllergyToTypeFn TANGIBLE-TYPE)</code> denotes a specialization of #$Allergy-Condition in instances of which some organism is experiencing the ongoing state of being allergic to <code>TANGIBLE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typeIsAllergenInAllergyConditionType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$AllergyToTypeFn.  <code>(#$typeIsAllergenInAllergyConditionType TANGIBLE-TYPE ALLERGY-TYPE)</code> states that <code>ALLERGY-TYPE</code> is the collection of #$Allergy-Conditions that are allergies to <code>TANGIBLE-TYPE</code>.  Instances of <code>ALLERGY-TYPE</code> are not acute reactions (for that, see #$AllergicReaction).  Rather, they are ongoing states of being hypersensitive to instances of <code>TANGIBLE-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CameraMotionType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, instances of which are common types of ways of moving or focusing a camera.")
(comment FilmingWhileFn "<code>(#$FilmingWhileFn GUIDANCE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$FilmingAVisualImage done while the camera used is undergoing an instance of <code>GUIDANCE</code>, an instance of #$CameraMotionType.<p>For example, <code>(#$FilmingWhileFn #$TiltingACamera)</code> is the collection of filming events done while the camera is tilting.")
(disjointWith Pitch-Upward Pitch-Downward)
(comment CameraMotionFeatureTypeFn "<code>(#$CameraMotionFeatureTypeFn FILM-TYPE)</code> dentoes the collection of instances of #$VisualInformationBearingThing that are the direct result (see #$ibtGenerated) of an instance of <code>FILM-TYPE</code>, an type of #$FilmingAVisualImage that is an instance of #$CameraVisualIBTGenerationCapabilityType.  <p>For example, <code>(#$CameraMotionFeatureTypeFn (#$FilmingWhileFn #$ZoomingInWithCamera))</code> denotes the collection of visual IBTs that are generated by zooming in a camera on a subject and filming while doing so.")
(comment CameraVisualIBTGenerationCapabilityType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$FilmingAVisualImage into subcollections based on what common type of camera manipulation (see #$CameraMotionType) is used.")
(comment typeCarryingCapacityForPortalType "(#$typeCarryingCapacityForPortalType TRANSDUCED-TYPE PORTAL-TYPE NUMBER TIME-PERIOD) means that the largest number of individuals of TRANSDUCED-TYPE that a #$Portal of type PORTAL-TYPE can admit during a period of TIME-PERIOD is NUMBER.")
(comment PanningACamera "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a #$Camera is  moved linearly sideways or along a vertical axis (#$Yaw-Orientational).")
(comment PanningACameraLeft "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a   #$Camera is  moved linearly sideways  or along a vertical axis (#$Yaw-Orientational) generally towards the left of its current position.")
(comment PanningACameraRight "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a   #$Camera is  moved linearly sideways or  along a vertical axis (#$Yaw-Orientational) generally towards the right of its current position.")
(comment TiltingACamera "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a #$Camera is  moved along a horizontal axis  (#$Pitch-Orientational).")
(comment TiltingACameraUpward "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a #$Camera is moved along a horizontal  axis (#$Pitch-Orientational) generally upwards.")
(comment TiltingACameraDownward "It is a type of #$MovementEvent, where a  #$Camera is moved along a horizontal  axis (#$Pitch-Orientational) generally  downwards.")
(comment ZoomingACameraInOrOut "The union of #$ZoomingInWithCamera  and   #$ZoomingOutWithCamera events.")
(comment ZoomingOutWithCamera "The camera operation, which generates a   #$ZoomingOutOnSomething visual effect. (This is currently not really represented   by the KE.)")
(comment ZoomingInWithCamera "The camera operation, which generates a    #$ZoomingInOnSomething visual effect. (This is currently not really represented    by the KE.)")
(comment Pitch-Upward "Turning along a horizontal axis, where the direction  of rotation is generally upwards compared to the current orientation.")
(comment Pitch-Downward "Turning along a horizontal axis, where the  direction  of rotation is generally downwards compared to the current  orientation.")
(comment changesToValue "<code>(#$changesToValue TEMPORAL-THING OBJECT BIN-PRED VALUE)</code> means that over the course of the temporal extent of <code>TEMPORAL-THING</code>, an instance of #$TemporalThing, the value of <code>BIN-PRED</code> applies to <code>OBJECT</code> changes from one value to <code>VALUE</code>.")
(comment changesFromValue "<code>(#$changesFromValue TEMPORAL-THING OBJECT BIN-PRED VALUE)</code> means that over the course of the temporal extent of <code>TEMPORAL-THING</code>, an instance of #$TemporalThing, the value of <code>BIN-PRED</code> applies to <code>OBJECT</code> changes from <code>VALUE</code> to a different value.")
(comment effectOfSituationOnObject "<code>(#$effectOfSituationOnObject OBJ SIT SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that by virtue of being involved in the situation <code>SIT</code>, the object <code>OBJ</code> is caused to <code>OBJ</code> would play the role <code>ROLE</code> in an instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment TransdermalAdministration-Patch "An instance of #$LearnedActivityType and a specialization of #$TransdermalAdministration. Instances of #$TransdermalAdministration-Patch are events in which some portion of a drug substance is made to contact the skin via a #$TransdermalPatch, and is absorbed through the skin into the bloodstream.")
(comment TransmucosalAdministration "Administering a substance, usually a drug, by allowing it to diffuse into the body across a mucous membrane such as the tissues inside the mouth.")
(comment PharmacyProductTypeByRateOfRelease "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$PharmacyProductTypeByRateOfRelease are collections of drug products characterized by how quickly their instances release their drug substance to the body.")
(comment ImmediateReleaseDrugDeliveryProduct "A collection of #$PartiallyTangible objects, each containing one or more doses of a #$DrugSubstance, intended to be used in instances of #$AdministeringADrug, which have the property that the drug is released into the body quite quickly. Examples include #$InjectableLiquid-Medical and #$InhaledDosageForm.  ")
(comment ExtendedReleaseDrugDeliveryProduct "A collection of #$PartiallyTangible objects, each containing one or more doses of a #$DrugSubstance, intended to be used in instances of #$AdministeringADrug, which have the property that the drug is released into the body slowly, over an extended period of time.  Examples include drugs packaged as a #$TransdermalPatch and tablets that are designed to dissolve slowly (#$TabletTimeRelease).")
(disjointWith ExtendedReleaseDrugDeliveryProduct ImmediateReleaseDrugDeliveryProduct)
(comment QSTwoVariableTernaryQueryFn "<code>(#$QSTwoVariableTernaryQueryFn PRED THING N)</code> identifies the question-suggestion query whose query sentence's operator is the ternary predicate <code>PRED</code> and whose non-variabilized argument position is <code>N</code>, filled by <code>THING</code>.")
(comment qsTwoVariableTernaryQuery "The predicate that corresponds to #$QSTwoVariableTernaryQueryFn, <code>(#$qsTwoVariableTernaryQuery PRED THING N QUERY)</code> identifies <code>QUERY</code> as the question-suggestion query whose query sentence's operator is the ternary predicate <code>PRED</code> and whose non-variabilized argument position is <code>N</code>, filled by <code>THING</code>.")
(comment plausibleQueryPredicateFixedArgPositionForTwoVariableQuery "<code>(#$plausibleQueryPredicateFixedArgPositionForTwoVariableQuery TERNARY-PRED N)</code> means that the ternary predicate <code>TERNARY-PRED</code> is used to suggest two-variable queries where the <code>N</code>th argument bound.")
(comment ProteinFunctionalPartType "A #$SecondOrderCollection whose instances are collections of
parts of proteins which have an important role in the function of the
protein. Positive examples include #$HydrophilicChemicalObjects,
#$HydrophobicChemicalObjects, protein domains, etc. Negative examples
include individual atoms which are parts of proteins, except in cases
where a particular atom serves, e.g., as a binding cite. In most
cases, instances will denote collections of functional groups or
larger molecular components.")
(comment roleTypesAbsent "<code>(#$roleTypesAbsent SIT TYPE)</code> means that the instance of #$Situation <code>SIT</code> is unusual with respect to other instances of some collection of which it is an instance, in that it is lacking an instance of <code>TYPE</code> as a role player, either in <code>SIT</code> itself or in one of its sub-situations.")
(comment sandwichBread "<code>(#$sandwichBread SANDWHICH BREAD)</code> identifies <code>BREAD</code> as the complete bread surrounding sandwich.")
(comment ProtonPump "Instances of #$ProtonPump are #$TransmembraneProteins  in a biological membrane (see #$BiologicalMembrane) that actively move #$Protons across the membrane from the side with a low concentration to the side with a high concentration. In reality, the protons are not free on the high-concentration side, but immediately associate with some other molecule.  E.g., they may associate with molecules of water to form #$HydroniumIons.<p> #$ProtonPumps occur in the membranes of each #$Mitochondrion, where they concentrate protons in the intermembrane space.  They also act to eject protons from #$Osteoclasts in order to acidify a region where bone is to be resorbed.")
(comment ProteinChannel "The collection of all channels formed by #$TransmembraneProteins, taken as #$DirectedPath-Generics through the protein, and consequently the membrane in which the protein is embedded. All #$ChannelProteins have #$ProteinChannels, but other, more complex proteins may have them as well (e.g., #$ATPSynthaseMolecule)")
(comment PassiveTransportProtein "Each instance of #$PassiveTransportProtein is a #$ProteinMoleculeOrProteinComplex that naturally occurs as part of the membranes of living cells and transports ions or molecules - usually a specific type, depending on the type of transporter - down a concentration gradient across the biological membrane of which the protein is a part. ")
(comment RadarStation-Facility "A specialization of #$Building.  Each instance of #$RadarStation-Facility is a structure equipped with a radar system and whose primary purpose is to support the functioning of that #$RadarDevice.")
(comment HighlyPollutedRegion "A specialization of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural. Instances include regions where the concentration of harmful gases like #$CarbonDioxide and #$SulfurDioxide is above a threshold. (See #$hasPollutionIntensity).")
(comment concentrationOfPollutantInAreaType "<code>(#$concentrationOfPollutantInAreaType POLLUTANT AREA-TYPE CON)</code> states that the concentration of <code>POLLUTANT</code> within areas of type  <code>AREA-TYPE</code> is <code>CON</code>.")
(comment HighTrafficRegion "A specialization of #$InanimateObject-NonNatural. Instances include regions where traffic volume is consistently, extremely large, either during rush hours or perpetually.")
(comment AtmosphereAroundTypeFn "(#$AtmosphereAroundTypeFn TYPE) takes a spec of #$GeographicalRegion <code> TYPE </code> and returns the collection of #$atmosphereChunk that could be said to be around instances of <code> TYPE </code>. ")
(comment atmosphereAroundType "A predicate corresponding to the function #$AtmosphereAroundTypeFn. ")
(comment SecondLawOfThermodynamics "An instance of #$LawOfThermodynamics (q.v.).  According to the second law of thermodynamics, heat cannot spontaneously move from a cooler system to a warmer system.")
(comment PhysicalSystem "A specialization of #$System.  Each instance of #$PhysicalSystem is a part of the physical universe that has been selected for analysis in terms of physics.")
(comment ThermodynamicSystem "A specialization of #$PhysicalSystem.  Each instance of #$ThermodynamicSystem is a part of the physical universe that has been selected for analysis in terms of the laws of thermodynamics.")
(comment ThermodynamicSystem-Open "A specialization of #$ThermodynamicSystem.  Each instance of #$ThermodynamicSystem-Open is a thermodynamic system that can transfer energy and matter with its surroundings.")
(disjointWith ThermodynamicSystem-Open ThermodynamicSystem-Isolated)
(comment environmentOfPhysicalSystem "(#$environmentOfPhysicalSystem SYSTEM ENV) means that, relative to the #$PhysicalSystem SYSTEM, ENV is the rest of the physical universe.")
(comment Condensation "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$Condensation, a gas is cooled to (or its pressure lowered to) the point where the relative humidity (or similar partial pressure measure if something other than water is condensing) is greater than 100%, changing part of a component of the gas from the #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter to the #$Liquid-StateOfMatter.")
(comment EnergyTransferEvent "A specialization of #$Translocation.  Each instance of #$EnergyTransferEvent is an event in which energy is transferred from at least one instance of #$PartiallyTangible to at least one other instance of #$PartiallyTangible.  Important specializations of #$EnergyTransferEvent include #$Freezing and #$Condensation.")
(comment MembraneTransportProtein "Each instance of #$MembraneTransportProtein is a #$TransmembraneProtein that naturally occurs as part of the membranes living cells and is involved in controlling the movement of #$Ions or #$Molecules across the membrane of which it is part.")
(comment ThermodynamicSystem-Isolated "A specialization of #$ThermodynamicSystem.  Each instance of #$ThermodynamicSystem-Isolated is a thermodynamic system that is unable to transfer matter or energy with its surroundings.")
(comment Oxidation-ChemicalReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Each instance of#$Oxidation-ChemicalReaction is a reaction in which an instance of #$ChemicalObject either loses one or more electrons, oxygen atoms are added to the instance, or hydrogen atoms are removed from the instance.  #$Oxidation-ChemicalReaction and #$Reduction-ChemicalReaction occur together. For the combined event, see #$RedoxReaction.")
(comment EnergyConversion-PotentialToKinetic "A specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-PotentialToKinetic convert the potential energy of a system or object into kinetic energy.")
(comment EnergyConversion-KineticToPotential "A specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-KineticToPotential convert the kinetic energy of a system or object into potential energy.")
(comment DecarboxylationOfAlphaKetoglutarateInKrebsCycle " A specialization of #$DecarboxylationReaction. Instances involve conversion of #$AlphaKetoglutarateAnion to #$CarbonDioxide and an intermediate.  This is one step of a three-step reaction (see #$SuccinylCoAProductionInKrebsCycle). ")
(comment DecarboxylatedIntermediateInSuccinylCoAProduction "The collection of chemical objects with the formula C4H4O3 which are the result of the first, decarboxylation step of the transformation of #$AlphaKetoglutarateAnion into #$SuccinylCoenzymeA.  ")
(comment RedoxStepInSuccinylCoAProduction " A specialization of #$SimpleRedoxReaction. Instances involve oxidation of the #$DecarboxylatedIntermediateInSuccinylCoAProduction and reduction of NAD to NADH.  This is the second step of a three-step reaction (see #$SuccinylCoAProductionInKrebsCycle).")
(comment AttachmentOfCoAInSuccinylCoAProduction " A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. Instances involve attachment of a #$CoenzymeAMolecule to an oxidized intermediate.  This is the third and final step of a three-step reaction (see #$SuccinylCoAProductionInKrebsCycle.")
(comment OxidizedIntermediateInSuccinylCoAProduction "The collection of chemical objects with the formula C4H4O3 which are the result of the second, oxidation step of the transformation of #$AlphaKetoglutarateAnion into #$SuccinylCoenzymeA.  ")
(comment nthObjectOfTypeDerivedFromDescriptionContext "<code>(#$nthObjectOfTypeDerivedFromDescriptionContext OBJ N TYPE CONTEXT)</code> means that the instance <code>OBJ</code> of <code>TYPE</code> is the <code>N</code>th such instance that Cyc has identified and reified from its reasoning about the contents of <code>CONTEXT</code>.")
(comment Diphenhydramine "The collection of all diphenhydramine.")
(comment TheEvolutionOfLifeOnEarth "The instance of #$Evolution that subsumes all other instances of #$Evolution that take/took/will take place on #$PlanetEarth.")
(comment TheEvolutionOfFn "<code>(#$TheEvolutionOfFn LIFE-TYPE)</code> identifies the instance of #$Evolution in which <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> undergoes evolutionary changes.")
(comment evolvesIn "The predicate that corresponds to #$TheEvolutionOfFn, <code>(#$evolvesIn LIFE-TYPE EVOLUTION)</code> identifies the <code>EVOLUTION</code> as the instance of #$Evolution in which <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> undergoes evolutionary changes.")
(comment TheEmergenceOfLifeTypeFn "<code>(#$TheEmergenceOfLifeTypeFn LIFE-TYPE)</code> identifies the event in which biological living objects of type  <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> first appear.")
(comment lifeTypeEmerges "The predicate that corresponds to #$TheEmergenceOfLifeTypeFn, <code>(#$lifeTypeEmerges LIFE-TYPE EMERGENCE)</code> identifies <code>EMERGENCE</code> as the event in which biological living objects of type <code>LIFE-TYPE</code> first appear.")
(comment SouthSudanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SouthSudan, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment emergenceOfFirstTypeOfType "A predicate used to describe events in the evolution of some class of #$BiologicalLivingObject, <code>(#$emergenceOfFirstTypeOfType EMERGENCE GENL NEW-GENL)</code> means that in the instance <code>EMERGENCE</code> of #$Adaptation-BLOTypeLevel, the first instances of <code>GENL</code> that are also of type <code>NEW-GENL</code> appear.")
(comment Adaptation-BLOTypeLevel "The collection of instances of #$Adaptation in which the adapting \"actors\" are best characterized as types of living organisms and structures, rather than individual living things.")
(comment AnatomicalAdaptation "A specialization of #$Adaptation-BLOTypeLevel.  Instances are events in which members of a class of organism begin to develop #$anatomicalParts that their ancestors did not have, where these parts enable those organisms to survive and reproduce in their current environment.")
(comment interlockingSurfaceLayers "<code>(#$interlockingSurfaceLayers OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means
that <code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> are structurally
complementary in the sense that their surface
layers (e.g. #$EntireSurfaceLayerFn) could be brought into
more-or-less complete contact over a significant portion of both
surfaces.")
(comment interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes "<code>(#$interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes TYPE1 TYPE2)</code>
means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> is structurally
complementary to an instance of <code>TYPE2</code>, in the sense of
#$interlockingSurfaceLayers.")
(comment interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes-Universal "<code>(#$interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes-Universal TYPE1
TYPE2)</code> means that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> is
structurally complementary to every instance of <code>TYPE2</code>, in
the sense of #$interlockingSurfaceLayers, and vice versa. This
requires that all instances of <code>TYPE1</code> have a similar shape
to one another, and likewise for <code>TYPE2</code>, and that these
common shapes are complements of one another in a sense similar to
#$interlockingSurfaceLayers.")
(comment Interlocking-Configuration "A specialization of Touching-Configuration. Instances are
ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation-Statics in which significant areas
of external parts of two objects are in complete contact. It is
required that #$interlockingObjects holds between the two
configuredObjects (i.e., #$interlockingSurfaceLayers holds either
between the objects themselves or between #$externalParts of the
objects, or between an external part of one object and the other
object.")
(comment interlockingObjects "<code>(#$interlockingObjects OBJ1 OBJ2)</code> means that
<code>OBJ1</code> and <code>OBJ2</code> either are or have parts which
are structurally complementary in the sense of
#$interlockingSurfaceLayers. Unlike #$interlockingSurfaceLayers,
#$interlockingObjects does not entail that significant surface areas
of both objects are interlocking.")
(comment interlockingObjectTypes "<code>(#$interlockingObjectTypes TYPE1 TYPE2)</code> means
that every instance of <code>TYPE1</code> is or has a part that is
structurally complementary to an instance of or a part of an instance
of <code>TYPE2</code>, in the sense of #$interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes.")
(comment interlockingObjectTypes-Universal "<code>(#$interlockingObjectTypes-Universal TYPE1
TYPE2)</code> means that #$interlockingSurfaceLayerTypes-Universal
holds either between <code>TYPE1</code> and <code>TYPE2</code>,
between #$externalPartTypes of each, or between one of these and an
#$externalPartTypes of the other.")
(comment TopLevelMetabolicPathwayType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection that facets #$MetabolicPathway into two top-level specializations, based on the general \"directionality\" of those pathways: #$AnabolicPathway, which is constructive and #$CatabolicPathway, which is degradative.")
(comment Trajectory-BallisticMissileFlightPhase "A specialization of #$Trajectory whose instances involve the trajectory followed by some #$BallisticMissile during the #$BallisticFlightPhase-Missile of a #$BallisticMissileLaunch-Complete.")
(comment BallisticTrajectory "The collection of all instances of #$Trajectory that are the paths of thrown or launched projectiles moving exclusively under the influence of gravity.")
(disjointWith GP120Protein (CollectionDifferenceFn ChemicalObject GP120Protein))
(comment chemicalEquation-Simplified "A quintary predicate used to describe a mathematically simplified form of the balanced chemical equation for a given type of #$ChemicalReaction. In a gaf of the form (#$chemicalEquation-Simplified R-TYPE LIST1 LIST2 LIST3  LIST4), LIST1 and LIST3 are lists of chemical substances, and LIST2 and LIST4 are list of numbers each of which is the balancing coefficient of the corresponding element in, respectively, LIST1 and LIST3. Thus, (#$chemicalEquation-Balanced R-TYPE (#$TheList COMPOUND-1 COMPOUND-2) (#$TheList 2 3) (#$TheList PRODUCT-1 PRODUCT-2) (#$TheList 1 4)) means that in the type of chemical reaction denoted by R-TYPE 2 units of COMPOUND-1 and 3 units of COMPOUND-2 result in 1 unit of PRODUCT-1 and 4 units of PRODUCT-2. Just as in the case of #$chemicalEquation-Balanced, one should not assume that the equilibrium of REACTION-TYPE lies entirely to the right of the equation.")
(comment chemicalEquation-SimplifiedUnbalanced "(#$chemicalEquation-SimplifiedUnbalanced REACTION-TYPE REACTANT-LIST PRODUCT-LIST) means that in #$ChemicalReactions of type REACTION-TYPE instances of the substances included in REACTANT-LIST react to form instances of the substances included in PRODUCT-LIST, where the elements of REACTANT-LIST and PRODUCT-LIST are derived from a mathematically simplified version of the balanced equation. As such, the REACTANT-LIST and PRODUCT-LIST may lack some chemicals found in the true, balanced equation, having replaced them with more general classes of chemical that share a common proportion of atomic decomposition..")
(comment ChangeInRelativeAbundanceOfOrganism "A collection of events in which the relative abundance of an organism  changes due to external conditions or #$Adaptation. ")
(comment PositiveChangeInRelativeAbundanceOfOrganism "A collection of events in which there is a positive change in the relative abundance of an organism in a given region  due to external conditions or #$Adaptation. ")
(comment NegativeChangeInRelativeAbundanceOfOrganism "A collection of events in which there is a negative change in the relative abundance of an organism in a given region  due to external conditions or #$Adaptation. ")
(comment relativeAbundanceOfTypeIncreasesInEventType "(#$relativeAbundanceOfTypeIncreasesInEventType <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>  <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code>) means that the relative abundance of <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code> increases in events of type <code> EVENT-TYPE </code>. ")
(comment relativeAbundanceOfTypeDecreasesInEventType "(#$relativeAbundanceOfTypeDecreasesInEventType <code>EVENT-TYPE</code>  <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code>) means that the relative abundance of <code>ORGANISM-TYPE</code> decreases in events of type <code> EVENT-TYPE </code>. ")
(comment PositiveChangeInRelativeAbundanceOfC4Plants "A collection of events in which there is a positive change in the relative abundance of #$C4Plant in a given region  due to external conditions or #$Adaptation. ")
(comment PositiveChangeInRelativeAbundanceOfC3Plants "A collection of events in which there is a positive change in the relative abundance of #$C3Plant in a given region  due to external conditions or #$Adaptation. ")
(comment IncreaseInTemperature "A specialization of #$IncreaseEvent. Instances include events in which the #$temperatureOfObject of an individual increases.")
(comment EnergyConversion-ChemicalToKinetic "A specialization of #$EnergyConversion-PotentialToKinetic. Instances of #$EnergyConversion-ChemicalToKinetic convert the potential #$ChemicalEnergy of a system or object into #$KineticEnergy.")
(comment ComplexityQuantity "A specialization of #$MeasurableQuantity.  A measure of how complex something is.")
(comment hasComplexity "(#$hasPhysicalQuantity OBJ COMPLEXITY) means that OBJ has the complexity COMPLEXITY.")
(comment FossilFuelCombustion "The sub-collection of #$CombustionProcess in which instances of #$FossilFuel are consumed.")
(comment WaterTypeInBodyOfWaterTypeFn "(#$WaterTypeInBodyOfWaterTypeFn BODY-TYPE) denotes the collection of waters that are in bodies of type BODY-TYPE.  For example, (#$WaterTypeInBodyOfWaterTypeFn #$HotSpring) denotes the collection of waters in hot springs.")
(comment waterTypeInBodyOfWaterType "(#$waterTypeInBodyOfWaterType BODY-TYPE WATER-TYPE) means WATER-TYPE is the collection of waters that are in bodies of type BODY-TYPE.")
(comment EnzymeTypeOfOrganismTypeFn "<code>(#$EnzymeTypeOfOrganismTypeFn ORG-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of enzymes coded for by the DNA of organisms that are instances of <code>ORG-TYPE</code>.")
(comment Injecting-Epidural "Injecting a fluid, usually containing a drug, into the epidural space (the outermost portion of the spinal cavity, just outside the #$DuraMater and surrounded by the #$Vertebrae.")
(comment headOfGovernmentOf "The #$HeadOfGovernment of a country, not to be confused with the #$HeadOfState if a country has both.")
(comment DuraMater "The collection of all dura maters.  An instance of #$DuraMater is the outermost and toughest of the three #$Meninges surrounding the #$Brain and the #$SpinalCord.  The #$DuraMater is #$sheetSurfaceConnected to the #$Skull and contains the #$SuperiorSagittalSinus.  Significant parts of the #$DuraMater include the #$FalxCerebri, which separates the two #$CerebralHemispheres, the #$TentoriumCerebelli, which separates the #$Cerebellum from the #$Cerebrum, and the #$FalxCerebelli, which partially separates the two hemispheres of the #$Cerebellum.")
(comment CureTaskDefiningActivity "The collection of human activities that are considered Cure task defining activities.")
(comment defaultWellformednessCheckingMtForTask "<code>(#$defaultWellformednessCheckingMt TASK MT)</code> means that in the CAE/CURE task, MT should be used for default wff-checking.")
(comment defaultQueryMtForTask "<code>(#$defaultQueryMtForTask TASK MT)</code> means that in the CAE/CURE task, MT should be used for querying information pertaining to the domain.")
(comment EcologicalConcernType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, instances of which are types of #$PhysicalEvent that, whether currently instantiated or not, are considered by scientists to be potential problems for the environment.")
(comment generateSentenceForInstancesTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a concept to a #$CycLSentence.  (#$eventTypeSubEventTypeSentence CONCEPT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is a \"generateFoo\" sentence relevant to concept used to generate sentences for the CAE or Cure. ")
(comment definitionalTaskDefiningTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a concept to a #$CycLSentence.  (#$definitionalTaskDefiningTypeSentence CONCEPT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is a definitional sentence relevant to defining the task that is the focal entity of the session. ")
(comment generateFormulasWithTermForInstancesForTask "(#$generateFormulasWithTermForInstancesForTask COLLECTION TERM TASK) means that any time an instance of COLLECTION is seen, TERM will be used to  create formulas in the context of TASK.")
(comment generateSentenceForSpecsTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a concept to a #$CycLSentence.  (#$eventTypeSubEventTypeSentence CONCEPT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is a \"generateFoo\" sentence relevant to concept used to generate sentences for the CAE or Cure. ")
(comment generateFormulasWithTermForSpecsForTask "(#$generateFormulasWithTermForSpecsForTask COLLECTION TERM TASK) means that any time a specialization of COLLECTION is seen, TERM will be used to  create formulas in the context of TASK.")
(comment visuallyDominantObjects "<code>(#$visuallyDominantObjects IBT OBJ)</code> means that the visual inforamtion bearing thing <code>IBT</code> is dominated by <code>OBJ</code>; i.e., the visual \"real estate\" of <code>IBT</code> is filled to a large degree by the portion that represents <code>OBJ</code>.")
(comment Garage "The most general collection of garages, instances of #$VehicleStorageConstruct designed for the storage of automobiles.")
(comment videoWorkDirector "A binary predicate that relates a given #$VideoConceptualWork to the agent(s) who directed it.  <code>(#$videoWorkDirector WORK DIRECTOR)</code> means that <code>DIRECTOR</code> directed <code>WORK</code>.  For example, <code>(#$videoWorkDirector #$CitizenKane-TheMovie #$OrsonWelles)</code> holds.  When the work is an instance of #$Movie-CW, use the more specific #$movieDirector.")
(comment videoWorkActors "A binary predicate that relates a given #$VideoConceptualWork to the agent(s) who played a role in it.  <code>(#$videoWorkActors WORK ACTOR)</code> means that <code>ACTED</code> acted in <code>WORK</code>.  When the work is an instance of #$Movie-CW, use the more specific #$movieActors.")
(comment BacterialCellMembrane "The collection of #$CellMembranes which are barts of #$Bacteriums.")
(comment formatingSentenceTypeSentence "A binary #$TermSummaryPredicate and specialization of #$interestingSentence that relates a concept to a #$CycLSentence.  (#$formatingSentenceTypeSentence CONCEPT SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is a formatting sentence relevant to defining the task that is the focal entity of the session. ")
(comment specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArgForTask "<code>(#$specPredsRelevantToTermSummaryPredWRTInstancesInArgForTask PRED TERM-SUMMARY-PRED TYPE N TASK)</code> means that if a thing <code>THING</code> is an instance of <code>TYPE</code>, then any assertions in which a specialization of <code>PRED</code> occurs in arg 0 and <code>THING</code> occurs as arg <code>N</code> should appear in the fact sheet for <code>THING</code> under the category associated with <code>TERM-SUMMARY-PRED</code> when the user is engaged in TASK.")
(comment MissileDefenseAgency "The #$MissileDefenseAgency's mission is to develop, test, and field an integrated and layered ballistic missile defense system to defend the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and its deployed forces and allies against all ranges of enemy ballistic missiles in all phases of flight.")
(comment AIMSMARTTerm "The collection of all #$CycLTerms deemed highly salient for the #$AIMSMARTProject.")
(comment AIMSMARTPhaseOneTerm "The collection of all #$CycLTerms created in part to support the #$AIMSMARTProject in Phase One of the STTR.")
(comment AIMSMARTConstant "The collection of all #$CycLConstants deemed highly salient for the #$AIMSMARTProject.")
(comment AIMSMARTPhaseOneConstant "The collection of all #$CycLConstants created in part to support the #$AIMSMARTProject in Phase One of the STTR.")
(comment relationExistsManyInstance "A ternary #$RuleMacroPredicate that can    be used to state that a given binary predicate stands in a certain relationship    with respect to a given collection and a given thing.     (#$relationExistsManyInstance BINPRED COL THING) means that there are many    instances INST(i) of COL such that (BINPRED INST(i) THING) holds.  It is    equivalent to (#$relationExistsRangeInstance BINPRED COL THING #$Many-Quant), and    thus to the more complex form (for which it can in effect be used as shorthand):   <p>(#$thereExistRange #$Many-Quant ?INST(#$and(#$isa ?INST COL2(BINPRED ?INST    THING))) .<p>For example, `(#$relationExistsManyInstance #$genls #$Collection    #$HittingAnObject)' means that there are many collections which generalize to    #$HittingAnObject.  See also #$relationExistsRangeInstance.")
(comment HighTemperatureSituation "A specialization of #$Situation. Instances include situations in which the #$temperatureOfObject in the #$situationLocation of the event is higher than a known threshold. ")
(comment adaptationTypeInOrganismTypeForSituationType "(#$adaptationTypeInOrganismTypeForSituationType ORGANISM-TYPE ADAPTATION-TYPE SITUATION-TYPE) means that organisms of type <code> ORGANISM-TYPE </code> are #$bodilyDoers of <code> ADAPTATION-TYPE </code> to better adapt to conditions arising from situations of type <code> SITUATION-TYPE </code> . ")
(comment NonSalicylateAnalgesic "A #$TherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which are not #$OpioidDrugs, and which are not salicylates (so this group excludes aspirin, aka #$AcetylsalicylicAcid).")
(comment ConservationOfFn "<code>(#$ConservationOfFn TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instance of #$Conservation in which instances of <code>TYPE</code> are conserved (see #$resourceTypeConserved).")
(comment resourceTypeConserved "<code>(#$resourceTypeConserved CONSERVATION RESOURCE-TYPE)</code> means instance of <code>RESOURCE-TYPE</code> are conserved (protected or sustained) in <code>CONSERVTION</code>, an instance of #$Conservation.")
(comment CalvinCycle-Extended "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In this reaction, the reactants of #$CalvinCycle are converted to #$Glyceraldehyde3Phosphate, which is then transformed to #$Glucose. ")
(comment Seabed "An #$Seabed is any of the areas of ocean or sea floor.")
(comment pharmaceuticalLabelText "(#$pharmaceuticalLabelText PHARM-TYPE TEXT) means that the label text for PHARM-TYPE is TEXT.")
(comment actionProtectsFromAttackOfType "(#$actionProtectsFromAttackOfType ACT ATTACK) means that the action ACT prevents events of type ATTACK from happening. Note this predicate takes an individual #$Event as its first argument and a subcollection of #$Event as its second.")
(comment ModelingAndSimulationSystem "The collection of all #$AgentAndInstrumentSystems whose #$focalActivityType is #$ModelBasedSimulation.")
(comment ModelSpecification "The collection of all #$AspatialInformationStores that can be considered specifications of 'models', that is, theories such that conformity with them is a salient issue.")
(comment modelSpecificationExecuted "(#$modelSpecificationExecuted EXECUTION SPEC) means that the #$ModelSpecification SPEC is executed by EXECUTION, according to some rational interpretation of EXECUTION and its #$executingSystem.")
(comment executingSystem "(#$executingSystem EXECUTION SYSTEM) means that there is a rational interpretation according to which the #$FunctionalSystem SYSTEM can be said to execute the #$ModelExecution EXECUTION in accord with some #$ModelSpecification (the #$modelSpecificationExecuted.")
(comment executesModelBasedSimulation "(#$executesModelBasedSimulation SIM SYSTEM) means that the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM is executed by the #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem SYSTEM.")
(comment evaluatesSimulationResults "(#$evaluatesSimulationResults SIM SYSTEM) means that SYSTEM is a #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem tasked with evaluating the data output by the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM.")
(comment simulationEmulatesSituationOfType "(#$simulationEmulatesSituationOfType SIM SIT-TYPE) means that the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM shares certain features with instances of SIT-TYPE which are salient from the standpoint of making SIM 'count' as a simulation of a typical or prototypical instance of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment simulationIsa "(#$simulationIsa SIM SIT-TYPE) means that the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM is an instance of SIT-TYPE in virtue of the #$modelSpecificationExecuted and that the purpose of the #$executingSystem in SIM is to realize such an instance of SIT-TYPE under 'controlled conditions'.")
(disjointWith NonSalicylateAnalgesic Opioid)
(disjointWith AcetylsalicylicAcid NonSalicylateAnalgesic)
(comment NarcoticDrug "The collection of all narcotics. Many #$NarcoticDrugs are also #$Analgesics.")
(comment FDBSpecificTherapeuticClassType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections of #$DrugSubstances characterized by their therapeutic intent or action. ")
(comment NarcoticAnalgesic "An #$FDBSpecificTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which typically are or contain as an ingredient some #$OpioidDrug.")
(comment FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType "A collection of collections.  Instances are collections of drug substances consisting of mixtures of compounds, each of which may belong to a different therapeutic class.  For example, a portion of drug substance that contains both #$Acetaminophen and #$CodeinePhosphate would be an instance of the #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType, #$AnalgesicWithNarcoticAndNonSalicylate.")
(comment AnalgesicWithNarcoticAndNonSalicylate "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) of some #$NarcoticAnalgesic and some #$NonSalicylateAnalgesic.")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive "An #$FDBSpecificTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with antitussive (cough-suppressing) properties, which typically are or some #$OpioidDrug.")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-DecongestantCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive and a #$Decongestant. The resulting drug has properties of both. ")
(comment Antihistamine-FirstGeneration "Instances are portions of #$Antihistamine which relieve symptoms of allergy (see #$AllergicReaction) by non-selectively blocking action of #$Histamine by preventing it from attaching to histamine H1 receptors.")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-1stGenerationAntihistamineCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive and an #$Antihistamine-FirstGeneration. The resulting drug has properties of both. ")
(disjointWith Antihistamine NarcoticAnalgesic)
(comment NarcoticAnalgesicAnaestheticAdjuntAgent "An #$FDBSpecificTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances which are #$NarcoticAnalgesic used as an adjunct to #$Anesthesia.")
(disjointWith OpioidReceptorAntagonist OpioidDrug)
(comment OpiateWithdrawalTherapyAgent "Instances of #$OpiateWithdrawalTherapyAgent are #$DrugSubstances given to help a patient overcome addiction to #$OpioidDrugs.  Some formulations are single-ingredient, containing an opioid that prevents withdrawal symptoms and has a lower abuse potential and dependence liability than abused opioids.  Other formulations are multi-ingredient, and contain an #$OpioidReceptorAntagonist in addition.")
(comment OpioidReceptorAntagonist "Instances of #$OpioidReceptorAntagonist bind to opioid receptors more strongly than opioid agonists (e.g., #$OpioidDrugs), but do not activate them. These substances can be used to block the action of #$Endorphins and #$OpioidDrugs.")
(comment BeliefSystemCultureFn "A function from an instance of #$BeliefSystem to an instance of #$Culture-Practice, <code>(#$BeliefSystemCultureFn BELIEF-SYSTEM)</code> denotes the extended event of practices and customs associated with an influenced by the instance <code>BELIEF-SYSTEM</code> of #$BeliefSystem.")
(comment beliefSystemAssociatedCulture "The predicate that corresponds to #$BeliefSystemCultureFn, <code>(#$beliefSystemAssociatedCulture BELIEF-SYSTEM CULTURE)</code> identifies <code>CULTURE</code> as the instance of #$Culture-Practice whose constituent customs and practices are influenced by <code>BELIEF-SYSTEM</code>, an instance of #$BeliefSystem.  See also #$cultureBeliefs, which relates an instance of #$Culture-Practice a specific beliefs; in general, the #$cultureParticipants of a given culture <code>C</code> need not accept each and every #$cultureBeliefs of a belief system <code>S</code> where <code>(#$beliefSystemAssociatedCulture S C)</code> holds, nor must every proponent of <code>S</code> be a #$cultureParticipants of <code>C</code>, but there will in general be high overlap.\")")
(comment PreparingDrinkFn "<code>(#$PreparingDrinkFn DRINK-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of events in which instances of <code>DRINK-TYPE</code> are prepared.  For example, (#$PreparingDrinkFn #$Margarita-Cocktail) denotes the collection of events in which instances of #$Margarita-Cocktail are prepared.")
(comment PreparingDrink "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink.  Each  instance of #$PreparingDrink is an event in which a single #$Drink is prepared to  make it ready to drink.  For example, instances of (#$PreparingDrinkFn  #$CocktailDrink) or pouring Sunny-D into a glass")
(comment HumanCultureWithRegionalBasis "This is the collection of #$HumanCultures that are defined by customs and practices that originate from a particular geographical region.  This includes both cultures defined by a region (and whose participants live in that region -- see #$RegionalCulture), as well as \"national\" cultures (c.f. #$NationalCulture) that may be dispersed across multiple regions, including countries outside the source nation.")
(comment CultureWithRegionalOriginFn "(#$CultureWithRegionalOriginFn REGION) is the #$HumanCultureWithRegionalBasis whose regional basis, or origin, is <code>REGION</code>.  This is a partial function because not all regions have a specific culture.")
(comment cultureOfRegionalOrigin "The predicate that corresponds to #$CultureWithRegionalOriginFn, <code>(#$cultureOfRegionalOrigin CULTURE REGION)</code> identifies <code>CULTURE</code> as the most expansive instance of #$Culture-Practice that has <code>REGION</code> as its regional basis, or origin.")
(comment ExtremelyFormalEvent "The collection of instances of #$SociabilityBasedAction that are exceedingly formal in nature.  Instances include state weddings, state funerals, Presidential inaugurations etc..")
(comment PlayEquipment "The collection of all  equipment designed for play including #$PlaygroundEquipment  and #$Toy")
(comment HumanOccupationConstructObject "A specialization of both #$Artifact and #$HumanScaleObject.  Each instance of #$HumanOccupationConstructObject is an artifact that is of a type typically found in some indoor place where humans live, work or play -- i.e. in some instance of #$HumanOccupationConstruct.  Since these objects are normally found indoors, they are all roughly \"human-sized\".  Instances of #$HumanOccupationConstructObject include everything from furniture  to tools, appliances to artwork, medical examining tables to church altars and pews.")
(disjointWith BrideWalksDownTheAisleAccompaniedByFather BrideAndGroomWalkDownTheAisleWithParents)
(comment VideoClipTypeOfSubjectTypeFn "<code>(#$VideoClipTypeOfSubjectTypeFn SUBJECT-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of #$VideoRecordedObject that depict instance(s) of <code>SUBJECT-TYPE</code>, a type of #$SpatialThing-Localized.")
(comment videoClipTypeOfSubjectType "The predicate corresponding to #$VideoClipTypeOfSubjectTypeFn, <code>(#$videoClipTypeOfSubjectType VIDEO-TYPE SUBJECT-TYPE)</code> identifies <code>VIDEO-TYPE</code> as the collection of instances of #$VideoRecordedObject that depict instance(s) of <code>SUBJECT-TYPE</code>, a type of #$SpatialThing-Localized.")
(comment maxCardinalityOfRolePlayersOfTypeInSubSituationType "<code>(#$maxCardinalityOfRolePlayersOfTypeInSubSituationType SIT-TYPE COL SUB-SIT-TYPE ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves sub-situations of type <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code> such that no more than <code>N</code> or more instances of <code>COL</code> play <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment maxCardinalityOfRolePlayersOfTypeInSituationType "<code>(#$maxCardinalityOfRolePlayersOfTypeInSituationType SIT-TYPE COL ROLE N)</code> means that a situation of type <code>SIT-TYPE</code> always involves no more than <code>N</code> instances of <code>COL</code> play <code>ROLE</code>.")
(comment Chuppah "A specialization of #$CanopyTheShelter used traditionally in Jewish weddings -- the bride and groom stand inside the chuppah while they exchange vows.")
(comment ReadingOfTheKetubah "The reading aloud of the married couple's marriage contract, done as part of a traditional Jewish wedding ceremony.")
(comment Exocytosis "The collection of #$VesicularTransportEvents in which the destination is a #$CellMembrane. Nearly all instances initiate at the #$GolgiApparatus, and all result in the secretion of substances into the #$ExtracellularMatrix and the addition of the #$VesicleMembrane material to the #$CellMembrane.")
(comment mSSystemStandardName "(#$mSSystemStandardName M&SSYSTEM NAMESTRING) means that NAMESTRING is the standard or official name by which the #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem M&SSYSTEM is designated.")
(comment mSSystemStandardAcronym "(#$mSSystemStandardAcronym M&SSYSTEM ACRONYM) means that ACRONYM is the standard or official acronym by which the #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem M&SSYSTEM is designated.")
(comment mSSystemTextDescription "(#$mSSystemTextDescription M&SSYSTEM DESCRIPTION) means that DESCRIPTION is a textual description of the #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem M&SSYSTEM.")
(disjointWith SalicylateAnalgesic Opioid)
(disjointWith SalicylateAnalgesic NonSalicylateAnalgesic)
(comment SalicylateAnalgesic "Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which include compounds based on salicylic acid.  The most notable member of this group is aspirin, aka #$AcetylsalicylicAcid).")
(comment AnalgesicWithNarcoticAndSalicylate "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) of some #$NarcoticAnalgesic and some #$SalicylateAnalgesic.")
(comment AnalgesicWithNarcoticAndNSAID "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) of some #$NarcoticAnalgesic and some #$NonSteroidalAntiInflammatory.")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-1stGenerationAntihistamine-DecongestantCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive an #$Antihistamine-FirstGeneration, and a #$Decongestant. The resulting drug has properties of all three. ")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-ExpectorantCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive and an #$Expectorant. The resulting drug has properties of both. ")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-Decongestant-ExpectorantCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive,  a #$Decongestant and an #$Expectorant. The resulting drug has properties of all three. ")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-Decongestant-Analgesic-ExpectorantCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive,  a #$Decongestant, a non-narcotic #$Analgesic and an #$Expectorant. The resulting drug has properties of all four. ")
(comment AnticholinergicDrug "The collection of all drugs with anticholinergic properties.  #$AnticholinergicDrugs operate by blocking the binding of #$Acetylcholine to its receptors in the #$NervousSystem. ")
(comment NarcoticAntitussive-AnticholinergicCombo "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances are mixtures (see #$DrugCocktail) containing a #$NarcoticAntitussive  and an #$AnticholinergicDrug. The resulting drug has properties of both. ")
(comment NarcoticAnalgesicPlusDietarySupplement "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances which are mixtures of some #$NarcoticAnalgesic and some #$DietarySupplement.")
(comment NarcoticPlusSalicylateAnalgesic-Barbiturate-XanthineCombination "An #$FDBCombinationTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances which are mixtures of some #$NarcoticAnalgesic, some #$SalicylateAnalgesic, some #$Barbiturate and some xanthine derivative.")
(comment NonNarcoticAnalgesic "An #$FDBSpecificTherapeuticClassType. Instances are collections of drug substances with analgesic (pain-relieving) properties, which typically are or contain as an ingredient some #$DrugSubstance which is not an #$OpioidDrug.")
(comment Tablet-Ingestible "The collection of all #$Pills in tablet form.  An instance of #$Tablet-Ingestible is a solid #$Pill, in which some #$ConsumableProduct such as a #$DrugSubstance or #$DietarySupplement is mixed with a binder and compressed to make a hard, swallowable object.  Note that while all instances of #$Tablet-Ingestible have as constituents substances that can be consumed, some - effervescent tablets in particular (see #$TabletEffervescent) - are not intended to be swallowed as is but should be dissolved in water first.")
(comment ExtendedReleaseTablet-DurationUnspecified "The collection of all tablets with extended-release properties for which the duration of release is unknown or not specified.  The contents of these tablets are released into the body over some unspecified, measured interval of time.")
(comment ExtendedReleaseTablet-12Hour "The collection of all tablets with extended-release properties which release their contents within the body over a period of about 12 hours.  Therefore, to maintain a therapeutic level within the body medicines with this dosage form are typically taken twice a day.")
(comment ExtendedReleaseTablet-24Hour "The collection of all tablets with extended-release properties which release their contents within the body over a period of about 24 hours.  Therefore, to maintain a therapeutic level within the body medicines with this dosage form are typically taken once a day.")
(comment ExtendedReleaseTablet-Multiphase24Hour "The collection of all tablets with both immedate-release and extended-release properties which release their contents within the body over a period of about 24 hours. ")
(comment Tablet-RapidDissolving "The collection of all #$Tablet-Ingestible instances which are soluble, and which are designed to dissolve rapidly.")
(comment electromagneticRadiationInteractionEnergySignature "<code>(#$electromagneticRadiationInteractionEnergySignature INTERACTION INCIDENT ABSORBED REFLECTED TRANSMITTED)</code> states that, in the instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiationInteractingWithMatter, <code>INTERACTION</code>, <code>INCIDENT</code> is the amount of energy striking the #$PartiallyTangible which is the #$objectActedOn in <code>INTERACTION</code>, and <code>ABSORBED</code>, <code>REFELCTED</code> and <code>TRANSMITTED</code>, respectively, are the amounts of energy which are absorbed, reflected and transmitted.")
(comment ActiveBarrierTransport "The collection of all instances of #$SelectiveBarrierTransport wherein the #$itemAdmitted moves from the #$regionOfLowConcentration of an associated #$ConcentrationGradient to the #$regionOfHighConcentration of that same gradient (see #$transportedUpAGradientIn).")
(comment passiveTransportOfSingleGranuleOfTypeFromTo "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of 
#$PassiveTransportOfSingleGranuleOfTypeFromToFn.  (#$passiveTransportOfSingleGranuleOfTypeFromTo OBJECT-TYPE FROM-LOC TO-LOC TRANSPORT-TYPE) means that TRANSPORT-TYPE is the class of all instances of #$PassiveBarrierTransport wherein exactly one instance of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE is passively transported across the #$selectiveBarrier from the location FROM-LOC to the location TO-LOC.")
(comment NetPassiveTransportsOfGranulesOfTypeFromToFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$NetPassiveTransportsOfGranulesOfTypeFromToFn OBJECT-TYPE MOSTLY-FROM-REGION MOSTLY-TO-REGION) denotes the class of all #$PassiveBarrierTransports wherein some granules of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE passively cross the #$selectiveBarrier from MOSTLY-FROM-REGION to MOSTLY-TO-REGION and some granules of OBJECT-TYPE cross from the MOSTLY-TO-REGION to the MOSTLY-FROM-REGION, and more granules cross from MOSTLY-FROM-REGION to MOSTLY-TO-REGION than cross from MOSTLY-TO-REGION to MOSTLY-FROM-REGION.")
(comment solutionIsotonicFor "(#$solutionIsotonicFor SOLUTION CELL) means that, if CELL is immersed in SOLUTION, a situation will result wherein passive diffusion of water molecules across the cell membrane from the interior to the exterior of the cell will be in equilibrium with passive diffusion of water molecules across the membrane from the cellular exterior to the cellular interior.")
(comment solutionHypotonicFor "(#$solutionHypotonicFor SOLUTION CELL) means that, if CELL is immersed in SOLUTION, a situation will result wherein the number of water molecules that passively diffuse across the cell membrane from the interior to the exterior of the cell exceeds the number of water molecules that passively diffuse across the membrane from the cellular exterior to the cellular interior.")
(comment solutionHypertonicFor "(#$solutionHypertonicFor SOLUTION CELL) means that, if CELL is immersed in SOLUTION, a situation will result wherein the number of water molecules that passively diffuse across the cel membrane from the exterior to the interior of the cell exceeds the number of water molecules that passively diffuse across the membrane from the cellular interior to the cellular exterior.")
(comment PassiveBarrierTransport "The collection of all instances of #$SelectiveBarrierTransport wherein the #$itemAdmitted moves from the #$regionOfHighConcentration of an associated #$ConcentrationGradient to the #$regionOfLowConcentration of that same gradient (see #$transportedDownAGradientIn).")
(comment PassiveTransportOfStuffTypeFn "A collection-denoting function.  Where the collection STUFF-TYPE is an #$ExistingStuffType, (#$PassiveTransportOfStuffTypeFn STUFF-TYPE) denotes the collection of every instance of #$PassiveBarrierTransport such that STUFF-TYPE is the #$stuffTypeAdmitted.  Intuitively, (#$PassiveTransportOfStuffTypeFn STUFF-TYPE) is the class of all #$PassiveBarrierTransports wherein some instances of STUFF-TYPE is the #$itemAdmitted through the #$selectiveBarrier. (#$PassiveTransportOfStuffTypeFn STUFF-TYPE) includes cases where instances of STUFF-TYPE are transported bidirectionally across the barrier.")
(comment passiveTransportOfStuffType "The corresponding predicate of #$PassiveTransportOfStuffTypeFn.  Where the collection STUFF-TYPE is an #$ExistingStuffType, (#$passiveTransportOfStuffType STUFF-TYPE TRANSPORT-TYPE) means that TRANSPORT-TYPE is the collection of every instance of #$PassiveBarrierTransport such that STUFF-TYPE is the #$stuffTypeAdmitted.")
(comment PassiveTransportOfSingleGranuleOfTypeFromToFn "A collection-denoting function.  (#$PassiveTransportOfSingleGranuleOfTypeFromToFn OBJECT-TYPE FROM-LOC TO-LOC) denotes the class of all instances of #$PassiveBarrierTransport wherein exactly one instance of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE is passively transported across the #$selectiveBarrier from the location FROM-LOC to the location TO-LOC.")
(comment allNetPassiveTransportsOfGranulesOfTypeFromTo "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of  #$NetPassiveTransportsOfGranulesOfTypeFromToFn.  (#$allNetPassiveTransportsOfGranulesOfTypeFromTo OBJECT-TYPE MOSTLY-FROM-REGION MOSTLY-TO-REGION TRANSPORT-TYPE) means that TRANSPORT-TYPE is the class of all #$PassiveBarrierTransports wherein some granules of the #$ExistingObjectType OBJECT-TYPE passively cross the #$selectiveBarrier from MOSTLY-FROM-REGION to MOSTLY-TO-REGION and some granules of OBJECT-TYPE cross from the MOSTLY-TO-REGION to the MOSTLY-FROM-REGION, and more granules cross from MOSTLY-FROM-REGION to MOSTLY-TO-REGION than cross from MOSTLY-TO-REGION to MOSTLY-FROM-REGION.")
(comment FossilFuelConsumption "A specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess. Instances include events in which fossil fuels are used by humans for satisfying their energy needs.")
(comment ReturnOfExcitedChlorophyllMoleculeToGroundState "A specialization of #$ChemicalObjectExcitedStateDecay. Instances include events in which an excited #$Chlorophyll returns to its ground state.  ")
(comment mSSystemKeyWords "(#$mSSystemKeyWords M&SSYSTEM KEYWORD) means that KEYWORD is a commonly-used key word for referencing the #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem M&SSYSTEM.")
(comment DoingAnArithmeticOperation "The collection of all calculations, which are events in which an arithmetic result is derived. A type of #$DoingMath and #$HumanActivity. The collection #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation is an #$AccomplishmentType and a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment SolvingProblemOfTypeFn "<code>(#$SolvingProblemOfTypeFn PROBLEM-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of events in which an agent devises a solution to a problem of type <code>PROBLEM-TYPE</code>.")
(comment solvingProblemOfType "<code>(#$solvingProblemOfType PROBLEM-TYPE SOLVING)</code> means <code>SOLVING</code> is the collection of events in which an agent devises a solution to a problem of type <code>PROBLEM-TYPE</code>.")
(comment CalculatingTotalTabWithTip "A specialization of #$SolvingAProblem.  Each instance of #$CalculatingTotalTabWithTip is an event in which someone calculates the amount of a total tab as the sum of the base amount with a tip.")
(comment SubEventTypeOfTypeFn "<code>(#$SubEventTypeOfTypeFn SUPER-TYPE SUB-TYPE)</code> denotes the collection of instances of <code>SUB-TYPE</code> that are sub-events of some instance of <code>SUPER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment subEventTypeOfType "<code>(#$subEventTypeOfType SUPER-TYPE SUB-TYPE SUB-TYPE-SPEC)</code> means that <code>SUB-TYPE-SPEC</code> is the collection of instances of <code>SUB-TYPE</code> that are sub-events of some instance of <code>SUPER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment coveringOfEvent-Nonoverlapping "<code>(#$coveringOfEventType-Nonoverlapping EVT LIST-OF-EVTS)</code> means that: <p> (1) each element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> is a proper sub-situation of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (2) there is no further sub-situation of <code>EVT</code> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some some element of<code> LIST-OF-EVTS</code>; <p> (3) the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> starts at the starting of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (4) after the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code>, each subsequent element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> starts after the end of the instance of the prior element in <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code>.")
(comment coveringOfEvent "<code>(#$coveringOfEventType EVT LIST-OF-EVTS)</code> means that: <p> (1) each element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> is a proper sub-situation of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (2) there is no further sub-situation of <code>EVT</code> that is not spatiotemporally subsumed by some some element of<code> LIST-OF-EVTS</code>; <p> (3) the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> starts at the starting of <code>EVT</code>; <p> (4) after the first element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code>, each subsequent element of <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code> starts after the start of the instance of the prior element in <code>LIST-OF-EVTS</code>.")
(comment DoingDivision "The collection of all mathematical division. A type of #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation. #$DoingDivision is a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment dividendInDivision "(#$dividendInDivision DIVISION DIVIDEND) means that DIVIDEND is the dividend in the #$DoingDivision, DIVISION.")
(comment divisor "(#$divisor DIVISION DIVISOR) means that DIVISOR is the divisor in the #$DoingDivision, DIVISION.")
(comment quotient "(#$quotient DIVISION QUOTIENT) means that QUOTIENT is the quotient in the #$DoingDivision, DIVISION.")
(comment factor "(#$factor MULTIPLICATION FACTOR) means that FACTOR is a factor in the #$DoingMultiplication, MULTIPLICATION.")
(comment productOfMultiplication "(#$productOfMultiplication MULTIPLICATION PRODUCT) means that PRODUCT is the product in the #$DoingMultiplication, MULTIPLICATION.")
(comment addend "(#$addend ADDITION ADDEND) means that ADDEND is an addend in the #$DoingAddition, ADDITION.")
(comment sum "(#$sum ADDITION SUM) means that SUM is the sum in the #$DoingAddition, ADDITION.")
(comment solutionDevised "(#$solutionDevised SOLVING-PROBLEM SOLUTION) means that SOLUTION is the solution devised to the problem addressed in the #$SolvingAProblem, SOLVING-PROBLEM.")
(comment pharmaceuticalSpecificTherapeuticClass "(#$pharmaceuticalSpecificTherapeuticClass PHARM-TYPE STC) means that PHARM-TYPE is in the theraupeutic class, STC.")
(comment pharmaceuticalSKSpecificTherapeuticClass "(#$pharmaceuticalSKSpecificTherapeuticClass PHARM-TYPE STC) means that the SK classification places PHARM-TYPE in the theraupeutic class, STC.")
(comment pharmaceuticalGC3Code "(#$pharmaceuticalGC3Code PHARM-TYPE GC3) means that PHARM-TYPE has the GC3 code, GC3.")
(comment pharmaceuticalSKClassCode "(#$pharmaceuticalSKClassCode PHARM-TYPE SK) means that PHARM-TYPE has the SK specific class code, SK.")
(comment simulationIncludesEmulatingSituationOfType "(#$simulationIncludesEmulatingSituationOfType SIM SIT-TYPE) means that the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM includes a proper sub-situation (#$properSubSituations) SUB-SIM such that SUB-SIM is also a #$ModelBasedSimulation and emulates (#$simulationEmulatesSituationOfType) a situation of type SIT-TYPE.")
(comment membraneSurface-Role "<code>#$membraneSurface-Role CONF SURFACE)</code> means that in the #$MembraneSidedness-Configuration <code>CONF</code>, <code>SURFACE</code> is one of the membrane surfaces in the bilayer configuration.")
(comment situationOccursOnSurface "<code>(#$situationOccursOnSurface SIT SURF)</code> means that for at least one individual <code>IND</code> such that <code>( #$situationConstituents SIT IND)</code> holds,  <code>(#$touches IND SURF)</code>.")
(comment situationOccursOnSurface-Tangible "<code>(#$situationOccursOnSurface-Tangible SIT SURF)</code> means that for at least one individual <code>IND</code> such that <code>( #$situationConstituents SIT IND)</code> holds,  <code>(#$touches IND SURF)</code>. Any such situation therefore either is a #$PhysicalContactSituation or has one as a #$subSituations.")
(comment equationFormFor "<code>(#$equationFormFor THING EQUATION)</code> means that <code>EQUATION</code> is the form of a mathematical equation that describes important characteristics of <code>THING</code>.  For example, if <code>THING</code> is a physical principle, such as #$NewtonsSecondLaw, then that law, as it is commonly expressed, corresponds to the equation <code>F=ma</code>, where <code>F</code> is the sum of the forces acting on an object, <code>m</code> is its mass and <code>a</code> is its acceleration, so the following is true:  <br> <code>  (equationFormFor             NewtonsSecondLaw                   (numericallyEquals                       (The ForceVector)                 (TimesFn  (The LinearAccelerationVector) (The Mass))))  </code> .")
(comment secondSubEvents "A #$SubEventPredicate that is a specialization of #$properSubEvents (q.v.). (#$secondSubEvents EVENT SECOND) means that SECOND is the second step of EVENT.  That is, SECOND is a proper subevent of EVENT that starts after the first subevent of EVENT. ")
(comment thirdSubEvents "A #$SubEventPredicate that is a specialization of #$properSubEvents (q.v.). (#$thirdSubEvents EVENT THIRD) means that THIRD is the third step of EVENT.  That is, THIRD is a proper subevent of EVENT that starts after the second  subevent of EVENT. ")
(comment cardinalityOfEventSteps "(#$cardinalityOfEventSteps EVENT N) means that a covering of EVENT (see #$coveringOfEvent).")
(comment mathematicalResult "(#$mathematicalResult MATH RESULT) means that RESULT is the result of MATH.  For example, if MATH is #$DoingMultiplication, RESULT is the product.")
(comment mathematicalInput "(#$mathematicalInput MATH INPUT) means that INPUT is an input to MATH.  For example, if MATH is #$DoingMultiplication, INPUT is one of the factors.")
(comment termForOperation "(#$termForOperation  EVENT TERM) means that the solution to EVENT can be determined by evaluating TERM.")
(comment ThirdInListFn "(#$ThirdInListFn LIST) returns the second element of LIST.  For example, (#$ThirdInListFn (#$TheList #$Dog #$Cat #$Horse)) returns #$Horse.")
(comment addend-First "(#$addend-First ADDITION ADDEND) means that ADDEND is in some sense the \"first\" addend in the #$DoingAddition, ADDITION.  It may be considered \"first\" simply to distinguish it from other addends.  Cf. #$addend-Second.")
(comment addend-Second "(#$addend-Second ADDITION ADDEND) means that ADDEND is in some sense the \"second\" addend in the #$DoingAddition, ADDITION.  It may be considered \"second\" simply to distinguish it from other addends.  Cf. #$addend-First.")
(comment factor-Second "(#$factor-Second MULT FACTOR) means that FACTOR is in some sense the \"second\" factor in the #$DoingMultiplication, MULT.  It may be considered \"second\" simply to distinguish it from other factors.  Cf. #$factor-First.")
(comment factor-First "(#$factor-First MULT FACTOR) means that FACTOR is in some sense the \"first\" factor in the #$DoingMultiplication, MULT.  It may be considered \"first\" simply to distinguish it from other factors.  Cf. #$factor-Second.")
(comment nestingOfSubOperatonTerms "(#$nestingOfSubOperatonTerms SOLVING NESTED-TERM) means that one way to calculate a devised solution to the problem addressed in SOLVING is by evaluating NESTED-TERM.  It is assumed that all of the terms of the subproblems of SOLVING (see #$termForOperation) are nested to produce NESTED-TERM.")
(comment gratuityRate "(#$gratuityRate GIVE GRAT-RATE) means that in the #$GivingAGratuity, GIVE, the rate of the gratuity is GRAT-RATE.")
(comment GratuityPercent "A specialization of #$IntervalOnNumberLine.   A #$GratuityPercent is a rate that can be specified as the value of #$gratuityRate applied during an instance of #$GivingAGratuity.")
(comment BaseBillAmount "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue.   A #$BaseBillAmount is the amount of a bill before such things as tax and tip are added to it.")
(comment BillAmountIncludingGratuity "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue.   A #$BillAmountIncludingGratuity is the amount of a bill that is equivalent to the base bill amount (see #$BaseBillAmount) plus the tip.")
(comment GratuityAmount "A specialization of #$MonetaryValue.   A #$GratuityAmount is the amount of a gratuity that is added to a #$BaseBillAmount to result in the #$BillAmountIncludingGratuity.")
(comment Chemiosmosis-Chloroplast "A specialization of #$Chemiosmosis.  In  instances of #$Chemiosmosis-Chloroplast, the movement of #$HydrogenPlusIons down their concentration gradient from the #$ThylakoidSpace to the #$ChloroplastStroma powers the synthesis of ATP (#$AdenosineTriphosphate).")
(comment TransferOfHydrogenPlusIonsFromThylakoidLumenToStroma "A specialization of #$MembraneTransportOfHydrogenPlusIon.  Each instance of #$TransferOfHydrogenPlusIonsFromThylakoidLumenToStroma is an event in which H   ions are transferred from the #$ThylakoidSpace to the #$ChloroplastStroma. These events play an important role in ATP synthesis.")
(comment Photophosphorylation-Chloroplast "A specialization of #$BiochemicalPathway. In an instance of #$Photophosphorylation-Chloroplast, the energy of sunlight is used to produce ATP.  ")
(comment TransferOfHydrogenPlusIonsIntoThylakoidLumen "A specialization of #$MembraneTransportOfHydrogenPlusIon.  Each instance of #$TransferOfHydrogenPlusIonsIntoThylakoidLumen is an event in which H   ions are pumped into thylakoid lumen during photosysthesis.")
(comment ATPProductionByATPSynthase "The collection of all events in which a phosphate group is added to #$AdenosineDiphosphate, forming #$AdenosineTriphosphate, by an #$ATPSynthaseMolecule as a part of #$OxidativePhosphorylation or #$Photophosphorylation-Chloroplast.")
(comment NonRenewaleSourceOfEnergy "It is the collection of all nonrenewable sources of energy.")
(comment RenewableSourceOfEnergy "It is the collection of all renewable sources of energy.")
(comment Mass-CatholicChurchService "The collection of instances of #$ChurchService held by Catholic churches.")
(comment BreakingOfTheGlass-WeddingRitual "The reading aloud of the married couple's marriage contract, done as part of a traditional Jewish wedding ceremony.")
(comment WeddingMass "A kind of ritual mass, in which a wedding is held.")
(comment pharmaceuticalDEACode "(#$pharmaceuticalDEACode PHARM-TYPE CODE) means that PHARM-TYPE has the DEA code (a one-character string indicating scheduling according to the US Controlled Substances Act), CODE.")
(comment USControlledDrugProductTypeBySchedule "A third-order collection.  Each instance of #$USControlledDrugProductTypeBySchedule is a collection of types of pharmaceutical products (a collection of collections of drug products) listed on one of five particular schedules of US Code.  These schedules were established by the Controlled Substances Act in 1970, and are amended by the #$DrugEnforcementAdministration and the #$FoodAndDrugAdministration.")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActScheduleIDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are placed on Schedule I by the US Controlled Substances Act (See #$USControlledSubstanceScheduleI).  Placement on this schedule means it is illegal to make, sell, possess or use such drug products.")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActScheduleIIIDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are placed on Schedule III by the US Controlled Substances Act or by subsequent action of the #$DrugEnforcementAdministration and/or #$FoodAndDrugAdministration (See #$USControlledSubstanceScheduleIII).  ")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActScheduleVDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are placed on Schedule V by the US Controlled Substances Act or by subsequent action of the #$DrugEnforcementAdministration and/or #$FoodAndDrugAdministration (See #$USControlledSubstanceScheduleV).  ")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActScheduleIIDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are placed on Schedule II by the US Controlled Substances Act or by subsequent action of the #$DrugEnforcementAdministration and/or #$FoodAndDrugAdministration (See #$USControlledSubstanceScheduleII).  ")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActScheduleIVDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are placed on Schedule IV by the US Controlled Substances Act or by subsequent action of the #$DrugEnforcementAdministration and/or #$FoodAndDrugAdministration (See #$USControlledSubstanceScheduleIV).  ")
(comment USControlledSubstancesActUnscheduledDrugProductType "Instances are drug products which are not on any of the five schedules established by the US Controlled Substances Act.  ")
(comment ConvertingAPercentageValueToADecimalValue "A specialization of #$SolvingAProblem and #$DoingMath. Each instance of #$ConvertingAPercentageValueToADecimalValue is an event in which someone converts a percentage value to a decimal value.")
(comment FormulaForMathematicalProcessFn "(#$FormulaForMathematicalProcessFn PROCESS) denotes the formula for calculating the result of perfoming an instance of PROCESS.")
(comment formulaForMathematicalProcess "(#$formulaForMathematicalProcessFn PROCESS FORMULA) means FORMULA is the formula for calculating the result of perfoming an instance of PROCESS.")
(comment billAmount "(#$billAmount BILL AMOUNT) means that the amount of compensation requested by BILL is AMOUNT.")
(comment billWithGratuityAmount "(#$billWithGratuityAmount BILL AMOUNT) means that the amount of compensation requested by BILL plus a gratuity is AMOUNT.")
(comment billGratuityAmount "(#$billGratuityAmount BILL AMOUNT) means that the amount of gratuity paid with BILL is AMOUNT.")
(comment billGratuityPercent "(#$billGratuityPercent BILL GRAT-PERCENT) means that the percentage of the gratuity to be paid with BILL is GRAT-PERCENT.")
(comment sustainsStaticSituation "<code>(#$sustainsStaticSituation SUSTAINER SUSTAINED)</code>
means that <code>SUSTAINER</code> is at least in part responsible for
maintaining the static situation <code>SUSTAINED</code>.")
(comment sustainsStaticSituation-TypeType "#$sustainsStaticSituation-TypeType is the type-level
correlate of
#$sustainsStaticSituation. <code>(#$sustainsStaticSituation-TypeType
SUSTAINER-TYPE SUSTAINED-TYPE)</code> means that every static
situation of type <code>SUSTAINED-TYPE</code> is maintained by some
instance of <code>SUSTAINER-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ibtReadFrom "<code>(#$ibtReadFrom READING TEXT)</code> means that in the #$ReadingAloud event <code>READING</code>, the #$ibtRead is the #$TextualMaterial <code>TEXT</code>, and the words spoken are those read.")
(comment ibtRead "<code>(#$ibtRead READING TEXT)</code> means that the #$Reading event <code>READING</code> is a reading of the #$TextualMaterial <code>TEXT</code>.")
(comment objectsHeld "<code>(#$objectsHeld HOLDING OBJ)</code> means that the instance <code>OBJ</code> of #$PartiallyTangible is one of the things held in <code>HOLDING</code>, an instance of #$HoldingAnObject.")
(comment ModelExecution "The collection of all physical #$Situations whose characters are at least indirectly determined by #$ModelSpecifications of how the #$Situation in question is to be implemented.")
(comment ModelBasedSimulation "The collection of all instances of #$ModelExecutions wherein the #$modelSpecificationExecuted closely concerns the #$objectOfSimulation of the corresponding #$Simulation-Activity.")
(comment sustainingSimulationActivity "(#$sustainingSimulationActivity SIM SIM-ACT) means that SIM-ACT is the #$Simulation-Activity whereby the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM is maintained as a simulation with respect to its model (#$modelSpecificationExecuted).")
(comment InteractionStrength "The net strength of the forces resulting in a given interaction effect.")
(comment InteractionStrengthFn "<code>(InteractionStrengthFn SIT)</code> denotes the net
strength of the forces which result in a given interaction effect.")
(comment strengthOfInteraction "A #$MeasurableQuantitySlot that relates an interaction event
to its #$InteractionStrength --- the net force which results in the
interaction effect.")
(comment greaterThan-TypeInteractionStrength "<code>(#$greaterThan-TypeInteractionStrength TYPE1
TYPE2)</code> means that the net force
involved (q.v. #$strengthOfInteraction) in any instance of
<code>TYPE1</code> is greater than the net force involved in any
instance of <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment simulationSimulatesSituationOfType "(#$simulationSimulatesSituationOfType SIM SIT-TYPE) means that, while SIM is <i>not</i> itself an instance of SIT-TYPE, it replicates certain causal features of instances of SIT-TYPE which are relevant for purposes of simulation.")
(comment simulationIncludesSimulatingSituationOfType "(#$simulationIncludesSimulatingSituationOfType SIM SUBSIT-TYPE)  means that the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM includes a proper sub-situation (#$properSubSituations) SUB-SIM such that SUB-SIM is also a #$ModelBasedSimulation and such that (#$simulationSimulatesSituationOfType SUB-SIM SUBSIT-TYPE). (#$simulationIncludesSimulatingSituationOfType SIM SUBSIT-TYPE) also has the implication that no instance of SUBSIT-TYPE is in fact a #$properSubSituations of SIM.")
(comment Glassblower "The collection of all glass-blowers. A type of #$TradeWorker. #$Glassblower is a #$PersonTypeByOccupation.")
(comment trajectoriesThroughPassThrough "<code>(#$trajectoriesThroughPassThrough OBJ1 OBJ2)</code>
means that any trajectory passing through <code>OBJ1</code> also
passes through <code>OBJ2</code>.")
(comment trajectoriesThroughTypePassThroughType "<code>(#$trajectoriesThroughTypePassThroughType TYPE1 TYPE2)</code>
means that any trajectory passing through an instance of <code>TYPE1</code> also
passes through and instance of <code>TYPE2</code>.")
(comment likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject "<code>(#$likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject MOL OBJ LIKELIHOOD)</code> means that, under normal conditions, the likelihood of molecule <code>MOL</code> translocating via brownian motion along a trajectory through (roughly from one side to the other) the object <code>OBJ</code> is <code>LIKELIHOOD</code>. See also the type-level correlate #$likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject-TypeType. Note that for most cases where <code>OBJ</code> is not a #$FluidTangibleThing, such motion will be very unlikely.")
(comment likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject-TypeType "<code>(#$likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject-TypeType MOL-TYPE OBJ-TYPE LIKELIHOOD)</code> means that, under normal conditions, the likelihood of an instance of <code>MOL-TYPE</code> translocating via brownian motion along a trajectory through (roughly from one side to the other) an instance of <code>OBJ</code> is <code>LIKELIHOOD</code>. See also the instance-level correlate #$likelihoodOfBrownianMotionThroughObject. Note that for most cases where <code>OBJ</code> is not a #$FluidTangibleThing, such motion will be very unlikely.")
(comment minuend "(#$minuend SUBTRACTION MINUEND) means that MINUEND is the minuend in the #$DoingSubtraction, SUBTRACTION. (A subtraction has the form: minuend - subtrahend = difference.) Cf. #$subtrahend and #$difference.")
(comment subtrahend "(#$subtrahend SUBTRACTION SUBTRAHEND) means that SUBTRAHEND is the subtrahend in the #$DoingSubtraction, SUBTRACTION. (A subtraction has the form: minuend - subtrahend = difference.) Cf. #$minuend and #$difference.")
(comment DoingSubtraction "The collection of all mathematical subtraction. A type of #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation. #$DoingSubtraction is a #$SkilledActivityType.")
(comment TheoryAboutTheMechanismOfPhotosynthesis "A specialization of #$TheoryAboutBiology, this is the collection of all theories about the mechanism of #$Photosynthesis-Generic.")
(comment SplittingOfCarbonDioxide "A Specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In #$SplittingOfCarbonDioxide , #$CarbonDioxide is split into #$Carbon and #$Oxygen. ")
(comment ColoredGold "A specialization of #$MetalAlloy, instances are pieces of metal that are comprised mostly of #$Gold, but alloyed with another substance to obtain a particular color, other than #$GoldColor.")
(comment ritualTypeSignificantSymbolicObjectTypes "<code>(#$ritualTypeSignificantSymbolicObjectTypes RITUAL-TYPE OBJ-TYPE)</code> means that <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> is a type of object that is symbolically signficant for the type of ritual <code>RITUAL-TYPE</code>, so that \"properly executed\" instance of <code>RITUAL-TYPE</code> must include one or more instances of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> in some specific capacity (specified via a #$BinaryRolePredicate when <code>RITUAL-TYPE</code> is represented as a script.")
(comment difference "(#$difference SUBTRACTION DIFF) means that DIFF is the difference in the #$DoingSubtraction, SUBTRACTION. (A subtraction has the form: minuend - subtrahend = difference.) Cf. #$minuend and #$subtrahend.")
(comment RoundingAScalarInterval "The collection of all roundings of scalar intervals. A type of #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation.")
(comment RoundingToInteger "The collection of all roundings of numerical values to integers. A type of #$RoundingAScalarInterval.")
(disjointWith RoundingUp RoundingDown)
(comment RoundingAMonetaryValueToTheNearestWholeMonetaryUnit "A specialization of #$RoundingAScalarInterval. The collection of all roundings of monetary values to the nearest whole monetary unit.")
(comment inputToRounding "(#$inputToRounding ROUNDING SCALAR) means that SCALAR is the value to be rounded in the #$RoundingAScalarInterval, ROUNDING.")
(comment outputOfRounding "(#$inputOfRounding ROUNDING SCALAR) means that SCALAR is the result of the #$RoundingAScalarInterval, ROUNDING.")
(comment RoundingUp "The collection of all roundings of scalar intervals toward plus infinity. A type of #$RoundingAScalarInterval.")
(comment RoundingDown "The collection of all roundings of scalar intervals toward minus infinity. A type of #$RoundingAScalarInterval.")
(comment Exponentiation "The collection of all exponentiations. A type of #$DoingAnArithmeticOperation.")
(comment baseOfExponentiation "(#$baseOfExponentiation EXPONENTIATION SCALAR) means that SCALAR is the base in the #$Exponentiation, EXPONENTIATION.")
(comment exponent "(#$exponent EXPONENTIATION REAL) means that REAL is the exponent in the #$Exponentiation, EXPONENTIATION.")
(comment productOfExponentiation "(#$productOfExponentiation EXPONENTIATION SCALAR) means that SCALAR is the product of the #$Exponentiation, EXPONENTIATION.")
(comment useTypeOfObjectTypeInSimulation "(#$useTypeOfObjectTypeInSimulation SIM USE-TYPE ACTOR-TYPE ROLE) means that in the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM, certain simulation-relevant causal effects of an instance of ACTOR-TYPE playing the role ROLE in an instance of USE-TYPE are duplicated.")
(comment useTypeOfObjectTypeSimulatedInSimulation "(useTypeOfObjectTypeSimulatedInSimulation SIM USE-TYPE ACTOR-TYPE ROLE) means that, while certain simulation-salient causal effects of an instance of ACTOR-TYPE playing ROLE in an instance of USE-TYPE are re-created in the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM, no actual instance of USE-TYPE such that an instance of ACTOR-TYPE plays ROLE in it exists as a subsituation of SIM.")
(comment objectTypeInSimulation "(#$objectTypeInSimulation SIM OBJ-TYPE) means that certain salient causal effects occasioned by a certain kind of use of an instance of OBJ-TYPE appear in and are important in SIM.")
(comment objectTypeSimulated "(#$objectTypeSimulated SIM OBJ-TYPE) means that certain salient types of causal effect that are characteristic of certain kind of use of an instance of OBJ-TYPE are deliberately instantiated in the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM for purposes of study, but that no instance of OBJ-TYPE actually plays any role of any kind in SIM.")
(comment useTypeOfObjectTypeActualInSimulation "(#$useTypeOfObjectTypeActualInSimulation SIM USE-TYPE ACTOR-TYPE ROLE) means that in the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM, certain simulation-relevant causal effects of an instance of ACTOR-TYPE playing the role ROLE in an instance of USE-TYPE are duplicated in virtue of *actually having* a subsituation of type USE-TYPE occur wherein a real instance of ACTOR-TYPE plays the role ROLE.")
(comment objectTypeUsedInSimulation "(#$objectTypeUsedInSimulation SIM OBJ-TYPE) means that an instance of OBJ-TYPE plays the role of #$instrument-Generic in the #$ModelBasedSimulation SIM.")
(comment claimOfPatient "(#$claimOfPatient CLAIM PATIENT) means that the claim filed in the #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim, CLAIM is filed for goods or services provided top PATIENT.")
(comment Vasoconstrictor "The collection of all vasoconstrictors. The collection #$Vasoconstrictor a #$TherapeuticClassType.")
(comment Mucolytic "Drugs which are used to dissolve mucus.")
(comment constrainedRole "The predicate that corresponds to #$ConstrainedRoleFn, <code>(#$constrainedRole CONS-ROLE TYPE ROLE)</code> identifies <code>CONS-ROLE</code> as the specialization of <code>ROLE</code> that is restricted to apply to instances of <code>TYPE</code> in its arg2.")
(comment ConstrainedRoleFn "<code>(#$ConstrainedRoleFn TYPE ROLE)</code> denotes the instance of #$ConstrainedBinaryRolePredicate <code>PRED</code> that is a restriction on the possible arg2 values of <code>ROLE</code> to instances of <code>TYPE</code>.")
(comment constrainableRoles "<code>(#$constrainableRoles SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that there are (possibly unreified) facetings of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> into sub-collections, where those subcollections may differ with respect to what types are possible #$arg2SometimesIsa constraints on <code>ROLE</code>.  For example, <code>(#$constrainableRoles #$WeddingEvent-Entire #$weddingOfficiant)</code> means that there are subcollections of #$WeddingEvent-Entire that differ in terms of the kind of officiant (e.g., #$Rabbi, #$Priest, etc.).")
(comment applicableConstrainedRoles "<code>(#$applicableConstrainedRoles SIT-TYPE ROLE)</code> means that the instance <code>ROLE</code> of #$ConstrainedBinaryRolePredicate can be substituted in place of its unconstrained generalization (i.e., the value of <code>GENL</code> such that <code>(#$constrainedRole ROLE TYPE GENL)</code>) in all (non-opaque) propositions about <code>SIT-TYPE</code> or any instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> without a change in truth-value.")
(comment typicalLocationTypeOfActorInEventType "<code>(#$typicalLocationTypeOfActorInEventType SIT-TYPE ROLE LOC-TYPE)</code> means that in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> the typical location of objects playing <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, is at an instance of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(comment typicalLocationTypeOfObjTypeInEventType "<code>(#$typicalLocationTypeOfObjTypeInEventType SIT-TYPE OBJ-TYPE LOC-TYPE)</code> means that in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> the typical location of instances of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code> involved in (are #$situationConstituents in) <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, is at an instance of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(comment ConstrainedBinaryRolePredicate "The collection of instances of #$BinaryRolePredicate <code>ROLE</code> that are more restrictive in their #$arg2SometimesIsa than their unconstrained generalizations (i.e., than their generalization <code>GENL</code> such that <code>(#$constrainedRole ROLE TYPE GENL)</code> for some value of <code>TYPE</code>).")
(comment SplittingOfHydrogenSulfide "A Specialization of #$ChemicalReaction. In #$SplittingOfHydrogenSulfide , #$HydrogenSulfide is split into #$Hydrogen and #$Sulfur. ")
(comment MelvinCalvin "An American chemist known for discovering #$CalvinCycle.")
(comment TreeBranch "The collection of all tree branches (which ordinarily make up the canopy of a #$Tree-ThePlant). A type of #$PlantPart, #$LongThinObject, #$ExternalAnatomicalPart, and #$Protrusion. The concept #$TreeBranch is a #$PlantPartType and a #$SpatiallyDisjointObjectType.")
(comment typicalLocationTypeOfActorInSubEventType "<code>(#$typicalLocationTypeOfActorInSubEventType SIT-TYPE SUB-SIT-TYPE ROLE LOC-TYPE)</code> means that in instances of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> the typical location of objects playing <code>ROLE</code> in instances of <code>SUB-SIT-TYPE</code>, is at an instance of <code>LOC-TYPE</code>.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC TentlikeShelter)
(disjointWith Building TentlikeShelter)
(comment systemOfEnterprise "(#$systemOfEnterprise ENT SYSTEM) means that ENT is the #$DODEnterpriseProgram which is the primary reason for, and 'life process' of, the #$AgentAndInstrumentSystem SYSTEM.")
(comment AgentAndInstrumentSystemByControllingAuthority "A #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType faceting #$AgentAndInstrumentSystem.  Each collection instance is a collection of #$AgentAndInstrumentSystems with a common operational controlling authority.")
(comment AgentAndInstrumentSystemOperationallyControlledByFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent, (#$AgentAndInstrumentSystemOperationallyControlledByFn AGT) denotes the collection of all #$AgentAndInstrumentSystems that AGT operationally controls.")
(comment allAgentAndInstrumentSystemsOperationallyControlledBy "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$AgentAndInstrumentSystemOperationallyControlledByFn. Where AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent, (#$allAgentAndInstrumentSystemsOperationallyControlledBy AGT SYS-TYPE) means tha SYS-TYPE is the collection of all #$AgentAndInstrumentSystems that AGT operationally controls.")
(comment ModelingAndSimulationSystemByControllingAuthority "A #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType faceting #$ModelingAndSimulationSystem.  Each collection instance is a collection of #$ModelingAndSimulationSystems with a common operational controlling authority.")
(comment ModelingAndSimulationSystemOperationallyControlledByFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Where AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent, (#$ModelingAndSimulationSystemOperationallyControlledByFn AGT) denotes the collection of all ModelingAndSimulationSystems that AGT operationally controls.")
(comment allMSSystemsControlledBy "The corresponding predicate (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical) of #$ModelingAndSimulationSystemOperationallyControlledByFn. Where AGT is an #$IntelligentAgent, (#$allMSSystemsControlledBy AGT SYS-TYPE) means that SYS-TYPE is the collection of all #$ModelingAndSimulationSystems that AGT operationally controls.")
(comment OralSurgeon "The collection of all oral surgeons. A type of #$Dentist.")
(comment EyeCareProfessional "A specialization of #$Doctor-Medical.  Specializations include #$Optometrist and #$Ophthalmologist.")
(comment NaturopathicDoctor "A specailization of #$MedicalCareProfessional.  Instances of #$NaturopathicDoctor are doctors that specialize in naturopathy.")
(comment prescriberAssociatedWithClaim "(#$prescriberAssociatedWithClaim CLAIM PROVIDER) means that the claim filed in the #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim, CLAIM is filed for a prescription that was prescribed by PROVIDER.")
(comment providerAssociatedWithClaim "(#$providerAssociatedWithClaim CLAIM PROVIDER) means that the claim filed in the #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim, CLAIM is filed for service rendered by PROVIDER.")
(comment FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim "A specialization of #$FilingAnInsuranceClaim.  Each instance of #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim is an action of filing a claim against an insurance company for the purchase of a prescription drug.")
(comment pharmaceuticalOfClaim "(#$pharmaceuticalOfClaim CLAIM PHARM-TYPE) means that in the claim filed in the #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim, CLAIM is filed for the pharmaceutical type PHARM-TYPE.")
(comment claimHasPrescriberWithNPI "(#$claimHasPrescriberWithNPI CLAIM STRING) means that in the claim filed in the #$FilingAHealthInsuranceClaim, CLAIM is filed for services rendered by a provider whose NPI is STRING.")
(comment FerredoxinNADPPlusReductase "An specialization of #$EnzymeMolecule.  Instances are molecules which catalyze the transfer of an electron from #$Ferredoxin to #$NicotinamideAdenineDinucleotidePhosphate.")
(comment KAObjectType "A #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType whose collection instances are salient types of #$KATemplateObject.")
(comment kAObjectTypeCurrentStateComputingAssertion "A #$DistributingMetaKnowledgePredicate used to link salient classes of #$KATemplateObject (salient #$KAObjectTypes) to the rules that determine how updating works for instances of those classes.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (negationPreds runningMates opponentsInConflict)) "Generalize this.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (isa shareholders IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate)) "A company can \"buy back\" shares of its stock from a stockholder; but the company is <i>not</i> thereby a shareholder of itself.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (genls SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality SpatialThingTypeByShape))) "dimensionality is orthogonal to shape.  E.g., something that is an instance of #$NotVeryRoundObject might be 1-Dimentional, 2-Dimensional, or 3-Dimensional. ")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (notAssertibleCollection ELRelation)) "There should be no direct instances of #$ELRelation; use a spec of #$ELRelation instead.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (arg1Isa bank-Role Situation)) "needs something tighter.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (genls GeographicalRegion SpatiallyBoundedThing))) "Though every geographical region has spatial boundaries, the collection #$SpatiallyBoundedThing excludes spatially discontinuous objects.  Currently, #$GeographicalRegion includes objects, such as the territory of the United States of America, whose physical extent is not spatially continuous.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (isa hasBeenNear SymmetricBinaryPredicate))) "This assertion permits #$eventOccursNear to be a spec-inverse of #$hasBeenNear.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (negationPreds isa candidateIsa)) "This is a critical defining feature for #$candidateIsa:  (#$candidateIsa CAND-INST CAND-COL) cannot be mutually asserted with (#$isa CAND-INST CAND-COL) in the same reasoning context.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (genls Communicating InformationTransferEvent))) "The required roles for #$InformationTransferEvent include                                     #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination, which are negation                          preds.                                                                                                                                                                                      If #$Communicating were a spec of #$InformationTransferEvent, #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination would become                       required roles -- so in a group discussion, someone would *have* to play                      the #$informationOrigin role, and that someone could not also play the                        #$informationDestination role.  Similarly, someone would *have* to play                       the #$informationDestination role without playing the #$informationOrigin                      role.                                                                                                                                                                                       <p>By having:                                                                                                                                                                                   <pre>
   (#$genls #$CommunicationAct-Single #$InformationTransferEvent)
   (#$subEventTypes #$Communicating #$CommunicationAct-Single)</pre>                                                                                                                                </code>      we were able to avoid this problem, while maintaining the ability to                          represent that there are #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination                     role-players *during* any communcating event, in the sense that there are                     such role players *in* the individual info-transfers that are parts of the                    communciating event.                                                                                                                                                                        <p>The negation was added to draw cyclists' attention to the problem, to help them avoid succumbing to the temptation of adding the genls link, thereby re-introducing the                          
required roles problem.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (disjointWith AsymmetricBinaryPredicate SymmetricBinaryPredicate))) "Although probably no reified predicate should ever be an instance of both 
#$SymmetricBinaryPredicate and #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate, note that 
these collections are not strictly disjoint.  Since both collections 
are defined with respect to the condition (on a predicate PRED) that 
(PRED THING1 THING2) holds (for a given THING1 and THING2), a binary
predicate with a necessarily empty extension is trivially both 
symmetric and asymmetric.  For example, a predicate that was (aptly)
named 'equalToAndDifferent' would likely be of this sort.  Still, it 
is not clear what practical reason there could be to individually 
represent any such predicate in the Cyc Knowledge Base.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (genls HistoricFigure FamousHuman))) "#$FamousHuman is the collection of instances of #$HomoSapiens (i.e., living humans) who are also instances of #$FamousIndividual.  Though #$HistoricFigure is also a specialization of #$FamousIndividual, many instances of #$HistoricFigure are dead, and many were never famous during their own lifetimes, and so were never instances of #$FamousHuman.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (disjointWith IntelligentAgent VegetableMatter)) "Possible counterexamples: The man-eating plant from \"Little Shop of Horrors\"")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (rewriteOf FormulaRuleTemplate (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn FormulaTemplate querySpecificationForFormulaTemplate CycLRuleQuerySpecification))) "This defines #$FormulaRuleTemplate to be simply the collection of all #$FormulaTemplates that have #$CycLRuleSpecifications as their #$querySpecificationForFormulaTemplate.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (typedGenlPreds textualPCWSections textualPCWSubSections))) "For example, the sections of the United States Code (see #$UnitedStatesCode) are sub-works of the chapters of the USC, but are not the sections of the chapters of the USC.")
(comment (ist UniversalVocabularyMt (not (genlPreds sksiEquals equals))) "Purposefully not a specPred of #$equals so that inference engine equality reasoning does not apply.")
(genls TentPole Pole-Rod)
(genls PitchingATent (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn Assembling assemblyInputs (PartsFn-Device Tent)))
(genls ChoosingACampsite SelectingSomething)
(genls Tent ShelteringArtifact)
(genls ModalPredicate Predicate)
(genls TemporalObjectType ObjectType)
(genls ChemicalSubstanceType TangibleStuffCompositionType)
(genls EquivalenceRelation SymmetricBinaryPredicate)
(genls PhysiologicalConditionType TemporalStuffType)
